const Map<int, String> _mokhtasar = {
  1000:
      "The Opening (Surah Al-Fatihah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nActualizing complete servitude to Allah the Exalted.\n•    Explanation:    \nSurah Al-Fatihah is called 'The Opening Chapter' because Allah begins the Quran with it. It is also referred to as Umm Al-Quran (Mother of the Quran) because it encompasses the Quran's themes, from the principles of faith to worship, among other matters. It is also called 'The Seven Oft-Repeated Verses.'",
  1001:
      "In the name of Allah the Exalted, I begin reading the Quran, seeking His aid and blessing by invoking His name. The basmalah consists of three of Allah's beautiful names: 1- Allah, meaning the One worthy of worship, and this is the most exclusive of names of Allah the Exalted. 2- Ar-Raḥmān, i.e., the Possessor of all-encompassing mercy, the Most Merciful in His Essence. 3- Ar-Raḥīm, i.e., the Bestower of mercy that reaches all He desires, for He bestows His Mercy upon whomever He wills from His creation, including His believing slaves.",
  1002:
      "Complete praise and all forms of extolment of majesty and perfection belong exclusively to Allah alone; He is the Lord of everything, its Creator, and its Manager. Al-Ālamūn (worlds) is the plural of Al-'Ālam (world) and refers to all in existence other than Allah.",
  1003:
      "Further extolling Allah, the Exalted, that He is the Most Merciful and Compassionate after praising Him in the preceding verse.",
  1004:
      "Glorification of Allah the Transcendent that he is the Owner of everything on the Day of Resurrection when a soul will not possess anything for another. The “Day of Judgment” is the Day of Recompense and Reckoning.",
  1005:
      "We single You out alone in all forms of worship and obedience, and we do not associate anyone with You. We seek help in all of our affairs from You alone, for all virtue belongs with You, and there is no helper other than You.",
  1006:
      "Guide us to the Straight Path, put us firmly upon it, and increase us in guidance. As-Sirat al-Mustaqim is the clear path in which there is no crookedness, and that is Islam, which Allah sent Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم with.",
  1007:
      "The path of those slaves whom You have bestowed with guidance, such as the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the pious, for they are the ones worthy of companionship. [And do not guide us] to the path of those who have earned Your anger after recognizing the Truth and not following it (i.e., the Jews) and not of those who went astray for being neglectful in seeking the Truth and being guided by it (i.e., the Christians).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah starts His scripture with ‘In the name of Allah’, showing us that we should start our actions and speech in this way, asking for His help and His aid.\n2. Surah Al-Fatihah is the greatest surah in the Qur’an, because it contains the rights that belong to Allah only, and explains the way to reach Him.\n3. All gratitude and praise belong to Allah, because He is the Lord of everything: He brought everyone into life; He regulates our lives; and cares for us through His blessings.\n4. The surah shows that faith is perfected through sincerely worshipping Allah and seeking His help alone.\n5. A Muslim needs to be careful about following the path of the People of the Book who earned Allah’s anger and became misled.",
  2000:
      "The Cow (Surah Al-Baqarah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nCommand to establish life on earth by implementing submission and servitude to Allah (i.e., Islam) and warns against the condition of the Israelites.\n•    Explanation:    \nSurah Al-Baqarah is called the Chapter of the Cow because of the mention of the story about the Israelites' cow. The surah's name points to the necessity of hastening to apply Allah's law and avoid stalling as the Jews did.",
  2001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm – letters like these begin certain surahs (chapters) of the Quran. Although separated letters (Alif, Baa, Taa, etc.) of the alphabet have no meaning in and of themselves, they do have wisdom and significance, as there is nothing in the Quran devoid of divine wisdom. Among the significance of these letters is their allusion to the linguistic miracle of the Quran, which comprises letters they know and speak with. Therefore, surahs beginning with letters are usually followed by the mention of the Quran, as we see in this surah.",
  2002:
      "This is the Mighty Quran in which there is nothing of doubt, neither in terms of its origin nor in terms of its words and meaning. It is the word of Allah, guiding those who are mindful of Allah to the path leading to Him.",
  2003:
      "They are those who have faith in that which cannot be perceived through the senses and is hidden from us. However, Allah and His Messengers informed us about these matters, such as the Last Day. They perform the prayer in the manner that Allah legislated: its prerequisites, its pillars, its obligatory, and its highly recommended components. And they spend from that which Allah provided them as obligatory alms (Zakat) or voluntary charity (Ṣadaqah), hoping for Allah's reward. They are the ones who believe in the revelation that Allah sent down upon you, O Muhammad, just as he sent it upon the rest of the prophets (may peace be upon them) before you without prejudice. And they are those who firmly believe in the Hereafter and what it contains from reward and punishment.",
  2004:
      "They are those who have faith in that which cannot be perceived through the senses and is hidden from us. However, Allah and His Messengers informed us about these matters, such as the Last Day. They perform the prayer in the manner that Allah legislated: its prerequisites, its pillars, its obligatory, and its highly recommended components. And they spend from that which Allah provided them as obligatory alms (Zakat) or voluntary charity (Ṣadaqah), hoping for Allah's reward. They are the ones who believe in the revelation that Allah sent down upon you, O Muhammad, just as he sent it upon the rest of the prophets (may peace be upon them) before you without prejudice. And they are those who firmly believe in the Hereafter and what it contains from reward and punishment.",
  2005:
      "The people who possess these characteristics are on the path of guidance and will be successful in this world and the next, attaining their wishes and being saved from what they fear. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an contains conclusive proof that it came from Allah, the Wise, the Knowing.\n2. It is those who are mindful of Allah and glorify Him who benefit from the great guidance within the Qur’an.\n3. Believing in [Al-Ghaib] is one of the greatest degrees of faith, because it means accepting what Allah alone knows about [the Ghaib] and what He has told the Prophet (peace be upon him) about it. Al-Ghaib: literally means the unrealisable i.e. things that are beyond our senses of touch, sight, hearing etc. This includes belief in Allah, Angels, Revealed Scripture, Allah’s messengers. Day of Recompense, and Al-Qadar (divine pre-ordainments). It also includes what Allah and His Messenger informed about the past, present and future e.g. the creation of the heavens and earth, botanical and zoological life, stories about the nations of the past and about Paradise and Hell etc.\n4. Allah often mentions prayer and giving Zakat together. Prayer shows sincerity to Allah, and giving Zakat shows kindness to creation. Together they are the route to happiness and success.\n5. Having faith in Allah and doing good works leads to guidance and success in this world and the next.",
  2006:
      "When Allah describes the characteristics of the pious believers who are inwardly and outwardly sound, He mentions the characteristics of a group of disbelievers who are inwardly and outwardly corrupted, stating: \n Those upon whom the decree of Allah to disbelieve manifested will continue in their misguidance and stubbornness, so whether you warn them or not, it's the same.",
  2007:
      "This is because Allah has sealed their hearts, locking their falsehood inside them. He has sealed their hearing, so they do not listen to or accept the truth. He has covered their eyes so they do not see the truth despite its clarity. For them, a great torment awaits in the Hereafter.",
  2008:
      "After Allah describes the characteristics of the disbelievers who are inwardly and outwardly corrupt, He describes the characteristics of the hypocrites who are inwardly corrupt and appear outwardly sound to people, stating: \n There is a group of people who claim faith, saying it with their tongues out of fear for their lives and wealth, but inwardly, they remain disbelievers.",
  2009:
      "They ignorantly believe they can deceive Allah and the believers by outwardly showing faith while hiding their disbelief inside. However, in reality, they are unwittingly deceiving themselves; Allah knows all that is secret and hidden, and He has informed the believers about their attributes and characteristics.",
  2010:
      "This is because their hearts contain uncertainty, so Allah increases their doubtfulness by adding further hesitation to their uncertainty; hence, the punishment befits the crime. They will suffer painful torment in the lowest depths of the Fire for their lies against Allah and the people and for rejecting the message brought by Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  2011:
      "When they are told not to prevent corruption on earth through disbelief, disobedience, and the like, they deny doing so, claiming to be people of righteousness and reform.",
  2012:
      "But in reality, they are people of corruption, but they don't realize it, nor feel that their actions are the essence of corruption.",
  2013:
      "When they are commanded to have faith as the companions of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم did, they reply with deprecation and mockery, proclaiming: Should we have faith like the simple-minded had faith? On the contrary, it is they who are the fools, but they are ignorant of their foolishness.",
  2014:
      "And when the hypocrites meet the believers, they say, 'We affirm what you believe,' out of fear of the believers. But when they are alone with their leaders, they assert with steadfastness, 'We are actually with you and upon your path, but we only agree with the believers as a form of mockery and sarcasm.'",
  2015:
      "Allah mocks them for their mocking of the believers, and He will repay them in equal measure for their behavior. They are treated as believers in this world but will be repaid for their disbelief and hypocrisy in the next life. He grants them respite so they become increasingly lost and tyrannical, leaving them further confounded and perturbed.",
  2016:
      "Those hypocrites who are described with these qualities are the ones who exchanged faith for disbelief. But their trade did not yield a profit; they lost their faith in Allah and did not attain guidance to the truth. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Those whose hearts Allah has sealed because of their stubbornness and disbelief will not benefit from the signs of Allah, no matter how great they may be.\n2. Allah allows those who reject faith and do wrong to do as they please, not because He does not know what they are doing or is unable to stop them, but to allow them to accumulate sins for which they will be held responsible in the next life.",
  2017:
      "Allah gives two examples for the hypocrites: one with fire and one with water. In the example with fire, they are like the ones who lit a flame to light up their surroundings. However, just when they started to benefit from the light emanating from the fire, its flame died down, its radiance leaving them with its burning. As a result, the people who lit it find themselves in complete darkness, unable to see anything and unable to find a path out from it.",
  2018:
      "They are deaf: unable to hear or accept the truth. They are dumb: unable to speak the truth. They are blind: unable to see the truth. Because of this, they do not turn back from their misguidance.",
  2019:
      "In the example with water: They are like a heavy rain consisting of thick clouds of layered darkness, thunder, and lightning, descending upon a people and afflicting them with tremendous panic. The intensity of the thunderclaps and the fear of death that results causes them to plug their ears with the tips of their fingers. And Allah is All-Encompassing of the disbelievers, and they do not escape Him.",
  2020:
      "The brightness of the lightning almost blinds them. Whenever it flashes, lighting up the surroundings, they proceed forward, and when there is no light, they remain in darkness, unable to move. If Allah willed, He could take away their hearing and their sight, in His absolute power over all things, and not return it to them due to their turning away from the truth. The rain in the example refers to the Quran. The enveloping darkness refers to the hypocrites' doubts and misconceptions regarding the Quran. The thunderclaps refer to the warnings and the lightning to the truth that sometimes becomes apparent to them. The plugging of their ears from the thunderclaps is likened to their turning away from the truth and not responding to it. The hypocrites are similar to the people in these examples because they receive no benefit from their surroundings. In the example of the fire, all they receive is darkness and a smoldering fire. In the example of the rainstorm, all they receive is terror and panic from the thunder and lightning. Such are the hypocrites who see nothing in Islam except difficulty and harshness.",
  2021:
      "After mentioning the believers, the disbelievers, and the hypocrites, Allah calls upon everyone to serve Him alone, stating: \n O people, worship no one other than your Lord, for He created you and nations that preceded you so that you may place protection between you and His punishment by following His commands and avoiding what He has prohibited.",
  2022:
      "It is He Who made the Earth like a carpet spread out in front of you, and it is He Who firmly constructed the sky over you. Through His Grace, rain falls, producing a variety of fruits from the Earth as sustenance for you. Hence, do not make others partners and equals to Allah when you realize that there is no Creator except for Allah, Exalted and Sublime be He.",
  2023:
      "And if you, O Stubborn Disbelievers, are skeptical of the Quran sent down to Our slave Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, then We challenge you to bring one surah (chapter) akin to it, even if it is akin to its shortest surah, and call whoever you can from your supporters if you are truthful in what you claim.",
  2024:
      "And if you can't do that---and you will never be able to---then fear the Fire fueled by the people who deserve punishment and by the types of stones, including those they used to worship. Allah has prepared this Fire for the disbelievers. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah leaves the hypocrites in their greatest need, as repayment for their hypocrisy and for turning away from guidance.\n2. We should worship Allah alone Who created for us everything that is in the universe and put them at our service.\n3. The inability of people to produce anything similar to a surah of the Qur’an shows that it came down from Allah, the Wise and Knowing.",
  2025:
      "As the warnings in the previous verses were for the disbelievers, then give glad tidings -O Prophet- to the believers in Allah who do righteous deeds, of what will please them from gardens with rivers flowing beneath their palaces and trees.Whenever they are given its pure fruits to consume, they will comment on their striking resemblance to the fruits of the earth, saying, 'This is just like what we used to be provided before.' They will be given fruits with the same name and shape, so they recognize and desire them, but they will be different in taste and flavor. In Paradise, they will have spouses free of any unpleasant qualities and traits people have on Earth. They will live there in eternal, everlasting bliss, unlike the temporary and transient bliss of worldly life.",
  2026:
      "Verily, Allah does not shy away from using whatever example He wishes, whether that be of a gnat or anything bigger or smaller than it. These examples are given to two types of people: believers and disbelievers. As for the believers, they know and trust that there is wisdom in the use of such examples. As for the disbelievers, they mockingly ask one another why Allah uses examples with lowly creatures, such as mosquitoes, flies, and spiders. Allah replies that guidance, direction, and a test for people lie in these examples. There are many whom Allah will misguide through these examples because they refuse to ponder them. Likewise, He will guide many along the right path because they take lessons from them. He does not misguide anyone except those who deserve misguidance. They are those who stray far from obedience to Him, such as the hypocrites.",
  2027:
      "They are those who break the promise they made with Allah to serve Him alone and follow the Messenger whom other messengers before him foretold of. They are those who cut off what Allah enjoined, such as blood relations. They strive to spread corruption upon the earth with sinful actions. These are the ones who are unfortunate in this world and the Hereafter.",
  2028:
      "Verily, your affair, O disbelievers, is strange! How can you disbelieve in Allah while you witness the signs of His power in your very own existence? You were nonexistent, and He brought you to existence and gave you life. Then He will bring you death and bring you back to life a second time and return you to Him to recompense you for what you did.",
  2029:
      "It is Allah alone Who created everything on earth for you, such as the countless rivers and trees from which you benefit, enjoying all that he made subservient to you. Then He turned to the sky, making it into seven leveled heavens. And it is He whose knowledge encompasses everything.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The pleasures of the Garden are not spoiled by anything, nor mixed with any hardship.\n2. The examples Allah uses are only of benefit to the believers, because they really wish to be guided, and truly ask to be guided.\n3. The most obvious features of those who deviate from the truth are that they break their promises with Allah and His creation, leave what Allah told them to hold on to and their actions cause trouble on the earth.\n4. The origin of things is that they are allowed and pure - unless the sacred law prohibits them - because Allah blessed humanity, making everything on the earth for them.",
  2030:
      "Allah informs the angels that He would put humans on earth who would give birth to other humans and inhabit it to worship Allah. The angels asked their Lord, trying to understand, what the wisdom behind making the children of Adam guardians of the earth was when they would spread ruin within it and unjustly spill blood, saying: while we [the angels] are obedient to You, extol You, praise You, glorify Your Majesty and Perfection without hesitation. Allah replied to their question, stating: I know what you do not know of the incredible wisdom in their creation and the great objectives behind their succession.",
  2031:
      "To illustrate the status of Adam (peace be upon him), Allah taught him the names of everything: living things and objects, with their pronunciation and meanings. Then he put these things before the angels, asking: Tell me their names if you are truthful in what you say, that you are a nobler and better creation than Adam.",
  2032:
      "They acknowledged their shortcomings and attributed all merit to Allah, replying: We exalt and glorify You, O our Lord, without any opposition to Your judgment and law, for we do not know anything except what You have given us knowledge of. Verily, You are the Omniscient Whom nothing is hidden from, and You are the All-Wise Who puts all affairs in their proper place according to Your decree and law.",
  2033:
      "Then Allah told Adam: Tell them the names of those things. When Adam told the angels what Allah had taught him, Allah told the angels: Did I not inform you that I know everything hidden in the heavens and the earth, and I know everything you reveal from your affairs and what you say within yourselves?",
  2034:
      "Allah reveals that He commanded the angels to prostrate to Adam out of recognition and respect. They quickly prostrated in their readiness to obedience towards Him, except for Iblis (Satan), who was originally from the Jinn. Iblis refused, objecting to Allah's command to prostrate, and out of arrogance towards Adam, causing him to become among the unfaithful.",
  2035:
      "And We said: O Adam, live with your wife, Eve, in Paradise, and eat from the delightful, vast variety of food from anywhere in Paradise without disturbance. But avoid approaching this tree I forbade you to eat from, lest you become among the wrongdoers by disobeying what I commanded you to do.",
  2036:
      "Satan continued whispering to them to eat from it. He embellished the matter until he caused them to slip and fall into sin by eating from the tree that Allah forbade them from. As a result, Allah took them out of the Paradise they were in and said to them and Satan: Go down to the earth as enemies of each other, and for you on the earth is stability, survival, and enjoyment of the bounties within it until the end of your prescribed lifespan and the establishment of the Hour.",
  2037:
      "Adam then received the words granted to him by Allah and was inspired to supplicate, seeking forgiveness with them, which are mentioned in Sūrat Al-A'rāf, Verse 23: {They said, 'O Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we will certainly be among the losers.'} Allah accepted Adam's repentance and forgave him, for He is Most-Forgiving and Merciful to His creation towards His creation. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Even if we cannot identify Allah’s wisdom behind some of His creation or His sacred law, we must still trust that there is a divine wisdom which we do not know.\n2. The Qur’an gives a high status to knowledge, making it a measure of people’s value.\n3. Pride is the root of disobedience, and the base of every difficulty sent down upon creation. It was the first sin, causing rebellion against Allah.",
  2038:
      "We told them: Descend all of you from Paradise to Earth. And when guidance comes to you through My messengers, then whoever follows it and believes in My messengers will have nothing to fear in the Hereafter, nor will they feel sorrow for what passed them by on earth.",
  2039:
      "As for those who disbelieve and deny Our signs, then those are the dwellers of the Fire; they will never leave it.",
  2040:
      "O Children of Allah's Prophet Jacob, remember Allah's successive blessings upon you and show gratitude for them. And commit yourselves to fulfill My covenant to you by believing in Me and My messengers and acting in accordance with My laws. If you fulfill your covenant, I will fulfill my covenant of what I promised you all: a good life in this world and a beautiful reward on the Day of Resurrection. Therefore, fear Me alone, and do not break My Covenant.",
  2041:
      "Have faith in the Quran, which I revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, confirming what came in the Torah---before its alteration concerning the Oneness of Allah and the prophethood of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم---and beware of becoming the first group to disbelieve him. And do not exchange My verses that I revealed for the small price of position or leadership, and avoid My displeasure and punishment.",
  2042:
      "Do not conflate the truth I revealed to My messengers with lies that you fabricate. And do not conceal the fact that came in your books regarding the description of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم despite your knowledge and certainty of it.",
  2043:
      "And perform the prayer completely with its pillars, obligations, and recommended components. And give Zakat from your wealth, which Allah has put in your hands. And humble yourselves to Allah with those who humble themselves from Muhammad's nation صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  2044:
      "How shameful it is that you command others to believe and do good, and you yourselves turn away, forgetting yourselves, while you read the Torah and know what it contains regarding the command to follow Allah's religion and to believe His messengers. Do you not benefit from your minds?",
  2045:
      "Ask for help in all of your religious and worldly affairs through patience and prayer, which bring you close to Allah and allow you to reach Him so that He will help you, protect you, and take away anything harmful from you. Verily, prayer is a hardship except for those who humble themselves before their Lord.",
  2046:
      "They are the ones who are certain that they will meet their Lord on the Day of Resurrection, that they will return to Him, and will be held accountable for their actions.",
  2047:
      "O Children of Allah's Prophet Jacob, remember the religious and worldly blessings I bestowed upon you. And remember that I favored you over the people of your time who were contemporaries with you in prophethood and dominion.",
  2048:
      "And place a veil of protection between you and the torment of the Day of Resurrection by obeying commands and avoiding prohibitions. On that day, no soul will be able to help another in any way. No intercession on their behalf will be accepted to benefit them or protect them from harm except with Allah's permission. No ransom will be taken, even if it were to be the earth filled with gold. They will have no helpers on that day. Without appeal, ransom, or helper, where will they turn? \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the most disgraceful things is to tell people to do good while not doing it yourself.\n2. Patience and prayer are two of the most helpful actions for easing the servant’s affairs.\n3. On the Day of Judgement, appeals and ransoms will not remove the punishment from anyone: only their good actions will benefit them.",
  2049:
      "O Israelites, remember the time We saved you from the followers of Pharaoh who would make you taste various forms of punishment, slaughtering your sons so you would not survive and letting your women live so they could serve them, taking great pains to humiliate and insult you. And in your salvation from the onslaught of Pharoah and his followers and his people was a great test for you from your Lord, that perhaps you may be thankful.",
  2050:
      "Remember Our blessing upon you when We parted the sea, making it a dry path for you to cross through. We saved you while drowning your enemies, Pharaoh and his followers, before your very eyes as you looked on at them.",
  2051:
      "And remember that the forty nights appointed to Moses were from Allah's blessings, in which the revelation of the Torah, with its light and guidance, was completed. Yet you went and worshipped the calf during that period, becoming transgressors through your actions.",
  2052:
      "Then We forgave after your repentance and did not take you to account for it so that you might be thankful to Allah by worshipping Him well and obeying him.",
  2053:
      "Remember that among Our blessings upon you was when we gave Moses (peace be upon him) the Torah as a criterion between truth and falsehood. It distinguished between guidance and misguidance so that you might be guided to the truth through it.",
  2054:
      "And remember from these blessings was Allah granting you the ability to repent after worshipping the calf, when Moses (peace be upon him) told you: You have wronged yourselves by taking the calf as a deity and worshipping it. So repent and return to your Creator and Originator by some of you killing others (those that transgressed). Repenting to Him in this way is better for you than persisting in disbelief, which would lead to an eternity in the Fire. So, you did this with Allah's guidance and aid, and He accepted your repentance, for He is Oft-Forgiving and Merciful toward His slaves.",
  2055:
      "And remember the time you brazenly addressed Moses (peace be upon him), proclaiming: We will not believe you [O Moses] until we see Allah with your own eyes, unveiled and before us. As a result, a burning fire took and killed you as you looked at one another.",
  2056:
      "Then, We brought you back to life after death so that you might be thankful to Him for the blessing of life that He granted you.",
  2057:
      "And from Our blessing upon you was sending clouds to shade you from the sun's heat when you were wandering the earth. And We sent down from our bounties a sweet drink resembling honey (called Manna) and a small bird with good meat resembling that of quails (called Salwa). We said to you: Consume the good things We have provided for you. We [Allah] lost nothing through their denial and rejection of these blessings. Instead, they only wronged themselves by losing their share of the reward and exposing themselves to suffering. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Israelites received many great blessings from Allah, which only increased their pride and stubbornness.\n2. The verses show the vast extent of His patience and mercy with His servants, even if they do great wrong.\n3. Revelation is the criterion between truth and falsehood.",
  2058:
      "Remember from Allah's blessings upon you: when We [Allah] told you: Enter Jerusalem and eat abundantly of the good things within from wherever you wish. And bow in humility to Allah when you enter Jerusalem, saying, 'O Our Lord, relieve us of our sins,' so that We may answer you. And We will increase the reward of those who excel in their deeds for their excellence.",
  2059:
      "The wrongdoers among them distorted what they were commanded to do and say. They entered dragging themselves on their backs, proclaiming: 'A grain in a hair,' in an attempt to mock Allah's command, may He be Exalted. Allah sent down punishment from the sky upon these wrongdoers for transgressing the limits of the law and violating the command.",
  2060:
      "Remember from Allah's blessings upon you when you were in the desert and afflicted with extreme thirst. So Moses (peace be upon him) prayed to his Lord and asked that He give you all water. Thus, We commanded him to hit the rock with his staff. When he hit it, twelve springs burst forth from it, corresponding with the number of your tribes. Water gushed from them, and We specified the place of drink designated for each tribe so that there would be no conflict between you all. And We told you: Eat and drink from what Allah provided and brought for you, without any effort or toil on your part, and do not attempt to spread corruption upon the earth.",
  2061:
      "And remember the time you expressed ungratefulness for the blessings of your Lord, becoming bored of the Manna and Salwa Allah sent down to you, declaring: We will not continue to endure eating the one type of unchanging food. So you asked Moses (peace be upon him) to ask Allah to produce plants from the earth to eat consisting of herbs, vegetables, cucumbers (specifically referring to the Armenian cucumber/snake melon), grains, lentils, and onions. Moses condemned their request, telling them: Would you exchange the nobler and better Manna and Salwa which came to you without effort or toil, for that which is inferior and worse? Go down from this land to any town, and you will find what you are asking for within its fields and markets. By following their whims and repeatedly turning away from what Allah chose for them, they were afflicted with constant disgrace, poverty, and misery. They earned Allah's wrath because they turned away from His religion, disbelieved in His signs, and unjustly and brutally killed His prophets – all because they rebelled against Allah and kept transgressing His limits. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Those who manipulate and distort the texts of sacred law, as the Israelites did, will get what they deserve from Allah.\n2. Mocking the sacred law of Allah deserves a severe punishment.\n3. The verses highlight the great favour Allah showed to the Israelites, and their great ingratitude, stubbornness and turning away from Allah and His laws in return.\n4. We should be extremely grateful when given great blessings. Ingratitude for these blessings is a great wrong and deserves a stem punishment.\n5. The verses state the severe misfortune that results from people rebelling against and transgressing the limits of Allah, bringing humiliation and shame to the offenders and allowing their enemies to have power over them.",
  2062:
      "Those who believe in Allah and the Final Day from this nation and the previous nations before the deputation of Muhammad, from the Jews, the Christians, and Sabians [a group of followers of one of the prophets] will have their reward with their Lord. They will not fear what awaits them in the Hereafter nor grieve over what they lost on earth.",
  2063:
      "Remember when We took your firm covenant, O Children of Israel, to believe in Allah and His Messenger. We raised the mountain over you as a warning and to instill fear of the consequences of not abiding by the covenant, telling you: Take the Torah that we have revealed to you with seriousness and diligence, without taking it for granted or being lazy about it. And protect what it [the Torah] contains and ponder upon it so that you might start working to protect yourself against Allah's punishment.",
  2064:
      "Yet even after making a firm covenant, you turned away and rebelled. Had it not been for Allah's favor upon you, His tolerance towards you, and His Mercy in accepting your repentance, you would surely be among the losers for abandoning the covenant and your disobedience.",
  2065:
      "You know with absolute certainty about your ancestors' story when they transgressed with their hunting on Saturday, a day on which they were prohibited from fishing. So they would cheat by setting up nets before Saturday and pulling them out on Sunday. As a result of their tricks, Allah turned these deceivers into ostracized and outcast monkeys, a consequence of their deception.",
  2066:
      "Allah made an example out of this transgressing village for surrounding villages and an example to those who came after so that they would not engage in the same behavior and become deserving of its consequences. And We made it a reminder for the pious who fear Allah's punishment and His retribution for transgressing His limits.",
  2067:
      "From the stories of your ancestors, remember what happened between them and Moses (peace be upon him) when he told them that Allah had commanded them to sacrifice a cow among the cattle. Instead of hastening to comply, they stubbornly asked: Are you trying to make a mockery out of us?! Moses responded: I seek refuge in Allah from being among those who lie about Allah and mock people.",
  2068:
      "Then they asked Moses: Call upon your Lord for us so He can clarify the characteristics of the cow that He commanded us to sacrifice. Moses responded: Allah says that it be a cow that was neither old nor young but was between the two, so hasten to comply with your Lord's command.",
  2069:
      "They continued debating and being stubborn, telling Moses (peace be upon him): Call upon your Lord to clarify the color of the cow for us. Moses replied: Allah says that it be a yellow cow, bright in color, pleasing to everyone who sees it. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah sometimes punishes disobedient people in this life, before the Afterlife, as a way of cautioning other people, so that they are careful of going against Allah’s sacred law.\n2. Trying to cheat the sacred law is forbidden, because Allah is not deceived.\n3. When people would make open matters of the sacred law more difficult and strict for themselves than they are, Allah would sometimes make things even stricter for them as a result.",
  2070:
      "They persisted in their stubbornness, saying: Call upon your Lord to further clarify its description for us as many cows fit the current description, and therefore we cannot identify it. They insisted that they would then if Allah willed, be guided to the cow required to be sacrificed.",
  2071:
      "So Moses replied: Allah says that the cow is not used for plowing or irrigating the earth; it is free from defects and has no other marks of color except its yellow color. They then replied: Now you have brought a detailed description that accurately identifies the cow. They sacrificed the cow after almost not having done so due to their arguing and stubbornness.",
  2072:
      "Remember the time you murdered one of your own and defended yourselves, with each person defending themselves against the accusation of murder and, in turn, accusing the other until you started a conflict within yourselves. But Allah revealed what you were hiding regarding the murder of the innocent person.",
  2073:
      "So We said to you: Strike the murdered man with a piece of the cow which you were commanded to sacrifice, for verily Allah will bring him back to life to inform you who the murderer was. They did this, and the dead man informed them of his murderer. And just as this man was brought back to life, Allah will bring the dead back to life on the Day of Resurrection. And He gives you clear signs of His power that perhaps you will understand and have true faith in Allah, the Exalted.",
  2074:
      "Then your hearts hardened after these profound admonitions and extraordinary miracles until they became like rocks or even harder. The states of these hearts never change, whereas rocks change and transform. Verily, there are rocks from which rivers burst forth, and some of them split, and water comes out of them, gushing and flowing through the earth, from which people and animals benefit. Some of them fall from the tallest of mountains out of fear of Allah and awe. Your hearts are not like this. And Allah is not heedless of what you do. Rather, He is well aware of it and will recompense you accordingly.",
  2075:
      "Do you then hope, O Believers, after knowing their true nature and obstinacy, that they will believe and respond to you?! A group of their scholars would hear the word of Allah revealed to them in the Torah and then proceed to alter its words and meanings after they had understood and become familiar with it. And they did this fully aware of the magnitude of their crime.",
  2076:
      "One of the contradictions of the Jews and their deviousness would occur when some of them would meet believers and confess the truth of the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم and the validity of his message, which is what the Torah testifies to. But when the Jews were alone with one another, they would blame each other because of these confessions because the Muslims would establish their confessions as evidence against them and the truth of the prophethood. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some people have hearts harder than stone, unmoved by good advice or compassion.\n2. Signs of Allah, even if they are great, do not benefit someone if their heart does not surrender in awe of Allah.\n3. These verses exposed the true nature of the Israelites: they have inherited habits of carelessness, deception and manipulation of religion.",
  2077:
      "These Jews follow this disgraceful path as if they are unaware that Allah knows what they conceal from their words and actions and what they reveal. But He will reveal and expose them to His slaves.",
  2078:
      "Among the Jews is a group who do not know the Torah except for its recitation and do not understand what it means. These people have nothing but lies that they heard from their elders and think it is the Torah revealed by Allah.",
  2079:
      "Misery and great suffering await those who write the scripture with their own hands and then falsely allege that it comes from Allah. They exchange the truth and guidance for a small gain in this world, such as wealth or leadership. They will experience destruction and immense torment for what their hands have written, through which they lie about Allah. They will also attain destruction and immense torment for whatever wealth or leadership they gain through these lies.",
  2080:
      "And they falsely and delusionally said: The Fire will not touch us, and we won't be in it except for a few days [even if it did]. Tell them, O Prophet: Did you have a definite promise from Allah that this will be the case? If so, then Allah never breaks his covenant. Or are you telling lies and falsehoods about Allah, speaking about that which you do not know?",
  2081:
      "The matter is not as they imagine, for Allah punishes those who earn the evil of disbelief and whose sins surround them from every side. And He will recompense them with permanent admission into the Fire, where they will live eternally.",
  2082:
      "And those who have faith in Allah and His Prophet and do good will be rewarded with permanent entry into Paradise, where they will live eternally.",
  2083:
      "Remember, O Israelites, the firm covenant that We took from you: to worship Him alone, and not worship anyone with Him; to be kind to parents, relatives, orphans, and the needy and destitute; to say kind words to people, telling them to do what is right and forbidding evil, without harshness or coercion; to perform the prayer completely as instructed; to give Zakat to its rightful recipients with a contentful heart. But after you took this promise, you turned away from fulfilling it except for some of you whom Allah protected, and they fulfilled their promise and covenant to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some of the People of the Scripture claim knowledge of what Allah has revealed, when they do not really have knowledge of it, and what they say is only from their imagination and ignorance.\n2. Some of the greatest wrongdoers are those who lie about Allah and His Messenger.\n3. The favours and blessings that Allah gave to the Israelites made them lose their way, because they thought, not understanding Allah and His divine wisdom, that He would not punish them after He had given them such blessings.\n4. The great promises that the Israelites made with Allah only made them turn away more, due to their rejection of them.",
  2084:
      "Remember the firm covenant We took from you in the Torah: forbidding you from spilling each other's blood and forcing people to leave their homes. You then admitted that We took that covenant from you while you bore witness to its validity.",
  2085:
      "Then you broke this covenant: you killed one another, and some of you forced a group among you to leave their homes, assisted by their enemies, oppressively and aggressively. When those among you became prisoners in the hands of enemies, you would strive to pay their ransom and rescue them from their captivity, even though forcing them out of their homes was forbidden to you. How can you believe in parts of the Torah (like the obligation to pay ransom for captives) and reject other parts (prohibitions regarding spilling blood and forcing people out of their homes)? For those among you who do that, only humiliation and disgrace await you in this life and the most severe torment in the Hereafter. Allah is not unaware of what you do. Rather, He is fully aware of it, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  2086:
      "They are the people who exchange the Hereafter for worldly life, preferring that which is temporary to that which is eternal. As a result, their punishment will not be lightened in the Hereafter, and they will have no one to help them on that day.",
  2087:
      "We gave Moses the Torah and followed him with other messengers who took after him. We gave Jesus, the son of Mary, clear signs of the truth of what he came with, such as bringing the dead back to life and healing the blind and the lepers. We also strengthened him with the angel Gabriel, the Holy Spirit (peace be upon him). Yet why is it, O Israelites, that whenever a messenger from Allah comes to you with something that does not correspond to your whims, you become arrogant towards the truth, looking down on the messengers of Allah, rejecting some amongst them, and killing others?",
  2088:
      "The Jews' evidence for not following Muhammad was their saying: Our hearts are covered such that nothing you say reaches them, and they do not understand. However, the matter is not as they claim. Rather, Allah has expelled them from His mercy due to their disbelief, so only a few of them believe in what Allah has sent to the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the worst forms of disbelief is to have faith in one part of Allah’s scripture and to then reject other parts of it. Whoever does this has made their own desires into their Allah.\n2. Some of the Israelites exchanged the Afterlife for worldly prestige, as a result of stubbornness, following their own desires, and manipulating what Allah had revealed to them.\n3. It is from Allah’s blessings and mercy to His creation that He sent many messengers and scriptures to guide them.\n4. Allah repays those who turn away from guidance and stubbornly refuse to obey with a seal on their hearts, depriving them of His mercy. As a result, they will not be guided to the truth, and will not act according to it.",
  2089:
      "The Quran came to them from Allah, agreeing with what the Torah and the Gospel contain. Before it was revealed, they used to say that they would be helped against the polytheists, who worship others alongside Allah and would have success over them when a prophet was sent since they would have faith in him and follow him. But they disbelieved him when the Quran and Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم came to them, according to the description they recognized and the truth they knew. Allah curses those who disbelieve Him and His Prophet.",
  2090:
      "Miserable is what they have purchased in exchange for their portion of belief in Allah and His messengers. They disbelieved in what Allah revealed and unjustly and enviously rejected His messengers because He gave prophethood and the Quran to Muhammad. So they deserved Allah's multiplied anger for disbelieving in Muhammad and distorting the Torah beforehand. Those who disbelieve in the prophethood of Muhammad will receive a humiliating torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  2091:
      "When these Jews were told to believe in the truth and guidance that Allah revealed to His Prophet, they replied: We believe in what had been revealed to our prophets, and they reject anything besides this which was revealed to Muhammad, although this Quran is the truth, confirming what Allah had already revealed to them. Had they truly believed in what had been revealed to them, they would have believed in the Quran. So, ask them then, O Prophet: Why did you kill the prophets of Allah before if you believed in the truth they brought?",
  2092:
      "And your prophet Moses brought clear signs to you, proving his truthfulness. But after that, you made the calf into a deity and worshipped it when Moses had gone to meet his Lord. You were wrongdoers for worshipping others alongside Allah since only He is worthy of worship.",
  2093:
      "Remember when We made a binding promise with you to follow Moses and accept what he brought from Allah? We raised the mountain over you to scare you and told you: Take the Torah seriously, which We had sent to you and listen to accept and submit; otherwise, We would make the mountain fall upon you; then you said: We heard with our ears and disobeyed with our actions. The worship of the calf took hold of their hearts because of their disbelief. O Prophet, say: How evil is what this belief instructs you to do: disbelieving in Allah – if you are true believers – because true belief cannot be accompanied by disbelief.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Jews were so jealous because the Prophet (peace be upon him) was not one of them that it led them to disbelieve in Allah and reject what He revealed.\n2. The Jews knew that what was revealed to the Prophet was completely true, but they disbelieved it out of envy and outrage.\n3. Having real faith in Allah means believing in all the scriptures He revealed, and in all the messengers He sent.\n4. Turning away from truth and guidance when you know it to be true, and have had proof of it being so, is one of the biggest wrongs you can commit.\n5. Despite the many binding promises and contracts Allah made with the Israelites, they broke them and went back on their promises many times.",
  2094:
      "O Prophet, say: O Jews, if Paradise in the Hereafter is just for you, and no other people will enter it, then wish for death, and ask for it, so that you reach this place quickly and can rest from the burdens and worries of the life of this world if you are truthful about what you claim.",
  2095:
      "They will never wish for death because of what they have done, such as disbelieving in Allah, rejecting His Messengers, and distorting His Books. Allah is Omniscient of the wrongdoers among them and others and will recompense them for their deeds accordingly.",
  2096:
      "You will find, O Prophet, that the Jews are the most greedy for life despite its lowliness and insignificance. They are more greedy for it than the polytheists, who do not believe in the resurrection and the reckoning. Despite being People of the Book and believing in the resurrection and the reckoning, they would love to live a thousand years. However long a life they might be given would not distance them from Allah's torment. Allah is aware of all that they do. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for it accordingly.",
  2097:
      "O Muhammad, tell those of the Jews who claim that Gabriel is our enemy among the angels: Whoever is an enemy to Gabriel, then it is he who brought down the Quran to your (Muhammad's) heart, with Allah's permission, affirming the sacred Books that came before it, such as the Torah and the Gospel, guiding towards virtue, and bringing glad tidings to the believers of the bliss Allah has prepared for them. Thus, whoever is an enemy to an angel of such a description and duty is misguided.",
  2098:
      "Whoever is an enemy to Allah, His angels, His messengers, and His two angels, Gabriel and Michael, then indeed Allah is an enemy to the disbelievers from among you and other than you. And whoever has Allah as an enemy, then he faces evident loss.",
  2099:
      "We have revealed to you, O Prophet, clear signs proving the truthfulness of your prophethood and revelation. Despite its clarity, the only people who reject these signs are those who have abandoned Allah's religion.",
  2100:
      "Due to the corrupt state of the Jews, whenever they took a covenant upon themselves, including the duty to believe in what the Torah revealed about the prophethood of Muhammad, they would always break any commitment they made. Instead, most of them do not believe in what Allah revealed because true belief leads to fulfilling commitments and promises.",
  2101:
      "When Muhammad came to them as a prophet from Allah, and he fitted the Torah's description of him, a group of them turned away from their Book that showed this, throwing it behind their backs, unmindful of it, not benefitting from its truth or guidance, like an ignoramus.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The faithful wish for eternal bliss with Allah, and for this reason look forward to meeting Him, and do not fear death.\n2. The verses show the greed of some Jews for the life of this world, even if it is a life of humiliation and disgrace.\n3. Whoever makes an enemy of the close friends of Allah, he will become an enemy of Allah.\n4. Some Jews turned away from the prophethood of Muhammad (peace be upon him) despite their scriptures informing them that he was truly a prophet.\n5. A person who does not benefit from his knowledge can accurately be described as ignorant, because his state is like that of an ignorant person.",
  2102:
      "When they abandoned Allah's religion and instead followed the lies that the devils fabricated about Prophet Solomon's kingdom (peace be upon him), claiming that he established his kingdom through black magic, Solomon did not disbelieve by practicing black magic, as the Jews claimed. Instead, the devils disbelieved when they taught people black magic revealed to the two angels, Harut and Marut, in the city of Babylon, Iraq. These two angels would only teach black magic to someone after warning and explaining: We are simply a trial and test for people, so do not disbelieve by learning black magic. Those who did not heed their advice and learned black magic from them would, through it, separate a man and his wife by sowing hatred between them. These sorcerers could not harm anyone except with Allah's permission and will. They learned what harmed them and did not benefit them. This group of Jews knew that whoever exchanged Allah's scripture for black magic would have no portion in the Hereafter. What an evil thing they sold their souls for when they traded Allah's revelation and sacred law for black magic! If they had known what would benefit them, they would not have done something so disgraceful and clearly misguided.",
  2103:
      "If only the Jews truly believed in Allah and feared Him by obeying Him and not disobeying Him, Allah's reward would have been far better for them if they only knew what benefits them.",
  2104:
      "Allah, the Exalted, directs the believers to be careful in choosing their words when addressing the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, telling them not to say 'rā'inā', meaning 'consider our condition/affairs' or 'shepherd us.', because the Jews would distort and address the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم with it, thereby changing its meaning to 'foolish' or 'heedless.' So, Allah prohibited them from using this phrase to shut the door to mockery. Instead, He prescribed His slaves to say: 'unẓurnā,' meaning 'wait for us to understand what you are saying', as this phrase has no negative connotation while conveying the same meaning. For the disbelievers lies an excruciating and painful torment with Allah.",
  2105:
      "The disbelievers, whether from the People of the Book or among the polytheists, do not like that Allah sends down any good thing, big or small, to you. Through His mercy, Allah favors who He wills of His slaves with prophethood, revelation, and belief. Allah is the possessor of great grace. No one in creation gets any good except that it is from Him, and it is from His grace that He sent His Prophet and revealed His Book to us.\n\n • Beneficial Points:\n1. Whoever knowingly turns away from guidance, Allah will make him follow what is false.\n2. Some of the Jews lack proper respect for the prophets of Allah, claiming that Solomon (peace be upon him) practised black magic; but Allah cleared Solomon of their false claim.\n3. Black magic is a reality and it affects the mind and the body. Those who practise it are disbelievers, and should face capital punishment.\n4. Nothing happens, be it good or evil, except that it is with Allah’s knowledge and with His permission.\n5. Faith and mindfulness of Allah are the best things anyone can store away for themselves for the next life.\n6. The objectives of the sacred law require the prohibition of anything that leads to harm. Therefore, any words or actions that might lead to corruption must be avoided.\n7. Grace is in Allah’s hands, and He favours whomever He wills with it through His mercy and wisdom.",
  2106:
      "Allah, the Exalted, makes it clear that whenever He removes the ruling of a verse or its words from the Quran, and people forget them, He (may He be Exalted) replaces them with something more beneficial for the immediate moment or for later, or with what is similar. Such cases occur because of Allah's wisdom and knowledge. You know, O Prophet, that Allah is the Most Capable of everything. He does as He wills and judges as He wishes.",
  2107:
      "You know, O Prophet, Allah is the Owner of the heavens and the earth. He judges as He wishes, instructs His slaves, forbids them from doing what He wills, establishes the sacred law, and abrogates what He wills. Your only protector is Allah, Who will take care of your affairs, and you have no other helper to protect you from harm. Allah is the protector and guardian of all and has power over everything.",
  2108:
      "O believers, it is not your nature to question your Prophet out of opposition and intransigence as the people of Moses questioned him before, like when they said: {Show us Allah openly} [Al-Nisa:153]. Whoever exchanges belief for disbelief has strayed from the middle way, the straight path.",
  2109:
      "Many Jews and Christians, out of envy, wish to turn you back to disbelief after belief, worshipping idols as you did before when it has become clear to them that what the Prophet came with is the truth from Allah. O believers, forgive them for their actions and pardon them for their ignorance and the evil in their souls until Allah's instruction concerning them comes, which has come: the disbeliever is given a choice between embracing Islam, paying the Jizyah (poll tax), or fighting [the Muslims]. Allah is Omnipotent, and they cannot hinder Him.",
  2110:
      "After instructing the believers to be patient in the face of harm, Allah commands them to remain steadfast in their religion and strengthen their faith, stating: \n Establish the prayer entirely with all its pillars, obligatory and recommended acts, and give Zakat from your wealth to those who deserve it. Whatever righteous deeds you do in life before death will be a treasure for yourselves: the reward you will find with your Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and He will requite you. Allah sees all that you do and will recompense everyone accordingly.",
  2111:
      "The Jews and the Christians each said: Paradise would be for them exclusively. The Jews said: Only a Jew will enter Paradise, and the Christians said: Only a Christian will enter Paradise. These are just their vain desires and imaginings. Tell them, O Prophet, in reply: Bring proof of what you claim if you are truthful.",
  2112:
      "The matter is not as they claim. Only those who are sincere in directing themselves to Allah and do good in worshipping Him by following what the Prophet brought will enter Paradise, no matter what group they come from. They will have their reward with their Lord. They will not fear what awaits them in the Hereafter nor grieve over what they lost on earth. These descriptions only apply to Muslims after the Prophet Muhammad's mission.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Authority only belongs to Allah. He changes whatever He wills of His rulings and His sacred laws, and leaves those He wills as they are, in His wisdom and knowledge.\n2. Many of the People of the Scripture felt envy towards the Muslim nation because Allah favoured them with faith and with following the Messenger; and so they wished that they would return to disbelief, as they were before.",
  2113:
      "The Jews say: The Christians are not upon the correct religion, and the Christians say: The Jews are not upon the correct religion. They say this even though both of them recite their respective Books, which Allah has revealed, and they contain the instruction to believe in all the prophets without distinction. They are similar to the ill-informed among the polytheists who reject all messengers and the Books sent with them. Hence, Allah will judge between all those who disagreed [with one another] on the Day of Resurrection with His fair judgment of which He has informed His slaves: There is no success except through belief in all that Allah is revealed.",
  2114:
      "No one does more wrong than those who prevent the name of Allah from being mentioned in His Houses of worship: They prevent the prayer, Allah's remembrance, and the recitation of the Quran, trying to destroy and ruin them, through tearing them down or preventing people from worshipping in them. Those who try to destroy these places of worship should not enter them, except fearfully and with trembling hearts, after their disbelief and having stopped people from worshipping in them. They will have shame and humiliation in their life on earth at the hands of the believers, and in the Hereafter is a great torment for preventing people from Allah's Houses of worship.",
  2115:
      "To Allah belong the East and the West and whatever is between them. He instructs His slaves as He wills. Wherever you turn, you will find Allah. If He instructs you to face Jerusalem or the Kaaba, or you make a mistake in the direction of prayer, or you cannot face it, then it is not an issue because all directions belong to Allah. Allah is All-Encompassing; He encompasses His creation with mercy and ease. He knows their intentions and actions.",
  2116:
      "The Jews, the Christians, and the polytheists said: Allah had taken a son. He is free and sanctified from such a thing because He does not need His creation, and no one has a son unless he is needy. To Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. All creation is His slaves, in submission to Him, and He deals with them as He wills.",
  2117:
      "Allah is the Originator of the heavens, earth, and all that is in them without precedent. If He decrees and wants something, He only says to it 'Be,' and it is as He wanted it. Nothing can stop His command and His decree.",
  2118:
      "Those without knowledge from among the People of the Book and the polytheists asked, in their stubbornness against the truth: Why did Allah not speak to us directly, or why was a tangible miracle not sent to us? The rejecting nations said similar things to their messengers in the past; despite different times and places, their hearts are identical to those of their disbelieving, stubborn, and insolent predecessors. Allah clarifies His signs to people convinced of the truth when made apparent to them; they are not afflicted with doubt, nor do they stubbornly resist.",
  2119:
      "We have sent you, O Prophet, with the religion of truth, in which there is no doubt: to bring the good news of Paradise to those who believe and to warn the disbelievers about the Fire. Allah will not ask you about the companions of the Inferno who did not believe in you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Disbelievers are all the same, even if they are from different races and places. They are alike in their disbelief, and in what they say about Allah without any knowledge.\n2. The ones who commit the greatest wrongs are those who prevent people from following the path of Allah and obstruct those who wish to do good.\n3. Allah is far too great to have a son or a spouse. Glory be to Him! He is not in need of His creation in any way.",
  2120:
      "Allah addresses His Prophet, directs, and warns him: The Jews and the Christians will never be satisfied with you unless you leave Islam and follow what they are on. If you or anyone from your followers were to follow them after the clear truth came to you, you would not find any assistance or support from Allah. This explains the danger of leaving the truth and conforming to the people of falsehood. Otherwise, Allah has protected His Prophet from that, which serves as a warning for his nation after him.",
  2121:
      "The Noble Quran speaks about a group from the People of the Book who act upon the revealed books they have been given and follow them correctly. They find signs pointing to the truth of the Prophet Muhammad in these books, and because of this, they hasten to believe in him. Another group persists in disbelief, which will result in their loss.",
  2122:
      "O Israelites, remember My favors, religious and worldly, which I gave you, and remember that I favored you over those of your time with prophethood and kingdom.",
  2123:
      "Protect Yourselves from the torment of the Day of Resurrection by following Allah's instructions and avoiding His prohibitions because, on that Day, no soul will be able to help another soul in any way; no ransom will be accepted from it, no matter how great; and no one interceding on its behalf will benefit it, no matter how high their position. On that Day, a soul will have no helper besides Allah.",
  2124:
      "And remember when Allah tested Abraham (peace be upon him) by instructing him to fulfill laws and obligations. Abraham obeyed, fulfilling the orders completely. Allah told His prophet Abraham: I will make you an example in actions and character for people to follow. Abraham said: O my Lord, make my descendants leaders who people would follow. Allah replied to him: My promise to you of sacred leadership would not extend to the wrongdoers among your descendants.",
  2125:
      "And remember when Allah made the sacred house a place for people to return to connect their hearts to it. Whenever they travel from it, they return to it. He also made it a safe place for them not to be attacked. Allah told the people: Take the place of the stone that Abraham stood on while building the Kaaba as a place of prayer. We advised Abraham and his son Ishmael to purify the sacred house of filth and idols and prepare it for those who wish to worship through Tawaf (circumambulation), seclusion, praying, and so on.",
  2126:
      "Remember, O Prophet, when Abraham prayed to his Lord: O my Lord, make Mecca a safe place, where no one would be faced with evil; and provide the people who live there with all types of fruits and a special provision for those who believe in You and the Final Day. Allah said: Whoever disbelieves among them, then I will give them some enjoyment by giving them a small provision in this life; but in the Hereafter I will force them into the torment of the Fire, what a miserable destination to which they will return on the Day of Resurrection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Jews and Christians who read the Scripture properly know that what the Prophet (peace be upon him) came with is true guidance, and is from Allah.\n2. No matter what a Muslim does of good, the Jews and the Christians will not be pleased till they abandon Islam and follow them in their error.\n3. Leadership in faith is only given to those who are certain of the truth and are patient in carrying out Allah’s commandments.\n4. The blessing of the prayer of Abraham (peace be upon him) for Makkah has meant that Allah made it a safe place for people and blessed those who live there with abundance.",
  2127:
      "Remember, O Prophet, when Abraham and Ishmael were raising the foundations of the Kaaba. While they did so, they said, with submissiveness and humility: O Lord, accept our deeds, among which is the building of this house, for You are the Responder to our supplications and Omniscient of our intentions and deeds.",
  2128:
      "O our Lord, make us surrender in devotion to Your command, humble towards You, not worshipping anyone alongside You, and make our descendants a nation who also surrenders in devotion to You. Teach us how to worship You and forgive us for our faults and shortcomings in Your obedience. You are the Acceptor of repentance from those who repent among Your slaves and compassionate towards them.",
  2129:
      "O our Lord, send a messenger from among them from the descendants of Ishmael to recite Your revealed verses, teach them the Quran and the Sunnah, and purify them from polytheism and vice. You are the Mighty, Dominant, and Wise in Your actions and laws.",
  2130:
      "No one turns away from the religion of Abraham to other religions except those who wrong themselves through foolishness and bad decisions to leave the truth for misguidance and are contented with humiliation. We chose him as a messenger and a friend in this world, and in the Hereafter, he will be one of the righteous people who fulfilled what God required them to do, and thus, they reached the highest levels.",
  2131:
      "Allah chose Abraham for his swiftness in submitting [to Allah]. When his Lord told him: Devote your worship to Me sincerely and submit to Me in obedience. Abraham answered to His Lord: I have submitted myself to Allah in devotion, the One who created His slaves, provided for them, and handled their affairs.",
  2132:
      "Abraham advised his sons with the statement: 'I have submitted to the Lord of all worlds', and Jacob told his sons to do the same. They both summoned their sons and told them: Allah chose for you the religion of Islam, so hold tightly to it such that death comes to you while you submit to Allah outwardly and inwardly.",
  2133:
      "Were you present at the time of Jacob's death when he asked his sons: What will you worship after my death? They replied to him: We will worship your God and the God of your fathers: Abraham, Ishmael, and Isaac, One God without partners, and we will surrender in devotion alone and submit to Him.",
  2134:
      "That was a nation that has passed on like other nations. They have proceeded to the deeds they sent forth, and they will face [the consequence of] what they earned of either good or evil, and you will face [the consequence of] what you have earned. You will not be asked about their deeds, and they will not be asked about your deeds. No one will be held accountable for the sins of another; instead, everyone will be recompensed for their own deeds; thus, the deeds of those who came before you should not distract you from paying attention to your own deeds because, after Allah's mercy, nothing will benefit a person except his own righteous deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The mindful believer is not dazzled by his own good actions, but worries that they might not be accepted from him by Allah. For this reason, the believer should often ask Allah to accept his good actions.\n2. The blessing of the prayer of the father of the prophets, Abraham (peace be upon him), meant that Allah accepted his prayer, and made the seal of His prophets (Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) from the people of Makkah.\n3. The verses show the correctness of asking Allah to accept our prayers through His divine names and attributes, and not through the innovation of intermediaries, such as by the right or position of someone else.\n4. The religion of Abraham is the true faith, which is the natural way of life for us. Only a fool who goes against his own nature rejects it.\n5. It is valid to instruct children to follow guidance, and make them promise to hold tightly to the truth.",
  2135:
      "The Jews told this nation: Become Jews, you will tread the path of guidance, and the Christians said to them: Become Christians, you will tread the path of guidance. O Prophet, respond to them: Rather, We follow the religion of Abraham, who turned away from other false religions to the religion of truth. He did not worship others alongside Allah.",
  2136:
      "O Believers tell the Jews and Christians who make these false claims: We believe in Allah and the Quran, which was revealed to us, and in what was revealed to Abraham and his sons Ishmael and Isaac, and Jacob, and in what was revealed to the prophets from the descendants of Jacob. We believe in the Torah, which Allah gave to Moses, and the Gospel, which He gave to Jesus, and in all the books that He gave to every one of the prophets, with no distinction between them, believing in all of them, not only believing in some and rejecting others. We humbly submit to Him alone; may He be Exalted.",
  2137:
      "If the Jews, Christians, and other disbelievers believe in the same way you do, then they have been guided to the straight path that Allah is satisfied with. Yet if they turn away from belief because they reject all the prophets or some of them, then they are in disagreement and are against you. Do not grieve, O Prophet, because Allah will protect you from their harm and evil and give you victory over them. Allah is All-Hearing of their statements and Omniscient of their intentions and actions.",
  2138:
      "Hold tightly to Allah's religion, upon which He has created you externally and internally. This religion agrees with the natural disposition, benefiting us in every way and preventing harm from us. And say: We worship Allah alone and do not worship anything alongside Him.",
  2139:
      "O Prophet, say to them: Do you argue with us, O People of the Book, that you have more right to Allah and His religion than we do because your religion is older and your Book came before ours, then it will not benefit you. Allah is our Lord, and He does not exclusively belong to You. We have our deeds which you will not be asked about, and you have your deeds which we will not be asked about. Everyone will be recompensed accordingly for their deeds. We are sincerely devoted to Allah in worship and obedience and do not associate any partner with Him.",
  2140:
      "Or do you say, O People of the Book, that Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and the prophets from Jacob's descendants were on Judaism or Christianity? Ask, O Prophet, in reply to them: Are you more knowledgeable or Allah? If they claim that these prophets were Jews or Christians, they have lied because they were sent and died before the revelation of the Torah and the Gospel, respectively. This shows that what they say is a lie against Allah and His messengers and that they conceal the truth of what was revealed to them. No one does more wrong than someone who hides firm testimony that they have from Allah, as some of the People of the Book did. Allah is not unaware of your deeds, and He will recompense you all accordingly.",
  2141:
      "That was a nation that has passed on before you. They have proceeded to the deeds they sent forth, and they will face the consequence thereof, and you will face [the consequence of] what you have earned. You will not be asked about their deeds, and they will not be asked about your deeds. No one is held accountable for the sins of another. Only belief and fear of Allah will be of benefit; instead, everyone will be recompensed for their own deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The claim of the People of the Scripture that they follow the truth will not benefit them if they disbelieve in what Allah revealed to His Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him).\n2. Faith in the scriptures which Allah revealed and in the prophets He sent to people is obligatory.\n3. Recognition of Allah’s Lordship is natural to all of His creation. His creation is only led away from this by Satan and his helpers.",
  2142:
      "The weak-minded, ignorant ones from the Jews and those like them from the hypocrites will say: What caused the Muslims to turn away from their Qiblah (direction of prayer), Jerusalem, that they used to pray towards?! O Prophet, say in response to them: Allah alone owns the dominion of the lands to the East and the West and in every direction. He turns who He wills from His slaves to any direction He wills. He (may He be Exalted) guides whom He wills from His slaves to the straight path free from crookedness and deviation.",
  2143:
      "Just as We made a direction of prayer that We approved of for you, we made you the finest, most just and balanced nation among all other nations in matters of belief, acts of worship, and dealings. This is so that you may be witnesses for the messengers of Allah on the Day of Resurrection, to confirm that they delivered the messages Allah instructed them to deliver to their people, and so that the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم will also witness that he delivered the message he was sent to deliver to you. We [Allah] did not change the direction of prayer that you used to face (Jerusalem) except to reveal---and recompense---who was content with Allah had decreed and submitted to it by following the Messenger; to reveal who would renounce their religion to follow their own desires and not submit to what Allah had decreed. The change of the first direction of prayer was a significant issue, except for those to whom Allah granted faith that whatever He decrees for His slaves has profound, far-reaching wisdom behind it. Allah will not make you lose your faith in Him or the prayers you prayed before the change in prayer direction. Allah is kind and compassionate with people; He does not overburden them or cause the rewards of their good deeds to go to waste.",
  2144:
      "We have seen you, O Prophet, turning your face and sight towards the sky, anticipating revelation regarding the direction of prayer and changing it to the direction you love. So, we will turn you to a direction of prayer that you love and are pleased with, the Sacred House of Allah, instead of Jerusalem. So, turn your face toward the Sacred House of Allah in Mecca. Wherever you are, O believers, face its direction to perform the prayer. Those who have been given the book from the Jews and the Christians know that changing the direction of prayer is the truth sent down from their Creator and the One who manages their affairs because it is mentioned in their book. Allah is not unaware of what those who turn away from the truth do. He (may He be Exalted) is aware of that and will recompense them accordingly.",
  2145:
      "By Allah, if you, O Prophet, were to bring every sign and proof to the Jews and Christians that changing the direction of the prayer is truth, they would not face your prayer direction out of stubbornness towards what you have brought and being too arrogant to follow the truth. Also, you would not face their prayer direction after Allah has turned you away from it. Likewise, they do not face each other's prayer direction because they consider each other disbelievers. If you were to follow their desires in matters of the prayer direction and other laws and rulings, after authentic knowledge which has no doubt has come to you, then you would be from the wrongdoers for leaving guidance and following desires.This verse was addressed to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم to show the enormity of following them even though Allah has protected His Prophet from ever doing that, and it is a warning for his nation after him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Turning away from the sacred law of Allah and ignoring its importance is a sign of foolishness and weak-mindedness.\n2. The verses teach the virtue and honour given to this nation, since Allah praised them and described them as the moderate and just nation among all others.\n3. The believers are warned against following the wishes of the People of the Scripture, because they knowingly turned away from the truth.\n4. There was a possibility during the period of revelation that certain sacred laws might be replaced by others, as the direction of prayer was changed from Jerusalem to the Sacred Mosque in Makkah.",
  2146:
      "Those who have been given the book from the scholars of the Jews and the Christians know that changing the prayer direction is one of the signs of Muhammad's صلى الله عليه وسلم prophethood with them. They recognize this as well as they recognize their own children and can distinguish them from others. Despite this, a group of them hide the truth he brought due to their envy. They do that even though they know that it is the truth.",
  2147:
      "This is the truth from your Lord. So, O Messenger, do not be from those who doubt its validity.",
  2148:
      "Every nation has somewhere to turn to, either physically or spiritually. Part of that is that different nations have different prayer directions and different legislations from Allah. Their various directions cause no harm if they are due to the commands and legislation of Allah. So, O believers, rush to do the good deeds that you have been ordered to do. Allah will gather you all together on the Day of Resurrection from wherever you may be to recompense your deeds. Allah is indeed the Most Capable of everything; He is not incapable of gathering you and recompensing you.",
  2149:
      "Wherever you leave from and wherever you are, O Prophet, you and your followers are to face towards the Sacred Mosque (the Kaaba in Mecca) when you want to pray. It is the truth that has been revealed to you by your Lord, for Allah is not unaware of what you do. Rather, He is Well-Acquainted with all you do and will recompense you accordingly.",
  2150:
      "Wherever you leave from, O Prophet, when you want to pray, turn towards the direction of the Sacred Mosque; wherever you may be, O believers, turn your faces towards it if you want to pray. This is so that people have no argument or proof to use against you, except those who are unjust from amongst them; they will remain stubborn, arguing against you with the weakest of arguments. Do not fear them, but rather fear your Lord alone, following His commands and avoiding what He has prohibited. Allah prescribed you to face the Kaaba to perfect His blessings upon you, distinguishing you from all other nations and guiding you to the most honorable direction of prayer for people.",
  2151:
      "Likewise, we gave you another blessing by sending a messenger from among you. He recites Our verses unto you and purifies you by ordering you with virtuous and good deeds and prohibiting you from evil and wrong actions. He teaches you the Quran and Sunnah and teaches you what you did not know before about your religious and worldly lives.",
  2152:
      "So, remember Me with your hearts and limbs, and I will remember you with praise and protection because the recompense for deeds matches the nature of the deeds. Also, show gratitude to Me for The favors I have given you, and do not show ingratitude by denying them or using them in prohibited ways.",
  2153:
      "O you who believe, seek assistance through patience and prayer in carrying out My obedience and submission to My instructions. Allah is with those who are patient. He guides and assists them.",
  2154:
      "Do not say, O believers, about those who are killed while fighting in Allah's path: They are dead just as others are; instead, they are alive with their Lord, but you do not realize and understand their life because it is a unique life which can only be understood through revelation from Allah, the Exalted.",
  2155:
      "We will surely test you with different types of hardships: some with fear of your enemy; hunger because of lack of food; lack of wealth because of losing it or difficulty in gaining it; loss of lives due to death from diseases and tragedies that kill people, or being martyred in Allah's path; and a lack of produce from the earth. Give good news, O Prophet, to those who are patient in the face of these hardships, of what will make them happy in this world and the Hereafter.",
  2156:
      "The patient ones are those who, when they are afflicted by one of these hardships, say with satisfaction and submission: We belong to Allah, He deals with us as He wills, and we will return to Him on the Day of Resurrection, and it is He Who created us and showers us with different favors; so, to Him is our return and end.",
  2157:
      "Those who possess this quality are praised by Allah in the Highest Assembly of angels, and mercy descends on them. They are the ones guided to the path of truth.",
  2158:
      "The two mountains known as Safa and Marwah near the Kaaba are clear landmarks of the sacred law. So, whoever goes to the Kaaba to perform the ritual of Hajj or Umrah, there is no sin in walking between the two mountains. By clarifying that there was no sin in doing this action, Allah was setting the minds of those Muslims at ease who avoided walking between the mountains because they feared it was an unacceptable action from the Days of Ignorance (i.e., pre-Islam); Allah made it clear that walking between the mountains was from the rituals of Hajj. And whoever sincerely does what is recommended of voluntary acts, Allah is Appreciative, accepts it from them, and will recompense them for it. He is Omniscient of those who do good and deserve to be rewarded.",
  2159:
      "Those who hide the clear signs We have revealed that prove the truth of the Prophet and what he brought, from among the Jews and Christians, after We exposed it to the people in their Books, Allah will expel them from His mercy, and the angels, prophets and all of the rest of humanity will supplicate against them to remove them from Allah's mercy.",
  2160:
      "Except for those who return to Allah in regret for concealing those clear signs, rectifying their hidden and apparent deeds, and clarifying the truth and guidance they concealed, I will accept their return to My obedience. I am Acceptor of repentance from those who repent among My slaves and compassionate towards them.",
  2161:
      "Those who disbelieve and die in disbelief, not having repented, are cursed by Allah by being removed from His mercy, and the angels and all of humanity supplicate for them to be removed and excluded from Allah's Mercy.",
  2162:
      "They will always be cursed, their torment will not be lightened, not even for a day, and they will not be given any respite on the Day of Resurrection.",
  2163:
      "O people, your true God is One and unique in His essence and attributes. There is none worthy of worship except [Allah] the Merciful, the Possessor of expansive mercy. He is Compassionate with His slaves, bestowing them with innumerable favors. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s custom is to test people: He promises to greatly reward those who are patient with the tests and to give them the noblest ranks.\n2. One of the worst wrongs, with the severest punishment, is hiding the truth which Allah has revealed and deceiving people and leading them away from the guidance that the prophets brought.\n3. The verses establish the validity of walking between Safa and Marwah for whoever goes to the Kaaba on Hajj or Umrah.",
  2164:
      "The following are clear proofs of the Oneness of Allah, the Exalted, for those who comprehend and understand the evidence and proofs: the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the wonders of creation within them; the succession of night and day; the ships that sail through the waters of the seas carrying food, clothing, trade and other things that people need and are useful; water that Allah sends down, bringing the earth to life with the agriculture and pasture that grows in it; the living creatures He spread out across the earth; the changing of the winds from one direction to another; and the clouds, suspended between the sky and the earth.",
  2165:
      "Even with these clear signs, some take other deities [to worship] besides Allah, making them out to be rivals to Allah the Exalted, loving them as they love Allah. However, the love for Allah within those who truly believe him is more than the love that these people have towards their falsely worshipped deities. This is because they do not worship others besides Allah; they love Him in times of ease and hardship. As for the others, they only love their false deities in times of ease, but in times of hardship, they don't call to anyone besides Allah. If the transgressors were to see their condition upon witnessing the punishment that awaits in the Afterlife for those who engage in idolatry and commit sins, then they would know that the sole bearer of all power is Allah and that He is severe in punishing those who rebel against him. If they were to see this, then they would not worship anyone besides Allah.",
  2166:
      "Leaders will dissociate themselves from their weak followers when they bear witness to the terrors and adversities of the Day of Resurrection and when all ties and means of escape will be cut off from them.",
  2167:
      "The weak and the followers will say, 'If only we could go back to the earth, we would dissociate ourselves from our leaders the way they dissociated themselves from us.' And just as Allah showed them the severe punishment in the Afterlife, He will show them the consequence of following their leaders in falsehood, accompanied by regrets and sorrow, and they will never leave the Fire.",
  2168:
      "O people: eat from what is on the earth from meat, vegetation, and trees, from what was lawfully earned, and from what is pure and not harmful. Do not follow the paths of the Devil that he promotes; he is an enemy to you, harboring a clear animosity. It is not allowed for a rational person to follow his enemy, who is eager to harm and mislead him.",
  2169:
      "The Devil only commands you to do the worst sins and greatest offenses, inciting you to speak about Allah with regard to faith and sacred laws without knowledge that came to you from Allah or his messengers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has created things and signs which show how amazing He is, highlight His power, and that He alone is worthy of being worshipped. Only those who reflect understand this.\n2. Those who really have faith in Allah love Him more than the rest of creation, because they are devoted to Him in hardship and in ease, and do not worship anyone besides Him.\n3. On the Day of Judgement, all connections between people will be broken, friends will leave one another and everyone will stand alone, except the relationships that were only for the sake of Allah.\n4. There is no excuse for those who followed their leaders into misguidance, not using their own intellects, and going against their own nature.\n5. The verses show the great favour of Allah to His creation, putting everything on earth at their disposal, and making it lawful and good.",
  2170:
      "If these disbelievers are told to follow the guidance and light which Allah revealed, they stubbornly respond: 'Rather, we will follow the beliefs and traditions we found our forefathers upon.' Do they follow their forefathers even though they don't try to consider anything from guidance or the light, and therefore not guided to the truth that Allah is pleased with?",
  2171:
      "The example of those who disbelieve by following their forefathers is like the example of the shepherd who shouts, calling to his livestock. They hear his voice but don't understand what he says. They are, therefore, deaf to hearing the truth in a way that they can benefit, dumb as their tongues have become mute in speaking the truth, and blind to seeing the truth as such. Because of this, they do not understand the guidance you call them toward.",
  2172:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, eat from the good things that Allah has provided and allowed for you [to eat]; and thank Allah, outwardly and inwardly, for the blessings He has graciously bestowed upon you. Part of being thankful to Him is to obey Him and avoid disobeying him if you truly worship Him alone and do not associate any partners with Him.",
  2173:
      "Allah has only forbidden you from food which has died without being sacrificed in accordance with the sacred law, from flowing blood, from pork, and from that which had other than Allah's name mentioned over it when it was sacrificed. However, if someone is forced to eat something of these forbidden types of food, and he is not seeking to transgress by eating from it without dire need, and he does consume it over the bounds of necessity, then there is no sin upon him, and nor will he be punished. Verily, Allah is Most-Forgiving and Most-Merciful to whoever repents to Him from His slaves, and it is from His mercy that He overlooks the eating of these forbidden things in times of dire need.",
  2174:
      "Those who hide what Allah revealed in the scriptures and the signs of the truth and prophethood of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم – as the Jews and Christians did, in exchange for getting something menial in return for what they hide, such as leadership, status or money – they only eat into their bellies that which will cause them to suffer in the Fire. And on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will not speak to them with what they will like, but rather what will cause them grief; He will not praise them nor purify them [of their misdeeds], and they will receive a painful punishment.",
  2175:
      "They are the ones who are described and those who hide the truth that people are in need of. They are the ones who exchanged guidance for misguidance, as they hid true knowledge, thereby exchanging the forgiveness of Allah for His punishment. How enduring they are to do what will lead them into the Fire as if they do not care the punishment it contains [for them] given their indulgence!",
  2176:
      "That is the recompense for hiding knowledge and guidance. This is because Allah revealed the sacred scriptures with the truth, which necessitates that it [the truth] must be made clear and not concealed. And those who disagree with the sacred scriptures, believing some of it and hiding some of it, oppose the truth and have departed from it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. People often go the wrong way because they do not use their reason, and follow whoever came before them in their error, copying them blindly without thinking.\n2. If someone does not benefit from the blessings Allah has given them - in terms of their mind, hearing and sight - then it makes them like those who have lost these blessings.\n3. Some of those with the severest punishment on the Day of Judgement are those who hide the knowledge that Allah revealed and the guidance that His messengers came with.\n4. It is from Allah’s blessings for His faithful servants that He only made a few things prohibited and made what is al¬ lowed vast.",
  2177:
      "Doing good that pleases Allah does not just mean turning towards the east or the west or differing over it. Rather, all virtue is in the one who has faith in Allah as the sole deity, the Day of Resurrection, all of the angels, all of the revealed scriptures, and all of the prophets without discrimination. He is the one who spends in charity, despite his love and desire for it, towards his relatives, the orphan (i.e. the one who lost his father before the age of puberty), the poor, the stranger who is cut off from his family and homeland while traveling, those who encounter a need that causes them to ask people for help, and to free slaves from enslavement and captivity. He is the one who establishes the prayer and performs it completely as Allah instructed and pays the Zakat that is obligatory on him. They uphold their promises if they make one, have patience through poverty, hardship, illness, and do not flee in the heat of battle. The people described with these characteristics are the ones who are true to Allah in their faith and their actions. They are the ones who are truly pious in that they follow what Allah has commanded them to do and refrain from what Allah has prohibited for them.",
  2178:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, it is decreed for you that in cases where someone deliberately attacks and kills someone, the punishment for the murderer should be the same as their crime: the freeman is to be killed for the freeman; the slave for the slave; and the female for the female. If the person killed had forgiven before his death, or his guardian has forgiven in return for the payment of blood money (a sum of money paid by the murderer in return for being pardoned), then the person who forgives should ask for the sum of money in a good way, without reminding them of your favors or harm them. The murderer should also pay the sum of money in a good way, without hesitation or delay. Forgiveness and taking blood money instead is a relief and mercy for this Muslim nation. So whoever attacks the murderer after his pardon and the acceptance of the blood money will receive a painful punishment from Allah.",
  2179:
      "And there is life for you in what Allah has decreed from legal retribution because it spares your blood and prevents further transgressions from occurring between you. Those with foresight and sound judgment will understand this: the ones who are mindful of Allah, keeping to His sacred law and doing as He instructs.",
  2180:
      "It has been decreed for you that if one of you is showing signs or causes of death and is leaving a large amount of wealth behind, then they should make a will to distribute it to parents and close relatives per the sacred law, which is not to exceed one-third of the wealth (the rest of the wealth would be distributed according to the laws of inheritance). Making this will is a firm duty upon those who are heedful of Allah. This ruling was established before verses about inheritance were revealed. When the verses about inheritance were revealed, they made it clear who was eligible to inherit and how much they could inherit.",
  2181:
      "Whoever then changes a will, whether adding to it, subtracting from it, or preventing something after knowing what the will contains, the sin of it will be upon those who altered it and not the owner of the will. Indeed, Allah hears all that His slaves say and knows all that they do, and He is aware of every detail of the situations they are in.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The devotion that Allah loves lies in the completion of faith and doing good actions; but outward obedience alone is not enough.\n2. The practice of the law of equivalent punishment, which Allah decreed for you in matters of life and other things, is one of the greatest way to save lives and stop transgression and oppression.\n3. The verses demonstrate the importance of the will, especially for those who have something to leave to their relatives, and highlights the sin of anyone changing the will of someone who has died.",
  2182:
      "Whoever knows that there is an error in judgment or injustices committed by the person who made the will and rectifies the matter by advising the owner of the will or reconciles between parties who disagree about the will, then there is no blame on them. Rather, this person is rewarded for rectifying these matters. Indeed, Allah is Most Forgiving and Most Compassionate towards those among His slaves who repent to him.",
  2183:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, fasting has been decreed upon you by your Lord, as He decreed it on those before you, so that you may become mindful of Allah, protecting yourself from His punishment through righteous acts, and fasting is one of the greatest of them.",
  2184:
      "The prescribed fast is for a small number of days from the year. But whoever among you is ill with an illness that makes fasting difficult or traveling, then they do not need to fast, and they can make up for these days by fasting the same number of other days. Those who can fast but do not should compensate by feeding a poor person every day they did not fast. Whoever feeds more than one poor person per day or feeds and makes up the fast as well, then that is better. Fasting is better for you than not fasting and feeding a poor person instead if you only knew the distinction of fasting. This was the first of Allah's decreed laws about fasting: whoever wanted to fast could do so, and whoever did not want to fast was permitted not to do so and instead feed a poor person. Afterward, Allah made fasting a mandatory obligation for every able person who has reached puberty.",
  2185:
      "The Quran was first revealed to the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم on the Night of Decree in the month of Ramadan. Allah revealed it as a guide for people, with clear proof of its guidance and the criteria to distinguish truth from falsehood. Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is in sound health is required to fast. Whoever is ill such that fasting is difficult or is traveling is allowed not to fast. If they do not fast, then they must make up these fasts for the days they missed at another time. Allah intends to have you traverse the path of ease and not hardship in what He decrees for you. He wants you to complete fasting all days of the month and glorify Him upon the completion of Ramadan, on the day of Eid, as He aided you and made it possible for you to fast. This is so you thank Allah for guiding you to this religion, which He has approved for you.",
  2186:
      "If they ask you, O Prophet, about how close Allah is and about His answering of prayers, Allah is close to them and knows everything about them. He hears their prayer, and they do not need intermediaries to raise their voices. Allah responds to the call of whoever calls Him sincerely, praying to Him; so, let them be devoted to Him and His sacred law, firm in their faith, as that is the best route to Allah's response – perhaps in that way, they might be rightly guided in worldly and sacred matters.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah made fasting obligatory on Muslims and on people who came before them, because it brings about mindfulness of Allah, and helps sustain it.\n2. Allah distinguished the month of Ramadan by revealing the Qur’an in it. It is the month of the Qur’an, which is why the Prophet (peace be upon him) would study it with Gabriel during Ramadan.\n3. The sacred law of Islam is based, in its principles and practice, on making things easy and removing difficulty. Allah has not, therefore, made things difficult for us in following this way of life.\n4. The verses instruct the believers to glorify Allah by chanting the takblr on the night and day of the Eid, thanking Allah for His blessings and recognizing His gifts.\n5. The verses remind the believers of the closeness of Allah to His servants, and that He surrounds them, knowing everything about them, and that He listens to their prayers and responds to them.",
  2187:
      "At first, a man was not allowed to eat or approach his wife if he had gone to sleep on the night of a fast and then woke up before dawn. Allah replaced this ruling, allowing you, O believers, to have relations with your wives during the nights of fasting. They are a protection for you, keeping you chaste, and you are a cover for them, keeping them chaste. You both need each other. Allah knew that you were betraying yourselves by doing what you were not allowed to do, so He showed mercy, turned to you when you asked for forgiveness and made things easier for you. So, have relations with them, and seek the children Allah has decreed for you, and eat and drink as you please during the whole night until the break of true dawn appears with the light of dawn separated from the darkness of the night. Then, complete your fast by abstaining from anything that breaks the fast from the break of dawn until sunset. And do not have relations with your wives while you are in a spiritual retreat in the mosques because that invalidates the retreat. These laws are Allah's limits: between what is allowed and what is forbidden– so do not ever go near them. Whoever goes near the limits of Allah comes close to falling into that which is prohibited. By setting out a clear explanation of these laws, Allah makes His verses obvious to people so that they may be mindful of Him by doing what He instructs and leaving what He has prohibited.",
  2188:
      "Do not unlawfully take each other's wealth, such as by stealing it, taking it by force, or by cheating. Do not create legal disputes with rulers to obtain others' wealth wrongfully while you know that Allah has prohibited you from doing this. Sinning while knowing of its prohibition is more shameful and greater in punishment.",
  2189:
      "They ask you, O Messenger, about the formation of the new moons and their changing states. Tell them in reply about the wisdom behind this: that they are a way for people to measure time so they know when to perform their acts of worship, such as the months of Hajj and fasting and the completion of the year for Zakat. It is also so that they know the time for their transactions, such as the deadlines for paying blood money or debts. It is not righteousness or piety that you come to houses from the rear wearing your iḥrām for Hajj or Umrah, as you used to claim pre-Islam. Rather, true righteousness lies in those mindful of Allah, outwardly and inwardly. Entering houses from their correct doors is easier for you and less troublesome. Allah does not overburden you with difficulty and hardship, so create a barrier from the punishment of Allah through good deeds, so perhaps you may be successful in achieving what you desire, and attaining salvation from what you fear.",
  2190:
      "Fight with the desire to raise the word of Allah against those among the disbelievers who fight you to turn you away from the religion of Allah. But do not overstep Allah's limits by killing children, women, the elderly, or by mutilating the dead, and so on. Allah does not love those who overstep the limits He has established and made sacred.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The rulings of the sacred law are based on making things easier and less troubling, because Allah understands the weakness of His servants.\n2. The legislation of i’tikaf- staying in spiritual retreat in the mosque for worship - involves not doing anything that goes against the aims of i’tikaf, including being affectionate with women.\n3. The verses demonstrate the prohibition of taking the wealth of others unjustly, and of using any ways that achieve this, including bribery.\n4. True righteousness and mindfulness is through following the sacred law and honouring its limits.\n5. Injustice or overstepping the limits is prohibited, because the religion of Islam is based on justice and kindness.",
  2191:
      "And kill them where you come across them and expel them from the place they expelled you from - which is Mecca. The calamity that results from preventing those who believe from worship and returning them to disbelief is worse than killing. And do not initiate fights within the Sacred Mosque out of veneration for it unless they start fighting you there. If they initiate fighting in the Sacred Mosque, then kill them. A disbeliever's death is the recompense if they attack within the Sacred Mosque.",
  2192:
      "If they cease fighting you and stop disbelieving, then stop fighting them. Allah forgives whoever repents to Him and does not hold them to account for their past sins. He is Compassionate with them and does not rush to punish them.",
  2193:
      "Fight the disbelievers until they cease preventing people from Allah's path and there is no polytheism or disbelief within them, and until the apparent way of life is the religion of Allah. But if they cease disbelieving and stop deterring others from the path of Allah, then stop fighting them. There is no enmity except against transgressors who disbelieve and deter others from the path of Allah.",
  2194:
      "The sacred month in which Allah enabled you to enter the Sacred Mosque and perform Umrah (Year 7 AH) is to compensate for the sacred month in which the polytheists prevented you from entering the Sacred Mosque (in Year 6 AH). The Law of Legal Retribution applies when the limits are overstepped concerning sacred things, such as the sacred land, the sacred month, and being in a state of ritual consecration (Ihram) for pilgrimage to the Sacred Mosque. When someone wrongs you in any of these, do unto them, as they did unto you, but do not go beyond what they have done: Allah does not love those who overstep His limits. And fear Allah in going beyond what He has permitted for you. Know that Allah is with those who are mindful of Him by granting them success and supporting them.",
  2195:
      "Spend your wealth in obedience to Allah, in striving for His sake, and do not throw yourselves into destruction by leaving the struggle and spending for His sake or by throwing yourselves into something that will lead to your demise. Behave with excellence and kindness in your worship, transactions, and behavior. Allah loves those who strive toward excellence in all of their affairs, giving them a greater reward and leading them to true guidance.",
  2196:
      "Perform Hajj and Umrah completely, seeking only Allah's pleasure. If you are prevented from completing them by illness or an enemy, then you should sacrifice what is easily available of sacrificial animals, such as camels, cows, or sheep, before you take off your Ihram, and do not shave your heads or cut your hair until the sacrificial animals have reached the place where slaughtering them is permissible. If you are prevented from entering the Sacred Sanctuary, then perform the slaughter (of the sacrificial animal) wherever you have stopped; yet if you can enter the Sacred Sanctuary, perform it on the Day of Sacrifice (10th of Dhul-Hijjah) or within the following days of tashriq (11th, 12th and 13th of Dhul-Hijjah). Whoever among you is ill or has a problem with his hair or head, such as lice or the like, and shaves his head for that reason, then that is not a problem. He should, however, fast for three days, or feed six poor people from the area of the Sanctuary, or sacrifice a sheep to be distributed among the poor within the Sanctuary. If you are living in times of peace, then whoever takes the opportunity to perform Umrah in the months of Hajj, enjoying in between those things that are not allowed when performing the pilgrimages, should sacrifice whatever is easily available: a sheep or a seventh of a camel or cow. If they cannot make a sacrifice, they must fast for three days during the days of Hajj to make up for it and seven more days when they return home, making ten days altogether. This practice of having a break between Umrah and Hajj and sacrificing an animal or fasting for those unable to make a sacrifice is only for people who do not live within or close to the Sanctuary of the Sacred Mosque. As for those who live within the Sanctuary or close to it, they do not do this because they do not need to due to their constant presence and enjoyment of being able to make Umrah or Tawaf freely any other time of the year. Be mindful of Allah by following what He makes sacred law, respecting His limits, and understanding that Allah is firm in punishing those who go against what He instructs. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The goal of fighting or struggling for the sake of Allah is to establish Allah’s order and to remove whatever stops people from hearing the truth or listening to it.\n2. Not struggling for the sake of Allah is a cause of the nation’s destruction, because it leads to its weakness and encourages enemies against it.\n3. The verses emphasise the obligation of completing Hajj and Umrah, and the permission to complete them with the sacrifice of an animal for those who are prevented from entering the Sanctuary.",
  2197:
      "The time of the Hajj is within the well-known months, starting with the month of Shawwal and ending on the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah. Sexual relations and things that lead to it are prohibited for any person who decides to perform the Hajj in these months once he enters the state of iḥrām. In addition, the prohibition of going against Allah by committing sins becomes even more emphasized at this time due to the sacredness of the time and place. The pilgrim may not quarrel with anyone, causing them to become angry and leading to a fight. If you do any good, Allah knows and will reward you for it. To perform the Hajj, take an adequate amount of food and drink, but remember that the best provision for all of your affairs is being always mindful of Allah. O people of sound mind, fear Me (Allah) by fulfilling My instructions and avoiding My prohibitions.",
  2198:
      "There is no sin in seeking lawful provision by trading or other ways during the Hajj. When you leave Arafat after having spent the day there on the 9th of Dhul-Hijjah, and when you head towards Muzdalifah that night of the 10th of Dhul-Hijjah, remember Allah by exalting and praising Him and by supplicating to Him at Al-Mashʿar Al-Ḥarām (The Sacred Grove) in Muzdalifah. Remember that Allah has guided you to the teachings of His path and the sacred rites of Hajj to His House, for you were unaware of His Sacred Law before this.",
  2199:
      "Then leave Arafat just as the people who followed Abraham (peace be upon him) used to do, and do not leave out stopping at Arafat as the People of Ignorance (i.e., pre-Islam) used to do. Seek forgiveness from Allah for any shortcomings and defects in performing the rites that He ordained upon you. Indeed, Allah forgives those of His slaves who repent, and He is Merciful towards them.",
  2200:
      "When you have completed the rites of Hajj, remember Allah and increase your praise of Him, just as you exalt and praise your forefathers – or even more than that, for every favor you enjoy comes from Him. People are different: some are disbelieving polytheists who only believe in this worldly life. Such people will only ask Allah for the blessing and adornments of this world in the form of health, wealth, and children. However, they will not receive anything of what Allah has prepared for His faithful slaves in the Afterlife. This is due to their desire for this world and neglect of the Afterlife.",
  2201:
      "Yet there is another group of people who have faith in Allah and the Afterlife who ask their Lord for the blessings of this world and the ability to do righteous deeds, just as they ask Him to receive entry into Paradise and safety from the punishment of the Fire.",
  2202:
      "Those who pray for the good of this world and the Afterlife will receive their share of the great reward for their good actions in the world, for Allah is Swift in taking account of actions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1.Hajj is an act of worship in which the believer pays respects to the symbols of Allah. For this reason, Allah has prohibited any indecent word or action that goes against this.\n2.It is permissible to trade and seek provision during the Hajj as there is no conflict between the two acts.\n3. The pilgrim must spend the night preceding the 10th of Dhu Al-Hijjah in Muzdalifah.\n4. The pilgrim must remember Allah much when he completes the acts of Hajj.\n5. People have different goals: some are concerned with this world only and do not ask Allah for anything else; whereas others ask for the best of this world and the Afterlife, and that is the correct way.",
  2203:
      "Remember Allah by saying, 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is Greatest!), and, 'Lā ilāha illā Allah' (There is no deity except Allah) on the 11th, 12th, and 13th of Dhul-Hijjah. If anyone is in a hurry, he may leave Minā after pelting stones on the 12th of Dhul-Hijjah – and there will be no sin as Allah has granted that permission. It is also acceptable if someone stays to pelt stones on the 13th of Dhul-Hijjah – this is better as it was the practice of the Prophet (peace be upon him). All of this applies to those who are mindful of Allah during their Hajj and carry it out following Allah's instruction. Be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Realize that you will return to Him alone, and He will recompense you for your actions.",
  2204:
      "There is a type of person who is a Hypocrite, but his speech concerning the life of this world impresses you, O Prophet, which may lead you to consider him to be sound of mind and even honest and sincere because of his words. However, he only means to protect himself and his financial interests. He calls Allah to witness that he has faith and goodness in his heart while he is, in fact, lying; he bears great hostility and hatred for the Muslims.",
  2205:
      "When this Hypocrite leaves you, he works hard to cause corruption in the world by committing sins, and he destroys crops and kills animals. Allah does not love corruption in the world, and He does not love those that cause it.",
  2206:
      "When this person who causes corruption is advised to be mindful of Allah by respecting His limits and avoiding His prohibitions, his pride and arrogance prevent him from repenting, and he continues to sin. The only appropriate reward for him is entry into Hell. What a terrible place of residence for its inhabitants!",
  2207:
      "There is another type of person who is a believer who will forfeit his soul to follow his Lord and to strive in His path, seeking His pleasure. Allah's mercy for His slaves is vast, and He is Kind to them.",
  2208:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, enter Islam completely and do not leave out any part of it as the People of the Scripture do by believing in some parts of the book and disbelieving in other parts. Do not follow the paths of the Devil because he has made it clear that he is your enemy.",
  2209:
      "If you slip up or go astray after clear proofs have come to you in which there is no ambiguity, then know that Allah is Mighty in His ability and power, Wise in His planning and establishing of sacred laws. So, fear and glorify Him.",
  2210:
      "These people who follow the path of the Devil instead of the path of truth are only waiting for Allah to come to them, as befits His majesty, on the Day of Resurrection in the shadows of clouds to judge them and for the angels to come and surround them from all sides. At that time, Allah will judge them once and for all. To Allah alone shall all affairs relating to creation return.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. In reality, righteousness is not simply the performance of many good actions; but it also means following and obeying the sacred laws.\n2. People will not be judged by their forms and words, but by the reality of their actions which show what is hidden in their hearts.\n3. Causing corruption on the earth is a common feature of those who are arrogant. Allah does not love corruption and those that cause corruption.\n4. A person has not truly submitted to Allah Almighty unless he totally accepts this way of life inwardly and outwardly.",
  2211:
      "O Prophet, ask the Jews reprimandingly about how many clear signs proving the truthfulness of the messengers were given to them by Allah. Despite this, they denied it and turned away from them. If anyone exchanges Allah's favor with disbelief and denial after being aware of it and after it has become apparent, then Allah is intense in punishing the disbelievers and the deniers.",
  2212:
      "For those who disbelieve in Allah, the worldly life and its temporary pleasures and enjoyments have been made to seem glamorous. They mock those who have faith in Allah and the Last Day. Those who are mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will be above such people in the Afterlife when Allah will make them live in the gardens of Paradise. Allah gives without limit or account to whichever of His creations He wishes.",
  2213:
      "People were one community. All of them were united upon guidance, following the way of their father, Adam, until the devils misguided them. They were then split into believers and disbelievers. For this reason, Allah sent messengers bringing glad tidings of the mercy of Allah for those who had faith in Him and followed Him and warning the disbelievers of Allah's severe punishment. With the messengers, Allah also sent books containing the undoubtable truth so they could judge between people concerning their disagreements. Only those given the Torah differed concerning Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم and his message despite it being clear. They did this out of injustice and jealousy. Allah then enabled the believers to recognize guidance from misguidance by His permission and will. Allah guides whomever He wishes to a perfectly straight path: the path of faith.",
  2214:
      "Do you believers think you will enter Paradise while you have not faced a trial like the people of the past? They were afflicted with severe sickness and poverty and were shaken by frightening events to the extent that they wanted the help of Allah to come as quickly as possible, and the messenger and the believers with him began saying, 'When is the help of Allah coming?' The help of Allah is close to those who have faith and trust in Him.",
  2215:
      "Your Companions, O Prophet, ask you what they should spend from their diverse wealth and where they should allocate it. Say to them in reply: Any permissible and pure wealth you spend should be given to parents, close relatives in need, needy orphans, the poor who have no wealth, and the traveler who is cut off from his family and home. Allah knows of any good you do as believers, no matter how small. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will reward you for it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1.Being ungrateful for Allah’s favours and not using them in His service will result in their disappearance and them being turned into a source of hardship.\n2. Allah has created His servants on the natural path of monotheism and belief in Him. Satan and his helpers are the ones who then turned some of them away from this natural path to idolatry.\n3. The greatest loss leading to failure is when the nation differs in its book and sacred law, and begin cursing one another and declaring one another disbelievers.\n4. Guidance to the truth of what people differ in and recognizing the right path is in Allah’s Hand. It can be requested from Him by believing in and submitting to Him.\n5. It is from Allah’s natural law that He tests His faithful servants according to their degree of faith and reliance on Him.\n6. The greatest thing that will assist in being patient at the time of calamity is to follow the example of the righteous.",
  2216:
      "Fighting in Allah's path has been chosen for believers even though it is something that is naturally disliked because it means risking one's life and wealth. However, you may dislike something when, in reality, it is good and beneficial. An example of this is fighting in Allah's path. In addition to the great reward, you attain victory against the enemy and promote Allah's word. On the other hand, you may like something when, in reality, it is bad and harmful to you, such as staying behind from fighting: this will result in you being defeated and the enemy gaining authority over you. Allah knows full well what is good and what is not, whereas you do not. Therefore, follow His commands, for that is better for you.",
  2217:
      "The people ask you, O Prophet, about the law regarding fighting in the sacred months of Dhū Al-Qa'dah, Dhul-Hijjah, Muḥarram, and Rajab. Say to them: Fighting in these months is a serious offense in the sight of Allah and is detested, just as the polytheists' preventing from the path of Allah is also disapproved. Blocking the believers' access to the Sacred Mosque and removing the people of the Sacred Mosque from it is worse than fighting in a sacred month in the sight of Allah. The idolatry that they are engulfed in is worse than killing. O believers, the polytheists will continue their oppression by fighting you until they turn you away from your religion of truth towards their false religion if they can. If anyone turns back from his religion and dies upon disbelief in Allah, his good deeds will become void, and his outcome in the Afterlife will be the Fire, wherein he will live eternally.",
  2218:
      "Those who believe in Allah and His Messenger, leave their homes as emigrants towards Allah and His Messenger, and fight to promote and ensure Allah's word reigns supreme are the ones who are eager for Allah's mercy and forgiveness. Allah is Most Forgiving of the sins of His slaves and is All-Merciful towards them.",
  2219:
      "O Prophet, your Companions ask you about wine (which refers to anything that impairs the mind or intoxicates it), specifically concerning the legality of its drinking, selling, and purchasing. They also ask you about gambling (which refers to wealth taken in a competition between two people in which both contribute to the winning total). In response to them, say: They both have many spiritual and worldly harms, such as loss of intellect and wealth and breeding hatred and enmity. On the other hand, there are a few benefits, such as a financial reward for the winner of a bet. However, the harm and sin resulting from them outweigh the benefits, so a logical person should avoid such actions. This statement of Allah lays the foundation for the prohibition of wine. They also ask you, O Prophet, how much they should spend on charity. Say in reply to them: Spend whatever is easy and in excess of your needs. With such clear explanations, Allah describes the sacred law to you so that you may reflect. Initially, this was the law regarding charity, but later, Allah established the obligation of Zakat, which requires paying a set amount on certain possessions if one has owned such possessions for a particular period of time.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Not knowing the end result of a thing sometimes makes a person dislike a thing that benefits him and like a thing that harms him. A person must ask Allah to guide him to the right path.\n2. Islam came to preserve goodness and prohibit any violation of it: the worst form of violation is preventing people from the path of Allah.\n3. The disbelievers will remain enemies of Islam and Muslims until they remove them from their path. Allah will weaken the plot of the disbelievers.\n4. Faith in Allah, emigration to Him and striving in His path are the most effective means by which a person can gain Allah’s mercy and forgiveness.\n5. In consideration of people’s best interests, the sacred law has prohibited anything where the harm is greater than the benefit, even though there may be some benefit in it.",
  2220:
      "Allah has established these rules so that you may think about what benefits you in this world and the Afterlife. Your Companions ask you, O Prophet, about the guardianship of orphans and how they should deal with them: whether they can incorporate their wealth with orphans for expenses, food, and accommodation. Say in reply to them: If you are kind to them by arranging their affairs without taking anything in return and without touching their wealth, it is better in the sight of Allah and carries greater reward, better, and safer for their wealth. However, there is no harm if you combine their wealth with yours for living expenses, as they are your brothers in faith, and it is customary for brothers to help and look after the affairs of one another. Allah knows the guardian who, by combining the wealth of orphans with his, means harm and the one who means well. If He wished to make it difficult for you concerning orphans, He would have done so. Instead, He has made it easy for you to deal with them, as the sacred law is based on ease. Allah is Mighty, and nothing can overpower Him. He is Wise in His planning and legislation.",
  2221:
      "Do not get married, O believers, to those women who give partners to Allah until they have faith in Him alone and enter the path of Islam. A woman who is a slave but has faith in Allah and His Messenger is better than a free woman who worships idols, even though you may be impressed by her beauty and wealth. Do not give Muslim women in marriage to men who are polytheists. A slave man who has faith in Allah and His Messenger is better than a free man who is an idolater, even though he may seem impressive to you. Men and women who commit idolatry, invite by their statements and actions, towards that which will lead to entering the Fire. Allah, on the other hand, invites virtuous deeds, which will lead to entry into Paradise and forgiveness of sins by His permission and grace. Allah makes His verses clear for people so that they may learn and act obediently.",
  2222:
      "O Prophet, your Companions ask you about menses (which is the blood of menstruation that naturally comes out of the womb at certain times of the month). Say in reply to them: Menses are harmful to the man and woman, so avoid sexual intercourse during this time. Do not approach them for sexual intercourse until the blood stops and they have cleaned themselves by taking a bath. If the blood has stopped and they have cleaned themselves, then you may have sexual intercourse with them through the vagina in the manner that Allah has permitted for you. Allah loves those who frequently repent from their sins and are extra mindful of cleanliness.",
  2223:
      "Your wives are a place to sow your seed: they produce children for you just as the land produces crops. So approach the plantation, which is the vagina, from whichever direction and in whichever manner you wish as long as intercourse takes place in the vagina. Send forth something good for yourselves, such as having sexual intercourse with the intention of gaining closeness to Allah and with the hope of pious offspring. Be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions, such as those relating to women. Know that you are to meet Him on the Day of Resurrection and will have to stand before Him to receive the reward for your actions. O Prophet, give the believers good news of everlasting blessings that will surely please them when they meet their Lord: seeing His Blessed Face.",
  2224:
      "Do not use the name of Allah in your oath as an excuse for not doing good, e.g., being mindful of Him, being virtuous, and reconciling between people. Rather, if you have taken an oath not to do any good actions, then do good actions and make an expiation for the oath. Allah hears your statements, knows your actions, and will recompense you for them accordingly. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Marriage between Muslims and idolaters is prohibited due to the huge gap between faith and idolatry.\n2. The verses indicate that a guardian is necessary for the contract of marriage, since Allah addresses the guardians with respect to the prohibition of giving women in marriage to idolaters.\n3. Sexual intercourse with a woman during menstruation is prohibited until she becomes clean and takes a bath. But intimate acts except intercourse are permitted during menstruation and before a purifying bath.\n4. The sacred law requires physical purity from all types of filth.\n5. The believer is encouraged to focus on the Afterlife in everything, even in acts of pleasure, and to do good actions that will benefit him in the next life.",
  2225:
      "Allah will not take you to account for those oaths that you swear unintentionally, such as if someone carelessly says, 'No, by Allah!' or 'Yes, by Allah!' For such oaths, there is no need to make any expiation nor any further consequences. However, He will take you to account for intentional oaths. Allah forgives and tolerates the sins of His slaves and does not hasten to send punishment.",
  2226:
      "For those who swear an oath not to have sexual intercourse with their wives, there is a waiting period not longer than four months, starting from the date of the oath. This is known as al-Elaa (Oath of Abstinence). If he abandons the oath and engages in sexual intercourse after having sworn not to, and this happens within the four months, then Allah forgives them. Allah is merciful and has established expiation as a way out from such an oath.",
  2227:
      "If such a man is determined to continue his oath and passes the four-month period, intending by a divorce, then Allah hears their statements, including the divorce, and He knows their states and intentions and will recompense them accordingly.",
  2228:
      "Divorced women must not remarry after a divorce for three menstrual periods. If they are true in their faith in Allah and the Last Day, they may not hide the fetus that Allah has created in their wombs. Their husbands, who issued the divorce, have the first right to recall them during the waiting period if they intend to live well with them and to cancel what has occurred because of the divorce. Wives have rights and obligations like husbands in a manner that people are accustomed to. Men have a higher rank than them regarding responsibility and divorce matters. Allah is Mighty, and nothing can overcome His decree. He is Wise in His legislation and planning.",
  2229:
      "The divorce, after which a husband may recall his wife, can only happen twice. He may divorce her the first time, recall her, divorce her again, and recall her again. After two divorces, he must either keep her in his marriage, living in a good way with her or divorce her for the third time, being good to her by fulfilling her rights. At the time of divorce, husbands may not take any part of the dowry that they had given their wives. However, if a woman is unhappy with her husband because of his character or looks, and the couple is of the view that, because of this, they will not be able to fulfill the rights of marriage, then they should present the matter to a person related to them or someone familiar with them. If they feel that the couple will not be able to fulfill their marital rights, then there is no harm if the woman offers to give something to the husband in return for a divorce. These laws of the Shariah are the criterion for the lawful and unlawful, so do not overstep them. Whoever violates the limits of Allah with regard to the lawful and the unlawful, then such people are wronging their souls, bringing themselves to destruction, and exposing themselves to Allah's anger and punishment.",
  2230:
      "If the husband divorces her for the third time, he may not remarry her until she gets married to another man in a valid marriage that is genuine and not merely contracted to make her lawful for the original husband and where sexual intercourse has taken place. Should the second husband divorce her or pass away, then there is no sin upon the woman and her first husband for returning to one another with a new marriage contract and dowry if they think they will likely be able to fulfill one another's rights in accordance with sacred law. These laws are made clear by Allah for people who know His laws and limits, as they are the ones who benefit from them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah explains the laws of marriage and divorce in full so that people know the limits of the lawful and the unlawful and do not overstep these limits.\n2. In married life, the couple must behave in a good manner. If this is not possible, then there is nothing wrong in divorce; and either of the partners may ask for it.",
  2231:
      "When you divorce a woman, and they approach the end of their waiting period, you have the right to take them back or to leave them in a good way until their waiting period is over. Do not take them back to oppress and harm them, as was the practice in pre-Islamic times. Whoever acts intending to cause harm to them has wronged himself by exposing himself to sin and punishment. Do not make Allah's words the object of mockery and play out of insolence. Remember Allah's favors upon you, the most important of which is the revelation you have received in the form of the Quran and Sunnah, through which He reminds you through encouragement and warning. Fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Know that Allah knows everything, and nothing is hidden from Him, and he will compensate you for your actions accordingly.",
  2232:
      "When you divorce women less than three times and their waiting period ends, do not stop them from returning to their husbands with a new marriage contract if they wish to do so in mutual agreement with their husbands. This law prohibiting them from being prevented is a reminder for those among you who have faith in Allah and the Last Day. If you obey, this will bring you greater growth in goodness and is better at keeping your honor and deeds free of impurities. Allah knows the reality and outcome of matters, whereas you do not.",
  2233:
      "Mothers who intend to complete the breastfeeding period should nurse their children for two full years. The father of a child is responsible for the maintenance and clothing of a divorced mother who breastfeeds her child in accordance with the customs of society so long as they do not contradict sacred law. No soul is burdened beyond what it can handle. No parent is allowed to use the child as a means to harm the other. The heir (who would inherit from the child if the child were to pass away leaving behind wealth) shall be responsible, if the father dies without leaving any wealth, for the same obligations as the father's. If the parents decide to wean the child before two years finish, then there is no sin on them if this is done after mutual consultation and agreement that it is indeed in the child's best interests. If you wish to hire wet nurses for your children instead of their mothers, there is no sin in doing so, provided you pay the agreed wages of such wet nurses without any shortchanging or delay. Be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, and know that Allah sees everything you do and nothing is hidden from Him. He will recompense you for any deed you do.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A man is prohibited from keeping his wife in marriage with the intention of causing harm to her if he does not wish to live with her - this is oppression.\n2. It is prohibited for a guardian to prevent a woman from getting married to a suitable match or from going back to her first husband, if she so desires.\n3. Following the sacred law with respect to family relations brings goodness.\n4. The sacred law has secured the mother’s right to nurse her child, even if she is divorced. The husband, in this case, is still required to provide her maintenance as long as she nurses his child.\n5. Allah has prohibited the married couple from using their children as a means of causing harm to one another.\n6. It is encouraged that all affairs related to married life be based on consultation and agreement between the married couple.",
  2234:
      "For those who pass away and leave behind women who are not pregnant, the widow must wait for a period of four months and ten days, during which she must not leave the husband's home, beautify herself, or get married. Once this period ends, there is no blame on their guardians if these women do these actions, which were previously prohibited during the waiting period, as long as it is done in accordance with societal norms and sacred law. Allah is well aware of what you do. None of your private or public actions are concealed from Him, and He will compensate you accordingly.",
  2235:
      "There is no sin on you if you hint at your desire to propose to a woman who is still in her waiting period after a divorce or after the death of her husband without explicitly declaring it. For example, a person may say, 'When your waiting period is over, let me know'. There is also no sin on you if you keep the desire to marry a woman who is in her waiting period to yourselves. Allah knows that you will mention them because of your strong desire for them, so He has allowed you to give a hint without being explicit. Beware of secretly making any promise to marry them while they are still in their waiting period, except in an acceptable manner (i.e., giving a hint to them). Do not ratify the marriage contract during the waiting period. Know that Allah knows what you are concealing, so be mindful of Him and do not go against His command. Know that Allah Forgives the person who repents to Him and that He is Tolerant and does not hasten to punish.",
  2236:
      "There is no sin on you if you divorce your wives with whom you have entered into marriage before you have sexual intercourse with them and before you fix a dowry for them. If you must divorce them in such a situation, they will not be entitled to any dowry from you, but they must be given something that they will enjoy to make it easy on their feelings. This must be done by both a rich and a poor man in accordance with their financial abilities. This gift is binding on those who wish to excel in their actions and dealings.",
  2237:
      "If you divorce your wives with whom you have entered into marriage before having sexual intercourse with them and you had fixed the amount of the dowry, you will have to pay half of this amount to them unless they give up this right of theirs or the husband wishes to pay the full dowry. To give up your right is closer to fearing Allah and obeying Him. Do not forget to show kindness and compassion to one another regarding rights. Allah sees what you do, so try to do what is best to earn His reward.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A waiting period is established for a widow in which she is not permitted to beautify herself or get married for a period of four months and ten days.\n2. A proposal may not be made to a woman whilst she in the waiting period, but a hint of the desire to marry her may be given without any clear mention of it. This applies even if the woman has been divorced by her husband three times.\n3. A believer is aware that Allah is watching him; and this makes him mindful of Allah and stops him from going against His sacred law.\n4. If a man divorces his wife before consummation of the marriage, he must give her half of the fixed dowry. If there was no fixed dowry, he must give her a gift that she is happy with.\n5. Dealings between spouses and relatives should be in an acceptable manner, based on forgiveness and pardon.",
  2238:
      "Guard your prayers by fulfilling them completely as Allah has instructed. In particular, guard the middle prayer, which is the 'Asr (afternoon) prayer, and stand before Allah in submission and devotion.",
  2239:
      "If you fear danger from an enemy or the like, and you are unable to perform the prayer in its full manner, then pray whilst walking or riding on camels, horses, or in any way you can. If the fear of danger has subsided, remember Allah in all the ways of remembrance He has taught you, and from them is performing prayer in its entirety. He has taught you what you did not know from light and guidance.",
  2240:
      "Those of you who pass away leaving behind wives must make a bequest for them to be provided with accommodation and maintenance for one year in which your heirs may not remove them. This is to make up for the loss they have suffered and out of respect for the deceased. If they leave before the end of the year by their own choice, there will be no sin on either you or them for what they do with themselves in terms of beautification and making themselves pleasant. Allah is Mighty, and no one can overpower Him. He is Wise in His planning, legislation, and decree. It should be noted that the majority of Quranic exegetes are of the opinion that the law contained in this verse has been abrogated by the verse: {When someone passes away and leaves behind a wife who is not pregnant, these women must wait for a period of four months and ten days} [Baqarah:234]",
  2241:
      "Divorced women should be gifted something such as clothing, money, or the like. This is to help make up for their emotional suffering because of the divorce. Such provision must fall within the husband's financial ability, and it is the duty of those who are mindful of Allah to fulfill His instructions and avoid His prohibitions.",
  2242:
      "As with the previous explanation, Allah explains these verses – containing His limits and laws – to the believers so that they understand and practice them to achieve the good of this world and the Hereafter.",
  2243:
      "Do you not know, O Prophet, about those who left their homes in huge numbers, fearing death due to plague or the like? This refers to a group of people from the Israelites. Allah said to them, 'Die!' and they did. Then Allah brought them back to life to show them that all matters are in His hands and that they have no control over any benefit or harm that may befall them. Allah is Gracious and Bountiful to people, but most people are not thankful to Allah for His favors.",
  2244:
      "Fight, O believers, the enemies of Allah, in support of His religion and to elevate His Word. Know that Allah hears your statements and knows your intentions and actions and that He will compensate you for them accordingly.",
  2245:
      "Who will act as a lender and spend his wealth in the path of Allah willingly with a good heart and intention so that this may come back to him multiplied? Allah restricts and widens provision and health in accordance with His wisdom and justice. In the Afterlife, you will return to Him alone, and He will recompense you for your actions accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses encourage people to guard the prayers and offer them perfectly by fulfilling all their essentials and prerequisites. If this is difficult, a person may pray in whichever manner is easy for him.\n2. Allah’s mercy towards His servants is obvious, as He has explained to them His verses in a perfect manner.\n3. At times, Allah tests some of His servants by reducing their provision and He tests others by giving them much provision: He does all of this in accordance with His absolute wisdom.",
  2246:
      "Do you not know, O Prophet, about those nobles from the Israelites after the time of Moses who said to a prophet of theirs, 'Appoint for us a king, and we will fight alongside him in Allah's path'. The prophet replied: 'It may be that if Allah makes fighting obligatory, you will not fight!'. They denied his suspicion that this would happen and insisted, 'What would stop us from fighting in Allah's path when our enemies have expelled us from our homes and have taken our children as prisoners? We will fight to restore our homeland and free our prisoners!' Yet, when Allah made fighting obligatory on them, they all turned away without remaining loyal to what they had promised - except for a few. Allah knows the wrongdoers who broke their promise and turned away from what He commanded, and He will recompense them for that.",
  2247:
      "Their prophet told them: Allah has appointed Saul as your king, under whose banner you must fight. Their leaders defiantly objected to this choice and said: How can he rule over us when we have a greater right to rule than he does since he is not from a royal progeny and has not been given vast wealth which he can use in his rule! Their prophet replied: Allah has selected him over you and has given him great knowledge and physical strength. Allah grants authority to whomever He wishes under His wisdom and mercy. Allah is Bountiful and grants to whomever He wishes. He knows which among His creations is most deserving.",
  2248:
      "Their prophet told them that the mark of his being truly chosen as their king was that Allah would return to them the Ark. This was a chest revered by the Israelites, which was taken away from them. In it, there was tranquility, and it contained relics left behind by the family of Moses and Aaron, such as the staff and a few tablets. In that, there is a clear sign if you truly are believers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the main reasons for fighting is in response to oppression of people who remove them from their homes and violate their rights.\n2. The verses indicate the most important attributes of a leader who is qualified to lead people: knowledge of what he leads them in and strength in that.\n3. The verses remind those who lead people not to be deceived by their words and to confirm and test their actions.\n4. Allah chooses whomever He wishes from His creation. Authority is in His control and He gives it to whomever He wishes in accordance with His wisdom and knowledge.\n5. Sometimes the rules used by people to judge others are not the same as those used by Allah.",
  2249:
      "When Saul set out with his warriors, he told them: Allah will test you with a river. If anyone drinks from it, he will not be on my path and must not join me in fighting. The person who does not drink from it will be on my path and will join me in the fight. If someone drinks a handful of water, this will be forgiven. When they reached the river, all the warriors drank from its water except a few who held back despite being extremely thirsty. After Saul had crossed the river with the believers, some of the warriors said: We do not possess the ability to fight Goliath and his army. Those who were convinced that they would meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection replied: How many are the instances of believing groups, small in number, defeating a larger group of disbelievers with Allah's permission and assistance? Victory is based on faith and not numbers. Allah is with the patient ones among His slaves, assisting them and leading them to victory.",
  2250:
      "When they came out to face Goliath and his army, they prayed to Allah, saying: Our Lord, grant us patience in our hearts, make our feet firm so that we do not flee or lose courage before our enemies, and give us Your assistance and support against the disbelieving people.",
  2251:
      "They defeated them by Allah's will. The prophet of Allah, David, killed their leader, Goliath, and Allah gave him kingship and prophethood and taught him many sciences as He willed, including those that are beneficial for this world and those for the Hereafter. If it were not for the established way of Allah to drive back the evil of some people through others, there would be corruption on earth as the evildoers would gain authority. However, Allah is Bountiful to all of His creation.",
  2252:
      "Those are the clear words of Allah which are recited to you, O Prophet, and they contain true stories and just laws. You are one of the messengers of the Lord of the Worlds.",
  2253:
      "We favored some of those messengers mentioned to you over others with respect to revelation, followers, and ranks. Some of them Allah spoke to, such as Moses. Others He granted a high rank, such as Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم – who was sent to all of humanity as the last of the prophets and whose nation was preferred over all other nations. We gave Jesus, son of Mary, clear miracles confirming his prophethood, such as bringing the dead to life and curing the leper and the blind. We also supported him with the angel Gabriel to give him strength in fulfilling Allah's instruction. If Allah had willed, those who came after the messengers would not have fought amongst themselves after receiving clear signs, but they disagreed and were divided. Some of them believed in Allah, while others did not. If Allah had willed, they would not have fought with each other, but Allah does as He wills: He guides whomever He wills to believe through His mercy and grace, and He allows whoever He wills to go astray through His justice and wisdom.",
  2254:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, spend from what We have provided you of various lawful wealth before the Day of Resurrection comes. On that day, there will be no transaction in which a person will gain what benefits them, nor friendship that will help them in times of distress, nor intercession that will ward off harm or bring benefit except after Allah's permission to whoever He wills and is pleased with. The disbelievers are truly the wrongdoers for their disbelief in Allah, the Exalted.",
  2255:
      "Allah is the One who alone deserves to be worshipped. He is the One who possesses a perfect life without death or deficiency. He is the Self-Existent and does not need any of His creation. All of creation only exists through Him and is in constant need of Him. Drowsiness or sleep does not come upon Him due to the perfection of His life and existence. He alone is sovereign over the heavens and the earth. No one can intercede before Him without His permission and acceptance. He knows the affairs of His creation in the past and what will happen to them in the future. The creation cannot encompass His knowledge unless He wills to reveal it to them. His Kursi [footstool] encompasses the vastness of the heavens and the earth. It is neither difficult nor overbearing for Him to preserve the heavens and the earth. He is Exalted in His essence, attributes, and control. He is the Greatest in His dominion and authority.",
  2256:
      "No one is forced to enter the religion of Islam; it is a clear, true religion, and as such, there is no need to compel anyone to believe in it. Guidance stands clear from misguidance. Whoever rejects all that is worshipped besides Allah, freeing oneself from them, and believes in Allah alone has held on to the religion's strongest, unbreakable means for salvation on the Day of Resurrection. Allah is All-Hearing of the words of His slaves, All-Knowing of their deeds, and He will recompense them accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has given different ranks to the various messengers and prophets in accordance with His knowledge and wisdom.\n2. Allah spoke directly to some messengers, such as Moses and Muhammad (peace be upon them).\n3. Faith, guidance, disbelief and misguidance are all based on Allah’s will and decree. To Him belongs perfect wisdom: if He willed, He would have guided the entire creation.\n4. The verse of the Throne (verse 255) is the greatest verse in the Qur’an, because of what it mentions within it of the attributes of Allah’s Lordship (Rububiyyah) and that only He has the right to be worshipped (Uluhiyyah) as well as a clarification of some of His Attributes.\n5. The act of entering into Islam and becoming a Muslim must be based on sincere acceptance and willingness because there is no compulsion in the path of Allah.\n6. The best way to gain happiness in this world and success in the Afterlife is by holding on to the Qur’an and Sunnah of the Prophet (peace be upon him).",
  2257:
      "Allah takes care of those who believe in Him. He grants them success and victory and takes them out of the darkness of disbelief and ignorance into the light of belief and knowledge. The allies of the disbelievers are the idols, who beautify disbelief to them and take them from the light of belief and knowledge into the darkness of disbelief and ignorance. They are the people of the Fire who will remain therein forever.",
  2258:
      "After mentioning the two groups, Allah gives two comparisons of the two groups, stating: \n O Prophet, have you seen the audacity of the tyrant who argued with Abraham about Allah's Lordship and Oneness? This happened because Allah had given him the power to rule, yet he transgressed. Abraham explained to him the attributes of his Lord by saying: My Lord is the One Who gives life to the creation and causes them to die. The tyrant stubbornly said: I, too, can give life and cause death. I can kill whomever I wish and pardon whomever I want to. Abraham then put forward another stronger argument by saying to him: The Lord I worship is the One Who brings the sun from the direction of the east; so, you try to bring it from the west! The tyrant was overcome by the compelling argument. Allah does not allow wrongdoers to be guided and traverse His Path due to their oppression and tyranny.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A leader should put his army through various types of tests in order to prove those who are patient from those who are not.\n2. Victory does not lie in numbers and preparation only, but the help and support from Allah plays a crucial part in achieving victory. patient. time of battle.\n3. At the time of hardship and difficulty only those whose hearts are filled with conviction of faith in Allah will remain\n4. Calling upon Allah with a sincere heart and with humility is a sure way for prayers to be answered, especially at the\n5. It is Allah’s order and wisdom that He repels the evil of some on earth by using others.\n6. The Qur’an contains true stories and just laws that prove the truth of the prophethood and message of Muhammad (peace be upon him)",
  2259:
      "Or have you seen the example of the one who passed by a town where the roofs had fallen, the walls had collapsed, and the people had died, making it a deserted ruin? Surprised, This man said: How will Allah ever bring these people back to life? Allah then caused him to die for one hundred years, brought him back to life, and asked him: How long were you dead for? He replied: I remained like that for one day or less than a day. Allah then said to him: In fact, you were like this for one hundred years. Look at the food you had with you, which has not gone bad despite this long period of time that has passed! Look at your dead donkey! We want to make you a clear sign to show people the Power We have to bring them back to life. Look at the bones of the donkey that are scattered. We will lift them, put them together, clothe them with flesh, and give them life again. When he saw this, the reality became clear to him, and he recognized Allah's omnipotence and admitted: I know Allah is the Most Capable of everything. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The distinguishing feature of the people of faith is that they have guidance and insight from Allah in all their worldly and religious affairs, unlike the people of disbelief.\n2. One of the main causes of rebellion is a person being deceived by power and authority making him blind to his reality.\n3. It is acceptable to debate with the people of falsehood in order to explain the truth to them and show them their error.\n4. Allah’s power is great and He is able to do anything, including giving life after death.",
  2260:
      "O Prophet, remember when Abraham said: O My Lord, show me how the dead come back to life. Allah asked him: Do you not believe in this? Abraham replied: I do believe, but I just want to put my heart at ease. So, Allah instructed him: Take four birds and tame them. Then, cut them up into pieces and place a part of each bird on the mountains around you. Then call those birds, and you will see that they will come quickly to you, being brought back to life. Know, O Abraham, that Allah is Mighty in His dominion and Wise in His instruction, legislation, and creation.",
  2261:
      "The similitude of the reward of the believers who spend their wealth in Allah's path is like a grain planted by a farmer in fertile ground. This grain then produces seven spikes, each carrying a hundred grains. Allah multiplies the reward for whomever of His slaves He wishes and gives them without anything in return. Allah is Bountiful and Generous, and He knows who deserves their reward multiplied.",
  2262:
      "Those who spend their wealth in Allah's obedience and pleasure and do not nullify their reward afterward by reminding people of their favor by their words or actions will receive their reward from their Lord. They will not fear what awaits them, nor will they grieve over the past because of the great bliss they will enjoy.",
  2263:
      "A kind word that makes a believer happy or forgiving the ill-mannered one is better than charity, followed by the harm caused by reminding the person of the favor. Allah does not need His slaves; He is clement as He has not hasten to punish them.",
  2264:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not spoil the reward of your charity by boasting about it and harming the person to whom you gave it. A person who does this is like one who spends to be seen and praised by people and disbelieves in Allah and the reward and punishment of the Day of Resurrection. This is like a smooth stone on which there is some soil: when heavy rain falls onto it, the soil is washed away, and the stone is left smooth with nothing on it. Similarly, the reward of the deeds and charity of those who show off does not remain in the sight of Allah. Allah does not guide disbelievers to what pleases Him and what will benefit them regarding their deeds and charity. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The levels of faith and stages of conviction have no limit. The more a person thinks about the universal signs of Allah, the more his faith and conviction increases.\n2. The resurrection of people after their death is a clear proof of Allah’s perfect ability and greatness.\n3. There is great virtue and a huge reward for spending in Allah’s path when this is done with a good intention and is not followed by insults or reminders.\n4. One of the best things a person can do is to show good character by saying or doing something good and forgiving the person who is bad to him.\n5. The reward of charity is lost when a person reminds people of it.",
  2265:
      "The example of the believers who spend their wealth seeking Allah's pleasure, with firm conviction in their hearts of Allah's promise, is like that of a garden on high, fertile ground where heavy rain falls and causes it to produce double its crops. In addition, if it does not receive heavy rain, the light rain that falls on it is sufficient because the land is fertile. In the same way, the little that the sincere ones spend is accepted by Allah, and its reward is multiplied. Allah sees what you do: He knows who is sincere and who is not and will reward everyone accordingly.",
  2266:
      "Then Allah gives an example that depicts the state of one who spends his money to show off, stating: \n Do any of you wish to have a garden with date palms and grapevines through which sweet waters flow, containing all varieties of wholesome fruit? When the owner of such a garden becomes old and is no longer able to work and earn, and he has vulnerable young children who also cannot work, a solid fiery wind strikes this garden, and it burns down completely at a time when he is most in need of it because of his old age and for his young dependable children. The condition of a person who spends his wealth to show people is like that of this man: when he comes before Allah on the Day of Resurrection, he will have no good actions when he most needs them. In this manner, Allah explains what will benefit you in this world and the Hereafter so that you may reflect.",
  2267:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, spend from the lawful, pure wealth you have earned and the produce we have taken out for you from the ground. Do not look for what is inferior to spend because if given to you, you would not take it willingly, except with closed eyes, because of its poor quality. How can you be satisfied with offering Allah what you yourselves would not accept? Know that Allah does not need your spending, and He is praised in His essence and actions.",
  2268:
      "After instructing them to spend their wealth in virtue, Allah warns them about Satan's plots and whispers, stating: \n The Devil makes you afraid of poverty by encouraging you to be stingy, and he invites you to commit sins. Allah, on the other hand, promises you forgiveness for your sins and vast provision. Allah is very bountiful, and He knows the condition of His slaves.",
  2269:
      "Allah grants the ability to whoever of His slaves He wishes to be steadfast in speech and deeds. Anyone who is given this ability has been given much good. However, only those with sound minds who seek enlightenment through His light and follow His guidance will pay attention and benefit from the signs of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The true believers in Allah are sure of His promise and reward: they spend their wealth without any fear or grief.\n2. It is Allah’s grace and favour that He blesses what is spent by the believers when it is done with sincerity.\n3. The believer trusts in Allah and pays no attention to the whisperings of Satan, who tries to stop him from spending by making him afraid of poverty and need.\n4. The biggest loser is the person who shows off his good actions, because the only thing he will receive as a reward is the praise of people.",
  2270:
      "Whatever you spend, be it a little or a lot, seeking the pleasure of Allah, or any action you have obligated yourselves to do for Allah without having been required to do it, Allah knows of it, and it will not be lost. He will recompense you greatly for it. Those who do wrong by not fulfilling their obligations and transgressing Allah's limits will have no helpers to protect them against the torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  2271:
      "It is noble if you openly declare what you spend on charity. But if you conceal it and give it to people experiencing poverty privately, this is better as it indicates sincerity. Charity of the sincere ones is the means of their sins being covered up and forgiven. Allah knows what you do; nothing from your circumstances is hidden.",
  2272:
      "O Prophet, you are not responsible for making them believe and submit to the truth: your duty is to direct them to the truth and explain it to them. Only Allah can guide them to accept the truth, and He guides whomever He wishes. The benefit of any good you spend returns to you; Allah does not need it. So, let your spending be only for Allah's sake: true believers spend only for Allah's pleasure. You will receive the full reward for whatever you spend, no matter how little, because Allah does not wrong anyone.",
  2273:
      "After calling upon believers to spend their wealth for His sake, Allah defines the causes they should be spending upon, stating: \n Spend on those poor people who, because they are busy striving in Allah's path, cannot travel to earn a living. Due to their not asking, an uninformed person will think they are not in need. However, the person who knows will recognize them by the apparent signs on their body and clothing. They are unlike other poor people who beg persistently. Allah knows of any wealth you spend and will recompense you greatly.",
  2274:
      "Those who spend their wealth for Allah's sake at night and during the day, secretly and openly, without showing off or looking for fame, will be rewarded by their Lord on the Day of Resurrection. As a favor and blessing from Allah, they will not fear what awaits them or grieve over what they missed out on in this world.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whatever the believers spend is not hidden from Allah: He knows of it and will reward those who are sincere with the best reward.\n2. If a believer is sincere in his spending and charity, there is no harm if he reveals it or hides it, even though hiding it carries greater reward.\n3. The believers are called to pay attention to those who are in need but are too dignified to reveal this to people.\n4. The verse shows that one should always spend in Allah’s path and that Allah promises that this carries great reward in this world and the Afterlife.",
  2275:
      "After encouraging spending for His sake due to the cooperation and solidarity that it builds between Muslims, Allah warns about usury, which nullifies this, stating: \n Those who indulge in usury and receive it will rise from their graves on the Day of Resurrection like a person who is afflicted by the Devil: they will stand up from their graves and then abruptly fall like a person who just suffered a seizure. This is because they made usury permissible and made no distinction between usury and that which Allah has permitted in terms of profit earned through trade and sales transactions. They claimed that trade is like usury, meaning both are lawful since both lead to increased wealth. Allah refutes their analogy and explains that He has permitted trade because of the general and specific benefit it contains, and He has prohibited usury because it is oppressive and leads to unjustly eating people's wealth without an exchange [of goods or services]. The person who repents from this sin and stops indulging in usury upon receiving Allah's prohibition and warning against it may keep the money that he received in the past from it, without any sin. Then, whatever he does from then on, Allah will judge it. Whoever returns to dealing with usury after knowing of the prohibition and evidence established against doing so deserves to enter the Fire and remain there eternally. The reference to remaining in the Fire eternally could either be for a person who justifies the indulgence in usury or referring to a long period of time for those who indulge in it while still believing in the Oneness of Allah. Eternal Hell is solely for disbelievers; as for true monotheists (Muslims), they will not remain in the Fire eternally.",
  2276:
      "After mentioning spending for His sake and engaging in usury, Allah explains the difference between the two in reward, stating: \n Allah destroys usury-based wealth by either physically destroying it or removing its blessing. Yet He increases charity and makes it grow by multiplying its reward by ten times up to seven hundred times or even more and blesses the wealth of those who give charity. Allah does not love a stubborn disbeliever who considers the prohibited as lawful and persists in sins.",
  2277:
      "Those who believe in Allah, follow His Messenger, do righteous deeds, completely fulfill their prayers, and give Zakat to those deserving will receive their reward from their Lord. They will not fear what awaits them or grieve over what missed them of the world and its pleasures.",
  2278:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, fear Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions. Do not demand any usury owed to you that remains with people if you genuinely believe in Allah and in what He has prohibited you, such as usury.",
  2279:
      "If you do not obey the sacred law, be aware and confident of waging a war against Allah and His Messenger. If you repent to Allah and abandon usury, you may keep the initial amount you had given as a loan from your capital in a manner that does not wrong anyone by taking more than your initial capital or receiving less than it.",
  2280:
      "If the person from whom you demand your debt is going through difficult times and cannot repay the debt, then delay asking until he can obtain money and pay the debt. And to give charity to him by not demanding the debt or giving up a part of it is better for you if you know that virtue in the sight of Allah.",
  2281:
      "Fear the punishment of a day when you all will be returned to Allah, and you will have to stand before Him. Then, every soul will be recompensed for its good or evil actions. They will not be wronged by receiving less reward than they deserve for their good deeds or more punishment for their evil deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the most serious major sins is usury. For this reason, Allah has warned of war from Him and His Messenger for the person who takes usury.\n2. Obeying the sacred law of commercial transactions brings blessings and growth.\n3. It is virtuous to be patient with a person in financial difficulty and to make things easy for him by giving up the debt in part or in full.",
  2282:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, when you enter a transaction that involves a debt, such as when you give a loan to one another for a fixed period, then write it down. The person who can write should write it down according to the legislation and should not refuse to justly write down the debt according to the writing Allah has taught him. He should note what is dictated by the person against whom the right [debt] is so that it serves as an acknowledgment from him. He should fear Allah and not reduce anything from the value or description of the debt. In cases where the debtor is not experienced in undertaking transactions or is young, insane, or unable to dictate due to being mute or for some other reason, his authoritative guardian should dictate justly. Also, call two sane and upright men as witnesses. If two men are not found, contact one man and two women whose religion and honesty you are satisfied with so that if one of the women forgets, the other can remind her. The witness should not refuse to be a witness to a debt and must testify if required. Do not be lazy to write down the debt, no matter how small the amount, as this is more just in Allah's law, more reliable as evidence, and more likely to remove any doubt in the type of debt, amount, or period. However, if the transaction is for an item that is present in exchange for a spot price, there is no harm in not writing it down since there is no need to do so. Calling witnesses is legislated so that disputes do not arise. It is unlawful to cause any harm to the witnesses or those who write, nor may they cause any harm to those who request them to write or stand witness. If anyone causes harm, he is going against Allah's sacred law. O believers fear Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions. Allah will teach you what is best for you in this world and the Hereafter. Allah knows everything, and nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Debts and all commercial transactions should be recorded to prevent any disagreement or dispute.\n2. Transactions involving debt and all types of leases must have fixed periods.\n3. The sacred law commands guardianship over those who are not able to look after their affairs due to being disabled, weak-minded or minors.\n4. There should be witnesses to acknowledgments of debts and rights.\n5. The best and most just way to write is to use the correct phrases and words relevant to the transaction.\n6. No one should be harmed when recording debts and rights by the holders of such rights or those that record or witness them.",
  2283:
      "If you are traveling and do not find anyone to write down the debt for you, the debtor can give property to the creditor as collateral for his right until the debt is paid. If you trust one another, writing the debt down, calling witnesses, or providing collateral is unnecessary. In such cases, the debt will be the debtor's responsibility, which he must fulfill and fear Allah regarding it by not denying it later. If he later denies it, the person present during the transaction must give evidence and may not hide it. If anyone should hide evidence, it indicates that his heart is sinful. Allah knows what you do; nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for your deeds accordingly.",
  2284:
      "To Allah belongs everything in the heavens and earth: He created, owns, and controls all of it. Whether you show or hide what is in your heart, Allah knows and will call you to account for it. Then, He will forgive whoever He wishes out of His grace and mercy and punish whoever He wishes out of His wisdom and justice. Allah is the Most Capable of everything.",
  2285:
      "The Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم believes in everything that was revealed to him by his Lord, as do the believers. All of them believe in Allah, all His angels, all His books revealed to the various prophets, and all His messengers that He sent. They believe in all of them and say: We make no distinction between any of Allah's messengers. They say: We have heard Your instructions and prohibitions, and we obey You by doing what You have instructed us and abandoning what You have prohibited us from. We ask You to forgive us, O our Lord, for our return is to You alone in all our matters.",
  2286:
      "Allah only burdens a soul with deeds that it can do. Allah's religion is based on ease and not difficulty. If any person does good, he will receive the reward for it in full. If any person does evil, he will be punished for his sin, and no one will carry it. The Messenger and the believers said: O Lord, do not punish us if we forget or make a mistake in doing something or saying something unintentionally. O Lord, do not burden us with what is difficult for us and which we cannot do as you had tasked those before us who were punished for their wrongs, such as the Jews. Please do not give us such instructions and prohibitions which are difficult for us and which we cannot fulfill. By Your grace, overlook our sins, forgive us, and have mercy on us. You are our guardian and helper, so give us victory over the disbelievers. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A promise should to be taken to secure rights if it is not possible to record them, unless the contracting parties trust one another.\n2. It is forbidden to hide evidence; and the person who does so is sinful.\n3. Allah’s knowledge and awareness of His creation is perfect. He is completely able to call them to account for their actions.\n4. The verses describe the essentials of faith and explain their fundamentals.\n5. This religion is based on ease and removal of harm and difficulty from people. Allah only burdens people with what they are able to do, and will not make them accountable for what they cannot do.",
  3000:
      "Family of 'Imran (Surah Al 'Imran)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nProving that Islam is the truth, in response to the doubts cast by the People of the Book, and strengthening the believers' resolve.\n•    Explanation:    \nIt is a Medinan surah. It is named Al 'Imran due to the mention of the family of 'Imran in the 33rd verse of the surah.",
  3001:
      "(الٓمٓ) Alif Lām Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. They indicate the inability of the Arabs to bring a Quran like this one even though it is composed of letters similar to the ones at the beginning of this Sūrah, which also form parts of their own speech.",
  3002:
      "Allah is the One who alone deserves to be worshipped. He is the One Who possesses perfect life without any death or deficiency. He exists by Himself and does not need any of His creation. The creation only exists through Him and is always in need of Him.",
  3003:
      "He has revealed to you, O Prophet, the Quran with true stories and just laws that agree with the previous divine books, and there are no contradictions between all these divine books. Before revealing the Quran to you, He revealed the Torah to Moses and the Gospel to Jesus (peace be upon them both). These sacred books are full of guidance and instruction to direct people toward what is good for their religion and worldly lives. Likewise, Allah revealed the Criterion (the Quran) to distinguish between truth and falsehood and guidance from misguidance. Those who disbelieve in the verses of Allah that He revealed to you will receive a painful torment. Allah is the Almighty, and nothing can overcome Him, and He will take revenge on those who reject His messengers and oppose His command.",
  3004:
      "He has revealed to you, O Prophet, the Quran with true stories and just laws that agree with the previous divine books, and there are no contradictions between all these divine books. Before revealing the Quran to you, He revealed the Torah to Moses and the Gospel to Jesus (peace be upon them both). These sacred books are full of guidance and instruction to direct people toward what is good for their religion and worldly lives. Likewise, Allah revealed the Criterion (the Quran) to distinguish between truth and falsehood and guidance from misguidance. Those who disbelieve in the verses of Allah that He revealed to you will receive a painful torment. Allah is the Almighty, and nothing can overcome Him, and He will take revenge on those who reject His messengers and oppose His command.",
  3005:
      "Nothing on earth or in the sky is hidden from Allah. He knows everything, whether it is apparent or concealed.",
  3006:
      "It is He Who creates you as He wills in different forms inside the wombs of your mothers, either as a male or female, handsome or unattractive, black or white. There is no one worthy of being worshipped besides Him. He is Almighty who cannot be overpowered. He is the All-Wise in His creation, planning, and legislation.",
  3007:
      "O Prophet, He is the One who revealed to you the Quran, which contains verses with clear and unambiguous meaning. These verses are the foundation of the Book, forming the majority of its verses, and are referred to when there is a dispute. However, it also includes other verses that may have multiple meanings unclear to most people. Those who seek other than the truth leave the clear verses and focus on the unclear ones, trying to cause doubts and mislead people. They interpret them in a way that suits their corrupt views. No one knows the actual meanings of such verses except Allah. Those firmly grounded in knowledge say: We believe in the entire Quran because it is all from Allah. They interpret the unclear verses according to the clear ones. Only those who have sound intellects pay attention to this.",
  3008:
      "Those grounded in knowledge say: O our Lord, do not let our hearts turn away from the truth after you have shown it to us. Save us from what happened to those who deviated and turned away from the truth. Grant us vast mercy, guiding our hearts and protecting us from misguidance. O Our Lord, Indeed you are the Bestower who gives plentifully.",
  3009:
      "O our Lord, You will gather all the people back to You: to reckon them on a day in which there is no doubt. O our Lord, indeed, You do not break promises. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has established proof against the creation and left them no excuse for disbelief by sending messengers and books to guide them to the truth and warn them against falsehood.\n2. Allah’s knowledge is perfect and He knows everything about His creation. Nothing in the heavens or earth is hidden from Him, whether it is open or hidden.\n3. One of the principles of the people of faith who are firm in knowledge is that they interpret the unclear verses by referring to the clear ones.\n4. A person should pray to Allah for firmness on the truth and for guidance, especially at the time of trouble and disagreements amongst the people.",
  3010:
      "The wealth and children of those disbelieving in Allah and His messengers will not protect them from Allah's torment in this life or the Hereafter. On the contrary, such disbelievers will be the fuel that Hell will be lit with on the Day of Resurrection.",
  3011:
      "The matter of these disbelievers is like that of the people of Pharaoh and those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His signs before them. As a result, Allah tormented and punished them for their sins – their wealth and children did not benefit them. Consequently, Allah severely punishes those disbelieving in Him and rejecting His signs.",
  3012:
      "O Messenger, say to those who disbelieve, regardless of their religion: The believers will defeat you, and you will die as disbelievers. Allah will then gather you in the Fire, and what an evil resting place it will be for you!",
  3013:
      "There was a clear sign and lesson in the two groups that met to fight in the Battle of Badr. One group was made up of believers, and this was the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and his Companions: They were fighting in the path of Allah and to elevate His Word over the word of those who disbelieve. The other group consisted of the disbelievers of Mecca, who had come out in pride and arrogance. The believers saw the disbelievers as double their number, but Allah helps His allies and supports whoever He wishes. In that, there is a lesson and a warning for those who have the insight to realize that the help of Allah can come to the believers even though they may be few in number and that defeat can come to those upon falsehood even though they may be more in number.",
  3014:
      "Allah mentions that He has made the love of desirable things in this world attractive to people to test them. These desirable things include women, children, abundant gold and silver piled up, beautifully trained horses, livestock such as camels, cows, sheep, and farmlands – all of which are fleeting pleasures of this life lasting only a few short moments. Therefore, a believer should not become attached to these things as Allah alone has the best place of return – Paradise, which is as vast as the heavens and the earth.",
  3015:
      "Upon mentioning how the desires of this world become cut off, Allah draws attention to what was better, stating: \n Say (to the people), O Messenger: Should I inform you about something better than those desirable things? Those who fear Allah by obeying Him and avoid disobeying Him will have gardens with trees and palaces beneath which rivers flow, wherein they will live forever. They will also have wives that are void of any defects in their form and character. Moreover, they will gain the pleasure of Allah, and Allah will never be angry with them. Allah sees the conditions of His slaves; nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for it accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A disbeliever’s wealth and children will be of no use to him on the Day of Resurrection against the punishment of Allah.\n2. Victory, in reality, is not dependent on numbers and preparation, but on Allah’s assistance and support.\n3. Allah has made various forms of desirable things of the world attractive as a test for people. He knows those who observe His limits from those who overstep them.\n4. All the enjoyment and pleasures of the world are only for a little while, and cannot be compared to the eternal bliss of the Afterlife.",
  3016:
      "The people of Paradise are the ones who say in their supplications: O our Lord, indeed we believed in You and in what You revealed to Your messengers, and we have followed Your sacred law. So, forgive the sins we have committed and keep us far away from the torment of the Fire.",
  3017:
      "They are the ones who show patience while doing good actions, avoiding evil acts, and when calamity befalls them. Those who are truthful in speech and deeds, wholeheartedly fulfill Allah's sacred law, spend their wealth in the path of Allah, and ask for forgiveness in the last part of the night when supplications are more likely to be accepted, and the hearts are void of any distractions.",
  3018:
      "Allah testifies that He alone is worthy of worship based on the legislative and universal signs indicating His divinity. The angels and people of knowledge also attest to this by declaring and calling to His Oneness. They testified to the most significant thing anyone can testify to: the absolute right of Allah to be worshipped and the perfect justice in His creation and sacred law. This is the greatest thing that anyone can testify to. There is no god but Him, the Almighty, who can never be overpowered, and the One who has complete wisdom regarding His creation, planning, and legislation.",
  3019:
      "The religion of Islam is the only religion Allah will accept. It is the surrendering and devotion of all acts of worship to Allah alone, submission to Him in servitude, and belief in all of the messengers, including the final Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم with whom revelations came to an end, and no other legislation other than his will be accepted. Due to envy and greed for worldly things, the Jews and Christians split up into groups and sects after evidence was established against them in the form of knowledge that had come to them. Whoever disbelieves in the verses of Allah revealed to His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, then Allah will be swift in reckoning those who disbelieve in Him and reject His messengers.",
  3020:
      "If they argue with you, O Messenger, about the truth revealed to you, then say to them: I and the believers who follow me have submitted to Allah. Then, O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, say to the People of the Book and the polytheists: Do you submit to Allah sincerely, following what I have brought? If they submit to Allah and follow your sacred law, they are on the path of guidance. But, on the other hand, if they turn away from Islam, then you only have to convey your message to them; then their affair is with Allah. He watches over His slaves and will recompense them accordingly for their deeds.",
  3021:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah's evidence, which He has revealed to them, and unjustly and belligerently kill His prophets and those who command with justice by commanding good and forbidding evil – convey to these murderous disbelievers tidings of a painful torment.",
  3022:
      "The deeds of those doing such things are nullified and will not benefit them, not in this world or the Hereafter. There will be no one to help them repel the torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The greatest thing that will wipe out sins and save a person from the punishment of the fire of Hell is faith in Allah and following what the Messenger (peace be upon him) brought.\n2. The greatest testimony and reality is that Allah is the only One to be worshipped. For this reason, Allah Himself testifies to this, as do His angels and the people of knowledge.\n3. The religion of Islam brought by the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the true religion which Allah has sent as His final message: no other religion is acceptable to Him.",
  3023:
      "O Prophet, do you not see the state of Jews whom Allah gave a portion of knowledge from the Torah proving your prophethood? Yet, when they were called to refer to the Book of Allah, the Torah, so that it could decide what they differed in, a group of their scholars and leaders turned away, ignoring the judgment of the Torah, because it did not agree with their desires. The right thing for them to have done, having claimed that they were followers of the Torah, was to be the foremost among people to judge according to it.",
  3024:
      "They turned away from the truth and ignored it because they used to claim that the Fire would only touch them for a few days, and they would then enter Paradise. This ill-conceived notion that they concocted from lies and fabrications deceived them and made them daring against Allah and His religion.",
  3025:
      "What will be their state, and how much will they regret? It will be incredibly terrible when We gather them to give account on the Day of Resurrection, in which there is no doubt. Every soul will be given the reward of its deeds according to what it deserves, without being wronged by its good acts being reduced and its evil actions increased.",
  3026:
      "O Messenger, say in praise of your Lord and declaration of His greatness: O Allah, the Lord of the entire dominion in this world and the Hereafter. You give sovereignty to whoever of Your creation You wish and remove it from whoever of Your creation You wish. You honor whomever You wish and disgrace whomever You wish. All of this is done according to Your wisdom and justice. All good lies only in Your hand. Therefore, you are the Most Capable of everything.",
  3027:
      "A demonstration of Your power is that You cause the day to become longer by extending it into the night, and You cause the night to become longer by extending it into the day. You bring out the living from the dead – as in a believer from a disbeliever and crops from seed – and You bring out the dead from the living – as in a disbeliever from a believer and a chick from an egg. You give provision to whomever You wish, in abundance, without limit or count.",
  3028:
      "O believers, do not take disbelievers as allies you love and support instead of other believers. Whoever does this is disassociated from Allah, and Allah is disassociated from them. However, suppose you are under their authority and fear for your lives. In that case, there is no sin upon you if you avoid their harm by being nice to them in your speech and actions openly while hating them inside. Allah warns you of Himself, so fear Him and do not become the subject of His anger by committing sins. All slaves will return to Allah alone on the Day of Resurrection to be recompensed for their deeds.",
  3029:
      "Say, O Prophet: Whether you conceal within your hearts or reveal what Allah has forbidden, such as allying with the disbelievers, Allah knows about it. Nothing is hidden from Him. He knows whatever is in the heavens and the earth. He is the Most Capable of everything; nothing can hinder Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Guidance and success is only from Allah. Even if a very knowledgeable person reaches the highest of positions, it will be of no benefit to him without Allah’s grace.\n2. Authority belongs to Allah: He is the One Who gives and holds back, and the One Who gives honour and disgrace. All matters rest with Him, so no one else should be asked for anything.\n3. It is necessary to befriend believers and to leave disbelievers.",
  3030:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, every soul will find the good it did in front of it without anything missing. Those who did wrong will wish there was a great distance between them and their evil actions – but wishing it (on that day) will be useless! Allah warns you of Himself, so do not become the subject of His anger by committing sins. Allah is kind to His slaves and thus gives them this stern warning.",
  3031:
      "O Messenger, say (to the people): If you genuinely love Allah, then follow what I have brought, inwardly and outwardly. Doing this will gain Allah's love, and He will forgive you for your sins. Allah is All-Forgiving and All-Merciful to those who repent to Him.",
  3032:
      "O Messenger, say: Obey Allah and His Messenger by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions. If they turn away from that, then know that Allah does not love the disbelievers who oppose His and His Messenger's instruction.",
  3033:
      "Allah selected Adam (peace be upon him) by making the angels prostrate before him; Noah by making him the first messenger to the people of the earth; the family of Abraham by making prophethood remain among his descendants; and the family of 'Imran [the father of Mary – which is a reference to Jesus (peace be upon him)]. He selected all of them and preferred them over the people of their time.",
  3034:
      "These prophets [We] mentioned, along with their progeny were descendants of each other, following the same path of declaring Allah's Oneness and doing righteous deeds. They passed on noble characteristics and virtues to one another. Allah hears the statements of His slaves and knows their deeds, and therefore chooses whoever He wills from them.",
  3035:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the wife of 'Imran, the mother of Mary, said: O my Lord, I have made it a duty on myself to fully dedicate my unborn child to You, to serve You and Your House, so accept this act from me. You are the One who hears my supplication and Omniscient of my intentions.",
  3036:
      "When she reached the end of her pregnancy and gave birth, she said apologetically, as she had hoped for a boy: O my Lord, I have given birth to a girl, while Allah is more aware of what she gave birth to. But, of course, a girl does not have the same strength and form as a boy as she had hoped for. So she said: I have named her Mary and ask for Your mercy in protecting her and her children from the Devil, whom You banished from Your mercy.",
  3037:
      "Allah graciously accepted her vow and brought her up well. He made the hearts of His pious slaves incline caringly towards her and put her in the care of Prophet Zechariah (peace be upon him). Whenever Zechariah entered her place of worship, he would find wholesome provision. So, he asked her: O Mary, where did you get this provision from? She replied: This provision is from Allah. Allah gives to whoever He wishes in abundance without limit.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s great status and the harshness of His punishment will make any sensible person be mindful of going against His sacred law.\n2. The proof of true love for Allah and His Messenger is following the instructions and prohibitions of the sacred law. The claim of love without proof is weak.\n3. Through His wisdom and mercy, Allah chooses whomever of His servants He wishes for prophethood and prophetic miracles.",
  3038:
      "When Zechariah saw the provision that Allah miraculously gave to Mary, daughter of 'Imran, he became hopeful that Allah would give him a child despite being very old and his wife being barren. So he said: O my Lord, give me a good child. So indeed, You hear and grant the supplication of the person who supplicates to You.",
  3039:
      "The angels called out to him while he stood in prayer in his place of worship, saying: Allah gives you good news of a child to be born to you whose name will be John. He will confirm a word from Allah – which refers to Jesus, son of Mary, as Allah uniquely created him with a word from Him. This child will lead his people in knowledge and worship. He will be innocent, avoiding desires, including approaching women. He will dedicate himself to worshipping His Lord and be a prophet among righteous people.",
  3040:
      "When the angels gave him the good news about John, Zechariah said: O my Lord, how can I have a child after I have become old and my wife cannot bear children? Allah replied: The example of John's creation, despite your old age and your wife being barren, is like the creation of anything Allah wishes to create, even though it is out of the ordinary. This is because Allah is the Most Capable of everything and does whatever He wills in His wisdom and knowledge.",
  3041:
      "Zechariah said: O my Lord, give me a sign that my wife is pregnant. Allah said: The sign you want is that you cannot speak for three whole days, except by using gestures, and this will not be because of any disability. So, remember Allah much and exalt Him at the start and end of every day.",
  3042:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the angels said to Mary (peace be upon her): Allah has chosen you because of your praiseworthy qualities. He has purified you from all defects and chosen you over all the other women of your time.",
  3043:
      "O Mary, lengthen your standing in prayer, prostrate to your Lord, and bow down with His righteous slaves who bow down to Him.",
  3044:
      "The story of Zechariah and Mary is knowledge of the unseen, which We reveal to you, O Messenger. When they argued about who was most entitled to bring up Mary, you were not there with those scholars and righteous people. So they eventually decided to draw lots by throwing their pens, and the pen of Zechariah (peace be upon him) won.",
  3045:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the angels said: O Mary, Allah gives you good news of a child who will be created without a father: merely by a word from Allah, such as 'Be', and he will become a child by Allah's will. This child's name will be the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary. He will have a high rank in this world and the Hereafter and be one of those brought close to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah takes special care of His friends by protecting them from anything bad and by answering their prayers.\n2. Mary has special virtue in Islam, as Allah had chosen her over all the other women, purified her from defects and blessed her.\n3. The greater the favour Allah gives to a person the more he has to be thankful.\n4. The sacred law accepts the drawing of lots when there is a dispute which cannot be resolved due to lack of any evidence or clues.",
  3046:
      "This child will miraculously speak to people when he is a small baby and speak to them when he grows up and becomes a man. He will tell them what is best for them in their religious and worldly affairs. He will also be one of those who are righteous in speech and deeds.",
  3047:
      "Mary was surprised that she was to have a child without a husband and said in astonishment: How can I have a child when no man has come near me lawfully or unlawfully? The angel told her: Just as Allah will create a child for you without a father, He creates whatever He wishes, even though it may be out of the ordinary. When Allah wishes for something, He says 'Be,' and it is. Nothing can render Him incapable.",
  3048:
      "Allah will teach him to write and say and do things correctly; He will teach him the Torah that He had revealed to Moses (peace be upon him) and the Gospel that He will reveal to him.",
  3049:
      "Allah will likewise make him a messenger to the Israelites, instructing him to say to them: I am Allah's Messenger to you. I have brought you a sign proving my prophethood: I will fashion a bird using clay, then breathe into it, and it will become a living bird with Allah's permission. I will cure the one who was born blind so that he can see and the leper who will recover from his illness, and I will bring the dead back to life. I will do all of this with Allah's permission. I will tell you about what you consume and hide in your homes. All these extraordinary things I mentioned to you, which human beings cannot do, are a clear sign that I am Allah's Messenger to you if you wish to believe and accept the proof.",
  3050:
      "I have come to you to confirm the revelation of the Torah that was before me and to make some of what was unlawful in the past lawful: making things easy for you. I have brought clear proof of the truthfulness of what I say, so fear Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions, and follow that which I invite you to.",
  3051:
      "Allah is my Lord and your Lord; He is the only One who deserves to be obeyed and feared. So, worship Him alone. This worship of Allah and fear Him that I instruct you to do is the straight path with no crookedness.",
  3052:
      "When Jesus realized they would continue in disbelief, he addressed the Israelites: Who will help me in inviting towards Allah? His select followers said: We are the ones who will help Allah's religion. We believe in Allah, and we follow you. Be a witness, O Jesus, that we submit to Allah by accepting His Oneness and obeying Him. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah was gracious to Mary and her son, the Messiah, by blessing them with many miracles.\n2. Writing is considered a noble skill, as Allah mentioned it before other things.\n3. Allah’s custom is that He supports His messengers with miracles which are beyond the capacity of human beings, indicating their truthfulness.\n4. Jesus came to make some of the laws of the Torah easy for the Israelites.",
  3053:
      "The disciples also said: O our Lord, we have believed in the Gospel that you revealed, and we have followed the Messenger, Jesus (peace be upon him), so make us of those who are witnesses to the truth and who believe in You and Your messengers.",
  3054:
      "The disbelievers from the Israelites plotted to kill Jesus (peace be upon him), so Allah plotted against them and left them in their misguidance. He made another person resemble Jesus (peace be upon him) when they tried to kill him. Allah is the best of plotters because nothing can be more severe than His plot against His enemies.",
  3055:
      "Allah also plotted against them by saying to Jesus: O Jesus, I will take you away alive, raise your body and soul to Me, rid you of the filth of those who disbelieved you, and distance you from them. I will make those who follow you be upon the true religion, which includes acceptance of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, be above those who disbelieve until the Day of Resurrection in proof and honor. Then to Me alone will be your return on the Day of Resurrection, and I will pass judgment in truth between you regarding your differences.",
  3056:
      "As for those who disbelieved in you and the truth you brought to them, I will torment them severely in this life by being killed, imprisoned, and disgraced, and in the Hereafter, I will torment them in the Fire. They will have no one to help them against that torment.",
  3057:
      "As for those who had faith in you and the truth that you came with and performed righteous deeds (such as prayer, charity, fasting, keeping family relations, etc.), Allah will grant them the reward of their actions in full without any reduction. This verse refers to the Messiah's followers before the advent of the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, whose emergence the Messiah confirmed himself. Allah does not love those who transgress, and among the greatest forms of transgression is to ascribe partners to Allah and to reject His messengers.",
  3058:
      "This account of Jesus We recited to you indicates the authenticity of what was revealed to you. Therefore, it reminds those who fear Allah as it contains no falsehood.",
  3059:
      "The creation of Jesus (peace be upon him) with Allah is similar to the creation of Adam, who was created from dust without a father or mother. Allah said to him: Be a human, and he came into existence just as Allah willed. How do they then claim that Jesus is a deity because he has no father, while they affirm that Adam is human despite having no father or mother?",
  3060:
      "The truth about Jesus, wherein there is no doubt, is revealed to you by your Lord, so do not be one of those who harbor doubt and are skeptical. Instead, be firm on the truth that you are upon.",
  3061:
      "O Messenger, if any of the Christians from Najran dispute with you regarding the matter of Jesus and claim that he was not Allah's slave after the correct knowledge has come to you, then say to them: Come, let us call all our sons, all of our womenfolk, all of ourselves; and let us gather together in one place and then invoke the curse of Allah upon the liars.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The testimony that is acceptable and of use is that which is true and based on knowledge.\n2. There is an explanation of the correct belief regarding Jesus (peace be upon him), which counters those that are misguided regarding him.\n3. Allah, with His perfect power, acts against those who plot against His religion and His friends by manoeuvring against them.\n4. The sacred law accepts that two disputants may invoke the curse of Allah on one another, in the manner described.",
  3062:
      "What We have mentioned to you about Jesus (peace be upon him) is the truth that contains no lie or doubt. Therefore, there is no one worthy of worship besides Allah alone. Indeed, Allah is the Almighty in His dominion—the All-Wise in His planning, command, and regarding His creation.",
  3063:
      "If they turn away from what you have brought and do not follow you, then it is because of their corrupt ways. Allah knows those who cause corruption on earth, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  3064:
      "O Messenger, say (to them): O Jews and Christians, People of the Book, let us unite upon a common word in which we are all equal: that we worship Allah alone and we do not worship anyone besides Him, no matter what his rank or how high his status; and that we do not take one another as lords to be worshipped and obeyed instead of Allah. Suppose they turn away from the truth and justice you invite them to. In that case, O believers, say to them: Bear witness that we have surrendered to Allah and submitted through obedience [to Him].",
  3065:
      "O People of the Book, why do you dispute about the religion of Abraham? (You) The Jews claim he was a Jew, and (you) the Christians claim he was a Christian; all the while, you know very well that Judaism and Christianity did not appear until long after him. Can you not see how false your statement is and the error of your claim?",
  3066:
      "Here you are, O People of the Book, you have disputed with the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم with your knowledge of your religion and what was revealed to you. But why do you dispute regarding Abraham and his religion, which you do not know, as it is not in your Book, and your prophets did not discuss it? Allah knows the reality of matters and what is hidden, and you do not know.",
  3067:
      "Abraham was not a Jew or Christian in belief, but he was opposed to all false religions and obedient to Allah alone. He was also not one of those who ascribed partners to Allah – contrary to the polytheists of the Arabs, who claimed to follow his religion.",
  3068:
      "The people most worthy of affiliating themselves to Abraham are those who followed him in his time, as well as this Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and those who have believed in him from this nation. Thereby, Allah helps and protects the believers.",
  3069:
      "O believers, the scholars of the Jews and the Christians, desire to mislead you from the truth Allah has guided you to. Yet they only deceive themselves because their attempt to mislead the believers only increases their misguidance, and they are not aware of the consequences of their actions.",
  3070:
      "O People of the Book (Jews and Christians), why do you disbelieve in Allah's signs sent down to you that prove the prophethood of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, while you are witness to the fact that it is the truth presented in your (own revealed) books?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. All divine messages agreed on one upright saying: to declare Allah’s Oneness and to forbid associating partners with Him.\n2. It is important to know history as it is sometimes used as a proof to refute those that make false claims.\n3. The people who are most entitled to belong to Abraham are those who follow his belief and tenets of faith. A mere claim to belong to him is of no use if a person goes against him.\n4. The verses indicate that the disbelievers from the People of the Scripture are keen to mislead the believers of this nation because of their envy.",
  3071:
      "O People of the Book, why do you mix the truth revealed in your books with falsehood you have made up yourselves? Why do you hide the truth and guidance in your Book, such as the truthfulness of the prophethood of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, when you know what is the truth from falsehood and what is guidance from misguidance?",
  3072:
      "A group of Jewish scholars said: pretend to accept the Quran, which was revealed to the believers at the start of the day, and then reject it at the end of the day so that, after seeing this, the believers will begin to have doubts about their religion and turn back from it saying: These people know better about Allah's Books, and they have turned their backs.",
  3073:
      "They also said: Do not accept anyone unless he follows your religion. Say, O Messenger: Guidance to the truth is the Guidance of Allah, not the rejection and stubbornness that you display, fearing that anyone else could be given a bounty similar to what you were given or that they would argue with you before your Lord if you acknowledged what was revealed to them. Say, O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم: Bounty is in Allah's Hand, and He gives it to whoever of His slaves He wills: His bounty is not restricted to any one nation. Allah is Bountiful, and He knows who is deserving.",
  3074:
      "He chooses whoever of His creation, bestowing on them His mercy and blessing them with guidance, prophethood, and countless favors. Allah's bounty is vast and has no limit.",
  3075:
      "There are some People of the Book who, if you entrust them with a large amount of wealth, will honor the trust. On the other hand, there are some among them; if you entrust them with a small amount, they will not return the trust unless you persistently demand it from them. That is because they wrongly believe and say: There is no sin on us for any crime we commit against the Arabs or if we consume the wealth of the Arabs since Allah has permitted that for us. They speak such lies, knowing it to be a fabrication against Allah.",
  3076:
      "It is not as they claimed; rather, they are sinful. However, anyone who fulfills his covenant with Allah by believing in Him and His messengers and fulfills his covenant with people to fulfill their trust and fear Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions. In such a case, Allah loves those who fear Him and will recompense them with the most generous of rewards.",
  3077:
      "Those who take a small amount of this world in exchange for Allah's advice to follow His revelation and His messengers, and in exchange for the oaths they took to fulfill Allah's covenant, will have no share in the reward of the Hereafter. Allah will not speak to them that which will make them happy and will not look at them mercifully on the Day of Resurrection. They will receive a painful torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some of the scholars of the People of the Scripture deceive the followers of their religion and do not show them the truth contained in their books which was brought by their prophets.\n2. Allah is the Giver and the Bountiful. He gives whomever He wishes through His grace, and He withholds from whomever He wishes through His justice and wisdom. His grace can only be gained by following Him.\n3. The People of the Scripture are not all the same with respect to their honesty and trustworthiness: there are some of them who fulfil their trusts and others who do not.\n4. Anything of the world taken in exchange for faith in Allah and fulfilment of His pledge - no matter how much it may be - is little and worthless when compared to the reward and ranks in the Afterlife.",
  3078:
      "There is a group of Jews who distort the Torah when reciting it by saying words that were not revealed by Allah so that you think that they are reciting from the Torah, whereas it is not from the Torah. Instead, it is their lies and fabrications against Allah. They say: What we recite has been revealed by Allah – whereas Allah did not reveal it. They say lies about Allah when they know they are lying against Allah and His messengers.",
  3079:
      "It is not befitting for a man whom Allah gives a revealed book, blesses him with knowledge and understanding, and chooses him as a prophet, to say then to people: Become slaves of me instead of Allah. Instead, he should say to them: Be righteous scholars that act upon their knowledge, nurturing people, rectifying their affairs by virtue of your continuous teaching of the revealed Book, and by your constant studying of it by memorizing and understanding it.",
  3080:
      "It is also not befitting for such a man to instruct you to take the angels and the prophets as lords to be worshipped instead of Allah. Is it possible that he would command you to disbelieve after you have become devoted and have surrendered to Him?",
  3081:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Allah took a firm covenant from the prophets, saying to them: If I give you a revealed book, teach you wisdom and make you reach a high rank and status, and then My Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم comes to you confirming the Book and wisdom that you have, then you must accept what he brings and help him as his followers. Do you, O prophets, accept this and fully commit to Me? They replied: We accept that. So Allah said: Be witnesses over yourselves and your nations, and I will also be a witness over you and them.",
  3082:
      "Whoever turns away after this firm covenant witnessed by Allah and His messengers are the ones who abandon the religion of Allah and His obedience.",
  3083:
      "Are those who have abandoned the religion of Allah and obedience to Him looking for something other than Islam that Allah has chosen for His slaves? Every creature in the heavens and earth surrenders to Him, whether willingly like the believers or unwillingly, like the disbelievers. Subsequently, all of creation will return to Him on the Day of Resurrection for the final reckoning and recompense for their deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the misguidance of those Jewish scholars and how they plotted in distorting the word of Allah. They also lied to people by making up things about Allah.\n2. Any person who claims to follow one of the religions of the prophets of Allah but does not have faith in Muhammad (peace be upon him) has broken his promise with Allah.\n3. The men of Allah, who combine practice with knowledge and teach people to do the same, are those who hold the highest rank in Allah’s sight.\n4. The worst form of misguidance is to turn away from the religion of Allah to Whom all of creation, good and bad, surrender.",
  3084:
      "Say, O Messenger: We have believed in Allah as the one to be worshipped, having obeyed what He commanded. We have believed in the revelation that was sent down to us, and what was revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, and Jacob, and in what was revealed to the prophets among Jacob's descendants, and in the books and miracles that were given to Moses, Jesus, and all the prophets by their Lord. Also, we make no distinction between them, believing in all of them and that we all submit to Allah alone, surrendering in devotion to Him.",
  3085:
      "Those who seek a religion other than what Allah is pleased with, the religion of Islam, will not have it accepted by Allah. They will be of those who have incurred a great loss to themselves by entering the Fire.",
  3086:
      "How would Allah guide to belief in Him and His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم a people who disbelieved after they had once believed in Him and having witnessed that the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought the truth, and after clear proofs of the truth came to them? Allah does not guide wrongdoers to believe in Him and those who choose misguidance over guidance.",
  3087:
      "The recompense for those wrongdoers who chose falsehood then upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all of humanity; as a result, they will be excluded and far removed from the mercy of Allah.",
  3088:
      "[These disbelievers] will live eternally in the Fire, never to leave! Their suffering will not be lightened, and they will not be given more time to repent, ask for forgiveness, or make excuses.",
  3089:
      "[This torment is for everyone] except those who repent to Allah, asking for forgiveness after their disbelief and wrongdoing and rectify their deeds. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Compassionate to those from His slaves who repent to Him.",
  3090:
      "Those who disbelieved after believing and remained in this state until death, their repentance will not be accepted from them when they are near their end as it will be too late. Such people are misguided from the straight path that leads to Allah, the Exalted.",
  3091:
      "Indeed, for those who disbelieved and died as disbelievers, no ransom will be accepted from any of them, even if they offer the weight of the earth in gold in exchange for their release from the Fire. They will suffer a painful punishment and have no helpers on the Day of Resurrection who can repel the torment from them. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has made it obligatory to believe in all of the prophets Allah sent, and all the scriptures which He revealed to them, without making any distinction between them.\n2. Allah will not accept any way of life, whatever it may be, after He sent the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), except the path of Islam: surrendering in devotion to Allah, which he came with.\n3. Whoever stubbornly continues in their error, Allah will not give them success in repenting to Him and in finding guidance.\n4. The opportunity for repentance is open to everyone until the time of death, or when the sun will rise from where it sets.\n5. A person will only be saved from the suffering of the fire of Hell on the Day of Judgement by the good they have done. No wealth - even if it were equal to the entire earth - can help them in any way.",
  3092:
      "O believers, you will not attain the reward of the people of righteousness and their rank until you spend from the wealth you love in the path of Allah. Whatever you spend, a little or a lot, Allah is aware of your intentions and deeds, and He will recompense everyone according to their deeds.",
  3093:
      "All pure food was permissible to the Istralites, and nothing from it was forbidden to them except what Jacob prohibited for himself before the revelation of the Torah. It is not as Jews allege that the prohibitions were in the Torah. Say to them, O Prophet: Then bring forward the Torah and recite it if you are truthful regarding your claim. Instead, they fabricated lies and did not bring forth the Torah. It is an example demonstrating the false accusations of Jews against the Torah and a distortion of its contents.",
  3094:
      "So, whoever fabricates lies against Allah after the appearance of proof that Jacob (peace be upon him) prohibited it for himself without a prohibition from Allah are the ones who oppress themselves by abandoning the truth after the appearance of its proof.",
  3095:
      "Say, O Prophet: Allah has told the truth about what He has informed of from Jacob (peace be upon him) and everything He has revealed and legislated. So, follow the religion of Abraham, peace be upon him. For surely, he was someone who shunned all religions and turned towards Islam. And he never associated partners with Allah.",
  3096:
      "Indeed, the first house built to worship Allah on earth for all people is the House of Allah, the Holy Sanctuary, which is in Mecca. It is a blessed House holding many religious and worldly benefits. And there is guidance in it for all the worlds.",
  3097:
      "There are apparent signs of the nobility and virtue of this House, like the religious rites and rituals performed in its precincts. Among these signs is the Stone upon which Abraham stood when he set about erecting the wall of the Kaaba. Also, among them is that for whoever visits it, fear disappears from him, and harm does not affect him. Allah obligates people to travel to this House in order to fulfill the rites of the pilgrimage, for whoever is able to reach it. And whoever denies the obligation of the pilgrimage, surely Allah is not in need of such a disbeliever, nor is He in need of all the worlds put together.",
  3098:
      "Say, O Prophet: \"O People of the Book among the Jews and Christians, why do you deny clear proofs of the veracity of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم? And among them are clear proofs presented in the very Torah and Bible?! Allah is well aware of this action of yours. He is a witness of it, and He will requite you for it.\"",
  3099:
      "Say, O Prophet: \"O People of the Book among the Jews and Christians, why do you deter from the religion of Allah he who believes among the people; seeking to pose in the religion of Allah as a means of diversion from truth to falsehood; and to pose as a means of deviation from guidance for its people. All the while, you are witnesses to the fact that this religion is the truth and a confirmation of what is in your own scriptures. Allah is not unaware of what you commit of Disbelief in Him and posing as an obstruction from His path. He will recompense you for it.\"",
  3100:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, if you obey a group of the People of the Book among the Jews and Christians in what they say and you accept their thinking in what they allege, they will cause you to return to Disbelief after Belief due to what is in them of jealousy and deviation from guidance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Jews falsely claimed that the foods which Jacob (peace be upon him) had made unlawful were revealed in the Torah.\n2. The Sacred House is the greatest and most honoured place of worship, as it was the first House established for the worship of Allah, and has special characteristics that are not found anywhere else.\n3. Every Muslim who is sane, adult and able is obligated by the sacred law to perform the Hajj. Those who fulfil these conditions should not delay making Hajj, nor make excuses for not doing so.",
  3101:
      "How can you disbelieve in Allah after believing in Him while there is accompanying you the greatest reason for affirming belief!? The verses of Allah are being recited to you, and His Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is clarifying them for you. Whoever holds fast to the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, then Allah has indeed guided him to a straight path in which there is no crookedness.",
  3102:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, fear your Lord as He deserves to be feared. That is by following his commands, staying far away from what He prohibits, thanking Him for His favors, and holding fast to your religion until death arrives while you are in that state.",
  3103:
      "Hold fast, O believers, to the Book and the Sunnah. And do not commit actions that will cause you to fall into disunity. Remember the favors of Allah upon you. There was a time when you were enemies before Islam, fighting over the pettiest reasons. Then, He joined your hearts through Islam, and you became brothers in the religion, merciful towards one another and mutually sincere to each other in advice through His grace. Before that, you were on the verge of entering the Fire through your Disbelief. Then, Allah rescued you from it with Islam, and He guided you towards Faith. Just as Allah made this clear to you, He also makes clear to you that which will rectify your conditions in the worldly life and the Afterlife – so that you may be guided to the right path and traverse the straight path.",
  3104:
      "Let there be from among you, O believers, a group inviting to every good that Allah loves, commanding the good that the law establishes and sound reason promotes while preventing evil that the laws prohibit and sound reason abhors. Those described with this quality are the people of complete victory in the worldly life as well as the Afterlife.",
  3105:
      "Do not be, O believers, like the People of the Book who divided themselves and became factions and partisans. They differed regarding their religion after clear signs had come to them from Allah, the Exalted. And these ones mentioned have a severe torment from Allah.",
  3106:
      "This torment will befall them on the Day of Resurrection when the faces of the Faithful will be illuminated out of joy and happiness. And the faces of disbelievers will be darkened from sadness and grief. As for those whose faces will be darkened during that grievous day, it will be said to them reproachingly: \"Did you deny Allah's Oneness and the covenant He accepted on the basis that you do not associate any partners with Him- after your attestation and confirmation of it?! So, taste the torment of Allah, which He promised you because of your disbelief.\"",
  3107:
      "As for those whose faces will be illuminated, their position will be in gardens of delight, dwelling in them forever, in a delight that will not diminish nor fade.",
  3108:
      "Those verses, including the promise and threat of Allah, We recite upon you, O Prophet, with truthful information and just rulings. Allah does not wish to oppress anyone in the worlds. Rather, no one will be punished except by that which his own hand has earned. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Following the desires of the People of the Scripture leads to error and leaving the sacred path of Allah.\n2. Strictly following the guidance in the Book and the traditions of the Prophet is the best way to become firm in the truth, and to be protected from error and becoming divided.\n3. The division and disagreements of today in the Muslim nation concerning issues of faith also occurred among the People of the Scripture who came earlier.\n4. A Muslim must call to what is right and forbid what is wrong, because this is the way that the nation will succeed and grow.",
  3109:
      "And Allah (the Transcendent) alone is sovereign over what is in the heavens and earth, in both of creation and command. He (the Exalted) is the one to which every matter of His creation will return. Then, He will recompense all of them according to what each one deserves.",
  3110:
      "You, O nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم are the best nation Allah has brought forward for all humanity in your Faith and your actions. You are the most beneficial of people for all humanity in that you command the good that the law establishes and sound reason promotes. You prohibit the evil which the law forbids and sound reasoning abhors. You believe in Allah with decisive faith, whose actions prove to be true. If the People of the Book, among the Jews and Christians, would believe in Muhammadصلى الله عليه وسلم that would be better for them in terms of their worldly life and their Afterlife. A small number of the People of the Book believe in what Muhammadصلى الله عليه وسلم brought. However, most of them turn away from the religion and legislation of Allah.",
  3111:
      "Among them is an enemy who will not harm you, O believers, in your religion nor yourselves except the injury caused by their tongues in terms of religious defamation, mockery of you, and similar things. If they fight you, they will flee defeated before you and never be helped against you.",
  3112:
      "Disgrace and humiliation are caused to surround the Jews, encompassing them wherever they are found. So, they are not safe except through a covenant or guarantee of security from Allah, the Exalted, or the people. They bring about anger from Allah while need and poverty are caused to surround them. What is brought against them is because of their disbelief in the signs of Allah and their oppressive killing of His Prophets. It is also because of their disobedience and transgression of the limits of Allah. When Allah made clear the prevailing condition of the People of the Book, He also made clear the condition of a group among them who seek to be upright and stand up for the truth. So, He said:",
  3113:
      "After highlighting the condition of the majority of the People of the Book, Allah mentions a group of believers among them who remain committed to the truth, stating: \n The People of the Book are not all equal in their condition. Rather, there is a group of them who are upright in Allah's religion, upholding Allah's commands and prohibitions, reciting Allah's verses in the hours of the night while praying to Allah. This group existed before the mission of the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. Those among them who came to know of this mission accepted Islam.",
  3114:
      "They believe in Allah and the Last Day with decisive faith. They command what is right and virtuous and prohibit what is wrong and evil. They take the initiative in good deeds and take advantage of times for acts of obedience. Those described with these qualities are among the slaves of Allah whose intentions and actions are upright.",
  3115:
      "Whatever good these people do, whether a little or a lot, their repayment will not be lost, nor their reward. Allah knows the fearful who follow His commands and avoid what He prohibits. Nothing of their actions is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the greatest features that distinguished the Muslim nation, after faith in Allah, is the instructing of what is right and forbidding what is wrong.\n2. Allah has decreed humiliation for the People of the Scripture due to their turning away from Allah’s sacred way of life, and because they did not fulfil their promises.\n3. The People of the Scripture are not all the same. Among them are those who do what Allah instructs, follow the religion, and respect His limits; and so, they will have a great reward. Such people existed before the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent.",
  3116:
      "For those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger, neither their wealth nor their children will defend them at all from Allah- they will not deter His punishment or earn His mercy for them. Rather, [their wealth and children] will only increase their torment and distress. They will be companions of the Fire, remaining in it.",
  3117:
      "A parable for what these disbelievers spend in the causes of benevolence and what they expect of rewards for it is like a freezing wind that hits and ruins the crops of a people. So, their crops were ruined when they had expected a great amount of good. Just as this wind ruined the crops and ruined the benefit in them, likewise, disbelief ruins the reward of actions in which they had hope. Allah does not wrong them---He is far above that---rather, they only wrong themselves because of their disbelief in Him and their denial of His Messengers.",
  3118:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not take disbelievers as close and true friends, letting them know your secrets and the particulars of your state of affairs. They will not slacken in seeking to harm you and corrupt your state of affairs. They wish for the occurrence of what will harm you and cause difficulty for you. Aversion and hostility have appeared on their tongues through defamation of your religion, incidents between you, and spilling your secrets. The aversion they conceal in their chests is even greater. Evident proofs of what is in your best interest in the worldly life and the Afterlife have been made clear to you, O believers, if only you would realize what your Lord has revealed to you.",
  3119:
      "There you are, O believers, loving these people and wishing them well while they do not love you or wish you well. Rather, they hate you while you believe in all the books, including their books. Yet, they do not believe in the Book that Allah revealed to your Prophet. When they meet you, they say with their tongues: We accept it as true. And when they are away from you with each other, they bite the tips of their fingers out of sorrow and rage because of your unity, your unanimity, the prestige of Islam, and because of their own humiliation. Say, O Prophet, to these people: Remain as you are until you die out of sorrow and rage. Surely, Allah knows what is in the chests of faith and disbelief as well as the good and evil.",
  3120:
      "If a blessing happens for you, O believers, in the form of victory over an enemy or an increase in wealth and children, worry and sadness befalls them. And if calamity strikes you, such as the victory of an enemy or a decrease in wealth or children, they are happy with that, rejoicing at your misfortune. But, if you are patient with His commands and decrees and shelter yourself from His anger, then their plots and nuisances will not harm you. Surely, Allah is Well-Acquainted with what they scheme. And He will cause them to be unsuccessful.",
  3121:
      "Remember, O Prophet, when you departed from Medina at the beginning of the day to fight the polytheists at Uhud. You were occupied with the believers being accommodated in their places for battle. So, you made each individual's position clear. And Allah hears your statements, and He is knowledgeable of your actions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whatever the disbelievers spend in the path of good will not be of any benefit to them with Allah, because they do not fulfil the conditions of having faith in Allah and following His sacred law.\n2. The believers are prohibited from becoming close friends with the disbelievers, and from telling them their private business and secrets.\n3. The disbelievers are happy when something bad happens to those who have faith, and feel rage when something good happens to them.\n4. Protection from the plots and schemes of the disbelievers is through patience, not showing fear; and by being Mindful, which brings about strength and victory.",
  3122:
      "Remember, O Prophet, what happened between two groups of believers from the tribes of Salamah and Haritha, when they weakened and were on the verge of retreat when the hypocrites withdrew. However, Allah aided them by making them firm in fighting and turning them away from what they were on the verge of doing. So, let the believers rely on Allah alone in every circumstance.",
  3123:
      "Allah gave you victory over the polytheists during the Battle of Badr, while you were considered weak due to your small numbers and meager resources. Therefore, be fearful of Allah that perhaps you may be thankful for His blessings granted you.",
  3124:
      "Remember, O Prophet, when you said to the believers during the battle of Badr, as reassurance for them after they heard that reinforcements for the polytheists were incoming: Is it not sufficient that Allah will help you with three thousand angels sent down from Him, the Exalted, to reinforce you in battle?",
  3125:
      "Indeed, that should suffice you. There is the good news of other aid from Allah: if you are patient in fighting and fearful of Allah and the reinforcements of your enemies come rushing at you – if that takes place - your Lord will help you with five thousand angels, marking themselves and their horses with apparent signs.",
  3126:
      "Allah did not grant you this help and reinforcement with angels except for it to be delightful news to settle your hearts. In fact, the real victory is not through these external means. Rather, true victory is only from Allah, the Almighty, whom none can conquer- the All-Wise in His discretion and sacred laws.",
  3127:
      "The intention behind this victory that materialized for you in the Battle of Badr was so that one group of disbelievers would be destroyed by death, and another group would be disgraced with their defeat, enraging them. Then, they would retreat, fainthearted and humiliated.",
  3128:
      "When the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم supplicated for the destruction of the polytheists' leaders after what transpired on their part during the Battle of Uhud, Allah said to him: \"Nothing of their affair is for you [to determine]. Rather, all matters are for Allah [to determine]. So, be patient until Allah decides between you: either by guiding them to repentance and the acceptance of Islam; or by their persisting in disbelief. Then, He will punish them. In that case, they would indeed be oppressors deserving of punishment.\"",
  3129:
      "To Allah belongs the creation and management of all that is in the heavens and the earth. He forgives the sins of whomever He wills among His slaves through His Mercy. And He punishes whomever He wills through his justice. Allah is Forgiving and Merciful to those who repent to Him.",
  3130:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, keep far away from receiving usury- increasing and doubling the capital that you advance to others as was done by the people pre-Islam. Be fearful of Allah by following His commands and staying away from what He has prohibited so that perhaps you may attain the good you seek of the worldly life and the Afterlife.",
  3131:
      "Place a shield between yourselves and the Fire that Allah has prepared for disbelievers through righteous deeds and leaving behind what is prohibited.",
  3132:
      "Obey Allah and His Messenger by following the commands and staying away from the prohibitions so that perhaps you may receive mercy in the worldly life and the Afterlife.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The blessings and trials that people have should be mentioned as an example for others.\n2. Being constantly mindful of Allah and patient during the difficulties of fighting are some of the biggest reasons for Allah giving victory to His servants.\n3. Every matter is in Allah’s dominion. He decrees and judges as He wills, and the true believer surrenders wholeheartedly to Allah, submitting to His wisdom.\n4. Sins in general, and usury in particular, is one of the biggest causes for people’s ruin, especially in countries where conditions are difficult.\n5. Being mindful of Allah and obeying Him are some of the biggest causes for Allah’s mercy and kindness to people.",
  3133:
      "Take the initiative and compete with one another in performing good deeds and drawing near to Allah through different types of obedient acts. Do this in order to obtain significant forgiveness from Allah and to be admitted into a garden as wide as the heavens and the earth, which Allah has prepared for those among His slaves who are fearful of Him.",
  3134:
      "Those who fear Allah spend generously from their wealth in the path of Allah, in a state of ease and hardship. They resist anger despite the ability to retaliate, and they overlook those who oppress them. Allah loves the benevolent who are described with these elements of good conduct.",
  3135:
      "They are the ones who, if they were to commit a major sin or wrong themselves by committing a lesser sin, remember Allah, the Exalted, His warning to the disobedient, and His promise to the fearful. Then, they seek from their Lord that He covers their sins and not censure them, remorseful for what they did. This is because no one except Allah alone can forgive sins, and they do not persist in their sins. They know that they are sinners and that Allah can forgive all sins.",
  3136:
      "The reward of those who are described with these praiseworthy characteristics and outstanding qualities is Allah's covering their sins and overlooking them. In the Afterlife, they will have gardens with rivers flowing below their palaces, where they will reside forever. How excellent is that recompense for those who act in obedience to Allah!",
  3137:
      "When the believers were tested with what befell them on the day of Uḥud, Allah said to them as consolation: The established divine practice of the destruction of disbelievers has passed before you. He made the end for the believers after testing them. So, travel through the Earth, carefully consider, and take a lesson from the ultimate destiny of those who deny Allah and His Messengers: their homes are now empty, and their reign has disappeared.",
  3138:
      "This noble Quran clarifies the truth and warns about falsehood for all people. It shows the path to guidance and restraint for the fearful because they are the ones who can take advantage of the guidance and direction within it.",
  3139:
      "Do not become weak, O believers, and do not be sad over what befell you on the day of Uḥud. That is not appropriate because you are superior through your faith, superior through Allah's help and your hope of His victory- if you are believers in Allah and His promise to His fearful slaves.",
  3140:
      "If you suffered injuries and deaths, O believers, on the day of Uḥud, then the disbelievers suffered the same injuries and deaths you did. Allah distributes such days between people, their believers, and their disbelievers, giving victory and defeat as He wills for reasons of far-reaching wisdom. Among these reasons is for the believers to be distinguished clearly from the hypocrites. Another reason is for whomever He wills to be honored with martyrdom in His path. Therefore, Allah does not love those who oppress themselves by giving up fighting in His path.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believer is encouraged to hasten to do good actions, taking advantage of the time left in life before it is too late.\n2. One of the things that make the Mindful worthy of entering Paradise is that they spend from their wealth in every situation, control their anger, forgive people and are kind to creation.\n3. Looking at what happened to peoples of the past is one of the best ways to learn lessons - those who have hearts are able to understand this.\n4. Those who fight for Allah’s cause are different from the idolaters, even if they receive the same pain and hurt in this world as the idolaters do. This is because of their hope of reward from Allah, and hope of His victory.",
  3141:
      "A part of this wisdom is the purification of believers from their sins, the rescue of their ranks from the hypocrites, and the destruction of the disbelievers and their eradication.",
  3142:
      "Did you think, O believers, that you would enter Paradise without trials and [demands of] patience by which the true fighters in the path of Allah are distinguished, including those who are patient with the trials that befall them in [that path]?",
  3143:
      "Indeed, you, O believers, wished to encounter the disbelievers to obtain martyrdom in the path of Allah, as your brothers earned on the day of Badr before you experienced the various means of death and its severity. Now, on the day of Uḥud, you saw what you wished for with your own eyes.",
  3144:
      "When news spread among the people on the day of Uhud that the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم had been killed, Allah revealed the following as a rebuke to those from among the believers who refrained from fighting further due to this, stating: \n Muhammad is but a messenger like the messengers of Allah who preceded him: they passed away or were killed. If he were to die or be killed, would you apostate from your religion and abandon the fight? Whoever among you apostates from his religion will not harm Allah in any way. He is the Omnipotent, the Almighty. The apostate only harms themself through exposure to the loss in the worldly life and the Afterlife. Allah will abundantly reward those thankful to Him by making them firm in His religion and their fighting in His path.",
  3145:
      "Not a soul dies except by the Divine Decree of Allah after the time Allah has written for them ends. He has fixed a time that cannot be increased or decreased. Whoever intends worldly gain through his actions, He will grant him in accordance to whatever has been decreed for him of [worldly gain]. There will be no share for him in the Afterlife. Whoever intends by his actions the recompense of Allah in the Afterlife, He will grant its reward. Moreover, He will greatly reward those who are grateful to their Lord.",
  3146:
      "How many a prophet among the prophets of Allah fought while a larger number of followers accompanied him? They did not cower from fighting due to what befell them of death and injuries in the path of Allah. They did not weaken from fighting the enemy or surrender to him. Rather, they were patient and steadfast. Allah loves those who are patient upon hardships and adversities in His path.",
  3147:
      "When these trials struck them, those who were patient said nothing except: \"Our Lord forgive us our sins and our overstepping the limits in our affairs. Plant our feet firmly when we encounter our enemy, and grant us victory against people who disbelieve in You.\"",
  3148:
      "So, Allah gave them the reward of the worldly life in their victory, making it possible for them. He also gave them the most excellent reward of the Afterlife, in their contentment and residing with eternal bliss in gardens of delight. Allah loves those who hold the highest standards in their worship and transactions. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Giving people trials is a divine custom, which distinguishes those who truly and patiently struggle for the sake of Allah from those who do not.\n2. Striving for the sake of Allah, and calling to His path, should not be dependent on a particular person, no matter how important they may be.\n3. The length of life that people will have is fixed by Allah: it will not be made longer by mere hope or acting cowardly, nor made shorter by being courageous in battle.\n4. The goals and intentions of people differ: some desire the reward of Allah, and some desire this world. Everyone will be rewarded according to their intentions and actions.",
  3149:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, if you obey those who disbelieve among the Jews, Christians, and polytheists in the misguidance they order you to commit, then they will return you to what you used to be upon of disbelief after your Belief. Then, you would return to being losers in the worldly life and the Afterlife.",
  3150:
      "These disbelievers will not stand by you if you obey them. Rather, Allah is your defender against your enemies. So, obey Him, for He, the Exalted, is the best of defenders, and you will not need anyone after Him.",
  3151:
      "We will cast dread into the hearts of those who disbelieve to the point that they are not able to stand firm to fight you. This is because of their association of false gods with Allah. They worshiped them based on their desires when no proof for it was sent down to them. The abode they will return to in the Afterlife will be the Fire. What a miserable abode is the Fire for the oppressors!",
  3152:
      "Allah has fulfilled the victory He promised you over your enemies on the day of Uḥud. You were engaging them in a fierce battle, by Allah's permission, until you cowered and weakened in your resolve to do as the Messenger had commanded you. And you differed about whether to remain at your posts or leave them to gather the spoils of war. You disobeyed the Messenger's command to remain in your positions no matter what happened. You did this after Allah showed you the victory over the enemies you wished for. Among you are those who want the spoils of the worldly life, and they are the ones who left their posts. Also, among you are those who want the reward of the Afterlife, and they were the ones who remained in their positions, obeying the Messenger's command. Then, Allah diverted you from them and gave them authority over you to test you. So, the believer, patient with trials, would be distinguished from the one whose foot slipped and his soul became weak. Allah had indeed pardoned you for what you committed when you went against the command of the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Allah possesses great preference for the believers when He guides them to faith, pardons their misdeeds, and rewards them for the calamities they suffer.",
  3153:
      "Remember, O believers, when you were driven off through the earth as fugitives on the day of Uḥud. It was due to what befell you of weakheartedness because you went against the command of the Messenger. You could not even look at one another, and the Messenger called you as you turned away while he was between you and the polytheists, saying, \"Come to me, slaves of Allah! Come to me, slaves of Allah!\" Allah repaid you for this with pain and distress in the form of the victory and spoils of war you forfeited. He followed that up with more pain and distress in the form of rumors circulating between you that the Prophet had died. He brought this down on you for you not to grieve over what you forfeited of victory and spoils, what befell you of death and injuries. And after realizing that the Prophet had not been killed then, each calamity and pain was made easy for you to bear. Allah is well aware of everything you do, and nothing about the condition of your hearts is hidden from Him, nor are the actions of your limbs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believers are warned against obeying the disbelievers and being guided by their desires: this leads to loss in this world and in the Afterlife.\n2. One of the ways Allah gives victory to the believers is by instilling fear into the hearts of the enemies of Allah.\n3. One of the biggest causes of defeat in battle is attachment to this world and the desire for the gains of war.\n4. Another reason for defeat in battle is going against the commander of the army and not obeying his orders.\n5. Allah cares for the believers in every circumstance, even in the trials and tests He gives to them.",
  3154:
      "Then He sent down peace and security after the pain and distress, prompting sleep to envelop a group among you who were confident in Allah's promise, resulting in a feeling of safety and serenity in their hearts. Another group, the hypocrites, did not receive a sense of safety or sleepiness. They only worried about their own safety, mired in anxiety and fear. They held negative presumptions about Allah, thinking that He would not grant His Prophet victory or support His slaves. They presumed just like the people of the Age of Ignorance who did not assess Allah as He deserved. Due to their ignorance of Allah, these hypocrites say: \"We do not have a say about the command to march forth for battle. If we did, we would not have marched forth.\" Say, O Prophet, in reply to these people: \"Truly, the entire matter is for Allah to decide. For He is the one who foreordains whatever He wills, He determines whatever He wills, and He is the One who decreed your marching forth.\" These hypocrites hide within themselves doubts and negative presumptions that they do not express to you, considering that they say: \"If we had a say in the matter of marching forth, we would not have been killed in this location.\" Tell them, O Prophet, in rebuking them: \"Even if you had remained in your homes, far from the locales of killing and death, those among you for whom Allah had written death would surely have departed for wherever their deaths would take place. Allah did not write that except to test the intentions and motives in your chests and to distinguish what they contained of Belief and hypocrisy. Allah knows what is in the chests of His slaves, and nothing in them is hidden from Him.",
  3155:
      "Those of you, O Companions of Muhammad, who faced defeat on the day the polytheists encountered the Muslims at Uḥud, it was only because the Devil caused them to slip due to what they earned from disobedience. Nonetheless, Allah has indeed pardoned them and will not take them into account as a favor and mercy on His part. Surely, Allah is Forgiving and Forbearing towards those who repent, and He does not hasten to punish.",
  3156:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not be like the disbelievers among the hypocrites when others travel to earn a living or go out on a raid, and they die or are killed, [the disbelievers] say to their close relatives: \"If only they had stayed near us, not marched forth, and not raided, then they would not have died and been killed.\" Allah placed this conviction in their hearts to increase their regret and grief. Allah alone is the one who grants life and causes death by His will. Sitting in place does not prevent His Decree, and marching forth does not hasten it. Allah sees everything you do. Your actions are not hidden from Him, and He will requite you based on them.",
  3157:
      "If you are killed or die in Allah's path, O believers, Allah has immense forgiveness for you, and He will bestow mercy upon you. His forgiveness and mercy are better than this whole world and all that its people accumulate in it of its fading pleasures. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Ignorance of Allah and His attributes leads to wrong belief and the corruption of actions.\n2. Allah cares for those close to Him and protects them in every situation.\n3. The lifespan of people is fixed and determined: being daring and courageous does not shorten life; and being cowardly and careful does not lengthen it.\n4. Allah tests people: to distinguish the good from the bad.\n5. One of the greatest and most noble ranks before Allah the Exalted is the rank of the martyr for the sake of Allah.",
  3158:
      "If you die, regardless of your manner of death, or you are killed, you will all return to Allah alone. Truly, He will requite you according to your actions.",
  3159:
      "Due to Allah's great Mercy, your disposition, O Prophet, is easygoing with your Companions. They would have dispersed from around you if you were hard-hearted and severe in your speech and actions. Therefore, overlook their shortcomings concerning your rights and seek forgiveness for them. Seek out their opinions in whatever requires joint consultation. When you decide on a matter after mutual consultation, proceed and have complete trust in Allah. Allah loves those who fully trust Him so He can grant them success and support.",
  3160:
      "If Allah supports you with His aid and help, no one can overcome you, even if everyone on earth gathers against you. If He abandons helping you and entrusts you to yourselves, no one can help you afterward. Help is in His hand alone. So, let the believers rely on Allah and no one else besides Him.",
  3161:
      "It was not for any Prophet among the Prophets to act treacherously by taking anything from the spoils of war other than what Allah assigned explicitly to him. Whoever among you acts treacherously by taking something from the spoils of war will be punished by being disgraced on the Day of Judgment. So, he will come carrying whatever he took in front of all creation. Then, every soul will be given the full requital of what he earned without decrease. They will not be oppressed by any addition to their sins or subtracting from their good deeds.",
  3162:
      "Not equal according to Allah is he who observes the Faith and good deeds by which he will obtain the good pleasure of Allah, and he who disbelieves in Allah and commits sins. The latter shall incur Allah's wrath and Fire as their abode. What an evil refuge and abode!",
  3163:
      "They differ in their ranks in the worldly life and Afterlife, according to Allah. Allah sees what they do. Nothing is hidden from Him. He will recompense every person according to their deeds.",
  3164:
      "Allah favored the believers and did well for them when He sent them a Messenger from their kind who recited the Quran to them, purified them from polytheism and depravity, and taught them the Quran and Sunnah. Before this Messenger was sent, they had been steeped in clear misguidance, far from guidance and the right path.",
  3165:
      "When a calamity struck you, O believers, during your defeat at Uḥud, and among you were those who were killed, you had already achieved twice as much from your enemies on the day of Badr in terms of the dead and captured. You said: Where did this calamity come from? We are believers, and the Prophet of Allah is among us! Say, O Prophet: What happened only reached you because of yourselves- you disputed with the Messenger and disobeyed him. Allah is Omnipotent over everything, giving victory to whomever He wills and forsaking whomever He wills.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. True victory comes from Allah the Exalted. He is the Powerful, Who cannot be fought against; the Mighty, Who cannot be overcome.\n2. The state of someone in the world who follows the guidance of Allah and acts accordingly is not the same as the state of someone who turns away from it and rejects it, just as they will not be the same in rank in the Afterlife.\n3. From the grace and blessings of Allah to the believers is that He sent a messenger to them who was like them, who spent time with them and was their friend, and made it easy for them to learn from him and to act as he did.\n4. The misfortune and distress that a person is given in this world may be because of their disobedience, or it may be a test that will raise them up in rank. However, it must be remembered that Allah pardons and overlooks many sins.",
  3166:
      "The death, wounds, and defeat you suffered on the day of Uḥud when your army and the army of the polytheists met was by the permission and decree of Allah, with far-reaching wisdom behind it so that the truthful believers would emerge.",
  3167:
      "And so that the hypocrites would emerge who, when it was said to them: 'Fight in Allah's path or defend with your additional men the Muslim masses,' they replied: Had we known that there would be fighting, then we would have followed you. However, we did not think there would be any fighting between you and the people. Their state at that time was closer to what proved their disbelief than what proved their faith, saying with their tongues what was not in their hearts. Allah knows best what they hide in their chests, and He will punish them for it.",
  3168:
      "They are the ones who failed to fight and said to their close relatives who suffered losses on the day of Uḥud: \"If [your loved ones] had obeyed us and not marched forth to fight, then they would not have been killed.\" Say, O Prophet, as a refutation of them: \"So ward off death from yourselves when it befalls you if you are truthful in your claim that they would not have been killed if they had obeyed you. And [if you are truthful] that the reason for your escape from death was because you refrained from fighting in Allah's path.",
  3169:
      "Do not think, O Prophet, that those killed fighting in the path of Allah are dead. Rather, they live a special life near their Lord in an abode of His honor, being provided with all types of delights that no one knows of except Allah.",
  3170:
      "Happiness engulfs them, and joy encompasses them through what Allah has bestowed on them from His favor. They hope for and anticipate meeting their brothers who remained in the worldly life. [They also hope for and anticipate] that [their brothers], if killed during the fighting, will receive the same favor. They fear not in terms of what awaits them from the matters of the Afterlife. Therefore, they are not sorrowful over any worldly prosperity that passed them by.",
  3171:
      "Along with this, they rejoice in the immense reward that awaits them from Allah and the tremendous addition on top of the reward. [They also rejoice] that Allah, the Exalted, does not recant the reward of the believers. Rather, He grants their rewards completely and even adds to them.",
  3172:
      "They are the ones who carried out the command of Allah and His Messenger when they were called to march forth to fight in the path of Allah and meet the polytheists in the battle of Hamra' Al-Asad, which immediately followed the battle of Uḥud. This was after they had suffered injuries on the day of Uhud. Nevertheless, their injuries did not stop them from answering the call of Allah and His Messenger. For those who did well in their efforts and feared Allah by following His commands and keeping away from what He prohibited, there is a tremendous reward from Allah- and it is Paradise.",
  3173:
      "Some of the polytheists said to them: \"The Quraysh, led by Abu Sufyan, had gathered large numbers together to fight and eradicate you. So, beware of them and fear encountering them.\" These words and the intimidation increased their faith in Allah and the trustworthiness of His promise. So, they marched forth to meet them, saying: \"Allah, the Exalted, is sufficient for us, and what an excellent one for us to entrust our affairs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the customs of Allah is to test His servants so as to distinguish the real believer from the lying hypocrite.\n2. Allah has a great regard for those striving for good and He rewards such people with the highest ranks.\n3. The divine will and decree of Allah is an absolute reality, and there is no way to escape it.\n4. The virtue of the Companions and their high rank in this world and in the Afterlife, is because of what they sacrificed from themselves and their wealth for the sake of Allah.",
  3174:
      "They returned after marching towards the battle of Ḥamrā' Al-Asad with an immense reward from Allah, an increase in their ranks, and security from their enemy. In addition, they did not suffer any death or injury. They followed what pleased Allah by obeying Him and refraining from disobedience. Allah possesses tremendous favor for His believing slaves.",
  3175:
      "Only the Devil attempts to frighten you, terrorizing you with his helpers and supporters. Do not cower from them, for they have no power or strength. Rather, fear Allah by obeying Him if you truly believe in Him.",
  3176:
      "Do not be brought down into sadness, O Messenger, by those among the hypocrites who rush to disbelief, turning on their heels. They cannot cause Allah any harm. Rather, they only harm themselves by distancing themselves from faith and obedience to Allah. Allah intends for them to be defeated, to lack success, and to have no share in the bliss of the Afterlife. They will suffer a severe punishment in the Fire.",
  3177:
      "Those who exchange faith for disbelief cannot harm Allah in any way. Instead, they only harm themselves. They will have a painful punishment in the Afterlife.",
  3178:
      "Those who disbelieve in their Lord and stubbornly resist His legislation should not presume that their respite and the extension of their lives upon disbelief, just as they are, is better for them. It is not as they presume. We only grant them respite to allow them to increase in sin, with an abundance of disobedience on top of their sin. They will have a humiliating punishment.",
  3179:
      "It is not from Allah's wisdom to leave you, O believers, as you are, mixed with the hypocrites with no distinction between you, without making clear who truly are the believers. He will distinguish you through different responsibilities and trials to differentiate the pure believers from the filthy hypocrites. It is also not from Allah's wisdom to inform you of all the Unseen so you can distinguish between the believer and the hypocrite. Rather, Allah chooses whomever He wills among His Messengers and informs them about some of the Unseen, just as He informed His Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم about the circumstances of the hypocrites. Therefore, realize your faith in Allah and His Messenger, genuinely believe in and fear Allah by following His commands and staying away from what He has prohibited. Thus, you shall attain an immense reward from Allah.",
  3180:
      "Some are miserly with the comforts Allah has bestowed upon them as a favor from Him, and thus, they withhold the rights of Allah therein. They should not presume that it is a good intended for them. Rather, it is an evil intended for them because that in which they are miserly will become a collar wrapped around their necks, tormenting them on the Day of Resurrection. All that is in the heavens and earth must return to Allah alone. He is the Ever-Living after all His creation has perished. Allah knows the tiniest details of everything you do and will recompense you accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believers should not pay attention to Satan trying to intimidate them with his assistants and helpers from among the disbelievers, because everything is up to Allah.\n2. A person should not be misled by Allah giving them respite; rather, they should rush to repent to Allah, asking for His forgiveness in the time given to them before it passes.\n3. It is Allah’s custom to put His servants to the test through different trials: to distinguish those who are bad from those who are good, and the believer from the hypocrite.\n4. The miser who withholds the bounty Allah has given him only harms himself by depriving himself of rewards and gains from Allah, the Generous, the Giving, and exposing himself to the consequences of such behaviour on the Day of Judgement.",
  3181:
      "Allah certainly heard the Jews when they said: Indeed, Allah is poor since He asks us for a 'loan,' while we are rich because of the wealth we have. Allah will record this slander and lie they have uttered against their Lord and their killing the prophets of Allah without right. We will tell them: Taste the torment of burning in the Fire.",
  3182:
      "That punishment is because of disobedient and disgraceful acts you, O Jews, committed by your own hands. Allah does not oppress a single one of His slaves.",
  3183:
      "They are the ones who spoke lies and slanders, saying: Allah has instructed us in His books and on the tongues of His prophets to not believe in a Messenger unless he comes to us with something to verify his claim. Moreover, he will seek a means to Allah through an offering that would be consumed by a fire sent down from heaven. So, they lied against Allah in attributing such instructions to Him and restricting proofs of the truthfulness of the Messengers to what they mentioned. Due to this, Allah ordered His Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم to ask them: Messengers have come to you before with clear proofs of their truthfulness, and even with what you mentioned of an offering being burned by fire from heaven- so, why did you deny them and kill them if you were truthful in what you said?",
  3184:
      "If they deny you, O Prophet, do not be sad because it is normal for disbelievers. Many Messengers who came with clear evidence were denied before you, books containing exhortations and heart-softening accounts, and the Book guiding people with legal rulings and legislation.",
  3185:
      "Every soul, no matter what, must taste death. No created being should be deceived by this worldly life. On the Day of Judgment, you will be granted the reward for your actions in full, without omission. Whoever Allah keeps far from the Fire and admits into Paradise has achieved all that he could hope for of goodness and has been rescued from all that he could fear of evil. The worldly life is nothing but fading possessions. Only those who are deceived are attached to them.",
  3186:
      "You will undoubtedly be tested, O believers, in fulfilling the rights your wealth requires and in calamities sent down along with it. You will certainly be tested in your souls with regard to fulfilling the responsibilities of Divine legislation and in different types of trials sent down to you. You will undoubtedly hear many things from those who were given the books before you and those who associate partners with Allah, things that will hurt you, criticizing you and your religion. If you have patience with the calamities and trials that afflict you, are fearful of Allah by doing what He commands and staying away from what He has prohibited, then that is from among the matters that require resolve and only the genuine contenders [for Allah's favor] will compete for it. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. These verses indicate the extent of the bad behaviour of the Jews and their lies against Allah and His prophets.\n2. Some of the bad actions of these Jews included their attacks on the prophets of Allah, rejecting and killing them.\n3. Allah has decreed death for everyone, so no one can escape it. The intelligent person should, therefore, make efforts to prepare for it.\n4. Every success in this world is deficient, and complete success is only in the Afterlife, by being saved from the fire of Hell and entering Paradise.\n5. One way a believer is tested is through what harm comes to them from the People of the Scripture and the idolaters, and when this happens, it is necessary to have patience and to be Allah-conscious.",
  3187:
      "Remember, O Prophet, when Allah took a firm covenant from the scholars among the Jews and Christians to clarify the Book of Allah for people, not to hide what it contains of guidance and what proves the prophethood of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. No one was among them except they cast off and did not observe the covenant. They concealed the truth and expressed falsehood. They traded the covenant of Allah for a trifling price, like for the prestige and wealth they had obtained. How terrible is this price for which they traded Allah's covenant!",
  3188:
      "Do not assume, O Prophet, that those who are happy with the repugnant actions they have committed and who love that people praise them for the good they did not perform- do not assume that they are rescued and safe from punishment. Instead, Jahannam is their final abode, where they will be in excruciating torment.",
  3189:
      "To Allah alone, and no one else, belongs the dominion of the heavens and earth and everything in them concerning their creation and management. Allah is Omnipotent over everything.",
  3190:
      "Indeed, for those of sound intellect, there are clear proofs in the generation of the heavens and the earth from nothing without a previous example, the alternation of the night and day, and their varying between long and short. These proofs are evidence of the Creator of the universe, who alone deserves acts of worship.",
  3191:
      "They are the ones who remember Allah in all circumstances- while standing, sitting, and lying on their sides. They reflect on the creation of the heavens and earth, saying: \"O Lord! You did not generate this wonderful creation in vain. You are far from frivolity. So, spare us from the punishment of Fire by enabling us to do righteous deeds and preserving us from evil deeds.",
  3192:
      "For indeed You, Our Lord, have humiliated and disgraced those among Your creation that You introduce into the Fire. On the Day of Judgment, wrongdoers will have no assistants to prevent Allah's torment and punishment of them.",
  3193:
      "O our Lord, we have heard someone inviting us to faith, and he is Your Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم saying: \"Believe in your Lord who is One God.\" Then, we believed in what he invited us to and followed his legislation. So, cover over our sins, do not expose us, overlook our evil deeds, and do not take us to account for them. Let our souls be taken while accompanying the righteous by guiding us to do good deeds and abandoning evil deeds.",
  3194:
      "O our Lord, grant us the guidance and help in the worldly life that You promised us upon the tongues of Your messengers. Do not disgrace us on the Day of Judgment by placing us in the Fire. Indeed, You, O Lord, are generous and do not break Your promise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Among the characteristics of the bad scholars among the People of the Scripture is their hiding of knowledge, following desires and liking the praise of people despite their corrupt nature and what they hide of evil.\n2. The best lessons and evidences for people of deep thought in recognizing the Creator are found in what Allah has created in the universe and in people’s own selves.\n3. Thinking about the creation of Allah leads to certainty in the greatness of Allah and perfect humility towards Him, the Mighty and Majestic.\n4. Calling on Allah and humility of the heart to Him are among the most perfect expressions of worship.",
  3195:
      "Their Lord responded to their supplication: \"I do not let perish the reward of your deeds, great or small, whether the doer is male or female. So, the principle concerning one another is the same in religion- a person is not given more for being male, and a person is not given less for being female. Those who emigrated in the path of Allah, forced from their homes by disbelievers, suffered harm to obey their Lord. They fought in the path of Allah and were killed so that the Word of Allah would be the highest. I will undoubtedly forgive and overlook their sins on the Day of Judgment and admit them into gardens with rivers flowing under their palaces as a reward from Allah. The best recompense which has no equal is with Allah.",
  3196:
      "The movement of the disbelievers in the land, their command of it, and the abundance of their trade and livelihood should not deceive you, O Prophet, to the point that you feel anxiety and grief at their circumstances.",
  3197:
      "This worldly life is a small commodity that has no perpetuity. After that, the fate they will resort to on the Day of Judgment will be Hell. What a terrible bed is the Fire for them!",
  3198:
      "However, those who fear their Lord by following His commands and staying away from what He has prohibited will receive gardens with rivers flowing under their palaces, dwelling in them forever as recompense prepared for them by Allah, the Exalted. What Allah has prepared for the righteous among His slaves is better and more superior than any worldly pleasures the disbelievers may be wallowing in.",
  3199:
      "The People of the Book are not all the same. A group among them believes in Allah, the truth, and the guidance He revealed to you. They also believe in what was revealed to them in their books, and they do not make distinctions between the messengers of Allah, humbling themselves, submissive to Allah, and wishing for what is with Him. They do not trade the verses of Allah for a small profit in the wares of worldly life. The ones described with these qualities shall have a tremendous reward with their Lord. Indeed, Allah is swift in taking deeds into account and swift in requital for them.",
  3200:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, be patient with responsibilities under the Divine law and the worldly calamities that strike. Defeat the disbelievers through patience, for they are not more patient than you. Take care to fight in the path of Allah. Fear Allah by following His commands and staying away from what He has prohibited so that you may obtain what you seek of safety from the Fire and enter Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is from Allah’s grace and mercy with His servants when He is quick to respond to their prayers and listen to their calls.\n2. It is from the perfect justice of Allah that He does not distinguish between men and women in their rewards for His obedience.\n3. The hann that a believer experiences in the sacred struggle for the sake of Allah when forced to emigrate from his home because of his faith is one of the greatest means by which sins are forgiven and rewards are multiplied.\n4. What the disbeliever may be given in this world in terms of wealth and enjoyment, even if great, is unimportant because it is passing. The only thing that is important is the reality of what happens to them in the Afterlife in the abode of eternity.\n5. Among the People of the Scripture are those who bear witness to the truth which is in their books: they have faith in what was revealed to them and in what was revealed to the believers, so they have a double reward.\n6. Patience with the truth and struggling against those who reject it, while striving for the sake of it, is the path to success in the Afterlife.",
  4000:
      "The Women (Surah An-Nisa)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nOrganizing the Muslim community, building its relationships, preserving rights, encouraging armed struggle, and invalidating the claim that Christ was killed.\n•    Explanation:    \nIt was named as such due to the mention of women and the details of many rulings pertaining to them.",
  4001:
      "O people, fear your Lord, for He created you from a single soul- your father, Adam. From Adam, He created his spouse, Eve, your mother. From the two of them, He dispersed a great multitude of people, both male and female, throughout the regions of the earth. Be fearful of Allah when asking one another by invoking Him, such as: I ask you, by Allah, to do such-and-such.Also, be fearful of severing ties of kinship, which link you together. Allah keeps a close watch over you, and not a thing from your actions escapes Him. Rather, He calculates them and recompenses you based on that.",
  4002:
      "O guardians, for those whose fathers have died and have not yet reached puberty, i.e., orphans, give them their wealth in full when they reach puberty. Do not turn what is permitted into what is prohibited by taking what has an excellent value from the property of orphans and exchanging it for something inferior or of no value from your property. Do not take the property of orphans and combine it with your own – that is a great crime, according to Allah.",
  4003:
      "If you fear that you will not be just when marrying female orphans under your guardianship – either by reducing their dowry from what their status demands or by mistreating them – then leave them alone and marry who is agreeable among other women. If you wish, marry two, three, or four. However, if you fear that you will not be equitable between them, restrict yourself to just one, or enjoy what you possess of slave women since their rights are not the same as the rights of wives. That which is mentioned in the verse concerning orphans and restricting oneself to marrying a single woman or enjoying slave women is the closest to not being unjust and being biased.",
  4004:
      "Give women their rightful dowries as required. Yet, if they gladly relinquish anything from the dowry to you without being forced to, use it as permitted and do not be bothered about it.",
  4005:
      "O guardians, do not give property to those not proficient in disposing of it. Allah made this property a way to provide for the welfare and living expenses of slaves, and such individuals are not qualified to manage and protect property. So, spend on them and clothe them from that property. Speak to them in a good way. Prepare them well so you can give them their property when they reach puberty and become proficient at managing it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. All of humankind has the same origin. So they must be mindful of their Lord Who created them, and should be merciful to each other.\n2. Allah commands kindness to those who are weak among women and orphans, so that the treatment of them should be just and generous.\n3. It is permissible for a Muslim man to have up to four wives, with the condition of being just between them, and being able to support them.\n4. It is legitimate to place the incompetent person who does not behave correctly under guardianship, for his own good and to protect him from wasting his wealth, which is used for his welfare in this world.",
  4006:
      "O guardians, test orphans when they reach the age of puberty by giving them a part of their wealth to manage. If they dispose of it well, and their maturity is evident to you, hand over their property in full without holding it back from them. Do not consume their wealth when the need arises, overstepping the limit Allah has permitted you. Do not rush to use it up for fear that they will take it when they reach maturity. Those with enough wealth to suffice them should refrain from taking the wealth of orphans. He among you who is poor and has no wealth should only use it proportionately to his need. When you hand over the property after they reach puberty and their maturity is apparent, there should be a witness to that hand-over to protect the rights involved and to prevent causes for disagreement. Allah is sufficient as a witness to that and as an accountant for slaves regarding their actions.",
  4007:
      "Men are to have a share of what is left behind after death by their parents or relatives, such as brothers and uncles, whether it is a large or small sum. Women are also to have a share of what their relatives leave behind, contrary to the Age of Ignorance, when women and children, were left out of the inheritance. As Allah obligates, this share is a right, and its amount is clearly determined.",
  4008:
      "If relatives, orphans, and the poor, who do not inherit, are present at the time the inheritance is divided, then give them, on the basis it is a recommendation, some of the wealth before it is divided. Give whatever your souls find agreeable since they may be hoping for a share, and it came to you without any hardship. Also, kindly speak to them without any meanness.",
  4009:
      "Those who would leave behind young, weak children if they died should fear they would be left in ruins. They should fear Allah regarding orphans under their guardianship by avoiding unfairness towards them. This is so that Allah will facilitate for them after death someone who will treat their children as well as they did. They should conduct themselves excellently concerning the rights of children present at his last will by telling them statements that correspond to the truth. This is so that his heirs are not wronged in his last will after he is gone. Nor should he deprive himself of this good deed by not leaving a last will.",
  4010:
      "Those who take the property of orphans and spend it wrongly and unjustly only consume a Fire into their stomachs that sets fire to them. The Fire will incinerate them completely on the Day of Judgment.",
  4011:
      "Allah entrusts and orders you concerning your children's inheritance to divide it between them as follows: a son gets a share equal to the share of two daughters. If the deceased left two daughters or more without a son, they get two-thirds of what is left behind. If there is just one daughter, she gets half of what is left behind. Each of the deceased's parents gets a sixth of what is left behind if he has a male or female child. If he has no children or heir except for his parents, the mother gets a third, and the father gets the rest as an unfixed share. If the deceased has two or more siblings, male or female, full siblings or half-siblings, his mother gets a sixth share as a fixed share, and the father gets the rest as an unfixed share. There is nothing for the siblings. This division of the inheritance is after execution of the bequests that the deceased ordered on the stipulation that his bequests cannot be more than a third of his total wealth and his debts have been repaid. Allah has divided inheritance like this because you do not know who among your parents and children are most beneficial to you in the worldly life and Afterlife. The deceased may presume the best of one of his heirs and leave everything to him or presume the worst of someone and forbid him from receiving anything. Then, it turns out that the circumstances were contrary to that. The one who is aware of all of that is Allah. He is the one from whom nothing is hidden. For this reason, the division of inheritance was made clear, and He made it an obligation for His slaves. Allah knows everything, and nothing is hidden from Him concerning the welfare of His slaves. He is All-Wise in His legislation and management. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The inheritance laws of Islam give men and women their rights, so ensuring justice between them.\n2. The sanctity of the wealth of orphans is firmly established in the sacred law, and overstepping the limits with it or wasting it in any way is prohibited.\n3. The division of the inheritance in sacred law is based on ensuring justice between the inheritors and keeping in mind what will best serve their welfare.\n4. Due to the fact that wealth is one of the biggest reasons for disputes between people, Allah details the division of it through the laws of inheritance.",
  4012:
      "Half of what your wives leave behind is for you, O husbands, if they have no male or female children with you or someone else. If they have male or female children, you get a fourth of the wealth they leave behind. You receive your share after the execution of her bequests and the repayment of her debts. Wives get a quarter of what you leave behind, O husbands if you have no male or female children with them or another woman. If you have male or female children, wives receive an eighth of what you leave behind, to be divided after the execution of your bequests and the repayment of your debts. If a man or woman dies without any parents or children to inherit from them, and the deceased has a brother or sister from the same mother, then each receives a fixed sixth share. If they have more than one male or female sibling from the same mother, they share a third fixed share, with males and females receiving an equal share. They only take their share after the execution of the deceased's bequests and the repayment of his debts, stipulating that the bequest does not involve harming the inheritors, such as it being more than a third of his wealth. The rulings contained in the verses are a trust from Allah to you, which He has obligated. Allah knows what is in the best interest of His slaves in the worldly life and Afterlife. He is forbearing and does not rush to punish the disobedient.",
  4013:
      "The rulings mentioned concerning orphans and others are the laws of Allah that Allah has legislated for His slaves to act upon. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger by following His commands and staying away from what He has prohibited, Allah will admit him into gardens with rivers flowing beneath their palaces, residing where destruction cannot catch up with them. That divine reward is the great success that no other success comes near to.",
  4014:
      "Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger by denying His rulings, neglecting to act upon them, or doubting them and overstepping the limits He has legislated, He will insert him into a fire. There, he will dwell in humiliating torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The inheritance wealth is not divided between the inheritors until any debts that the person who died had have been settled, and their lawful bequests have been taken from it, which cannot be more than a third of the total wealth.\n2. There is here a warning against being careless about the division of the inheritance, because it is Allah’s contract and His commandment to His believing servants, so it is forbidden to disregard it or to be careless about it.\n3. The characteristics of faith include following what Allah instructs and respecting what He has prohibited, and stopping at the limits He has established.\n4. Allah has made obligatory upon His servants these laws related to inheritance and its division between the inheritors and warned them against being complacent about them.\n5. It is from Allah’s justice and wisdom that He promises the greatest reward to those who are devoted to Him, and the greatest punishment to those who oppose Him and overstep His limits.",
  4015:
      "For those of your women who commit the disgrace of fornication, whether married or unmarried, seek out four Muslim men of integrity to bear witness against her. If they give testimony against them for its commission, then confine them to their homes as a punishment until the end of their lives or until Allah makes a way for them other than being confined. After this, Allah made a path for them by legislating that previously unmarried women be lashed one hundred times and banished for a year. A previously married woman is stoned.",
  4016:
      "If two men commit the disgrace of fornication, whether previously married or not, apply to both of them verbal and physical punishment that results in humiliation and reproach. If they desist from what they were doing and rectify their actions, then stop harming them. The one who is repentant from sin is like the one who has no sin. Indeed, Allah turns to those who repent among His slaves and is compassionate with them. This punishment was considered adequate at the beginning of Islam. Afterward, it was abrogated by lashing those previously unmarried, banishing them, and stoning previously married individuals.",
  4017:
      "Allah only accepts repentance from those who dared commit sins and disobedience due to their ignorance of the punishment and evil involved. This is the situation for everyone who sins, intentionally or unintentionally, then returns repentant to their Lord before their death. Allah will accept their repentance and overlook their sins. Allah knows the circumstances of His creation, and He is All-Wise in His decree and legislation.",
  4018:
      "Allah does not turn in mercy and forgiveness to those who continue in their disobedience, overstepping the limits and insisting on overstepping them, and not turning away from doing this until they are dying, then saying that they regret what they did and asking for Allah's forgiveness. Also, Allah does not turn in mercy and forgiveness to those who die in disbelief. He has prepared a painful punishment for them.",
  4019:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, you are not allowed to inherit the wives of your fathers in the way wealth is inherited or marry them, give them in marriage, or stop them from marrying. Also, it is forbidden for you to retain your wives whom you do not like to get them to give back some of what you gave to them unless they have had illegal sexual relations. In that case, you can get them to return what you gave them. Be good companions to your women, not hurting them, and be kind to them. If you do not like them for worldly reasons, be patient with them. Allah may put much good in what you do not like, both in the life of this world and in the Afterlife.",
  4020:
      "If you, O husbands, want to divorce a woman and replace her with another, then there is no harm. However, if you gave the one you intend to divorce a great deal of wealth as a dowry, you are not allowed to take anything back from it. Returning what you gave them would be considered open defamation and a clear sin.",
  4021:
      "How could you take what you gave to them as a dowry after what occurred between you of connection, friendship, enjoyment, and sharing secrets? Greed for the wealth they possess, despite all this, is detestable and shameful. They took a covenant from you that was strongly attested by which they became lawful to you through the Word of Allah, the Exalted, and His legislation.",
  4022:
      "Do not marry women whom your fathers married. That is forbidden except for what happened before Islam, in which case you will not be taken to account for it. Sons marrying their fathers' wives is a practice of immense repulsiveness, a cause for earning Allah's anger for its perpetrator, and an evil path for whoever traverses it.",
  4023:
      "Allah has prohibited for you to marry the following: your mothers, even if far removed through an ascended relationship, in other words, your grandmother and great-grandmother, whether paternal or maternal; your daughters, even if far removed through descended relationship, in other words, your granddaughters and great-granddaughters; likewise, the daughters of your son and daughters of daughters, even if far removed through descended relationship; your full sisters and half-sisters; your paternal aunts and great-aunts of your fathers and mothers, even if far removed through ascendant relationship; your maternal aunts and maternal great-aunts of your father and mothers, even if far removed through ascendant relationship; the daughters of your full brother and full sister, and their children, even if far removed through descendant relationship; your mothers through breastfeeding and your sisters through breastfeeding; the mothers of your wives, whether you have consummated the marriage or not; and the daughters of your wives raised mostly in your home whom she had with someone else, if you have consummated the marriage. However, if you have not consummated the marriage, then there is no harm in marrying their daughters. You are also forbidden to marry your sons' wives from your loins, even if they did not consummate the marriage. Included in this ruling are the wives of your sons through breastfeeding. It is prohibited for you to marry two sisters at the same time who are related by blood or breastfeeding, except if this happened in the Age of Ignorance. In this case, Allah has pardoned it. Allah is forgiving and compassionate to His slaves who are repentant towards Him. In the authentic examples set by the Prophet, the prohibition of simultaneously marrying a woman and her paternal or maternal aunt is also confirmed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has allowed a couple to divorce, and has put this in the hands of the man.\n2. If a man has sexual relations with his wife, the dowry is fixed. He is not, then, allowed to touch it or covet it, even if he wishes to separate from her and divorce her.\n3. Allah has prohibited marriage to the wives of fathers, because it is an evil which anyone in their right mind with a wholesome nature hates.\n4. Allah clearly detailed which women it is allowed to marry, and which of them it is prohibited to marry, whether this is due to one’s family relationship with them, or relationship by marriage or wet-nursing, this is to honour her and protect her from transgression.",
  4024:
      "Those who are already married are prohibited to you, except those whom you have captured while fighting in Allah's path: intimate relations with them are allowed to you after making sure they are not pregnant by the arrival of a menstruation cycle – this is an emphatic obligation from Allah. Aside from that, Allah has permitted you to seek to protect your chastity and theirs with your wealth in a lawful way without pursuing fornication. Give those you enjoy in marriage their dowry, which Allah has made an obligation for you. However, there is nothing wrong if you mutually agree, after the obligation of the dowry has been set, to increase it or to give up part of it. Allah knows His creation, and nothing of them is hidden from Him. He is All-Wise in His management and His legislation.",
  4025:
      "O men, those of you who cannot marry free women due to a lack of resources are allowed to marry a slave owned by someone else- if they appear to be believers. Allah knows best the reality of your faith and the innermost aspect of your circumstances. You are equal to them in religion and humanity, so do not be too proud to marry them. Marry them with the permission of their owners and give them their dowries without reducing the amount or delaying it. This is if they are chaste and not open fornicators. Do not be among those who have intimate relationships to commit fornication with women in secret. If they get married and then commit the disgraceful act of adultery, their legal punishment is half the punishment for a free woman: fifty lashes and not stoning, contrary to the punishment for women previously married. The permissibility of marriage to chaste, believing slave women is a dispensation for those who fear falling into fornication and are unable to marry free women. Patience is preferable to marrying slave women, so that the children do not become slaves. Allah is Forgiving and Compassionate to those of His slaves who repent. From His mercy, He legislated marriage to slaves for those who fear fornication in the case of not being able to marry free women.",
  4026:
      "By legislating these rulings, Allah (may He be Exalted) wishes to clarify His laws and religion and what is in your best interests in the worldly life and Afterlife. He also wishes to guide you to the ways of the previous prophets in allowing and prohibiting matters, their noble qualities, and praiseworthy lives so that you can follow them. He wishes to bring you from disobedience to His obedience. Allah is Omniscient about what is in the best interests of His slaves, and He legislates accordingly. He is All-Wise in His legislation and in managing their affairs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whether they be free women or slaves, it is not permissible to marry wives until they have completed their time of waiting (‘iddah), whatever the reason for this time of waiting may be.\n2. The woman’s dowry is obligatory after consummation of the marriage; but it is allowed for some of the dowry to be reduced if it is from her own free will.\n3. It is permissible to marry a believing slave if one is unable to marry a free woman, when one fears falling into illicit sexual relations.\n4. One of the aims of the sacred law is to make guidance clear from misguidance and to lead people to the ways of guidance which will bring them back to Allah.",
  4027:
      "Allah wants to pardon you and forgive your sins, while those who march forward in life behind their own pleasures want you to become distant from the straight path.",
  4028:
      "Allah wants to reduce the burden of what He legislates for you. Therefore, He does not burden you with what you cannot bear because He knows the weakness of human beings in their nature and disposition.",
  4029:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not take the money of others falsely, by force, theft, bribery, or other unjust means. Instead, money should come from trade through mutual agreement and goodwill between the contracting parties. In this way, it will be lawful for you to consume and dispose of such money. Do not kill one another, do not kill yourselves, and do not cast yourselves into ruin. Allah is Merciful with you and made your blood, wealth, and honor inviolable out of mercy.",
  4030:
      "Whoever does the things Allah has prohibited – consuming the wealth of others or wronging them by killing and the like, purposely exceeding [limits], not out of ignorance or forgetfulness – Allah will admit them to a tremendous fire on the Day of Judgment. There, they will suffer its burning heat and torment. That is insignificant for Allah because He is All-Powerful, and nothing is impossible for Him.",
  4031:
      "O believers, if you avoid acts of major disobedience like joining partners with Allah, ingratitude towards your parents, murder, and receiving interest on loans, then Allah will overlook your lesser sins by wiping them out, erasing them. And We will admit you into a noble place near Him: Paradise.",
  4032:
      "O believers, do not wish for that by which Allah favors some of you over others, lest that leads to resentment and envy. Women should not wish for what Allah has given to men in particular. Indeed, both genders have a share of acts that suit them. Call upon Allah to increase what He grants you. Allah knows everything, so He gives each of them what is consistent with their actions.",
  4033:
      "For every one of you, We have made relations to inherit from what parents and relatives leave in their inheritance. For those with whom you have solemnly sworn to be an ally and helper, give them their share of the inheritance. Indeed, Allah is a witness to everything, and His witness is over your oaths and covenants. Granting inheritance utilizing oaths took place at the beginning of Islam, then it was abrogated.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s mercy towards His servants is vast. He - glory be to Him - loves that they repent to Him; and He loves making things easier for them. As for the people of desires, they only want to lead them astray from guidance.\n2. The sacred law guards the rights of people, forbidding wrongdoing against people’s lives, wealth and honour and put in place the severest of punishments for it.\n3. Staying away from the major sins is a reason for entering Paradise and being forgiven for minor sins.\n4. Being content with Allah’s decree, not wishing for what other people have, keeps a person away from envy, and from resenting the decree of Allah.",
  4034:
      "Men take care of women and manage their affairs because of the favor over [women] by which Allah has distinguished [men]. It is also because He has obligated [men] to spend on and look after them. Righteous women are obedient to their Lord, obedient to their husbands, and protectors of their honor for [men] in their absence through Allah granting them success. Those [women] you fear are too proud to obey their husbands, in words or actions, begin, O husbands, by reminding them and urging them to fear Allah. If they do not respond favorably, then forsake them in bed by turning his back to her and not being intimate with her. If they still do not respond favorably, then strike them non-violently. If they return to obedience, do not transgress against them with injustice or reproach. Indeed, Allah possesses loftiness over everything and is tremendous in His Divine Self and Attributes. So, fear Him.",
  4035:
      "If you fear, O appointed representative of the two spouses, that the disagreement between the two of them will lead to enmity and mutual hostility, then send a just man from the family of the husband and a just man from the family of the wife to determine the advantages of separation or reconciliation - which is more preferred and worthier. If the two judges want reconciliation and they both pursue the best methods for it, Allah will reconcile the two spouses and remove the disagreement between them. Nothing about His slaves is hidden from Allah, and He is All-Knowledgeable of the minute things they conceal in their hearts.",
  4036:
      "Worship Allah alone by submission to Him, and do not worship any others with Him. Be good to your parents by honoring and treating them with benevolence. Be good to relatives, orphans, and the poor. Be good to the neighbor with whom you share kinship and the neighbor with whom you do not. Be good to the friend who accompanies you. Be good to the traveler who is a stranger and has no means to complete their journey. Be good to those you own [slaves]. Allah does not like the ones who are amazed by themselves, arrogant with His slaves, and given to praising himself by boasting to others.",
  4037:
      "Allah does not love those who refuse to spend from His bounty that He has given them as obligated. And yet, they order others with speech and actions to do just that while hiding Allah's favors in terms of bounty, knowledge, and other things Allah has given them. Instead of clarifying the truth for people, they hide it and manifest falsehood. These are among the traits of disbelief, and We have prepared a humiliating punishment for disbelievers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses confirm men’s trusteeship over women because of Allah favouring them, and because of what is obligatory upon them regarding rights of maintenance.\n2. The husband has the right to try to improve the behaviour of his wife if she behaves in a way which is not loyal to him, following a gradual progression of measures without oppression or aggression.\n3. The verses declare the importance Allah places on the rights of the parents, putting them together with His rights, and stresses the importance of kindness to the various categories of people.\n4. Allah warns against traits of bad character, such as pride, boasting, stinginess, and hiding knowledge as well as not making it clear to people.",
  4038:
      "We have likewise prepared punishment for those who spend their wealth so that people notice them and praise them. They do not believe in Allah and the Day of Judgment. We have prepared that shameful punishment for them. It is through following the Devil that they have gone astray. Whoever has the Devil as an inseparable friend, then what an evil companion he has.",
  4039:
      "What harm would it have done these people if they had faith in Allah and the Day of Judgment and spent their wealth in the path of Allah, being sincere to Him? Rather, that is the sum of all things good. Allah is All-Knowledgeable about them. Nothing about their condition is hidden from Him, and everyone will be requited according to their actions.",
  4040:
      "Allah is Just and does not wrong His slaves in any way. He does not decrease their good deeds by the amount of a tiny ant or add to their sins at all. If a good deed is worth an atom's weight, He multiplies its reward as a favor from Him. And along with the multiplication, He grants an immense reward.",
  4041:
      "How will it be on the Day of Judgment, when We bring a prophet for each nation to bear witness for what they did, and We bring you, O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, as a witness for your nation?",
  4042:
      "On that momentous Day, those who disbelieved in Allah and disobeyed His Messenger will wish they could become dirt so they could be equal to the earth. They will not be able to hide from Allah anything they did because Allah will seal their mouths so they cannot speak, and He will allow their limbs to bear witness to their actions against them.",
  4043:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not pray while intoxicated until you recover and can distinguish what you are saying- this was before intoxicants were forbidden entirely. Do not pray when you are in a state of post-sexual impurity. Do not enter mosques in that state, except just passing through without remaining in them, until you have performed the major ritual bath. If you fall ill and cannot use water, are traveling and have emitted a minor impurity, or have had sexual relations with a woman and you cannot find water - then find clean earth and wipe your faces and hands with it. Allah pardons your shortcomings and is Forgiving towards you.",
  4044:
      "O Messenger, do you not know about the Jews to whom Allah gave a portion of knowledge in the Torah, and they exchanged guidance for misguidance? They persist in misleading you, O believers, from the straight path with which the Messenger came so you can traverse their crooked path.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From Allah’s perfect justice and mercy is that He does not wrong His servants in any way, no matter how little, and is gracious to them, multiplying their good actions.\n2. The disbeliever will wish to be dust because of the great horror of the Day of Judgement and the immense punishment that is waiting for him.\n3. Major ritual impurity prevents one from offering the prayer or staying in a mosque, although it is allowed to briefly pass through it.\n4. Allah makes things easy for His servants by permitting dry ablution when there is no water, or when it is not possible to use it.",
  4045:
      "Allah, the Lofty and Sublime, knows your enemies better than you do, O believers. So, He informs you of them and clarifies their hostility towards you. Allah is sufficient as an ally, keeping you safe from their harm. And Allah is enough as a helper, defending you from their plots and harassment while granting you victory over them.",
  4046:
      "Among the Jews are evil people who alter the speech Allah has sent down, misconstruing it. They say to the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم when he commands them in something: We hear what you said, and we disobey your command. They also mockingly say: Listen to what we say. You did not hear [properly]. [Muslims] received a false impression when [Jews] said, \"Rā`inā\" thinking that they meant \"lend us your ear,\" when they intended imprudence by twisting [the meaning] in their language, intending to supplicate against the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. They intended to insult the religion. If they had said, \"We hear your statements and obey your commands,\" instead of \"We hear your statements and disobey your commands\"; \"Listen,\" instead of \"Listen to us, you did not hear\"; and \"Wait for us to understand what you say,\" that would have been better and more just for them than what they said at first. In [saying what is better and more just], there is excellent etiquette befitting the honor of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. However, Allah cursed them and removed them from His mercy due to their disbelief, for they do not believe in a way that benefits them.",
  4047:
      "O Jews and Christians who were given the Book, believe in what We sent down to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم which came as a confirmation for what remains with you from the revelations to Moses and Jesus before We obliterate all [enjoyment] of the senses in the faces [of disbelievers] and We make the locus of [their senses] behind them, or We expel them from the mercy of Allah just like We expelled those who violated the Sabbath by hunting after We forbid it for them. Thus, Allah transformed them into apes. Allah's command and decree are taking place unavoidably.",
  4048:
      "Allah does not forgive that anything from His creation should be joined as partners with Him. Through His favor, He will overlook anything besides polytheism and disbelief in terms of acts of disobedience for whomever He wills. Or through His justice, He will punish those He wills among them according to their sins. Whoever joins others as partners with Allah has committed a terrible sin that is not forgiven for the one who dies in that state.",
  4049:
      "O Messenger, do you not know the affair of those full of praise for themselves and their actions? Allah alone praises and declares as righteous whomever He wills among His slaves. He is All-Aware of what is hidden in the hearts, and He will not decrease the reward of their actions at all, even if the amount of a thread on a date stone.",
  4050:
      "Look, O Messenger, how they fabricate lies against Allah through praise for themselves. That suffices as a clear sin for their misguidance.",
  4051:
      "O Messenger, do you not know and wonder at the condition of the Jews whom Allah gave a portion of knowledge? They believe in the things they worship beside Allah and flatter the polytheists by saying that they are more guided than the Companions of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah Help is sufficient for the believers and His Assistance suffices them.\n2. The Jews were guilty of distorting the word of Allah and displayed bad behaviour towards His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him).\n3. The verses confirm show the danger of associating partners with Allah and disbelief in Him, and that those who die commiting these sins will not be forgiven. Other sins still being commited at the time of death may be forgiven.",
  4052:
      "Allah has removed from His mercy those who hold onto these corrupt beliefs. And whoever Allah removes from it will find no helper to protect him.",
  4053:
      "They do not have any share in the dominion. And if they did, they would not give anyone anything from it, not even the amount of a speck on the surface of a date stone.",
  4054:
      "Rather, they envy Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم and his Companions because of the prophethood, faith, and strength in the land Allah has given them. Why do they envy them when previously Allah gave the offspring of Abraham the revealed Book and what We revealed to them aside from the Book? Why, when We gave them vast power over people?",
  4055:
      "Some People of the Book believed in what Allah revealed to Abraham صلى الله عليه وسلم and the Prophets among his offspring. Some of them turned away from belief in that. This is also their position with regard to what was sent down to the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. The Fire is a sufficient punishment for whoever disbelieves among them.",
  4056:
      "On the Day of Judgment, We will enter those who disbelieve in Our verses into a fire that will completely encircle them. Whenever their skins have been charred, We will replace them with another so that the punishment is perpetual for them. Allah is All-Mighty, and nothing can contend with Him. He is All-Wise in what He arranges and determines.",
  4057:
      "On the Day of Judgment, We will admit into gardens with rivers flowing beneath their palaces those who believe in Allah, follow His messengers, and perform acts of obedience. They will reside in them forever. In these gardens, they will have spouses purified from all defilement, and We will admit them into expansive refreshing shade wherein there is neither heat nor cold.",
  4058:
      "Allah commands you, O believers, to reunite everything entrusted to you with their owners. He commands that you be just when judging between people and not be biased and oppressive regarding Allah's laws. How excellent is that with which Allah reminds you and that to which He guides you in all of your conditions! Allah is All-Hearing concerning your statements and All-Seeing about your actions.",
  4059:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, obey Allah and obey His Messenger by doing what he commands and staying away from what he prohibits. Obey those entrusted with your affairs as long as they do not order you to commit disobedience [of Islamic law]. If you disagree about something, refer it to Allah's Book and the Sunnah of His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم if you believe in Allah and the Last Day. Referring to the Book and the Sunnah is better than persisting in disagreements and holding onto mere opinions. They will also bring about the best result for you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the biggest reasons for the disbelief of the People of the Scripture is their envy of the believers because of the prophethood and the establishment on earth which Allah has blessed them with.\n2. The sacred law establishes a duty to look after things that are put in your care, and to return them to the people who own them.\n3. Humankind must judge between people with justice, because they are prohibited from oppression and injustice.\n4. Allah has made it a duty to follow those in authority as long as they do not instruct disobedience, and to refer to the judgement of Allah and His Messenger, for this necessitates true faith.",
  4060:
      "Have you not seen, O Messenger, the hypocrites among the Jews contradicting one another, falsely claiming that they believe in what was sent down to you and what was sent down to the Messengers before you? They want to judge their disputes not by what Allah has legislated but by what man has fabricated. They had already been commanded to disbelieve in such things. The Devil wants to lead them far away from the truth and that they not be guided along with it.",
  4061:
      "If these hypocrites are told, 'Come to the law that Allah has sent down in His Book, and to the Messenger to judge between you in your claims against one another,' you will see them, O Messenger, turning completely away from you for someone else to judge.",
  4062:
      "How will the hypocrites' situation be when calamities befall them because of the sins they committed? Then, they will come to you, O Messenger, making excuses to you, swearing by Allah: We did not intend by choosing someone else to judge between us except to bring about the best result and reconciliation for the feuding parties. They are lying about that. The best result is in resorting to the judgment of Allah's law between His slaves.",
  4063:
      "Allah knows what hypocrisy and ulterior motives these people hide in their hearts. So, leave them alone, O Messenger, turn away from them, and make clear the laws of Allah through exhortation and admonishment. Tell them deeply profound, grave words that will penetrate their souls.",
  4064:
      "We have not sent a Messenger except for him to be followed in what he commands by Allah's will and His discretion. When they wronged themselves through disobedience, if they had come to you, O Messenger, during your lifetime, confessing what they had done, regretful, repentant, and seeking forgiveness from Allah, and you had asked for forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah forgiving and merciful with them.",
  4065:
      "The situation is not as these hypocrites claim. Allah swore by His Self, may He be Exalted, that they will not truly believe until they refer judgment in every disagreement between them to the Messenger during his lifetime and to his legislation after his death. Then, they are happy with the Messenger's ruling without feeling anxiety or doubt about it, and they submit entirely to it, with external and internal submission.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Seeking a decision not from the law of Allah, while being happy with it, goes against having faith in Allah.\n2. One of the most notable characteristics of the hypocrites is their lack of satisfaction with the law of Allah, and their giving priority to the judgement of false Allahs over the judgement of Allah.\n3. The believers are ordered to turn away from the people of ignorance and delusions and exhorted to be mindful of Allah.\n4. Complete faith is only with turning for a decision to the sacred law, with satisfaction of the heart and outside and inside acceptance of what the sacred law rules.",
  4066:
      "If We had obligated them to kill each other or to depart from their homes, no one would have obeyed Our command except a small number. So, they should be grateful to Allah for not imposing what would be difficult for them. If they had done what was mentioned out of obedience to Allah, it would have been better than the contrary and stronger in firming up their faith. We would have granted them an immense reward and guided them to the path that leads to Allah and His Paradise.",
  4067:
      "If We had obligated them to kill each other or to depart from their homes, no one would have obeyed Our command except a small number. So, they should be grateful to Allah for not imposing what would be difficult for them. If they had done what was mentioned out of obedience to Allah, it would have been better than the contrary and stronger in firming up their faith. We would have granted them an immense reward and guided them to the path that leads to Allah and His Paradise.",
  4068:
      "If We had obligated them to kill each other or to depart from their homes, no one would have obeyed Our command except a small number. So, they should be grateful to Allah for not imposing what would be difficult for them. If they had done what was mentioned out of obedience to Allah, it would have been better than the contrary and stronger in firming up their faith. We would have granted them an immense reward and guided them to the path that leads to Allah and His Paradise.",
  4069:
      "Those who obey Allah and the Messenger will be with the Prophets and truthful ones whom Allah has blessed with entry into Paradise. They are the ones who had complete faith in what the Messengers came with, and they acted upon it. They will also be with the martyrs who were killed in Allah's path and the righteous who rectified their external and internal states and, thus, their actions were righteous. What excellent companions these are in Paradise!",
  4070:
      "That reward mentioned is Allah's favor upon His slaves. Allah is All-Knowing regarding their circumstances and will reward each of them according to his actions.",
  4071:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, be on guard against your enemies by adopting the means to help you fight them. Go out to fight them one group after another and go out altogether. Each manner of going out should be done according to what is in your best interests and whatever entails defeat for your enemies.",
  4072:
      "There are among you, O Muslims, some people who procrastinate going out to fight your enemies because of their cowardice. They also try to delay others. They are hypocrites and weak in faith. If death or defeat happens among you, one of them says while happy that he is safe: Allah has favored me! Thus, I was not there to fight alongside them. Otherwise, what befell them would have happened to me.",
  4073:
      "If Allah's favor through victory and spoils of war happen to you, O Muslims, this person who stayed behind from fighting will say, as if not one of you and as if there was neither friendship nor affinity between you and him: If only I were with them in that fighting! Then, I would have had the great victory that they enjoyed.",
  4074:
      "Let the truthful believers – who sell the life of this world in exchange for the Afterlife, desiring the Afterlife more than the goods of this world – fight in the path of Allah so that Allah's Word is supreme. Anyone who fights in the path of Allah so that His Word is supreme, whether he is killed as a martyr or defeats His enemy and is victorious, Allah will give him a great reward: Paradise and the pleasure of Allah. \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The law of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is based on ease and people are not responsible for doing more than they are able to do.\n2. The reward of obeying Allah and His Messenger is getting the companionship of the prophets, the devout, the martyrs and the righteous in Paradise.\n3. The duty to take precaution and care in all matters and hence making all appropriate preparation to fight the enemy.\n4. The verses contain a warning against being slow to engage in sacred struggle or opposing such a duty, because sacred struggle is the greatest of reasons for Muslims being strengthened and prevents the enemy from overpowering them.",
  4075:
      "What is preventing you, O believers, from fighting in the path of Allah to raise His Word high and rescue the weak men, women, and children who call to Allah, saying: O Lord of ours! Take us out of Mecca because of the oppression of its people who associate partners with Allah and are hostile toward His slaves. Appoint us someone near to You with whom we can entrust leadership and protection of our affairs and appoint a helper to defend us from harm.",
  4076:
      "The truthful believers fight in the path of Allah to raise His Word high. On the other hand, the disbelievers fight in the path and way of their deities. So, fight the supporters of the Devil. If you fight them, you will defeat them because the Devil's strategy is weak, and it cannot harm those who place their complete trust in Allah, the Exalted.",
  4077:
      "O Messenger, do you not know about the condition of some of your Companions who asked that striving in Allah's path be ordained for them, but they were told: Hold back from fighting, establish the prayer, and give Zakat (obligatory alms). That was before fighting in Allah's path was obligated. Islam became strong when they migrated to Medina, and fighting was obligated. Some of them found it difficult and began fearing people as they should fear Allah or even more so. They said: O our Lord! Why did You obligate fighting for us? Why did You not delay it for a while so we could enjoy the worldly life? Say to them, O Messenger: The enjoyment of the world, no matter how much, is insignificant and vanishing. Meanwhile, the Hereafter is better for the one who fears Allah, the Exalted, because its delights are everlasting. Your righteous deeds will not be reduced, not even the amount of the thread on a date stone.",
  4078:
      "At any time and place, death will surely come to you when you reach your prescribed life term, even if you are in guarded palaces far from battle. And when these hypocrites receive something pleasing, such as a child or wealth, they say: This is from Allah. Yet when they face difficulty concerning their children or wealth, they attribute a bad sign and misfortune to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and say: This evil is because of you. Say, O Messenger, in response to these people: Everything, good or evil, occurs by Allah's decree and decision. What is the matter with these people who say such things and hardly understand anything you tell them?",
  4079:
      "O child of Adam: Any good that reaches you, regarding your wealth and children, is from Allah's favor upon you. Whatever evil reaches you, regarding your wealth and children, is from yourself because of the disobedient acts you committed. We have sent you, O Prophet, as a messenger from Allah to all people to communicate the message of your Lord. Allah is enough of a witness to the truth of what you communicate from Him because of the evidence and clear proofs He has given you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The sacred law has made it a duty to fight in order to raise the Word of Allah and to help the oppressed; and rebukes fear, cowardice, and opposition to the laws of Allah.\n2. The Afterlife is better than this world and what is in it, in terms of material things and desires, for whoever is mindful of Allah and obeys Allah.\n3. No matter how people try to protect themselves, the means of death will find them, even if they are in the strongest of fortresses.\n4. Good and evil is all according to the decree of Allah, and Allah may test His servants with some evil in this world for different reasons, such as sins and disobedience.",
  4080:
      "Whoever obeys the Messenger by complying with his commands and avoiding what he prohibits has fulfilled Allah's command. Whoever turns away from obeying you, O Messenger, do not feel sad about him because I have not sent you as a sentinel to watch over his actions. We are the Ones Who will watch his actions and take him into account.",
  4081:
      "The hypocrites say to you with their mouths: We will obey your commands and comply with them. Then, when they leave you, they secretly plan the opposite of what they said to you. Allah knows what they are planning, and He will requite them for their deception. So, do not pay any attention to them, as they will not harm you at all. Consign your affairs to Allah and rely on Him alone. Allah suffices you as one to entrust and rely upon.",
  4082:
      "Why do these people not reflect on the Quran and study it until it is proven to them that no contradictions or inconsistency can be found in it!? They should do so until they know the truth with which you arrived. Had it been from anyone other than Allah, the Exalted, indeed, they would have found inconsistencies in its rulings and many contradictions in its meanings.",
  4083:
      "Whenever these hypocrites happen upon a matter dealing with the safety of Muslims, their private affairs, or issues of fear and sadness, they rush to spread it. If they had waited and referred the matter to Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and to the possessors of critical thinking, knowledge, and counsel, they would have understood and investigated what should be done concerning spreading such news or concealing it. If it were not for Allah's favoring you with Islam and His having mercy on you with the Quran, O believers, and thus, protecting you from what these hypocrites were afflicted with, all except a few of you would have followed the whispers of the Devil.",
  4084:
      "Fight, O Prophet, in Allah's path to raise His Word high. You will not be questioned about or held accountable for others. You are only responsible for prompting yourself to fight, exhorting, and urging the believers to do so. Perhaps Allah will repel the might of the disbelievers by your fighting. Allah is stronger in might and more severe in punishment.",
  4085:
      "Whoever strives to direct another person towards some evil will receive a share of the sin. Allah is a witness to everything a person does, and He will requite them for it. So, whoever among you is a vehicle for achieving some good will receive a share and a portion of it. Whoever is a vehicle for achieving evil, some part of it will reach him.",
  4086:
      "When anyone offers a greeting of peace to you, then respond to him with something better than what he offered or return a similar greeting. To respond with something better is more virtuous. Allah keeps watch over what you do, and He will requite each person for his actions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Reflecting over the noble Qur’an creates certainty of its being Allah’s revelation, because it is free of inconsistencies and the superiority of its laws will become clear.\n2. It is unlawful to spread news that creates instability to the security of the Muslims or spread fear amongst them.\n3. Discussions about the affairs of the Muslims and related public matters must be done by people of knowledge and those in authority.\n4. It is recommended to make a good intercession that does not contain any sin or infringement on the rights of people; and it is prohibited to make any intercession which contains sin or oppression.",
  4087:
      "Allah—there is nothing rightfully worshiped except Him. Verily, He will gather together on the Day of Resurrection, the first and last of you, a day about which there is no doubt. This is to recompense you for your actions. There is no one more truthful in speech than Allah.",
  4088:
      "What is the matter with you, O believers, that you have become two groups differing over how to deal with the hypocrites? One group wants to fight against them because of their disbelief, and another group wants to leave them because of their belief. You should not differ over them, for Allah has returned them to disbelief and misguidance because of their actions. Do you wish to guide those Allah has not guided to the truth? Whoever Allah misguides, you will never find a road toward guidance for him.",
  4089:
      "The hypocrites wish that you would disbelieve in what was sent down to you as they have disbelieved. They want you to be equal with them in disbelief. Due to their animosity, do not take them as allies until they migrate in Allah's path from the land of polytheism to the land of Islam- as proof of their belief. If they turn away and persist upon their condition, seize and kill them wherever you find them. Do not take any allies from among them to support you with your affairs, nor anyone to assist you against your enemies.",
  4090:
      "Except for those who reach people with whom you have a peace treaty or those who come to you reluctant to fight against you or their people. If Allah wanted, He could have made them stronger than you, and they would have fought you. Therefore, accept Allah's protection and do not set out to kill or capture them. If they withdraw without fighting and yield to you peacefully, giving up the fight against you, then Allah has not provided you a way to fight or take them as prisoners.",
  4091:
      "You, O believers, will find another group of hypocrites exhibiting faith to you to protect themselves. When they return to their people who are disbelievers, they exhibit disbelief to them in order to be safe from them as well. They fall head first into it whenever they are invited to disbelief in Allah and polytheism. If these people do not give up fighting you and come to you peacefully, restraining themselves, then seize and kill them wherever you find them. We have provided you with clear proof for seizing and fighting the people fitting this description because of their betrayal and deception.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The occurrence of the Final Hour and the ressurection after death is the truth in which there is no doubt. It is Allah’s true promise.\n2. The verses explain how to deal with hypocrites according to the situation and what is best.\n3. Migration in Allah’s path is one of the most noticeable features of the believers and displays the reality of their faith.\n4. Striving in Allah’s path will expose the hypocrites, as they will try to make excuses to remain behind.",
  4092:
      "A believer ought not to kill another believer unless by mistake. Whoever kills a believer by mistake must free a believing slave as an expiation for his actions. The inheritors of the killer are responsible for paying blood money to the inheritors of the victim unless they forgo that right. If the victim was a believer and belonged to a people at war with you, the killer must free a believing slave, and no blood money is owed. Suppose the victim was not a believer and he belonged to a people living in an Islamic state under a covenant of protection. In that case, the inheritors of the killer are responsible for paying blood money to the inheritors of the victim, and the killer must free a believing slave as an expiation for his action. If he cannot find anyone to free or afford to pay the cost, he must fast continuously for two consecutive months so that Allah may forgive him for what he has done. Allah is All-Knowing about the actions and intentions of His slaves, and He is All-Wise in His legislation and planning.",
  4093:
      "Whoever intentionally kills a believer without right, his requital is to enter Hell eternally. Allah's anger is upon him. He removes His mercy from him and prepares a severe punishment for him because of his commission of a heinous crime.",
  4094:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, when you go out to fight in Allah's path, be sure about the affair of those you fight. Do not tell someone who proves he is a believer: You are not a believer! You only displayed Islam out of fear for your blood and wealth. Then, you kill him in pursuit of worldly life's trivial, material goods, such as the spoils of war. Allah possesses abundant spoils that are greater than this. In the past, you were like this person who hid his faith from his people. Then Allah favored you with Islam and protected your blood. So be sure, as none of your actions are hidden from Allah. Even if it is minuscule, He will recompense you for it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an declares the sanctity of a believer’s life and prohibits violation of it, with a warning of the most severe punishment for such a crime.\n2. The person who kills a believer by mistake will have to make amends by freeing a believing slave and paying monetary compensation to the successors of the victim.\n3. Allah, in His sacred law, has given a victim’s successors the right to pardon a killer and give up the blood money.\n4. It is necessary to be careful when fighting and not to be hasty in judging people - in order to ensure that an innocent person is not attacked.\n5. When making a judgement about people, their outside appearance is accepted and given preference. If a person pronounces their acceptance of Islam, this must be accepted and he must be treated as a believer. His inside condition should be left for Allah to judge.",
  4095:
      "Those believers who remain behind from fighting in Allah's path – besides those who have an excuse, such as sickness and the blind – are not equal to those who fight in Allah's path, giving their wealth and lives. Allah has favored those who fight in His path a rank above those who remain behind. Those who fight and stay behind with a valid excuse shall receive the reward they deserve. Allah has preferred those who fight over those who stay behind by giving them a greater reward.",
  4096:
      "This reward is in levels, some above others, with forgiveness of their sins and mercy. Allah is Ever-Forgiving and Merciful with them.",
  4097:
      "When angels take the souls of those who wronged themselves by not migrating from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam, at the time of grasping hold of their souls, the angels will say in rebuke of them: What condition were you in and in what way were you distinguished from the polytheists? They will reply, presenting the excuse: We were weak, having no power nor might to defend ourselves. The angels will again rebuke them, saying: Were the lands of Allah not spacious enough for you to depart for in order to secure your religion and lives from humiliation and domination? The Fire is the abode in which those who do not migrate will settle down. What an evil place of return it will be for them!",
  4098:
      "Exempted from this warning are the weak men, women, and children with an excuse. They had no power to defend themselves from oppression and subjugation. They could not discover a path to free themselves from their subjugation. Perhaps Allah will pardon such people through His mercy and benevolence. Allah is Ever-Pardoning of His slaves and Oft-Forgiving of whoever repents among them.",
  4099:
      "Exempted from this warning are the weak men, women, and children with an excuse. They had no power to defend themselves from oppression and subjugation. They could not discover a path to free themselves from their subjugation. Perhaps Allah will pardon such people through His mercy and benevolence. Allah is Ever-Pardoning of His slaves and Oft-Forgiving of whoever repents among them.",
  4100:
      "After mentioning the threat of punishment for abandoning the hijra (emigration from Mecca to Medina) despite having the capability to do so, Allah encourages them to do it, stating: \n Whoever emigrates from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam, seeking Allah's pleasure, will find a place altered and different than the land they left behind. In this new land, they will acquire honor and ample provision. Whoever leaves his home as a migrant to Allah and His Messenger and death arrives before reaching the land he was migrating to, his reward is certain with Allah. It will not be held against him if he was unable to reach the land he was emigrating to. Allah is Ever-Forgiving and Merciful to whoever repents among His slaves.",
  4101:
      "When you travel in the land, there is no sin in shortening the four-unit prayer to a two-unit prayer if you fear harm from disbelievers will befall you. Indeed, the disbelievers have open, apparent animosity towards you. The permissibility of shortening the prayer while traveling in a state of safety is established by authentic Sunnah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the superiority of striving in Allah’s path and the great reward that those who do so will be given, having been exclusively promised high ranks in Paradise.\n2. Those with reasonable excuses are not required to strive in Allah’s path; yet they will receive a reward based on their good intentions.\n3. The verses show the virtue of migrating to an Islamic land and its necessity for those who are able to do so and who fear for their religion in their homeland.\n4. The prayer may be shortened when travelling.",
  4102:
      "When you, O Messenger, are in the army at the time of fighting the enemy, and you wish to pray with them, then divide the army into two groups: one group should stand and pray with you, keeping their weapons with them during the prayer; while the other group guards you. When the first group has completed one unit of prayer with the leader, they must complete the rest on their own. So, when they finish praying, they will be behind you, facing the enemy. After the first group finishes one unit of prayer, the group keeping guard who has not prayed should come and pray one unit of prayer with the leader. When the leader completes the prayer by sending peace and mercy, they should complete the remainder of it. They should take precautions with their enemy and keep their weapons with them. The disbelievers wish that you become unmindful of your weapons and supplies when you pray, so they can all attack you at once while you are heedless. There is no sin on you to not carry your weapons when harm strikes because of heavy rain, illness, and the like. However, be cautious with the enemy as much as possible. Allah has prepared for disbelievers a humiliating punishment.",
  4103:
      "When you, O believers, have finished the prayer, remember Allah in all circumstances by exalting Him, thanking Him, and declaring His Oneness while standing, sitting, or lying on your sides. When fear subsides, and you are safe, establish the prayer with its pillars, obligations, and recommended acts, as commanded of you. Prayer is an obligation for believers restricted to particular times, and delaying them without an excuse is not permissible. This applies while at home. However, you are allowed to combine and shorten prayers while traveling.",
  4104:
      "Do not slacken or become idle, O believers, in pursuit of your enemy among the Disbelievers. If you suffer because of the death and injuries that afflict you, then they, too, are suffering just like you, and what afflicts you also afflicts them. Their patience cannot be greater than yours because you have hope in Allah's reward, help, and approval, which they have no hope for. Allah is All-Knowing about the conditions of His slaves and All-Wise in His planning and legislation.",
  4105:
      "I have sent down the Quran to you, O Messenger, containing the truth so that you can settle all matters between the people following what Allah has taught and inspired you with, not with your inclinations and thoughts. Do not defend those who betray their own selves and their promises, deterring someone from seeking his rights from them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verse describes the manner and rules relating to prayer at the time of fear (salat Al-khawf).\n2. A believer is instructed to adopt normal worldly means in all circumstances, and is not excused from doing so even at the time of worship.\n3. A person should remember Allah at all times, as this gives life to the heart and brings spiritual tranquility.\n4. Prayer must be established at its set times without any delay.\n5. It is prohibited to show weakness and laziness when fighting the enemy and it is necessary to be patient at this time.",
  4106:
      "Seek forgiveness and pardon from Allah. Allah is Oft-Forgiving and Merciful towards His slaves who repent to Him.",
  4107:
      "Do not argue on behalf of a person who betrays and exaggerates in concealing his deception. Allah does not like these deceitful liars.",
  4108:
      "When perpetrating acts of disobedience, they hide from people out of fear and shame, but they cannot hide from Allah. He is with them through His knowledge of them. Nothing about them is hidden from Him when they secretly plan to say things He is not pleased with, such as defending a sinner or falsely accusing an innocent person. Allah is well aware of what they do secretly and openly. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will requite them for their actions.",
  4109:
      "Here you are, O people concerned with these people who commit an offense, arguing on their behalf regarding worldly life to prove their innocence and defend them from punishment. Who will argue on their behalf with Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He knows their true status? Who will be their representative on that day? Without a doubt, no one will be able to do that.",
  4110:
      "Whoever commits an evil act or wrongs himself by perpetrating disobedience then seeks forgiveness from Allah, admitting his sin, remorseful over it, abandoning it- he will find Allah Ever-Forgiving towards his sins and merciful with him.",
  4111:
      "The punishment for whoever commits a minor or major sin is on him alone. He cannot transfer it to someone else. Allah is All-Knowing about the slaves' actions and All-Wise in His planning and legislation.",
  4112:
      "If a person makes a mistake or commits a sin intentionally, then accuses an innocent person of that sin, he has taken a grave lie and a clear sin upon himself.",
  4113:
      "If not for Allah's favor of protecting you, O Messenger, from this group of people who deceive themselves and their determination to mislead you about the truth, you would have passed an unfair judgment. In reality, they only mislead themselves. The punishment for what they perpetrated in attempting to misdirect [blame] is returning against them. Allah sent down the Quran and Sunna to you, and He taught you the right guidance and light, which you did not know beforehand. Allah's favor upon you, in the form of prophethood and protection, is tremendous.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is prohibited to defend and argue for those in the wrong, because that amounts to assisting them in sin and oppression.\n2. The true believer should fear, respect and be ashamed before Allah more than he is before anyone else.\n3. Allah’s mercy and forgiveness is open to the person who wrongs himself, no matter what he did, if he is sincere in his repentance and he leaves the sin.\n4. The verse warns against accusing an innocent person of a crime he did not commit and tells us that the person who does so is guilty of a serious lie and sin.",
  4114:
      "There is no good or benefit in the majority of discourse that people secretly partake in unless it is to urge voluntary charity, a good deed introduced by divine law and verified by the intellect, or to call for reconciliation between disputing parties. Whoever does that, seeking Allah's pleasure, We will give him a magnificent reward.",
  4115:
      "Whoever opposes and contradicts what the Messenger has brought after the truth is made clear to him and follows a way other than that of the believers, We will abandon them to what he has chosen for himself. We will not lead him to the truth because he deliberately turns away. We will enter them into the Fire to suffer in its heat. What an evil retreat for its people!",
  4116:
      "Allah does not forgive that a partner be associated with Him. Rather, the polytheist will reside eternally in the Fire. Through His mercy and favor, He may forgive whomever He wills for anything aside from polytheism. Whoever associates a partner with Allah has completely lost his way and strayed far from the truth, as he has made the creation equal with the Creator.",
  4117:
      "These polytheists do not worship and call upon anything alongside Allah except false idols assigned female names like al-Lāt and al-'Uzzā. There is neither benefit nor harm attributable to them. In reality, they only worship a devil with no good in him, who rebelled against his Lord. It is he who commands them to worship false idols.",
  4118:
      "Due to that, Allah removed the Devil from His mercy. The Devil then said to his Lord: I will surely appoint for myself a certain portion of Your slaves to mislead from the truth.",
  4119:
      "[The Devil said]: I will obstruct them from Your straight path and give them hopes with false promises that will beautify their misguidance. I will order them [to invent customs in dedication to false idols], like cutting the ears of cattle to forbid what Allah has made lawful. I will command them to alter Allah's creation and its natural disposition. Whoever takes him as an ally, entrusting and obeying him, has suffered a manifest loss through loyalty to the Devil, the accursed.",
  4120:
      "The Devil makes false promises and gives them false hopes. In fact, he does not promise them but falsehood for which there is no reality.",
  4121:
      "The residence of those who follow the footsteps and dictates of the Devil is the Fire, from which they will find no sanctuary to escape it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There is no good in most private discussions held by people, which often consist of sin, with very little discussion about goodness and generosity.\n2. The end result of opposition to the Messenger (peace be upon him) and going against the way of the believers is being distanced from Allah and entering Hell.\n3. Every sin, depending on Allah’s will, may be forgiven, besides the sin of associating partners with Allah, which Allah will never forgive if one did not repent from it in the wordly life.\n4. Satan’s goal is to turn people away from the worship of Allah. One of his main methods of doing this is to make falsehood seem attractive by deceptive hopes and false promises.",
  4122:
      "After mentioning the recompense for those who followed the Devil, Allah notes the reward of those who followed the messengers, stating: \n We will admit those who have faith in Allah and do righteous acts that bring them close to Him into gardens with streams flowing beneath its palaces, where they will live eternally. This is a promise from Allah, and His promise is true. He does not break promises, and no one is truer than Allah in terms of speech.",
  4123:
      "The issue of salvation and success, O Muslims, is not dependent on what you or the People of the Book hope and wish for. Rather, it is dependent on actions. Whoever among you does an evil act will be repaid for it on the Day of Judgment. He will not find any protector to bring any benefit nor any helper to repel harm from him.",
  4124:
      "Any person, male or female, who does righteous actions and is a true believer in Allah, the Exalted, thereby combining faith and action, will enter Paradise. The reward of their efforts will not be reduced in the least, not even to the extent of a speck on a date stone.",
  4125:
      "No one is more excellent in religion than the one who surrenders to Allah outwardly and inwardly, sincere in his intentions for His sake, excelling in his actions by following what He legislated and following the religion of Abraham, which forms the basis of the religion of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. He turns away from polytheism and disbelief towards monotheism and faith. Allah chose His Prophet Abraham (peace be upon him) for complete love from among all of His creation.",
  4126:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of everything in the heavens and the earth. With His knowledge, power, and planning, Allah surrounds everything in His creation.",
  4127:
      "They ask you, O Messenger, about the rights and duties of women. Say: Allah clarifies what you have asked about and what is recited to you in the Quran concerning orphan girls in your care, to whom you do not give their dowry and inheritance as Allah has obligated. You do not wish to marry them, yet you prevent them from marrying because of your greed for their wealth. He also clarifies that your obligation concerning helpless minor children is to give them their due right from the inheritance and not wrong them by confiscating their wealth. He clarifies your obligation of being just towards orphans and looking after their best interests in terms of the worldly and Afterlife. Allah knows of any good you do for orphans and others, and He will repay you for it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The reward that is with Allah cannot be achieved by simple hopes and claims. Instead, a person must have faith and do good actions.\n2. Rewards and recompense are linked to the action: if a person does evil, he will be requited for it. However if a person does good, he will be given something better as a reward.\n3. The test for the acceptance of actions with Allah is sincerity and following the sacred law.\n4. Islam has given great importance to the rights of weak groups, such as women and minors. It has prohibited infringing on such rights and made it a duty to give consideration to the interests of such individuals in the light of the laws it has set-down.",
  4128:
      "If a woman fears disdain and a loss of desire from her husband, there is no sin in reaching a compromise where the woman gives up some of the rights owed to her, such as maintenance and spending the night together. Reconciliation is better for both of them than divorce. People have a natural tendency towards greed and miserliness. So, they are not keen on giving up rights owed to them. Therefore, spouses should cure this behavior by cultivating tolerance and benevolence. If you achieve excellent conduct in all your affairs and fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding what He prohibits, then Allah is All-Aware of what you do. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will repay you for it.",
  4129:
      "You, O husbands, will not be able to be entirely just towards your wives concerning inclinations of the heart, even if you aspire to that. This may be due to circumstances and factors beyond your control. So do not disincline too far away from the one you do not love and leave her hanging suspended to the point where she does not have a husband to fulfill her rights, nor is she unmarried so that she may marry someone else. If you make right what is between you by pushing yourselves to not insist on having things your way, giving the wife her due rights, and fearing Allah concerning her, then Allah is Ever-Forgiving and Merciful with you.",
  4130:
      "If a couple should separate by divorce or annulment, then Allah will suffice both through His vast Bounty: He will suffice the man with a wife better than her, and He will suffice the woman with a husband better than him. Allah's favor and mercy are vast. He is All-Wise in His planning and assessment.",
  4131:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of everything in the heavens, the earth, and all that is between them. We struck a covenant with the People of the Book among the Jews and Christians, and We struck a covenant with you to fulfill Allah's commands and avoid what He has prohibited. If you denied this covenant, you would only harm yourselves. Allah does not need your obedience because He has dominion over everything in the heavens and earth. He is in no need of any of His creation. He is worthy of praise for all His attributes and actions.",
  4132:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of everything in the heavens and the earth, and He deserves to be obeyed. Allah is sufficient for arranging all the affairs of His creation.",
  4133:
      "If He wills, He can destroy you, O people, and bring others besides you who will obey Allah and not disobey Him. Allah is fully capable of doing that.",
  4134:
      "Whoever among you, O people, only wishes to gain the reward of this worldly life by his actions should know that with Allah is the reward of the worldly life and Afterlife. He should seek the reward of both from Him. Allah is All-Hearing concerning your statements and All-Seeing concerning your actions. He will repay you for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is recommended that reconciliation be reached between a married couple who are in dispute. This should be done by giving up some rights in order to maintain the marriage bond.\n2. Allah has ordered the husband with more than one wife to be fair between his wives, especially in material things which are within the husband’s control. However, the sacred law overlooks those non-material things in which fairness is not possible, such as love and inclination.\n3. There is no harm if a couple separate when it is no longer possible to live together.\n4. A comprehensive piece of advice to humankind - every single one of them - is to be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  4135:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, stand up for justice in all circumstances: testify to the truth concerning every person, even if that requires the truth to be proven against yourself, your parents, or close relatives. Do not be motivated to give or withhold testimony due to anyone's poverty or wealth. Allah knows best what is in the interest of the poor and wealthy among you. Do not follow your whims in testimony, lest you deviate from the truth. If you falsify testimony by giving it inaccurately or refuse to provide it, then Allah is All-Aware of what you are doing.",
  4136:
      "O you who believe, be firm in your faith in Allah, His Messenger, the Quran which He sent down to His Messenger, and the books He revealed to the messengers before him. Whoever disbelieves in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Day of Judgment has strayed far from the straight path.",
  4137:
      "Those who repeatedly disbelieve after accepting faith – by entering into the faith, then leaving it, entering into it again, then leaving again, and so on – and then insist on disbelief until they die upon it, Allah will not forgive their sins and nor will He lead them to the straight path that leads to Him.",
  4138:
      "O Prophet, announce to the hypocrites who manifest faith externally and hide disbelief internally that Allah has a tormenting punishment for them on the Day of Judgment.",
  4139:
      "This punishment is because they took disbelievers as helpers and supporters instead of believers. How astonishing is that which made them take disbelievers as allies?! Were they seeking power and strength by which to advance? All power and strength belong to Allah.",
  4140:
      "Allah has already sent down to you, O believers, in the noble Quran that if you sit in a gathering and you hear someone disbelieving in Allah's verses, making fun of them, then you are obligated to get up and leave their gathering until they begin speaking about something other than disbelief in Allah's verses and making fun of it. If you sit with them after hearing them disbelieve in and mock Allah's verses, then you are like them in opposing Allah's command. This is because you disobeyed Allah by sitting with them just as they disobeyed Him by their disbelief. Surely, Allah will gather the hypocrites who exhibit Islam but hide disbelief and the disbelievers together in the Fire on the Day of Judgment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is necessary to be just when passing judgement between people and when giving testimony, even if the right is owed by the person himself or any of his relatives.\n2. A believer must work hard to do actions with his heart and limbs that will increase his faith and make it firm in his heart.\n3. The verses show the great danger that the hypocrites pose to Islam and the Muslims. It is for this reason that Allah has warned them of the most severe punishment in the Afterlife.\n4. If a believer is not able to refute a person who speaks against Allah’s words and the sacred law, he is not permitted to remain sitting with such a person.",
  4141:
      "Those who wait in anticipation to see whether good or evil happens to you will say if Allah gives you victory and spoils of war: Were we not alongside you, witnessing what you saw? That is to obtain some spoils of war. If the disbelievers have some success, they say to them: Did we not protect you and defend you against the believers by assisting you instead of them? Allah will judge between all of you on the Day of Judgment, rewarding the believers by admitting them into Paradise and repaying the hypocrites by entering them to the lowest depths of the Fire. Allah, by His favor, will never provide the disbelievers with proof against the believers on the Day of Judgment.",
  4142:
      "The hypocrites try to deceive Allah by exhibiting Islam on the outside while hiding disbelief. Allah deceives them because He protects their lives despite knowing about their disbelief. In the Afterlife, He has prepared the most severe punishment for them. When they stand for prayer, they do so lazily, with reluctance. They only remember Allah a little when they see the believers.",
  4143:
      "These hypocrites are wavering in confusion. Outwardly and inwardly, they are neither with the believers nor the disbelievers. On the outside, they are with the believers; inside, they are with the disbelievers. You, O Messenger, will never find a way to lead out of misguidance whomever Allah misguides.",
  4144:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not take those who disbelieve in Allah as close friends, taking them as allies instead of believers. By doing so, do you wish to give Allah clear evidence against you, proving that you deserve punishment?!",
  4145:
      "Allah will place the hypocrites in the lowest place in the Fire on the Day of Judgment. You will never find any helper to defend them against the punishment.",
  4146:
      "Except for those who return to Allah repenting from their hypocrisy, rectifying themselves internally, holding firmly to Allah's covenant, performing their actions sincerely for Him, without showing off- those described with these characteristics will be with the believers in this worldly life and the Afterlife. Allah will give the believers a considerable reward.",
  4147:
      "There is no need for Allah to punish you if you are thankful to Him and believe. He is the One who is Kind and Merciful. He only punishes you for your sins. If you rectify your actions, you are thankful to Him for His favors and believe in Him both outwardly and inwardly, He will never punish you. Allah is Ever-Grateful to the person who acknowledges His favors, and the reward for them is abundant. He is All-Knowing regarding the faith of His creation and will requite every person for his actions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses describe the attributes of the hypocrites, such as their greed for their share, whether it is with the believers or the disbelievers.\n2. One of the main characteristic of the hypocrites is their wandering and confusion as regards to Faith. In reality, they are neither with the believers, nor the disbelievers.\n3. The verses strongly prohibit taking disbelievers as friends instead of believers.\n4. Having faith and doing good actions is the best means by which a person can save himself from Allah’s punishment in the Afterlife.",
  4148:
      "Allah does not like evil words to be said in public. Rather, He hates it and threatens to punish it. However, if someone has been wronged, he may mention the evil words to complain about who wronged him and to supplicate against him. But it is better for the person who is wronged to be patient instead of mentioning such evil. Allah hears what you say and knows your intentions, so beware of saying or intending any evil.",
  4149:
      "Whether you make your good deeds known, keep them secret, or overlook someone who acted negatively towards you, Allah is eternally Pardoning and Powerful. Therefore, have a pardoning character so that Allah may pardon you.",
  4150:
      "Indeed, there are those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers, and who want to make a distinction between Allah and His messengers by believing in Allah yet rejecting His messengers by saying, 'We accept some messengers and reject others'. They want to take a path between disbelief and belief, but are severely deluded in thinking that this will save them.",
  4151:
      "Those who that do that are, in fact, disbelievers because whoever disbelieves in the messengers, or some of them, has actually disbelieved in Allah and all of His messengers. We have prepared a humiliating torment for disbelievers on The Day of Resurrection as a punishment for their refusal to have faith in Allah and His messengers.",
  4152:
      "Upon mentioning the recompense for the disbelievers, Allah subsequently notes the recompense for the believers, stating: \n As for those who have faith in Allah, worship Him alone, do not make any partners with Him, and believe in all His messengers without distinguishing between them as the disbelievers do, Allah will reward them tremendously for their belief and the righteous deeds they do based on that belief. Allah is always forgiving and merciful to His repenting slaves.",
  4153:
      "O Messenger, the Jews ask you to bring them a complete book from the sky, just like what happened to Moses, to prove that you are telling the truth. Do not be surprised by them, as their ancestors asked Moses for much greater than that when they asked him to show them Allah. They were then struck by a thunderbolt as a punishment for their actions and brought back to life. Then, they worshipped the calf instead of Allah even after receiving clear evidence that Allah is One, the only Lord of everything and the only One worthy of worship. Then, we forgave them and gave Moses clear evidence against his people.",
  4154:
      "To take a solemn pledge from them, frighten them, and make them carry out its stipulations, We raised the mountain over them and said to them: Enter the gate of Jerusalem prostrating by bowing your heads. However, they entered by dragging their behinds on the floor. We also told them: Do not disobey me by fishing on the Sabbath. Despite this, they rebelled and did what We commanded them not to do. We took a firm and solemn pledge from them regarding this, but they broke it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A person who is wronged may speak about the wrong and the person who wronged him to someone who can help him get his right, even if this means saying something the wrongdoer will not like.\n2. It is better for a person who is wronged to have patience instead of speaking about the wrong. The reward for this will be Allah’s forgiveness.\n3. It is not permissible to make a distinction between the messengers by having faith in some and not others. Instead, it is necessary to accept all of them.\n4. The verses show the methods the Jews used to disbelieve the messengers by asking them for impossible things and by breaking the promise taken from them by the Lord of the Worlds.",
  4155:
      "We distanced them from Our mercy because they broke the promise that was taken from them, and because of their disbelief in Allah's signs, and their boldness in killing prophets sent to them, and for telling Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم: 'Our hearts are covered, so we cannot understand what you say.' That is not the case. Instead, Allah has sealed their hearts due to their disbelief, so no good reaches their hearts. They only have a little faith, which will not be of any use to them.",
  4156:
      "We expelled them from our Mercy due to their disbelief and because they slandered Mary (peace be upon her) by falsely accusing her of fornication.",
  4157:
      "I cursed them because they proudly, but falsely, said: We killed the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, the messenger of Allah. They did not kill him as they claimed, nor did they crucify him, but they killed and crucified a man whom Allah made to resemble Jesus, so they thought the person who was killed was Jesus. Those Jews who claimed to have killed him and those Christians who surrendered him over to them are in doubt and confusion regarding the matter. They have no knowledge, but make guesses that are of no worth against the truth. Truly, they did not kill Jesus nor crucify him.",
  4158:
      "Rather, Allah saved him from their plot and raised him up (body and soul) to Him. Allah is eternally Mighty in His sovereignty; nobody can overcome Him. He is eternally Wise in His management, decree, and legislation.",
  4159:
      "There will be none from the People of the Book except that they will believe in Jesus (peace be upon him) before his death after he returns towards the end of time. Then, on the Day of Resurrection, Jesus (peace be upon him) will bear witness to which of their actions agreed with the legislation and which opposed it.",
  4160:
      "As the Jews did wrong, we prohibited some of the good foods previously permitted for them, such as animals with undivided hoofs and the fat of cows and sheep, except for the back fat. This was also because they prevented themselves and others from Allah's path to the extent that they became known for obstructing others from doing good.",
  4161:
      "This was also due to them dealing with usury after Allah prohibited them from taking it and because they misappropriated people's wealth without any legal right. We have prepared an excruciating torment for the disbelievers among them.",
  4162:
      "After mentioning the shortcomings of the People of the Book, He acknowledges the believers among them, stating: \n But those Jews who are firmly grounded in knowledge and the Believers believe in the Quran that Allah sent to you (O Messenger) and the books that He sent to the messengers before you, like the Torah and the Gospel. They also establish the prayer, pay Zakat (obligatory alms) from their wealth, believe that Allah is the only One worthy of worship without any partner, and believe in the Day of Resurrection. We will give a great reward to those that have such qualities.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Jews were cursed and distanced from Allah’s mercy due to their breaking the laws, disbelieving and killing prophets.\n2. When hearts are sealed, they are deprived of understanding.\n3. The verses show the hatred the Jews had for the Prophet of Allah Jesus (peace be upon him), to the extent that they attempted to kill him.\n4. Allah declared the Jews to be false in their claim of having killed the Messiah; and He clarified that the person who was killed was only a man who had been made to resemble the Messiah.\n5. The verses explain the ignorance and confusion of the Christians with respect to the issue of the crucifixion and their false assumptions in that regard.\n6. The verses show the excellence of knowledge, as the firm knowledge of some of the People of the Scripture led them to having faith in the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him).",
  4163:
      "I have sent revelation to you, O Messenger, as I had sent revelation to the prophets before you. This revelation to you is not something strange or unexpected. I had sent revelation to Noah and to the prophets who came after him. I sent revelation to Abraham and his two sons, Ishmael and Isaac, and to Jacob, the son of Isaac, and to the Tribes (which refers to the prophets that were from the twelve tribes of the Israelites from the children of Jacob). I also gave David a book called the Psalms.",
  4164:
      "We have sent messengers that we have mentioned to you in the Quran, and we have also sent messengers that we have not mentioned to you. We did not tell you about them for a reason. Allah spoke directly to Moses with the revelation without any intermediary, speaking in a way that befits Him (The Exalted and Most High) to honor Moses.",
  4165:
      "We sent them as bearers of glad tidings of a generous reward for those who believe in Allah and to warn those who disbelieve in Him of a painful torment. That is so that the people have no proof to use against Allah to excuse themselves after He had sent the messengers. Allah is eternally Mighty in His sovereignty and eternally Wise in his decree.",
  4166:
      "Even if the Jews disbelieve in you, Allah testifies to the truth of what He sent to you, O Muhammad, from the Quran. In it, He has revealed the knowledge that He wants His slaves to know from what He loves, likes, dislikes, and condemns. The angels bear witness along with the testimony of Allah that what you have brought is true. Sufficient is Allah as a witness, for his testimony is enough without needing anyone else's.",
  4167:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieve in your prophethood and hinder people from embracing Islam have strayed far from the truth.",
  4168:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers and wrong themselves by persisting in disbelief never will Allah forgive them so long as they keep disbelieving, nor will He guide them to the path that leads them to salvation from the punishment of Allah.",
  4169:
      "Except for the path that leads them to enter Hell, where they will abide forever. That is easy for Allah, as there is nothing that He cannot do.",
  4170:
      "O people, verily the Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has come to you with guidance and the true religion from Allah, the Exalted. Therefore, have faith in what has been brought to you, as it is better for you both in this world and the Hereafter. But if you disbelieve in Allah, know that Allah does not need your faith, and your disbelief does not harm him, for He owns all that is in the heavens, all that is on the Earth, and everything in between. He is eternally Knowledgeable of those who deserve His guidance (and so makes it easy for them) and those who do not (and so makes them blind to it). He is eternally Wise in His speech, actions, legislation, and decree.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Noah and Abraham were prophets and messengers and as were others from their progeny.\n2. There are other messengers besides the ones mentioned in the Qur’an. The Qur’an has not mentioned them for a reason known to Allah.\n3. Allah spoke directly to Moses (peace be upon them).\n4. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) is comforted by being told that Allah, as well as the angels, bear witness to the truthfulness of his claim of prophethood.",
  4171:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the Christians who received the Gospel: Do not overstep the limits of your religion, and do not say anything but the truth about Allah concerning Jesus. The Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, is only Allah's messenger sent with the truth. He created him by His word, which He sent with Gabriel to Mary, which was the word 'Be,' and he became. It was a breath from Allah that Gabriel blew with Allah's instruction. So have faith in Allah and all His messengers without making a distinction between them. Do not say, 'The Divine is three' (i.e., Trinity). Avoid saying this corrupt, false statement, and it will be better for you in this world and the Hereafter. Allah is One, free of any partner or child. He is Self-Sufficient. The dominion of the heavens, the Earth, and whatever is in between the two belong to Him. He is sufficient as a guardian to carry out the affairs of His creation.",
  4172:
      "Jesus, Son of Mary, will never be too proud or object to being a slave of Allah. Likewise, the angels who Allah has brought close to Him and elevated their status will not reject being slaves of Allah. So, how can you then take Jesus as a deity?! Or how can the polytheists worship the angels?! Whoever is too proud to worship Allah and looks down on that, Allah will gather them before Him on the Day of Resurrection and give each one what he deserves.",
  4173:
      "After Allah mentions that He will gather everyone together before Him, he defines their recompense, stating: \n As for those who have faith in Allah, believe in His messengers, and do righteous deeds purely for His sake according to the legislation, Allah will give them their full reward for what they have done and give them even more from His bounty and kindness. But for those who were too proud to worship Allah and obey Him, and behaved arrogantly, He will punish them with excruciating torment. They will not have any ally besides Allah who can help or protect them from harm.",
  4174:
      "O people, verily, a decisive proof has come to you from your Lord that does not leave any excuses and removes all doubts, which is Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. We have also sent down to you a clear light, and that is the Quran.",
  4175:
      "As for those who believe in Allah and adhere to the Quran sent to their prophet, Allah will have mercy on them by admitting them into Paradise, increasing their reward, raising their rank, and guiding them to travel the straight path that has no bends, which is the path that leads to the Garden of Eden.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show that the Messiah and his mother were both human and that the Christians who were deviated went to an extreme with respect to them by claiming that they had attributes of divinity.\n2. Allah shows the falsehood of the idolatry of the Christians who believed in the Trinity, and that Allah is free of having any partner, likeness or equal. It is also established that Allah is unique in His Oneness of essence, names and attributes.\n3. Jesus (peace be upon him), as well as all the angels, are created servants of Allah who are not too proud to admit their servitude to Allah and to submit to His laws. How can they be taken as Allahs when they themselves are the servants of Allah?",
  4176:
      "They ask you, O Messenger, for a ruling concerning the inheritance of the one without any descendants or ascendants as heirs, such as no father or child. Say: Allah explains the ruling clearly concerning them: If a person dies without leaving behind a parent or child but has either a full sister or a half-sister, she should receive half of the wealth he left as her prescribed amount. His full brother or half-brother inherits what is left from the inheritance as a residuary if there are no other heirs. As for if there are other heirs, they inherit what is left. If there is more than one full sister or half-sister, they inherit two-thirds as a prescribed amount. When there is more than one full sibling or half-sibling (sisters and brothers), they inherit as residuaries according to the general principle: 'one male inherits the equivalent share of two females,' such that a male receives double that of a female. Allah explains the rulings concerning the one who leaves behind no descendants or ascendants and the other inheritance laws so that you will not go astray regarding them. Allah Knows everything, and nothing is hidden from Him.",
  5000:
      "The Tablespread (Surah Al-Ma'idah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe command to fulfill contracts and warning against being similar to the People of the Book in breaking them.\n•    Explanation:",
  5001:
      "O you who believe, fulfill all of the firm covenants you have with your Creator or His creation. As a mercy for you, Allah has allowed [the consumption of] livestock (camels, cows, and sheep) except what he has prohibited of hunted meat whilst you are in ihram (a ritual state where specific things are forbidden for pilgrims) for Hajj or Umrah. Allah decides to permit or prohibit what He wills according to His Wisdom. No one can force Him or object to His decision.",
  5002:
      "O you who believe in Allah, follow His Messenger, and practice His laws, do not violate the sanctity of those things that Allah has instructed you to honor. Stay away from those things that are prohibited when you are in the state of pilgrim sanctity, such as wearing your normal clothing, and those things that are prohibited within the Sanctuary, such as hunting. Do not regard fighting in the sacred months of Dhū Al-Qa'dah, Dhul-Hijjah, Muḥarram, and Rajab to be permissible. Do not violate the sacrificial animal by seizing it or preventing it from reaching its place of sacrifice. Do not violate those animals with garlands indicating that they are offerings. Do not violate those intending to go to the Sacred House of Allah, seeking profit in their trade and Allah's pleasure. When you come out of the state of ihram (ritual sanctity), and you leave the Sanctuary, you may hunt if you wish. The hatred for a people who prevented you from the Sacred Mosque should not cause you to be oppressive and unfair towards them. Help one another, O believers, to do what you have been instructed and to leave what you have been prohibited from. Fear Allah by holding on to His obedience and avoiding His disobedience. Allah's punishment for the one who disobeys Him is severe, so be careful of it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The laws and cases of inheritance for the person who dies without direct heirs, with a clarification of the shares of the heirs that arise in each case.\n2. The principle of the sacred law is that it is permissible to eat all animals besides those excluded with a proof of prohibition, or land game that comes before a person in the state of sanctity during the pilgrimage of Hajj or Umrah.\n3. It is prohibited to regard as lawful those things that have been made unlawful. These include things prohibited when in the state of Ihram, hunting in the Sanctuary, fighting in the sacred months and violation of the sanctity of the sacrificial animal by taking it or by preventing it from reaching its place of sacrifice.\n4. It is permissible to hunt after coming out of the state of pilgrim sanctity for Hajj or Umrah and after leaving the Sanctuary.",
  5003:
      "Allah has forbidden you from eating those animals that die without being ritually slaughtered. He has also forbidden you from spilled blood, pig's meat, any animal on which other than the name of Allah was taken at the time of slaughter, any animal that was strangled or beaten to death, or one that fell from a high place, or any animal that was gored by another animal and any animal that was hunted by a predator, such as a lion, tiger or wolf, unless you reach any of these animals while they are alive and you slaughter them – in which case they will be lawful for you. He has forbidden you from those animals that were sacrificed for idols. He has also prohibited you from drawing lots to know whether something is destined for you or not or to use as a means of making a decision when intending to do something or not. By doing these prohibited things, a person is leaving obedience to Allah. Today, the disbelievers have lost hope that you will leave the religion of Islam because they see its strength. So do not fear them, but fear Me alone. Today I have perfected for you your religion, which is Islam. I have completed My apparent and hidden favors upon you. I have selected Islam as your religion, so I will not accept any other. If anyone is forced due to hunger to eat from an animal that was not slaughtered correctly, with no inclination to sin, there is no sin on such a person to do so. Allah is Forgiving and Compassionate.",
  5004:
      "After mentioning what He prohibited to eat, Allah mentions what He has permitted the consumption of, stating: \n Your Companions ask you: O Messenger, what has Allah allowed them to eat? Say, O Messenger: Allah has permitted all pure food, and also what was caught by your hunting animals, those that have canine teeth like dogs and cheetahs, and those that have talons like birds of prey. You trained them to hunt as Allah blessed you with knowledge on how to do that, such that they obey when ordered and leave what they are told to leave. So, eat what they catch when hunting for you, even if they kill it, and mention the name of Allah upon releasing [the hunting animal]. Be fearful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. Indeed, Allah is swift to account for your deeds.",
  5005:
      "On this day, Allah has allowed you to eat wholesome food. He has also allowed you to eat slaughtered meat from the People of the Book (the Jews and the Christians) and allowed them to eat what you slaughter. He has permitted that you marry free, chaste women from the believers and from the Jews and Christians who received revelation before you, so long as you pay their dowries and were chaste, not committing immoral actions with them, nor taking them as secret lovers to fornicate with them. Whoever rejects the rulings Allah has legislated for His slaves will find his deeds nullified due to not fulfilling the prerequisite for accepting his action, which is true faith. He will be among the losers on the Day of Resurrection due to entering the Fire, where he will abide for all eternity.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is prohibited to eat animals that die without being slaughtered, blood that spills forth from an animal at the time of slaughter, the meat of the pig, animals on which other than the name of Allah was taken at the time of slaughter and any animal that died by strangulation, being beaten to death, falling from a high place, being gored or by being hunted by a wild animal. The exceptions to this rule are those animals that are found alive and are slaughtered in the manner set-down by the sacred law.\n2. Those animals hunted by trained animals with canines or birds with talons are lawful.\n3. Animals slaughtered by the People of the Scripture are permitted. It is also permitted to marry women from the People of the Scripture who are free and chaste.",
  5006:
      "O you who believe, when you want to establish the prayer, and you are in a state of minor impurity, then perform Wudhu (ritual ablution) by washing your faces and then your hands, including the elbows, then by wiping your heads and washing your feet together with the ankle bones that protrude from the shin. But, if you are in a state of major impurity, perform Ghusl (ritual bathing). If you are sick and you fear that the sickness will get worse or it will take longer to recover, or if you are well but on a journey, or if you are in a state of minor impurity after going to the toilet, for example, or in a state of major impurity after sexual intercourse, and you do not find water to purify yourselves with, despite having searched for it, then use the earth by striking it with your palms and then wiping over your faces and hands. Allah does not wish to make His rulings difficult by making you use water when it will harm you. So, He has legislated an alternative when you cannot use water because it is unavailable or you are sick to complete His favor upon you so that you may be thankful for what Allah blessed you with and not be ungrateful.",
  5007:
      "Remember Allah's favor upon you by guiding you to Islam, and also remember the covenant He made with you when you pledged to hear and obey the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم in ease and difficulty, saying: We hear your words and obey your commands. Fear Allah by fulfilling His orders (which include His covenants) and abstaining from His prohibitions. Allah knows what is in the hearts; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  5008:
      "O you who believe in Allah and His Messenger, uphold Allah's rights upon you sincerely seeking His face and be witnesses justly and not oppressively. Do not let the hatred of a people cause you to abandon justice, for justice is required for friend and foe. So, be just with both of them because justice is like fearing Allah, while oppression is a kind of disrespect towards Him. Be fearful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. Indeed, Allah knows all that you do; none of your deeds are hidden from Him, and He will recompense them.",
  5009:
      "Allah, who does not break any promise, has promised those who have faith in Allah and His Messenger and do righteous deeds that He will forgive their sins and give them a great reward, which is entry into Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The principle with respect to purification is that water should be used for ablution when in the state of minor ritual impurity or for taking a full bath when in the state of major ritual impurity.\n2. In the event of it being difficult to reach water or to use it because of an illness or due to extreme cold, then dry ablution (with sand) has been legislated for the removal of the state of ritual impurity (whether minor or major).\n3. The verses instruct that justice be implemented and injustice be avoided, even when dealing with opponents.",
  5010:
      "But those who disbelieve in Allah and reject His signs are the companions of the Fire; they will enter it as a punishment for their disbelief and rejection, remaining in it as a person stays with his companion.",
  5011:
      "O you who believe, make remembrance with your hearts and tongues of what Allah blessed you with from security and striking fear in the hearts of your enemies when they wanted to lay hands on you and attack you. Allah turned them away from you and protected you from them. Therefore, fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. Let the believers rely solely on Allah to achieve their worldly and religious interests.",
  5012:
      "Verily, Allah took a solemn pledge from the Israelites (which will be mentioned shortly) and put twelve chiefs over them. Each one would lead those under him. Then, Allah told the Israelites: I am with you with My aid and support if you fully establish the prayer, give zakat from your wealth, believe in all My Messengers without exception, honor them, aid them, and spend in good causes. If you do all of this, I will expiate the sins that you have committed, and on the Day of Resurrection, I will enter you into Paradise that has rivers flowing below its palaces. So, whoever disbelieves after taking this solemn pledge has knowingly and willingly strayed from the true path.",
  5013:
      "Because they broke their covenant, We distanced them from Our mercy and made their hearts so hard that they could not receive any good or admonition. They distorted [the revelation] by changing the actual words or interpreting their meaning according to their desires and abandoned some of what they were told to do. O Messenger, you will keep uncovering their treason against Allah and His believing slaves, except for some who fulfilled what the covenant required of them. Therefore, pardon them and do not call them accountable. Instead, overlook what they do as it is kind, and Allah loves those who are kind.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses indicate the great favour of Allah on the Prophet (peace be upon him) and his Companions when He protected them from the attack and the harm of the disbelievers.\n2. Having faith in and supporting the messengers, establishing the prayer and giving Zakat in the required manner are effective means of achieving closeness to Allah and gaining victory, strength, forgiveness and entry into Paradise.\n3. Breaking the promises that require following the messengers is a means for the hearts becoming hard.\n4. The verses condemn the practice of the Jews in distorting the divine scriptures that Allah revealed to them.",
  5014:
      "Just as We took a firm binding covenant from the Jews, We also did so from those who claim to follow Jesus (peace be upon him). However, they did not follow through with everything they were instructed to do, just like their predecessors, the Jews. So, We placed enmity and intense hatred between them until the Day of Resurrection, causing them to fight and kill each other, with each side declaring the other disbelievers. Allah will inform them about what they used to do and recompense them for that.",
  5015:
      "When Allah mentions all of the covenants He made with them and how they continually broke them, He commands them to believe in Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, stating: \n O People of the Book (the Jews of the Torah and the Christians of the Gospel), verily, Our Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has come to you, explaining much of what you have concealed from what was revealed to you and overlooking much of what had no benefit for you except to disgrace you. Verily, the Quran has come to you as a book from Allah. It is a light to guide you and a clear book explaining everything everyone needs for the affairs of this life and the next.",
  5016:
      "Through this book, Allah guides whoever follows what pleases Him of faith and righteous deeds to the safe path away from Allah's punishment. These are the paths that lead to Paradise. He brings them out of the darkness of disbelief and disobedience into the light of faith and obedience with His permission. He guides them to the straight path, the path of Islam.",
  5017:
      "Those Christians who say that 'Allah is the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary' have committed disbelief. Say to them, O Messenger: Who is able to prevent Allah from destroying the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, as well as his mother, and all of those on Earth if He wishes to do so? If no one is able to stop Allah from this, it is a clear indication that there is no Allah but Allah and that all of those people (Jesus, son of Mary, his mother, and all of creation) are all Allah's creation. The dominion of the heavens and the Earth, and whatever is between them, is Allah's. He creates whatever He wishes, and one such creation of His was Jesus (peace be upon him), who was His slave and messenger.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Not acting on Allah’s pledges can lead to enmity, the spread of hatred for another and infighting amongst those who go against Allah’s instruction.\n2. The noble Qur’an guides to the paths that lead to safety from the fire of Hell and entry into Paradise.\n3. The verses refute the Christians who say that Allah became incarnate in the Messiah (peace be upon him) and it makes their disbelief and misguidance clear.\n4. One of the proofs for the falseness of the claim of divinity for the Messiah is that if Allah wished to destroy the Messiah, his mother and all of those on earth, then no one would be able to prevent Him. This proves that they are human.\n5. One of the proofs for the falseness of the claim of divinity for the Messiah is that Allah indicates in the verses to ‘His creating whatever He wishes’. This shows us that the creation of Jesus (peace be upon him) without a father is by no means a proof for his divinity, as this form of creation was not something unique. In fact, there was a more astonishing form of creation when Adam (peace be upon him) was created without a father or a mother.",
  5018:
      "Both the Jews and the Christians claimed to be the children and loved ones of Allah. Say, O Messenger, in response to them: Why does Allah punish you for the sins you commit?! For if you were His loved ones as you claim, He would not punish you with killing and maiming in this life and with the Fire in the Afterlife because he does not punish those He loves. Rather, you are just like any other human. He rewards those who do good with Paradise and punishes those who do evil with the Fire. Allah forgives whom He wills due to His grace and punishes whom He wills due to His justice. The dominion of the heavens, the earth, and everything in between belongs only to Him, and to Him alone is the return.",
  5019:
      "O People of the Book from the Jews and Christians, Our Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has come to you after a period without Messengers and a dire need for one to be sent so that you will not make excuses saying: No messenger came to us to give us the good news about Allah's reward and warn us about His punishment. So, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has come to you, giving you the good news about His reward and warning about His punishment. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing can hinder Him. From His Omnipotence is the ability to send messengers, the final one being Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  5020:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Moses said to his people, the Israelites: O my people, remember with your hearts and tongues how Allah blessed you when he made prophets among you, calling you to guidance, and made you kings in charge of yourselves after you were subjugated slaves, and gave you blessings that He had not given to anyone else in the world during your time.",
  5021:
      "Moses said: O my people, enter the purified land (Jerusalem and the surrounding lands), which Allah has promised that you will enter and fight the disbelievers there. Do not be weak in front of the tyrants, as this will result in loss in both this life and the next.",
  5022:
      "His people responded: O Moses, there is a strong and fierce nation in the Holy Land that prevents us from entering. So we will not go in while they are there because we have no power or strength to fight them. But if they leave, we will enter.",
  5023:
      "Two companions of Moses, who feared Allah and His punishment, and whom Allah had blessed with guidance to obey Him, urged their people to fulfill Moses' (peace be upon him) commands by saying: Enter upon those tyrants by the city gate and once you storm the gate, you will overpower them by Allah's permission. It is from the way of Allah to grant victory to those who take the means for that, such as having faith in Allah and preparing the material resources. If you truly have faith, rely on Allah alone and place your trust in Him because having faith necessitates relying on Him (may He be Exalted).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The fact that Allah punished some of the disbelievers of the Israelites by disfiguring them and by other means proves the falseness of their claim that they were Allah’s children and loved ones.\n2. Placing reliance on Allah is a means of gaining Allah’s assistance.",
  5024:
      "Those from the Israelites who persisted in disobeying the order of their prophet Moses (peace be upon him) said: We will never enter the city so long as the tyrants are still there, so you (O Moses) and your Lord can go and fight them. As for us, we will stay behind here and not fight alongside you.",
  5025:
      "Moses said to his Lord: O my Lord, I do not have any power over anyone except myself and my brother Aaron, so separate us from those who refuse to obey You and Your messenger.",
  5026:
      "Allah said to His prophet Moses (peace be upon him): Indeed, Allah has prohibited the Israelites from entering the Holy Land for a period of forty years. During this time, they will wander the desert, aimless and confused. So do not, O Moses, feel sorry for those who disobey Allah because they were only punished for their own disobedience and sins.",
  5027:
      "O Messenger, tell those jealous wrongdoers from the Jews the true and undoubtable story of Adam's two sons, Cain and Abel. They offered a sacrifice to gain closeness to Allah (may He be Exalted), so Allah accepted Abel's sacrifice because he feared Allah, but He did not accept Cain's sacrifice because he did not fear Allah. Cain was upset with jealousy that Abel's sacrifice was accepted and said: I am going to kill you, Abel. Abel replied: Allah only accepts the sacrifice of those who fear Him by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions.",
  5028:
      "If you stretch out your hand to kill me, I will not retaliate in the same manner, not due to cowardice but because I fear Allah, Lord of all creation.",
  5029:
      "He told him these terrifying words: I want the sin of murdering me to be added to your previous sins so that you become one of the people of the Fire who will enter it on the Day of Resurrection. That is the recompense for the transgressors, and I do not want to become one of them by committing the same sin.",
  5030:
      "But Cain's evil self drove him to murder his brother, and he killed him. As a result, he became one of those who have caused themselves to lose out both in this world and the next.",
  5031:
      "Allah sent a crow to dig the earth in front of him to bury another dead crow and teach him how to cover his brother's body. He then became regretful. Regret is the end result of those who commit sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Going against the messengers results in punishment, as occurred to the Israelites when Allah punished them by their wandering aimlessly.\n2. The story of the two sons of Adam apparently indicates that the first sin to occur on earth was envy and oppression.\n3. The caution displayed by the son of Adam who was killed indicates the duty of leaving oppression and retaliation lest one meets his Lord having shed blood.\n4. Shedding blood without a valid reason results in loss and regret.\n5. Any person who sets a bad example or publicises and encourages an evil action will receive the equivalent sin of those who follow him.",
  5032:
      "Due to Cain killing his brother, we taught the Israelites that whoever kills anybody without a just reason, like capital punishment for causing corruption in the land through treason and warmongering or for legal retribution, then it is as if he has killed all humanity because he does not distinguish between the guilty and the innocent. But whoever refrains from killing a soul that Allah (the Exalted) has prohibited from killing, believing that it is forbidden and does not kill him, then it is as if he has saved all humanity because by doing this, he is taking care of everyone's safety. Verily, Our messengers brought clear signs and undeniable evidence to the Israelites. Yet, despite that, many of them transgressed the limits set by Allah by being disobedient and opposing their messengers.",
  5033:
      "Those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and show him enmity by causing corruption in the land through killing, looting, and highway robbery have no punishment except for being put to death by being crucified or by some other method or having their right hand and left leg cut off. Then, if they do it again, the left hand and the right leg, or by exiling them. That punishment is a humiliation for them in this life, and there is great torment for them in the Afterlife.",
  5034:
      "Except for those who repent before you (people of authority) apprehend them, then know that Allah forgives them after their repentance. He is merciful to them, and overlooking their punishment is from His mercy.",
  5035:
      "O you who believe, fear Allah by obeying His commands and abstaining from his prohibitions. Seek nearness to Him by fulfilling what He has ordered you to do and staying away from what He has prohibited. Fight the disbelievers seeking His pleasure so that by doing so, you may attain what you seek and avoid what you fear.",
  5036:
      "Had those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers owned everything in the Earth and the likeness of it and gave all of that to ransom themselves from Allah's punishment on the Day of Resurrection, such ransom would not be accepted from them. And they will receive a painful punishment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The sacred law requires that a dead person be buried and covered with soil, which is a practice that Allah has taught human beings.\n2. The verses show the sanctity of the human soul, and that protecting it and giving life to it is like having done so for all of mankind. On the other hand, destroying or harming one human soul is like doing it to all of mankind.\n3. The punishment for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger by spreading corruption on earth by killing, looting and cutting off roads is that they be killed without being crucified, or killed by crucifixation, or that their limbs on opposite sides be cut off, or by exiling them from the land in accordance with the offence they committed.\n4. The repentance of those who spread corruption by waging war and cutting off roads before the ruler gets hold of them necessitates pardon.\n5. The verses stress that ransom will not be accepted on the Day of Judgement - even if it be all that is on earth - from those for whom the punishment of Hell is obligatory.",
  5037:
      "They will want to escape the Fire after entering it. Do they deserve that?! They will never get out and will be tormented there for eternity.",
  5038:
      "After mentioning the ruling of those who openly take people's wealth, Allah explains the ruling of those who secretly steal, stating: \n Cut off, O rulers, the right hand of both the male and female thief as recompense and punishment from Allah for them unjustly taking people's wealth, as well as to deter them and others from theft. Allah is Mighty; nothing can overpower Him. He is Wise in His decree and legislation.",
  5039:
      "Whoever repents to Allah for stealing and reforms their actions, Allah will accept their repentance due to His grace. This is because Allah forgives the sins of His slaves who repent and is merciful towards them. However, repentance does not excuse them from the prescribed punishment if their case reaches the ruler.",
  5040:
      "Verily, O Messenger, you know that Allah owns the dominion of the heavens and the Earth, doing with them as He wills. He torments whom He wills out of His justice and forgives whom He wills due to His grace. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing can hinder Him.",
  5041:
      "O Messenger, do not be saddened by those who rush to display their disbelief to irritate you. These are hypocrites who pretend to be believers while hiding their disbelief. Also, do not be saddened by the Jews who listen to and believe the lies of their elders, mindlessly following their leaders who arrogantly avoid you. They replace Allah's words in the Torah with words that agree with their desires and say to their followers: If the law of Muhammad agrees with your desires, then follow it, but if not, then beware. Whoever Allah wants to leave misguided, you will not find (O Messenger) anyone who can save them from misguidance and guide them to the right way. The Jews and hypocrites who have these characteristics are the ones that Allah does not want to purify their hearts from disbelief. They are humiliated and disgraced in this life and will have a great torment in the Afterlife, which is the punishment of the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The wisdom behind the legal punishment for theft is to prevent the thief from wrongfully taking people’s wealth and to make others afraid of doing the same.\n2. The legal punishment for theft is to cut-off the right hand.\n3. The repentance of a thief is accepted as long as the matter does not reach the ruler. Once it reaches the ruler, the law is binding and will not be cancelled by repentance.\n4. A caller to Allah should not become sad and distressed because of the disbelief, plotting and conspiracy of others, because Allah will foil the plots of such people.",
  5042:
      "Those Jews often listen to lies and consume much illicit wealth, such as usury. So, when they come to you for judgment (O Messenger), you may judge between them or refrain as you wish. You can choose either one or the other. If you do not judge between them, they will not be able to harm you in any way. But if you do, then do so justly. If they are oppressors and enemies, Allah loves those who judge justly, even between their enemies.",
  5043:
      "Their situation is bizarre. They disbelieve in you yet come to you for arbitration, eager for you to judge according to their desires. Meanwhile, they claim faith in the Torah, which contains Allah's laws. Then, they disregard your judgment if it goes against their desires. So, they combine disbelief in what is in their book with disregard for your judgment, which is not what believers do. Therefore, they are not from those who have faith in you and what you have brought.",
  5044:
      "Indeed, we revealed the Torah to Moses (peace be upon him). In it is guidance and light, directing towards good. The prophets of the Israelites who submitted to obeying Allah judged according to it, as did the scholars and jurists who would teach the people because Allah had entrusted them with His book, making them custodians to protect it from distortion and change. They are witnesses to it being the truth, and the people refer to them regarding it. So do not (O Jews) fear the people, but fear Me alone, and do not exchange the laws that Allah revealed for something as cheap as leadership, honor, or money. Whoever does not judge according to what Allah has revealed and permits that, or prefers to judge by something else, or considers other than it to be equal to it, are truly disbelievers.",
  5045:
      "In the Torah, we ordered the Jews that whoever has murdered someone should be killed in retribution. Likewise, whoever intentionally gouged someone's eye out, cut off the nose or the ear, or pulled out another person's tooth should have the same done to him [as punishment]. We have prescribed that the perpetrator should be punished in kind in cases of wounding. However, whoever voluntarily pardons the offender will have his sins expiated because he pardoned someone who has wronged him. Whoever does not judge according to what Allah revealed in matters of legal retribution and other issues has transgressed the limits set by Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses explain some of the attributes of the Jews, such as lying, consuming of usury and the desire to have their matters decided by other than the sacred law, in order to show their misguidance and warn against it.\n2. The verses explain the legitimacy of just retribution with respect to life and injury, which was something that Allah had ordered for those before us.\n3. The virtue of pardon from retribution is encouraged and the great reward for the same, represented by the compensation of sins, is explained.\n4. The verses warn against passing judgement with respect to retribution and other matters in accordance with something other than what Allah has revealed.",
  5046:
      "After the prophets of the Israelites, I sent Jesus, son of Mary, as a believer in the Torah, giving judgment in accordance with it. I also gave him the Gospel that contained guidance to the truth and evidence to remove doubts and solve difficult cases of rulings: it corresponded to the Torah that came before it, except in a few rulings that it replaced. I made the Gospel a guide and a means to restrain people from doing that which was prohibited.",
  5047:
      "So let the Christians believe in what Allah has revealed in the Gospel and judge according to the truth contained within it before the sending of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. Whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed has left Allah's obedience and abandoned the truth in favor of falsehood.",
  5048:
      "After mentioning and praising the Torah and the Gospel, Allah praises the Quran, stating: \n We have revealed the Quran to you (O Messenger) with the truth without any question or doubt about it being from Allah. It confirms what was in the previously revealed books and protects them. So, whatever agrees with the Quran is the truth, and whatever contradicts it is falsehood. Therefore, judge between the people according to what Allah has revealed to you in it, and do not follow their desires that caused them to abandon what Allah revealed to you of unquestionable truth. We have made laws for every nation to practice and a clear path to guide them. If Allah had willed to unite them upon one legislation, He would have, but He made separate laws for each nation to test them all and distinguish the obedient from the sinner. So, hasten to perform good deeds and abandon evil deeds. You will all return to Allah alone on the Day of Resurrection. He will inform you about everything you used to differ and recompense you for everything you did.",
  5049:
      "Judge between them (O Messenger) according to what Allah has revealed to you, and do not follow the opinions that stem from them following their desires. Beware of them misleading you from some of what Allah has revealed to you because they will not spare any effort in that. If they refuse to accept the judgment that is according to what Allah revealed to you, then know that Allah only wants to punish them for some of their sins in this life and all of their sins in the Afterlife. Indeed, many people do not obey Allah.",
  5050:
      "Are they turning away from your judgment, seeking the judgment of the people of ignorance who worship idols and judge according to their desires?! The people of sure faith who have understood what Allah has revealed to His messenger all consider that no one can judge better than Allah. But those people of ignorance and desires who only accept what agrees with them, even if it is falsehood, do not.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. All prophets are in complete agreement with respect to the fundamentals of religion, despite there being a few differences between them with regards to secondary matters of the sacred law.\n2. It is necessary to pass judgement in accordance with Allah’s sacred law and to ignore all false beliefs besides it.\n3. The verses condemn the passing of judgement in accordance with the customs and laws of the people of the period of ignorance.",
  5051:
      "O you who believe in Allah and His Messenger, do not take supporters and close friends from the Jews and the Christians allying with them. The Jews only ally with the people of their religion, and the Christians only make alliances with other Christians. But they will both unite against you. Whoever allies with them has joined their ranks. Indeed, Allah does not guide those who have become wrongdoers by taking the disbelievers as allies.",
  5052:
      "You will see O Messenger, the hypocrites who are weak of faith making alliances with the Jews and Christians, saying: We are afraid that they will be victorious and then cause us harm when they come into power. Perhaps Allah will grant victory to His Messenger and the believers, or an order may come from Him repelling the forces of the Jews and their allies. Then, those who rushed to join forces with them will regret the hypocrisy they hid in their hearts because the weak connections they clung to were false.",
  5053:
      "The believers will express surprise at the condition of these hypocrites and say: Are these the ones who swore their most binding oaths that they are with you (O believers) in faith, support, and alliance?! Their good deeds have been nullified, and they have become losers by failing to achieve their goal and due to the torment that has been prepared for them.",
  5054:
      "O you who believe, whoever from you renounces their religion for disbelief, Allah will replace them with a people who He loves, and they love Him due to their righteousness. They are merciful to the believers and harsh towards the disbelievers. They strive with their wealth and lives to make Allah's word victorious. They do not fear those who torment them because they prioritize pleasing Allah over pleasing the creation. Allah grants this to those who He wills from His slaves. Allah has vast bounty and kindness. He knows who deserves it and gives it to them, and he prohibits it from those who do not deserve it.",
  5055:
      "After prohibiting allegiance to Jews, Christians, and non-believers, Allah instructs believers on whom to ally with, stating: \n Neither the Christians, nor the Jews, nor other disbelievers are your allies. Rather your only allies and supporters are Allah and His Messenger, and the believers who perform all their prayers correctly, pay the Zakat (obligatory alms), and submit humbly to Allah.",
  5056:
      "Whoever allies with Allah, His Messenger, and the believers by supporting them is from the party of Allah. The party of Allah will be victorious because they have Allah's support.",
  5057:
      "O you who believe, do not take supporters and close friends from those who mock your religion and take it as a game, neither from those who received a [revealed] book before you like the Jews and the Christians nor from the polytheists. If you truly believe in Allah and what He has revealed, then fear Him by abstaining from what he has prohibited, like taking [the disbelievers] as allies.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses indicate the principle of Al-wala’ wa’l-bara’ (loyalty and disowning): which is, essentially, to be loyal to and love Allah, His Messenger and the believers, and to hate the people of disbelief and avoid loving them.\n2. One of the attributes of the hypocrites is that they take Allah’s enemies as friends.\n3. Carelessness and negligence in supporting the religion may result in the person who is negligent being replaced with someone else, and the honour of supporting the religion being taken away from him.\n4. It is necessary to befriend Allah, His Messenger and the people of faith and to support Allah’s religion.\n5. The verses warn against coming close to, loving and befriending those disbelievers and hypocrites who poke fun at and mock Allah’s religion.",
  5058:
      "They likewise mock and play around when you call them to establish the prayer, the greatest form of worship, because they do not understand the true meaning of worshipping Allah and what the law He has legislated for the people means.",
  5059:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those people of the book who are mocking: Are you criticizing us because we believe in Allah and what He revealed to us and revealed to those before us, and that we believe that most of you have left the obedience of Allah by abandoning faith and neglecting to fulfill His commands?! We regard what you criticize us for as a virtue, not a fault.",
  5060:
      "Say, O Messenger: Shall I tell you about those who are more at fault and whose punishment is worse than these people? They are their predecessors whom Allah has removed from His mercy, transformed into monkeys and pigs, and made some of them worshippers of false deities. The Arabic word ţāghūt refers to any being that is worshipped besides Allah without coercion. Those mentioned will be in a worse position on the Day of Resurrection, and their efforts are further away from the straight path.",
  5061:
      "When the hypocrites from them come to you, O believers, they hypocritically display their faith to you. In reality, they were covered in disbelief when they came just as they left. Allah knows the disbelief they conceal, even if they pretend to have faith, and He will recompense them.",
  5062:
      "You will see, O Messenger, many Jews and hypocrites rush to commit sins like lying, oppressively attacking others, and illicitly consuming people's wealth. How evil is what they do!",
  5063:
      "Why do their leaders and scholars not prevent them from rushing towards lying, bearing false testimony, and wrongfully consuming people's wealth? How evil it is that they do not prohibit them from doing bad deeds!",
  5064:
      "Whenever the Jews faced struggles and drought, they would say: Allah's Hand is closed, not giving out any goodness or generosity; He is keeping what he has from us. Their hands were kept from doing good or being generous, and they were flung far from Allah's mercy due to what they said. Rather, His (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) Two Hands are open-wide with goodness and generosity. He spends as He wills. He gives and withholds. No one can stop Him or force Him. What was revealed to you, O Messenger, only makes the Jews more extreme and disbelieve more because of their jealousy. We have placed hatred and enmity between the different groups of Jews. Whenever they would join forces for war, prepare for it, and make plans, Allah divided their ranks and took their strength away. They will not stop doing what causes corruption in the land by attempting to eradicate Islam and plotting against it. Allah does not like corrupt people.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses condemn the practice of the hypocrites who profess outside that they have faith while keeping disbelief and hatred for Islam and the Muslims hidden within themselves.\n2. The verses condemn the scholar who remains silent in the face of the sins of his people and who does not denounce their evil actions and warn them against such behaviour.\n3. The Jews were ill-mannered with Allah when they described His Hands as being ‘tied’ and withholding good.\n4. In Allah’s hands lie all things and He is the most generous and most giving, may He be glorified.\n5. The verses make reference to the differences and hatred between the various Jewish sects as a result of their disbelief and leaving the truth.",
  5065:
      "If the Jews and Christians had believed in what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought and feared Allah by abstaining from sins, We would have wiped out the wrongdoings that they had committed, even if they were many, and entered them into the gardens of bliss on the day of resurrection, where they would enjoy endless delights.",
  5066:
      "If the Jews had implemented what was in the Torah, and the Christians what was in the Gospel, and both of them had implemented what was revealed to them in the Quran, We would have made it easy for them to get provisions by sending down rain and making crops grow. Some people from the people of the book are moderate and adhere to the truth, but most of them do evil because they lack faith.",
  5067:
      "O Messenger, convey everything revealed to you from your Lord, and do not hide any of it. If you hide anything from it, then it is as if you have not communicated your Lord's message (Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم did indeed convey everything that he was ordered to; whoever claims otherwise has fabricated an enormous lie against Allah). After today, Allah will protect you from the people so they will not be able to cause you any harm, so you only have to convey [the message]. Allah will not bless the disbelievers who do not want to be guided with guidance.",
  5068:
      "Say, O Messenger: O Jews and Christians, you are not practicing the religion until you implement what is in the Torah and the Gospel and practice what was revealed to you in the Quran. Your faith is invalid until you believe in it and implement it. What was revealed to you from your Lord will send many of the people of the book to higher levels of transgression and disbelief because of their jealousy. So do not feel sorry for those disbelievers. The believers that follow you are more than enough.",
  5069:
      "Indeed, whoever among the believers, the Jews, the Sabeans (a group from the followers of some of the prophets), and the Christians who believe in Allah, the last day, and do righteous deeds, will not fear anything from his future and not grieve anything that passed him from his share of this world.",
  5070:
      "I took firm promises from the Israelites that they will listen and follow. But they broke their promises and followed their desires by ignoring what their messengers brought and by disbelieving some and murdering others.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Following what Allah revealed is a means of expiating evil actions and gaining entry into Paradise as well as securing vast provision in the worldly life.\n2. Those who call to Allah are reminded that the propagation that is correct and worthy of consideration is the one that is complete without deletion or alteration and that which is done according to revelation.\n3. No belief is worthy of consideration, unless the person who holds such a belief can prove that it is from Allah.",
  5071:
      "They thought that breaking their promises and covenants, lying, and murdering prophets would not bring about any harm. But it brought consequences that they could not even think of. They were blind and deaf to the truth and could not be guided. Then, Allah accepted their repentance due to His generosity. However, they became blind and deaf to the truth again, which happened to many of them. Allah sees all they do; nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for their actions.",
  5072:
      "Verily, the Christians who claim that Allah is the Messiah, Jesus, Son of Mary, have committed disbelief by ascribing divinity to other than Allah. Meanwhile, the Messiah, Son of Mary, himself, said to them: O Israelites, worship Allah alone. He is my Lord and your Lord. We are all His slaves because Allah will prevent anyone who associated partners with Him from ever entering Paradise, and they will dwell in the Hellfire forever. They will not find any help or support before Allah, and no one can rescue them from the torment that awaits them.",
  5073:
      "Verily, the Christians have committed disbelief by saying, Allah is part of a trinity; the father, the son, and the holy spirit (Allah is Transcendent and far beyond what they claim). Allah is not many; He is One God alone without any partner. If they do not cease from this heinous statement, they will undoubtedly face an excruciating torment.",
  5074:
      "Will they not retract what they said in repentance to Allah and seek forgiveness from Him for the polytheism they committed?! Allah forgives whoever repents to Him, no matter what their sin is. Even if the sin was disbelief, He is merciful to the believers.",
  5075:
      "The Messiah, Jesus, Son of Mary, is only a messenger like other messengers. He will experience death like the others did. His mother, Mary (peace be upon her), was sincere and truthful. They both ate food because they needed it. How could they, therefore, be gods while they needed food?! Look, O Messenger, and ponder how we make the signs clear to them which show that Allah is one and that their exaggeration of ascribing divinity to other than Him (may He be Exalted) is falsehood, yet they reject these signs. Then, look and ponder how they are directed away from the truth despite these clear signs showing Allah's oneness.",
  5076:
      "Say, O Messenger, as an argument against their worship of others besides Allah: Do you worship what cannot bring you any benefit nor protect you from any harm?! Those objects of worship are powerless, and Allah is high above any incapacity. Allah is the only one who hears everything you say without missing anything. He is Omniscient of your actions; none of them are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for them.",
  5077:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the Christians: Do not transgress the limits of your orders to follow the truth, and do not exaggerate in reverence of those whom you were ordered to revere, like the prophets, such that you believe they are divine like you did with Jesus, Son of Mary, because you followed your predecessors from the people of misguidance who misled many people and strayed from the true path.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some Jewish sects used to murder prophets and break their covenants.\n2. The disbelief of the Christians who claimed Lordship for the Messiah (peace be upon him) is explained.\n3. Belief in the Trinity is refuted by explaining its falseness and warning against embracing such a belief. The verses also call for repentance from such a belief.\n4. One of the proofs that the Messiah and his mother were human is that they used to eat food and do the actions that arise from that.\n5. The inability to protect from harm and to bring benefit is one of the clearest proofs that those being worshipped besides Allah were not entitled to Lordship, as they are helpless.\n6. Extremism and overstepping the limits of the sacred law when dealing with the righteous servants of Allah is prohibited.",
  5078:
      "Allah, the Exalted, mentions in the book He revealed to David (the Psalms) that He distanced the disbelieving Israelites from His mercy. He also informs about it in the book (the Gospel) He revealed to Jesus, Son of Mary. He did this because they committed sins and violated what Allah had made sacred.",
  5079:
      "They never used to forbid each other from committing sins. Instead, they would openly commit sins and evil because no one would tell them otherwise. How evil it was for them to abandon the practice of forbidding evil.",
  5080:
      "You will see, O Messenger, many of the disbelievers from among the Jews showing affection towards the Christians and inclining towards them. At the same time, they oppose you and the believers who worship Allah alone. How evil it is that they take the disbelievers as allies. For this reason, Allah is angry with them and will place them in the Fire, where they will reside eternally and never leave.",
  5081:
      "If those Jews had genuinely believed in Allah, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, and what Allah revealed to him in the Quran, they would not have taken the polytheists as allies, loving them and inclining towards them over the believers. That is because they were prohibited from taking the disbelievers as allies. But many Jews disobey Allah and do not side with Allah and the believers.",
  5082:
      "You will find, O Messenger, that the people with the most hostility towards those who believe in you and that which you brought are the Jews, due to their malice, jealousy, and arrogance, as well as the polytheists and others who associate partners with Allah. You will also find that the people who are closest in affection to those who believe in you and that which you brought are those who call themselves Christians. The [reason for the] affection of these Christians towards the believers is that there are scholars and worshippers among them who are humble and not arrogant. Good does not enter the heart of an arrogant person.",
  5083:
      "And these people, such as Najashi and his companions, have soft hearts. When they listen to [any part of] the Quran that has been revealed, they cry in submission as they recognize that it is the truth due to knowing what Jesus (peace be with him) brought. They say: O Our Lord, we believe in what You have revealed to Your Messenger, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, so count us, O Our Lord, among the nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم who will be a proof against the people on the Day of Resurrection.",
  5084:
      "What prevents us from believing in Allah and the truth that He has revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم? We hope to enter Paradise with the prophets and their followers who obeyed Allah and feared His punishment.",
  5085:
      "So, Allah recompensed them for their belief and recognition of the truth with gardens that have rivers flowing beneath its palaces and trees, where they will live eternally. That is the recompense of those who do good by following the truth and submitting to it without any restriction or condition.",
  5086:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger and reject the verses Allah revealed to His Messenger will remain in the blazing Fire eternally and never leave.",
  5087:
      "O you who believe, do not regard as unlawful the pleasures of food, drink, and women [that Allah has made lawful for you]. Do not treat these things as unlawful due to asceticism and devotion. Do not transgress the limits of that which Allah has declared forbidden upon you because Allah does not love those who transgress His limits; rather, He hates them.",
  5088:
      "Consume the lawful and pure things that Allah gives to you from His provision. But do not consume the unlawful, such as something that is taken wrongfully or is impure. Fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions because He is the one you believe in, and your belief in Him requires you to fear Him.",
  5089:
      "Allah will not take you to account, O believers, for the oaths that you utter unintentionally. He will only take you to account for those oaths you break after making them with a firm intention in your hearts. The sin of breaking an oath that has been made can be atoned for by one of three options: feeding ten poor people with the average food of your city by giving each poor person half a ṣā' of food, or clothing them with what society considers to be a suit of clothing, or freeing a believing slave. If the person required to make an expiation does not find any of these three things, then the needed expiation is fasting for three days. That is the expiation for your oaths, O believers, when you break them. Guard your oaths against being taken falsely in Allah's name and breaking them unless it is better to do so. If it is better to break your oath, do so and perform the expiation. Just as Allah has explained the expiation for oaths, He also explains to you His laws, which make clear what is lawful and unlawful, so that you might thank Allah for having taught you what you did not know.",
  5090:
      "O you who believe, intoxicants that affect the mind, gambling with a contribution from both sides, stone altars on which the polytheists offer sacrifices to honor them or which they erect for worship, and divining arrows to seek out their share of the unseen – these are all sinful acts that the Devil has made attractive. Avoid such actions so that you successfully achieve a noble life in this world and the bliss of Paradise in the hereafter.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. We are instructed to look for pure provisions and to leave out the impure.\n2. A person will not be taken to task for an oath that is taken unintentionally but will be taken to task for an oath taken, to do or not to do something, with a firm intention in the heart.\n3. The atonement for a broken oath is to feed or clothe ten poor people, or free a believing slave. If a person is unable to do any of these things, then he must atone for his oath by fasting for three days.",
  5091:
      "By making intoxicants and gambling seem attractive, the Devil's only intention is to create animosity and hatred for each other in their hearts and to turn them away from Allah's remembrance and prayer. So will you, O believers, leave these evil acts? Without a doubt, [abandoning these acts] is the right thing to do, so avoid them.",
  5092:
      "And obey Allah and the Messenger by complying with the commands of the Sacred Law and avoiding its prohibitions. Be careful of contradicting it. If you turn away from this, know that Our Messenger's duty is only to convey to you what Allah has ordered him to, and he has already done so. If you are guided, then it is for your own good. If you do wrong, it will be to your detriment.",
  5093:
      "When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, some believers questioned the status of those who died as Muslims before its prohibition. This led to the revelation of the following verse: \n There is no sin on those who believe in Allah and do righteous deeds to gain closeness to Him for consuming intoxicants before it was made unlawful. As long as they now stay away from prohibited things, take heed of Allah's anger, believe in Him and do righteous deeds, and then increase their awareness of Allah until they worship Him as if they see Him. Allah loves those who worship Him as if they see Him because they know Allah is always watching them. This awareness of Allah leads believers to perfect their deeds.",
  5094:
      "O you who believe, Allah will certainly test you by giving you land game when you are in the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity). You could catch the smaller game with your hands and the bigger ones with your spears. Allah will do this to make known and hold accountable those who fear their Creator without seeing Him due to their complete belief in Allah's Knowledge. Therefore, they avoid hunting due to the fear of their Creator, from whom nothing is hidden. Whoever transgresses the limits and hunts in the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity) shall receive a painful torment on the Day of Resurrection for violating Allah's prohibition.",
  5095:
      "O you who believe, do not kill the land game when you are in the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity). Whoever of you does so deliberately shall be liable for recompense equivalent to the game they killed from camels, cattle, or sheep. Two men known to be upright amongst the Muslims will judge this. The animal they decide on shall be treated like a sacrificial animal and sent to Mecca to be slaughtered in the Haram (Sanctuary). Another option for the recompense is that the equivalent value should be distributed to the poor within the Haram; every poor person should receive half a sa` of grain, or the fast of one day should be kept for every half sa` of grain. All of that is so that the hunter may taste the consequences of his actions. Allah has overlooked the game of the Haram, which were killed in the past, and the person who hunted the land game in the state of Ihram before the prohibition. If anyone repeats this after the prohibition, then Allah will take retribution from them by punishing them for the same. Allah is Mighty and Powerful. Due to His Might, He can take revenge on those who disobey Him if He wishes; nothing can stop Him from doing so.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The consequences of all the actions of a servant - whether the good of obedience or the harm of sin -return to the servant alone.\n2. A person will not be sinful for performing something before it was forbidden or if he was unaware of the prohibition.\n3. Hunting is unlawful for a person in the state of pilgrim sanctity for Hajj or Umrah.\n4. One reason for Allah making certain things unlawful is so that He can test whether the servants will obey or not.\n5. The verses explain the atonement if a person in the state of pilgrim sanctity kills game.\n6. One reason for the rules of atonement is to punish the offenders and to stop them from repeating the sin.",
  5096:
      "Allah has permitted you to fish and permitted what the sea throws out, dead or alive, to benefit the resident or to nourish the traveler. On the other hand, He has made hunting land game unlawful as long as you are in the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity). Therefore, fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions because He is the One to whom you will return on the Day of Resurrection, and He will recompense you for your deeds accordingly.",
  5097:
      "Allah has made the Kaaba, the Sanctified House, an establishment for people, which secures their religious interests, such as prayer, Hajj, and Umrah, and worldly interests, such as security in the Sanctuary and the import of different fruits. He has also made the sacred months (Dhu Al-Qa'dah, Dhu Al-Hijjah, Muharram, and Rajab) an establishment for people to be safe from anyone fighting against them in these months. Then, He made the sacrificial animals and the garlands that indicate they are being taken to the Haram (Sanctuary), an establishment for people where their owners are safe from anyone harming them. All of this is Allah's favor to you so that you are aware that Allah knows everything in the heavens and the earth. His legislation of such laws that secure your interests and protect you from harm proves that He knows what is best for His slaves.",
  5098:
      "Know, O people, that Allah's punishment for those who disobey Him is severe and that He is Forgiving and Compassionate towards those who repent.",
  5099:
      "The duty of the Messenger is only to convey what Allah has ordered him to. It is not his duty to make people accept the guidance: that is only in Allah's Hand. Allah knows what you reveal and keep hidden, whether guidance or misguidance. He will recompense you for that accordingly.",
  5100:
      "Say, O Messenger: Evil is not the same as good, even if the abundance of evil impresses you. Its abundance does not prove its virtue. Therefore, fear Allah, O people of intellect, by abandoning evil and doing good so that you may successfully achieve Paradise.",
  5101:
      "O you who believe, do not ask your Messenger about things you do not need and will not help you in your religion. If such things were shown to you, they would upset you because of their difficulty. If, despite the prohibition, you ask about these things while the revelation is being sent to the Messenger, they will be made clear to you. That is easy for Allah. Allah has omitted and remained silent about certain things in the Quran, so do not ask about them. If you ask about them, you must follow the law that is then revealed concerning them. Indeed, Allah forgives the sins of His slaves when they repent. He is Forbearing not to hasten their punishment.",
  5102:
      "A people before you had asked about similar things [not initially revealed to them]. When they were then instructed to do them, they did not carry out the order; and became disbelievers as a result.",
  5103:
      "Allah has made livestock lawful for you [to consume]. He has not made unlawful what the polytheists declared unlawful for themselves when dedicating them to their idols, such as: bahirah, a she-camel whose ear is cut after it gives birth to a certain number, or Sa'ibah, a she-camel that is left for the idols after it reaches a certain age; or wasilah, a she-camel that gives birth to one female after another; or hami, a male camel stud that mates with other camels and produces a given number of offspring. But, the disbelievers falsely claimed that Allah had forbidden these things. Most disbelievers do not differentiate between truth and falsehood and between the lawful and the unlawful.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is permitted to eat animals that the sea throws out whether they are alive or dead.\n2. The principle is that Allah’s symbols have come to secure benefits for His servants in this world and the Hearafter, and to remove harm from them.\n3. The duty of a caller to Allah is to convey the message clearly. Giving of guidance is entrusted to Allah.\n4. A person should not be impressed with abundance. The abundance of something is not an indication of its permissibility or purity. The indication for such is contained only in the Sacred Law.\n5. When asking for a legal verdict (fatwa), the question should be restricted to the important facts, without adding unnecessary details.\n6. The verses condemn the practice of the idolaters in declaring certain livestock - such as the bahlrah, sa’ibah, wasllah and haml - to be unlawful.",
  5104:
      "When it is said to these people who make up lies about Allah concerning forbidding certain livestock: Come towards the Quran that Allah revealed and to the sunnah (way) of the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, so that you can learn the lawful and the unlawful, they say: The beliefs, statements, and deeds we have taken and inherited from our predecessors is enough for us. How could this be enough for them when their predecessors did not know anything and were not guided to the truth? Only the person who is more ignorant and misguided than them follows them. Thus, they are misguided ignoramuses.",
  5105:
      "O you who believe, you are only responsible for yourselves, so only do that which benefits you. Those who are misguided and do not respond to you will not harm you if you are guided. Being guided includes enjoining the good and forbidding the evil. On the Day of Resurrection, you will return to Allah alone. He will inform you about what you used to do in the worldly life and recompense you accordingly.",
  5106:
      "O you who believe, when death draws close to any of you, by showing one of its signs, then call to witness two upright Muslim men or two men from the disbelievers if the need arises due to there being no Muslims; [for example] if you are traveling at that time and death approaches. If there is any doubt regarding their testimony, keep them back after one of the prayers and let them both take an oath in Allah's name that they will not sell their share from Allah for any amount nor give preference to any relative. Also, they will not conceal any testimony for Allah within them. [Tell them that] if they do that, they will be sinners, disobeying Allah.",
  5107:
      "If, after the oath is taken, it is established that the witnesses lied or betrayed in their testimony or oath, then let two others closest to the deceased take an oath on the truth in their place. These new witnesses should take an oath by Allah saying: Our testimony about their lying and deceit is closer to the truth than their testimony about their honesty and trustworthiness. We have not taken a false oath. If we do so, we will be from the wrongdoers who transgress Allah's limits.",
  5108:
      "What is mentioned about these oaths to be taken by the two witnesses after the prayer when you doubt their testimony and the case of rejecting their testimony increases the likelihood that they will testify in the way required by the sacred law without them distorting the facts deceitfully. Witnesses are more likely to give accurate testimony for fear of being disgraced if their oaths are refuted, and the heirs give conflicting testimony. Therefore, fear Allah by not lying or being deceitful in your testimony and oath. Listen receptively to what you are instructed to do. Allah does not guide those who abandon His obedience.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. If a person firmly adheres to following Allah, instructing what is right and forbidding what is wrong, according to their ability the misguidance of anyone will not harm them. They will not be questioned about other people, especially those who are astray.\n2. Writing a bequest and calling upright persons to witness the same is encouraged.\n3. The verses explain how witnesses to a bequest are to be questioned according to the sacred law.",
  5109:
      "Remember, O people, the Day of Resurrection when Allah will gather all the messengers and ask them: What did your nations respond to you? They will leave the answer to that question to Allah and say: We do not know. You have all knowledge, O our Lord. You alone know all things unseen.",
  5110:
      "Remember when Allah will address Jesus (peace be upon him) and say to him: O Jesus, son of Mary, remember My favor upon you when I created you without a father; and My favor upon your mother, Mary (peace be upon her), when I chose her over all the women of her time; and upon you when I strengthened you with Gabriel (peace be upon him.). You used to speak to people as a breastfed baby, inviting them to Allah, and you spoke to them in adulthood, telling them what Allah had sent you with. From among my favors upon you was I taught you how to write; I taught you the Torah which I had revealed to Moses (peace be upon him); the Gospel which I revealed to you, and I taught you the secrets of the sacred law, its benefits, and wisdom. Also, another favor was that you would mold a bird from clay, blow into it, and it would become a living bird. You used to cure the person who was born blind, and you would treat the leper and heal his skin. You also used to bring the dead to life by supplicating to Allah to give them life. All of this happened with My permission. Another favor I favored you with was that I protected you from the Israelites when they intended to kill you after you brought clear miracles to them. The only thing they could do was disbelieve in them, and they said: Jesus has brought nothing but clear magic.",
  5111:
      "Another favor that I graced you with was that I facilitated for you helpers when I inspired the disciples to believe in you and Me. They submitted to that and responded: We believe. Be a witness, O our Lord, that we submit to You in devotion.",
  5112:
      "Remember when the disciples said: Can your Lord send down a table spread from the sky if you supplicate to Him? Jesus (peace be upon him) responded by instructing them to fear Allah and not to ask for such a thing, as it may prove to be a trial for them. He told them: Place your trust in your Lord in seeking provision if you are truly believers.",
  5113:
      "The disciples said to Jesus: We want to eat from this table spread so that our hearts can be satisfied with Allah's perfect power and that you are His Messenger, and to know for certain that you have told us the truth about what you have brought from Allah, and to be witnesses to it for those people who are not present.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah will gather the entire creation, whether honourable or not, on the Day of Judgement.\n2. Jesus (peace be with him) was human and he performed physical miracles such as bringing the dead to life and curing the person who was bom blind and the leper.\n3. The aim of the miracles of the prophets is to strengthen their followers and to silence their opponents. But it must be remembered that these miracles are not from the prophets themselves, but occur only with Allah’s permission.",
  5114:
      "Jesus gave in to their request and supplicated to Allah, saying: O our Lord, send down to us a table spread of food so that we can hold a festival on the day it comes down to honor You out of gratitude. It will also be a sign and proof of Your Oneness and the truth of what I have been sent with. So give us such provision that will help us worship You. You, O our Lord, are the best provider.",
  5115:
      "Allah responded to the supplication of Jesus (peace be upon him) and said: I will send down the table spread that you have requested, but whoever disbelieves after I have sent it down should blame only themselves. I will torment them with a severe torment, unlike any other, due to them seeing an overwhelming sign and disbelieving only out of stubbornness. So Allah fulfilled His promise and sent down the table spread to them.",
  5116:
      "Remember, [O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم], when Allah will address Jesus, son of Mary (peace be upon them) on the Day of Resurrection, saying: O Jesus, son of Mary, did you tell the people to worship you and your mother instead of Allah? Jesus will reply, exalting his Lord: It was not right for me to tell them anything but the truth. If I had said that, You would know it because nothing is hidden from You. You know what I keep hidden within myself, but I do not know what is with You. You alone know everything unseen, hidden, and apparent.",
  5117:
      "Jesus will say to His Lord: I only told people what You ordered me to tell them: to worship You alone. I observed what they were saying as long as I remained among them. When my time with them ended, and I was raised to the sky alive, You, O Lord, were watching their deeds. You are a witness to everything, and nothing is hidden from You, so You know what I said to them and what they said after me.",
  5118:
      "If you punish them, O my Lord, they are Your slaves, and You can do with them as You wish. If You graciously forgive those of them who believe, nothing can stop You from doing so because You are the Almighty, Who cannot be overpowered, and the Wise in Your planning.",
  5119:
      "Allah will say to Jesus (peace be upon him): this [the Day of Resurrection] is the Day on which the truthfulness of those who were truthful in their intentions, statements, and deeds will benefit them. They will receive gardens with rivers flowing beneath its palaces and trees, where they will live eternally, with death never coming to them. Allah will be pleased with them and will never become displeased with them. They will be pleased with Allah because of the everlasting bliss they have received. Such reward and pleasure are a great success, and no success comes close to it.",
  5120:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of the heavens, Earth, and every creation within them. He is their Creator and the One who plans their affairs. He has power over everything, and nothing can hinder Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah warns those who persist in disbelief and stubbornness after clear proof has been established against them.\n2. The Messiah (peace be with him) is declared innocent of the claim of the Christians that he informed them that he is Allah or the son of Allah or that he claimed lordship or divinity.\n3. On the Day of Rising, Allah will question even the prophets who were the most noble and the greatest amongst people, so what about those who are below them in rank?\n4. The verses show the great virtue of truthfulness and Allah’s praise for those who are truthful. They also show the benefit that truthfulness will bring on the Day of Judgement for those who were truthful.",
  6000:
      "The Cattle (Surah Al-An'am)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming pure monotheism and responding to the deviations of polytheists.\n•    Explanation:",
  6001:
      "Only Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth without precedent, is described, in adoration, with perfection and praised with the loftiest, most beautiful attributes. He created the night and the day, which follow one another. He created the night for darkness and the day for light. Yet, despite all this, some of His slaves disbelieve in Him, equate others with Him, and associate partners with Him.",
  6002:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One who created you, O people, from clay when He created your father, Adam (peace be upon him) from it. Then He (may He be Exalted) fixed a period for your stay in the life of this world. He also set another term, which only He knows, when He will resurrect you back to life on the Day of Resurrection. Despite this, you still doubt His power (may He be Exalted) to resurrect you.",
  6003:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One worthy of worship in the heavens and the earth. Nothing is hidden from him: He knows the intentions, statements, and deeds you keep hidden and those you make public, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  6004:
      "No proof from their Lord comes to the polytheists except that they ignore it without paying attention. Clear proofs and evidence of the Oneness of Allah, as well as miracles proving the truthfulness of the messengers, have now come to them; yet despite this, they turned away and paid no attention [to these signs and miracles].",
  6005:
      "Besides turning away from these clear proofs and evidence, they had previously turned away from something even clearer: they rejected the Quran that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought. They will soon realize, when they see the torment on the Day of Resurrection, that what they used to poke fun at and what he brought to them was, in fact, the truth.",
  6006:
      "Do these disbelievers not know Allah's established practice of destroying nations that do wrong? Allah has destroyed many nations before them. They were more firmly established on the Earth than these disbelievers. Allah sent down continuous rain upon them and made rivers flow beneath their homes. Yet, they disobeyed Allah, so He destroyed them because of their disobedience. Then, after them, He created other nations.",
  6007:
      "If We had sent down to you, O Messenger, a book written on paper, and they had seen it with their eyes and touched it with their hands, they would not have accepted it out of stubbornness and rejection. They would have said: What you have brought is nothing more than clear magic, and we will never believe in it.",
  6008:
      "These disbelievers said: We will believe if Allah sends down an angel with Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم who speaks to us and bears witness that he is a messenger. If We had sent down an angel of the kind they wished, We would have destroyed them if they did not believe, and they would not be given time to repent.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the extreme stubbornness of the disbelievers and their persistence in disbelief despite the establishment of proof against them by means of tangible evidence.\n2. Humankind is reminded of how Allah dealt with past people in order to know the causes of their destruction, so as to avoid doing the same.",
  6009:
      "If We had sent an angel to them, We would have made him in the form of a man so that they could listen and learn from him, as they would not be able to learn from an angel in the original form that Allah created him. If We had made him in the form of a man, they would have been confused about him.",
  6010:
      "If these people poke fun at you by asking for an angel to be sent down with you, nations in the past also poked fun at their messengers. Then, the punishment, which they used to deny and mock when warned about it, encompassed them.",
  6011:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these people who reject and mock you: Travel throughout Earth and then think about what happened to those who disbelieved in Allah's messengers. Allah's punishment descended upon them after they were in a position of strength and power.",
  6012:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: To whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth, and whatever is between them? Say: The entire dominion belongs to Allah. Out of His Grace, He has obligated upon Himself mercy towards His slaves and will, therefore, not rush to punish them. He will gather them together for reckoning and recompense on the Day of Resurrection. There is no doubt about this. Those who have lost themselves due to their disbelief in Allah will not believe and rescue themselves from loss.",
  6013:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of everything, all that rests in the night and the day. He is All-Hearing of His slaves' words and Omniscient of their deeds and will recompense them accordingly.",
  6014:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists who worship idols and other things alongside Allah: Does it make sense that I take anyone other than Allah as a helper and guardian from whom I seek help while it is He who created the heavens and the earth without precedent? There was no creator before Him. He is the One who gives provision to whichever of His slaves He wishes, and none of His slaves provide for Him. He does not need His slaves, but His slaves need Him. Say, O Messenger: My Lord (may He be Exalted) has instructed me to be the first one from this nation to submit and be humble. He has prohibited me from being from those who associate others as partners with Him.",
  6015:
      "Say, O Messenger: If I disobey Allah by committing that which He has made unlawful, such as associating partners with Him and other than it or by abandoning what He has instructed me to do, such as believing [in Him] and other acts of obedience, then I fear that He will torment me with a great torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  6016:
      "Whoever Allah distances from the torment on the Day of Resurrection has attained success through the mercy of Allah. Such salvation from torment is a clear success that no other success comes close to.",
  6017:
      "If any calamity from Allah afflicts you, O son of Adam, no one can remove it from you besides Allah. If any good from Him comes to you, no one can stop Him and withhold His grace. He has power over everything, and nothing can render Him incapable.",
  6018:
      "He is the Predominant over His slaves and the One who subdues them. He is exalted above them in all regards, and nothing can overpower or defeat Him. Everything is subservient to Him. He is above His slaves in a manner that befits His majesty; may He be Exalted. He is the Wise in His creation, planning, and legislation. He is All-Aware, and nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The wisdom of Allah’s sending messengers of the same species as those to whom they were sent is that it is more effective with respect to their listening, paying heed and accepting the message.\n2. People are called to consider that a repetition of the ways of the people of the past with regards to disobedience may result in a repetition of Allah’s system of dealing with them in the form of punishment.\n3. It is necessary to be afraid of sin and its consequences.\n4. Only Allah can remove a calamity that affects a person and only Allah can stop any good from reaching a person.There is no one who can hold back Allah’s grace and no one who can stop His favour.",
  6019:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists who reject you: What is greatest and most honored as a witness to my truthfulness? Say: Allah is the greatest and most honored witness to my truthfulness. He is a witness between you and me. He knows what I have brought to you and how you respond. Allah has revealed this Quran to me to warn you with it and to warn any human or jinn it reaches. You, O polytheists, believe that there are other deities worthy of worship alongside Allah. Say, O Messenger: I do not bear witness to what you have acknowledged because it is false. Allah is the only One worthy of worship: He has no partner. I am free from all that you associate as partners with Him.",
  6020:
      "The Jews who were given the Torah and the Christians who were given the Gospel recognize the Prophet Muhammad completely, just as they recognize their children from other children. They are the ones who have lost themselves by causing themselves to enter The Fire, and they will not believe.",
  6021:
      "No one does more wrong than someone who associates a partner with Allah, worshipping it alongside Him, or rejects His verses, which He has revealed to His Messenger. Those who do wrong by associating partners with Allah and rejecting His verses will never succeed if they do not repent.",
  6022:
      "Remember the Day of Resurrection when We will gather them all together, not leaving any of them out. Then, as a way of reprimand, We will say to those who worshipped others alongside Allah: Where are your partners that you falsely claimed to be Allah's partners?",
  6023:
      "After this test, they will have no excuse except to declare themselves free of what they worshipped by dishonestly saying: By Allah, our Lord, we did not associate partners with You in the worldly life. Instead, we believed in You and were monotheists who worshipped You alone.",
  6024:
      "Look, O Muhammad, how these people lied about themselves by denying they associated partners with Allah. The partners they set up with Allah in this worldly life have disappeared and deserted them.",
  6025:
      "Some of the polytheists listen attentively to you, O Messenger, when you recite the Quran. However, they do not benefit from listening to it because We have placed covers on their hearts that prevent them from understanding it. We did this due to their stubbornness and rejection. We have made their ears deaf, not able to listen for benefit. Therefore, no matter how many clear indications and glaring evidence they see, they still do not believe in them, such that when they come to you to debate the truth with falsehood, they say: What you have brought is taken from the books of earlier people.",
  6026:
      "They prevent people from believing in the Messenger while they keep their distance from him. They do not let others benefit from him just as they do not benefit. They are only destroying themselves by doing this, but they fail to realize that their actions will cause their destruction.",
  6027:
      "If you, O Messenger, could only see when they will be exposed to the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, you would be amazed at their bad situation. Then, they will say with regret: If only we could be sent back to the world, not reject Allah's signs/verses, and be from those who believed in Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses explain the wisdom behind sending the Prophet (s) with the Qur’an in order to convey and explain the message. Calling towards Allah’s oneness was the most significant part of this.\n2. The verses negate Allah having any partner and refutes the fabrications of the idolaters in this regard.\n3. The verses explain that the Jews and Christians actually recognised the Prophet (peace be upon him), despite their external rejection and disbelief.",
  6028:
      "Their saying that they would believe if sent back is a lie. Instead, the statement they used to keep hidden, which was: \"By Allah, we were not polytheists,\" appeared to them when their limbs testified against them. If they were supposedly sent back to this world, they would return to the disbelief and associating partners with Allah they had been prohibited from. So, they are lying in their promise that they will believe if they are sent back.",
  6029:
      "These polytheists say: There is no life except the life we presently have, and we will not be resurrected for the reckoning.",
  6030:
      "If you, O Messenger, could only see when those who rejected resurrection will be made to stand before their Lord, you would be amazed at their bad situation when Allah will say to them: Is the resurrection that you used to reject not the truth about which there is no doubt? They will say: We swear by our Lord who created us; it is true, and there is no doubt about it. At this juncture, Allah will then say to them: So, taste the torment which is a result of your disbelief of this Day, which you used to reject in the worldly life.",
  6031:
      "Those who reject the resurrection on the Day of Judgment and consider standing before Allah farfetched will be in utter loss. Until, when the Hour comes upon them unexpectedly without prior knowledge, they will say out of extreme regret: Alas for us and what loss and disappointment, due to our negligence towards Allah by disbelieving in Him and not preparing for the Day of Resurrection. They will carry sins on their backs. How terrible are the sins that they carry?!",
  6032:
      "The worldly life you are inclined towards is nothing but play and deception for those who do not do deeds to please Allah. The abode of the Hereafter is better for those who fear Allah by doing what He has ordered, such as believing [in Allah] and obeying Him, and avoiding what He has prohibited, such as associating partners with Allah and disobedience. Do you, O polytheists, not understand this so that you can believe and do righteous deeds?",
  6033:
      "We know, O Messenger, that their outward rejection grieves you. However, they do not deny you inwardly because they know your truthfulness and honesty. They do wrong by rejecting what you have brought outwardly, while inwardly, they firmly believe in it.",
  6034:
      "Do not consider that such rejection only concerns what you have brought. Instead, messengers before you were also rejected and harmed by their people, but they faced this patiently, inviting towards Allah and fighting in Allah's path until His help came. No one can hold back the help of Allah if He has written and promised it to His messengers. O Messenger, information has come to you about previous messengers, their experiences with their people, and how Allah gave them victory over their enemies by destroying them.",
  6035:
      "If their rejection and turning away from the truth you have brought is difficult for you, O Messenger, then see if you can find a tunnel into the ground or a ladder into the sky so that you may bring them proof and evidence in addition to what I have already given you. If Allah willed to direct them to the guidance that you brought, He would have done so. However, He has not willed this because of His far-reaching wisdom. So [O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم] do not be among those who are ignorant of this and lose yourself in regret over them because they do not believe.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah, in His justice, will gather the worshipper and the one worshipped as well as the follower and the one followed on the plains of resurrection to testify against one another.\n2. Not every one who listens to the Qur’an benefits from it. Sometimes there is an obstacle to this such as the sealing of the heart, deafness or the like.\n3. The verses explain that even though the idolaters outwardly reject the Prophet (s), inwardly they are certain of his truthfulness.\n4. The Prophet (peace be upon him) is consoled by being informed that the denial of his prophethood did not only occur to him, but previous idolaters acted in the same way with previous prophets as well.",
  6036:
      "Only those who listen and understand the speech will respond to what you have brought. The disbelievers are dead and useless, for their hearts have died. Allah will resurrect the dead on the Day of Resurrection, and then they will be returned to Him to be recompensed accordingly for the deeds they have sent forth.",
  6037:
      "The polytheists, delaying the acceptance of belief, say stubbornly: Why has no extraordinary sign been sent down to Muhammad as proof from His Lord about the truth of what he has brought? Say, O Messenger: Allah can send down a sign as they wish, but most of these polytheists who demand that a sign be sent down do not know that signs are only sent down in accordance with Allah's wisdom and not per their demands. If He was to send it down and they still did not believe in it, He would destroy them.",
  6038:
      "There are no animals on earth or birds in the sky except that they are species like you, O children of Adam, with respect to being created and provided for. We have not left out anything from the Preserved Tablet. The knowledge of all of them is with Allah. Then, they will all be gathered to their Lord on the Day of Resurrection for the final decision, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  6039:
      "Those who reject Our verses/signs are like the deaf who cannot hear, the mute who cannot speak. Moreover, they are in total darkness and cannot see. How can such a person be guided? Allah misguides from among the people whomever He wills and guides whomever He wills by placing them on a straight path with no crookedness.",
  6040:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Tell me, if Allah's torment or the Hour that you have been promised comes to you, will you call on anyone besides Allah at that time to remove the calamity and difficulty that has descended on you? [You would] if you are truthful in your claim that those whom you worship can bring benefit or prevent harm.",
  6041:
      "The truth is that when the Hour comes, you will not call on anyone besides Allah, Who created you. He removes the calamity and takes away harm as He is worthy of that and can do so if He wills. As for what you worshipped as deities, you will leave them because you know that they cannot bring benefit nor cause harm.",
  6042:
      "We sent messengers to nations before you, O Messenger, but they rejected these messengers and turned away from what they brought to them. We punished them with difficulties such as poverty and illness so they could submit and humble themselves before their Lord.",
  6043:
      "If only they humbled themselves when the calamity came to them and begged Us to remove it, We would have shown them mercy, but they did not do that. Instead, their hearts became hard, and they did not reflect and take lessons. The Devil made their disbelief and disobedience attractive, so they continued with those actions.",
  6044:
      "When they ignored the warning of extreme poverty and illness and did not act on Allah's orders, We enticed them further away from the truth by opening the doors of provision to them and giving them wealth after they were poor and good health after they had suffered illness. This continued until they were steeped in their arrogance and enjoyment of life; then, Our punishment came upon them suddenly, and they were overtaken by despair and lost all hope.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers are likened to those who are dead because life in reality is the life of the heart when it accepts the truth and follows the path of guidance.\n2. Part of Allah’s wisdom with respect to calamities is that He sends them down on those who disobey Him in order to soften their hearts and bring them back to their Lord.\n3. The possession of wealth and blessings by those who are astray does not indicate that Allah loves them. It is merely a means of His enticing them and a test for them as well as others besides them.\n4. A proof of Allah’s lordship is that if Allah took away people’s hearing and sight, they would not be able to restore them.",
  6045:
      "The last of the disbelievers was cut off by being wiped out altogether by destroying them while the messengers were helped. All thanks and praise are only for Allah, Lord of the worlds, for destroying His enemies and giving victory to His friends.",
  6046:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Tell me, if Allah were to make you deaf by snatching away your hearing, make you blind by removing your sight, and seal your hearts so that you cannot understand anything, what other being deserving worship is there that will bring all of these back to you? Think, O Messenger, about how We explain the proofs to them in various ways, yet they still turn away from it.",
  6047:
      "O Messenger, tell them: Tell me, if Allah's torment comes to you suddenly or openly before your eyes, no one will be punished except the wrongdoers who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers.",
  6048:
      "We have sent Our messengers only to give the pleasing news to those who believe and obey [Allah] of eternal bliss that will never end and to warn those who disbelieve and disobey [Allah] of Our severe torment. So, whoever believes in the messengers and sets his deeds right will have no fear for what awaits them in the Hereafter, nor will they grieve and regret over the pleasures of this world that they missed.",
  6049:
      "Those who reject our signs will be punished for abandoning Allah's obedience.",
  6050:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: I do not say to you that I have Allah's treasures of provision with me and that I can do with them as I please. Nor do I not tell you I know the unseen besides Allah's revelation. I also do not say that I am an angel. Instead, I am Allah's Messenger and only follow what is revealed to me. I do not claim that which I do not have. Say to them, O Messenger: Is the disbeliever whose sight is blind to the truth equal to the believer who sees the truth and believes in it? O polytheists, do you not reflect using your intellect about the signs around you?",
  6051:
      "O Messenger, warn with this Quran those who fear they will be gathered before their Lord on the Day of Resurrection that they will have no ally besides Allah to bring them any benefit nor any intercessor to remove harm from them, so they may fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. These are the people who will benefit from the Quran.",
  6052:
      "O Messenger, do not dismiss the poor Muslims who continuously worship Allah sincerely at the beginning and end of the day from your gathering. Do not dismiss them to win favor with the leaders of the polytheists. You are in no way accountable for these poor people. They, too, are in no way accountable for you. If you dismiss them from your gathering, you will be of those who transgress Allah's limits.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Prophets are human beings and have no attributes of lordship whatsoever. Their task is to convey the message. They have no control over the creation, nor do they know the unseen. They also have no control over the treasures of provision and the like.\n2. A caller to Allah must show concern for his followers, especially those weak ones amongst them who only seek the truth. He must bring them close and must not distance them in order to please the disbelievers.",
  6053:
      "So, We tested some by means of others. We made them different in relation to their worldly fortunes [some of them rich and others poor]. We tested them in this way so that the rich disbelievers say about the poor believers: Are these poor people the ones whom Allah has favored with guidance out of all of us? If belief [in Allah] were any good, they would not have beaten us to it because we are the people who come first. Does Allah not know those who show gratitude for His favors such that He guides them to belief, from those who are ungrateful for these favors, so He abandons them to disbelief? Certainly, Allah knows best about them.",
  6054:
      "O Messenger, when those who believe in our signs that indicate the truth of what you have brought come to you, then respond to their greeting of peace to honor them. Then, give them the good news of Allah's vast mercy because He has obligated mercy on Himself as a favor from Him. So, whoever of you commits a sin out of ignorance and foolishness (and this is the state of anyone who sins intentionally or unintentionally), then repents and sets their deeds right, then Allah will forgive them, for Allah is forgiving and merciful to His slaves who repent.",
  6055:
      "Just as We have explained what was previously mentioned, We present Our proofs and evidence against the people of falsehood and make clear the way and path of the criminals so that it can be avoided and steered clear from.",
  6056:
      "Say, O Messenger: Allah has prohibited me from worshipping those whom you worship instead of Allah. Say, O Messenger: I do not follow your desires in worshipping other than Allah. If I had followed your vain desires, I would have gone astray from the path of truth and not been guided to it. This is the condition of everyone following their desires without proof from Allah.",
  6057:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: I stand on clear evidence from my Lord, not on vain desires, yet you have rejected this evidence. I do not possess the torment and the extraordinary signs that you demand and are in such haste to bring about. That is only in Allah's hands. The decision for anything, including your requests, is only Allah's. He speaks the truth and decides accordingly. Allah (may He be Exalted) is the best who distinguishes those who are upon truth from those who are upon falsehood.",
  6058:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: If I possessed the torment you are in such haste to bring about, I would have brought it down on you. If that happens, the matter between you and me will be settled, and Allah knows best the duration of respite for the wrongdoers and when to punish them.",
  6059:
      "The treasures of the unseen are with Allah alone: no one besides Him knows them. He knows everything created on the land, such as animals, plants, and inanimate objects. He knows whatever animals or plants there are in the sea. No leaf falls in any place, nor is there any seed of grain hidden in the earth, nor anything moist or dry, except that it is recorded in a clear book, the Preserved Tablet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah makes some of His servants a test for others and they therefore differ in their levels of provision and in their disbelief and faith. Disbelief and faith are not related to the abundance of provision or the lack thereof.\n2. One of the qualities of a caller to Allah is that he has a cheerful countenance and that he brings cheer and happiness to his companions.\n3. A caller to Allah must avoid following lowly desires as regards to his belief, method and conduct.\n4. Only Allah has knowledge of the Ghaib and His knowledge in this regard is vast: He misses nothing and nothing of His creation is hidden from Him. Everything is recorded with Him, including the smallest details.",
  6060:
      "Allah is the One who temporarily takes away your souls at night as you sleep, and He is the One who knows the deeds you do during the day when you are active. He then restores you to life in the day after taking away your souls through sleep so that you may carry out your tasks. This will continue until the decreed period of your lives ends, as known to Allah. Then you will return to Him alone when He resurrects you on the Day of Resurrection. He will then inform you about what you used to do in the worldly life and recompense you accordingly.",
  6061:
      "He is the Predominant over His slaves and the One who subdues them. He is exalted above them in all regards. Everything is subservient to Him. He is above His slaves in a manner that befits His majesty; may He be Exalted and Transcendent. O people, He sends down to you honorable angels to record your deeds. This will continue until the person's life ends with the angel of death and his helpers taking his soul. They never fail to do what they are ordered to do.",
  6062:
      "Then all of those whose souls were taken away will be returned to Allah, their true Master, so that He may recompense them for their deeds accordingly. To Him belongs the effectual decision and fair judgment between them. He is the swiftest of those who take account of your deeds.",
  6063:
      "O Messenger, ask these polytheists: Who rescues and delivers you from these dangerous situations you encounter in the darkness of the land and sea? You supplicate to Him alone, submissively and humbly in secret and public, saying: If our Lord delivers us from these deadly situations, we will certainly be of those who show gratitude for His favors upon us and not worship anyone besides Him.",
  6064:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: Allah is the One who rescues you from it and delivers you from every distress. But, after that, when times are good, you associate partners with Him in worship. What can be more wrong than that which you do?!",
  6065:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Allah is able to send upon you a torment that will come from above you, such as stones, thunderbolts, and floods, or that will come from below you, such as earthquakes and sinking into the ground. He can also cause disunity between your hearts, making each person follow their vain desire and making you fight one another. Think, O Messenger, how We diversify the evidence and proofs and explain it to them so that they understand that what you have brought to them is the truth and that what they have is false.",
  6066:
      "Your people have rejected this Quran, while it is the truth. There is no doubt that it is from Allah. O Messenger, tell them: I have not been appointed to watch over you. I am but a warner to you before a severe torment.",
  6067:
      "Everything has a time in which it occurs and an endpoint which it reaches, including your end. Soon, you will know it when you are resurrected on the Day of Resurrection.",
  6068:
      "When you, O Messenger, see the polytheists speaking about Our verses by mocking and poking fun at them, then distance yourself from them until they enter into a discussion free of such mockery. If the Devil makes you forget, and you sit with them, but you remember afterward, leave that gathering and do not sit with these transgressors.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Sleep is a form of death and souls are taken away at the time of sleep and are returned upon awakening.\n2. Allah’s divinity is proved by innate nature. The disbelievers, by their natural inclination, believe in Allah and return to Him at the time of extreme need and sure destruction, and then ask of Him alone.\n3. The conduct of the idolaters is used as a proof against them and evidence is established against the transformation in their nature by their seeking Allah’s assistance at sea at the time of difficulty and thereafter associating partners with Him when He saves them and brings them to the shore.\n4. It is not permissible to sit in the gatherings of the people of falsehood and nonsensical talk. A person must leave such company and not return to them until they stop such talk.",
  6069:
      "Those who fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions are in no way responsible for the account of these wrongdoers. They only have to prohibit them from the evil they are doing so that they may also fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  6070:
      "Leave, O Messenger, these polytheists who have made their religion a thing of play and distraction and mock and poke fun at it. The life of this world, with its temporary pleasures, has deceived them. Advise people, O Messenger, with this Quran so that no soul is delivered to destruction because of the evil actions they have done. If they so act, they will have no one to help them nor any intercessor to protect them against Allah's torment on the Day of Resurrection. If they have to offer any ransom to be saved from Allah's torment, such will not be accepted. Those are the ones who have been delivered to their destruction because of the sins they committed. On the Day of Resurrection, they will have a scalding drink and a painful torment because of their disbelief.",
  6071:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Should we worship idols, instead of Allah, that do not possess the ability to benefit, nor can they harm us? Should we leave belief after Allah has guided us to it? If we do so, we will be similar to the one the devils have misguided, leaving him confused and without guidance. His companions on the straight path call him to the truth, but he refuses to respond to their call. Therefore, O Messenger, say to them: Allah's guidance is the true guidance, and Allah has ordered us to submit to Him (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) by devoutly sticking to singling Him out and worshiping Him alone because He is the Lord of the Worlds.",
  6072:
      "Allah has ordered us to establish the prayer perfectly and to fear Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. He, alone, is the One to whom the slaves will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, and He will recompense them accordingly for their deeds.",
  6073:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) is the One who created the heavens and the earth for a purpose. \"On the Day that He will say to something: Be, and it will become\" means: On the Day of Resurrection, when He says Rise, they will all rise. His word is the truth that will undoubtedly occur. To Him alone (may He be Exalted) belongs the dominion on the Day of Resurrection when the angel Israfil will blow the trumpet a second time. He, Allah, knows the unseen and what can be seen. He is Wise in His creation and planning. He is Aware of the hidden just as He knows the apparent, and nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A caller to Allah is not responsible for taking anyone to account. Their duty is only to convey the message and to remind.\n2. One of the evidences for monotheism is that something which has no control over any benefit or harm can obviously not be entitled to being worshipped as a Allah besides Allah.",
  6074:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Abraham (peace be upon him) said to his father, Azar, a polytheist: O my dear father, do you make the idols into deities you then worship besides Allah? I think you and your people who worship idols are misguided and confused about the path of truth because you worship others instead of Allah. Allah alone (may He be Exalted) deserves worship, and no deity besides Him is worthy of worship.",
  6075:
      "In the same way that We showed him the misguidance of his father and his people, We also showed him the dominion of the heavens and the earth so that he could use that vast dominion as evidence of the Oneness of Allah and that Allah alone deserves to be worshipped and so that he be from those who certainly know that Allah is One without any partner and He is Omnipotent over everything.",
  6076:
      "So, when the darkness of the night came, he saw a star and said: This is my Lord, but when it disappeared, he said: I do not like that which disappears because the One worthy of worship is always present and never disappears.",
  6077:
      "When he saw the moon appear, he said: This is my Lord. But when it disappeared, he said: If Allah does not guide me to His Oneness and His worship, I will undoubtedly become of those who are distant from the true religion.",
  6078:
      "When he saw the sun rising, he said: This thing that is rising is my Lord. It is bigger than the star and the moon. But, still, when it disappeared, he said: O my people, I disassociate myself from what you associate as partners with Allah.",
  6079:
      "When they asked him what he worshiped after disavowing what they worshiped besides Allah, he replied: \n I have sincerely devoted my religion to Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth without precedent, inclining away from polytheism towards pure monotheism. I am not one of the polytheists who worship others besides Allah.",
  6080:
      "His people, who were polytheists, argued with him concerning Allah's Oneness (may He be Exalted). They threatened him with their idols. He asked them: Do you argue with me concerning Allah's Oneness and worshipping Him alone when my Lord has guided me to it? I do not fear your idols because they do not possess the ability to harm or benefit me except if Allah wills. Whatever He wills happens. Allah's knowledge encompasses everything; nothing in the earth or heavens is hidden from Him. Are you not mindful, O my people, of your disbelief and associating partners with Allah instead of believing in Him alone?",
  6081:
      "How can I fear the idols you worship besides Allah when you have no fear of associating partners with Allah with things that He created while not having any proof for doing so? Which of the two groups, the monotheists or the polytheists, is more deserving of safety and security? If you know which group is more deserving, then follow that group. The more deserving group is undoubtedly the believers who are monotheists.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Abraham’s debate with his community demonstrate true nature of Allah, His oneness, Lordship and Divinity.\n2. It is permissible to debate and use logical arguments against one’s opponent.\n3. It is permissible to put forward arguments that agree with the convictions of an opponent and then use them to make the opponent return to given facts, which are accepted as proceeding from that point, to establish matters of faith.",
  6082:
      "Those who believe in Allah, follow what He has legislated, and do not mix their belief with polytheism will be the only ones who will be safe and secure. They are guided. Their Lord directed them to the path of guidance.",
  6083:
      "The argument, which is the statement of Allah: \"Which of the two groups is more deserving of safety and security...?\" which Abraham used to defeat his people in debate, is Our argument, which We showed and gave to him to use against his people. We raise in ranks whoever of Our slaves We will in this world and the Hereafter. Your Lord, O Messenger, is Wise in His creation and planning, and He knows all about His slaves.",
  6084:
      "We provided Abraham with his son Isaac and his grandson Jacob (peace be upon them), guiding all of them to the straight path. Before them, We guided Noah to the path of truth, and from the descendants of Noah, We guided David, his son Solomon, Job, Joseph, Moses, and his brother Aaron (peace be upon them). Just as We reward the prophets for doing good, We will similarly reward all those, besides the prophets, who do good.",
  6085:
      "Similarly, We guided Zechariah, John, Jesus, the son of Mary, and Elijah (peace be upon them). All these prophets were of the righteous, who Allah chose to be messengers.",
  6086:
      "Similarly, We guided Ishmael, Elisha, Jonah, and Lot (peace be upon them). We favored all of them, with Muhammad being the best of them, over all the people of their time.",
  6087:
      "We also guided some of their forefathers, descendants, and brothers, whom We had willed to guide. We selected them and guided them to tread the straight path: the path of Allah's Oneness and obedience.",
  6088:
      "They received Allah's guidance, which He grants to whoever of His slaves He wills. If they had associated others as partners with Allah, their deeds would be void because associating partners with Allah nullifies righteous deeds.",
  6089:
      "Those prophets mentioned are the ones to whom We had given Books, wisdom, and prophethood. Suppose your people reject any of these things which We have given them. In that case, We have prepared other people who do not disbelieve but instead believe and hold firm onto it. They are the Muhajireen (Emigrants), the Ansar (Supporters), and all those who follow them in goodness until the Day of Recompense.",
  6090:
      "Those prophets and their forefathers, descendants, and brothers mentioned are the people of guidance, so follow and imitate them. Say, O Messenger, to your people: I do not want any reward from you for conveying this Quran. The Quran is simply an admonishment for the worlds of human beings and the jinn so that they can seek guidance to the straight and correct path through it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the virtues of monotheism is that it guarantees safety for the servant, especially in the afterlife at a time when people will be terrified. abilities.\n2. The verses establish that all the previous prophets conveyed their message through Allah’s grace and not by their\n3. All prophets are unanimous in inviting towards Allah’s oneness, despite their differences in sacred laws relating to worship.\n4. Following the prophets is a praiseworthy practice, especially with respect to the core of monotheism.",
  6091:
      "The polytheists did not revere Allah as He should be revered when they said to His Messenger, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم: Allah has not sent down any revelation to any human being. Say to them, O Messenger: Who is the One who sent down the Torah to Moses as a light and guidance for his people? The Jews put it into sheets, showing what agrees with their desires and concealing what does not, such as the description of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. You, O Arabs, were taught the Quran, which neither you nor your predecessors knew. Say to them, O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم: Allah sent it down, then leave them to their ignorance and misguidance until certainty comes to them.",
  6092:
      "And this Quran is a book that We revealed to you, O Messenger. It is a blessed book that confirms the heavenly books that preceded it so that you could warn the people of Mecca and all the people in the East and West until they are guided. Therefore, those who believe in the Hereafter believe in this Quran, practice it, and guard their prayer by maintaining its pillars, obligatory, and recommended acts during times legislated in sacred law.",
  6093:
      "No one does more wrong than the one who makes up a lie against Allah by claiming that Allah has not revealed anything to any human being, or by falsely saying that Allah had sent revelation to him when Allah did not, or by saying that he will reveal the like of the Quran that Allah has revealed. O Messenger, you would see a terrible sight if you could only see these wrongdoers afflicted by the pangs of death while the angels stretch out their hands to punish, beat, and reprimand them, saying: Give up your souls because we are here to take them. Today, you will be recompensed with a torment that will disgrace and humiliate you because of your lies against Allah by claiming prophethood, revelation, or the ability to reveal what Allah has revealed, and because of your arrogance [preventing] you from believing in His signs.",
  6094:
      "They will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Today, you have come to Us alone. Now, you do not have any wealth or leadership, and you have come to Us just as We had created you in the first place: barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. You have reluctantly left behind what We had given you in the world. Today, We do not see with you the deities you claimed will intercede for you and that they are Allah's partners in worship. All ties between you have been cut. Your false claim of their intercession and that they are Allah's partners has let you down.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Revelation of scriptures to prophets is Allah’s practice with respect to those sent with the message. The Prophet (s) is also one of them.\n2. The worst liar is the one who lies about Allah and attributes or negates something with respect to Allah without any proper evidence.\n3. Every person will be raised on the Day of Judgement alone, stripped of all positions and titles, and each will be taken to account seperately.",
  6095:
      "Allah alone is the One who splits open the seed, from which crops emerge, and the date stone, from which the date palm sprouts. He brings forth the living from the dead, just as man and all other animals are formed from sperm. He brings forth the dead from the living, just as sperm comes out of a human being and a chicken lays an egg. The One who does this is Allah, the One Who created you. How are you, polytheists, then misled from the truth despite witnessing His amazing creation?",
  6096:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) splits the light of dawn from the darkness of the night. He is the One who has made the night still, in which people can rest from the tiring and hard work of the day. He is the One who has made the sun and the moon move according to a precise calculation. That amazing creation is the determination of the Almighty, whom no one can overpower, Omniscient of what is best for His creation.",
  6097:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) is the One who created for you, O children of Adam, the stars in the sky, so that you may find your way during your travels when the routes on land and sea are unclear. We have explained the evidence and proofs that indicate Our power for people who reflect and take benefit from them.",
  6098:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) is the One who created you from a single soul, the soul of your father, Adam. He began your creation by creating your father, Adam, from clay, and then He created you from him. He also created for you a place to settle in, which is the wombs of your mothers, and a depository in which you are stored, which is the loins of your fathers. We have explained the signs to people who can understand Allah's speech.",
  6099:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) is the One who sent down rainwater from the sky, and then with it, We caused all types of vegetation to grow. From the vegetation, We produce crops and green trees, from which We produce grain packed one on top of the other, as it is found in spikes. From the spathe of the date palm comes clusters that are close to any person standing or sitting. We also brought forth grape orchards; and produced olives and pomegranates, the leaves of which are similar, but the fruit is different. Look, O people, at the fruit when it first appears and when it ripens. O people, in that there are clear proofs of Allah's power for a people who believe in Allah. Such people are the ones who will benefit from these proofs and evidence.",
  6100:
      "Yet the polytheists made the jinn partners with Allah in worship, believing that jinn could independently bring benefit and cause harm. Allah alone had created them, so He is most worthy of worship. They attributed sons to Allah, as the Jews did concerning Ezra, the Christians with respect to Jesus, and daughters as the polytheists did with respect to the angels. Allah is free and above what the people of falsehood claim about Him.",
  6101:
      "He (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) is the Creator of the heavens and the earth without precedent. How can He have a child when He has no mate? He has created everything and knows everything. Nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Using the evidence of creation and provision (creation of vegetation, its growth, transformation of its form and size and the falling of rain) to prove Allah’s oneness in His Lordship and His entitlement to divinity is something clear and apparent.\n2. Using the evidence of motion (motion within orbits and the arrangement and precision of such movement) to prove Allah’s oneness in His Lordship and His entitlement to divinity is also something clear and apparent.\n3. The verses show the misguidance and foolishness of the idolaters in worshipping the jinn.",
  6102:
      "O people, the One described with these divine attributes is your Lord. You have no lord besides Him, and no one is worthy of worship besides Him. He is the Creator of everything, so worship Him alone, as He is the only One deserving of worship and takes care of everything.",
  6103:
      "Vision cannot encompass Him, but His Vision, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, covers and encompasses all things. He is the One who is Subtle with His righteous slaves and is Aware of them.",
  6104:
      "Clear evidence and proofs from your Lord have come to you, O people. Whoever attempts to understand them and submits to them, then the benefit will return to them. Whoever is blind to them and does not try to understand and submit to them will only lead themselves to their own loss. It is not my duty to watch over you and record your deeds; I am only a messenger from my Lord. He is the One Who watches over you.",
  6105:
      "Just as We vary the evidence and proofs of Allah's Power, We also vary the verses concerning promises, threats, and admonition. However, the polytheists will say: This is not revelation; it is merely something you learned from the People of the Book before you. [And We did this] to explain the truth to the believers of the nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, as they are the ones who accept the truth and follow it.",
  6106:
      "O Messenger, follow the truth that your Lord revealed to you. There is no one worthy of worship besides Him (may He be Exalted). Do not let the disbelievers and their stubbornness occupy your heart, as their affair is left to Allah.",
  6107:
      "If Allah had willed them not to associate anyone as a partner with Him, they would not have done so. We have not made you, O Messenger, a guardian to record their deeds, nor are you in charge of them. You are only a messenger, and your duty is only to convey the message.",
  6108:
      "O believers, do not insult the idols they worship alongside Allah, even though they are insignificant and deserving of that, for then the polytheists would have the audacity to insult Allah out of ignorance of what befits Him (may He be Exalted). Just as He made their misguidance attractive to them, He made every nation's behavior, be it good or bad, seem attractive to them, so they act accordingly. Then their return on the Day of Resurrection is to their Lord, Who will inform them about what they used to do in the world, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  6109:
      "The polytheists swear by Allah with their strongest oaths: If Muhammad brings them one of the signs they suggest, they will surely believe in it. Say to them, O Messenger: I do not have signs; they are only with Allah, Who sends them down as He wills. And what will make you realize, O believers, that even if these signs come, as they suggested, they still will not believe? Instead, they will persist in their stubbornness and denial because they do not desire guidance.",
  6110:
      "We turn away their hearts and sight by preventing them from being guided to the truth, just as We prevented them from believing in the Quran the first time because of their stubbornness. We will leave them confused and wandering in their misguidance and rebellion against their Lord.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is exalted from the injustice that the belief of fatalism (jabr) entails. The verses explain that those who disbelieve or associate partners with Allah do so out of free choice.\n2. It is not within the capacity of any prophet to bring a sign (miracle) by himself, or whenever he wishes. Instead, this is a matter that rests with Allah. He alone has the ability to do this. He is Wise and determines the type of miracle and the time of its appearance.\n3. Insulting the Allahs of the idolaters is prohibited for fear of the greater evil that this may lead to, namely their responding by throwing insults at the Lord of all people.\n4. Sometimes Allah intervenes between a servant and guidance, and turns his sight and heart away from obedience, as a punishment for his choosing disbelief.",
  6111:
      "If we had responded to them by bringing what they requested and sent down the angels for them to see, made the dead speak to them and inform them of your truthfulness regarding what you brought, and gathered everything they asked for before their eyes, they would not believe in what you brought, except those whom Allah wished to guide. However, most are ignorant of this and do not turn to Allah for guidance.",
  6112:
      "And just as we tested you with the hatred of these polytheists towards you, we tried every Prophet that came before you. So we made enemies for each one of them, from the transgressors from amongst humanity and Jinn alike, each of them whispering to the other. Thus, they beautify the falsehood to deceive them. And if Allah had willed them not to do that, they wouldn't have. But Allah willed that for them as a test. So leave them and that which they fabricate of disbelief and falsehood, and do not toil over them.",
  6113:
      "And so that the hearts of those who do not accept the Hereafter may incline towards what they whisper to one another, happily accepting such things for themselves, and persist in committing the sins and wrongs they were doing.",
  6114:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists who worship others with Allah: Does it make sense for me to accept anyone other than Allah as a judge between us? For Allah is the One who has revealed the Quran, which sufficiently explains everything. The Jews, to whom I gave the Torah, and the Christians, to whom I gave the Gospel, know that the Quran has been revealed to you because the proof is found in their scriptures. So do not be of those who doubt what I revealed to you.",
  6115:
      "The Quran is the pinnacle of truthfulness in its statements and reports and the pinnacle of justice in its rulings. No one can alter His words. He is All-Hearing of His slaves' words and Omniscient; nothing is hidden from him, and He will recompense those who strive to change His words accordingly.",
  6116:
      "If you, O Messenger, were to follow most people on earth, they would mislead you from Allah's religion. Allah's way has always been that the truth is with the minority. Most people follow nothing but speculation that has no basis, and they think that those they worship will bring them closer to Allah, whereas they are utterly wrong in believing this.",
  6117:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, knows best those people who are misled from His path, and He knows best those who are rightly guided to it. Nothing of that is hidden from Him.",
  6118:
      "Eat, O people, from that which was slaughtered in Allah's name if you truly accept His clear proofs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The main goal of a servant is to follow the truth, to look for it in the ways that Allah has explained, to practise on it, to hope for the Lord’s assistance in following it and not to rely on one’s self, strength or ability.\n2. In fairness to the knowledgeable believing minority the Qur’an attributes ignorance and misguidance to the majority of creation.\n3. One of Allah’s practices amongst the creation is the existence of enemies, from amongst humans and the jinn, for the prophets and their followers because truth is recognised through falsehood which is its opposite.\n4. The Qur’an is truthful in its narrations and just in its laws. Nothing contrary to reality will be found in its narrations and nothing contrary to the truth will be found in its laws.",
  6119:
      "What prevents you, O believers, from eating what was slaughtered in Allah's name when Allah has clarified what is unlawful for you? It is, therefore, necessary for you to leave that which is forbidden unless you are forced by necessity to eat it, in which case it will be lawful. But unfortunately, many of the misguided polytheists mislead their followers with their incorrect views. They consider lawful that which Allah has made unlawful (such as the flesh of animals that died without being slaughtered), and they consider unlawful that which Allah has made lawful (such as the baḥīrah - a she-camel whose ear is cut after it gives birth to a certain number, waṣīlah - a she-camel that gives birth to one female after another, ḥāmī - a male camel stud that mates with other camels and produces a given number of offspring, etc.). Your Lord, O Messenger, knows best those who overstep His limits, and He will recompense them for their transgression.",
  6120:
      "O people, leave off committing sins openly or in secret. Those who commit sins, secretly or publicly, will be recompensed by Allah for what they did.",
  6121:
      "O Muslims, do not eat that which was not slaughtered in the name of Allah, whether the name of someone other than Allah was mentioned over it or not. Eating such forbidden food favors Allah's disobedience over His obedience. The devils whisper to their friends, filling them with doubts so they argue with you about eating carrion. If you, O Muslims, were to follow them in the doubts they present for the lawfulness of carrion, you would be equal to them in associating partners with Allah.",
  6122:
      "Is the one who was dead before receiving Allah's guidance (due to his disbelief, ignorance, and sins), and then He gave him life (by guiding him to faith, knowledge, and obedience) equal to the one who cannot leave the darkness of disbelief, ignorance, and sins, and to whom the paths have become unclear and dark? Just as polytheism, the consumption of carrion, and false arguments were made fair-seeming to these polytheists, the sins of the disbelievers were made to seem good to them so that they are recompensed for them on the Day of Resurrection with a painful punishment.",
  6123:
      "Just as what transpired with those leaders of Mecca who committed polytheism and barred others from the Way of Allah, He has placed leaders and influential people in every town who use various means and schemes to call towards the path of the Devil and oppose the messengers and their followers. Their scheming and planning will eventually harm them only, but they do not realize this due to their ignorance and their following of desires.",
  6124:
      "And when there comes to any of these leaders a verse or a sign which Allah reveals to His Prophet proving his truthfulness, they say: We will never accept this until Allah bestows upon us the Prophethood as He did to those Prophets before us. Allah refutes them by saying that He knows best who is most suitable to be appointed to carry out the mission's duties, and He only selects the finest people for prophethood and to be messengers. Therefore, these transgressors will be afflicted with disgrace and humiliation for their arrogance and rejection of the truth and with severe punishment for their scheming.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The default with respect to all things including food is permissibility. If the Sacred Law has not declared something unlawful it remains permissible.\n2. Any person who says something about religion without knowledge or calls people to something about which he does not know whether it is true or false, is a transgressor who is wronging himself and wronging others by misguiding them. The same applies to a person who issues a religious verdict without being qualified to do so.\n3. The servant must leave all wrong that will place him in sin and difficulty, whether this relates to Allah’s rights of the rights of Allah’s servants.\n4. The benefit of a believer is not restricted to himself, but extends to other people as well.",
  6125:
      "Whomever Allah wishes to guide to the right path, He opens their heart to Islam so they accept it willingly. Whomever He wishes to abandon and not guide, He makes their chest extremely narrow and unable to accept the truth, such that they become like a person climbing into the higher layers of the atmosphere while finding it increasingly difficult to breathe. Just as Allah made this extreme narrowness the condition of the person who goes astray, He will punish those who do not have faith in Him.",
  6126:
      "This religion that I have given you, O Messenger, is My straight path, in which there is no crookedness. I have made the verses and signs clear for the one who understands them.",
  6127:
      "Such people will be awarded Paradise [on the Day of Judgment], where they will be safe from harm and discomfort. Allah will be their Friend, Protector, Supporter, and Guardian. This will be their reward for the good actions they used to do.",
  6128:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the day when Allah will gather both the jinns and humanity. He will address the jinns and tell them they had misled many people and prevented them from Allah's path. Their followers from amongst humanity will say in response to their Lord: O our Lord, we benefited from one another: the jinns benefited by having human beings follow them, and the human beings benefited by using the jinns to obtain their desires. And now we have reached the term You have appointed for us: the Day of Resurrection. Allah will tell them that the Fire will be their home, where they will live eternally, except for those sinful monotheists whom Allah wills to remove from it. Your Lord, O Messenger, is Wise in His planning and handling of matters; He knows which of His slaves deserve the punishment.",
  6129:
      "Just as I gave some of the rebellious jinns the ability to mislead some people and we allowed them to influence some of the people to misguide them, I will give authority and power to every evil sinner so that they may influence other sinners, prompting them to do evil and turn them away from good. This is a just recompense for the sins they used to commit.",
  6130:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, I will address the jinns and humanity and ask them if messengers from amongst them had not come to them, reciting what Allah had revealed to them and warning them that they will meet this day, the Day of Resurrection. They will say: Of course they did. Today, we confess against ourselves that Your messengers did communicate Your message to us and told us about the meeting of this day, but we had rejected Your messengers and denied the meeting of this day. The life of the world, with its fleeting beauty, decorations, and luxuries, had deceived them, and they will bear witness against themselves that they disbelieved in Allah and His messengers in the worldly life. Yet this confession and acceptance will not be of any use to them, as the time for its usefulness would have already passed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s system with respect to misguidance and guidance is that both of these come from Him and are created and brought into existence by Him. They occur by the action of the servant by his choice after Allah’s will.\n2. Allah’s friendship and protection towards the believers is in accordance to their good actions. The more good actions they do the greater is Allah’s friendship towards them.\n3. Allah’s custom is to give authority to one wrongdoer over another, so that they urge and encourage one another towards evil and to create a dislike and aversion in his heart for good.",
  6131:
      "The reason for sending messengers to humanity and the jinns is so that no one is punished for their crimes without a messenger being sent to warn them and the invitation reaching them. I only punished a nation after sending messengers to them.",
  6132:
      "Each one of them will have ranks in accordance with their actions. The person who did a great deal of evil will not be equal to the one who did less. The followers will not be equal to those who were followed. Similarly, the reward for those who do good will be different. Your Lord is not unaware of what they used to do. Instead, He is well aware of that. Nothing of it is hidden from Him, and He will requite them for their actions accordingly.",
  6133:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, is Self-sufficient and is not in need of His slaves. He does not need them or their worship of Him. Their disbelief in Him does not harm Him. On the contrary, despite His not needing them, He is Merciful towards them. If He wished to destroy you, O disobedient slaves, He would destroy you with His punishment, and then after this, He would bring others who would have faith in Him and obey Him, just as He created you from the progeny of other people who had come before you.",
  6134:
      "O disbelievers, the resurrection, revival, reckoning, and punishment you are promised will most certainly happen. You cannot escape from your Lord by running away: He will seize and punish you.",
  6135:
      "Say, O Messenger: O my people, remain on your path of disbelief and misguidance if you choose, as I have fulfilled my obligation having established the evidence against you by communicating the message to you. I am, therefore, not concerned about your disbelief and misguidance. Instead, I will remain firm on the path of truth I follow. Soon, you will come to know who will be victorious in this world and inherit the Earth and who will receive the home of the Afterlife. The polytheists will not succeed either in this world or the Afterlife. Their end result will be a loss even though they may have some enjoyment in the world.",
  6136:
      "The polytheists innovated and made false claims in their religion concerning Allah by assigning a share of the crops and livestock that He created to Him and giving the other share to their idols. Yet the share they give to their partners does not reach those avenues which Allah requires them to be spent in, such as on the poor and needy. But what they gave to Allah reaches the idols and is spent on them. How evil their judgment and distribution are!",
  6137:
      "Just as the Devil made this unfair judgment fair-seeming to the polytheists, the devils – who were their partners and associates – made it seem good to them that they should kill their children out of the fear of poverty. The devils inspired them with this to destroy them by committing the act of murder, which Allah had made unlawful, and to make their religion confusing for them such that they did not know anymore what Allah had commanded or prohibited for them. If Allah had willed them not to do this, they would not have done so. However, He willed it out of His wisdom. So leave, O Messenger, these polytheists and their fabrications about Allah because that will not harm you, and entrust their matter to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The various levels of the creation with respect to acts of sin and obedience requires that their ranks with respect to the levels of punishment and reward also be different.\n2. Allah rightly condemned the idolaters because of seven characteristics that they possessed: loss, foolishness, ignorance, making unlawful what Allah provided, fabricating against Allah, misguidance and not following the right path.",
  6138:
      "The polytheists said that certain animals and crops were prohibited, and only certain people may eat of them, such as those who worship the idols and others, according to their flawed thinking and fabrication. They also said that the backs of certain animals were forbidden and that no one could ride or carry a load on those animals. Then they claimed that the name of Allah must not be mentioned over certain animals at the time of slaughter and the names of idols must be taken instead. They falsely attributed all of this to Allah. Allah will requite them with His punishment because of what they made up about Him.",
  6139:
      "They said: The fetus in the wombs of these reserved animals, if born alive, is permitted for our males and forbidden to our women. But, if it is stillborn, the males and females will share in it. Therefore, Allah will justly requite them for this statement. He is Wise in His sacred laws and in handling the affairs of His creation, and He knows full well about them.",
  6140:
      "Those who killed their children due to their foolishness and ignorance and made unlawful the animals that Allah provided for them, falsely attributing this to Allah, are ruined. This is because they have strayed from the straight path and are not guided to it.",
  6141:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is the One who created gardens raised above the ground through stems and trellises and spread out gardens on the surface of the Earth without any stems. He is the One Who made the date palm. He produced crops that differed in their shape and taste. He is the One Who created the olive and the pomegranate, the leaves of which are similar, but their fruit is different. Eat, O people, from its fruit when it bears fruit and pay its Zakat on the day of its harvest. Do not overstep the limits of the sacred law concerning eating and spending because Allah does not love those who exceed His limits in this and other respects. Instead, He hates such people. The One Who created all of this is the One Who has made it lawful for His slaves. Therefore, the polytheists have no right to declare it unlawful.",
  6142:
      "He is the One who produced some animals for you that are suitable for carrying loads (such as large camels) and other animals not suitable for that purpose (such as small camels, goats, and sheep). Eat, O people, of the permissible things that Allah has provided for you, and do not follow the footsteps of the Devil by considering as lawful what Allah has forbidden and making unlawful what Allah has permitted, as the polytheists do. O people, the Devil is your clear enemy as He wants you to oppose Allah by doing so [by making lawful that which is unlawful and vice verse].\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Ones own desires are the cause for making unlawful what Allah has permitted and considering as lawful what Allah has forbidden.\n2. Zakat is due on crops and fruit when they are harvested. It is permissible to eat of them before paying the Zakat and this will not be included in the Zakat.\n3. It is allowed to enjoy pure things without wastage and without overstepping the limits with respect to eating and spending.\n4. Satan is man’s enemy and he must not be followed in his instructions and prohibitions.",
  6143:
      "He created eight types for you: two types of sheep, male and female, and two types of goats. Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists: Did Allah make the two males unlawful because of their being male? If they say yes, ask them: Why do you regard the females as unlawful? Or did He make the two females unlawful because of their being female? If they say yes, ask them: Why do you regard the males as unlawful? Or did He make what the wombs of the two females contain unlawful because of being contained in the womb? If they say Yes, ask them: Why do you differentiate between what the wombs contain by making the male unlawful sometimes and making the female unlawful at other times? Tell me, O polytheists, what proper knowledge do you base this on if you are truthful in your claim that the prohibition for this is from Allah?",
  6144:
      "The remainder of the eight types are two types of camels, male and female, and two types of cattle, male and female. Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists: Did Allah make any of them unlawful due to their being male or female or due to being contained in the womb? Were you, O polytheists, present when Allah gave the instruction for the prohibition of the animals that you regard as unlawful, according to your claim? There is no greater transgression and offense than a person who makes up lies about Allah by attributing to Him the prohibition of that which He has not prohibited to mislead people from the straight path without any basis. Allah does not guide those who do wrong by making up lies about Allah to the right path.",
  6145:
      "Say, O Messenger: I do not find in what Allah has revealed to me anything forbidden except that which dies without being properly slaughtered, blood that is flowing, the meat of a pig – for that is impure and unlawful – or that which is slaughtered in the name of other than Allah (such as animals slaughtered in the name of idols). Whoever is forced by necessity to eat these forbidden things due to extreme hunger, without seeking enjoyment by eating them and without exceeding the limit of need and necessity, there will be no sin on him in that. Your Lord, O Messenger, is Forgiving towards the person who is compelled to eat from that and is Compassionate towards such a person.",
  6146:
      "When Allah mentions what He has forbidden upon this nation, He mentions what He forbade for the Jews. This was to demonstrate that the polytheists forbidding livestock was not based on anything that came from Allah, but rather what Satan dictated to them, stating: \n We made unlawful for the Jews animals whose toes were not separated (such as camels and ostriches). We also made the fat of cattle and sheep unlawful, except for what was attached to their backs or on their intestines or what was mixed with the bone (such as the rump or flank). We recompensed them for their disobedience by making these things unlawful for them. We are truthful in all that we relate.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses indicate to the validity of debate with respect to matters of knowledge and the validity of the use of reasoning and analogical deduction.\n2. Revelation and what is inferred from it is the method to recognise the lawful and the unlawful.\n3. It is wrong for a person to issue a verdict with respect to a religious matter unless he is reasonably sure that the verdict he issues is correct and will please Allah.\n4. It is the mercy of Allah towards His servants that He permits them to consume things which are forbidden at the time of necessity.\n5. All forbidden things are dirty and impure, and they are of the filthy things which Allah has made unlawful for His servants in order to protect and honour them.\n6. One of the objectives of the sacred laws is to take into consideration religious and worldly interests and to guard the interests of the individual and that of society.",
  6147:
      "If they deny you, O Messenger, and do not accept what you brought from your Lord, tell them to encourage them: Your Lord is One, The Possessor of vast mercy. Because of His mercy, He has given you relief and has not taken you to task by punishing you. Also, say to them as a warning: His punishment is not averted from those who commit sins.",
  6148:
      "The polytheists will say, using Allah's will and decree as proof for their associating partners with Him: If Allah had willed that we and our ancestors did not associate any partners with Him, we would not have done so; and if He had willed that we do not make anything unlawful for ourselves, we would not have done so. Those before them also denied their messengers with similar worthless proofs, saying: If Allah had willed that we do not prohibit them, we would not have done so. So they persisted in denying it until they tasted the punishment I sent down on them. Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Do you have any evidence indicating that Allah is pleased that you associate others with Him and that you make lawful what He has prohibited and unlawful what He has allowed? Just because you did these actions does not mean He is pleased with them. You are following nothing but speculation with respect to this, and speculation holds no weight against the truth. You are only lying.",
  6149:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists: If you only have these weak arguments, then Allah has a decisive argument against which the excuses you present hold no weight and before which the doubts you cling to will disappear. If Allah had willed to guide all of you to the truth, O polytheists, He would have done so.",
  6150:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists who make unlawful what Allah has allowed and who claim that it is Allah who has made it unlawful: Bring your witnesses to testify that Allah has made these things unlawful. If they testify without any knowledge that Allah has made these things unlawful, then do not believe their testimony, O Messenger, because it is false testimony. Do not follow the desires of those who let their desires rule over them. They denied His verses when they made unlawful what Allah had allowed. Do not follow those who do not have faith in the Afterlife and who associate others with their Lord. How can a person who deals with his Lord in this way be followed?",
  6151:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the people: Come! I will read to you what Allah has made unlawful. He has made it unlawful that you associate any creation as a partner to Him, disobey your parents for it is your duty to be good to them, and kill your children due to poverty as the people during the period of ignorance used to do. I provide for you and for them. He has also made it unlawful that you go near immoral acts, whether done openly or in secret and that you kill the soul that Allah has prohibited you from killing unless it is done rightfully (such as in the case of adultery and apostasy). He has instructed you with what was mentioned so that you understand Allah's instructions and prohibitions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses contain a warning against offences that lead to Allah’s punishment because Allah’s punishment, when He wills it, will not be averted from those who are guilty.\n2. An argument must be based on knowledge and proof. If it based merely on speculation that holds no weight against the truth it is not valid.\n3. Using the Divine decree as an argument for disobedience after Allah has given mankind free will is clearly wrong and based on stubbornness.\n4. The verses indicate that a servant will carry out Allah’s instructions in proportion to his or her understanding.\n5. The prohibition of going near immoral acts is more profound than the prohibition of committing them because it includes a prohibition of those things that lead to those acts as well.",
  6152:
      "He has prohibited you from dealing with the wealth of orphans – those who lose their father before maturity – until they become mature and are considered to be sensible unless you do so in a manner that brings benefit and an increase in that wealth. He has also prohibited you from cheating in weights and measures; instead, you must be fair and just when taking or giving anything in a transaction. He does not burden a soul more than it can bear, and you will not be taken to task for any increase or decrease in the measure that is unintentional. He has, likewise, prohibited you from saying that which is false when relating an incident or giving testimony, displaying unfair preference to a relative or friend. He has, too, prohibited you from breaking Allah's pledge. If you make a pledge with Allah or in Allah's name, then such pacts must be fulfilled. Allah has instructed you with the above in the hope that you would ponder over the outcomes of your actions.",
  6153:
      "He has prohibited you from following the paths of misguidance. You are required to follow Allah's straight path, in which there is no crookedness. The path of misguidance will lead you far away from the path of truth. Allah instructs you to follow the straight path in the hope that you will become mindful of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding what He has prohibited.",
  6154:
      "After all this, We relate to you that We gave the Torah to Moses as a completion of our favor and a reward for his good actions, to clarify that which is required in the religion, and as a mercy in the hope that they would have faith in the meeting with their Lord on the Day of Resurrection and prepare for it with good actions.",
  6155:
      "This Quran is a book that We have revealed, and it is full of blessings due to the religious and worldly benefits contained within. So follow what is revealed in it, and be mindful of going against it in the hope that you will be shown mercy.",
  6156:
      "This Book was revealed so that you, polytheists, do not say: Allah only revealed the Torah and the Gospel to the Jews and the Christians before us, and He did not reveal any scripture to us. I do not know how to read their scriptures as they are in their language, not ours.",
  6157:
      "Likewise, I sent this Book so that you do not say: If Allah had revealed scripture to us, just as He did to the Jews and Christians, we would have been more upright than them. So now Allah has revealed the Book to your Prophet, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, in your language: a clear proof, guidance, and mercy for the entire nation. So then, do not offer false excuses and give invalid reasons for rejecting it. Undoubtedly, the greatest wrongdoer is the person who denies Allah's revealed verses and turns away from them. Allah will punish those who turn away from His words with severe punishment by causing them to enter the Fire as recompense for turning away and ignoring them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is not permissible to transact in the wealth of orphans except within the limits of their best interests. Their wealth will only be given to them once they reach the age of discernment.\n2. All orders of the sacred law, out of Allah’s Mercy, are only charged according to ones ability.\n3. Judges are required to be fair between disputants.\n4. It is Allah’s responsibility to provide sustenance for His creatures.\n5. The paths of misguidance are many but it is only Allah’s path that leads to salvation.\n6. False excuses and weak arguments will never be of benefit to those who make use of them.",
  6158:
      "O Messenger, those who deny the truth are not waiting for anything but for the angel of death and his assistants to come to them to take away their souls in this world or for their Lord to come in the Hereafter on the Day of Separation, the day when decisions regarding reward and punishment, in order to make the final decision about them; or for some of your Lord's signs to come that indicate the approach of the Final Hour. On the day when some of your Lord's signs come – such as the rising of the sun in the West – the faith of a disbeliever will not be of any benefit to him, nor will the good action of a believer who did not do good previously be of benefit to him. Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists who deny this: Wait for one of these things; I am also waiting.",
  6159:
      "O Messenger, you have nothing to do with those Jews and Christians who divided their religion by taking a part of it and leaving out another part and dividing themselves into various sects. You are free from the misguidance that they adopt. Your duty is only to warn them. Their matter is entrusted to Allah, and then, on the Day of Judgment, He will tell them about what they used to do in the worldly life and requite them for that.",
  6160:
      "Whoever of the believers brings a good action on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will multiply it for them ten times. Whoever brings an evil action will only be punished with its equivalent amount, and not more than that. On the Day of Resurrection, they will not be wronged by a reduction in the reward of good actions, nor by an increase in the punishment for evil actions.",
  6161:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists who are in denial: My Lord has guided me to a straight path: the path of the religion that maintains the interests of this world and the Afterlife. It is the faith of Abraham, who was inclined to the truth and who was never one of those who associated others with Allah.",
  6162:
      "Say, O Messenger: My prayer and sacrifice is for Allah and in His name, not for anyone else. My life and death are only for Allah, the Lord of all creation; no one else has any share in that from me.",
  6163:
      "He (may He be Exalted) has no partner. There is no one else worthy of worship besides Him. Therefore, Allah has instructed me to accept this pure monotheism, and I am the first of those who acknowledge Him from amongst this nation.",
  6164:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Shall I search for someone other than Allah as a Lord when He (may He be Exalted) is the Lord of everything? He is the Lord of those things that you worship besides Him. Therefore, no innocent person will bear the sin of another. Your return will be to your Lord alone on the Day of Resurrection, and He will inform you about religious matters that you used to differ about when you were in the life of this world.",
  6165:
      "Allah is the One who made you the successors of those who came before you on Earth so that you inhabit it after them. He has raised some of you in rank over others – in terms of physical form, livelihood, and other aspects – to test you through what He has given you. Your Lord, O Messenger, is quick in delivering justice, so everything that is approaching is close. He is also Forgiving and Compassionate towards those of His slaves who repent to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Religion demands unity and solidarity, and prohibits disunity and division.\n2. Procrastination in doing good deeds is not permissible as the time for doing good may suddenly end by death or by the appearance of the major signs of the Day of Rising.\n3. Allah’s perfect justice and kindness is that He repays an evil deed with its like and a good deed with ten times its like, which is the minimum that it may be multiplied.\n4. The true and proper religion requires that all religious activities must be performed for Allah. The servant must turn only to Him in his prayer, worship, rites, sacrifices and all acts of good in his life, as well as the bequests he makes to be carried out after his death.",
  7000:
      "The Heights (Surah Al-A'raf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nTriumph of truth in its struggle against falsehood, and mentioning consequences for the arrogant in this world and the Hereafter.\n•    Explanation:",
  7001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm Sād – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  7002:
      "The noble Quran is a scripture revealed by Allah to you, O Prophet, so do not let there be any distress or doubt in your heart regarding it. He revealed it to you to warn people by it, for you to establish the proof by it, and to remind those who have faith through it because it is they who benefit from being reminded.",
  7003:
      "Follow, O people, the Scripture that your Lord has revealed to you and the traditions of your Prophet. Do not follow the desires of those whom you think are your friends and protectors amongst the devils or evil scholars, turning to them instead and leaving what was revealed to you because of your desires. How little do you remember! If you had remembered, you would not have preferred falsehood over the truth, and you would have followed what your Messenger came with, acting in obedience to it and leaving anything besides it.",
  7004:
      "How many a city has Allah destroyed through His punishment because they persisted in their disbelief and their misguidance? Allah sent His punishment down on them in their obliviousness at night or during the day: they could not do anything to avoid the punishment, and their false gods could do nothing to protect them from it.",
  7005:
      "All they could do when the punishment came down to them was admit that they had done wrong by disbelieving in Allah.",
  7006:
      "Allah will undoubtedly question the communities He sent messengers to on the Day of Resurrection about how they received the messengers. Also, He will undoubtedly ask the messengers whether they delivered what they were instructed to deliver and how their communities responded to them.",
  7007:
      "Allah will inform everyone about what they did in the life of this world through His knowledge because He was always aware of whatever they did. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He was never, at any point, absent from them.",
  7008:
      "The weighing on the Day of Resurrection of what they did will be with justice, with no one being wronged in the least. Those whose good actions weigh more than their bad actions have succeeded in reaching the goal and being saved from what they feared.",
  7009:
      "Those whose bad actions weigh more than good ones are those who have lost themselves, attaining their destruction on the Day of Resurrection and being excluded from eternal bliss because they rejected Allah's signs and verses.",
  7010:
      "Allah certainly established you, O children of Adam, on the earth and gave you the means of making a living. You should be thankful to Allah for that, yet you show little gratitude.",
  7011:
      "O people, Allah created your father, Adam, making him in the best form and design. Then He commanded the angels to prostrate to him, honoring him, so they did so; all of them prostrated, except for Iblis (Satan), who refused to prostrate out of arrogance and stubbornness.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the aims of the revelation of the Qur’an is to warn the disbelievers and proud ones, as well as to serve as a beneficial reminder for the believers.\n2. Allah revealed the Qur’an to the believers so that they would follow it and act according to it. If they do this the formation of their good character will be perfected, and the blessing upon them will be complete, and they will be guided to the best of deeds and good character.\n3. The weighing of the deeds of people on the day of Judgement will be with justice and fairness, without any injustice or wronging anyone.\n4. Allah made the earth for humanity so that they could benefit from it, build on it, cultivate it and extract what was in it for their benefit.",
  7012:
      "Allah asked Satan, rebuking him: What stopped you from following My command to prostrate to Adam? Satan replied: What prevented me is that I am better than Adam as You created me from fire and Adam from clay, and fire is better than clay.",
  7013:
      "Allah told Satan: Go down from Paradise because it is not appropriate for you to be arrogant in it, as it is a place for those who are good and pure-hearted. You are, O Satan, disgraced and humiliated, even though you consider yourself superior to Adam.",
  7014:
      "Satan said to Allah: O my Lord, give me relief until the Day of Resurrection so that I can tempt and misguide whomsoever I wish from the children of Adam.",
  7015:
      "Allah told Satan: You, O Satan, are given respite till the first blast of the trumpet when all created beings will die, and the Creator alone will remain.",
  7016:
      "Satan said: Because You have made me fall into error and misguidance as I did not follow Your command to prostrate to Adam, I will surely sit in wait for the children of Adam who will be upon Your straight path, to turn them away and mislead them from it, just as I was misled and misguided due to me not prostrating to Adam.",
  7017:
      "Then, I will surely come to them from every direction, causing them to neglect the Afterlife and desire the life of this world, sowing in them doubts and making their low desires seem beautiful to them. And You will not find, O my Lord, most of them thankful to You because of the denial and ingratitude I will lead them to.",
  7018:
      "Allah said: Go down from Paradise, O Satan, humiliated and removed from My mercy. I will certainly fill Hell with you and all those who follow and obey you and go against My command.",
  7019:
      "Then Allah told Adam: O Adam, go and dwell you and your wife Eve in Paradise, and eat from the good things in it, but do not approach and eat from that tree, for if you both eat from that tree after I have prohibited it, you would be of those who transgress My limits.",
  7020:
      "Satan said to them a word in secret in order to expose that which had been covered from their Awrah (the private areas) and said: Allah has only forbidden you from eating from that tree because He does not want you to become angels or to live eternally in Paradise.",
  7021:
      "Satan swore to them, saying: By Allah, I am to you both, O Adam and Eve, a sincere advisor in what I direct you to.",
  7022:
      "So, the Devil brought them down from their high position through trickery and deception. When they ate from the tree they had been forbidden to eat from, their private parts became exposed and visible to them. So they started fixing leaves from Paradise onto themselves to cover up. Their Lord called to them: Did I not forbid you both from eating from this tree, and did I not warn you that the Devil is your clear enemy?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Iblis was the first to draw an incorrect analogy and went far astray.\n2. The verses show that whoever goes against their Lord is made lowly.\n3. Allah’s response to Iblis, giving him time, was actually an announcement of something that had already taken place, and not a response to his request, because he is too contemptible to have his request answered.\n4. Satan announced his enmity towards the children of Adam, and promised to prevent them from following the straight path in every means and every way.\n5. Whoever is like Adam, through acknowledging, asking for forgiveness, regretting and giving up wrongdoing if they have sinned, their Lord will choose them and guide them.\n6. Whoever is like Satan when he sins, by persisting in it and being stubborn, they will only increase in distance from Allah.",
  7023:
      "Adam and Eve said: O our Lord! We have wronged ourselves by doing what You forbade us from. Surely, if You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we will be amongst the losers, losing our share of the worldly life and the Hereafter.",
  7024:
      "Allah told Adam, Eve, and Satan: Go down from Paradise to the Earth, where some of you will be enemies of others, and where you would have a place to settle, enjoying what is on the Earth until an appointed time.",
  7025:
      "Allah addressed Adam and Eve and their descendants: On this Earth, you will live for the length of time that I decree for you, and on this Earth, you will die. After being buried, you will be taken out from your graves and brought back to life.",
  7026:
      "O children of Adam, Allah made for you clothing necessary for covering your state of undress, and clothing for you to adorn yourselves with, and the clothing of Taqwa (Being mindful of Allah and fearing him), which is through following what Allah instructs and staying away from what He has not allowed, which is better than the physical types of clothing. Therefore, what is mentioned here about clothing is from among the signs of Allah, showing His power over everything so that people may remember His blessings to them and be thankful for them.",
  7027:
      "O children of Adam, do not let the Devil deceive you by making disobedience look beautiful to you, making you leave covering your state of undress with clothing, or leave the clothing of Taqwa (Being mindful of Allah and fearing him). Do not be deceived as he tricked your parents, making eating from the tree seem good to them, and the result of that was that he got them expelled from Paradise, and their nakedness became clear to them. The Devil and his tribe watch and see you, while you cannot see or watch them, so always be on your guard against him and his tribe. Allah made the devils friends and helpers of those who do not have faith in Allah. As for those who have faith and do good, the devils have no way against them.",
  7028:
      "If the polytheists commit an indecent act, they defend it, saying they found their fathers doing it and Allah commanded them to do it. Tell them, O Muhammad: Indeed Allah does not command that which is wrong; rather, He forbids it, so how can you claim such a thing about Him? Or are you, O polytheists, inventing things about Allah and saying about Him that which you do not know?",
  7029:
      "Say O Muhammad: Indeed, my Lord commands justice, not indecency or sin. And He commands loyalty to Him in worship in general, and particularly in places of worship, that you call on Him alone, sincere in your dedication to Him. As He created you from nothing the first time, He will bring you back to life a second time. He Who is able to create you in the first place is able to bring you back to life.",
  7030:
      "Allah made people into two groups: one group of them He guided, making it easy for them to find guidance and removing the barriers to it; and another He made go astray from the path of truth because they made the devils their friends and helpers instead of Allah, ignorantly becoming bound to them, considering themselves to be correctly guided to a straight path.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There are two types of clothing: outer clothing that covers a person’s body parts that should be covered; and inner clothing, which is Mindfulness, and it is to be a permanent characteristic of the servant, as in beauty of the heart and the soul.\n2. Many of the helpers of Satan call for the removal of outward clothing to reveal the parts of the body which should be covered, making it easy for people to do reprehensible things and to commit immorality.\n3. The commands and prohibitions of sacred law are based on perfect wisdom and contain the best interests of humanity.\n4. Guidance is by Allah’s grace; and misguidance is by His forsaking someone who Satan takes control of, so that he acts with ignorance and disobedience, which causes his own misguidance.",
  7031:
      "O children of Adam, wear clean, pure, beautiful clothes that cover your nakedness when you pray and when you circumambulate around the Kaaba. Eat and drink whatever you like from the good things that Allah has allowed. But do not be extravagant in this, nor go beyond what is allowed. Allah does not love those who go beyond the limits.",
  7032:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists who forbid what Allah has allowed of clothing and food: Who has forbidden you from wearing clothes as adornment, and who has forbidden you from eating the good things I have provided you to eat and drink? Say to them, O Messenger: These good things to eat, drink, and wear are for the believers in this world. While others may share in them in this world, they are exclusively for the believers on the Day of Resurrection when the disbelievers will not have a share in them because they have been forbidden Paradise. Allah makes His signs and verses clear in this way for people who reflect because it is they who benefit from them.",
  7033:
      "Say, O Messenger, to inform the polytheists who have forbidden what Allah has allowed: Indeed Allah has only forbidden lewd, indecent acts done openly or secretly, all forms of disobedience, and transgressing unjustly against people with regards to their selves, wealth, or honor. And He has forbidden worshipping others with Him – for which there is no proof to do so. And He has prohibited you from saying things about Him without knowledge regarding His Names, Attributes, Actions, and Sacred Law.",
  7034:
      "For every generation and people, there is an appointed time. If their decreed time arrives, they cannot delay it, even by a small amount, and they cannot move it forward either.",
  7035:
      "O children of Adam, if messengers from amongst you come to you from Allah, reciting what Allah has revealed from His Scripture to them, then follow them and what they bring. Those who are mindful of Allah by complying with His commands, staying away from His prohibitions, and setting their deeds right will have no fear upon them on the Day of Resurrection and will not grieve about the pleasures that passed them by in this world.",
  7036:
      "As for the disbelievers who reject Allah's signs, do not have faith in them, and are too arrogant to act in accordance with what their messengers bring to them, they are the dwellers of the Fire, where they will live eternally.",
  7037:
      "Who is more unjust than the person who invents a lie about Allah considering Him to have a partner, says He is deficient in some way, says something about Him that He has not said, or rejects His clear signs and verses that guide to the straight path? Those who do such things will receive the portion of worldly pleasure that is destined for them in the Preserved Tablet until the angel of death and his helpers come to them to take their souls, and they are asked: Where are the deities you used to worship besides Allah, claiming they would help you? Call on those idols if they can benefit you! The polytheists will say to the angels: The deities we used to worship have gone, and we do not know where they are! Then, they will admit that they were disbelievers, but their admission at that time will be proof against them and will not benefit them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believer is instructed to respect the rituals of Allah through covering what should be covered of the body and dressing beautifully when praying and especially when going to the mosque.\n2. From Allah’s complete concern for His creatures He made the good things permissible for them, to help them in their devotion to Allah, just as He forbade harmful things which have a negative effect in this world and in the Hereafter.\n3. The verses establish that the believers will not feel fear or sorrow on the Day of Judgement, nor will terror or panic reach them; and if they do suffer some harm, they will nevertheless be safe in the end.\n4. The greatest of wrongdoers are people who obstruct others from understanding the religion of Allah. This may happen in two ways: suppressing that which shows His Way, or deluding people into following that which is contrary to His Command.",
  7038:
      "The angels will say: Enter you, O polytheists, the Fire with the crowds of nations from the jinns and humanity who passed away before you in disbelief and error! Whenever a nation enters the Fire, it condemns its sister nation, which entered the Fire before it, until they all reach one another and are gathered together. The last of them to enter, who are the lowly people and followers, will ask concerning the previous nations who were their leaders and masters: O our Lord! These are the ones who led us astray from the proper guidance, so give them a double punishment, for they beautified for us the path of misguidance. Allah will reply to them: Each group of you will receive a doubled share of the punishment, but you do not perceive it.",
  7039:
      "The leaders and chiefs will exclaim: You do not have, O followers, over us any preference that makes you deserving of any lightening of the punishment, as it results from your own actions. You do not have any excuse for having followed what was false. So taste then, O followers, the punishment just as we taste it because of what you earned through your own disbelief and disobedience.",
  7040:
      "Those who reject Allah's clear signs and verses and are too proud to follow them have lost everything because the gates of heaven will not open to their actions because of their disbelief, nor will they open for their souls when they die. Such people will never enter Paradise until the camel – one of the largest animals – goes into the eye of a needle – one of the smallest things. The aforementioned is impossible, and so is the idea that they will ever enter Paradise. In such a way, Allah recompenses those who stubbornly do wrong.",
  7041:
      "For these people who rejected the truth because they were too arrogant, there is a bed of Hell to lie on, and above them is a covering of torment. This is how Allah recompenses those who overstep His limits by disbelieving in Him and turning away from Him.",
  7042:
      "But those who have faith in their Lord and do good actions to the best of their ability – and Allah does not burden a soul with more than it can bear – are the dwellers of Paradise, entering it and living there eternally.",
  7043:
      "Their bliss in Paradise is perfected by Allah removing whatever hatred and resentment is in their hearts, with rivers flowing beneath them. When they come to live there and settle in their homes, they will exclaim while recognizing Allah's blessings on them, praising Him: All praise and thanks belong to Allah, Who allowed us to do the good actions that brought us to this place. We would not have been able to do that if Allah had not enabled us to do so. The messengers of our Lord came with the truth about which there was no doubt, true in its promises of good for the righteous and true in its threats for the wrongdoers. It will then be announced to them: This, truly this, is the Paradise that Allah has made you inherit out of His Mercy for the good actions you used to do seeking the countenance of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The friendship and closeness that was between those who denied the truth in this world will turn into hatred and condemnation on the Day of Judgement.\n2. The doors of heaven will be opened to the souls of the believers dedicated to the command of Allah, trusting His signs, until they ascend to Allah, and rejoice in the nearness to their Lord, and the position of favour with His pleasure.\n3. The doors of heaven will not open to the souls of those who denied the truth, who turn away. When they die they rise up to the heavens and ask for permission to ascend but are not given it. They did not rise in the worldly life to have faith in Allah, and to know Him and love Him, so they also do not rise after death. Ultimately they will only reap what they sowed.\n4. The people of Paradise are saved from the fire of Hell by Allah’s pardon, and enter Paradise with Allah’s mercy. Though they share the ranks given to them according to their good actions, which is also from His Kindness and of the highest expressions of His Mercy.",
  7044:
      "The dwellers of Paradise will call unto the dwellers of the Fire when they have all entered their places, saying: Indeed we have found what our Lord promised us about Paradise to be true, as we have entered into it. Have you found what Allah promised you about the Fire to be true? The disbelievers will reply: We have found what was promised about the Fire to be true. Then, a caller will proclaim that the wrongdoers be removed from Allah's mercy because the doors of His mercy were open to them, and they turned away from them in their worldly life.",
  7045:
      "These wrongdoers used to turn away from Allah's religion and used to turn others away from it, wanting to make the path of truth seem crooked so that people would not follow it. They also rejected the Afterlife, neither believing in nor preparing for it.",
  7046:
      "Between these two groups – the dwellers of Paradise and the dwellers of the Fire – is a partition called al-A'rāf (the Heights). On this partition are people whose good and bad actions are equal. They know the dwellers of Paradise by their signs, such as the light on their faces, and the dwellers of the Fire by their signs, such as the darkness on their faces. These people of the partition call to the companions of Paradise, honoring them, saying: Peace be upon you. They will not have entered Paradise yet but hope to enter it through Allah's mercy.",
  7047:
      "When their eyes turn to the people who are the people of the Fire, and they see the severe punishment they are afflicted with, they pray: O our Lord! Do not put us with the wrongdoers who disbelieved and worshipped others besides you!",
  7048:
      "The people of the Heights will call to people in the Fire who had disbelieved, whom they recognize by their marks, such as the darkness of their faces and the blue shade of their eyes: Your gathering of wealth and men did not benefit you in the slightest, nor did arrogantly turning away from the truth.",
  7049:
      "Allah will say, rebuking the disbelievers: Are these faithful people those you swore Allah would not show mercy to? Then, these people who have faith will be told to enter Paradise, not fearing what awaits them and not grieving over the pleasures of the world that passed them by because of the eternal bliss they find themselves in.",
  7050:
      "The dwellers of the Fire will call unto the dwellers of Paradise, begging them to pour some water or provide them with some of the food they have been given. The companions of Paradise will tell them that Allah has forbidden both of these for the disbelievers because of their disbelief and that they will not help them in what Allah has forbidden for them.",
  7051:
      "These disbelievers are the ones who used to mock and make fun of faith and were deluded by the life of this world, being engrossed in its pleasures and luxuries. On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will forget them, and they will be left to suffer the punishment because they forgot the meeting of the Day of Resurrection, which they neglected despite having full knowledge of it. They rejected Allah's signs and proofs in condemnation despite knowing and recognizing the truth of His message.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Lack of faith in the resurrection is a direct reason for following vain desires.\n2. People will realise clearly on the Day of Judgement that the promise of Allah, to those devoted to Him as well as to the disbelievers, was the absolute truth.\n3. People will be in two groups on the Day of Judgement: one group in Paradise and one group in Hell. Yet between them will be a group in the middle whose good actions and bad actions were equal on the balance. In spite of that, their ultimate destination will be Paradise.\n4. Those who possess wealth, rank, and followers, must realise that all of this will not help them in any way before Allah, and will not save them from Allah’s punishment if they deserve it.",
  7052:
      "And Allah has indeed sent them this Quran, the Scripture revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, explaining it and clarifying all things with His Knowledge. It guides the believers to the right path and to the truth and is a mercy for them because of what it guides them to, of goodness in this world and in the Afterlife.",
  7053:
      "The disbelievers wait only for what they have been warned about, a painful punishment in the Afterlife as a result of their actions. The believers were also foretold about the reward of that day. Those who ignored the Quran in the life of this world, not acting according to what is in it, will then say: Indeed, the messengers of our Lord came with the truth, in which there was no doubt. If only there were a mediator who could now plead on our behalf so we could be excused from the punishment. Or if only we could return to the worldly life to do good actions that would save us instead of the bad we committed! The disbelievers have driven themselves to loss, earning their own ruin due to their disbelief. Those whom they used to worship beside Allah have abandoned them and can be of no help to them.",
  7054:
      "O people, your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens and the Earth in six days, with no precedent. He established Himself on the Throne in a way befitting His Majesty. He made the darkness of the night disappear into the light of the day and the light of the day into the darkness of night, both chasing each other quickly so that neither is delayed. He also created the sun, the moon, and the stars, all subservient under His dominion. Is the whole of creation not His? Who besides Him is the creator? His alone is the command. He is High above any flaw. He is described with the attributes of splendor and perfection- the Lord of the Worlds.",
  7055:
      "O believers, call on your Lord with complete humility, silently and in private, sincere in your prayer, not showing off, and not worshipping others along with Allah in your prayers. He does not love those who overstep the limits in their prayers, and one of the worst ways someone can do this is by invoking others besides Him, as the polytheists do.",
  7056:
      "Do not ruin things on Earth by committing sins after Allah has put it right by sending the messengers (peace be upon them) and establishing things in accordance with His laws. Instead, call on Allah alone, fearing His punishment and hoping for His reward. The mercy of Allah is truly close to those who do good, so be from among them.",
  7057:
      "It is Allah who sends the winds as good news of coming rain until they carry a cloud filled with water. He drives the cloud to a barren land and sends down rain on it, bringing out all kinds of fruits and crops. The way this vegetation is brought out is similar to how the dead will be brought out of their graves and back to life. This is, O people, so that perhaps you will then reflect on the power of Allah and the wonder of His creation and that He is able to bring the dead to life.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The noble Qur’an is a book of guidance detailing that which humanity needs, as a mercy from Allah.\n2. Allah’s promise will definitely come true, and then the disbelievers will be certain of the truth of Allah’s promise.\n3. Allah created the heavens and the earth in six days for a wisdom He willed, glory be to Him. If He had wanted He could have said to it ‘Be! ’ and it would have been created immediately.\n4. It is necessary for the believers to call upon Allah Most High with complete humility and supplication until He responds to them through His grace.\n5. Causing corruption on the earth in any way or form is forbidden.",
  7058:
      "Good land produces vegetation in abundance, by Allah's permission. Likewise, the believer understands the teachings they are given, and they benefit from them, acting accordingly with righteousness. On the other hand, the rotten, salty land only produces vegetation in small amounts, and there is little goodness in what it produces. Likewise, the disbelievers will not benefit from the true teachings they receive and will not perform good actions that benefit them. Through such variation, Allah reveals His signs and proofs in different ways to confirm the truth to people who are thankful for Allah's blessings, do not reject them, and follow their Lord.",
  7059:
      "Indeed, We sent Noah as a messenger to his people, calling them to single out Allah and leave off worshipping anything besides Him. Noah said to them: O people! Worship Allah alone; you have no deity worthy of worship except Him. I fear for you, O people, the punishment of a great day if you persist in your disbelief.",
  7060:
      "The leaders and notables among his people said: O Noah! Indeed, we think you are in clear error.",
  7061:
      "Noah told the leaders of his people: I am not in error, as you claim, but rather I am on guidance from my Lord, and I am a messenger from Him who is my Lord, your Lord, and the Lord of all creations.",
  7062:
      "I only convey to you the revelation Allah has sent me with. I only want what is good for you when I encourage you to follow what Allah has instructed and to receive the reward for doing so, and I warn you of what Allah has prohibited and the punishment you would receive for disobeying Him. I know from Allah (may He be Exalted) what you do not know because of the knowledge Allah has given to me through revelation.",
  7063:
      "Do you find it strange, O people, that revelation and good teaching has come to you from your Lord on the tongue of a man from amongst yourselves whom you know well?! I have grown up amongst you and have never been a liar or misguided, nor have I come to you from another people. I have come to warn you about the punishment of Allah so that you might comply with His commands and avoid His prohibitions, hoping that then you would receive mercy through having faith in Him.",
  7064:
      "However, Noah's people rejected him and did not have faith in Allah but continued in their disbelief. Noah, at last, asked Allah to destroy the disbelievers. Allah saved Noah and those who were with him and had faith from drowning by enabling them to retreat upon the ark. He destroyed those who rejected His signs and continued rejecting them, drowning them in a great flood as their punishment. Indeed, they were a people whose hearts were blind to the truth.",
  7065:
      "And I sent to the people of 'Ād a messenger whose name was Hūd (peace be upon him). Hūd said to them: O people! Worship Allah alone, for you have no true God except Him. Will you not then be mindful of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions so that you would be saved from His punishment?",
  7066:
      "The leaders and notables among his people who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His Messenger said: Indeed we only think of you, O Hūd, as someone foolish and backward, calling us to worship Allah alone and to leave the worship of our idols. In fact, we are certain that you are a liar in claiming that Allah has sent you!",
  7067:
      "Hūd replied: O my people, I am not foolish or backward, but I am a messenger from the Lord of the Worlds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Good earth is given as an example for good hearts; and just as rain is the substance of life, likewise, the Revelation that descends is the substance of life for the hearts. When Revelation comes to good hearts, they recognise it, accept it, and grow according to their good foundation and characteristics, and likewise the opposite is true.\n2. The prophets and messengers felt compassion for people even more than the compassion of their fathers and mothers.\n3. It is Allah’s way to send each messenger from his own people and in their language, uniting the hearts of those whose natural disposition has not been corrupted, and making recognition and understanding the religion easier.\n4. Among the greatest fools are those who reject and deny the truth, too proud to follow scholars and advisers, their heart submitting to every scheming satan.",
  7068:
      "I am only conveying what Allah had instructed me to deliver to you, that you believe in Allah's Oneness and His sacred law. I am a trustworthy adviser to you all, delivering what I am instructed, no less, no more.",
  7069:
      "Is it strange and amazing that a reminder should come to you from your Lord, from a man amongst you, and from your likeness, not through an angel or a jinn? Thank Allah and praise Him for having established you on the Earth, making you successors to the people of Noah who were destroyed because of their disbelief. Thank Allah for having favored you by making you strong in stature, and remember Allah's great blessings on you so that you may be successful, attaining what you desire and avoiding what is feared.",
  7070:
      "Hūd's people said: Have you come to tell us to worship Allah alone and to leave what our parents and ancestors worshipped? Bring us the punishment you promise if you are truthful in what you claim.",
  7071:
      "Hūd said: The punishment of Allah and His Anger is already on its way! Do you argue with me about idols you and your fathers have called gods when you have no basis for doing so since Allah has not sent down any proof of their divinity for you to use? Wait then for the punishment you ask for; I am also waiting, for indeed, it is on its way.",
  7072:
      "So Allah saved Hūd (peace be upon him) and those of the believers who were with him through Mercy from Him, and He removed and destroyed those who rejected His signs, did not have faith, and deserved their punishment because of their denial.",
  7073:
      "Then Allah sent to the tribe of Thamūd, their brother Saleh, to call them to believe in the Oneness of Allah and to worship Him alone. Saleh said: O People! Believe in Allah alone; you have no other deity worthy of being worshipped. I have come to you with a sign proving the truth of what I have brought you: namely, a camel that will come out of a rock. It has an allocated time to drink from the water, and for you, a separate time to drink has been allocated. Allow her to eat within Allah's land, and do not harm her in any way, or a painful punishment will befall you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One should show patience in calling people to Allah, following the example of the Prophets, peace be upon them.\n2. Some of the main priorities in calling people to Allah are calling them to worship Allah alone, without any partners, and to reject and dismiss associating anything with Him.\n3. Being dazzled by material and physical strength distracts one from responding to what Allah has instructed and forbidden.\n4. The prophet is like his people, but he is the most noble of them in lineage, the highest of them in rank, the best of them in society, and the highest of them in character and morals.\n5. The prophets and their inheritors meet the foolish with patience, overlooking the bad things they say with forgiveness and pardon.\n6. The result of rebelliousness, pride and tyranny is ruin and destruction.\n7. It is the custom of Allah to save the believers and destroy those who turn away.",
  7074:
      "Praise Allah for making you representatives on the Earth after the destruction of the people of 'Ād who had persevered in disbelief, and thank Him for establishing you in the land so that you could enjoy it and satisfy your desires. You build palaces in the plains and carve houses for yourselves out of the mountains. Remember Allah's blessings upon you and thank Him for them. Do not strive to cause corruption on Earth, and leave off your disbelief in Allah and your disobedience to Him.",
  7075:
      "The leaders and the important people who looked down in arrogance on the people who had faith, those they considered to be weak, asked them: Do you really know that Saleh is a messenger from Allah? The believers replied: We have sure faith in him and agree with and submit to what he has brought us.",
  7076:
      "The arrogant among his people said: Indeed we disbelieve in what you have faith in, O believers, and we will not have faith in it nor act in agreement with its sacred laws.",
  7077:
      "So they killed the camel, which they had been forbidden to harm, too proud to follow Allah's command. Doubting what Saleh had promised would happen, they mocked him, saying: O Saleh! Bring the painful punishment you have told us would afflict us if you really are a messenger from Allah!",
  7078:
      "When the punishment the disbelievers had asked for arrived, they were taken by a great earthquake so that they lay fallen in the morning, their faces and knees on the Earth, none escaping from the destruction.",
  7079:
      "Saleh (peace be upon him) turned away from his people, having given up all hope for them. He said: O people, I had delivered what Allah had instructed me to deliver to you and had advised you well, encouraging you and warning you, but you were a people who did not have any love for sincere advisers who wanted to lead you to goodness and distance you from evil.",
  7080:
      "And remember when Lot denounced his people, saying: Do you commit such a forbidden and shameful act as sodomy when no one before you has committed such a crime!",
  7081:
      "Do you go to men to satisfy your lust instead of women, who you were supposed to go to?! Then, in that case, you have not followed any sense or any sound report or even what is natural! Rather, you have gone beyond the limits of Allah, overstepping the bounds of moderation, good sense, and the natural nobility of humanity.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride often comes from having a lot of wealth or high rank, while having little wealth and position often leads to faith and trust and devotion.\n2. It is permissible to build great buildings, such as palaces and the like, because beautiful buildings, alongside gratitude to the Giver of blessings, are from the signs of divine bounty.\n3. For the most part when the Prophets call people to Allah the weak and the poor rush to listen to the words of truth which they bring, while the nobles and leaders are insolent and think themselves above it.\n4. The punishment of Allah can fall upon the whole society, including good people, if there is a great deal of evil in it and a lack of condemnation of it.",
  7082:
      "His people, who committed this shameless act they had been forbidden from doing, only responded by turning away from the truth, saying: Drive Lot and his followers out of your city. They are a people who have kept away from this action of ours, so it is not befitting that they stay living here among us.",
  7083:
      "So Allah saved Lot and his family by instructing them to leave the city by night. His family was saved except for his wife, who remained behind in the city and suffered the same punishment as the rest.",
  7084:
      "And we sent down upon them a great rain of rocks of baked clay, overturning the city and turning it upside down. So consider what the end of the sinful people of Lot was. Their end was ruin and eternal disgrace.",
  7085:
      "To the tribe of Midian, Allah sent their brother Shuayb (peace be upon him). He said: O people! Worship Allah alone, for you have no deity worthy of worship other than Him. A clear proof from Allah has come to you confirming what I bring to you from your Lord is the truth. Give people their rights by measuring and weighing things correctly, not short-changing people by saying bad things about their goods or by cheating them, and do not cause corruption on Earth through disbelief and disobedience after things have been set right through the sending of prophets. All of this is better for you and more beneficial if you are believers because then you would leave disobedience and draw close to Allah by doing what He has commanded.",
  7086:
      "And do not sit waiting on every road seeking to threaten the people therein to steal from their possessions and to prevent those who want to be guided to the path of Allah, wanting the path of Allah to be crooked so that people would not follow it. Remember the blessings of Allah upon you so that you might be thankful, for you had been few in the land, and He increased your numbers. Reflect on what had been the end of those who caused corruption in the Earth before you since their end had been destruction and ruin!",
  7087:
      "And if there is a group among you who believe in what I have brought from my Lord and another group who do not believe in it, then you, O deniers, should wait to see how Allah judges between the two groups. He makes the best judgments and the most just rulings.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Sodomy is an immoral act that leads to the degeneration of one’s natural disposition. It does great damage, and it has a severe punishment.\n2. The prophets’ calling people to Allah, among them Shu’ayb (peace be upon him), was based on two principles: establishing the rights of Allah, which includes recognition that there is only one Allah and the belief in prophethood; and compassion to Allah’s creation, which means not neglecting their rights, causing corrupting, or doing any type of harm.\n3. Causing corruption in the earth after things have been put right is a social crime against humanity, because putting things right on earth through correct beliefs and right behaviour is beneficial for everyone, and causing corruption on earth is a crime against people.\n4. One of the greatest and most immoral sins is to take someones belongings or property without right, for it comprises injustice, and the approving of wrong publicly.\n5. The end of those who cause corruption is disgrace and being made an example of, and for this reason it is necessary to keep away from corruption and disobedience.\n6. Knowledge alone is not enough to correct society, rather what is necessary for correcting communities and people is goodly instruction and teaching, convincing people thereby of the benefits of virtues, such as truthfulness, trustworthiness, and justice, and of the disadvantages of deviation and vices. This is because Allah-given self-restraint is stronger and greater than any legal deterrent or sanction.\n7. It is necessary for the believers to show patience until Allah helps them against the people of falsehood, making them overcome them.",
  7088:
      "The heads and leaders who were arrogant among Shuayb's people said to him: We will surely drive you, O Shuayb, out of this town of ours, you and those who have believed with you, or you will most certainly return to our religion. Shuayb said critically and in astonishment: Are we to follow your creed and religion, even if we hate it because we know the falsehood of what you are upon?",
  7089:
      "We would have invented lies about Allah if we believed in the idolatry and disbelief you are upon after Allah has saved us from it by His grace. It would not be valid or right for us to return to your false creed unless Allah, our Lord, wills us to do so, as all accede to His Will, may He be Exalted. Our Lord surrounds us with the knowledge of everything. Nothing is hidden from Him. We rely on Allah alone to make us firm on the straight path and protect us from the roads of the Inferno. O our Lord, judge between us and our disbelieving people with the truth. So help the wronged person of truth against the obstinate wrongdoer, for You, O Lord, are the best of judges.",
  7090:
      "The disbelieving heads and leaders of his people rejecting the call to Tawheed (singling out) [Allah in worship and attributes] and warning against Shuayb and his religion, said: O our people, if you enter Shuayb's religion, and leave your religion and that of your ancestors, you would indeed be surely destroyed by that.",
  7091:
      "Then, a severe earthquake seized them, so in the morning, they were destroyed in their houses, fallen to their knees and faces, dead and still in their homes.",
  7092:
      "Those who rejected Shuayb were all destroyed. It was as if they had never lived in their homes nor enjoyed themselves within them. Those who rejected Shuayb were the losers because they lost themselves and what they possessed. And the believers from his people were not the losers as these rejecting disbelievers claimed.",
  7093:
      "Their prophet Shuayb turned aside from them when they perished, and he addressed them, saying: O my people, I have delivered what my Lord instructed me to convey to you, and I sincerely gave you advice, so you did not take my advice nor yield to my guidance. How, then, can I grieve for people who disbelieve in Allah and are insistent on their disbelief?",
  7094:
      "We did not send a prophet to any town and then its inhabitants rejected and disbelieved, except that We seized them with suffering, poverty, and illness in the hope they might humble themselves to Allah and thus leave what disbelief and arrogance they were upon. This is a warning to Quraysh and all who disbelieve and reject by mentioning Allah's way with rejecting nations.",
  7095:
      "Then We replaced them, after seizing them with suffering and illness, with goodness, well-being, and security, until they numbered many, their wealth increased, and they said: What afflicted us of good and evil is a perpetual norm. It occurred to our predecessors before. They did not recognize that what afflicted them was intended to teach them a lesson, while the good they were given was meant to draw out [their punishment]. Then Allah suddenly seized them with the torment they did not sense or expect.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From the manifestations of the generosity of Allah to His righteous servants is his opening the doors of knowledge to them, through making clear what is true from what is false, and saving the believers and giving a the punishment to the disbelievers.\n2. It is the way of Allah among his servants to give them time, so that they learn lessons from events and root out whatever sins and destructive behaviour they may engage in.\n3. Many show patience when facing difficulty, and bear its hardship. As for trials caused by having great wealth, few are patient in such circumstances and remain within the limits of Allah’s sacred law.\n4. Faith and good actions cause blessings to descend from the heaven and appear on the earth upon the nation.",
  7096:
      "If the people of these towns to which We sent Our messengers had believed in what their messengers brought them and had been heedful of their Lord by abandoning disbelief and acts of disobedience and complying with His commands, then We would have opened to them the gates of goodness from every direction. But instead, they did not believe and were not heedful of Him. Instead, they rejected what their messengers came with. So We suddenly seized them with torment because of what they used to earn of sins and transgressions.",
  7097:
      "So, have the people of these rejecting towns felt safe from Our torment coming to them at night while they are asleep, deep in their rest and tranquility?",
  7098:
      "Or have they felt safe from Our torment coming to them at the beginning of the day while they are amused and unaware due to their preoccupation with their worldly life?",
  7099:
      "Look at what Allah granted them of postponement [of torment]. By it, He blessed them with strength and abundance of provision, drawing out [punishment] for them. So, have these rejecting people among the people of those towns felt safe from Allah's designs and His subtle planning? No one feels secure from Allah's plans except the perishing people. As for the successful, then indeed, they fear His designs, so they do not become deluded with what Allah bestowed upon them. They merely recognize His favor upon them, so they thank Him.",
  7100:
      "Has it not become apparent to those who follow in the earth after the destruction of their predecessors among the nations because of their sins? Then, they do not take lessons from what befell them. Rather, they did their [very same] actions. Has it not become apparent to these [people] that if Allah wanted to strike them for their sins, He certainly would have done so, as is His Way? He seals upon their hearts so they do not accept any admonishment, and no reminder benefits them.",
  7101:
      "[Regarding] those previous nations: the townships of the people of Noah, Hūd, Saleh, Lot, and Shuayb; We recite and relate their narratives to you, O Messenger, and what they were upon of rejection and stubbornness, and of the destruction that befell them. [That is] to serve as a lesson for those who accept lessons and an admonishment to those who accept admonishment. The Messengers of the people of these towns had undoubtedly come with clear proofs of their truthfulness, so when the Messengers came, those people were not to believe; that is, in regards to what preceded from Allah's knowledge that they would reject it. In the same way that Allah sealed the hearts of the peoples of these towns who rejected their messengers, Allah seals the hearts of the disbelievers in Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم so that they are not guided to faith.",
  7102:
      "In most nations to whom the messengers were sent, We did not find fulfillment and adherence to what Allah prescribed to them, and We did not find them following His commands. We merely found most of them outside of Allah's obedience.",
  7103:
      "Then, after those Messengers, We sent Moses (peace be upon him) to Pharaoh and his people with Our convincing arguments and clear evidence demonstrating his truthfulness. However, they only rejected those miracles and disbelieved in them. So reflect, O Messenger, how Pharoah and his people ended up, for Allah has destroyed them by drowning them and followed them up with curses in the world and the hereafter.",
  7104:
      "When Allah sent him to Pharaoh, and he came to him, Moses said: O Pharaoh, I am sent from the Creator of all creation, their owner and determiner of all their matters.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The strong link between the abundance of provision and Mindfulness, and if Allah give blessings to the disbelievers this is a way of leading them on and deluding them.\n2. There is no security from the sudden punishment of Allah which could come at any hour of the night or day.\n3. The Qur’an tells the stories of the people who came before to strengthen the believers and caution the disbelievers.\n4. Causing corruption on earth is one of the worst crimes, and the punishment for those who corrupt things is strong, as was the case with Pharaoh.",
  7105:
      "Moses said: Since I have been sent as a messenger from Him, it is only appropriate for me to tell the truth about Him. I have brought clear proof indicating my truthfulness and that I am indeed sent from my Lord to you. So, release the Israelites from the captivity and coercion they have been in.",
  7106:
      "Pharaoh said to Moses: If you have brought a sign, as you allege, then bring it if you are truthful in your claim.",
  7107:
      "So Moses threw his stick, and it changed into a great snake, clear for those witnessing it.",
  7108:
      "And he took and revealed his hand from the opening in his shirt near his chest or under his underarm. So it came out white, not because of vitiligo (a skin disease), radiating brilliantly to onlookers due to its extreme whiteness.",
  7109:
      "Once they witnessed the transformation of Moses's staff into a snake and his hand becoming white without vitiligo, the heads and leaders said: Moses is nothing but a sorcerer well-versed in sorcery.",
  7110:
      "By the feats he performs, he intends to drive you all out of this land of yours: Egypt. Then Pharaoh sought counsel with them regarding the matter of Moses (peace be upon him), saying to them: What opinion do you advise me with?",
  7111:
      "They said: Delay Moses and his brother Aaron and send those who would gather the sorcerers in the cities of Egypt.",
  7112:
      "Those you send to gather the sorcerers from the cities will bring you every sorcerer skilled in sorcery and proficient in his craft.",
  7113:
      "So, Pharaoh dispatched individuals to gather the sorcerers. Then, when the sorcerers came to Pharaoh, they asked him: Would there be compensation for them if they were to defeat Moses with their magic and overcome him?",
  7114:
      "So Pharaoh answered them, stating: Yes, indeed, [there is] compensation and reward for you, and you will be close [to me] in the ranks.",
  7115:
      "Trusting they would be victorious over Moses, the magicians pompously and arrogantly said: Choose, O Moses, what you wish from [either] you beginning by casting what you want, or us beginning with that.",
  7116:
      "So Moses answered them, trusting in the victory of His Lord and not worried about them: Throw your ropes and your staffs. Then, when they threw them, they bewitched the people's eyes by distorting them from their proper perception. They terrified them and came with potent sorcery in the eyes of the onlookers.",
  7117:
      "Allah inspired His prophet and conversant Moses (peace be upon him): Throw your staff, O Moses. So he threw it, then the stick changed into a snake swallowing up their ropes and staffs, which they would use to alter [appearances from] reality and deceive people that they were crawling snakes.",
  7118:
      "So the truth became apparent, and the truthfulness of what Moses (peace be upon him) came with became apparent, as well as the falsehood of the sorcery the sorcerers had performed.",
  7119:
      "So, they were defeated and routed. Moses (peace be upon him) triumphed over them in that exhibition and returned humiliated and compelled.",
  7120:
      "When the magicians witnessed the greatness of Allah's ability and saw the clear signs, they could only fall and prostrate to Him, Exalted and Transcendent is He.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From Allah’s wisdom and mercy He made the miracle of each prophet of the kind that was predominant among the people of that time, so when magic was predominant among the people of the time of Moses, peace be upon him, his miracle was similar to magic, although it was different to magic in its reality.\n2. Pharaoh was a lowly, humble, helpless servant, or he would not have needed to turn to the magicians to try and protect himself from Moses.\n3. The prostrating of the magicians to Allah and their faith in Him, glory be to Him, is a proof of the profound effect of faith in the souls of humankind.",
  7121: "The sorcerers said: We have believed in the Lord of all creation.",
  7122:
      "The Lord of Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them), for He is worthy of worship [alone] without anyone from the alleged gods.",
  7123:
      "Pharaoh said to them, threatening them after their faith in Allah alone: You believed in Moses before I have permitted you? Indeed, your faith in him and affirmation of what Moses has come with is undoubtedly a trick and scheme you and Moses planned to drive out the city's people. Then you will know, O sorcerers, what punishment will inflict you and what penalty will strike you.",
  7124:
      "I will surely cut off the right hand and left foot or the left hand and right foot of each of you. Then I will surely suspend you all upon palm trunks, making an example of you and terrifying whoever sees you in that state.",
  7125:
      "In reply to Pharaoh's threat, the sorcerers said: Indeed we will return to our Lord alone, so we are not concerned with what you threaten with.",
  7126:
      "O Pharaoh, you are not objecting and angry with us except for our belief in the signs of our Lord when they came to us at the hands of Moses. If this can be considered a sin deserving of blame, then it is our sin. They then turned to Allah in supplication, pleading: O our Lord, pour patience upon us until it engulfs us so that we be firm on the truth. Take our lives [while we are] submitting to You, yielding to Your command, and following Your Messenger.",
  7127:
      "The leaders and notables among Pharaoh's people said to Pharaoh, provoking him to act against Moses and the believers with him: Will you leave Moses and his people to spread corruption in the land, abandon you and your gods, and call to worship Allah alone? Pharaoh said: We will kill the sons of the Israelites and keep their women to serve. We will overcome them with compulsion, domination, and control.",
  7128:
      "Advising his people, Moses said: O my people, ask for assistance from Allah alone to avert harm and bring benefit to you. And be patient with the trials you are facing, for indeed, the earth belongs to Allah alone, and it does not belong to Pharaoh or anyone else for him to control it. Allah exchanges [control of it] between people according to His Will. However, the noble end on earth is for the believers who comply with the commands of their Lord and avoid His prohibitions, for it is for them despite the tests and trials that inflict them.",
  7129:
      "Moses's people from the Israelites said to Moses (peace be upon him): O Moses, we were tried at the hands of Pharaoh with the murder of our sons and preservation of our women before you came to us and after. Advising them and giving good news of relief, Moses said to them: It is hopeful that Allah will destroy your enemy, Pharaoh, and his people and establish you in the earth after them. Then He would see what you do after that [out of] thankfulness or ingratitude.",
  7130:
      "We had undoubtedly punished the people of Pharaoh with drought and aridity. We tested them with a shortage of fruits of the earth and its yields, hoping they would reflect and take a lesson that what happened to them from [all] that was but a punishment for their disbelief so that they would repent to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The position of the magicians and the courageous and direct announcement of their faith shows that people, stripped of their own desire, submitting to reason and sound thought, rush to faith when the proofs appear to them.\n2. The people who have faith in Allah and the last day are those with the strongest resolve among people, and the bravest and most patient in times of crises, trials, and conflict.\n3. Those who benefit from power instigate and stir up power to face the people of faith, because in the continuation of their power lies the continuation of their best interests.\n4. Wrongdoing and corruption are some of the reasons for the withholding of rain and the rise of high prices.",
  7131:
      "So whenever the people of Pharaoh experienced luxury, healthy produce, and low prices, they said: We have been given this because we deserve it and are privileged by it. And if a misfortune reaches or inflicts them, of drought, aridity, prevalence of disease, and other calamities, they would blame their bad fortune on Moses and the Israelites who were with him. The truth is that what struck them from all that was only by the decree of Allah, may He be Exalted. Neither they nor Moses (peace be upon him) had any part in the affair apart from Moses's supplications against them. But most do not know, so they attribute it to other than Allah.",
  7132:
      "The people of Pharaoh said to Moses (peace be upon them), out of their stubbornness against the truth: Whatever sign or evidence you bring to us, and whatever proof you establish to invalidate what we have, to turn us away from it and to affirm what you have come with: we will not believe in you.",
  7133:
      "Then, as a punishment for their rejection and stubbornness, We sent abundant water, so it flooded their crops and fruits; sent locusts upon them so they ate their yields; sent small creatures upon them called lice striking their crops or harming humans in their hair; sent frogs upon them, so they filled their vessels, ruined their food and kept [people] awake in their places of sleep; and We sent the blood so the water in their wells and rivers turned into blood. We sent all of that as clear and distinct signs, one after another. Despite all that struck them of punishments, they were too pompous to have faith in Allah and believe in what Moses (peace be upon him) brought. They were people who committed wrongs, would not give up falsehood, and would not be guided to the truth.",
  7134:
      "And when the torment with these matters inflicted them, they sought refuge with Moses (peace be upon him), so they said to him: O Moses, by the prophethood He has privileged you with and what He pledged to removing the torment by repentance, supplicate to your Lord for us that He uplift the torment that has inflicted on us. Then indeed, if you uplift that from us, we will certainly believe in you and send the Israelites with you and set them free.",
  7135:
      "Then, when We lifted the torment from them for a set time, before their destruction by drowning, they reneged from what they had taken upon themselves to believe and release the Children of Israel. So they persisted in their disbelief and did not allow the Israelites to go with Moses (peace be upon him).",
  7136:
      "So when the appointed time came for their destruction, We unleashed Our punishment on them by drowning them in the sea because they rejected the signs of Allah and turned away from the indisputable truth which the signs had indicated.",
  7137:
      "We made the Israelites, whom Pharaoh and his people would humiliate, inherit the eastern areas of the land and the western regions of it, referring to the Levant. Allah blessed this land by making its crops and fruits grow in the most perfect fashion. The good word of your Lord was fulfilled, O Messenger, where Allah says: {We wish to grant favor to those who were weakened in the earth and make them leaders and make them the inheritors} [Al-Qasas:5]. So Allah established them in the land because of their patience in the face of the harm they had suffered from Pharaoh and his people. We destroyed the farms and homes that Pharaoh would construct and the palaces they would build.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Good and evil are all by the Divine will and decree of Allah, and nothing is independent of this.\n2. The condition of people in times of trial and misfortune is to seek refuge in Allah alone, driven by their natural inclination to Monotheism.\n3. The believer should consider the signs of Allah and His standard practice in dealing with His creation, thinking about their purposes and outcomes.\n4. The power of individuals and nations vanish before the great power of Allah, and faith in Allah is the source of all power.\n5. Allah rewards His believing servants who are patient by giving them strength in the land after they were considered to be weak.\n6. Allah destroys tyrants, no matter how great their power or how long their time in power.",
  7138:
      "And We made the Israelites cross the sea when Moses hit it with his staff, and then it parted. So they passed by a people who were lingering upon the worship of [some] idols of theirs, worshipping them instead of Allah. The Israelites said to Moses (peace be upon him): O Moses, make us an idol to worship as these people have idols to worship other than Allah. Moses said to them: You are a people who are ignorant of that which due to Allah from reverence and Tawheed (singling out) [in worship and attributes], and that which does not befit Him of associating partners [with Him] and worshipping other than Him.",
  7139:
      "Indeed, [regarding] those people lingering upon worshiping their idols: destroyed is the worship of other than Him which they are upon, and invalid are all acts of worship that they would do out of their association of others in worship with Allah.",
  7140:
      "Moses said to his people: O my people, how can I seek a god for you to worship other than Allah when you have witnessed what you have from His great signs, and He, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, has favored you upon the [the inhabitants] of the worlds of your time with what he bestowed upon you from the destruction of your enemy, your inheritance [of control] in the land, and your established governance in it?",
  7141:
      "Remember, O Israelites, when We saved you from your abasement by Pharaoh and his people when they would subject you to varieties of degradation, from killing your sons and preserving your women to serve. There [was] a great test from your Lord in your rescue from Pharaoh and his people, obliging gratitude from you.",
  7142:
      "Allah promised His messenger Moses thirty nights for a private conversation with Him. Then Allah completed them with the addition of ten, so they became forty nights. When he wanted to leave for the private conversation with his Lord, Moses told his brother Aaron: O Aaron, be my successor within my people and make their affairs right with fine leadership and gentleness. Do not follow the path of the corrupters by engaging in acts of disobedience, and do not be a helper to the disobedient [to Allah].",
  7143:
      "When Moses came for the private conversation with his Lord at the appointment designated for him, which was a full forty nights, and his Lord spoke to him with commands, prohibitions, and otherwise, Moses yearned to see his Lord, so he asked to look upon Him. So, Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, replied: You will not see Me in the worldly life because of your inability to endure that, but look, instead, at the mountain when I reveal Myself to it, for if it remains in its place, unaffected, then You will see Me; and if it becomes leveled to the ground, then you will not be able to see Me in the [life of this] world.Then, when Allah revealed Himself to the mountain, He made it leveled to the ground, and Moses fell unconscious. Then, when he recovered from the unconsciousness that overtook him, he said: I declare Your Perfection, O Lord, far above all that which does not befit You. Here I am, turned to You in repentance from what I asked You of seeing You in the world, and I am the first believer among my people.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The events show that the Israelites moved from one error to another despite Moses, the prophet of Allah, being among them.\n2. One sign of a people being forsaken by Allah is when they see evil as good, and see what is good as evil and incorrect, due to their false opinions and whims.\n3. The rectification of people and closing the doors of corruption and evil are amongst the lofty aims of the prophets and those who invite to the truth.\n4. It is Allah’s decree that no one from among His creation is to see Him in this world, and He will honour whomever He loves of His servants with seeing Him in the Afterlife.",
  7144:
      "Allah told Moses: O Moses, I have chosen you and favored you over the people with My messages when I sent you to them. I also favored you with My [direct] speech to you without any intermediary. So take the generous honor I have given you, and be among those thankful to Allah for such a great gift.",
  7145:
      "And We wrote for Moses on the Tablets, of wood or otherwise, everything that the Israelites would need for their religious and worldly affairs, as an admonishment for those among them who would accept admonishment and elaboration for the rulings that needed explanation. So take this Torah, O Moses, with seriousness and utmost effort, and instruct your people, the Israelites, to take hold of the best within it from that whose reward is more significant, such as doing what was commanded in the most perfect way, and such as patience and pardoning. I will show you [all] the consequence of he who went against My commands and left obedience to Me and the ruin and destruction that he ends up in.",
  7146:
      "[Regarding] those who are unjustly pompous against the slaves of Allah and the truth, I will turn them away from taking lessons from My signs in the horizons and in themselves and from understanding the verses of My Book. Even if they see every sign, they will not believe in them due to their objection to and turning away from them and for opposing Allah and His Messenger. If they see the path of truth leading to Allah's contentment, they do not follow it or desire it. And if they see the way of misguidance and error leading to Allah's wrath, they follow it. That which inflicted them only struck them because of their rejection of Allah's great signs, which indicated the truthfulness of what the messengers came with and due to being oblivious from reflecting upon them.",
  7147:
      "Those who rejected Our signs, which indicate the truthfulness of Our messengers, and rejected meeting Allah on the Day of Resurrection, their actions that were among the acts of obedience will be invalidated, and they will not be rewarded for them because they were missing their condition, which is faith. They will not be requited on the Day of Resurrection except for what they would commit of disbelief in Allah and associating partners with Him. The requital of that is living eternally in the Fire.",
  7148:
      "After Moses had gone to privately converse with his Lord, his people established a statue of a calf made from their ornaments; it did not possess a soul, but it made a sound. Did they not know that this calf could not speak to them nor guide them to any path of good, [be it] material or spiritual, and that it could not bring anything of benefit to them or remove any harm from them? They took it as an object of worship and wronged themselves by doing so.",
  7149:
      "When they regretted their actions, became bewildered, and realized that they had gone astray from the straight path by taking the calf as an object of worship alongside Allah, they said: If our Lord does not have mercy on us by granting us success to obey Him and forgive us for the worship of the calf which we engaged in, then we will undoubtedly be among those who lose their worldly life and Afterlife.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From being grateful is that the servant should show the grace and blessings of Allah upon him, and thankfulness will cause an increase in blessings.\n2. The servant should always strive to reach excellence as regards to his speech and actions.\n3. It is necessary to accept the sacred law with determination and seriousness and to resolve to follow and carry out what is transmitted in it, in terms of righteousness and putting things right and preventing corruption and perversion.\n4. A nation will be revered and strong as long as it holds fast to its sacred way of life, otherwise it will fall apart and lose its strength.\n5. You reap what you sow, so whoever has faith and does good deeds, for them is Paradise, and whoever disbelieves and does bad deeds, for them is the fire.\n6. If the servant makes a mistake or falls short with regards to His Lord’s rights, he must acknowledge the enormity of the crime he committed, and that there is no refuge from Allah’s chastisement except through Him.",
  7150:
      "When Moses returned to his people from his private conversation with His Lord, full of anger towards them and sadness upon finding them worshipping the calf, he said: What a terrible condition you have fallen into after me, O my people, for what it leads to of ruin and misery. Did you become bored of waiting for me, so you proceeded to worship the calf? Moses threw the Tablets because of the intensity of the anger and sadness that struck him and took his brother Aaron by the head and beard, dragging him towards him for remaining with them and not rectifying the worship of the calf that he saw. Aaron said to his brother Moses, in excuse and seeking clemency from him: O son of my mother, indeed the people considered me weak, so they belittled and almost killed me. So do not punish me with what would please my enemies, and do not include me, out of your anger, among the wrongdoers from the people due to their worship of other than Allah.",
  7151:
      "So Moses supplicated to his Lord: O my Lord, forgive me and my brother Aaron, and enter us into Your Mercy, and make it surround us from all sides. You, O our Lord, are more merciful to us than any merciful one.",
  7152:
      "Indeed, [regarding] those who made the calf a god, worshipping it; severe anger from their Lord and humiliation will strike them in this life for angering their Lord and belittlement of Him. With the like of this recompense, We requite those who fabricate lies about Allah.",
  7153:
      "Those who do evil deeds from associating partners with Allah and committing acts of disobedience, and then repent by believing in Him and desisting from the acts of disobedience they were upon, [then] indeed, O Messenger, after this repentance and return from associating partners to faith, and from acts of disobedience to obedience, your Lord is certainly forgiving to them by concealment [of their sins] and pardon and is merciful to them.",
  7154:
      "When the anger of Moses (peace be upon him) had subsided and he calmed down, he picked up the Tablets which he had thrown in anger. These Tablets contained guidance from misguidance, clarification of the truth, and mercy for those who fear their Lord and are afraid of His punishment.",
  7155:
      "Moses chose seventy men among the best of his people to apologize to their Lord for the worship of the calf that the fools among them had committed. Allah promised them a time and place for them to attend. Then, when they attended, they were brazen with Allah and asked Moses to let them see Allah with their eyes. So an earthquake seized them, and they were struck down by its intensity and destroyed. So Moses begged his Lord, saying: O my Lord, if You had willed to destroy them, and me with them before they had come, You would have certainly destroyed them. Would You destroy us because of what the feeble-minded amongst us did? For the worship of the calf that my people committed is only a trial and test by which You lead astray whom You will, and You guide whom You will. You are in charge of our affair, so forgive us our wrongs, and have mercy on us with Your vast Mercy. You are the best of those who forgive wrongdoing and pardon sin.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A Muslim should become angry for the sake of Allah and not for himself, disturbed when he sees Allah’s commands being violated.\n2. In the verses is proof that a mistake in making an independent judgement in spite of the clarity of the evidence, is not forgiven for the person who makes it when passing judgement on him, an the jurists would call this type of independent judgement a far-fetched interpretation.\n3. It is from the etiquette of making a prayer to begin with oneself, since Moses, peace be upon him, began his prayer by asking for forgiveness for himself, out of respect towards Allah concerning the anger he demonstrated, then he asked for forgiveness for his brother for any negligence or carelessness he had shown in preventing people from worshipping the calf.\n4. All lying is evil, and the dignity of whoever does it falls in front of people.\n5. In the verses is the awakening of the desire for wrongdoers to turn to Allah, asking for forgiveness, and the prohibition of despairing of the mercy of Allah, even if their sins are great.\n6. It is necessary to avoid Allah’s anger, and to fear His might. Consider the position of Moses (peace be upon him) with His Lord, and then consider his fear of His Lord’s anger.",
  7156:
      "And make us among those You have honored in this life with blessings and well-being, given success to do good works, and among Your righteous slaves for whom You have prepared Paradise in the Afterlife. Indeed, we have turned to You in repentance and turned back, admitting our deficiencies. Allah, exalted is He, said: I inflict My torment to whom I will among those who act upon the causes of misery, and My Mercy encompasses everything in the world. So there is no creation except that Allah's Mercy has reached, and His favor and benevolence [has] enshrouded. I will decree My Mercy in the Afterlife for those who heed Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, who give the zakat (obligatory alms) from their wealth to the people deserving of it, and who have faith in Our signs.",
  7157:
      "Those who follow Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, the illiterate prophet who cannot read or write, His Lord merely inspires him. He is the one whom they find his name, description, and prophethood written in the Torah sent down to Moses (peace be upon him), and the Gospel sent down to Jesus (peace be upon him). He commands them with that whose good and righteousness is known, and forbids them from that whose horridness is known in right minds and sound natures; he permits for them the delightful matters which contain no harm from food, drink, and intercourse, and he forbids from them the foul amongst them; he removes the onerous burdens which they were burdened with. So those who believed in him, from among the Israelites and others, aggrandized and honored him, supported him against whoever takes him as an enemy from the disbelievers, and followed the Quran which was revealed to him: those are the successful ones who attain what they seek and are averted from what they fear.",
  7158:
      "Say, O Messenger: O people, I am a Messenger of Allah [sent] to all of you, Arabs and non-Arabs, Who He alone owns the dominion of the heavens and the earth. There is nothing rightfully worshipped other than Him, may He be Exalted. He brings life to the dead and brings death to the living. So believe, O people, in Allah and believe in Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم His Messenger Prophet, who neither reads nor writes; he has merely come with the revelation revealed to him by his Lord. He believes in Allah and what has been revealed to him and the other Prophets before him without any differentiation. And follow him in that which he has come with from his Lord, in hopes that you would be guided to that which holds your benefit in the [life of this] world and the Afterlife.",
  7159:
      "After mentioning the Israelites' worship of the calf, Allah notes the presence of a group that opposed it, stating: \n A group of Moses's people from the Israelites are upright upon the true religion. They direct people to it and rule with justice so they do not oppress.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The mercy of Allah surrounds all things, but the mercy of Allah for His servants varies and increases according to the level of their faith and good actions.\n2. From the Justice of Allah and the just nature of the narrative in the Qur’an, is Allah’s fairness in mentioning the attributes of a nation or a people. Since He mentions the blameworthy attributes of some of the Children of Israel, a reader may assume that these attributes were general and true for all of them. Therefore, Allah mentions that among them was a group who were upright, guided, and guiding others.\n3. The Torah and the Gospels contained clear proofs that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, would be sent and attesting to the truth of what he came with.\n4. A prayer can be general or particular, according to circumstances. Moses was general in his prayer in the situation mentioned above.",
  7160:
      "We divided the Israelites into twelve tribes. When Moses's people requested that he ask Allah to give them drink, We revealed to him: Strike, O Moses, the rock with your staff. So, Moses struck it. Then, twelve springs gushed out from it according to the number of their tribes. Every tribe knew their specific spring to drink from, so no other tribe would share it with them. We also shaded them with the clouds, making them go where they would go and stop where they would stop. And from our blessings, We sent down a drink sweet like honey and small birds with excellent meat similar to quail. We told them: Eat from the pure things We have provided you. Their wrongdoing, denial of blessings, and not giving those blessings their due appreciation did not diminish Us in any way. Instead, they wronged themselves by diminishing their allotments when they brought themselves to the roads of ruin by opposing the command of Allah and denying His blessings.",
  7161:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Allah said to the Israelites: Enter Jerusalem and eat from the fruits of the town anywhere within it anytime you like. Ask your Lord to efface your misdeeds and enter the gate, bowing humbly to your Lord. Then, if you do that, We will overlook your wrongs and give the good-doers even more of the good of this life and the next.",
  7162:
      "So the unjust among them altered what they were commanded to say, so they said: a grain in a hair, instead of what they were commanded with of requesting forgiveness. They manipulated the action that they were commanded with, and so they entered crawling on their behinds instead of entering humbled to Allah, raising their heads; so We sent a torment upon them from the sky because of their injustice.",
  7163:
      "O Messenger, ask the Jews, in reminder to them of what Allah punished their predecessors with, about the story of the town near the sea when they would transgress the bounds of Allah by fishing on Saturday after they were prohibited from that; when Allah tested them such that the fish would come to them, apparent on the sea's surface on Saturday, and on the remaining days of the week, the fish would not come. Allah tested them with that because they abandoned obedience to Allah and committed acts of disobedience. So, they used trickery, casting their nets and digging their holes so the fish would get caught in them on Saturday. Then, on Sunday, they would take them and eat them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Rejection and disbelief are reasons for the removal of blessings.\n2. Among the reasons for a the arrival of consequences and the sending down of a punishment is the use of tricks to get around sacred law, because this is wrongdoing and overstepping the limits set by Allah.\n3. Allah decreed humiliation and poverty for the wrongdoers, and that He would, due to their disobedience and deviation, send people to punish them until the day of Resurrection.",
  7164:
      "Mention, O Messenger, when a group among them prohibited them from this objectionable act and warned them against it. Then, another group said to them: Why do you advise a group who either Allah will destroy in this life due to the sins it committed or torment it severely on the Day of Resurrection? The advising ones said: Our advice to them is an excuse to Allah by doing what we were commanded with of enjoining good and forbidding evil so that we are not taken to account for leaving that off. And so that they might benefit from the admonishment and then abstain from the acts of disobedience they are engaged in.",
  7165:
      "Then, when the disobedient disregarded what the admonishers reminded them of and did not refrain, We saved those who forbade evil from the torment and seized those who did wrong with their transgression of fishing on Saturday, with a severe torment because they departed from the obedience of Allah and their insistence on the act of disobedience.",
  7166:
      "So when they transgressed the limits by disobeying Allah out of arrogance and stubbornness and did not accept admonishment, We said to them: O disobedient ones, be abased monkeys. Then, they became what We willed. Our command for something, when We will it, is merely saying: Be, then it is.",
  7167:
      "Mention, O Messenger, when Allah declared clearly, in no uncertain terms, that the Jews will certainly be ruled by those who will humiliate and belittle them in this worldly life until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is surely swift to punish those who disobey Him, such that He might [even] hasten their punishment to be in this life. Indeed, He is surely forgiving of the sins of His slaves who repent to Him and is Merciful to them.",
  7168:
      "We distributed them throughout the earth and divided them into sects after they were once united. Some of them were righteous, upholding the rights of Allah and the rights of His slaves. Some of them were moderate. Others were excessive upon themselves with acts of disobedience. We tested them with ease and hardship, hoping they would turn back from what they were doing.",
  7169:
      "Then, after those, the people of evil came to follow. They took the Torah from their predecessors, reading it and not acting upon what it contained. They took the lowly commodities of this life as a bribe for their distortion of the book of Allah and to judge with other than what Allah sent down in it. They would also speak favorably about themselves that Allah would forgive their sins. If any meager worldly payment came to them, they would take it time and time again. Did Allah not take covenants and contracts with them that they should not say anything about Allah except the truth without making any distortions or changes? They did not unknowingly leave off acting upon the book, but rather, they knew. They read what was in it and knew it, so their sin is even worse. The abode of the hereafter and the everlasting bliss within it are better than those passing commodities for the ones who take heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Will those who took such measly commodities not realize that what Allah has prepared in the hereafter for the heedful is better and longer lasting?",
  7170:
      "Those who hold tightly to the book, implement it, and establish the prayer by maintaining its stated times, prerequisites, obligations, and supererogatory elements will be recompensed by Allah according to their deeds, for Allah does not lose the reward of those whose work is righteous.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. If the punishment of Allah descends upon a people because of their sins, Allah saves those from them who instruct people to do right and tell them not to do wrong.\n2. One should be careful of the punishment of Allah, since it could be terrible in this world, as was the case when Allah, glory be to Him changed a group of the Israelites into monkeys because of their rebellion.\n3. The bliss of this world, no matter how great it may seem, is little and trivial next to the eternal bliss of the Hereafter.\n4. The best action after having faith is to establish the prayer, because it is the basis of the Religion.",
  7171:
      "Mention, O Muhammad, when we uprooted the mountain and raised it over the Israelites when they refused to accept what was in the Torah. The mountain became like a cloud shading their heads, and they were sure it would fall upon them. It was said to them: Take what We have given you with seriousness, diligence, and determination, and remember the rulings in it that Allah has legislated for you and do not forget them, in hopes that you will take heed of Allah if you do that.",
  7172:
      "Remember, O Muhammad, when your Lord brought out the descendants of Adam's children from their loins and had them affirm His lordship with the acknowledgment he placed in their innate nature that He is their Creator and Lord, saying to them: Am I not your Lord? They all said: Rather, You are our Lord. He said: We only tested you and took the covenant upon you so that you would not deny Allah's argument against you on the Day of Resurrection and say that you had no knowledge of that.",
  7173:
      "Or argue that your forefathers were the ones who broke the covenant, for they made partners with Allah, and that you were blindly following your forefathers in the polytheism you found them upon and then say: Do You, O our Lord, hold us accountable for the actions of our forefathers who invalidated their deeds by associating partners with Allah and thus torment us? So there is no sin on us for our ignorance and blind following of our forefathers.",
  7174:
      "Just as We clarified the signs regarding the destination of the disbelieving nations, We clarify them to these people in hopes that they revert from the polytheism they are upon to the Oneness of Allah and worshipping Him alone, just as is in their covenant with Allah that they committed themselves to.",
  7175:
      "Recite, O Messenger, to the Israelites the news of a man from among them whom We gave Our signs to such that he knew them and understood the truth they indicated. But he did not act according to them. Rather, he left them and removed himself from them. Then the Devil followed him and became a close companion for him, so he became one of the misguided and ruined after he had been among the guided and saved.",
  7176:
      "If We wished to benefit him through these signs, We would have raised him in rank by allowing him to act according to them, thus rising in this world and the Afterlife. But he chose what would lead to his abandonment when he leaned towards the lusts of the worldly life, preferring his worldly life to his Afterlife. Thus, his example, in his extreme greed for this world, is like the example of a dog, which pants with its tongue in any circumstance, whether it is left alone or chased away. That example is the example of those misguided by their rejection of Our signs. So relate the stories to them, O Messenger, in hopes that they think, then abstain from the rejection and misguidance which they are in.",
  7177:
      "None is worse than the people who rejected Our arguments and proofs and did not believe them, wronging their souls with that by bringing them to the roads of ruin.",
  7178:
      "Whomever Allah gives success of guidance to His straight path is truly the one who is guided, and whomever He distances from the straight path, those are truly the ones undermining their own fortunes, who lost themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection. Is that not the clear loss?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The aim of revealing the divine texts is for people to act according to them, not just to recite them, as this is a form of neglecting them.\n2. Allah created the innate ability to understand the signs of the Oneness of Allah in people, from the time they were formed; if their nature is sound and not corrupted, they will recognise these signs, and act accordingly.\n3. In the verses is a lesson for those who have been given success in acting according to the verses of the Qur’an: that they should know the grace of Allah upon them in enabling them to act according to them, and that they should purify themselves.\n4. The necessity of reflecting upon and learning from the stories of the Qur’an, because they are the stories of truth.\n5. In the verses is the encouragement to act according to knowledge, through which Allah raises people up, and through which they are protected from Satan; and a cautioning against not acting according to knowledge.\n6. Muslims are encouraged to repent to Allah, asking for guidance from Him, and protection from the dangers of misguidance.",
  7179:
      "And We made for Hell many people from humanity and the jinn because of Our Knowledge that they would do the actions of its people. They have hearts with which they do not understand what will benefit them and [what will] harm them; eyes which they do not use to see the signs of Allah within themselves and upon the horizons so that they can learn from them; and they have ears which they do not use to listen to the verses of Allah so that they might reflect what they contain. Those described by these characteristics resemble cattle in their lack of reasoning. Rather, they are further in misguidance than the cattle. Those are the ones oblivious to faith in Allah and the Last Day.",
  7180:
      "To Allah (may He be Exalted) belong the most beautiful names that indicate His majesty and perfection. So use them to call on Allah when you ask for whatever you wish and praise Him with them. And leave those who turn away from the truth of these names by assigning them to others, negating them from Him, distorting their meanings, or making others similar to Him with them. We will repay these people who deviate from the truth regarding them with painful torment for what they used to do.",
  7181:
      "Among those whom We created is a group of people who are guided by the truth within themselves and call others to it so that they are [also] guided. They rule with justice so they do not oppress.",
  7182:
      "[As for] those who rejected Our signs and did not believe in them, but rather denied them, We will open the gates of provision for them, not to honor them, but rather to lead them on gradually such that they continue upon the misguidance they are upon. Then, Our torment will strike them at a moment of unawareness.",
  7183:
      "I delay punishment from them until they think they will not be punished, so they persist in their rejection and disbelief until their torment is multiplied upon them. Indeed, My Planning is strong, so I show benevolence to them while I intend to forsake them.",
  7184:
      "Do those who reject the signs of Allah and His Messenger not ponder such that they would work their minds so it would be clear to them that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is not insane? He is but a messenger from Allah, Who sent him as a clear warner of Allah's torment.",
  7185:
      "Do these people not look with a gaze of reflection to the dominion of Allah in the heavens and the earth, all that Allah created within them of animals and plants and other things, and at their own life spans, the end of which may be near, so that they might repent to Allah before the time has gone? If they do not have faith in the Quran and what it contains of promises and threats, then what other book will they believe in?",
  7186:
      "Whoever Allah forsakes from guidance to the truth, sending them away from the right path, there is no guide to direct them back to guidance. Allah leaves them in their misguidance and disbelief, confused, not guided to anything.",
  7187:
      "Those who reject the truth and are stubborn ask you about the Hour: When will it occur and be known? Say to them, O Muhammad: the knowledge of it is not with me, nor anyone else. Knowledge of it is with Allah alone. None will reveal it at its decreed time except Allah. The matter of its emergence is hidden from those in the heavens and those in the earth, and it will only come upon you unexpectedly. They ask you, O Muhammad, about the Hour as if you are eager to know about it, not realizing that you did not ask about it because of the perfection of your knowledge of your Lord. Say to them, O Muhammad: The knowledge of the Hour is with Allah alone, but most people do not know that.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Human beings have been bestowed with the senses in order to understand the signs and gain knowledge, so that they may attain benefit and avoid harm.\n2. Calling on Allah with His beautiful names in one’s supplication is a means of achieving His response. One should use the name that is most appropriate to the request; for example, ‘O Forgiver-forgive me!’\n3. People are required to reflect on the greatness of the heavens and earth to reach the conclusion that Allah alone is worthy of being worshipped because He is the only One Who creates and designs.",
  7188:
      "Say to them, O Muhammad: I cannot bring good to myself or remove any harm from myself, except by Allah's will. Those things only belong to Allah, and I only know what Allah taught me. Thus, I do not know the unseen. If I did know the unseen, I would have used the means that I know to bring me benefits and protect me from ruinous affairs due to my knowledge of things before they happen and what they result in. I am only a messenger from Allah, alarming of a painful punishment, and bringing the good news of Allah's generous reward for a community who believe that I am a messenger from Him (may He be Exalted) and affirm what I have come with.",
  7189:
      "It is He who brought you into being, O men and women, from one soul, Adam (peace be upon him), and created from Adam (peace be upon him) his wife, Eve. He made her from his rib so he would find comfort and tranquility in her. When a husband had relations with his wife, she became pregnant with a light load, not noticing it because it was at the beginning of the pregnancy. She continued with this pregnancy of hers, going about her needs without heftiness. Then, when she became heavy with it upon having grown in her belly, both spouses called upon their Lord, saying: O our Lord, if You grant us a healthy child, we will surely be among the thankful for Your blessings.",
  7190:
      "Then, when Allah responded to their prayer and gave them a healthy child as they asked, they made partners with Allah in what He granted them, for they made their child a slave [in name] to other than Him. Transcendent is Allah and far above [having] any partner, for He is the Singular in lordship and godship.",
  7191:
      "Do they make these idols and other things to be partners with Allah in worship when they know that they do not create anything such that they would deserve worship? Rather, they [themselves] are created, so how do they make them partners with Allah?",
  7192:
      "These objects of worship cannot help their worshippers or even help themselves, so how do they worship them?",
  7193:
      "And If you, O polytheists, call these idols which you take as gods instead of Allah who guides to guidance, they will not respond to what you call them to, nor will they follow you. So it is the same to them whether you call them or keep silent because they are just inanimate objects; they do not reason, hear, or speak.",
  7194:
      "Indeed, those you worship, O polytheists, instead of Allah, were created for Allah and belong to Him, so they are the same as you in that way. However, you are in a better state because you are living: you speak, walk, hear, and see, while your idols are not. So call on them and let them respond to you if you are telling the truth in what you claim about them.",
  7195:
      "Do these idols, which they took as gods, have feet they walk with such that they go in pursuit of their needs? Or hands they firmly defend you with? Or do they have eyes with which they see what is unseen to you so they inform you? Or ears with which they hear what is hidden from you so they relate its knowledge to you? If they are incapable of all that, then how do you worship them, hoping to bring benefit or fend off harm? Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Call upon those whom you have made equal with Allah. Then plot to hurt me and give me no respite.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses clarify that supplicating to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to bring about benefit or protect from harm is ignorance. Benefit only comes through following the instructions he was sent with.\n2. Allah, from His Kindness and Mercy, made a man’s wife from the same source as him, so that he would feel close to her, treat her well, and for them to enjoy each other’s company, and to realise the divine wisdom in having children.\n3. It is not appropriate for the Children of Adam who are the best and most noble of creation, to worship false Allahs made of insignificant paltry items such as stone and wood and the like.\n4. It is incumbent on the one of sound mind that he directs his worship to Allah alone, for it is Allah alone Who gave us the the Faith through the revelation of His scripture, which contains the knowledge of spiritual matters and worldly matters and benefits, and protects and helps the righteous among his creation, so that they are not harmed by those who oppose them.",
  7196:
      "Truly, my supporter and helper is Allah, Who keeps me safe so I do not put my hope in anyone besides Him. I fear nothing from your idols, for He is the One who sent down the Quran upon me as a guidance for the people, and it is He Who takes charge of those who do good among His slaves, so he protects and supports them.",
  7197:
      "Those you call upon, O polytheists, from amongst these idols are unable to support you nor themselves, for they are utterly incapable. So, how can you call upon them instead of Allah?",
  7198:
      "If you, O polytheists, call your idols, which you worship instead of Allah, to uprightness, they will not hear you calling them. You see them facing you with fashioned eyes, inanimate objects that cannot see, for they used to make statues in the form of people or animals. They had hands, feet, and eyes but were inanimate, with no life in them nor motion.",
  7199:
      "Accept from people, O Messenger, what they are able to do, and the actions and character that are easy for them. Do not burden them with what their natures do not allow, for that will drive them away. Command with every beautiful saying and excellent action, and turn away from the ignorant so do not face them with their ignorance. So whoever harms you, do not harm them, and whoever denies you [something], do not deny them.",
  7200:
      "And if you feel, O Messenger, that the Devil has inflicted you with a whisper or deterrence from doing good, then turn to Allah for security and seek refuge with Him, for He hears what you say and knows what you do when you seek protection, so He will protect you from the Devil.",
  7201:
      "Those who are heedful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, when inflicted by a whisper from the Devil, then commit wrongs; they remember the splendor of Allah, His punishment for the disobedient, and His reward for the obedient. So they repent from their wrongs and turn back to their Lord. Then [suddenly] they have become upright upon the truth, awoken from what they were upon and desisted.",
  7202:
      "And [as for] the brethren of the devils from among the wicked and disbelievers, the devils increase them in misguidance with sin after sin. They do not cease: neither the devils from deviating and misguiding nor the wicked from the humans from submitting and doing evil.",
  7203:
      "And if you, O Messenger, come with a sign, they reject it and turn away from it; and if you do not come to them with a sign, they say: Would you not invent a sign yourself and create it? Say to them, O Messenger: It is not for me to come with a sign from myself. I do not follow except that which Allah reveals to me. This Quran I recite to you is [a collection of] arguments and proofs from Allah, your Creator and the disposer of your affairs, and [it is] guidance and mercy for the believers among His slaves. As for those other than the believers, then they are lost and wretched ones.",
  7204:
      "When the Quran is recited, listen to its recitation, do not speak, and do not busy yourself with other than it in hopes that Allah will have mercy on you.",
  7205:
      "And remember, O Messenger, your Lord Allah humbly, modestly, and fearfully. Make your supplication moderate between raising the voice and lowering it at the beginning and end of the day for the virtue of these two times. And do not be among those inattentive to the remembrance of Allah Exalted.",
  7206:
      "Indeed, those with your Lord, O Messenger, from the angels, never abstain from His worship, may He be Exalted. Rather, they yield to it submissively and unceasingly. They declare the perfection of Allah, day and night, from that which does not befit Him and prostrate to Him alone.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. These verses contain good news for the Muslims who follow the path of their Prophet (peace be upon him): Allah will help them as he helped his prophet and his allies.\n2. The traits of good character that a believer should possess include forgiving those who wrong them, giving to those who deny them something, and mending relations with those who break them.\n3. It is incumbent on the servant if Satan overpowers him and he commits a sin, then they should ask Allah for forgiveness, correcting what he did wrong, repenting sincerely to Him and doing good actions to erase what he did.",
  8000:
      "Spoils of War (Surah Al-Anfal)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nGratitude for Allah's victory at Badr and enumerating the patterns of triumph and defeat.\n•    Explanation:",
  8001:
      "Your companions ask you, O Messenger, about the war booty, how it should be distributed, and to whom. Say, O Messenger, in answer to their question: The spoils of war are for Allah and His Messenger, and it is for Allah and His Messenger to judge what to do with it and how to distribute it. You only have to submit and comply. So take heed of Allah, O believers, by complying with His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. Resolve whatever is between you of severed relations and abandonment with affection, reconciliation, good character, and pardon. Adhere to obeying Allah and His Messenger if you truly believe because faith leads to obedience and staying far away from disobedience. This question was raised after the battle of Badr.",
  8002:
      "The true believers are merely those whose hearts have fear when Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, is mentioned, which leads their hearts and bodies to obedience; when Allah's verses are recited, they ponder them, which increases their faith; and they rely on their Lord alone to bring about what is good for them and to ward off what harms them.",
  8003:
      "Those who consistently offer the prayer on time in its complete form and spend from what We have provided them on what is obligatory and recommended.",
  8004:
      "Those described as having these qualities are true believers because they combine the qualities of faith and open [practice of] Islam. Their recompense will be high stations with their Lord, forgiveness for their sins, and a generous provision, which is the bliss that Allah has prepared for them.",
  8005:
      "Just as when Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, took the distribution of the spoils of war from you all after you differed and disputed over its distribution and He made the decision for Allah and His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, Your Lord also ordered you, O Messenger, by sending revelation to you to leave Medina to meet the polytheists [in battle] while a party of the believers disdained doing that.",
  8006:
      "This group of believers argued with you, O Messenger, about fighting the polytheists after it became clear to them that it would happen, [arguing] as if being driven to death, looking at it with their own eyes. They argued due to the severity of their disdain for going out to battle because they had not gotten ready for it nor prepared its preparations.",
  8007:
      "Remember, O arguing believers, when Allah promised you victory over one of the two parties of polytheists, either the caravan and the wealth it contained so you would take it as booty, or the squad so you would fight and defeat them. You preferred victory over the caravan due to the simplicity and ease of conquering it without fighting. However, Allah wanted the truth established by ordering you to fight to kill the polytheists' leaders and capture many of them so that the strength of Islam would become apparent.",
  8008:
      "So that Allah would establish the truth by making Islam and its people victorious by demonstrating the affairs that bear witness to its truthfulness, and so that He (may He be Exalted) expose the falsehood by showing proof against it. Even if the polytheists hate that, Allah will show it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A believer should strengthen and increase his faith, because faith increases and decreases. It increases with worship and doing good actions, and decreases with not worshipping and by doing bad actions.\n2. Debate is appropriate when the truth of something is not clear; but once something becomes clear, then it is only right to follow it and act according to it.\n3. The division of the gains of war was consigned to the Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him), and all decisions concerning it were referred to Allah and His Messenger alone.\n4. The verses confirm the believers’ desire for divine help, to establish the truth and show falsehood for what it is.",
  8009:
      "Recall the day of Badr when you all asked for assistance from Allah in defeating your enemies. Then, He answered you, O believers, in that He would reinforce and assist you with one thousand successive angels, one following the other.",
  8010:
      "Allah only reinforced you, O believers, with angels as glad tidings of His support for you against your enemies and so that your hearts would be tranquil in the assurance of victory. Victory is not due to the strength of numbers or the supply of arms. It is only from Allah, may He be Exalted. Indeed, Allah is Mighty in His sovereignty, and no one can overpower him. He is Wise in His legislation and decree.",
  8011:
      "Remember, O believers, when Allah cast drowsiness upon you as a safeguard from the fear of your enemies which befell you and sent down rain upon you from the sky to cleanse you from impurities, remove the whisperings of the Devil, make your hearts firm so that your bodies are firm when meeting the enemy, and make your feet steady by clumping the sandy ground so that [your] feet would not slip on it.",
  8012:
      "When your Lord, O Prophet, revealed to the angels whom Allah had reinforced the believers with at Badr: I am with you, O angels, in aid and support, so strengthen the believers' resolve to fight their enemies. I will cast intense fear into the hearts of those who disbelieve. So, O believers, strike the necks of the disbelievers so that they die and strike their joints and limbs so they are incapacitated from fighting you.",
  8013:
      "That killing and striking of limbs which befell the disbelievers was because they opposed Allah and His Messenger. So, they did not fulfill what they were ordered to do and did not cease what they were forbidden from. Whoever opposes Allah and His Messenger in that, then indeed, Allah is severe in punishment to them with killing and capture in this life and with the Fire in the Afterlife.",
  8014:
      "That is the torment mentioned for you, O opposers to Allah and His Messenger, so taste it in advance in this worldly life. Then, if you die upon your disbelief and obstinance, you will have the torment of the Fire in the hereafter.",
  8015:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, when you meet the polytheists at close quarters in battle, do not part them in defeat and turn your backs to them in retreat, but rather, stay firm facing towards them and be patient upon meeting them [in battle], for Allah is with you with His aid and support.",
  8016:
      "Whoever turns his back to them, fleeing from them, not in inclination to battling them by exhibiting retreat as a trick from him while he intends to return to them, nor joining forces with a group of the Muslims present [on the battlefield] seeking support from it, then he will come back with Allah's anger and rightly deserve it. His place in the hereafter will be Hell. What a miserable fate and destination he reached.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show Allah’s care for the believers, making things easier for them by sending ways of strengthening their faith and making their footholds firm, and taking away difficulty and the whisperings of Satan from them.\n2. Victory is in Allah’s hands, and is from Him, and does not depend on the number of people fighting or their weapons and preparations, notwithstanding the importance of the duty to make the best preparation for war that one can.\n3. Running away from fighting without an excuse is a great sin.\n4. These verses teach the believers about the laws of fighting in war, among which are obeying Allah and His Messenger, being patient before the enemy, steadfast during fighting, and remembering Allah much.",
  8017:
      "O believers, you did not kill the polytheists on the Day of Badr with your own power and strength; rather, Allah helped you with that. And you did not throw, O Prophet, at the disbelievers when you threw; rather, Allah threw at them when He made your throw reach them. And He will certainly test the believers with victory over their enemies, which He blessed them with, despite their meager numbers and equipment, so that they thank Him. Indeed, Allah hears your supplication and speech and knows your actions and what benefits you.",
  8018:
      "The aforementioned killing of the polytheists, throwing at them until they were defeated and fled, and blessing the believers with victory over their enemy, is [all] from Allah. Allah weakens the plot of the disbelievers who plot against Islam.",
  8019:
      "If you, O polytheists, request that Allah inflict His torment and affliction upon the transgressing wrongdoers, then Allah has inflicted upon you what you requested, for He has brought down on you that which was a punishment for you and a lesson for the heedful. If you refrain from requesting that, then it is better for you. And if you go back to requesting it and killing the believers, we will go back to inflicting torment upon you and giving victory to the believers. Neither your faction nor your supporters will avail you, even if they were much in numbers and equipment while the believers are few, and because Allah is with them in support and aid. Whoever Allah is with, then none can defeat them.",
  8020:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, obey Allah and obey His Messenger by complying with His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. Do not turn away from Him by violating His orders and engaging in His prohibitions while you hear the verses of Allah being recited to you.",
  8021:
      "O believers, do not be like the polytheists and hypocrites who, when the verses of Allah are recited upon them, say: We have heard with our ears what has been recited to us from the Quran, while they do not listen to ponder or take admonishment, so they do not benefit from what they listen to.",
  8022:
      "Indeed, in the sight of Allah, the worst creatures that tread the earth are the deaf, who do not listen to the truth with acceptance, and the mute, who do not speak the truth, for they are the ones who do not understand what Allah commands nor what He forbids.",
  8023:
      "If Allah had known that these polytheist deniers had [any] good in them, He would have surely made them hear with a hearing with which they would benefit and ponder His proof and evidence. However, He knows that there is no good in them. If He (may He be Exalted) had made them hear, hypothetically and theoretically speaking, they would have stubbornly turned away from faith, shunning [it].",
  8024:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, answer Allah and His Messenger when they call you to the truth that gives you life by submitting to what they have commanded and avoiding what they have prohibited. Be certain that Allah can do anything so He can come between you and submission to the truth if you desire it after rejecting it. Therefore, hasten to it and be certain that you will be gathered to Allah alone on the Day of Resurrection. Then He will recompense you for your actions in the [life of this] world.",
  8025:
      "Beware, O believers, of a torment that will not only reach the sinners among you but rather reach them and others. That will be when there is open wrongdoing, and then it goes unchanged. Be certain that Allah is strong in punishing those who disobey Him, so beware of disobeying Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whoever Allah is with will be aided and given victory, even if they are weak or few in number; and His being with them and aiding them is according to their faith and good actions.\n2. The believer is expected to take the necessary means and precautions in order to help fulfil their responsibilities they have been given by Allah. They should then trust in Allah, entrusting their affairs to Him and leaving the outcome to Him.\n3. The might of the disbelievers becomes insignificant before the power and ability of Allah. He makes the plotting of the disbelievers come to nothing and puts fear in their hearts.\n4. The verses show that Allah does not prevent anyone from faith and goodness except those who have no good in them, who faith would not help or benefit.\n5. It is good to frequently supplicate to Allah with the prayer: ‘O turner of the hearts! Keep our hearts firm on your faith.’\n6. Allah instructs the believers not to allow disobedience to become widespread among them, so that punishment does not come upon them all.",
  8026:
      "Remember, O believers, when you were few in number in Mecca. Its residents considered you weak and overpowered you. You feared that your enemies would quickly seize you. Then, Allah took you into a shelter you could seek refuge in, which was Al-Medina, and strengthened you with victory over your enemies on the battlefields, including Badr. He provided for you with pure things; among them was the war booty you took from your enemies. [All that] so that you might be grateful to Allah for His blessings so He would give you more of them, and that you not be ungrateful for them, then He would seize it from you and torment you.",
  8027:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, do not betray Allah and the Messenger by abandoning compliance with the commands and avoidance of the prohibitions. Also, do not betray what you have been entrusted with regarding religion and other matters, while you know what you would do is betrayal, for then you would be among the treacherous.",
  8028:
      "Given that the love of wealth and children leads a slave to betrayal, Allah informs us that they are both sources of temptation, stating: \n Know, O believers, that your wealth and children are only a trial and test for you from Allah, for they might obstruct you from working towards the Afterlife and lead you to treachery. Know that Allah has a great reward with Him, so do not lose out on this reward by [your] tending to your wealth and children, and treachery for their sake.",
  8029:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, know that if you take heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, Allah will make for you that by which you can distinguish between truth and falsehood, so you will not be confused between them. He will also wipe away the evil deeds that you have committed and forgive you your sins. Allah is the possessor of great bounty, and from His great bounty is His Paradise that He has prepared for the heedful among His slaves.",
  8030:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the polytheists joined forces against you, conspiring to capture, kill, or exile you from your land to another. They plot against you, but Allah turns their plot back against them. Allah plans, and He is the best of planners.",
  8031:
      "When our verses are recited to them, they say in obstinance and arrogance to the truth: We have heard this sort of thing before. If we had wanted speech like this Quran, we would have spoken it. This Quran, which we heard, is just the lies of the ancients, so we will not believe in it.",
  8032:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the polytheists said: O Allah, if what Muhammad has brought is true, then drop stones from the sky upon us that would destroy us or bring us a severe torment. They said that in exaggeration of their denial and objection.",
  8033:
      "Allah would not torment your nation, whether they are from the nation that answered [your call] or from the nation of being called, with a torment that would eradicate them while you, O Muhammad, are alive and present among them. Thus, your presence among them is a safeguard for them from torment. Also, Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness from Allah for their sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Thankfulness is a great blessing which increases the blessings of Allah; and blessings decrease when thankfulness is neglected.\n2. Trustworthiness is one of the essential qualities of a good Muslim, which should be firmly established amongst the numerous good character traits. Having it is a proof of the integrity of the soul and the balance of its actions.\n3. The reward with Allah for restraining the self from things which are forbidden is better than any apparent advantage gained from dealings with ones wealth and children in a blameworthy way.\n4. The verses confirm the virtue and blessings of asking for forgiveness, and that it is something that prevents a people from receiving a punishment.\n5. The verses illustrate the foolishness of those people who turned away from the guidance because they did not ask Allah that, if what Muhammad brought was true, they be guided to it.",
  8034:
      "What could prevent their torment while they have committed what obliges it, including preventing people from praying and making tawaf (circumambulation) in the Sacred Mosque? The polytheists are not the allies of Allah, for Allah's allies are only the heedful who take heed of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. But most polytheists are unaware when they claim that they are His allies while they are not.",
  8035:
      "The prayer of the polytheists in Sacred Mosque was only whistling and clapping. So taste the torment, O polytheists, by being slain or captured on the day of Badr for your disbelief in Allah and your rejection of His Messenger.",
  8036:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieve in Allah spend their wealth to prevent people from Allah's religion. So they will spend it and not accomplish what they sought. Then, the result of spending their wealth will be regret due to losing it and losing what was intended by it. Then, they will be defeated by the believers' victory over them. Those who disbelieve in Allah will be driven to Hell on the Day of Resurrection, so they will enter it and stay there for all eternity.",
  8037:
      "These disbelievers who spend their wealth to obstruct from the path of Allah will be driven to Hellfire so that Allah separates the group of filthy disbelievers from the group of pure believers and [so that] He piles up the filthy people, deeds, and wealth one atop the other, then put them in Hellfire. Those are the losers because they lost themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection.",
  8038:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those from your people who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger, that indeed if they abstain from their disbelief in Allah and His Messenger and [abstain from] obstructing those that believe in Allah from His path, Allah will forgive them whatever preceded from their sins because Islam wipes out what preceded it. But if they go back to their disbelief, Allah's way of dealing with the ancients has preceded that, if they rejected and persisted in their disbelief, He hastened their punishment.",
  8039:
      "O believers, fight your enemies from the disbelievers until there is no more polytheism, no obstruction to the Muslims from Allah's religion, and religion and obedience be for Allah alone without any partner in them. So if the disbelievers cease the polytheism and obstruction from Allah which they are upon, then leave them [alone], for indeed, Allah sees their actions. No hidden thing is concealed from Him.",
  8040:
      "And if they turn away from what they were ordered to do and from desisting from disbelief and obstruction from the way of Allah, then be certain, O believers, that Allah will support you against them. What an excellent sponsor for whom He sponsors, and what an excellent supporter for whom He supports. So whoever is sponsored by Him will triumph, and whoever is supported by Him will be victorious.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Preventing others from the Sacred Mosque is a great offence for which the offender deserves a punishment in this world prior to the punishment in the Hearafter.\n2. Upkeep of the Sacred Mosque and taking charge of it is an honour that only Allah’s allies who are mindful of Him deserve.\n3. The verses contain a warning to the disbelievers that their spending their wealth for falsehood will not accomplish anything. They will soon be overcome with regret and extreme remorse.\n4. Allah’s call to the disbelievers to repent and to believe is an open call to them despite their persistent stubbornness.\n5. The person whose protector and helper is Allah can have no fear. The person whose enemy is Allah can have no honour.",
  8041:
      "And know, O believers, that whatever you took from the disbelievers by force in Jihad (striving) for the sake of Allah shall be divided into five-fifths. Four-fifths shall be distributed to Mujahideen (those who fight for the sake of Allah), and the remaining fifth divided into five partitions: a portion for Allah and His Messenger, to be spent on the general expenses of the Muslims; a portion for the relatives of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم from the children of Hashim and the children of Al-Muttalib, a portion for orphans, a portion for the poor and the needy, and a portion for travelers who were stranded. Obey this if you believe in Allah and what We have revealed to our slave, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, on the day of the Battle of Badr, in which Allah made a distinction between truth and falsehood by giving you victory over your enemies. And Allah, who gave you victory, is able to do everything.",
  8042:
      "And remember, when you were on the near side of the valley towards Medina, the polytheists were on the far side towards Mecca, and the caravan was at a spot lower than you by the Red Sea. If you and the polytheists had agreed to meet at Badr, neither of you would have missed each other. But Allah (may He be Exalted) gathered you at Badr without an agreement to complete a matter that was to pass: the victory of the believers, the desertion of the disbelievers, the honoring of His religion, and the humiliation of polytheism. [That was] so that whoever died amongst them would die after proof had been established against him through the believers' victory despite their lack of numbers and equipment, and whoever lived would live after evidence and proof that Allah made apparent to him. So, no one will have any proof to argue against Allah. Allah hears everyone's statements and knows their actions. None of those are hidden from Him, and He will compensate them based on them.",
  8043:
      "Remember, O Messenger, one of Allah's blessings upon you and the believers was when Allah showed you a dream in which the polytheists were few. So you informed the believers about this; they took it as a good omen, and their determination to face the enemy in battle was strengthened. If Allah had shown the polytheists to you to be many, the morale of your Companions would have decreased, and they would have become afraid of fighting. However, Allah saved you all from that and protected them from losing courage. He, therefore, made them seem few in the eye of His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Indeed, he knows what the hearts contain and what the souls conceal.",
  8044:
      "And remember, O believers, when Allah showed the polytheists to you when you met them as few and made you bravely go forward towards fighting them. He also made you seem few in their eyes, so they came forward to fight you without thinking of leaving. Moreover, Allah would bring a predetermined matter by taking revenge on the polytheists by them being killed or captured and favoring the believers with victory and defeat of their enemies. To Allah alone, things return, and He will recompense the one who does evil for wrongdoing and the one who does good for good deeds.",
  8045:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow His Messenger, when you fight against a group of disbelievers, be patient when you meet them and do not become cowardly. Moreover, mention Allah much and call on Him because He is the One who can help you against them. Furthermore, pray to Him to grant you what you desire and protect you from what you fear.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Gains of war belong to Allah and He allocates them as He wills, without anyone else dictating the terms.\n2. Allah paves the way for the victory of the Muslims by giving them the right support that they need at the correct moment.\n3. Patience, steadfastness and remembering Allah much are among the main causes of victory.",
  8046:
      "Oblige Allah's obedience and the obedience of His Messenger in all of your statements, actions, and conditions. Do not differ in opinion because disagreement leads to weakness, cowardice, and losing strength. Be patient when meeting your enemy. Indeed, Allah is with those who are patient with victory, support, and help. Whoever Allah is with him is the victor inevitably.",
  8047:
      "Do not be like the polytheists who left Mecca with arrogance and showing off to people, and they turn people away from Allah's religion and prevent them from entering it. Allah encompasses what they do; nothing of their deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  8048:
      "Remember, O believers, among the blessings of Allah upon you is when the Devil made the polytheists' deeds seem good to them and encouraged them to meet the Muslims and fight them. He said: No one can defeat you today because I am your helper and refuge from your enemy. When the two teams met [the team of believers who had the angels as their support and the group of polytheists with them the Devil who will let them down], the Devil turned away [escaping] and said to the polytheists: I am innocent of you. I see the angels who have come to support the believers. I fear that Allah will destroy me. Allah's punishment is severe, and no one can bear His punishment.",
  8049:
      "Remember when the hypocrites and those weak in faith were saying: The religion of these Muslims, which promises them victory over their enemies despite lack of numbers and feeble equipment and the significant number of their enemy and the strength of their gear, has deceived them. They have not understood that he who relies upon Allah alone and trusts in the victory that He has promised, then indeed, Allah will support him and not abandon him, however weak he may be. Allah is Mighty; no one can overcome Him. He is Wise in His predetermination and legislation.",
  8050:
      "And if you watch, O Messenger, those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers when the angels take and snatch their souls, striking their faces when they face towards them. Moreover, striking their backs when they try to run away, and they say to them: Taste, O disbelievers, the burning torment! If you watched that, you would see a severe heart-wrenching sight.",
  8051:
      "That painful torment when your souls are taken, O disbelievers, and the burning torment in your graves and the Hereafter is caused by what your hands have earned in this world. For Allah does not wrong people, but He judges between them with justice, for He is the just judge.",
  8052:
      "This torment befalling those disbelievers is not exclusive to them. Instead, Allah's established way of dealing with disbelievers is what He preordained every time and place. The family of Pharaoh and the nations before them were tormented when they disbelieved in the signs of Allah (may He be Exalted). So, Allah punished them for their sins with His might and power. Indeed, Allah is Strong and cannot be overpowered or defeated, and He severely penalizes those who disobey Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride is a serious illness that affects an individual’s personality and quickly ruins his nature.\n2. Patience helps in coping with hardships and difficulties. Also, Allah sends divine help to the person who is patient in obeying His sacred law. This is something witnessed in various walks of life.\n3. Quarrels and disputes lead to disunity in the community and warn of defeat, withdrawal and loss of strength, support and power.\n4. The verses show that entitlement to favours depend on correct beliefs, good actions and high morals.\n5. Faith makes a person go forward to do amazing things which even great armies will not advance to do.\n6. One of Allah’s customs is to punish those who do wrong by sinning.",
  8053:
      "That severe punishment is because when Allah favors a people a blessing from Him, He does not take it away from them until they change themselves—from their pure state of faith, righteousness, and thanks for the blessings—to a bad state of disbelief in Allah, disobeying Him and rejecting His blessing. Verily, Allah hears the statements of His slaves and knows about their actions; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  8054:
      "The case of these disbelievers is like that of others who disbelieved in Allah, such as the people of Pharaoh and those who rejected Allah before them. They rejected the signs of their Lord, so Allah destroyed them because of the sins they committed. Allah destroyed the people of Pharaoh by causing them to drown in the sea. The people of Pharaoh and the nations before them were all wrongdoers because they disbelieved in Allah and their association with Him. They, therefore, deserved His punishment (may He be Exalted), so He inflicted it on them.",
  8055:
      "The worst of those who move on the earth are those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers. Likewise, they do not believe even if every sign was to come to them because of their insistence on disbelief. So, their means of guidance have been disrupted, such as intellect, hearing, and sight.",
  8056:
      "Those with whom covenants and promises [such as Banu Qurayza] were concluded. Then, they break the covenant every time you make it with them. Furthermore, they have no fear of Allah, so they do not fulfill their promises nor abide by the covenants taken from them.",
  8057:
      "If you meet those, O Messenger, who break their covenants in war, then make a severely exemplary punishment of them so that others hear about it. They may learn from that and become afraid of fighting you and supporting your enemies against you.",
  8058:
      "And if you fear, O Messenger, that a people with whom you made a covenant will cheat and break the covenant with a sign that appears to you, then inform them that the covenant is canceled so that they are equal with you in the knowledge of that. And do not attack them suddenly without informing them because doing so will be a betrayal on your part. Indeed, Allah does not love the traitors, but He hates them, so beware of treachery.",
  8059:
      "Those disbelieving should not think they have skipped Allah's punishment and escaped it because they cannot do so. Instead, it will surely fall upon them.",
  8060:
      "Prepare, O believers, what you can prepare in terms of numbers and equipment, such as archery. Moreover, prepare for them whatever horses you have stored for the sake of Allah to terrify the enemies of Allah and your enemies from the disbelievers lurking around you. Moreover, to frighten other people with it whom you do not know, and you do not know the hostility they harbor against you. Instead, Allah alone is the One who knows them and knows what they have in their hearts. Whatever money you spend in the cause of Allah, whether small or large, Allah will reward you in this world and give you its full, undiminished reward in the Hereafter. So hasten to spend in His cause.",
  8061:
      "And if they lean toward reconciliation and giving up fighting, then, O Messenger, incline toward it: make a covenant with them and place your reliance and trust in Allah because He will never let you down. He is All-Hearing of their words, Omniscient of their intentions and actions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the benefits of the legal punishments for crimes is that they deter many from committing those crimes. They also deter those who have committed them from repeating the offence.\n2. One of the characteristics of the believers is that they fulfil the pledges they make with others, unless it is proven that they were treacherous.\n3. The Muslims must remain prepared with various types of weapons and plans to frighten the enemy.\n4. It is permissible to make peace with the enemy if it is in the best interests of the Muslims.",
  8062:
      "And if, by inclining to reconciliation, they intend to deceive you, O Messenger, so that they can prepare to fight you, then Allah is sufficient for you against their scheming and deception. It is He who strengthened you with His victory and the victory of the believers among Al-Muhajireen (the Emigrants) and Al-Ansar (the Supporters).",
  8063:
      "Likewise, He brought together the hearts of the believers [with whom He assisted you] after it was dispersed. If you had spent all the wealth on earth to get their dispersed hearts together, you would not have been able to do so. However, Allah alone brought them together. He is Mighty in His dominion, and nothing can overpower Him. He is Wise in His decree, planning, and sacred laws.",
  8064:
      "O Prophet, Allah protects you from the evil of your enemies, and He protects the believers with you. So, trust in Allah and rely on Him.",
  8065:
      "O Prophet, urge the believers to fight and encourage them to do so in a way that strengthens their determination and lifts their spirits. If there are twenty of you, O believers, who are patient in fighting the disbelievers, they will overcome two hundred of the disbelievers. Likewise, if there are one hundred who are patient among you, they will overcome one thousand of the disbelievers. That is because the disbelievers are a people who do not understand Allah's Sunnah (the way of Allah) by giving victory to His allies and defeating His enemies. They also do not realize the purpose of fighting, for they are fighting for superiority in this world.",
  8066:
      "Allah has made it easier for you now, O believers, since He knows your weakness. Therefore, he has made it easier for you [with His kindness] and has made it obligatory that one of you remains patient against two disbelievers instead of ten. So, if there are one hundred among you who remain patient in fighting against the disbelievers, they will defeat two hundred. Likewise, if there are one thousand among you who remain patient, they will vanquish two thousand of the disbelievers by Allah's permission. Therefore, with His support and victory, Allah is with those believers who remain patient.",
  8067:
      "It should not be for a prophet to have prisoners among the disbelievers who fight against him until he kills many of them. Thus, the terror enters their hearts, so they do not return to fighting. By taking captives from Badr, O believers, you want to receive ransom, but Allah desires the Hereafter [for you], which is obtained by making religion victorious and powerful. Allah is Mighty in His essence, His attributes, and His domination. No one can overcome Him. He is Wise in His decree and sacred laws.",
  8068:
      "Had it not been for a book from Allah that preceded his decree and destiny [in which it had already been decided] that He permitted you the spoils and allowed you to ransom the prisoners, a severe torment would have occurred to you because of what you took from the spoils of war. Likewise, the ransom you took from the prisoners [at Badr] before a revelation came down from Allah to permit that.",
  8069:
      "So consume, O believers, what you took from the disbelievers of the spoils of war, for it is lawful for you. And fear Allah by obeying His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Indeed, Allah is forgiving to His faithful slaves, Merciful to them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses contain a promise from Allah to His believing servants that He will be sufficient for them and aid them against their enemies.\n2. Muslims are obligated to go forward striving in Allah’s path with high spirits, remarkable bravery, unwavering patience and firm determination.\n3. Muslims are obligated to remain patient in front of the enemy, unless there is a valid excuse to do otherwise.\n4. Allah loves noble things for His servants and dislikes that which is trivial. He therefore urges them to seek the eternal reward of the Afterlife.\n5. The ransom of captives or their release can only take place after complete domination and authority over the disbelievers is achieved and the supremacy of the Islamic state is demonstrated to others.",
  8070:
      "O Prophet, say to those who fell into your hands among the polytheist captives you captured on the day of Badr: If Allah knows good in your hearts and good intentions, He will give you better than what was taken from you as a ransom. So do not grieve over what was taken from you. Allah is Forgiving and Merciful to those of His slaves who repent, and He [also] forgives your sins. This promise of Allah was fulfilled for Al-Abbas, the uncle of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, and for others like him who accepted Islam after being captured.",
  8071:
      "And if they intend, O Muhammad, to betray you by the words they utter, then they have betrayed Allah before, and Allah has given you victory over them, so some of them were killed, and others were taken captive. They should, therefore, wait for something similar to happen if they return to their evil. And Allah is All-Knowing of His creation and what works for them, Wise in His planning.",
  8072:
      "Those who believed in Allah believed in His Messenger, acted upon His sacred law, migrated from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam or to a place where they could worship Allah safely, and strived by spending their money and their lives to raise the word of Allah. Likewise, those who hosted them in their homes and supported them - those emigrants and those locals who supported them are allies and friends of one another in providing support and assistance. As for those who believed in Allah but did not emigrate from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam, it is not upon you, O believers, that you help them and protect them until they migrate for the sake of Allah. If the disbelievers oppress them and they [the weak believers] seek your victory and help, then help them against their enemies unless a covenant between you and their enemy is still in place and they [the disbelievers] did not break. Allah sees everything you do. Nothing of your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  8073:
      "And those who disbelieve in Allah are united in their disbelief, so they support each other. A believer should not be loyal to them. Suppose you do not support the believers and stand hostile to the disbelievers. In that case, there will be a Fitnah (suffering weakness, wars, battles, polytheism, etc.) for the believers as they did not find anyone to support them from among their brothers in religion. And there will be grand corruption on earth by obstructing Allah's path.",
  8074:
      "Those who believed in Allah and emigrated in His path and those who provided shelter and assistance to the emigrants for Allah's sake are the ones who can be genuinely described as having faith. Their reward from Allah is forgiveness for their sins and a generous provision from Him, which is Paradise.",
  8075:
      "And those who believed in Allah after the faith of those who preceded Islam from among Al-Muhajireen (the Emigrants) and Al-Ansar (the Supporters), who emigrated from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam and strived in Allah's path so that Allah's Word may be the highest and the word of the disbelievers may be the lowest – they are part of you, O believers. They will have the same rights and obligations as you have. Under Allah's final sacred inheritance laws, family members are closer to one another than in the previous Islamic inheritance system based on faith and emigration. Allah knows everything. Nothing is hidden from Him, for He knows what is best for His slaves, so He legislates it for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believers must encourage captives to accept faith.\n2. The verses contain glad tidings for the believers that they will continue to be assisted against the idolaters as long as they hold on to the material and spiritual means for such assistance.\n3. If Muslims are not united against the people of disbelief their strength will not become apparent and great corruption will arise because of that.\n4. Fulfilment of pledges and treaties holds great virtue in the Sacred Law of Islam, even if this is opposed to the interests of some Muslims.\n5. When Muslims cooperate together they become powerful and can then defeat their enemies.",
  9000:
      "The Repentance (Surah At-Tawbah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDisassociating from the polytheists and hypocrites and struggling against them while keeping the door of repentance open for those who turn in penitence.\n•    Explanation:",
  9001:
      "This is a declaration of dissociation from Allah and His Messenger. And an announcement of the termination of the covenants that you, O Muslims, had made with the polytheists in the Arabian Peninsula.",
  9002:
      "So travel safely, O polytheists, on earth for a period of four months, after which there will be no covenant for you or protection. And be sure that you will never escape Allah's torment and punishment if you continue to disbelieve in Him. Also, be sure that Allah humiliates the disbelievers by being killed or taken captive in this world and entering The Fire on The Day of Resurrection. This includes those who broke their covenant and those who had an open covenant without any fixed period. As for those with whom you made a covenant for a limited period, their covenant will be completed until the end of the specified period, even if this is longer than four months.",
  9003:
      "Proclamation from Allah and proclamation from His Messenger to all people on the Day of Sacrifice that Allah (may He be Exalted) is unassociated with the polytheists as His Messenger. So if you, O polytheists, repent from your polytheism, then your repentance is better for you. If you turn away from repentance, then be certain that you will not get away from Allah and will not escape from His punishment. O Messenger, inform those who disbelieved in Allah with that which will upset them: a painful torment that awaits them.",
  9004:
      "Except those of the polytheists with whom you made a covenant, and they fulfilled your covenant. Moreover, they did not shorten anything from it [they honored the covenant in full], so complete the fulfillment of their covenant until its term expires. Allah loves those who fear Him by obeying His commands, including completion of the covenant, and avoiding His prohibitions, including treason.",
  9005:
      "When the sacred months (Dhū Al-Qa'dah, Dhul-Hijjah, Muḥarram, and Rajab) during which you assure the safety of your enemies end, then kill the polytheists wherever you meet them, capture them, besiege them in their fortresses and lie in wait in watch for them on their paths. Then, if they repent to Allah from their polytheism, establish the prayer, and give the zakat (obligatory alms) from their wealth, they have become your brothers in Islam, so desist from fighting them. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful towards those of His slaves who repent to Him.",
  9006:
      "And if one of the polytheists, whose blood and wealth is permissible, comes to you, O Messenger, and requests your protection, respond to his request so that he can hear the Quran. Then, take them to a place where they will be safe. That is because the disbelievers are a people who do not know the realities of this religion. So, if they learn it from hearing the recitation of the Quran, they may be guided.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There is a clear indication in the verses, that Islam necessitates making external relations with enemies based on peace, security and mutual understanding.\n2. Islam values treaties and requires fulfilment of them. It regards the upholding of treaties to be a result of faith and a necessary element of Mindfulness.\n3. It is permissible to enter into a truce, treaty and agreement with non-Muslims in order to realize certain interests if they adhere to the provisions contained therein.\n4. Keeping up the prayer and giving charity is an indication of being a Muslim. Doing such actions will protect life and wealth and will grant the person who does them the rights of Muslims in terms of the sanctity of their lives and wealth. This will apply unless Islam permits them as in the case of commission of a capital offence such as murder of an innocent person or treason.\n5. The granting of protection and safety to a war enemy who requests it is permissible. This is so that they may learn about Islam. Such a law shows a high level of leniency and respect when dealing with disbelievers, and indicates that peace is a preferred way of acting for Muslims.",
  9007:
      "It is not correct for those who associate partners with Allah to have a covenant and an assurance of safety from Allah and His Messenger, except for the covenant you made, O Muslims, with those polytheists at the Sacred Mosque during the al-Hudaybiyah peace treaty. As long as they uphold the covenant with you and do not break it, then you should also remain upon it and not break it. Indeed, Allah loves those of His slaves who take heed of Him by obeying His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  9008:
      "How can they have a covenant with you and an assurance of safety when they are your enemies? And if they win over you [and conquer you], they will not consider Allah concerning you or respect any kinship relationship or covenant. But instead, inflict severe torment on you?! They please you with the pleasing words that their tongues utter, but their hearts do not obey and agree with their tongues, so they do not fulfill what they say, and most of them are out of obedience to Allah for breaking the covenant.",
  9009:
      "They took compensation and replaced following the verses of Allah, including the fulfillment of covenants, for a trivial worthless price from the wreckage of the world with which they reach their lusts and whims. So, they prevented themselves from following the truth, turned away from it, and prevented others from the truth. They have gone wrong with the work they were doing.",
  9010:
      "They do not respect Allah, kinship, or covenant with a believer because of their hostility. They transgress the limits of Allah because of their injustice and aggression.",
  9011:
      "If they repent to Allah from their disbelief, pronounce the two testimonies, establish the prayer, and give the Zakat (obligatory alms) from their wealth. They have become Muslims, and they are your brothers in religion. They then have the same rights and duties you have, and it is not permissible for you to fight them. Their acceptance of Islam protects their blood, money, and honor. Allah explains the verses clearly to people who know, as they are the ones who will benefit from them and will cause others to benefit as well.",
  9012:
      "And if those polytheists with whom you pledged not to fight for a known period break their covenants and promises and insult your religion and belittle it, then fight them, for they are the leaders of disbelief and its chiefs. Furthermore, they have no covenants nor promises to spare their blood. Fight them in the hope that they will end their disbelief, breaking of covenants, and derogation of the religion.",
  9013:
      "Why do you, O believers, not fight a people who have broken their covenants and treaties and who have strived in their meeting at Dār Al-Nadwah, to expel the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم from Mecca? They started the fight against you in the first place when they assisted [the Children of] Bakr, allies of Quraysh, against [the Children of] Khuzā'ah, allies of the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Is it because you fear to meet them in battle? Then Allah (may He be Exalted) is more rightful for you to fear if you are true believers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show that fighting against the idolaters who broke their treaty was due to many reasons, the most important of which was their breaking of the treaty.\n2. The treaty that is respected by Allah and His Messenger is with those who do not break it. Any person who upholds his treaty will be treated accordingly.\n3. The verses contain proof that those who do not discharge the ritual prayer or the prescribed charity will be fought against until they discharge the same -as was done by Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him.)\n4. Some scholars use the words ‘insult your religion’ as evidence that the person who deliberately insults and mocks the religion must be put to death.\n5. The verses indicate that the believer who fears Allah alone should be the bravest of all people in a fight.",
  9014:
      "O believers, fight these polytheists. If you fight them, Allah will torment them with your hands by killing and humiliating them with defeat and captivity. Also, He will grant you victory over them by making you [believers] overcome them and healing the hearts of believing people who did not witness the fighting with what happened to their enemy in terms of killing, captivity, defeat, and the victory of the believers over them.",
  9015:
      "He removes the rage from the hearts of His believing slaves because of the victory they gained over them. Allah accepts repentance from whom He wills among those who were stubborn if they repented, as happened to some of the people of Mecca on the day of the conquest. Allah knows the sincerity of those who repent. He is Wise in His creation, planning, and legislation.",
  9016:
      "Did you, O believers, think Allah would leave you without a test? Testing is one of Allah's established ways. You will be tested until Allah [clearly] proves those who strive with sincerity for Him, who did not take besides Allah, His Messenger, or the believers, a lining from the unbelievers to be loyal to them. Likewise, do not make intimate friends with the disbelievers. Allah knows what you do, and nothing is hidden from Him. He will recompense you accordingly.",
  9017:
      "The polytheists should not attend or care for the mosques of Allah, with worship and types of obedience, while they admit themselves to disbelief in what they show of it. Those whose deeds have been invalidated because the condition of their acceptance, which is faith, has been lost. On the Day of Resurrection, they will enter the Fire to abide in it forever unless they repent of polytheism before their death.",
  9018:
      "Only those who deserve to sustain the mosques and fulfill their rights are those who believe in Allah alone, do not associate anyone with Him, believe in the Day of Resurrection, establish prayer, give the zakat on their wealth, and do not fear anyone except Allah the Exalted. These are the ones who are hoped to be guided to the straight path, but the polytheists are far from that.",
  9019:
      "Have you, O polytheists, made those in charge of giving water to the pilgrims and taking care of the Sacred Mosque like those who believed in Allah, did not associate any partner with Him, believed in the Day of Resurrection, and strived with their lives and money so that the word of Allah would be the highest, and the word of the unbelievers the lowest? They are never equal to Allah, and Allah does not profit the oppressors with polytheism, even if they do good deeds, such as giving water to the pilgrim.",
  9020:
      "Those who combine a belief in Allah with migration from the lands of disbelief to the lands of Islam and striving for Allah's sake with money and souls have the greatest rank with Allah than others, and those who are characterized by these qualities are the prizewinners of Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points: 1 The verses show the love of Allah for His believing servants, and His care for them in their different situations, making the aim of His sacred law the healing of what is in their breasts and the removal of their anger. 2 The legislation of fighting to achieve this great aim, to make clear the true believers who are dedicated to the religion of Allah from those who are liars, and claim that they have faith. 3 The rightful maintainers of places of worship are those who have true faith, and who do righteous deeds, among the most important of which are performing the prayer and giving the charity which is a duty, and who have awe of Allah, which is the root of all goodness. 4 Striving for Allah’s sake and having faith in Him is much better than giving water to the pilgrim and maintaining the Sacred Mosque, because faith is the root of the religion, while striving for Allah’s sake is the highest level of this.",
  9021:
      "Allah tells them, their Lord, what makes them happy of His mercy and bestows His satisfaction so that He will never be angry with them. Likewise, by entering paradises in which they have perpetual bliss that never ceases.",
  9022:
      "They will remain in those paradises for an endless stay as a reward for them for the righteous deeds that they used to do in this world. Indeed, Allah greatly rewards those who obey His commands, avoid His prohibitions, and are faithful to His religion.",
  9023:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow what His Messenger brought, do not take your fathers and brothers in bloodlines and others from your kinship a close and trustworthy friend allying with them. Likewise, by divulging the secrets of the believers to them and consulting with them if they prefer disbelief over faith in Allah alone. Whoever makes them allies while they remain in disbelief and shows them affection has disobeyed Allah and oppressed himself by placing himself in a doom situation because of disobedience.",
  9024:
      "Say, O Messenger: If your fathers, O believers, your children, brothers, spouses, relatives, the wealth you have earned, the trade you love to flourish and fear to decline, and your homes where you are pleased to live. If all of these are more beloved to you than Allah, His Messenger, and striving for His sake, wait for what Allah will send down on you of torment and punishment. Allah does not help those who abandon His obedience to do what pleases Him.",
  9025:
      "Allah has certainly supported you, O believers, against your enemies among the polytheists in many battles, despite your deficient numbers and weak equipment, when you relied on Allah and took the appropriate measures. You were not impressed by your abundance, for abundance was not the cause of your victory over them. And We supported you on the day of Hunayn when you were impressed by your abundance, so you said: We will not be defeated today from deficiency. Then your abundance which impressed you did not benefit you at all, so your enemy overwhelmed you, and the earth became constricted upon you, despite its vastness. Then you ran away from your enemies, fleeing in defeat.",
  9026:
      "Then, after you [believers] fled from your enemy, Allah sent down tranquility upon His Messenger and sent it down to the believers, so they stood firm to fight. Moreover, He sent down angels that you did not see and punished those who disbelieved [for what happened to them] in terms of killing, captivity, taking money, and capturing offspring. Likewise, the compensation these people were rewarded is the recompense of the disbelievers who rejected their Messenger and denied what he came with.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The great ranks of those who strive for Allah’s sake, for them is the highest rank before Allah among all those of rank, for them is the highest privilege and position, and they are successful, triumphant, and are saved, they are those who their Lord gives the good news of eternal bliss to.\n2. In the verses is the greatest proof of the necessity of love for Allah and His messenger, and the precedence of this love over the love of anything else.\n3. The special mention of the day of Hunayn among other battles, because it was an example of Allah’s help coming because of following the command of Allah and His messenger, peace be upon him, and defeat coming because of preferring worldly pleasure to following them.\n4. The verses show that victory is only through Allah’s help, and not due to being great in number, since they did not triumph because of their great numbers.\n5. The blessing of the sending down of calm from Allah. The calm sent to the Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him, reassured him concerning the Muslims with him, and gave him certainty of Allah’s support, and the calm sent to the believers made them stand firm and gave them courage, after their anxiety and fear.",
  9027:
      "Then, whoever repents of his disbelief and misguidance after that torture, Allah repents of him and accepts his repentance. Moreover, Allah is Forgiving to those of His slaves who repent, Merciful to them, as He accepts their repentance after disbelief and committing sins.",
  9028:
      "O you who believed in Allah and His Messenger and followed the sacred law that He legislated for them, the polytheists are indeed unclean because of their disbelief, injustice, reprehensible morals, and bad habits. So, they do not enter the sacred area of Mecca [including the Sacred Mosque] even if they want to perform Hajj or Umrah after this year, which is the ninth year of the Hijra. If you fear, O believers, poverty because of the interruption of what they used to bring to you of various foods and trades, then Allah will suffice you of His bounty if He wills. Indeed, Allah knows the situation that you are in, and He is wise in what He manages for you.",
  9029:
      "Fight, O believers, the disbelievers who do not have faith in Allah as their deity without any partner; do not believe in the Day of Resurrection; do not avoid what Allah and His Messenger prohibited for them of carrion, pork, intoxicants, usury, and other matters; and who do not submit to what Allah legislated, among the Jews and Christians, until they pay the Jizyah [tax] with their [own] hands, humbled and subdued.",
  9030:
      "The Jews associated partners with Allah when they claimed that Uzair was the son of Allah. Likewise, the Christians associated partners with Him when they claimed that the Messiah Jesus was the son of Allah. That saying that they fabricated, they spoke with their mouths without establishing proof of it. They are similar in this saying to the polytheists saying before them who said: The angels are the daughters of Allah. Allah is Transcendent and far beyond that. May Allah destroy them. How do they turn away from the straightforward truth to falsehood?!",
  9031:
      "The Jews made their scholars lords instead of Allah, as did the Christians with their monks. They would permit for them what Allah prohibited them from and prohibit them from what Allah permitted for them. The Christians made the Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, a deity with Allah. Allah did not command the Jews' scholars and Christians' monks, nor Ezra and Jesus, son of Mary, except that they worship Him alone and not associate any partners with Him, for He, may He be glorified, is one deity. There is no rightful object of worship besides Him. Exalted is He from having a partner, as these polytheists and others say.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some of the greatest blessings for the Muslims have been when their warring enemies have become Muslims too, as occurred with the Hawazin tribe and the Tartars.\n2. The verses show that the heart is allowed to be concerned with the ways of gaining provision and it is not contrary to relying on Allah.\n3. The verses show that provision is not due to effort, but is a blessing from Allah Who controls its distribution.\n4. The Jizyah tax is one of three choices Islam offers its enemies, and the aim of all three choices is to strengthen the Muslims and weaken the disbelievers.\n5. The Jews associated partners with Allah and did not recognise His greatness, glory be to Him!\n6. Allah encourages the believers to engage with the Jews and Christians on account of idolatry and lack of respect for the sacred laws.",
  9032:
      "These disbelievers and others who are in a sect of disbelief, with their fabrications and their denial of what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought, want to destroy and invalidate Islam. Likewise, they want to invalidate the clear arguments and clear proofs of Allah's Oneness and that what His Messenger got is true. Allah (may He be Exalted) refuses except to complete His religion, show it, and elevate it over others. If the unbelievers hate His religion's completion, manifestation, and elevation, Allah will complete, show, and elevate it. If Allah wills something, the will of others is invalidated.",
  9033:
      "It is Allah (may He be Exalted) who sent His Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم with the Quran, which is a guide for people. Likewise, He sent him with the religion of truth (Islam's religion) to elevate it with its arguments, proofs, and rulings over other faiths, even if the polytheists hate that.",
  9034:
      "O you who believe in Allah and do what Allah has prescribed for them, many of the scholars of the Jews (Rabbis) and many of the worshipers of the Christians (Monks) take people's money without a legitimate right. They take it by bribery and other things, preventing people from entering Allah's religion. And those who collect gold and silver and do not pay what is required of them of its Zakat (obligatory alms), then inform them, O Messenger, of the painful torment that will afflict them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  9035:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, what they collected and denied its right will be kindled in the Fire. And when it is incredibly heated, it will be placed on their foreheads, sides, and backs. It will be said to them as a way of reprimanding: This is the money you collected and did not fulfill its due rights, so taste the evil consequences of what you used to collect and not fulfill rights and the consequence of that.",
  9036:
      "In Allah's judgment and decree, the number of months of the year is 12 months, as Allah established in al-Lawh al-Mahfuz (the Preserved Tablet), the first thing He created the heavens and the earth. Of these 12 months, there are four months in which Allah has forbidden fighting. Three are consecutive (Dhu'l-Qa'dah, Dhu'l-Hijjah, and Muharram), and one is not (the month of Rajab). The aforementioned are the number of months in the year, and the prohibition of four is the straight religion. Do not wrong yourselves in these sacred months by fighting within them and violating their sanctity. Moreover, fight all polytheists as they fight you all. Know that Allah is with those who fear Him -by obeying what He commanded and avoiding what He prohibited- with victory and steadfastness. Whomever Allah is with, no one will defeat him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The religion of Allah is apparent and victorious, no matter how its enemies may try to harm it out of their envy.\n2. The emergence of Islam over other ways took place in the world through many people from different parts of the world adopting it, despite the people and the leaders of their communities disliking this, and opposing it in any way they could.\n3. Unjustly using up the wealth of people is forbidden, as is preventing people from Allah’s way.\n4. Hoarding money without spending it for the sake of Allah is forbidden.\n5. The importance of being Mindful privately and publicly, especially when fighting against those who deny the truth, since the believer is mindful of Allah in every situation.",
  9037:
      "Delaying the sanctity of the month of Muharram to a month that is not Muharram and making it in its place [as the Arabs used to do during the Jahiliyyah (the time of ignorance, i.e., pre-Islam)] is an increase in disbelief over their disbelief in Allah. They disbelieved in His rule in the sacred months. The Devil misled those disbelieving in Allah when He enacted this evil/lousy practice. They would declare a sacred month not to be sacred for one year, exchanging it for one of the permissible months, and they keep it sacred for a year to agree with the number of months that Allah has made sacred, even if they violate its specifics. They do not make a month permissible except that they forbid a month in its place, so they make permissible what Allah has forbidden from the sacred months and violate his rule. The Devil made their evil deeds seem attractive, so they did them, including what they invented by postponing the sacred months. And Allah does not grant success to the disbelievers who insist on their disbelief.",
  9038:
      "O you who believed in Allah and His Messenger and did what He legislated to them. What is the matter with you if you were called to the Jihad (striving/fighting) for the sake of Allah to fight your enemy, you slowed down, and you tend to settle in your homes?! Have you been satisfied with the fleeting enjoyment of this worldly life and its intermittent pleasures instead of the everlasting bliss of the Hereafter that Allah has prepared for the Mujahideen (the fighters) for His sake?! The enjoyment of this worldly life in comparison to the Hereafter is nothing but despicable, so how can a sane person choose a mortal over an eternal and a despicable over a great?!",
  9039:
      "If you do not go out, O believers, for striving for the sake of Allah to fight your enemy, Allah will punish you with persecution, humiliation, and other things. He will replace you with people who are devoted and obedient to Allah, who rush to fight when called. And you do not harm Him [in anything] by violating His command, for He is self-sustaining of you, and you are the poor to him. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing can hinder Him. He is capable of supporting His religion and His Prophet without you all.",
  9040:
      "If you do not help, O believers, Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and respond to his call to strive for the sake of Allah, then Allah has already helped him without you being with him. It was when the polytheists took him and Abu-Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) out, and there was no third with them when they were in the cave of Thawr, hiding from The disbelievers who were searching for them. The Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said to his companion Abu-Bakr Al-Siddiq when he feared that the polytheists would reach him: Do not grieve, for Allah is with us in His support and victory. Then, Allah sent down His tranquility upon the heart of His Messenger and sent down soldiers you do not see, which are angels supporting him. He made the word of the polytheists the lowest and the word of Allah the highest when He elevated Islam. Allah is Mighty in His Essence, power, and dominion, and no one can overpower Him. He is Wise in His planning, His decree, and His Legislation.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Practices that go against sacred law, which continue without being rejected, people stop seeing them as incorrect, and they may start thinking they are good practices.\n2. Not rallying for battle when called upon to do so is one of the great sins, which earns a firm punishment, because of the great harm it causes.\n3. The sending down of peace and security which Allah causes to enter the hearts is one of the perfect blessings of Allah to His servant in times of difficulty and fear, when hearts are confused. It comes according to someone’s understanding of the nature of their Lord, and their trust in His true promise, and according to their faith and courage.\n4. Even the best of believing servants feel grief, especially when they fear the loss of something for the general good.",
  9041:
      "March forth, O believers, for striving for the sake of Allah in hardship and ease, whether young or old, and striving with your wealth and selves. Going out and striving for the sake of Allah with money and life is more beneficial in the life of this world and the Hereafter than sitting and becoming attached to your wealth and self. If you truly know that, then be eager to obey.",
  9042:
      "If what you call upon those of the hypocrites who asked you for permission to stay behind were an easy spoil and a journey without hardship, they would have followed you, O Prophet. However, the distance you called them to travel to the enemy was too far for them, so they fell behind. Likewise, those who asked permission [from the hypocrites] to stay behind will swear by Allah when you return to them, saying: If only we could go out to strive with you, we would go out. They destroy themselves by exposing themselves to Allah's punishment because of their backwardness and this false oath. Allah knows they are liars in their claim and their oath.",
  9043:
      "May Allah forgive you, O Messenger, for your diligence in allowing them to stay behind. Why did you permit it? Was it to discern who among them was truthful in their excuses and who was lying, so that you could authorize the honest and not the liars?",
  9044:
      "It is not the business of those who truly believe in Allah and the Day of Resurrection with sincere faith to ask you, O Messenger, for permission to stay behind from striving for Allah's sake by their wealth and themselves. Instead, it is their business to rally when they are called to fight and to strive by their wealth and themselves. Allah knows those among His slaves who are fearful and do not seek your permission except for excuses preventing them from going out with you.",
  9045:
      "Those who ask you, O Messenger, for permission to stay behind from striving for the sake of Allah are hypocrites who do not believe in Allah or the Day of Resurrection. Their hearts were struck by doubt about Allah's religion. Likewise, they hesitate in their doubts, are confused, and are not guided to the truth in their doubts.",
  9046:
      "If they were truthful in their claim that they wanted to go out with you to strive for the sake of Allah, they would have prepared for it by preparing the equipment. However, Allah hated their going out with you, so it was burdensome for them to go out until they preferred to sit in their homes with the sick, weak people, women, and children.",
  9047:
      "Allah reassured the believers that their deployment in battle was more harmful than their staying back, despite the demoralizing effect of their staying behind, stating: \n It is good that these hypocrites do not go out with you. If they go out with you, they will only increase corruption among you by demoralizing people and casting doubts. Moreover, they would hasten in your ranks to spread gossip to disperse you. And among you, O believers, who listen to what they spread of lies, accept and spread it, and then disagreement arises between you. Allah is All-Knowing of the unjust hypocrites who cast intrigues and doubts among the believers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A person has a duty to strive with their body and wealth whenever there is a need.\n2. True worship only occurs with sincerity and following what is instructed, no matter what the situation. Those who do this are honoured by Allah.\n3. Fighting for the sake of Allah has a great reward, leading to one of two good things: either victory, raising the word of Allah and making the Muslims strong, or being martyred for the sake of Allah, ensuring the bliss of the Afterlife and the enjoyment of being in Paradise eternally.\n4. False oath brings about ruin.\n5. The importance of not being too hasty, and of making sure of things, taking the time to consider them, not being deceived by the way things seem, scrutinising and checking them.\n6. Those who have faith in Allah and the Last Day do not ask to be excused from striving with their wealth and their selves.\n7. Preventing the hypocrites from going out with the believers was a way that Allah took care of the believers, as a mercy and kindness, so that those who would harm them did not accompany and mix with them.",
  9048:
      "These hypocrites were keen to corrupt you by dividing the word of the believers and dispersing their unity before the Battle of Tabuk. They diversified and diverted matters for you, O Messenger, by planning tricks. Perhaps their tricks affect your determination to fight. Until Allah's victory and support for you came, strengthened His religion, and subdued His enemies. They hated this because they wanted the victory of falsehood over the right.",
  9049:
      "Among the hypocrites is the one who brings various excuses, saying: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to forsake striving [in battle against the disbelievers] and do not press me to depart with you so that I would not fall into sin due to the tribulation of the women of the enemy, the Romans, when I witness them. Have they not fallen into a tribulation greater than what they claimed: the tribulation of hypocrisy and forsaking? Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, Hell will surely surround the disbelievers, none of them eluding it, nor will they find an escape from it.",
  9050:
      "If you obtain a blessing from Allah, O Messenger of Allah, with what makes you happy regarding victory or spoil, they hate that and grieve for it. On the other hand, if a calamity befalls you due to the severity or victory of an enemy, these hypocrites say: We took precautions for ourselves. Moreover, we took firmness when we did not go out to fight as the believers did, so they [the believers] were afflicted by killing and captivity. Then, these hypocrites go back to their families, rejoicing in their safety.",
  9051:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these hypocrites: We will only get what Allah has written for us. For He [Almighty] is our master and refuge to whom we seek shelter, and we rely on Him in our affairs. To Him alone, the believers delegate their affairs, for He is sufficient for them and the best guardian.",
  9052:
      "Say, O Messenger, to them: Are you waiting for anything but victory or martyrdom to happen to us?! Yet we are waiting for Allah to send down on you a torment from Him that will destroy you or punish you with our own hands by killing and capturing you [if He permits us to fight you. Wait for our consequence, for we are waiting for your consequence.",
  9053:
      "Say, O Messenger, to them: Spend what you spend of your money, willingly or unwillingly. What you spend on it will not be accepted by you because of your disbelief and your deviation from Allah's obedience.",
  9054:
      "Nothing prevented them from accepting their expenses except for [three things]: their disbelief in Allah and His Messenger, their laziness and burden when they pray, and that they do not spend their money voluntarily. Instead, they spend it unwillingly and with hatred because they do not hope for a reward in their prayers or spending.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The hypocrites are devoted to trying to cause harm to the Muslims through scheming and spying.\n2. Staying behind from striving for the sake of Allah is a great tribulation, and is disloyalty to Allah and to His Messenger.\n3. In the verses, the Muslims are taught not to be grievous about what afflicts them, so that they do not become weak and lose hope; and that they should accept Allah’s decree for them, and hope for the pleasure of their Lord, because surely Allah wants His Religion to be victorious.\n4. Entrusting everything to Allah, after taking appropriate measures, is one of the foundations of faith.\n5. One of the signs of weak faith is being lazy in the performance of the prayer and in spending charity, due to a lack of desire and hope for the reward these actions bring.",
  9055:
      "O Messenger, do not admire the wealth of the hypocrites or their children or think it to be good. Yet the end of their wealth and their children is awful. Allah makes it a torment for them with toil and fatigue when collecting it and with the misfortunes that come down in it until Allah expels their souls in the state of their disbelief. Furthermore, they are tormented with eternity in the lowest depths of the Fire.",
  9056:
      "The hypocrites swear to you, O believers, yet they are liars. They are among your group and not among you in their hearts. Even if they show that they are among you, they fear that what happened to the polytheists will happen to them regarding killing and captivity, so they show Islam as Taqiyyah (pretend to be Muslim).",
  9057:
      "If these hypocrites find shelter in a fortress where they protect themselves, caves in the mountains to hide in, or find a tunnel to enter, they would take refuge in it and enter it hastily.",
  9058:
      "Among the hypocrites are those who criticize you, O Messenger, for dividing the charities when they do not get what they want from it. If you give them what they ask for, they will be satisfied with you, and if you don't give them what they ask for, they show grumbling.",
  9059:
      "It would be better if those hypocrites who criticize you in the division of charities were satisfied with what Allah had imposed for them and what His Messenger gave them from it. Also, if they said Allah is sufficient for us, Allah will give us what He wills from His bounty and His Messenger from what Allah has given him, and we ask Allah alone to enrich us and give us His bounty. If they did that, it would be better for them than to criticize you.",
  9060:
      "When they criticized the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم for his distribution of charity, Allah vindicated him by explaining how it is disbursed and who its beneficiaries were, stating: \n The Zakat (obligatory alms) must be spent on the poor, [which are the needy] who have money from a profession or a job. However, it is not enough for them, and their condition is not noticed. Also, it is for those in need who have almost nothing, and it is obvious to people because of their condition or what they tell people. Moreover, it is for the couriers [those employed] whom the imam sends to collect it. It is also for the disbelievers as a sign of friendship to bring them closer to Islam or for those of weak faith to strengthen their faith or prevent their evil. Likewise, it is to be disbursed to slaves to free them and debtors without extravagance or disobedience if they do not find fulfillment in their debt. Also, it is for equipment to be disposed of for the Mujahideen (fighters) for the sake of Allah and for the traveler whose expenses have been cut off. Restricting the disbursement of the obligatory charity to these people is an obligation from Allah, and Allah knows the interests of His slaves, Wise in His planning and His legislation.",
  9061:
      "Among the hypocrites are those who hurt Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم through their words, so they say when they witness his kindness صلى الله عليه وسلم -: he hears from everyone and believes him, and does not distinguish between truth and falsehood. Say to them, O Messenger, the Messenger only hears the good. Also, he believes in Allah and what the true believers tell him and shows mercy to them. His mission is mercy for those who believe in him, and those who harm him صلى الله عليه وسلم with any harm will have a painful torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Wealth and children can be reasons for suffering in this world, and for suffering in the Afterlife, so the believer should treat them in a way that is pleasing to Allah, in order to gain salvation through them.\n2. A believer should make his desires in accordance to what is pleasing to Allah.\n3. Had all the wealthy Muslims paid their obligatory charity there would not remain a single poor person, and there would be enough wealth whereby the frontiers could be defended and the enemies of Islam fought, and whereby many matters of the religion may have been rectified.\n4. Zakat is given for distribution by those in charge of society, who make decisions about the needs of the different categories of people and the money available for that.\n5. Harming the Messenger (peace be upon him) in a way related to his message is disbelief, which leads to a serious punishment.\n6. The believer should listen to what is good and not listen to what is evil. In other words he should be keen to listen to what is beneficial and good, and turn away from listening to what is sinful and corrupt.",
  9062:
      "The hypocrites swear by Allah to you, O believers, that they did not say anything to hurt the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. They do this so that you may become pleased with them, but Allah and His Messenger are more deserving of being pleased by their accepting faith and doing righteous deeds if they are indeed believers.",
  9063:
      "Do these hypocrites not know that by doing this, they are hostile to Allah and His Messenger and that whoever is hostile to Allah and His Messenger will enter the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, where they will stay forever?! That is an excellent indignity and humiliation.",
  9064:
      "The hypocrites fear that Allah will send down a surah (chapter) to His Messenger, revealing the disbelief they conceal in their hearts to the believers. Say, O Messenger: Continue, O hypocrites, upon your mockery and denigration of the religion, for Allah will bring out what you fear by sending down a surah or by informing His Messenger about it.",
  9065:
      "If you asked, O Messenger, the hypocrites about the stabbing and insulting that they said against the believers after Allah told you about it, they would say we were just joking when we said that and were not serious. Say, O Messenger: Was it Allah and His verses and Messenger that you were mocking?!",
  9066:
      "Do not apologize, O hypocrites, with these false excuses, for you have shown disbelief by your mocking after you had been hiding it. If We will pardon a group of you for leaving hypocrisy, repenting from it, and being faithful to Allah, We will torment a group of you for their persistence in hypocrisy and not repenting.",
  9067:
      "The hypocrites [men and women] agree in the states of hypocrisy. They are, in contrast (not like) the believers, as they enjoin evil and prohibit what is good. Moreover, they are stingy with their money, so they do not spend it for the sake of Allah. They forgot Allah and disobeyed Him, so Allah left them out of His success. The hypocrites are those [who are] out of obedience to Allah, the path of truth to His disobedience, and the way of misguidance.",
  9068:
      "Allah has promised the hypocrites and disbelievers who did not repent that He would enter them into the Fire to stay therein forever. It is enough for them as a punishment, and Allah expelled them from His mercy. They have continuous torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The hypocrites committed many bad actions, including their willingness to take false oaths, opposition to Allah and His Messenger, making fun of the Qur’an, the Prophet and the believers, being afraid that a surah would be revealed in the Qur’an exposing their reality and their making excuses that they were only joking and playing around when they were insulting the religion. Such excuses proved they were guilty of disbelief and the excuse was worse than the offence itself.\n2. Joking about Islam or any of its laws is never acceptable, and speaking in such a manner about Allah’s Book, His messengers and His attributes is considered disbelief.\n3. Repentance from hypocrisy or disbelief is accepted by Allah. Whoever repents shall be pardoned; but whoever persists in disbelief or hypocrisy shall be punished in Hell.",
  9069:
      "You, O hypocrites, are in disbelief and mockery like the lying nations before you. They were more significant in strength than you and had more wealth and children. They enjoyed the share written for them from the pleasures and desires of this world, so you, O hypocrites, enjoyed your share destined for you from that like the previous lying nations enjoyed their share. Likewise, you got in denying the truth and slandering the Messenger as they denied the fact and defamed their messengers. Those characterized by these reprehensible qualities are the ones whose deeds are invalidated by their corruption with Allah by disbelief. They are the losers who have lost themselves by bringing themselves to the sources of perdition.",
  9070:
      "Has the news of what the lying nations have done not come to these hypocrites? What was done to them [the people of Noah, the people of Hūd, the people of Saleh, the people of Abraham, the inhabitants of Midian, and the villages of the people of Lot] in terms of punishment? Their messengers came to them with clear proofs and arguments so Allah would not have wronged them. Their messengers warned them, but they were wronging themselves because they disbelieved in Allah and refused His messengers.",
  9071:
      "The believing men and women are helpers and supporters of each other because of the faith that unites them. They enjoin what is right, which is all that Almighty Allah loves in terms of obedience to Him, such as monotheism and prayer. Likewise, they forbid evil, which is all that Almighty Allah hates from disobedience, such as disbelief and usury. Moreover, they perform the prayer thoroughly in the most total way, and they obey Allah and His Messenger. For those who are characterized by these praiseworthy qualities, Allah will enter them into His mercy. Allah is Mighty. No one overpowers him, and He is Wise in His creation, planning, and legislation.",
  9072:
      "Allah has promised the believers in Allah, both men and women who believe in Him, that He will admit them on the Day of Resurrection to gardens under which rivers flow beneath their palaces. They will remain forever, in which they will not die and whose bliss will not be interrupted. He promised them that He would admit them to suitable dwellings in gardens of residency, and the satisfaction that Allah will bestow upon them is more significant than all of that. That reward mentioned above is a great win that is unparalleled.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Hypocrisy is a deep-rooted chronic illness in human beings. Those suffering from this illness in every age resemble each other in their commanding of evil and prohibition of good, and their failure to spend in Allah’s path on those things that they are required to spend on.\n2. The final repayment by Allah matches the action performed by the servant. The person who fails to obey Allah’s instructions and commits His prohibitions is left out of Allah’s mercy.\n3. The reason for the punishment of disbelievers and hypocrites is the same in all eras: their preferring and enjoying the pleasures of this world over the Afterlife, and the rejection of, plotting against and being treacherous towards the prophets.\n4. In the destruction of communities and nations of the past, because of their disbelief and rejection of the prophets, is a lesson and warning for those intelligent people who take lessons.\n5. Punishment from Allah only happens because of a sin committed by a person.\n6. The people of faith, men and women, are one united nation who co-operate and support each other. Their hearts are united and filled with mutual love and compassion.\n7. The pleasure of the Lord of the earth and the heavens is greater than the luxuries of Paradise, because spiritual happiness is superior to physical happiness.",
  9073:
      "O Messenger, strive against the disbelievers by fighting them with the sword and strive against the hypocrites with the tongue (well-expressed words) and argument. Be hard on both groups because this is what they deserve. Their abode on the Day of Resurrection is Hell, so this fate is their fate.",
  9074:
      "The hypocrites swear a false oath by Allah that they did not say what you were told about them, which is insulting you and faulting your religion. Yet they have said what has been reported to you about them, of what makes them unbelievers, and they have shown disbelief after they have shown faith. They had intended to assassinate the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, but with what they could not achieve it. Moreover, they did not deny anything except something that cannot be denied: Allah favored them by enriching them from the spoils that He bestowed upon His Prophet. If they repent to Allah from their hypocrisy, then their repentance [from their hypocrisy] will be better for them than staying on it. Yet if they turn away from repentance to Allah, He will torture them with a painful torment [in this world] by killing and capturing. Furthermore, He will torture them with a painful torment in the Hereafter by the Fire. They will have no guardian to take care of them and save them from the torment and no helper to avert the torment from them.",
  9075:
      "Among the hypocrites are those who made a covenant with Allah, saying: If Allah gives us [from] His bounty, we will provide charities to the needy. Moreover, we will be among the righteous whose deeds are right.",
  9076:
      "When Allah Almighty gave them [from] His bounty, they did not fulfill what they had promised Allah. Instead, they withheld their wealth, did not give anything to charity, and turned away from faith.",
  9077:
      "So He made their consequence a constant hypocrisy in their hearts until the Day of Resurrection, as a punishment for their disobedience to Allah's covenant and lying.",
  9078:
      "Did the hypocrites not know that Allah knows what they conceal of plotting and cunning in their gatherings and that Allah, the Exalted, is the Omniscient of the Unseen? Nothing of their deeds is hidden from him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  9079:
      "Those who fault the volunteers among the believers by giving small charities, who find nothing but a little that is the sum of what they are capable of. They ridicule them, saying: What is the value of their charities?! Allah mocked them as a reward for their mockery of the believers, and they will have a painful torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is an obligation to strive against the disbelievers and hypocrites: striving against the disbelievers physically, with all available means of warfare and striving against the hypocrites with well-formed arguments.\n2. The hypocrites are the worst people, because they are treacherous and they return good treatment with evil.\n3. The verses indicate that the breaking of a pledge or promise creates hypocrisy. It is therefore necessary that Muslims try their best to honour such agreements.\n4. The verses praise having a strong body and good work, which can take the place of wealth. This is an important principle when considering public wealth and honouring the status of the labourer.",
  9080:
      "Ask, O Messenger, forgiveness for them, or do not ask for it. If you ask for it seventy times, it will not lead to Allah's forgiveness [for them]. They are disbelievers in Allah and His Messenger, and Allah does not guide those who deliberately deviate from His sacred law and intentionally.",
  9081:
      "The hypocrites who stayed behind from the Battle of Tabuk rejoiced because they abstained from striving for the sake of Allah, opposing Allah's Messenger. They hated striving with their money and themselves for Allah's sake as the believers strive. They discouraged their brothers among the hypocrites by saying: Do not march in the heat, and the Battle of Tabuk was in a time of heat. Say to them, O Messenger: The Fire that awaits the hypocrites is much hotter than the heat they ran away from if they only knew.",
  9082:
      "Let these hypocrites who lag behind Jihad (fighting in Allah's path) laugh a little in their mortal worldly life and cry a lot in their eternal Afterlife. That is a reward for what they had earned from disbelief, disobedience, and sins in this world.",
  9083:
      "If Allah returns you, O Prophet, to a group of these hypocrites who are steadfast in their hypocrisy, and they ask you for permission to go out with you on another battle, then say to them: You will never go out, you hypocrites, with me in striving for the sake of Allah, ever. This is as a punishment for you and as a cautionary measure against the evils resulting from your presence with me. You have accepted being left behind in the Battle of Tabuk, so sit back and stay with those left behind from among the sick, women and children.",
  9084:
      "Do not perform the prayer, O Messenger, for any dead hypocrite, ever. Likewise, do not stand at his grave to pray for his forgiveness because they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were out of obedience to Allah. Whoever is like that is not prayed for or supplicated for him.",
  9085:
      "Do not, O Messenger, admire the money of these hypocrites or their children. However, Allah wants to torture them with it in the life of this world. That is because of the hardships they suffer for its sake and the misfortunes they suffer in it. Moreover, their souls leave their bodies while they are in [their] disbelief.",
  9086:
      "When Allah sent down a surah (chapter) to His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that included the command to believe in Allah and strive in His way, those who are rich and wealthy asked for permission to lag behind you. They said: Leave us to lag with those with excuses, such as the powerless and sick.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Asking forgiveness and doing good actions will not benefit the disbelievers as long as they remain as disbelievers.\n2. The joy of the hypocrites will soon disappear and only crying will remain.\n3. The verses indicate the short sightedness of people as they generally look at the present situation they are in and they do not look at the future occurrences that are still to come.\n4. The verses do not indicate that a little laughter is forbidden, but consistently laughing a lot causes the heart to die.\n5. The verses contain evidence for the legitimacy of offering the funeral prayer over believers, visiting their graves and praying for them after their death, just as the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to do for the believers.\n6. One should not be deceived in this world by the wealth and children that Allah has given the disbelievers and hypocrites, because they are not an honour for them but are a way to deceive and entice them to their destruction.",
  9087:
      "These hypocrites accepted humiliation and shame for themselves when they accepted being left behind with those with excuses. Allah sealed their hearts because of their disbelief and hypocrisy, for they do not know what is in their best interest.",
  9088:
      "As for the Messenger and the believers with him, they did not lag in Jihad (striving) for the sake of Allah like these, but instead, they strove for the sake of Allah with their money and their lives. Their reward from Allah was getting worldly benefits, such as victory and spoils. They will be getting the benefits of the Hereafter, including entering Paradise, winning what is desired, and deliverance from what is feared.",
  9089:
      "Allah has prepared for them [the believers] gardens with rivers flowing beneath their palaces, where they will stay forever, and no annihilation (devastation) will follow them. That reward is the great success that no success can compare to.",
  9090:
      "A group of nomads from Medina and its surroundings came to apologize to Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم so that he would permit them to lag (remain behind) from going out and striving (fighting) in Allah's path. Other people lagged and did not even apologize for going out because they did not believe in the Prophet or the promise of Allah. Because of their disbelief, they will suffer and receive painful torment.",
  9091:
      "There is no sin on women, children, the sick, the infirm, the blind, and the poor who do not have enough money to spend on equipment. There is no sin on all these people if they fail to go out because their excuses exist. If they are sincere to Allah and His Messenger and work according to His law, there is no way for the do-gooders who have these excuses to inflict punishment on them. Allah Forgives the sins of the do-gooders and is Merciful to them.",
  9092:
      "Likewise, there is no sin on those absent from you [in the battle] if they came to you, O Messenger, asking you to give them an animal to carry them, and you replied to them: I cannot find an animal to carry you, they turned away from you with eyes pouring tears out of sorrow that they did not find what could be spent from themselves or from you.",
  9093:
      "When Allah clarified that there is no way to punish those with excuses, He mentioned those who deserve punishment and accountability, for He said: \n Indeed, the way of punishment and accountability is only for those who ask you, O Messenger, for permission to be absent from jihad (fighting the disbelievers for the sake of Allah) while they are capable of it by having the means. They have accepted humiliation and shame for themselves by remaining with the laggers in their homes. Allah has sealed their hearts so that they are not affected by any sermon, and because of this seal, they do not know what is in their best interest to choose and what is in their harm to avoid.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Those who strive in Allah’s path will receive the good things of this world. If they do not get this world, they will gain Paradise and salvation from the punishment in the Afterlife.\n2. In principle, those who do good to people out of kindness will not be taken to task if they fall short.\n3. Those who intend to do good, and together with this firm intention they strive to do what they can, but are unable to do so, will be in the rank of those who actually did that good action.\n4. Islam is a religion of justice and logic. For this reason, Islam has imposed punishment and sin on the hypocrites who ask for permission to not strive with their lives and wealth in the path of Allah while they are wealthy and able.",
  9094:
      "The hypocrites who stay behind during battle make pathetic excuses to the Muslims when they return. Allah directs His Messenger and the believers to respond by saying: Do not make false excuses; we will never believe them. Indeed, Allah has informed us what is in your souls. Allah and His Messenger will see whether you will repent so that Allah accepts your repentance or continue upon hypocrisy. Then you will return to Allah, the One who knows everything, and He will inform you of what you used to do and recompense you accordingly. So hasten in repentance and perform righteous deeds.",
  9095:
      "O believers, when you return to them, those who stayed behind will swear by Allah to emphasize their false excuses so that you desist from blaming and reprimanding them. So leave and abandon them furiously; they are filthy and impure inside. They will take refuge in Hell as an abode, as a recompense for their hypocrisy and sins.",
  9096:
      "Those who stayed behind will swear to please you, O believers, so that you accept their excuses; so do not be pleased with them. If you were to do so, you would have indeed gone against [the commands] of your Lord. Indeed, Allah is not pleased with people disobeying Him through committing disbelief and hypocrisy. So Muslims, beware that you are happy with that which Allah is displeased with.",
  9097:
      "Those among the Bedouins who disbelieve and commit hypocrisy are worse in disbelief and hypocrisy than the disbelievers who live within the city. Since they are more likely to be ignorant of the religion and most certainly will not know the obligatory, the supererogatory, and the legislative rulings revealed to His Messenger. Moreover, they are harsh and rough and do not mix with other people. Allah is aware of their situation; nothing is hidden from Him. He is Wise in controlling His affairs and His legislation.",
  9098:
      "Some of the hypocrites from the Bedouins consider whatever wealth they spend in Allah's path to be a loss and a punishment because they think that there will be no reward for spending and that Allah will not punish them if they do not spend. Despite this, they sometimes spend to show off, hiding their real beliefs. They wait for evil to come to you, O believers, so they can get rid of you. Instead, Allah has made the evil and the turn of fortune that they wished to afflict the believers with occur on them instead. Allah hears what they say and knows what they keep hidden in their hearts.",
  9099:
      "However, among the Bedouins are those who believe in Allah and the Last Day and make what they spend in the path of Allah a way to gain closeness to Allah and a means of receiving the prayers of the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and his seeking forgiveness for them. Indeed, their spending in the path of Allah and the Messenger praying for them will bring them closer to Allah. They will find the reward with Him. Allah will admit them into His vast Mercy that includes His forgiveness and Paradise. Indeed, Allah forgives His slaves when they repent and is Merciful to them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The field of action and obligations is the best witness to expose the lies of the hypocrites.\n2. The hypocrites are filthy and impure and it is necessary to stay away from them and not to have any love for them or be pleased with them.\n3. When the people of the desert do not have faith, they are stronger in their disbelief and hypocrisy than people of the city, due to the effect of their harsh and uncivilised environment.\n4. The verses encourage spending in Allah’s path with a sincere intention and it mentions the great reward for doing so.\n5. The verses indicate the virtue of knowledge and that the person who lacks knowledge is more likely to commit mistakes.",
  9100:
      "Allah is pleased with and has accepted the obedience of the foremost in faith, the first emigrants who immigrated from their homes and lands for the sake of Allah, the helpers who helped His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, and those who followed them in goodness; in their creed, good speech and action. They are pleased with Him for what He will grant them of His great reward, and has prepared gardens with rivers flowing beneath its palaces: That is the utmost success.",
  9101:
      "There are hypocrites among the Bedouins living close to Medina. There are also hypocrites among the people of Medina, who have remained obstinate in their hypocrisy. You do not know them, O Prophet; Allah truly knows who they are. Therefore, Allah will punish them twice: in the worldly life by exposing their hypocrisy and with execution and captivity, and then in the hereafter, with the punishment of the grave. Then, they will be returned on the Day of Resurrection for a painful punishment in the lowest depths of the Fire.",
  9102:
      "Some of the people of Medina did not participate in battle without a valid excuse. They admitted to this and did not come up with false reasons. So they have mixed obedience to Allah (by doing righteous actions, adhering to His legislation, and battling in His path) with evil, hoping Allah would accept their repentance and overlook their [evil deeds]. Indeed, Allah is most forgiving to those of His slaves who repent and is Merciful to them.",
  9103:
      "In order to purify them from the impurity of disobedience and sins, [O Prophet] take alms out of their property, hoping they are replaced with good deeds, and pray for them. Indeed, your prayer is mercy and safety for them. Allah hears your prayer and knows their good actions and intentions.",
  9104:
      "Those who did not participate in battle and repent to Allah should understand that Allah accepts the repentance of His slaves and the voluntary charity [given for His sake], while He does not need it. He will reward the one who spends in charity, and it is He (may He be Exalted) who is the Acceptor of repentance when His slaves repent and is the most Merciful to them.",
  9105:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who had stayed behind from fighting in Allah's path and have repented from their sin: Make up for the harm caused by what you missed and be sincere in your deeds to Allah. Do what pleases Him because Allah, His Messenger, and the believers will soon see your deeds. Then you will be returned, on the Day of Resurrection, to your Lord, the One Who knows everything. He knows what you hide and what you make public, and He will inform you about what you used to do in this world and recompense you for that accordingly.",
  9106:
      "There are others from among those who stayed behind from the battle of Tabuk who did not have any valid excuse. The matter of these people has been deferred to Allah's decree and decision regarding them. Allah will judge them as He wishes; either He will torment them if they do not repent to Him, or He will accept their repentance if they do. Allah knows who is deserving of His punishment and who deserves His pardon. Allah is Wise in His legislation and planning. This was referring to Murarah bin Al-Rabi, Ka'b bin Malik, and Hilal bin Umayyah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the virtue of the Emigrants and Helpers over other people.\n2. The verses show the virtue of rushing towards faith, migration in Allah’s path, assisting the religion and following the path of the pious predecessors.\n3. The knowledge of the Ghaib belongs exclusively to Allah. No one but Allah knows what is in people’s hearts.\n4. There is hope for those believers who commit sin that Allah will turn to them and forgive them, if they repent and set right their actions.\n5. Zakat is an obligation which carries a great reward and has an effect in causing wealth to grow, and purifying the soul from miserliness and other evil qualities.\n6. Every person is accountable for his actions. Allah knows about what people do and will repay them for their actions on the Day of Judgement.",
  9107:
      "Among the hypocrites are those who built a mosque not for Allah's obedience but to harm the Muslims, to support disbelief by strengthening the people of hypocrisy, to cause disunity among the believers, and as preparation and anticipation for those who had waged war against Allah and His Messenger before the construction of the mosque. These hypocrites swear to you: We only intended goodness for the Muslims. Allah is a witness that they are lying in this claim of theirs.",
  9108:
      "O Prophet, do not accept the invitation of the hypocrites for you to pray in such a mosque. Instead, the Mosque of Quba, founded from its beginning upon fear of Allah, is more worthy of you praying in it than this mosque founded upon disbelief. In the Mosque of Quba, there are men who love to purify themselves from ritual and physical impurities with water, as well as from sins with repentance and seeking forgiveness. Allah loves those who purify themselves from ritual and physical impurities and sins.",
  9109:
      "Can those who founded their building upon the fear of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions and upon His pleasure by doing all forms of good be equal to those who built a mosque to cause harm to the Muslims, strengthen disbelief, and cause disunity among the believers? They can never be equal! The first group has a strong structure with a good foundation, so it will not collapse. Yet, the second group is like a person who built a structure on the edge of a pit that is about to collapse, and then it collapses with him into the depths of Hell. Allah does not guide those who do wrong by committing disbelief, hypocrisy, and other evils.",
  9110:
      "The mosque they built to cause harm will continue to be a source of doubt and hypocrisy in their hearts until their hearts are torn apart through death or by being killed by the sword. Allah knows the deeds of His slaves, and He is Wise in the judgments He passes with respect to recompensing them for their good or evil.",
  9111:
      "After Allah exposed the disgrace of the hypocrites who neglected jihad, He mentioned the reward of those who fight for His cause, stating: \n Allah (may He be Exalted) has purchased from the believers their lives, despite them belonging to Him, out of His grace for a high price: Paradise. They will fight the disbelievers so that Allah's Word is highest, killing the disbelievers or being killed by them. Allah has made this true promise in the Torah, the Book of Moses, the Gospel, the Book of Jesus, and the Quran, the Book of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. No one is more faithful to his promise than Allah; may He be Exalted. So, rejoice, O believers, with the deal you made with Allah because you gained such a huge profit from it. That deal is a great success.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. What the hypocrites say should not be believed, because Allah has testified about their lies.\n2. Those who purify themselves from bodily and spiritual impurities are guaranteed the Love of Allah.\n3. The person who does an action to please Allah is not equal to the one who does an action in support of disbelief and to oppose the Muslims. The action of the first person will remain and become a source of happiness for the one who does it, whilst the action of the second person will disappear and become a cause of misfortune for the person who does it.\n4. The verses encourage striving in Allah’s path and explain that the reward for doing so is Paradise.\n5. The duty to strive in Allah’s path and encouraging others to do so was founded in the religions before Islam as well.\n6. Any situation that causes disunity amongst the believers is a sin which must be avoided and removed. On the other hand, any situation that creates unity amongst the believers must be followed and encouraged.",
  9112:
      "These people who will receive this great reward return from what Allah dislikes and despises to what He loves and approves of; they submit out of awe and humility to Allah and obey Him; they praise their Lord in all conditions; they fast and pray; they instruct and prohibit what Allah and His Messenger instructs and prohibits; they guard Allah's instructions through following them and His prohibitions through avoiding them. O Messenger, tell the believers with these qualities the good news of what will make them happy in this world and the Hereafter.",
  9113:
      "It is not appropriate for the Prophet and the believers to seek forgiveness from Allah for the polytheists, even if they are their relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are the people of the Fire because they died on polytheism.",
  9114:
      "Abraham's seeking forgiveness for his [polytheist] father was only because of a promise he had made to do so, hoping he would submit. When it became clear to Abraham that his father was an enemy of Allah, due to the advice not being of benefit to him or due to him knowing through revelation that he would die as a disbeliever, he disassociated himself from him. He had asked forgiveness for him based on his own reasoning and not in contradiction of any law that Allah had revealed to him. Abraham (peace be with him) used to turn to Allah in humility frequently, and he used to overlook and pardon his people who were wrongdoers.",
  9115:
      "Allah would never consider a people misguided after He had guided them until He clarifies to them those forbidden things they must avoid. If they do what Allah had forbidden after it has been declared forbidden and made clear to them, He will consider them misguided. Allah knows everything. Nothing is hidden from Him. He has taught you what you did not know.",
  9116:
      "The dominion of the heavens and the Earth belongs to Allah. He has no partner in this; nothing in them is hidden from Him. He gives life to whoever He wills and causes to die whoever He wills. You, O people, do not have, besides Allah, any guardian to take care of your affairs nor any helper to guard you against evil and assist you against your enemy.",
  9117:
      "Allah has forgiven the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم since he permitted the hypocrites to stay behind from the battle of Tabuk. He has also forgiven the Muhajireen and the Ansar, who did not stay behind but followed him in the battle of Tabuk despite the intense heat, the lack of means, and the strength of the enemy. This was after the hearts of a group of them who intended to abandon the expedition almost deviated because of the great difficulty they faced. Then Allah inspired them to be patient and to go out for that battle. He forgave them, for He (may He be Exalted) is Kind and Merciful towards them. Because of His mercy, He inspired them to repent to Him and accepted their repentance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses explain the qualities that believers should have, so that they become worthy of receiving good news that will make them happy.\n2. It is forbidden to ask forgiveness for a person who passed away as an idolater.\n3. It is not valid to use the action of Abraham (peace be with him) initially asking for forgiveness of his father as proof for the permissibility of asking forgiveness for idolaters.\n4. Sins and evil actions are the cause of disasters, disappointment and failure.\n5. Allah is the Owner of everything. He is our friend and protector; we have no friend or protector besides Him.\n6. The verses show the virtue of the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) over all other people.\n7. Allah sends His mercy on the people of faith by protecting them from misguidance and giving them guidance.",
  9118:
      "Allah forgave the three, Murarah bin Al-Rabi, Ka'b bin Malik and Hilal bin Umayyah. Their repentance and acceptance were delayed after they stayed behind instead of going to Tabuk with Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم instructed people to stay away from them, making them feel sadness and grief. The Earth seemed narrow to them despite its vastness, and their hearts felt constricted because of their loneliness. They were certain there was no place of refuge or help they could go to except Allah alone. Allah was Merciful to them by inspiring them to repent to Him and accepting their repentance. Allah is the One who accepts the repentance from His slaves and is full of mercy and compassion for them.",
  9119:
      "O you who have believed in Allah, followed His Messenger, and acted according to His sacred law, fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, and be with those who are truthful in their belief, statements, and deeds, as there is no salvation except in truthfulness.",
  9120:
      "It is not for the people of Medina, or the Bedouins around them, to stay behind after [the departure of] Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم if he himself goes out to fight, nor should they be stingy and give preference to their own safety over the safety of the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Instead, they should sacrifice themselves for him. This is because they suffer no thirst, fatigue, or hunger in Allah's path, nor do they settle anywhere by which their presence angers the disbelievers, nor do they make a gain over their enemy, killing or capturing them, acquiring booty or defeating them, except that Allah records for them the reward of a righteous deed, which He accepts from them. Allah does not allow the reward of those who do good to be lost. Instead, He gives this reward to them in full and increases it for them.",
  9121:
      "And they do not sacrifice any wealth, small or large, or cross a valley except that their sacrifice or journey is recorded so that Allah may repay them, giving them in the Hereafter the reward for the best of what they used to do.",
  9122:
      "It is not appropriate for believers to go out all together to fight lest they be wiped out if their enemy overcomes them. Why does one group not go out to fight, and another group remain behind to accompany Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and learn the religion by listening to the Quran and sacred laws from him so they can advise their people when they return to them of what they have learned so that they are aware of Allah's torment and punishment and comply with His instructions and avoid His prohibitions? This concerned the troops that Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم would send to different areas, choosing a group from among his companions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The obligation of being mindful of Allah and sticking with those who are truthful.\n2. It is obligatory for a Muslim to prefer Allah and His Messenger over everything else.\n3. Spending for the sake of Allah is a great virtue.\n4. Gaining understanding of the sacred path of life is as important as striving for the sake of Allah.\n5. People of knowledge and people who strive for the sake of Allah are the supports of Islam.",
  9123:
      "Allah instructed the believers to fight those disbelievers near them due to the danger they pose to the believers because of their proximity and to show strength and power to frighten them and repel their evil. Allah, the Exalted, is with the God-fearing believers with His help and support.",
  9124:
      "When Allah revealed a surah [chapter] to the Messenger, some of the hypocrites would ask by way of ridicule and mockery: Which of you believers has increased in belief in what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has brought due to this surah? As for those who believed in Allah and His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, the surah's revelation had indeed increased their belief, and they were happy with the revelation because of the benefit it contained for them in this world and the Hereafter.",
  9125:
      "As for the hypocrites, the revelation of the Quran, with its laws and stories, increases their sickness and wickedness because they reject what is revealed. So, the disease of their hearts increases with the revelation of the Quran because whenever something is revealed, they doubt what it contains and die in disbelief.",
  9126:
      "Do the hypocrites not see and learn how Allah has tested them by exposing their condition and hypocrisy once or twice a year? Then, despite knowing that Allah did this to them, they do not repent from their disbelief, abandon their hypocrisy, or consider what happened to them and that it is from Allah.",
  9127:
      "Whenever Allah reveals a surah [chapter] to His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, mentioning the condition of the hypocrites, the hypocrites would look at one another, saying: Is anyone watching you? If no one is watching them, they leave the gathering. Behold! Allah turned their hearts away from guidance and goodness and deserted them because they are a people who do not understand.",
  9128:
      "There has come to you, O Arabs, a Messenger from among yourselves, who is an Arab like you. What is difficult for you is concerning to him. He is greatly concerned for your guidance and is kind and compassionate with the believers.",
  9129:
      "If they turn away from you, O Messenger, not believing in what you brought, then say: Allah is sufficient for me; none is worthy of worship except Him. I rely on Him alone, and He (may He be Exalted) is the Lord of the Great Throne.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is necessary to fight against those who oppose the truth, who are nearest in proximity to the Muslims, if Islam has spread and there is a need for such fighting.\n2. The state of the hypocrites when the Qur’an was revealed was one of unhappiness and anxiousness.\n3. The Prophet (peace be upon him)was merciful with and concerned about the believers.\n4. The verses indicate that faith increases and decreases, and that the believer should keep an eye on his faith and commit to it, so that it is renewed and grows, and is always increasing.",
  10000:
      "Jonah (Surah Yunus)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming prophethood through evidence, inviting rejectors to faith, and threatening them with divine torment.\n•    Explanation:",
  10001:
      "Alif Lām Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. The verses recited in this surah are from the verses of a clear and perfect Quran containing wisdom and laws.",
  10002:
      "Are the people amazed that We have sent revelation to a man from among themselves, instructing him to warn them about Allah's torment and to inform those who believe in Allah with news that will make them happy; that they will receive a high rank with their Lord (may He be Exalted) as a reward for the righteous deeds they did? But the disbelievers said that the man who brought these verses was clearly a magician.",
  10003:
      "O those who are amazed, surely, your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens despite their greatness and the Earth despite its vastness in six days and then ascended and rose above the Throne. Why are they amazed that Allah has sent a man from among you? Allah alone determines and decrees in His vast dominion, and none can intercede with Him on behalf of anything unless Allah permits and is pleased with the one who intercedes. That is Allah, your Lord, so sincerely worship Him alone. Do you not heed all these proofs and evidence of His Oneness? Whoever heeds this reminder will know that and believe in Him.",
  10004:
      "To Him alone is your return on the Day of Resurrection to recompense you for your deeds. Allah has made a truthful promise to humanity that He will not break, and He is well capable of that. He initiated creation without precedent. He will bring them back again after their death to recompense justly those who believed in Allah and did righteous deeds, neither decreasing their good actions nor increasing their bad actions. As for those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messengers, they will have a drink of scalding water that will cut their intestines and will have a painful torment because of their disbelief.",
  10005:
      "It is He Who made the sun radiate light and the moon reflect it, determining its progression through twenty-eight phases, a phase being the change it goes through every twenty-four hours so that you, O people, would know the number of days through the sun and the number of months and years through the moon. Allah did not create the heavens, the Earth, and what they contain except with the truth, revealing His power and greatness to people. Allah makes clear these obvious signs and evidence of His Oneness for people who know how to draw conclusions from such facts.",
  10006:
      "Indeed, in the alternation of the night and day, the darkness and light that accompany this, the shortness of one and length of the other, and the creation in the heavens and the Earth, are signs showing the power of Allah for a people who fear Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.\n\n• Beneficial Points: 1. A confirmation of the prophethood of Muhammad (peace and blessing be upon him) and the fact that his sending was something logical, and not a cause for astonishment.\n2. The task of the Messenger was to give the good news of Paradise to the believers, and to warn the wrongdoers about the fire of Hell.\n3. A confirmation of Allah’s Lordship and Divinity.\n4. Confirmation of the greatness of the Throne, and that Allah established Himself upon it in a way befitting His Glory and Majesty.\n5. Those who act as intercessors on the Day of Judgement will only be able to intercede if Allah gives permission to them and was pleased with them in the worldly life.\n6. There is a confirmation of the Day of Judgement and the rewards and punishments of it.\n7. It is proven that Allah has made the movement of the sun and the phases of the moon to help determine the date, by days months and years.",
  10007:
      "The disbelievers who do not expect the meeting with Allah, thus not fearing or desiring it, who are satisfied with the fleeting life of this world instead of the eternal life of the Hereafter, feeling content in this world, and who are heedless and turn away from the signs and proofs of Allah,",
  10008:
      "Their dwelling place on the Day of Resurrection will be the Fire because of what they earned through their disbelief and rejection of the Day of Resurrection.",
  10009:
      "Those who believe in Allah and do righteous deeds, Allah will guide them, because of their belief, to do more righteous deeds that lead to His Pleasure. Then, on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will admit them into gardens of eternal bliss with rivers flowing beneath them.",
  10010:
      "Their supplication in Paradise will be the exaltation of Allah. Allah's greeting to them, the angels, and their greeting to each other will be: Peace, and the end of their supplication will be the praise of Allah, the Lord of all creation.",
  10011:
      "If Allah were to hasten in responding to people who supplicate for evil against themselves, their children, or their wealth when they are angry, in the way He responds to them when they pray for good, they would have been destroyed. But Allah gives them time. He abandons those who do not expect to meet Him because they do not fear torment or hope for a reward, leaving them wavering, confused, and doubtful about the Day of Resurrection.",
  10012:
      "And whenever an affliction such as illness or misfortune touches the man who transgresses against himself, he supplicates to Us, humbly and submissively, whether lying on his side, sitting or standing, hoping for the affliction to be removed from him. However, when We respond to his supplication and remove the affliction, he continues doing what he had been doing before, as if he had never supplicated to Us to remove the affliction. Just as continuing in misguidance is made attractive to this person who turns away, the disbelief and sins of those who transgress the limits are made attractive to them, so they do not give them up.",
  10013:
      "And We destroyed nations before you, O polytheists, because they rejected the messengers of Allah and committed sins. Though their messengers came to them with clear proofs proving the truthfulness of what they brought from their Lord, they were not keen to believe, so Allah deserted them and did not guide them. Just as We recompensed those previous wrongdoing nations, We recompense those who are like them in all times and places.",
  10014:
      "Then We made you successors to these nations who rejected the truth and were destroyed, to see what you would do and whether you would do good, for which you would be rewarded; or do evil, for which you would be tormented.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The repayment for the disbelievers on the Day of Judgement is the fire of Hell, because of what they earned through their disbelief and rejection.\n2. The reward of those who have faith is Paradise, because of the good that they did.\n3. Allah is merciful with humankind by not answering their prayers when they ask for harmful things for themselves or their children when they are angry and not thinking clearly.\n4. People often pray to Allah during times of difficulty, but turn away from Him during good times. Therefore, we should be careful not to be like this.\n5. Previous communities were destroyed because of their overstepping the limits through disobedience.",
  10015:
      "When the clear verses of the Quran are recited to them proving the Oneness of Allah, those who deny the resurrection, do not hope for a reward, and do not fear torment, say: O Muhammad, bring a Quran other than this Quran that insults the worshipping of idols or change it by abrogating some or all of it according to what agrees with our desires. O Messenger, tell them: It is not up to me to change it, let alone bring something other than it. Instead, it is Allah alone Who changes what He wills of it, and I only follow what Allah reveals to me. I fear that if I disobey Allah by responding to your request, I will be punished on a great Day, the Day of Resurrection.",
  10016:
      "O Messenger, say to them: If Allah had willed, I would not have recited the Quran nor conveyed it to you. And if Allah had willed, He would not have made the Quran known to you through my tongue. For I have lived among you for a long time, for forty years, not reading or writing, and I did not seek this type of knowledge nor search for it. Do you not realize that what I have brought you is from Allah and not from myself?",
  10017:
      "There is no greater wrongdoer than he who fabricates a lie against Allah, so how could I change the Quran, fabricating against Him? The matter is such that those who transgress the limits of Allah by fabricating lies against Him will not succeed.",
  10018:
      "The polytheists worship what they claim to be deities instead of Allah, which cannot benefit or harm them. But the One deserving of worship can benefit and harm whenever He wills. They say about their deities: These are our intercessors who will intercede for us with Allah, so He will not torment us because of our sins. O Messenger, tell them: Are you informing Allah, the Omniscient, that He has a partner while He is unaware that He has a partner in the heavens or the Earth? Sanctified and Exalted is Allah above the falsehood and lies of the polytheists.",
  10019:
      "And humanity was just one nation believing in Allah's Oneness; then they differed: some remained upon belief in Allah, while others disbelieved. Had it not been for Allah's prior decree that He would not judge between them in what they differed about in this world and that He would only judge between them on the Day of Resurrection, He would have judged between them in what they differed about in this world by saving the believers and destroying the rejecting disbelievers.",
  10020:
      "The polytheists say: Why has no sign been sent to Muhammad from his Lord to prove the truth of what he says? O Messenger, say to them: The sending down of signs is [of the] unseen, which Allah alone knows, so wait for the physical signs you ask for, as I am also waiting along with you for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an is the Word of Allah, and no one can change or distort it, because it is safeguarded.\n2. The magnitude of making up lies about Allah or distorting His words, as the Jews did with the Torah, is clearly demonstrated.\n3. Only Allah alone can benefit or harm people.\n4. The falsehood of the idolaters saying that their Allahs would plead on their behalf with Allah is established.\n5. Following desires and going against the sacred path of life are the reasons for people differing with one another.",
  10021:
      "When We give the polytheists the taste of a blessing, such as rain and abundance after drought and suffering, they mock and reject Our signs. O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Allah is quicker at plotting, enticing, and luring you and quicker in tormenting. The angels record what you plan in the way of scheming, and nothing escapes them, so how could it escape their Creator? Allah will recompense you for your scheming.",
  10022:
      "Allah is the One who enables you, O humanity, to travel by land, foot, riding, or aboard ships on the sea. To the passengers' delight, they sail in them with good winds. Suddenly, a gale wind comes to them, and the waves of the sea come to them from every side until they are certain they are doomed; they start to supplicate to Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, saying: If You save us from this deadly situation we will be truly thankful for what You have favored us with.",
  10023:
      "But when He answers their supplication and saves them from their distress, they cause corruption upon the Earth, disbelieving, committing wrongs and sins. Wake up and realize, O People! The evil consequences of your sins and transgression only fall upon yourselves, and do not harm Allah in any way. You enjoy it in the life of this world, which is fleeting. Then you will return to Us on the day of Resurrection, and We will inform you of the wrongdoing you used to do and recompense you for it.",
  10024:
      "The example of the life of this world that you enjoy and how quickly it comes to an end is like that of the rain, which is absorbed by the plants of the earth, from which people eat grains and fruits, and animals benefit from its vegetation. When the earth has taken on its bright color and looks beautiful because of the different plants growing on it, and the people think that they will be able to harvest and gather what has grown, Our decree comes to destroy it, and We make it as if it had been harvested and not been full of anything such as trees and plants a short while ago. Just as We have clarified the nature of the world and how quickly it ends, We clarify the evidence and proofs for those who reflect and take lessons.",
  10025:
      "And Allah invites all people to His Paradise, the Home of Peace, where people will be safe from difficulties, worries, and death. Allah enables whom He wills of His slaves to come to Islam, leading them to this Home of Peace.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is quicker at scheming against those who scheme against His believing servants.\n2. An evidence of the weak and shameful state of most people, because of their sincerely praying to Allah alone in difficulty, yet forgetting Him in ease.\n3. People’s overstepping of Allah’s limits returns upon themselves, and does not harm anyone except themselves.\n4. The reality of this world is made clear, in how quickly it will come to an end and disappear, and that there is no happiness in it that is not short-lived.\n5. People should not be deceived by this world, and what they do should be for the Afterlife.\n6. Paradise will be the home of the believer, with its bliss and safety from hardship and worry.",
  10026:
      "Those who do good, including that which Allah made obligatory on them, and avoid the sins that Allah has prohibited will receive the best reward, Paradise, and even more, which is to see the noble face of Allah. Neither dust, humiliation, nor disgrace will cover their faces. Such people who do good are the companions of Paradise; they will remain therein eternally.",
  10027:
      "Those who do evil deeds such as disbelief and sins will receive Allah's torment as an equal recompense in the Hereafter for the sins they committed in this life. Their faces will be covered in humiliation and disgrace, and no one will save them from the torment Allah will send upon them. It will be as if their faces have been covered by the blackness of the night because of the significant amount of smoke and blackness that will reach them from the Fire. Such people are the companions of the Fire, wherein they will live eternally.",
  10028:
      "And remember, O Messenger, the Day of Resurrection, when We will gather together all of creation and tell those who associated partners with Allah in the worldly life: O polytheists, stay in your place, you and the deities you used to worship instead of Allah. Then We will separate the deities from their worshippers, and those deities will disassociate themselves from their worshippers, saying: It was not us that you used to worship.",
  10029:
      "Their so-called gods, which they used to worship, will disassociate themselves from them, saying: Allah is sufficient as a witness that We were not happy being worshipped by you, nor did we instruct you to do so, nor were we aware of your worship!",
  10030:
      "In that great place of gathering, each soul will be informed of what it did in the life of this world. Then the polytheists will be returned to their true Lord, Allah, Who will carry out their reckoning, and the intercession of the idols they made up will fail them.",
  10031:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Who is it that provides for you from the sky, sending down rain; who provides for you from the earth, with the plants that grow in it and what it contains of metals and minerals; and who owns the hearing and sight that you enjoy; and who brings out the living from the dead, like the human from a drop of semen and the bird from the egg; and who brings out the dead from the living, like semen from animals, and the egg from the bird? Who governs the entire creation in the heavens and earth, and what is in them? They will reply that Allah is the One who does all of this. Say to them: Will you not know that and then fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions?!",
  10032:
      "The One who does all that, O people, is Allah, the Truth, your Creator, and the Planner of your affairs. So what is beyond the truth except misguidance? Where are your minds wandering away to from this clear truth?",
  10033:
      "Just as the true Lordship of Allah is established, O Messenger, His Decree that those who abandoned the truth out of stubbornness will never believe has become binding.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Performing many good actions is highly encouraged because this will result in happiness and in seeing the noble Face of Allah in Paradise.\n2. Doing bad actions is clearly warned against because this will result in suffering, disgrace and humiliation.\n3. The disowning by every ‘Allah,’ whatever it may be, of whoever worshipped it on the day of Judgement.\n4. On the day of Judgement every soul will be informed of the good and evil it did.\n5. Showing the power of Allah, and that He has power over all things.\n6. Believing in Allah’s lordship alone and yet associating others with Him in divinity and worship is futile and will not benefit the worshipper on the Day of Judgement, as it is necessary to believe in His lordship and His divinity without associating anything with Him.\n7. If Allah decrees that a people will not be guided to faith, then they will not believe.",
  10034:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Can any of your partners you worship instead of Allah originate creation without precedent and then bring it back to life after death? Tell them: Allah originates creation without precedent and then brings it back to life after death, so how can you, O polytheists, be deluded from the truth to falsehood?",
  10035:
      "Tell them, O Messenger: Are there from among your partners who you worship instead of Allah those who guide to the truth? Say to them: Allah alone guides to the truth. So, is He who guides people to the truth and invites them to it more deserving of being followed, or your deities who cannot guide themselves except if others guide them? So, how do you judge with falsehood by claiming they are Allah's partners? Allah is Transcendent and far beyond what they say.",
  10036:
      "Most of the polytheists follow matters they do not know about, only guessing and conjecturing. Mere conjecture cannot replace knowledge and is useless against it. Allah knows everything they do; nothing of what they do is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  10037:
      "This Quran could not be fabricated and attributed to anyone but Allah because people cannot come up with anything similar to it. It confirms the books that were revealed before it and clarifies the laws in them. Thus, there is no doubt that the Lord of the creation revealed it (may He be Exalted and Transcendent).",
  10038:
      "Or do these polytheists say that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم made up the Quran himself and then attributed it to Allah? O Messenger, say to them: If I, as a human being like you, have made it up, then bring a chapter like it and invite whoever you can to assist you if you are telling the truth in claiming that the Quran is a made-up lie. However, you will not be able to do so. Your inability, even though you are masters of the Arabic language and eloquent in it, proves that Allah has revealed the Quran.",
  10039:
      "Yet they did not respond [to these challenges]; instead, they hastened to reject the Quran before even understanding or reflecting upon it, and the punishment about which they have been warned has not yet come to them, although it is near! In the same way, previous nations rejected, and then the torment came down upon them. So reflect upon the end of these nations who rejected the truth, for Allah destroyed them.",
  10040:
      "Some polytheists will eventually believe in the Quran before their death, while others will not out of stubbornness and arrogance until they die. O Messenger, your Lord Allah knows best those who persist in their disbelief and will recompense them for it.",
  10041:
      "If your people reject you, O Messenger, then say to them: I will be rewarded for my deeds and take responsibility for the consequences thereof, and you will be rewarded for your deeds and face the consequences thereof. You are free from the consequences of what I do, and I am free from what you all do.",
  10042:
      "And some polytheists listen when you, O Messenger, recite the Quran, not wanting to accept it and submit to it. Are you able to make deaf people hear? Likewise, you cannot guide those deaf to the truth, as they will not understand it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses confirm the belief that humankind will be brought back to life after death.\n2. It is Allah alone, the Guider to the truth, and no one else, Who gives guidance.\n3. The necessity of following articles of faith with certainty and without conjecture.\n4. The miraculous nature of the Qur’an in its eloquence and law-giving is a proof that the Qur’an is from Allah.\n5. No one until the Day of Judgement will be able to produce even an verse like the noble Qur’an.\n6. The verses make clear the pride and stubbornness of the idolaters in their rejection of the Prophet (peace be upon him).",
  10043:
      "And some of them look at you, O Messenger, with their normal eyesight but not with insight. Is it possible for you to make the blind see? You will not be able to do so; likewise, you cannot guide those lacking insight.",
  10044:
      "Allah is free from wronging His slaves; He does not wrong them by even an atom's weight. Instead, they wrong themselves by bringing about their own destruction by clinging to falsehood, arrogance, and stubbornness.",
  10045:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, when Allah will gather people to reckon them, it will be as if they had lived in the world and the Barzakh [Transitory Stage] for only an hour and no more. They will recognize each other on that Day, but then their acquaintance will be cut off because of the intensity of the horrors they witness on the Day of Resurrection. The losers will be those who rejected the meeting with their Lord on the Day of Resurrection and, in the worldly life, did not believe in the Day of Revival so that they could safeguard themselves from loss.",
  10046:
      "Whether We show you, O Messenger, some of the torment We have promised them before your death or cause you to die before that, in both scenarios, you will return to Us on the Day of Resurrection. Moreover, Allah is aware of what they used to do; none of it is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly for their deeds.",
  10047:
      "Every previous nation had a messenger sent to them. When the messenger delivered to them what he was instructed to, and they rejected him, it was judged justly between him and them. Allah saved the messenger through His grace and destroyed them through His justice, and they were not wronged in any way in the recompense for what they did.",
  10048:
      "The disbelievers say stubbornly and challengingly: When will the torment you promised us occur if you are truthful in your claim?",
  10049:
      "O Messenger, say to them: I have no power to benefit or harm myself, so how can I benefit or harm other people besides what Allah wills? How, then, can I know the unseen? Allah has appointed a set time for the destruction of every nation, but only Allah knows the time. If the time of their destruction arrives, it cannot be brought forward or delayed by even a moment.",
  10050:
      "O Messenger, tell these people who wish to hasten the torment: Inform me if Allah's torment were to come to you at any time of the night or day, what is it of this torment precisely that you are hastening?!",
  10051:
      "Or will you believe after the promised torment has come down upon you when belief will not benefit anyone who had not previously believed? Is it now that you will believe, whereas before, you wanted to hasten the torment because you rejected it?!",
  10052:
      "Then, after being put in the torment and requesting to be removed from it, it will be said to them: Taste the everlasting torment of the Hereafter. Are you not being rewarded except for your disbelief and sins?",
  10053:
      "The polytheists ask you, O Messenger: Is this torment which we have been promised true? Tell them: By Allah! It is the truth, and you cannot escape it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. People bring ruin upon themselves: Allah is High and Exalted, that He would wrong anyone.\n2. The believers must prepare themselves for the Day of Judgement and the terrors and events of it.\n3. Those who deny the Day of Judgement and their meeting with Allah have lost everything.\n4. The task of the Messenger is to deliver his message, and Allah will judge between him and his people, if they reject him, on the day of Judgement.\n5. Benefit and harm is in Allah’s hands, glory be to Him, and no one in creation has control over harm or benefit for himself or anyone else.\n6. Every nation has a set time for their length which only Allah has knowledge of. This time cannot be brought forward or delayed for even a second.\n7. Believing at the point of death and the soul leaving the body will not be of any benefit.",
  10054:
      "If every polytheist were to possess all the valuable wealth on Earth, they would offer it as ransom from Allah's torment if they were allowed to do so. The polytheists will hide their regret for their disbelief when they see the torment on the Day of Resurrection. Allah will judge between them with justice, and they will not be wronged; they will only be recompensed accordingly for their deeds.",
  10055:
      "Behold! The dominion of whatever is in the heavens and Earth is only Allah's. Allah's promise of torment for the disbelievers will undoubtedly occur, but most do not know that and are therefore in doubt.",
  10056:
      "He (may He be Exalted) resurrects the dead and causes the living to die. You will be returned to Him alone on the Day of Resurrection. He will then recompense you for your deeds accordingly.",
  10057:
      "O people, the Quran has come to you, a powerful reminder, encouragement, and warning. It is a cure for the illnesses of doubt and uncertainty that are in the hearts. It contains guidance to the path of truth and is a mercy for the believers, who are the ones who benefit from it.",
  10058:
      "O Messenger, say to the people: The Quran I brought you is Allah's grace and mercy. So rejoice in Allah's grace and mercy to you through the revelation of this Quran, and not in anything besides this. What Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought to them from His Lord is better than what they gather from the trivial things of this temporary world.",
  10059:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Inform me about Allah's favor of the provision that He sent down for you, of which you acted according to your desires by making some unlawful and some lawful. Say to them: Did Allah permit you to declare those things lawful or unlawful, or are you making up lies against Allah?",
  10060:
      "What do those who make up lies against Allah think will happen to them on the Day of Resurrection? Do they think they will be forgiven? Never! Allah is Bountiful to people by giving them respite and not punishing them immediately, but most people deny Allah's favors and are not grateful for them.",
  10061:
      "You, O Messenger, are not engaged in any matter, do not recite a portion of the Quran, nor do you, O believers, do any deed, except that We see you, knowing when you are about to act and hear you. An atom's weight, in the sky or on Earth, is not hidden from the knowledge of your Lord. Nor is there anything lesser or more in weight, except that it is recorded in a clear book that does not omit anything, no matter how small or big it may be.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the seriousness of the punishment that awaits those who associate partners with Allah, to the extent that they will wish to protect themselves from it with everything that is on earth; but even that will not be accepted from them.\n2. Allah’s punishment will most certainly fall on the disbelievers.\n3. The Qur’an is a cure for the believers from the illnesses of the heart, because of the guidance and advice it contains.\n4. A believer should rejoice in the blessing of Islam and faith and not in the trivial things of this world.\n5. The legislation of what is lawful and unlawful is only from Allah.\n6. We should be aware of Allah’s watching over us in secret and in public. Allah is aware of all our actions.\n7. Everything a person does is recorded by Allah in a book that does not leave out anything, no matter how small or big it may be.",
  10062:
      "Behold! The friends of Allah will not fear the terrors to come on the Day of Resurrection, and they will not grieve over the pleasures of this world that they missed.",
  10063:
      "These friends of Allah are described as those who believe in Allah and His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  10064:
      "They have good news from their Lord in this worldly life, which will make them happy, such as righteous dreams or people praising them. They will also receive good news from the angels when their souls are taken, after their death, and at the Hashr [gathering]. There is no change to the promise of Allah. That reward is a great success because it entails achieving what they desire and salvation from what they fear.",
  10065:
      "Do not grieve, O Messenger, over what these people say in an attempt to attack or slander your religion. Control and domination belong to Allah; nothing can hinder Him. He is All-Hearing of their words, Omniscient of their deeds, and will recompense them accordingly.",
  10066:
      "The dominion of whoever is in the heavens and Earth belongs to Allah. What is it that the polytheists who worship partners instead of Allah are following? In reality, they are only following doubt and are lying when they attribute partners to Allah. Allah is Transcendent and far beyond their statements.",
  10067:
      "It is He alone Who has made the night for you, O people, to take rest from tiredness. He has brightened the day for you to work and earn your livelihood. In that, there are clear indications for people who listen intending to take lessons and accept them.",
  10068:
      "Some of the polytheists said: Allah has taken the angels as daughters. Allah is free of their statement because He (may He be Exalted) is Self-sufficient and does not need any of His creation. The dominion of whatever is in the heavens and the Earth belongs to Him. You, O polytheists, do not have any proof for your statement. Are you making such a severe statement about Allah by attributing a child to Him, even though you do not know the reality and have no proof?",
  10069:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Those who make up lies against Allah by attributing a child to Him will not achieve what they desire and will not be saved from what they fear.",
  10070:
      "They should not be deceived by the luxuries of this world that they enjoy. This is a brief and temporary enjoyment, and then their return will be to Us on the Day of Resurrection. We will then make them taste the severe torment because they disbelieved in Allah and rejected His Messenger.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The friends of Allah are the ones who will be safe on the Day of Judgement and they will not grieve over what they missed.\n2. Allah’s friendship is for those who have faith in Him, fulfil His instructions, avoid His prohibitions and follow His Messenger (peace be upon him).\n3. The believers will receive good news from their Lord: either by having good dreams or at the time of death and other times.\n4. Power belongs entirely to Allah; He is the Owner of Control. Those things that are worshipped besides Him have no reality.\n5. The verses encourage reflecting over Allah’s creation, because that leads to faith in Him and His Oneness.\n6. The verses show the serious offence of disbelief committed by the person who attributes a child to Allah.\n7. It is unlawful to lie about Allah; and the person who does so will never be successful.\n8. The things that the disbelievers enjoy in this world are considered little because of the punishment that awaits them. A believer should not be deceived by this.",
  10071:
      "Relate, O Messenger, to these rejecting polytheists the story of Noah (peace be upon him) when he said to his people: O my people, if my presence among you is unbearable, and my reminders to you of Allah's signs and advising you is too much for you, and you have decided to kill me, then I have placed my trust in Allah alone to make your plots fail. So make a firm decision about your matter; destroy me and call upon your deities by seeking their help, and do not let your plot be an obscure secret. After your plan to kill me, carry out what you secretly intend, and do not give me a moment of respite.",
  10072:
      "If you turn away from my invitation, then you know that I have not asked for any reward from you for conveying the message of my Lord to you. My reward is only from Allah, whether you believe in me or not. Allah has instructed me to be of those who submit to Him with obedience and righteous deeds.",
  10073:
      "Noah's people rejected and did not accept him, so We saved him and those believers with him on the ship. We made them the successors of those before them and destroyed through the Flood those who rejected the signs and evidence he brought. So reflect, O Messenger, over the fate of the people Noah warned (peace be upon him) but did not believe.",
  10074:
      "Then, some time after Noah, We sent messengers to their people. The messengers came to their nations with signs and proofs. But they had no desire to believe due to their previous persistence in rejecting the messengers. Allah, therefore, sealed their hearts. Just as We sealed the hearts of the followers of the earlier messengers, We will seal the hearts of the disbelievers of every time and place who transgress Allah's limits by committing disbelief.",
  10075:
      "Some time after these messengers, We sent Moses and his brother, Aaron, to Pharaoh, the king of Egypt, and the nobles from his people. We sent them with signs indicating their truthfulness, but Pharaoh and his people were too arrogant to believe in what these messengers brought. They were criminals because they disbelieved in Allah and rejected His messengers.",
  10076:
      "When the religion brought by Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them) came to Pharaoh and the nobles from his people, they said about the signs indicating the truthfulness of what Moses brought: it is clear magic and not the truth.",
  10077:
      "Moses said to them in disapproval: After the truth has come to you, are you calling it magic? No way! This is not magic. I know a magician can never succeed, so why would I practice magic?",
  10078:
      "The people of Pharaoh responded to Moses: Have you brought this magic to turn us away from the religion we found our fathers following so that you and your brother can gain control? We do not believe the two of you are messengers sent to us.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses encourage looking at the example of the people of the past because there are many lessons and warnings in their history.\n2. The weapon of the believers when facing their enemies is reliance on Allah.\n3. Believers should seek the reward of their calling to Allah only from Him except in the case of necessity, when one may ask for a wage for food/drink etc.\n4. The fate of a believer is salvation and success whereas the fate of a disbeliever is loss and punishment.\n5. Persistence in disbelief and rejection of the messengers results in the hearts being sealed and unable to ever accept faith.\n6. The condition of the enemies of the messengers is the same: they always describe guidance as magic or lies.\n7. A magician will never succeed.",
  10079:
      "Pharaoh said to his people: Bring me every person knowledgeable and skilled in magic.",
  10080:
      "When the magicians were brought to Pharaoh, Moses told them with complete confidence that he would defeat them: Throw down, O magicians, whatever you will throw.",
  10081:
      "When they cast their magic, Moses told them: What you have produced is magic. Allah will make it useless and of no effect. You cause corruption on Earth through your magic, and Allah does not set right the action of a person who causes corruption.",
  10082:
      "Allah establishes the truth and consolidates it with His words of decree and with the proofs and evidence contained in His legislative words, even though the sinful disbelievers from the people of Pharaoh dislike it.",
  10083:
      "The people were determined to turn away, and none accepted Moses (peace be upon him) despite the open miracles and clear proofs he brought, all except a few youths of his people, the Israelites, while fearing that Pharaoh and the nobles of his people would turn them away from their belief by having them taste torment if their affair became exposed. Pharaoh was tyrannical in his authority over Egypt and its people, and he transgressed the limits by disbelieving in Allah and killing and torturing the Israelites.",
  10084:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to his people: O my people, if you truly believe in Allah and are Muslims [who submit to Him], then place your trust in Him alone. Placing your trust in Allah will protect you from harm and bring you good.",
  10085:
      "They responded to Moses (peace be upon him) and said: In Allah alone, we have placed our trust. O our Lord, do not appoint the wrongdoers over us because they will turn us away from our religion by torturing us, killing us, and tempting us.",
  10086:
      "Save us through Your mercy, O our Lord, from the hands of the disbelieving people of Pharaoh because they have made us into slaves and have harmed us by torturing and killing us.",
  10087:
      "We revealed to Moses and his brother, Aaron (peace be upon them): Select and make homes for your people to worship Allah alone; and make your homes face the direction of the qiblah (which was then Jerusalem); and then perform the prayer with perfection. O Moses, inform the believers of news that will please them: the news of Allah's assistance and support for them, the destruction of their enemy, and making them successors on Earth.",
  10088:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: O our Lord, You have given Pharaoh and the nobles of his people the glitz and glamour of this world. You have also given them wealth in this worldly life, but they were not grateful to You for what You gave them. Instead, they used that to mislead others from Your path. O our Lord, utterly destroy their wealth. Make their hearts hard so that they do not believe unless they see the painful torment at a time when their belief will not benefit them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Having trust in Allah and His assistance should be among the qualities of a strong believer.\n2. Eventually, truth will be victorious no matter how high and overpowering falsehood becomes.\n3. It is obligatory to place trust in Allah and to rely on Him alone.\n4. The verses explain the importance of prayer and that it is one of the qualities of those who rely on Allah.\n5. Establishing the ritual prayer is paramount and it is an obligation in all revealed religions and in all circumstances.\n6. It is acceptable in the sacred law to make a prayer against an oppressor.",
  10089:
      "Allah said: Your prayer, O Moses and Aaron, against Pharaoh and the nobles of his people has been responded to. So, remain firm on your religion and do not deviate from it by following the path of the ignorant ones who do not know the path of truth.",
  10090:
      "We made it easy for the Israelites to cross the sea safely after We split it open. Pharaoh and his soldiers pursued them unjustly and oppressively. Then, when the sea closed on him, bringing him to the point of drowning, he lost all hope of being saved and said: I believe that there is none worthy of worship except the One whom the Israelites believed in, and I am one of those who submit to Allah in obedience.",
  10091:
      "Since facing death impedes the acceptance of repentance, Allah the Transcendent states: \n Do you believe now after despairing of life? You, O Pharaoh, had disobeyed Allah before the torment came down upon you by disbelieving in Him and preventing others from His path, and you were one of those who spread corruption because of your own misguidance and misguiding others.",
  10092:
      "So today, We will take you out, O Pharaoh, from the sea and place you on high ground so that those who come after you can take a lesson from you. But many people are unmindful of Our proofs and evidence indicating Our power, and they do not reflect over them.",
  10093:
      "We settled the Israelites in a commendable place in the blessed lands of the Levant, and We provided them with pure and lawful provision. They did not differ in the matter of religion until the Quran came to them, confirming what they read in the Torah about the description of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. When they denied the revelation, their homelands were taken away from them. Your Lord, O Messenger, will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection regarding the things they differed about; He will recompense those who were on truth and those who were on falsehood with what they deserve.",
  10094:
      "If you, O Messenger, are in doubt or confused about the reality of the Quran that We have revealed to you, ask those Jews who read the Torah and the Christians who read the Gospel to confirm it. They will tell you that what was revealed to you is the truth because they have the description of it in their books. The truth, about which there is no doubt, has come to you from your Lord, so do not be of those who have doubt.",
  10095:
      "Do not be of those who reject Allah's proofs and evidence because that will make you one of those who have lost themselves by bringing themselves to the point of destruction because of their disbelief. All these warnings are meant to show the seriousness of doubt and rejection, even though the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم is protected from such things.",
  10096:
      "Those against whom Allah's decree is established will die as disbelievers due to their persistence in disbelief, and they will never believe.",
  10097:
      "Even if every sign in the creation or verse were to come to them until they witness the painful torment and believe at a time when their belief will not benefit them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is necessary to remain firm on the religion and not to follow the path of those who are sinful.\n2. The repentance of a person whose soul is about to leave the body is not accepted, nor is the repentance of the person who witnesses the beginning of a divine punishment.\n3. The Jews and Christians knew the attributes of the Prophet (peace be upon him), but pride and stubbornness prevented them from accepting him.",
  10098:
      "No town to which We sent messengers benefitted from their belief upon seeing the torment because they did not believe until seeing it, except the people of Jonah. When they truly believed, We removed the torment of disgrace and humiliation from them in the worldly life and allowed them enjoyment until the end of their lives.",
  10099:
      "Had your Lord, O Messenger, willed for everyone on Earth to believe, they would have done so. However, He did not will it to be so based on wisdom. He misguides whoever He wills through His justice and guides whoever He wills through His grace. You cannot force people to become believers: their guidance to belief lies only in Allah's Hand.",
  10100:
      "It is not possible for any soul to believe by itself unless Allah permits it. Belief only happens with His will, so do not lose yourself in grief over them. Allah places torment and disgrace on those who do not apply their minds to His proofs, commands, and prohibitions.",
  10101:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists who ask you for signs: Ponder upon the signs in the heavens and the Earth, which indicate Allah's Oneness and power. However, sending down signs, proofs, and messengers is useless for people who are not prepared to believe because of their persistence in disbelief.",
  10102:
      "Are these rejectors waiting for something similar to what Allah imposed on the previous rejecting nations? Say to them, O Messenger: Wait for Allah's torment. I, too, am waiting with you for my Lord's promise.",
  10103:
      "Then We will send the punishment upon them and save Our messengers and those who believe with them so that they are not afflicted by what afflicted their people. Just as We saved those messengers and the believers with them, We will most certainly save Allah's Messenger and the believers with him, which is Our duty to them.",
  10104:
      "Say, O Messenger: O people, if you are in doubt about my religion that I invite you towards, the religion of monotheism, then I am sure of your religion being false, so I will not follow it. I will not worship those you worship instead of Allah. I will only worship Allah, the One who will cause you to die. He has instructed me to be of those who are sincere to Him in religion.",
  10105:
      "He has also instructed me to remain firm on the true religion, inclining away from all other religions, and He has prohibited me from being one of those who associate partners with Him.",
  10106:
      "And, O Messenger, do not worship, besides Allah, the idols and false deities that cannot benefit you, nor can they inflict harm on you. If you worship them, you will be one of the wrongdoers who transgress against Allah's right and their right.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Faith is the way a person rises to the highest ranks and enjoys the life of this world.\n2. No one has the ability to make someone accept faith, because this is reserved for Allah alone.\n3. The verses prove the power of Allah’s will, and that nothing happens without His permission and will.\n4. Signs and warnings are of no benefit to a person who is insistent on disbelief and persists in it.\n5. Faith will save the believer and disbelief will destroy the disbeliever.\n6. It is necessary to be firm on the true religion and to completely distance oneself from idolatry and false religions.",
  10107:
      "If Allah afflicts you, O Messenger, with a calamity and you seek to remove it, then know that no one can remove it except Him; may He be Exalted. If He wants ease for you, no one can repel His grace. He makes His grace reach whomever He wills of His slaves. No one can compel Him. He is Forgiving and Merciful to those of His slaves who repent to Him.",
  10108:
      "Say, O Messenger: O people, the Quran has come to you as a revelation from your Lord. Whoever chooses to be guided and believes in it will be for his own benefit because Allah does not need the obedience of His slaves. Yet, whoever is misguided only harms himself with his misguidance because Allah is not affected by the disobedience of His slaves. I am not a guardian over you, to watch over your deeds and to reckon you for them.",
  10109:
      "Follow, O Messenger, what your Lord reveals to you and act on it. Be patient with the harm caused by those who oppose you from your people while you convey the message as instructed. Remain firm on this path until Allah passes judgment concerning them by giving you victory over them in this world and punishing them in the Hereafter if they die as disbelievers.",
  11000:
      "Hud (Surah Hud)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nStrengthening the faith of the Prophet and the believers by recounting the stories of the past prophets while also emphasizing the consequences of disbelief.\n•    Explanation:",
  11001:
      "Alif Lām Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. The Quran is a book whose verses are perfect in arrangement and meaning, in which you will see no flaw or deficiency. Then, it was detailed by mentioning the lawful and unlawful commands and prohibitions, promises and threats, narrations, etc. It is from the One who is Wise in His planning and legislation and Who is Aware of the condition of His slaves and what is in their best interests.",
  11002:
      "The content of these verses revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم prohibits the slaves from worshiping anyone alongside Allah. I, O people, warn you of Allah's torment if you disbelieve in Him and disobey Him, and I give you good news of His reward if you believe in Him and practice His sacred law.",
  11003:
      "O people, seek forgiveness for your sins from your Lord and repent with remorse over your neglect of Him. He will give you good provision in the worldly life until your fixed lifespan ends. He will give every person who has merit, in obeying Him and doing good, a full reward for such behavior without any decrease. If you turn away from believing in what I have brought from my Lord, then I fear for you the torment of a Day whose horrors are intense, which is the Day of Resurrection.",
  11004:
      "To Allah alone is your return, O people, on the Day of Resurrection, and He (may He be Exalted) is Omnipotent over everything; nothing can hinder Him. He is not incapable of bringing you back to life and taking you into account after reviving you from your death.",
  11005:
      "These polytheists lean down to conceal their doubts about Allah due to their ignorance of Him. Allah knows what they conceal and reveal when they cover their heads with their clothing. He knows what their chests hide.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Good and bad, benefit and harm, are all in Allah’s Hand and no one else’s.\n2. It is necessary to follow the Book and the Sunnah, to be patient over harm and to wait for relief from Allah.\n3. The verses of the Qur’an are perfectly constructed and no flaws or falsehood can be found in them. The laws it contains have been explained in full.\n4. The aim of the verses of the Qur’an is to prohibit people from worshipping anyone besides Allah.\n5. It is necessary to hurry towards repentance and to show remorse for sins in order to achieve what is desired and to be safe from what is feared.",
  11006:
      "No creature walks on the face of the Earth, wherever it may be, except that Allah has undertaken, through His grace, to provide for it. He (may He be Exalted) knows where each creature will settle on Earth, and He knows where it will die. So, the provision, place of living, and final resting place are all written in a clear book, the Preserved Tablet.",
  11007:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is the One who created the heavens and the Earth in their magnificent form and all that exists between them in six days. Before He made them, His Throne was on water. All of this He created to see which of you, O people, will be best in doing actions that please Allah and which of you will do actions that cause His anger. He will compensate each group according to what they deserve. O Messenger, If you say to them: O people, indeed you will be resurrected after you die and held to account, then those who disbelieve in Allah and reject the resurrection will surely say: This Quran that you recite is nothing but magic, and so clearly false.",
  11008:
      "If We were to delay the polytheists from receiving the punishment they deserve in this world for a few days, they would mock the punishment by asking for it to come quickly, saying: What is it that is holding back the punishment from us? But, of course, the punishment they deserve has a fixed time with Allah, and on the day when it comes to them, they will not find a way to avert it from themselves. So, instead, the punishment they used to mock openly by asking for it to come quicker will fall upon them, engulfing them from all sides.",
  11009:
      "If We give a man a blessing from Us, such as health or wealth, and then We take that blessing away from him, he loses all hope of the mercy of Allah and becomes hugely ungrateful for His blessings, and forgets them as soon as Allah takes them away from him.",
  11010:
      "If We open up many provisions and good health for such a person after he endured poverty and illness, he will say: My troubles have gone, and the crisis is over. However, he does not show gratefulness to Allah for such blessings; instead, he becomes boastful and self-conceited, holding his head high and looking down on people because of what Allah has blessed him with.",
  11011:
      "Except those who are patient during hard times, continue to do acts of obedience, and avoid sins. Such good people are different from the arrogant ones described previously, as they do not lose hope in times of adversity, nor are they ungrateful for Allah's blessings or arrogant. So, they will receive forgiveness from their Lord and a great reward in the Afterlife.",
  11012:
      "Perhaps you, O Messenger, might leave off conveying some of what Allah has ordered you to convey to them from what is difficult for them to implement due to their disbelief, stubbornness, and demand for signs. Perhaps your chest is strained in conveying it lest they say: Why has no treasure been sent down to him to enrich him or an angel to verify his truthfulness? Do not leave some of what is revealed to you because of that; you are only a warner who conveys what Allah has instructed you to convey. It is not upon you to bring the signs that they request; Allah is the Guardian over all things.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show how vast Allah’s knowledge is and that He has taken it on Himself to provide for all of His creation, including human beings, animals, and other than them.\n2. The reason for creation is here explained: to test the servants’ obedience of Allah’s instructions and avoidance of His prohibitions.\n3. A person should not be deceived by Allah’s granting respite to those who commit sin: He may seize them suddenly, when they are unaware.\n4. The verses show man’s condition in the case of both prosperity and hardship, and the believer who is patient and grateful is praised.",
  11013:
      "Rather, do the polytheists say that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم forged the Quran and that it is not a revelation from Allah? Say, O Messenger, challenging them: Bring ten forged chapters similar to the Quran without maintaining truthfulness in it, just like the Quran which you claim is forged. Call upon whomsoever you can call upon in order to seek assistance by that in this (pursuit) if you are truthful in your claim that the Quran is forged!",
  11014:
      "If they do not bring what you have asked them to due to their lack of ability, then know with certainty, O believers, that the Quran is none other than what Allah sent down to His Messenger with His complete knowledge, that it is not forged, and that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah. Then will you not surrender to Him in devotion after these conclusive proofs (and become from those who submit to Islam and become Muslims)?",
  11015:
      "Whoever seeks the life of this world and its fleeting pleasures with their actions and does not seek the reward of the Hereafter with them, We will compensate them for their actions in this worldly life: good health, safety, and vastness in provision, not decreasing in the reward for their actions in any way.",
  11016:
      "Those people with this blameworthy trait will not be rewarded on the Day of Resurrection, except for the Fire, which they will enter. The reward of their actions will disappear and be useless because they were not based on faith or good intention, and they did not desire the face of Allah and the abode of the Hereafter through their actions.",
  11017:
      "The disbelievers are not equal to the believers who believe in the Quran and the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, who has clear proof from His Lord, the Exalted. A witness from Allah (Jibreel) who follows him, and the Torah revealed to Moses (peace be upon him) also testify to the truthfulness of his prophethood. He was sent as a role model and mercy to people. Therefore, he and those who believe in him are not the same as those who stray in error. For those who disbelieve in it from the different religions, the Fire will be their promised destination on the Day of Resurrection. So, O Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, do not doubt the Quran and their destination because it is the truth in which there is no doubt. However, despite the many clear signs and evidence, most people do not have faith.",
  11018:
      "No one is a worse transgressor than someone who makes up a lie about Allah, associating a partner or a son with Him. Those who make up lies about Allah will be brought before their Lord on the Day of Resurrection to be asked about their actions. The witnesses from the angels and the messengers will say: These were the ones who lied about Allah by attributing a partner or son to Him. Allah will deprive them of His mercy due to the lies they spread about Him.",
  11019:
      "Those who prevent people from Allah's straight path seek to make it appear crooked so that no one follows it, and they reject the belief in the Afterlife.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s challenge to the idolaters is to produce ten surahs like the Qur’an; and it is highlighted that they will be unable to do this.\n2. Even if the disbeliever is given what they desire in this world, it will be meaningless when they only have the fire of Hell in the Afterlife.\n3. It is demonstrated that the Muslims who have a clear sign from their Lord are not the same as those without a clear sign, who only follow each other blindly and in ignorance, such as the disbelievers with their idols.\n4. The great sin of someone who makes up a lie about Allah is clearly emphasised.",
  11020:
      "People such as this will not be able to escape Allah's punishment in this life, and they have no allies or protectors besides Allah who can stop the punishment of Allah from reaching them. So, their punishment on the Day of Resurrection will be increased because they turned away and turned others away from Allah's path. Thus, in the life of this world, they were not able to hear the truth and guidance in a way that led them to accept it, nor were they able to see Allah's signs throughout the universe in a way that benefited them because of their total disregard of the truth.",
  11021:
      "These people have incurred great loss upon themselves because they took the path of destruction by associating partners with Allah. The partners and intercessors they invented will all abandon them.",
  11022:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, they will undoubtedly be the greatest losers because they exchanged faith for disbelief, the next life for this life, and mercy for punishment.",
  11023:
      "Those who believe in Allah and His messengers and do good actions are humble and fear Allah. They are the people of Paradise and will live therein eternally.",
  11024:
      "The example of the two groups, the disbelievers and the believers, is like a group of blind and deaf people who neither see nor hear and another group that can hear and see. The disbelievers do not listen in a way that leads them to accept the truth and do not see in a beneficial way. Meanwhile, the believers both hear and see. Are these two groups the same in their state and depiction? Of course, they are not the same. Will you then not consider how truly different they are to each other?",
  11025:
      "When it became apparent that the polytheists were turning away from belief, Allah consoled the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم by reminding him that he was not the first to be rejected. He then recounted the stories of previous prophets, stating: \n Indeed, We sent Noah (peace be upon him) as a messenger to his people. Noah said to them: O my people, I have been sent to warn you of Allah's punishment and make the message I have been sent with very clear to you.",
  11026:
      "I call you to worship Allah alone; therefore, do not worship anyone besides Him. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a painful day.",
  11027:
      "Those who disbelieved from his people among the notables and leaders said: We will not respond to your call, as you have no distinction over us. Rather, you are a man like us. We only see those who appear lowly to us following you. Also, you do not have wealth, rank, or status above us that qualifies you to be followed by us. In fact, we think that you are not truthful in what you are calling us to.",
  11028:
      "Noah asked his people: O people, tell me, if I were upon evidence from my Lord that proved my truthfulness, and you had to believe in me, and [my Lord] showed me mercy, in the form of prophethood and the messengership, but due to your ignorance, it was hidden from you; would we force you to believe and place faith in your hearts? We would never be able to do that because Allah alone grants people the ability to believe.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbeliever does not benefit from his hearing or his sight in a way that leads him to faith, so it is as if he does not have them at all, unlike the believer.\n2. Allah’s custom with the followers of the messengers is that they are largely poor and weak, while their adversaries are largely important people and leaders.\n3. The verses demonstrate the pride of most of those who are important and are leaders, who look down on others.",
  11029:
      "My people, I do not ask for your wealth in exchange for bringing you the message, as my reward is with Allah. Therefore, I will not push away the poor believers like you have asked me to. Indeed, they will meet their Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will reward them for their faith. I see you as a nation that does not understand the reality of this call when you ask me to push away the weak believers.",
  11030:
      "Noah said: My people, who would repel Allah's punishment from me if I unjustly drove away these poor believers for no crime? Will you not reflect and strive for what is best and most beneficial to you?",
  11031:
      "My people, I do not claim that I possess the treasures of Allah, which I can spend on you if you believe. Nor do I claim to know the unseen nor that I am an angel; instead, I am a man like you. I also do not say about these weak people, whom you see as inferiors or hold in such disregard, that Allah will not give them success and guidance. Allah knows best their intentions and their circumstances. If I did make such a claim, I would undoubtedly be among those wrongdoers who deserve the punishment of Allah.",
  11032:
      "Noah's people said to him, out of stubbornness and pride: O Noah, you have debated and disputed with us long enough; bring on the punishment you are threatening us with if you are truthful in what you claim.",
  11033:
      "Noah said to them: I cannot bring the punishment upon you; only Allah can do that if He wishes to, and you would not be able to escape from the punishment of Allah if He decides to punish you.",
  11034:
      "Noah told them that his advice and counsel would not benefit them if Allah wills that they are led astray from the straight path and if He wills to leave them without guidance because of their stubbornness. He is their Lord and has control over their lives, so He can lead them astray if He wills. To Him alone, they will be returned on the Day of Resurrection, when they will be recompensed for their actions.",
  11035:
      "The reason for the people of Noah disbelieving [in the message] is that they claimed that Noah had lied about the religion he came with, so Allah ordered His Prophet to tell them that if he had invented it, he would have been a wrongdoer. Therefore, the punishment for his crime would fall upon him alone. But, on the other hand, if they rejected the truth that he had brought them out of stubbornness and pride, they were the wrongdoers, and he was not responsible for their crime in any way. Instead, he was free from it.",
  11036:
      "Allah revealed to Noah that none of his people would believe except those who had already believed. He told him not to be saddened by their rejection and mockery of him over the many years [he had been calling them].",
  11037:
      "Build [O Noah] the Ark under Our observation and protection. Learn how to make it with Our revelation to you. Do not address Me requesting to give time to those who wronged themselves through their disbelief. No doubt, they will be drowned in the Flood as a consequence of persisting in their disbelief.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Someone who calls to Allah hopes for a reward from Him alone.\n2. It is forbidden to drive away poor believers, and they must be treated with generosity and honour.\n3. Knowledge of the Ghaib is Allah’s alone.\n4. Debate and argumentation with those who deny the truth is religiously legitimate.\n5. Advice will not benefit someone if Allah does not will for them to be guided.",
  11038:
      "Noah followed the command of his Lord and immediately started building the Ark. Whenever the leaders and noblemen among his people passed by, they made fun of him because he was building the Ark as there was no water or rivers around. When they continued to mock him, he said to them: If you, O noblemen, mock us today as we build the Ark, then we also mock you for being ignorant of the fact that you will drown.",
  11039:
      "[Noah told them] You will come to know who will be punished in a disgraceful and humiliating way in this world and who the eternal punishment will descend upon on the Day of Resurrection.",
  11040:
      "Noah (peace be upon him) finished building the Ark that Allah had commanded him to build. Then Our command to destroy them came, and the water boiled up from the furnace they used to bake in, signaling the beginning of the Flood. Allah told Noah (peace be upon him) to place onboard the Ark a pair of every type of animal on Earth, a male and a female, and to take his family, except for those who had already been determined to drown because they did not believe. He was also told to bring those who believed in him from among his people. But unfortunately, only a small number of his people believed in him, despite the long time he had remained among them, calling them to have faith in Allah.",
  11041:
      "Noah said to those who believed from his family and his people: Board the Ark, and its sailing and landing will be in the name of Allah. My Lord is Forgiving of the sins of those of His slaves who repent to Him and is Compassionate with them. His mercy on the believers is that He saved them from perishing.",
  11042:
      "The Ark sailed with the people and animals through great waves like mountains. Noah (peace be upon him), with the affection of a father, called to his son, who did not believe and was in a place isolated from his father and his people. Noah told him to get onto the Ark with them so that he could be saved from the Flood, and he told him not to be with the disbelievers, or he would be drowned as they would be.",
  11043:
      "Noah's son said to his father: I will take refuge on a high mountain so the water will not reach me. Noah told his son: Nothing will save anyone from Allah's punishment of being drowned by the Flood, except those whom Allah saves with His mercy. Then, a wave came between Noah and his disbelieving son, and his son was drowned by the Flood because of his disbelief.",
  11044:
      "After the Flood, Allah said: O Earth, absorb the water, and O sky, hold back and do not send down rain. The water decreased until the land became dry. By then, Allah had destroyed the disbelievers. The Ark stopped on Mount Jūdī. It was said: Be gone and ruined, O people who had transgressed the limits of Allah through disbelief.",
  11045:
      "Noah (peace be upon him) called upon his Lord, seeking his aid, saying: My Lord, indeed my son is from my family that you promised to save. Your promise is always true; you are the most just and knowledgeable.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The idolaters are in the habit of mocking and sneering at the prophets and their followers.\n2. The custom of Allah with people is that most of them do not have faith.\n3. The story of Noah with his people shows the truth of Allah’s promise to them that they would be drowned and destroyed.",
  11046:
      "Allah said to Noah: Indeed, your son that you asked me to save is not from your family because he is a disbeliever. Your question, O Noah, is not a befitting action for someone of your status. Therefore, do not ask me something you have no knowledge of. I warn you from being among the ignorant folk by questioning [a decision] you do not know about.",
  11047:
      "Noah (peace be upon him) said: My Lord, prevent me from asking You about something I do not know about. And if You do not forgive my sins and have mercy on me, I will be among the losers who lose their share of the Afterlife.",
  11048:
      "Allah said to Noah (peace be upon him): O Noah, disembark and go on land in safety and security, with many blessings from Allah upon you and on the believing descendants of those with you on the Ark who will come after you. Unfortunately, there will also be others from their descendants who will disbelieve. For a time, Allah will give them enjoyment and livelihood in the life of this world, but then a painful punishment from Him will come to them.",
  11049:
      "This story of Noah is from the news of the unseen, which you, O Messenger, or your people did not know beforehand until We revealed it to you. Therefore, be patient with the harm you suffer from the rejection of your people, just as Noah صلى الله عليه وسلم was patient. Help and victory are for those who comply with Allah's commands and avoid what He has prohibited.",
  11050:
      "We sent to the people of 'Ād their brother Hūd (peace be upon him). He said to them: O my people, worship Allah alone and do not associate anyone with Him; you do not have a deity that deserves to be worshipped except Him, may He be Exalted; you are not telling the truth in claiming he has a partner.",
  11051:
      "[Hūd said] O my people, I do not seek from you reward for what I have conveyed from my Lord and my calling you to Him. My reward is only from Allah, Who created me. Will you not think about this and respond to what I am calling you to?",
  11052:
      "[Hūd said] O my people, ask for forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him from your sins, the greatest of which is associating others with Him. He will reward you by sending down abundant rain and will strengthen you by increasing your descendants and wealth. Therefore, do not turn away from what I am calling you to because you will become wrongdoers due to turning away from my call and your disbelief in Allah and rejection of what I have brought.",
  11053:
      "Hūd's people said: O Hūd, you have not brought us unmistakable proof to make us believe you. We will not abandon our gods because of what you are saying without evidence. We do not believe your claim that you are a messenger.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Prophets cannot plead on the behalf of those who disbelieve in Allah, even if they are their children.\n2. The verses make clear that the goal of relating the stories of the prophets was to console the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the believers.\n3. There is great virtue in asking for forgiveness and turning to Allah, which are reasons for rain being sent down and for an increase in descendants and wealth.",
  11054:
      "Hūd's people said to him that their gods had inflicted him with madness because he had told them not to worship them. So Hūd said: I call upon Allah to bear witness and that you too should bear witness, that I am innocent of worshipping any gods you worship besides Allah. So, go ahead and plot against me with your gods, which you claim have inflicted me with madness, and do not give me any respite.",
  11055:
      "Hūd's people said to him that their gods had inflicted him with madness because he had told them not to worship them. So Hūd said: I call upon Allah to bear witness and that you too should bear witness, that I am innocent of worshipping any gods you worship besides Allah. So, go ahead and plot against me with your gods, which you claim have inflicted me with madness, and do not give me any respite.",
  11056:
      "I trust in Allah and rely upon Him alone in my affairs because He is my Lord and yours. Nothing walks on the Earth except that it is under His power and control, and He deals with it as He wills. My Lord is upon truth and justice and will not give you power over me since I stand for the truth and you stand for falsehood.",
  11057:
      "Should you continue to turn away from what I brought you, I have no responsibility to do more than convey the message. I have conveyed everything Allah has sent me and instructed me to convey. The proof has been established against you. My Lord will destroy you and bring other people to succeed you. You will not harm Allah in the slightest by rejecting and turning away because He does not need His creation. My Lord watches over everything and protects me from the evil you plot against me.",
  11058:
      "When Our command came to destroy them, We saved Hūd and those who believed in him as a mercy from Us, and We saved them from a stern punishment given to the disbelievers among his people.",
  11059:
      "Such were the people of 'Ād. They disbelieved in the signs of Allah, their Lord, and went against His Messenger Hūd. They followed the instruction of every arrogant tyrant against the truth, not accepting it or dedicating themselves to it.",
  11060:
      "They were then cursed with humiliation and removed from Allah's mercy in this world. On the Day of Resurrection, they will also be without Allah's mercy. Due to their disbelief in Allah, the Exalted, He distances them from every good and allows them to draw closer to every evil.",
  11061:
      "We sent to the people of Thamūd their brother Saleh. He said: O my people worship Allah alone; you have no god worthy of worship other than Him. He created you from the Earth's soil when He created their father Adam from it and made them settle in it. He told them to ask for forgiveness from Him and that his Lord was Near to those who devoted themselves to worshipping Him, responding to their supplications.",
  11062:
      "Saleh's people told him: O Saleh, you had a high position among us before this, and we had hoped you would be wise, a person of advice and sound counsel. Do you prevent us from worshipping what our forefathers used to worship? Indeed, we have doubts about the worship of Allah alone that you are calling us to; we even suspect you are making things up about Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The call of all the messengers was the same: to worship Allah alone, and not to associate anything with Him.\n2. It is established that the rejection and stubbornness of the idolaters occurs in the same way in every time and place.",
  11063:
      "In reply, Saleh asked his people: O my people, tell me if I am upon a clear proof from my Lord, and He has given me mercy, which is prophethood, who would protect me from His punishment if I disobeyed Allah by not delivering what He instructed me to convey to you? You would only increase me in error, distancing me from Allah's pleasure.",
  11064:
      "O my people, this she-camel of Allah is a sign of my truthfulness. So please leave it to graze on Allah's land and do not harm it; else punishment will come to you as soon as you cause it harm.",
  11065:
      "They slaughtered it, further increasing their denial. So Saleh told them: Take joy in your land for the next three days. After that, the punishment of Allah will come to you, and the coming of His punishment was a real threat that could not be denied, but rather, it was a truthful promise.",
  11066:
      "When Our command came to destroy them, We saved Saleh and those who believed with him out of mercy from Us, and We saved them from the disgrace and humiliation of that day. Therefore, O Messenger, without doubt, your Lord is the most powerful, the Mighty Whom no one can overcome. Consequently, He destroyed the nations that disbelieved.",
  11067:
      "The great scream overtook the people of Thamūd, so they perished from its sheer intensity. When morning time came, they lay face down on the ground.",
  11068:
      "It was as if they had never lived in their land in comfort and ease. Indeed, Thamūd disbelieved in Allah, their Lord, so they remained far removed from His mercy.",
  11069:
      "Then the angels came to Abraham (peace be upon him) in the form of men, giving good news to him and his wife of Isaac and Jacob. The angels said: Peace, so he said: Peace. Then he quickly brought them a roasted calf to eat, thinking they were men.",
  11070:
      "But when Abraham saw that their hands were not reaching for the calf and that they were not eating it, he was confused and frightened by them. When the angels saw his fear of them, they told him not to be afraid and that Allah had sent them to the people of Lot to punish them.",
  11071:
      "Abraham's wife, Sarah, was standing and laughed in amazement at what she heard. Then, they told her something that greatly pleased her: that she would bear Isaac and that Isaac would have Jacob.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s custom with the first peoples was to send them messengers who brought good news and warned them, until the proof was against them, then He destroyed those who disbelieved and saved those who had faith.\n2. The sign of Salih (peace be upon him) was one of the greatest signs, but his people did not believe it.\n3. It is highly desirable to give the believers news that brings them joy.\n4. It is correct behaviour to say ‘Peace’ when entering someone’s house and for the hosts to reply in the same way.\n5. The sacred law instructs people to honour their guests.",
  11072:
      "When the angels gave Sarah this good news, she asked: How can I have a child when I am an old woman with no hope of having children, and my husband is elderly?! Having a child at such an age is extraordinary and not normal at all.",
  11073:
      "When Sarah was amazed at the news, the angels asked her: Are you amazed by Allah's decree and command? People like you know that Allah can do such things. Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you, O people of the house of Abraham! Allah is Praiseworthy in His attributes and actions, the Possessor of Glory and Grandeur.",
  11074:
      "Once the fear had abated from Abraham (peace be upon him) that was brought on by his guests not eating his food and the discovery that the guests were angels, then, receiving the joyous news that he would have Isaac, who would have Jacob, he started to debate with Our messengers about the people of Lot, asking that the punishment be delayed and that Lot and his family be saved.",
  11075:
      "Abraham was forbearing by wanting to delay the punishment, often praying to his Lord, calling upon Him, and turning to Him.",
  11076:
      "The angels said: Turn away from this discussion, O Abraham, about the people of Lot. The command of your Lord has come. They will receive the punishment He has decreed for them. A great punishment is coming to the people of Lot, which no debate or supplication can prevent.",
  11077:
      "When the angels came to Lot in the form of humans, he was distressed by their coming to him, and he became anxious and feared for their well-being because his people would approach men with desires instead of women. So Lot said it was a terrible day because he thought his people would force themselves on his guests.",
  11078:
      "The people of Lot came rushing to him, intending to commit lewd acts with his guests. They were used to going to men with desire instead of women. To put his people off his guests, Lot told them: These are my daughters; you can marry them because they are purer for you than the evil acts you are trying to commit. So fear Allah, and do not disgrace me concerning my guests. Is there not a single right-minded man among you who can tell you not to commit such a shameful act?",
  11079:
      "His people told him: You know we have no need or desire for your daughters or the women among your people. You know very well what we want; we desire men only.",
  11080:
      "Lot said: If only I had the strength to use against you or people to support me, I would have come between you and my guests.",
  11081:
      "The angels said to Lot (peace be upon him): O Lot, we are messengers sent by Allah, and your people will not be able to touch you with their evil. Leave town tonight, when it is dark, with your family. Let no one turn to look at what is behind them except for your wife, who will turn back wrongly because the punishment that will befall your people will also come upon her. The appointed time for their destruction will be the morning, which is very near.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue and rank of the family of Abraham is clearly demonstrated.\n2. It is established that it is permissible to plead for those whom you hope will have faith before their case is decided by Allah.\n3. The story highlights the rank of Abraham (peace be upon him) as the friend of Allah.\n4. The story also shows the atrocious shamefulness of the actions of the people of Lot.",
  11082:
      "When Our command to destroy the people of Lot came, We turned their towns upside down by raising and turning them over together with the people. We rained down on them stones of hard-layered baked clay that came cascading down.",
  11083:
      "These stones were sent by Allah and came with specific markings, and they are not too far away from the oppressors of Quraysh. Rather, they are near and will come down on them when Allah decrees it.",
  11084:
      "We sent to Midian their brother, Shuayb, who said: O my people, worship Allah alone. You have no other deity that deserves to be worshipped besides Him. Do not give people short measure or weight when you deal with them. I see you in prosperity and with blessings, so do not change Allah's favor to you by committing sins. I fear for you the punishment of an encompassing day that will reach every one of you and from which you will not find any place to run to or seek refuge in.",
  11085:
      "He said: O my people, give complete and just measure and weight when you measure and weigh for others. Do not cheat people of their rights by giving short measures and deceiving them. Do not spread corruption on Earth by killing and committing other sins.",
  11086:
      "[He further said] The lawful that Allah leaves for you after you give people their rights in full and with fairness is of more benefit and contains more blessing than the extra obtained through using short measures and spreading corruption on Earth. If you are indeed believers, then be content with what remains. It is not my duty to watch over you, record your actions, and hold you to account for them. The One who watches over you is the One Who knows all secrets and private conversations.",
  11087:
      "The people of Shuayb said to him: O Shuayb, does your prayer that you pray to Allah instruct you [to tell us] to leave the worship of the idols our fathers used to worship? Does it instruct you [to tell us] to stop dealing and investing with our wealth as we wish? You are indeed a sensible and wise person. We knew you as someone with intellect and wisdom before this call [you are making]. What happened to you?",
  11088:
      "Shuayb said to his people: O my people, tell me what will be your condition if I am on clear proof and insight from my Lord, and He has given me lawful provision from Him, as well as prophethood? I do not wish to prohibit you from something and go against you and then do it myself. I just want to set your matter right, to the best of my ability, by inviting you to declare your Lord's Oneness and obey Him. My success in achieving this is only with Allah; may He be Exalted! Therefore, I trust Him alone and turn to Him in all my affairs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s custom is to destroy the wrongdoers with the most horrific and severe punishment.\n2. It is unlawful to give short measure and to cheat people of their rights.\n3. It is necessary to be satisfied with what is lawful, even if it is little.\n4. It is unlawful to spread any type of corruption on earth.\n5. The verses indicate the virtue of instructing good and prohibiting evil and the necessity of practicing what Allah instructs and abstaining from what He prohibits.",
  11089:
      "[He continued] O my people, do not let your hatred for me make you deny what I have brought. [On the contrary, you should] be afraid that you will suffer like the people of Noah, Hūd, or Saleh. The people of Lot are not far from you in terms of time or place. You know what happened to them, so take heed.",
  11090:
      "Seek forgiveness from your Lord. Then repent to Him from your sins. My Lord is Compassionate to those who repent and is Most Loving to those who turn to Him.",
  11091:
      "The people of Shuayb said to him: O Shuayb, we do not understand much of what you have brought. We regard you as weak and not one of the notables or leaders. If it were not for your clan following our religious beliefs, we would have stoned you to death. You are not mighty enough for us to be afraid of killing you. The only reason we have not killed you is out of respect for your clan.",
  11092:
      "Shuayb told his people: O my people, is my clan more respectable and honorable to you than Allah, your Lord? You rejected Allah when you did not believe in the Prophet He sent to you. My Lord knows well what you do. No action of yours is hidden from Him. He will recompense you this life with destruction and in the Afterlife with punishment.",
  11093:
      "O my people, do what you can in the manner you wish, and I, too, will do what I can in the manner I wish. Soon, you will know which of us will receive a humiliating punishment and who is lying in their claim. So wait for Allah's decision, and I will also wait with you.",
  11094:
      "When Our command to destroy the people of Shuayb came, We rescued Shuayb and the people of faith with him through mercy from Us. However, those of his people who did wrong were afflicted with the intense sound and died. In the morning, they were found lying on the ground with their faces in the dust.",
  11095:
      "It was as if they had never resided there previously. Without a doubt, Midian was distanced from Allah's mercy when His punishment fell on them, just as Thamūd was driven away from it by Allah sending down His anger on them.",
  11096:
      "Indeed, We sent Moses with Our signs that indicated the Oneness of Allah and with clear evidence that proved the truth of what he brought.",
  11097:
      "We sent Moses to Pharaoh and the notable people among them. These notable people followed Pharaoh's command to disbelieve in Allah. The command of Pharaoh was not right for it to be followed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses condemn those ignorant people who do not understand the signs brought by the prophets.\n2. The verses condemn and declare foolish those who follow the instructions of people while ignoring Allah’s sacred law.\n3. The verses demonstrate the role of the family in supporting the call and the callers towards Allah.\n4. The idolaters are driven away from Allah’s mercy.",
  11098:
      "Pharoah will precede his people into the Fire on the Day of Resurrection until he enters them into it. What an evil place he will lead them to!",
  11099:
      "With the destruction and drowning that afflicted them, Allah followed that with a curse and their being driven away and far-removed from His mercy in this world and on the Day of Resurrection. What an evil thing that happened to them: they became the subject of two successive curses and punishment in this life and the Afterlife!",
  11100:
      "We inform you, O Messenger, of the tales of the towns mentioned in this Surah. The landmarks of some of these towns still exist, and the landmarks of others have been wiped out without any trace.",
  11101:
      "O Messenger, We did not wrong them by afflicting them with destruction. However, they wronged their souls by bringing destruction upon themselves when they disbelieved in Allah. The gods they used to worship besides Allah did not repel the punishment that came down on them when the command of your Lord came for their destruction. On the contrary, these gods of theirs only increased them in loss and destruction.",
  11102:
      "Such is the grip and annihilation with which Allah seizes the towns that deny in every time and place [across history]. His grip on such disobedient towns is painful and severe.",
  11103:
      "In Allah's severe punishment of those disobedient towns, there is a lesson and warning for the one who fears the punishment of the Day of Resurrection. Allah will gather people on that day to take them to account, and all people on the plains of the resurrection will witness it.",
  11104: "We only postpone that witnessed day until a specific time.",
  11105:
      "No soul can present any argument or intercession when that Day comes except after He gives permission. People on that Day will be of two types: a wretched person who will enter the Fire and a delighted person who will enter Paradise.",
  11106:
      "Because of their disbelief and corrupt actions, those who are wretched will enter the Fire, in which their voices and breath will be raised due to the severity of the blazing Fire they will suffer from.",
  11107:
      "They will live in it eternally and not come out of it for as long as the heavens and the Earth last, except for those sinful monotheists whom Allah wills to remove. Your Lord, O Messenger, is the One who does whatever He wishes, and nothing can force Him to do something.",
  11108:
      "Their delight from Allah preceded those who were delighted because of their faith and good actions. Therefore, they will live in Paradise eternally for as long as the heavens and the Earth last, except for those sinful monotheists whom Allah wills to enter into the Fire for a time. Therefore, the delight Allah will provide for the people of Paradise will never be cut off from them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses warn against following the leaders of evil and corruption; and they explain the misfortune that results in both the worlds because of following them.\n2. Allah is innocent of being accused of injustice when He destroys those who associate partners with Him and commit sin.\n3. The Allahs of the idolaters will not be of any benefit on the Day of Judgement to those who worshipped them and they will not be able to save them from the punishment.\n4. People will be divided into two groups on the Day of Judgement: the fortunate who will live eternally in Paradise and the wretched who will live eternally in the Hellfire.",
  11109:
      "So, O Messenger, do not doubt the invalidity of what these polytheists worship. They have no proof based on logic or any proof from the sacred law to justify such worship. The only thing that makes them worship other than Allah is their blind following of their forefathers. Therefore, We will give them their full portion of the punishment without any reduction.",
  11110:
      "We had given Moses the Torah, but people disagreed: some believed, while others did not. Had it not been for Allah's prior decree that the punishment would not come quickly but be postponed until the Day of Resurrection for a reason, the punishment they deserve would have come down on them in this world. Instead, the disbelieving Jews and polytheists are in doubt about the Quran, which creates uncertainty in them.",
  11111:
      "And for everyone who is mentioned among the dissenters, your Lord desires for them, O Messenger, the appropriate recompense for their deeds. So what was good within the deeds, their reward will be good, and what was evil within them, their reward will be evil. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of the most minute aspects of what they do, and nothing from their actions is ever hidden from Him.",
  11112:
      "So remain patient, O Messenger, as Allah has instructed you. Fulfill His instructions and stay away from His prohibitions. Let those believers who have repented with you also remain patient. Do not overstep the limits by committing sins because He sees what you do. No action of yours is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for what you do.",
  11113:
      "Do not incline toward the disbelievers who do wrong by being kind to or showing them love, or the Fire will afflict you because of such inclination. You will not have any friends besides Allah to save you from it. Then you will not find anyone to help you.",
  11114:
      "Maintain, O Messenger, the prayer in the best manner at both ends of the day. Also, maintain the prayer during the hours of the night. Good actions wipe out minor sins. This is a warning for those who pay attention and a lesson for those who take heed.",
  11115:
      "Be patient in doing what you have been instructed to do concerning being upright and avoiding the things you have been prohibited from, such as transgression and inclining towards the wrongdoers. Allah will not cause the reward of those who do good to be wasted. Instead, He will accept from them the best of what they did and give them their reward according to their best actions.",
  11116:
      "If only there were, among the communities who were punished before you, remnants of the people of virtue and piety who prohibited those communities from disbelief and spreading corruption throughout the Earth with sins. But there were no such remnants among them, except for a few who used to prohibit corruption and whom We saved when We destroyed their people who did wrong. So, the wrongdoers from their people pursued the luxuries they had and were wrong in doing so.",
  11117:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, will not destroy any town if its inhabitants act correctly on Earth. He will only ruin it if the inhabitants are causing corruption through disbelief, disobedience, and sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s decree has already been passed that the punishment in the world will be postponed until the Day of Judgement. This is for a reason intended by Allah.\n2. It is necessary to remain firm on Allah’s religion.\n3. The verses warn against leaning towards the disbelievers who do wrong, by being kind to them or showing them love.\n4. The verses explain the times of the five ritual prayers which are to be offered at the two ends of the day and during the early hours of the night.\n5. The verses explain Allah’s custom of having evil actions wiped out by good actions.\n6. It is encouraged to create a group consisting of people of virtue who instruct good and prohibit corruption and evil.\n7. Allah’s custom is that He does not destroy any town if its people are setting things right on earth.",
  11118:
      "If your Lord, O Messenger, wanted to make everyone into one nation upon the truth, He would have done so. However, He did not do that, so they continue to differ because they follow their desires and commit transgressions.",
  11119:
      "Except for those whom Allah shows mercy upon by guiding them. They do not differ concerning His Oneness; may He be Exalted. Allah created them to test them in that disagreement; some wretched, and others delighted. The word of your Lord, O Messenger, in which He decreed to fill Hell with jinn and humans who follow the Devil will be fulfilled.",
  11120:
      "Every incident We relate to you, O Messenger, from the lives of the messengers before you is to make your heart firm on the truth and to strengthen it. In this chapter, the truth, about which there is no doubt, has come to you. There has been a warning for the disbelievers and a reminder for the believers (who benefit from such a reminder).",
  11121:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who do not have faith in Allah and do not accept His Oneness: Act according to your way of ignoring the truth and preventing others from it. We will also act according to our way of remaining firm on the truth, inviting towards it, and being patient with it.",
  11122:
      "Wait to see what descends on us. I am also waiting to see what descends on you.",
  11123:
      "To Allah alone belongs the knowledge of the unseen in the heavens and the Earth. Nothing is hidden from Him. The entire matter will return to Him alone on the Day of Resurrection. So worship Him alone, O Messenger, and rely upon Him for all your affairs. Your Lord is not unaware of what you do. Instead, He knows about it and will recompense each person for what they did.",
  12000:
      "Joseph (Surah Yusuf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nRecognizing Allah's kindness in managing His allies and establishing them towards a noble end.\n•    Explanation:",
  12001:
      "Alif Lām Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. The verses revealed in this surah are from the verses of the Quran, which are clear in their meaning.",
  12002:
      "We have revealed the Quran in the language of the Arabs so that you, O Arabs, can understand its meanings.",
  12003:
      "O Messenger, by revealing this Quran to you, We narrate the best of stories due to their accuracy, the soundness of their words, and their eloquence. Before its revelation, you were unaware of these stories, without any knowledge of them.",
  12004:
      "We inform you, O Messenger, about when Joseph told his father, Jacob: O my father, I dreamt of eleven stars and saw the sun and the moon. I saw all of them prostrating to me. This dream was an early sign of good news for Joseph (peace be upon him).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Unnecessary disagreement is condemned in Islam.\n2. The reason for Qur’anic stories is stated in these verses: to make the heart of the Prophet (peace be upon him) firm and to advise the believers.\n3. Knowledge of the unseen is exclusive to Allah and no one shares this with Him.\n4. The reason for the Qur’an being revealed in Arabic was for the Arabs to understand it and convey it to others.\n5. The Qur’an contains the best of stories.",
  12005:
      "Jacob told his son, Joseph: O my son, do not mention your dream to your brothers because they will understand it and become jealous of you. They will then plot against you because of their envy. The Devil is a clear enemy of man.",
  12006:
      "Just as you have seen that dream, your Lord will choose you, O Joseph, and teach you the interpretation of dreams. He will perfect His favor on you by giving you prophethood, just as He completed His blessing on your two forefathers before you, Abraham and Isaac. Your Lord knows all about His creation and is the most Wise in His planning.",
  12007:
      "In the story of Joseph and his brothers, there are lessons and admonitions for those who ask about the event.",
  12008:
      "At that time, the brothers said among themselves: Joseph and his full brother are more beloved to our father than we are, whereas we are a large group. So why does he prefer them over us? We think our father is mistaken in doing so without an apparent reason.",
  12009:
      "[It was further said] Kill Joseph or expel him to a far-off land, and your father's attention will be all yours, and he will love you completely. Then, after killing him and expelling him, you can be righteous when you repent from your sin.",
  12010:
      "One of the brothers said: Do not kill Joseph, rather throw him into a well, and some passers-by may find him and take him; this is a lesser evil if you want to get rid of him.",
  12011:
      "When they agreed to get rid of him, they said to their father, Jacob: O our father, why will you not trust us with Joseph? We have compassion for him and will take care of him against anything that might harm him. We want good for him, so we will protect and look after him until he comes back to you safely. So, what stops you from sending him with us?",
  12012:
      "Let us take him with us tomorrow so he can have a good time and play with us, and we will protect him from any harm that may come to him.",
  12013:
      "Jacob said to his sons: It saddens me that you take him because I cannot bear to be away from him. I also fear that a wolf may eat him when you are not paying attention to him, distracted by your games and idle play.",
  12014:
      "They said to their father: If a wolf were to eat Joseph while there are so many of us, then, in such a case, we would have no good left in us. Therefore, we would be losers if we were unable to stop a wolf from eating him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The occurrence of truth-revealing dreams is established by the sacred law and it is pennissible to interpret them.\n2. It is allowed in the sacred law to hide some facts if some harm may occur by revealing them.\n3. The verses explain the virtue of the children of the family of Abraham and that they were chosen over other people for prophethood.\n4. Favouring one child with more love creates hatred and envy amongst brothers and sisters.",
  12015:
      "So Jacob sent Joseph with his brothers. They took him a long distance and were determined to throw him to the bottom of a well. Then, We sent revelation to Joseph saying: You will inform them of this act of theirs at a time when they will not realize that it is you.",
  12016:
      "The brothers of Joseph came to their father in the evening, pretending to cry for him to believe their plot.",
  12017:
      "They said: O our father, we went racing with one another and shooting arrows, and we left Joseph to look after our clothes and provisions. Then, a wolf ate him. Will you not believe us, even though we are truthful in what we are saying?",
  12018:
      "They confirmed their story with false evidence. They brought the shirt of Joseph stained with the blood of something else, giving the impression that it was a sign that a wolf had eaten him. Jacob realized that they were lying because the shirt was not torn, and he told them: The matter is not as you have said. Instead, your souls have made an evil action you committed fair-seeming. Therefore, I will exercise beautiful patience without any complaint. Allah is the One from Whom aid is requested against what you mention about Joseph.",
  12019:
      "A passing caravan came by, and they sent someone to draw water for them. He lowered his bucket into the well, and Joseph caught hold of the rope. When the person who had lowered the bucket saw him, he happily said: Good news! Here is a boy! The water drawer and a few others hid him from the rest of the caravan, regarding him as merchandise they could trade. Allah knew what they were doing with Joseph when they treated him as an item of sale. No action of theirs was hidden from Him.",
  12020:
      "The water drawer and his companions sold him in Egypt for an insignificant amount of a few silver coins that could be easily counted due to the small quantity. They sold him cheaply because they wanted to get rid of him quickly. Moreover, they realized from his condition that he was not a slave, and they were afraid of his family. Therefore, Allah was Merciful to him by not keeping him with them for very long.",
  12021:
      "The man from Egypt who had purchased him said to his wife: Be good to him and look after him well. He may benefit us by doing what we need, or we may adopt him as a child. Just as We saved Joseph from being killed, removed him from the well, and made the minister's heart soft towards him, We established him in Egypt to teach him the interpretation of dreams. Allah is in complete control of His affair, and His affair will come into effect. No one can compel Him; may He be Exalted, but most people, who are disbelievers, do not know that.",
  12022:
      "When Joseph reached the height of his spiritual and physical strength, We gave him understanding and knowledge. Just as We gave him this reward, We reward those who do good by worshipping Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses explain the seriousness of envy, which caused the brothers of Joseph to plot against him and conspire to kill him.\n2. The sacred law allows acting on clues when trying to establish a legal case.\n3. In the story of Joseph (peace be upon him), despite all the odds Allah’s plan for him prevailed, and He gave Joseph authority and power and taught him the interpretation of dreams.",
  12023:
      "The minister's wife tried to seduce Joseph (peace be upon him) by tricking him into committing an indecent act. She shut the doors tight to ensure they were alone and said to him: Come towards me! Joseph said: I seek protection in Allah from what you are calling me to. My master has cared for me during my stay here, and I will never betray him. If I betray him, I will be a wrongdoer, and those who do wrong do not succeed.",
  12024:
      "She had desired to commit the indecent act, and the same thing would have crossed his mind. Had he not seen Allah's signs, he would not have been prevented from the act or distanced himself from it. We showed him Our proof to keep him pure from evil and distance him from unlawful sexual relations and betrayal. Joseph was one of Our slaves whom We chose for [conveying] the message and prophethood.",
  12025:
      "They raced for the door: Joseph to save himself, and she to prevent him from leaving. She caught hold of his shirt to stop him from leaving and tore it from behind. At the door, they found her husband. The minister's wife deceptively said to him: Is not the punishment for the person who intended to commit an indecent act with your wife, O minister, prison, or that he be given a painful punishment?",
  12026:
      "Joseph (peace be upon him) said: It was she who tried to get me to commit an indecent act. I did not intend it from her. Allah then made a child from her family speak in the cradle. It testified, saying: If Joseph's shirt is torn from the front, then it indicates that she is truthful because she was trying to stop him from coming on to her, and then he will be lying.",
  12027:
      "But if his shirt is torn from behind, that indicates that he is truthful because she was trying to seduce him while he was running away, and she will be lying.",
  12028:
      "When the minister saw that Joseph's shirt was torn from behind, he realized Joseph was telling the truth. So he said: This accusation you cast on him is part of your deceit, O women. Your deception is undoubtedly strong.",
  12029:
      "He told Joseph: O Joseph, ignore this issue and do not mention it to anyone. And you, woman, ask forgiveness for your sin, for you committed a sin by trying to seduce Joseph.",
  12030:
      "The news spread in the city, and a group of women disapprovingly said: The minister's wife is trying to seduce her slave. Passion for him has penetrated her heart. Therefore, we think she is misguided in her effort to seduce and have an intense desire for him while he is her slave; this is a clear error [of judgment].\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. In certain instances, the schemes of women can be great.\n2. It is evil to betray someone who does good to you with respect to his family and wealth. This was what Joseph mentioned as one of the reasons for his refusal to commit the indecent act.\n3. The verses show that prophets are innocent and that Allah has protected them from falling into evil and indecency.\n4. It is necessary to push away indecency and run away to rid oneself of it.\n5. The sacred law allows people to defend themselves against an unjust accusation.\n6. The sacred law can be established by using indications of fact.",
  12031:
      "When the minister's wife heard of their disapproval and gossip about her, she invited them to come and see Joseph so that they would excuse her. She prepared for them a place with cushions and pillows and gave each one of the women a knife to cut food. She then told Joseph (peace be upon him): Go out to them! When they saw him, they were taken aback by his beauty and stunned by his handsomeness. As a result, they cut their hands with knives meant for cutting food and said: Allah is free of faults! This boy is not human. The beauty he possesses is not found in human beings. He can only be one of the noble angels.",
  12032:
      "The minister's wife said to those women when she saw what happened to them: This is the slave whom you blamed me for loving. I desired and tried to entice him, but he remained pure and refused. If he does not, in the future, do what I desire, he will go to prison and will become one of those who are disgraced.",
  12033:
      "Joseph (peace be upon him) supplicated to his Lord, saying: O my Lord, prison, which they threaten me with, is preferable to me than the shameful act they call me towards. But, if You do not remove their scheme from me, I may incline to them, and I will become one of the ignorant ones if I give in to them and do what they want me to do.",
  12034:
      "Allah answered his supplication and revealed the scheme of the minister's wife and the city's women. He (may He be Exalted) is Omniscient of Joseph's supplication and the supplication of any who call upon Him. He is Omniscient of Joseph's condition and anyone else.",
  12035:
      "Then, the view of the minister and his people, after they had seen evidence of his innocence, was that they should put him in prison for an unknown period so that the scandal would not be exposed.",
  12036:
      "They put him in prison, and two youths entered with him. One of these youths told Joseph: I saw in my dream that I was pressing grapes to make wine.The other said: I saw that I was carrying bread on my head, from which birds were eating. Tell us, O Joseph, what is the interpretation of what we saw? We regard you as one of those who do good, so be good to us by interpreting our dreams.",
  12037:
      "Joseph (peace be upon him) said: No food allocated to you by the king or anyone else will come to you, except that I will explain its essence and form before it arrives. The interpretation I give you is what my Lord has taught me. It is not soothsaying or astrology. I have left the religion of a people who do not have faith in Allah and denounce the Afterlife.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses show the beauty of Joseph (peace be upon him), which was the reason for the women becoming infatuated with him.\n2. Joseph (peace be upon him) gave preference to prison over going against Allah.\n3. The interpretation of dreams was one of the gifts that Allah gave Joseph (peace be upon him).",
  12038:
      "I follow the path of my fathers, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob: worshipping Allah alone. It is wrong for us to associate anything with Allah, Who is alone in His Oneness. The monotheism and belief that I and my fathers are upon is from the grace of Allah upon us. It was also from the grace of Allah upon all people since He sent the prophets to them with that message. Yet, most people are not thankful to Allah and are ungrateful for His blessings; instead, they disbelieve in Him.",
  12039:
      "Joseph then addressed the two men in the prison: Is worshipping many gods better or worshipping Allah, the One, Who has no partner, the Prevailing over all else, Whom none can prevail over?",
  12040:
      "What you worship besides Allah are names you made up, which you and your ancestors named as gods, while they have no share in divinity, and Allah did not designate or send any proof showing that these names are correct. The command in all creation is Allah's alone and does not belong to these names, which you and your ancestors had come up with. Allah (may He be Exalted) has instructed that you worship Him alone and has forbidden you to associate others with Him. Worshipping Allah alone is the straight path, which has no deviation in it. Most people do not know this; therefore, they associate other things with Allah, worshipping some of what Allah has created.",
  12041:
      "Joseph told his two companions in prison that he would interpret their dreams for them. He told them that the one who dreamed he was pressing grapes to make wine would get out of prison, return to work, and serve the king. As for the one who dreamt that he was carrying bread on his head that the birds were eating from, he would be killed and crucified, and the birds would eat from his head. The matter they asked for an opinion on was settled and would come to pass. It was an inevitable reality.",
  12042:
      "Joseph asked the one he thought would be saved of the two, the wine bearer of the king: mention my story and situation to the king so that he might release me from prison. But unfortunately, the Devil made the man forget to mention Joseph to the king, so he was imprisoned for several years afterward.",
  12043:
      "One day, the king said: I had a dream in which I saw seven fat cows being eaten by seven thin ones, seven green ears of corn, and seven dry ears of corn. O chiefs and noble ones, tell me the meaning of this dream if you know how to interpret dreams.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. People must follow the path of Abraham: withdrawing from associating partners with Allah and people who do this.\n2. People must worship Allah alone, because only He possesses the right to command.\n3. All the Allahs which are worshipped with Allah are only names for things that people have made-up without permission from Allah, and which have no share in divinity.\n4. People must take advantage of every opportunity to call others to Allah, as Joseph (peace be upon him) did in prison.",
  12044:
      "They said: Your dream is a mixture of visions, and because of this, it can not be interpreted. We are not knowledgeable about interpreting such dreams.",
  12045:
      "The wine bearer, who was the one saved from the two men who had been imprisoned, then remembered Joseph (peace be upon him) after some time and that he was able to interpret dreams, so he said: I will tell you the interpretation of the king's vision after asking someone who knows how to interpret it. Send me. O King, to Joseph, so that he can interpret your dream.",
  12046:
      "When the man who had been saved reached Joseph, he asked: O Joseph, the truthful one, inform us of the interpretation of someone dreaming about seven fat cows being eaten by seven thin cows, and seven green ears of corn and seven dry ears of corn, so that I might return to the king and his entourage, and so they can know the interpretation of the king's dream and also know your virtue and rank.",
  12047:
      "Joseph explained this dream and said: plant well for seven consecutive years. And what you harvest in each of these seven years, you should leave in its ears so that it will not rot, except for the few grains you need to eat.",
  12048:
      "Then, after these seven fertile years in which they successfully grow food, seven barren years will come, when the people will eat all they had harvested in the fertile years, except for a little of what they had stored, which will be used as seeds for sowing.",
  12049:
      "Then after these years of drought, a year will come in which there will be rainfall, the crops will grow, and the people will press those things that need pressing, such as grapes, olives, and sugar cane.",
  12050:
      "When Joseph's explanation of his dream reached him, the king told his slaves: Release Joseph from prison and bring him to me. When the king's messenger came to Joseph, he told him to go back to his master, the king, and ask him about the story of the women who cut their hands so that his innocence would be made clear before he left the prison. Joseph said: My Lord knows how they tried to seduce me, as nothing is hidden from Him.",
  12051:
      "The king, addressing the women, asked what happened when they called Joseph through trickery. Was it to commit immorality with them? The women replied: Allah forbid that Yusuf be accused! By Allah, we do not know any evil from him! Then the wife of the minister confessed what she had done and said: Now the truth has become clear; I tried to seduce him, and he did not try to seduce me. He was truthful in claiming that he was innocent of what I had accused him of.",
  12052:
      "The wife of the minister said: This disclosure was so that Joseph would know through my confession that it was me who had tried to seduce him and that he was truthful and that I had not lied about him in his absence, as it had become clear to me from what had happened that Allah does not give success to those who lie and hatch plans.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Joseph had perfect knowledge of explaining dreams correctly.\n2. People should clear their name when wrongly accused of something, by using the facts to establish the truth.\n3. The merit of speaking the truth, even if it is against oneself, is highlighted in the confession of the minister’s wife.",
  12053:
      "The minister's wife continued speaking, saying, I am not free of blame for wanting evil, and I was not trying to justify myself; the human self often commands evil. This is because of its inclination towards what it desires and the difficulty of refraining from it, except for those souls whom Allah shows mercy, preventing their egos from commanding them to evil. Allah is Forgiving and Compassionate towards those of His slaves who repent to Him.",
  12054:
      "The king said when Joseph's innocence became evident and apparent to him: Bring him; I will make him exclusively for me. So they brought Joseph to him, and his knowledge and intellect became clear when Joseph spoke to him. So the king said to him: Verily you, O Joseph, from this day, you are someone of rank, status, and trust.",
  12055:
      "Joseph told the king: Put me in charge of maintaining the storehouses of wealth and provision in the land of Egypt, for I am a trustworthy guardian with knowledge and insight of what I take charge of.",
  12056:
      "Just as Allah proved Joseph's innocence and released him from prison, He also established him in Egypt so that he could go and live anywhere he wished. So likewise, Allah gives His mercy to whomever of His slaves He wills in this world and does not allow the reward of those who do good to be lost, giving it to them in total and nothing less.",
  12057:
      "Allah's reward, which He has prepared in the hereafter, is undoubtedly better than the reward of this worldly life for those who have faith in Allah and who take heed of Him, following what He has commanded and refraining from what He has prohibited.",
  12058:
      "The brothers of Joseph came to Egypt with their merchandise and entered upon him. He recognized that they were his brothers, but they did not realize that he was their brother. This was because of the time that had passed and how much his appearance had changed. After all, he was only a boy when they threw him in the well.",
  12059:
      "When Joseph had given them the supplies and provisions they asked for, and after they had informed him that they had a brother on their paternal side who they had left behind with their father, Joseph asked them to bring their brother on their paternal side and that he, in return, would give them an extra camel-load of supplies. He asked them if they had yet to see that he had given them full measure, not subtracting from it, and that he was the best of hosts.",
  12060:
      "If you do not bring the brother I asked for, you will be clearly lying about your claim that you have a paternal brother. Therefore, I will not give you a measure of provision and do not come close to my country.",
  12061:
      "So his brothers answered him, saying, we will request him from his father and strive to do so. We will do what you commanded of us without fail.",
  12062:
      "Joseph told his slaves to return the merchandise of those people so that they would realize on their return that they did not do trade with it; this would force them to return with their brother to prove their honesty to Joseph so that he would receive their merchandise from them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The ego is an enemy to the believer, so you must watch it carefully, correcting its deviation.\n2. Being humble and admitting disobedience and shortcomings when they occur are some of the most beautiful qualities of good conduct.\n3. The story highlights the state of knowledge and trustworthiness that someone who is given a position serving the general good should have.\n4. Allah the Exalted sends a great bounty and His abundant blessings in this world and the Afterlife upon those who do good and who are patient.\n5. It is emphasised in the verses that the bounty of Allah in the Afterlife is much better and more lasting for the people of faith than the blessings of this world.\n6. It is permissible for a man to ask for a position and to praise himself if there is a need, in order to do good and put things right.",
  12063:
      "When they returned to their father and told him about the generosity of Joseph to them, they said, O father, the measure of merchandise had been denied to us unless you send our brother with us, so send him with us. If you send him with us, we will be given a measure of provision; we take an oath to you to protect and return him safely.",
  12064:
      "Their father responded: Should I entrust you with him except as I entrusted you with Joseph's full brother before? For I had entrusted you with keeping him safe, and you swore to protect him, yet you did not fulfill your oath. I have no confidence in your oath to protect him. Rather, my confidence is in Allah, for He is the best Guardian for those He wants to guard, and He is the Most Merciful to whom He wants to have mercy on.",
  12065:
      "And when they opened the baggage containing the food they had brought, they found what they had used to pay for it was also returned to them. So they told their father, what more can we ask of this minister [Joseph] after all of this generosity? The minister returned the price we used to pay for the provision as a show of generosity. So we will get food for our family, protect our brother from what you had feared might happen to him, and get an extra camel-load of merchandise because of our brother accompanying us; after all, an extra camel-load is an easy matter for the minister.",
  12066:
      "Their father told them: I will not send him with you until you swear an oath by Allah promising to bring him back to me lest you be surrounded by a source of destruction that will encompass you all such that none of you remain and nor can you repel or return from it. So when they gave him the oath of Allah on their promise, he [Jacob] said: Allah is a witness over what we say. His witnessing is sufficient for us.",
  12067:
      "And their father advised them saying, do not enter Egypt from one gate all together, but enter from different gates. This would be safer in terms of someone harming all of you if they wished to do so. I do not tell you this to repel harm from you that Allah may have willed for you nor to gain you benefit that Allah had not willed. The decree is none but the decree of Allah, and the matter is none but by His command; upon Him alone I rely in all my affairs, and upon Him alone may the people rely on in their affairs.",
  12068:
      "So they journeyed with Joseph's full brother. When they entered through different gates, as their father had instructed them, it did not stop what Allah had decreed for them in any way. Instead, it was to show Jacob's compassion for his children. He advised them, knowing that the decree is for none but Allah alone. He knew what Allah had taught him regarding faith in the divine decree and taking precautions, but most people do not know this.",
  12069:
      "When the brothers of Joseph came before him, together with his full brother, he drew his full brother close to him. He said to him privately that he was his brother Joseph and he should not feel sad about the reckless behavior of his other brothers, hurting and resenting the two of them and throwing Joseph in the well.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. People are instructed to take precaution and care against those who have betrayed someone - the believer is not stung from the same hole twice.\n2. One of the elements of taking precaution is obtaining a firm promise with an oath from someone. Also, it is permissible to take an oath when fearful about whether another person will keep trusts and promises.\n3. A person is allowed to ask someone to make a promise, except for conditions that would be beyond the power of the person making the promise.\n4. Taking appropriate measures includes taking precautions against things that bring about ruin.",
  12070:
      "So when Joseph instructed his slaves to load his brothers' camels with food, he placed the king's golden measuring bowl to measure out provisions into the bag of his full brother without their knowledge; this was to get his brother to stay with him. When they set out to travel back to their family, a caller called out after them, saying, O owners of the camels loaded with provision, you are thieves.",
  12071:
      "Joseph's brothers turned towards the caller and those with him and asked, what has gone missing so that you would accuse us of stealing?",
  12072:
      "The caller and those with him told Joseph's brothers: The king's golden measuring bowl used to measure provision has gone missing, and whoever produces it before we search will get a reward, a camel load. I am a guarantor for that.",
  12073:
      "Joseph's brothers answered him, saying: By Allah, as you have seen our situation, you know of our integrity and our innocence of this crime. And we have not come to the land of Egypt to be corrupt therein, and we have never in our lives been thieves.",
  12074:
      "The caller and those with him asked, then what is the punishment of theft among you if you are proven to be liars in your claim of innocence?",
  12075:
      "Joseph's brothers said: The punishment for any thief among us is that if the stolen item is found in his bag, he will be surrendered to the person he stole from and made to become his slave. To be made a slave is how we punish thieves.",
  12076:
      "So they returned them to Joseph to search their bags. To conceal Joseph's plot, he started by searching the bags of his half-brothers before the bag of his full brother. He then searched the bag of his full brother and retrieved the king's golden measuring bowl from it. As Allah planned things for Joseph by arranging to have the bowl placed into the bag of his brother, He also arranged – for the benefit of Joseph – that his brothers would be given the punishment of their country, which was the enslavement of the thief. This would not have been achieved if it had been according to the king's punishment for thieves: beating and fining. Therefore, except by the will of Allah, another arrangement had been achieved, and He is able to achieve it; We raise in rank whom We will of Our slaves as We have raised the status of Joseph. And above every possessor of knowledge is someone more knowledgeable, and above the knowledge of everyone is the knowledge of Allah, Who knows all things.",
  12077:
      "The brothers of Joseph said: If he stole, then it is not surprising, for his full-brother -meaning Joseph (peace be upon him- had stolen even before him. Joseph concealed his hurt at what they said. He said to himself: In this circumstance, what you have preceded in wrongdoing and envy is in and of itself evil. Allah the Exalted knows this defamation you have committed.",
  12078:
      "Joseph's brothers addressed him, O minister, he has an elderly father who is of the utmost age, who loves him very much; take one of us instead of him; we see that you are a doer of good in how you have treated us and how you have treated other than us, be good to us in that.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A trick which makes the truth apparent is permissible, as long as it does not harm others.\n2. It is permissible for someone who is searching for something, or who has lost something, to offer a reward, specifying its worth and description for whoever helps them to return it.",
  12079:
      "Joseph (peace be upon him) said, we seek refuge in Allah that we may take an innocent soul, and we leave the one whom we found the king's measuring bowl in his bag. If we were to do this, we would be wrongdoers, for we have punished an innocent soul and let a guilty one go free.",
  12080:
      "When they despaired of Joseph responding to their request, they isolated themselves from the people to consult each other. Finally, their eldest brother said, I remind you that your father had taken a firm oath affirming that you will return his son to him, except that you be overwhelmed with something you cannot repel. He reminded them also, and before this, your neglect of Joseph, you never fulfilled your oath to your father in it. Therefore, I will not leave the land of Egypt until my father permits me to return to him or Allah decrees that I take my brother back, for Allah is the Best of Judges, judging with truth and justice.",
  12081:
      "The eldest brother said, return to your father, and tell him that his son had stolen, and the minister of Egypt has taken him as a slave as a punishment for his theft, and we only relate to you what we have knowingly witnessed; the golden measuring bowl was retrieved from his bag, we had no knowledge that he had stolen if we had known, we would have never taken an oath to return him.",
  12082:
      "To confirm we are telling the truth, ask - O our Father - the people of Egypt where we were, and ask the caravan that we came with; they will inform you what we have informed you; we are telling the truth in what we have informed you of his theft.",
  12083:
      "Their father said: The matter is not how you describe it in that he had stolen; instead, your evil-inclined selves led you to plot against him just as you plotted before against his brother Joseph. My patience is a beautiful patience; there is no complaint in it except to Allah. Perhaps Allah will return them all to me: Joseph, his full brother, and their eldest brother. He, the Exalted, is Omniscient of my condition and All-Wise in managing my affair.",
  12084:
      "He turned away from them and said: O, my dire sorrow over Joseph. The blackness of his eyes became whitened from how much he cried over him. He was filled with sadness and worry but hid his sadness from the people.",
  12085:
      "Joseph's brothers told their father, by Allah, you continue - O our father - remembering Joseph, grieving over him, until sickness will overtake you or you will die outright.",
  12086:
      "Their father told them: I only complain about the grief and worry I've been afflicted with to Allah alone. And I know of Allah's gentleness, His kindness, His response to those in need, and His reward to those afflicted more than any of you will ever know.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is not permissible to take an innocent person for the crime of someone else. Another person cannot take the place of the criminal.\n2. Patience that is of a beautiful type is one where complaints are directed to Allah alone.\n3. The believer should have absolute certainty that Allah will release him from his distress.",
  12087:
      "Their father told them: O my sons, go and find out news of Joseph and his brother, and do not despair that Allah may alleviate and bring relief to His slaves. Indeed, no one despairs from receiving relief and alleviation from Allah except disbelieving people, for they are ignorant of His Ability and Favor upon His slaves.",
  12088:
      "So they followed their father's command and went out searching for Joseph and his brother. When they entered upon Joseph, they told him, great poverty and hardship have afflicted us, and we have come with poor and inferior goods, so weigh us out a sufficient measure as you had done for us before; be charitable to us by increasing our measure or by overlooking our poor merchandise. Indeed, Allah rewards those who are charitable with the best rewards.",
  12089:
      "So when he heard their words, he felt kind to them as a mercy to them, and he made himself known to them, telling them, you know what you had done with Joseph and his brother when you were ignorant of the consequences of what you did to them!",
  12090:
      "So they were surprised and asked if he was Joseph. He told them: Yes, I am Joseph, and this person you see with me is my full brother; Allah has favored us by saving us from our situation and raising our rank. For whoever fears Allah by fulfilling His commands, avoiding His prohibitions, and being patient with tribulation, that person's actions are righteous. Allah does not allow the rewards of those who do good to be lost; rather, He preserves them for them.",
  12091:
      "His brothers, apologizing for what they had done to him, said, by Allah, Allah has favored you over us by what He has given you of the traits of perfection. We were wrong and oppressive in what we did to you.",
  12092:
      "So Joseph accepted their apology and said today, no blame on you necessitates your punishment or rebuke. I ask Allah to forgive you; He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.",
  12093:
      "So Joseph gave them his shirt when they informed him of what had happened to his father's eyesight and said: Lay this on my father's face, and his eyesight will be restored, and bring all of your family back to me.",
  12094:
      "And when the caravan set out of Egypt and left the inhabited area, Jacob (peace be upon him) said to his sons and those who lived with him: I smell the scent of Joseph, although you might make me out to be a fool and consider me senile, by saying: he is a senile old man, he does not know what he is saying.",
  12095:
      "Those with him of his sons said, by Allah, you are still in a state of your previous delusion concerning Joseph's importance to you and the possibility of seeing him again.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A person is to take all appropriate measures to achieve what is desired, trusting in Allah, and not despairing of His mercy.\n2. It shows good character when a wrongdoer apologises for their sins, confessing against themselves, and asks for forgiveness from those they have harmed.\n3. The one who asks for forgiveness from Allah is the one who truly apologises.\n4. A person should accept the apology of the wrongdoer and not seek revenge, especially when it is possible to do so, and not criticise someone for what happened in the past.",
  12096:
      "So when the person bearing good news for Jacob came, he laid Joseph's shirt on his face, and he could see again. At that moment, he told his sons: Did I not tell you that I know of Allah's Gentleness and Kindness that which you know not?",
  12097:
      "His sons said, apologizing to their father Jacob, peace be upon him for what they did to Joseph and his brother: O father, seek forgiveness from Allah for our previous sins. We were sinners and wrongdoers for what we did to Joseph and his brother.",
  12098:
      "Their father told them: I will seek forgiveness from my Lord for you. He is the One who forgives the sins of those who repent among His slaves. He is Merciful to them.",
  12099:
      "Jacob and his family set out from their land, intending to Joseph in Egypt. When they entered upon him, he embraced his mother and father closely and told his brothers: Enter Egypt by Allah's will safely; nothing will harm you.",
  12100:
      "He had his parents sit on the throne he would sit at, and his parents and eleven brothers greeted him by prostrating to him. This prostration was done to honor and not for worship; this was the realization of the dream as decreed by Allah, which is why Yusuf said to his father, this greeting with prostration to me is the explanation of the dream that I saw and narrated to you before. My Lord has made it a reality through its occurrence. My Lord bestowed grace upon me when He took me out of prison and brought you all from the desert after the Devil spoiled things between my brothers and me. Indeed my Lord is delicate in managing what He wills to occur, Omniscient regarding the conditions of His slaves, All-Wise in His management.",
  12101:
      "Then Joseph invoked his Lord, saying, O Lord, You have given me something of the sovereignty of Egypt, and You have taught me something of dream interpretations, O Creator and Innovator of the heavens and the earth like nothing that came before them, You are the protector of my affairs in this worldly life, and You are the protector of all of my affairs in the hereafter, take my soul as a Muslim at the end of my life, and join me with the prophets and the pious from my father and others in Al-Firdaws, the highest garden of Paradise.",
  12102:
      "That which was mentioned from the story of Joseph and his brothers in what We revealed to you, O Messenger, you did not know of it, as you were not present with the brothers of Joseph when they decided to throw him in the bottom of the well and conceived what they did of their plot. Rather, We revealed that to you.",
  12103:
      "And most people are not believers, even if you strive, O Messenger, very hard that they believe, so do not lose yourself in grief over them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is desirable to give good news, because it brings joy to the heart of the Muslim.\n2. Devotion to parents, by respecting and honouring them, is a duty.\n3. The explanation of a dream may take place many years after it was dreamt.\n4. People are warned against the whisperings of Satan and whoever tries to create a division between those who are close to each other.\n5. No matter how well someone may be raised in their spiritual or worldly life, their success all goes back to the grace and blessings of Allah upon them.\n6. A person is to ask Allah for a good end, safety and success on the Day of Judgement and to join the company of the righteous in Paradise.",
  12104:
      "If they had any sense, they would believe in you because you did not - O Messenger - ask of them any reward for the Quran nor for what you call them to. The Quran is only a reminder for all the people.",
  12105:
      "And many signs that are evidence of His Oneness, Exalted is He, are transmitted in the heavens and the earth. The disbelievers pass by them, yet they turn away from contemplating and considering them. They pay no attention to them.",
  12106:
      "And most people do not believe that Allah is the Creator, the Sustainer, the Giver of Life, or the Causer of Death, except that they worship alongside Him idols and false deities, and they claim that He has a son, far Exalted is He.",
  12107:
      "Do the polytheists feel safe from a punishment in this world enveloping and overwhelming them so that they cannot repel it, or from the Hour coming to them suddenly, when they are unaware so they might prepare for it? Is it because of this that they do not believe?",
  12108:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those whom you call [unto the way of Allah]: This is my path, which I invite people to follow based on clear evidence; I call to this path, and so do those who follow me. Adhere to my guidance and follow my Sunnah (way). Exalted be Allah in His Perfection from the falsehoods attributed to Him that do not befit His Majesty, or contradict His Perfection, for I am not among the polytheists who ascribe partners to Allah the Exalted, but rather a monotheist who worships Him alone.",
  12109:
      "And We have not sent before you - O Messenger- except men, in human form, not angels. We reveal to them as We have revealed to you from the people of the towns and not from the people of the deserts; their people denied them, so We destroyed them. Therefore, will not those who reject you walk the earth, contemplate the result of those deniers before them, and thus be admonished? And what is in the abode of the hereafter from bliss is better for those who fear Allah in this worldly life. Do you not realize that it is better so you would fear Allah and fulfill His commands - the greatest of which is belief - and avoid His Prohibitions, the greatest of which is associating partners with Allah?",
  12110:
      "We give respite to the enemies of those Messengers We send; We lure them gradually by not bringing their punishment on quickly. So when their destruction is overdue, and the messengers feel the despair of it, and the disbelievers think that the promise of doom and salvation for the believers was nothing but a lie, Our aid comes to Our Messengers. We save the Messengers and the believers from the destruction that befalls the deniers. Our punishment is never turned away from criminal people when We bring it down on them.",
  12111:
      "The stories of the Messengers and their people, as in the story of Joseph and his brothers, are lessons that people of sound minds can learn from. The Quran, which contains this, is not made up words and fabrications against Allah. Rather, it affirms the heavenly scriptures sent down from Allah. It is a detailed explanation of everything that needs elaborating from the rulings and legislations, a guide to all good, and a mercy to a people believing in it; they are the ones that can truly benefit from what is in it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is not for a person, no matter how high his station is, to know the Ghaib of his own accord, as that is something that Allah makes particular to Himself.\n2. From Allah’s grace, He gives His prophets some knowledge of things in the Ghaib for particular ends and wisdom.\n3. The caller to truth is not able to change people’s hearts or to bring them to devotion, and most of the creation are not from the people of guidance.\n4. Criticism of those who turn away from the signs of Allah in creation and proofs spread throughout the universe that there is only one Allah.\n5. Verse 108 contains some of the pillars of calling people to the truth: the existence of a path; calling to Allah being based on knowledge, with insight; and there being people who are called to it.\n6. That the prophets and messengers were human and male, rather than female.\n7. One way of convincing people when calling to the truth is for them to reflect on what happened to those in the past, and leam from their stories, which the noble Qur’an mentions.\n8. The stories in the Qur’an are pure truth, not mixed with the impurities of fabrication or compilation, and the lies of the falsifiers do not enter into it.",
  13000:
      "The Thunder (Surah Ar-Ra'd)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nResponding to those who deny revelation and prophethood by enumerating the manifestations of Allah's greatness.\n•    Explanation:",
  13001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. These sublime verses in this surah (chapter) and the Quran that Allah has revealed upon you, O Messenger, is the absolute truth in which there is no uncertainty. There is no doubt that it is from Allah. However, most people do not believe in it out of stubbornness and arrogance.",
  13002:
      "Allah is the One who has created the heavens high without any support structures that you can see. He then ascended and rose above the Throne in an ascension befitting of His Majesty; Exalted is He, without modality or likening. He subjugated the sun and the moon for the benefit of His creation. Both the sun and the moon run along a specified period in the knowledge of Allah. He, the Exalted, disposes the affairs of the heavens and the earth as He wills. He makes clear the signs that are proof of His ability in the hope that you will be certain of meeting your Lord on the Day of Judgment so that you will prepare for it by righteous deeds.",
  13003:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One who spread out the earth and created on it firm mountains so that it does not cause the people to become unsettled. He made two kinds from all types of fruit, like male and female animals. He draws the veil of night over the day so that it becomes dark after being bright. In that which is mentioned, there are signs and proof for people who reflect and ponder over Allah's creation, for they are the ones who benefit from such signs and proof.",
  13004:
      "On Earth, there are plots close to one another; in them are gardens of vineyards, plants, and palms sharing one origin and other palms with different sources. These gardens, palms, and plants are irrigated with the same water. Yet, despite their proximity and irrigation with the same water, we make some of them better than others in taste and other benefits. In that are signs and proofs for a people of reckoning, for they are the ones who pay heed to it.",
  13005:
      "If you are amazed, O Messenger, at anything, then you should surely be amazed at their denial of resurrection and their statement of proof for their denial: And when we die and become dust and decayed and decomposed bones, shall we be resurrected and restored to life? Those who reject the resurrection after death are the ones who disbelieve in their Lord, and as a result, they deny His Power to resurrect the dead. They are the ones around whose necks chains of fire will be placed on the Day of Judgment. They will be the inhabitants of the Fire, and they will remain there forever, without ceasing to exist and without their punishment coming to an end.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is Almighty may He be glorified. How wondrous is the creation of the heavens, without any pillars that support them despite their huge and vast form.\n2. Allah is most Powerful and perfect in His lordship. He causes huge plants to grow out of small seeds, and despite nourishing them with the same water and sunlight, the fruits and crops vary in size, colours and taste.\n3. Allah’s extraction of huge trees from small seeds, after their being non-existent, contains a refutation of the idolaters who disbelieved in the resurrection. To re-assemble the parts of human remains that are scattered and decomposed into the earth and to once again resurrect them after they had once been in existence, is easier than extracting something non-existent from a seed.",
  13006:
      "The polytheists ask you, O Messenger, to bring on the punishment, and they enquire why it is taking so long to come on them before they enjoy entirely the favors Allah has decreed for them. Many such punishments had come before on people like them from the nations who disbelieved. Why do they not take a lesson from them? Your Lord, O Messenger, pardons people despite their wrongdoing. He, therefore, does not rush to take retribution from them, giving them a chance to repent to Allah. On the contrary, he severely punishes those who persist in denial if they do not repent.",
  13007:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah - persisting in their rejection and obstinance - say: Why has no sign been sent down to Muhammad from his Lord, just as was sent down to Moses and Jesus? You, O Messenger, are only a warner who warns people of Allah's punishment. You only have signs that Allah has given you. Every nation has a prophet who shows and guides them to the path of truth.",
  13008:
      "Allah knows what every female bears in her womb. He knows everything about it. He knows about any shrinking, swelling, health, or illness in the womb. By Him, Exalted is He; everything is determined with a measure that will neither decrease nor increase.",
  13009:
      "It is because He, the Exalted, knows about everything not perceived by His creation, as well as everything that they perceive. He is the Majestic in His Attributes, Names, and Actions; The Supreme above all His creation, by His Essence and Attributes.",
  13010:
      "He knows what is secret and what is even more hidden. Whether you, O people, hide your statements or proclaim them, it is the same in His knowledge. A person who hides from the eyes of people under the darkness of the night and one who acts openly in the light of day are equally known by Him.",
  13011:
      "He, the Exalted, has angels that are successive, one after another, upon humans. Some of them come at night, and some during the day. They encompass a person on all sides. Allah's command protects them from many decrees that Allah has written to be withheld from them. They record a person's statements and actions. Allah does not change the good condition of a people for the worse unless they change the state of gratitude within themselves. When Allah, Exalted is He, wills destruction for a people, no one can ward off what He wills. And you - O humanity - do not have anyone apart from Him who will take charge of your affairs and to whom you can resort to ward off the calamity that afflicts you.",
  13012:
      "He shows you, O humanity, the lightning, inspiring both fear of the lightning bolts and the hope of rain. It is He who forms heavy clouds laden with abundant rainwater.",
  13013:
      "The thunder exalts and praises for its Lord the Exalted. The angels exalt their Lord in awe of Him and out of reverence and honor of Him. He sends thunderbolts to strike and eliminate whichever of His creation He wills. Yet the disbelievers still dispute Allah's Oneness. Allah is mighty in power and strength. He does not will anything except that He does it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s immense forgiveness and tolerance of the wrongs of the children of Adam. They arrogantly challenge His messengers and prophets but despite that He provides for them, keeps them safe and overlooks their faults.\n2. The vastness of Allah’s knowledge of what it is in the darkness of the womb. He knows about the drop of sperm that comes into the womb, its then being formed into a male or female, its health and sickness, its sustenance and term and whether it is wretched or fortunate. His knowledge of it is full and comprehensive.\n3. Allah’s great care for the children of Adam and the presence of angels who guard and protect them such as the recording angels.\n4. Allah changes the condition of a person for the better when He sees him adopting the means of guidance. Being blessed lies in following the guidance of Allah’s words.\n5. Proof that thunder glorifies Allah, most High, may He be glorified.",
  13014:
      "The calling of Oneness is for Allah alone, and no one shares this with Him. The idols that the polytheists invoke besides Allah do not answer the invocations of those who call upon them in any matter at all. Their invocations to them are nothing more than a thirsty person stretching his hand to water to reach his mouth so that he may drink from it, yet the water will never reach his mouth. The supplications of the disbelievers to their idols are nothing but misguidance and a departure from correctness because they cannot bring benefit to them nor repel harm.",
  13015:
      "All in the heavens and on earth submit themselves in prostration to Allah alone. A believer and disbeliever are equal, except that a believer submits and prostrates to Him willingly. In contrast, a disbeliever unwillingly submits even though his natural disposition dictates that he should do so willingly. The shadow of every creature that has a shadow submits to Him at the beginning and the end of the day.",
  13016:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the disbelievers who worship others with Allah: Who is the Creator and the controller of the heavens and the Earth? Say, O Messenger, Allah is their Creator and Controller, and you acknowledge this. Say, O Messenger, to them: Have you taken for yourselves protectors other than Allah who are helpless! They cannot draw any benefit for themselves nor remove any harm. How, then, will they be able to do so for others? Say to them, O Messenger, is the disbeliever, who has no insight, equal to the believer who can see and is guided? And is disbelief, which is layers of darkness, equal to faith, which is light? Have the partners associated with Allah (may He be Exalted) created anything like Allah's creation so that their creation is distinguishable from His? Say to them, O Messenger, Allah alone is the Creator of all things. He has no partner in creation. He is the Only deity who solely deserves to be worshipped, and He is the One who is Dominant over everything.",
  13017:
      "Allah gives an example of the erosion of falsehood and the survival of truth with rainwater that comes down from the sky and causes riverbeds to flow, each according to its size, whether big or small. The overflowing water carries surface scum and foam that rise above the water. He then gives another example of falsehood and truth with some of the metals that people put into a furnace to melt them down and make ornaments for people. Falsehood is like the scum and foam that floats above the water and the slag expelled by smelting the metal. Truth is like the pure water that can be drunk, which causes fruits, grass, and vegetation to grow, and like the metal that remains after smelting, which benefits people. Just as Allah has given these two examples, He gives many examples to people so that truth may be distinguished from falsehood.",
  13018:
      "Those believers who responded to their Lord when he called them towards His Oneness and obedience will have the best reward, which is Paradise. But those disbelievers who did not respond to His call towards His Oneness and obedience, even if they possessed all the different types of wealth on earth and twice as much, would offer all that to ransom themselves from the punishment. Those who did not respond to His call will be taken to account for all their wrong deeds, and the home in which they will reside will be Hell— What a miserable abode the Fire is to rest and settle in.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Description of the deviation of the idolaters in their calling on other than Allah for assistance. Resemblance of their condition to that of a person who wants to drink but stretches his hands towards the water without getting any. He cannot drink in this manner, as he did not adopt the proper means for doing so.\n2. One of the methods of explanation used in the Qur’an is: Proverbs, which is to liken something abstract to something tangible and to give a mental image that helps one understand the meaning.\n3. All things in existence submit and prostrate to Allah, willingly or unwillingly, because submission to Him, may He be glorified, is something dictated by natural disposition.",
  13019:
      "The one who knows what Allah has revealed to you, O Messenger, which is undoubtedly the Truth from your Lord, who has faith in and responds to Allah, cannot be equal to someone who is blind, disbelieves in Allah, and does not respond to Him. Only those with sound understanding will pay heed to and take a lesson from this.",
  13020:
      "Those who respond to Allah are the ones who fulfill the pledges they made to Allah or the commitments they made to His slaves. They are the ones that do not break their covenants with Allah or others.",
  13021:
      "They are the ones who maintain everything that Allah commanded them to maintain, like keeping the ties of kinship. They are in awe of Allah, inspiring them to fulfill His commands and avoid His prohibitions. They fear Allah will hold them accountable for what they have done in sin, for any person scrutinized in their reckoning will perish.",
  13022:
      "They remained steadfast in obeying Allah and in what Allah decreed upon them of hardship and ease. And they remained firm in refraining from sinning against Him, thus seeking His pleasure. They kept up the prayer perfectly, discharged their obligations from the wealth that We gave them, and willingly gave from that wealth, secretly to avoid ostentation and openly so that others could follow their example. They repel the evil of those who harm them by doing good to them. These people with these qualities will have a praiseworthy outcome on the Day of Judgment.",
  13023:
      "This praiseworthy outcome is gardens in which they will permanently reside in bliss. To complete the favor, those of their fathers, mothers, wives, and children who were upright will enter these gardens together to make their stay more enjoyable by meeting them. In addition, the angels will visit and congratulate them from every door of their homes in Paradise.",
  13024:
      "The angels will greet them whenever they visit them, saying: Peace be on you, i.e., You are safe from calamities because of your being steadfast in following Allah and in difficult times and being firm in not going against Him. What a wonderful final abode your outcome is!",
  13025:
      "Upon noting the characteristics of the believers, Allah mentions the traits of the disbelievers who turned away, stating: \n Those who break their pledge with Allah after it has been made binding and cut off the ties that Allah has commanded to keep are the unfortunate and wretched ones who will be distanced from Allah's mercy, and they will have a dreadful outcome in the Fire.",
  13026:
      "Allah expands provision for anyone He wills and restricts it for any of His slaves that He wills. Being given abundant provision is not a sign of being fortunate or having attained Allah's love. Similarly, restriction of provision is not a sign of being wretched. The disbelievers rejoiced in the life of this world and were inclined to it, becoming comfortable therein. Yet the life of this world, compared to the Hereafter, is only a brief enjoyment that will soon pass.",
  13027:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah and His verses say: If only a physical sign were sent down to Muhammad from his Lord proving his truthfulness, then we would believe. Say - O Messenger - to those who suggest this: Allah, through His justice, leaves whoever He will to go astray, and through His grace, He guides to Himself those who turn towards Him in repentance. Guidance is not in their hands, so they could link it to the sending down of signs.",
  13028:
      "These people whom Allah guides are those who have faith and whose hearts find comfort in the remembrance of Allah, in His exaltation, praise, and in reciting and listening to His Book. Indeed it is only natural that in the remembrance of Allah, hearts find comfort.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Knowledge is virtuous and those who possess it are not equal to those who do not.\n2. Encouragement towards a number of moral virtues that lead to Paradise, including: good relations, awe of Allah, fulfilment of pledges, patience, spending and repaying an evil deed with a good one.\n3. Warning against some attributes that result in being cursed and distanced from Allah’s mercy, including: breaking Allah’s pledge, cutting off what Allah has ordered to be joined and spreading corruption on earth.\n4. The keys to provisions are in Allah’s hands, may He be glorified. The expansion or restriction by Allah in the provision of a servant should not necessarily be a cause of joy or sorrow as it is not an indication of Allah’s pleasure or anger in respect of that servant.\n5. Guidance is not necessarily linked to the sending down of the signs and miracles requested by the idolaters.\n6. One of the effects of the Qur’an on the believing servant is that it brings about tranquility in the heart.",
  13029:
      "These people who have faith in Allah and do righteous deeds that bring them closer to Allah will have a pleasant life in the Afterlife and a beautiful outcome in Paradise.",
  13030:
      "Just as we sent previous messengers to their nations, We sent you - O Messenger -to your nation so that you may recite the Quran We revealed. It is sufficient proof for your truthfulness, yet the condition of your people is that they reject this miracle because they deny the Benevolent One as they associate others with Him as partners. Say, O Messenger, The Benevolent One, with whom you associate others as partners, He is my Lord; no one deserves to be worshipped but He; in Him, I put my trust for all my affairs, and to Him, I turn in repentance.",
  13031:
      "If any of the divine scriptures had the quality of being able to make the mountains move from their places or the earth split and turn into rivers and springs, or be recited to the dead who would then come to life, it would have been this Quran that is revealed to you - O Messenger - for its evidence is clear. Its effect would be profound if only their hearts were mindful, but they rejected it. Instead, sending down miracles and other things is entirely in Allah's control. Do those who believe in Allah not know that if Allah willed to guide all the people together without sending down any miracles, He would have done so? But He did not will that. Those who reject Allah continue to be struck with a severe disaster that shakes them, or such disaster falls close to their homes until Allah's promise of endless punishment comes to pass. Allah does not fail to accomplish what He promised when the specified time for it comes.",
  13032:
      "You are not the first messenger to be rejected and mocked by his people. The nations before you - O Messenger - mocked and rejected their messengers. But I gave respite to those who rejected their messengers until they thought I would not destroy them. Then, I seized them after that respite, with various forms of punishment. Have you not seen My punishment of them? It was a severe wrath.",
  13033:
      "Is the One who watches over the actions of every soul and who recompenses it for its deeds more deserving of worship, or these idols who do not have that right? The disbelievers have unjustly and falsely made them partners to Allah. Say to them - O Messenger -: Tell us the names of the partners you worship with Allah if you are genuine in your claim. Or are you informing Allah of partners on earth that He does not know of? Or are you informing Him with a show of words that have no reality? Instead, the Devil has beautified the evil designs of the disbelievers. Whomever Allah misguides from the path of righteousness has no guidance to be guided by.",
  13034:
      "There is a punishment for them in this world in the form of being killed and imprisoned at the hands of the believers. Still, the punishment of the Hereafter that awaits them is heavily more severe than the punishment of this world because of its never-ending severity and continuity. They will have no one to protect them from Allah's punishment on the Day of Judgment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The main purpose of every revealed scripture is to provide guidance and not to bring down signs and miracles. These are in the control of Allah who decrees them when and how He wills.\n2. Allah consoles the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informs him that the denial that he is experiencing with the idolaters is not something new, but was faced by the previous prophets.",
  13035:
      "The description of Paradise for those mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions is that rivers flow under its trees and palaces. Its fruits are everlasting and never cease, unlike this world's fruit. Its shade lasts without ever retracting. That outcome awaits those mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. The outcome of the disbelievers is the Fire, which they will enter to remain there forever.",
  13036:
      "Those Jews to whom We gave the Torah and those Christians to whom We gave the Gospel, rejoice in what has been revealed to you - O Messenger - because it conforms to some of what was revealed to them; this is the condition of those who believe from the people of scripture. There are sects from among the Jews and Christians who deny parts of what has been revealed to you because it does not conform to their desires or it describes them as having altered or distorted their religion. Tell them - O Messenger - Allah has commanded me to worship Him alone; I do not associate any partners with Him. He alone I call upon, and I do not call anyone but Him. To Him alone is my return. This is what the Torah and Gospel came with.",
  13037:
      "Just as We sent down the previous scriptures in the language of their people, We have sent down to you, O Messenger, the Quran as a decisive word indicating the truth in the Arabic language. If you, O Messenger, follow the desires of the People of the Scripture, in their request to you to delete what does not conform to their desires, after you have received the knowledge that Allah has taught you, you will not have anyone to take charge of your affairs and to assist you against your enemies, and you will not have anyone to protect you from Allah's punishment.",
  13038:
      "And We have sent messengers before you, O Messenger, who were human, so you are not an innovation amongst the messengers. We gave them wives and children like other human beings. We did not make them angels who do not marry and have children. You are one of those messengers who is human, marries, and has children. So why are the polytheists surprised that you are that way? It is not befitting that a messenger comes up with a verse from himself except that Allah permits him to bring it forth. In every matter Allah has decreed, there is a book that mentions it and a prescribed time that is not delayed or prolonged.",
  13039:
      "Allah removes whatever good, evil, fortune, or misfortune He wills to remove and confirms whatever He wills. With Him is the Preserved Tablet, which is the source of all of that, and any erasure or confirmation that appears conforms to what is in it.",
  13040:
      "And if We were to show you - O Prophet - some of the punishment that We promise them before your death, then that is for Us. If We were to cause you to die before showing you that, then you only must convey what We have commanded you to convey. It is not your duty to recompense them or take them to account - that is for Us.",
  13041:
      "Have not the disbelievers seen that We come to the land of disbelief, diminishing it from its sides by spreading Islam and the Muslims conquering it? Allah judges and decrees whatever He wills amongst His slaves. No one reverses, amends, or alters His decision. He (may He be Exalted) is swift in the reckoning, and He will take the earlier people and the later ones to account within one day.",
  13042:
      "The previous nations had plotted and devised schemes against their prophets, and they rejected what they brought to them. What did they manage to do with such plots? Nothing! This is because the effective plan is only that of Allah and no other. May He be Exalted, is the One Who knows what their souls earn, and He will recompense them for it. Then they will know how wrong they were in not believing in Allah and how truthful the believers were as they would have acquired Paradise and the best outcome.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Arousing the desire for Paradise by giving its description of flowing rivers and perpetual provision and shade.\n2. Clarification that messengers are human beings, who have wives and offspring, and that our Prophet (peace be upon him) is nothing new among them. He is just like them in that aspect.",
  13043:
      "Those disbelieving say: O Muhammad - Allah has not sent you. Tell them - O Messenger- Allah is sufficient as a witness between you and me to the fact that I have been sent from my Lord to you. And those who know the heavenly scriptures that contain my description. The one for whom Allah is a witness to his truthfulness is not harmed by the rejection of those who deny Him.",
  14000:
      "Abraham (Surah Ibrahim)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming the messengers' duty to convey a clear message and warn of punishment for those who turn away from following them.\n•    Explanation:",
  14001:
      "Alif Lām Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. This Quran is a book that We revealed to you, O Messenger, so that you may remove people from disbelief, ignorance, and misguidance and bring them to faith, knowledge, and guidance (referring to the religion of Islam), which is the way of Allah, the Mighty whom no one can overpower, the One who deserves praise in everything.",
  14002:
      "Allah, to whom alone belongs whatever is in the heavens, and to whom alone belongs whatever is on Earth. He alone is the One who deserves to be worshipped and that nothing of His creation be associated as a partner to Him. Those who disbelieve in Allah will receive a severe punishment.",
  14003:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah prefer the life of the world and its temporary pleasures over the Afterlife with its eternal bliss. They turn people away from Allah's path and seek to distort it. Making it diverge from the truth and moving away from uprightness is so no one will tread it. Those described with such attributes are in error, far from the truth and righteousness.",
  14004:
      "We have not sent any messenger except that We sent him speaking his people's language so they could easily understand what he brought from Allah. We have not sent him to force them to believe in Allah. Allah causes misguidance to whoever He wills out of His justice and guides whoever He wills through His grace. He is the Mighty, whom no one can overpower, and the Wise in His creation and planning.",
  14005:
      "We have sent Moses and supported him with miracles indicating his truthfulness and that His Lord sent him. We commanded him to exit his people from disbelief and ignorance to belief and knowledge. We commanded him to remind them of the days of Allah in which He blessed them with His favors. Those days are clear signs of Allah's Oneness and His Great decrees and blessings upon the believers. This is something that will be of benefit to those who are steadfast in following Allah and who constantly show gratitude for His favors and approbations.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The function of the Qur’an and the purpose of its revelation is guidance - by removing people from the darkness of falsehood to the light of truth.\n2. Messengers are sent in the language of their people because this is more effective for their being understood, accepted and followed.\n3. The function of messengers are summarised in their guiding and leading people out of darkness to light.",
  14006:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Moses fulfilled the command of his Lord and said to his people, the Israelites, reminding them of Allah's blessings on them: O my people, remember Allah's favor on you when He saved you from the people of Pharaoh and gave you safety from their affliction. They were making you suffer greatly, killing your sons so that no one would be born amongst you to take over Pharaoh's kingdom, and letting your women live to humiliate and disgrace them. In their doing so was a great test of patience for you. Allah then rewarded you for your patience in this trial by saving you from the affliction of the people of Pharaoh.",
  14007:
      "And Moses told them: Remember when your Lord clearly announced to you: If you are grateful to Allah for the aforementioned favors that He has blessed you with, then He will give you more of His favor and grace. But, if you deny His blessings to you and do not show gratitude for them, His punishment is severe for those who reject His favors and are not grateful for them.",
  14008:
      "And Moses told his people: O my people: if you and all the people on earth reject the truth, then the harm of your rejection will only be on you. Allah is self-sufficient and deserving of praise by Himself. The faith of the believers does not benefit Him, and the denial of the disbelievers does not harm Him.",
  14009:
      "Has it not come to you - O disbelievers - the news of the demise of the denying nations before you? The people of Noah, the 'Ād, the people of Hūd, Thamūd - the people of Saleh - and the nations that came after them, which are so numerous that their actual number is known only to Allah? Their messengers came to them with clear signs as well as miracles. But they returned their hands to their mouths and bit their fingertips in rage against the messengers. Telling their messengers: We reject what you have been sent with. We have disturbing doubts about what you are calling us to.",
  14010:
      "Their messengers responded: Can there be any doubt about Allah's Oneness and about worshipping Him alone when He is the Creator of the heavens and the earth, who brought them into existence without any precedent? He calls you to believe in Him so that He can wipe clean your previous sins and defer you until you can complete your fixed period of life in your worldly lives. Their people said to them: You are only human like us. You have no merit over us. You want to turn us away from what our forefathers used to worship; bring forth clear proof indicating the truthfulness of your claim that you are messengers from Allah to us.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the means of calling towards Allah is to remind those addressed of Allah’s favours to them, especially if that is linked to a great favour such as victory over or salvation from an enemy.\n2. It is Allah’s grace that He promised His servants more favours in lieu of their gratitude. On the other hand. His threat is severe to those who reject Him.\n3. The rejection by His servants does not harm Allah at all, just as the faith of His servants does not benefit Him. He is self-sufficient and praiseworthy by His self.",
  14011:
      "In response, their messengers said: We are people like you, so we are not blaming you for imitating your forefathers in that respect. Just because you are people, it does not mean that you should imitate them in everything. Amongst His slaves, Allah bestows unique favors on whomever He wishes, so He will choose some to be messengers to humanity. We are forbidden to grant you whatever evidence you desire, except if Allah so chooses. It is not within our power to bring you such evidence; Allah alone is the One capable of doing so. Those who entrust all of their affairs to Allah will have trust in Him.",
  14012:
      "What sort of objection or excuse would cause us to cease trusting Him? He has guided us to the clearest and most upright path. We will be patient against the harm you caused by belying and mocking us. Those who trust Allah will entrust all of their affairs to Him alone.",
  14013:
      "When those who disbelieved in Allah, from amongst the people to whom the messengers were sent, could not respond to the messengers' arguments, they said: \"We will drive you out from our town, or you will have to reject your religion and return to ours.\" Allah then sent revelation to His messengers to strengthen them: \"We will surely destroy the wrongdoers who disbelieved in Allah and His Messengers.\"",
  14014:
      "And We will surely make you dwell - O Messengers and those who followed you - on the earth after the rejecting disbelievers' destruction. The believers and their messengers dwelling in the land after their demise is for those who reflect on My Majesty and observance of it and those who fear My warning of punishment.",
  14015:
      "The Messengers asked their Lord to make them victorious over their enemies. Every arrogant and stubborn person will lose as they did not follow it when it was made clear to them.",
  14016:
      "In front of this arrogant person on the Day of Judgment is Hell. It is lying in wait for him; he will be made to the puss that oozes from the people of the Fire. It does not quench his thirst. Instead, he will continue to be punished by being thirsty, among other forms of punishment.",
  14017:
      "He will feel burdened to drink it repeatedly because of how bitter, rancid, and hot it is. He will not be able to swallow it. Death overcomes him from all directions because of the severity of what he faces of torment. He will not be allowed to die to rest; he is kept alive, suffering the torture. In front of him is an even more extreme punishment awaiting him.",
  14018:
      "The parable of what the disbelievers put forth of righteous deeds such as charity, kindness, and mercy to the weak is like ash that the wind has taken hold of on a windy day. It is carried away by the wind and scattered all over the place till no trace of it remains. Likewise, the deeds of the disbelievers have been blown away by their disbelief. It will not benefit them on the Day of Judgment. Deeds not established on firm belief are nothing but misguidance far away from the path of truth.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Prophets and messengers are people of the children of Adam, except that Allah, the Exalted, honored them by causing them to carry the message, and He chose them for it from amongst the children of Adam.\n2. The preacher who wishes to instill change must expect that he will be confronted by difficulties, including verbal and physical actions of dismissal, denial, and harm.\n3. Preachers and righteous people are promised victory and vicegerency on earth.\n4. The horrible fate of the wrongdoers and enemies of the Messengers, and demonstrating the punishments that Allah has prepared for them in the afterlife.\n5. Showing how the deeds of the disbelievers will be rejected and not considered due to their disbelief.",
  14019:
      "Do you not know - O humanity - that Allah created the heavens and the earth with truth, and He did not create them in vain? If He so wills, He can remove you - O humanity - and bring forth a new creation that will worship and obey Him in your place. It is easy and effortless for Him.",
  14020:
      "Destroying and replacing you with a different creation is not difficult for Him; may He be Exalted. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  14021:
      "Creation emerged from their graves towards Allah on the Day of Appointment. The weak followers said to their eminent leaders: \"O masters, we were followers to you. We were commanded by your command and forbidden by your prohibition. Will you then protect us against any of Allah's punishments? The eminent leaders said: \"If Allah had directed us towards guidance, we would have ushered you towards it. Then, we would all have been saved from His punishment. However, we were misguided, and we led you astray. It is the same for both of us; whether we are too weak to bear the punishment or are patient, there is no escaping the punishment for us\".",
  14022:
      "When the people of Paradise entered Paradise, and the people of Hell entered Hell, Iblis said: \"Indeed Allah gave you a true promise, and he carried out his promise to you. I gave you a false promise, and I failed to fulfill my promise to you. And with whatever strength I had, I compelled you in the worldly life towards disbelief and misguidance. I invited you towards disbelief and made sins attractive to you, so you were quick to follow me. Do not blame me for what befell you of misguidance, but blame yourselves because you are more deserving of blame. I will not help you in averting your penalty, and you will not help me in averting my penalty. I denounce that you made me a partner with Allah in your worship. Those who do wrong by associating partners with Allah in the worldly life and disbelieving in Him have a painful penalty that awaits them on the Day of Judgment.",
  14023:
      "Upon mentioning the fate of the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection to instill fear, Allah mentions the fate of the believers as a source of motivation, stating: \n In contrast to the fate of the wrongdoers, Allah caused those who believed and did righteous deeds to enter Paradise with rivers flowing under its palaces and trees, dwelling therein eternally by the permission and power of their Lord. They greet one another, the angels greet them, and their Lord, exalted is He, greets them with peace.",
  14024:
      "O Messenger, do you not know how Allah drew a comparison for the statement of monotheism, \"There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah\"? He compared it to a good tree, the date palm; its trunk is firmly rooted in the earth, it drinks water with its good roots, and its branches reach out into the sky, drinking from the dew and inhaling good air.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Demonstrating the fate of the follower and the followed one when they both engage in wrongful acts.\n2. Demonstrating that Satan is the greatest enemy to the children of Adam, and that he is a liar, forsaken and weak. He will have no claim for himself nor his followers on the Day of Judgment.\n3. Iblis’s admission that the promise of Allah, the Exalted, is the truth, and that Satan’s promise is purely a lie.\n4. Likening the monotheistic phrase to a tree of sweet fruits, high branches and firm trunks.",
  14025:
      "This good tree gives forth its good fruit at all times by the command of its Lord. Allah, Exalted is He, draws parables for the people so that they may reflect.",
  14026:
      "And the parable of the word of wicked polytheism is like that of a wicked tree, the bitter apple; it is removed from its foundation without any firmness in the earth. It does not extend into the sky. It dies, and the wind scatters it. The word of disbelief is bound for ruin; its owner's good deeds will not ascend to Allah.",
  14027:
      "Allah keeps the believers steadfast through the firm word of monotheism, believing it in this worldly life and dying upon it. They are also made firm in their graves during the Transitory Stage. He keeps them firm on the Day of Resurrection. Allah causes the wrongdoers to go astray by associating partners with Him and their disbelief, which is far from the correct rationale. Allah does what he wills through His justice, from causing misguidance to whom He wills to misguide and guiding by His grace whom He wills to guide the Exalted.",
  14028:
      "You had seen the condition of the Quraysh, who disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger when they rejected Allah's favor of keeping them safe in the Noble Sanctuary and sending Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم to them. Their rejection was to show ingratitude to the blessing of Allah when they denied what the Messenger brought from his Lord. Thus, they have descended their followers into disbelief and to the abode of ruin.",
  14029:
      "The abode of ruin is entering Hell. They will suffer its heat, and the worst dwellings will be theirs.",
  14030:
      "The polytheists made idols and counterparts to Allah so that they would lead their followers away from Allah's path after they had been led away from it. O Messenger, say to them: Enjoy the desires you find yourselves in and the spreading of doubt in the worldly life. On the Day of Judgment, your return will be the Fire, and you will not have any other return except to it.",
  14031:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the believers, perfectly perform your prayers and spend in the way of your Lord from the provisions We have given you for both mandatory and voluntary charity. Spend secretly, fearing ostentation, and openly so others may take you as examples. Do this before a day comes to you in which there will be no trade or ransom to redeem yourselves from Allah's punishment. There will be no friendship so that a friend could intercede for another.",
  14032:
      "Allah has constructed the heavens and the earth in an unprecedented manner. He has brought down rain from the heavens, and by that water - O humanity - He has brought forth various crops as a sustenance for you. According to His decree, He has subjugated ships that float on the water for you. He has subjugated rivers from which you drink water and irrigate your crops and livestock.",
  14033:
      "He has subjugated the sun and the moon for you to run their course continuously. He has subjugated the night and the day that alternate. The night is for your sleep and rest, while the day is for striving and activity.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Comparing the word of disbelief to the crawling colocynth, which does not grow upwards, produce sweet fruit or endure.\n2. The link between commanding prayer and Zakat and mentioning the Hereafter is to convey the feeling that both prayer and charity lead to salvation in the afterlife.",
  14034:
      "He has granted you all that you have asked for and all that you have not asked for. If you were to count the blessings of Allah, you would not be able to enumerate them because of their plentitude and variety. What was mentioned to you were examples of them. People are oppressive to themselves and are very ungrateful for the blessings of Allah; Exalted is He.",
  14035:
      "And recall, O Messenger, when Abraham said, after relocating his son Ishmael and Ishmael's mother, Hajar, to the valley of Mecca: O Lord! Make this city, Mecca, where I have inhabited my family, a city of peace wherein no blood is shed and no person oppresses another. Distance myself and my children from the worship of idols.",
  14036:
      "O Lord! The idols misguided many people when they believed they would intercede for them. They were allured to the idols and worshipped them instead of Allah. Whoever follows me in claiming Allah as One and obeying Him, then he is among my party and followers. Whoever disobeys me and does not follow me in claiming Allah as One and obeying Him, then You, O Lord, are Forgiving of the sins of whomever You wish, and You are Merciful towards them.",
  14037:
      "O our Lord, I have placed some of my progeny, my son Ishmael and his children, in a valley (Mecca) with no crops or water beside your Sacred House. O our Lord, I have inhabited them next to it so that they will establish prayer in it, so incline compassionately - O Lord - people's hearts towards them, and to this city, and sustain them with crops in the hope that they will be grateful for Your blessings upon them.",
  14038:
      "O our Lord, You know all that we keep secret and make known. Nothing on Earth or in the heavens remains hidden from Allah. He knows of it, so our need and dependence on Him are not unknown to Him.",
  14039:
      "Thanks and praise to Allah, the Exalted, who answered my call to grant me from the righteous. So He has given me, in my old age, Ishmael from Hager and Isaac from Sarah. My Lord, the Exalted, hears the call of those who call on Him.",
  14040:
      "O Lord, make me able to perform my prayer perfectly and make my progeny do that. O Our Lord, answer my prayer and make it accepted by you.",
  14041:
      "O our Lord, forgive me my sins, and forgive the sins of my father (he said that before he knew that he was an enemy of Allah, and when it became clear to him that his father was Allah's enemy, he disavowed him). And forgive the sins of the believers on the day that humanity goes forth to be taken to account in front of their Lord.\"",
  14042:
      "O Messenger, do not think that if Allah delays the wrongdoers' punishment, He neglected their acts of lying, obstructing the path to Allah and other such deeds. Allah is aware of these things, and nothing remains hidden from Him. Indeed, Allah delays their punishment until the Day of Resurrection, when people's eyes stare in horror at the terror they will witness.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Signalling to the severity of disbelief of some of the Children of Adam despite the profuse favors Allah (the Exalted) has gifted them.\n2. Demonstrating the excellence of Makkah, which Allah’s prophet (peace be upon him), Ibrahim, supplicated for.\n3. Showing that it remains necessary for an individual, no matter how much his rank is elevated by doing what is asked of him and servitude, to continue fearing for himself and his descendants from falling into idolatry, whether its manifestation are significant or not.\n4. Ibrahim’s (peace be upon him) supplication indicates that a servant, no matter how much his rank is raised, remains dependent upon Allah, the Exalted, and in need of Him.\n5. One of the techniques of rearing: praying for the righteousness, correct belief and guidance of one’s children in upholding rites of the religion.",
  14043:
      "When people rise from their graves, hurrying towards the caller, their heads raised and anxiously gazing at the sky. Their gaze does not return to them but remains fixed because of the horror they witness. Their hearts are void and are unable to comprehend, and they have no sense of understanding due to the terror they witness.",
  14044:
      "And make your people fear, O Messenger, the torment of the Day of Resurrection. Those who wronged themselves by disbelieving in Allah and associating partners with Him will say: O Our Lord, give us respite, and delay our punishment. Return us to the world briefly so we may believe in You and follow the Messengers You sent us. They will be given a reprimanding response: Did you not swear, while you were on earth, that you would not be transferred from the world to the Afterlife, and you disbelieved in the resurrection after death?",
  14045:
      "You took residence in the living spaces of previous nations, who before you had wronged themselves by disbelieving in Allah, such as the nations of Hūd and Saleh. The destruction I caused to befall them was made clear to you. We also gave you examples in the book of Allah so that you would be warned, but you did not take them as a warning.",
  14046:
      "Those who took up residence in the living spaces of the wrongful nations arranged a plot to kill the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم and end his mission. Allah knows of their plans, and nothing remains hidden from Him. Their plan was weak, for it could not move the mountains or anything else, contrary to Allah's plan against them.",
  14047:
      "Do not think, O Messenger, that Allah, Who promised His messengers' victory and the establishment of the religion, has given up on His promise to His Messengers. Allah is Exalted in Might, and nothing defeats Him. He will strengthen and support His allies while reserving severe vengeance for His enemies and the enemies of His Messengers.",
  14048:
      "This revenge against the disbelievers will occur on the Day of Resurrection. On that day, this earth will be exchanged for a barren and dustless plain, and the skies will be exchanged for different skies. People will exit their graves with their bodies and deeds to stand before Allah, Who alone is the Possessor and Owner of Dominion and Majesty. He subdues and is never subdued, and He defeats and is never defeated.",
  14049:
      "On the day that the Earth will become a different Earth and the heavens will transform, you will see, O Messenger, the disbelievers and polytheists bound to each other in fetters. Their arms and legs will be chained to their necks. Their garments will be made from pitch (a highly flammable substance), and the fire will cover their grim faces.",
  14050:
      "On the day that the Earth will become a different Earth and the heavens will transform, you will see, O Messenger, the disbelievers and polytheists bound to each other in fetters. Their arms and legs will be chained to their necks. Their garments will be made from pitch (a highly flammable substance), and the fire will cover their grim faces.",
  14051:
      "Allah will recompense each soul for the good and evil it did. Allah is swift in recompensing deeds.",
  14052:
      "This Quran, which was revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, is a forewarning from Allah to humanity so that they may take heed of the warnings and severe threats found therein. So they may know that the One who is obeyed in truth is Allah alone, so they will worship Him and not associate any partners with Him. Also, those with sound intellects will be admonished and warned by it, as they are the ones who will benefit from admonitions and warnings.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Illustrating the scenes of the Day of Judgement, people’s grief, their fear, their weakness, their terror and the changing of the earth and the heavens.\n2. Describing the severity of the punishment and humiliation that will befall the people of disobedience and disbelief on the Day of Judgement.\n3. Indeed the servant has control over the affairs of his life in this world, so he ought to strive towards doing what is asked of him. Allah, the Exalted, will not grant him another opportunity when He resurrects him on the Day of Judgement.",
  15000:
      "The Rocky Tract (Surah Al-Hijr)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThreatening those who mock the Quran and promises to preserve it in a way that supports and validates the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.\n•    Explanation:",
  15001:
      "Alif Lām Rā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. These verses hold great significance, indicating they were revealed by Allah. They are verses of the Quran that clarify monotheism and the sacred law.",
  15002:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, when things become clear, the disbelievers will wish they were Muslim. The falsity of their ways in this world, such as their disbelief, will be exposed.",
  15003:
      "O Messenger, leave these rejectors to eat as livestock eat, let them enjoy themselves with the world's fleeting pleasures, and let their [false] hopes distract them from believing in Allah and working righteous deeds. They will soon come to know the loss they are in when they are returned to Allah on the Day of Resurrection.",
  15004:
      "We did not send down destruction upon a wrongdoing town except it had an appointed time according to Allah's Knowledge. Therefore, the destruction will neither come before nor after its time.",
  15005:
      "A nation will not be destroyed before its appointed time, and its destruction will not be delayed when its time arrives. Therefore, the wrongdoers should not be deceived [to think] that Allah is deferring their fate.",
  15006:
      "The disbelievers of Mecca said to the Messenger: O you to whom the remembrance was revealed, as you claim, your claims make you out to be one who is insane, and you behave as the insane people do.",
  15007:
      "Why do you not bring the angels to testify on your behalf that you are a prophet sent [by Allah] and that the torment will descend upon us if you are truthful?",
  15008:
      "Allah said, refuting their request to bring the angels: We will not send the angels except according to divine wisdom when your time comes to be punished. When We bring the angels, and they do not believe, they will not be given any respite; instead, they will be punished immediately.",
  15009:
      "We alone revealed this Quran upon the heart of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم as a reminder for people. Therefore, we will guard the Quran against anything being added to it, removed from it, changed, or distorted.",
  15010:
      "O Messenger, We sent messengers before you to previous groups of disbelievers, and they rejected them. So, being rejected by your nation is not something exclusive to you as one of the messengers.",
  15011:
      "Previous groups of disbelievers did not receive a messenger except that they rejected and ridiculed him.",
  15012:
      "As We instilled rejection into the hearts of those nations, We will also instill it into the hearts of the polytheists of Mecca because of their turning away and stubbornness.",
  15013:
      "They do not believe in this Quran revealed upon Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. But, at the same time, Allah's established way of destroying those who reject what their messengers brought has occurred before. Therefore, those who reject you should consider that.",
  15014:
      "These rejectors will remain stubborn even if clear proof makes the truth evident. Even if We opened a door for them from the sky and they proceeded to ascend through it,",
  15015:
      "They would still not believe and would rather say: Our eyes have been dazzled! Or rather, we saw the effects of magic, so we have been bewitched.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The noble Qur’an is possessed of the attributes of perfection in every way, clarity and exposition.\n2. The disbelievers will regret their disbelief on the Day of Judgment, and they will wish they had been Muslims.\n3. Disbelievers normally concern themselves with materialistic things, so you find them entrenched in their desires and passions, deluded by a false sense of security, busying themselves with the world more than the Hearafter.\n4. The destruction of the disbelieving nations that belied the messengers because of their ignorance, disbelief, and belying the verses of Allah and His messenger.\n5. The destruction of the nations is determined to be on a specific date, decided for a specific time, it will not be made earlier nor later and Allah will not make it faster for the sake of anyone.\n6. Allah, the Exalted, made it is responsibility to preserve the noble Qur’an from being altered or changed and being added to or subtracted from until the Day of Judgment.",
  15016:
      "We placed massive stars in the sky to guide people on their travels in the darkness of the land and the sea. We also beautified them for those who behold and look at them so that they would use them as evidence indicative of Allah's Power; may He be Exalted.",
  15017:
      "We protected the sky against every devil far removed from Allah's mercy,",
  15018:
      "except for those who try to listen to the highest assembly secretly, they will be struck with a flaming meteor that will burn them.",
  15019:
      "We flattened the earth so that people would dwell on it. We placed sturdy mountains on it so that it would not shake the people, and We made various crops grow in due proportion, determined by wisdom.",
  15020:
      "O people, We have placed foods and drinks on the earth for you that would sustain you so long as you are in the worldly life. Likewise, We have placed sustenance for other people and animals for whom you do not provide.",
  15021:
      "There is nothing that benefits humanity or animals except that We can produce it and bring benefit to humanity by it. Nevertheless, We do not provide such things except according to a specific quantity determined by Our Wisdom and Will.",
  15022:
      "We sent the winds to fertilize the clouds, then the rain down from the fertilized clouds, and nourish you with that rainwater. O people, you do not store this water on earth in springs and wells; instead, Allah is the One who keeps the water in them.",
  15023:
      "We bring life to the dead by creating them out of nothing and resurrecting them after death. And We cause the living to die when they have completed their time while We will remain and inherit the earth and whatever is upon it.",
  15024:
      "We certainly know those who were born and have gone before you and those who will be born and die after [you]. None of that is hidden from Us.",
  15025:
      "O Messenger, your Lord will gather them all on the Day of Resurrection to recompense the doers of good for their good and the doers of evil for their sins. He is Wise in His planning and knowledgeable; therefore, nothing is hidden from Him.",
  15026:
      "We created Adam from dried clay; if it is struck, it makes a sound. The clay he was created from is black and of an altered scent because it has been left for a lengthy duration.",
  15027:
      "We created the father of the jinn from scalding fire before We created Adam (peace be upon him).",
  15028:
      "O Messenger, remember when Allah told the angels and Iblis, who was among them: I will create a human being from dried clay; if it is struck, it makes a sound; it is black and of an altered scent.",
  15029:
      "When I fashion his image and perfect his creation, then prostrate to him in obedience to My instruction and as a greeting to him.",
  15030:
      "The angels obeyed, so they all prostrated as their Lord commanded them.",
  15031:
      "But Iblis, who was with the angels but was not one himself, refused to prostrate to Adam along with the angels.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It calls on the servant to reflect and ponder over the sky and its decoration, and to take it as an indicator of Allah’s existence.\n2. All types of wealth and decrees are controlled by Allah alone. Its treasures are in His hand and He gives to and takes away from whom He wills according to His wisdom and mercy.\n3. The earth is created, paved and extended to accommodate human life on it. It is stabilised by high mountains so that it would not move with its inhabitants on it. It has on it different crops of known quantities in accordance with wisdom and welfare.",
  15032:
      "After Iblis refused to prostrate to Adam, Allah asked him: What kept and prevented you from prostrating with the angels, who prostrated out of obedience to My command?",
  15033:
      "Iblis arrogantly said: It is not proper for me to prostrate to a human being who You created out of dried clay that used to be black, altered clay.",
  15034: "Allah said to Iblis: Exit from Paradise, for you are banished.",
  15035:
      "My curse is upon you, and you are banished from My mercy until the Day of Resurrection.",
  15036:
      "Iblis said: O My Lord, grant me respite and do not cause me to die until the day the creation will be resurrected.",
  15037: "Allah said: You are of those granted respite whose end is delayed.",
  15038:
      "Until the time when all created things will die upon the first blow of the Horn.",
  15039:
      "Iblis said: O My Lord, because You misguided me, I will make [Your] disobedience seem attractive to them on Earth, and I will lead them all astray from the straight path.",
  15040: "Except for Your slaves whom You selected for your worship.",
  15041: "Allah said: This is a straight path that leads to Me.",
  15042:
      "You have no power or sway in misleading My sincere slaves except those who follow you from the misguided ones.",
  15043:
      "Hell is the promised abode of Iblis and all those who follow him who have been led astray.",
  15044:
      "Hell has seven gates through which they will enter. For each of its gates, there is a known amount of the followers of Iblis who will enter through it.",
  15045:
      "Those who fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will have gardens and springs.",
  15046:
      "When they enter, it will be said to them: Enter it with safety from any misfortune and security from any fears.",
  15047:
      "We will remove whatever hatred and animosity they had in their hearts. Instead, they will be brothers who love one another, sitting upon couches and looking at each other.",
  15048:
      "Fatigue will not affect them in it, and they will not be made to leave it. Instead, they will remain in it eternally.",
  15049:
      "O Messenger, inform My slaves that I will forgive whoever among them repents and show mercy to them.",
  15050:
      "And inform them that My torment is painful, so they should repent to Me to receive My forgiveness and be safe from My torment.",
  15051:
      "And inform them of the story of Abraham's guests (peace be upon him), who were angels. They brought him the good news of a child and informed him of the destruction of the people of Lot.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s commandment to the angels to prostrate to Adam ennobles mankind.\n2. In these verses is an indication for the mutual visitations amongst the pious, their gatherings and the uprightness of their character towards one another such that each of them is accepting of one another and not antagonistic.\n3. It is important for a servants heart to always be feeling both fear and hope as well as desire and aversion.\n4. All the angels prostrated to Adam to greet and ennoble him, except for Iblis who rejected and abstained.\n5. Over those who Allah has guided, selected and chosen, Iblis has no power to cause them to fall into sin and prevent them from receiving Allah’s forgiveness.\n6. Teaching guests to uphold the manners of offering greetings and peace upon the arrival of others.",
  15052:
      "When they came to him, they said: Salam (peace on you). He responded to them with a greeting that was better than theirs and presented them with a roasted calf because he thought they were human. When they did not eat from it, he said: We are afraid of you.",
  15053:
      "The messengers, who were angels, said: Do not be afraid! We will tell you something that will make you happy. You are going to have a very knowledgeable son.",
  15054:
      "Surprised at the good news of a son, Abraham said: Do you bring me this good news despite the fact that I have been afflicted with old age? What kind of good news are you bringing me?",
  15055:
      "The messengers, who were angels, said to Abraham: We bring you good news of the truth in which there is no doubt, so do not be among those who despair from the good news we bring you.",
  15056:
      "Abraham said: And who despairs from the mercy of his Lord except he who has deviated from Allah's straight path?!",
  15057:
      "Abraham said: What is the matter that has brought you, O messengers, from Allah?",
  15058:
      "The messengers, who were angels, said: Allah has sent us to destroy the people of Lot who are guilty of great corruption and evil.",
  15059:
      "Except for the family of Lot and the believers that follow him, for the destruction will not encompass them, and We will save them all from it.",
  15060:
      "Except for his wife, We have decreed her to be one of those who remain behind, included in the destruction.",
  15061:
      "So, the messengers, who were angels, came to the family of Lot in the form of men.",
  15062: "Lot (peace be with him) said to them: You are an unfamiliar people.",
  15063:
      "The messengers, who were angels, said to Lot: Do not fear! We have brought to you, O Lot, the destructive torment your people used to doubt",
  15064:
      "We have brought to you the truth in which there is no joke, and we are truthful in the information we give you.",
  15065:
      "So, travel with your family after some of the night has passed. Travel behind them, and no one should turn back to see what happens to them. Instead, proceed to where Allah has ordered you to go.",
  15066:
      "We informed Lot through revelation this matter that We had decreed. Those people will be annihilated by the last of them being destroyed when morning comes.",
  15067:
      "The people of Sodom came rejoicing at the guests of Lot with the desire to commit indecency.",
  15068:
      "Lot told them: These people are my guests, so do not disgrace me by what you want [to do] with them.",
  15069:
      "Fear Allah by abandoning this indecent behavior, and do not humiliate me by committing your heinous act.",
  15070:
      "His people told him: Did we not forbid you from hosting anyone?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The need to guide towards something that is permissible and not unlawful, just as Lot guided his people to marriage.\n2. The person whom Allah has blessed with guidance and knowledge can never become despondent of Allah’s mercy.\n3. It is Sunnah to hasten when passing the ruins of people whom Allah has destroyed, as these are places of anger and curse.\n4. Allah prohibited Lot and his followers from turning back when the punishment was descending on the people of Lot so that they do not become overtaken by pity for them.\n5. The resolve of the people of Lot to commit indecency with these guests is an indication of their nature being effaced and the extremity of their immorality.",
  15071:
      "Lot (peace be with him) said, offering an excuse for himself in front of his guests: These are the women of my people, who are like daughters to me. Therefore, marry them if you want to satisfy your desires.",
  15072:
      "By your life, O Messenger, the people of Lot wandered mindlessly in pursuit of their lusts.",
  15073: "Then, they were seized by a severe destructive cry at sunrise.",
  15074:
      "We turned their towns upside down and caused stones of hard clay to rain down on them.",
  15075:
      "In the incident of the punishment that descended on the people of Lot, there are signs for those who ponder.",
  15076:
      "The towns of the people of Lot are on an established road and can be seen by travelers who pass by.",
  15077: "That incident has a sign in it for the believers to reflect on.",
  15078:
      "The people of Shuayb, who lived in a town surrounded by intertwined trees, were wrongdoers because they rejected Allah and His Messenger, Shuayb (peace be upon him).",
  15079:
      "So We took retribution from them, and the punishment seized them. The towns of Lot's people and the homes of Shuayb's people are on a road clear to those who pass by.",
  15080:
      "Thamūd, the people of Hijr [a place between Hijaz and the Levant], had, in effect, rejected all the messengers when they rejected their prophet, Saleh (peace be upon him).",
  15081:
      "We gave them proofs and signs to indicate his truthfulness in what he brought from his Lord. One of these proofs was the she-camel. But they did not take lessons from those signs and paid no attention to them.",
  15082:
      "They used to carve houses from the mountains where they lived, safe from what they feared.",
  15083: "Then, the bolt of the torment seized them in the morning.",
  15084:
      "The wealth and homes they had accumulated did not repel Allah's torment from them.",
  15085:
      "We did not create the heavens, the Earth, and everything between them in vain and devoid of wisdom. We created all of it with a true purpose. The Hour will certainly come. So, O Messenger, turn away from those who reject you and pardon them graciously.",
  15086: "Your Lord, O Messenger, is the Creator and Omniscient of everything.",
  15087:
      "We have given you the Opening Chapter, Surah Al-Fatihah, which consists of seven verses and it is the Great Quran.",
  15088:
      "Do not look longingly to the temporary enjoyments We have given to some classes of disbelievers; do not grieve over their rejection and be humble with the believers.",
  15089:
      "Say, O Messenger: I am a warner of Allah's torment, clear in my warning.",
  15090:
      "I warn you of being afflicted by a torment similar to what Allah sent down on those who divided Allah's books into parts, believing in some and rejecting others.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. When Allah intends to destroy a town, their evil and transgression increases. When it reaches its peak He imposes on them the retribution they deserve.\n2. In the story of Lot there is a lesson and admonition for true believers.\n3. It is disliked to enter places of punishment.\n4. The sight of a believer should not long for the ornaments of the world when he has knowledge of the Mighty and Majestic Master.\n5. A believer must remain far from the idolaters and must not grieve if they do not have faith. He must be close to the believers, humble before them and loving towards them - even if they are poor.",
  15091:
      "Those who divided the Quran into parts and then say: It is magic, soothsaying, or poetry.",
  15092:
      "By your Lord, O Messenger, We will question all who divide the Quran into parts on the Day of Resurrection.",
  15093: "We will question them for their disbelief and sins in the world.",
  15094:
      "So announce, O Messenger, the invitation towards Allah that He has instructed you to do and do not pay any attention to what the polytheists say and do.",
  15095:
      "Do not be afraid of them, for We are enough for you against the plot of those leaders of disbelief from the Quraysh who mock you.",
  15096:
      "Those who take another deity along with Allah will soon know the evil outcome of associating partners with Allah.",
  15097:
      "O Messenger, We know your heart is distressed by the rejection and mockery that emanates from them.",
  15098:
      "So, resort to Allah by declaring His transcendence from everything inappropriate for Him, praising Him with attributes of perfection, and be of those who worship and pray to Him. In that, there is a cure for the distress of your heart.",
  15099:
      "Continue worshipping your Lord as long as you are alive until death comes to you while in that state.",
  16000:
      "The Bee (Surah Al-Nahl)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nA reminder of the blessings that demonstrate the generosity of our Benefactor, Allah, the Exalted and Transcendent.\n•    Explanation:",
  16001:
      "The torment Allah has decreed for you, O disbelievers, is close. So do not ask for it to come sooner than its time. Allah is free from and exalted above all that the polytheists associate as partners with Him.",
  16002:
      "Allah, through His decree, sends down the angels to whoever of His Messengers He wills with revelation [saying]: Warn, O messengers, the people against associating partners with Allah, for none is deserving of worship besides Me. Therefore, fear Me, O People, by complying with My commands and avoiding My prohibitions.",
  16003:
      "Allah created the heavens and the Earth without precedent for an actual purpose. He did not create them in vain but to serve as a sign of His greatness. He is free from what they ascribe as partners to Him.",
  16004:
      "He created man from a despised drop of fluid, who then progressed from one form to another. Then suddenly, he became a harsh disputer using falsehood to attempt to invalidate the truth, being a clear opponent in his disputation.",
  16005:
      "He also created livestock such as camels, cattle, and goats for your benefit, O People. Some benefits include deriving warmth from their wool and hair and other benefits from their milk, skin, and backs. In addition, some of them serve as food that you eat.",
  16006:
      "There is [also] beauty in them for you in the evening and in the morning when you take them out to graze.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. In the verses there is proof that all people will be questioned: both disbelievers as well as believers, with the exception of those who enter paradise without reckoning.\n2. Allah’s care and attention to protecting the Prophet (peace be upon him) from the harm of the idolaters.\n3. Glorifying, praising and praying to Allah is the cure for worries and grief and the way out of crises, dilemmas and anguish.\n4. A Muslim is required to go on worshipping, in the form of ritual prayer, until death comes to him, as long as his mind is not overcome by a state of unconsciousness or loss of memory.\n5. The creation of the heavens and the earth and the creation of man is a clear sign of Allah’s power, existence and oneness.\n6. Similarly the creation of livestock and their many benefits of which mankind enjoys is another sign of Allah’s power and oneness.\n7. Allah has given us ownership of livestock and animals and subjugated them to us. He has permitted us to control and take benefit from them, out of His mercy for us.",
  16007:
      "This livestock We created for you carries your heavy goods when you travel to places you can only reach after bearing great hardship on yourselves. Your Lord, O People, is Kind and Merciful to you as He has subjugated this livestock for you.",
  16008:
      "He created horses, mules, and donkeys for you to ride and carry your goods on and for them to be an adornment for you that you can beautify yourselves with when among people. He creates that which you do not know of as He wishes.",
  16009:
      "It is upon Allah alone to clearly show the straight path leading to His pleasure, Islam. Some paths are the paths of the Devil that deviate away from the truth. Any path other than the path of Islam deviates. Had Allah been willing to guide you all to believe [in Him], He would have done so.",
  16010:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One who sent down water from the clouds for you. From this water, you have what you and your livestock can drink. You also get vegetation from it, which you can use to graze your livestock.",
  16011:
      "With that water, Allah causes crops to grow for you to eat. He also causes olives, date palms, grapes to grow, and other types of fruit. The water and the things it produces are a sign of Allah's power for people who ponder His creation and use it as a sign of His greatness; may He be Exalted.",
  16012:
      "Allah has subjugated the night for you so that you can find tranquility and rest in it and the day so that you can earn your livelihood in it. He subjugated the sun and made it bright and the moon a source of light. The stars are subjugated for you by His decree, which you use for navigation in the darkness of the sea and land, and by which you come to know the time etc. The subjugation of all these things is clearly indicative of Allah's power for people who apply their minds, for they are the ones who will grasp the wisdom in them.",
  16013:
      "He (may He be Exalted) also subjugated for you the things on Earth that He created, having diverse colors such as minerals, animals, plants, and crops. These things that He has created and subjugated for you are clearly indicative of Allah's power (may He be Exalted) for people who reflect and realize that Allah is Powerful and a Benefactor.",
  16014:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One who subjugated the sea for you and enabled you to travel on it and to extract what is in it so that you can eat the fresh and soft meat of the fish that you catch and that you can extract from it jewelry that you and your wives can wear such as pearls. You see the ships splitting the waves of the ocean, and you travel on these ships in search of Allah's bounty in the form of profit, which you gain from trade. All of this is for you to be grateful to Allah for the favors He has given you and to worship Him alone.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s statement: (He creates what you do not know) includes all modern means of transportation and travel.\n2. Allah created the stars as a means of beauty for the sky, for guidance in the darkness of the land and sea, and to know the time and seasons.\n3. Praise and gratitude for Allah who has blessed us with things that improve our lives and standard of living.\n4. The sending down (of water) and causing plants to grow is a sign of Allah’s power, existence and oneness for people who ponder and reflect.\n5. Allah has favoured us by subjugating the sea so that its meat (fish) is eaten, its pearls and coral are extracted, and it is travelled on for purposes of trade and defending the lands from the harm and aggression of an enemy.",
  16015:
      "He placed mountains on Earth to keep it firm so that it does not shake and cause you to become unsettled. He caused rivers to flow so that you could drink from them and give water to your livestock and crops. He carved pathways in it for you to tread and reach your destinations without losing your way.",
  16016:
      "He made clear landmarks on Earth for you to be guided by when traveling during the day. He also made stars for you in the sky so that you may find your way.",
  16017:
      "Is the One who created all these things like the One who does not create anything?! Are you not reminded of Allah's greatness, who created everything, and then worship Him alone without associating those things that cannot create anything as partners with Him?",
  16018:
      "If you, O people, attempt to count and list Allah's many favors that He has favored you with, you will not be able to do so because they are so numerous and diverse. Allah is Forgiving, as He did not take you to task for being neglectful of showing thanks to Him, and Merciful, as he did not stop these favors from you because of your sins and failure to thank Him.",
  16019:
      "Allah knows the deeds that you, O slaves, hide and those that you reveal. None of those deeds are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for them accordingly.",
  16020:
      "Those whom the polytheists worship instead of Allah cannot create anything, no matter how insignificant. Those who worship them instead of Allah are the ones who make them. How do they worship idols instead of Allah, which they make with their own hands?!",
  16021:
      "In addition to their worshippers making them with their hands, they are also inanimate things without life or knowledge. Therefore, they do not know when they will be resurrected with their worshippers on the Day of Resurrection, to be thrown together with them into the Fire.",
  16022:
      "The one worthy of your worship is One without any partner, and that is Allah. The hearts of those who do not believe in the resurrection and the recompense reject the Oneness of Allah because they lack fear [of Allah]. Therefore, they do not believe there will be any reckoning or punishment. Consequently, they are arrogant and refuse to accept and submit to the truth.",
  16023:
      "Truly, Allah knows the deeds these people hide, and He knows the deeds they reveal. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for that accordingly. He (may He be Exalted) does not love those who are too arrogant to worship and submit to Him. Instead, he detests them intensely.",
  16024:
      "When these people who deny the Oneness of the Creator and reject the resurrection are asked: What did Allah reveal to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم? They say: Allah has not revealed anything to him. He has only brought stories and fables of the earlier people.",
  16025:
      "So their outcome will be that they will carry their sins without any reduction, and they will also carry some of the sins of those they misled from Islam on account of ignorance and blind imitation. How terrible will it be that they will bear some of their sins and the sins of their followers?",
  16026:
      "The disbelievers before these people plotted against their messengers. Allah then destroyed their buildings from the foundations, so their roofs fell on them from above. So the torment came to them from where they did not expect as they had expected their buildings to protect them, but instead, they were destroyed by them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There is an indication in the verses to the utilisation of the means to something, for Allah was able to make the earth stable without the mountains.\n2. The verses contain a significant amount of the various types of Allah’s favours to His servants, in brief and in detail. By this Allah calls the servants to be thankful to Him and to remember Him and pray to Him.\n3. The nature of man is to do wrong and to dare to commit sins and be neglectful of the rights of his Lord, being ungrateful for Allah’s favours. Only those whom Allah has guided show thanks and acknowledge His favours.\n4. It was out of compassion that Abraham (peace be on him) prayed for the forgiveness and mercy of Allah for the sinners.\n5. Allah causes the plot of His enemies to fail and their plot become became a burden for them since it was their own scheming that caused their destruction!\n6. A clarification of the state of the misguided and those who caused their misguidance, and that the latter are worse in position on the Day of Judgment.\n7. Allah grasps sinners at the time of death in a severe manner because of the sudden and terrible nature of His seizure, unlike something that occurs gradually and gently which has less effect.",
  16027:
      "Then, on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will humiliate and disgrace them with the torment. He will ask them: Where are my partners whom you used to associate with me in worship and because of which you used to oppose the prophets and the believers? The righteous scholars will respond: Indeed! On the Day of Resurrection, Humiliation and punishment will befall the disbelievers.",
  16028:
      "Those whose souls are taken by the angel of death and his helpers while wronging themselves by disbelieving in Allah will submit with total surrender when death comes to them. They will deny the disbelief and sins they used to do, thinking that such denial will benefit them. It will be said to them: You have lied. You were disbelievers who used to commit disobedience. Allah knows everything that you used to do in this world. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for that accordingly.",
  16029:
      "It will be said to them: Enter, based on your deeds, through the doors of Hell to live therein eternally. What an evil place of residence for those too arrogant to believe in Allah and worship Him alone.",
  16030:
      "Those who feared their Lord by obeying His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will be asked: What did your Lord send down to your Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم? They will reply: Allah has sent down to him great good. For those who worshipped Allah well and treated His creation well in this worldly life, there is an excellent reward, which includes victory and abundance of provision. And the reward Allah has prepared for them in the Hereafter will be better than what He already gave them in this world. Therefore, what an excellent abode is the abode of the Hereafter for those who fear their Lord by obeying His commands and avoiding His prohibitions!",
  16031:
      "They will enter gardens of residence and permanence with rivers flowing below their palaces and trees. In these gardens, they will have every type of food, drink, and other pleasures that they desire. This type of reward, which Allah gives to those who fear Him from the nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, He also gives to those who feared Him from the previous nations.",
  16032:
      "Those whose souls are taken by the angel of death and his helpers while their hearts are pure from disbelief, the angels will address them saying: Peace be on you. You are safe from every difficulty. Enter paradise because of the correct belief and righteous deeds you used to do in this world.",
  16033:
      "Are these rejecting polytheists waiting for anything but the angel of death and his helpers to take their souls and strike their faces and backs, or [are they waiting] for Allah's command to eradicate them through torment in this world? Similar to those polytheists who came before who were destroyed because of their polytheism, the polytheists of Mecca may perhaps meet the same fate. Allah did not wrong them when He destroyed them, but they wronged themselves by bringing themselves to the places of destruction because they disbelieved in Allah.",
  16034:
      "So, the consequences of the deeds they used to do came down on them, and they were surrounded by the torment they used to mock whenever they were reminded of it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue of the people of knowledge and that they are the ones who speak the truth in the world and on the day when the witnesses will stand; and that their statement is given consideration by Allah and His creation.\n2. It is Allah’s generosity and grace that He will give the people of paradise everything they desire, to the extent that He will remind them of bounties they desire that they will not be aware of.\n3. Action is the cause and basis for entering paradise and being saved from the fire, and this will happen by Allah’s mercy and favour to the believers - not by their own efforts or design.\n4. The etiquette of the Angels with Allah is that they attributed knowledge to Allah without saying: “We know what you used to do”, indicating that the only way they knew is because Allah taught it to them.”",
  16035:
      "Those who associated others with Allah in worship said: Had Allah willed for us to worship Him alone and not to associate any partners with Him, we would not have worshipped anything besides Him, neither us nor our forefathers before us. Had He willed for us not to regard anything unlawful, we would not have done so. The disbelievers of the past also mentioned such false arguments. The duty of the messengers is only to convey what they have been ordered to clearly, and they have done so. The disbelievers cannot use the decree of Allah as an argument after Allah has given them free will and choice and sent His messengers to them.",
  16036:
      "We had sent to every previous nation a messenger to command his nation to worship Allah alone and abandon the worship of others besides Him, such as idols, devils, etc. Allah guided some of them; they believed in Him and followed what His messenger brought. Others rejected Allah and went against the messenger. Thus, He did not assist them, and misguidance befell them. So travel through the earth to see for yourselves what the result of those who rejected [Allah] was after the torment and destruction came upon them.",
  16037:
      "Even though, O Messenger, you try everything to invite these people and are eager for them to be guided, Allah will not direct those whom He misguides to guidance. They will have no one besides Allah to assist them in averting the torment away from them.",
  16038:
      "These people who rejected the resurrection swore their most solemn oaths: Allah will not resurrect anyone who dies. At the same time, they have no proof supporting their claim. Yes, Allah will resurrect everyone who dies, this being a binding promise. However, most people do not know that Allah will resurrect the dead, and they, therefore, deny the resurrection.",
  16039:
      "Allah will resurrect them all on the Day of Resurrection to make clear to them the reality of the things they differed about, such as His Oneness, resurrection, and prophethood, and so that the disbelievers may realize that they were lying in their claim that Allah has partners and their denial of the resurrection.",
  16040:
      "When We want to bring the dead to life and resurrect them, nothing will prevent Us from doing so. When We want something to happen, all We say is: Be! And it is!",
  16041:
      "Those who left their homes, families, and wealth and emigrated from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam in search of Allah's pleasure after having been persecuted and punished by the disbelievers, We will make them settle in an abode in this world in which they will be honored. However, the reward of the Hereafter is greater because it includes Paradise. If those who remained behind knew the reward of those who emigrated, they would not have stayed behind.",
  16042:
      "These emigrants in the path of Allah are the ones who were patient when harmed by their people and separated from their families and lands. They were patient in Allah's obedience. They rely only on their Lord in all their affairs, and Allah gave them this great recompense.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The mission and goal of Messengers in all communities in general is one, which is to call towards the worship of Allah alone and to leave the worship of false Allahs.\n2. The intelligent person is the one who takes lesson from what occurred to the misguided deniers, and their eventual min, devastation, suffering and destruction.\n3. The wisdom behind resurrection and the return to the afterlife is for Allah to show the tmth about the things that people differed in such as resurrection and everything else.\n4. The virtue of patience and reliance. Patience because of what it necessitates of controlling ones soul, and reliance because of turning ones heart away from the creation and focusing on Allah.\n5. The reward for the emigrants who left their homes and wealth and were patient against harm having relied on their Sustainer will be a better place of residence, a good position, a pleasant life, abundant and pure sustenance, victory over enemies and sovereignty over the lands and people.",
  16043:
      "We did not send before you, O Messenger, except men who were human beings, to whom We sent revelation. We did not send messengers that were angels. This is Our constant way. If you [people] deny that, ask the people of the previous books, and they will tell you if you did not know that messengers were only human beings; they were not angels.",
  16044:
      "We sent these human messengers with clear signs and revealed books. We have revealed to you, O Messenger, the Quran so that you can clarify to the people that which requires clarification and so that they can apply their minds and take lessons from its contents.",
  16045:
      "Do those who make plots to prevent people from Allah's path feel secure that Allah will not cause the Earth to cave in with them as He caused it to cave in with Qarun, or that the torment will not come to them from where they least expect?",
  16046:
      "Or [do they feel secure] that the torment will not afflict them while they go about their journeys and quest for earnings? They will not escape nor protect themselves from it.",
  16047:
      "Or do they feel secure that Allah's torment will not come to them while they fear it? Allah can torment them in all conditions. Your Lord is compassionate and merciful. He does not rush to punish His slaves; perhaps they will repent to Him.",
  16048:
      "Do these people who reject not look with contemplation at Allah's creation? Their shadows incline to the right and the left, following the sun's movement in the day and that of the moon at night, in humility and literal prostration to their Lord while they are submissive to Him.",
  16049:
      "It is to Allah alone that all creatures in the heavens and on Earth prostrate. It is to Him alone that the angels prostrate. They are not too proud to worship Allah and obey Him.",
  16050:
      "Despite their constant worship and obedience, they fear their Lord (who is above them in His essence, Dominance, and Authority) and carry out acts of obedience their Lord commands them to do.",
  16051:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) said to all His slaves: Do not take two beings of worship. The being deserving of worship is only One who has no second nor any partner. So fear only Me and do not fear others besides Me.",
  16052:
      "To Him alone belongs everything in the heavens and on Earth; He created, owns, and plans everything. To Him alone, obedience, submission, and sincerity are always due. Will you, then, fear anyone other than Allah? No, instead, fear Him alone!",
  16053:
      "Whatever blessing you possess, O people, whether religious or worldly, is from Allah (may He be Exalted) and not from anyone else. Then, when some calamity, sickness, or poverty afflicts you, it is to Him alone that you plead in supplication to remove what has afflicted you. Thus, the One who grants favors and removes difficulties is the One Who deserves to be worshipped alone.",
  16054:
      "When He answers your supplications and removes harm from you, a group of you suddenly begin associating partners with their Lord and worshipping others with Him. What unjust behavior is this?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue of the people of knowledge, for Allah instructed those who do not know to refer to them in all incidents. This is an implicit attestation to their integrity and credibility as He instructed that they be asked.\n2. A sinner should be ashamed of His Lord, that his sins ascend to Him, whilst Allah’s blessings descend on him all the time!\n3. The people of disbelief, denial and sin should be afraid that Allah may seize them with punishment while they are unaware.\n4. All blessings are from Allah, whether these are material blessings such as sustenance, safety and health or intangible blessings such as security, prestige, position and the like.\n5. Humans finds no refuge from difficulties except by calling on Allah, thus inevitably call on Him because they knows that no one can remove difficulties except Him.",
  16055:
      "Their associating partners with Allah meant that they rejected Allah's favors upon them, including Allah removing their distress. It was said to them: Enjoy the favors you have been given until Allah's torment comes to you sooner or later.",
  16056:
      "The polytheists allocate to their idols, which do not know anything as they are lifeless objects that can neither benefit nor harm, a portion of their wealth that We have provided for them as a means of seeking closeness to those idols. By Allah, O polytheists, you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection about your false claims that these idols are deities and that they are entitled to a portion of your wealth.",
  16057:
      "The polytheists attribute daughters to Allah, believing that these are the angels. Thus, they attribute lineage to Allah and ascribe to him what they do not like for themselves. He is Pure, Exalted, and Sanctified from what they ascribe to Him. Then, they ascribe to themselves the male offspring that they desire. What crime is greater than this?!",
  16058:
      "When one of these polytheists is given the news of the birth of a female, his face darkens due to the extreme dislike of such news, and his heart is filled with worry and grief. Then, he attributes to Allah what he does not like for himself?!",
  16059:
      "He hides from his people because of the bad news of the birth of a girl that was given to him. He asks himself: Shall he keep this girl he was given news of with humiliation and dejection, or shall he bury her alive and hide her in the sand? How evil the polytheists' judgment is when they assigned to their Lord what they disliked for themselves.",
  16060:
      "The disbelievers who do not believe in the Hereafter have evil attributes, such as ignorance, disbelief, and the need to have offspring. Allah has lofty, praiseworthy attributes of majesty, perfection, independence, and knowledge. He (may He be Exalted) is Mighty in His dominion, and nothing can overpower Him. He is Wise in His creation, planning, and legislation.",
  16061:
      "If Allah (may He be Exalted) were to punish people for their wrongs and rejection of Him, He would not leave behind a single human or animal on Earth that walks on its surface. But He (may He be Exalted) delays them until a fixed time per His knowledge. Then, when that appointed time, per His knowledge, comes, they will not be able to delay it nor advance it for even a short while.",
  16062:
      "They assign females to Allah (may He be Exalted) females, which they dislike to attribute to themselves. They falsely claim that if they are resurrected, they will have the best rank with Allah. Truly, for them is the Fire, and they will be left therein, never to come out of it.",
  16063:
      "By Allah, We have sent messengers to nations before you, O Messenger. However, the Devil made their evil deeds of polytheism, disbelief, and sins attractive to them. He is their so-called helper on the Day of Judgment, so let them ask him for help. They will have a painful torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  16064:
      "We did not reveal the Quran to you, O Messenger, except for you to clarify to all people what they differ about in respect of Allah's Oneness, resurrection, and the details of sacred law, and for the Quran to be a guidance and mercy for those who believe in Allah, His messengers and what the Quran has brought, for they are the ones who will benefit from the truth.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some of the errors of the idolaters are the attribution of daughters to Allah and the attribution of sons to themselves and their disdain of daughters. Their faces display grief and sorrow at the birth of a female and they hide from and avoid contact with people because of the extreme grief, humiliation and shame on account of having a daughter.\n2. It is Allah’s practice to give respite to the disbelievers and not to punish them immediately to give them an opportunity to have faith and repent.\n3. The time of a person’s death and the end of his life will not come earlier or later by even one hour or moment.\n4. Allah’s practice amongst His servants is to send Messengers with clear proofs and a full explanation. Muhammad (peace be upon him) is therefore like other Messengers.\n5. The major task of the Prophet (peace be upon him) is to explain what is contained in the Qur’an and to clarify what the people of the various creeds and beliefs differed about with respect to religion and sacred laws, so that his clarification can be a proof against them.",
  16065:
      "Allah sends down rain from the sky, with which He revives the Earth by bringing forth vegetation from it after it has been dry and arid. The sending down of the rain from the sky and bringing forth the vegetation of the Earth through it is a clear indication of Allah's power for people who listen to the Speech of Allah and ponder over it.",
  16066:
      "There is a lesson for you to take, O people, in camels, cows, and goats: We give you milk to drink from their udders that comes out between the waste that the stomach contains and the blood in the body. But, despite this, it comes out as pure milk that is tasty and pleasant to those who drink it.",
  16067:
      "There is a lesson for you in date palm trees and grapes that We provide for you. From them, you make intoxicants that affect the mind, which is not good, and you also take from them a good provision that benefits you, such as dates, raisins, vinegar, and molasses. In this, there truly is an indication of Allah's power and favor upon His slaves for people who use their reason, for they are the ones who reflect.",
  16068:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, inspired the bees and guided them [saying]: Make homes for yourselves in the mountains, the trees, and the structures and shelters that people build.",
  16069:
      "[Addressing the bees]: Then eat the fruits you desire, and go along the pathways your Lord inspires you to take that are made subservient for you. From the bellies of those bees emerges honey of varying colors, such as white and yellow, among others, containing a cure for people they use to treat diseases. Such inspiration of bees and the honey that emerges from their bellies indicate Allah's power and planning His creation's affairs for people who think, for they are the ones who derive lessons.",
  16070:
      "Allah created you without precedent. He will then cause you to die when your life's term ends. The lifespan of some of you will be extended to the worst stage of life, which is severe old age when a person will no longer know anything about what he used to know. Allah is Omniscient, and no deed of His slaves is hidden from Him. He is Omnipotent, and nothing can overpower Him.",
  16071:
      "Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, has preferred some of you over others in the provision that He has granted you, making some among you rich and others poor, some of you leaders and others subjects. However, those to whom Allah has given preference in provision are not willing to pass on what Allah has given them to their slaves so that these slaves become equal partners in their ownership. How, then, are they pleased for Allah to have partners from among His slaves when they are not pleased with it for themselves to have partners from amongst their slaves who will be equal to them? What injustice is this, and what rejection of Allah's favors can be worse than this?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has kept for His servants in the fruit of the date-palm and grapes many benefits and advantages such as the good provision that the servants can consume fresh and ripe in the present or the future in the form of food or drink.\n2. In the creation of tiny bees and the delicious honey that comes out of their bellies with different colours in accordance with the various lands and pastures there is a sign of Allah’s complete care and kindness for His servants and that no one besides Him should be divinely loved and called on in worship.\n3. One of the great favours of Allah to His servants is that He made for them spouses that they could find comfort in and He made from their spouses children who are the coolness of their eyes, who serve them and fulfil their needs and from whom they can benefit in numerous ways.\n4. In the verses there is an indication towards the permissibility of utilising milk for drinking and other purposes.\n5. In the bee there are many benefits for the trees and plants themselves and for man as well. Likewise in honey there are benefits and a cure for man.",
  16072:
      "Allah has made for you, O people, spouses from the same species as you whose company you can enjoy. He has made for you from your spouses, children, and grandchildren; and has provided you with wholesome foods such as meat, grains, and fruit. Will they then falsely believe in idols and statues, reject Allah's innumerable favors, and not be grateful to Allah through belief in Him alone?!",
  16073:
      "These polytheists worship idols besides Allah, who have no power to provide them with any provision from the heavens or the Earth. They will never be able to do so because they are inanimate objects with no life or knowledge.",
  16074:
      "So, O People, do not make Allah similar to these idols that do neither benefit nor harm. Allah has no likeness for you to associate others with Him in worship. Allah knows the attributes of Majesty and Perfection that He possesses. You do not know that, so you associate partners with Him and claim that your idols are similar to Him.",
  16075:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) presents an example to refute the polytheists: A bonded slave that is unable to do anything and who has nothing to spend compared to a free person to whom We have given lawful wealth that he uses as he wills and spends from it secretly and openly as he wills. These two men are not equal. How, then, do you make Allah, Who is the Owner of everything, who does what He wills in His dominion, similar to those powerless idols? Praise be to Allah, Who is deserving of all praise. However, most polytheists do not recognize Allah's Oneness in His divinity and that He deserves to be worshipped alone.",
  16076:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) presents another example to refute them, which is the example of two men: One of them is mute and cannot hear, speak, or understand due to his deafness and muteness. He is unable to benefit himself or others. He is a heavy burden on the one in charge of him who looks after him. Whichever direction he sends him, he brings no good and does not attain the objective. Can the person whose condition is like this be equal to one who is sound of hearing and speech and who benefits others? He instructs people to be just, and he is upright. He is on a clear path that has no confusion or crookedness. How then do you, O polytheist, equate Allah, Who possesses the attributes of majesty and perfection, with your idols who cannot hear or speak and who cannot bring any benefit or remove any harm?!",
  16077:
      "To Allah alone belongs the knowledge of the unseen of the heavens and the Earth. He has the exclusive knowledge of that as opposed to anyone of His creation. The coming of the Hour is only known to Allah; when He wills, it will come quicker than in the blink of an eye, or rather, it is even closer than that. Allah has power over everything. Nothing can overpower Him. When He intends something, He says: Be, and it is.",
  16078:
      "Allah brought you, O people, out of your mothers' wombs after the completion of the term of pregnancy as babies unable to comprehend anything. And He gave you hearing to hear with, eyesight to see with, and hearts to understand, with the hope that you may be grateful to Him for these favors that He has given you.",
  16079:
      "Have the polytheists not seen the birds that are subdued and designed to fly in the air because of the wings that Allah granted them, along with the lightness and delicate nature of the air? He inspired them to flap their wings. No one keeps them from falling out of the sky except Allah, the Powerful. This subjugation and holding them there from falling are indications for people who believe in Allah because they are the ones who benefit from such signs and lessons.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has kept great wisdom in the distribution of sustenance amongst His servants. He has made some of them rich, some poor and others middle-class, so that the world can be complementary and people can live with one another by serving one another.\n2. The two examples in the verses show the deviation of the idolaters and the falsehood of the worship of idols, because the deity that deserves to be worshipped is the one that has control and power to do things, to benefit those who worship Him, and to instruct goodness and justice.\n3. The knowledge of the Ghaib in the heavens and earth is exclusive to Allah. No one knows it except a prophet or angel to whom Allah gives knowledge thereof.\n4. One of the favours of Allah and a display of His power, is the creation of human beings in the wombs of their mothers in a state of not knowing anything. Then He provides them with the means of realisation and knowledge, which is their hearing, sight and hearts, by which they come to know and understand.",
  16080:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) has made for you the homes you build out of stone and other items to settle and rest therein. He has made tents and canopies for you in the desert from the skins of camels, cows, and goats that are like urban homes. These are light for you to carry when you travel from one place to another and easy to erect when you camp. He has made for you, from the wool of sheep and the hair of camels and goats, furnishings for your homes, garments, and coverings that you can enjoy for a limited time.",
  16081:
      "Allah has made the trees and buildings you use as shade from the heat. He has made for you tunnels, caverns, and caves in the mountains that you use as a cover from the cold, heat, and your enemies. He has made shirts and robes for you from cotton and other materials that protect you from the heat and cold. He has made armor that protects you from the strikes of others in war so that their weapons do not pierce your bodies. Just as Allah has given you the above favors, He completes His favors upon you in the hope that you will submit to Him alone and not associate anything as partners with Him.",
  16082:
      "If they turn away from believing in you and accepting what you have brought, then your responsibility, O Messenger, is only to clearly convey what you have been ordered. It is not your duty to guide.",
  16083:
      "The polytheists recognize the favors Allah has given them, such as sending the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. Still, they then deny His favors by not giving thanks to Him and rejecting His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Most of them reject His favors; may He be Exalted.",
  16084:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the Day when Allah will resurrect the messenger sent to every nation to testify of the belief of those who believed and the disbelief of those who disbelieved. After that, those who disbelieved will not be allowed to present an excuse for their rejection, and they will not be returned to the world to do deeds pleasing to their Lord, as the Hereafter is the place of reckoning and not the place of deeds.",
  16085:
      "When the wrongdoing polytheists see the torment, it will not be lightened for them, nor will they be given respite by it being delayed. Instead, they will enter it to live therein eternally.",
  16086:
      "When the polytheists see the false deities they used to worship besides Allah, in the Hereafter, they will say: O our Lord! These are our partners that we used to worship besides You. They will say this to make them carry their burdens. Allah will cause their deities to speak, and they will respond to them by saying: You, O polytheists, were liars in worshipping a partner with Allah, for He has no partner deserving of worship.",
  16087:
      "The polytheists will surrender and submit to Allah alone, and all the fabricated claims that their idols will intercede for them before Allah will disappear.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The abundance of favours is a reason that draws the servants to an increase in gratitude and praise for Allah.\n2. The condition of those who disbelieved in Allah on the Day of Judgement is that no excuse will be accepted from them, the retribution will not be removed from them, their partners will abandon them and they will acknowledge that they were guilty of disbelief.\n3. The witness that will give testimony against every nation will be the purest and most just witness. These are the Messengers on whose testimony judgement will be passed.\n4. The verses indicate the permissiblity of using wool and animal hair in all conditions.\n5. One of Allah’s favours to His servants that is deserving of gratitude: Are the homes we live in and enjoy.\n6. In the verse: “garments to protect you from your violence” there is an indication that the servants must make preparations of equipment for striving in Allah’s path so that they can be used when fighting the enemy.",
  16088:
      "For those who disbelieved and turned others away from the path of Allah, We will increase their torment above and beyond what was due to them because of their disbelief, corruption, and corrupting others by misleading them.",
  16089:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the Day We will raise a messenger from every nation who will testify against them about their rejection or belief. This messenger will be from them and speak their language. We have brought you, O Messenger, as a witness against all nations. We revealed the Quran to you to clarify everything that requires clarification of the lawful and unlawful, reward and punishment, etc. We also revealed it as a guidance to the truth for people, as a mercy to those who believe in it and practice what it contains, and as the good news of everlasting bliss that awaits those who believe in Allah.",
  16090:
      "Allah orders His slaves to be just by discharging Allah's rights and the rights of the slaves of Allah and by not giving preference in judgment to anyone unless with a right that demands such preference. He commands them to be good by doing more than what is mandatory, such as voluntarily spending and forgiving the oppressor. He instructs them to see to the needs of their relatives. He forbids everything vile, in words, such as obscene speech, or deeds, such as zina (illicit sexual relations). He forbids oppression and arrogance over people. Allah advises you with the commands and prohibitions in this verse, hoping you will heed His advice.",
  16091:
      "Fulfill every pledge that you have made with Allah or with people. Do not break oaths after binding them by swearing by Allah when you have made Allah a witness to the oath you swore. Allah knows what you do. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for that accordingly.",
  16092:
      "Do not be foolish and dim-witted by breaking your pledges, like a lady who tired herself by spinning her wool or cotton. After it was firmly spun, she broke it open and unraveled it! She exhausted herself by spinning and then breaking it and did not obtain the desired result. You make your oaths as a means of deception to deceive one another so that your nation can be more in number and stronger than the nation of your enemies. Allah only tests you with fulfilling your pledges; will you fulfill or break them? Allah will make clear to you on the Day of Resurrection those things you differed about in this world. He will distinguish those who were on truth from those who were on falsehood and the truthful from the liars.",
  16093:
      "Had Allah willed, He would have made you one nation in agreement on the truth, but He (may He be Exalted) leads astray, through His justice, whom He wills from the truth and from fulfilling their oaths. He guides, through His grace, whom He wills. You will surely be questioned on the Day of Resurrection about what you used to do in this world.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers who prevent others from Allah’s path will receive multiplied punishment on account of their spreading corruption in the world by their disbelief and sin.\n2. The earth is not without people of righteousness and knowledge. They are the leaders of guidance and representatives of the prophets. The scholars are the guardians of the sacred law of the prophets.\n3. The verses have defined the pillars of Muslim society in the private and public life of the individual, the community and the state.\n4. The necessity of fulfilling pledges and covenants and the prohibition of breaking them.\n5. The prohibition of bribery and acceptance of money for breaking one’s pledge.",
  16094:
      "Do not make your oaths a means of deception, allowing you to trick and deceive one another, following your desires - breaking them whenever you wish and fulfilling them whenever you wish. If you do so, your feet will slip from the straight path after being firm on it. You will taste the torment because of your deviation from Allah's path and misleading others, and you will receive torment that has been multiplied.",
  16095:
      "Do not exchange the pledge you took in Allah's name for a small amount, failing to abide by it. The victory and booty that Allah has in this world and the everlasting bliss that He has in the Hereafter are better for you than the small amount that you take for breaking your pledge; if only you realized that.",
  16096:
      "The wealth, pleasures, and luxuries you have, O people, will end no matter how much it may be. But the reward with Allah will remain. How, then, do you prefer that which is fleeting over that which is lasting? We will certainly reward those who remain steadfast on their pledges and do not break them with a reward according to the best of what they used to do by multiplying it by ten to seven hundred times or even more.",
  16097:
      "Whoever does righteous deeds in accordance with sacred law, whether male or female, while believing in Allah, We will grant them a good life in this world. They will be pleased with Allah's decree, content, and guided towards obedience. And in the Hereafter, We will reward them according to the best virtuous deeds they used to do in this world.",
  16098:
      "When you intend to recite the Quran, O believer, ask Allah to protect you from the whispering of the Devil, who is far removed from Allah's mercy.",
  16099:
      "The Devil has no authority over those who believe in Allah and rely only on their Lord in all their affairs.",
  16100:
      "His authority is only through whispering to those who take him as an ally and obey him in his tempting. Because of this temptation, they associate partners with Allah, whom they worship along with Him.",
  16101:
      "When We abrogate the ruling of a verse of the Quran with another verse, and Allah knows well about the part of the Quran that is abrogated for a reason and the part that is not abrogated, they say: You, O Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, are only a liar making up lies about Allah. But most of them do not know that abrogation occurs for a divine reason with far-reaching wisdom.",
  16102:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: This Quran has been brought down by Gabriel (peace be with him) from Allah (may He be Exalted) with the truth that contains no error, alteration or distortion to keep those who believe in Allah firm on their belief whenever new verses are revealed, and a part thereof is abrogated. It also guides them to the truth and gives good news to the Muslims about the generous reward they will receive.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The person who gives preference to that which is despicable and perishable over that which is valuable and lasting is not intelligent.\n2. Good action accompanied by faith makes life pleasant.\n3. The need to abstain from that which is harmful to a person; that which causes him to become unmindful of Allah’s rights and what Allah has made obligatory on him.\n4. The path to safety from the evil of Satan is to resort to Allah and to seek His protection.\n5. The believers must make the Qur’an their leader and be guided by the knowledge it contains, adopt its ethics and use its light. In this way both their religious and worldly affairs will be set right.\n6. Seeking Allah’s protection from Satan, the rejected, is required when commencing with the recitation of the Qur’an, whether in the ritual prayer or outside of it. This is so that Satan cannot interfere with the reciter by his whisperings and prevent him from reflecting over the Qur’an and practicing its teachings.\n7. Satan has no authority and power whatsoever to mislead into disbelief those believers who have faith in Allah and His Messenger, because Allah has taken away his power over them.\n8. Abrogation of verses occured in the Qur’an during the period of its revelation for reasons, such as; to take into account overall interests, events, and changing circumstances.",
  16103:
      "We know very well that the polytheists say that it is a human teaching Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم the Quran. They are lying in their claim. The language of the person they claim is teaching him is not Arabic. In contrast, this Quran has been revealed in clear and highly eloquent Arabic. How, then, do they claim that he received it from a non-Arab?!",
  16104:
      "Those who do not believe that the verses of Allah are, in fact, from Him (may He be Exalted) will not be directed by Allah to guidance if they persist on that. They will receive a painful torment for rejecting Allah and His verses.",
  16105:
      "Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is not lying about what he brought from His Lord. Lies are made up by those who do not believe in Allah's verses because they do not fear any torment or hope for any reward. Those described as disbelievers are liars, as lying is a habit they are accustomed to.",
  16106:
      "Whoever disbelieves in Allah after believing in Him - not those who are forced to disbelieve and utter words of disbelief while their hearts are at peace with their belief [in Allah] - but rather those who embrace disbelief wholeheartedly and choose it over belief [in Allah] and utter it voluntarily then such people are apostates from Islam. The anger of Allah is on them, and in the Hereafter, they will receive a great punishment.",
  16107:
      "Such apostasy from Islam is because they preferred the trivial things of this world as compensation for their disbelief instead of the Hereafter and because Allah does not guide people who disbelieve to believe. Instead, He abandons them.",
  16108:
      "Those who are described as being apostates after believing are the ones who Allah has sealed their hearts so they do not understand the admonition, and sealed their hearing so they do not hear anything that benefits them. He has also sealed their sight so they do not see the signs indicating belief. They are the ones who are unaware of that which brings happiness and wretchedness [in the Hereafter] and the punishment that Allah has prepared for them.",
  16109:
      "Truly, they will be the losers on the Day of Resurrection, for they have lost themselves because of disbelieving after believing. Had they held onto their belief, they would have entered Paradise.",
  16110:
      "Then your Lord, O Messenger, is Forgiving and Merciful towards those vulnerable believers who emigrated from Mecca to Medina after being persecuted and tested by the polytheists to the extent that they uttered words of disbelief while their hearts were at peace with their belief [in Allah]. Then they strove in Allah's path to make the Word of Allah supreme and the word of the disbelievers lowest, and they were patient upon its difficulties. Therefore, after the persecution they underwent, your Lord is Forgiving and Merciful towards them because they only uttered words of disbelief under duress.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Concession is granted to a person under duress to utter words of disbelief whilst his heart is at peace with faith.\n2. The severe consequences for those who leave the religion in both worlds.\n3. Apostates are deserving of Allah’s anger and punishment because they preferred the life of the world over the afterlife and they are deprived of Allah’s guidance. Allah has sealed their hearts, hearing and sight and they have been made heedless of the severe punishment that will await them on the Day of Judgement.\n4. Allah has written forgiveness and mercy for those who have faith, who migrated after being persecuted and who were patient in striving in Allah’s path.",
  16111:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the Day when every person will come arguing on behalf of himself. He will not argue on anyone else's behalf due to the situation's magnitude. Every soul will be given in full the recompense for what it had done, whether good or bad, and they will not be wronged by any deduction from their good actions or addition to their evil actions.",
  16112:
      "Allah presents the example of a town, Mecca, that was secure and stable, with its people not living in fear, while people around it lived in fear. Their provisions were coming to them abundantly and easily from every direction. But then its people became unappreciative of Allah's favors upon them and did not thank Him. Allah then recompensed them with hunger and intense fear that was visible in the panic [on their faces] and the emaciation on their bodies to the extent that this became like a garment for them due to their disbelief and rejection.",
  16113:
      "And a Messenger from among them, whose honesty and truthfulness they knew, who was Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, had come to the people of Mecca. Still, they rejected what Allah had revealed to him. As a result, Allah's torment in the form of hunger and fear came on them while they were wronging themselves by taking themselves to the means of destruction: associating partners with Allah and rejecting His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  16114:
      "So eat, O slaves of Allah, of the lawful and wholesome things that Allah (may He be Exalted) has provided for you, and be thankful for the favors Allah has given you by acknowledging them and using them in a way pleasing to Allah if it is Him that you worship alone without associating partners with Him.",
  16115:
      "Allah has made it unlawful for you to consume that which died without being slaughtered according to the sacred law, [to consume] blood that spills forth from an animal at the time of slaughter, all parts of the pig, and what was slaughtered by a person as an offering to other than Allah. This prohibition applies at the time when a person has a choice. Suppose someone is forced to eat any of these forbidden types and does so without desiring the forbidden thing itself and without going beyond the limit of what is necessary. In that case, there is no sin on them. Allah is Forgiving and will forgive them for what they consume. He is Merciful in that He permitted that when it is necessary.",
  16116:
      "Do not say, O polytheists, about what your tongues describe falsely about Allah: This thing is lawful, and this thing is unlawful, to make up lies about Allah concerning making unlawful what Allah did not make unlawful, or making lawful what Allah did not make lawful. Those who make up lies about Allah will not succeed in attaining their objective and will not be saved from what they fear.",
  16117:
      "They will have a brief and insignificant enjoyment by following their desires in this world, and on the Day of Resurrection, they will receive a painful torment.",
  16118:
      "Upon mentioning the foods He has forbidden for this nation, Allah mentions what He forbade for the Jews, stating: \n We had made unlawful for the Jews what We had told you about in verse 146 of Surah Al-An'am. We did not wrong them by making that unlawful, but they wronged themselves when they committed those deeds that caused Allah's punishment to come. We thus recompensed them for their transgression, and We made that unlawful for them as a punishment upon them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has only made impure things unlawful for us out of His grace to protect us from filth.\n2. The necessity of having faith in Allah and the Messengers, of worshipping Allah alone, of thanking Him for His numerous favours and blessings and that divine punishment will afflict every person who denies Allah and goes against Him and who rejects Allah’s favours to him.\n3. The recompense corresponds to the act. When the people of the town rejected the favour, they were given the opposite instead, which was the elimination and withdrawal of the favour. They then fell into extreme hunger after satiation, and into fear and panic after security and comfort, and into a lack of resources after sufficiency.",
  16119:
      "Then your Lord, O Messenger, after their repentance, forgives the sins and is merciful towards those who do evil actions out of ignorance of the consequences even though they do so deliberately but then repent to Allah afterward and rectify their corrupt acts. Indeed, your Lord, after they repented, forgives their sins and is merciful towards them.",
  16120:
      "When the polytheists claimed to follow Abraham's religion, Allah rejected their claim, stating: \n Indeed, Abraham (peace be upon him) possessed all the attributes of goodness, always obeyed His Lord, and turned away from all other religions to the religion of Islam. He was never a polytheist.",
  16121:
      "He was thankful for the favors that Allah had given him. Allah had selected Him to be a prophet and had guided him to the true religion of Islam.",
  16122:
      "We gave him prophethood, praiseworthy mention, and pious children in this world. In the Hereafter, he will be from the righteous for whom Allah has prepared the highest ranks in Paradise.",
  16123:
      "Then, We revealed to you, O Messenger: Follow the religion of Abraham in terms of monotheism, disassociation from the polytheists, inviting towards Allah, and practicing Allah's sacred law. He turned away from all other religions to the religion of Islam. He was never a polytheist, as the polytheists claim, but he was a man of pure monotheism.",
  16124:
      "Honoring the Sabbath was only made obligatory for the Jews, who differed about it, so that they could free themselves on that day from their occupations for the sake of worship. This was after they had strayed from the day of Friday in which they were ordered to free themselves [for worship]. Your Lord, O Messenger, will judge between these people, who differ, on the Day of Resurrection about what they used to differ in. He will recompense each person with what they deserve.",
  16125:
      "Invite, O Messenger, to the religion of Islam and the believers who follow you in a manner appropriate for the person being invited and with admonition that contains encouragement and caution. Argue with them in the best manner in terms of speech, thought, and politeness, for it is not your duty to guide people. You are only required to convey the message to them. Your Lord knows best who has strayed from Islam and knows best those rightly guided to it, so do not lose yourself in grieving over them.",
  16126:
      "If you want to retaliate against your enemy, retaliate to the same degree that they harmed you and not more. But suppose you are patient and do not retaliate despite having the ability to do so. In that case, that is better for the patient amongst you than taking revenge by retaliating against them.",
  16127:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, upon the harm they afflict you. Your ability to be patient is only by Allah's guidance. Do not grieve over the disbelievers turning away from you, and do not let your heart be distressed by the schemes and plots they carry out.",
  16128:
      "Allah is with those who fear Him by abandoning sin and those who do good by doing acts of obedience and fulfilling what they have been commanded to do. Allah's help and support are with them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The permissibility of what is lawful and pure and not harmful and the prohibition of what is impure and harmful that leads to harm. All this also requires being thankful for the favour.\n2. There are four main things that are unlawful to consume in the sacred law: These are carrion, blood, pork and animals sacrificed for other than Allah such as the idols.\n3. In the case of necessity, when it is most likely that abstention will lead to loss of life, it is permitted to consume something that is prohibited.\n4. The believers are warned against resembling the disbelievers in making lawful the unlawful and declaring the lawful unlawful without evidence from the sacred law.\n5. The mercy of Allah demands that He accepts the repentance of His servants who do wrong such as disbelief and sins and then repent and reform their actions, and as a result Allah forgives them.\n6. It is good for a Muslim to take Abraham (peace be upon him) as a role model.\n7. Those inviting others to Allah’s religion must follow these three methods: Wisdom, effective counsel, and debate in the best manner.\n8. Retaliation is only allowed to be carried out to the same extent to that which one was harmed. Thus an oppressed person is prohibited from increasing the reprisal against the oppressor.\n9. In cases of life for life retaliation the law requires that the act is done in the same manner as the one who was killed-i.e. if a person used a sharp instrument or a stone to murder someone he may be killed with the same or similar object in the same way.",
  17000:
      "The Night Journey (Surah Al-Isra)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAllah's confirmation and support for His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم with clear signs and the glad tidings of victory and steadfastness.\n•    Explanation:",
  17001:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is Exalted from everything that does not befit him as He can do what none other than He can do. It is He who took His slave, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, on the night journey from the sacred masjid in Mecca to the masjid of Al Aqsa in Jerusalem, whose surroundings We have blessed with fruit, crops, and dwellings of prophets (peace be upon them), for him to see some of Our signs which show Allah's power and ability, may He be Exalted. He is the One who hears everything; no sound escapes Him, and the One who sees everything; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  17002:
      "We also gave Moses (peace be upon him) the Torah, and We made it a guide and a manual for the Israelites. Therefore, We said to them: Do not take any guardian besides me to whom you entrust your affairs. Instead, place your reliance on Me alone.",
  17003:
      "You are from the progeny of those whom We had favored with Noah (peace be upon him) by saving them from drowning in the flood. So remember this favor and thank Allah by worshipping and following Him alone. In this, follow the example of Noah, for he was very grateful to Allah.",
  17004:
      "And We told the Israelites and informed them in the Torah that indeed they will be guilty of corruption on Earth by their sin and arrogance twice, and they will rise over people with injustice and oppression, transgressing the limits in their rise.",
  17005:
      "When the first corruption occurred, We set against them slaves of Ours, possessing great might and power, who killed and displaced them. They ransacked their homes, destroying everything they passed by. Allah's promise was indeed fulfilled.",
  17006:
      "Then, once again, I gave you, O Israelites, the upper hand and dominance over those who were set against you when you repented to Allah. I supplied you with wealth after your wealth had been stolen and children after your children were taken as captives, and I made you a force outnumbering your enemies.",
  17007:
      "If you do good actions, O Israelites, in the manner that is required of you, then the compensation of that will be to your benefit, for Allah is in no need of your actions. If you do bad actions, the consequences of that will be to your detriment. Your good actions do not benefit Allah, and nor do your bad actions harm Him. When the second corruption occurs, I will set your enemies against you to humiliate you and make shame appear on your faces due to the various types of disgrace they will make you taste. They will enter Jerusalem, destroy it just as they entered and destroyed it the first time, and completely ruin all the lands they conquer.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue of the Sacred Mosque and the Farthest Mosque.\n2. Explanation of the virtue of gratitude and following in the footsteps of those prophets and Messengers who were thankful.\n3. The benefit of doing good and remaining firm on following Allah returns to the person himself. Similarly the evil of doing bad actions and going against Allah’s instructions goes back to the person himself.\n4. It is from Allah’s wisdom and practice that He sends against those who do corruption people who will stop them from that, so that Allah’s wisdom of reformation is realised.\n5. A warning to this nation against committing sin, so that they are not afflicted by what the Israelites were afflicted by. Allah’s practice is the same and does not change.",
  17008:
      "Perhaps your Lord - O Israelites - will be merciful to you after this severe reprisal if you repent to Him and do good actions. But if you revert to causing corruption a third time or more than that, I will revert to taking reprisals from you. I have made Hell a prison for the disbelievers, from which they will not find any release.",
  17009:
      "This Quran that is revealed to Muhammad (peace be on him) guides to the best way, which is the way of Islam, and it informs those who have faith in Allah and who do good deeds of that which will please them, which is that they will receive a great reward from Allah.",
  17010:
      "It informs those who do not have faith in the Day of Resurrection of what will displease them, which is that I have prepared a painful punishment for them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  17011:
      "Because of his ignorance, man prays for evil against himself, his children, and his wealth when angry, just as he prays for good for himself. If we had to answer his prayer for evil, he would be ruined, along with his children and wealth. Human beings are naturally hasty and, therefore, may hastily bring on something that is harmful.",
  17012:
      "I have created the night and the day as two signs indicating Allah's oneness and power due to their differences in terms of being long or short, hot or cold. I made the night dark for rest and sleep and the day bright so people could see and work for their livelihood. This was so that by the alternation of day and night, you could know the number of years and calculate the months, days, and hours that you require. I have explained everything in detail so that things become clear and to distinguish the truthful from the liars.",
  17013:
      "We have bound every person's destiny to their neck (Every action a person does is attached to him just as a necklace is attached to a neck). They (the person's actions) will not be detached from him until he is taken to account for them. On the Day of Resurrection, I will bring out a book for him that contains every good or bad deed that he did, which he will find spread open before him.",
  17014:
      "I will say to him on that day: O human! Read your book and take an account of your soul for your deeds. You are enough to take an account of yourself on the Day of Resurrection.",
  17015:
      "Whoever is guided to faith, then the reward of his being guided is for his own good; and whoever goes astray, the punishment for his going astray is to his detriment. No soul carries the sin of another soul, nor do I ever punish a people until I establish proof against them by sending Messengers to them.",
  17016:
      "When We decided to destroy a town because of its wrongdoing, We instructed those who became reckless because of affluence to obey Allah, but they did not comply. Instead, they disobeyed Him and transgressed, so the word of the decimating punishment became justified against them (meaning that Allah's sentence against them was passed), and We destroyed them completely.",
  17017:
      "We have destroyed many generations after Noah, such as 'Ād and Thamūd (from the nations and people of the past). Your Lord - O Messenger - is sufficient as a Knower and Seer of the sins of His slaves. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will requite them for the same.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whoever follows the guidance of the Qur’an is the most perfect, most upright and most guided of people in all his affairs.\n2. The Qur’an contains good news, warnings and the means by which the good news can be attained.\n3. Warning against praying for evil for one’s self or children.\n4. The divergence of the night and day by increasing and decreasing and by their alternation, and the light of the day and darkness of the night, are all signs of Allah’s oneness and existence and His perfect knowledge and power.\n5. The cycle of night and day makes us come to know the corresponding number of years, months and days.\n6. The day is the appropriate time for work, action and going about on earth to earn a livelihood and obtain provision.\n7. Every person’s deeds are fixed to him, whether good or bad, they are specifi and bound to him.\n8. The verses affirm the principle of individual responsibility and Allah’s justice and mercy to His servants.",
  17018:
      "Whoever desires, by doing acts of goodness, the life of this world and does not have faith in the Afterlife nor pays any attention to it, I expedite for him the luxury that I want to give him, not what he wants. Then I have made Hell for him to enter on the Day of Resurrection to suffer from its heat, being condemned for choosing this world and denying the Hereafter, banished from Allah's mercy.",
  17019:
      "But whoever desires, by doing acts of goodness, the reward of the Hereafter, and pursues it as it should be pursued, without showing off and seeking fame, while he has faith in that which Allah has made faith obligatory in; these people who have these attributes - their effort will be accepted by Allah, and He will recompense them for it.",
  17020:
      "To both these groups, the sinners and the dutiful, we freely extend the provision of your Lord, O Messenger. The provision of your Lord in this world is not withheld from anyone, whether sinner or dutiful.",
  17021:
      "O Messenger, reflect on how we favored some over others with provisions and rank in this world. Yet the Hereafter is greater in the disparity between the ranks of luxury than that of the world and greater in favors, so a believer should be eager for that.",
  17022:
      "O slave, do not set up another deity that you worship alongside Allah, or you will become condemned in the sight of Allah and His righteous slaves, and you will be forsaken by Him.",
  17023:
      "Your Lord, O slave, has instructed and made obligatory that you worship none but Him, and He has instructed that you be good to your parents, especially when they become old. If either of them or both of them reach old age with you, do not become annoyed with them by uttering words that indicate the same, do not scold them, and do not be harsh when speaking to them, but say to them kind words that are soft and courteous.",
  17024:
      "Humble yourself before them in humility and out of compassion, and say: O My Lord, be merciful to them as they have brought me up in my childhood.",
  17025:
      "Your Lord, O people, knows best what is within you of the sincere devotion to Him in worship, acts of goodness, and being dutiful to parents. If the intention in your acts of worship, treatment of your parents, and other acts is righteous, then He (may He be Exalted) is Forgiving of those who frequently turn to Him in repentance. If anyone repents from his prior failure to be dutiful to his Lord or his parents, Allah will forgive him.",
  17026:
      "O believer, give the relative his rights by keeping family ties, give to the poor and needy, and give to the traveler who is stranded. Do not spend your wealth in sin or in a wasteful manner.",
  17027:
      "Those who spend their wealth in sin and those who are wasteful in their spending are the brothers of the devils; they follow their instructions of being wasteful and extravagant, and the Devil is ever ungrateful towards His Lord, and he only does things that are sinful and only instructs that which displeases His Lord.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A person should do the good that he can and intend to do what he cannot, so that he receives the rewards for all of that.\n2. Allah’s wisdom and mercy demands that both believers and disbelievers are given provision in the world. Thus His gifts is not withheld from anyone.\n3. Having favours in the world are not to be taken as an indication of Allah’s pleasure, because worldly pleasures may be attained despite the end result being Allah’s punishment.\n4. Being good to parents is an obligatory imposition. Allah paired being grateful to them with being grateful to Him due to its great virtue.\n5. Islam forbids wastefulness, which is to spend wealth in undeserving avenues.",
  17028:
      "But if you refrain from giving to these people, due to not having anything to give them, while waiting for Allah to bless you with provision, then say to them gentle and polite words such as praying for them to have abundant provision or promising to give them if Allah grants you wealth.",
  17029:
      "Do not withhold your hand from spending, and do not be wasteful when spending; if you do, you will be blameworthy amongst the people for your miserliness, or you will become unable to spend due to your extravagant expenditure.",
  17030:
      "Your Lord expands the provision for whomever He wills and restricts it for whoever He wills based on far-reaching wisdom. He is All-Aware and Observant of His slaves. Nothing of theirs is hidden from Him, and He deals with respect to them however He wills.",
  17031:
      "Do not kill your children for fear of facing poverty in the future by spending on them; I take charge of providing for them and for you too. Killing them is a major sin, as they have done nothing wrong, and no reason necessitates them to be killed.",
  17032:
      "Beware of fornication and stay away from things that prompt it. It is an extremely detestable and evil path to traverse as it leads to the mixing of lineages and punishment from Allah.",
  17033:
      "Do not kill the soul whose life Allah has protected through faith or a pledge of security, except if the killing is merited on the basis of treason or legal retribution. If someone is killed unjustly, without a valid reason permitting his being killed, I have given his successor, who takes charge of his affairs, certain authority over the killer. He may demand that the killer be killed in retribution, forgive him without asking for anything in return, or forgive him and take the blood money. But he should not mutilate the killer, nor kill him with something he did not use to kill, nor kill someone other than the killer, even if he was a helper and supporter.",
  17034:
      "Do not transact in the property of a child whose father has passed away, except in his best interests, such as investing or preserving it until he reaches the age of mental and prudential maturity. Fulfill any pledge between yourselves and Allah, or between yourselves and His slaves, without breaking or falling short in them. Allah will question the one who made a pledge on the Day of Resurrection. Did he fulfill it? In which case, He will reward him. Or did he not fulfill it? In which case, He will punish him.",
  17035:
      "Give full measure when you measure for others, and do not cheat them. Weigh with an accurate scale that does not diminish or undervalue anything. Giving full weight and measure is better for you in this world and the Hereafter than giving short measure or weight.",
  17036:
      "Do not follow, O son of Adam, that which you have no knowledge of by following suspicions and conjecture. A person will be questioned about the good or bad that he used his hearing, sight, and heart for, and he will be rewarded for the good and punished for the bad.",
  17037:
      "Do not walk on the Earth with pride and arrogance. If you walk haughtily on Earth, you will not be able to split the Earth, nor will your stature reach the mountains in height and elevation. Why, then, are you so proud?!",
  17038:
      "O humanity, the evil of all that has been mentioned above is prohibited by your Lord. Allah is not pleased with those who perpetrate this; rather, He detests them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Noble conduct is to respond politely to relatives, to promise to give to them during times of prosperity and to offer an acceptable excuse to them.\n2. Spending that is deserving of praise is that which is moderate without stinginess or wastefulness.\n3. Allah shows more mercy to children than their parents. He therefore prohibited parents from killing their children out of fear of poverty and He took on the responsiblity of providing for all of them.\n4. The prohibition of coming close to fornication is more effective than the mere prohibition of the act itself, because that includes the prohibition of all things that lead to and prompt it.\n5. In the verses there is evidence that the right to kill is that of the close relative and retribution cannot be taken without his consent. If he forgives any right to legal retribution is lifted.\n6. It is Allah’s grace and mercy to the orphan that He instructed his guardians to take care of him and his wealth and to do what is best for it and grow it until he reaches maturity.\n7. The necessity for fairness and the just fulfilment of weight and measure without any reduction or decrease, so that blessings descend on the servant.\n8. A person will be questioned about his statements and actions.",
  17039:
      "Those instructions, prohibitions, and laws that we have explained to you are part of what your Lord has revealed to you. Do not take, O humanity, another deity together with Allah, for you will be thrown into Hell on the Day of Resurrection, blamed by yourself and by people, and banished from every good.",
  17040:
      "O you who claim that the angels are Allah's daughters! Has your Lord chosen you, O polytheists, to have male children while taking daughters from among the angels for Himself? Allah transcends far beyond what you are saying. You are saying a terrible thing about Allah by ascribing children to him and claiming that He has daughters، so persisting in your disbelief.",
  17041:
      "We have made clear in this Quran rulings, exhortations, and parables so the people may learn from them, then follow what benefits them and leave off what harms them. However, the situation of some of them whose nature has taken a step back is that it does not increase them in anything except distance from the Truth and hatred of it.",
  17042:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: If there were other deities along with Allah, as they are as a fabrication and lie, then those supposed deities would have sought a way to Allah, the Owner of the Throne, to try to defeat and contest Him over His dominion.",
  17043:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is pure and sanctified from what the polytheists attribute to Him, and He is far above what they say.",
  17044:
      "The heavens exalt Allah. The Earth exalts Allah. Every creation in the heavens and the Earth also exalts Allah. There is nothing except that it declares His purity together with His praise, but you do not comprehend their manner of exalting Him. This is because you only understand the exaltation of those who do so in your language. He is Forbearing and not quick to punish. And He forgives those who repent to Him.",
  17045:
      "When you, O Messenger, recite the Quran and they hear the warnings and admonitions it contains, I place a barrier between you and those who do not have faith in the Day of Resurrection that prevents them from understanding the Quran as a punishment for their turning away from it.",
  17046:
      "We have made covers on their hearts so that they cannot understand the Quran and heaviness in their ears so that they cannot listen to it in a beneficial manner. When you mention your Lord alone in the Quran and do not mention their so-called gods, they turn on their heels, distancing themselves from accepting Allah's pure Oneness.",
  17047:
      "I know best the way their leaders listen to the Quran. They do not want to take guidance from it, but they want to mock it and disrupt your recitation. I also know best what they secretly confer about with respect to their denial of and preventing others from it, when these people who wrong themselves by their denial say: You, O People, are only following a man who is bewitched and confused.",
  17048:
      "O Messenger, consider and be surprised at the various blameworthy attributes they describe you with. They have deviated from the truth and are confused. As a result, they cannot find the true path.",
  17049:
      "The polytheists said in denial of resurrection: When we die and become bones and our bodies decompose, will we be resurrected again? This is impossible.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The claim that the angels are Allah’s daughters is a huge fabrication and an extremely sinful statement in the sight of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.\n2. The verses of Allah only increase most people in aversion, due to their detestation for the truth and their love for the falsehood they adopt.\n3. There is not a single creation in the heavens and the earth that does not glorify Allah together with praising Him. Hence a servant should not let other creations surpass him in glorification.\n4. On account of Allah’s tolerance with His servants, He does not punish them quickly for their neglect and bad conduct. Allah’s mercy precedes His anger.\n5. The idolaters deny the occurrence of resurrection and the Hearafter.\n6. After resurrection people will consider that they only remained in the world for a brief period of time, due to the length of their stay in the Hearafter.\n7. If a person is astonished at the restoration of life to decomposed bones and fragments, it is because of his lack of comprehension, weakness of ability and a deficiency in his mental faculties.",
  17050:
      "Say, O Messenger: Become, if you can, O polytheists, as hard as stones or as strong as iron, but you will never be able to do this.",
  17051:
      "Or become some other creation greater than them, which is considered great in your hearts. Allah shall restore you just as He initiated you, and He shall bring you back to life just as He created you in the first instance. These opponents will say: Who will bring us back to life after we die? Say to them: He who created you in the first instance without any precedent shall restore you. Then they will shake their heads, mocking your response to them, and say unbelievingly: When will this restoration be? Say to them: Perhaps it is near, as everything that is coming will soon arrive.",
  17052:
      "Allah will restore you on the day when He shall call you toward the plain of resurrection. You will then respond to Him, complying with His command and praising Him, and you will think you have not stayed in the grave except for a while.",
  17053:
      "Say, O Messenger, to my believing slaves that they should say good words when speaking and refrain from bad, off-putting words because the Devil exploits them to spread between them what will spoil their worldly life and their Hereafter. Surely, the Devil is an open enemy, so it is necessary to be wary of him.",
  17054:
      "Your Lord, O people, knows you best. Nothing of yours is hidden from Him. If He wishes to have mercy on you, He will grace you with having faith and doing good deeds. And if He wishes to punish you, He can punish you by depriving you of faith, leaving you to die in disbelief. He has not sent the Messenger to be a deputy over people, to force them to believe, to stop them from disbelief, or to record their deeds. The Messenger is only a conveyor of what Allah has ordered him to convey on His behalf.",
  17055:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, has full knowledge of all who are in the heavens and Earth, and He fully knows their conditions and what they deserve. I preferred some prophets over others with their many followers and revealing books to them. And I granted David my book, the Psalms.",
  17056:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: O polytheists, call upon those you claim to be gods besides Allah when some harm befalls you. They will neither be able to remove the harm from you nor can they transfer it to someone else due to their inability. Anything incapable cannot be a god.",
  17057:
      "Those angels and others whom they call upon are themselves seeking good actions to bring them closer to Allah and competing to see who is closest to Him by obeying Him. They hope He has mercy on them, and they fear His punishment. The punishment of your Lord, O Messenger, is what should be feared.",
  17058:
      "And there is no town or city except I will send upon it punishment and destruction in this worldly life, or afflict it with a mighty punishment such as being killed, due to their disbelief. This destruction and punishment is a divine decree written in the Preserved Tablet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Humankind will not have any choice when called to come out of their graves except to comply and do as asked, and this will occur very quickly.\n2. Good speech is the origin of every good characteristic and righteous action, because whoever controls his tongue controls all his affairs.\n3. Allah elevated some prophets over others, according to His knowledge and wisdom.\n4. Allah does not intend for His servants except that which is good and He only commands them to what is beneficial for them.\n5. The sign of love for Allah is a servant’s striving to do every action which brings him closer to Allah and competing in His closeness by making all actions sincerely for Allah.\n6. Nobody besides Allah Mighty and Majestic can remove the harm of poverty, illness, affliction or anything else.",
  17059:
      "I did not stop sending tangible miracles that the polytheists requested, such as reviving the dead, except due to having sent them to previous nations, but they rejected them. I had given Thamūd a great, clear sign, namely the camel, but they rejected it, so I hastened their punishment. I do not send miracles at the hands of the Messengers except as a warning for their people so that they believe.",
  17060:
      "And remember, O Messenger, when I said to you: Your Lord has encompassed the people in His power, and they are in His control. Allah will protect you from them, so convey what you have been ordered to convey. I did not make what I clearly showed you on the Night Journey except as a test for the people; do they believe it or reject it? And I did not make the tree of Zaqqum, which is mentioned in the Quran as growing from the bottom of the Inferno, except as a test for them. Thus, if they do not believe in these signs, they will never believe in anything else. I frighten them by sending signs, but they do not increase through them except in disbelief and descending further into misguidance.",
  17061:
      "And remember, O Messenger, when I said to the angels: Prostrate to Adam, as a prostration of greeting, not worship, so they complied and all prostrated to him. However, Iblis refused to prostrate to him out of arrogance, saying: Should I prostrate to the one You created out of clay, whereas You created me out of Fire? I am better than him.",
  17062:
      "Iblis said to his Lord: Do you see this creature You have honored above me by ordering me to prostrate to him? If You keep me alive until the end of this worldly life, I shall allure his children and misguide them from Your straight path, except for a few whom You have saved and are Your chosen slaves.",
  17063:
      "His Lord said to him: Go with those amongst them who obey you because Hell is your recompense and their recompense; a complete and full compensation for your actions.",
  17064:
      "And mislead those whom you can mislead through your voice, which calls to disobedience. Call out to them through your horsemen and foot soldiers who invite them towards your obedience. Become a partner to them in their wealth by making every action that opposes the sacred law attractive, and become a partner to them in their children by falsely making a claim to them, attaining them through adultery, and making them worship others besides Allah when naming them. Make attractive to them false promises and futile aspirations; the Devil only makes false promises that deceive them.",
  17065:
      "You have no control, O Iblis, over My believing slaves who act in My obedience because Allah has repelled your evil from them. Allah is sufficient as a guardian for one who relies upon Him in his affairs.",
  17066:
      "Your Lord, O people, is the One who makes the ships sail for you in the sea in the hope that you seek your sustenance through the profits from trade and the like. He is Merciful to you as He facilitated these means for you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is from Allah’s mercy that He does not send the signs which the deniers request, so that Allah does not punish them immediately if they deny them.\n2. Allah tests the servants through the satan, who calls them through his speech and actions towards disobeying Allah.\n3. One form of the satan becoming a partner to man with respect to wealth and children is to not mention Allah’s name when eating, drinking and having intercourse, and not to teach one’s children manners.",
  17067:
      "And when you are afflicted, O polytheists, by some calamity or misfortune at sea such that you fear destruction, those you worship besides Allah leave your thoughts, and you only remember Allah and seek His assistance. Then, when He assists you and saves you from your fears, and you return to land, you turn away from His Oneness and from supplicating to Him alone, returning to your idols. Humanity is constantly rejecting the blessings of Allah.",
  17068:
      "So do you feel secure, O polytheists, when Allah has delivered you safely to land that He will not make it collapse beneath you? Or do you feel secure that He will not make stones rain down on you as He did with the people of Lot? Then, you will not find any protector to protect you nor any helper to save you from being destroyed.",
  17069:
      "Or do you feel secure that Allah will not return you to sea again and send a strong wind upon you, drowning you because you are ungrateful for Allah's blessings after He saved you the first time? Then, you will not find any claimant against Him for what He did to you to defend you.",
  17070:
      "And I have honored the children of Adam through intellect, making the angels prostrate to their father, and I subjugated for them the animals and vehicles that carry them on land and the ships that carry them by sea. I provided them with good food, drink, spouses, and other things and granted them much virtue over many of My creation. Therefore, they must be grateful for Allah's favors upon them.",
  17071:
      "And remember, O Messenger, when every group will be called out by their leader whom they used to follow in life. So whoever is given his book of deeds in his right hand will read their books happily, and nothing will be decreased from their reward, even if it is as tiny as the thread on a date seed.",
  17072:
      "And whoever's heart is blind to accepting and submitting to the truth in this worldly life will be more blind on the Day of Resurrection, not finding guidance to the path of paradise and straying from the path of guidance. The reward will be appropriate for the deed.",
  17073:
      "And the polytheists were about to turn you away, O Messenger, from the Quran I revealed to you so that you invent something else in my name which conforms to their desires. And if you did what they wanted, they would have chosen you as their beloved friend.",
  17074:
      "And had I not favored you by making you firm on the truth, you were about to incline towards them slightly and then agree with them in what they requested of you due to their severe deception and scheming, alongside your extreme eagerness for them to have faith. However, I protected you from inclining towards them.",
  17075:
      "And had you inclined towards them in what they requested you, I would have given you multiplied punishment in this life and the Hereafter, then you would not find any helper to assist you against Me and avert the punishment from you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Humans are ungrateful for Allah’s favours, except the one whom Allah guides.\n2. Every nation will be called to its religion and book, to see if they practiced upon it or not. Allah does not punish anyone except after the proof against him has been established and he has opposed it.\n3. Good people will be given their book of deeds in their right hand and they will have great happiness and joy, whilst the opposite will be of bad people.\n4. The hatred of the wrongdoers and deniers towards the Messengers and their inheritors is apparent, due to the truth they carry, but it is not towards them personally.\n5. Allah protected the Prophet from the causes of evil and from people, making him firm and guiding him to the straight path. His followers also enjoy this according to how well they follow him.",
  17076:
      "And the disbelievers were close to troubling you, due to their enmity towards you, by exiling you from Mecca. However, Allah stopped them from exiling you until you yourself migrated on the command of your Lord. And had they exiled you, they would not have remained after exiling you except for a short while.",
  17077:
      "The issue of their not remaining after you except for a short while is Allah's established practice with respect to the Messengers before you, namely that whenever a Messenger was exiled by his people, Allah sent punishment upon them. And you will not find, O Messenger, any change in my practice, but rather, you will find it to be established and constant.",
  17078:
      "Establish the prayer by performing it in a complete manner in its times, which are the declining of the sun from the middle of the sky (this includes the Dhuhr and Asr prayers) until the darkness of night (this includes the Maghrib and Isha prayers). And establish the Fajr prayer, lengthening the recitation therein, as the Fajr prayer is attended by the angels of the night and the angels of day.",
  17079:
      "And in part of the night, O Messenger, stand and pray, so that your prayer increases your rank, seeking for your Lord to raise you on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for the people from the horrors of the Day of Resurrection, and so that you attain the position of the major intercession, for which all from the first to the last will praise you.",
  17080:
      "Say, O Messenger: O my Lord, make all my entrances and exits in Your obedience and for Your pleasure, and give me from Yourself a clear proof through which You help me against my enemy.",
  17081:
      "And say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Islam has come, the help has come as Allah promised, and idolatry and disbelief have gone. Surely, falsehood is going and will disappear, unable to remain in the face of truth.",
  17082:
      "I reveal in the Quran that which cures the hearts from ignorance, disbelief, and doubt, and cures the bodies when treated through it, and that which is a mercy for the believers who act upon it. And this Quran only increases the disbelievers in destruction, as listening to it angers them and makes them deny and turn away from it even more.",
  17083:
      "And when I grant man a blessing such as health and wealth, he turns away from thanking Allah and obeying Him and moves further away out of pride. But when illness, poverty, or the like befalls him, he becomes extremely despondent and loses hope of Allah's mercy.",
  17084:
      "Say, O Messenger: Every man acts on the path that resembles his condition in either guidance or misguidance. But your Lord knows best who is most guided towards the truth.",
  17085:
      "O Messenger, the disbelievers among the People of the Book ask you regarding the reality of the soul. Say to them: The soul is from the command of my Lord. And the knowledge you and all the creation of Allah have been granted is little in comparison to the knowledge of Allah.",
  17086:
      "By Allah, if We wanted to take away, O Messenger, the revelation We sent to you by erasing it from the hearts and books, We could take it away, then you would not find anyone to help you and take the responsibility to bring it back.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The unchanging custom of Allah with all nations is that every nation which rejected its Messenger and exiled him was quickly punished by Allah.\n2. These verses prove how needy the servant is of Allah making him steadfast, and that he should always earnestly praise his Lord to keep him firm upon faith.\n3. When the truth manifests, falsehood vanishes. Falsehood does not rise except in times and places where the people of truth become complacent.\n4. The cure contained within the Qur’an includes curing the hearts of doubts, ignorance, incorrect ideas, deviation and evil objectives.\n5. These verses prove that if a person is asked regarding a matter which is not beneficial to the questioner, it is better to avoid answering it, and instead tell him what he needs and guide him to what will benefit him.",
  17087:
      "However, We did not take it away by way of mercy from your Lord, and We left it preserved. Surely, your Lord's grace on you is great, as He made you a Messenger, sealed the prophets upon you, and revealed the Quran to you.",
  17088:
      "When the polytheists used the excuse that this Quran is similar to human speech and proposed changing it, Allah challenged them to come up with something like it, stating: \n Say, O Messenger: If all of humanity and jinn united to bring the like of this Quran which was revealed to you, in its eloquence, excellent sequence, and pure style, they would never be able to bring anything like it, even if they were to all assist and help one another.",
  17089:
      "And I have explained to people in this Quran and brought all types of advice, reminders, commands, prohibitions, and stories they can take lessons from, in the hope they will believe. But most people have refused all except to reject and deny this Quran.",
  17090:
      "When they were unable to do so, they began proposing what they considered impossible, suggesting the following: \n The polytheists said: We will never believe you until you extract a spring from the ground of Mecca for us that does not stop flowing.",
  17091:
      "Or you have a garden with many flowers in which you make rivers flow profusely.",
  17092:
      "Or you make the sky fall upon us, as you mentioned, as fragments of punishment, or you bring Allah and the angels visibly before us so they can testify to the truth of what you claim.",
  17093:
      "Or you have a house adorned with gold and other things, or you ascend to the sky. And if you do ascend to it, we will never believe you have been sent unless you come down with a book written by Allah in which we can read that you are Allah's Messenger. Say, O Messenger: My Lord is pure; I am only a human Messenger like all other Messengers. I do not have the ability to bring anything, so how can I bring what you have requested?",
  17094:
      "The only thing that stopped the disbelievers from believing in Allah and His Messengers and acting upon what the Messenger brought was their refusal to accept that a Messenger can be from humanity, as they said denyingly: Did Allah send a Messenger from humanity?",
  17095:
      "Say, O Messenger, in response to them: Had there been angels on Earth who reside therein and walk about securely, as is your condition, we would have sent an angel Messenger to them from their own kind because it is he who can make them understand what he has been sent with. It would not be wise to send them a Messenger from humanity; likewise this is the case with you.",
  17096:
      "Say, O Messenger: Allah is sufficient as a witness between you and me that I am a Messenger who has been sent to you, and I have conveyed what I was sent with to you. Surely, He encompasses and is fully aware of the conditions of His slaves, nothing of them being hidden from Him, and He sees all the secrets of their selves.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has clearly explained in the Qur’an everything that can serve as a lesson, such as advice, reminders, commands, prohibitions and stories, in the hope they will believe.\n2. The Qur’an is the Word of Allah and the everlasting miracle of the Prophet, and nobody can ever bring anything like it.\n3. The extreme stubbornness of the idolaters towards the Prophet and their lack of faith in him have been explained.\n4. It is part of Allah’s mercy on His servants that He sent towards them humans from amongst them, because they are unable to acquire from the angels.\n5. Part of Allah’s testimony for His Messenger are the miracles He aided him with, the verses He revealed to him, and His assisting him against his enemies and opponents.",
  17097:
      "And whoever Allah grants guidance to is truly guided. Whoever He removes from it and leads astray, you will never find for them, O Messenger, protectors to guide them to the truth, repel harm from them, and bring them benefit. I will gather them on the Day of Resurrection, being dragged on their faces, not seeing, speaking, or hearing. Their abode towards which they will go is Hell. Whenever the flames begin to subside, I will make them burn even more.",
  17098:
      "That punishment which they will meet is their recompense due to their denial of my signs which were sent down upon (given to) my Messengers, and because they said, considering resurrection to be improbable: When we die and turn into decomposed bones and scattered particles, will we be resurrected after this as a new creation?",
  17099:
      "When they mentioned what they obstinately cling to in order to deny the Resurrection, Allah responded to them by stating: \n Do these deniers of the resurrection not know that Allah, who created the heavens and who created the Earth despite their greatness, has the power to create the likes of them? So, whoever has the power to create something great has the power to create something smaller. And Allah has given them limited time in this world in which their lives will come to an end, and He has made a time for their resurrection in which there is no doubt. But despite the proofs for resurrection being clear, the polytheists refuse all except to reject the resurrection.",
  17100:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: If you possessed my Lord's treasures of mercy which never deplete or finish, you would abstain from spending them, fearing they would run out, making you turn poor. And it is human nature to be miserly, except if one is a believer who spends hoping for Allah's reward.",
  17101:
      "When the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم faced the rejection that he faced from the polytheists, his solace came through the story of Moses with Pharoah and his people. Allah states: \n I granted Moses nine clear proofs, which bore testimony for him. They are the staff, the hand, the famine, the decrease in fruits, the hurricane, locusts, lice, frogs, and blood. O Messenger, ask the Jews about when Moses brought these miracles to their predecessors, and Pharaoh said: I consider you, O Moses, a man afflicted by magic, as you bring strange things.",
  17102:
      "Moses said in response to him: O Pharaoh, you know for sure that these signs have not been sent except by Allah, the Lord of the heavens and the Earth. He has sent them as proofs of His power and the truthfulness of His Messenger. But you have rejected them. And I know, O Pharaoh, that you are going to be a destroyed loser.",
  17103:
      "So Pharaoh intended to punish Moses (peace be upon him) and his people by exiling them from Egypt, so I destroyed him and all the armies with him by drowning them.",
  17104:
      "And I said to the Israelites after destroying Pharaoh and his armies: Settle in the land of the Levant. Then, when the Day of Resurrection comes, I shall bring you all to the plain of gathering for the reckoning.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah alone is responsible for guidance and misguidance. Whoever He guides is truly guided, and whoever He misguides and abandons has nobody to guide him.\n2. The abode of the disbelievers and their residence is Hell. Whenever its fire will cool, Allah will increase it with burning fire.\n3. It is necessary to hold firm to Allah when the transgressors and tyrants are threatened.\n4. The transgressors and tyrants resort to using dominance and power when they face the people of truth, because they are unable to face them with proof and explanation.",
  17105:
      "With truth, I revealed the Quran to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, and with truth, it came down upon him without any change or tampering. And I did not send you, O Messenger, except to give glad tidings of paradise to the God-fearing and to warn the disbelievers and those who are sinful of the Fire.",
  17106:
      "I sent it as a Quran, which I have divided into parts and explained in the hope that you read it to people slowly and carefully, as this is more effective for understanding and reflecting. And I revealed it part by part according to incidents and conditions.",
  17107:
      "Say, O Messenger: Believe in it, for your belief will not increase it in any way (will not benefit it), or do not believe in it, for your disbelief will not decrease it in any way (harm it in any way). Surely, those who read the previous divine books and understand the revelation and prophecy when the Quran is recited to them fall on their faces, prostrating to Allah out of gratitude.",
  17108:
      "And they say in their prostration: Our Lord will never break His promise. The promise He made of sending Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is going to happen. Surely, our Lord's promise of this and other matters will definitely occur.",
  17109:
      "They fall on their faces, prostrating to Allah and crying in awe of Him. Listening to the Quran and contemplating its meanings increases their submission to Allah and awe of Him.",
  17110:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who criticize you for supplicating by saying, 'O Allah, O Merciful': Allah and the Merciful are names of His, so supplicate to Him with either of them or other names of His. For Him are all beautiful names, and these two are amongst them, so supplicate to Him through these two or His other beautiful names. Do not recite loudly in your prayer in case the polytheists hear you, and do not recite so quietly that the believers cannot hear you, but rather choose a middle path between the two.",
  17111:
      "Say - O Messenger: All praise is for Allah, who deserves all types of praise and who is exalted from having a child or a partner; thus, He has no partner in His kingdom. And He is not afflicted by disgrace or weakness; hence, He has no need for anyone to help and support Him. So exalt Him abundantly, and do not attribute any child or partner to Him nor any helper or supporter.",
  18000:
      "The Cave (Surah Al-Kahf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining the manner of dealing with trials and tribulations.\n•    Explanation:",
  18001:
      "Praise - with the attributes of perfection and majesty and for the apparent and hidden favors - is for Allah alone, who revealed the Quran to His slave and Messenger and did not put any crookedness or diversion from the truth in this Quran.",
  18002:
      "Rather, He made it upright without any contradiction or discrepancy in it to frighten those who deny the truth of a severe punishment that awaits them from Allah and to tell the believers who do good actions that which will please them, namely that there is a good reward for them which no other reward compares to.",
  18003:
      "(The believers will be) Living in this reward forever, without it being cut off from them.",
  18004:
      "And it frightens the Jews, Christians, and some of the polytheists who said: Allah has taken a son.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah revealed the Qur’an which comprises truth, justice, the sacred law and the best rule.\n2. It is permissible to cry in prayer out of fear of Allah.\n3. Supplication or recitation in prayer should be moderate between being loud and silent.\n4. The noble Qur’an comprises every good action which leads to what makes the souls happy and joyous.",
  18005:
      "These fabricators have no knowledge nor evidence for their claim that Allah has a son, and nor did their fathers whom they followed in this regard have any knowledge. This statement, which has escaped their mouths without any understanding, is heinous. They only speak a lie that has no basis or support.",
  18006:
      "Then perhaps, O Messenger, you will end up destroying yourself out of grief and remorse if they do not believe this Quran. But do not do this, as making them accept guidance is not your responsibility; you are only responsible for conveying it.",
  18007:
      "Surely, I have made the creation on the face of this Earth an adornment for it, so I can test them to see which of them does the best actions, which please Allah, and which of them is worst in actions, so that I may reward everyone with what they deserve.",
  18008:
      "And I am going to turn the creation on the face of this Earth into dust free from vegetation, and this will be after the lifespan of the creation on Earth expires, so let them take heed of this.",
  18009:
      "Do not think, O Messenger, that the story of the people of the cave and the tablet on which their names were written are from our amazing signs. In fact, other signs, such as creating the heavens and Earth, are more amazing.",
  18010:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when the believing youngsters took refuge in the cave, fleeing with their religion. Then they said in their supplication to their Lord: O Our Lord, give us mercy from Yourself by forgiving our sins and saving us from our enemies and grant us guidance towards the right path and correctness in the matter of migrating from the disbelievers and having faith.",
  18011:
      "Then after they went and took refuge in the cave, We put a barrier on their ears from hearing, and We put them to sleep for many years.",
  18012:
      "Then, after their lengthy sleep, We woke them up to demonstrate which of the two groups disputing their duration of stay in the cave knows this duration best.",
  18013:
      "We are informing you, O Messenger, of their affair truthfully and without any doubt. Surely, they were youngsters who believed in their Lord and obeyed Him, and We increased them in guidance and firmness on the truth.",
  18014:
      "And We strengthened their hearts with faith and firmness on it, and to be patient in leaving one's homeland for its sake, when they stood to proclaim their faith in Allah alone in front of the disbelieving king, and they said: The Lord we believe in and worship is the Lord of the heavens and Earth. We will never worship the gods you have falsely claimed besides Him. We will have said an unjust and far-off statement if we worship others besides Him.",
  18015:
      "Then they turned to each other, saying: These are our people who have taken deities which they worship besides Allah. They do not have any clear proof for worshipping them, so there is no greater oppressor than one who falsely attributes a partner to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One who calls to Allah must convey and strive to the best of his ability, whilst relying on Allah in this regard. If people are guided, it is good, but he should not grieve or regret if they do not.\n2. Knowledge of the duration the people of the cave stayed shows precise counting and recognising the complete power, wisdom and mercy of Allah.\n3. The verses contain clear proof for fleeing with one’s religion and leaving one’s family, children, relatives, friends, home and wealth out of fear of trials.\n4. It is important to pay attention to proper upbringing of the youth, as they are more pure-hearted and enthusiastic, and they are responsible for the revival of nations.\n5. The youngsters combined between affirming Allah alone being the Lord and He alone being worthy of worship, and they maintained this. This is the biggest proof of their recognising Allah perfectly and Allah increasing them in guidance.",
  18016:
      "Now that you have moved away from your people and have left what they worship instead of Allah, and you have worshipped Allah alone, take refuge in the cave, fleeing to protect your religion. Allah (may He be Exalted) will shower His mercy on you to protect you from your enemies and make for you an easy means of livelihood that you could benefit from in place of the life you had when living amongst your people.",
  18017:
      "They thus fulfilled the instruction, and Allah put them to sleep and protected them from their enemy. You - O one who looks at them - will see the sun when it rises from the east, inclining away from their cave to the right of one entering it; and at the time of sunset, it moves away from the cave towards the left but does not strike it directly. Therefore, they are in perpetual shade, unaffected by the sun's heat. They are in a wide space within the cave where the air they require reaches them. The abovementioned occurrences, namely, their taking refuge in the cave, their being put to sleep, the sun's deviation from them, the spaciousness in the cave, and their salvation from their people, are all wondrous acts of Allah that indicate His power. Whoever Allah guides to the path of guidance is truly guided. Whoever Allah forsakes and lets go astray, you will never find anyone to help and guide him to the right path. This is because guidance is in Allah's Hand and not in his.",
  18018:
      "You - O one who looks at them - will think they are awake because their eyes are open, though, in actual fact, they are asleep. I turn them over in their sleep, sometimes to the right and sometimes to the left, so that the earth does not consume their bodies. Their dog that accompanied them stretches out its forelegs at the entrance of the cave. If you had come across them and seen them, you would have turned and run away, being afraid of them, and you would have been filled with fear of them.",
  18019:
      "Just as I did to them the wondrous acts that I have mentioned, I awakened them after a long period of time, and they began to ask one another about the period that they had spent asleep. One of them responded: I remained asleep for one day or part of one day. One of them, to whom it was not clear how long they had spent asleep, responded: Your Lord knows best about the period you had remained asleep, so entrust the knowledge of that to Him and get busy with what concerns you. Send one of you with these silver coins to the city we know and let him see which of the inhabitants of that city are most pure in their food and earnings. He should proceed cautiously when entering and leaving and dealing with them. He must also be tactful and not let anyone find out where you are because that will result in great harm.",
  18020:
      "If your people discover you and find out where your whereabouts are, they will kill you by stoning you, or they will force you to return to their deviated creed that you used to follow before Allah favored you by guiding you to the true religion. If you return to that, you will never succeed - not in this world nor in the Hereafter. Instead, you will suffer a great loss in both places on account of your leaving the true religion to which Allah had guided you and your returning to that deviated creed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It was out of Allah’s wisdom and power that He turned them onto their sides, right and left, so that the earth does not spoil their bodies. This is a lesson from Allah to His servants.\n2. The permissibility of using dogs when needed for hunting or guarding.\n3. The benefit a person derives from keeping company with good and righteous people even if he is lesser than them in status. The mention of the dog was preserved because it had accompanied people of virtue.\n4. The verses indicate the legitimacy of appointing a proxy and to be diplomatic and gentle when dealing with people.",
  18021:
      "Just as I did those wondrous acts of putting them to sleep and awakening them after many years, which shows Our Power, We caused them to be discovered by the people of their city so that those people would know that the promise of Allah to help the believers and of resurrection [from the graves] is true and that the [Day of] Resurrection is coming without a doubt. After the matter of the people of the cave was exposed, and they had passed away, those who discovered them differed: What should they do with regard to them? One group said: Build over the entrance of the cave a building that will conceal and preserve them. Their Lord knows best about their condition, and their condition requires that they have some special status with Him. The influential people who did not have knowledge or a proper call said: We will set up over them a place of worship in their honor and as a memoir of their location.",
  18022:
      "Some of those who delve into their incident will say about their number: They were three, and their dog was the fourth among them. Others will say: They were five, and their dog was the sixth amongst them. Both groups only said this as a guess without any proof. Some of them will say: They were seven, and their dog was the eighth among them. Say, O Messenger: Your Lord knows best about their number. No one knows their number except for a few people whom Allah has informed about their number. So do not dispute with regard to their number or any other matter of theirs with the people of the scripture or with others except with an obvious argument and without delving into the matter, limiting it to the revelation that has come down to you with respect to them. Do not ask any of them about the details of their matter because they do not know about it.",
  18023:
      "Do not say, O Prophet, about anything that you want to do tomorrow, \"I am going to do this tomorrow,\" because you do not know whether you will do it or you will be prevented from doing so. This is a directive for every Muslim.",
  18024:
      "Unless you suspend doing so on Allah's will by saying: I will do it - if Allah wills - tomorrow. Remember your Lord by saying: \"If Allah wills\" - if you forget to say it - and say: I have hope that my Lord will guide me to something closer than this in guidance and success.",
  18025:
      "The people of the cave remained in their cave for three hundred and nine years.",
  18026:
      "Say, O Messenger: Allah knows best about how long they remained in the cave, and He has told us about the period they remained there. No statement can be considered after Allah's; May He be Exalted. To Him alone (may He be Exalted) belongs everything hidden in the heavens and on Earth. He created and knows all of it. How well He sees! May He be Exalted! He sees everything. How well He hears! He hears everything. They have no one to take charge of their matter besides Him. He does not share His rule with anyone. He alone passes judgment.",
  18027:
      "After mentioning that dominion belongs to Allah alone, He commands His messenger to recite what was revealed to him about Allah's sovereignty and the obligation to follow Him, stating: \n Read, O Messenger, and implement what Allah has revealed to you in the Quran. Nothing can change His words because they are completely true and just. You will not find any refuge to resort to or place of protection to take cover in beside Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Setting up places of worship over graves, praying in them and building on them is not permissible in our sacred law.\n2. In the story there is evidence of Allah’s power to gather and resurrect bodies from their graves and take them to account.\n3. The verses indicate that a commendable dispute and debate has the attribute of being in a manner that is best.\n4. The practice and etiquette in the sacred law is to suspend future matters on Allah’s will.",
  18028:
      "Remain close to your poor companions who sincerely call on their Lord in worship and supplication at the beginning and the end of the day. Do not let your eyes overlook them, intending to sit with people of affluence and prestige. Do not follow the one whose heart I have made neglectful of Our remembrance by sealing it and who instructed you to remove the poor from your gathering, giving preference to following his desire over following His Lord. His actions and deeds are thus foolish, excessive, and in vain.",
  18029:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who neglect Allah's remembrance due to the heedlessness of their hearts: What I have brought to you is the truth. It is from Allah and not from me. I cannot accede to your request to chase away the believers. Whoever amongst you wishes to have faith in this truth, then let him do so, for he will be pleased with the reward. Whoever amongst you wants to reject it, let him do so, for he will be grieved by the punishment that awaits him. We have prepared for those who wrong themselves by choosing disbelief, a huge fire whose walls will surround them, and as a result, they will not be able to escape from it. If they were to seek water as relief from the severe thirst they experience, they would be given water like murky oil that will be extremely hot and scald their faces due to its heat. What a terrible drink this drink is that will be provided for their relief! It will not quench their thirst but will make it worse, and it will not put out the flames burning their faces. What a miserable destination and place of residence is the Fire!",
  18030:
      "When Allah mentions the punishment that He has prepared for the transgressors, He mentions the generous reward that He has prepared for the believers, stating: \n Those who believe in Allah and do righteous actions have done well in what they have done and will receive a huge reward. We do not let the reward of those who do good go to waste. Instead, we give them their reward in full without any reduction.",
  18031:
      "Those who are described as having faith and doing righteous actions will receive gardens to reside in, with the sweet rivers of paradise flowing beneath their homes. They will be adorned with bracelets of gold and wear green garments of fine and thick silk. They will recline on couches decorated with beautiful coverings. Theirs will be an excellent reward, and paradise will be an excellent home and place for them to reside in.",
  18032:
      "Upon mentioning the recompense of the transgressors and believers, He gives a parable for both, stating: \n O Messenger, give an example of two men: a disbeliever and a believer. We gave the disbeliever two gardens of grapes, surrounding them with date palms, and in the vacant parts of the land, we caused crops to grow.",
  18033:
      "Each garden produced its fruit of dates, grapes, and crops and did not fall short thereof in anything but bore it in full. We caused a river to flow between the two gardens so that they could be irrigated easily.",
  18034:
      "The owner of the two gardens had other wealth and fruit, and he said to his friend, as he spoke to him in conceit to make an impact on him: I have more wealth than you, more support, and a stronger family.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue of keeping company with good people and applying self-restraint to be in their company and mixing with them even if they are poor, for being in their company carries innumerable benefits.\n2. Islam is a religion of equality. There is no difference in the law between a person of high-standing and one of low-standing, rich and poor and a leader and his subordinates.\n3. Two principles for reward and the basis of salvation: Faith and righteous action, because Allah based reward in the world and the afterlife on these two things.",
  18035:
      "The disbeliever entered his garden along with the believer to show it to him whilst he was wronging himself by his disbelief and conceit. The disbeliever said: I do not think that this garden that you see will ever perish because I have taken all measures for its survival.",
  18036:
      "I also do not think that the resurrection will occur. Life will simply continue. If it does occur and I happen to be resurrected and returned to my Lord, then I will find that what I will go back to after resurrection will be better than this garden of mine. My being rich in this world means that I will be rich after the resurrection as well.",
  18037:
      "His believing friend said to him whilst having this conversation: Do you reject the One who created your father, Adam, from dust? Then He created you from sperm. Then He made you into a male human being and proportioned your limbs, making you complete? The One who has the power to do all of that is able to resurrect you.",
  18038:
      "But I do not profess this statement of yours. I simply say: He, Allah (may He be Exalted), is my Lord, who has showered us with His blessings, and I do not associate anyone with Him in worship.",
  18039:
      "If only, when you entered your garden, you had said: Whatever Allah wills. No one has any power except through Allah. He is the One who does as He pleases, and He is the One of strength. If you regard me as someone poorer than you and one with fewer children,",
  18040:
      "I anticipate that Allah will give me something better than your garden and that He will send upon your garden a punishment from the sky, making it a barren piece of land on which feet will slip due to it being so smooth.",
  18041:
      "Or its water may sink so deep into the ground that you will never be able to reach it again in any way. Once the water sinks deep, the garden will not survive.",
  18042:
      "What the believer anticipated occurred. Destruction engulfed the fruit of the disbeliever's garden. The disbeliever began wringing his hands on account of extreme regret and remorse over the money that he had spent on its maintenance and upkeep. As the garden had fallen over the supports on which the grapevines were spread out, he said: I wish I had believed in my Lord alone, and I had not associated anyone with Him in worship.",
  18043:
      "This disbeliever had no group to protect him from the punishment that fell on him, whereas he was the one who used to boast about his group. He himself, too, could not stop Allah from destroying his garden.",
  18044:
      "In that situation, victory is for Allah alone. He (may He be Exalted) is best in rewarding His allies who have faith, as He multiplies the reward for them, and He is best in outcome for them.",
  18045:
      "O Messenger, give an example for those who are deceived by the world. In its temporality and fleeting existence, it is similar to rainwater that We sent down from the sky. On account of this water, the vegetation of the Earth grew and ripened. Then this vegetation is broken down into pieces, the wind carries it away to far-lying places, and the Earth once again becomes as it was previously. Allah has full power over all of that. Nothing is outside His ability. He gives life to whatever He wishes and causes whatever He wishes to perish.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A believer must not surrender before the might of a wealthy disbeliever. He must advise and guide him to have faith in Allah, acknowledge of His Oneness and be grateful for His favours and blessings on him.\n2. Any person impressed by any of his possessions or children must attribute the blessing to the One who bestowed it on him by saying: As Allah wills. There is no power except through Allah.\n3. When Allah intends good for a person He gives him an early punishment in the world.\n4. The permissiblity of praying for the ruin of the wealth of a person whose wealth is the cause for his transgression, rejection and loss.\n5. The result of Allah’s assistance or the lack thereof will only become clear when the dust settles and retribution is due. This is when those who had worked will find their reward.\n6. Wealth and children are of no use if they do not assist a person in following Allah.\n7. The temporality and fleeting nature of the world. Allah alone is the Everlasting, Who has the power to create, destroy and revive everything.",
  18046:
      "Wealth and children are things of adornment in this worldly life. Wealth will only be of benefit in the Afterlife if it is spent on that which pleases Allah. Actions and statements that are pleasing to Allah are better in reward than all the beauty in the world. That is the best thing a person can have hope in because the beauty of the world will perish while the reward for actions and statements that are pleasing to Allah will last.",
  18047:
      "Remember the day when I will remove the mountains from their places, and you will see the Earth as an open plain as all the mountains, trees, and buildings on it will be gone. I will gather all created things together and resurrect them, leaving no one.",
  18048:
      "People will be presented to your Lord in rows, and He will hold them to account. It will be said to them: Now you have come to Us individually, barefoot and naked, as We created you the first time, although you claimed that you would never be resurrected and that We will not set for you a time and place in which We will recompense you for your actions.",
  18049:
      "The book of deeds will be placed. Some people will take the book in their right hand, and some will take it in their left hand. You, O man, will see the disbelievers fearful of its contents because they are aware of the disbelief and sins that they sent forward. They will say: May we be destroyed! What is with this book that leaves no action of ours, small or big, but it has recorded and enumerated it? They will find all the sins they had done in their worldly life written and recorded. Your Lord, O Messenger, does not wrong anyone. He does not punish anyone for no reason, and He does not reduce the reward of those who follow Him.",
  18050:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when We told the angels to prostrate to Adam as a salutation. So all of them prostrated to him in fulfillment of the command of their Lord except Iblis. He was one of the Jinn and was not an angel. He refused and was too proud to prostrate. Thus he went against following His Lord. Will you, O people, then take him and his children as friends with whom you ally yourselves instead of Me while they are your enemies? How do you take your enemies to be your friends? How bad and ugly is the act of the wrongdoers who make the Devil their friend instead of befriending Allah?!",
  18051:
      "Those you have taken as friends instead of Me are all slaves like you. I did not make them witness the creation of the heavens and the Earth when I created them. In fact, they did not even exist then. I did not make some of them witness the creation of others. I am alone in creation and planning. I would not take those human and jinn devils who lead others astray as My assistants, as I am in no need of any assistants.",
  18052:
      "Mention to them, O Messenger, the Day of Resurrection, when Allah will say to those who had associated partners with Him in the worldly life: Call My partners whom you claimed were partners to Me so that they can help you. They will call them, but they will not answer their call, and they will not come to their assistance. We will place between the worshippers and those whom they worshipped a pit of destruction, which will be for both groups, and this is the Fire.",
  18053:
      "The polytheists will see the Fire, and they will be completely certain that they are going to fall into it. They will not find any place to escape from it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A servant must do a lot of lasting good works, which refers to any righteous statement or action that lasts till the Hear- after.\n2. A servant must remember the terrors of the Day of Judgment and work for this day so that he can be saved from its terrors and enjoy the favours of Allah’s paradise and pleasure.\n3. Allah honoured our father, Adam (peace be upon him), and the human race as a whole by instructing the angels to prostrate to him when he was first created as a sign of honour and as a salutation.\n4. The verses exhort to treating Satan as an enemy.",
  18054:
      "We have explained in different ways, in this Quran that was revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, many types of examples so that they will take a lesson and pay heed. But the most apparent thing in man, especially the disbeliever, is to argue wrongfully.",
  18055:
      "Nothing prevented the obstinate disbelievers from having faith in what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought from his Lord. Lack of explanation did not prevent them from seeking Allah's forgiveness for their sins, for many examples were given to them in the Quran, and clear proof came to them. The only thing that prevented them was their stubborn request for the punishment of the previous communities to be imposed on them and for them to see the punishment that they were promised.",
  18056:
      "We do not send any of Our Messengers except to give good news to the people of faith and obedience and to warn the people of disbelief and disobedience. They do not have the authority to make hearts accept the guidance. Those who disbelieved in Allah dispute with the Messengers despite their having clear proof in an attempt to use their falsehood to remove the truth that was sent down to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. They took the Quran and what they were warned of as a joke and mocked it.",
  18057:
      "There is no one more oppressive than the person who was reminded of the verses of his Lord, did not pay any attention to the threat of punishment contained therein, and turned away from taking a lesson, forgetting the disbelief and sins he had done in his worldly life without repenting. We have placed covers on the hearts of people with this description that prevent them from understanding the Quran and deafness in their ears so that they cannot listen to it acceptingly. If you call them to faith, they will never respond to what you call them towards as long as there are covers on their hearts and deafness in their ears.",
  18058:
      "To avoid keeping the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم in anticipation of his deniers being treated with a punishment, Allah told him: By your Lord, O Messenger, the Forgiver of the sins of His repentant slaves, the One whose Mercy encompasses everything, it is from His Mercy that He gives the sinners respite so that perhaps they may repent to Him. If he were to inflict punishment upon those who turned away, he would have punished them immediately in this world. But because He is The Most Forbearing and The Most Merciful, he has delayed their torment so that they repent. Rather, they are designated a specific place and time in which they will be disciplined for their disbelief and their shunning [of Allah's religion] if they do not repent. They will not find a refuge where they can seek shelter from what will befall them.",
  18059:
      "We destroyed those disbelieving towns close to you, such as the towns of the people of Hūd, Saleh, and Shuayb, when they wronged themselves by disbelief and sins, and We set an appointed time for their destruction.",
  18060:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Moses (peace be upon him) said to his slave, Joshua, the son of Nun: I will continue traveling until I reach the place where the two seas meet, or I will travel until such time that I meet the righteous slave and I learn from him.",
  18061:
      "So they both traveled and forgot the fish they had carried as provision when they reached the place where the two seas meet. Allah gave life to that fish, and it made a pathway in the sea like a tunnel, such that the water did not come together.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The greatness, grandeur and generality of the Qur’an as it contains every path leading to beneficial knowledge and perpetual bliss and every path that protects one from evil.\n2. It is from Allah’s wisdom and mercy that He made for those who are wrong and who argue with the truth using falsehood the greatest of means to the clarity of truth and the plainness and corruption of falsehood.\n3. The verses contain a warning to the person who leaves the truth after knowing it that he will be prevented from it and will not be able to come back onto it thereafter, which is the greatest warning and deterrent for that.\n4. There is no one more unjust than the person who is reminded of the verses of his Lord but he neglects them and turns away from accepting them and leaving his disbelief and sins and does not repent from that.\n5. It is Allah’s practice in the earlier and later generations that He does not punish them quickly. Instead he invites them to repent. If they repent He forgives them and shows them mercy. If not, He sends down His punishment.\n6. The virtue of knowledge and travelling to seek it, taking the opportunity to meet the virtuous and the scholars even though they may be living in far-off places.",
  18062:
      "When they passed that place, Moses (peace be upon him) said to his slave: Bring us our lunch; we have experienced extreme tiredness in this journey.",
  18063:
      "The boy said: Do you remember what happened when we rested by the rock? I forgot to tell you about the fish. It was only the Devil who made me forget to mention it to you. The fish came to life, and amazingly, it found its way into the sea.",
  18064:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to his slave: That is what we were looking for, for that is the sign of the place of the righteous slave. So they turned back, retracing their steps, so that they would not lose the way until they reached the rock, and from there, they reached the entry point of the fish.",
  18065:
      "When they reached the place at which the fish was lost, they found there one of Our righteous slaves (who was Khidr, peace be upon him), to whom We had given mercy and to whom We had taught knowledge that people were not aware of, which is what is contained in this story.",
  18066:
      "Moses humbly and politely said to him: May I follow you so that you can teach me some of the knowledge that Allah has taught you, which constitutes guidance to the truth?",
  18067:
      "Khidr said: Indeed, you will not be able to be patient with what you see of my knowledge because it will not correspond with your knowledge.",
  18068:
      "How will you bear with patience over the actions that you see for which you do not know the proper reason because you judge them according to the limit of your knowledge?!",
  18069:
      "Moses said: You will find me, Allah willing, patient over those actions of yours that I see and committed to following you. I will not go against any instruction that you give me.",
  18070:
      "Khidr said to Moses: If you follow me, then do not ask me about anything that you see me doing until I myself tell you the reason behind it.",
  18071:
      "When they agreed to that, they set out to the seashore, where they came across a ship, which they boarded for free as an honor to Khidr. Khidr then made a hole in the ship by removing one of its planks. Moses said to him: Did you make a hole in the ship whose owners let us board for free in the hope that they may drown? You have done something confusing and puzzling.",
  18072:
      "Khidr said to Moses: Did I not say: Indeed, you will not be able to be patient with me in what you will see from me?",
  18073:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to Khidr: Do not take me to task on account of my breaking the pledge forgetfully, and do not make it difficult and hard for me to accompany you.",
  18074:
      "After they disembarked from the ship, they set out walking along the seashore when they saw a young boy who was still not an adult playing with the other boys. Khidr killed him, and Moses said to him: Did you kill a pure soul that is still a minor for no sin? You have really done something evil!!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The permissiblity of taking a servant whether at home or on a journey to take care of matters and for the sake of comfort.\n2. The recommendation that a person’s servant be intelligent and smart so that he can achieve his objective.\n3. Divine assistance descends on a servant in accordance with his fulfilment of his obligation. A person who fulfils Allah’s instructions is assisted more than others.\n4. Being courteous to the teacher and the student’s addressing him in the most polite manner.\n5. Forgetfulness does not require a person to be taken to task. A person is not held liable for it and no law is linked to it.\n6. An accomplished learned person can learn a science that he has not mastered from the one who has mastered it, even though the latter may be many ranks lower than the former in knowledge.\n7. To attribute knowledge and other virtues to Allah, most High, to acknowledge this and thank Allah for it. 8 Beneficial knowledge is knowledge that guides one to good.\n9. The virtue of patience. Whoever practices and observes patience will attain anything he works towards.",
  18075:
      "Khidr told Moses (peace be upon Him): Verily, I had told you: Indeed, O Moses, you will not be able to be patient with what matter I will carry out.",
  18076:
      "Moses (peace be upon him said): If I ask you about anything after this time, then depart from me, for I have reached the furthest extent in which you would be excused from leaving my company, as I contradicted your order twice.",
  18077:
      "So they then walked until, when they came to the people of a town, they asked for food from them. So, the townspeople refused to feed them and fulfill the right of hospitality to them. Then they found a wall in the town leaning to the point that it was about to collapse and be destroyed, so Khidr evened it until it was straight. So Moses (peace be upon him) said to Khidr: If you wanted to take payment for fixing it, you certainly could have, as we need it after they refused to host us.",
  18078:
      "Khidr told Moses: This objection to my not taking payment for erecting the wall is the point of separation between you and me. I shall inform you of the explanation of what you could not be patient with from what you witnessed me doing.",
  18079:
      "As for the ship you criticized me for making a hole in, it belonged to weak people who worked on it in the sea and could not protect it. So I wanted to make it defective with what I caused in it so that it would not be overtaken by a king up ahead of them, who would forcefully take possession of every good ship from its owners and leave every defective ship.",
  18080:
      "As for the boy you criticized me for killing, his parents were believers, and he was, according to Allah's knowledge, a disbeliever. So we feared that if he grew up, he would push them to transgress and disbelieve in Allah out of their excessive love for him or their severe need for him.",
  18081:
      "So we wanted Allah to compensate them with a child better in religion, piety, purity from sins, and closer to mercy to his parents than him.",
  18082:
      "As for the wall I fixed, and you criticized me for repairing, it belonged to two children in the city we went to whose father had passed away. Beneath the wall was wealth buried for them, and the father of these two children was righteous. So your Lord, O Moses, wanted them to reach the age of maturity and grow up, and take out their buried wealth underneath it because if the wall fell now, their property would certainly be exposed and susceptible to loss. This planning was a mercy to them from your Lord, and I did not do this of my own determination. That is the explanation of what you were unable to be patient with.",
  18083:
      "After mentioning the story of Khidr, Allah mentions the story of Dhul-Qarnayn as they both strive to protect the weak, stating: \n And the polytheists and Jews ask you as a test, O Messenger, regarding Dhul-Qarnayn. Say: I shall recite upon you a part of his story, which you can take a lesson from.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is important to take one’s time, verify and not rush towards passing judgment on a matter until one knows what is intended thereby and what the objective is.\n2. The future actions of the servants should be made contingent on Allah’s will.\n3. The upshots of matters are according to the apparent, and worldly rulings regarding wealth, life etc., all depend on the apparent.\n4. A greater evil is averted by carrying out a smaller evil and the greater benefit is taken into consideration by leaving the lesser benefit.\n5. It is permissible to do something with the wealth of others when it is beneficial and to remove harm, be it without permission, and even if it means some portion of the wealth of others is destroyed.\n6. To serve the pious or those connected to them is better than serving others.\n7. A person should not separate from his companion and leave his company under any circumstances, until he has admonished him and excused himself from him.\n8. One should be respectful with Allah by attributing good towards Him and not attributing bad towards Him.\n9. Allah protects a pious servant and his children.",
  18084:
      "Indeed, We gave him a foothold on earth and granted him a path in everything relevant to his goals, allowing him to reach his objectives.",
  18085:
      "So he used the means and paths We granted him to reach his objectives, so he headed West.",
  18086:
      "And he walked the earth until he reached the end of the land towards the sunset, in the eye of the beholder. He saw it as though it was setting in a hot spring of black mud. And he found a community of disbelievers near the setting place of the sun. We said to him, by way of giving discretion: O Dhul-Qarnayn, either you torment these people with killing or other means, or you be good to them.",
  18087:
      "Dhul-Qarnayn said: As for the one who associates partners with Allah and persists in that after our call to him to worship Allah, then we shall punish him by killing [him] in this life. Then he will return to his Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and He shall then torment him with a terrible torment.",
  18088:
      "And as for who among them believes in Allah and does good deeds, for him is Paradise, as a reward from his Lord for his faith and good deeds. And We shall say to him from Our command that which contains gentleness and lenience.",
  18089:
      "Then, he took a different path than his first one, heading towards the sunrise.",
  18090:
      "And he walked until when he reached the place where the sun rises, in the eye of the beholder, he found the sun rising on a people whom We had not given protection [to stand] before the sun by means of houses or the shade of trees.",
  18091:
      "Such was the matter of Dhul-Qarnayn. Our knowledge has encompassed what he possessed of power and authority in detail.",
  18092:
      "Then, he followed a path different from the first two, standing between the East and West.",
  18093:
      "He walked until he reached a pass between two mountains, where he came across a group of people who could barely understand the speech of outsiders.",
  18094:
      "They said: O Dhul-Qarnayn, indeed Gog and Magog (referring to two immense nations from the Children of Adam) cause corruption on the earth by the killing and other matters they engage in, so should we give you wealth so that you can make a barrier between us and them?",
  18095:
      "Dhul-Qarnayn said: The dominion and authority my Lord has given me is better than any wealth you would give me, so assist me with men and tools so that I can construct a barrier between you and them.",
  18096:
      "Bring pieces of iron. So they brought them to him. Then he began building with them between the two mountains until he made it level between the two. He said to the workers: Ignite fire upon these pieces [of iron]. [They did so] until when the iron pieces turned red, he said: Bring copper for me to pour on it.",
  18097:
      "So Gog and Magog could not surmount it due to its height, nor could they pierce it from beneath due to its solidity.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. DhuT-Qarnayn was one of the believing kings who ruled the world and dominated its people. Allah had granted him a vast kingdom, and gifted him with wisdom and beneficial knowledge.\n2. It is one of the duties of the king or ruler to support the people in defending their homes and maintaining their borders through his own wealth.\n3. Good, sincere people are zealous to do things to seek the pleasure of Allah.",
  18098:
      "Dhul-Qarnayn said: This barricade is a mercy from my Lord. It comes between Gog and Magog and corruption on the earth, preventing them from it. So when the time Allah has appointed for their release comes before the Hour, He will level it to the ground. And the promise of Allah to raze it to the ground and release Gog and Magog is established and will not be broken.",
  18099:
      "We left some of the creation of the end of times to agitate and mix with one another. The Trumpet will be blown. Then, We will gather all of creation for reckoning and recompense.",
  18100:
      "And We shall reveal Hell to the disbelievers without obscurity so they visually witness it.",
  18101:
      "We shall reveal it to the disbelievers who were blind to the remembrance of Allah in the world due to the obstructive veil on their eyes, which barred them from that. They could not hear the verses of Allah in an accepting way.",
  18102:
      "So did those disbelieving in Allah think to make My slaves of angels, messengers, devils, and others to be worshipped besides me? Indeed, We have prepared Hell as a residing place for the disbelievers.",
  18103:
      "Say, O Messenger: Should we inform you, O people, who will be the most significant loser regarding his action?",
  18104:
      "Those who, on the Day of Resurrection, will see that the effort they used to make in this world has been lost, while they thought they were doing good in their efforts and would benefit from their actions. The reality will be in contrast to that.",
  18105:
      "Those are the ones who disbelieved in the signs of their Lord that indicate His oneness and disbelieved in meeting Him. Hence, their actions became void due to their denial of those matters, so they have no value with Allah on the Day of Resurrection.",
  18106:
      "That recompense prepared for them is Hell due to their disbelief in Allah and their making mockery of My messengers and revealed verses.",
  18107:
      "After mentioning the recompense of the disbelievers, Allah mentions the recompense of the believers, stating: \n Indeed, those who believe in Allah and do good actions will have the highest gardens as a place in honor of them.",
  18108:
      "Staying therein forever, not asking to move from it, as no reward comes close to it.",
  18109:
      "Say, O Messenger: Indeed, the words of my Lord are plentiful. So if the sea were ink for them to write with, the water in the sea would deplete before His words would end, may He be glorified. And if We were to bring more seas, they would also deplete.",
  18110:
      "Say, O Messenger: I am only human like you, [except that] it is revealed to me that your rightful object of worship is one, who has no partner, and that is Allah. Therefore, whoever fears meeting his Lord should do actions that conform to His legislation, be sincere to his Lord in them, and not associate any partners with the worship of his Lord.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is established that the resurrection and gathering will take place, by gathering jinn and mankind on the plains of judgment with the second blowing of the Trumpet.\n2. The biggest losers on the Day of Judgment are those whose effort in the world goes to waste, whereas they think they are doing good by worshipping others besides Allah.\n3. It is impossible to enumerate the words of Allah, His knowledge, wisdom, and secrets, even if the seas and oceans were ink without bounds to write with.",
  19000:
      "Mary (Surah Maryam)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDeclaring the Christians' and polytheists' creed of ascribing a child to Allah as baseless and elucidating the extent of Allah's mercy toward His slaves.\n•    Explanation:",
  19001:
      "Kāf Hā Yā 'Ayn Sād – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  19002:
      "This is a mention of your Lord's mercy on His slave Zechariah (peace be upon him). We relate it to you to take lessons from.",
  19003:
      "When he supplicated to his Lord, may He be glorified, secretly so that it would more likely to be accepted.",
  19004:
      "He said: O my Lord, indeed, my bones have become weak, the white hairs on my head have become plentiful, and I have not been unsuccessful in supplicating to You. Rather, You responded to me every time I supplicated.",
  19005:
      "And I fear that my relatives will not be able to fulfill the rights of the religion after my death because they are preoccupied with this worldly life. And my wife is barren and unbearing, so grant me from Yourself a child [who would be a] supporter.",
  19006:
      "Inheriting prophethood from me and the family of Jacob (peace be upon him), and O Lord, make him satisfactory in his religion, character and knowledge.",
  19007:
      "So Allah responded to his supplication and called out to him: O Zechariah, indeed, We are informing you of what will please you, for We have accepted your supplication and granted you a boy named John. We have not given this name to anyone before him.",
  19008:
      "Zechariah said, in amazement at the power of Allah: How will a child be born to me when my wife is barren and unbearing, and I have reached the limit of old age and the weakness of bones?",
  19009:
      "The angel said: The matter is as you said, that your wife does not bear and that you indeed have reached the limit of old age and the weakness of bones. However, your Lord said: Your Lord's creation of John from a barren mother and father at the limit of old age is easy. And I had created you, O Zechariah, before that and you were nothing to be mentioned because you were non-existent.",
  19010:
      "Zechariah (peace be upon him) said: O my Lord, give me a sign I can feel reassured with, indicating that the glad tidings the angels gave me will be attained. He said: Your sign of attaining what you were given glad tidings of is that you will not be able to speak to people for three nights without any illness, but rather you will be healthy and sound.",
  19011:
      "Then Zechariah went out to his people from his place of prayer and gestured to them without speaking to exalt Allah at the beginning and end of the day.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. White hair is a sign of weakness and old age, and the envoy, forerunner and warner of death.\n2. Weakness and helplessness are amongst the most beloved means to seek closeness to Allah, because they show absolving oneself from any power or strength and show attachment of the heart with the power and strength of Allah.\n3. It is recommended for a person to mention Allah’s favours on him in his supplication and that which is appropriate to submission.\n4. One should be eager for religious benefit and give it priority over all other benefits.\n5. It is permissible to pray for a child and it is permissible to beseech Allah for the guidance of one’s child, in following the prophets (peace and blessings upon them) and the noble.\n6. Keeping names with good meanings is recommended.\n7. These verses contain proof of Allah’s clear power: just as Allah created man from nonexistence when he was nothing, He has the power to create John and bring him into existence.\n8. It is permissible to act according to understandable signs.",
  19012:
      "So John was born to him. Then, when he reached an age where he could be addressed, We said to him: O John, take hold of the Torah with resolve and utmost diligence. And We granted him understanding, knowledge, resolution, and determination while still at the age of a child.",
  19013:
      "And We granted him mercy from Us and kept him pure from sins. And he was heedful, abiding by the commands of Allah and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  19014:
      "And he was dutiful to his parents, gentle and benevolent to them. And he was not arrogantly against obedience to His Lord nor them, and was not disobedient to his Lord nor them.",
  19015:
      "And peace and safety from Allah be on him on the day he was born, the day he dies and leaves this life, and the day he will be revived to life on the Day of Resurrection. These three points are the most desolate a person goes through, so if he is safe in them, he shall not have fear in other situations.",
  19016:
      "And mention, O Messenger, in the Quran revealed to you, the story of Mary (peace be upon her) when she retreated from her family and stayed separately in a place towards the east of them.",
  19017:
      "Then she placed a screen between herself and her people concealing her so they could not see her when she worshipped her Lord. Then We sent Gabriel (peace be upon him) to her, so he appeared to her in the form of a perfectly-formed human. So she thought he had ill intentions towards her.",
  19018:
      "Thus, when she saw him in the form of a perfectly-formed human heading towards her, she said: I seek the protection of the Merciful from you that any harm should come to me from you; if you are heedful, fearing Allah.",
  19019:
      "Gabriel (peace be upon him) said: I am not a human. I am merely a messenger from your Lord. He sent me to you to grant you a wholesome and pure child.",
  19020:
      "In amazement, Mary said, How can I have a child when neither a husband nor anyone else has come near me, nor am I fornicator for me to have a child?",
  19021:
      "Gabriel told her: The matter is as you mentioned, that no husband or anyone else has touched you, nor are you a fornicator. However, your Lord said: Creating a child without a father is easy for Me. And it is so that the child bestowed on you will be a sign to the people of the power of Allah, and mercy from Us to you and whoever believes in him. The creation of this child of yours is a fixed decree from Allah, written in the Preserved Tablet.",
  19022:
      "So she conceived him after the angel blew [the soul], and then she withdrew with him to a place far from people.",
  19023:
      "Then her labor pains started and caused her to take refuge by the trunk of a date palm tree. Mary (peace be upon her) said: If only I had died before this day, and I was something unmentioned so that people would not think bad of me.",
  19024:
      "Then Jesus called to her from beneath her feet: Do not grieve. Your Lord has made a stream of water beneath you from which you can drink.",
  19025:
      "And get hold of the date palm trunk and shake it; it will drop soft fresh dates on you, harvested at that moment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Being patient in fulfilling religious obligations is required.\n2. Allah takes care of His prophets and chosen people.\n3. One who disobeys his parents is a wretched tyrant.\n4. Righteousness towards one’s parents has a very high status with Allah, as Allah mentioned it alongside gratitude to Him.\n5. Allah praised those who obey Him.",
  19026:
      "So eat of the fresh dates, drink from the water, be pleased with your child, and do not grieve. And if you see anyone among the people asking you regarding the matter of the child, tell him: I have bound myself to silence from speech for my Lord's sake, so I will not speak to anyone today.",
  19027:
      "Then Mary came to her people carrying her son. Her people said to her, in objection: O Mary, you have come with a tremendous matter of falsehood, in that you have come with a child without a father.",
  19028:
      "You who resembles Aaron (a righteous man) in worship, your father was not an adulterer, nor was your mother. Thus, you are from a pure household known to be righteous, so how can you come with a child without a father?",
  19029:
      "So she pointed towards her son Jesus (peace be upon him), who was in a cradle. So the people said in bemusement: How can we talk to a child while he is [so young that he is still] in the cradle?",
  19030:
      "Jesus (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, I am the slave of Allah. He gave me the Gospel and appointed me as one of His prophets.",
  19031:
      "And He made me a source of great benefit for the slaves [of Allah] wherever I go. And He ordered me to perform prayer and give zakat (obligatory alms) for as long as I live.",
  19032:
      "And He made me benevolent to my mother. And He did not make me arrogant against the obedience of my Lord, nor did He make me disobedient to Him.",
  19033:
      "And security from the Devil and his helpers is upon me on the day of my birth, the day of my death, and the day I shall be revived to life on the Day of Resurrection. So the Devil will not corrupt me in these three desolate situations.",
  19034:
      "The one described with those qualities is Jesus, son of Mary. This speech is the statement of truth regarding him, unlike what is said by misguided people who are filled with doubt about him and differ.",
  19035:
      "It does not befit Allah to have a son, sanctified and hallowed He is from that. When He intends something, it is enough for Him to say regarding that matter: Be, then it undoubtedly is. So He who is like that is hallowed from having a son.",
  19036:
      "And indeed Allah, may He be glorified, is both my Lord and your Lord, so make worship sincere for Him alone. This, which I have mentioned to you, is the straight path that leads to the pleasure of Allah.",
  19037:
      "So the differing people disagreed regarding the matter of Jesus (peace be upon him), and then became separate factions among his people. Thus, some of them believed in him and said: He is a Messenger.Some disbelieved in him, such as the Jews, just as some groups exaggerated his status so they said: He is Allah.And some of them said: He is the son of Allah.Exalted is Allah from that. So woe to those who differ regarding his matter from witnessing the Day of Resurrection due to what it holds of scenes [of dread], reckoning, and punishment.",
  19038:
      "How hearing and seeing they will be on that day. They will hear when hearing will not benefit them, and they will see when seeing will not benefit them. Instead, the unjust in the worldly life are in clear misguidance from the straight path. Therefore, they will not prepare for the Afterlife until it comes to them abruptly while they are upon their injustice.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The power of Allah is most perfect. All means are ineffective by themselves but only through the decree of Allah.\n2. Ordering Mary to remain silent shows the virtue of keeping quiet in certain situations.\n3. It is not permitted in our sacred law to vow to remain silent.\n4. Jesus (peace be upon him) was granted safety by Allah on the day he was bom in this life from the whispering of the satan, on the day of his death in the grave and on the Day of Judgment in the Hereafter.\n5. The way Jesus was created as told by the Qur’an is the definite tmth in which there is no doubt. All the false lies besides this do not befit the messengers.\n6. In this world, a disbeliever is deaf and blind to the tmth, but he will hear and see in the afterlife when he will see the punishment. However, that will never benefit him.",
  19039:
      "And warn the people, O Messenger, of the Day of Regret when the evildoer will regret his evil-doing, as will the virtuous for not gathering many acts of obedience, when the scrolls of the slaves [of Allah] will be rolled up, their reckoning is finished, and each draws towards what he put forth. During their worldly life, they are deceived by it and distracted from the hereafter and do not believe in the Day of Resurrection.",
  19040:
      "Indeed, We will be who remains after the creation has perished, We inherit the earth and all those therein because they would have all perished, and We will remain after them, and We own them, do with them as We wish and to the Us alone shall they return to on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and recompense.",
  19041:
      "And mention, O Messenger, in the Quran which has been revealed to you, the story of Abraham (peace be upon him). Indeed, he was very truthful and affirming of the signs of Allah, and was a prophet [sent] from Allah.",
  19042:
      "When he said to his father Azar: O father, why, instead of Allah, do you worship an idol which does not hear your supplication if you supplicate to it, does not see your worship if you worship it, does not remove harm from you, and does not bring you benefit?",
  19043:
      "O my father, indeed knowledge has come to me through revelation which has not come to you, so follow me, and I shall guide you to the straight path.",
  19044:
      "O my father, do not worship the Devil by obeying him. Indeed, the Devil was disobedient to the Merciful when He ordered him to prostrate to Adam, and then did not prostrate.",
  19045:
      "O my father, indeed I fear that a torment from the Merciful will afflict you if you die upon your disbelief, so you will be a companion to the Devil in torment due to your alliance to him.",
  19046:
      "Azar said to his son Abraham (peace be upon him): Are you turning away from my idols that I worship, O Abraham? I shall certainly pelt you with stones if you do not stop cursing my idols. Stay away from me for a long time, and do not gather with me.",
  19047:
      "Abraham (peace be upon him) said to his father: [Greetings of] peace be upon you from me. You will not face from me what you dislike. I shall seek forgiveness and guidance from my Lord for you. Indeed, He is very gentle with me, may He be glorified.",
  19048:
      "And I shall leave you [all] and your objects of worship which you worship instead of Allah, and supplicate to my Lord alone, without associating any partners with Him. Perhaps if I supplicate to Him, He will not deprive me such that I would be wretched in the supplication to Him.",
  19049:
      "So when he abandoned them and their gods which they used to worship besides Allah, We compensated his loss of family, for We bestowed him his son Isaac and his grandson Jacob. And We made each one of them a prophet.",
  19050:
      "And out of Our mercy, We gave them much good alongside prophethood. And We established for them good praise remaining on the tongues of [Allah's] slaves.",
  19051:
      "And mention O Messenger, in the Quran revealed upon you, the story of Moses (peace be upon him). He was specially chosen, and was a messenger and a prophet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Day of Judgment will be a Day of Regret for the disbelievers and a day of happiness for the believers.\n2. A person must be respectful, kind and soft when speaking to one’s parents, and one should choose the best name when addressing them.\n3. Sins deprive the servant of Allah’s mercy and close its doors on him, just as obedience is the greatest means of attaining His mercy.\n4. Allah has promised to spread true praise of every righteous person according to his righteousness. Abraham (peace be upon him) and his children are among the leaders of the righteous.",
  19052:
      "We called him from the right side of the mountain in relation to where Moses (peace be upon him) was, and We brought him near in communion, where Allah let him hear His speech.",
  19053:
      "We gave him, out of Our mercy and favor, his brother Aaron (peace be upon him) as a prophet in answer to his prayer when he asked his Lord for that.",
  19054:
      "And mention, O Messenger, in the Quran revealed to you, the story of Ishmael (peace be upon him). He was true to his promise; whenever he made a promise, he fulfilled it and was a messenger and prophet.",
  19055:
      "He used to instruct his household to establish the prayer and give zakat, and his Lord was well pleased with him.",
  19056:
      "And mention, O Messenger, in the Quran which has been revealed to you, the story of Idris (peace be upon him). He was very truthful and affirming of the signs of his Lord, and he was one of the prophets of Allah.",
  19057:
      "We raised his mention by the prophethood We bestowed upon him; therefore, he was of high rank.",
  19058:
      "Those who were mentioned in this surah (chapter), beginning with Zechariah and ending with Idris (peace be upon them), are the ones whom Allah blessed with prophethood, from the children of Adam (peace be upon him), and from the children of those whom I carried in the Ark with Noah (peace be upon him), and from the children of Abraham and the children of Jacob (peace be upon them), and from those whom We granted success to the guidance of Islam and whom We chose and made prophets. When they heard the verses of Allah being recited, they prostrated to Allah, weeping out of fear of Him.",
  19059:
      "Then after these chosen prophets, there came followers of evil and deviation. They neglected the prayer by not offering it in the manner that was called for. They perpetrated sins their souls craved such as fornication. So those people will face evil and loss in the Hell.",
  19060:
      "Except those who repented from their shortcomings and transgressions, believed in Allah, and did righteous deeds, for those who possess such attributes will enter Paradise, and the reward of their actions will not be diminished, even if it were little.",
  19061:
      "Gardens to live and settle therein [permanently], which the Most-Merciful promised His righteous slaves in the unseen that He enter them into. They did not see it, then they believed in it. So Allah's promise of Paradise, even though it is hidden, will undoubtedly come to pass.",
  19062:
      "There, they will not hear any futile or obscene talk. Instead, they will listen to the [greeting of] peace from one another and the [greeting of] peace from the angels to them. They will be given whatever food they desire at any time they wish.",
  19063:
      "This Paradise described with the above attributes is that which We will pass on to be inherited by Our slaves who complied with the commands and avoided the prohibitions.",
  19064:
      "After mentioning the reward of the heedful, Allah notes that true heedfulness means not acting except by His command, stating: \n And say, O Gabriel, to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم: The angels do not descent of their own accord. They only descend at Allah's command. Everything ahead of us in the hereafter, everything behind us in this world, and everything in between belongs to Allah. O Messenger, Your Lord does not forget anything.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A preacher is always in need of assistants to help him in his call.\n2. Proof of the attribute of speech for Allah, the Exalted.\n3. Being true to one’s promise is praiseworthy and is the character trait of the prophets and messengers. The opposite, which is to breaks one’s promise, is blameworthy.\n4. The angels are Allah’s messengers who bring revelation. They do not descend on any of the prophets or messengers from amongst humans except with Allah’s instruction.",
  19065:
      "He is the Creator and possessor of the heavens and the earth, and He controls the affairs of both. He is also the Creator, Owner, and Controller of what is between them, so worship Him alone, for He alone deserves worship. Remain firm in worshipping Him, for He has no match or peer who have a share in His worship.",
  19066:
      "The disbeliever, who denies the Resurrection, mockingly says: When I die, will I come out of my grave alive for a second time? This seems certainly far-fetched.",
  19067:
      "Does the person rejecting the Resurrection not remember that We created him previously when he was nothing? Then the first creation can be used as evidence for the second creation, though the second creation is easier and simpler.",
  19068:
      "So by your Lord, O Messenger, We will certainly take them out of their graves to the place of gathering along with the devils who had misled them. Then We will bring them outside Hell, humiliated and on their knees.",
  19069:
      "Then We shall severely and aggressively extract from each of the groups of deviation those who were most disobedient and those are their leaders.",
  19070:
      "Then We surely know best those who most deserve to enter the Fire and endure and suffer its heat.",
  19071:
      "O people, all of you, without exception, will cross over the bridge that stretches over Hell. Your Lord has decreed this as a resolute ruling, thus no one can push back His decree.",
  19072:
      "Then after crossing the bridge, We will deliver those who were heedful of their Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. We will leave the wrongdoers on their knees without being able to escape from it.",
  19073:
      "When Our clear verses sent down to Our Messenger are recited to people, the disbelievers say to the believers: Which of our two parties is better in residence and dwelling and superior in assembly and gathering: Our party or your party?",
  19074:
      "How many a nation have We destroyed prior to these disbelievers who take pride in their material superiority! [Those nations] surpassed them in riches and outward appearance due to the luxury of their clothing and gratification of their bodies.",
  19075:
      "Say, O Messenger: The Merciful will grant respite to those treading in their misguidance so that they fall further into it until when they see what they had been threatened with, from [either] the hastened punishment in the world or the postponed [one] on the Day of Resurrection, then they will realize who is in a worse position and who has fewer supporters. Is it their party or the party of the believers?",
  19076:
      "In contrast to the deferring [of punishment] for those people so that they increase in their misguidance, Allah gives more faith and obedience to those who are guided. Righteous deeds that lead to eternal bliss are more beneficial, in the sight of your Lord, O Messenger, in terms of their recompense and better in outcome.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Believers must busy themselves with what they have been instructed and be consistent in that within the limits of their capacity.\n2. The gathering of all creation for the reckoning is an established matter that will take place after they are resurrected from their graves.\n3. Allah will present the disbelievers kneeling on their knees around Hell. Due to the severity of the terrors they will face, they will not be able to stand.\n4. Allah will take out from every community and from the followers of every false religion those who were the most insolent and disobedient, who are the leaders, to multiply the punishment for them.\n5. All created beings will arrive at the Fire, i.e. pass over the bridge without entering the fire. This is something that will most certainly occur.\n6. Allah will save those who were mindful of Him and will release them from the fire of Hell. He will let the disbelievers remain there forever.\n7. The correct standards and concepts of religion differ from the ideas of those who are ignorant and the lay people.\n8. Allah destroyed many communities and groups who had more luxuries and wealth on account of their disbelief.\n9. Allah leaves the person who is drowned in misguidance and rooted in disbelief, in the excess of his ignorance and disbelief, so that his delusion is prolonged and this makes his punishment more severe.\n10. Allah keeps the believers firm on guidance and increases His grant of success and help to them. He sends down verses that become a means for an increase of their conviction as a reward for them.",
  19077:
      "Have you, O messenger, seen the man who disbelieves in Our proofs, rejects Our threat and says: If I die and am resurrected, I will undoubtedly be given much wealth and children.",
  19078:
      "Does he know the unseen and therefore speaks based on evidence? Or does he have a pledge from his Lord to enter him into Paradise and to give him wealth and children?",
  19079:
      "The matter is not as he claims. We will undoubtedly record what he says and does, and We will punish him even more because of the falsehood that he claims.",
  19080:
      "We shall inherit the wealth and children he leaves behind after We destroy him. He will come to Us on the Day of Resurrection all alone, deprived of the wealth and prestige he used to delight in.",
  19081:
      "The polytheists worship things other than Allah so that they may be supporters and helpers to attain victory with.",
  19082:
      "The matter is not as they claim. These things that they worship besides Allah will deny the polytheists' worship of them on the Day of Resurrection. They will disassociate themselves from them and become their enemies.",
  19083:
      "Have you, O Messenger, not seen that We sent the devils and gave them authority over the disbelievers inciting them to commit sins and prevent others from Allah's religion?",
  19084:
      "Do not be hasty, O Messenger, in asking Allah to punish them quickly. We merely tally their ages until when their respite ends, We will punish them with what they deserve.",
  19085:
      "Mention, O Messenger, the Day of Resurrection, the Day We shall gather the heedful of their Lord, by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, to their Lord as an honored, dignified delegation.",
  19086: "And We will drag the disbelievers to Hell while they are thirsty.",
  19087:
      "These disbelievers will not have the power to intercede for one another, except for those who had taken a pledge with Allah in the world by having faith in Him and His messengers.",
  19088:
      "The Jews, the Christians, and some polytheists said: The Merciful had a child.",
  19089: "You who say this, have indeed come with something tremendous.",
  19090:
      "The heavens are on the verge of splitting because of this objectionable statement, the earth is about to fracture, and the mountains almost falling into ruin.",
  19091:
      "All of this is because they have attributed a son to the Merciful. Allah is vastly exalted above that.",
  19092:
      "It is not befitting of the Merciful to take a child due to His sanctity from that.",
  19093:
      "Everyone in the heavens and the earth, from the angels, men, and jinn, shall be brought before their Lord on the Day of Resurrection, in submission.",
  19094:
      "He has full knowledge of them and has numbered them exactly. Nothing of theirs is hidden from Him.",
  19095:
      "Each of them will come to Him alone on the Day of Resurrection, without any helper or wealth.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The verses indicate the absurdity of the disbeliever and the naivety of his thinking by his having sweet hopes but he will find the complete opposite in the world of the Hearafter.\n2. Allah has given authority to the satans over the disbelievers by their misleading them, inciting them to do evil and removing them from obedience to sin.\n3. The people of virtue, knowledge and righteousness will intercede with Allah’s permission on the Day of Judgment.",
  19096:
      "Those who believe in Allah and do righteous actions that Allah is pleased with, Allah will create for them love by His loving them and by making them beloved to His slaves.",
  19097:
      "O Messenger, We have merely made this Quran easy by revealing it in your language so that you may bring glad news to the heedful who comply with My commands and avoid My prohibitions, and [so that] you may warn people who are severe in argumentation and arrogance to yielding to the truth.",
  19098:
      "How many a nation have We destroyed before your people! Do you perceive a single one of those nations today or hear any soft sound from them? What afflicted them could afflict others when Allah permits.",
  20000:
      "Ta-Ha (Surah Taha)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe joy of following the Quran's guidance and carrying its message, and the misery that results in violating it.\n•    Explanation:",
  20001:
      "Tā Hā – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  20002:
      "We have not revealed the Quran to you, O Messenger, to cause you self-exhaustion in grief over your people turning away from belief in you.",
  20003:
      "We only revealed it to be a reminder for those whom Allah has given success to fear Him.",
  20004:
      "It was sent down by Allah, Who created the earth and the high heavens. It is thus a great Quran, as it was sent down by one who is Great.",
  20005:
      "The Merciful who ascended and rose over the Throne in a manner that is befitting for His Majesty, may He be glorified and exalted.",
  20006:
      "Everything in the heavens and the earth, what lies between them, and beneath the soil belongs to Him alone, may He be glorified, in creation, dominion, and determination.",
  20007:
      "If you, O Messenger, proclaim or conceal your speech, may He be glorified, knows all of that. He knows the secrets and what is even more hidden, such as someone's thoughts. Nothing is of that is hidden from Him.",
  20008:
      "There is no rightful object of worship besides Allah. To Him alone belong Names that are the very pinnacle of perfection and excellence.",
  20009:
      "When the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم suffered rejection from his people, his consolation came in the story of Moses (peace be upon him). The Exalted states: \n The story of Moses, son of 'Imran (peace be upon him), has surely come to you, O Messenger.",
  20010:
      "When he saw a fire while traveling, he told his family: Stay here. I saw a fire. Perhaps I will bring you a torch from it or find somebody to guide me to the path.",
  20011:
      "When he came to the Fire, Allah (may He be Exalted) called out to him, saying: O Moses.",
  20012:
      "Indeed I am your Lord. Remove your shoes in preparation for your conversation with me. You are in the purified valley of Tuwa.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The revelation of the grand Qur’an was not to cause hardship to the soul in worship or to make it taste great difficulty. It is only a book that serves as a reminder, from which those who fear their Lord benefit.\n2. Allah has mentioned the creation and the instruction together. Just as there is wisdom in the creation, similarly He only instructs and prohibits with justice and wisdom.\n3. It is a man’s duty to provide maintenance for his family (wife) in the form of food, clothing, accommodation and the means of warmth when it is cold.",
  20013:
      "And I have chosen you, O Moses, to convey My message, so listen to what I reveal.",
  20014:
      "Indeed, I am Allah; there is no rightful object of worship but Me. So worship Me alone and perform the prayer in the most perfect manner so that you may remember Me in it.",
  20015:
      "Indeed, the Hour is most definitely coming and occurring. I almost keep it hidden for no creation knows its time, though they are aware of its signs by the information given to them by the prophet sent to them; so that each soul is rewarded for what it did, whether good or evil.",
  20016:
      "Do not let the disbelievers, who do not believe in it and follow their unlawful desires, turn you away from believing in it and preparing for it with righteous actions; for you would be destroyed on account of that.",
  20017: "What is that in your right hand, O Moses?",
  20018:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: It is my staff: I lean on it when walking, I beat down tree leaves with it for my sheep and goats [to eat], and it has other uses besides those I mentioned.",
  20019: "Allah said: Throw it, O Moses.",
  20020:
      "Moses threw it, and it turned into a snake moving swiftly and lightly.",
  20021:
      "Allah said to Moses (peace be upon him): Take hold of the staff and do not be frightened when it changes into a snake. We will return it to its former state when you take hold of it.",
  20022:
      "And hold your hand to your side, and it will come out white, without vitiligo (a skin disease); a second sign for you.",
  20023:
      "We have shown you these two signs, O Moses, to show you some of Our most significant signs that indicate Our power and that you are indeed a messenger [sent] from Allah.",
  20024:
      "Go, O Moses, to Pharaoh, for he has overstepped the bounds in disbelief and rebellion against Allah.",
  20025:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: Lord, expand my breast for me so that I can bear the harm.",
  20026: "And make my task easy.",
  20027: "Give me the ability to speak eloquently.",
  20028:
      "So that they understand my speech when I convey Your message to them.",
  20029: "Grant me a helper from my family to assist me in my affairs.",
  20030: "[Let it be] Aaron, the son of Imran, my brother.",
  20031: "Strengthen my back by him.",
  20032: "And make him my partner in the message.",
  20033: "So that we can glorify You much.",
  20034: "And remember You much.",
  20035:
      "Indeed, You are watching over us. Nothing of our matter is hidden from You.",
  20036: "Allah said: O Moses, I have granted you your request.",
  20037:
      "And I have certainly favored you another time.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The necessity of listening properly in important matters, the most important of which is revelation sent down from Allah.\n2. The first revelation sent to Moses contained two principles of faith, which are: Acknowledgment of Allah’s oneness and faith in the Hour (the rising) and the most important religious obligation after faith which is prayer.\n3. Cooperation amongst those calling to Allah is necessary to achieve the objective. Allah made for Moses his brother Aaron a prophet to assist him in carrying out the mission.\n4. The importance of a preacher having the skill to make those who are called understand.",
  20038:
      "When We inspired your mother with that which Allah protected you from Pharaoh's plot.",
  20039:
      "For We had instructed her when We inspired her: Throw your child, after he is born, into a box and then cast it into the Nile River. The river will cast him onto the bank by Our command, and he will be taken in by an enemy of Mine and his, who is Pharaoh. I placed love upon you from Me, so people loved you, and so that you would be reared under My eye, protection, and care.",
  20040:
      "When your sister went out following the chest, moving whenever it moved, then said to those who took it: Shall I guide you to who will care for him, nurse him and rear him? So We granted favor upon you by returning you to your mother so that she could rejoice with your return to her and not grieve over you. Then You killed the Copt you punched, so We granted favor upon you by saving you from the punishment. And we saved you time and again from every test that you faced. You then left and stayed among the people of Midian for years, and then you came at the time that was specified for you to come to be spoken to, O Moses.",
  20041:
      "I have chosen you as My messenger to convey to people the what I reveal to you.",
  20042:
      "O Moses, you and your brother Aaron go with Our signs that show Allah's power and oneness. Do not slacken in calling towards Me and in remembering Me.",
  20043:
      "Go to Pharaoh, for indeed he has overstepped the boundaries in disbelief and rebellion against Allah.",
  20044:
      "Then speak to him gently without harshness, in hopes that he may remember and fear Allah, then repent.",
  20045:
      "Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them) said: We fear that he will hasten to punish us before we can fully deliver the call to him or that he will transgress the limit in oppressing us with killing or otherwise.",
  20046:
      "Allah said to them: Do not be afraid; Indeed, I am with you in support and assistance. I hear and see what occurs between you and him.",
  20047:
      "So go to him and tell him: We are the messengers of your Lord, O Pharaoh, so send the Israelites with us and do not punish them by killing their sons and letting their women live. We have come to you a with proof from your Lord regarding our truthfulness. Security from Allah's torment is for those who have faith and follow Allah's guidance.",
  20048:
      "Allah has revealed to us that the torment in this world and the Afterlife falls on whoever rejects the signs of Allah and turns away from what the messengers brought.",
  20049:
      "In denial of what they brought, Pharaoh said: Who is your Lord, that you claim has sent you to me, O Moses?",
  20050:
      "Moses said: Our Lord is the One who gave everything the shape and form suitable for it, and then He guided all created things to what they were created for.",
  20051:
      "Pharaoh said: What about the previous nations who had disbelieved?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s complete care for Moses (peace be upon him) and all messengers and prophets. Their successors also receive some of this care in accordance with their states with Allah.\n2. Those who follow the straight path and adopt the clear sacred law will be safe in this world and the Hearafter.\n3. Part of the general guidance for all created things is that every created thing strives towards the benefits for which it was created and towards warding off harm from itself.\n4. The verses show the virtue of instructing the good and prohibiting evil and that should be done through gentle speech by the person who has power and whose protection is guaranteed.\n5. The person who is right must listen to the speech of the person who is false and respond to him without offence or alienation.\n6. Allah alone possesses knowledge of the Ghaib in the past, present and future.",
  20052:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to Pharaoh: The knowledge of what those nations did is with my Lord, recorded in the Preserved Tablet. My Lord does not err in His knowledge of them nor does he forget what he knows of them.",
  20053:
      "[That knowledge is] with My Lord Who spread the earth for you to live on and made pathways for you to travel on. He sent down rainwater from the sky then brought forth various kinds of plant with that water.",
  20054:
      "Eat, O people, of the pure things We brought forth for you, and graze your cattle. Indeed, those mentioned favors are evidences of Allah's power and oneness for the people of intellect.",
  20055:
      "From the soil of the earth, We created your father, Adam (peace be upon him). Into it, We shall return you when you are being buried therein when you pass away, and from it, We shall take you out again for revival on the Day of Resurrection.",
  20056:
      "We had certainly showed Pharaoh all nine of Our signs. He witnessed them all then rejected them and refused to respond accepting [the call] to faith in Allah.",
  20057:
      "Pharaoh said: Have you come to remove us from Egypt with the sorcery you have brought, O Moses, so you can reign over it?",
  20058:
      "We will undoubtedly bring, O Moses, sorcery similar to yours, so make an appointed time between you and us at a known time and specified place, which neither of us will fail to keep. Let the place be between the two sides and level.",
  20059:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to Pharaoh: The appointment between you and us will be on the day of the festival when people will gather to celebrate their festival in the forenoon.",
  20060:
      "Pharaoh went back and gathered his plots and tricks. Then he came at the specified time and place for the contest.",
  20061:
      "Moses advised Pharaoh's sorcerers: Beware, do not invent lies against Allah by using sorcery to deceive people, or He will eliminate you with a torment from Him. Whoever invents lies against Allah has lost.",
  20062:
      "The sorcerers debated among themselves when they heard what Moses (peace be upon him) had to say, and they conferred secretly.",
  20063:
      "The sorcerers said to one another secretly: Moses and Aaron are sorcerers. They intend to drive you out of Egypt with the sorcery they brought and do away with your exalted way of life and lofty school of thought.",
  20064:
      "So make a firm decision and do not differ therein. Then go forward in rows and throw what you have all at once. Whoever defeats his opponent today has attained his objective.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of Allah’s favours is that He rolled out the earth like a spread and made it firm so that people can settle on it and it is suitable for life.\n2. Bringing forth various types of plants of varying colours from the earth is a clear sign of Allah’s Power and the existence of the Creator.\n3. The verses mentioned two clear logical evidences for resurrection: Bringing forth plants from the earth after its demise and bringing forth people from it when they were first created.\n4. The people of intelligence are the ones who benefit from the verses and who consider it carefully.\n5. Pharaoh’s disbelief was one of obstinacy, because he had seen the signs with his own eyes and was convinced of them deep within himself.\n6. Moses selected the day of the festival so that Allah’s word will be supreme, His religion will be victorious and disbelief will be repressed before all people in a public place so that the news of it spreads.\n7. The distinguishing feature of the prophets was their sincerity in calling towards Allah and their seizing the suitable opportunity to announce their invitation.",
  20065:
      "The sorcerers said to Moses (peace be upon him): O Moses, you have one of two options: Either you will be the first to throw down the magic you have, or we will be the first to do so.",
  20066:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: Rather, you throw what you have first. So they threw what they had, and it appeared to Moses that their ropes and sticks were like snakes moving quickly on the ground due to the sorcery.",
  20067: "Moses hid the fear he was feeling from what they did.",
  20068:
      "Allah reassured Moses (peace be upon him), saying: Do not fear the illusion. You, O Moses, will overcome them in victory and triumph.",
  20069:
      "Throw down the stick in your right hand: it will turn into a snake and swallow up the sorcery they have produced. They have only produced a plot of sorcery; a sorcerer will never be victorious wherever he is.",
  20070:
      "So Moses threw down his stick, which turned into a snake, and swallowed up what the sorcerers had produced. The sorcerers prostrated to Allah once they learned that what Moses had was not sorcery. It was only from Allah. They said: We believe in the Lord of Moses and Aaron, the Lord of all created things.",
  20071:
      "Pharaoh said in objection to the sorcerers' faith and as a threat to them: Have you believed in Moses before I permitted you to do so? Indeed, Moses must be your leader, O sorcerers, who taught you sorcery. So I shall certainly cut off from each of you one hand and foot from opposite sides and I will surely crucify your bodies on the trunks of palm trees until you die. You will become a lesson for others, and then you will certainly know which of us has a more intense and lasting torment: I or the Lord of Moses?",
  20072:
      "The sorcerers said to Pharaoh: We shall not prefer following you, O Pharaoh, over following the clear signs that have come to us. We will not prefer you to Allah, Who created us. So do whatever you want to us. You only have authority over us in this temporary life, and your authority will vanish.",
  20073:
      "We believe in our Lord, with the hope that He will erase from us our past sins of disbelief and other vices and that He will erase from us the evil of sorcery that you forced us to learn, practice and challenge Moses with. Allah has a better reward than what you promise us, and His torment lasts longer than the torment you threaten us with.",
  20074:
      "The gist of the matter is that those who come to their Lord on the Day of Resurrection as disbelievers will enter the Fire to remain there forever. Therein, they will not die and be relieved of its torment, nor will they live a pleasant life.",
  20075:
      "Those who come to their Lord on the Day of Resurrection believing in Him, having done righteous actions, then the ones described with those great qualities will be rewarded with lofty abodes and high ranks.",
  20076:
      "Those ranks are Gardens of settlement with rivers flowing under their palaces, remaining therein forever. That is the reward of those who purify themselves from disbelief and acts of disobedience.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Good manners is of benefit in this world and the Hearafter. Since the magicians gave Moses the option to throw first or to let them throw first, this brought them the benefit of being blessed with faith.\n2. A magician will never succeed or survive wherever he may go or practice his tricks. He will never obtain his objective through magic, whether good or bad.\n3. An intelligent person should compare the pleasures of world against the pleasures of the afterlife and the punishment of this world against the punishment of the Hearafter.\n4. Faith does miracles. The faith of the magicians was more firm than the mountains and therefore the punishment of the world was easy for them to bear and they were not concerned by Pharaoh’s threats.\n5. The habit of the transgressors is that they threaten the people of truth with severe punishment in order to humiliate and disgrace them.\n6. The rejecting disbeliever in Hell will neither live nor die.\n7. The reward of those who purify themselves from disbelief and sins will be gardens of eternity that have rivers of wine, honey, milk and water flowing under their abodes.",
  20077:
      "And We certainly revealed to Moses: go with My slaves by night from Egypt so that nobody notices them, and make for them a dry path in the sea after striking the sea with the staff, without fear of Pharaoh and his elites catching up with you nor fear of drowning in the ocean.",
  20078:
      "Then Pharoah, accompanied by his armies, followed them until they were all engulfed by the sea [as the water crashed down over them], the reality of which only Allah knows. They all drowned and perished, while Moses and those with him were saved.",
  20079:
      "And Pharaoh misguided his people by making disbelief appear good to them and by deceiving them through falsehood. He did not direct them toward the path of guidance.",
  20080:
      "And We said to the Israelites after saving them from Pharaoh and his armies: O Children of Israel, We saved you from your enemy, and We promised you that We will speak to Moses to the right of the valley next to Mount Sinai, and We sent down to you, while you were aimlessly wandering, food you can eat which is sweet like honey, and [the flesh of] birds which resemble quails.",
  20081:
      "Consume from the lawful wholesome foods We have provided you with, and do not go beyond what We have made lawful, lest you consume what We have made forbidden. Otherwise, My anger will fall on you. Whomever My anger falls upon will be destroyed in this life and the next.",
  20082:
      "And I am extremely forgiving and pardoning to one who repents to Me, does good deeds, and is firm on the truth.",
  20083:
      "And what has made you hurry [here and depart from] your people, O Moses, leaving them behind?",
  20084:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: Here they are behind me, and shall catch up with me. I preceded my people in coming to You so that You become pleased with me for coming towards You quickly.",
  20085:
      "Allah said: We have tested your people whom you left behind through worshipping the calf. Samiri called them to worship it and misguided them through that.",
  20086:
      "Moses returned to his people, angered by their worship of the calf and grieving over them. Moses (peace be upon him) said: My people, did Allah not make you a good promise that He will send the Torah to you and enter you into paradise? Had a long time passed upon you that you forgot? Or did you intend through this action of yours that your Lord's anger should descend upon you and His punishment befall you, and this is why you broke your promise to me to stay firm on obedience until I return to you?",
  20087:
      "The people of Moses said: We did not break your promise, O Moses, willingly, but rather by compulsion. We carried large weights of the jewelry of Pharaoh's people and threw them into a ditch to get rid of them. But as we threw them into the ditch, the Samiri threw into it some dust he had from the hoof of the horse of Gabriel (peace be upon him).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is Allah’s custom to take retribution from the wrongdoers through which the believers’ hearts are relieved, they find solace and the anger of their hearts is removed.\n2. Destroying is Allah’s custom as an end result of disbelief, misguidance and not following Allah’s guidance.\n3. Whoever treads the straight path, follows the Noble Messenger, follows the firm religion, Allah forgives his sins and pardons his previous mistakes and persistent disobedience.\n4. A tyrant is a misfortune for himself and his people, because he leads them astray from guidance, and he does not guide them towards good or salvation.\n5. Blessings require protection and gratitude which brings more, whereas rejecting them necessitates Allah’s anger descending.\n6. Allah is always Forgiving to one who repents from associating partners with Allah, disbelief and sinning, who believes in Him and does good deeds and who then remains steadfast on the truth until he dies on it.\n7. Although hastiness disliked in general, promptness is praiseworthy in religious matters.\n8. Moses (peace be upon him) had every right to return to his people in extreme anger and grief, due to the worship of the calf they committed after him.",
  20088:
      "So Samiri brought out, from that jewelry of the Israelites, a lifeless body of a calf, which made a noise like that of a cow. Those amongst them whom the Samiri's action had tempted said: This is your object of worship and that of Moses. He forgot it and left it here.",
  20089:
      "Do these people who were tempted by the calf and then worshipped it not see that the calf does not speak or respond to them, nor does it have the ability to remove harm from them or others or benefit itself or others?",
  20090:
      "Aaron had said to them before Moses returned: The making of the calf from gold and its mooing is only to test you, to distinguish the believer from the disbeliever. And your Lord, O people, is Allah, so follow me by worshipping Him alone and obey my command to leave worshipping others besides Him.",
  20091:
      "Those who were put to trial through worship of the calf said: We will continue worshipping it until Moses returns to us.",
  20092:
      "Moses said to his brother Aaron: What prevented you when you saw them go astray by worshipping the calf beside Allah, from leaving them and joining me? Did you disobey my order when I left you in charge of them?",
  20093:
      "Moses said to his brother Aaron: What prevented you when you saw them go astray by worshipping the calf beside Allah, from leaving them and joining me? Did you disobey my order when I left you in charge of them?",
  20094:
      "When Moses grabbed his brother by his beard and head, dragging and scolding him for what he did, Aaron said to him, seeking his compassion: Do not hold my beard and the hair on my head, for I have a reason for staying with them. I feared that if I left them alone, they would have dispersed. Then you would have said I split them up and did not maintain your advice regarding them.",
  20095:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to Samiri: What is the matter with you, O Samiri? What drove you to do what you did?",
  20096:
      "Samiri said to Moses (peace be upon him): I saw what they did not see: I saw Gabriel on a horse, so I took a handful of soil from the footsteps of his horse and threw it on melted jewelry, which was molded into the form of a calf. From this, the body of a calf with a mooing sound was formed. And this is how my soul made what I did appealing to me.",
  20097:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to the Samiri: Go from here, for it is written for you that you will say as long as you live: I am not to touch or be touched. You will live as an outcast and have a promised time on the Day of Resurrection in which you will be taken to account and punished. Allah will never break this promise with you. And look at the calf, which you took as something to worship, and continued to worship besides Allah. We shall burn it in a fire until it melts, then we shall scatter it into the sea until no trace of it remains.",
  20098:
      "Your rightful object of worship, O people, is Allah. There is no rightful deity of worship besides Him. He has encompassed everything in His knowledge; only He knows everything, and nothing escapes His knowledge.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Deceiving people by distorting the truth is the way of the misguided.\n2. Anger when the sacred laws of Allah are violated is commendable.\n3. These verses contain the basis for exiling and leaving people of innovation and disobedience, and that they should not be associated with.\n4. These verses show it is necessary to contemplate and recognise Allah through His actions in the Universe.",
  20099:
      "Just as We related to you, O Messenger, the story of Moses, Pharaoh, and their people, We relate the incidents of the prophets and nations before you so that they are a solace for you. And We have given you a Quran through which those who heed reminders are reminded.",
  20100:
      "Whoever turns away from this revealed Quran to you, does not believe in it, and acts accordingly will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying great sin and deserving of a painful punishment.",
  20101:
      "Perpetually remaining in that torment. How awful a burden they will be carrying on the Day of Resurrection.",
  20102:
      "The Day when the angel blows the Trumpet a second time for the Resurrection, We shall gather the disbelievers this day, blue-eyed. Their complexion and eyes change color when facing the terrible horrors of the Afterlife.",
  20103:
      "They will talk to one another quietly, saying: You did not stay in the Barzakh (the life between this world and the hereafter) after death except for ten nights.",
  20104:
      "We know best what they secretly say amongst themselves, with nothing escaping Us, when the most intelligent of them says: You did not stay in the Barzakh for no more than one day.",
  20105:
      "They ask you, O Messenger, about the mountains on the Day of Resurrection. Say to them: My Lord will pull the mountains from their roots and scatter them until they become dust.",
  20106:
      "He will then level the earth, which used to carry [the mountains] and leave it flat, with no buildings or vegetation.",
  20107:
      "O onlooker, you will not see any curve, elevation, or dip on the earth because it is so flat.",
  20108:
      "On that Day, people will follow the sound of the caller towards the gathering place. There will be nothing to divert them from following it. The voices will become silent out of fear for [Allah] the Merciful; hence you will not hear anything but whispers on that day.",
  20109:
      "On that great Day, without the permission of Allah, no intercession from any intercessor can benefit another person unless Allah is pleased with what he says for the intercession.",
  20110:
      "Allah knows what people will face in the final Hour, and He knows what they left behind in their worldly life. All the slaves together cannot encompass the knowledge of Allah's essence and His attributes.",
  20111:
      "The faces of the slaves will be humbled and submissive before [Allah] the Living, who does not die and takes care of His slaves' affairs by managing and disposing of them. And the one who bears sin will be in loss because he led himself to destruction.",
  20112:
      "Whoever does good deeds while believing in Allah and His messengers will be rewarded. They will neither fear injustice by being punished for a sin they did not commit nor a decrease in the reward of their good deeds.",
  20113:
      "Such as the Quran, which We have revealed in clear Arabic just as We revealed the stories of the previous prophets. We have explained with various [degrees of] threats and fear-inducing warnings, in the hope they will fear Allah or that the admonition of the Quran will cause them to reflect.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The stories of the Qur’an which mentions the incidents of the nations before are a lesson and admonition for all people.\n2. All of the Qur’an is a reminder and lesson for nations, tribes and individuals, and dignity and honour for mankind.\n3. Intercession will not benefit anyone, besides the intercession of one whom the Merciful allows and whom He approves to speak for intercession.\n4. The Qur’an discloses the horrors of the Day of Judgment, and the earthquakes and shakings which will occur in it.\n5. The Qur’an comprises that which is sufficient for all levels of people.\n6. The Qur’an comprises rulings whose beauty and perfection is attested to by the intellect and human nature.\n7. Amongst the etiquette of dealing with the Qur’an is to receive it with acceptance, submission and respect, to take direction through its light towards the straight path, and to devote oneself to it through learning and teaching.\n8. The wrongdoers will regret on the Day of Judgment because of wasting much time, spending it absentmindedly and in play, turning away from what benefits them and occupying themselves with what harms them.",
  20114:
      "Exalted, sanctified, and majestic be Allah. He is the King, to whom belongs the dominion of everything, Who is true and speaks the truth. Exalted is He from what the polytheists ascribe to Him. Do not hasten, O Messenger, in reciting the Quran with Gabriel before it is fully conveyed to you. Say: O Lord, increase my knowledge on top of what You have already taught me.",
  20115:
      "When Allah narrates the story of Moses, including Pharaoh's denial and the Israelites' neglectfulness, He cites the story of Adam (peace be upon him) as an example to encourage the heedless to return to Allah's obedience, stating: \n And We enjoined Adam beforehand not to eat of the tree, and We forbade him from this and explained to him its consequences. But he forgot the instruction and ended up eating from the tree and could not resist it. And We did not see in him the resolve to observe what We enjoined him with.",
  20116:
      "And remember, O Messenger, when I said to the angels: Prostrate to Adam as a greeting. All of them prostrated besides Iblis (Satan), who was with them but not from them. He refused to prostrate out of arrogance.",
  20117:
      "So We said: O Adam, Iblis is your enemy and your wife's enemy. Let him not take you and your wife out of Paradise by obeying him in what he whispers; otherwise, you will suffer difficulties.",
  20118:
      "It is a right that Allah has given you that He will feed you, so you will not get hungry, and clothe you, so you will not be unclothed.",
  20119:
      "And to give you water so you do not get thirsty, and to shade you so that the sun's heat does not affect you.",
  20120:
      "But the Devil whispered to Adam: Shall I show you a tree that whoever eats from it will live forever and possess an everlasting kingdom that will never fall into decay or come to an end?",
  20121:
      "Then Adam and Eve ate from the forbidden tree. Their private areas that were previously covered became exposed, and they began to pluck the leaves of the trees of Paradise and cover themselves. Adam opposed the command of his Lord, as he did not comply with His order to prevent himself from eating from the tree. So, he transgressed the limit and did what was not permissible for him to do.",
  20122:
      "Then Allah chose him, accepted his repentance, and gave him success to guidance.",
  20123:
      "Allah said to Adam and Eve: Both of you and Iblis descend from Paradise because he is your enemy and you are his. If there comes to you from Me enlightenment of My path, then whoever amongst you follows it, acts accordingly, and does not divert from it, he will not go astray from the truth, nor will he suffer the misfortune of being punished. Instead, Allah will enter him into Paradise.",
  20124:
      "And whoever turns away from My reminder and does not accept or respond to it shall have a constricted and miserable life in this world and in the Barzakh (the life between this world and the hereafter). I shall lead him towards the gathering place on the Day of Resurrection without eyesight or argument [to defend himself].",
  20125:
      "This person will say: O my Lord, why did you gather me [being] blind today when I could see in the world?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of proper etiquette in acquiring knowledge, and that the one listening to knowledge should be calm and patient until the one dictating and teaching has completed his task.\n2. Adam forgot and so his children forgot. He did not remain steadfast on firm resolve and they are also the same. He quickly repented so Allah forgave him, and whoever resembles his father has not been unjust.\n3. The virtue of repentance, as Adam (peace be upon him) was better after repentance than before.\n4. It is important to beware of the satan, the enemy of humans, who is stationed to constantly stay with him day and night.\n5. Life of misery in this worldly abode, in the Transitory Stage, and in the afterlife for the disbelievers and misguided.",
  20126:
      "Allah refuted him by saying: This is like what you did in the world; when Our signs came to you, you turned away from them and abandoned them. Likewise, you will be abandoned today in torment.",
  20127:
      "And this is the kind of recompense We give to the one engrossed in unlawful desires and who turns away from believing in the clear proofs from his Lord. And the punishment of Allah in the Hereafter is even more horrible, severe, and lasting than the life they will have in this world and the Barzakh.",
  20128:
      "Is it not apparent to the polytheists how many nations We destroyed before them? They walk into the homes of these ruined nations and see the effects of what befell them. The destruction and demise in these many nations are lessons for people of intellect.",
  20129:
      "O Messenger, had a word not preceded from your Lord that He will not punish anyone before establishing the proof against him, and had there not been a timespan that He determined for them, the punishment would have surely come to them quickly because they deserved it.",
  20130:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with the false things those who disbelieve in you say about you. Exalt and praise your Lord at Fajr time before sunrise; at 'Asr before sunset; in the hours of the night during Maghrib and 'Isha prayers; and at Dhuhr just after the zenith, which is the end of the first part of the day and the beginning of the second part; in the hope of attaining reward with Allah which you will be pleased with.",
  20131:
      "And do not look on to what We made a delight for various groups of the rejectors to enjoy from the glitters of the worldly life so that We may test them. For indeed, what We have given them from that will disappear. And the reward of your Lord, which He has promised you so that you will be pleased, is better and more enduring than what He provided as comfort in the world from disappearing comforts, because it does not cease.",
  20132:
      "O Messenger, order your family to perform the prayer and remain committed to it yourself. We do not ask you for your sustenance or that of others; We will take care of your sustenance. The commendable outcome in this world and the Afterlife is for the pious who fear Allah, [those who] carry out His commands and refrain from His prohibitions.",
  20133:
      "These disbelievers who reject the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: Why does Muhammad not bring us a sign from his Lord which proves his truthfulness and that he is a Messenger? Has the Quran, which confirms the previous divine books, not come to these rejecters?",
  20134:
      "And if We were to destroy these rejectors of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم by sending punishment on them due to their disbelief and obstinacy, before sending a messenger to them and revealing a book to them, they would say on the Day of Resurrection, as an excuse for their disbelief: O Lord, if only You had sent a messenger to us in the world, so that we could have believed in him and followed the verses that he brought before disgrace and humiliation befell us through Your torment.",
  20135:
      "O Messenger, tell these rejectors: All of us await what Allah will carry out, so you, too, wait. You will most certainly come to know who the people of the straight path are and who are rightly guided: you or us?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There will be no excuse for a disbeliever on the day of judgment after the signs and proofs of the Oneness of Allah and His orders and prohibitions had come to him in the worldly life.\n2. The disbelievers will come to know that divine help is for the one who is guided to the true religion.\n3. Divine signs benefit the believers, and through them their faith and conviction increase. As for those who turn away from them and oppose them, they do not believe in them nor benefit from them.\n4. Amongst the means which help one bear the harm of those who oppose the message is to spend virtuous times in glorification and praise of Allah.\n5. It is necessary for the servant, when he notices in himself a yearning for worldly adornment, to compare its temporary and deficient pleasure to the perfect and everlasting pleasure of the Hearafter.\n6. It is necessary for the servant to establish prayer properly. When any matter befalls him, he should perform prayer and order his family to do so, and be patient in offering them, thereby emulating the Messenger (peace be upon him).\n7. The beautiful praiseworthy outcome, paradise, is for the people of piety.",
  21000:
      "The Prophets (Surah Al-Anbiya)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nEstablishing the mission and demonstrating the unity in the Prophets' objectives and Allah's care for them.\n•    Explanation:",
  21001:
      "The time for humanity's reckoning of their deeds on the Day of Resurrection has drawn near. Still, they are turning away from the Hereafter in their heedlessness due to preoccupation with this world.",
  21002:
      "And no newly revealed part of the Quran comes to them except they listen to it without benefiting from it. Instead, they listen playfully, without caring about its contents.",
  21003:
      "They listened to it while their hearts were heedless of it. Those who do wrong by disbelieving concealed their private conversation where they said: Is this person who claims to be a messenger but a man like you, without any distinction over you? What he has brought is magic. So will you follow him knowing that he is a man like you and what he has brought is magic?",
  21004:
      "The Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم said: My Lord knows the conversation you concealed, for He knows everything said by anyone in the heavens and the earth. He is All-Hearing of His slaves' words and Omniscient of their deeds, and He will recompense His slaves for them.",
  21005:
      "Rather, they are confused regarding what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has brought. Sometimes, they would say: [It is] confused dreams that have no meaning. Other times, they said: No, in fact, he made it up without any basis. And sometimes they said: He is a poet. If he was truthful in his claim, he should bring us a miracle like the previous messengers, as they brought miracles like the staff of Moses and the she-camel of Saleh.",
  21006:
      "Not a single town before these [polytheists] who are making requests [for miracles] ever requested divine signs to be sent down was then granted them as requested and believed. In fact, they denied them, so We destroyed them. So, will these people believe?",
  21007:
      "And We did not send before you, O Messenger of Allah, except men from humanity to whom We would send revelation. We did not send them as angels, so ask the People of the Book before you if you do not know this.",
  21008:
      "And We did not make the messengers We sent as possessors of bodies who did not need food, nor were they immortal. They used to eat as others ate and were not to stay in this world forever without dying.",
  21009:
      "Then We fulfilled what We promised Our messengers, as We saved them and whoever We wished among the believers from destruction. And We destroyed those who transgressed the limits through disbelieving in Allah and committing sin.",
  21010:
      "We have revealed to you the Quran in which lies your honor and pride if you believe in and act according to its contents. Will you not understand this so that you hasten towards believing in it and practicing what it contains?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Day of Judgment is near, making it necessary to prepare for it.\n2. The Qur’an is revealed anew according to incidents and occurrences.\n3. The preoccupation of the hearts in futile things diverts them from the truth.\n4. Falsehood is unable to counter the truth through proof.\n5. Allah’s knowledge encompasses every saying and action of His servants.\n6. The idolaters’ differing in their stance towards the Prophet (peace be upon him) shows their disarray and confusion.\n7. Proof and miracles are of no benefit to stubborn opponents.\n8. Allah is with His messengers and those who believe, by aiding and helping them against the enemies.\n9. The Qur’an is an honour for one who believes in it and practices it.",
  21011:
      "There are many towns which We destroyed due to their wrongdoing by disbelieving [in Allah]! Then, We created other people after them.",
  21012:
      "Then, when those who were destroyed saw Our annihilating punishment, they began to run from their towns to flee the destruction.",
  21013:
      "They were asked mockingly: Do not flee, but return to the luxuries you enjoyed and your homes so that you can be questioned a little regarding your worldly possessions.",
  21014:
      "These wrongdoers confessing their sins said: Woe to us, and may we be destroyed. We were wrongdoers due to our disbelief in Allah.",
  21015:
      "So they continued confessing to their sins and praying for their own destruction until We made them like harvested crops, dead and lifeless.",
  21016:
      "And We did not create the heavens and the Earth, and whatever is in between in vain. Instead, We created them to prove Our power.",
  21017:
      "If We wanted to take a partner or child, We would have done so on Our part. But, We did not do this as We are free from this.",
  21018:
      "Instead, We throw the truth which We reveal to Our messengers at the falsehood of the disbelievers, and [the truth] destroys it, so their falsehood goes and disappears. And for you, O you who say Allah has taken a wife or son, is destruction, due to you describing Him with that which does not befit Him.",
  21019:
      "After mentioning how the taking of a spouse or child indicates insufficiency, Allah, the Exalted and Transcendent, explains that He is the Owner of this universe, stating: \n And to Him alone belongs the dominion of the heavens and Earth. And the angels with Him are neither too arrogant to worship Him, nor do they tire.",
  21020: "They constantly exalt Allah and are not bored of doing so.",
  21021:
      "But, the polytheists took deities besides Allah, which cannot revive the dead, so how do they worship something unable to do this?",
  21022:
      "If there were numerous deities in the heavens and the Earth, they would have been ruined due to the deities disputing their sovereignty. But the reality is not like this. Allah, Lord of the Throne, is free from the lie the polytheists describe Him with, namely that He has partners.",
  21023:
      "And Allah is unique in His dominion and decree. Nobody can question Him regarding what He has decreed and ordered, while He will ask His slaves about their deeds and recompense them accordingly.",
  21024:
      "But they took other deities besides Allah. O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Bring your proof that these deities are worthy of worship. This book which has been revealed to me and the books revealed to the [previous] messengers contain no proof of that. Instead, most polytheists only rely on ignorance and blind following. They turn away from accepting the truth.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Oppression is a cause of destruction for individuals and communities.\n2. Allah has not created anything in vain, because He is exalted from doing anything vain.\n3. The victory of truth and the defeat of falsehood are a divine custom.\n4. The angels have been inherently designed and created to obey Allah.\n5. The belief of idolatry has been broken through the proof of mutual negation.",
  21025:
      "And We have not sent any messenger before you, O Messenger, except that We have revealed to him that there is no true deity except Me, so, worship Me alone and do not associate any partner with Me.",
  21026:
      "The polytheists said that Allah has taken the angels as daughters. He (may He be Exalted) is free and sanctified from the lie they tell. The angels are the slaves of Allah, honored by Him and close to Him.",
  21027:
      "They do not precede their Lord in speech, so they do not speak until He orders them, and they act according to His command and do not oppose Him in any command.",
  21028:
      "He knows their past and future deeds. They do not ask to intercede except with His permission for those He approves intercession. They are wary out of their fear of Him, the Exalted. Thus, they do not oppose Him in any command or prohibition.",
  21029:
      "Hypothetically, if any of the angels were to say that he is worthy of worship instead of Allah, We would punish him for saying this with the torment of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. He will remain therein forever. And with this torment, We punish those who do wrong by disbelieving and associating partners with Allah.",
  21030:
      "Do those who disbelieved in Allah not know that the heavens and the Earth were joined without any gap between them, such that no rain could come down from the sky, then We split them apart? And We made every animal and plant from the water that comes down from the sky. Do they not consider this and believe in Allah alone?",
  21031:
      "And We created firm mountains on the Earth so that it does not shake those on its surface. We have made wide paths and ways through it so that they may find their way in their journeys towards their destinations.",
  21032:
      "And We made the sky a roof protected from falling without any pillars and protected from eavesdropping. But the polytheists turn away and do not reflect over the signs in the sky, such as the sun and moon.",
  21033:
      "Allah alone is the One who created the night for relaxation, the day for earning one's livelihood, the sun as a sign of the day, and the moon as a sign of night. The sun and moon run in specific orbits without moving away or deviating.",
  21034:
      "O Messenger, We have not given immortality in this life to any human before you. So, if your term ends in this life and you pass away, will they live forever after you? Never.",
  21035:
      "Every believing and disbelieving soul will taste death in this world. And We will test you, O people, in this worldly life through duties, favors, and difficulties. Then, after your death, you shall be returned to Us alone and nobody else. Then, We shall recompense you for your deeds accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. All the prophets are united on calling towards monotheism and rejecting idolatry.\n2. Allah is pure of having a child.\n3. The status of the angels with Allah is that they are His servants He has created for His obedience. They are not described as either male or female, but rather they are honoured servants.\n4. Intercession will only occur through Allah’s permission and His being pleased with the one being interceded for.\n5. The heavens and the earth were created in gradual steps.\n6. Death is the route of every living being. Neither the pious nor impious are immune from it.\n7. Tests can be through good, just as they are through bad.",
  21036:
      "O Messenger, when these polytheists see you, they only mock you, making [you] repulsive to their followers by saying: Is this the one who insults the idols you worship? At the same time, they reject the Quran that Allah revealed to them and the favors He favored them with, together with mocking you. So, they are more entitled to be criticized due to their accumulating every evil.",
  21037:
      "Man was created intrinsically to be hasty, so he wants things to happen before their due time. The polytheists asking for torment is a result of that nature. O you who are seeking My torment in haste! I shall show you precisely what you hastily seek, so there is no need to ask for it.",
  21038:
      "The disbelievers who reject resurrection say in haste: O Muslims! If you are truthful in what you claim, when will this resurrection happen that you promise us?",
  21039:
      "If only these disbelieving rejecters of the Resurrection were to know of the time when they will not be able to repel the Fire away from their faces and backs, and that there will be no one to help relieve them of the torment, and were convinced of that, they would not be so hasty.",
  21040:
      "This Fire they shall be punished with will come upon them suddenly, without them anticipating it. They will not be able to repel it or be given respite to repent and be granted mercy.",
  21041:
      "When Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم suffered from his people's mockery of him and their disbelief in him, Allah consoled him with His words: \n O Messenger, even if your people mock you, you are not unique because many messengers before you were also mocked. After their messengers warned them of it, the very torment the disbelievers made a mockery of engulfed them in this world.",
  21042:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these people hastily seeking the torment: Who will protect you through the night and day from the torment and destruction The Merciful intends to send upon you? Instead, they are turning away from the admonition and proofs of their Lord. They foolishly and ignorantly do not ponder over any of it.",
  21043:
      "Do they have deities that will protect them from Our torment? They are not capable of helping even themselves by removing any harm or acquiring any benefit! Whoever cannot help himself, how can he help others? Nor will they be protected from Our torment.",
  21044:
      "Instead, We have allowed these disbelievers and their forefathers to enjoy all Our favors with which We favored them. As time passes, they become deceived by these favors and remain firm in their disbelief, gradually leading themselves to destruction. Do these people, deceived by Our favors and hastily seeking Our torment, not see that We are reducing the land down from its borders by Our subdual of its inhabitants and conquering them? Do they not take lessons from that, lest the same not happen to them? These people will not be victorious; instead, they will be defeated.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The declaration of disbelief for the one who mocks the Messenger, regardless of whether it is through speech, action, or gesture.\n2. Being hasty is in the nature of a human, whilst calmness is a virtuous trait.\n3. Mocking the truth and the people of the truth is a trait of the disbelievers, past and present.\n4. No one can protect from the punishment of Allah, except Allah.\n5. For the disbelievers, blessings are means of gradually luring them into further destruction.\n6. The final outcome of falsehood is non-existence, whereas the final outcome of the truth is eternity.",
  21045:
      "Say, O Messenger: O people, I only warn you of Allah's torment through divine revelation that my Lord reveals to me. When those deaf to the truth are warned of Allah's torment, they do not listen to it [with the intention to] accept.",
  21046:
      "O Messenger, if some of your Lord's torment were to afflict these people seeking it hastily, they would say: Woe to us may we be destroyed! We were wrong in ascribing partners to Allah and rejecting what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought to us!",
  21047:
      "We will set up the scales of justice for the people [on the Day] of Resurrection to weigh their deeds. On that Day, no soul will be wronged by having its good actions decreased, or evil actions increased. Even if the weighed action is minute, like the weight equal to a mustard seed, We shall include it. And sufficient are We as a Reckoner.",
  21048:
      "We gave Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them) the Torah, which distinguished between the lawful and the unlawful; it was a means of guidance for those who believed in it and a reminder for those who feared their Lord.",
  21049:
      "Those who fear their Lord's punishment, Who they believe in, despite having not seen Him, and are fearful of the Hour.",
  21050:
      "This Quran, revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, is a reminder and an admonition for those who want to heed it. It contains an abundance of benefits and goodness. Despite all that, do you still reject it? Do you not acknowledge its contents, and will you not practice it?",
  21051:
      "And We gave Abraham, in his childhood, proof against his people, and We knew him well. We gave him the proof he deserved according to Our knowledge.",
  21052:
      "Remember when he told his father Azar and his people: What are these idols that you have made with your own hands and which you constantly worship?",
  21053:
      "His people told him: We found our forefathers worshipping them, so we also worship them following their example.",
  21054:
      "Abraham said to them: O you followers, you and your forefathers who are followed are in clear deviance from the path of truth!",
  21055:
      "His people asked him: Are you serious about what you said, or are you joking?",
  21056:
      "Abraham said: No, I am serious! Your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the Earth. He created them without precedent. I am from those who testify that He is your Lord and the Lord of the heavens and the Earth and that your idols have no share in that!",
  21057:
      "And Abraham said, in a manner inaudible to his people: By Allah! Once you have left them (the idols) to go to your festival, I will surely plot against them [in a way that] you will hate.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Heedlessness is a barrier from accepting the truth.\n2. The disbelievers cannot bear the least of the punishment; how will they bear the most severe?\n3. The fruit of acknowledging error is only acquired after repenting from it before the opportunity slips.\n4. The deeds of the servants of Allah will be weighed on the scales on the day of Judgement.\n5. Affirmation of the attribute of justice for Allah, and negation of oppression on His part.\n6. The importance of the strength of evidence in calling towards Allah.\n7. The harm of following blindly.\n8. Calling towards Allah is a serious call, not one to be taken as a joke.\n9. Gradual progression in changing evil; the need to start with the easiest to change first, and then onwards. Abraham started off by trying to change the evil of his people through speech and presenting evidences, then moved on to changing it by taking action.",
  21058:
      "So Abraham smashed their idols into small pieces and left the largest idol, hoping the people would return to it to ask who smashed the others.",
  21059:
      "So, when they returned and found their idols smashed into pieces, they asked one another: Who smashed our idols? Indeed, the one who has smashed them is from the wrongdoers because he has degraded that which deserves respect and reverence.",
  21060:
      "Some said: We heard a young man speaking badly about them and finding fault with them. He is called Abraham; perhaps he smashed them.",
  21061:
      "Their chiefs said: Bring Abraham in front of the people so they may witness his confession to what he did, and his confession will be your evidence against him.",
  21062:
      "So they brought Abraham (peace be upon him) and questioned him, blaming him: Was it you who did this heinous act to our idols, O Abraham?!",
  21063:
      "Abraham sarcastically exposed the idols' inability to the people, saying: I did not do it; rather, the biggest idol did. Ask your idols if, indeed, they are capable of speaking!",
  21064:
      "So they turned to one another, contemplating and considering. It then became clear to them that their idols do not benefit or harm in any way, so they were wrong in worshipping them instead of Allah.",
  21065:
      "They then returned to their stubbornness and denial, saying: O Abraham! Surely, you know these idols cannot speak, so how can you tell us to ask them? They intended it to be evidence in their favor, but it was evidence against them.",
  21066:
      "Abraham rebuked them: Do you then worship, instead of Allah, idols that do not benefit nor harm you; and are unable to remove harm or bring benefit to even themselves?",
  21067:
      "Shame on you, and shame on these idols you worship instead of Allah, which neither benefit nor harm! Do you not understand that? Will you not abandon their worship?",
  21068:
      "They resorted to force when they found themselves incapable of countering Abraham with proof. They said: If you are going to give Abraham a deterring punishment and seek revenge for your idols that he broke and destroyed, then burn him in a fire.",
  21069:
      "They lit a fire and threw Abraham into it, so We said: O fire! Become cool and peaceful for Abraham! And so it became such, and no harm came to him.",
  21070:
      "Abraham's (peace be upon him) people planned to burn him, and We foiled their plan. Instead, We made them the ones who were destroyed and defeated.",
  21071:
      "We saved Abraham and Lot and relocated them to the Levant that We had blessed by having sent many prophets to it and by scattering therein many forms of goodness for the creation.",
  21072:
      "And We gifted Abraham with Isaac when he supplicated to his Lord to grant him a child. In addition, We also blessed him with Jacob. We made each of the three (Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob) pious and obedient to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The permissibility of using various strategies in expounding the truth and counteracting falsehood.\n2. The insistence of the people of falsehood on their falsehood is due to their stubbornness, not the strength of their evidence, nor the weakness of the evidence of the people of tmth.\n3. The people of falsehood hold onto evidence they assume to be in their favour, but which are in reality against them.\n4. Being harsh in speech can sometimes be a means of changing evil, if there is no greater harm that arises due to it.\n5. Resorting to using force is proof of incapability to counteract using evidence.\n6. Allah’s help for His believing servants and His saving them from difficulties comes from ways that are unanticipated.",
  21073:
      "We made them into leaders whom the people followed in goodness. They would invite people to worship Allah alone with His, the Exalted's, permission. We also revealed to them: Do good actions, perform prayer perfectly, and give Zakat. They were obedient to Us.",
  21074:
      "And to Lot, We granted the ability to judge fairly between disputing parties, together with sound knowledge of his religion. We also saved him from the torment We sent upon the people of his town (Sodom) who were involved in a shameful act. Indeed, they were corrupt people who abandoned the worship of their Lord.",
  21075:
      "And We admitted him into Our Mercy when We saved him from the torment that befell his people. Indeed, he was of those who obeyed Our commands and avoided Our prohibitions.",
  21076:
      "O Messenger, remember the story of Noah when he called upon Allah before the time of Abraham and Lot. So We responded to him by granting him what he asked for. We saved him and his believing family members from great distress.",
  21077:
      "We saved him from the plot of those of his people who rejected the signs that We supported him with, those signs that pointed to his truthfulness. Indeed, they were evil, corrupt people, so We destroyed them all by drowning them.",
  21078:
      "O Messenger, remember the story of David and his son Solomon (peace be upon them) when they were passing judgment in the case brought to them regarding the two people who disputed. One of them had a herd of sheep that went into the field of the other at night and ruined the crops. We witnessed the judgment of David and Solomon; no part of their judgment evaded Our knowledge.",
  21079:
      "We gave Solomon the complete understanding of the case but not his father David, yet We granted each one with messengership and knowledge of the sacred law, not exclusively Solomon only. We subjugated the mountains for David, which would exalt [Us] along with him. We also subjugated the birds for him. We were the One Who gave the understanding, the ability to judge fairly, knowledge, and subjugation [of the mountains and birds].",
  21080:
      "We exclusively taught David, and not Solomon, the art of making body armor to protect you from anyone who tries to attack you with weapons. O people, will you show gratitude for this favor We [Allah] favored you with?",
  21081:
      "And We subjugated the raging wind for Solomon. At his command, whenever he would command it to, it would blow to the Levant, which We had blessed by sending prophets and the goodness We showered within it. We know everything; nothing is hidden from Us.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Doing good deeds, prayer and Zakat are from those things the Heavenly Religions agreed upon.\n2. Saving the people of the truth and destroying the people of falsehood is a divine code.\n3. Indulgence in immorality is the means to being afflicted in an annihilating punishment.\n4. Uprightness is a means of entering into the Mercy of Allah.\n5. Divine help is in favour of the people of the truth over the people of falsehood.\n6. Prayer is a means of salvation from troubles.",
  21082:
      "We subjugated some devils who would dive into the oceans for him and extract pearls, and do other things like construction. We supervised their numbers and work; nothing escapes Us.",
  21083:
      "O Messenger, remember the story of Job (peace be upon him), when he supplicated to his Lord, the Exalted, at the time of affliction, saying: O my Lord! I have been afflicted with an illness and loss of family, yet You are the Most Merciful of all those who show mercy, so remove the afflictions that have befallen me.",
  21084:
      "And so We responded to his supplication and removed the harm that had befallen him. We granted him the family he had lost and more along with them. We did all that out of Our Mercy so that it serves as a reminder for everyone who is submissive in worshipping Allah so that they may exercise patience just as Job did.",
  21085:
      "O Messenger, remember Ishmael, Idris, and Dhul-Kifl (peace be upon them). Each of them was from the patient ones during times of affliction and [patient] in carrying out whatever responsibility Allah placed on them.",
  21086:
      "We admitted them into Our mercy, made them prophets, and admitted them into Paradise. Indeed, they were among the pious slaves of Allah who acted on Allah's obedience and whose private and public lives were ones of piety.",
  21087:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the story of the companion of the whale, Jonah (peace be upon him), when he left [his people] without His Lord's permission, angry with his people for their insistence on sin. He thought We would not constrain him by punishing him for leaving, but then he was afflicted with a severe form of constraint and imprisonment when the whale swallowed him. He then supplicated in the veils of the darkness of the whale's belly, the ocean, and the night, acknowledging his sin and repenting to Allah for it, saying: None is worthy of worship except You. You are pure and sanctified. Indeed, I am one of the wrongdoers.",
  21088:
      "So, We responded to his supplication and saved him from severe distress by removing him from the veils of darkness and the belly of the whale. As We saved Jonah from this distress, We will save the believers when they fall into distress and supplicate to Allah.",
  21089:
      "Also, remember, O Messenger, the story of Zechariah (peace be upon him), when he supplicated to his Lord, saying: O my Lord! Do not leave me alone, childless. You are the best of those who remain, so grant me a child that remains after me.",
  21090:
      "We responded to his supplication and granted him a child, John. [In the process], We also cured his wife, and she became fertile after she had been barren up until that point. Indeed, Zechariah, his wife, and their son were quick to do righteous deeds and would supplicate to Us, eager for Our reward and fearful of Our punishment, totally humbling themselves before Us.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Patience is a quality of the prophets (peace be upon them).\n2. Piety is a means of Mercy.\n3. Acknowledging one’s sin is one of the etiquettes of supplication.\n4. Turning to Allah is a way of relieving one’s troubles.\n5. There is virtue in seeking children who live on after you die.\n6. Continue to be mindful of Allah in prosperity, Allah will acknowledge you at times of difficulty.",
  21091:
      "Also, remember O Messenger, the story of Mary (peace be upon her), who guarded her private part against fornication. Allah sent Gabriel (peace be upon him) to her, and he blew into her. Consequently, she became pregnant with Jesus (peace be upon him). They were both signs for the people of Allah's Power and that nothing can render Allah incapable, as He created Jesus without a father.",
  21092:
      "O people, this is your creed, the only creed: monotheism, the religion of Islam. I am your Lord, so only worship Me.",
  21093:
      "The people differed: some were monotheists, others were polytheists, some were disbelievers, and others were believers. All these different types of people will return to Us alone on the Day of Resurrection, and We will recompense them for their deeds accordingly.",
  21094:
      "So whoever from among them does righteous deeds while believing in Allah, His messengers, and in the Last Day, will not be denied the due of his righteous deeds. Instead, Allah will express gratitude and then multiply his reward for him. He will find it recorded in his book of deeds on the Day he is resurrected, and he will be pleased.",
  21095:
      "It is impossible for the people of a town that We destroyed due to their disbelief to return to this world to repent and for that repentance to be accepted.",
  21096:
      "[They will never return], even once the barrier of Gog and Magog is opened, and they, on that Day, emerge hurriedly descending from every high piece of land.",
  21097:
      "[The Day of] Resurrection is close to their emergence, and the horror and difficulties of the Day of Resurrection will be on display. [At this time], the disbelievers will be left wide-eyed because of its horror, saying: Oh, may we be destroyed! We were indulged in futility, preoccupied instead of preparing for this great day. Instead, we were wrongdoers by disbelieving and committing sins.",
  21098:
      "All of you, O polytheists, the idols you worship, and the people and jinn who are content with you worshipping them instead of Allah shall be the fuel of Hell. You and everything you worship will surely enter it.",
  21099:
      "If these things that are worshipped were, in reality, gods worthy of being worshipped, they would not be entering the Fire with their worshippers. Yet they will all be entering it, having to remain in it forever, never to come out.",
  21100:
      "They will find it hard to breathe due to the severity of the pain they will experience. They will be unable to hear anything due to the immense and dreadful horror that will afflict them.",
  21101:
      "When the polytheists said that indeed, Jesus and the angels who were worshipped would therefore enter the Fire, Allah said: Verily, those regarding whom it was decreed in the Knowledge of Allah that they would be from the people of happiness [in the Hereafter], such as Jesus (peace be upon him), will be distanced from the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Reference made to chastity and mention of its virtue.\n2. Unanimity of the divine messages in monotheism and the fundamental acts of worship.\n3. Faith in monotheism is a prerequisite for the acceptance of good deeds.\n4. The opening of the barrier of Gog and Magog is one of the major signs preceding the Hour.\n5. Negligence in preparing for the Day of Judgment leads to having to suffer from its horrors.",
  21102:
      "The sound of Hell will not reach their ears, while they shall reside among whatever luxuries and enjoyment they desire. Their bliss will never end.",
  21103:
      "When it covers its inhabitants, the great horror of the Fire shall not scare the people of happiness. The angels will welcome them with glad tidings, saying: This is your day that you were promised in the worldly life and given glad tidings of its bliss.",
  21104:
      "On that Day, We will roll up the heavens like the rolling up of a scroll and gather the creation in the state they were created in the first instance. We have promised that it will happen, a promise that there is no going back on. We shall indeed fulfill Our promise.",
  21105:
      "Indeed, We had written in the books that We revealed to the messengers after We had written it in the Preserved Tablet that the Earth would be inherited by the pious, obedient slaves of Allah, the nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  21106:
      "Verily, in the admonition We revealed, there is a message for people who worship their Lord according to what He has legislated for them. It is they who truly benefit from it.",
  21107:
      "O Muhammad, We have not sent you as a messenger except to be a mercy to all creation because you are eager to guide people and save them from Allah's torment.",
  21108:
      "Say, O Messenger: It is only revealed to me from my Lord that your true deity is only One; He has no partner, and He is Allah. So submit by believing in Him and performing acts of obedience to Him.",
  21109:
      "O Messenger, if these people turn away from what you have brought to them, then tell them: I have informed you that we are entirely dissociated from each other, and I do not know when Allah's promised torment will descend upon you.",
  21110:
      "Indeed, Allah knows of the speech you disclose and that which you keep secret. Nothing from that evades Him, and He will recompense you for it accordingly.",
  21111:
      "I do not know whether your respite from punishment is a test for you or whether it is to lure you further [into destruction] and let you enjoy yourself by persisting in disbelief and misguidance until a time decreed that only Allah knows.",
  21112:
      "Supplicating to his Lord, Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم said: O my Lord! Judge well between us and those of our people who have persisted in disbelief. We seek help solely from our Merciful Lord against your statements of disbelief and rejection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Piety is a means to achieving power on Earth.\n2. The Prophet peace be upon him is a mercy for the worlds.\n3. The Messenger peace be upon him does not know the Ghaib.\n4. Allah is ever aware of what His servants say.",
  22000:
      "The Pilgrimage (Surah Al-Hajj)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nGlorifying Allah, Exalted and Transcendent, and venerating His symbols, and submitting to His command.\n•    Explanation:",
  22001:
      "O people, fear your Lord by complying with what He has ordered you with and desisting from what He has forbidden you. The earthquake and other horrors accompanying the Day of Resurrection are dreadful. They must be prepared for through deeds that please Allah.",
  22002:
      "On that Day, you will witness every nursing mother neglecting her nursing child, and every pregnant being will abort her pregnancy from intense fear. You shall see people losing themselves, like drunkards, due to the extreme horror of the situation, and not from alcohol. Rather, the severity of Allah's punishment will cause them to lose their minds.",
  22003:
      "After mentioning the horrors that will accompany the establishment of the Day of Judgment, Allah responds to those who deny the Revival and Resurrection, stating: \n Amongst people is he who argues regarding Allah's power to resurrect the dead, without any knowledge to take support from, and who in belief and word follows every rebel against His Lord from among the devils and leaders of misguidance.",
  22004:
      "It has been decreed regarding such rebellious devils among humans and jinn that whoever follows them and believes in them will be misguided by them from the path of truth. They will send these people towards the torment of Hell through disbelief and acts of disobedience that lead towards it.",
  22005:
      "O people, if you have any doubt regarding Our power to resurrect you after death, think about your creation: We created your father, Adam, from soil; then We created his children from sperm which the man ejaculates into the woman's womb; then the sperm turns into solid blood; then the solid blood turns into a lump of flesh; then the lump of flesh turns into either a fully formed creation which remains in the womb until it comes out alive as a child or into an unformed creation which the womb aborts, to show Our power by creating you in stages. We then settle in the wombs, whatever fetus We wish until it is born in a fixed period of nine months. Then, We bring you out of your mothers' wombs as infants so that you reach your full strength and intelligence. Amongst you are some who die before this, and amongst you are those who reach old age where strength and intelligence weaken to the extent that they become worse than a child, no longer knowing anything they used to know. And you will see the Earth dry without any plants on it. Then, when We send down rainwater on it, it opens up with plants, rises due to the plants growing, and brings forth every type of beautiful plant.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is necessary to prepare for the Day of Judgment through the provision of piety.\n2. Compassion has been established for mothers, especially during breastfeeding.\n3. The horrors of the Day of Judgment are severe.\n4. Those who deny resurrection have no proof they rely on.\n5. To create gradually is the custom of Allah.\n6. The initial creation is a proof for the possibility of resurrection.\n7. The phenomenon of rain and the subsequent growing of plants on earth is a physical proof of the resurrection of the dead.",
  22006:
      "That which We have mentioned to you; namely the beginning of your creation, its stages, and the conditions of those born amongst you, is so that you believe that Allah Who created you is the Truth in which there is no doubt, as opposed to the idols you worship and so that you believe He will revive the dead, and that He is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  22007:
      "And so that you believe the Hour is to come, without any doubt, and that Allah will resurrect the dead from their graves to recompense them for their deeds accordingly.",
  22008:
      "When Allah the Exalted mentions the condition of misguidedness resulting from blind following in the third verse, He cites the state of the misguidance of the leaders of disbelief in this verse, stating: \n Among the disbelievers is he who argues regarding the Oneness of Allah without any proof to reach the truth, nor a guide to direct them to it, nor an illuminating book revealed by Allah to guide them to it.",
  22009:
      "He turns his face away in arrogance to direct people away from believing and entering the religion of Allah. He who fits this description shall have disgrace in this world due to the punishment which will befall him, and We shall make him taste the torment of the burning Fire in the Hereafter.",
  22010:
      "He will be told: That torment you tasted is due to the disbelief and the acts of disobedience you committed. Allah does not punish any of His creation except due to a sin.",
  22011:
      "Amongst people is a conflicted person who worships Allah in doubt. If good, such as health and wealth, come to him, he remains on his belief and worship of Allah. But, if an affliction like illness or poverty afflicts him, he perceives his religion as a bad omen and then renounces it. He has lost this world because his disbelief will never increase him in a share of the world not written for him, and he has lost his Hereafter due to Allah's torment, which will meet him. That is the clearest loss.",
  22012:
      "He worships idols instead of Allah, which cannot harm him if he disobeys them, nor can they benefit him if he obeys them. Supplication to idols that can neither harm nor benefit is misguidance far from the truth.",
  22013:
      "This disbeliever who worships idols calls upon idols whose harm is more likely than their benefit. Evil is the deity whose harm is more likely than its benefit. How bad it is as a helper to the one who seeks its help and as a companion to those who accompany it.",
  22014:
      "Allah will admit those who believe in Him and do righteous deeds into gardens with rivers flowing beneath its palaces. Allah does what He pleases by showing mercy to whom He wants to show mercy and punishing whom He wants to punish. Nothing can compel Him; may He be Exalted.",
  22015:
      "Whoever thinks Allah will not help His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم in this world and the Hereafter should extend a rope to the ceiling of his house and then strangle himself by hanging himself above the ground. Then, he should see if that removes the anger he feels in his heart. Allah is the Helper of His Prophet, whether his opponents like it or not.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride is a characteristic which stops a person from being guided to the truth.\n2. It is from the justice of Allah that He only punishes due to sins.\n3. Faith and good actions are a means of entering paradise.\n4. Allah helps His Prophet and His religion, even if the disbelievers dislike it.",
  22016:
      "Just as We clarified the clear proofs for resurrection, We revealed the Quran to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم as clear verses. Allah directs whomever He wishes through His grace to the path of guidance and righteousness.",
  22017:
      "Those who believe in Allah from this nation, the Jews, the Sabians (a group of followers of one of the prophets), the Christians, the Magians (fire-worshippers), the polytheists; Allah will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection, then He will admit the believers amongst them into Paradise and admit the others into the Fire. Allah is a Witness to all the sayings and deeds of His slaves, with nothing hidden from Him, and He shall recompense them for these deeds accordingly.",
  22018:
      "O Messenger, do you not know that the angels in the heavens and the believing humans and jinn on Earth prostrate to Allah out of obedience? The sun, moon, stars in the sky, mountains, trees, and creatures on Earth prostrate to Him compliantly. As do many people prostrate to Him out of obedience. But many refuse to prostrate to Him out of obedience; thus, Allah's torment became justified for them due to their disbelief. Whoever Allah decrees disgrace and shame for, due to his disbelief, has nobody to honor him. Allah does what He wishes. None can compel Him; may He be Exalted.",
  22019:
      "After mentioning those who prostrate to Him in obedience and those who refrain, Allah the Exalted and Transcendent proceeds to comment on their respective destinations, stating: \n These are two groups arguing regarding their Lord as to which of them is right: The group of believers and the group of disbelievers. The Fire will encompass the disbelievers, just as clothes cover the person wearing them, and boiling water will be poured on their heads.",
  22020:
      "The intestines in their abdomens will melt due to its intense heat, which will reach their skin and melt it.",
  22021:
      "Iron hammers are in the Fire for them, with which the angels will hit their heads.",
  22022:
      "Whenever they try to leave the Fire, due to the severe distress they will face, they will be returned to it and told: Taste the punishment of the burning Fire.",
  22023:
      "Allah will admit the party of believers who believed in Allah and did righteous deeds into gardens with rivers flowing beneath its palaces and trees. Allah will adorn them with gold bracelets, embellish them with pearls, and their clothes therein will be silk.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Guidance is in Allah’s hands; He grants it to whomever He wishes amongst His servants.\n2. Allah watches over all the actions and conditions of His servants.\n3. All the creation of Allah submit to Him by decree, and the believers submit to Him in obedience.\n4. The punishment will befall the people of disbelief and disobedience, and mercy is established for the people of faith and obedience.",
  22024:
      "Allah guided them in this worldly life towards the best of speech, such as [saying the] testimony that there is no one worthy of worship besides Allah, takbir (proclaiming Allah's greatness), and tahmid (praising Allah). He guided them toward the praiseworthy path of Islam.",
  22025:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah, turn others away from entering Islam and prevent people from the Sacred Mosque, such as what the polytheists did in the year of Hudaybiyah; we will cause them to taste a painful punishment. That (the Sacred Mosque) is the mosque which We have made the direction for people in their prayers and one of the rites of Hajj and Umrah, and in which the resident of Mecca and one who comes there who is not from the people of Mecca are equal. Should anyone intend to deviate by purposefully doing an act of disobedience therein, We will cause him to taste a painful punishment.",
  22026:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when We clarified to Abraham (peace be upon him) the place of The House and its boundaries after it was unknown. We revealed to him: Do not associate anything with Me in worship but rather worship Me alone. And purify My House from physical and abstract impurities for those who circumambulate it and perform prayer therein.",
  22027:
      "And proclaim amongst the people inviting them towards pilgrimage of this House We ordered you to build. They will come to you walking and riding on every lean camel due to the difficulty it endured from traveling. The camels will bring them, carrying them from every distant path.",
  22028:
      "So that they come to what will bring them benefit such as forgiveness of sins, attaining reward, unity, and so forth; and so that they mention the Name of Allah on the sacrificial animals they slaughter on appointed days, which are: the tenth of Dhul-Hijjah and three days after it, in gratitude to Allah for the camels, cows, and sheep He granted them. So eat of these sacrificial animals and feed from them those who are extremely poor.",
  22029:
      "Then, they should complete what remains of their Hajj rites, coming out of the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity) by shaving their heads, clipping their nails, and removing the dirt that accumulated on them due to the state of Ihram. They should then fulfill the Hajj, Umrah, or sacrifice of an animal that they made binding on themselves. They should perform the Tawaf al-Ifadah (obligatory circumambulation) of the House, which Allah freed from the control of tyrants.",
  22030:
      "That which you have been ordered with, i.e., coming out of the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity) by shaving the head, clipping the nails, removing dirt, fulfilling the vow, and circumambulating the House, is what Allah has made obligatory on you. So respect what Allah has made obligatory on you. Whoever avoids what Allah has ordered him to avoid during the state of Ihram (ritual sanctity), out of respect for not transgressing the limits of Allah and not making lawful its prohibitions, then this is better for him in this world and the Hereafter in the sight of his Lord, may He be Exalted. O people! Camels, cows, and sheep amongst livestock have been made lawful for you. Allah has not made unlawful for you hami, bahirah, or wasilah. He only made what you find in the Quran unlawful for you, such as carrion, blood, etc. Stay far away from filth, such as idols and false speech, which includes lying against Allah or His creation.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Paradise is free from actions and statements that would spoil it.\n2. The sanctity of the Sacred House demands being cautious of sins therein more than other places.\n3. It is necessary to purify the houses of Allah from symbolic and physical impurities.\n4. The House of Allah is the refuge of the believers’ hearts in every era and place.\n5. The benefits of Hajj, be they worldly or of the Hearafter, return to the people.\n6. Being grateful for blessings necessitates compassion on the weak.\n7. It is necessary to purify the hearts of corrupt beliefs and to purify the tongues of lying.",
  22031:
      "Refrain from this, turning away from every religion besides the religion He is pleased with, without associating any partner with Him in worship. Whoever associates a partner with Allah, it is as though He has fallen from the sky and is either snatched away by birds or swept by the wind to a remote place.",
  22032:
      "This is from the monotheism, sincerity to Allah, abandonment of idols, and refraining from false speech that Allah has ordered. Whoever honors the signs of the religion, amongst them sacrificial animals and the rites of Hajj, then such honoring is part of the hearts fearing their Lord.",
  22033:
      "There are benefits for you in the sacrificial animals you slaughter at the House. For example, riding [it], wool, breeding, and milk, up until the time appointed for its slaughter when you are near the House of Allah that He freed from the control of tyrants.",
  22034:
      "For every previous nation, We made rites to shed blood [of a sacrificial animal] as a means of closeness to Allah, in the hope they will mention Allah's name at the time of slaughtering these sacrificial animals in gratitude to Allah for the camels, cows, and sheep He granted them. The one deserving of worship, O people, is One God who has no partner, so submit to Him alone through submission and obedience. And O Messenger, tell those who are humbly submissive and sincere what will please them.",
  22035:
      "Those who, when they remember Allah, fear His punishment and thus distance [themselves] from opposing His command, perform their prayer completely, exercise patience if any calamity befalls them, and spend in the different avenues of righteousness from what Allah has given them.",
  22036:
      "And We have made the camels and cows taken to the House amongst the sacred signs and symbols of the religion. In them are worldly and religious benefits for you, so say \"in the name of Allah\" when slaughtering them after their feet have been lined up while standing and one of their feet has been tied so they do not flee. Then, when they fall on their sides after being slaughtered, eat of them, O those who are sacrificing, and give of them to those poor who desist from begging and the poor who come forward to be granted a share of them. Just as We made them submissive to you so that you place loads on them and ride them, We have also made them submissive to you so they are led to the place you slaughter them in, as a means of closeness to Allah, so that you may be grateful to Allah for the favor of making them submissive to you.",
  22037:
      "Neither the meat of the sacrificial animals you offer nor their blood ever reach Allah, nor is it raised towards Him. Instead, your fear of Allah therein is raised towards Him through being sincere to Him in your obedience, seeking closeness to Him through it. In that way, Allah made them submissive to you so that you proclaim Allah's greatness (takbir), thanking Him for the truth He has directed you to. O Messenger, inform those who excel in worshipping their Lord and dealing with His creation of what will please them.",
  22038:
      "Allah defends those who believe in Him from the evil of their enemies. Allah does not love anyone who is treacherous in his trust and who is ungrateful for the favors of Allah by not showing thanks to Him for it; in fact, Allah despises him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Using examples to make intangible forms easy through giving them a physical form is a great educational objective.\n2. Respecting the signs of Allah stems from the piety of the hearts.\n3. The one who benefits from obedience is the servant himself.\n4. Humility is virtuous.\n5. The sacrificial animal is amongst the signs of Allah.\n6. Feeding the pauper who refrains from begging and the beggar is one of the objectives of establishing the sacrifice of animals.\n7. The acceptance of actions depends on sincerity for Allah.\n8. Doing good is a means of good fortune.\n9. Faith is a means of Allah defending and taking the servant into consideration.",
  22039:
      "Allah the Exalted and Transcendent mentions that He defends the believers such that their hearts become reassured. He then gives them permission to fight the disbelievers, stating: \n Allah has permitted the believers to fight the polytheists who fought them because their enemies oppressed them. Allah has the power to help the believers against their enemies without fighting. However, the wisdom of Allah required that the believers be tested by fighting the disbelievers.",
  22040:
      "Those whom the disbelievers unjustly exiled from their homes, not due to any crime they committed but because they said: \"Our Lord is Allah; we have no Lord besides Him.\" Had Allah not legislated for the prophets and believers fighting against their enemies, they would have transgressed against the places of worship, destroying the monasteries of the monks, Christian churches, Jewish synagogues, and the mosques of the Muslims which have been made for prayer and in which the Muslims remember Allah abundantly. Allah will help those who help His religion and Prophet. Allah has the power to help whoever helps His religion and is Almighty, with nobody able to overcome Him.",
  22041:
      "These people who have been promised help are those who, if We establish them on Earth by helping them against their enemies, would perform prayer perfectly, give Zakat of their wealth, command what the sacred law has commanded, and forbid what it has forbidden. To Allah alone is where matters return, with respect to reward and punishment.",
  22042:
      "O Messenger, if your people reject you, be patient. You are not the first messenger to be rejected by his people. Before your people, the people of Noah rejected Noah, Ād rejected Hūd, and Thamūd rejected Saleh.",
  22043: "Abraham's people rejected him, and the people of Lot rejected Lot.",
  22044:
      "The people of Midian rejected Shuayb, and Pharaoh and his people rejected Moses. I delayed the punishment of their people, gradually leading them to destruction. I then seized them with the torment. So contemplate how I reproached them; I destroyed them due to their disbelief.",
  22045:
      "How many towns that did wrong because of their disbelief have We destroyed with an obliterating punishment? Their homes are ruined and empty of inhabitants. How many wells are there with nobody to drink from due to being destroyed? How many lofty decorated palaces are there which could not save their residents from the torment?",
  22046:
      "Did these people who reject what the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم brought not travel throughout the land to see the remains of those destroyed towns so that they would reflect with their minds to take heed and listen to their stories to learn from them? Blindness is not the blindness of eyesight, but rather destructive blindness is the blindness of insight, where such a person does not reflect or take lessons.\n\n• Beneficial Points\n1. Striving in Allah’s path is a test for the believer.\n2. All honour and power belongs to Allah.\n3. The legality of striving in Allah’s path is established, to protect places of worship.\n4. Divine help is attached to those who help the religion.\n5. Establishing the religion is a means through which Allah’s assistance is attained for his believing servants.\n6. The Messenger (peace be upon him) was consoled through knowing he is not the only one whose people rejected him and the outcome of the rejecters is destruction.\n7. Blindness of the heart is a barrier to reflecting over the signs of Allah.",
  22047:
      "O Messenger, the disbelievers amongst your people hastened to seek immediate punishment in this world and deferred punishment in the Hereafter when they were warned of them [coming]. Allah will never break what he has promised them. Amongst the immediate punishment is what befell them on the day of Badr. And one day of torment in the Hereafter is equivalent to a thousand years of what you count in worldly years due to the suffering it contains.",
  22048:
      "How many a town of transgressing disbelievers did I give respite to, did not punish them instantly to bring them around? Then, I punished them with an obliterating punishment. To Me alone is their return on the Day of Resurrection, and then I will recompense them for their disbelief with everlasting torment.",
  22049:
      "O humanity, I am only a warner to you, conveying to you what I have been sent with and clear in my warning.",
  22050:
      "So those who believe in Allah and did righteous deeds will be forgiven of their sins by their Lord, and they will receive a noble provision in Paradise that will never end.",
  22051:
      "Those who strive to reject Our verses, assuming they will be able to render Allah powerless and escape Him so that He cannot punish them, are the companions of the Inferno, constantly remaining in it just as companions remain with one another.",
  22052:
      "O Messenger, We did not send any messenger or prophet before you except that when he read the Book of Allah, the Devil cast in his recitation that which confuses the people [to think] that it is revelation. Then Allah would nullify what the Devil cast and affirm His verses. Allah knows everything. Nothing is hidden from Him. He is Wise in His creating, decreeing, and planning.",
  22053:
      "The Devil casting [confusion] in the recitation of the Prophet is so that Allah makes what he casts as a test for the hypocrites and those polytheists whose hearts have hardened. The wrongdoers amongst the hypocrites and polytheists show enmity towards Allah and His Messenger and are distant from the truth and guidance.",
  22054:
      "And so that those whom Allah gave knowledge are convinced that the Quran revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is the truth Allah revealed to you, O Messenger, thus increasing their faith in it and so that their hearts submit and humble themselves before it. Allah is the Guide of those who have faith toward the straight path of truth, which contains no crookedness, as a reward for submitting to it.",
  22055:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah and reject His Messenger will remain in doubt about the Quran Allah revealed to you. They will continue upon that until the Hour comes to them suddenly or the punishment of a Day comes to them in which there is no mercy or good for them, which is the Day of Resurrection.\n\n• Beneficial Points\n1. Injustice is one of the causes of nations being destroyed.\n2. Gradually leading the oppressor away until he exceeds the bounds in his oppression is a divine custom.\n3. Allah has protected His Book from changes and tampering, and He has turned the schemes of the satan’s supporters away from it.\n4. Hypocrisy and hardness of the heart are two destructive illnesses.\n5. Knowledge is a means of distinguishing between falsehood and truth.\n6. Faith is the result of knowledge, and humbling and submitting to Allah’ orders is the result of faith.",
  22056:
      "Dominion on the Day of Resurrection - when the punishment they were promised shall come to them - will only be for Allah alone. He will have no competitor for it. He (may He be Exalted) will judge between the believers and the disbelievers. He will judge each of them as they deserve: those who believed and did righteous deeds will be granted a great reward in gardens of everlasting bliss that will never end.",
  22057:
      "And those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected the signs/verses He revealed to His Messenger will be humiliated with a humiliating punishment in Hell.",
  22058:
      "And those who left their homes and homelands seeking Allah's pleasure and in honor of His religion and were killed while striving in His path or died, Allah shall grant them an everlasting provision in Paradise. Indeed, Allah (may He be Exalted) is the Best of providers.",
  22059:
      "Allah will admit them into a place they shall be pleased with (i.e., Paradise). Allah knows their deeds and intentions; He is forbearing in that He did not hasten to punish them for their negligence.",
  22060:
      "Regarding what was mentioned about those who emigrate in the path of Allah being admitted into Paradise and permission for the oppressed to retaliate justly without incurring sin, if the transgressor returns to his transgression, Allah helps the one subjected to transgression. Allah pardons the sins of the believers and forgives them.",
  22061:
      "Helping the one subject to transgression is because Allah is capable of doing as He wishes. His capabilities include merging the night into the day and the day into the night by increasing one and decreasing the other. Allah also hears the statements of His slaves and knows their deeds; nothing is hidden from Him, and He shall recompense them for it accordingly.",
  22062:
      "What was mentioned about merging the night into the day and the day into the night is because Allah is the Truth. Consequently, His religion is true, His promise is true, and His helping of the believers is also true. The idols that the polytheists worship instead of Allah are false and have no basis. And Allah is the Most High, above His creation, in essence, power, and subjugation. Allah is the Grand to Whom all majesty, grandeur, and exaltedness belong.",
  22063:
      "O Messenger, do you not see that Allah sends the rain from the sky, and so the Earth becomes green owing to the vegetation that grows upon it after the rain has fallen? Allah is kind to His slaves by sending rain to them and making the Earth grow crops. He is also aware of their requirements; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  22064:
      "To Him alone belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth. He is The Independent who never needs His creation; the Praiseworthy in all conditions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The status of migration in Islam and its virtue.\n2. The permissibility of seeking revenge equally.\n3. The help of Allah for the one wronged can come in the world or the Hearafter.\n4. Affirmation of sublime attributes for Allah as befits His exaltedness; like the attributes of hearing, sight and highness.",
  22065:
      "O Messenger, do you not see that Allah has made the animals and other objects on Earth subservient to you and people's needs and benefits? He also made subservient for you the ships that sail the oceans with His command and subjugation, sailing from land to land. He also holds back the sky so it does not fall onto Earth except with His order. If He allowed it to fall, it would. Allah is Kind and Merciful, so He subjugated these things for them despite their wrongdoing.",
  22066:
      "Allah is the only One Who gave you life because He brought you into existence when you were nonexistent. He will then cause you to die when your lives expire and then revive you after death to hold you accountable for your deeds and recompense you for them accordingly. Verily, man is ever in denial of the favors of Allah by worshipping other than Allah, despite those favors being so apparent.",
  22067:
      "I have made a set of laws for people of every creed. O Messenger, do not let the polytheists and people of other religions dispute your law with you because you are more deserving of the truth than them, as they are the people of falsehood. Invite the people towards sincerely proclaiming the oneness of Allah; indeed, you are on a straight path in which there is no deviation.",
  22068:
      "If they insist on arguing with you after the evidence has become clear, leave their matter to Allah and warn them: Allah knows the deeds you do, none of your deeds are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for them accordingly.",
  22069:
      "Allah will judge between the believers and the disbelievers from among His slaves on the Day of Resurrection in the matters of religion they differed over in this world.",
  22070:
      "O Messenger, do you not know that Allah knows all that is in the heavens and on Earth; nothing in them is hidden from Him, and His knowledge of it is recorded in the Preserved Tablet. Knowing all of that is easy for Allah.",
  22071:
      "The polytheists worship idols instead of Allah; idols which Allah did not reveal any proof of their worship [being acceptable] in His books. Neither do they have any evidence of knowledge for it; their only support for that is blind following of their forefathers. The wrongdoers will have no helper that will protect them from Allah's torment that will befall them.",
  22072:
      "When you recite Our clear verses of the Quran to them, you will recognize the objecting frowns on the faces of the disbelievers when they hear them. It is as if their extreme anger would make them violently assault those who recite Our verses to them. O Messenger, say to them: Shall I inform you of something worse than this anger and frowning? It is the Fire that Allah has promised to admit the disbelievers into. How terrible their abode is!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From among the bounties of Allah is His making that which is in the heavens and on earth in favour for them.\n2. Affirmation of the attributes of benevolence and mercy for Allah.\n3. The knowledge of Allah encompassing everything that is in the heavens and earth.\n4. Following blindly was the reason the idolaters persisted on their ascribing partners to Allah.\n5. The people of falsehood resort to violence because they are incapable to challenging evidence with evidence.",
  22073:
      "O people, a parable is about to be presented, so listen carefully and take a lesson from it. Indeed, those idols and other things you worship instead of Allah cannot even create a fly despite its small size because of its inability. Even if they were to convene to try to create it, they would not be able to achieve it. And if a fly were to take anything away from them, such as perfume, etc., they would not have the power to reclaim it. Their inability to create a fly and reclaim anything from it makes their inability to do anything greater than that evident. How can they worship these idols instead of Allah, despite their inability? This pursuer - i.e., the worshipped idol incapable of reclaiming whatever the fly has taken from it- and the pursued, the fly, are both weak.",
  22074:
      "They did not revere Allah as He deserves to be revered when they worshipped some of His creation along with worshipping Him. Indeed, Allah is Strong, and He created the heavens, the Earth, and everything within them due to this strength and power. He is the Almighty; no one can overpower Him, unlike the idols of the polytheists, which are weak and powerless [unable] to create anything.",
  22075:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) selects messengers from the angels and humans. He sends some of the angels to the prophets, like Gabriel, whom He sent to the human messengers, and He also sends human messengers to humanity. Allah hears what the polytheists say regarding His messengers and is insightful of who He selects to convey His message.",
  22076:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) knows the affairs of His messengers, from both the angels and humans, even before their creation and after their death. To Allah alone shall all matters return on the Day of Resurrection, when He will resurrect His slaves and recompense them accordingly for the deeds they sent forth.",
  22077:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, bow down and prostrate to Him alone in your prayer; do good through charity and joining family ties, etc., hoping you succeed in your objective and achieve salvation from that which you fear.",
  22078:
      "And strive in the path of Allah sincerely for His sake. He has selected you and made your religion a religion of ease, in which there is no constriction and difficulty. This easy creed is the creed of your forefather Abraham (peace be upon him). Allah has named you 'Muslims' in the previous books and in the Quran, so that the Messenger can be a witness against you in that he conveyed the message he was commanded to convey, and so that you can be witnesses against the previous nations in that their messengers also conveyed their messages respectively. So show gratitude to Allah for that by performing prayer as perfectly as possible, giving Zakat from your wealth, seeking refuge in Allah, and relying upon Him in all your matters, for He is the best protector (may He be Exalted) for those believers who He aids, and the best of helpers for those of them who seek His help. So seek His aid, He will aid you, and seek His help, He will help you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of giving examples for clarity of meaning. It is an important method of teaching.\n2. The idols’ incompetence in creating even the most insignificant of things is proof of their incapability of creating anything else.\n3. The reason behind ascribing partners to Allah is not revering Him.\n4. Affirmation of the attributes of strength and might for Allah, and the importance of a believer always keeping the meanings of these qualities in mind.\n5. Worshipping Allah and doing good leads to success.\n6. There being no difficulty in religion.",
  23000:
      "The Believers (Surah Al-Mu'minun)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDetailing the believers' success and the non-believers' loss.\n•    Explanation:",
  23001:
      "The believers in Allah who implemented His legislation have succeeded by attaining what they seek and being saved from what they dread.",
  23002:
      "Those who, when in prayer, are humble, their limbs have become tranquil therein, and their hearts are free of distractions.",
  23003:
      "Those who turned away from falsehood, futility, and sinful speech and actions.",
  23004:
      "Those who purified themselves of evil characteristics and purified their wealth by paying their Zakat (obligatory alms).",
  23005:
      "Those who safeguarded their private parts by keeping them far from fornication, homosexuality, and shameful actions. Thus, they are pure and chaste.",
  23006:
      "Except with their wives and what they own of female slaves, they are blameless for enjoying them through sexual intercourse and the like.",
  23007:
      "So whosoever seeks pleasure from other than his wives and female slaves that he possesses, he is transgressing the limits of Allah by delving into that which Allah has forbidden, without keeping to that which He has kept lawful.",
  23008:
      "And those who fulfill and do not neglect the trusts Allah has entrusted them with or any of His slaves have entrusted them with. Instead, they are loyal to fulfilling them.",
  23009:
      "And those who consistently keep their prayers and perform them punctually with all its pillars, obligations, and recommended acts.",
  23010: "Those possessing these characteristics are the true inheritors.",
  23011:
      "They will inherit the loftiest level of paradise, wherein they will abide forever. Their bounties in it will never finish.",
  23012:
      "And We have created Adam, the father of humanity, from clay, which was extracted from water mixed with the soil of the Earth.",
  23013:
      "Then, We created his progeny, who procreate through a drop of sperm that settles in the womb until birth.",
  23014:
      "Then, We made the settled drop of sperm into a clingy, red blood clot. Then, We made that clingy, red blood clot into a masticated piece of flesh. We then made the piece of flesh into solid bones. We then covered the bones with flesh. We then made it into a different creation by breathing the soul into it and bringing it to life. So Blessed is Allah, the Best of Creators.",
  23015:
      "Then you, O Humanity, after developing through all those stages, will die when your appointed times end.",
  23016:
      "Then, after your death, you shall be resurrected from your graves on the Day of Resurrection so that you may be held to account for whatever deeds you put forward.",
  23017:
      "Indeed, We have created above you, O Humanity, seven heavens, one above the other. We were never neglectful of Our creation nor forgetful of it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There are various means to achieving success. Their recognition is advisable, so too is endeavouring to achieve them.\n2. Gradual progress in creation and legislation is a divine custom.\n3. Allah’s knowledge of His creation is all-encompassing.",
  23018:
      "And We have sent rainwater down from the sky as needed, not an excessive amount to cause ruin, nor in scarcity that is not enough. We have caused it to settle on earth so that humans and animals may benefit from it. We can take it away so you will not benefit from it.",
  23019:
      "And with that water, we assembled orchards of palms and vineyards for you. In them, you have various fruits of different shapes and colors, like figs, pomegranates, and apples, and from them, you eat.",
  23020:
      "And We created the olive tree, which originates from Mount Sinai. It produces oil, which is extracted from its fruit. It is used as an ointment and is eaten.",
  23021:
      "And indeed, O humanity, you have a lesson to take from grazing livestock (camels, cows, and sheep) in that you can find evidence of the power of Allah and His kindness to you. We give you drink from their bellies; pure milk, palatable to those who drink it. You get many other benefits from them, like conveyance, wool, fur, and bristles, and you eat from their meat.",
  23022: "You are carried on the camels across land and the ships at sea.",
  23023:
      "Indeed, We sent Noah (peace be upon him) to his people, calling them to Allah. He said to them: O my people, worship Allah alone; you have no one worthy of worship but Him, may He be Exalted. Will you not fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions?",
  23024:
      "So the noblemen and leaders from his people who disbelieved in Allah said to their followers and the masses: This man that claims to be a messenger is only a human like yourselves; he only desires leadership and rule over you. If Allah wished to send a messenger to you, He would have sent one from the angels, not from the humans. We have not heard anything like what he claims from our predecessors!",
  23025:
      "He [The messenger] is only a madman. He does not understand what he is saying. Wait and see when his true reality becomes apparent to the people.",
  23026:
      "Noah (peace be upon him) said: O my Lord, grant me victory against them by avenging me for their rejection and defiance.",
  23027:
      "So We revealed to him: Construct a ship under Our direction and Our tutorship to you on how to build it. And if Our command comes to destroy them, and the water gushes out from the place We told you it would then enter upon the ship a male and female from all living creatures so procreation will continue. Then join your family except those who preceded the decree of destruction, like your wife and son. Do not address me concerning those disbelieving wrongdoers by asking that they be saved and not destroyed. They will be destroyed, without a doubt, by drowning in the great flood.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s kindness towards His servants is evident by His sending down rain and making it easy to benefit from it.\n2. Reference is made to the status of the olive tree.\n3. There is a lesson to be learnt from the livestock being sub-servient for the people.\n4. The idolaters’ belief of the divinity of the stone while rejecting the prophethood of a human being is clear evidence of their foolishness.\n5. Allah’s help and victory for His messengers occurs after their people reject their message.",
  23028:
      "When you board the ship with the believers achieving salvation, say: All praise is for Allah, Who saved us from the disbelieving people and destroyed them.",
  23029:
      "And say: O my Lord! Cause me to disembark in a blessed place, for You are the best of those who cause to disembark.",
  23030:
      "Indeed, what was mentioned from the saving of Noah and the believers with him and the destruction of the disbelievers is clear evidence of Our Power in Aiding Our messengers and destroying their rejectors. We had indeed tested the people of Noah by sending him to make the believer apparent from the disbeliever and the obedient one from the sinner.",
  23031:
      "Then, We brought into existence another nation after the destruction of the people of Noah.",
  23032:
      "We sent them a messenger from amongst them calling them to Allah. He told them: Worship Allah alone; you have no one worthy of worship but Him; may He be Exalted. Will you not fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions?",
  23033:
      "The noblemen and leaders from his people who disbelieved in Allah denied the hereafter and what it has of reward and punishment and transgressed against the vastness of the worldly blessings we gave them, told their followers and the masses: He is nothing but a human like you, he eats what you eat and drinks what you drink, he has no virtue over you to be sent as a messenger to you.",
  23034:
      "And if you were to obey another human like you, you would be losers as you would not benefit from obeying him by leaving your deities and following someone with no virtue over you.",
  23035:
      "Does this person who claims to be a messenger promise you that if you were to die and become dust and bones, you would somehow come out of your grave alive? Is this conceivable?",
  23036:
      "The promise that you will return to life after being dead and dusty bones in your grave is far-fetched.",
  23037:
      "Life is only this worldly life, and there is no Afterlife. Our living will die and will never live again. Others born after us live on. We will never come out of our graves after death to be held to account on the Day of Resurrection.",
  23038:
      "This person who claims he is a messenger to you is nothing but a man who fabricated a lie against Allah by this claim. We will never believe him.",
  23039:
      "The Messenger said: O Lord, grant me victory over them by avenging me for their rejection of me.",
  23040:
      "So Allah answered him, saying: Very soon, the ones who have rejected what you came with will be regretful for what they did.",
  23041:
      "So they were seized by a deafening shriek for what they deserved as punishment for their defiance. It killed them all, rendering them like the foam of floodwater. Destruction is for the wrongdoing people.",
  23042:
      "Then after their destruction, We created other peoples and nations, such as the people of Lot, the people of Shuayb, and the people of Jonah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The obligation of praising Allah for His blessings.\n2. Luxury in this world is outwardly a blessing, but in reality a test.\n3. The idolaters’ rejection of resurrection is a result of their materialistic ideology.\n4. The end result of a disbeliever is regret and loss.\n5. Transgression is a means of being distanced from the mercy of Allah.",
  23043:
      "None of these rejecting nations will precede the time fixed for their destruction, nor will they be delayed from it, regardless of whatever means they have at their disposal.",
  23044:
      "We then sent Our Messengers in succession, one after the other. Each time a messenger came to his nation, they rejected him, so We successively destroyed them, leaving nothing but the tales of people regarding them. So destruction be to the nation that does not believe in what their messengers came with from their Lord.",
  23045:
      "We then sent Moses and his brother Aaron with Our nine signs (the staff, the hand, locusts, lice, frogs, blood, floods, droughts, and a shortage of crops) along with a clear argument.",
  23046:
      "We sent both of them to Pharaoh and the noblemen of his people, but they displayed arrogance and did not submit to believing in them. They imposed themselves on the people by subduing and oppressing them.",
  23047:
      "They said: Why should we believe in two humans like us, who have no virtue over us, while their tribe (the Israelites) are subservient and subdued to us?",
  23048:
      "So they rejected whatever message they brought to them from Allah. And because of their rejection, they were destroyed by drowning.",
  23049:
      "And Indeed, We gave Moses the Torah in the hope that his people would be guided to the truth by it and act upon it.",
  23050:
      "And We made Jesus, the son of Mary, and his mother Mary, signs evident of Our capability, as she conceived him without a father. We sheltered them on high, level ground suitable for their shelter, having fresh, flowing water.",
  23051:
      "O Messengers, eat appealingly from what I have made lawful for you. Do righteous deeds in accordance with the law; I am Ever-Knowing of what you do; none of your actions are hidden from Me.",
  23052:
      "And your religion, O Messengers, is one religion, and that is Islam. And I am your Lord; you have no other Lord but Me. So fear Me by fulfilling My commands and avoiding My prohibitions.",
  23053:
      "After they passed away, their followers were divided in religion. They became sects and groups, with each group conceited in believing that whatever it believed in was the true acceptable religion according to Allah, disregarding the views of anyone else.",
  23054:
      "So leave them, O Messenger, in whatever they are in of ignorance and confusion until the punishment descends upon them.",
  23055:
      "Do these conceited groups think that whatever wealth and offspring We bestow upon them is a prelude to the good they deserve? It is not as they think; we only give it to them as respite, gradually leading them into destruction, but they do not realize it.",
  23056:
      "Do these conceited groups think that whatever wealth and offspring We bestow upon them is a prelude to the good they deserve? It is not as they think; we only give it to them as respite, gradually leading them into destruction, but they do not realize it.",
  23057:
      "Those who, despite their belief and righteousness, are still fearful of their Lord.",
  23058: "And those who believe in the verses of His book.",
  23059:
      "And those who single out their Lord in worship and do not associate anything with Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s care for His servants by sending consecutive messengers to them, until finally sealing them with our Prophet, peace and blessings be with him and all prophets.\n2. Arrogance is a barrier to being able to recognise the truth.\n3. Consuming good food is a quality of the Allah-conscious servants of Allah.\n4. Monotheism is the creed of all prophets and their call.\n5. Bestowing a transgressor with favours is not honouring him; it is gradually leading him into destruction.",
  23060:
      "And those who strive in acts of benevolence and get closer to Allah by righteous deeds while they are fearful that Allah will not accept their spending and good deeds when they return to Him on the Day of Resurrection.",
  23061:
      "Those who are described by these great attributes hasten to righteous deeds and are first to do them; it is for those attributes they surpass everyone else.",
  23062:
      "And We do not charge a soul except with what it can do. We have a book that records the deeds of every doer. It speaks the truth in which there is no doubt. They will never be wronged by having their good deeds decreased or their bad deeds increased.",
  23063:
      "Rather, the hearts of the disbelievers are heedless to this Book, which states the truth, and also, the Book which was revealed to them. They have evil deeds besides the disbelief they are upon.",
  23064:
      "Until the affluent ones in this worldly life are punished on the Day of Resurrection, it is then that they will raise their voices seeking help.",
  23065:
      "It will be told to them in despair of Allah's mercy: Do not scream or seek help on this day. Verily, no helper for you will prevent Allah's punishment from you.",
  23066:
      "Allah's verses were recited to you in the worldly life, and you would turn away from listening to them because of your hatred of them.",
  23067:
      "You did that in arrogance over the people because you thought you were the people of the Haram (sanctuary) while you were not; the genuine people of the Haram are the ones who fear Allah. You also stayed up nights in idle talk near it and did not sanctify it.",
  23068:
      "Have not those polytheists contemplated what Allah has revealed of the Quran to believe in and act upon it? Or is it that something has come to them that did not come to their predecessors so they turned away from it and rejected it?",
  23069:
      "Or is it that they do not recognize Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم whom Allah has sent to them, and so they reject him? Indeed, they recognize him, his truthfulness, and his honesty.",
  23070:
      "Instead, do they say that he is insane? Indeed, they have lied. Rather, the truth has come to them, indisputably from Allah. The majority of them dislike the truth, hating it due to their jealousy within themselves and fanaticism over their falsehood.",
  23071:
      "If Allah were to have let matters run and arrange them according to their desires, the heavens, Earth, and all their inhabitants would fall into ruin due to their ignorance of the outcome of matters and their inability to differentiate between good and evil plans. Instead, we have brought them what gives them honor and might, yet they turn away.",
  23072:
      "Have you, O Messenger, asked for compensation from them for what you brought? And is that why they rejected your calling? This did not occur from you. The reward and recompense of your Lord are far greater than their reward and the reward of others. He, The Exalted, is the Best of Providers.",
  23073:
      "And indeed you, O Messenger, call those people and others towards a straight path that has no deviation; it is the path of Islam.",
  23074:
      "And indeed, those who do not believe in the Hereafter, accountability, punishment, and reward by the path of Islam are inclined towards other crooked paths that lead to the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The believer should fear his good deeds not being accepted.\n2. Out of Allah’s mercy for His servants, they are not obliged to do things beyond their capabilities.\n3. Affluence is one of the barriers to steadfastness, and is a means to destruction.\n4. Arrogance is a barrier from guidance reaching the hearts.\n5. The human intellect is incapable of understanding many requirements.\n6. Not believing in reward and punishment is one way that leads to deviation and misguidance.",
  23075:
      "And if We were to have mercy on them and lift their famine and hunger, they would continue being misguided from the truth, confused and stumbling.",
  23076:
      "And We have tested them with various calamities, yet they did not humble themselves to their Lord, nor submit to Him. They did not invoke Him submissively to relieve the calamities from them after they befell them.",
  23077:
      "Until We opened a door of severe punishment upon them, they showed despair to every relief and good.",
  23078:
      "Since denial of the Resurrection should not result from someone who benefits from their hearing, sight, and mind, Allah reminds them of what He has bestowed upon them, stating: \n And it is Allah (may He be Exalted) who created for you, O deniers of the resurrection, hearing that you hear with, eyesight that you see with, and hearts to comprehend with. Despite all of those blessings, you are not grateful except slightly.",
  23079:
      "And He created you, O People, on Earth, and you will be gathered before Him alone on the Day of Resurrection for the recompense and the reckoning.",
  23080:
      "And He alone (may He be Exalted) can give life; there is no giver of life except Him. He alone can cause death; none causes death except Him. To Him alone belongs the decree of the alternation of the night and day in terms of their darkness and light, length and shortness. You cannot fathom His power and uniqueness in creating and planning.",
  23081:
      "Rather, they said similar to what their forefathers and predecessors in disbelief said.",
  23082:
      "They said, unbelievingly and denyingly: When we die and turn into dust and decomposed bones, will we be raised alive to be held to account?",
  23083:
      "We were promised this, which is resurrection after death, and so were our predecessors, but we did not see this promise fulfilled. These are only the false tales and lies of the olden people.",
  23084:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those disbelievers who deny the resurrection: To whom do this Earth and those upon it belong, if you should know?",
  23085:
      "They will say the Earth and those upon it belong to Allah. Then say to them: Do you not ponder that the One who the Earth and those upon it belongs to can bring you back to life after death?",
  23086:
      "Tell them: Who is the Lord of the seven heavens? Who is the Lord of the Great Throne, which no creation is greater than it?",
  23087:
      "They will say the seven heavens and the Great Throne belong to the ownership of Allah, then tell them: Will you not fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions so that you may be saved from His punishment?",
  23088:
      "Tell them: In whose Hand is the realm of all things while nothing escapes His dominion; He aids whomever He wills of His slaves, and no one can stop any harm He wills to afflict anyone, thus repelling punishment; if you have any knowledge?",
  23089:
      "They will say the ownership of everything is in His Hand; may He be Exalted. Then tell them: If you acknowledge that, how do your minds wonder and worship others besides Him?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers not considering the blessings or calamities that befall them is a sign of their corrupt nature.\n2. Being ungrateful for blessings is a quality of the unbelievers.\n3. Holding onto blind following stops one reaching the truth.\n4. Affirming the Lordship of Allah will not save a person unless it is accompanied with affirming He alone is worthy of worship.",
  23090:
      "The matter is not as they claim. But instead, We have brought them the truth in which there is no doubt. They are lying in their claim that Allah has a partner and child. Allah is Transcendent and far beyond from what they say.",
  23091:
      "Allah has not taken a child as the disbelievers claim, nor is there any truly worshiped deity alongside Him. Hypothetically, if there were to be any true deity alongside Him, then every deity would take their share of the creation they made, and they would dominate one another, causing the order of the universe to become corrupt. The reality is that none of this has occurred, proving that the only truly worshiped god is Allah alone. He is Pure and Holy of what the polytheists describe Him with, namely partners and children, which are unbefitting.",
  23092:
      "He knows all that is hidden from His creation. He knows all things that are witnessed and perceived by the senses. Nothing of that is hidden from Him. Far Exalted and Exalted is He above having a partner.",
  23093:
      "Say, O Messenger, My Lord, if You should show me that which those polytheists are promised from the punishment.",
  23094:
      "My Lord, if You punish them and I witness that, then do not make me amongst them so that I would be afflicted with the punishment that afflicts them.",
  23095:
      "And We have the power to make you witness and see the punishment We have promised them. We are not powerless to do this or anything else.",
  23096:
      "Repel, O Messenger, by the character of what is best, any wrongdoing towards you, by forgiveness and being patient towards harm. We know best of their description of polytheism and denial. We also know best what unbecoming things they describe you with, such as insanity and sorcery.",
  23097:
      "And say: My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the incitements of the devils and their whisperings.",
  23098:
      "And I seek refuge in You, my Lord, that they are present with me in my affairs.",
  23099:
      "When death comes to one of these polytheists, and he sees what will befall him, he says while regretting his life that has escaped him and his deficiency regarding Allah: O Lord, return me to the worldly life.",
  23100:
      "I may do good actions when I return to it. Never! The matter is different from what you requested. It is only a statement he is uttering. If he were to return to worldly life, he would not fulfill what he promised. These people who have died will remain in a barrier between the world and the Afterlife until the Day of Resurrection. Thus, they will not return from it to the world to make up for what they lost and to correct what they spoiled.",
  23101:
      "Then when the angel appointed to blow the Trumpet will blow the second time, which will announce the Day of Resurrection, there will be no relations between them to boast through due to their being engrossed in the horrors of the Hereafter, and they will not question one another due to their being absorbed in what concerns them.",
  23102:
      "So whoever's scales are made heavy by their good deeds outweighing their bad ones are the winners who have attained what they desired and been saved from what they feared.",
  23103:
      "And whose scales were made light by bad deeds outweighing good ones, then they are the ones who have lost their soul by doing what harms it, abandoning what benefits it from belief and righteous deeds. They will live in the Hellfire and will not exit it.",
  23104:
      "The Fire will burn their faces, and the resulting frowning will cause their upper and lower lips to shrivel up, exposing their teeth.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The stability of the system of the Universe is proof for the oneness of Allah.\n2. Allah’s knowledge encompasses everything.\n3. Behaving well with a wrongdoer is a great part of Islamic etiquette which has a deep effect on the opponent.\n4. It is important to seek refuge in Allah against the whisperings of the satan and his tricks.\n5. The disbeliever will be regretful when regret will not benefit.\n6. Consideration on the Day of Judgment will be of actions, not lineage.\n7. The intense horrors of the Day of Judgment will make one forget the ties of lineage and relations.\n8. Numerous good actions are the means of good fortune and numerous bad deeds are the means of wretchedness.",
  23105:
      "And it will be said to them, chastising them: Were not the verses of the Quran recited to you in the worldly life, yet you denied them?",
  23106:
      "They will say: O Our Lord, our wretchedness which You already know of overcame us, and we were a people astray from the truth.",
  23107:
      "O our Lord, take us out of the Fire, and if we go back to what we were upon of disbelief and misguidance, we will have truly wronged ourselves and will have no excuses.",
  23108:
      "Allah will say: Live in the Fire, disgraced and humiliated, and do not speak to Me.",
  23109:
      "There was a group of My slaves who believed in Me, saying: Our Lord, we have believed in You, so forgive our sins and grant us Your mercy, and You are the best of those who show mercy.",
  23110:
      "So you took those believers who called on their Lord as a joke, mocking and ridiculing them. That ridicule made you forget the remembrance of Allah. You would taunt and laugh at them mockingly.",
  23111:
      "And I have rewarded those believers by granting them Paradise on the Day of Resurrection for being patient in obeying Allah and with the harm they would receive from you.",
  23112:
      "When they ask to return to this world to correct what they had corrupted, Allah reminds them of what they had done in it, enabling them to repent if they wanted to. \n He will say: How many years did you spend on Earth? And how much time did you waste therein?",
  23113:
      "They will respond by saying: We only spent a day there or a part of a day, so ask those who pay attention to counting days and months.",
  23114:
      "He will say: You only spent a short time in the world, which should have made patience and obedience easy for you if you only knew the length of your stay.",
  23115:
      "So do you think, O humanity, that We created you uselessly without wisdom, with no reward and punishment like animals, and that you would not return to Us on the Day of Resurrection for account and recompense?",
  23116:
      "So Exalted is Allah, the King, who does as He wishes with His creation. It is He who is Truth and whose promise and statement are true. No one is worthy of worship, but He, Lord of the Noble Throne, the greatest of creation, and who is a Lord of the greatest of creation, is a Lord of all of creation.",
  23117:
      "Whoever calls upon another god besides Allah for which he has no proof for worship (and this is the case with every god besides Allah), the recompense of his bad action is with his Lord (may He be Exalted), as He is the One who will hold him to account by punishing him. The disbelievers will not attain what they desire or be saved from what they fear.",
  23118:
      "And say, O Messenger: My Lord, forgive my sins and have mercy on me. You are the best in showing mercy toward the one with sins, and then you accept his repentance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbeliever is lowly and disgraced in the eyes of Allah.\n2. Mocking the righteous is a great sin which makes the perpetrator deserving of punishment.\n3. Being patient upon harm is one of the qualities of the believers.\n4. Wasting one’s life is one of the necessary outcomes of disbelief.\n5. Success is the share of the believers whilst loss is the share of the disbelievers.\n6. Praising Allah is one of the displays of etiquette in supplication.",
  24000:
      "The Light (Surah An-Nur)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nCalling to chastity and protecting one's honor.\n•    Explanation:",
  24001:
      "This is a chapter (surah) that We have revealed. We have made acting upon its rulings mandatory and brought down clear verses in it in the hope that you be reminded of what is in it of commands and act upon them.",
  24002:
      "The unmarried fornicating man and woman flog each one with a hundred lashes and let no softness or mercy overtake you that you would not establish the prescribed penalty or lessen it on them; this is if you believe in Allah and the Last Day. Establishing the prescribed punishments should be witnessed by a group of believers as a means to publicize the crime and as a deterrent to them and others.",
  24003:
      "To show the gravity of fornication, Allah mentions that those inclined to it do not wish to marry except someone like them; another female fornicator, or a polytheist who does not refrain from fornication though marrying them is prohibited. A female fornicator inclined to fornication does not want to marry except another male fornicator or a polytheist inclined to it, even though marriage to them is prohibited. It has been made unlawful for believers to marry male and female fornicators.",
  24004:
      "Those who accuse chaste women of adultery (and chaste men likewise) and do not then bring four witnesses to testify to the adultery they have accused them of, flog them, O judges, with eighty lashes, and never accept their testimony. Those who accuse chaste women have exited the obedience of Allah.",
  24005:
      "Except those who repent to Allah after what they did and rectify their actions, for Allah will accept their repentance and testimony. Allah forgives those of His slaves who repent and is Merciful to them.",
  24006:
      "And those men who accuse their wives but do not have witnesses to testify to the authenticity of what they have accused them of besides themselves, one amongst them will testify by Allah four times that he is truthful in the accusation of adultery he has made against his wife.",
  24007:
      "Then, on his fifth testimony, he will add that he deserves a curse if he is lying about what he has accused her of.",
  24008:
      "She deserves, through this, the prescribed punishment of adultery. The punishment could be repelled from her if she were to testify by Allah four times that he is lying in what he has accused her of.",
  24009:
      "Then, on her fifth testimony, she will add a supplication upon herself that the anger of Allah be on her if he is truthful in what he has accused her of.",
  24010:
      "Had it not been for Allah's grace on you, O people, and His mercy on you, and that He accepts those who repent amongst His slaves and is Wise in His managing and legislating, He would have quickly punished you for your sins and disgraced you through them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Any type of discussion concerning great matters should be done in such a way as to indicate their greatness.\n2. The fornicator loses respect and mercy in the Muslim community.\n3. Implementing the fixed punishments is amongst the means of protecting against crimes.\n4. The social boycott against fornicators is a means of protecting the community against them, and a means of deterring them from adultery.\n5. Categorising the punishment of one who accuses of adultery into a tangible punishment (the fixed punishment) and an immaterial one (rejecting his testimony and labelling him as immoral) is proof to the danger of this action.",
  24011:
      "Those who brought the slander—accusing the Mother of the Believers Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) of adultery—are a group that affiliates themselves to you, O believers. Do not consider the slander they made as bad for you. Rather, it is good due to the reward and expiation for the believers and the clearing of the name of the Mother of the Believers it brings with it. For each person who shared in accusing her of adultery is the sin they earned by uttering the slander. And there is a great punishment for the one who bore most of the slander by initiating it. The one meant by that is the leader of the hypocrites, Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul.",
  24012:
      "When hearing this great slander, should not the believing men and women think well of their falsely accused believing brethren and say this is a clear lie?",
  24013:
      "Should not those who falsely accused the Mother of the Believers Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, bring four witnesses upon their grave accusation to testify to the authenticity of what they attributed to her? But if they do not bring four witnesses on that, and they will never be able to bring them, they are liars in the judgment of Allah.",
  24014:
      "Had it not been for Allah's grace on you, O believers, and His mercy on you, as He did not quickly punish you and He accepted the repentance of those amongst you who repented, a great punishment would have afflicted you, due to the lie and accusation against the Mother of the Believers you delved into.",
  24015:
      "You were relating it to one another and passing it to one another through word of mouth, despite its falseness and you not knowing anything about it. You thought that was an easy, insignificant thing to do while it was grievous with Allah because it contains lies and accusing an innocent person.",
  24016:
      "Should you not have said to yourself when you heard this slander, it is not right for us to speak about such a grievous issue? Purity belongs to You, our Lord. The slander they accused the Mother of the Believers of is a great lie.",
  24017:
      "If you truly believe in Allah, Allah reminds and advises you never to return to this kind of slander that you accuse an innocent person of adultery.",
  24018:
      "Allah makes clear for you the verses which comprise His rulings and admonitions. Allah is all Knowing of what you do, and nothing is hidden from Him. He will recompense you accordingly. He is the all Wise in His disposition and legislation.",
  24019:
      "Those who love for immoral acts to spread amongst the believers, one of them being to defame with fornication, will have, by establishing the penalty of defamation, a painful punishment in this worldly life. And in the hereafter, they will have the punishment of hell. Allah knows their lies and the outcome of His slaves' affairs. He knows what benefits them, while you do not know that.",
  24020:
      "If it were not for Allah's grace and mercy upon you, O those who fell into this slander, and if it were not for Allah's mercy and compassion with you, He would have punished you quickly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The hypocrites focus on breaking the centres of reliance in the Muslim community, by spreading false accusations.\n2. The hypocrites sometimes tempt some of the believers to join them in their actions.\n3. A believer’s affliction is an expiation for his sins and raising of his status.\n4. The Mother of the Believers Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was honoured by having her innocence declared from above the seven heavens.\n5. The punishment of those sharing in a sin varies according to their role therein.\n6. It is necessary to remain firm in the face of false rumours.\n7. Adultery is not established except through evidence, and claiming it without evidence is slander.\n8. Staying far from taking part in spreading lies is what is befitting a believer.",
  24021:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act upon His sacred law, do not follow the paths of the Devil in the way they are adorned in falsehood. Whoever follows his paths, then he commands hideous sayings and actions and condemns the divine legislation. And if it were not for the grace of Allah upon you, O believers, He would not have purified any of you by accepting your repentance.",
  24022:
      "The people of virtue in religion and abundance in wealth should not swear an oath to stop giving their needy (due to their poverty) relatives amongst the migrants in Allah's way because of a sin they committed. They should pardon them and overlook them. Do you not love that Allah should forgive your sins when you pardon and overlook them? Allah forgives those who repent amongst His slaves and is Merciful to them, so His slaves should follow Him. This verse was revealed regarding Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) when he swore an oath to stop spending on Mistah due to his joining in the slander.",
  24023:
      "Those who accuse chaste, unaware, and believing women of adultery, while those women are not inclined to it, are removed from the mercy of Allah in this world and the next, and they will be punished severely in the Hereafter.",
  24024:
      "They will get that punishment on the Day of Resurrection, when their tongues will testify against them as to the falsehood they spoke, and their hands and feet will testify against them as to what they used to do.",
  24025:
      "On that day, Allah will justly give them their full recompense, and they will know Allah (may He be Exalted) is the Truth. Every piece of information, promise, or warning that comes from Him is true without any doubt in it.",
  24026:
      "Every evil man, woman, saying, and action is suited to what is evil and conforms to it, whereas every good of those mentioned is suited and conforms to good. Those good men and women are innocent of what the evil men and women say about them. They will have forgiveness from Allah, who will pardon their sins, and generous sustenance, which is Paradise.",
  24027:
      "Since looking at private parts can arouse desire that leads to committing adultery, which is mentioned at the beginning of the Surah, Allah commands seeking permission to enter homes to protect one's gaze from seeing private parts, stating: \n O you who believe in Allah and act upon His sacred law, do not enter houses besides your own without first taking permission from their inhabitants to enter upon them. Greet them peacefully and seek consent by saying: peace be unto you, may I enter? The command to seek permission is better for you than suddenly entering upon them. Perhaps you will remember what I commanded you and act on it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The deception of the satan and his whisperings are a call towards committing sins, so a believer should refrain from it.\n2. The ability to repent and do good deeds is from Allah, not from the servant.\n3. The people of virtue and excellence are far from taking revenge and treating one who does bad in a like manner.\n4. Forgiving and overlooking one who does bad is a means of sins being forgiven.\n5. Slandering chaste women is amongst the major sins.\n6. That which befits evil is its like and that which befits good is its like.\n7. Seeking permission has been legislated to protect the gaze and to preserve the sanctity of homes.",
  24028:
      "But if you do not find anyone in those houses, enter them once permitted by those with the authority to give permission. And if their owners tell you to return, return and do not enter them, as this is purer for you in the sight of Allah. Allah knows what you do; none of your actions are hidden from Him, and He shall reward you accordingly.",
  24029:
      "There is no blame on you for entering public places that are not specific to anyone without asking permission. These places, such as libraries and shops in the marketplace, are prepared for the general public's benefit. Allah knows the actions and conditions you display and hide; none of that is hidden from Him, and He shall reward you for them.",
  24030:
      "Since looking is a precursor to adultery, Allah commanded averting one's gaze as a protection from it, stating: \n O Messenger, tell the believing men to stop their eyes from looking at women and private areas that are unlawful for them and to protect their private parts from indulging in the unlawful and from exposing them. Refraining from looking at what Allah has made unlawful is purer for them in the sight of Allah. Allah is Aware of what you do.",
  24031:
      "And tell the believing women to stop their eyes from looking at the private parts Allah has made unlawful for them to look at and protect their private parts by staying far from indecency and covering themselves. And they should not display their beauty to strangers except that which is apparent and cannot be hidden, such as clothing. They should draw their coverings over the openings at the top of their clothes to cover their hair, faces, and necks. They should not expose their hidden beauty except to their husbands, or their fathers, or their husbands' fathers, or their sons, or their husbands' sons, or their brothers, or their brother's sons, or their sister's sons, or their women who are believers, be they Muslim or disbelievers, or the slaves they own, be they male or female, or male attendants who have no desire for women, or children who have not become aware of the private aspects of women due to their young age. Women should not strike their feet to make known the adornment they are hiding, such as anklets. And all of you repent to Allah, O believers, for the gaze and so forth which affects you, in the hope that you are successful in attaining the goal and are saved from what is feared.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is permissible to enter public buildings without permission.\n2. It is necessary for men and women to lower their gazes from what is unlawful for them.\n3. It is necessary for a woman to cover herself, with the Islamic Hijab.\n4-It is permissible for a woman to display her beauty to her husband or to those who are unlawful to marry due to kinship or marriage relations.\n5. It is impermissible to use means of incitement.",
  24032:
      "As spinsterhood is one of the reasons for the spread of adultery, Allah commands helping young women to marry, stating: \n O believers, marry off the unmarried free men and women amongst you and marry off the believers amongst your male and female slaves. Allah will make them wealthy through His vast grace if they are poor. Allah is vast in sustenance, which does not decrease by making any of you rich. He knows the condition of His slaves.",
  24033:
      "Upon commanding the believers to marry unmarried women, Allah commands unmarried men to abstain from fornication if they do not have the means to marry, stating: \n Those who cannot marry due to poverty should seek chastity from fornication until Allah makes them wealthy through His vast grace. Those slaves who wish to make a contract with their masters to pay money so that they can be free, then their masters should accept that from them if they know they can fulfill it and are upright in religion. Their masters should give their slaves the wealth Allah gave them to help pay off a part of their contract of bondage. And do not force your female slaves into fornication for money as Abdullah bin Ubay did with his two female slaves when they asked to be chaste and distant from fornication. And whoever among you forces them to do that, know that Allah is forgiving and merciful to them after they have been forced. They were under duress, and the sin was on the ones who forced them.",
  24034:
      "And We have sent down to you, O people, clear verses detailing the truth from falsehood. We have also sent down to you an example from those who lived before you, from among the believers and unbelievers. We sent down to you a warning to be contemplated by those who fear their Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  24035:
      "Allah is the Light of the heavens and the Earth and the Guide of all those therein. The parable of His light in the heart of a believer is like a small niche in an unpenetrated wall that contains a lantern. The lantern is in a bright glass, as though it is a shining star like a pearl. The oil of a blessed tree lights the lantern, the olive tree. Nothing conceals the tree from the sun, neither in the morning nor evening. The oil almost glows due to its purity, even though a fire has not touched it, so imagine how it will be when it touches it. The light of the lantern is on the light of the glass. Likewise is the believer's heart when the light of guidance shines in it. Allah enables whomever He wishes amongst His slaves to follow the Quran. And Allah makes things clear through their likenesses by giving examples. Allah knows everything; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  24036:
      "This lantern is lit in the mosques Allah commanded to be built and revered. His name is mentioned therein by the call to prayer, remembrance, and the prayer itself. People pray in these mosques, morning and evening, seeking the pleasure of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Celibacy is to be limited, by helping the unmarried to be relieved of it, so that it does not become a means of indecency spreading.\n2. A person unable to marry due to his poverty is ordered to stay far away from indecency.\n3. Relief from slavery can be through making a contract to pay for one’s freedom and the slave should be supported with wealth in order to become free, so that he does not form part of the lowly class which uses indecency to make a living.\n4. The trade of people’s honour by making prostitution a way to earn money is to be combatted.\n5. The heart of a believer is enlightened with the light of nature and the light of divine guidance.\n6. Mosques are the houses of Allah on earth, which have been established for Him to be worshipped in, so it is necessary to keep them far from physical and immaterial dirt.",
  24037:
      "Men who neither commerce nor trade stop them from remembering Allah (may He be Exalted), praying in the most perfect manner, and giving Zakat (obligatory alms) where applicable. They fear the Day of Resurrection, when their hearts will fluctuate between the hope of salvation and the fear of punishment. Eyes will also fluctuate, anxiously wandering in all directions.",
  24038:
      "They do that so that Allah may reward them upon the best of their actions and increase their reward through His grace. Allah provides without account for whomsoever He wishes, according to their deeds. Rather, He grants them in multitudes over the value of their deeds.",
  24039:
      "There is no reward for the deeds of those who disbelieve in Allah; it is like a mirage that a thirsty person sees on a low-lying piece of land and assumes it to be water. He walks towards it until he reaches it and finds no water. Likewise is a disbeliever: he thinks his deeds shall benefit him until he dies and is resurrected but does not find their reward. Instead, he finds his Lord in front of him, who takes him to account fully for his deeds; and Allah is swift in taking account.",
  24040:
      "Or their deeds are like darkness in the depth of the ocean, over which is a wave, over which is another wave, over which is a cloud covering the navigating stars. Compounded layers of darkness, one above the other; if the one in such darkness were to place his hand in front of him, he would barely see it due to the extent of that darkness. Likewise is a disbeliever: the darkness of ignorance, doubt, confusion, and a sealed heart have compounded over him. Whoever Allah does not grant guidance over misguidance and knowledge of His book has no guidance to be guided by nor a book to illuminate his path.",
  24041:
      "O Messenger, do you not know that all the inhabitants of the heavens and Earth from the creation of Allah exalt Him? The birds that fly in formation also praise Him. Allah knows the prayer of each one of those creatures. He knows their exaltation of Him, such as the birds. Allah knows everything they do; nothing of their actions is hidden from Him.",
  24042:
      "To Allah alone belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth, and to Him alone is the return on the Day of Resurrection to be taken to account and recompensed.",
  24043:
      "O Messenger, do you not know that Allah drives the clouds, then joins parts of them together, then makes them into layers, one above the other? You then see the rain coming out from the clouds and falling from the sky from parts of cloud-like mountains, falling as hail. That hail reaches whoever Allah wills from His slaves, and He turns it away from whomsoever He wills. The intense light from bolts of lightning almost blinds the eyesight.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is incumbent that a believer strikes a balance between worldly occupations and affairs concerning the Hearafter.\n2. The deeds of a disbeliever will become void due to lacking the requisite of faith.\n3. The disbeliever is one who is glaringly disobedient from all the other creations of Allah, who are generally obedient and glorify Him.\n4. All stages of rainfall are part of the creation and decree of Allah.",
  24044:
      "Allah alternates between the length of the day and night. Indeed, that alternation is a lesson in the power of Allah and His Oneness for those with foresight.",
  24045:
      "And Allah has created all living things that appear on earth from a drop of semen. Some, like snakes, crawl on their bellies. Others walk on two feet like birds and humans, while others walk on four like animals. Allah creates what He wills from what was mentioned and what was not. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  24046:
      "Indeed, I revealed clear verses unto Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, wherein there is no ambiguity. Allah guides whomever He wishes to the straight path without deviance, leading him to Paradise.",
  24047:
      "The hypocrites say: We have believed in Allah and His Messenger, and obeyed Allah and His Messenger, then a group of them turn away, disobeying Allah and His Messenger in the matter of jihad in Allah's cause and the like. In truth, those who turn away from the obedience of Allah and His Messenger are not believers, despite claiming to be.",
  24048:
      "If these hypocrites are called to Allah and the Messenger so that the Messenger can judge between them in matters they dispute among themselves, they reject his judgment due to their hypocrisy.",
  24049:
      "Yet if they know the truth to be in their favor and that he will judge in their favor, they come to him submissive and humble.",
  24050:
      "Is there a chronic illness in the hearts of these people, or is it that they are in doubt as to whether he is Allah's Messenger? Or do they fear Allah or His Messenger will wrong them in judgment? No, it is none of the aforementioned; rather, it is because of a defect within their souls due to their turning away from his judgment and their opposition to him.",
  24051:
      "When discussing the negative stance of hypocrites towards Allah and His Messenger's rules, Allah highlights the positive attitude of the believers who are satisfied with it, stating: \n When the believers are called towards Allah and His Messenger for him to judge between them, their only reaction is that they say, we have heard his statement and obeyed his order. Those who possess this characteristic are the ones who are successful in this world and the Hereafter.",
  24052:
      "Whoever obeys Allah and obeys His Messenger, fears the outcome of sins, and prevents the punishment of Allah upon themselves by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions; only they are the ones who achieve success in both this world and the Hereafter.",
  24053:
      "The hypocrites take their strongest and most vigorous oaths possible upon Allah that they will go forth if they are called to go out for jihad. Tell them, O Messenger, do not take oaths, for your dishonesty and fake obedience are known. Allah knows what you do; nothing of your actions is hidden from Him, no matter how much you try to conceal them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The diversity in the creation of Allah is evidence of His power.\n2. From among the traits of the hypocrites is their turning away from the Judgement of Allah, except if it is in their favour. Doubting, spiritual illness and thinking ill of Allah are also some of their traits.\n3. Submitting to the Judgement of Allah is one of the qualities of the believers, even though it may not be in their favour.\n4. Obedience to Allah and His Messenger, together with fearing Allah are both the means to achieving success in both the worlds.\n5. Taking false oaths is common behaviour among the hypocrites.",
  24054:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those hypocrites, obey Allah and His Messenger both outwardly and inwardly. If you turn away from obeying Allah and His Messenger, then the Messenger has fulfilled what he was tasked with, and upon you is what you have been tasked with of obedience and acting on what he came with. If you obey him in what he has commanded you and avoid what he has prohibited, you will be guided to the truth. Only clear conveyance is upon the Messenger; he cannot carry you to guidance or force it upon you.",
  24055:
      "Allah has promised those who believe in Him and perform righteous deeds that He will aid them against their enemies and make them viceroys on Earth, just like He enabled the believers before them to be viceroys on Earth. He has promised to make their religion, Islam, the religion He preferred for them, dominant and triumphant. He has vowed to replace their fear with security. They worship Me alone and do not associate any partners with Me. Whoever disbelieves after all those blessings has indeed exited the obedience of Allah.",
  24056:
      "And perform prayer to perfection, give Zakat (charity) on your wealth, and obey the Messenger in whatever he commands you with, together with leaving whatever he prevents you from, in the hope that you shall be safe from your fears and be successful in your objectives.",
  24057:
      "Do not think, O Messenger, that those who disbelieve in Allah will escape Me if I bring down punishment upon them. Their destination will be hell on the Day of Resurrection, and what an evil abode hell is for those destined to it.",
  24058:
      "Allah previously mentions the rules for free adults seeking permission before entering. He then mentions regulations pertaining to slaves, free children pre-puberty, and children post-puberty who wish to enter, stating: \n O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, your free adolescent children, male slaves, and female slaves should seek permission from you thrice, at three times: before the morning prayer at the time of changing from nightwear into daily clothes, in the afternoon when changing clothes for the siesta and after the night prayer because it is the time when you remove your daywear and change into your nightwear. These are three times of privacy for you; they should not enter your rooms except after taking your permission. Apart from these times, there is no harm in them entering your rooms or you entering theirs because you frequently have to move around one another. So, it would be inconvenient to prevent them from entering except with permission. Just as Allah has clarified for you the rulings of seeking permission, He also clarifies the verses that show the rulings He has laid down for you. Allah is All-Aware of the requirements of His slaves, Wise in whatever laws He passes for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Following the Messenger peace be upon him is a sign of being upon guidance.\n2. Conveying the message is the responsibility of the Messenger, whilst guidance is from Allah alone.\n3. It is necessary for the caller to Allah to expend efforts in calling to Him, but the results are in Allah’s hands.\n4. Faith and good deeds are means to attaining authority on earth and peace.\n5. Establishing prayer, giving Zakat and obedience to the Messenger: are means to acquiring mercy.\n6. The servants and children should be disciplined in seeking permission at times where people’s privacy is compromised.\n7. Difficulty in matters should bring ease in rulings.",
  24059:
      "When your children reach the age of puberty, they should seek permission at all times before entering your homes, as has been mentioned regarding adults previously. Just as Allah clarifies the rulings of seeking permission for you, He also clarifies His verses. And Allah is All-Aware of the requirements of His slaves, Wise in whatever laws He passes for them.",
  24060:
      "And the elderly women that no longer menstruate, can no longer give birth, and have no desire to marry again, there is no sin upon them if they do not wear some of their outer garments, i.e., the cloak over the robe and the veil over the headscarf, as long as they do not expose the beauty they have been commanded to conceal. However, for them to wear those garments is better for them than to discard them, enhancing veiling and chastity. Allah is all-hearing of your statements; none are hidden from Him, and He shall requite you for them.",
  24061:
      "There is no sin upon the blind who has lost his eyesight, the cripple, or the sick if they leave those responsibilities they can no longer fulfill, like jihad in the way of Allah. O believers! There is no sin upon you in eating from your own homes or the homes of your sons, nor in eating from the homes of your fathers, mothers, brothers, sisters, paternal uncles and aunts, nor maternal uncles and aunts, nor those houses which you have been entrusted with safeguarding, e.g., garden-keeper. There is also no sin in eating at your friend's house as is customary to please him. It is fine whether you eat alone or together in groups. So when you do enter any places like the ones mentioned above or any others, greet those within them with peace by saying: \"Peace be upon you,\" and if there is no one inside them, then greet yourselves by saying: \"Peace be upon the pious slaves of Allah and us.\" This is a blessed greeting from Allah; He has legislated it for you because of the love and affection it spreads among you. It is also a pleasant greeting in that it pleases the soul of the one who hears it. Just like the aforementioned clarity in this Surah, Allah clearly explains His verses in the hope that you will implement whatever they contain.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is permissible for elderly women to not wear some outer garments; any doubts about that are settled.\n2. Taking precaution in religion is a characteristic of the Mindful.\n3. Genuine excuses are means having responsibility lessened.\n4. A Muslim community is one in which there is shared responsibility, cooperation and brotherhood.",
  24062:
      "Upon mentioning the need to seek consent to enter, Allah mentions the need to seek permission to leave, stating: \n The believers who are genuine in their faith believe in Allah and His Messenger. When they are summoned to convene by the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم for a matter concerning the affairs of the Muslims, they do not leave until they seek his permission to do so. O Messenger, indeed, those who seek your permission before leaving, they are the ones who truly believe in Allah and His Messenger; so if they seek your consent to leave due to some important matter that concerns them, grant permission to whomsoever you wish from them and ask Allah to forgive their sins. Indeed, Allah forgives the sins of whoever repents from His slaves and is merciful to them.",
  24063:
      "O Believers, honor Allah's Messenger; when you call out to him, do not call him by name, e.g., \"O Muhammad!\" or the name of his father, e.g., \"O the son of Abdullah!\" like you call one another. Instead, say, O Messenger of Allah, O Prophet of Allah. And when he summons you for a general matter, do not treat his summoning like each other in petty issues; rather, hasten to answer his summon. Verily, Allah knows of those of you who leave covertly without seeking permission, so those who go against the command of Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم should fear that Allah can afflict them with trials and afflictions or with a painful punishment they cannot bear.",
  24064:
      "Know well that to Allah belongs everything in the heavens and on Earth: in terms of being His creation, under His supreme authority and control. O people, He knows whatever conditions you are in; nothing is hidden from Him, and on the Day of Judgment, when you return to Him after the resurrection, He will inform you of all the deeds you did in this world. Allah knows everything; nothing in the heavens or the Earth is hidden from Him.",
  25000:
      "The Criterion (Surah Al-Furqan)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nVictory for the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and the Quran, and dispelling doubts of the polytheists.\n•    Explanation:",
  25001:
      "Blessed is Allah, who revealed the Quran as a criterion distinguishing between truth and falsehood unto His slave and Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم so that he could be a Messenger towards the humans and the Jinn and a warner to them of the punishment of Allah.",
  25002:
      "The One to whom alone belongs authority over the heavens and Earth, Who did not beget a child, nor has any partner in His authority, Who created everything appropriately and foresaw its creation according to His knowledge and wisdom to perfection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The religion of Islam is one of order and etiquettes.\n2. There is blessing and goodness in holding fast to etiquettes.\n3. The status of the Messenger of Allah peace be upon him demands reverence and respect, more than that of anyone else.\n4. Misfortune is in contradicting the way of the Prophet peace be upon him.\n5. The authority of Allah and His knowledge encompass everything.",
  25003:
      "Instead of Allah, the polytheists adopted deities who cannot create anything small or large but are themselves created. Indeed, Allah created them from non-existence, and they cannot fend off any harm from themselves nor bring themselves any benefit, nor can they cause death to any living thing, give life to any dead thing, or raise the dead from their graves.",
  25004:
      "Upon reminding them of their polytheism, Allah mentions their position with regard to His scripture and His Messenger, stating: \n And those who disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger said, this Quran is nothing but a lie which Muhammad has fabricated and blasphemously attributed to Allah. Other people have also helped him in its fabrication. These disbelievers themselves have made a false statement because the Quran is the speech of Allah; humans and jinn cannot come up with anything like it.",
  25005:
      "And those rejecters of the Quran said the Quran is vain tales of the previous people which they used to record; Muhammad has copied them. They are recited to him throughout the day.",
  25006:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these rejectors: The Quran was revealed by Allah, Who knows of everything in the heavens and the Earth. It is not made up as you think it to be. Then He said to them, encouraging them to repent: Indeed, Allah forgives those of His slaves who repent and is merciful to them.",
  25007:
      "The polytheists who rejected the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: What is wrong with this man that claims he is a messenger from Allah when he eats food just as other people do and walks around the markets in search of livelihood? Why did Allah not send an angel who would accompany him, proclaim his truthfulness, and help him?",
  25008:
      "Or send down a treasure for him from the heavens, or that he has a garden from which he eats fruits so that he does not need to walk around the markets in search of livelihood? The wrongdoers also said: O believers, you are not following any messenger; you are only following a man whose intellect has been overwhelmed by magic.",
  25009:
      "O Messenger, you should see and be amazed at how they can describe you with such false attributes, i.e., they said he is a magician, has been spellbound, and is insane, so they deviated from the truth because of that. They are incapable of treading the path towards guidance and have no way to question your truthfulness and honesty.",
  25010:
      "Blessed is Allah, who can, if He wishes, give you the good they think up for you like the gardens under the trees of which streams flow and the fruits of which you can eat, and can also grant you palaces in which you can live in luxury.",
  25011:
      "The statements that came from them were not said in search of the truth or evidence; instead, they were rejecting the Day of Resurrection. And for whoever rejects the Day of Resurrection, We have prepared a blazing fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The true deity is One Who has the ability to create, benefit, give life, and cause death; the idols are incapable of doing all those things.\n2. The disbelievers turn away from the truth relying on baseless doubts.\n3. Affirmation of the qualities of forgiving and mercy for Allah.\n4. Messengership does not necessitate negation of humanity from the Messenger.\n5. The humility of the Prophet peace be upon him in that he lived as normal people live.",
  25012:
      "When the Fire sees the disbelievers being brought towards it from a distance, they will hear an unsettling, severe boiling sound emitting from it due to its anger upon them.",
  25013:
      "And when these disbelievers are thrown into hell from a tight place, with their hands chained to their necks, they will invoke destruction upon themselves, hoping to escape from hell.",
  25014:
      "O disbelievers, do not invoke one type of destruction for yourselves today; invoke many types, and it will make no difference; you will not be granted what you seek. Instead, you will remain in painful punishment forever.",
  25015:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Is the punishment described for you better, or the everlasting Paradise with its eternal blessings that never cease? It is the same one that Allah promised His pious slaves as a reward and abode they will return to on the Day of Resurrection.",
  25016:
      "In Paradise, they will have whatever blessings they desire; that is a promise from Allah which His pious slaves will ask Him for. And the promise of Allah will be fulfilled because He never breaks promises.",
  25017:
      "On the Day when the rejecting polytheists will be gathered, together with whatever they worshipped instead of Allah, He will say to those worshipped, rebuking those who worshipped them: Did you lead My slaves astray by commanding them to worship you, or did they go astray of their own accord?",
  25018:
      "The worshipped ones will say: Our Lord, You are exalted from having any partner. It was not becoming for us to take any guardians instead of You, so how could we call Your slaves to worship us instead of You? Our Lord, You granted these polytheists and their forefathers enjoyment through the world's pleasures, gradually leading them into their destruction until they forgot Your remembrance and worshipped others with You. They were people doomed due to their wretchedness.",
  25019:
      "O polytheists, indeed, those you worshipped other than Allah have belied you in your claims against them, so you cannot fend off the punishment from yourselves nor help them due to your incapability. O believers, whoever oppresses from amongst you by ascribing partners to Allah, We shall make him suffer a great punishment, just like We will make the ones mentioned suffer.",
  25020:
      "When the polytheists criticized the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم for eating food and walking in the markets, Allah responded to them, stating: \n O Messenger, all the messengers We sent before you were humans who would eat food and walk in the markets; you are not a unique messenger. O, people, I have made you trials for each other by granting you varying degrees of affluence, poverty, health, and sickness; throughout these different circumstances, will you bear whatever you are afflicted with so that Allah may reward you upon your patience? Your Lord is ever-aware of those who are patient and those who are not, those who obey Him and those who disobey Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The blend of inciting fear of the punishment of Allah, together with awakening a longing for His reward.\n2. Those worshipped will proclaim innocence from those that worshipped them on the Day of Judgment.\n3. Pleasures of the world make one forget the remembrance of Allah.\n4. The Messengers being humans is a blessing of Allah for the people, because it is easier to relate to them.\n5. People being in varying levels of blessings and trials is a test from Allah for His servants.",
  25021:
      "The disbelievers who do not wish to meet Us or fear Our punishment said: Why doesn't Allah send the angels down to us to tell us about Muhammad's truthfulness? Or Why can't we see our Lord with our own eyes so He can inform us about it? They became so conceited, to the point that it prevented them from having faith. They surpassed the limit of disbelief and transgression with their statements.",
  25022:
      "On the Day these people see the angels at the time of their death, when they are in the Barzakh, when they are resurrected, when they are led to their judgment, and when they enter the Fire, there will not be any glad tidings for them on these occasions. In contrast to the believers, the angels will say to them: Glad tidings from Allah are forbidden for you.",
  25023:
      "We shall turn to the righteous deeds that the disbelievers did in their lives and make them like the scattered particles of dust that are visible in the light rays that pass through a window. This is due to their falsehood and lack of benefit because of their disbelief.",
  25024:
      "On that Day, the believers, the people of Paradise, will have a better abode and shelter than these disbelievers. This is due to their faith in Allah and their righteous deeds.",
  25025:
      "Mention, O Messenger, the Day when the sky will be rent asunder to reveal thin white clouds, and the angels will be sent down to the plains of the Gathering in immense numbers.",
  25026:
      "The true, established Kingdom on the Day of Resurrection will be for the Merciful, the Exalted. That will be a difficult Day for the disbelievers, in contrast to the believers, for whom it will be easy.",
  25027:
      "Mention, O Messenger, the Day the transgressor will bite down on his hand in regret due to not following the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, and say: If only I had followed the Messenger in what he brought from his Lord, and taken a path with him to salvation.",
  25028:
      "Due to extreme grief, he will curse himself, saying: Woe to me! If only I had not taken that disbeliever as a friend!",
  25029:
      "That friend led me away from the Quran after it had been conveyed to me through the Messenger. Indeed, the Devil has ever been a betrayer to humanity, and when a calamity befalls humanity, he renounces him.",
  25030:
      "On that Day, the Messenger will complain about the condition of his people: O my Lord, my people whom You sent me to have abandoned this Quran and turned away from it.",
  25031:
      "Similar to your experience with your people, O Messenger, regarding the harm and the prevention of others from following your path, We had assigned to every Prophet before you an enemy from the criminals of his people. Your Lord is a sufficient guide to the truth and a sufficient supporter against your enemies.",
  25032:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah said: Shouldn't the Quran have been revealed to him in one go instead of intermittently? We revealed the Quran intermittently to make your heart firm, O Messenger, by revealing it in portions gradually. We revealed it to you progressively to make it easy to understand and memorize.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Arrogance is a barrier from guidance to the truth.\n2. Disbelief prevents the acceptance of righteous deeds.\n3. Disbelief will be the cause of great regret on the Day of Judgement.\n4. The danger of evil friends.\n5. The harm of abandoning the Qur’an.\n6. The enmity of the people of falsehood for the people of truth is ongoing.\n7. One of the wisdoms behind revealing the Qur’an gradually is to reassure the Prophet (peace be upon him) and to facilitate his understanding, memorisation and practice.\n8. Refutation of the doubts raised by the disbelievers with regard to the gradual revelation of the Qur’an.",
  25033:
      "The polytheists do not bring any argument to you, O Messenger, except that We give you a true and firm response to it and a better explanation.",
  25034:
      "Those who will be dragged on their faces to Hell on the Day of Resurrection, it is they who will be in the worst situation. Because their abode will be Hell, and it is the furthest path from the truth because their path is the path of disbelief and deviation.",
  25035:
      "And We Indeed gave Moses the Torah and appointed his brother, Aaron, as a Messenger to support him.",
  25036:
      "We then said to them: Go to Pharaoh and his people, those who denied Our signs. They fulfilled Our order, went to them, and invited them to Allah's Oneness. However, they rejected them, and so We completely destroyed them.",
  25037:
      "Likewise were the people of Noah when they rejected the Messengers by rejecting Noah (peace be upon him). We destroyed them by drowning them in the flood, and We made their destruction a sign of Our Ability to utterly eliminate the transgressors. And We have prepared a painful punishment on the Day of Resurrection for the transgressors.",
  25038:
      "We also destroyed 'Ād, the people of Hūd, as well as Thamūd, the people of Saleh. We destroyed the people of the Well and many a nation between them.",
  25039:
      "To all of those who were destroyed, We described the destruction of the previous nations before them as well as the reasons behind their destruction so that they may take heed. And each of them We utterly destroyed because of their disbelief and obstinacy.",
  25040:
      "On their journey to the Levant, those who rejected the truth from your people passed by the town of the people of Lot. The town which had rocks rained down upon them as a punishment for their immoral behavior so that they may take heed. Were they blinded to this town and did not see it? No! Rather, they did not believe they would be resurrected and taken to account thereafter.",
  25041:
      "Whenever these deniers of truth meet you, O Messenger, they ridicule you by mockingly saying in denial; Is this the one Allah sent as a Messenger to us?!",
  25042:
      "He almost led us away from worshiping our gods. Were it not that we remained steadfastly worshiping them, he would have turned us away from them with his clear proofs and evidence. When they see the punishment with their own eyes in their graves and on the Day of Resurrection, they will come to know who is really on the stray path. Is it them or him? And they will come to know which of the two is astray.",
  25043:
      "Have you not seen, O Messenger, those who have turned their desires into a god and obeyed them? Are you the one who is going to be a guardian over them, bringing them back to faith and preventing them from disbelief?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Rejection of Allah and denial of His signs is a cause for communities to be destroyed.\n2. The lack of faith in resurrection is the cause for not taking heed.\n3. Mocking the people of truth is the trait of the disbelievers.\n4. The danger of following one’s desires.",
  25044:
      "Rather, O Messenger, do you think most of those whom you call to Allah's Oneness and obedience listen acceptingly or understand the evidence and proofs? They are only like cattle regarding their hearing, thinking, and understanding. Rather, they are even more astray from the path than cattle.",
  25045:
      "Do you not see, O Messenger, the effects of Allah's creation? How your Lord extends shade over the surface of the Earth. If He had willed to make it still, without moving, He could have made it so. Then, We made the sun as an indicator for shade, extending and shortening in accordance with it.",
  25046:
      "Then, We retract the shade, reducing it gradually, little by little, in accordance with the rising sun.",
  25047:
      "It is Allah who rendered the night as a garment that covers you and all other things. It is He who made sleep a rest for you from work. It is He who made the day for you to go out and work.",
  25048:
      "It is He who sends the winds as heralds of the good news of rain, a Mercy to His slaves. We sent down pure rainwater from above, which they use for purification.",
  25049:
      "With this falling rainwater, We revive barren land void of vegetation, causing various plants to sprout, spreading vegetation. We also provide drinking water for the many people and animals we created.",
  25050:
      "In the Quran, we have clarified evidence and clear proof in various ways so that they might take heed. But most people persist in their rejection and denial of the truth.",
  25051:
      "If We wished, We would have sent a Messenger to every village to warn them of Allah's punishment. But We did not will it. We sent Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم as a Messenger to all people.",
  25052:
      "So, do not follow the disbelievers' demands for concessions and proposals. Strive against them with this Quran that was sent down to you by being patient over harm and tolerating difficulties in calling them to Allah.",
  25053:
      "It is Allah, the Exalted, who merged the water of the two seas, one sweet and the other salty, and put a barrier, dividing and preventing them from mixing.",
  25054:
      "It is He who created humanity from the discharge of a man and woman. From the creation of humanity, He established kinship by blood and inlaws through marriage. Your Lord, O Messenger, is all-powerful; nothing is beyond His ability. Through His Power, He created humanity from the discharge of a man and woman.",
  25055:
      "The disbelievers worship idols instead of Allah, which can neither benefit them if they obey them, nor harm them if they disobey them. The disbeliever has always followed the Devil in that which angers Allah, the Exalted.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbeliever stoops to a level lower than that of the animals on account of his rejection of Allah.\n2. The phenomenon of shade is one of the signs of Allah that indicate His Power.\n3. The creation of the night for rest and the day for work is a blessing of Allah.\n4. Rain is a form of Allah’s mercy for His creation.\n5. Diversification of arguments and proofs is an effective educational style.\n6. Calling by means of the Qur’an is one of the forms of striving in Allah’s path.",
  25056:
      "And we have not sent you, O Messenger, except as a bearer of glad tidings for those who obey Allah, by having faith and performing righteous actions, and as a warner to those who disobey Him, by committing disbelief and sin.",
  25057:
      "Say, O Messenger, I do not ask you for any reward for conveying the message, except that those of you who wish can take a path to please Allah by spending in His cause.",
  25058:
      "And rely, O Messenger, in all your affairs on Allah, the Ever-Living, the Everlasting who never dies, and exalt Him, the Exalted. Sufficient is He in knowing the sins of His slaves. None of their sins are hidden from Him, which He will recompense them for.",
  25059:
      "The One who created the heavens and Earth and everything between them in six days and then rose above the Throne in a manner that befits His Majesty. He is the Merciful, so ask about Him, O Messenger, one who is well informed. He is Allah, the One who knows everything and from Whom nothing is hidden.",
  25060:
      "And when it is said to the disbelievers, Prostrate to the Merciful, they say: And who is the Merciful? We do not know him, nor do we recognize him. Should we prostrate to whomever you are ordering us while not knowing him? His order to prostrate to the Merciful only increased their aversion to faith in Allah.",
  25061:
      "Blessed is He who made places in the heavens for the planets and orbiting stars. He placed therein a sun that radiates light and a luminous moon that illuminates the Earth with the light reflected from the sun.",
  25062:
      "It is Allah who has rendered the night and day in succession, each one following the other, for whoever desires to contemplate the signs of Allah and attain guidance or desires to be grateful to Allah for His favors.",
  25063:
      "When Allah mentions in this Surah the disbelievers who reject faith and obedience to Him, He mentions the characteristics of His righteous slaves who are willingly obedient to Him, stating: \n The slaves of the Merciful are the believers who walk with humility and dignity upon the Earth. When the foolish address them, they do not retaliate in a similar manner. Rather, they speak to them cordially without being rude.",
  25064:
      "Those who spend their nights prostrating on their foreheads and standing on their feet in prayer to Allah.",
  25065:
      "Those who say in their prayers to their Lord: Our Lord, distance us from Hell's punishment. For indeed, the punishment of Hell is perpetual and everlasting for those who die as disbelievers.",
  25066:
      "It is indeed a terrible place of settlement for those who will settle therein and a terrible residence for those who will reside therein.",
  25067:
      "Those who spend their wealth without being exorbitant or restrictive with those they are responsible for providing for, whether it is themselves or others. Their spending is just and balanced, midway between exorbitance and miserliness.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The person who calls to Allah does not seek a reward from people.\n2. Allah transcends His creation.\n3. The Merciful (Al-Rahman) is one of the names of Allah that no one has ever shared with Him. It indicates to one of His attributes which is the attribute of Mercy.\n4. The servant is assisted by the night and day coming one after the other to make up any act of obedience missed in any one of them.\n5. Some of the attributes of the servants of the Merciful is their humility and tolerance, their obedience to Allah when people are neglectful, their fear of Allah and their adherence to moderation in spending and in other matters.",
  25068:
      "Those who do not call on any other deity besides Allah, the Exalted, nor do they take the life of anyone whose life Allah has prohibited, except for what Allah has allowed (such as the killing of a murderer, one who has forsaken his religion, or a married adulterer), and those who do not fornicate. And whoever commits these major sins will face punishment for their sins on the Day of Resurrection.",
  25069:
      "The punishment will be doubled for them on the Day of Resurrection, and they will remain in the punishment in disgrace and humiliation for eternity.",
  25070:
      "But those who repent to Allah, believe, and practice righteous deeds that prove the sincerity of their repentance, Allah will turn their sins into righteous deeds. Allah is ever forgiving towards the sins of His slaves who repent to Him. He is ever Merciful towards them.",
  25071:
      "And whoever repents to Allah and proves the sincerity of their repentance by observing righteous deeds and forsaking sin, indeed, their repentance is accepted.",
  25072:
      "Those who do not attend falsehood, such as places of sin or prohibited forms of entertainment, and when they come across vain speech and behavior, they hurry, maintaining their dignity by avoiding them.",
  25073:
      "Those who, when reminded of Allah's signs, which are heard or witnessed, do not close their ears to the signs that are heard, nor shut their eyes to the signs that are witnessed.",
  25074:
      "Those who say in their prayers to their Lord: Our Lord, make our spouses and offspring the apples of our eyes due to their acceptance and adherence to the truth. Make us leaders of truth who would be taken as examples by the righteous.",
  25075:
      "Those who possess these attributes will be rewarded with lofty chambers in the highest level of Paradise, Al-Firdaws, due to their steadfastness in obedience to Allah. There, they will be greeted by the angels with peace, and they will be safe and secure from all difficulties.",
  25076:
      "They will abide therein for eternity; a wonderful abode and residence for them to abide and reside in.",
  25077:
      "Say, O Messenger, to the disbelievers who persist in their disbelief: My Lord does not pay attention to you because of any benefit that He receives from your obedience. Were it not that He had slaves who pray to Him in praise and supplication, He would not have any concern for you. Indeed, you have rejected the message that the Messenger brought to you from your Lord. Therefore, the recompense of this rejection will be inseparable from you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Some of the attributes of those who are servants of the Merciful include: Staying away from idolatry, avoiding taking a life unjustly, staying away from fornication and falsehood, taking a lesson from Allah’s signs and praying to Him.\n2. Sincere repentance requires the leaving of the sin and the doing of good deeds.\n3. Patience is a means for entering the highest stage in paradise.\n4. Allah is not in need of the disbelievers’ having faith.",
  26000:
      "The Poets (Surah Al-Shu'arah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating Allah's signs of supporting the messengers and destroying the rejectors.\n•    Explanation:",
  26001:
      "Tā Sīn Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  26002: "These are the verses of the Quran that clarify truth from falsehood.",
  26003:
      "Perhaps due to your eagerness, O Messenger, you are killing yourself with sorrow and keenness for their guidance because of the disbelievers rejecting you and not believing in your message.",
  26004:
      "If We wished to send down a sign from the heavens that would compel them to believe, We would send it to them. Their heads would remain bowed in utter humility before it. But We do not wish that to test whether they would believe in the Unseen or not.",
  26005:
      "A new reminder that proves His Oneness and the truthfulness of His Prophet is not revealed by the Merciful to these polytheists, except that they turn away from listening and believing in it.",
  26006:
      "They have rejected what their Messenger brought them. So, the reality of what they used to mock will befall them, and the punishment will take them.",
  26007:
      "These people remained persistent in their disbelief. They did not reflect over the Earth. How many different types of vegetation, beautiful to look at and full of benefits, did we cause to grow on it?!",
  26008:
      "The varying types of vegetation made to grow on Earth clearly indicate that the One who has caused them to grow has the power to revive the dead. However, most of them are not believers.",
  26009:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Prevailing One who can never be overpowered, the Merciful to His slaves.",
  26010:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when your Lord called upon Moses, instructing him to go to the transgressors who disbelieved in Allah and enslaved the people of Moses.",
  26011:
      "They were Pharaoh's people. He was to gently instruct them to be mindful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  26012:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: I fear that they will reject the message I convey to them about you.",
  26013:
      "And that I will be distressed due to their rejection and not be able to speak. So send Gabriel (peace be upon him) to my brother Aaron so that he may support me.",
  26014:
      "They also have a charge against me because I had killed the Copt, and I fear they may kill me.",
  26015:
      "Allah said to Moses (peace be upon him): No! They will never be able to kill you. Go, you and your brother Aaron, with Our signs that prove your truthfulness. We shall be with you with Our support, listening to what you say and what is said to you. We will miss nothing of that.",
  26016:
      "Go to Pharaoh and tell him: We are two Messengers sent to you by the Lord of all created things.",
  26017: "That you send the Israelites with us.",
  26018:
      "Pharaoh said to Moses (peace be upon him: Did we not raise you as a child among us? Did you not live with us for many years of your life? So what has now made you claim prophethood?",
  26019:
      "You committed a serious crime by killing the Copt while defending one of your people. You deny my favors to you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The concern of the Messenger (peace be upon him) for the guidance of people.\n2. Affirmation of the attributes of might and mercy for Allah.\n3. Being gentle with those who are invited to Allah is required and desired.\n4. The importance for a preacher to be eloquent and open hearted.\n5. The calls of the prophets are a liberation from the servitude to other than Allah.\n6. The disbelievers employ their services to prevent others from Allah’s path.",
  26020:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said, admitting to Pharaoh: I killed that man while I was ignorant, before I received revelation.",
  26021:
      "After killing him, I fled from you to Midian, fearing that you would kill me. Then, my Lord bestowed me with knowledge and made me one of His Messengers that He sends to people.",
  26022:
      "Raising me without enslaving me while enslaving the Israelites is truly a reminder of your favor upon me. But that does not prevent me from calling you to the truth.",
  26023:
      "Pharaoh said to Moses (peace be upon him): What is the Lord of all created things, Whose Messenger you claim to be?",
  26024:
      "Moses responded: The Lord of all created things is the Lord of the heavens and the Earth. The Lord of everything between them if you have sure faith. Indeed, He is their Lord, so worship Him alone.",
  26025:
      "Pharaoh asked the noble of his people around him: Do you hear Moses's response and the false claims it contains?",
  26026:
      "Moses said to them: Allah is your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers.",
  26027:
      "Pharaoh said: This man who claims to be your Messenger is insane. He does not know how to respond and says things that do not make sense.",
  26028:
      "Moses said; Allah, the One I call you to, is the Lord of the East and the West, the Lord of everything between them. If only you had the intellect to reflect.",
  26029:
      "Unable to debate, Pharaoh said to Moses: If you worship any god other than Me, I will make you a prisoner.",
  26030:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said to Pharaoh: Would you imprison me even if I brought a clear sign of the truthfulness of the message I bring to you from Allah?",
  26031:
      "He said: Bring what you claim will prove your truthfulness if you are telling the truth!",
  26032:
      "So Moses cast his staff on the ground, and it suddenly turned into a snake that could be clearly seen.",
  26033:
      "He put his ordinary-looking hand into an opening of his garment, and he then drew it out a radiant white, not the white of vitiligo, for everyone to see.",
  26034:
      "Pharaoh said to the noble of his people around him: This man is a well-versed magician.",
  26035:
      "He means to drive you out of your land with his magic! So what do you suggest we do with him?",
  26036:
      "They said to him: Delay him and his brother and do not rush to punish them. Send people to the cities of Egypt who will gather the magicians.",
  26037: "They will bring you every well-versed magician.",
  26038:
      "Pharaoh assembled his magicians to challenge Moses at an appointed place and time.",
  26039:
      "The people were told: Will you not gather to see who triumphs: Moses or the magicians?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Adopting the means to protect oneself from the enemy does not negate faith and reliance in Allah.\n2. The creation of Allah indicates to His being the Lord and the One worthy of worship.\n3. Weakness of argument is one of the reasons for using violence.\n4. Inciting the masses against the people of religion is the style of the transgressors.",
  26040: "Let us follow the magician's religion if they triumph over Moses.",
  26041:
      "So when the magicians came before Pharaoh to challenge Moses, they asked him: Will we have a tangible or intangible reward if we triumph over Moses?",
  26042:
      "Pharaoh said to them: Yes, you shall have a reward. If you triumph over Moses, you shall become close to me by being appointed to lofty positions.",
  26043:
      "With confidence in Allah's support and clarifying what he possessed was not sorcery, Moses said to them; Cast whatever ropes and staffs you have.",
  26044:
      "So they cast their ropes and staffs while saying: By Pharaoh's greatness, we shall surely triumph, and Moses is the one who will be defeated!",
  26045:
      "So Moses cast his staff, which turned into a snake, swallowing the illusions they released over the people with their magic.",
  26046:
      "When the magicians saw Moses's staff swallowing up what they had cast, they fell into prostration.",
  26047: "They said: We believe in the Lord of all creation.",
  26048: "The Lord of Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them).",
  26049:
      "In condemnation of the magicians' faith, Pharaoh said to them: Have you believed in Moses before I have permitted? Indeed, Moses is your mentor who has taught you sorcery. You have all collaborated to exile the people of Egypt from their lands, and you will soon come to know the punishment I shall inflict upon you. I shall cut off the right foot and left hand of each of you from opposite sides or vice versa and crucify you on the trunks of palm trees. I shall spare none of you.",
  26050:
      "The magicians said to Pharaoh: There is no harm in the maiming and crucifixion you threaten us with in this worldly life because your punishment will end. And we shall return to our Lord who shall admit us into His everlasting mercy.",
  26051:
      "We indeed hope that Allah erases our past sins due to being the first to believe in Moses.",
  26052:
      "And We revealed to Moses, commanding him to lead the Israelites out by night because Pharaoh and his people would pursue them and force them back.",
  26053:
      "When Pharaoh learned of the Israelites' escape, he sent some soldiers to the cities to rally and gather the armies to bring them back.",
  26054:
      "Pharaoh said in belittlement of the Israelites: Indeed, they are a small group.",
  26055: "And they are doing what angers us.",
  26056: "And indeed, we are prepared for them and alert.",
  26057:
      "So We expelled Pharaoh and his people from Egypt, a wealthy land with abundant gardens and flowing streams.",
  26058: "A land with treasures of wealth and beautiful dwellings.",
  26059:
      "And just as We expelled Pharaoh and his people from these favors, We granted their likes to the Israelites in the Levant.",
  26060:
      "Pharaoh and his people followed the trail of the Israelites at sunrise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The relationship of the people of falsehood among themselves is based on materialistic interest.\n2. Moses was confident of the help of Allah over the magicians, believing in the promise of his Lord.\n3. The magicians eventually believing is proof that Allah is the turner of hearts; He turns them however He wishes.\n4. The people of tyranny take refuge in violence due to being incapable of challenging evidence with evidence.\n5. Tyranny and oppression is a cause of one’s authority diminishing.",
  26061:
      "So when Pharaoh and his people reached Moses and his people, whereas they were in sight of each other, Moses's people said: Pharaoh and his people will surely catch up to us, and we are powerless against them.",
  26062:
      "Moses said to his people: It is not as you imagine, for indeed, my Lord is with me with His support and aid. He shall guide and show me the path to salvation.",
  26063:
      "We revealed to Moses, commanding him to strike the sea with his staff, and so he did. The sea parted into twelve paths, the number of the tribes of the Israelites. Each path cut from the sea was like a tremendous and stable mountain from which water does not leak.",
  26064:
      "We allowed Pharaoh and his people to draw close until they entered the sea, thinking that the path was traversable.",
  26065:
      "And We saved Moses and those with him from the Israelites; none amongst them perished.",
  26066:
      "We then destroyed Pharaoh and his people by drowning them in the sea.",
  26067:
      "Indeed, the parting of the sea for Moses, his salvation, and Pharaoh's destruction is a sign proving the truthfulness of Moses. And the majority of those with Pharaoh were not believers.",
  26068:
      "And Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of them who repent.",
  26069: "O Messenger, recite unto them Abraham's story.",
  26070:
      "When he said to his father Azar and his people: What is it you worship instead of Allah?",
  26071:
      "His people said to him: We worship idols, and we remain steadfast and consistent in their worship.",
  26072:
      "Abraham said to them: Do the idols hear your prayers when you pray to them?",
  26073:
      "Or do they benefit you if you feed them, or harm you if you disobey them?",
  26074:
      "They responded: They do not hear us when we supplicate to them, nor do they benefit us when we feed them, nor do they harm us if we disobey them. However, the reality is that we found our forefathers doing that, so we imitate them.",
  26075:
      "Abraham said: Have you contemplated and looked at the idols you worship instead of Allah?",
  26076: "And what your forefathers worshiped?",
  26077:
      "Indeed, they are all enemies to me because they are all false except for the Lord of all creation.",
  26078:
      "The One who created me and therefore guides me to the best of this world and the Hereafter.",
  26079:
      "It is He alone who feeds me when I am hungry and gives me to drink when I am thirsty.",
  26080:
      "And when I am ill, He alone cures me; there is no healer for me except Him.",
  26081:
      "It is He alone who will cause me to die when my lifespan expires and resurrect me after my death.",
  26082:
      "It is He alone Whom I hope will forgive my sins on the day of requital.",
  26083:
      "Abraham, supplicating to his Lord, said: O my Lord, grant me a deep understanding of religion and unite me with the righteous prophets who came before me by admitting me into Paradise with them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A believer should have firm reliance in his Lord.\n2. Allah is always helping, supporting and saving his believing servants from difficulties.\n3. Allah is Mighty and Merciful.\n4. The foolishness of the idolaters in that they worship idols that do not hear and cannot cause benefit nor harm.\n5. The harm of following blindly.\n6. The hope a believer has in his Lord should be immense.",
  26084:
      "And grant me a beautiful and praiseworthy account with the generations after me.",
  26085:
      "And make me among those who inherit the dwellings of Paradise where your believing slaves shall reside in luxury; and grant me residence in them.",
  26086:
      "And forgive my father. Indeed, he was amongst those who deviated from the truth due to polytheism. Abraham supplicated for his father before it became apparent to him that he was from the people of the Inferno. After it became clear to him, he disassociated from him and no longer supplicated for him.",
  26087:
      "Do not humiliate me by punishing me on the Day people are resurrected to be taken to account.",
  26088:
      "The Day when the wealth humanity accumulated in this world shall be of no benefit, nor would the offspring that used to support them.",
  26089:
      "Except those who come with a sound heart, free of polytheism, hypocrisy, ostentation, and arrogance. For indeed, they would benefit from the wealth they spent in the path of Allah, and the offspring who prayed for them.",
  26090:
      "Paradise will be brought close to the righteous who complied with His commands and avoided His prohibitions.",
  26091:
      "And the Fire will be made visible on the plains of resurrection to those who went astray and deviated from the true religion.",
  26092:
      "It will be said to them in rebuke: Where are the idols you used to worship? Are they going to support you by preventing the punishment of Allah from you, or are they going to support themselves?",
  26093:
      "It will be said to them in rebuke: Where are the idols you used to worship? Are they going to support you by preventing the punishment of Allah from you, or are they going to support themselves?",
  26094:
      "They will be thrown into the Inferno one on top of the other, together with whoever they led astray.",
  26095: "Iblees's helpers are all devils without exception.",
  26096:
      "The polytheists who used to worship other than Allah, taking them as partners to Him, will say while arguing with those they used to worship,",
  26097: "By Allah, we were indeed clearly astray from the truth.",
  26098:
      "Since we held you on par with the Lord of all creatures, and so worshipped you as we worship Him.",
  26099:
      "And no one led us astray from the true path except the criminals who called us towards worshipping them instead of Allah.",
  26100:
      "So we have no intercessors today who will intercede for us before Allah to save us from His punishment.",
  26101:
      "Nor do we have a friend who sincerely loves us to defend and intercede for us.",
  26102:
      "If only we could return to our worldly life so that we could be amongst those who believed in Allah.",
  26103:
      "Indeed, in what was mentioned, in the story of Abraham (peace be upon him) and the ultimate destination of the deniers is a lesson for those who take heed. Although most of them are not believers.",
  26104:
      "And Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of them who repent.",
  26105:
      "The people of Noah rejected all the messengers when they rejected Noah (peace be upon him).",
  26106:
      "When Noah said to them: Will you not be mindful of Allah and leave the worship of other than Him out of fear for Him?",
  26107:
      "Indeed, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you. I am trustworthy and will not add or remove anything from what has been revealed to me.",
  26108:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26109:
      "I do not seek any reward from you for what I convey to you from my Lord. My reward is only from Allah, the Lord of all creation, not from anyone else.",
  26110:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26111:
      "His people said to him: O Noah, are we to believe in you, follow what you have brought, and apply it while your followers are the lowliest? There aren't any leaders or noblemen among them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of keeping the heart free of illnesses such as jealousy, ostentation and arrogance.\n2. Admitting the truth on the Day of Judgment will be of no benefit.\n3. Attributing the responsibility of deviance to those who lead people astray will not benefit the deviants.\n4. Those who call towards Allah await their reward from Allah, not His servants.",
  26112:
      "Noah (peace be upon him) said to them: What do I know of what these believers used to do? I am not an overseer over them to account for their deeds.",
  26113:
      "Their account is for Allah, who knows their secret and public affairs, not me. If you comprehended what you said, you would not have said it.",
  26114:
      "I am not going to throw out these believers from my gatherings to accommodate your requests, for you to believe.",
  26115: "I am only a clear warner warning you of the punishment of Allah.",
  26116:
      "His people said to him: If you do not stop calling to what you are calling us to, you will surely be vilified and stoned to death.",
  26117:
      "Supplicating to his Lord, Noah said: My Lord, indeed, my nation has rejected me. They have not believed in what I brought from you.",
  26118:
      "So judge between us such that they are destroyed due to their insistence on falsehood, and save me and the believers who are with me from the punishment you will destroy the disbelievers from my people with.",
  26119:
      "So We responded to his supplication and saved him and the believers with him in the Ark that was full of people and animals.",
  26120: "We then drowned the rest, who were the people of Noah.",
  26121:
      "Indeed, in the aforementioned story of Noah and his people, Noah's salvation and those with him, along with the destruction of the disbelievers, is a lesson for those who take heed. However, most of them are not believers.",
  26122:
      "And Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of them who repent.",
  26123:
      "The people of 'Ād rejected all the messengers when they rejected their messenger, Hūd (peace be upon him).",
  26124:
      "Mention when their brother, the prophet Hūd, said to them: Will you not be mindful of Allah and leave the worship of other than Him out of fear for Him?",
  26125:
      "Indeed, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you. I am trustworthy and will not add or remove anything from what Allah ordered me to relay.",
  26126:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26127:
      "I do not seek any reward from you for what I convey to you from my Lord. My reward is only from Allah, the Lord of all creation, not from anyone else.",
  26128:
      "Do you unnecessarily build a landmark in every elevated site without any benefit for you in this world or the Afterlife?",
  26129:
      "And you build forts and palaces as if you were to live eternally in this world, never departing from it?",
  26130:
      "And when you attack or battle, you attack like tyrants, showing no kindness or mercy.",
  26131:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26132:
      "And fear the wrath of Allah who has granted you favors you know well.",
  26133: "He has given you domestic animals and given you offspring.",
  26134: "He has given you gardens and flowing streams.",
  26135:
      "O my people, I fear for you, the punishment of a tremendous day, the Day of Resurrection.",
  26136:
      "His people said to him; It is the same to us whether you warn us or not, for we shall never believe in you and will never turn away from what we are upon.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The people of falsehood take refuge in violence when they are cornered with proofs.\n2. The oppressors being destroyed and believers being saved is a divine custom of Allah.\n3. The dangers of being wholly dependant on the world.\n4. The stubbornness of the people of falsehood and their insistence upon it.",
  26137:
      "This is only the religion, customs, and character of the people of the past.",
  26138: "And we are not going to be punished.",
  26139:
      "They continued to reject their prophet Hūd (peace be upon him), so We destroyed them due to their rejection by a barren wind. Indeed, there is a lesson in their destruction for those who take heed. And most of them were not believers.",
  26140:
      "And indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of His slaves who repent.",
  26141:
      "Thamūd rejected all the messengers when they rejected Saleh (peace be upon him).",
  26142:
      "When their brother Saleh asked them; Will you not fear Allah by forsaking worshiping others?",
  26143:
      "Indeed, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you. I am trustworthy and will not add or remove anything from what has been revealed to me.",
  26144:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26145:
      "I do not seek any reward from you for what I convey to you from my Lord. My reward is only from Allah, the Lord of all creation, not from anyone else.",
  26146:
      "Do you expect to be left alone in safety in the goodness and favors you enjoy without fear?",
  26147: "In gardens and flowing springs.",
  26148: "Among crops and palms with tender and ripe fruit.",
  26149: "And you skillfully carve out houses from the mountains to live in.",
  26150:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Obey me in what I command and prohibit.",
  26151:
      "And do not follow the commands of those who are excessive on themselves by committing sins.",
  26152:
      "Those who cause corruption on Earth by spreading sins and do not rectify themselves by steadfastly obeying Allah.",
  26153:
      "His people said to him; You are surely one who has been bewitched repeatedly until the sorcery has overcome your intellect and driven you mad.",
  26154:
      "You are nothing but a human like us; there is nothing special about you compared to us to make you a Messenger. So bring proof that you are a Messenger if you are indeed truthful in your claim.",
  26155:
      "After Allah had granted Saleh proof in the form of the she-camel, which Allah extracted from the rock, he said to them: This is a she-camel that is visible and tangible. It has a share of the water, as you also have a designated share. It will not drink on the day designated to you, nor shall you let your livestock drink on its appointed day.",
  26156:
      "Do not harm it by hitting or slaughtering it, lest the punishment of Allah comes upon you and destroys you on a dreadful day due to the afflictions coming down upon you.",
  26157:
      "So they agreed upon slaughtering it, and the most wretched one amongst them did it. They regretted what they did when they realized that the punishment was going to befall them inevitably. However, regret after seeing the punishment is of no benefit.",
  26158:
      "So the punishment that they were promised seized them: it was an earthquake accompanied by a scream. Indeed, in the aforementioned, i.e., the story of Saleh and his people, is a lesson for those who take heed. Although most of them do not believe.",
  26159:
      "And Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of His slaves who repent.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Rejecting one prophet means rejecting every Messenger.\n2. Reminding people of the bounties of Allah brings hope in servants believing and returning to Allah.\n3. Sins are a cause of corruption on Earth.",
  26160:
      "Lot's people rejected all the messengers by rejecting their prophet Lot (peace be upon him).",
  26161:
      "Remember when their brother in lineage Lot said to them: Will you not be mindful of Allah by leaving idolatry out of fear of Him?",
  26162:
      "Indeed, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you. I am trustworthy in what I convey to you from him and will not add or remove anything from what has been revealed to me.",
  26163:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26164:
      "I do not seek any reward from you for what I convey to you from my Lord. My reward is only from Allah, the Lord of all creation, not from anyone else.",
  26165: "Do you approach men [sexually] from their rears?!",
  26166:
      "And leave the private parts of your wives that Allah has created for you to fulfill your desires? You have indeed transgressed the limits of Allah by this detestable deviance.",
  26167:
      "His people said to him: O Lot, if you do not stop forbidding us from this act and rebuking us over it, you and those with you shall be exiled from our city.",
  26168: "Lot said to them: Indeed, I abhor this act that you engage in.",
  26169:
      "Supplicating to his Lord, he said: My Lord, save me and my family from the punishment that will afflict these people because of the evil they commit.",
  26170: "So We accepted his supplication and saved him and his whole family.",
  26171:
      "Except for his wife, for she was a disbeliever. So she was amongst the destroyed who perished.",
  26172:
      "After Lot and his family left the city of Sodom, We severely destroyed who remained from his people.",
  26173:
      "We rained stones from the sky down on them, just like rain. Disgraceful was the rain that befell those whom Lot used to warn of Allah's punishment if they continued committing their evil acts.",
  26174:
      "Indeed, in the aforementioned punishment that descended on the people of Lot due to their committing lewd acts is a lesson for those who take heed. And most of them were not believers.",
  26175:
      "And indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of His slaves who repent.",
  26176:
      "The People of the Thicket close to Midian rejected the Messengers when they rejected their prophet Shuayb (peace be upon him).",
  26177:
      "Their brother Shuayb said to them: Will you not fear Allah by forsaking worshiping others?",
  26178:
      "Indeed, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you. I am trustworthy in what I convey from him and will not add or remove anything from what has been revealed to me.",
  26179:
      "So fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And obey me in what I command you to do and what I forbid you from.",
  26180:
      "I do not seek any reward from you for what I convey to you from my Lord. My reward is only from Allah, the Lord of all creation, not from anyone else.",
  26181:
      "When you sell to the people, measure for them properly. Do not be people who reduce the measurement when selling to people.",
  26182: "Measure justly when you sell to others.",
  26183:
      "And do not violate people's rights and excessively cause corruption on Earth by committing sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Sodomy is an abnormality from nature and a grave evil.\n2. The people of corruption and falsehood being destroyed and the people of truth being saved is a divine custom of Allah.\n3. As long as worldly relationships are not accompanied with faith, they will not benefit when the punishment descends.\n4. It is obligatory to measure fully and forbidden to be deficient in measure.",
  26184:
      "And be fearful of the One who created you and past nations, fearing He sends down His punishment upon you.",
  26185:
      "Shuayb's people said to him: You are the only one who has been repeatedly afflicted with sorcery until it has overcome your intelligence and driven you mad.",
  26186:
      "You are nothing but a human like us; there is nothing special about you. So, how can you be a messenger? We believe you are lying about your claims of being a Messenger.",
  26187:
      "So, cause a piece of sky to fall upon us if you are truthful in your claim.",
  26188:
      "Shuayb said to them: My Lord knows the polytheism and sins you commit; none of your actions are hidden from Him.",
  26189:
      "They continued to reject him, and so a terrible punishment befell them. A cloud shaded them after a severely hot day; it rained fire upon them, burning them. The day they were destroyed was extremely horrific.",
  26190:
      "Indeed, in the aforementioned destruction of Shuayb's people is a lesson for those who take heed. And most of them were not believers.",
  26191:
      "And indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, the Merciful to those of His slaves who repent.",
  26192:
      "Indeed, this Quran that was revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was revealed by the Lord of creation.",
  26193: "It was brought down by the trustworthy Gabriel (peace be upon him).",
  26194:
      "He brought it down to your heart, O Messenger, so that you become of the Messengers who warn people and make them fearful of Allah's punishment.",
  26195: "He brought it down in a clear Arabic language.",
  26196:
      "And indeed, this Quran has been mentioned in the previous Books; previous divine books have given glad tidings of it.",
  26197:
      "Was it not a sign of your truthfulness for these people who reject you that the scholars of the Israelites, like Abdullah bin Salām, knew the reality of what has been revealed to you?",
  26198: "Had we revealed this Quran to non-Arabs who do not speak Arabic,",
  26199:
      "And it was read to them; they would not become believers because they would say: We do not understand it! So they should praise Allah that it was revealed in their language.",
  26200:
      "Likewise, we placed rejection and disbelief in the hearts of criminals.",
  26201:
      "They will not change their state of disbelief and will not believe until they see the painful punishment.",
  26202:
      "This punishment will come to them suddenly; they will not know of its approach until it befalls them.",
  26203:
      "So when the punishment will come upon them suddenly, they will say out of immense grief: Will we be given respite to repent to Allah?",
  26204:
      "Do these disbelievers hastily anticipate our punishment, saying: We will never believe in you until you cause the sky to fall upon us in pieces, as you claim.",
  26205:
      "So tell Us, O Messenger, if We let these dismissive disbelievers enjoy the bounties for a long time,",
  26206:
      "Then the punishment they were promised came to them after that period of enjoyment,\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Objections can be raised against the idolaters with the confessions of the moderate from among the people of the book that the Qur’an is from Allah.\n2. There is no benefit in bringing faith after seeing the destructive punishment.\n3. Whatever bounties of the world the disbelievers have are causes of them gradually falling into destruction, not hospitality.",
  26207:
      "What benefit would that worldly enjoyment be? Those bounties would surely have ended and would not be of any use.",
  26208:
      "We have not destroyed any nation except after they have been warned by sending messengers and revealing books to them.",
  26209:
      "Which served as admonition and warnings for them. We were not oppressive by punishing them after sending them Messengers and Books as excuses for them.",
  26210:
      "The devils did not come down with this Quran upon the heart of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم;",
  26211:
      "It is not permissible that they come down with it onto his heart. They are not even capable of doing that.",
  26212:
      "They cannot do so because they have been barred from its area in the heavens, so how would they reach it to bring it down?",
  26213:
      "So do not worship any deity with Allah, making it a partner to Him, lest you become amongst those who shall be punished.",
  26214:
      "And warn, O Messenger, your closest relatives, then those after them, so Allah does not punish them due to them remaining upon polytheism.",
  26215:
      "And be lenient, in action and speech, to those believers who follow you, out of mercy and gentleness.",
  26216:
      "If they disobey you and reject your commandments to single out Allah in worship and obey Him, then say to them: I am innocent of the polytheism and sins you commit.",
  26217:
      "And rely on the Almighty for all your affairs; the One who takes retribution from His enemies and is merciful to those who repent from amongst them.",
  26218:
      "The Exalted and Transcendent one, who sees you when you stand for prayer.",
  26219:
      "And sees you changing postures with those who pray. Nothing of what you, or other than you do, is hidden from Him.",
  26220:
      "Indeed, He is the All-Hearing who hears your recitation of the Quran and your supplications in your prayer, Omniscient of your intentions.",
  26221:
      "When they alleged that the devils came down with the Quran and that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was a poet, Allah responded to their false claim, stating: \n Shall I inform you of whom the devils reveal to? Those whom you claimed brought down the Quran.",
  26222:
      "They reveal to every perpetual liar and sinner amongst the fortune-tellers.",
  26223:
      "The devils eavesdrop on the exalted assembly of angels and then convey that information to their associates amongst fortune-tellers. The majority of fortune-tellers are liars; if they are truthful in one statement, they mix it with a hundred lies.",
  26224:
      "And as for the poets that you claim Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is from, those who are astray from the path of guidance and steadfastness follow them and relate their poetry.",
  26225:
      "Do you not see, O Messenger, that one of the manifestations of their errors is that they wander around, lost in every valley? At times engaged in praise, at others in criticism, and other than that!",
  26226: "And they indeed lie, saying they did something while they did not.",
  26227:
      "Except for poets who have faith, perform righteous deeds, abundantly remember Allah, and take retribution from Allah's enemies after they have been oppressed by them, like Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). Those who committed oppression by ascribing partners to Allah and showing hostility to His slaves will soon know which place they will return to; they will return to a tremendous standing and meticulous accounting.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Affirmation of justice for Allah and negating oppression from Him.\n2. Declaration of the Qur’an being free of any satans having approached it.\n3. The importance of gentleness and friendliness for the callers towards Allah.\n4. Good poetry is good, while repulsive poetry is repulsive.",
  27000:
      "The Ant (Surah An-Naml)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nBestowing the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم with the blessing of the Quran, expressing gratitude for it, and perseverance in conveying its message.\n•    Explanation:",
  27001:
      "Tā Sīn – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  27002:
      "These verses guide to the truth and give glad tidings to those who have faith in Allah and His Messengers.",
  27003:
      "Those who perform the prayer in its most complete manner, give the Zakat of their wealth to be spent on its rightful recipients and have a firm conviction of the reward and punishment in the Afterlife.",
  27004:
      "Indeed, the disbelievers who do not have faith in the Afterlife and the reward and punishment therein - We beautified their evil deeds for them, so they continued doing them. Thus, they are confused and unable to find the correct or sound path.",
  27005:
      "People with these descriptions will suffer in the worldly life through trials and humiliation. And in the Hereafter, they will be the greatest losers, losing themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection by entering and remaining in the Fire forever.",
  27006:
      "And you, O Messenger, receive this Quran, sent down to you from One who is Wise in His creation, His decree, and His legislation. He is all-Knowing; nothing of the interests of His slaves is hidden from Him.",
  27007:
      "Mention, O Messenger, when Moses said to his family: I have seen a fire. I shall bring information from the person who lit it to show us the way. Or bring a flame from it so you may light a fire and keep warm.",
  27008:
      "When he reached the place where he saw the Fire, Allah called unto him that the one in the Fire and the angels surrounding it are blessed. Praised is the Lord of creation from the unbefitting attributes the misguided ascribe to him.",
  27009:
      "Allah said to him: O Moses, it is I, Allah, the Mighty who cannot be overpowered, the Wise in My creation, decree, and legislation.",
  27010:
      "And throw down your staff. Moses obeyed. Then, when Moses saw it moving and shaking like a snake, he fled and did not return. So Allah said to him: Do not be afraid of it. For indeed, the Messengers do not fear snakes or anything else in my presence.",
  27011:
      "However, whoever wrongs himself by sinning then repents; I am Forgiving and Merciful to him.",
  27012:
      "And put your hand in the opening under the neck of your garment; it will emerge white like snow without being due to vitiligo, as one of nine signs which testify to your truthfulness. Along with the hand, they are the staff, famine, deficiency of fruit, floods, locusts, lice, frogs, and blood. [Signs] for Pharaoh and his people, they were indeed a people outside the fold of obedience of Allah due to disbelieving in him.",
  27013:
      "So when Our clear and apparent signs with which We aided Moses reached them, they said: What Moses has brought is clear sorcery.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an is guidance and glad tidings for the believers.\n2. Disbelief in Allah is a means of following false actions and statements, bewilderment and confusion.\n3. Allah granted security and protected His Messengers from all evil.",
  27014:
      "They disbelieved in these clear miracles and did not accept them despite being convinced they were from Allah. This is due to their oppression and their arrogance from accepting the truth. So contemplate, O Messenger, the outcome of those who cause corruption on Earth with their disbelief and disobedience; We have indeed destroyed and eradicated all of them.",
  27015:
      "I granted David and his son Solomon knowledge, part of which was the language of birds. David and Solomon said, in gratitude to Allah: All praise is for Allah who has given us virtue over many of His believing slaves through prophethood and subjugation of the Jinn.",
  27016:
      "And Solomon inherited prophethood, knowledge, and dominion from his father. Citing Allah's favor upon him and his father, he said: O people, Allah has taught us the language of birds and given us everything He gave prophets and kings. What He has given us is indeed a clear and apparent favor.",
  27017:
      "And Solomon's troops of men, Jinn, and birds were gathered for him and led orderly.",
  27018:
      "They continued to be led until they came to the valley of ants (a place in the Levant); an ant said: O ants, get into your homes so that Solomon and his armies do not destroy you, being unaware of your presence. If they were aware, they would not trample you.",
  27019:
      "When Solomon heard it, he smiled at its statement and called unto his Lord: O Lord, enable and inspire me to be grateful for Your favor which You have bestowed upon me and My parents, and allow me to practice righteous deeds which please you, and allow me to be amongst Your righteous slaves.",
  27020:
      "And Solomon inspected the birds but did not see the hoopoe, so he said: Why do I not see the hoopoe? Is there something preventing me from seeing it, or is it absent?",
  27021:
      "When its absence became clear to him, he said: I shall punish it severely or slaughter it as a punishment for its absence unless it brings clear proof for its excuse.",
  27022:
      "The hoopoe remained absent for a short period of time. When it arrived, it said to Solomon (peace be upon him): I discovered something that you are unaware of, and I have brought truthful news about the people of Sheba in which there is no doubt.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride is a hindrance to being guided to the truth.\n2. Being grateful for favours is the etiquette of the prophets and righteous with their Lord.\n3. Advising the people with what will prevent them from destruction is the way of intelligent individuals.\n4. One should make excuses for righteous people in their absence.\n5. Smiling is the laughing of dignified people.\n6. Citizens are managed by implementing punishment on those who deserve it and accepting the excuses of those who have a valid excuse.\n7. Sometimes juniors have knowledge which seniors do not.",
  27023:
      "Indeed, I found [there] a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things and has a great throne.",
  27024:
      "I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah, the Exalted. The Devil made their polytheism and sins seem pleasing to them and averted them from the correct path; thus, they are not guided to it.",
  27025:
      "The Devil has beautified their polytheism and sins for them so that they do not prostrate to Allah alone, the One who brings the rain which He has hidden in the skies and the plants on the Earth. He knows the actions you conceal as well as those you reveal. None of it is hidden from Him.",
  27026:
      "Allah, no deity is worthy of worship other than Him, Lord of the magnificent Throne.",
  27027:
      "Solomon (peace be upon him) said to the hoopoe: I shall see whether you are truthful in what you claim or a liar.",
  27028:
      "So Solomon wrote a letter, gave it to the hoopoe, and said: Take this letter of mine and give it to the people of Sheba. Then, remain close by so you can hear what they say regarding it.",
  27029:
      "The queen received the letter and said: O noble ones, a noble and magnificent letter has been given to me.",
  27030:
      "The content of this letter sent by Solomon begins with: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.",
  27031:
      "Do not be arrogant; come to me in submission to the monotheism I call to, and forsake the polytheism you are upon of worshiping the sun alongside Him.",
  27032:
      "The queen said to the nobles and leaders: Advise me regarding the right decision in this affair. I do not make any decisions in a matter until you come and tell me your opinions regarding it.",
  27033:
      "The nobles of her people said: We are mighty and forceful at war, but the decision is yours. So think about what you want to do, and we will be able to execute it.",
  27034:
      "The queen said: When kings attack a city, they destroy it by killing, seizing, and looting. They turn its leaders and nobles into the lowly after having honor and security. This is what kings always do when they conquer a city to sow awe and fear in the hearts of the masses.",
  27035:
      "I am sending a gift to the sender of the letter and his people, and I shall see what the messengers bring after sending this gift.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The hoopoe’s criticism of the people of Sheba for their idolatry and disbelief is a proof that faith is natural amongst the creation.\n2. It is necessary to investigate the one being accused and to verify his proofs.\n3. It is permissible to investigate the affairs of the enemies.\n4. Part of the etiquette of letters is to begin them with the name of Allah.\n5. Expressing the honour of a believer in the presence of the people of falsehood is a desired matter.",
  27036:
      "So when her messenger and his aides came carrying the gift to Solomon, he criticized them for sending the present, saying: Are you giving me wealth to turn me away from you? The prophethood, kingdom, and wealth Allah has given me is better than what He has given you. Rather, it is you who rejoices over the worldly riches gifted to you.",
  27037:
      "Solomon (peace be upon him) said to her messenger: Return to them with the present you brought, for we will go to her and her people with armies they will not have the power to face. We will remove them from Sheba disgracefully after being honorable if they do not come to me obediently.",
  27038:
      "Solomon (peace be upon him) addressed the people of his kingdom; Which of you will bring me her royal throne before they come to me obediently?",
  27039:
      "A rebellious Jinn replied: I will bring you her throne before you leave this gathering of yours. I have the strength to carry it and can be trusted with its contents; I will not take anything from it.",
  27040:
      "A righteous and knowledgeable man who had knowledge of the scripture, of which was Allah's greatest name, which He responds to when called with, said in the presence of Solomon: I will bring her throne to you in the blink of an eye, by praying to Allah to bring it. So he prayed, and Allah responded to his prayer. When Solomon saw her throne before him, he said: This is from my Lord, the Exalted's, favor upon me, to test whether I am grateful for his favors or not? Whoever is grateful to Allah, the benefit of his gratefulness will only return to him, for Allah is self-sufficient, in need of nothing. The gratefulness of His slaves does not increase Him in anything. And whoever doesn't show gratitude and denies Allah's favors, my Lord is self-sufficient and not in need of gratitude. [He is] Generous, and His generosity grants blessings to those who deny them.",
  27041:
      "Solomon (peace be upon him) said: Change her royal throne from its original form. We shall see if she is guided to recognize it as her throne or if she will be from those who are not guided to recognize their own things.",
  27042:
      "So when the queen of Sheba came to Solomon, as a test, it was said to her; Does this resemble your throne? She answered accordingly; It is as if it is [my throne]. Solomon said; Allah granted us knowledge before her because of His ability to do such things, and we submitted to Allah's order and obeyed Him.",
  27043:
      "And worshiping others besides Allah turned her away from the Oneness of Allah, following and blindly imitating her people. Indeed, she was from a people who disbelieved in Allah, so she was a disbeliever like them.",
  27044:
      "It was said to her: Enter the palace. It was like a plane surface. When she saw it, she thought it was water, so she uncovered her shins to walk through it. Solomon (peace be upon him) said: It is a palace made of smooth glass. He called her to Islam, and she accepted, saying: O Lord, I wronged myself by worshipping others besides You along with You, and I have submitted with Solomon to Allah, Lord of all created things.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The honour of faith protects a believer from being affected by the short-term riches of this world.\n2. Being happy with materialistic things and inclining towards them is a quality of the disbelievers.\n3. Supernatural acts are miracles for the pious and deception for the transgressors.\n4. A believer’s has an awakened realisation of Allah’s favors.\n5. Testing the intelligence of the opponent is so that he can be dealt with appropriately.\n6. Showing one’s superiority over the opponent is to affect him.",
  27045:
      "And we sent to Thamūd, their brother in lineage, Saleh (peace be upon him), telling them to worship Allah alone. But they split into two groups after he called them; one group was believers, and the other group was disbelievers arguing over who was on the truth.",
  27046:
      "Saleh (peace be upon him) said: Why do you seek to hasten the punishment before seeking Allah's mercy? Why do you not seek Allah's forgiveness for your sins in the hope that He will forgive you?",
  27047:
      "His people said to him, stubbornly rejecting the truth: We consider you and the believers with you a bad omen. Saleh (peace be upon him) said: The difficulties which have afflicted you are known to Allah; nothing of it is hidden from Him. Rather, you are a people being tested with the good you are granted and the bad that afflicts you.",
  27048:
      "There were nine men in the city of Hijr who caused corruption on Earth through disbelief and sin, and they would not cause rectification in it through faith and righteous actions.",
  27049:
      "They said to one another: Each one of you should swear by Allah that we will go to him and the believers with him at night, then we will kill them and then say to the one responsible for avenging his blood: 'We were not present at the murder of Saleh or the murder of his followers, and we are truthful in what we are saying.'",
  27050:
      "And they secretly plotted to destroy Saleh and his followers from the believers. We also plotted to support and save him from their scheme and destroy the disbelievers from his people while they were unaware.",
  27051:
      "So contemplate O Messenger, the result of their schemes. The result was that We uprooted them with Our punishment, so they were all destroyed.",
  27052:
      "So these are their homes whose walls have fallen on their roofs and remained empty of inhabitants due to their wrongdoing. Indeed, the punishment that has afflicted them due to their wrongdoing is a lesson for people who have knowledge; it is the believers who learn from the signs.",
  27053:
      "And We saved the believers from the people of Saleh (peace be upon him). They used to fear Allah by complying with His orders and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  27054:
      "And mention Lot, O Messenger, when he reprimanded and criticized his people, saying: Do you openly engage in the indecent act of sodomy in your gatherings while watching one another?",
  27055:
      "Do you approach men lustfully instead of women? You do not intend chastity or children, only to fulfill your animalistic lust? Rather, you are ignorant of your obligations of faith, purity, and refraining from sin.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Seeking forgiveness from sins is a means of Allah’s mercy.\n2. Taking bad omen from people and things is not from the qualities of the believers.\n3. The outcome of uniting upon evil and scheming against the people of truth is bad.\n4. Oppression is a cause of punishment descending on earth.\n5. Faith and piety are the means to salvation from Allah’s punishment.\n6. Openly committing evil is worse than doing it secretly.\n7. To condemn the people of vice and transgression is necessary.",
  27056:
      "His people had no answer except: Expel Lot's family from your village. They are a people who purify themselves from dirt and filth. They said this to mock Lot's family, who did not participate in the indecent act they would commit. Instead, they forbade them from it.",
  27057:
      "So, we saved him and his family, all except his wife. We ruled that she should remain to be tormented along with those who were destroyed.",
  27058:
      "We sent down a rain of stones from the sky upon them. It was a terrible and devastating rain for the ones warned of the torment but did not respond.",
  27059:
      "Say, O Messenger: All praise is for Allah for His favors and for protecting the Prophet's صلى الله عليه وسلم companions from His torment that He inflicted upon the people of Lot and Saleh. Who is better? Allah, who is worthy of worship and in His Hand is the dominion of everything, or the idols that the polytheists worship, which cannot bring about any benefit or harm!?",
  27060:
      "Is He [not better] Who created the skies and the earth from nothing, sent you, O people, rainwater from the sky, and caused beautiful gardens to grow while you cannot even make the trees grow in those gardens, but Allah can? Does any false idol do this alongside Allah?! No, but they have deviated from the truth by wrongfully making the Creator equal to the creation.",
  27061:
      "Is He [not better] Who made the Earth firm and stable, not being shaken, and made rivers flow through it, placed solid mountains on it, and made a barrier between the two oceans (salty and fresh), preventing the saltwater from mixing with and spoiling the freshwater and making it undrinkable. Did any of these false idols do this alongside Allah? Instead, most of them do not know. They would not have made any of the creations a partner besides Allah if they knew.",
  27062:
      "Is He [not better] who answers who calls upon Him while in hardship, relieves people from sickness, poverty, and other [troubles], and makes you successors in the Earth succeeding one another, generation after generation? Does any false idol do this alongside Allah?! How little do you take heed and consider!",
  27063:
      "Is He [not better] Who guides you through the darkness of the land and the sea using landmarks and stars that He has placed for you and sends winds as a sign of the coming rain as His mercy on His slaves? Does any false idol do this alongside Allah?! Allah is sanctified and far removed from the creatures they worship alongside Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The people of falsehood take refuge in violence when they are cornered with proofs.\n2. The relationship of marriage without faith will not benefit in the afterlife.\n3. The belief in Allah’s Oneness is made firm through reminding of Allah’s favours.\n4. Being distressed is one of the means of acceptance of prayers.",
  27064:
      "Is He [not better] Who begins creation in the womb stage by stage, then resurrects it after causing it to die, and provides for you by sending down rain from the sky and causing crops to grow from the earth? Does any false idol do this alongside Allah?! Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Bring your evidence for the idolatry that you do if you are honest in your claim about being upon the truth.",
  27065:
      "Say, O Messenger: No one in the heavens and on the Earth knows the unseen, but Allah alone is the One who knows that. Similarly, no one in the heavens and on the Earth knows when everyone will be resurrected for recompense, except Allah.",
  27066:
      "Are they seeking knowledge of the Afterlife to be sure about it? No, instead, they are doubtful and confused about it. Moreover, they do not give it any attention.",
  27067:
      "Those who disbelieve deplore: When we die and turn to dust, can we be brought back to life?",
  27068:
      "Verily, we have been promised, as had our fathers before us, that we will all be resurrected. But we have yet to see this promise fulfilled. It is but lies that those before us collected in their books.",
  27069:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who deny the resurrection: Travel in any direction throughout the Earth and think about how those criminals who rejected the resurrection ended up. Verily, we destroyed them for their rejection.",
  27070:
      "Do not be saddened by the polytheists turning away from your call, and do not let their plots make you anxious, as Allah will aid you against them.",
  27071:
      "The disbelievers from among your people who reject the resurrection ask: If your claims about the punishment you and the believers promise us are truthful, when will it happen?",
  27072:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: Maybe some of the torment that you want to come sooner has already come close to you.",
  27073:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, is generous to the people by not hastening to punish them while they commit disbelief and sin. But most people do not thank Allah for the favors He gives them.",
  27074:
      "Indeed, your Lord knows what His slaves keep hidden in their hearts and what they reveal. Nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for that.",
  27075:
      "There is nothing from the unseen in the skies, nor the Earth, except that it is in a clear book, the Preserved Tablet.",
  27076:
      "Indeed, this Quran revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم tells the Israelites most of what they differ about and exposes their deviations.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The knowledge of the Ghaib is specifically for Allah. Making a claim to it is disbelief.\n2. Taking heed from the previous nations, with respect to their outcome and conditions, is the way to salvation.\n3. The Messenger (peace be upon him) was consoled and made firm in the face of the scheming of the idolaters.\n4. Allah’s knowledge encompasses the actions of His servants.\n5. The Qur’an corrects the deviances of the Israelites and their tampering of their books.",
  27077:
      "Indeed, it (the Quran) is guidance and mercy to the believers who practice what is in it.",
  27078:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, will judge between the people; believers and disbelievers; on the Day of Resurrection, according to His just law. He will have mercy on the believer and torment the disbeliever. He is the Most-Mighty who retaliates against His enemies, and no one can overpower Him. He is the Omniscient who does not confuse the truthful with the liar.",
  27079:
      "So, trust in Allah and rely on Him in all your matters. Indeed, you are upon clear truth.",
  27080:
      "O Messenger, you cannot make the dead whose hearts have died to their disbelief in Allah hear, nor can you make those who have lost their hearing hear what you are calling them towards when they return turning away from you.",
  27081:
      "And you are not one to guide those whose eyes are blind to the truth, so do not grieve over them and tire yourself. Only those who believe in our verses will listen to your call because they submit to the orders of Allah.",
  27082:
      "When the final hour is near, and only the evilest people remain, the torment will become binding and be established upon them due to their persisting in disbelief and sin. Then, We will bring out to them one of the major signs of the hour; a creature from the Earth that will tell them in words that they understand that the people used to disbelieve in what was revealed to Our Prophet.",
  27083:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the day when we will gather a group of leaders from each nation that used to reject Our signs. The first to the last of them will be answerable, and then they will be led to the reckoning.",
  27084:
      "They will continue to be led until they arrive at the place of their reckoning. Allah will rebuke them, saying: Did you disbelieve in My signs that show that I am One and contain my legislation? You had no knowledge to say they were false, and so had no right to reject them! What were you doing, believing, or rejecting?",
  27085:
      "They will be tormented due to their wrongdoings of disbelieving in Allah and rejecting His signs. So, they will not speak to defend themselves because they will be unable to, and their arguments are false.",
  27086:
      "When they rejected the concept of resurrection, Allah drew their attention to the states that demonstrate it in their own lives: their sleeping, which resembles death, and their waking up, which resembles resurrection: \n Do those who reject the resurrection not see that We made the night for them to rest by sleeping and the day bright so that they can see and hasten to do their work? Indeed, that recurring death and resurrection contain clear signs for those who believe.",
  27087:
      "Remember, O Messenger, there will be a day when the horn will be blown a second time by the angel entrusted with it, and everyone in the heavens and the Earth will be terrified except those who Allah has exempted as a favor from Him. All Allah's creation will come to Him obedient and humble on that day.",
  27088:
      "On that day, although you may consider the mountains still and motionless, they will actually move swiftly like clouds. This is the doing of Allah. He is the One who will move them. He is aware of what you do, nothing from your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of putting one’s trust in Allah.\n2. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was commended by stating he was on the clear truth.\n3. Placing guidance in the hearts is in Allah’s hands alone, not in the hands of the Messenger (peace be upon him).\n4. Sleep is a sign and reminder for death and the awakening from sleep is a sign and reminder for the resurrection.",
  27089:
      "Whoever comes on the Day of Resurrection with faith and righteous deeds will enter paradise. They will be safe from the horrors of the Day of Resurrection due to Allah protecting them.",
  27090:
      "But whoever comes with disbelief and sins will be flung face-first into the Fire. They will be rebuked and humiliated by being told: Are you not being recompensed only for the disbelief and sins you used to commit in the worldly life?",
  27091:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: I have only been ordered to worship the Lord of Mecca, the city He has sanctified; no blood should be shed there, nobody should be oppressed there, none of its game should be hunted, and none of its trees should be cut down. Everything belongs to Him, the Exalted. I have also been ordered to be from those who submit to Allah and obey Him.",
  27092:
      "I have been ordered to recite the Quran to the people. Whoever is guided by it and implements what is in it, then his guidance will benefit him. But whoever is misguided, deviates from what is in it, rejects it, and does not implement it, then say: I am only one of the warners warning you about Allah's torment, and your guidance is not in my hands.",
  27093:
      "Say, O Messenger, all praise is due to Allah for His innumerable blessings. Allah will show you His signs in yourselves, the sky, the Earth, and your sustenance. Your recognition of them will guide you to the truth and clarify falsehood to you. Your Lord is not unaware of your actions. He sees them all, none of them are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  28000:
      "The Stories (Surah Al-Qasas)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating that Allah's established practice is to empower the oppressed believers and destroy the arrogant tyrants.\n•    Explanation:",
  28001:
      "Tā Sīn Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  28002: "These are the verses of the clear Quran.",
  28003:
      "We will read the story of Moses and Pharoah truthfully to you. The story that the believers do not doubt because they are the ones who benefit from what is in it.",
  28004:
      "Indeed, Pharoah was a tyrannical oppressor in the land of Egypt. He divided its people into groups, oppressing one of them, the Israelites, by killing their male children and enslaving their females to humiliate them. He used to corrupt the Earth with oppression, tyranny, and arrogance.",
  28005:
      "And I wanted to bestow a favor upon the Israelites who had been oppressed by the Pharaoh in Egypt, by destroying their enemy, liberating them from the oppression, making them leaders, to be followed by those who seek the truth and making them inheritors of Pharaoh's kingdom in Egypt after I drowned him and his armies.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Faith and good deeds are the means to achieving salvation from the horrors of the Day of Judgement.\n2. Disbelief and sins lead to entry into hellfire.\n3. It is forbidden to kill, oppress and hunt in the Haram sanctuary.\n4. Destruction is the ultimate outcome of the arrogant tyrants.\n5. Help of Allah and authority are the ultimate outcomes of the believers.",
  28006:
      "We wanted to empower them in the land by making them rule it, thereby demonstrating to Pharoah, his chief advisor Haman, and their army that enforced their rule what they feared most, which was losing power at the hands of one of the male offspring from the Israelites.",
  28007:
      "Upon mentioning the fate of Pharaoh's kingdom and how Moses and his people would be honored, Allah recalls the upbringing of Moses as Allah's messenger, stating: \n We inspired Moses' (peace be upon him) mother: Suckle him until you fear that Pharoah and his people will kill him, then place him in a basket and cast it into the Nile. Do not be afraid of him drowning or being harmed by Pharoah, and do not grieve over his separation from you. We will return him to you alive and make him one of Allah's messengers sent to His creation.",
  28008:
      "So, she did as she had been inspired and placed him in a basket, casting him into the river. Then, Pharoah's family discovered him. Thus Allah's will was realized by Moses becoming Pharoah's enemy stripping him of his kingdom and bringing about his people's grief. Indeed, Pharoah, his minister Haman, and their aides used to sin by disbelieving, oppressing, and causing corruption in the land.",
  28009:
      "When Pharoah wanted to kill Moses, Pharoah's wife said to him: This boy is a source of joy for both of us, so do not kill him. Maybe, he could serve us, or we could adopt him as our son. But they did not know what would happen to their kingdom due to him.",
  28010:
      "The heart of Moses' (peace be upon him) mother did not care about anything from the affairs of this world except Moses. She could hardly maintain her patience. To the point where her fierce attachment to him almost led her to reveal that he was her son, but we strengthened her heart and enabled her to persevere as a believer who relies on her Lord and is patient with His decrees.",
  28011:
      "And after she had cast him into the sea, Moses's mother said to his sister, \"Follow him so that you know what happens to him\", and so she observed him from a distance so that she was not implicated. Pharaoh and his people were not aware that she was his sister and that she was keeping an eye on him.",
  28012:
      "By the decree of Allah, Moses refused to breastfeed from the women. When his sister saw their eagerness to feed him, she said to them, \"Shall I tell you of a household who shall feed him and look after him, who will also treat him with goodwill?\"",
  28013:
      "We returned Moses to his mother so that her eyes, which had longed for him, could become joyful and at rest. This was to prevent her from being grieved by separation from him and to make her realize that Allah's promise to return him to her was undoubtedly true. However, most people were unaware of this promise, and no one knew she was his mother.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah decrees for His pious servants things which save them from the plots of their enemies.\n2. The plot of an oppressor leads to his own destruction.\n3. The strength of the affection of mothers towards their children is great.\n4. Taking precaution from enemies by hiding objectives and connections.\n5. Permissibility of using legal strategies to save oneself from the oppression of the oppressor.\n6. The promise of Allah will be fulfilled inevitably.",
  28014:
      "Upon mentioning Moses's childhood, Allah recalls the days of his youth, stating: \n When he grew up and reached his prime strength, We granted him understanding and knowledge of the Israelites' religion before he was sent as a prophet. Just as Moses was rewarded for his obedience, We reward all those who do good in every time and place.",
  28015:
      "Moses entered the city when the people were resting in their homes and found two men arguing and fighting. One was an Israelite from Moses' people, and the other was a Copt from the people of Pharaoh, who were Moses' enemies. The one from his people, the Israelite, asked Moses to help him against the one from his enemies, the Copt. Then, Moses punched the Copt so hard that he killed him. Moses then said: This is from the temptation and deception of the Devil. He is a clear enemy who misguides those who follow him. Whatever happened was due to the Devil's enmity and misguidance, and he intended to misguide me.",
  28016:
      "Knowing what he had done, Moses called upon His lord and said: O my Lord, I have wronged myself by killing this Copt, so forgive me for my sin. Allah showed us that He forgave Moses. Indeed, He forgives His slaves who repent and is merciful towards them.",
  28017:
      "Then, [In this ayah] Allah continues to inform us about Moses' supplication. Moses said: O my Lord, I will not support the criminals in their crimes because You have blessed me with strength, wisdom, and knowledge.",
  28018:
      "After the killing of the Copt occurred, Moses arose the following day in the city, afraid of what might happen. Suddenly, the Israelite who requested his aid and support against his Coptic enemy the day before sought his help against another Copt. Moses told him: You are a clear misguider and troublemaker.",
  28019:
      "When Moses (peace be upon him) wanted to attack his and the Israelite's enemy, the Copt, the Israelite thought he intended to attack him because he heard him say: Indeed, you are a clear troublemaker. So, he said to Moses: Do you want to kill me like you killed someone yesterday? You just want to be a tyrant in the land, killing and oppressing people, and you do not wish to reconcile people in dispute.",
  28020:
      "Once word got out, a man rushed over to Moses from the other end of the city, fearing that Moses would be persecuted. He said: O Moses, the leaders of Pharoah's people are discussing killing you, so escape the city. I offer you sincere advice and do not want them to catch and kill you.",
  28021:
      "So Moses accepted the man's advice and fled the country, fearing what may happen to him. He called upon his Lord, saying: O my Lord, save me from the oppressive nation so they cannot harm me.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Acknowledging one’s sin is from the etiquettes of beseeching Allah.\n2. Praiseworthy gratitude is the gratitude that spurs a servant into obeying his Lord and distancing himself from His disobedience.\n3. The importance of hastening towards offering advice, especially if it means saving a believer from destruction.\n4. The obligation of adopting means to safety and seeking refuge in Allah through beseeching Him.",
  28022:
      "As he started heading towards Midian, he said: I hope my Lord will guide me to the best route so I will not stray from it.",
  28023:
      "When he reached the watering hole of Midian, he found a gathering of people watering their animals. Away from them, two women kept their sheep back from the water until the rest of the people had finished. Moses (peace be upon him) asked them: Why do you not water [your sheep] with everyone else? They replied: We usually wait to give them water until after the herdsmen leave so that we do not mix with them. Also, our father is an elderly man who cannot do it himself, so we must water them.",
  28024:
      "So, he was kind to them and watered their sheep himself. Then, he went to some shade to rest and called upon His Lord, alluding to what he needed saying: O my Lord, whatever good you choose to send to me, that is what I need.",
  28025:
      "When they went back, they informed their father of Moses, so he sent one of them to him, inviting him. She approached him, walking modestly, saying, \"Indeed, my father is inviting you to meet him, intending to reward you for watering our livestock for us.\" When Moses came to their father and told him of his situation, he reassuringly told him, \"Do not fear, for you have escaped from an oppressive nation: Pharaoh and his crowd. They have no authority over Midian, so they will not be able to harm you.\"",
  28026:
      "One of his daughters said: O father, hire him to shepherd our sheep as he deserves that because he is both strong and trustworthy. His strength means he can fulfill his duties, and his trustworthiness means he will look after what he is entrusted with.",
  28027:
      "Their father addressed Moses, saying: I would like to marry one of these two daughters of mine to you, and her dowry will be for you to shepherd our flock for eight years. If you wish, you can extend the period to ten years as a favor from yourself, as the agreement is only for eight years. Whatever is over that is optional. I do not want to obligate something that would put you in hardship. You will find me, God willing, from the righteous people who fulfill their contracts and do not break them.",
  28028:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: What we have agreed is confirmed. Whichever duration I work for you, eight or ten years, I will have fulfilled whatever is upon me, so do not ask for more. Allah witnesses what we have agreed upon and watches over it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Seeking refuge with Allah is the path to salvation in the world and afterlife.\n2. The modesty of a Muslim woman leads to her nobility and elevated rank.\n3. Their is no sin in the conversing of two unrelated people of the opposite gender as long as their is a need and the conversation would not arise suspicion.\n4. The permissibility of a woman working if she is compelled to due to there being no one providing for her, provided there is no intermingling with males.\n5. Consulting daughters for their opinions and relying on them if their opinions are valid, is praiseworthy.\n6. Strength and trustworthiness are two qualities found within a successful employee.\n7. One should endeavour to remain chaste.\n8. It is permissible for dowry to be a service, as opposed to a tangible item.",
  28029:
      "When Moses completed the (longer) ten-year term and took his family from Midian to Egypt, he saw a fire at the side of Mount Tur. He told his family: Stay here. I have seen a fire. I could get news from there or bring embers to start your fire and ward off the cold.",
  28030:
      "When Moses reached the fire he had seen, his Lord, Exalted and Most High, called out to him from the right side of the valley, at the spot He blessed by the tree to speak to him: O Moses, indeed I am Allah, the Lord of all creation.",
  28031:
      "[Allah said]: Throw down your staff. So, Moses did as he was commanded. Then, when he saw it move and slither like a snake, he turned and fled, frightened. He did not return until His Lord called out: O Moses, come back and do not be afraid of it. You are from those who are safe from it and the other things you may fear.",
  28032:
      "Put your right hand into your shirt opening below the collar, and it will come out white (but not like vitiligo). So Moses did that, and his hand came out white as snow. [Allah said]: Draw your hand close to you to settle your fear. So Moses did so, and he was no longer afraid. These two things mentioned, the staff and hand, are proofs sent from your Lord to Pharoah and the leaders of his nation. They were a nation that would rebel against the obedience of Allah by disbelieving and committing sins.",
  28033:
      "Moses pleaded to his Lord: I killed one of them before, so I am afraid they will kill me if I come to them conveying what you sent me with.",
  28034:
      "My brother Aaron speaks clearer than I do, so send him with me as assistance to agree with what I say should Pharoah and his nation not believe me. I fear they might reject me as the previous nations who had messengers sent to them used to do.",
  28035:
      "Allah answered Moses' supplication: We will strengthen you, O Moses, by sending your brother as an aide and messenger. We will give you proof and support so the evil you detest will not reach you. Due to the signs we sent you, you and whoever follows you will be victorious believers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Fulfilling promises and agreements are qualities of the believers.\n2. Allah spoke to Moses directly.\n3. A caller to Allah sometimes needs people who support him.\n4. Eloquence is important for those who invite to Allah.\n5. The truth always prevailing is a divine custom.",
  28036:
      "When Moses (peace be upon him) brought Our clear signs to them, they said: This is nothing but lies that Moses has fabricated. We never heard of anything like this from our forefathers.",
  28037:
      "Moses told Pharoah: My Lord knows who is the truthful one who has brought guidance from Him (may He be Exalted) and knows who will have a praiseworthy end in the hereafter. The wrongdoers will never reach their goal, nor will they be saved from what they fear.",
  28038:
      "Pharaoh said to the leaders of his nation: O chiefs, I do not know of you worshipping other than me. O Haman, fire the clay [bricks] until they become set. Then, build a towering building for me to look at who Moses worships and find out about Him. However, I think that Moses' claim that he has been sent from Allah to me and my nation is a lie.",
  28039:
      "Pharaoh and his forces became so arrogant and sought to dominate the land of Egypt without any right. They denied the resurrection and thought they would not return to Us on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and punishment.",
  28040:
      "We seized him and his soldiers and flung them into the sea to drown them to death. O Messenger, reflect on the fate of the wrongdoers and their ultimate end, for indeed, it was only destruction.",
  28041:
      "We made them an example for all the tyrants and deviants that call to the Fire by spreading disbelief and misguidance. On the Day of Resurrection, no one will help and rescue them from the torment. Instead, the torment will be multiplied due to them establishing evil ways and calling to misguidance. They will be punished for their actions and the actions of those that followed them.",
  28042:
      "We piled upon them increasing punishment of humiliation and exclusion from the mercy of Allah in this life. They will be vilified and far from Allah's mercy on the day of resurrection.",
  28043:
      "We sent Our messengers to the previous nations, but they rejected them, so we destroyed them. Afterward, We gave Moses the Torah. It contains what causes the people to see what benefits them so they can implement it and what harms them so they can abandon it. It also guides them to goodness and mercy from the good found in this world and the next so that they might remember Allah's favors upon them, thank Him for that and believe in Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Tyrants and oppressors have a habit of rejecting the truth with specious arguments.\n2. Oppression is a means to loss.\n3. Arrogance prevents following the truth.\n4. Ostentatious people suffering a bad outcome is from the customs of the Lord of the worlds.\n5. Falsehood has its leaders, callers, different guises and manifestations.",
  28044:
      "O Messenger, you were not there at the mountain's western side (relative to Moses) when We concluded the matter by sending Moses to Pharaoh and his chiefs. Likewise, you were not there to witness the event and tell it to the people. Whatever you tell them is a revelation that Allah revealed to you.",
  28045:
      "We made nations and peoples after Moses. Then, so much time passed that they forgot Allah's covenants. You did not stay with the people of Midian, reciting our verses to them. But, We sent you as Our messenger and revealed the story of Moses and his stay in Midian to you, which you informed the people about.",
  28046:
      "When we called out to Moses and revealed what we revealed, you were not there at the side of Mount Tur so that you may tell the people about it. But we sent you as a mercy to the people from your Lord and revealed that incident to you so you could warn a nation that had not been warned before by any messenger. We did this so that they might take heed and believe in what you have brought to them from Allah; may He be Exalted.",
  28047:
      "If they had been punished for their disbelief and sins, they would have argued that a messenger was not sent to them, saying: Why did You not send us a messenger so we could follow Your verses and implement them? Then, we would have been from the believers who fulfill their Lord's commands. If it were not for that, We would have hastened their punishment. Instead, We delayed it so We could be excused by sending a messenger to them.",
  28048:
      "Then, when Muhammad brought the message from his Lord to the Quraysh, the Jews asked about him. So the Quraysh showed them this evidence, and they replied: Has Muhammad not been given signs that show he has been sent from his Lord like Moses had, such as the hand and the staff? Say, O Messenger, in refutation of them: Did the Jews not disbelieve in what Moses was given before? Did they not say that the Quran and Torah are magic supporting each other and that they disbelieve in both the Quran and the Torah?!",
  28049:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: If you are honest in your claim that the Quran and Torah are magic, then bring a book revealed from Allah that contains better guidance than them. If you can do so, I will follow it.",
  28050:
      "If the Quraysh do not answer your challenge to bring a book with better guidance than the Torah and the Quran, then you can be sure their rejection of them is unfounded. It is only based on following their desires, and no one is more astray than those who follow their desires without any guidance from Allah (may He be Exalted). Indeed, Allah does not grant guidance to people who have wronged themselves by disbelieving in Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) does not know the unseen (ghayb) except that which Allah has informed him of.\n2. Knowledge erodes over a long period of time.\n3. The people of falsehood have no legitimate excuse.\n4. The Jews disbelieved in the Torah and the Qur’an.\n5. The disbelievers are challenged with bringing forth anything which is better in guidance than the revelation of Allah to His Messengers.\n6. The disbelievers deviated due to following their desires, not due to following evidence.",
  28051:
      "Indeed, We have made the polytheists and Jews from the Israelites aware of what happened to the previous nations. We did not punish them for rejecting Our messengers in the hopes that they might take heed, believe, and thus avoid being afflicted by what befell those before them.",
  28052:
      "Those who had firm faith in the Torah before the Quran was revealed believe in the Quran because they can find out about it and its description in their books.",
  28053:
      "When it was recited to them, they said: We have believed in it. Indeed, it is the unquestionable truth that our Lord has revealed. Before this Quran came, we were already Muslims due to believing in what the messengers brought before it.",
  28054:
      "Those who possess the mentioned qualities will be rewarded twice by Allah because they persevered in belief in their book and then believed in Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم when he was sent. They warded off what sins they had earned by working righteous good deeds and spending from what we gave them on good causes.",
  28055:
      "When the believers from the people of the book hear falsehood, they ignore it and do not pay it any attention. They tell those who speak it: We will be recompensed for our deeds, and so will you. You are safe from us insulting and abusing you. We are not interested in staying with ignorant people as that causes harm and injury to both our religious and worldly life.",
  28056:
      "You, O Messenger, cannot guide those you love, like Abu Talib and others, to have faith in their hearts. But Allah is the One who guides who He wills. He is more aware of who He already knew will be guided to the straight path.",
  28057:
      "The polytheists of Mecca excuse themselves from following Islam and believing in it by saying: If we follow this Islam that you have brought, our enemies will immediately strip us of our land.Did we not make a sanctuary for these polytheists where spilling blood and oppression is forbidden? Did we not keep them safe from others invading them and send them all types of fruits as sustenance from Us?! However, most of them are unaware of Allah's blessings upon them and do not thank Him.",
  28058:
      "And how many were the towns ungrateful for Allah's blessings upon them and went overboard in sins and acts of disobedience? We punished them until they were destroyed. These are their homes now lying in ruins that people pass by. No one stayed in them after their owners were destroyed except a few travelers, for We alone will inherit the heavens, the earth, and everything they contain.",
  28059:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, does not destroy the towns until He sends a messenger to their major city so that they have no excuse, just like you were sent to the mother of all cities, Mecca. Likewise, We do not destroy their population while they are upright upon the truth. We only destroy them if they have done wrong by disbelieving and committing sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There is virtue for a person from the People of the Book who brings faith on Muhammad (peace be upon him) and he is rewarded twice.\n2. Enabling a person to accept guidance is in Allah’s hands, not in the hands of anyone else such as Messengers and others.\n3. Following the truth is a means of peace, not a cause for fear as the idolaters claim.\n4. Extravagance is dangerous for the individual and society.\n5. It is from Allah’s mercy that He does not destroy people except after giving them an opportunity by sending Messengers.",
  28060:
      "When the polytheists used the difficulties of war and the cutting off of trade as excuses for not following the Truth, Allah responded to them by stating: \n Whatever your Lord has given you is from the enjoyments and embellishments of the worldly life. They will eventually end. The great reward with Allah in the Afterlife is better and more lasting than any enjoyment or embellishment in this world. Will you not understand so that you prefer what lasts over what ends?!",
  28061:
      "Is the one I have promised paradise in the Afterlife and the everlasting pleasure it contains like the one I have given wealth and adornment to enjoy in the worldly life, then he will be on the Day of Judgment amongst those who will be presented to the Fire?",
  28062:
      "[Remember] the Day when your Lord (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) will call out to them saying: Where are the ones you used to worship besides Me claiming that they were My partners?",
  28063:
      "The callers to disbelief who must be tormented will say: Our Lord! Those that we misguided, we only misguided them just as we were misguided. We disassociate ourselves from them before you. They never used to worship us. Rather, they were worshipping the devils.",
  28064:
      "They will be told: Call upon your [so-called] partners to save you from the disgrace you are in. So, they will call upon them, but their call will not be answered. Then, they will see the punishment that was prepared for them and wish that when they lived, they were from those who were guided to the truth.",
  28065:
      "[Remember] the Day when your Lord will call them saying: How did you respond to My messengers that I sent to you?",
  28066:
      "They will not be able to come up with any argument, so they will not mention anything. Neither will they ask each other due to the shock of them being sure they are heading for the torment.",
  28067:
      "But those polytheists who repent from their disbelief, believe in Allah and His messengers, and work righteous deeds will reach what they seek and be saved from what they fear.",
  28068:
      "Your Lord, O Messenger, creates what He wills to create and chooses who He wills to be obedient and receive prophethood. The polytheists cannot decide to object to Allah. He (may He be Exalted) is entirely free of and holier than the partners that they worship alongside Him.",
  28069:
      "Your Lord knows what their hearts conceal and what they make known. Nothing of that is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them for it.",
  28070:
      "He is Allah (may He be Exalted). Nothing has the right to be worshipped except Him. He, alone, deserves all praise in this life and the next. His decrees are inevitable and always fulfilled. To Him alone, you will be returned for reckoning and recompense on the Day of Resurrection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The intelligent person is one who prefers the everlasting over the finite.\n2. The oppressors will disassociate themselves from one another on the day of judgment.\n3. Repentance cancels everything before it.\n4. The choice lies with Allah, not with His servants, so His servants have no right to object to Him.\n5. Allah’s knowledge encompasses whatever is apparent and hidden from the actions of His servants.",
  28071:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Tell me, if Allah makes an endless nighttime that continues uninterrupted until the Day of Resurrection, which of those worshipped besides Allah will be able to bring you light like the light of the day?! Will you not hear these proofs and realize that no God brings you that [light] except Allah?!",
  28072:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: Tell me, if Allah were to make the day last forever continuously until the Day of Resurrection, which of those worshipped besides Allah will bring you night so you can rest and relax from the hard work of the day?! Will you not observe these signs and recognize that no god except Allah brings all that to you?!",
  28073:
      "From His (may He be Exalted) mercy to you, O people, He made the night dark for you so you can rest after getting tired from the day's work, and He made the day bright for you so you can go and earn your living in it. He does all this so that you may be thankful for Allah's favors upon you and not be ungrateful for them.",
  28074:
      "[Warn them of] the Day when their Lord, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, will call out to them: Where are My [so-called] partners that you used to worship besides Me and claim they were My partners?",
  28075:
      "We will bring the prophet of every nation to testify against the disbelief and rejection that their nations were upon. Then we will say to the disbelievers of those nations: Bring forth your proofs and evidence supporting your disbelief and rejection. So, their proofs will be exhausted, and they will be sure that the truth in which there is no doubt is for Allah. The partners that they used to invent for Allah will all have vanished.",
  28076:
      "After mentioning Pharaoh's arrogance on earth due to his power, Allah mentions Qarun's tyranny due to his wealth, stating: \n Indeed, Qarun was from Moses' (peace be upon him) people but held his nose up to them. We gave him such vast wealth that even a strong group of people would find the keys of his treasure heavy to carry. So, his people said to him: Do not rejoice arrogantly. Allah does not love those who rejoice arrogantly but despises them and will torment them for that.",
  28077:
      "[Qarun's people continued:] Seek the reward of the Afterlife in what wealth Allah has given you by spending it charitably. At the same time, do not forget your share of food, drink, clothing, and other blessings, without being wasteful or arrogant. Deal well with your Lord and His slaves as He (may He be Exalted) does so with you. Do not try to cause corruption on Earth by committing sins and abandoning obedience. Allah does not love those who corrupt what is on Earth by doing that. Instead, he despises them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The succession of day and night is one of the blessings of Allah for which one must thank Him.\n2. The night is for rest and the day is for work.\n3. Transgression can be due to wealth, just as it can be through leadership and kingdom.\n4. Wealth is a blessing, but it can turn into an affliction if it is not utilised in what pleases Allah.\n5. Rejoicing arrogantly is a sin which Allah hates.\n6. It is important to sincerely advise a person whom we fear will be tempted.\n7. Allah dislikes those who cause corruption on earth.",
  28078:
      "Qarun said: I was only given this wealth due to my knowledge and capability, so I deserve it. Did Qarun not know that Allah destroyed powerful nations before him that had accumulated far more wealth?! Their power and riches did not benefit them. The criminals will not be asked about their sins on the day of resurrection, as Allah already knows about them. Any questioning of theirs will be to convict and rebuke them.",
  28079:
      "Qarun went out [one day] in his adornments, showing off his glamour. Those companions of Qarun who desired the embellishments of this worldly life said: If only we were given some of the decoration of this life that was given to Qarun. Qarun possesses a great fortune, indeed.",
  28080:
      "When those who were given knowledge saw Qarun in his adornments and heard the wishes of his companions, they said: Woe to you! The reward of Allah is in the Afterlife. The paradise He has prepared for those who believe and work righteous deeds is better than the glitter of this life that Qarun has been given. None can say this and act upon what it requires except those who patiently await the reward with Allah instead of the temporary provision of this life.",
  28081:
      "So we caused him, his home, and everything in it to sink into the Earth as retribution for his evil. No group could help him against Allah, nor could he save himself.",
  28082:
      "Those who wished for the wealth and adornment that Qarun had before the Earth swallowed him up began to take heed and say: Did we not know that Allah extends provision to who He wills from His slaves and restricts it from who He wills?! If Allah had not favored us by not punishing us for what we said, He would have caused the Earth to swallow us up as He did to Qarun. Indeed, the disbelievers are never successful in this life or the next. Instead, their fate and outcome is to lose in both.",
  28083:
      "This is the abode of the hereafter. We have made it a place of bliss and honor for those who, while on the Earth, were not too arrogant to believe and act upon the truth, nor did they intend any corruption in it. The praiseworthy conclusion is the enjoyment of paradise and the pleasure of Allah therein. [Such reward] is for those who feared their Lord by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions.",
  28084:
      "Whoever brings a good deed on the Day of Resurrection (like Salah, zakat, Fasting, etc.) will be recompensed with better than his good deed, as the reward will be increased tenfold. However, whoever brings an evil deed on the Day of Resurrection (like disbelief, consuming usury, fornication, etc.) will not be recompensed except for what he did, without any increase.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Every good and blessing in man is from the creation and decree of Allah.\n2. It is necessary upon the intelligent human to take heed from the conditions of those before him.\n3. The people of worldly pursuits are the quickest to be deceived by it and to fall into temptation.\n4. The people of knowledge are the people of wisdom and salvation from temptations, because knowledge directs a person toward what is correct.\n5. The outcome of haughtiness and arrogance on earth and spreading corruption is destruction and loss.\n6. The vastness of Allah’s mercy and His justice is through multiplying good deeds for the believer and not multiplying bad deeds for the disbeliever.",
  28085:
      "Indeed, the One who sent this Quran to you and obliged you to convey it and implement what is in it will send you back to Mecca victoriously. Say, O Messenger, to the polytheists: My Lord knows best who has brought the Guidance and who is undoubtedly astray from the Guidance and the truth.",
  28086:
      "Before prophethood, O Messenger, you did not expect Allah to reveal the Quran to you. His mercy (may He be Exalted) required it be sent to you. So do not assist the disbelievers in their misguidance.",
  28087:
      "Do not let the polytheists turn you away from Allah's verses after they have been revealed to you, such that you abandon reciting and conveying them. Call the people to believe in Allah, single Him out in worship, and implement His legislation. Do not be from the polytheists who worship others alongside Allah. Instead, be from the monotheists who do not worship anything except Allah alone.",
  28088:
      "Do not worship anything alongside Allah; nothing deserves worship besides Him. Everything will perish except His face (may He be Exalted). Judgment belongs to Him alone; He judges as He wills. To Him alone, you will be returned for reckoning and recompense on the Day of Resurrection.",
  29000:
      "The Spider (Surah Al-'Ankabut)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nCommanding perseverance and steadfastness during times of trial and tribulation and describing the positive outcome result of it.\n•    Explanation:",
  29001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  29002:
      "Do the people think that by saying 'We have believed in Allah,' they will be left without any test to clarify the reality of what they said and whether they are true believers?! The situation is not as they think.",
  29003:
      "Indeed, We tested those before them, so Allah will certainly make apparent those who have true faith and expose those who are lying about it.",
  29004:
      "Moreover, do those who commit sins like polytheism think they can overpower Us and be rescued from Our punishment? How disgusting their judgment is! No one can overcome Allah nor be saved from His punishment if they die as disbelievers.",
  29005:
      "Whoever hopes to meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection to be rewarded should know that the time appointed by Allah is coming soon. He is All-Hearing of His slaves' words and Omniscient of their actions; nothing escapes Him, and He will recompense His slaves accordingly.",
  29006:
      "Whoever pushes Himself to be obedient [to Allah] and stay far away from sins, and strives in the way of Allah, then he strives for himself because the benefit of that will be for him. Allah does not need any of His creation. Their obedience does not give Him anything, and their sins do not take anything away from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Helping the people of misguidance is forbidden.\n2. Holding firm to the Oneness of Allah and staying far from idolatry have been commanded.\n3. Afflicting the believers and testing them is Allah’s custom.\n4. Allah is Self sufficient, not in need and does not take benefit from the obedience of His servants.",
  29007:
      "Those who believe, who have patience when We test them, and who work righteous deeds, We will wipe out their sins due to the good deeds they did, and We will reward them in the hereafter according to the best of what they used to do in the worldly life.",
  29008:
      "We have commanded humanity to be good to their parents and treat them well. If your parents, O humanity, push you to ascribe a partner with Me that you know nothing of (as the mother of Sa'd bin Abi Waqas, may Allah be pleased with him, did), then do not obey them in that because there is no obedience to the creation if it involves disobedience to the Creator. To Me alone, you will return on the Day of Resurrection. Then, I will inform you of what you used to do in the worldly life and recompense you accordingly.",
  29009:
      "Those who believe in Allah and work righteous deeds, We will surely admit them among the righteous on the Day of Resurrection, raise them with them, and reward them as they are rewarded.",
  29010:
      "Some people say that they believe in Allah. Then, when the disbelievers harm them for their belief, they consider the torment of the disbelievers to be like the torment of Allah and leave the faith agreeing with them. But if you, O Messenger, are supported by your Lord, they will say: Indeed, we believe with you, O believers. Is Allah not fully aware of what is in the people's hearts?! Nothing of their faith or disbelief is hidden from Him. So how could they inform Allah about what is in their hearts while He knows what they contain better than they do?!",
  29011:
      "Indeed, Allah will make clear who has true faith and expose the hypocrites who pretend to believe while hiding their disbelief.",
  29012:
      "Those who disbelieved said to those who believed: Follow our religion and what we are upon. We will bear your sins and be recompensed for them instead of you. But they will not carry any of their sins and were speaking untruthfully.",
  29013:
      "It may be understood that disbelievers who invite others to go astray do not commit an additional sin. Allah removes this misconception by stating: \n Those polytheists who call to their falsehood will undoubtedly carry the sins that they committed themselves. They will also bear the sins of those who followed their call without diminishing anything from the sins of their followers. Indeed, they will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection about the falsehood that they used to invent in this worldly life.",
  29014:
      "Indeed, We sent Noah as a messenger to his people. He remained with them for 950 years, calling them to the Oneness of Allah. They rejected him and persisted in their disbelief. So, the flood seized them while they were doing wrong by disbelieving in Allah and rejecting His messengers, then they were destroyed by drowning.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah wipes out sins through good deeds.\n2. The emphasis on the obligation of being kind to one’s parents.\n3. Obedience to Allah comes before obedience to one’s parents.\n4. Faith in Allah demands patience upon being harmed in His way.\n5. Whoever establishes a bad practice, on him is its burden and the burden of those who practice it, without any of their burden decreasing.",
  29015:
      "So, We saved Noah and the believers with him on the Ark from destruction by drowning, and We made the Ark a lesson for the people to heed.",
  29016:
      "O Messenger, remember Abraham's story when he told his people: Worship Allah alone and fear His punishment by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions. What is being ordered is better for you if you could only know.",
  29017:
      "O polytheists, what you worship are but idols that can do no benefit nor harm. You make up lies when you claim they deserve to be worshipped. Those that you worship besides Allah have no power to provide you with sustenance. So, seek your provisions from Allah as He is the Provider. Worship Him alone and thank Him for the provisions He has blessed you with. You will be returned to Him alone for reckoning and recompense on the Day of Resurrection and not to your idols.",
  29018:
      "O polytheists, if you reject what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has brought, then so did the nations before you, like the people of Noah, 'Ād, and Thamūd. The Messenger only has to convey [the revelation] clearly, and He has communicated what his Lord has commanded him to inform you.",
  29019:
      "Do these deniers not see how Allah created the creation initially, then He shall restore it after it has finished? This is easy for Allah, as He is All-Powerful and nothing is beyond His ability.",
  29020:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who deny the resurrection: Travel through the land and think about how Allah creates. Then, after they have died, He gives life to the people for the resurrection and reckoning. Indeed, Allah can do anything; there is nothing He is incapable of. He is not unable to resurrect the people, just as He is not incapable of creating them in the first instance.",
  29021:
      "He torments who He wills from His creation due to His justice and has mercy on who He wills from them due to His grace. To Him alone, you will be returned on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning when you are brought out alive from your graves.",
  29022:
      "You can not escape your Lord and will not be able to flee His punishment, not in the heavens nor the earth. You do not have an ally besides Allah to take care of your affairs, nor do you have any supporter besides Allah who can lift His torment from you.",
  29023:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah's (may He be Exalted) signs and do not believe they will meet Him on the Day of Resurrection have no hope in My mercy. They will never enter paradise due to their disbelief, and an excruciating torment awaits them in the Afterlife.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Idols do not have the ability to provide, so they do not deserve worship.\n2. Provision is only to be sought from Allah who possesses the power to provide.\n3. The beginning of creation is a proof to the resurrection.\n4. Entering paradise is forbidden for one who dies in his disbelief.",
  29024:
      "After Abraham ordered his people to worship Allah alone and abandon the worship of idols besides Him, their only response was to say: Kill him or throw him in the Fire in support of your gods. So, Allah rescued him from the Fire. Indeed, Allah saving him from the Fire after he was thrown in it is a lesson for those who believe because only those who believe can benefit from such lessons.",
  29025:
      "Abraham (peace be upon him) said to his people: You only took these idols as gods to worship due to your acquaintances and mutual affection upon their worship in this worldly life. But on the Day of Resurrection, any affection you had will cease. When you see the torment, you will free yourselves from each other and curse one another. The Fire is the place where you will abide. You will have no supporter to defend you from the torment of Allah, not from the idols you used to worship besides Allah, nor from anyone else.",
  29026:
      "Lot (peace be upon him) believed in Abraham, and Abraham said: I am migrating to my Lord and the blessed lands of the Levant. Indeed, He is the Most Mighty who can never be overcome. He does not humiliate the one who migrates to Him. He is Wise in His decree and management.",
  29027:
      "We gave Abraham Isaac and Isaac's son, Jacob. Then we placed prophethood and the revealed books from Allah among his progeny. We rewarded him in this worldly life for being steadfast upon the truth by giving him righteous offspring and beautiful praise. In the hereafter, he will be given the reward of the righteous. What he was given in this life will not decrease the generous recompense prepared for him in the Afterlife.",
  29028:
      "Mention, O Messenger, when Lot told his people: You are committing a disgusting sin never perpetrated by anyone from all creation before you. You are the first to invent this sin which defies common sense.",
  29029:
      "Do you fulfill your desires with men's backsides and block the road so that travelers cannot pass you for fear of the sin that you commit? Do you commit evil actions in your gatherings, like nudity, and harm whoever passes by verbally and physically? The only response of his people after he forbade them from evil actions was to tell him: Bring Allah's torment that you are threatening us with if you are truthful in what you claim.",
  29030:
      "After the obstinance of Lot's people and they disregarded the torment by requesting it to be sent upon them, Lot called out to his Lord: Oh my Lord, help me against these people that corrupt the Earth by propagating disbelief and despicable sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s care for His righteous servants as He saves them from the plot of their enemies.\n2. The friendship of disbelievers will be severed in the afterlife and will turn into enmity.\n3. The virtue of migration to Allah.\n4. The greatness of the rank of Abraham and his family in Allah’s sight.\n5. Our prophet (peace be upon him) was definitely from the progeny of Abraham.\n6. Being given some reward in the world does not mean the reward in the afterlife will be diminished.\n7. The obscene act of homosexuality is one of the major sins.\n8. The evil of committing wrong acts in public gatherings.",
  29031:
      "When the angels we sent to give the glad tidings of Isaac and his son Jacob came to Abraham, they told him: We will destroy the people of Sodom, the town of Lot's people. The people there did wrong by committing obscene actions.",
  29032:
      "Abraham (peace be upon him) said to the angels: Lot is in this town that you want to destroy the people of, and he is not one of the wrongdoers. The angels said: We know very well who is there. We will save him and his family from the destruction that will be sent upon the people of his town, except his wife, who remained with those to be destroyed. We will destroy her with them.",
  29033:
      "When the angels that we sent to destroy the people of Lot's town came to Lot, he was troubled and upset by them coming. He feared the wickedness of his people because the angels came in the form of men, and his people lusted after men instead of women. The angels told him: Do not be afraid; your people will not harm you, and do not be sad about the destruction we informed you about. We will save you and your family from destruction, except your wife, who stayed with them. So, we will destroy her with them.",
  29034:
      "We will rain down stones of baked clay as torment from the sky upon the people of this town who used to commit wickedness; a punishment for them abandoning obedience to Allah by committing that disgusting, immoral act of fulfilling their lusts with men instead of women.",
  29035:
      "Indeed We left a clear sign from this town that we destroyed for those who think because they are the ones who take heed of these signs.",
  29036:
      "We sent their relative, Shuayb (peace be upon him), to Midian, who said: O my people, worship Allah alone and hope for the recompense on the last day by worshipping him. Do not corrupt the Earth by doing evil deeds and propagating them.",
  29037:
      "His people rejected him, so an earthquake struck them. They collapsed to the ground on their faces, where they remained motionless, their faces stuck to the debris of their homes.",
  29038:
      "And We also destroyed the peoples of the prophet Hūd and Thamūd, the people of the prophet Saleh. It was made evident to you, O people of Mecca, their dwellings in Ash-Shihr, from Hadramawt and Al-Hijr. Their destruction was made evident through their vacant dwellings that bear testament to their demise. The Devil beautified their disbelief and sinful acts that they were upon in their eyes, leading them astray from the Straight Path. They were clearly able to differentiate between truth and misguidance and righteousness and transgression because of their messengers' teachings. But they chose to follow their desires over following guidance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Oppression is a means that leads to destruction.\n2. Following the truth is a means that leads to salvation from destruction.\n3. Human relations are only of benefit if they are accompanied by faith.\n4. Concern for the safety and security of guests from being assaulted.\n5. The homes of those who were destroyed by the punishment is a lesson for those who wish to take lesson.\n6. Knowing the truth is of no benefit when one follows his desires and gives preference to it over guidance.",
  29039:
      "We destroyed Qarun by the Earth swallowing him and his home up when he oppressed the people of Moses. We also destroyed Pharoah and his minister, Haman, by drowning them in the sea. Indeed, Moses brought them clear signs testifying to his truthfulness, but they were too arrogant in the land of Egypt to believe in him. They could not escape from Us and save themselves from Our torment.",
  29040:
      "We seized each of those previously mentioned with Our destructive torment. There were the people of Lot who We sent down upon them stones of baked clay. The people of Saleh and Shuayb were seized by the blast (a tremendous cry from the sky). From them was Qarun, who the Earth swallowed up along with his home. From them were the people of Noah, Pharoah, and Haman, who We destroyed by drowning. Allah would not wrong them by destroying them for no sin. Rather, they wronged themselves by committing sins and so deserved the torment.",
  29041:
      "The similitude of the polytheists who worship idols besides Allah, hoping they will bring them some benefit or intercede for them, is that of the spider. It makes its home to protect it from being attacked, while the weakest home is that of the spider, as it cannot protect it from any enemy. Likewise, their idols can neither benefit nor harm nor intercede. If the polytheists knew that, they would not have worshiped idols besides Allah.",
  29042:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) knows what they worship besides Him. Nothing is hidden from Him. He is the Most Mighty (Al-Aziz); nothing can overpower him. He is the Most Wise (Al-Hakim) in His creation, decree, and management.",
  29043:
      "These examples that I draw for people, to awaken them and make them see the truth and guide them to it, can only be grasped in the desired manner by those who have knowledge of Allah's law and rule.",
  29044:
      "Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, created the heavens and the Earth for a true purpose. He did not create them out of falsehood or in vain. That creation is a clear indication of Allah's power for the believers because they are the ones who will see Allah's created things as evidence of the Creator (may He be Exalted). As for the disbelievers, they come across these signs upon the horizon and in themselves without paying any attention to the might and power of the Creator (may He be Exalted).",
  29045:
      "Read, O Messenger, what Allah has revealed to you from the Quran to the people and offer the prayer in a complete manner. When the prayer is offered most completely, it prevents the person from falling into sins and evil deeds because it places a light in the heart that prevents the committing of sins and guides to performing righteous deeds. Remembrance of Allah is more remarkable and far superior to anything else. Allah knows everything you do; none of your acts are hidden from Him. He will recompense you for your deeds. If your deeds are good, then the recompense will be good; if they are evil, then the recompense will be evil.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The various forms of punishment in the world.\n2. Allah is free of committing oppression.\n3. Attaching oneself to other than Allah is to attach oneself to the weakest means.\n4. The virtue of knowledge.\n5. The importance of prayer in setting right the behaviour of a believer.\n6. The virtue of the remembrance of Allah.",
  29046:
      "O believers, do not discuss or debate with the Jews and Christians to whom the divine books were revealed, except in the best of manners and most exemplary of ways: inviting them by exhortation and establishing clear proofs. As for those who oppress by showing stubbornness and arrogance, fight them until they submit or pay the Jizyah (protection tax paid by non-Muslims living under Muslim rule) from their hands while subdued. And say to the Jews and the Christians: I have believed in whatever Allah has revealed to us in the Quran and what was revealed to you in the Torah and Gospel. Our Lord is one, and so is yours; He has no partner in His Lordship, worship, or perfection, and we submit and humble ourselves to Him alone.",
  29047:
      "Just as We revealed the Books upon those before you, We revealed the Quran upon you. Some who read the Torah, such as Abdullah bin Salam, believe in the Quran because they find it described in their books. Some polytheists also believe in this Quran. Only those accustomed to rejection and denial disbelieve in Our signs, even though they are clear.",
  29048:
      "O Messenger, you had not been reading any book before the [revelation of the] Quran [began], nor did you write anything with your hand because you are unlettered and cannot read or write. If you could read and write, the ignorant people would have doubted your prophethood and used it as an excuse to say you were conveying [verses of the Quran] from the previous books.",
  29049:
      "Rather, the Quran revealed to you consists of clear verses preserved within the hearts of those believers who have been granted knowledge. Only those who wrong themselves by ascribing partners with Allah and rejecting Him deny Our verses.",
  29050:
      "The polytheists said: Why have no signs been given to Muhammad from his Lord, like those given to the messengers before him? O Messenger, say to them: Indeed signs are only in the control of Allah, may He be Exalted; He grants them whenever He wishes. It is not in my power to bring them; I am only a clear warner to you of the punishment of Allah.",
  29051:
      "O Messenger, is it not enough for these people that we have revealed the Quran upon you, which is recited to them? Indeed, the Quran is a mercy and exhortation to people who believe because they are the ones who truly benefit from whatever it contains. Therefore, whatever has been revealed to them is better than sending something similar to what was revealed to the previous messengers as they want.",
  29052:
      "O Messenger, say: Allah (may He be Exalted) is enough as a witness to my truthfulness in what I convey and to your rejection of it. He knows everything in the heavens and on Earth; nothing is hidden from Him. As for those who believe in the falsehood of worshipping anything instead of Allah while rejecting the One who alone is worthy of worship, they are the true losers because they chose disbelief over belief.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Debating with the people of the Book should only be done in the best of ways.\n2. It is a prerequisite of faith to believe in all Messengers without exception.\n3. The noble Qur’an is an everlasting miracle and sign of the truthfulness of the Prophet.",
  29053:
      "O Messenger, the polytheists want you to bring the punishment you warned them of quickly. Had it not been for Allah already having decreed a fixed time for their punishment, it would have come upon them suddenly while they were unaware.",
  29054:
      "They want you to hasten the punishment you warned them about. Indeed, the Hell that Allah warned the disbelievers of will surround them; they will not be able to escape its torment.",
  29055:
      "On the Day the punishment will cover them from above and spread under their feet, Allah will rebuke them by saying: Suffer the consequences of the polytheism and sins you used to commit.",
  29056:
      "O my slaves who believe in Me, leave the land where you cannot worship Me [to somewhere where you can]. Indeed, My land is vast, so worship Me alone and do not ascribe anyone as a partner to Me.",
  29057:
      "Let not the fear of death prevent you from migrating. Every soul shall taste death, and then to Us alone, you shall return on the Day of Resurrection to be taken to account and recompensed accordingly.",
  29058:
      "Those who have faith in Allah and perform good deeds through which they draw closer to Him, We will accommodate them in raised dwellings under which rivers flow, wherein they shall reside forever. How great is this reward of those who live in obedience to Allah!",
  29059:
      "How great is the reward for those who obey Allah and remain steadfast on that while refraining from disobeying Him, and they rely upon Him alone in all their affairs?",
  29060:
      "Every single animal that exists, and there are many, cannot store its provisions; [rather,] Allah sustains them and you. Therefore, not emigrating out of fear of starvation is not a valid excuse for you. He is All-Hearing of your words and Omniscient of your intentions and actions; none of them are hidden from Him, and He shall recompense you accordingly for them.",
  29061:
      "O Messenger, if you ask these polytheists who created the heavens and the Earth and who put the sun and moon into orbit such that they appear one after the other, surely they will say Allah is the one who created the heavens and the Earth and put the sun and moon into constant orbit. How can they turn away from believing in Allah alone to worshiping deities instead of Him that do not benefit or bring harm?",
  29062:
      "Allah increases the sustenance for whomever He wishes from His slaves and restricts it for whomever He wishes due to wisdom only He knows. Indeed, Allah knows everything; whatever is good for His slaves is not hidden from Him.",
  29063:
      "O Messenger, suppose you were to ask the polytheists who causes the rain to descend from the sky and consequently causes the earth to grow after it had been barren. In that case, they will say Allah is the one who causes the rain to fall from the sky and the earth to grow because of it. O Messenger, say [to them]: All praise is for Allah, Who has made the evidence clear against you. However, the crux of the matter is that most of them will not understand because if they were to understand, they would not worship idols that do not benefit or harm them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A disbeliever seeking the punishment early is proof of his foolishness.\n2. The door for emigration to protect the practice of one’s religious rituals is open.\n3. The virtue of patience and reliance on Allah.\n4. Acknowledging the lordship of Allah without acknowledging His exclusive worship does not grant a person salvation and true faith.",
  29064:
      "With all its temptations and enjoyments, this worldly life is only amusement and play for those attached to it; it will quickly perish. Indeed, the Afterlife's abode is the real life because it is eternal. If only they knew, they would not have preferred something temporary over that which is eternal.",
  29065:
      "Allah recorded the polytheists' contradictions against them, such as their belief in Allah's lordship when asked about the creation of the heavens and the Earth and their disbelief in Allah's absolute divinity when they worship other than Him. Allah records another contradiction when they fully devote themselves to Him alone when they fear drowning and returning back to associating partners with Him when they find safety, stating: \n When the polytheists board ships and sail the ocean, they call out to Allah alone, sincerely supplicating to Him to save them from drowning. After Allah saves them from drowning, they return to their polytheism, calling out to their idols along with Allah.",
  29066:
      "They return to their polytheism to continue showing ingratitude for Our favors upon them and continue enjoying the beauty of this worldly life. They will soon know the evil punishment that awaits them when they die.",
  29067:
      "Do these people who reject the blessings of Allah upon them not see another blessing of His after He saves them from drowning, that He made a sanctuary for them in which their lives and wealth are secure? This is while those around them are raided, killed, looted, and taken captive together with their wives and children. Do they still believe in their false deities and reject the bounties of Allah, not showing Him gratitude for them?",
  29068:
      "No one commits more wrong than the one who fabricates a lie regarding Allah by attributing a partner to Him or rejecting the truth that His Messenger brought. Undoubtedly, there is an abode in Hell for the disbelievers and those like them.",
  29069:
      "And those who exert themselves to seek My pleasure, We will certainly grant them the ability to tread the straight path. Indeed, Allah is with those who do good by helping, assisting, and guiding them.",
  30000:
      "The Romans (Surah Ar-Rum)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming the uniqueness of Allah in managing affairs and describing His divine established practice in creation.\n•    Explanation:",
  30001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  30002: "The Persians have defeated the Romans.",
  30003:
      "In the nearer lands of the Levant extending to Persia. The Romans, after their defeat, will be victorious over them again.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. During times of severe difficulty the idol worshippers only seek refuge and help from Allah while forgetting their idols. When the difficulty is removed and ease comes they ascribe partners to Allah. This is a clear proof of their misguidance.\n2. Striving in the path of Allah is a cause of being guided to the truth.\n3. The detailed announcement of future events in the Qur’an is clear evidence of this book being revealed from Allah.",
  30004:
      "Within a period of three to ten years. To Allah belongs the command before and after the Romans’ victory. And on the day the Romans defeat the Persians, the believers will be happy.",
  30005:
      "They will be happy that Allah helps the Romans because they are people of the Book. Allah helps whomever He wishes against whomever He wishes; He is the Almighty who cannot be overcome, the Merciful towards His believing slaves.",
  30006:
      "This victory was a promise from Allah, and with its fulfillment, the believers will increase in their conviction of Allah's promise of victory being true. As for the majority of people, they do not understand this due to their disbelief.",
  30007:
      "They do not know faith and the rulings of the legislation; they only know of the superficial realities of this worldly life related to earning a livelihood, while they turn away from the real life of the Afterlife, not paying any attention to it.",
  30008:
      "Do these rejecting polytheists not ponder in themselves as to how Allah has created them and arranged them together in their most complete forms? Allah did not create the heavens and the Earth except for a just cause; He did not create them in vain, and He appointed a fixed time for their existence in the worldly life. Indeed, many people reject the meeting of their Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and that is why they have not prepared for the resurrection by doing good deeds that are acceptable to their Lord.",
  30009:
      "Do these people not travel the earth so that they can ponder over what the outcome of the nations who rejected Allah before them was? Those nations were much stronger than them; they adapted the land for farming and construction and populated it much more than these people had. Their Messengers brought clear proof and evidence for the Oneness of Allah, but they were rejected. So when Allah punished them, He did not wrong them; instead, they wronged themselves by disbelieving and falling into destruction.",
  30010:
      "Then, the outcome of those who did evil deeds, i.e., polytheism and sins, was utterly terrible. That was because they rejected the signs of Allah and would mock and ridicule them.",
  30011:
      "Allah creates the creation without any precedent, then He causes it to die, then will resurrect it. Then, to Him alone will you return to be taken to account for and recompensed on the Day of Resurrection.",
  30012:
      "On the Day when the hour arrives, the criminals shall despair from the mercy of Allah, and their hopes in Allah's mercy will end just as their excuses to disbelieve in Allah end.",
  30013:
      "They will not have those they ascribed as partners to Allah (and used to worship in the worldly life) to intercede for them to save them from the torment. Instead, they will reject those partners they ascribed to Allah. They will forsake them when they need them most because they are all equally doomed.",
  30014:
      "And on the Day the hour arrives, the people will all be divided according to the recompense of their deeds in this world. Some will be elevated to the highest ranks, while others will be demoted to the lowest of the low.",
  30015:
      "As for those who believed in Allah and did good deeds pleasing to Him, they will be in Paradise, overjoyed with whatever everlasting bounties they gain therein.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Knowledge of that which rectifies the world whilst being neglectful of what rectifies one’s afterlife is of no benefit.\n2. The signs of Allah in the horizon as well as within ourselves are enough of an evidence that He alone should be worshipped.\n3. Oppression was the cause of the destruction of the previous nations.\n4. The disbeliever will lose all hope on the Day of Judgement just as his excuses will end.\n5. On the Day of Judgement, Allah shall elevate the believers and demote the disbelievers.",
  30016:
      "As for those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His signs that were revealed to His Messengers, the resurrection, and the Reckoning, they are the ones who will be in a state of constant punishment.",
  30017:
      "So exalt Allah when night enters, the time of the Maghrib and Isha prayers, and exalt Him when morning enters, the time of the Fajr prayer.",
  30018:
      "To Allah (may He be Exalted) belongs all praise; the angels praise Him in the heavens, and His creation praise Him on Earth. Exalt Him when the evening enters, which is the time of the 'Asr prayer, and exalt Him at the time of Zuhr.",
  30019:
      "He brings out life from the dead, like His creation of a human from a drop of semen and a chick from an egg. He also brings out life from the living, like His extracting a drop of semen from a human and an egg from a chicken. He revives the earth after it has become dry by sending down rain and regrowing it. Likewise, you will be resurrected from your graves for the final reckoning and recompense.",
  30020:
      "Among Allah's great signs, which prove His omnipotence and oneness, is that He created you, O people, from the Earth when He created your father from clay, and then you soon became many humans, increasing through reproduction and spreading over the Earth's east and west.",
  30021:
      "Among Allah's great signs, which demonstrate His omnipotence and oneness, is that He created for you, O men, wives from you so that you may find contentment in them due to your unique compatibility. He put love and affection between you. Indeed, the aforementioned are clear proofs and evidence for people who contemplate because they are the ones who benefit by using their intellect.",
  30022:
      "Among Allah's great signs, which demonstrate His omnipotence and oneness, is that He created the heavens and the Earth and your different languages and skin colors. In that, there are proofs and evidence for the people of knowledge and insight.",
  30023:
      "Among Allah's great signs, which demonstrate His omnipotence and oneness, is your sleeping by night and day so that you may rest from the toil of your work. And among His signs is that He made the day so that you may disperse, seeking sustenance from your Lord. Indeed, these are proofs and evidence for people who listen attentively and willingly.",
  30024:
      "Among Allah's great signs, which demonstrate His omnipotence and oneness, is that He shows you lightning in the sky, combining within it fear of the thunder and hope of rain. He also sends down rainwater for you from the heavens and revives the earth by the regrowth of plants after it has dried up. Indeed, there are clear proofs and evidence in that for people of understanding so that they may compare that with the resurrection after death for the final reckoning and recompense.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A servant filling up his times with prayer and glorification of Allah is a sign of him facing a good outcome.\n2. Conclusions can be drawn on resurrection by the continuity of life, in that Allah creates the living from the dead and vice versa.\n3. No one takes heed from Allah’s signs in the bodies and horizons except those who use their physical and mental faculties granted to them by Allah.",
  30025:
      "Among Allah's signs, which prove His omnipotence and oneness, is that by His command, the sky stays up without falling, and the Earth does not collapse in ruins. Then, when He calls you from the Earth by the angel blowing the trumpet, you will suddenly emerge from your graves to give account and be recompensed.",
  30026:
      "And to Allah alone belongs whoever is in the heavens and the Earth; Allah created them, owns them, and has complete control over them. All His creation in the heavens and the Earth obey Him and comply with His command.",
  30027:
      "He is the One who originates the creation without there being anything like it before. He resurrects it after it withers away. Bringing it back is easier than creating it the first time. However, both are easy for Him because whenever He intends something, He says, 'Be!' and it happens. He (the Mighty and Majestic) has the highest of praise in whatever qualities of majesty and perfection he is praised with. He is the Almighty who cannot be overcome; Wise in His creation and management.",
  30028:
      "O, polytheists, Allah gives you an example of yourselves: do you have partners from your slaves who are equal to you in everything you own, such that you fear them just as you fear each other? Would you be happy for yourselves with your slaves being such? Undoubtedly, you would not be pleased with such an arrangement, so Allah is more worthy that He does not have a partner from His creation in His kingdom. Similarly, Allah clearly explains different proofs and evidence for people of understanding because they are the ones who benefit from them.",
  30029:
      "Their deviance is not because of any deficiency in proofs or those not being explained; it is only because of following desires and their forefathers, So who is there that is capable of guiding those whom Allah has caused to deviate? No one can do that. They will have no helpers to keep the punishment away from them.",
  30030:
      "O Messenger, you and those with you should turn your faces towards the true religion which Allah has directed you, the religion of Islam upon which Allah inherently created people, and turn away from all other religions. There is no changing the creation of Allah; it is the correct and upright religion in which there is no deviation, but most people do not know this.",
  30031:
      "And return to Him (may He be Exalted) by repenting from your sins, fear Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, perform prayer in the best way you can, and do not be from the polytheists who go against nature and ascribe partners with Allah by worshipping them.",
  30032:
      "And do not be from those polytheists who changed their religion, believing in some of it and rejecting other parts of it. They split into groups and sects, each sect happy with whatever falsehood they were on, thinking that they alone were upon the truth and others were on falsehood.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Each creation of Allah is submissive to Him, either optionally or by force.\n2. The initial creation clearly proves resurrection.\n3. Giving examples to clarify the truth and falsehood is desirable.\n4. Following desires deviates and misleads.\n5. The religion of Islam is the only religion accepted by those of sound disposition.",
  30033:
      "When the polytheists are afflicted by a difficulty, i.e., poverty or drought, they supplicate only to their Lord (may He be Exalted), returning to Him, humbling themselves, and seeking refuge in Him to remove the affliction from them. Then, when He shows them mercy by removing whatever afflicted them, they return to their ways of idolatry by supplicating to others along with Him.",
  30034:
      "They show their ungratefulness for the favors of Allah, and from amongst them is removing their difficulty. So enjoy your ease in this life; you will surely come to know on the Day of Resurrection that you were in clear misguidance.",
  30035:
      "What made them ascribe partners to Allah without evidence supporting their claim? We did not send any evidence to them in the form of any scripture that they could use as proof for their ascribing partners with Allah, nor do they have any scripture in favor of their idolatry that upholds the validity of the disbelief they are on.",
  30036:
      "And when We give the people a taste of some of Our bounties, i.e., health and wealth, they become happy with it proudly and arrogantly. And if some harm reaches them, i.e., illness or poverty due to their sins, they begin losing hope in the mercy of Allah. They despair from the difficulty ever leaving them.",
  30037:
      "Do they not see that Allah increases the sustenance for whichever of His slaves He wishes, testing them to see whether they will show gratitude or ingratitude? He restricts sustenance upon whomsoever He wishes, to see whether they are patient or become angry. Indeed, the increasing provision for some and restricting it for others are proofs of the kindness and mercy of Allah.",
  30038:
      "O Muslim, give the relative whatever goodness and kinship he deserves, give the needy whatever he can fulfill his need with, and help the stranger whose path back home has been cut off. Giving to these causes is better for those who seek the pleasure of Allah. Those who give priority to this kind of assistance and rights are the ones who succeed by achieving their objective of Paradise and being granted safety from the feared punishment.",
  30039:
      "After mentioning what was meant by means of getting closer to Allah through work, Allah mentions what is meant by doing things for other than His sake, referring to petty, worldly gain, stating: \n Whatever wealth you give to anyone with the desire that they will return it to you with more, the reward of that wealth does not grow with Allah. And whatever wealth you provide to fulfill someone's need, desiring only the pleasure of Allah and not praise or reward from the people, the reward of that deed shall be multiplied for you by Allah.",
  30040:
      "Allah alone created you, granted you sustenance, will cause you to die, and will revive you for the resurrection. Are there any of your idols you worship that can do any of that? He is far removed and free of what the polytheists say and believe.",
  30041:
      "Corruption has appeared in the land and sea, such as drought, poor rainfall, increased illness, and disease due to the sins they commit. It has appeared so that Allah may give them a taste of some of their evil deeds in the worldly life so that they may repent to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The idolaters contradict themselves by sincerely worshipping Allah at times of severity, and ascribing partners to Him in times of ease.\n2. The happiness based on arrogance at times of enjoying bounties, and losing hope in mercy at times of trials are two traits of the disbelievers.\n3. Giving due rights to people is a cause of success.\n4. Interest is eradicated and the reward of spending in the path of Allah is multiplied.\n5. The effects of sins are evident in the spreading of plagues and spoiling of the environment.",
  30042:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Travel the earth and ponder the outcome of the nations that denied [tawheed] before you. Their outcome was evil; most would ascribe partners with Allah, worshipping others with Him, and because of that, they were destroyed.",
  30043:
      "O Messenger, turn to the correct religion of Islam, in which there is no deviation before the Day of Resurrection comes. When it comes, there will be no one to prevent it, and on that day, people will be divided: one group shall be blessed in Paradise, while the other shall be punished in the Fire.",
  30044:
      "Whoever disbelieves in Allah will suffer the consequences of his disbelief; an eternity in the Fire. Those who do good deeds seeking Allah's pleasure through them will enter into Paradise and derive enjoyment from whatever is within it, and they shall live in it forever.",
  30045:
      "Allah will separate the people and divide them into two groups so that He can reward those who have faith in Allah and perform good deeds that He is pleased with. Indeed, He does not love those who disbelieve in Him and His Messengers. Rather, He hates them severely and will punish them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  30046:
      "And among Allah's great signs that demonstrate His omnipotence and oneness is that He sends winds that give glad tidings of imminent rain to the slaves, and so that He may give you, O people, a taste of His mercy by the greenery and ease that follows the rainfall. And also so that the ships can sail the sea by His will and you can seek from His grace by trading across the ocean. Perhaps you will show gratitude for the favors of Allah so He may give you more of them.",
  30047:
      "O Messenger, verily, I have sent many messengers to their people before you, and they brought evidence proving their truthfulness. However, the people rejected whatever their messengers brought. Hence, we took retribution from those who committed evil and destroyed them with Our punishment, saving the messengers and those who believed in them from destruction. Rescuing the believers and helping them is a right that We have obligated upon Ourselves.",
  30048:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is the One who sends and drives the winds. Those winds form and move the clouds. He extends those clouds, whether many or few, across the sky as he wills and breaks them up. O observer, you can see the rain falling from those clouds. Then, when it rains on whoever He will from His slaves, they are happy with Allah's mercy upon them by sending down rain that brings forth vegetation from the earth, which they and their animals need.",
  30049: "Previously, they had lost all hope in any rain falling upon them.",
  30050:
      "O Messenger, look at the effects of the rainfall that Allah sends out of mercy for His slaves; how Allah revives the earth with the various plants that grow after it has dried up and become barren. Indeed, He who restored that dry earth is the One who will resurrect the dead back to life. He is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The people will be categorised on the Day of Judgment according to their deeds in the world, into either successful or wretched.\n2. Sending winds and rain, and causing the ships to sail in the sea: are blessings which require gratitude to be expressed for them.\n3. Destroying the criminals and saving the believers is a divine custom of Allah.\n4. The earth growing after it has become barren is evidence of resurrection.",
  30051:
      "If We were to send upon their farms and crops a wind that would spoil them, and they would see their crops turn a yellow color after they had previously been green, they would then be ungrateful for the numerous other bounties of Allah they enjoyed the time before that.",
  30052:
      "So just as you cannot make the dead and deaf hear, in the same way, after they have distanced themselves from you to make sure they cannot hear you, you cannot guide those similar to them (the dead and the deaf) if they turn away and do not benefit.",
  30053:
      "You cannot guide those who have deviated from the straight path onto taking the right path. Neither can you make anyone hear in a way that will benefit them, except those who believe in Our signs, because only they are the ones who will benefit from whatever you say and are submissive and compliant to Our command.",
  30054:
      "O people, Allah is the one who created you from a despicable fluid. He gave you the strength of youth after the weakness of childhood, then the weakness of old age after the strength of youth. Allah creates whatever He wishes of strength and weakness; He is the Omniscient of everything; nothing is hidden from Him. [He is] Omnipotent; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  30055:
      "When the Day of Resurrection is established, the criminals will swear that they have not been in their graves except for a very short period. Likewise, they were deluded in the worldly life by denying the truth.",
  30056:
      "Those prophets and angels to whom Allah has granted knowledge will say: You remained for as long as Allah decreed according to His infinite knowledge, until the day of your resurrection, which you would deny, but you did not know that the resurrection was a reality, and so you rejected it.",
  30057:
      "So on the day when Allah shall resurrect all of creation for the reckoning and recompense, all the excuses the wrongdoers make will not benefit them. They will not be asked to please Allah by repenting because the time has long expired.",
  30058:
      "In this Quran, We have mentioned every type of parable for the people so that the truth becomes clearly distinguished to them from falsehood. O Messenger, if you were to bring clear proof of your truthfulness to them, the disbelievers in Allah would say: you are nothing but fabricators of what you brought.",
  30059:
      "Allah seals the hearts of those who purposely reject the signs you bring them. Likewise, Allah seals the hearts of those who do not know that what you brought is the truth.",
  30060:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with the rejection you face from your people. Indeed, Allah's promise to you of help and empowerment remains. Let not those who do not believe they will be resurrected make you become hasty and impatient.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers despair of the mercy of Allah when a trial comes upon them.\n2. Placing guidance in the hearts is in Allah’s hands alone, not in the hands of the Messenger (peace be upon him).\n3. The stages of life are lessons for those who take heed.\n4. Sins are the cause of hearts becoming sealed.",
  31000:
      "Luqman (Surah Luqman)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe command to follow the wisdom outlined in the Quran and the warning against turning away from it.\n•    Explanation:",
  31001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  31002:
      "O Messenger, these verses revealed to you are verses of the Book that speaks wisdom.",
  31003:
      "It is guidance and mercy for those who do good by fulfilling the rights of their Lord and the rights of His slaves.",
  31004:
      "Those who perform prayer as best they can and give Zakat of their wealth while being certain of the resurrection, account, and reward in the Afterlife.",
  31005:
      "Those characterized as such are upon guidance from their Lord, and it is they who are successful by gaining whatever they seek and being distanced from what causes them fear.",
  31006:
      "After mentioning the traits of those who strive toward excellence, He mentions the traits of the evildoers, stating: \n Some people, like An-Nadr Muhammed bin Al-Harith, tell stories to distract people from Allah's religion with ignorance and take Allah's words as a joke, mocking them. Those who possess these characteristics will have a humiliating torment awaiting them in the Afterlife.",
  31007:
      "When you read Our verses to him, he turns away in arrogance, as if he has not heard them, as if his ears are oblivious to sounds. So, O Messenger, warn him of a painful punishment that awaits him.",
  31008:
      "Indeed, those who believe and do good deeds will have gardens of Paradise, where they shall live in luxury among everything Allah has prepared for them.",
  31009:
      "They will remain therein [forever]. Allah has made them a true promise of which there is no doubt. He is the Almighty whom no one can overcome; the Wise in His creation, decree, and legislation.",
  31010:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) created the heavens, which are raised without any pillars, and pitched mountains on the Earth to hold it firmly in place so that it does not shake in convulsion. He dispersed animals throughout the Earth and sent down rainfall from the sky, causing the Earth to grow delightful plants, from which both humans and animals benefit.",
  31011:
      "O, polytheists, these all are from Allah's creation, so show Me what those you worship other than Allah have created. Instead, the wrongdoers are in apparent deviance from the truth because they attribute partners to Allah that cannot make anything but are themselves created.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Obedience to Allah leads to success in the world and the afterlife.\n2. All speech and action that prevents from the straight path is forbidden.\n3. Arrogance prevents following the truth.\n4. Creation is an attribute solely belonging to Allah. He challenges the idolaters to show what their deities/Allahs have created.",
  31012:
      "Verily, I granted Luqman the understanding of religion and correctness in matters, and I told him: O Luqman, be grateful to your Lord for the blessing He has bestowed upon you of being able to obey Him. Whoever is thankful to his Lord, his gratefulness benefits only himself, for Allah is not dependent upon it. Whoever rejects His blessings, the harm of his rejection afflicts him alone, for his rejection does not hurt Allah in the slightest. Allah is independent of His creation and praiseworthy at all times.",
  31013:
      "O Messenger, remember when Luqman told his son while encouraging him to do good and warning him from evil: O my son, do not worship any of the creation along with Allah. Indeed, worshiping a deity besides Allah is a grave injustice to the self and is a cause for permanently staying in Hell.",
  31014:
      "And We commanded man to obey his parents and do good towards them in matters that do not lead to the disobedience of Allah. His mother carried him in her womb, facing difficulty upon difficulty, weaning him off breastfeeding within two years. We told him: Be grateful to Allah for every blessing He has bestowed upon you, then be thankful to your parents for their care and upbringing. To Me alone is your return, upon which I shall recompense each person according to what he deserves.",
  31015:
      "And even if your parents strive to incite you to ascribe partners to Allah according to their ignorant/arbitrary understanding, like what the mother of Sa'd bin Abī Waqqās did, then do not obey them in that because there is no obedience to the creation in the disobedience to the Creator. Instead, live with them in this world kindly, maintaining ties and friendship. And follow the path of those who proclaim My oneness repeatedly and obey Me. To Me alone is your return on the Day of Resurrection so that I may tell you of the actions you used to do in the world and requite you for them.",
  31016:
      "O my son, indeed, evil and good, no matter how small, even if equal to the weight of a mustard seed and in the middle of a rock unbeknown to anyone or any place in the heavens or Earth, Allah will make it known on the Day of Resurrection and recompense the slave. Allah is the Most Subtle, whose Knowledge encompasses all secret and hidden matters. He is Kind to His slaves and Aware of everything.",
  31017:
      "O my son, establish the prayer best you can, enjoin good and forbid evil, and bear patience upon whatever adversity you face. Indeed, my instructions to you are from those Allah has decided you should do, so you have no choice in doing or not doing them.",
  31018:
      "Do not turn your face away from the people in arrogance, and do not walk around with pride, amazed with yourself. Indeed, Allah does not like those who walk about arrogantly or are conceited in whatever blessings they have and do not thank Allah for them.",
  31019:
      "Be moderate in walking: not too hasty or overly slow, and show dignity. And lower your voice; do not raise it so it annoys others. Indeed, the most hideous of sounds is the braying of a donkey because of how loud it is.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The benefit of obedience and harm of sin returns to affect the servant.\n2. It is obligatory to take care of children by educating them and bringing them up well.\n3. Be obedient to parents, especially the mother.\n4. There is no obedience to the creation in the disobedience to the Creator.\n5. The accounting on the Day of Judgment will be meticulous.\n6. Islamic governance (on etiquettes) covers both the individual and social spheres.",
  31020:
      "O people, do you not witness that Allah has made it easy for you to benefit from whatever is in the heavens, such as the sun, moon, and stars? He has also made it easy for you to take advantage of the Earth's livestock, trees, and plants. He has completed His blessings upon you that you see, like a beautiful appearance and pleasant form, and those you do not see, like intelligence and knowledge. Despite all these blessings, some people dispute the Oneness of Allah without having any revealed knowledge from Allah or insightful intellect, nor any book revealed from Allah that clarifies [what they say].",
  31021:
      "When it is said to these people who dispute the Oneness of Allah: Follow the revelation Allah has revealed to His Messenger. They say: We will not follow it; instead, we will follow what we found our forefathers doing and worship our gods. Will they follow their forefathers even though the Devil calls them towards the punishment of a blazing fire on the Day of Resurrection by misguiding them to the worship of idols?",
  31022:
      "Whoever turns to Allah sincerely and devotes worship to Him by doing good deeds has held on to the firmest thing that those who hope for salvation can hold on to. He will not fear that whatever he has held on to will be cut off. To Allah alone return all affairs; He will recompense each person as they deserve.",
  31023:
      "O Messenger, whoever disbelieves in Allah, let not their disbelief grieve you. To Us alone, they will return on the Day of Resurrection. We will inform them of the evils they committed and recompense them for their bad deeds. Indeed, Allah knows what is in the hearts; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  31024:
      "We will let them enjoy whatever pleasures We have given them in this world for a short while, then compel them to a severe torment on the Day of Resurrection: the punishment of the Fire.",
  31025:
      "O Messenger, if you ask these polytheists: Who created the heavens and the Earth? They will say: Allah created them. Say to them: All praise is for Allah, who has made clear the evidence against you. However, most do not know who deserves all praise because of their ignorance.",
  31026:
      "To Allah alone belongs everything in the heavens and on Earth, in terms of being His creation, under His ownership and control. Allah is self-sufficient, not needing his creation, and praiseworthy in this world and the Hereafter.",
  31027:
      "If all the trees on Earth were to be cut and made into pens, and the seas turned into ink seven times over, the Words of Allah would not be depleted due to their infinite amount. Indeed, Allah is the Almighty whom none can overcome; the Wise in His creation and management.",
  31028:
      "O people, your creation and resurrection for full accountability and recompense on the Day of Resurrection are as easy as creating and resurrecting just one soul. Indeed, Allah hears everything; hearing one sound does not preoccupy Him from hearing another; He also sees everything; seeing one thing does not preoccupy Him from seeing another either. Likewise, creating something and resurrecting it does not preoccupy Him with creating and resurrecting another.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The blessings of Allah are a means to show gratitude and bringing faith in Him, not a means to disbelief.\n2. Blind following is dangerous, especially in matters of belief.\n3. Submitting to Allah in obedience and doing good deeds for His pleasure is very important.\n4. The Words of Allah never finish.\n5. Allah is capable of creating and resurrecting people.",
  31029:
      "Do you not see that Allah shortens the night to lengthen the day and then shortens the day to lengthen the night? He also set the orbits of the sun and the moon so each move in its orbit for a fixed time. Do you also not see that Allah is aware of everything you do; none of your actions are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for them?",
  31030:
      "That control and careful measure bear testimony that Allah alone is the truth. He is true in His being, attributes, and actions. It also bears testimony to everything that the polytheists worship, being unfounded falsehood and that Allah is the Exalted in His being and His attributes over all His creation; there is none higher than Him, and He is more significant than everything.",
  31031:
      "O people, do you not see the ships that sail the sea due to His Kindness and Facilitation so that He can show you His signs that prove His Power (may He be Exalted) and Kindness? Indeed, in that are proofs of His Power for every person who is patient upon harms that afflict him and grateful for whatever blessings he receives.",
  31032:
      "And when a wave the size of mountains and dark clouds surround them from all sides, they call out to Allah, sincerely supplicating and worshipping Him. Then, when Allah accepts their supplication and saves them from drowning, bringing them back to land, some of them are moderate in their praise, falling short of showing due gratitude to Him, while others reject the blessing of Allah. None reject Our signs except every deceitful person ungrateful for Allah's favors upon him, not thanking His Lord for what he has blessed him with, just like this one who promised to be grateful if Allah saved him.",
  31033:
      "O people, be mindful of your Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Fear His punishment on the day when no father will be able to benefit his child, nor a child benefit its father in the slightest. Indeed, the promise of Allah of requital on the Day of Resurrection is true and will inevitably be fulfilled, so let not the worldly life and whatever desires and amusements it contains deceive you, nor let the Devil deceive you by misunderstanding the forbearance of Allah and His delaying the punishment from you.",
  31034:
      "Indeed, Allah alone knows of the [last] Hour: He knows when it will occur; He sends the rain whenever He wishes, and He knows what is in the wombs: male or female, successful or wretched. No soul knows what good or bad it will do the next day or what land it will die in. Instead, Allah is the One who knows all of that; He is Knower and Aware of all that; nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The shortening and lengthening of the night and day, and the control over the sun and moon: are all signs of the power of Allah, may He be glorified, and bounties which are worthy of gratitude.\n2. Patience and gratitude are means that lead to pondering over the signs of Allah.\n3. The faith of an idolater at the time of severity and his consequent disbelief at the time of ease is grave wickedness.\n4. The Day of Judgment is so severe that a relative will not be able to benefit another.\n5. Fear of the Day of Judgment saves one from being deceived by the world, and by submitting to the whispers of Satan.\n6. Allah’s full knowledge of the Ghaib is all encompassing.",
  32000:
      "The Prostration (Surah As-Sajdah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nClarification of the reality of creation and the conditions of humanity in this world and the Hereafter.\n•    Explanation:",
  32001:
      "Alif Lām Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  32002:
      "This Quran that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has brought was revealed to him by the Lord of all the worlds. There is no doubt in it.",
  32003:
      "These disbelievers say: Indeed, Muhammad has fabricated it and attributed it to his Lord. It is not as they say. Instead, it is the truth in which there is no doubt, revealed from your Lord to you, O Messenger, so that you may warn a nation, to whom no Messenger has come before you, of the punishment of Allah, so that they may be guided to the truth, and follow and practice it.",
  32004:
      "Allah is the One who created the heavens and the Earth and created everything in between them in six days, while He is capable of making them in less than the time it takes to bat an eyelid. He then rose over His throne in a manner that befits His Majesty. O people, you do not have a guardian who cares for your affairs other than Him or an intercessor who intercedes for you in front of your Lord. Do you not think to worship Allah, who created you, and not to worship others besides Him?",
  32005:
      "Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, disposes of the affair of all creation in the heavens and the Earth. That affair then ascends to Him in a day, the duration of which is like a thousand of your years in this world.",
  32006:
      "The One who organizes all that is aware of everything present and absent; none of it is hidden from Him. He is the Almighty whom none can overcome; who takes retribution from his enemies and is Merciful towards His believing slaves.",
  32007:
      "He is the One who perfected everything He created and created man from clay without any precedent.",
  32008: "He then created his progeny after him from a delicate fluid: semen.",
  32009:
      "Then He completed the creation of man in his complete form, then blew His soul [that He created for him] into him by commanding the angel appointed with blowing the soul, and made for you, O people, ears so that you could hear with them, eyes so that you could see, and hearts so that you could understand. Seldom are you grateful for Allah's bounties, which He bestows upon you.",
  32010:
      "The polytheists who reject the resurrection say: When we die, and our bodies become dust and disappear into the earth, will we be resurrected back to life? That is inconceivable. Instead, they reject the resurrection and do not believe in it.",
  32011:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who reject the resurrection: The angel of death whom Allah has appointed to seize your souls shall do so, then to Us alone you will return on the Day of Resurrection to give account and to be recompensed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1.Revelation of the Book being from Allah necessitates hastening towards believing and practicing it.\n2. The wisdom behind sending Messengers is that they guide their people to the straight path.\n3. Creating the creation gradually was to educate the people of the value of doing something gradually, otherwise Allah is capable of having created it in less than the time it takes to bat an eyelid.\n4. Allah transcends His creation.\n5. The idolaters think of resurrection to be farfetched, despite clear evidences for it.",
  32012:
      "The criminals will soon emerge on the Day of Resurrection, bowing their heads in humiliation due to their rejection of the resurrection, feeling ashamed, and saying: Our Lord! We have seen the resurrection that we used to reject. Now we hear the confirmation of that which the Messengers brought from You. Therefore, return us to the worldly life so we can do good deeds that will make You pleased with us. Indeed, we are now convinced of the resurrection and the truth of whatever the Messengers brought. If you were to see the criminals in that state, you would see something genuinely profound.",
  32013:
      "And if I wished to give every soul guidance and success, I would have made them [follow the guidance]. However, it was necessary to pass the decree through wisdom and justice that I would fill Hell on the Day of Resurrection with the disbelievers from both assemblies of jinn and humanity because they chose the path of disbelief and error over the path of belief and steadfastness.",
  32014:
      "And on the Day of Resurrection, they will be told in rebuke and censure: Now taste the punishment due to your heedlessness of the meeting with Allah on the Day of Resurrection for accountability in the worldly life. I shall leave you in the punishment without caring for how much you suffer from it. Taste the punishment of the everlasting Fire that will not end because of the sins you used to commit in the worldly life.",
  32015:
      "After mentioning the condition of criminals, Allah mentions the condition of the believers, stating: \n Only those who believe in Our verses revealed to Our Messenger prostrate to Allah when reminded, exalting, and praising Him. They are not arrogant from worshipping Him or prostrating to Him in any condition.",
  32016:
      "They stay from their beds to worship Allah, supplicating to Him in their prayers, fearing His punishment, and hoping for His mercy. They also spend the wealth Allah has given them in His path.",
  32017:
      "So, no one knows what Allah has prepared for them that brings coolness and joy to the eyes as a reward for the good deeds they did in this world. Due to its magnitude, it is a reward that no one except Allah can fully comprehend.",
  32018:
      "The one who believes in Allah, acts upon His commands, and avoids His prohibitions is unlike the one who disobeys Him. According to Allah, the two groups are not equal in reward.",
  32019:
      "As for those who believe in Allah and do good deeds, the reward prepared for them is gardens in which they shall remain as an honor from Allah to them and a reward for the good deeds they used to do in this world.",
  32020:
      "As for those who left the obedience of Allah by disbelieving and committing sins, the abode prepared for them on the Day of Resurrection is the Fire in which they shall remain forever. They will be returned to it every time they attempt to come out of it. It will be said to them, rebukingly: Taste the punishment of the Fire you used to deny in the worldly life when your messengers used to warn you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Bringing faith on the Day of Judgement will not be of benefit to the disbelievers, because of them now being in the abode of requital not the abode of actions.\n2. The danger of being unmindful, in this life, of the standing before Allah on the Day of Judgement.\n3. Standing in prayer at night is way of the believers.\n4. Allah has prepared for His Allah-conscious servants things which no eye has ever seen, no ear has ever heard of, and no human heart has ever imagined.\n5. Just as the believer and transgressor do not match in qualities, they are not equal in requital either.",
  32021:
      "We will make these disbelievers who left the obedience of their Lord and do not repent suffer trials and afflictions in this worldly life before the major punishment, for perhaps due to those worldly afflictions, they will repent to Allah.",
  32022:
      "There is no one more wrong than the one who is admonished with the words of Allah but does not take heed and turns away without caring about them. Indeed, We will inevitably take retribution from the criminals because they commit disbelief and sins and turn away from the verses of Allah.",
  32023:
      "Verily, We gave Moses the Torah, so, O Messenger, do not be in doubt over you having met Moses in the Night Journey and the Ascension. We made the Book revealed to Moses a guide for the Israelites to stop them from falling into misguidance.",
  32024:
      "And We made some Israelites be leaders whom the people would emulate and follow. They became guides to the truth when they were patient in calling others to Allah, complied with the commands of Allah, avoided His prohibitions, and firmly believed in His words revealed to their Messengers.",
  32025:
      "O Messenger, indeed, your Lord is the One who will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection in matters they disputed in this world. He will make the one on truth clear from the one on falsehood and recompense each with what they deserve.",
  32026:
      "Are these people blind that they cannot see how many of the previous nations We destroyed before them? Here they are, walking past dwellings previously resided in by those who were destroyed, yet they do not take heed of their state. Indeed, the destruction of the previous nations due to their disbelief is a lesson from which the truth of their messengers, who came to them from Allah, can be proven. Will these rejecters of the words of Allah then not listen attentively using their intellects?",
  32027:
      "Do these resurrection deniers not see that We send rainwater to a barren land where there are no plants and then bring out the crops by that water, from which they and their cattle eat? Do they not see that and understand that whoever causes the barren earth to grow can revive the dead?",
  32028:
      "The rejectors of resurrection say while seeking the punishment in haste: When is this judgment that you claim between you and us on the Day of Resurrection, such that our abode will be the Fire, and your abode will be Paradise?",
  32029:
      "Say to them, O Messenger: This promise is the Day of Resurrection. It is the Day of Judgment between the slaves of Allah when those who disbelieve in Allah in this world will not benefit from believing in it after witnessing the Day of Resurrection, nor will they be given respite to repent to their Lord and turn back to Him.",
  32030:
      "Therefore, O Messenger, turn away from these people once they persist in their deviance and wait for what will befall them. Indeed, they await the punishment that you promised them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The punishment of a disbeliever in this world is a means to his repenting.\n2. Turning away from the verses of Allah is dangerous.\n3. Proof of our Prophet (peace be upon him) meeting Moses (peace be upon him) on the Night Journey and the Ascension.\n4. Patience and firm belief are qualities of the leaders in religion.\n5. Sending rain and causing the earth to grow is proof of resurrection on the Day of Judgement.\n6. Repentance from sins can only be done in the world, before seeing death.",
  33000:
      "The Combined Forces (Surah Al-Ahzab)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDeclaring Allah's care for His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and protecting him and his family.\n•    Explanation:",
  33001:
      "O Prophet, remain firm, you and those with you, upon piety, through complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, and fear Him alone. Do not obey the disbelievers and hypocrites in what they desire. Allah knows the plans of the disbelievers and hypocrites and is Wise in His creation and management.",
  33002:
      "And follow the revelation your Lord reveals to you. Allah is Aware of what you do. Nothing escapes Him, and He shall reward you for your actions.",
  33003:
      "And rely on Allah alone in all your affairs. He is sufficient as a protector for His slaves who trust Him.",
  33004:
      "Just as Allah has not placed two hearts in the chest of any man, as some of them believe, He did not make wives like mothers with respect to being forbidden to marry. Likewise, He did not make adopted sons like biological sons because Zihār, which is for a man to make his wife unlawful for himself, and claiming the children of others as one's own are practices of ignorance, which Islam has nullified. That making unlawful through Zihār and taking as sons those whose fathers you are not is a statement you repeat with your mouths, which has no reality. The wife is not a mother, nor is the adopted son rightfully for the claimant. Allah says the truth, so His slaves practice it, and He guides them towards the path of truth.",
  33005:
      "Attribute those you claim to be your sons towards their natural fathers because attributing them towards them is just in the eyes of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers to whom you can attribute them, then they are your brothers in religion and freed slaves, so call them \"O brother\" or \"O cousin.\" There is no sin on you if one of you makes a mistake and attributes a claimed son towards his claimant, but you will be sinful if you intentionally say that. Allah is forgiving to those of His slaves who repent and Merciful to them as He did not punish them due to mistakes.",
  33006:
      "The Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has more right over the believers than themselves in whatever he calls them to, even if they incline towards something else. And his wives are like mothers to all the believers. Hence it is unlawful for any believer to marry any of them after he passes away. Relatives are more deserving of one another in inheritance by Allah's decree than the believers and those who migrated for Allah's cause, who would previously inherit by means of the contractual agreement between themselves at the beginning of Islam. Then Allah abrogated their inheriting from one another after that. Except if you, O believers, do good towards your close associates besides the inheritors by making a bequest for them and being kind to them, then that is your right. That is a decree inscribed in the Preserved Tablet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There is nobody above being commanded to good and forbidden from evil.\n2. Likening wives to mothers is a grave evil and lie.\n3. It is unlawful to claim a child as one’s own.\n4. Accountability for unintentional mistakes has been removed from this nation.\n5. It is necessary to give preference to what the Prophet commands (peace be upon him) before one’s own desires.\n6. The high status of the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the unlawfulness of marrying them after him, as they are the mothers of the believers.\n7. All blood relatives are legitimate inheritors.",
  33007:
      "O Messenger, remember when We took a firm covenant from the prophets that they will worship Allah alone and not associate any partner with Him, and that they will convey the revelation sent to them. And We have taken it especially from you, and from Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, son of Mary. We have taken a firm covenant from them to fulfill the conveying of Allah's messages they have been entrusted with.",
  33008:
      "Allah took this firm covenant from the prophets to ask the truthful Messengers about their truthfulness to silence the disbelievers. Allah has prepared for those who disbelieve in Him and His Messengers a painful punishment on the Day of Resurrection, which is the Fire.",
  33009:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated, remember Allah's favor upon you when the armies of the disbelievers came to Medina, prepared to fight you, and the hypocrites and Jews supported them. Then We sent upon them the eastern winds through which the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم was helped, and We sent armies of angels you did not see. Then the disbelievers turned away, fleeing, unable to do anything. And Allah is Seeing what you do. None of that is hidden from Him, and He shall recompense you for your deeds.",
  33010:
      "That was when the disbelievers came to you from the top and bottom of the valley and the East and West when their eyes were fixed upon the enemy. The hearts reached the throats due to intense fear. You were thinking different thoughts regarding Allah; at times, you thought you would be aided, and other times, you despaired [of His help].",
  33011:
      "In that situation, in the Battle of the Trench, the believers were tested by what they encountered from the swarming of their enemies against them. And they were severely disturbed by the intensity of fear. This test revealed who was the [true] believer and [exposed] the hypocrite.",
  33012:
      "On that Day, the hypocrites and those of weak faith, whose hearts were full of doubts, said: Allah and His Messenger's promise of victory and being established on this land is false and baseless.",
  33013:
      "O Messenger, remember when a group of hypocrites said to the people of Medina: O people of Yathrib (the name for Medina before Islam), there is no stability for you next to the trench, so return to your homes. A group was seeking permission from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم to return to their homes, claiming that their homes were exposed to the enemy. However, they were not exposed as they claimed. They were only seeking to flee from their enemy through this pretext.",
  33014:
      "And if the enemy were to enter upon them in Medina from all its sides and ask them to return to disbelieving and associating partners with Allah, they would grant their enemy this. They would not hold themselves back from rebelling and turning back to disbelief except for a few of them.",
  33015:
      "And these hypocrites had promised Allah after they fled from fighting on the occasion of Uhud that if Allah were to make them witness another battle, they would definitely fight their enemy and not flee out of fear. However, they broke their promise, and the slave is responsible for the promises he makes to Allah and will soon be questioned about it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Messengers of Resolve have a special status.\n2. Allah helps His believing servants when difficulties befall.\n3. The test which the believers went through in the Battle of the Trench was great.\n4. The hypocrites desert the believers during tribulations.\n5. False claims and breaking pacts is a quality of the hypocrites.",
  33016:
      "O Messenger, tell these people: Fleeing will never benefit you if you flee from fighting out of fear of death or being killed because the appointed times are fixed. Fighting does not bring it closer, nor does fleeing delay it. And if you do manage to escape and your time has not come, you will only enjoy life for a short while longer.",
  33017:
      "O Messenger, tell them: Who can save you from Allah if He wants you to die or be killed, which you hate so much, or if He intends for you the safety and good you hope for? There is nobody to save you from that. These hypocrites will not find for themselves any associate besides Allah to take care of their affairs nor any helper to protect them from Allah punishing them.",
  33018:
      "Allah knows those of you who hold others back from fighting alongside Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and those who say to their brothers: Come to us and do not fight alongside him, lest you get killed, because we fear you will get killed. These forsaken people do not come to battle or participate in it except rarely, to remove blame from themselves, not to help Allah and His Messenger.",
  33019:
      "O believers, they are miserly with their wealth, so they do not help you by spending it; miserly with their souls, therefore they do not fight alongside you; and miserly with their love, thus they do not love you. Then when fear at the time of meeting the enemy comes, you will see them looking at you with their eyes wide open, rolling out of cowardice, just as the eyes of a person suffering the pangs of death roll. But when fear leaves them and they become content, they harm you verbally with abusive, sharp tongues. They are greedy for war booty, which they look for. Those described with these qualities have not truly believed, so Allah nullified the reward of their actions, and this was easy for Allah.",
  33020:
      "These cowards think the coalition conspiring to fight Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, and the believers will never leave until they destroy them. And suppose it is decreed that the coalition come another time. In that case, these cowardly hypocrites will wish they were not in Medina and with the Bedouins, asking about you: What happened to you after your enemies fought you? Even if they were amongst you, O believers, they would not have fought alongside you except a little, so do not pay attention to them or feel sorry for them.",
  33021:
      "There has been for you an excellent example in what Allah's Messenger said, carried out, and practiced, for he presented his own noble self and personally engaged in battle, so how after that can you be miserly with your souls over his soul? Only he who is hopeful of the Last Day, works for it, and remembers Allah abundantly will follow Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. As for the one who is not hopeful of the Last Day and does not remember Allah abundantly, he does not follow His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  33022:
      "When the believers saw the groups that had gathered to fight them, they said: This is the test and help Allah and His Messenger promised us [would happen], and Allah and His Messenger were true in this, for it has occurred. And seeing the groups only increased their conviction and submission to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The appointed times are fixed; fighting cannot bring them closer nor can fleeing from them distance them.\n2. Hindering from striving in Allah’s way in always the condition of the hypocrites.\n3. The hypocrites are few in number at the time of anxiety but many at the time of desiring something.\n4. The hypocrites do not bear worry for the nation.\n5. The Messenger (peace be upon him) is a role model for the believers in his sayings and actions.\n6. Reliance in Allah and submitting to Him is from the qualities of the believers.",
  33023:
      "Amongst the believers are men who were faithful to Allah, so they fulfilled what they promised Him: firmness and patience in striving in Allah's way. From them are those who died or were killed in Allah's path, while others await martyrdom in His cause. These believers did not change what they promised Allah as the hypocrites did with their promises.",
  33024:
      "So that Allah rewards the truthful who fulfilled what they promised Allah, by their honesty and fulfilling their promises, and punishes the hypocrites who broke their pledges if He wishes, by making them die before they can repent from their disbelief or by accepting their repentance by enabling them to repent. And Allah forgives the one who repents for his sins and is Merciful to him.",
  33025:
      "Allah repelled the Quraysh, Ghatafan, and those with them with distress, disappointment, and failure to get what they had hoped for. They were unsuccessful in destroying the believers as they intended, and Allah sufficed the believers [so they did not have to] fight them by sending winds and the angels. Allah is Powerful and Mighty; nobody attempts to overpower Allah except that He will be defeated and disheartened.",
  33026:
      "Allah brought the Jews who helped them down from their fortresses in which they would protect themselves from their enemy, and Allah put fear into their hearts. O believers, you will kill one group and take another captive.",
  33027:
      "After destroying them, Allah gave you possession of their land, along with the crops and date trees they contained. He made you owners of their homes and other wealth as well as owners of the land of Khaybar, which you have yet to step foot on, but you will soon walk on it. This is a promise and glad tidings for the believers. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  33028:
      "O Prophet, tell your wives if they seek increased spending [on them], at times you do not have more to spend: If you desire the worldly life and the adornment it contains, let me give you the provisions given to a divorced woman, and I will divorce you in the best of manners without causing you any harm.",
  33029:
      "But if you desire the pleasure of Allah and His Messenger, and you seek Paradise in the Afterlife, remain patient with your circumstances. Allah has prepared an excellent reward for those who do good through patience and fine companionship.",
  33030:
      "O wives of the Prophet, whoever amongst you commits an open sin, her punishment will be doubled on the Day of Resurrection due to her status and rank, and to protect the honor of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. And this increase is easy for Allah to do.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Companions of Allah’s Messenger (peace be upon him) have been commended, which is a great honour for them.\n2. When they are mindful of Allah, His assistance and support come from where they do not expect.\n3. The result of treachery of those who supported the coalition was grievous.\n4. The wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) choosing Allah and His Messenger is a proof to their strong faith.",
  33031:
      "Whoever continues to obey Allah and His Messenger from among you and does a righteous deed that pleases Allah, We will give her twice as much reward as other women. We have prepared for her in the Hereafter a generous reward: Paradise.",
  33032:
      "O wives of the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, you are not like other women in terms of virtue and honor. Rather, you are in a position of virtue and honor that no one else can attain if you comply with Allah's commands and avoid His prohibitions. Therefore, do not soften your tone or beautify your voice if you speak to non-Mahram (unrelated/foreign) men so those who have diseases of hypocrisy and forbidden lust in their hearts will not be tempted. And say something far from questionable by speaking seriously, without jest, as much as possible.",
  33033:
      "And remain in your homes; do not go out of them unnecessarily. Do not display your charms as women did before Islam in order to seduce men. Perform prayer properly, give the Zakat (obligatory alms) from your wealth, and obey Allah and His Messenger. O wives and relatives of Allah's Messenger, indeed, Allah (may He be Exalted) wants to remove evil and harm from you. He wants to purify your souls by adorning them with the virtues of morality, thoroughly cleansing them from their vices, and leaving no filth behind.",
  33034:
      "And mention the verses of Allah recited in your homes revealed to His Messenger and the purified Sunnah (the authentic prophetic tradition) of His Messenger. Allah favored you with kindness when He made you stay in the homes of His Prophet. He was Aware of you when He selected you as wives for His Messenger and chose you as mothers for all the believers of his nation.",
  33035:
      "Indeed, the males who submit to Allah and the females who submit; the male believers in Allah and the female believers; the males who obey Allah and the females who obey; the males who are truthful in their belief and their statements and the females who are truthful; the males who are patient in obedience, in refraining from sins and during trials and the females who are patient; the males who give in obligatory and optional charity from their wealth and the females who give in charity; the males who keep obligatory and optional fasts and the females who fast; the males who guard their private parts from exposure to those who are forbidden from seeing them and from the immorality of fornication and anything leading to it, and the females who guard their private parts; and the males who remember Allah abundantly in private and in public and the females who remember Allah, Allah has prepared His special forgiveness for them from their sins, and an immense reward on the Day of Resurrection which is Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) have virtue over all other women.\n2. From among the guidelines of the Qur’an towards the Muslim woman are: Prohibition of speaking softly and exposing beauty publicly, and instruction to remain in the home except when necessary.\n3. The virtue of the members of the household of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and his wives.\n4. Men and women are alike as regards to faith and good deeds, except for some deeds which the legislator has excluded for each gender (taking into consideration the unique natures of each).",
  33036:
      "And it is incorrect for a male or female believer if Allah and His Messenger pass judgment on a matter between them, that they choose between accepting or rejecting it. Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has clearly strayed from the straight path.",
  33037:
      "And when you say, O Messenger, to whom Allah blessed with Islam, and you granted manumission (referring to Zaid bin Haritha, may Allah be pleased with him, when he came to consult about the matter of divorcing his wife Zainab bint Jahsh), you told him: Hold on to your wife and do not divorce her, and fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding his prohibitions. You hid within yourself, O Messenger, what Allah had revealed to you about your marriage to Zainab, fearing people's reaction when Allah reveals Zaid's divorce and your eventual marriage to her. But Allah is more worthy of fearing regarding this matter. So when Zayd's content heart lost interest in Zainab and divorced her, We married you to her. This was ordained to demonstrate that there is no sin upon the believers to marry the wives of their adopted children if they divorce them and the iddah (waiting period) finishes. Allah's command will always come to pass; nothing can stop or obstruct it.",
  33038:
      "There is no sin or restriction on the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم in what Allah permitted of marrying his adopted daughter-in-law. In doing so, he is following the Sunnah (way) of the Prophets before him, and he is no different from the messengers. The Prophet had no choice or opinion in completing this marriage and invalidating the adoption Allah decreed. It was an effective judgment that cannot be reversed.",
  33039:
      "These prophets who convey the messages of Allah [that were sent to them] to their nations do not fear anyone except Allah (may He be Exalted). Likewise, they ignore what others say when they do whatever Allah has permitted. It is enough for Allah to preserve the deeds of His slaves to hold them accountable for it, and He will recompense them accordingly. If it is good, then with good. If it is bad, then with bad.",
  33040:
      "Muhammad is not the father of any of your men, so he is not the father of Zayd. Therefore, marrying Zayd's wife is not forbidden for him if Zayd divorces her. However, he is Allah's Messenger sent to the people and the Seal of the Prophets, so there is no prophet after him. Allah is the Knower of everything, and nothing is hidden from Him of the affairs of His slaves.",
  33041:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, remember Allah abundantly with your hearts, tongues, and limbs.",
  33042:
      "Exalt Him (may He be Exalted) though the Tasbeeh (praising Allah by saying Subḥan-Allah) and Tahleel (proclaiming His oneness by saying La-ilaha-illallah) at the beginning and end of the day due to their virtue.",
  33043:
      "He is the One who has mercy on you [O believers] and praises you. Moreover, His angels pray for you to bring you out of the darkness of disbelief into the light of faith. Allah is merciful to the believers, so He does not punish them if they obey Him by fulfilling His command and refraining from what He has prohibited.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory for a believer to submit to the decree of Allah and humble himself to it.\n2. Allah is aware of whatever is in the hearts.\n3. From among the virtues of the mother of the believers Zaynab bint Jahsh is: Allah fulfilled her marriage contract from above the seven heavens.\n4. The virtue of remembering Allah a lot, especially in the morning an evening.",
  33044:
      "The salutation of the believers on the day they meet their Lord is peace and safety from all evil. Moreover, Allah has prepared for them a generous reward, which is His Paradise, as a recompense for their obedience to Him and for staying away from His disobedience.",
  33045:
      "O Prophet, indeed, We have sent you to the people as a witness against them that you have conveyed the Message (Islam). Moreover, to bring good tidings to the believers of what Allah has prepared for them (Paradise) and to frighten the disbelievers of what He has prepared for them of His torment.",
  33046:
      "We also sent you as a caller to Allah's Oneness and obedience to Him by His command. Furthermore, We sent you as an illuminated lamp to enlighten all who want guidance.",
  33047:
      "Tell the believers in Allah, who do what He has legislated for them, of something that will please them: that they will have a great favor from Allah (may He be Exalted), which includes their victory in this world and their success in the Hereafter by entering Paradise.",
  33048:
      "Do not obey the disbelievers and the hypocrites in their call to prevent people from Allah's religion, but turn away from them. Perhaps this will make it more likely for them to believe in what you have brought them. Also, rely on Allah in all your affairs. Among that is your victory against your enemies. Allah is sufficient as a trustee upon whom the slaves can rely in all their affairs in this world and the Hereafter.",
  33049:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, when you tie the knot of marriage with a believing women, and then you divorce them before consummating the marriage with them, they are not required to go through the waiting period for you, regardless of whether it is through menstrual cycles or by counting months. This is because their wombs being free is known because you have not consummated the marriage with them. Also, give them some compensation according to your financial situation to console their broken emotions due to divorce and clear the way for them to return to their families without causing them any inconvenience.",
  33050:
      "O Prophet, We have permitted for you your wives whom you gave their dowries, and We have made it lawful for you in what you possess of the slave-girls that Allah has bestowed you from the captives. We also made the marriage of your paternal uncle's daughters, paternal aunts' daughters, maternal uncle's daughters, and maternal aunts' daughters who migrated with you from Mecca to Medina lawful for you. We also made it legal for you to marry a believing woman who gave herself to you without a dowry if you wanted to marry her. This type of marriage, without a dowry, is exclusive to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and is not permissible to anyone else from his Nation. Verily, We knew what we have made obligatory upon the believers regarding their wives, where they are not permitted to marry more than four women at once. We also know what we have legislated for them regarding their slave women, as they may enjoy whomever they want without restriction in number. We have also permitted for you from those mentioned earlier what We have not made permissible for others so that there is no distress or hardship upon you. Allah forgives those of His slaves who repent and is Merciful to them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Being patient upon harm is one of the qualities of successful callers towards Allah.\n2. It is permissible to divorce a woman before consummating the marriage.\n3. There is no waiting period for a woman who has been divorced before her marriage was consummated.\n4. It is preferable for the husband to give the wife he has just divorced before consummating the marriage, some wealth as a consolation.\n5. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was privileged by it being permissible for him to marry a woman who had presented herself to him unreservedly without dowry, although he did not take up the privilege.",
  33051:
      "O Messenger, postpone whoever of your wives you want to, so you do not spend the night with her. Likewise, join with whom you want to, so you spend the night with whichever of your wives you wish. Moreover, whomever you ask to spend the night from those you have postponed, there is no sin on you [in that]. This choice and broadening of options [for you] are more likely to make your wives content, comforted, and satisfied with what you have given them all. They know you have not left an obligation or skimped a right. Allah knows what is in your hearts, O men, of the inclination to some women over others. Allah knows His slaves' deeds; nothing is hidden from Him. He is Forbearing and does not hasten their punishment so they may repent to Him.",
  33052:
      "It is not permissible for you, O Messenger, to marry women other than your wives who are already in your custody. Moreover, neither is it permissible for you to divorce them or divorce some of them to marry other women, even if you like the beauty of whom you want to marry from women other than them. However, it is permissible for you to be pleased with what you possess from slave women without limitation to a specific number, and Allah is the guardian of everything. This ruling indicates the virtue of the mothers of the believers, as it was forbidden to divorce them and marry other than them.",
  33053:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except after he permits you to enter them by inviting you to food. Furthermore, do not sit for long waiting for the food to be cooked, but if you are invited to food, then enter, and after you eat, leave. Also, do not remain behind talking and socializing with each other because remaining behind causes inconvenience to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, but he feels embarrassed to ask you to leave. However, Allah is not ashamed to command you to do what is right, so He (the Exalted) commanded you to leave so that you do not cause inconvenience to him صلى الله عليه وسلم by staying for too long. If you ask for something from the wives of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم (i.e., utensils, etc.), then ask from behind a curtain, not face to face, in a manner that you cannot see them with your eyes. This is to protect them due to the importance and position of Allah's Messenger. Asking them from behind a curtain, O believers, is purer for your hearts and theirs, so the Devil cannot influence them through whispers and beautifying evil. Likewise, you, O believers, should not harm Allah's Messenger by staying to talk and socialize nor by marrying his wives after his death, for they are the mothers of the believers. It is also not permissible for anyone to marry his mother. Such abuse (including marrying his wives after his death) is forbidden and considered a grave sin by Allah.",
  33054:
      "If you show something of your deeds or keep it to yourselves secretly, nothing of it will be hidden from Allah. Indeed, Allah knows everything. Nothing of your acts or anything else is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for your deeds. If good, then good, and if evil, then evil.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is most knowledgeable and the most forbearing.\n2. It is obligatory to maintain good manners with the Messenger (peace be upon him) by not entering his houses without permission, and not remaining too long after eating upon his invitation.\n3. Bashfulness is one of the qualities of the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n4. It is necessary to maintain the stature of the mothers of the believers from the wives of the Prophet peace be upon him.\n5. It is forbidden to marry the mothers of the believers after the demise of the Prophet (peace be upon him).",
  33055:
      "There is no sin on the wives of the Messenger if their fathers, sons, brothers, nephews (brothers' sons), and the sons of their sisters by blood or breast-feeding, to see them and talk to them without a curtain. Moreover, there is no sin on them if the believing women or the slaves they possess speak to them without a curtain. Fear Allah, O believing women, in whatever He (may He be Exalted) has commanded you to do and forbade you from, for He is watching what appears from you and what you do.",
  33056:
      "Indeed, Allah praises the Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم in the presence of His angels, and His angels pray for him. O you who believe in Allah and do whatever He has legislated for His slaves, pray for the Messenger and greet him with peace abundantly.",
  33057:
      "When Allah commanded that the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم be venerated and prayed for, He forbade any harm to befall upon him, stating: \n Indeed, for those who harm Allah and His Messenger through speech or action, Allah has removed and expelled them from the vastness of His mercy in this world and the Hereafter. Moreover, He has prepared a humiliating torment for them in the Hereafter for what they have done by harming His Messenger.",
  33058:
      "Those who harm the believing men and women by speech or actions, without them having committed any wrong or crime that necessitates that harm, carry the burden of openly lying and sinning.",
  33059:
      "O Prophet, say to your wives, daughters, and the women of the believers: Let the outer robes you wear hang loosely over you so that your bodies are not revealed to unrelated men. That is closer to distinguishing them as free women, so they are not subjected to abuse like the slave girls are. Allah forgives the sins of whichever of His slaves repents, and He is merciful to them.",
  33060:
      "Suppose the hypocrites do not stop their hypocrisy [by harboring disbelief and demonstrating Islam]. And suppose those whose hearts are immoral due to their attachment to their desires and those who bring false news in Medina to divide the believers do not cease. In that case, We will command you, O Messenger, to punish them. Moreover, We will give you power over them. Then they will not reside with you in Medina except for a short period, to destroy or expel them from it because of their corruption on Earth.",
  33061:
      "They would be expelled from the mercy of Allah. Moreover, they would be seized and executed wherever they were found because of their hypocrisy and spreading corruption on Earth.",
  33062:
      "This is Allah's established practice against the hypocrites if they reveal their hypocrisy. Allah's established practice is fixed, and you will never find any change in it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The lofty high status of the prophet (peace be upon him) in the sight of Allah and His angels.\n2. It is forbidden to cause inconvenience to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in any way or form, to him personally or to his family members.\n3. It is forbidden to cause inconvenience to the believers without reason.\n4. Hypocrisy is a cause of punishment afflicting the hypocrite.",
  33063:
      "The polytheists ask you, O Messenger, a question of denial and rejection, and the Jews also ask you, regarding the final Hour: When will it occur? Say to them: The knowledge of the Hour is with Allah, so I have no knowledge of it. What could make you, O Messenger, feel that the Hour is close?",
  33064:
      "Indeed, Allah (may He be Exalted) has expelled the disbelievers from His mercy and prepared a flaring fire that awaits them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  33065:
      "They will remain in the torment of that fire [prepared for them] forever. They will not find a guardian that benefits them in it, nor a supporter who wards its torment off them.",
  33066:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, their faces will be turned in the Hellfire. They will say out of severe regret and remorse: If only we obeyed Allah by doing what He commanded us to and avoiding what He prohibited us from, and obeyed the Messenger in what he brought from his Lord.",
  33067:
      "They will bring a flimsy and invalid argument and say: Our Lord, indeed, we obeyed our leaders and the elders of our people, so they misled us from the straight path.",
  33068:
      "O our Lord, give these leaders and elders who misled us from the straight path twice as much torment as You have given us for misleading us. Moreover, expel them out of Your mercy with a great expulsion.",
  33069:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, do not harm your Messenger. If you do, you would be like those who hurt Moses by saying that he had a defect in his body, so Allah absolved him of what they said, and it became clear to them that he was innocent of what they said about him. Moses is highly ranked according to Allah. His requesting supplications were not rejected, nor were his endeavors disappointed.",
  33070:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, be mindful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding what He has prohibited, and speak rightly and truthfully.",
  33071:
      "Indeed, if you are mindful of Allah and speak correctly, Allah will rectify your deeds for you, accept them from you, erase your sins, and not hold you accountable for them. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has achieved a great success that no other success can come close to, which is gaining Allah's satisfaction and entering Paradise.",
  33072:
      "Indeed, We presented the legislated duties and what is kept of money and secrets to the heavens, the Earth, and the mountains. However, they refrained from bearing them and feared consequences, but man carried them. Indeed, he was unjust to himself, ignorant of the consequences of bearing them.",
  33073:
      "The human carried it as per the decree of Allah. So that Allah may punish the men and women who are hypocrites and polytheists for their hypocrisy and associating partners with Allah and forgive the believing men and women who carried the burden of obligation well. Allah forgives the sins of those who repent of His slaves and is Merciful to them.",
  34000:
      "Sheba (Surah Saba)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing people's different situations regarding blessings and Allah's established practice to change them.\n•    Explanation:\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The knowledge of the hour is exclusive to Allah.\n2. The disbeliever will severely regret his disbelief and negligence on the Day of Judgement.\n3. The followers shifting the responsibility of their deviance to their superiors will not absolve them of accountability.\n4. The prohibition of causing inconvenience to the Prophets through speech or action is severe.\n5. Being mindful of Allah and speaking the truth is a means of entering Paradise and being safe from the hellfire.\n6. The heavy responsibility/burden on the shoulders of mankind.",
  34001:
      "All praise belongs to Allah, to whom belongs everything that is in the heavens and everything that is on Earth, by way of being His creation, in His ownership and under His control. And for Him is all praise in the Hereafter; He is the Wise in His creation and disposing of His affairs, and the Knower of the state of His slaves. Nothing is hidden from Him.",
  34002:
      "He knows everything that enters the earth, i.e., water, seeds, and minerals; He knows whatever comes from it, i.e., plants, etc.; He knows what descends from the heavens, i.e., rain, angels, and sustenance, and He knows whatever ascends to the heavens, i.e., angels, the deeds of His slaves, and their souls. He is merciful to His believing slaves and forgiving of the sins of whoever repents to Him.",
  34003:
      "Those disbelieving in Allah said: The Hour will never come to us. O Messenger, say to them: No, by Allah, the very Hour you reject will definitely come to you, but its time is only known to Allah. He (may He be Exalted) is the Knower of whatever is hidden, such as the Hour; even the equivalent of the smallest ant is not hidden from His knowledge, nor anything smaller than that in the heavens or on Earth or larger, except that it is recorded in a clear book, which is the Preserved Tablet in which everything that is to happen until the Day of Resurrection is recorded.",
  34004:
      "Allah has recorded everything He has in the Preserved Tablet to recompense those who believe in Him and do good deeds. They will receive forgiveness from Allah for their sins; He will not take them to account for them, and on the Day of Resurrection, they will receive generous sustenance, His Paradise.",
  34005:
      "As for those who strived to refute the revealed verses of Allah and said they were sorcery, and claimed that Our Messenger is a fortune-teller, a sorcerer, and a poet, they will receive the most severe and terrible punishment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  34006:
      "Some scholars of the people of the book testify that the revelation Allah revealed to you is the truth without doubt and that it guides towards the path of Allah, the Mighty, who no one can overpower and who is praiseworthy in this world and the Hereafter.",
  34007:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah told one another in astonishment and to mock whatever the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم brought: Shall we lead you to a man who will tell you that when you die and decompose into pieces, you will be brought back to life again?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The knowledge of Allah is vast and encompasses everything.\n2. It is permissible to emphasise information by taking an oath in front of one who denies it.\n3. The people of knowledge have a virtue.\n4. The idolaters’ rejection of resurrection is a rejection of the power of Allah who created them.",
  34008:
      "And they said: Has this man fabricated and attributed a lie to Allah, claiming that we shall be resurrected after we die, or is he insane, talking nonsense? It is not as these people say; rather, the reality is that those who do not believe in the Hereafter will suffer a severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection and are very far astray.",
  34009:
      "Do these rejectors of the resurrection not see the earth [that We have made] in front of them and the sky above them? If We wished the ground beneath their feet to swallow them up, We would have caused it to happen, and if We wished to send down portions/pieces of the punishment from the heavens, We would have done so. Indeed, there is a clear sign in that for every repentant slave through which he witnesses the Power of Allah. The One capable of doing that can resurrect you after your death and the decomposition of your body.",
  34010:
      "And verily, We granted David (peace be upon him) messengership and a kingdom, and said to the mountains: O Mountains, make exaltation together with David. We said the same to the birds. We also made iron soft for him so he could make whatever tools he wanted.",
  34011:
      "O David, make broad armor which will protect your soldiers from the attacks of their enemies, and make the rivets in proportion to the rings so that they are not too fine such that they do not lodge in them, nor too thick such that they do not fit in them either. And do good deeds; [as] I am watching over your actions, none of them are hidden from Me, and I shall recompense you for them.",
  34012:
      "And We subjugated the wind for Solomon, the son of David. It would blow the distance of a month in the morning and the same distance in the evening. We also made springs of copper flow for him so that he could make whatever he wanted from it, together with employing the Jinn who would work in front of him by the command of his Lord. Whenever any of the Jinn would deviate from whatever We commanded them to do, We would let them taste the punishment of a raging fire.",
  34013:
      "These Jinn constructed for him whatever he wanted from places of worship, palaces, and lofty structures. As well as whatever containers he wanted, like giant water basins and fixed cooking pots that were so big they could not move. We said to them: O family of David, show gratitude to Allah for the blessings He has bestowed upon you. Very few of My slaves are grateful to Me for the blessings I grant them.",
  34014:
      "When We decreed for Solomon to die, the Jinn did not realize he had passed away until the woodworms had eaten away at the staff he was leaning on. When he fell, it became clear to the Jinn that they do not know the unseen because if they had known, they would not have remained subdued, continuing to carry out the difficult tasks imposed upon them, which they were doing for Solomon (peace be upon him) thinking that he was watching them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah honoured His Prophet David with messengership and kingship; by making the mountains and birds echo His glorification, and by softening iron for him.\n2. Allah honoured His Prophet Solomon (peace be upon him) with messengership and rule.\n3. The blessings of Allah require gratitude to be shown for them.\n4. Knowledge of the Ghaib is exclusive to Allah, so there is no basis in the claim that the Jinn or anyone else know anything from the Ghaib.",
  34015:
      "After mentioning what He blessed David and his son Solomon (peace be upon them) with, Allah mentions what He blessed the people of Sheba with. The difference is that David and Solomon (peace be upon them) were thankful to Allah, but the people of Sheba were ungrateful to Him. He states: \n In the dwellings where the tribe of Sheba lived, there was a clear sign of Allah's power and His favor on them, and the clear sign was two gardens: one on the right and the other on the left. We said to them: Eat of the provision of your Lord and thank Him for His favors. This is a pleasant city, and your Lord, Allah, is a forgiving Lord who absolves the sins of those who repent to Him.",
  34016:
      "But they turned away from thanking Allah and believing in His messengers, so We punished them by turning their favors into difficulties. Then, We sent a strong flood upon them, which destroyed their dam and flooded their fields. Thus, We replaced their two pleasant gardens with two that gave bitter fruit and contained fruitless tamarisk trees and a few lote trees.",
  34017:
      "That change occurred to their favors because of their disbelief and turning away from being thankful for those favors. We do not punish so severely except one who rejects Allah's favors.",
  34018:
      "We put many neighboring cities between the people of Sheba in Yemen and the cities of the blessed land of Levant, making the distance to travel easier for them so they may pass through these cities and towns, stopping when needed, without any difficulty until they reach the land of Levant. And we announced: Travel through them day and night in complete security from any enemy, hunger, or thirst.",
  34019:
      "But they arrogantly rejected Allah's favor of facilitating their journey and said: O Our Lord, make our journeys longer by removing those cities in between so that we can taste the exhaustion of traveling and make clear the excellence of our riding mounts. They wronged themselves by arrogantly rejecting Allah's favor and turning away from thanking Him, so We made them into tales which those after them talk of. We separated them in the lands so they could not reach each other. That which has been mentioned, namely favoring the people of Sheba and taking retribution from them, is a lesson for every person who is patient in his obedience to Allah and bearing what he has been afflicted with, and is thankful for Allah's favors on him.",
  34020:
      "Iblis confirmed through them what he assumed, i.e., that he is able to lead them astray and misguide them from the truth, as they followed him in disbelief and misguidance except for a group of believers who destroyed his hopes by not following him.",
  34021:
      "Iblis has no power over them, through which he can force them to be misguided. He only beautifies [evil] for them and entices them to lead them astray. We have given him permission to entice so we can make it clear the one who has faith in the Hereafter from the one who is in doubt about the Hereafter. Your Lord, O Messenger, is a Guardian over everything. He guards the actions of His slaves and will reward them for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Gratitude protects favours and rejecting them causes them to be seized.\n2. Safety is one of the greatest favours Allah has given the servants.\n3. Correct faith protects against following the misguidance of the satan, through the permission of Allah.\n4. The invalidity of the causes of idolatry and its openings are clear, such as claiming the idols have power or partnership will Allah, or help or intercession with Allah.",
  34022:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Call upon those whom you claimed were your gods besides Allah so that they can bring you benefit or remove harm from you. They do not have ownership of anything, not even something as small as a dust particle, nor are they partners with Allah in ownership, nor does Allah have any helpers from amongst them. He is Self-sufficient, in no need of anyone else.",
  34023:
      "Intercession does not benefit except the one whom Allah gives permission, and Allah does not permit to intercede except those He is pleased with due to His Greatness. And part of His Greatness is that when He speaks in the heavens, the angels flap their wings in submission to what He says until the fear disappears from their hearts; some of them say to others: What did your Lord just say? The angels reply that He said the truth and is High in His essence, the Great, that everything else is lesser than Him.",
  34024:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Who sends provisions to you from the skies by bringing out the crops, plants, and fruits? Then tell them: It is Allah who provides for you. O, polytheists, only one of us can be rightly guided while the other is on clear misguidance. There can be no doubt that the believers are on clear guidance and the polytheists are misguided.",
  34025:
      "O Messenger, say to them: You will not be asked on the Day of Resurrection about the sins we committed, nor will we be asked about what you used to do.",
  34026:
      "Say to them: Allah will gather you and us on the Day of Resurrection, then He will judge between you and us with justice, then He will manifest the truthful from the liar. He is the Judge who adjudicates with justice, the Omniscient of how to pass judgment.",
  34027:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Show me those whom you have made as partners with Allah that you associate with Him in worship. No, indeed, the matter is not as you have thought, i.e., that He has partners, but rather He is Allah, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in his creation, decree, and control.",
  34028:
      "And We did not send you, O Messenger, except for the sake of all of humanity, to give good news to the pious that for them is Paradise, and to warn the disbelievers and transgressors about the Fire, but most people do not know that. Had they known, they would not have denied you.",
  34029:
      "And the polytheists say, while hastily seeking the punishment you are warning them of: If you are truthful, tell us when this promise of punishment will occur.",
  34030:
      "O Messenger, tell these people hastily seeking the punishment: For you is a fixed appointed time. When the time comes upon you, it will not be delayed or preceded by the slightest. And this day is the Day of Resurrection.",
  34031:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah said: We will never believe in the Quran, which Muhammad claims is revealed to him, nor will we ever believe in the previous divine books. O Messenger, if you were to see when the wrongdoers are detained before their Lord on the Day of Resurrection for the reckoning. They will dispute with one another, each placing the responsibility and blame on the other. The subdued followers will say to their leaders who oppressed them in this life: If you had not led us astray, we would have been believers in Allah and His messengers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Softness with the one being called is necessary so that he does not resort to stubbornness and being unreasonable.\n2. The messengership of the Prophet (peace be upon him) incorporates the whole of mankind and j inns likewise.\n3. One of the conditions of the people on the day of judgment will be arguments between the followers and leaders, and each side disassociating themselves from the other.",
  34032:
      "The leaders who were arrogant to the truth will say to the followers they oppressed: Did we stop you from the guidance that Muhammad brought? No, rather, you were the wrongdoers and the people who were corruptly spreading immorality.",
  34033:
      "The followers who were oppressed by their leaders will say to their leaders who were arrogant to the truth: But your deceiving us night and day, when you would order us to disbelieve in Allah and to worship creations besides Him, prevented us from guidance. They will hide their regret over their disbelief in this world when they see the punishment and will know they are going to be punished. And We will put chains on the necks of the disbelievers. They will not be given this recompense except due to what they used to do in the worldly life, namely worshipping others besides Allah and committing sins.",
  34034:
      "To console the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم after his people rejected him, Allah reminds him that rejection was also the practice of the nations before him, stating: \n We have not sent a messenger to any city warning of Allah's punishment except that the affluent people in it amongst those of power, fame, and wealth said: O Messengers, we disbelieve in what you have been sent with.",
  34035:
      "And these people of fame said braggingly and arrogantly: We have more wealth and children. And your claim that we will be punished is a lie, as we will not be punished in this world nor the Hereafter.",
  34036:
      "O Messenger, say to those who have been deceived by the favors they have been given: My Lord increases the provision for whom He wants to test whether he is grateful or ungrateful, and He restricts it for whom He wants to test whether he is patient or becomes upset. But most people do not know that Allah is Wise. He does not decree a matter except due to complete wisdom known to those who know and which the ignorant are unaware of.",
  34037:
      "Your wealth and children, which you boast about, do not lead you to Allah's pleasure, but the one who believes in Allah and does good actions has acquired a multiplied reward. His wealth draws him closer to Allah by spending it in Allah's way, and his children are also a means for raising his rank through their supplications for him. So those believers who do good deeds are rewarded multiple times for the good they did, and they will be in the higher ranks of Paradise, safe from whatever they fear: punishment, death, and the end of their bliss.",
  34038:
      "And the disbelievers who make it their utmost effort to turn people away from Our signs and strive hard to achieve their goals are losers in this world and will be punished in the Hereafter.",
  34039:
      "O Messenger, say to them: My Lord increases the provision for whom He wants from His creation and restricts it for whom He wants. And whatever you spend in Allah's way, Allah will replace it for you in this world by giving you what is better than it and in the Hereafter with a great reward. Allah is the best of providers, so whoever seeks provision should seek it from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The leaders disassociating themselves from the followers and the followers from the leaders will not excuse either of them from their responsibility.\n2. Affluence distances from complying with the truth and submitting to it.\n3. A believer is benefited through his wealth and children whilst a disbeliever is not benefited through them.\n4. Spending in the path of Allah leads to recompensing wealth in this world and good reward in the Hereafter.",
  34040:
      "O Messenger, remember the day Allah will gather them all, then Allah will say to the angels to scold the polytheists and rebuke them: Are these the ones who used to worship you in the worldly life besides Allah?",
  34041:
      "The angels will say: Pure and Exalted are You; You are our guardian, not them, so there is no friendship between them and us, but rather, these polytheists used to worship the devils. They used to appear to them as angels so that they would worship them besides Allah; most were believers in them.",
  34042:
      "On the Day of Gathering and Reckoning, those worshipped will not be able to benefit those who worshipped them besides Allah in this world, nor will they be able to harm them. And We will say to those who wronged themselves through disbelief and sins: Taste the punishment of the Fire you used to deny in this world.",
  34043:
      "And when you recite Our clear verses revealed to Our Messenger, in which there is no ambiguity, to these denying polytheists, they say: This is a mere human who has brought this message to divert us from the path of our forefathers. They also say: The Quran is nothing but a fabricated lie against Allah. And those who disbelieved in Allah said regarding the Quran when it came to them from Allah: This is only obvious sorcery to separate between a husband and his wife, and a father from his son.",
  34044:
      "And We have not given them books they are reading, which may direct them to say the Quran is a lie Muhammad fabricated, nor did We send them, before sending you, O Messenger, a messenger who would warn them of Allah's punishment.",
  34045:
      "The previous nations, such as 'Ād, Thamūd, and the people of Lot, were deniers of faith. And the polytheists from your people have not reached even a tenth of the strength, might, and numbers the previous nations reached. Every one of them denied their messenger, so the wealth, strength, and numbers they were given did not benefit them, so My punishment befell them. So, see the outcome of My Reproach and that of My punishment.",
  34046:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: I only direct you to and advise you of one characteristic, which is that you stand free from desires, for Allah's sake, in pairs and individually, then think about the life of your companion and what you know of his intelligence, truthfulness, and trustworthiness, so that it becomes clear to you that he صلى الله عليه وسلم is not insane. He is only a warner of severe punishment if you do not repent to Allah from associating partners with Him.",
  34047:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who reject: I do not ask you for any reward or payment for the guidance and good I have brought you; if you are guided, it will be for your benefit. My reward is only with Allah alone; He is a Witness to everything. He witnesses that I have conveyed to you and witnesses your actions, and He will reward you in full for them.",
  34048:
      "After mentioning the evidence against the people of falsehood and polytheism, Allah the Exalted mentions that this is His established divine practice, stating: \n O Messenger, say: My Lord will empower the truth over falsehood, thus negating it, and He knows the unseen. Nothing in the heavens or the Earth is hidden from Him, and [especially] the actions of His slaves are not concealed from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The angels will disassociate themselves on the day of judgment from the claim of some of the idolaters that they used to worship them.\n2. The satans deceived the idolaters when they would claim to them that they are angels and so the idolaters would worship them.\n3. Blind following of forefathers diverts from guidance.\n4. Detaching oneself from desires and thinking objectively is a means of reaching the correct conclusion and right mindset.\n5. A caller towards Allah does not await reward from any person, but rather he only expects it from the Lord of people.",
  34049:
      "O Messenger, tell these rejecting polytheists: The truth, which is Islam, has come, and falsehood no longer has any sway, and its dominance will not return.",
  34050:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who reject: If I stray away from the truth in what I convey to you, the harm of my misguidance is confined to me. None of it will affect you. And if I am guided to Him, it is due to what my Lord reveals to me. He hears the sayings of His slaves and is Close to me; it is not difficult for Him to hear what I say.",
  34051:
      "O Messenger, if you were to see when these rejectors will be petrified when they see the punishment on the Day of Resurrection, there will be no place for them to run to, nor any refuge for them to take shelter in. They will be taken from a nearby place that is easy to reach from the beginning. If you were to see that, you would see a strange matter indeed.",
  34052:
      "And they will say when they see their fate: We believe in the Day of Resurrection. But how will they pursue and acquire faith when the place for accepting faith has gone far from them, by their leaving the worldly abode, the abode of action and no reward, to the home of the Hereafter, the abode of reward and no action?",
  34053:
      "How can they attain faith, and how can it be accepted from them when they disbelieved during this worldly life, casting conjecture from a side far from reaching the truth, such as calling the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم a magician, a soothsayer, and a poet?",
  34054:
      "And these deniers were prevented from what they desired, from the pleasure of this life and repenting from disbelief, salvation from the Fire, and returning to the worldly life, just as was done with those resembling them from the rejecting nations before them. They doubted what the messengers brought, i.e., believing the Oneness of Allah and faith in the resurrection.",
  35000:
      "Originator (Surah Fatir)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating the utter poverty of slaves before the Creator of the heavens and the earth and His absolute sufficiency from them.\n•    Explanation:",
  35001:
      "All praise is for Allah, Creator of the heavens and the Earth without precedent, Who appointed messengers from the angels who execute His preordained commands. Some convey the revelation to the Prophets and strengthen them to perform what they were entrusted with. Some of them have two, three, or four wings with which they fly to carry out what they have been ordered. Allah increases His creation in what He wishes of limbs, beauty, or voice. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  35002:
      "The keys to everything are in Allah's Hand. So whatever provision, guidance, or good fortune He opens up for people, nobody can prevent it. And whatever He stops of this, there is nobody who is able to send it after He has stopped it. And He is the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in His creating, decreeing, and planning.",
  35003:
      "O people, remember Allah's favor on you through your hearts and tongues, and through your limbs by action. Do you have any creator besides Allah who provides you from the sky with the water He sends to you and who provides you from the earth with the fruits and crops He grows? There is no true deity worthy of worship besides Him. So how now, after this, do you turn away from this truth and fabricate lies against Allah and claim that Allah has partners when He is the One who created all of you and provides for all of you?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The scene of the terror of the disbelievers on the day of judgment will be a great scene.\n2. The place where faith will benefit is this world, because it is the abode of action.\n3. The greatness of the creation of the angels shows the greatness of their Creator.",
  35004:
      "And if your people deny you, O Messenger, be patient because you are not the first messenger whose people denied him, as nations before you had rejected their prophets, such as 'Ād, Thamūd, and the people of Lot. And to Allah alone, all matters are returned, so He will destroy the deniers and help His Messengers and the believers.",
  35005:
      "O people, the resurrection and recompense on the Day of Resurrection, which Allah has promised you, are true without a doubt, so the pleasures of the worldly life and its temptations should not deceive you from preparing for this day through good actions, nor should the Devil deceive you by his beautifying of falsehood and by inciting you to incline towards the worldly life.",
  35006:
      "O people, the Devil is your enemy whose enmity is everlasting, so take him as an enemy by being committed to fighting him. The Devil only calls his followers towards disbelief in Allah so that their outcome is to enter the burning fire on the Day of Resurrection.",
  35007:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah by following the Devil will have a severe punishment. And those who believe in Allah and do good actions will have forgiveness from Allah for their sins and a great reward from Him, which is Paradise.",
  35008:
      "The one for whom the Devil has embellished his evil actions, such that he thinks them to be good, is unlike the one for whom Allah has beautified the truth, so he believes it to be the truth because Allah leads astray whom He wants and guides whom He desires without anyone to compel Him. So do not harm yourself, O Messenger, out of grief over the misguidance of the misguided. Allah knows what they do. Nothing of their actions is hidden from Him.",
  35009:
      "Allah is the One who sent the winds; then these winds move clouds, then We lead these clouds to a land where there are no plants, then We give life through its water, causing plants to grow after being dead and dry. So just as We gave life to this land after its death, through the plants We placed in it, the resurrection of the dead will happen on the Day of Resurrection.",
  35010:
      "Whoever wants honor in this world or the Hereafter should only seek it from Allah because Allah alone gives honor in both. His pure remembrance is elevated to Him, and the good deeds of His slaves are raised to Him. And those who plot evil plans, such as trying to kill the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, will have a severe punishment. The scheming of these disbelievers will perish, and no objective of theirs will be accomplished.",
  35011:
      "Allah is the One who created your father, Adam, from the soil; then He created you from a sperm-drop; then He made you men and women who marry one another. And no female conceives a fetus or gives birth except with His knowledge. Nothing of that is hidden from Him. And the lifespan of any of His creations is not increased or decreased except that it is written in the Preserved Tablet. All of this, i.e., creating you from the soil, creating you in stages, and writing your lifespans in the Preserved Tablet, is easy for Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Messenger (peace be upon him) has been consoled by mentioning the conditions of the messengers with their people.\n2. Being deceived by the world is a means of turning away from the truth.\n3. Taking the satan as an enemy is by adopting the means which help protect against Him, such as the remembrance of Allah, recitation of the Qur’an, acts of obedience and leaving sins.\n4. Allah is the Exalted.",
  35012:
      "The two seas are not comparable: One is extremely sweet and palatable due to its sweetness, and the other is salty and bitter, which is not drinkable due to its extreme saltiness. And from each of the abovementioned seas, you eat fresh meat, which is fish, and you extract rubies and coral from them, which you wear as adornment. And you see the ships, splitting the sea as they sail, coming and going, so you can seek the grace of Allah through trade and thank Allah for the many favors He has given you.",
  35013:
      "Allah slowly extends the night into the day, so it becomes longer, and the day into the night, so it becomes longer. And He made the sun and the moon subservient; each floats in its appointed orbit until a fixed time only Allah knows, which is the Day of Resurrection. Allah, your Lord, sets all of that and carries it out. To Him alone belongs the kingdom. And the idols you worship besides Him do not even possess the thin [flaky] membrane over the datestone, so how do you worship them besides Me?",
  35014:
      "If you call your gods, they cannot hear your call because they are inanimate objects with no life and cannot hear. And even if they could listen to you calling them, they would not be able to respond to you. And on the Day of Resurrection, they will disassociate themselves from your idolatry and your worshipping them. O Messenger, nobody can inform you more truthfully than Allah.",
  35015:
      "O people, you are the ones in need of Allah in all your affairs and all your situations. Allah is the Self-sufficient, who does not need you for anything. He is the Praiseworthy in this world and the Hereafter for what He decrees for His slaves.",
  35016:
      "If He wanted to eradicate you by destroying you, He would do so and bring into existence a new creation to take your place who would worship Him and not associate any partners with Him.",
  35017:
      "And eliminating you through annihilation and bringing a new creation into your place is not impossible for Allah.",
  35018:
      "No soul will carry the sin of another, but rather, every sinning soul will bear the burden of its evil. And if a soul burdened with sins were to ask someone to carry some of its sins, nothing would be taken, even if the one being asked were a close relative. O Messenger, you can only warn of Allah's punishment to those who fear their Lord in private and complete the prayer most perfectly, for they are the ones who will take heed of your warning. Whoever is purified from his sins, the greatest of them being polytheism, then his purification will only benefit himself when he returns to his Lord. Allah does not need His slave's obedience. To Allah is the return on the Day of Resurrection for the reckoning and recompense.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The subjugation of the sea, the alteration of the night and day and the subjugation of the sun and moon are all amongst Allah’s favours to the people, but the people are used to these favours and thus absentminded of them.\n2. The minds of the idolaters are foolish as they call upon idols which cannot hear or understand.\n3. Being needy towards Allah is a quality which is inseparable from humans and independence is a quality of perfection for Allah.\n4. Purification of the soul is dependent on the servant himself, for it is up to him to either protect it or ruin it.",
  35019:
      "The disbeliever and believer are not the same in status, just as blind people and those who can see are different.",
  35020:
      "And disbelief and belief are not the same, just as darkness and light are different.",
  35021:
      "And Paradise and Hell do not have the same impact, just as shade and hot winds are different.",
  35022:
      "And the believers and disbelievers are not the same, just as the living and the dead are different. Allah makes those whom He wants to guide listen attentively. And you, O Messenger, cannot make the disbelievers who are like the dead in the graves hear.",
  35023: "You are only to them a warner of Allah's punishment.",
  35024:
      "O Messenger, We have sent you with the truth in which there is no doubt to give good news to the believers of the generous reward Allah has in store for them and to warn the disbelievers of the painful punishment He has prepared for them. And there is no nation from those before except that there passed a messenger from Allah to warn them of His punishment.",
  35025:
      "And if your people reject you, O Messenger, be patient because you are not the first messenger whose people rejected him, as the nations before rejected their messengers, such as 'Ād, Thamūd, and the people of Lot. Their messengers came to them with clear evidence and overwhelming miracles that prove their truthfulness, and their messengers came to them with scrolls and the Scripture, which is enlightening for one who ponders over it and contemplates it.",
  35026:
      "But despite that, they disbelieved in Allah and His messengers and did not accept [the guidance] they came with from Him, so I destroyed those who disbelieved. So, imagine, O Messenger, how terrible my punishment was when I destroyed them.",
  35027:
      "O Messenger, have you not seen that Allah sends rainwater from the sky, then We extract fruits of different colors from that same water, amongst them red, green, yellow, and others, once We have watered their trees with it? And from the mountains are white, red, and pitch-black tracts.",
  35028:
      "And amongst men, animals, and cattle (camels, cows, and sheep) are different colors like that aforementioned. Only those who exalt Allah and have a genuine fear of Him are the knowledgeable ones because they recognize His attributes, His sacred law, and the proof of His power. Allah is Mighty; no one can overpower Him. He forgives the sins of His slaves who repent.",
  35029:
      "Those who read the Book of Allah, which We revealed to Our Messenger and practice what it contains, and complete the prayer in the best way, and who spend from what We have provided them, through Zakat and other forms, secretly and openly, seek through those actions a trade with Allah which will never bring them any loss.",
  35030:
      "So that Allah can give them the full reward for their actions and increase them from His grace, as this is His domain. He forgives the sins of those described with these qualities and appreciates their righteous efforts.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The vast difference between the people of truth and people of falsehood.\n2. The sending of a great number of messengers before the advent of Muhammad (peace be upon him) shows the greatness of Allah’s mercy, and the ungrateful nature of many people.\n3. The eventual destruction of disbelievers is a divine custom.\n4. Faith and its characteristics lead to all types of benefits and success, whilst the qualities of disbelief are a losing trade!",
  35031:
      "The Scripture We have revealed to you, O Messenger, is the truth in which there is no doubt. Allah has revealed it to affirm the precious scriptures. Allah is well-informed about His slaves, and He sees everything. He, therefore, reveals to the messenger of every nation what they need in their time.",
  35032:
      "Then We gave the Quran to the nation of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم whom We have chosen over other nations. Some wronged their souls by doing prohibited acts and leaving out their obligations. Some were moderate by doing their duties and leaving out prohibited acts while doing some recommended actions, and some disliked actions. By Allah's leave, some were foremost in good deeds, doing their obligations and recommended acts and leaving out prohibited and disliked actions. The abovementioned choosing of this nation and its being given the Quran is the most excellent favor to which no blessing can come close.",
  35033:
      "Gardens to settle in, which these chosen ones will enter. In it, they will wear bracelets of gold and pearls, and their garments therein will be silk.",
  35034:
      "They will say after they enter Paradise: Praise be to Allah, Who has removed from us all grief because of our fear of entering the Fire. Our Lord forgives the sins of those slaves of His who repent and thanks them for their obedience to Him.",
  35035:
      "The One who has placed us in the Everlasting Home, out of His bounty, not by our might or strength, where no toil or fatigue will affect us.",
  35036:
      "After mentioning the reward of His righteous servants, Allah also mentions the punishment for the vile among them, referring to the disbelievers. He states: \n Those who disbelieve in Allah will be in the Hellfire, where they will remain forever. It will not be decreed for them to die so that they can escape the punishment, nor will the punishment of Hell be alleviated for them in any way. In this way, We will recompense every person who denies the favors of His Lord on the Day of Resurrection.",
  35037:
      "They will cry out therein as loud as they can, seeking help by saying: Our Lord! Let us out from the Fire, and we will do righteous deeds, different from what we did before, so we can attain Your pleasure and be saved from Your punishment. Allah will respond to them thus: Did We not let you live a life long enough so that anyone who wanted to take heed could do so and do righteous deeds, and the Messenger came to you to warn you of Allah's punishment? Thus, you have no argument or excuses after all of this, so taste the chastisement of the Fire. Those who wrong themselves by disbelief and sin will have no helper to rescue them from Allah's punishment or lighten it.",
  35038:
      "Allah knows all that is hidden in the heavens and the Earth. Nothing of that passes Him by. He knows all the good and bad His slaves conceal in their chests.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtue of the nation of Muhammad (peace be upon him) over all other nation.\n2. The difference in the faith of the believers implies a difference in their rank in the world and the Hereafter.\n3. Paradise is a place of comfort and happiness, while the fire is a place of fatigue and misery.\n4. Time is a trust that must be guarded. Whoever wastes it will regret when regret will be of no use.\n5. Allah’s knowledge encompasses everything.",
  35039:
      "O people, He made you successors of one another on Earth. Those who disbelieve Allah and what the messengers brought, then the sin and retribution of their disbelief will come back on them. Their disbelief does not harm their Lord. Their disbelief only adds to their Lord's displeasure and hatred for them. Their disbelief adds only to their loss, as they will lose what Allah would have prepared for them in Paradise had they believed.",
  35040:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: Tell me about your partners that you worship instead of Allah; what have they created on Earth? Did they make its mountains? Did they create its rivers? Did they create its animals? Or do they have any share with Allah in the creation of the heavens? Or have We given them a book proving the validity of worshipping their idols? Nothing of that is true. Those who wrong themselves by disbelief and sins promise one another nothing but delusion.",
  35041:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) holds the heavens and the Earth, preventing them from disappearing, and were they to disappear, hypothetically, there is none after him (may He be Exalted) to keep them from doing so. He is Forbearing and does not rush to punish; He Forgives the sins of those of His slaves who repent.",
  35042:
      "These rejecting disbelievers swore a solemn and affirmed oath that if a messenger from Allah came to them to warn them of His punishment, they would be more guided and follow the truth more than the Jews, Christians, and others. Yet when Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم came to them after being sent by His Lord and warned them of Allah's punishment, his coming only increased their hatred of the truth and adherence to falsehood. They did not fulfill their solemn oaths to be more guided than those who preceded them.",
  35043:
      "The oaths they took in Allah's name were not taken in good faith and with a sound objective. It was only to be arrogant on Earth and to deceive people. An evil plot only rebounds on those who plotted it. So, are these arrogant plotters waiting for anything other than Allah's established practice, which is their destruction as He destroyed their predecessors like them? You will not find any change to Allah's method of destroying arrogant people such that the destruction evades them, nor is it diverted to others besides them because it is an established divine practice.",
  35044:
      "Have these deniers not traveled the Earth and reflected on how those nations before them who had denied [the truth] met their end? Did they not meet an evil end by Allah destroying them, although they were superior to these people in strength? Allah is not to be outdone by anything in the heavens or Earth. He is the One who knows about the actions of these deniers. Nothing of their actions is hidden from nor escapes Him. He has the power to destroy them whenever He wills.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Disbelief is a cause of Allah’s displeasure and a path to loss and wretchedness.\n2. The idolaters do not have any evidence for their idolatry, neither rational or textual.\n3. The wrongdoer’s plotting will only came back to destroy him sooner or later.",
  35045:
      "If Allah were to rush to punish people for the wrong they have done and the sins they perpetrated, He would have destroyed all the people on Earth at once, together with the animals and wealth they own. However, He (may He be Exalted) gives them respite until a fixed time, the Day of Resurrection. When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah is fully aware of what His slaves used to do, and nothing remains hidden from Him. He will then recompense them for their actions, whether good or bad.",
  36000:
      "Ya Sin (Surah Ya-Sin)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming the message, the resurrection, and detailing proof for both.\n•    Explanation:",
  36001:
      "Yā Sīn – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  36002:
      "Allah swears by the Quran, whose verses have been perfectly arranged and to which no falsehood approaches it from any direction.",
  36003:
      "You, O Messenger, are one of the messengers Allah sent to His slaves, instructing them to declare His Oneness and to worship Him alone.",
  36004:
      "Upon a straight methodology and upright law. This straight methodology and upright law are revealed from your Lord, the Mighty, whom no one can challenge. He is Merciful to His slaves who believe in Him.",
  36005:
      "Upon a straight methodology and upright law. This straight methodology and upright law are revealed from your Lord, the Mighty, whom no one can challenge. He is Merciful to His slaves who believe in Him.",
  36006:
      "We revealed it to you to warn and exhort a nation, the Arabs, to whom no messenger has come to warn them, and as a result, they are heedless of faith and monotheism. Likewise, every nation that has been cut off from the warning needs messengers, scholars, and preachers to remind them.",
  36007:
      "The punishment from Allah is necessary for most of these people after the truth from Allah conveyed to them by His Messenger reached them, and they did not believe in it and remained in their disbelief. They do not believe in Allah nor His Messenger and do not act on the truth that came to them.",
  36008:
      "Their example is like those who have shackles that cover their entire neck and whose hands are tied to their necks under their chins. As a result, they are forced to lift their heads to the sky and cannot lower them. These people are shackled from faith in Allah; therefore, they do not submit to it or lower their heads on its account.",
  36009:
      "We placed a barrier to the truth before and behind them. We covered their eyes from the truth so they could not see in a manner that benefited them. This happened to them after their stubbornness and persistence in disbelief became apparent.",
  36010:
      "It is all the same to these disbelievers who oppose the truth, whether you, O Muhammad, warn them or you do not warn them. They will not accept what you have brought from Allah.",
  36011:
      "The person who benefits from your warning is the one who accepts this Quran and follows what is in it and who fears His Lord in solitude where nobody else sees him. So, tell those with these attributes the pleasing news of Allah expiating their sins and forgiving them and of a great reward awaiting them in the Hereafter, which is entering Paradise.",
  36012:
      "Indeed, We shall bring the dead back to life by resurrecting them to give account on the Day of Resurrection. We record the good and the evil deeds that they send forth in this life to be rewarded for in the next, and we also record the excellent and harmful effects of their actions, such as the good that comes out of charity after they pass away and the evil that results of their misdeeds. We counted everything and recorded it in a clear book, which is the preserved tablet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Obstinacy is a barrier from guidance to the truth.\n2. Acting on the Qur’an and the fear of Allah are means to enter Paradise.\n3. The virtue of a righteous child, continually benefitting charity, and similar deeds where the good remains long after the believing servant has passed away.",
  36013:
      "Give O Messenger, these stubborn deniers, an example that will be a lesson for them, which is the story of the people of the town when their messengers came to them.",
  36014:
      "When We first sent them two messengers to call them to Allah's Oneness and His worship, they rejected them. Then we sent as reinforcement for these two a third Messenger with them. The three messengers said to the townspeople: All three of us have been sent to call you to Allah's Oneness and follow His law.",
  36015:
      "The people of the town said to those who were sent: You are only men like us. You do not have any special status over us. The Merciful has not sent down any revelation to you. You are only lying about Allah in this claim of yours.",
  36016:
      "The three messengers said in response to the denial by the people of the town: Our Lord knows that we have been sent by Him to you, O people of the city. That is enough evidence for us.",
  36017:
      "We only must convey what we have been instructed to. We have no control over your guidance.",
  36018:
      "The people of the town said to the messengers: We see an evil omen in you. If you do not stop calling us to monotheism, we will punish you by stoning you to death, and [in that way] you will receive a painful punishment.",
  36019:
      "The messengers responded: Your evil omen is within yourselves because you denied Allah and abandoned following His messengers. Do you see a bad omen if we remind you of Allah? You are a people who have gone too far in the perpetration of disbelief and sins.",
  36020:
      "From a far part of the town, a man came running, fearing his people's denial of the messengers and their threatening to kill or harm them. He said: O my people, follow what these messengers have brought.",
  36021:
      "O people, follow those who do not ask you for any reward for conveying what they brought and are rightly guided in the revelation of Allah that they bring to you. Whoever is like that deserves to be followed.",
  36022:
      "This man offering sincere advice said: What prevents me from worshipping Allah Who created me? What prevents you from worshipping your Lord Who made you, and you will return to Him when resurrected for the recompense?",
  36023:
      "Shall I take other deities to be wrongly worshipped instead of Allah, Who created me? If the Merciful intends harm for me, the intercession of these other deities will not benefit me at all, nor will they be able to save me from the harm Allah intended for me if I die as a disbeliever.",
  36024:
      "If I were to take them as deities besides Allah, I would be in clear error as I would have worshipped a being that does not deserve worship and abandoned worshiping the One who deserves it.",
  36025:
      "O my people, I have believed in our Lord, so listen to me. I do not care about the threats on my life that you make. But his people insisted on killing him, and Allah admitted him into Paradise.",
  36026:
      "It was said to honor this man after his people killed him: Enter Paradise after you were killed as a martyr. When he entered it and saw the delight therein, he said longingly: If only my people who rejected and killed me knew about the forgiveness of sins that I obtained and what my Lord has honored me with, they would have believed like how I believed, and they would have attained a reward similar to mine.",
  36027:
      "It was said to honor this man after his people killed him: Enter Paradise after you were killed as a martyr. When he entered it and saw the delight therein, he said longingly: If only my people who rejected and killed me knew about the forgiveness of sins that I obtained and what my Lord has honored me with, they would have believed like how I believed, and they would have attained a reward similar to mine.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of stories in calling towards Allah.\n2. Taking an evil omen is an act of disbelief.\n3. It is obligatory to wish well for the people of truth.\n4. To love good and wellbeing for people is an attribute of the people of faith.",
  36028:
      "And We did not send down an army of angels from heaven to destroy his people who rejected and killed him, nor do We need to send angels upon nations to destroy them. Their matter is easier for Us than that as We have decreed that their decimation would occur simply with a cry from the heavens, without sending down angels of torment.",
  36029:
      "Thus, the story of the destruction of his people was simply a single cry that We sent upon them, and suddenly, they fell down with nothing remaining. Their example is like a fire that was burning and then extinguished, leaving behind no trace.",
  36030:
      "Alas, for the slaves who rejected, how regretful will their situation be on the Day of Resurrection when they see the torment! That is because in this world, whenever any messenger from Allah came to them, they used to mock and ridicule him. Therefore, their outcome will be regret on the Day of Resurrection for neglecting their duty to Allah.",
  36031:
      "Did these people who reject and ridicule the messengers not see a lesson in the nations who preceded them? They passed away and did not return to this world a second time. Instead, they met the deeds they had sent forth, and Allah will recompense them accordingly for that.",
  36032:
      "All nations, without exception, will be brought before Us on the Day of Resurrection after being resurrected so that We may recompense them for their deeds accordingly.",
  36033:
      "A sign for those who reject the resurrection that the resurrection is true is this dry and barren land, on which We sent down rain from the sky, and We caused various types of plants and grains to grow therein for people to eat. The One who gave life to this earth by sending down the rain and bringing out the plants can give life to and resurrect the dead.",
  36034:
      "In this earth, on which We sent down rain, we have placed gardens of date palms and grapes and caused water springs to gush forth to irrigate them.",
  36035:
      "So that the people can eat fruits from those gardens that Allah has favored them with without any effort from themselves. Will they then not thank Allah for these favors by worshiping Him alone and believing in His messengers?",
  36036:
      "Sanctified and Exalted is Allah, Who created various types of plants and trees. He made people into males and females and made other creations of Allah that people do not know of on land, sea, and other places.",
  36037:
      "A sign that indicates people to Allah's Oneness is that We remove the daylight as the day draws to an end and night comes, and We bring the darkness as the day withdraws from it, then suddenly, the people are in complete darkness.",
  36038:
      "A sign to them that Allah is One is this sun that runs on a fixed course that Allah knows and does not go beyond that. That determination is the determination of the Mighty, who no one overpowers, the Omniscient from Whom nothing of the affairs of His creation is hidden.",
  36039:
      "A sign for them that indicates His Oneness (may He be Exalted) is this moon for which We have determined phases each night. It starts small, becomes big, and then small again until it becomes similar to a twisted, old date stalk, appearing thin, curved, yellow, and old.",
  36040:
      "These signs: the sun, moon, night, and day, are predetermined by Allah's divine determination and do not surpass what has been determined for them. The sun cannot catch up with the moon to change its course or take away its light, nor can the night outpace the day and enter upon it before its time ends. All these subservient creations and other creations, such as the stars and galaxies, have their courses as per Allah's determination and protection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. No one will return to the world after death.\n2. One of the evidence of resurrection is the revival of the lifeless earth with green plants and the production of grain from it.",
  36041:
      "Another sign that indicates to them Allah's Oneness and His favor to His slaves is that We carried those of Adam's progeny (peace be upon Him) who were saved from the flood in the time of Noah (peace be upon Him) in the ship that was filled with Allah's creations. Allah carried therein a pair of every species.",
  36042:
      "A sign that indicates to them Allah's Oneness and His favor to His slaves is that We created conveyances like the ship of Noah for them.",
  36043:
      "If We wished to drown them, We would have done so. Then there would be no one to help them if We wanted to drown them and no one to rescue them if they drowned by Our command and decree.",
  36044:
      "Except if We show mercy to them by rescuing them from drowning and returning them to enjoy themselves until a specified time that they will not go beyond so that they take a lesson and subsequently believe.",
  36045:
      "When these polytheists who turn away from belief are told to beware of what they are heading towards in the Hereafter and its difficulties and beware of the world behind them, in the hope that Allah will favor them with His mercy, they do not comply with that. Instead, they turn away from it without any care.",
  36046:
      "Whenever Allah's signs indicating His Oneness and His deserving being worshipped alone come to these stubborn polytheists, they turn away from it without taking heed.",
  36047:
      "When these stubborn people are told to assist the poor and the needy with the wealth Allah has provided them with, they disapprovingly reply to the believers: Should we feed those whom Allah could feed if He wanted to?! We do not want to oppose His will. You, O believers, are simply in clear error and far from the truth.",
  36048:
      "The disbelievers who deny the resurrection say in rejection of it, regarding it as far-fetched: When is this resurrection, O believers, if you are true in your claim that it is to occur?",
  36049:
      "But all these rejectors of resurrection who regard it as far-fetched are only waiting for the first blow when the trumpet will be blown, suddenly overtaking them while they are in their worldly pursuits of buying, selling, irrigating, herding, and other engagements.",
  36050:
      "When this cry surprises them, they will not be able to make a bequest for one another and will not be able to return to their homes and families. Instead, they will die while they are in their worldly occupations.",
  36051:
      "The trumpet will be blown a second time for the resurrection, and suddenly, they will all come out of their graves, rushing towards their Lord for reckoning and recompense.",
  36052:
      "These disbelievers who reject the resurrection will say in regret: What a loss of ours! Who has resurrected us from our graves? They will be given a response to their question: This is what Allah promised, and it must occur, and the messengers were truthful in respect to what they conveyed from their Lord in this regard.",
  36053:
      "The resurrection from the graves will only result from a second blowing of the trumpet, and all creation will be presented before Us on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning.",
  36054:
      "Judgment will be just on that day, and you, O slaves, will not be wronged in the least by increasing from your bad deeds or decreasing from your good deeds. You will simply be given the full recompense for what you used to do in this worldly life.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. One of the techniques of Allah’s educating His servants is that He placed before them signs, which they can use to deduce what will be of benefit to them in their religious and worldly affairs.\n2. Allah empowered His servant and gave them the ability to fulfil instructions and avoid prohibitions. If they leave out what they have been instructed to do, this is through their own choice.\n3. On the day of resurrection the mercy of their Lord will appear to the people of faith in a way that they never imagined.",
  36055:
      "The people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will be too preoccupied to think about others because of the permanent bliss and great success they will see. They will be enjoying that happily.",
  36056:
      "They and their spouses will comfortably recline on couches under lush shades in Paradise.",
  36057:
      "In Paradise, they will have various types of wholesome fruits, such as grapes, figs, pomegranates, and any form of enjoyment or bliss they ask for. Whatever they ask for, they will get.",
  36058:
      "Over and above this bliss, they will receive peace in the form of a statement from a Lord Who is merciful to them. So when He greets them with peace, they will attain safety in every sense of the word and receive a greeting that no other greeting can surpass.",
  36059:
      "The polytheists will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Step away from the believers because it is inappropriate for them to be with you due to the disparity between your recompense and theirs, and your attributes and theirs.",
  36060:
      "Did I not advise and instruct you on the tongues of My messengers and say to you: O children of Adam! Do not follow the Devil by committing various types of disbelief and acts of disobedience. The Devil is a clear enemy to you. How can any sensible person follow an enemy of his who has made his enmity apparent?",
  36061:
      "And I commanded you, O children of Adam, to worship Me alone and not associate anything with Me, for worshiping Me alone and obeying Me is a straight path that leads to My pleasure and entry into Paradise. But, you did not comply with what I advised and commanded you to do.",
  36062:
      "The Devil has misled many people from among you. Did you not have intellects that would instruct you to obey your Lord and worship Him alone (may He be Exalted) and warn you from obeying the Devil, your clear enemy?",
  36063:
      "This is Hell, which you were promised in the worldly life for your disbelief. It was a matter of the ghayb (unseen) to you, but today, you can see it with your own eyes.",
  36064:
      "Enter it today and endure its heat because you disbelieved in Allah in this worldly life.",
  36065:
      "Today, We will seal their mouths, and they will become mute, unable to deny the disbelief and acts of disobedience they committed. Their hands will speak to us about what they did in the world. Their feet will testify about the acts of disobedience they committed and walked towards.",
  36066:
      "If We wished to remove their sight, We could have done so, and they would have been unable to see; they would then have rushed towards the bridge to cross it into Paradise, but it is unlikely that they would cross it while their sight is lost.",
  36067:
      "If We wished to alter their form and make them sit on their feet, We could have done so, and they would have been unable to move forward or backward.",
  36068:
      "Whoever's life, among humanity, We extend by lengthening his lifespan; We will eventually return him to the stage of weakness. Will they not think with their intellect and understand that this abode is not one of permanence and immortality and that the everlasting abode is that of the Hereafter!?",
  36069:
      "We did not teach Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم poetry, nor is that appropriate for him because it is not his nature, nor does his disposition demand it. So, you cannot claim that he is a poet. We have only taught him a reminder and a clear Quran for those who ponder it.",
  36070:
      "To warn those whose hearts are alive and still have illuminated insight, for they are the ones who will benefit from it, and to appoint the punishment against the disbelievers when the evidence was established against them through its revelation and invitation reaching them, leaving them with no excuse.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The people of Paradise will be happily occupied with everything their souls desire, eyes find delight in and what they wish for.\n2. The person with a heart is one who is purified by the Qur’an and who increases his knowledge of it and practice. The Qur’an for his heart is like rain for land that is fertile and pure.\n3. The limbs of a person - which were an aid for their owner on the world - will become a witness against him on the day of resurrection.",
  36071:
      "Have they not seen that We have created livestock for them, and they control the affairs of that livestock by doing with it according to their interests?",
  36072:
      "We have subjugated livestock for them and made it submissive to them; they ride on the backs of some, transport their loads on the backs of some, and consume some of its meat.",
  36073:
      "They also have benefits in the livestock other than just riding and consuming its meat, such as wool, bristles, fur, and value, which they use to make spreads and clothing. They can also drink its milk. So, will they not show gratitude to Allah, who has blessed them with these and other favors?",
  36074:
      "The polytheists have taken other deities instead of Allah, whom they worship, hoping they will help them and save them from Allah's torment.",
  36075:
      "Those deities they have taken cannot help themselves, let alone help those who worship them instead of Allah. The worshippers and their idols will all be brought together to torment but will all protest innocence from one another.",
  36076:
      "O Messenger, do not let their words, \"You are not a messenger,\" or \"You are a poet,\" and other forms of slander, upset you. Indeed, We know what they say privately and publicly; nothing is hidden from Us, and We will recompense them for it accordingly.",
  36077:
      "Does the human who denies the resurrection after death not ponder that: We created him from semen, then he went through different phases until he was born and developed, turning into a very argumentative and quarreling person? Does he not ponder over that to conclude that resurrection is possible?",
  36078:
      "This disbeliever is heedless and ignorant when he uses decayed bones to prove the impossibility of resurrection, saying, \"Who will resurrect it?\" while forgetting his own creation from non-existence.",
  36079:
      "O Muhammad! Reply to them: Whoever created these bones in the first place will bring them back to life because the One who initially created them is not incapable of returning life to them. He (may He be Exalted) is the knower of everything; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  36080:
      "The One who has made for you, O people, lush green trees from which you can ignite a fire. So the One who [can] combine two opposites: the moisture of the green trees and the fire ignited from them, is also capable of reviving the dead.",
  36081:
      "Is the One who created the heavens and the Earth, despite their grandeur, incapable of bringing the dead back to life after causing their death? Of course not! He is capable of it; He is the Creator who created all of creation and is Omniscient of them, and nothing is hidden from Him.",
  36082:
      "The command and nature of Allah is such that when He intends to bring something into existence, all He says to it is \"Be!\" and then the thing that He intends comes into existence. Included in what He intends is to give life, cause death, resurrect, and so forth.",
  36083:
      "So free and sanctified is Allah of the incapability the polytheists ascribe to Him. He is the One to whom total dominion belongs over everything, and He does as He wishes with it; the keys to everything are in His Hand, and you shall all return to Him in the Hereafter, where He will recompense you for your deeds accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From among the favours and privileges of granted be Allah to the people, is that He has subdued the livestock for them and made them usable to the people for their necessities, i.e. mounting, consuming their meat and milk.\n2. From among the attributes of Allah is that His knowledge encompasses all His creation in all its conditions, at all times. He knows well the state of those buried in the earth from those whose bodies have decayed and those who body parts remain. And He knows the hidden and the apparent.",
  37000:
      "Those Arranged in Ranks (Surah As-Saffat)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDeclaring Allah's exaltedness from what the polytheists ascribe to Him and invalidating their claims regarding the angels and Jinn.\n•    Explanation:",
  37001: "I take an oath by the angels who form compact rows in their worship.",
  37002:
      "And He swore an oath by the angels who push the rainclouds and send them wherever Allah wills for it to rain.",
  37003: "And I take an oath by the angels who recite the Speech of Allah.",
  37004: "O people, your true deity is one and has no partner: He is Allah.",
  37005:
      "The Lord of the heavens, Earth, whatever is between them, and the Lord of the sun in all its rising and setting places throughout the year.",
  37006:
      "We have beautified the heaven nearest to Earth with beautiful decorations: stars that appear like sparkling jewels.",
  37007:
      "And We have protected the nearest heaven with shooting stars against every rebellious devil who abandons Allah's obedience.",
  37008:
      "These devils cannot hear the angels in the sky when discussing the sacred law and the divine decree Allah revealed to them. They (devils) are pelted with shooting stars from all sides.",
  37009:
      "To repel and drive them away from eavesdropping. And in the Hereafter, they will suffer a painful, everlasting punishment that will not end.",
  37010:
      "Except for those devils who happen to snatch something quickly, which is a statement that the angels discuss among themselves, which the people of the Earth have yet to receive information of. A shooting star then subsequently goes after him and burns him. Sometimes, the devil is able to pass that statement on to his companion before the shooting star burns him, and it reaches the fortune-tellers, who tell a hundred lies with it.",
  37011:
      "So, O Muhammad, ask the disbelievers who deny the resurrection if they are harder to create and greater in form than the heavens, the Earth, and the angels that We have created. We created them (disbelievers) from sticky clay, so how could they deny the resurrection when they were created from such a weak substance, sticky clay?",
  37012:
      "Rather you are amazed, O Muhammad, at Allah's power and planning the affairs of His creation; you are amazed at the polytheists rejecting the resurrection. Due to their severe rejection of the resurrection, these polytheists mock what you say about it.",
  37013:
      "When these polytheists are admonished with any admonishments, they do not take heed nor benefit from it because their hearts are hard.",
  37014:
      "And when they see a sign from the signs of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that proves his truthfulness, they exaggerate in mocking and showing astonishment at it.",
  37015:
      "And they say: This thing that Muhammad has brought is nothing but clear magic.",
  37016:
      "[They say:] So when we die and become dust and decomposed crumbling bones, will we be resurrected alive? That is, indeed, far-fetched.",
  37017:
      "[They say:] Will our forefathers who died before us also be resurrected?",
  37018:
      "O Muhammad! Say to them in reply: Yes, you shall be resurrected after you have turned into dust and decomposed bones, as will your forefathers. You will all be resurrected while you are in a despised and humiliating state.",
  37019:
      "It will only be one blow of the trumpet (the second blowing), and suddenly, they will all be looking at the horrors of the Day of Resurrection, awaiting what Allah will do to them.",
  37020:
      "The polytheists who reject the resurrection will say: May we be destroyed! This is the Day of Recompense on which Allah will recompense His slaves accordingly for whatever deeds they sent forth in the worldly life!",
  37021:
      "It will be said to them: This is the Day of Adjudication between the slaves, which you used to deny and reject in the worldly life!",
  37022:
      "On that Day, it will be said to the angels: Gather the polytheists and those like them who did wrong by associating partners with Allah, all those who followed them in rejection, and all the idols they used to worship instead of Allah. Then, show them all the path to the Fire; lead them on to it and drive them towards it because it is their destination.",
  37023:
      "On that Day, it will be said to the angels: Gather the polytheists and those like them who did wrong by associating partners with Allah, all those who followed them in rejection, and all the idols they used to worship instead of Allah. Then, show them all the path to the Fire; lead them on to it and drive them towards it because it is their destination.",
  37024:
      "[They will be told:] And hold them back [for a while] before admitting them into the Fire to give account because they are to be questioned. Then, after that, drive them towards the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah decorated the nearest heaven with stars for many beneficial reasons, from them are: to achieve beautification and protection from rebellious satans.\n2. The Sirat is a bridge over the hellfire which the people of Paradise will cross, and upon it the feet of the people of the fire will slip.",
  37025:
      "It will be said to them in rebuke: What is the matter with you that you are not helping each other like you used to in the worldly life, and you used to claim that your idols would help you?",
  37026:
      "Instead, Today, they are submissive to the command of Allah and humiliated. They will not help each other because of their incapability to do so and because of their lack of ploys.",
  37027:
      "And they will turn to each other, blaming each other and arguing when blaming and arguing will be useless.",
  37028:
      "The followers will say to their leaders: O, our seniors! You used to approach us in matters of religion and truth. You would beautify disbelief, associating partners with Allah and committing acts of disobedience to us while scaring us away from the Truth that the messengers brought from Allah.",
  37029:
      "The leaders will tell the followers: The matter is not as you claim. Rather, you, yourselves, were upon disbelief and were not believers; you were the deniers.",
  37030:
      "O followers, we had no power or authority over you to cause you to disbelieve, associate partners with Allah, or commit acts of disobedience. Rather, you were people who transgressed the limits in disbelief and misguidance.",
  37031:
      "So the threat of Allah has come to pass against us and you in His statement: \"I will surely fill Hell with you and those of them that follow you all together.\" (Ṣād: 85), and because of that, we will inevitably taste whatever our Lord has promised.",
  37032:
      "So, We invited you towards misguidance and disbelief. We had deviated from the path of guidance.",
  37033:
      "So, the followers and the leaders will share in the torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  37034:
      "Just as We did with these people by making them taste the torment, We will do the same with other criminals.",
  37035:
      "When these polytheists were told in this world that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah so that they could act upon its requirements and leave everything that contradicted it, they would reject responding and submitting to it purely out of arrogance and disdain towards the truth.",
  37036:
      "And they would say, justifying their disbelief: Should we leave the worship of our deities for the words of an insane poet?; referring to Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  37037:
      "Verily, they have fabricated a grave lie. The Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم was not insane nor a poet; he brought the Quran, which invites towards the oneness of Allah and following His Messenger. He corroborated the message of monotheism (i.e., Allah's Oneness) and affirmation of the Hereafter, which the previous messengers brought from Allah; he did not contradict them in anything.",
  37038:
      "O polytheists, you will surely taste the painful torment on the Day of Resurrection due to your disbelief and rejection of the messengers.",
  37039:
      "O polytheists, your recompense will only be for the disbelief and acts of disobedience you used to commit in this world.",
  37040:
      "However, the believing slaves of Allah whom Allah chose for His worship and who sincerely devoted worship to Him will be in a place of safety from this torment.",
  37041:
      "For those sincere slaves, a special provision will be granted to them by Allah, known for its purity, beauty, and eternity.",
  37042:
      "From this special provision, they will be provided with the purest fruits they have ever eaten and desired; on top of that, they will be honored with their ranks being raised and being able to see the noble Face of Allah.",
  37043:
      "They will get all of that in the gardens of everlasting permanent bliss that will never end or cease to exist.",
  37044: "They will recline on couches, facing one another.",
  37045:
      "Glasses filled from rivers flowing with wine that they see before them shall be passed around to them.",
  37046: "White in color, whoever drinks from it will enjoy it thoroughly.",
  37047:
      "It will not be like the wine of this world; it will not intoxicate by clouding the minds, nor will its drinkers experience headaches. The bodies and minds of those who drink it will remain healthy.",
  37048:
      "In Paradise, they will also have chaste wives with beautiful eyes who will not extend their eyesight [longingly] towards anyone other than their husbands.",
  37049:
      "In their white complexion blended with a tinge of yellowness, it will be as if they were bird eggs, protected and untouched by any hand.",
  37050:
      "The people of Paradise will turn to one another, asking about their past and what happened to them.",
  37051:
      "One of the believers will say: Indeed, I had a companion in the worldly life who would deny the resurrection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The cause of the punishment of the disbelievers is evil deeds, which are ascribing partners with Allah and committing sins.\n2. From among the bounties the people of Paradise will be granted is their gathering with one another and being able to see one another. This is from the perfection of happiness.",
  37052:
      "He would say to me in denial and mockingly: O my friend! Are you one of those who believe in the resurrection of the dead?",
  37053:
      "When we die and turn into dust and decayed bones, will we be resurrected and recompensed for the deeds we did in the world?",
  37054:
      "His believing companion will say to his companions of the people of Paradise: Take a look with me; let us see the outcome of that companion of mine who used to deny the resurrection.",
  37055: "Then, he will look and see his companion in the middle of Hell.",
  37056:
      "He will say: O my companion! By Allah, you were close to dooming me to the Fire by calling me towards disbelief and denying the resurrection!",
  37057:
      "Had it not been for Allah favoring me with guidance to belief and the ability to accept it, I would have been one of those brought to the punishment like you.",
  37058:
      "After finishing speaking to his companion from the people of the Fire, a person will turn to speak to their companions from the people of Paradise, stating: \n We, the people of Paradise, will never die.",
  37059:
      "Except our first death on Earth. Then, we will live forever in Paradise and not be tormented as the disbelievers will be.",
  37060:
      "Indeed, this which our Lord has recompensed us with, such as admission into Paradise, remaining therein eternally, and salvation from the Fire, is the greatest success, and no other success equals it.",
  37061:
      "It is for a great reward like this that everyone should strive for because this is a profitable trade.",
  37062:
      "Is that previously mentioned bliss Allah has prepared for His slaves whom He chose to obey Him, better and more virtuous in rank and honor than the cursed tree of Zaqqum in the Quran, which is the food of the disbelievers and neither nourishes nor satisfies hunger?!",
  37063:
      "We have made this tree a trial, with which those who do wrong through disbelief and acts of disobedience are tested when they say: Indeed, fire consumes trees, so it is impossible for it to grow in the Fire.",
  37064:
      "Indeed, the tree of Zaqqum is disgusting and comes out of the depths of the Inferno.",
  37065:
      "The fruits that come out of it are ugly, like the heads of devils. The ugliness of its appearance indicates the ugliness of its content, which means its fruit tastes disgusting.",
  37066:
      "The disbelievers will eat from its bitter, ugly fruits and fill their empty bellies with them.",
  37067:
      "Then, after having eaten from it, they will have a disgusting, boiling mixture to drink.",
  37068:
      "Then, their return after that will be to the torment of the Inferno; they will move from one torment to another.",
  37069:
      "Indeed, these disbelievers found their forefathers astray from the path of guidance and followed them blindly, not based on evidence.",
  37070:
      "So they hastily followed the footsteps of their forefathers in misguidance.",
  37071:
      "And most of the earlier generations also went astray. So, O Messenger, your people are not the first people to go astray.",
  37072:
      "We sent messengers to the previous nations who would warn them of the torment of Allah, but they disbelieved.",
  37073:
      "O Messenger, see what the consequence was for the nations who did not respond when warned by their messengers! Their outcome was entering the Fire and remaining therein eternally due to their disbelief and rejection of their messengers.",
  37074:
      "Except those whom Allah chose to believe in Him and His Oneness. They were saved from the torment, which was the outcome, of the disbelieving rejectors.",
  37075:
      "Our Prophet Noah (peace be upon him) supplicated to Us when he supplicated against his people who had rejected him, and how excellent are We in responding! We quickly answered his supplication against his people.",
  37076:
      "And We delivered him, together with members of his household and the believers, from the harm of his people and from drowning in the great flood, which was sent upon the disbelievers from his people.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Success through achieving the bounties of Paradise is the greatest success. It is this kind of reward the workers should try and strive towards.\n2. Indeed, the food of the people of the hellfire will be Az-Zaqqum: bitter, foul-smelling, difficult to swallow, painful to eat and disgusting fruits.\n3. Allah answered the supplication of Noah (peace be upon him) to destroy his nation; Allah is the best answerer and the best to call out to.",
  37077:
      "We made the offspring of Noah (peace be upon him) the sole survivors after the destruction of his people.",
  37078:
      "And We left for him a beautiful praise among the later nations with which they would extol him.",
  37079:
      "Safety and peace be on Noah from being spoken ill of among the later nations. Instead, praise and a favorable mention of him will remain.",
  37080:
      "Just as We rewarded Noah, We will reward those who do good in their worship and obedience to Allah alone.",
  37081:
      "Noah was one of Our slaves who believed and acted in obedience to Allah.",
  37082:
      "Then We drowned the rest of the people in the flood We sent upon them, and none remained.",
  37083:
      "Abraham was someone of the same religion as Noah, and he also invited to the Oneness of Allah.",
  37084:
      "Remember when he came to his Lord with a heart pure from ascribing partners to Allah and from doubts, full of sincerity to Allah, only wanting good for the creation.",
  37085:
      "When he rebuked his father and his polytheistic people, saying: What is it that you worship instead of Allah?",
  37086: "Is it false deities you are worshipping instead of Allah?",
  37087:
      "O my people, what do you think will happen when you meet the Lord of the worlds while you used to worship others instead of Him? What do you think He will do to you?",
  37088:
      "So Abraham glanced at the stars, hatching a plan to get out of having to go out with his people.",
  37089:
      "He said, presenting an excuse for not going with his people to their festival: I am sick.",
  37090: "So they left him behind and went.",
  37091:
      "He turned towards their deities [idols] they would worship instead of Allah. He said, mocking them: Will you not eat from the food the polytheists prepared for you?",
  37092:
      "What is the matter with you that you do not speak nor answer whoever asks you? Can this type of thing be worshipped instead of Allah?",
  37093:
      "Then, Abraham turned to them, hitting them with his right hand to break them.",
  37094: "Then the worshippers of these idols came rushing to him.",
  37095:
      "But Abraham countered them with steadfastness and rebuked them, saying: Do you worship deities instead of Allah, which you carve with your own hands?",
  37096:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) created you and your deeds; and from among your deeds is the making of these idols, so He is most deserving to be worshipped alone. None should be associated as partners with Him.",
  37097:
      "When they could not refute him with evidence, they resorted to violence. They consulted with each other about what they should do with Abraham. They said: Build a structure for him, fill it with firewood and set it on fire, then throw him into it.",
  37098:
      "So the people of Abraham intended to do evil to him by killing him to be relieved of him, but We made them the losers when We made the fire cool and safe for him.",
  37099:
      "Abraham said: I am going to emigrate to my Lord and leave the city of my people so that I can worship Him. My Lord will guide me to whatever is good for me in this world and the Hereafter.",
  37100:
      "O my Lord! Grant me a pious child who can help me and be a substitute for my people in exile.",
  37101:
      "So We responded to his supplication and gave him news which pleased him when We gave him the good news of a child who would grow up and become forbearing. This child was Ishmael (peace be upon him).",
  37102:
      "When Ishmael grew up and reached the age to work with his father, his father saw a dream. The dreams of prophets are a form of divine revelation, so Abraham told his son, informing him of the meaning of this dream: O my [dear] son! I saw in my sleep that I am slaughtering you, so tell me what you think. Ishmael replied to him, saying: O my father! Do whatever Allah has commanded you to do by slaughtering me. You will find me one of those who are patient and content with the order of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. From among the manifestations of the bounties of Allah upon Noah are: Noah being saved together with those who believed with him; his progeny being the ancestors for the rest of humanity after them, and the positive mention and praise remaining for him.\n2. The objective of the Prophets and messengers is one: calling towards the oneness of Allah and the roots of good character and virtue.\n3. Allah creates everything including the actions mankind chooses to do.\n4. Emigration and seclusion is legislated when a Muslim is unable to uphold the tenets of his religion. The first person to have done so was Abraham (peace be upon him).\n5. The son who was about to be slaughtered according to the implication of these verses was Ishmael (peace be upon him), because He was the one given glad tidings of in the first place. As for Isaac (peace be upon him). He was given glad tidings of after Ishmael (peace be upon him).",
  37103:
      "So when they submitted to Allah and obeyed Him, Abraham laid his son down on the side of his forehead to carry out the order given to him to slaughter his son.",
  37104:
      "We called out to Abraham while he was about to carry out the order of Allah to slaughter his son, saying: O Abraham!",
  37105:
      "You have fulfilled the dream you saw in your sleep by resolving to slaughter your son. Just as We have rewarded you by freeing you of this great trial, We also reward those who do good by saving them from trials and difficulties.",
  37106: "Indeed, this was a clear test that Abraham passed.",
  37107:
      "And We ransomed Ishmael in exchange for a huge ram to be slaughtered instead of him.",
  37108:
      "And We made a beautiful praise for Abraham remain among the later nations.",
  37109:
      "As a greeting for Abraham from Allah and a supplication to keep him safe from every harm and difficulty.",
  37110:
      "Just as We recompensed Abraham with this reward for his obedience, We also reward those who do good.",
  37111:
      "Abraham was one of Our believing slaves who fulfilled what servitude to Allah requires.",
  37112:
      "And We gave him glad tidings of another son, Isaac, who would become a prophet and a pious slave, as a reward for his obedience to Allah by resolving to slaughter his only son, Ishmael.",
  37113:
      "And We sent down upon him and his son Isaac Our special blessings and gave them both many favors, one of which was an increase in offspring. There were those among their progeny who did good by obeying their Lord and those who wronged themselves by disbelief and committing acts of disobedience.",
  37114: "And We favored Moses and his brother Aaron with prophethood.",
  37115:
      "We saved them and their people, the Israelites, from Pharaoh enslaving them and from drowning.",
  37116:
      "We also helped them against Pharaoh and his armies, giving them the upper hand over their enemies.",
  37117:
      "We gave Moses and his brother Aaron the Torah, a clear book from Allah that contained no confusion.",
  37118:
      "We also guided them towards the straight path in which there was no deviance. [This straight path] is the path of the religion of Islam that leads to the pleasure of the Creator; may He be Exalted.",
  37119:
      "And We left for them a beautiful praise and favorable mention among the later nations.",
  37120:
      "They have a beautiful greeting from Allah, praise, and supplication for their safety from every harm.",
  37121:
      "Just as We recompensed Moses and Aaron with this beautiful reward, We also recompense those who do good by obeying their Lord.",
  37122:
      "Moses and Aaron were among Our slaves who believed in Allah and acted on what He legislated for them.",
  37123:
      "Elijah was one of the messengers sent by his Lord. Allah blessed him with prophethood and messengership.",
  37124:
      "Remember when he told his people whom he was sent to from the Israelites: O my people! Do you not fear Allah by fulfilling His commands, which include monotheism, and refraining from what He has prohibited, including associating partners with Him?",
  37125:
      "Do you worship your idol Ba'l instead of Allah and leave the worship of Allah, who is the Best of creators?",
  37126:
      "Allah is your Lord who created you and your forefathers before you. So, He is the most deserving of worship. No one else from the idols who cannot benefit nor harm is worthy.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The statement of Ishmael: “You will find me, if Allah wills, of the steadfast.” was the cause of Allah granting him the ability to be patient, because he entrusted the matter to Allah.\n2. The saying of Allah: “And when they had both submitted” is proof that Abraham and Ishmael (peace be upon them) both were at the peak of their submission to the command of Allah.",
  37127:
      "The only response of his people was that they rejected him, and because of their rejection, they will be brought to the torment.",
  37128:
      "Except for those among his people who were believers and devoted in their worship to Allah, they will be saved from being brought to the torment.",
  37129:
      "And We left for him a beautiful praise and favorable mention among the later nations.",
  37130: "As a greeting from Allah and praise for Elijah.",
  37131:
      "Just as We recompensed Elijah with this beautiful reward, We will reward those who do good from Our believing slaves.",
  37132:
      "Indeed, Elijah was one of Our true believing slaves who sincerely believed in Me.",
  37133:
      "And Lot was one of the messengers of Allah who were sent to their people as bearers of good news and warners.",
  37134:
      "Remember when We delivered him and all his family from the torment sent upon his people.",
  37135:
      "Except for his wife, because she was a woman included in the torment of her people due to her being a disbeliever like them.",
  37136:
      "Then, We destroyed the rest of his people who rejected him and did not believe in what he had brought.",
  37137:
      "O people of Mecca, you pass their homes in your journeys towards the Levant in the morning.",
  37138:
      "And likewise, you also pass them at night. So, do you not understand and take heed from the outcome of these people after they rejected, disbelieved, and committed immoral actions, which were unprecedented?",
  37139:
      "And Jonah was one of the messengers of Allah who were sent to their people as bearers of good news and warners.",
  37140:
      "When he fled from his people without His Lord's permission and boarded a ship full of passengers and goods.",
  37141:
      "The ship was close to sinking because of its load, so the passengers drew lots to throw some of them overboard, fearing that it would sink because of too many passengers. Jonah was one of those that lost, so they threw him into the sea.",
  37142:
      "After they threw him into the sea, a whale took and swallowed him. He did that for which he was blameworthy because he went to the sea without His Lord's permission.",
  37143:
      "Had it not been that Jonah was among those who remembered Allah abundantly before what happened to him, and had it not been for his exalting Allah in the belly of the whale,",
  37144:
      "He would have remained in the belly of the whale until the Day of Resurrection, with it having become his grave.",
  37145:
      "So We cast him from the belly of the whale and placed him on a land with no trees and buildings while he was physically weak because of having remained in the belly of the whale for a while.",
  37146:
      "And caused a gourd tree to grow over him on that barren land, which would give him shade and from which he could eat.",
  37147:
      "And We sent him back to his people, their number being a hundred thousand or more.",
  37148:
      "They believed and had faith in what He brought, so Allah granted them enjoyment in their worldly lives until their appointed time came.",
  37149:
      "So, O Muhammad, ask these polytheists a rebuking question: Do you ascribe daughter to Allah, which you dislike, while ascribing sons to yourselves, which you prefer? What kind of distribution is this?",
  37150:
      "How could they claim the angels are female when they were not present at their creation and did not witness it?",
  37151:
      "Behold! The polytheists, due to their lies and fabrications against Allah, attribute a child to Him while they are liars in this claim of theirs.",
  37152:
      "Behold! The polytheists, due to their lies and fabrications against Allah, attribute a child to Him while they are liars in this claim of theirs.",
  37153:
      "Would Allah prefer daughters for Himself, which you dislike, over sons you prefer? Never!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The divine custom of Allah which will never change is: saving the believers and destroying the disbelievers.\n2. It is necessary to take heed and lessons from the outcomes of those who rejected the messengers, so that whatever came to them, does not come to us.\n3. It is permissible in the Sharia to draw lots because of the statement of Allah: “And he drew lots and was among the losers.”",
  37154:
      "O polytheists, what is wrong with you making this unjust judgment where you ascribe daughters to Allah and sons for yourselves?",
  37155:
      "Do you not reflect on the falsity of this corrupt belief you are upon? If you were to reflect, you would not say such words.",
  37156:
      "Or do you have clear proof and plain evidence from a [divine] book or a messenger [from Allah]?",
  37157:
      "Then bring your book, which bears evidence of this if you are truthful in your claim.",
  37158:
      "The polytheists established a lineage between Allah and the invisible angels when they claimed the angels were Allah's daughters. Yet the angels know that Allah will bring the polytheists to be reckoned.",
  37159:
      "Pure is Allah, and sanctified is He from what the polytheists describe Him with that which does not befit Him, such as having a child, partners, etc.",
  37160:
      "Except for Allah's chosen slaves, they do not describe Allah except with the attributes of majesty and perfection, which befit Him; may He be Exalted.",
  37161: "Surely, O polytheists, you and what you worship instead of Allah...",
  37162: "Cannot misguide anyone from the true religion.",
  37163:
      "Except for those whom Allah has decreed to be from the people of the Fire, Allah will fulfill His decree regarding them. They will thus disbelieve and enter the Fire. As for you and your deities, you do not have power over that.",
  37164:
      "And the angels said, stating their servitude to Allah and declaring their innocence from what the polytheists claimed: There is none among us except that he has a known position in worshipping and obeying Allah.",
  37165:
      "And we, the angels, stand in rows in Allah's worship and obedience and declare Him free from the attributes and descriptions which do not befit Him.",
  37166:
      "And we, the angels, stand in rows in Allah's worship and obedience and declare Him free from the attributes and descriptions which do not befit Him.",
  37167:
      "And the polytheists from the people of Mecca used to say before Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was sent: If we had a book of the books of the previous people, such as the Torah, for example, We would have worshipped Allah devotedly. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought them the Quran, but they disbelieved in it. Soon, they will know the severe punishment awaiting them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  37168:
      "And the polytheists from the people of Mecca used to say before Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was sent: If we had a book of the books of the previous people, such as the Torah, for example, We would have worshipped Allah devotedly. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought them the Quran, but they disbelieved in it. Soon, they will know the severe punishment awaiting them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  37169:
      "And the polytheists from the people of Mecca used to say before Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was sent: If we had a book of the books of the previous people, such as the Torah, for example, We would have worshipped Allah devotedly. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought them the Quran, but they disbelieved in it. Soon, they will know the severe punishment awaiting them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  37170:
      "And the polytheists from the people of Mecca used to say before Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was sent: If we had a book of the books of the previous people, such as the Torah, for example, We would have worshipped Allah devotedly. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought them the Quran, but they disbelieved in it. Soon, they will know the severe punishment awaiting them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  37171:
      "Our word, which none can reverse or repel, has already gone forth to Our messengers that they will be victorious against their enemies through what Allah has favored them with of evidence and strength. And Our army, which fights in Allah's path, will have the upper hand so Allah's word will prevail.",
  37172:
      "Our word, which none can reverse or repel, has already gone forth to Our messengers that they will be victorious against their enemies through what Allah has favored them with of evidence and strength. And Our army, which fights in Allah's path, will have the upper hand so Allah's word will prevail.",
  37173:
      "Our word, which none can reverse or repel, has already gone forth to Our messengers that they will be victorious against their enemies through what Allah has favored them with of evidence and strength. And Our army, which fights in Allah's path, will have the upper hand so Allah's word will prevail.",
  37174:
      "So turn away, O Messenger, from these stubborn polytheists until a period that Allah knows, which is when their torment comes.",
  37175:
      "And watch them when the torment comes down upon them, for they themselves will see when their sight will be of no benefit.",
  37176: "Then do these polytheists hastily seek Allah's torment?",
  37177:
      "Then when Allah's torment comes down upon them, what a bad morning will theirs be!",
  37178:
      "And turn away, O Messenger, from them when Allah decrees their torment.",
  37179:
      "And watch, for these people will see the torment and punishment of Allah come upon them.",
  37180:
      "O Muhammad, free and declare your Lord sanctified, the Lord of might, above the attributes of deficiency the polytheists describe Him with.",
  37181: "And Allah's greetings and praise be upon His noble messengers.",
  37182:
      "And all praise be to Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, as He is deserving of it, and He is Lord of all creation. They have no lord besides Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The divine custom of Allah is to help the messengers and those who inherit and pass on the knowledge of the message through proof and dominance, and there is a great glad tiding in the verses that the one described as being from Allah’s army will be dominant and helped.\n2. The verses contain proof of the helplessness of the idolaters and their idols from misguiding anyone, and a glad tiding for Allah’s chosen servants that Allah through His power will save them from the misguidance of those individuals who are misguided and aim to lead others astray.",
  38000:
      "The Letter \"Saad\" (Surah Sad)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nMentioning the issue of debating with falsehood and the consequences of doing so.\n•    Explanation:",
  38001:
      "Sād – The discussion on the disconnected letters has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. I take an oath by the Quran, which contains a reminder for humanity that benefits them in their worldly life and the Hereafter. The matter is not as the polytheists think, namely, that Allah has partners [deities].",
  38002:
      "But the disbelievers are in [a state of] prejudice and arrogance towards the Oneness of Allah, and in [a state of] opposition and hostility towards Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  38003:
      "How many generations who rejected their messengers before these polytheists have We destroyed? They then called out seeking help when the torment came down upon them. Then was not the time for them to be saved from the torment; thus, seeking help from Him was useless.",
  38004:
      "And they are astonished when a messenger comes to them from among themselves to warn them of Allah's torment if they continue in disbelief. When the disbelievers saw the proofs of the truthfulness of what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought, they said: This is a magician who performs magic on people and a liar in claiming that he is a messenger from Allah who receives revelation.",
  38005:
      "Has this man reduced numerous deities into one God, besides whom there is no deity? This act of his is extremely strange.",
  38006:
      "And their nobles and elders went forth, saying to their followers: Carry on with what you are upon and do not enter the religion of Muhammad. Remain firm upon worshipping your deities. That which Muhammad is inviting you towards, namely worshipping one God, is something planned that he wants so that he can reign supreme over us and we become his followers.",
  38007:
      "We have not heard about the Oneness of Allah that Muhammad is inviting us towards in what we found our fathers upon nor in the religion of Jesus (peace be upon him). What we have heard from him is nothing but a lie and fabrication.",
  38008:
      "Is it correct that the Quran is revealed to him out of all of us, he is chosen for it, and it is not revealed to us, whereas we are senior chiefs? But these polytheists doubt the revelation revealed to you, and they have not yet tasted Allah's torment, so they have been deceived due to being given respite. If they were to taste it, they would not have the audacity to disbelieve, associate partners with Allah, and doubt what is revealed to you.",
  38009:
      "Or is it because these rejecting polytheists possess the treasures of your Lord's favors, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, who gives what He wants to whom He wants? And from among His treasures of favors is prophethood; He gives it to whom He wishes. It is not up to them to give it to whom they want and prevent it from whom they want.",
  38010:
      "Or is it because the dominion of the heavens, the Earth, and everything in between belongs to them, so they may choose who they give it to or not? If this is their claim, let them adopt the means to go up to the heavens so they can decide what they desire regarding who should be given and who should be held back from. They will not be able to do that!",
  38011:
      "These people who reject Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم are a defeated army like those armies who came before them who rejected their messengers.",
  38012:
      "These people are not the first to reject; instead, the people of Noah, 'Ād, and the Pharaoh, who had stakes with which he punished people, rejected before them.",
  38013:
      "Also, Thamūd, the people of Lot, and Shuayb's people rejected. Those are the groups who were all united in rejecting their messengers and disbelieving in what they brought.",
  38014:
      "There is not one of these groups except that they rejected the messengers. So Allah's torment was justified against them, and His punishment befell them, even though it was delayed for a while.",
  38015:
      "These people who reject Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم are not waiting except for the second blowing of the Trumpet in which there shall be no return. Then, the torment will befall them if they had died while rejecting him.",
  38016:
      "And they said mockingly: O our Lord! Hasten for us our share of the torment in the worldly life before the Day of Resurrection.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah swore an oath by the great Qur’an, so it is necessary to receive it with faith and acceptance, and to dedicate oneself to extracting its meanings.\n2. The causes for the disbelievers to turn away from faith are: arrogance, tyranny, considering oneself above following the truth, and opposing Allah and the guidance of His Messenger (peace be upon him).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah swore an oath by the great Qur’an, so it is necessary to receive it with faith and acceptance, and to dedicate oneself to extracting its meanings.\n2. The causes for the disbelievers to turn away from faith are: arrogance, tyranny, considering oneself above following the truth, and opposing Allah and the guidance of His Messenger (peace be upon him).",
  38017:
      "O Messenger, be patient with what these rejectors say that does not please you, and remember My slave David, who had the power to fight his enemies and persevere in Allah's obedience. He used to turn to Allah frequently through repentance and deeds which pleased Him.",
  38018:
      "We subjugated the mountains with David: they would exalt Allah along with David at the end and the beginning of the day at sunrise.",
  38019:
      "And We subjugated the birds held in the air. All of them were obedient, exalting Allah, following David.",
  38020:
      "And We strengthened his kingdom by gifting him with stature, strength, and support against his enemies. And We gave him prophethood, correctness in his affairs, eloquence clarifying his every intent, and decisiveness in speech and judgment.",
  38021:
      "O Messenger, has the news of the two disputants reached you when they scaled David's (peace be upon him) place of worship?",
  38022:
      "When they dropped in on David suddenly, he was startled by the unusual and sudden way they dropped in. When they saw his fear, they said: Do not fear. We are two disputants: one of us has wronged the other, so judge between us justly and do not be unjust when you judge between us, and guide us to the right path, which is the correct path.",
  38023:
      "One of the disputants said to David (peace be upon him): This man is my brother. He has ninety-nine ewes, and I have one ewe. He asked me to give it to him, and he won the argument against me.",
  38024:
      "David eventually judged between them and addressed the claimant, saying: Your brother has wronged you in demanding you to add your ewe to his ewes. And many partners transgress against each other by taking their rights and not being fair, except the believers who do righteous deeds, for they are fair with their partners and do not wrong them. But those attributed with that are few. Then David (peace be upon him) knew that We had only trialed him through this dispute, so he sought forgiveness from his Lord, prostrated to get close to Him, and repented to Him.",
  38025:
      "So We responded to him and forgave him for that. He is among those close to Us, and he has a beautiful destination in the Hereafter.",
  38026:
      "[Allah said]: O David, We made you a deputy on Earth to execute the worldly and religious rulings and judgments, so judge between people with justice. And do not follow desires in your judgment between people by inclining towards one of the disputants due to a relationship or friendship or by turning away from one of them due to enmity, whereby desires will mislead you from Allah's straight path. Those who go astray from Allah's straight path will receive a severe punishment due to forgetting the Day of Reckoning because if they were to remember it and fear it, they would not be inclined to follow their desires.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The virtues of Allah’s Prophet David and the miracles Allah chose him with have been stated.\n2. The Prophets (peace be upon them) are protected from mistakes in conveying on Allah’s behalf, as the objective of messengership cannot be achieved except through that. However, sometimes certain things according to human nature, such as forgetfulness or absentmindedness from a ruling, occur from them, but Allah corrects them and quickly shows His grace to them.\n3. The scholars have proven the permissibility of partnership between two or more people from the saying of Allah: “And many associates oppress one another”.",
  38027:
      "And We have not created the heavens and the Earth in vain. That is the thinking of those who disbelieve. So, woe to these disbelievers who think this, for they will have the torment of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection when they die disbelieving and having bad thoughts about Allah.",
  38028:
      "We will never consider those who believe in Allah, follow His messenger, and do righteous deeds like those who spread corruption throughout the land through disbelief and committing acts of disobedience, nor will We consider those who fear their Lord by fulfilling His orders and avoiding His prohibitions like those who disbelieve and the hypocrites who are engrossed in acts of disobedience. Considering them both equal is an injustice that does not befit Allah. Instead, Allah will recompense the believers who fear Allah by admitting them into Paradise and punish the wretched disbelievers by admitting them into the Fire because they are not equal in Allah's sight. Thus, their reward is also not equal in His sight.",
  38029:
      "This Quran is a book We have revealed to you [Muhammad] which contains much good and benefit. [We have revealed it] so that people ponder over its verses and contemplate its meanings and so that the people of enlightened superior intellect take lessons from it.",
  38030:
      "And We granted David his son Solomon, as Our favor and grace to him so that he would be pleased. What an excellent slave Solomon was. He would abundantly repent and return to Allah.",
  38031:
      "Remember when, at the time of Asr, fast purebred horses were presented to him, standing on three feet with one foot raised. These purebred horses continued to be presented to him until sunset.",
  38032:
      "So Solomon said: I preferred the love of wealth, which includes these horses, over the remembrance of my Lord until sunset, and I delayed the afternoon prayer.",
  38033:
      "[He then said:] Bring these horses back to me. So they brought them back to him, and he began striking their legs and necks with his sword.",
  38034:
      "And We tested Solomon and placed on his throne a devil in the form of a human who took control of his kingdom for a short while. Then Allah returned his kingdom to him and gave him authority over the devils.",
  38035:
      "Solomon said: O my Lord, forgive me for my sins and grant me an exclusive kingdom, which no person will have after me. O my Lord, You give abundantly, and You are very generous.",
  38036:
      "So We responded to him and subjugated the wind for him. It would submit to his command [and blow] gently. Despite its strength and swift movement, there was no gale-force wind. It would carry him wherever he intended.",
  38037:
      "And We subjugated the devils for him, complying with his orders. Some were builders, and others were divers who would dive into the seas and take out pearls from them.",
  38038:
      "And among the devils, some rebellious ones were subservient to him. They were bound together in chains, unable to move.",
  38039:
      "O Solomon, this is Our gift, which We gifted you in response to what you asked of Us. So give and withhold from whoever you want, as you will never be held to account for your giving or withholding.",
  38040:
      "And Solomon is among the close ones with us. He will receive a beautiful destination, which he will return to: Paradise.",
  38041:
      "O Messenger, remember Our slave Job when he supplicated to Allah, his Lord: The Devil has afflicted me with a tiring and painful condition.",
  38042:
      "So We then said to him: Strike your foot on the ground. So he struck his foot on the ground, and water sprung forth for him from it, which he would drink and bathe from, and through it, his suffering and pain would disappear.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an has been revealed for us to contemplate over it.\n2. According to the soundness of a person’s heart and intelligence will be the admonition and benefit he takes away from the noble Qur’an.\n3. It is necessary to maintain etiquette when going to people of virtue and position.\n4. The verses contain proof for the famous principle: “Whoever leaves something for Allah, Allah gives him something better in its place”.",
  38043:
      "So We responded to him and removed the difficulty he was afflicted with: We gave him back his family and added to them a similar number of sons and grandsons as a mercy from Us to him and a recompense for his patience so that the people of superior intellect are reminded that the outcome of patience is relief and reward.",
  38044:
      "When Job became angry with his wife, he swore an oath that he would lash her a hundred times, so We said to him: O Job, take a bunch of twigs in your hand and hit her with them to fulfill your oath. And do not break the oath you made. He then took a bunch of twigs and hit her with them. We found him to be patient in what We tried him with. What an excellent slave he was. He would return to Allah and repent to Him abundantly.",
  38045:
      "O Messenger, remember Our slaves whom We chose and the messengers whom We sent: Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. They were people firm in obeying Allah and seeking His pleasure, and they were people of real insight into the truth.",
  38046:
      "We blessed them with a special favor for which We selected them, occupying their hearts with the remembrance of the abode of the Hereafter, preparing for it through righteous deeds, and inviting people towards doing deeds to gain it.",
  38047:
      "And they were in Our sight among those whom We chose for Our obedience and worship, and whom We selected to bear Our message and convey it to the people.",
  38048:
      "O Prophet, remember Ishmael, the son of Abraham, Elisha, and Dhul-Kifl, and praise them well as they deserve it. All these individuals were among the chosen and selected by Allah.",
  38049:
      "This is only a reminder for these people of good praise in the Quran. And for those who fear Allah by fulfilling His orders and avoiding His prohibitions, is a beautiful destination in the abode of the Hereafter.",
  38050:
      "This beautiful destination is the gardens of eternity; they will enter it on the Day of Resurrection through doors that will be opened to welcome them.",
  38051:
      "Reclining on couches that will be adorned for them. They will ask their attendants to bring them the many different types of fruit and drinks they desire, such as wine and other things.",
  38052:
      "And with them will be women whose gaze will be limited only to them, their husbands. They will be all of equal age.",
  38053:
      "This is the pleasant recompense you are being promised, O you who feared Allah, on the Day of Resurrection for the righteous deeds you used to do in the world.",
  38054:
      "This recompense that We have mentioned is our provision that We will provide those who fear Allah on the Day of Resurrection. It is a continuous provision that will never pause or end.",
  38055:
      "This that We have mentioned is the reward for those who fear Allah. And those who transgress the limits of Allah through disbelief and committing acts of disobedience will have a recompense different from those who fear Allah. They will have the worst destination they shall return to on the Day of Resurrection.",
  38056:
      "This recompense is Hell, which will surround them, and they will experience its heat and flames. They will have a place to lay down in it, and what an evil place they will have!",
  38057:
      "This torment is boiling water and pus flowing from the bodies of the people of the Fire being punished in it, so they should drink it as it is their drink. However, it is a drink which does not quench thirst.",
  38058:
      "And they will receive another torment similar to this one. They will receive various torments, which they will be punished with in the Hereafter.",
  38059:
      "And when the people of the Fire enter, they will dispute with one another, cursing and disassociating from one another. Some will say: This is a [new] group that will inhabit the Fire with you. They will respond: They are not welcome; they too will suffer the torment of the Fire like we are suffering.",
  38060:
      "The followers will say to their leaders who were followed: Instead, O leaders who were followed, you are not welcome, as you caused us this painful torment by misguiding and leading us astray. What a terrible settlement this is; the settlement of all of them is Hellfire.",
  38061:
      "The followers will say: O our Lord, whoever misguided us from the guidance after it came to us, double his torment in the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whoever is patient upon difficulty, Allah will reward him with an immediate and future reward, and respond to his call when he calls upon Him.\n2. The illness of Job (peace be upon him) was not repulsive, as he was a prophet who mixed with the people.\n3. The verses contain proof that the husband may withhold himself from his wife to correct her, as did Job (peace be upon him) with his wife.",
  38062:
      "And the arrogant tyrants will say: Why do we not see men with us in the Fire whom we used to consider among the wretched in the world and who deserve punishment?",
  38063:
      "Was mocking them a mistake thus they do not deserve to be punished, or was mocking them right, and they have entered the Fire, but we have not seen them yet?",
  38064:
      "This disputing of the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection, which We have mentioned to you, is the truth in which there is no doubt.",
  38065:
      "O Muhammad, say to the disbelievers from your people: I am only a warner to you of Allah's torment, lest it descends upon you due to disbelief and rejecting His messengers. And there is no deity worthy of worship besides Allah; may He be Exalted, as He is unique in His greatness, attributes, and names, and He is the Subduer who has subdued everything. So everything submits to Him.",
  38066:
      "And He is the Lord of the heavens, the Earth, and whatever is between them. And He is the Mighty in His kingdom, with nobody to overpower Him, and Forgiving of the sins of His slaves who repent to Him.",
  38067:
      "O Messenger, tell these rejectors: The Quran is news of great importance.",
  38068:
      "You are turning away from this news of great importance; you do not turn towards it.",
  38069:
      "I would not have knowledge of the discussion between the angels regarding the creation of Adam if Allah had not revealed it to me and taught me.",
  38070:
      "Allah only reveals to me what He reveals, and I am a clear warner to you of His torment.",
  38071:
      "Remember when your Lord said to the angels: I am going to create a man from clay, and he is Adam (peace be upon him).",
  38072:
      "So once I have fashioned his form, perfected his appearance, and blown My spirit into him, then prostrate to him!",
  38073:
      "So the angels fulfilled the command of their Lord, and all of them prostrated by way of honor, and none of them remained except that they prostrated to Adam.",
  38074:
      "But not Iblis, who was too arrogant to prostrate. And by being arrogant to the command of his Lord, he became one of the disbelievers.",
  38075:
      "Allah said: O Iblis, what prevented you from prostrating to Adam whom I created with My Own Hands? Did arrogance prevent you from prostrating to him, or have you always been arrogant and haughty against your Lord?",
  38076:
      "Iblis said: I am better than Adam because You created me from fire while You created him from clay. This was due to his claim that fire was a more noble substance than clay.",
  38077:
      "Allah told Iblis: Get out of Paradise because you are accursed and reviled.",
  38078:
      "And you are to be rejected from Paradise until the Day of Recompense, which is the Day of Resurrection.",
  38079:
      "Iblis said: Give me respite and do not cause me to die until the day You resurrect Your slaves.",
  38080: "Allah said: You are amongst those given respite.",
  38081: "Until the appointed day for your destruction.",
  38082:
      "Iblis said: I take an oath by Your [attributes of] power and subjugation that I shall misguide all of the children of Adam",
  38083:
      "Except those whom You protect from my misguidance and those whom You have chosen to worship You alone.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride prevents a person from following the truth.\n2. To make analogies and deduce in the presence of a clear text is a baseless method.\n3. The disbelief of Iblis is out of stubbornness.\n4. The satan has no power over those from the creation whom Allah has chosen for His worship.",
  38084:
      "Allah, the Exalted, said: The truth is from Me, and the truth is what I say. I do not say anything besides it.",
  38085:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, I shall fill Hell with you and those from the children of Adam who follow you in your disbelief, every last one of you.",
  38086:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: I do not ask you for any reward for the advice I convey to you, and I am not of the pretentious by bringing more than what I have been ordered with.",
  38087:
      "The Quran is only a reminder to those men and jinn who are legally competent.",
  38088:
      "And definitely, after a short time, when you die, you will come to know the news of this Quran and that it is true.",
  39000:
      "The Troops (Surah Az-Zumar)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nCalling to monotheism and sincerity while rejecting polytheism.\n•    Explanation:",
  39001:
      "The revelation of the Quran is from Allah, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, the Wise in His creating, planning, and legislating. No one besides Him revealed it; may He be Exalted.",
  39002:
      "O Messenger, We have revealed the Quran to you, which contains the truth, so all of its information is true, and all of its rulings are just. So worship Allah, declaring Him to be One and sincerely devoted to Him.",
  39003:
      "Indeed, sincere devotion is due only to Allah, pure of polytheism. And those who have taken guardians besides Allah, such as idols and any false deities which they worship instead of Allah, presenting an excuse for worshipping them by saying that they do not worship these except so that they bring them closer to Allah in status, present their needs to Him and intercede on their behalf with Him; Allah will judge between the monotheistic believers and the polytheistic disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection regarding Allah's Oneness, in which they used to differ. Allah does not inspire with guidance towards the truth those who lie against Him by associating a partner with Him and those who deny Allah's favors.",
  39004:
      "If Allah wanted to take a son, He would have chosen whom He wanted from His creation and taken him as a child. Free and sanctified is He, from what these polytheists say. He is One in His essence, attributes, and actions, having no partner in them, the Subduer of all His creation.",
  39005:
      "He created the heavens and the Earth with complete wisdom, not in vain, as the wrongdoers say. He merges the night into the day and the day into the night, so when one comes, the other disappears. And He has made the sun and the moon subservient; each one orbits for up until an appointed time, which is the end of this life. He (may He be Exalted) is the Mighty who takes retribution from His enemies, and nobody can overpower Him, Forgiving the sins of His slaves who repent.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The caller to Allah expects reward from Him. He does not seek reward from people for the truth he is calling them towards.\n2. Pretentiousness is not part of the religion.\n3. Faith, good deeds, Allah’s names and attributes are the only means a person may use to draw closer to Allah.",
  39006:
      "O humanity, your Lord created you from one soul, Adam, and then He created from Adam his wife, Eve. He created four pairs of livestock for your benefit: camels, cows, sheep, and goats, from each type, male and female. He creates you in the wombs of your mothers, stage after stage, in three layers of darkness: the stomach, womb, and placenta. He who creates all of that is Allah, your Lord. To Him alone belongs the dominion. There is no deity worthy of worship besides Him, so how are you turned away from His worship to worshipping those who create nothing but are instead created?",
  39007:
      "O humanity, if you disbelieve in your Lord, then Allah does not need your belief. Your disbelief does not harm Him. The harm of your disbelief only affects you. He does not approve for His slaves to disbelieve in Him, nor does He order them to disbelieve, because Allah does not order indecency and wrong. If you show gratitude to Allah for His favors and believe in Him, He will be pleased with your gratitude and reward you for it. No soul will carry the sin of another; instead, every soul will be retained for what it has done. Then, to your Lord alone is your return on the Day of Resurrection, and He will inform you of what you used to do in the world and recompense you for your deeds accordingly. He (may He be Exalted) is Knowing of what is in the hearts of His slaves; nothing of what is in them is hidden from Him.",
  39008:
      "And when the disbeliever is afflicted by a difficulty, such as illness, loss of wealth, or fear of drowning, he supplicates to his Lord (may He be Exalted) to remove the difficulty he experiences, turning to Him alone. Then, when Allah favors him by removing the difficulty that afflicted him, he abandons Allah, whom he used to beseech before, and he associates partners with Allah, whom he worships instead of Him. O Messenger, say to a person like this: Enjoy your disbelief for as long as you live, which is a short time, as you are among the people of the Fire who will be inseparable from it on the Day of Resurrection like a companion is inseparable from his friend.",
  39009:
      "Is he who is obedient to Allah, spending the time at night in prostration to his Lord and standing, fearing the torment of the Hereafter and hoping for the mercy of his Lord better, or that disbeliever who worships Allah in hardship but disbelieves in Him in times of ease and associates partners with Him? O Messenger, say: Are those who know what Allah has made obligatory upon them due to their knowledge of Allah and those who do not know any of this equal? Only people of sound intellect recognize the difference between the two.",
  39010:
      "O Messenger, say to my slaves who believe in Me and My messengers: Fear your Lord by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Those among you who do good deeds in this world will receive good in this world through divine assistance, health, and wealth, and in the Hereafter, they will receive Paradise. The land of Allah is vast, so migrate therein until you find a place where you can worship Allah without anything stopping you. The reward given to the patient on the Day of Resurrection will be immeasurable and unlimited due to its abundance and variety.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah looks after the human in the mother’s womb.\n2. Allah is Self Sufficient, no one can benefit Him, and He is pleased with those who are grateful to Him.\n3. The disbeliever recognising Allah in hardship and abandoning Him in ease is proof of his state of disorder and confusion.\n4. Fear and hope are qualities of the people of faith.\n5. A sinful disbeliever and an obedient believer are not the same.",
  39011:
      "Say, O Messenger: Allah has instructed me to worship Him alone, being sincerely devoted to Him.",
  39012:
      "He has instructed me to be the first to surrender and submit to Him from this nation.",
  39013:
      "Say, O Messenger: I fear, if I disobey Allah and I do not obey Him, the punishment of a great day, which is the Day of Resurrection.",
  39014:
      "Say, O Messenger: I worship Allah alone, being sincere in my devotion to Him. I do not worship others with Him.",
  39015:
      "So, O polytheists, worship whatever idols you wish instead of Him (this instruction is a threat). Say, O Messenger: The true losers are those who will lose themselves and their families, whom they will not meet in the Hereafter due to either being separated from their families when their families enter Paradise without them or their families will enter the Fire with them. Thus, they will never meet. That is indeed, and undoubtedly, the obvious loss.",
  39016:
      "They will have smoke, flames, and extreme heat above and beneath them. That torment is what Allah warns His slaves of. So, O My slaves, fear Me by complying with My commands and avoiding My prohibitions.",
  39017:
      "After mentioning the conditions facing the wrongdoers, Allah describes the conditions facing His righteous slaves, stating: \n Those who avoid the worship of idols and any other false gods instead of Allah and return to Allah in repentance will receive glad tidings of Paradise at the time of death, in the grave, and on the Day of Resurrection. So give glad tidings, O Messenger, to My slaves.",
  39018:
      "Those who attentively listen to what is said, distinguish between the good and evil of it, and then follow the best speech because of its benefit; those who possess these attributes are the ones whom Allah has given guidance, and they are the ones who possess sound intellect.",
  39019:
      "Those against whom the decree of torment has been justified due to their persistence in disbelief and misguidance, so, O Messenger, you have no means to guide them; can you, O Messenger, rescue such people from the Fire?",
  39020:
      "But those who fear their Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will have lofty mansions, one above the other, with rivers flowing beneath them. Allah has firmly promised this to them, and Allah does not break His promise.",
  39021:
      "You are well aware, by having seen, that Allah sends down rainwater from the sky and fills springs and rivers with it. Then, with this water, He produces crops of various colors. Then these crops become dry, and you, witnessing this, see them turning yellow after being green. Then, after they become dry, He makes them into chaff. In what has been mentioned, there is a reminder for those whose hearts are alive.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Dedicating worship to Allah is a condition for its acceptance.\n2. Sins necessitate Allah’s punishment and anger.\n3. Guidance to faith is in Allah’s hands, not in the hands of the Messenger (peace be upon him).",
  39022:
      "Then is he who Allah has opened his chest to Islam and is guided to it with insight from his Lord, like the one whose heart is hardened against Allah's remembrance? They can never be equal! Salvation is for those guided, and loss is for those whose hearts are hardened against Allah's remembrance. Such people are in clear misguidance from the truth.",
  39023:
      "Allah has sent down to His Messenger, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, the Quran, which is the best speech. He sent it down so that part of it resembles other parts in truthfulness, beauty, and consistency without contradiction. It contains numerous stories and rulings, promises and threats, attributes of the people of truth, attributes of the people of falsehood, and so forth. The skin of those in awe of their Lord trembles when they hear the threats and warnings it contains. Then their skin and hearts soften to Allah's remembrance when they hear the hope and glad tidings it contains. What has been mentioned about the Quran and its effect is Allah's guidance by which He guides whoever He wills. Those whom Allah leaves astray and does not guide have no one to guide them.",
  39024:
      "Is the person whom Allah guided, blessed in this world, and admitted into Paradise in the Hereafter equal to the person who disbelieved and died as a disbeliever and, as a result, entered the Fire with his hands and feet tied, unable to shield himself against the Fire except by his face that he was pulled upon?! Those who wronged themselves by disbelieving and committing acts of disobedience will be told by way of reproach: Taste the disbelief and acts of disobedience you used to earn, for this is your recompense.",
  39025:
      "The nations before these polytheists also rejected, and the torment came to them suddenly from where they did not expect. Thus, they could not prepare for it by repenting.",
  39026:
      "Allah made them taste through that torment, humiliation, disgrace, and shame in the worldly life. The punishment of the Hereafter that awaits them is greater and more severe, if they only knew.",
  39027:
      "In this Quran revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, We have given people various parables of good and evil, truth and falsehood, belief and disbelief, and so forth in the hope that they will take a lesson from these parables, act on the truth and abandon falsehood.",
  39028:
      "We have made it an Arabic Quran, without any defect, deviation, or confusion, in the hope that they will fear Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  39029:
      "Allah gives an example of a polytheist and a monotheist as that of a man owned by disputing partners - if he pleases some, he angers others, and he is thus confused and disturbed; and of a man who is devoted to one master alone who owns him and whose intentions he knows - he is, therefore, comfortable and calm. These two men are not the same. All praise is to Allah, but most of them do not know, and consequently, they associate others as partners with Allah.",
  39030: "You, O Messenger, will certainly die, and they will die too.",
  39031:
      "Then, O humanity, on the Day of Resurrection, you will dispute among yourselves before your Lord over that which you disagree with one another, and it will become clear who is on the truth and who is on falsehood.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The person who is on guidance from His Lord is not equal to the person whose heart is hard and who is in clear error.\n2. The noble Qur’an is the best speech because it is Allah’s speech and it is true in everything that it contains.\n3. The people of faith and Allah-consciousness are the ones who submit to listening to the Qur’an. The people of sin and betrayal are the ones who do not benefit from it.\n4. Denial of what the messengers brought is cause for the punishment’s coming down either in the world, the Hereafter or in both.\n5. The Qur’an did not leave out any matter pertaining to this world or the Hereafter, but it explained it either in brief or in detail and gave examples for it.",
  39032:
      "No one is more wrong than the person who attributes to Allah what does not befit Him, such as a partner, spouse, or child, and denies the Quran. Also, no one is more wrong than the person who rejects the truth that Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم brought. Is there not in the Fire an eternal abode for those who reject Allah and what His Messenger brought? Indeed, there is a dwelling for them therein.",
  39033:
      "After mentioning the outright liar, Allah mentions the reliable and truthful, stating: \n The prophets and those others who brought truth in speech and action, and those who had faith in it and acted according to it, are the ones who are genuinely Allah-fearing, comply with the commands of their Lord, and avoid His prohibitions.",
  39034:
      "They will have all the everlasting pleasures they wish for from their Lord. That is the reward of those who do good deeds sincerely for their Creator and spread good amongst His slaves.",
  39035:
      "So that Allah may erase from them the worst sins that they used to do in this world, as they had repented from them and turned back to their Lord, and reward them according to the best deeds they used to do.",
  39036:
      "Is not Allah sufficient for His slave, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, in his religious and worldly matters and to ward off his enemy? Indeed, He is sufficient. They try to intimidate you, O Messenger, because of their ignorance and foolishness, with the idols they worship besides Allah, [claiming] they will bring you harm. Those whom Allah abandons and does not bless with guidance will have no one to guide them.",
  39037:
      "Whomever Allah blesses with guidance, no one will be able to mislead. Is Allah not Mighty, whom no one can challenge, and the One who takes retribution from those who reject and go against Him? Indeed, He is Mighty and One who takes vengeance.",
  39038:
      "O Messenger, if you ask these polytheists who created the heavens and who created the Earth, they will say that Allah created them. Say to them, to show them the inability of their gods: Tell me about these idols you worship besides Allah. If Allah willed to harm me, do they have the power to remove that harm from me? Or if my Lord wished to grant me mercy from Himself, can they stop His mercy from reaching me? Say to them: Allah alone is enough for me. It is on Him that I rely in all my affairs. He is the only one relied upon by those who want to entrust their affairs.",
  39039:
      "Say, O Messenger: O my people, continue to act in that state that you have chosen of ascribing partners to Allah. I will continue to act on what my Lord has instructed me by calling towards His Oneness and devoting my worship to Him. Soon, you will come to know the outcome of each path.",
  39040:
      "Soon you will come to know who will be punished in this world in a way that disgraces and humiliates them and upon whom a perpetual punishment will descend in the Hereafter.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Affirmation of Allah’s protection for His messenger (peace be upon him) from being harmed by his enemies.\n2. Affirming Allah’s oneness in lordship only, without affirming His oneness in divinity, will not save a person from the punishment of the fire.",
  39041:
      "O Messenger, We sent you the Quran in truth for the people so you can warn them. Whoever follows the guidance will only benefit from it himself. Allah does not benefit from him following the guidance as He does not need it. Whoever strays, then the harm of him straying is to his own detriment. His straying does not harm Allah. You are not in charge of them to force guidance on them. You are only obliged to convey to them what you have been instructed with.",
  39042:
      "Allah is the One who takes away the souls when their term ends. He also takes the souls whose term has not ended when they sleep. He then withholds those for whom He has decreed death and releases those for whom He has not decreed death until a time fixed in His knowledge (may He be Exalted). In this taking away, release, and giving of death and life, there are signs for people who reflect that the One who does this can resurrect people after they die for reckoning and recompense.",
  39043:
      "The polytheists took their idols as intercessors, hoping to benefit from them instead of Allah. Say to them, O Messenger: Do you take them as intercessors even though they have no power to do anything for you or for themselves and do not understand? They are lifeless objects that cannot speak, hear, see, benefit, or harm.",
  39044:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists: All intercession belongs to Allah alone. No one can intercede before Him except with His permission, and the intercession can only be for those He approves. The control of the heavens and the control of the Earth belongs to Him alone. Then, to Him alone, you will return on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and recompense, and He will give you the outcome you deserve for your actions.",
  39045:
      "Whenever Allah alone is mentioned, the hearts of the polytheists who do not believe in the Hereafter and the resurrection, reckoning, and recompense become filled with hatred. But they become happy when the idols they worship besides Allah are mentioned.",
  39046:
      "Say, O Messenger: O Allah, Creator of the heavens and the Earth without any precedent, Knower of what is absent and what is present. Nothing of that is hidden from You. You alone will decide between Your slaves on the Day of Resurrection what they used to disagree about in this world. It will become clear who is right and who is wrong, and who is fortunate and who is not.",
  39047:
      "If those who wronged themselves by worshipping other than Allah and committing sins could have all of the wealth and treasures on this Earth to ransom themselves from the severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection, they would do so. However, even if they did, the ransom would not be accepted from them. Rather, they will face from Allah various types of torment they never used to expect.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Sleeping and waking up are two regular warnings reminding us of death and the resurrection.\n2. When Allah alone is mentioned to the disbelievers they are afflicted by anguish and sorrow, because they are reminded of what He had instructed what He had prohibited and they turn away from all of this.\n3. A disbeliever will try to ransom himself on the Day of Resurrection with everything he owns despite his miserliness with it in the world, but it will not be accepted from him.",
  39048:
      "The evils of polytheism and the sins they committed will appear to them, and the punishment they were warned of in this world, which they mocked, will engulf them.",
  39049:
      "When a disbelieving man is afflicted by sickness or poverty, he calls on Us to remove his affliction. Then, when We bless him with health or wealth, the disbeliever says: Allah has only given me this because He knows I deserve it. It is a test and a means of luring him to his destruction. But most disbelievers do not know this and are deceived by the blessings Allah gives them.",
  39050:
      "The disbelievers that came before them made this same statement, but the wealth and status they earned were useless to them.",
  39051:
      "The recompense for the evils of polytheism and the sins that they committed caught up with them. Those who wronged themselves by polytheism and sins, from those present [at that time], will also be caught up by the recompense for the evils of what they committed, just like those in the past. They will not escape from Allah nor defeat Him.",
  39052:
      "Do these polytheists say this and not know that Allah expands the provision for whomever He wills as a test for him to see if he is grateful or ungrateful? And he restricts it for whomever he wills as a test to see if he is patient or becomes angry with Allah's decree. In what has been mentioned about the increasing and decreasing of provisions, there are signs of Allah's planning for people who believe because they are the ones who benefit from such signs. On the other hand, the disbelievers pass by them without paying any attention to them.",
  39053:
      "Say, O Messenger, to My slaves who have gone beyond the limit against themselves by ascribing partners to Allah and committing sins: Do not lose hope of Allah's mercy and His forgiveness for your sins. Allah forgives all the sins of those who repent to Him. Indeed, He is All-Forgiving of the sins of those who repent and is Merciful towards them.",
  39054:
      "Return to your Lord through repentance and righteous actions, and submit to Him before the punishment comes to you on the Day of Resurrection. Then, you will not find anyone from your idols and families who can rescue you from the punishment.",
  39055:
      "Follow the Quran, which is the best of what your Lord has revealed to His Messenger. Act on its instructions and avoid its prohibitions before the punishment strikes you suddenly while you are oblivious to it. So prepare for it by always repenting.",
  39056:
      "Act now to avoid the soul's extreme regret when it declares on the Day of Resurrection: Alas, my grief is over my negligence in my duty to Allah by the disbelief and sins committed and the mocking of the people of belief and obedience in the worldly life.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbeliever calls on Allah in times of distress but forgets Him in times of prosperity.\n2. For the disbelievers, blessings are means of gradually luring them into further destruction.\n3. Allah’s mercy is vast for His creation.\n4. Regret that is of benefit is that which is in the world and which is followed by sincere repentance.",
  39057:
      "Or it will attempt to justify itself by using fate as an argument and say: If Allah had guided me, I would have been mindful of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  39058:
      "Or it will say in hope when it sees the punishment: If only I could return to the world and repent to Allah and be one of those who do good deeds.",
  39059:
      "The reality is different from what you now assert by wishing for guidance. My signs came to you, and you arrogantly denied them. You were of those who rejected and disbelieved in Allah, His signs, and His Messengers.",
  39060:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, you will see those who told lies about Allah by attributing a partner and son to Him, with their faces blackened, as a sign of their wretchedness. Is there not a [suitable] place in Hell for those too proud to believe in Allah and His messengers? Indeed, there is a place for them in it.",
  39061:
      "Allah will save those who were mindful of their Lord by complying with His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions from the punishment by entering them into their place of success, Paradise. The punishment will not touch them, nor will they grieve over the worldly pleasures they missed out on.",
  39062:
      "Allah is the Creator of everything. There is no creator besides Him. He is in charge of everything. He plans His affair and disposes of it as He wills.",
  39063:
      "To Him alone belong the keys to the treasures of all good in the heavens and the Earth. He grants it to whomever He wills and withholds it from whomever He wills. Those who reject Allah's signs are the true losers due to being deprived of faith in this worldly life and entering the Fire to live there forever in the next life.",
  39064:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who invite you to worship their idols: Do you instruct me, O you who are ignorant of your Lord, to worship other than Allah? None deserves to be worshipped except Allah alone, so I will never worship other than Him.",
  39065:
      "Allah has revealed to you, O Messenger, and to the messengers before you: If you worship others along with Allah, the reward of your good deeds will be annulled, and [as a consequence] you will be of the losers in this world due to the loss of your religion, and in the Hereafter due to the punishment.",
  39066:
      "Instead, worship Allah alone and do not ascribe a partner to Him and be of those who are grateful to Him for the favors He has given you.",
  39067:
      "The polytheists did not show devotion to Allah as He deserved when they ascribed others of His weak and feeble creation as partners to Him. They were heedless of Allah's power, one of the manifestations of which is that the Earth, together with the mountains, trees, rivers, and oceans in it, will be in His grasp on the Day of Resurrection and that the seven heavens will be folded up in His right hand. He is transcendent, pure, and above what the polytheists say and believe.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pride is a despicable and ominous quality that prevents a person from arriving at the truth.\n2. The blackening of faces on the Day of Resurrection is a sign of the wretchedness of such people.\n3. Ascribing partners to Allah destroys all righteous actions.\n4. Allah, may He be glorified, on the Day of Judgement, will grasp the heavens and the earth with His right hand, in a manner which befits His Majesty.",
  39068:
      "On the Day when the angel appointed to blow the trumpet will blow it, everyone in the heavens and the Earth will die except those whom Allah wills to not die. Then the angel will blow it a second time for the resurrection, and they will all stand up alive, looking on to see what Allah will do to them.",
  39069:
      "The Earth will light up when the Lord of Might appears to judge between the slaves. The records of deeds of all people will be laid open, the prophets will be brought, and the followers of Muhammed صلى الله عليه وسلم will bear witness for the prophets over their people. Allah will judge between them with justice, and they will not be wronged on that day. No person's evil deeds will be increased, nor will his good deeds be decreased.",
  39070:
      "Allah will give each soul its recompense in full, whether its actions were good or evil. Allah knows best what they did. Nothing of their actions, good or bad, is hidden from Him, and He will give them the recompense for their efforts on this day.",
  39071:
      "The angels will drive those who rejected Allah to the Fire in large crowds. When they come to Hell, the angels appointed as its keepers will open its gates and receive them by saying to them rebukingly: Did not messengers from your kind come to you reciting to you the signs of your Lord that were revealed to them, warning you of meeting the Day of Resurrection because of the severe punishment therein? The disbelievers will acknowledge that by saying: Indeed, that took place. However, the word of punishment is binding on the disbelievers, and we were disbelievers.",
  39072:
      "It will be said to them to humiliate them further so they may lose all hope in Allah's mercy and of ever coming out of the Fire: Enter the gates of the Fire to remain therein forever. How terrible the place of those who were proud and arrogant against the truth is.",
  39073:
      "The angels will gently lead the believers who feared their Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions to Paradise in large crowds honored [by Allah]. When they come to Paradise, its gates will open for them, and the angels appointed to it will say to them: Peace be on you from every difficulty and from everything you dislike. Your hearts and actions were pure, so enter Paradise to remain there forever.",
  39074:
      "The believers will say when they enter Paradise: Praise be to Allah, who fulfilled His promise to us on the tongues of His messengers. He had promised to gather us in Paradise. He has given us the land of Paradise, where we can live wherever we want. How excellent the reward of those who worked by doing righteous actions seeking the pleasure of their Lord is.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Evidence for the two blows of the trumpet.\n2. Explanation of the humiliation that the disbelievers will encounter and the honour that the believers will receive.\n3. Evidence of the disbelievers’ living forever in Hell and the believers’ living forever in bliss.\n4. Good actions bring about good reward.",
  39075:
      "The angels on that witnessed day will surround the throne, declaring Allah to be free from what the disbelievers say that is not befitting. Allah will judge between all creation with justice, honoring those whom He honors and punishing those He punishes. It will be said: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of all created things, for the judgment that He passed of mercy for His believing slaves and punishment for His disbelieving slaves.",
  40000:
      "The Forgiver (Surah Ghafir)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDetailing the situation of those who dispute Allah's verses and responding to them.\n•    Explanation:",
  40001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  40002:
      "The revelation of the Quran is from Allah—the Mighty whom none can overpower, the All-Knowing of His slaves' interests—to His Messenger, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  40003:
      "[It is from] The Forgiver of sins of the sinners, Accepter of the repentance of His slaves who turn to Him, Severe in retribution against those who do not repent, Possessor of bounty and grace. There is no being who deserves worship besides Him. To Him alone is the return of the slaves on the Day of Resurrection, and He will recompense them according to what they deserve.",
  40004:
      "No one disputes Allah's signs that indicate His Oneness and the truthfulness of His messengers except those who reject Allah due to their deficient intellects. Do not grieve over them or let the abundant provision and favors they enjoy deceive you. The respite given to them is part of the plan to gradually lure them into a false sense of security.",
  40005:
      "Before them, the people of Noah rejected [the message], as did the confederates after Noah, including 'Ād, Thamūd, the people of Lot, and the people of Midian. Pharaoh also rejected it. All of them refused to accept [the message]. Every nation plotted against their Messenger to capture and kill him. They argued using falsehood in order to eliminate the truth. But I seized all those nations. So, reflect on how my retribution against them was. It was a severe retribution.",
  40006:
      "Like how Allah decided to destroy those disbelieving nations, the Word of your Lord, O Messenger, is binding against the disbelievers, that they will be the inmates of the Fire.",
  40007:
      "The angels who carry the throne of your Lord, O Messenger, and those around it, declare their Lord to be free from all that does not befit Him. They believe in Him and seek forgiveness for those who have faith in Allah, saying in their supplication: O Our Lord, Your knowledge and mercy encompass everything, so forgive those who repent from their sins and follow Your religion, and protect them from being touched by the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Combining encouragement towards Allah’s mercy and caution against the severity of His retribution, is a praiseworthy method of calling others to do good.\n2. Seizing those communities who denied is a divine practice.\n3. The angels declare the transcendence of their Lord.\n4. Praising Allah is one of the etiquettes of supplication.\n5. Praying for a Muslim in his absence benefits the person praying as well as the person being prayed for.",
  40008:
      "The angels will say: O Our Lord, enter the believers into gardens of eternity which You promised, and admit those whose actions are good amongst their fathers, wives, and children. You are the Mighty with nobody to overpower You, Wise in your decreeing and planning.",
  40009:
      "And save them from their bad actions, so do not punish them as a result. Whomever You protect from punishment for their evil actions on the Day of Resurrection, then You have been merciful to them. This protection from the punishment and mercy through entry into Paradise is the great success which no success can compare with.",
  40010:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah and His messengers will be addressed on the Day of Resurrection when they enter the Fire hating and cursing themselves: Allah's contempt for you is greater than your contempt for yourselves while you were being called in the worldly life to believe in Allah, but you disbelieved in Him and set up gods beside Him [in worship].",
  40011:
      "The disbelievers will say confessing their sins when their confession will not benefit them: Our Lord, You decreed death for us twice, once before we existed, then You created us. Another time, You decreed death for us after having brought us into existence. Also, You gave us life twice by creating us from nothing and by restoring us for the resurrection. We have acknowledged our sins, so is there any route we can take to exit from the Fire so we can return to life to correct our actions so You become pleased with us?",
  40012:
      "The punishment you are suffering now is because when Allah alone was called upon, and no partner was associated with Him, you disbelieved in Him and ascribed partners to Him. And when partners were worshipped alongside Allah, you believed. So the judgment is with Allah alone, Lofty with His essence, decree, and dominance, the Great One Who is above all else.",
  40013:
      "Allah is the One who shows you signs in the horizons (in every direction) and in yourselves to prove His power and oneness to you. He sends down rainwater from the skies for you, so it becomes a cause for the provisions you receive, such as plants, crops, and so forth. And nobody takes lessons from the signs of Allah except one who turns to Him, sincerely repenting.",
  40014:
      "So call upon Allah sincerely, O believers, in worship and supplication, without associating partners with Him, even if the disbelievers dislike that, and it enrages them.",
  40015:
      "For He is worthy of sincere supplication and obedience, as He is elevated in ranks, separate from all of His creation. He is the Lord of the Great Throne. He sends revelation upon whomever He wants from His slaves so that they and others become alive. He warns people of the Day of Resurrection, in which the people from the start of time until the end will all meet one another.",
  40016:
      "On the Day when every person will be gathered on a single plane. Nothing of theirs will be hidden from Allah, neither their selves, actions, nor reward. All will be clear to see. He will ask: To whom belongs the kingdom today? There will only be one answer now: The kingdom is for Allah, the One in His essence, attributes, and actions, the Prevailing one who has dominated everything and for Whom everything humbles itself.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The place for repentance to be accepted is the worldly life.\n2. Those who repent often, turning to their Lord, benefit the most from the admonition.\n3. The steadfastness of the believer is not affected by the stance of the disbelievers who reject his religion.\n4. The tyrants and oppressors amongst the kings will humble themselves before Allah on the day of judgment.",
  40017:
      "Today, every soul will get what it deserves for its actions: if it is good, then the reward will be good, and if it is evil, then likewise, the result will be evil. There will be no injustice today because the judge is Allah, who is Just. Allah is swift in taking account of His slaves due to His All-encompassing knowledge of them.",
  40018:
      "O Messenger, warn them of the Day of Resurrection. This day of standing has drawn near and is soon to come, and anything coming soon is close. When the hearts rise, due to its intense horror, until they reach the throats, they will all be silent, with none of them able to speak except whom [Allah] the All-Merciful allows to speak. Those who wronged themselves through polytheism and sins will not have any friend, relative, or intercessor who will be listened to, even if they could intercede for them.",
  40019:
      "He knows what the eyes of the lookers secretly glance at and what the hearts conceal. None of that is hidden from Him.",
  40020:
      "Allah judges with complete justice, so He does not wrong anyone by decreasing His good actions or increasing His evil actions. And those whom the polytheists worship besides Allah cannot judge with anything because they do not possess anything. Allah Hears the words of His slaves and sees their intentions and actions, and He will recompense them for that.",
  40021:
      "Have these polytheists not traveled throughout the Earth so that they can reflect on the outcome of the disbelieving nations before them? Their end was evil. Those [previous] nations were stronger than they are, and they left an impression on Earth with buildings that these people have not done. However, Allah destroyed them because of their sins, and they had nobody to protect them from the punishment of Allah.",
  40022:
      "That punishment that befell them only befell them because they disbelieved in Allah and denied His messengers when they used to come to them with clear proofs and spectacular miracles. However, Allah seized them, despite their strength, and destroyed them. He is Powerful and severe in punishing those who disbelieve in Him and reject His messengers.",
  40023:
      "With the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم facing rejection from his people, Allah mentions the story of Moses and Pharaoh to give him the good news that, ultimately, he will be victorious. He states: \n Indeed, We sent Moses with Our clear signs and decisive proof.",
  40024:
      "[He was sent] To Pharaoh, his minister Haman, and Qarun. They said: Moses is a magician and a liar in his claim to be a messenger.",
  40025:
      "Then when Moses came to them with the proof to show his truthfulness, Pharaoh said: Kill the sons of those who have believed in Moses and keep their women alive, to disgrace them. And the plot of the disbelievers to attempt to reduce the number of believers will only perish and [ultimately] fail.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The horrors of the day of judgment will be intense.\n2. Allah’s knowledge will encompass His servants’ actions, be they hidden or apparent.\n3. The plot of the disbelievers will perish, regardless of how intense it may be.",
  40026:
      "Pharaoh said: Leave me to kill Moses, as a punishment for him, and let him call upon his Lord to save him from me. I do not care if he calls upon His Lord. I fear he will change your religion or that corruption will appear on Earth through killing and destruction.",
  40027:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) said: I have sought the protection of my Lord and your Lord from every person who is too arrogant to accept and believe in the truth, thus not believing in the resurrection, and being taken into account and punished on it.",
  40028:
      "A believing man from the family of Pharoah, who was concealing his belief from his people, said, criticizing them for deciding to kill Moses: Are you going to kill a man who has not committed any crime other than him saying: 'My Lord is Allah', despite the fact he brought you miracles and proof to show the truthfulness of his claim to be a messenger from his Lord? If he is a liar, his lying will expose him, but if he is truthful, some of the punishment he promises will soon befall you. Allah does not guide to the truth one who overreaches His limits and lies against Allah and His messengers.",
  40029:
      "O people, today you have the kingdom and dominate the land of Egypt. So, who will save us from Allah's punishment if it comes to us due to killing Moses? Pharaoh said: The opinion is my opinion, and the judgment is my judgment. I have decided to kill Moses to remove evil and corruption. I only guide you to what is upright.",
  40030:
      "And the one who believed said, advising his people: I fear for you, if you kill Moses out of injustice and transgression, a punishment [will befall you] like the punishment of the groups that united against their prophets previously, then Allah destroyed them.",
  40031:
      "Such is the habit of those who disbelieved and denied the messengers. For instance, the people of Noah, 'Ād, Thamūd, and those who came after them, Allah, destroyed them due to their disbelief and denial of their messengers. And Allah does not want to oppress the slaves. He only punishes them due to their sins.",
  40032:
      "O my people, I fear for you the Day of Judgment. People will call one another that day due to their blood relations, status, or thinking they can benefit them during that terrifying time.",
  40033:
      "On the Day you will turn away, running out of fear from the Fire, you will not have any protector to protect you from Allah's punishment. whoever Allah abandons and does not place faith in his heart, no one can guide him because a person being able to accept guidance is only in the Hand of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pharaoh’s heresy.\n2. The believer seeks refuge in his Lord to protect him from the plot of his enemies.\n3. The permissibility of hiding one’s faith due to a predominant interest or to ward off harm.\n4. Presenting advice to people is a quality of the believers.",
  40034:
      "Joseph came to you before Moses with clear proof of Allah's Oneness. However, you doubted him and remained in denial of what he brought until he died. Then, you only increased in doubt and uncertainty. You said: Allah will never send a messenger after him. Just as you are misguided from the truth, Allah leads astray every person who transgresses the limits of Allah and doubts His oneness.",
  40035:
      "Those who dispute the words of Allah to refute them without any proof or evidence that has come to them, their disputing is ever more despised in the eyes of Allah and those who believe in Allah and His messengers. Just as Allah sealed the hearts of those who argue about Our verses to refute them, Allah seals the hearts of every person who is tyrannical and arrogant to the truth. Thus, he does not find the path to what is correct, nor is he guided to good.",
  40036:
      "Pharaoh said to his minister Haman: O Haman, build a high building for me so that I can attain the means of access.",
  40037:
      "In the hope that I can access the paths that lead to the skies and see the God of Moses that he claims is the true God. In this way, Pharoah's evil deeds were adorned for him when he requested that from Haman and was turned from the true path to the path of misguidance. The plot of Pharaoh to make the falsehood he believed dominant and to refute the truth Moses brought was a total failure because it was ill-advised, a futile attempt, and led to perpetual damnation.",
  40038:
      "The man from the family of Pharoah, who believed in Allah, said, advising his people and guiding them to the proper path: O people, follow me; I shall show you and guide you to the correct way and guide you to the truth.",
  40039:
      "O people, this worldly life is only an enjoyment of fleeting pleasures, so let it not deceive you with its short-lived bliss. [However] With its everlasting pleasure, the abode of the Hereafter is the abode of permanent dwelling, so work for it by obeying Allah, and be wary of becoming preoccupied with your worldly life away from working towards the Hereafter.",
  40040:
      "Whoever commits an evil action will be recompensed with punishment befitting of what he did, without punishment being added to it. Likewise, whoever does a good action seeking Allah's pleasure through it, whether a male or female, as long as he [or she] is a believer in Allah and His messengers, will enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection. Allah will grant them therein provisions of fruits and everlasting pleasure without limits.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Arguing to refute the truth and establish falsehood is a bad characteristic amongst the characteristics of the misguided.\n2. Pride prevents one from being guided to the truth.\n3. The truth will always remain and any plot of the disbeliever to change it will fail.\n4. The necessity of preparing for the Hereafter and not being preoccupied from it due to the world.",
  40041:
      "O my people, why do you think I am calling you towards salvation so you do not lose out in this worldly life and the Hereafter by believing in Allah and doing good actions? Yet, you call me to enter the Fire by asking me to disbelieve in Allah or disobey Him?",
  40042:
      "You are calling me to your falsehood in the hope that I disbelieve in Allah and worship others alongside Him. At the same time, I do not know the validity of doing so. I am calling you to believe in Allah, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, the Most-Forgiving who has vast forgiveness for His slaves.",
  40043:
      "Truly, what you call me to believe in and obey has no right to be called to in this world or the Hereafter, nor does it respond to whoever calls upon it. The return of us all is to Allah alone, and those who transgress in disbelief and sins are the people of the Fire who will enter it forever on the Day of Resurrection.",
  40044:
      "But they rejected his advice, so he said: You will remember the advice I gave you, and you will regret not accepting it. I entrust all my affairs to Allah alone. Nothing of Allah's slaves' actions is hidden from Him.",
  40045:
      "So Allah protected him from their evil plot when they intended to kill him, and the punishment of drowning surrounded the followers of Pharaoh, as Allah destroyed him and all his armies in this world.",
  40046:
      "And after their death, they will be subjected to the Fire at the beginning and end of the day. Then, on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: Cast the followers of Pharaoh into the most severe and greatest punishment due to their disbelief, denial, and preventing others from Allah's path.",
  40047:
      "O Messenger, mention when the people of the Fire who were followers and leaders will argue so that the oppressed followers will say to the arrogant leaders: We were your followers in misguidance in the worldly life, so are you going to relieve us of some of Allah's punishment by bearing it on our behalf?",
  40048:
      "The arrogant leaders will say: We are in the Fire, regardless of whether we were followers or leaders. None of us will bear a part of the punishment of the Hereafter. Allah has decided between the slaves, giving everyone the punishment they deserve.",
  40049:
      "Those followers and leaders being punished in the Fire will say to the Fire's gatekeepers, once they have lost hope in leaving the Fire and returning to the worldly life to repent: Call upon your Lord to relieve us from one day of this everlasting punishment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Faith is a means of salvation and disbelief is a means of destruction.\n2. The importance of reliance upon Allah.\n3. The salvation of the caller to Allah from the plots of his enemies.\n4. Punishment in the Transitory Stage is real.\n5. The disbelievers will latch on to any means which can relieve them from the fire, even for a limited time, but this will never happen.",
  40050:
      "The gatekeepers of Hell will say in response to the disbelievers: Did your messengers not come to you with clear proof and evidence? The disbelievers will say: Indeed, they used to come to us with clear proof and evidence. The keepers will taunt them by saying: Go ahead and implore us, for we will not intercede for the disbelievers. The supplication of the disbelievers is futile and wasted, as it will not be accepted due to their disbelief.",
  40051:
      "After mentioning the story of Pharaoh and his people and their fate in this life and the Hereafter, Allah mentions the messengers and the faithful believers and the success they will attain in both worlds, stating: \n We will make Our Messengers and those who believe in what they brought victorious by manifesting their proof and supporting them against their enemies. And We shall make them victorious on the Day of Resurrection by entering them into Paradise and punishing their adversaries by casting them into the Fire. This is after the people of truth from the prophets, angels, and believers will all bear witness to the message that has been conveyed and to the denial of the disbelieving nations.",
  40052:
      "On the Day when making excuses will not benefit those who wronged themselves by disbelief and sin, they will be distanced from Allah's mercy and get an evil abode and painful punishment.",
  40053:
      "And We granted Moses knowledge to guide the Israelites to the truth. We made the Torah an inherited book among them, each generation passing it on to the next.",
  40054:
      "As a guide to the true path and a reminder to those of sound intellect.",
  40055:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with the rejection and harm you face from your people. Allah's promise of help and support to you is undoubtedly true. And seek forgiveness for your sin and exalt the praise of your Lord at the beginning and end of the day.",
  40056:
      "Those who dispute Allah's verses to invalidate them without any argument or proof from Him are motivated to do so only by the desire to show arrogance and superiority in the face of truth. They will not achieve the dominance they desire over it. So hold fast, O Messenger, to Allah, for He is All-Hearing of His slaves' words. He is All-Seeing of their deeds; nothing escapes Him, and He will recompense them.",
  40057:
      "The creation of the heavens and the Earth and their greatness and vastness is greater than the creation of humanity. So, the One who made them, despite their greatness, has the power to bring the dead back to life from their graves, to hold them to account and recompense them. But most people do not know, so they do not consider it proof of the resurrection despite it being so clear.",
  40058:
      "The blind are not equal to those who can see. In the same way, those who believe in Allah, affirm His messengers, and do good are not the same as those who do evil with corrupt beliefs and sins. Only a few among you reflect. Had you reflected, you would be aware of the difference between the two groups and strived to be amongst those who believed and did good deeds, seeking the pleasure of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s help for His messengers and the believers is an established divine practice.\n2. The excuse of the oppressor on the day of judgment will not benefit him.\n3. The importance of patience in facing falsehood.\n4. The creation of the heavens and the earth proving the resurrection, because He who created that which is great has the power to restore to life that which is smaller.",
  40059:
      "The Hour in which Allah will raise the dead for reckoning and recompense is coming, but most people do not believe it is coming, so they do not prepare for it.",
  40060:
      "O people, your Lord said: Call upon Me alone, worship Me alone, and do not associate any partner with Me. Those too arrogant to worship Me alone will enter the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, lowly and disgraced.",
  40061:
      "Allah is the One who has made the night dark for you so you can find harmony in it and rest, and He made the day bright and clear so that you can work in it. Allah is full of great bounty to the people when He grants them His apparent and hidden blessings. But most people do not thank Him for what He has blessed them.",
  40062:
      "That Allah, who graced you with His favors, is the Creator of everything; there is no Creator besides Him. There is nothing worthy of worship besides Him. So, how do you turn away from His worship towards worshiping others who possess neither benefit nor harm?",
  40063:
      "Just as these people turn away from believing in Allah and worshipping Him alone, those who reject Allah's signs, which prove His oneness, have turned away in every age and place. Thus, they do not find their way to the truth, nor are they rightly guided to it.",
  40064:
      "O people, Allah is the One who made the Earth a suitable place for you to dwell in. And He firmly formed the sky above you so it cannot collapse. He formed you in the wombs of your mothers, then perfected your form. And He granted you provision from lawful and natural foods. He who granted you these blessings is Allah, your Lord. So, blessed is Allah, Lord of all the creation. There is no lord besides Him.",
  40065:
      "He is the Ever-Living who will never die. There is nothing worthy of worship besides Him. So, call upon him in worship and supplication, seeking His pleasure alone, and do not associate any of His creation as partners with Him. All praise is for Allah, Lord of the creation.",
  40066:
      "O Messenger, say [to them]: Allah has forbidden me from worshipping those you worship besides Him, those which do not benefit nor harm, since clear proof and evidence have come to me regarding the falsehood of worshipping them. Allah has ordered me to submit to Him alone through worship, as He is the Lord of all the creation. There is no lord besides Him for them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Supplication is included in the meaning of worship which can only be directed towards Allah, as supplication is the essence of worship.\n2. The favours of Allah require gratitude from the servants.\n3. Allah is ever Living.\n4. The importance of sincerity in actions.",
  40067:
      "He is the One who created Adam from dust. After that, He created you from a sperm-drop, then after a sperm-drop from clotted blood, and after that, He takes you out of your mothers' wombs as small children so that you reach the peak of your strength and grow older until you become elders. And some of you die before that, reaching a fixed time in the knowledge of Allah, which you cannot decrease or increase. Perhaps you may benefit from this proof and evidence of His power and oneness.",
  40068:
      "He alone is the One in whose hand is giving life, and He alone is the One who causes death. So when He decides a matter, He only says to that matter: \"Be,\" and it comes into existence.",
  40069:
      "O Messenger, do you not see those who argue with you about the signs of Allah, denying them despite their clarity, so you may be astonished at their condition while they are turning away from the evident truth?",
  40070:
      "Those who denied the Quran and the truth We sent Our messengers with - these deniers will soon learn the outcome of their denial and they will witness a miserable ending.",
  40071:
      "They will learn its outcome when the shackles will be on their necks and the chains on their feet, with the angels of Hell dragging them.",
  40072:
      "The angels of punishment will drag them into boiling hot water. Then they will be used as fuel in the Fire.",
  40073:
      "Then it will be said to them, in a scolding and rebuking manner: Where are your so-called gods, that cannot benefit or harm, that you set up as partners by worshipping them besides Allah? The disbelievers will say: They have vanished, so we cannot see them. We did not worship anything that deserved to be worshipped. In the same way, Allah leads the disbelievers astray from the truth in every time and place.",
  40074:
      "Then it will be said to them, in a scolding and rebuking manner: Where are your so-called gods, that cannot benefit or harm, that you set up as partners by worshipping them besides Allah? The disbelievers will say: They have vanished, so we cannot see them. We did not worship anything that deserved to be worshipped. In the same way, Allah leads the disbelievers astray from the truth in every time and place.",
  40075:
      "It will be said to them: The punishment you are suffering is due to your rejoicing over the polytheism you were upon and your excess in rejoicing.",
  40076:
      "Enter the doors of Hell, staying therein forever. How wretched the abode in which those arrogant to the truth will reside is.",
  40077:
      "When Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم suffered from what his people did to him, Allah instructed him to be patient and consoled him with His promise of victory, stating: \n O Messenger, be patient with the harm and rejection of your people. The promise of Allah to help you is undoubtedly true. So We will either show you in your lifetime some of the punishment We promised them, as occurred in the Battle of Badr, or We will cause you to pass away before that. To Us alone, they will return on the Day of Resurrection. Thus, We will recompense them for their actions accordingly, casting them into the Fire where they will remain forever.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. We can learn from Allah’s divine custom of creating progressively that we must also fulfill our projects gradually.\n2. How hideous it is to rejoice over evil\n3. The importance of patience in our daily life especially those who enjoin the good",
  40078:
      "O Messenger, We have sent many messengers before you to their people, but they rejected them and caused them harm. The messengers were patient upon the rejection and harm they faced. Among these messengers are those whom We have related their stories to you and those whose stories We have not told. It is incorrect for a messenger to bring a sign to his people from his Lord, except if He, the Exalted, wills it. Thus, for the disbelievers to demand signs is transgression. For when Allah's decree for victory or judgment in favor of the messengers against their nations comes, He will judge between them fairly. The disbelievers will then be destroyed, and the messengers will be saved. At that point, when the judgment is made between the slaves, the people of falsehood will lose out by having put themselves in a position of destruction through their disbelief.",
  40079:
      "Allah is the One who created camels, cows, and livestock for you so that you can ride on some of them and consume the meat of some.",
  40080:
      "You have many benefits in these creations, which change with every era. You utilize them to acquire whatever necessities you desire to be fulfilled. And from the most apparent of these needs is transportation across the land through camels, among other means, and across the sea through ships.",
  40081:
      "And Allah shows you many of His signs that point to His power and oneness; so which of Allah's signs do you not acknowledge after it has been established they are His signs?",
  40082:
      "Do these rejectors not travel the Earth and ponder the outcome of the nations who rejected before them and take heed from it? Those nations were wealthier, stronger, and more influential upon the world than them, but their actions and strength did not help them when the destructive punishment of Allah came.",
  40083:
      "When their messengers brought them clear proof, they rejected them. They were content with their knowledge that contradicted whatever their messengers came with. So the same punishment they would mock when warned of it by their messengers befell them.",
  40084:
      "Then, when they saw Our punishment, they began to confess, at a time when confessing would not benefit them, saying: We believe in Allah alone and reject whatever partners and idols we worshipped instead of Him.",
  40085:
      "So believing after seeing Our punishment descending upon them will not benefit them. The way of Allah with His slaves has consistently been that believing after witnessing the punishment with their eyes is useless. The disbelievers condemned themselves at the time when the punishment descended by having put themselves in a place of destruction because they disbelieved in Allah and did not repent from that before seeing the punishment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah has messengers other than those specifically mentioned by name in the noble Qur’an.\n2. From among the favours of Allah is that He clearly marks out those signs of His that point to His oneness.\n3. Being happy with falsehood and its harmful consequences is dangerous.\n4. Bringing faith upon seeing the destructive punishment is of no use.",
  41000:
      "Explained in Detail (Surah Fussilat)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nMentioning the situation of those who turn away from Allah and detailing their end.\n•    Explanation:",
  41001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  41002: "This Quran is a revelation from Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.",
  41003:
      "It is a book in which the verses have been made completely clear. It has been made an Arabic Quran for people who know because they are the ones who will benefit from its meanings and be guided to the truth.",
  41004:
      "It gives glad tidings to the believers of the generous reward Allah has prepared for them. It warns the disbelievers of the painful punishment of Allah, but most of them turn away from it and do not listen with an open mind.",
  41005:
      "And they say: Our hearts are covered with multiple layers, so we do not comprehend what you are calling us to. Our ears cannot hear what you are saying. There is a barrier between you and us; none of your speech reaches us, so you carry on doing things your way, and we will do things our way. We will never follow you.",
  41006:
      "O Messenger, tell these opposers: I am only human like you are. I receive revelation from Allah that your true deity is only one deity, who is Allah. So devote your worship to Him alone and seek forgiveness from Him for your sins. Destruction and punishment are for the polytheists who worship others instead of Allah or ascribe partners to Him.",
  41007:
      "Those who do not pay Zakat on their wealth and disbelieve in the Hereafter, with its everlasting blessings and painful torment.",
  41008:
      "Indeed, those who believe in Allah and His messengers and do good deeds will have the everlasting reward of Paradise, which will never end.",
  41009:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists, rebukingly: Why do you disbelieve in Allah, who created the Earth in two days, and attribute equals to Him whom you worship instead of Him? He is the Lord of all creation.",
  41010:
      "He created firm mountains on it, which stabilize it and prevent it from shaking. And He blessed it, making it a continuous source of goodness for its people. He determined the sustenance of people and livestock in it for a period of four complete days, for those who wish to ask about that.",
  41011:
      "Then Allah (may He be Exalted) resolved to create the sky when it was smoke, saying to it and the Earth: Submit to My command willingly or unwillingly. They said: We submit willingly; O our Lord, we have no wish except your wish.\n\n• \n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers shut off all means of guidance that they had, deciding to remain on disbelief instead.\n2. The importance of Zakat is mentioned, that it is a pillar from the pillars of Islam.\n3. The whole universe has submitted and humbled itself to the command of Allah (may He be glorified).",
  41012:
      "Then Allah completed the creation of the heavens in two days. With that, the heavens and the Earth were created in six days. Allah inspired in every heaven whatever He would decree concerning it and whatever obedience and worship He would command. We also decorated the nearest heaven with stars, protecting it from the eavesdropping of the devils. All that is the decree of the Almighty, whom no one can overcome, and the Omniscient of His creation.",
  41013:
      "So if these people turn away from believing in what you have brought them, say to them: I have warned you of a punishment that will fall upon you, like the punishment that fell upon 'Ād, the people of Hūd, and Thamūd, the people of Saleh, when they rejected their messengers.",
  41014:
      "When their messengers came to them, each followed the other in bringing one message, instructing them to worship none other than Allah alone. The disbelievers said: If our Lord wished to send down angels as messengers to us, He would have sent them. Therefore, we reject whatever you have been sent with because you are humans like we are.",
  41015:
      "As for the people of Hūd, 'Ād, together with their disbelief in Allah, they displayed excessive arrogance on Earth and oppressed those around them. Having been deceived by their own strength, they said: Who is there that is stronger than us? They assumed that no one was stronger than them, so Allah replied to them: Do these people not know and see that the One who created them and gave them the strength that made them rebellious is stronger than them? They would reject the signs of Allah that Hūd (peace be upon him) brought to them.",
  41016:
      "So We sent them a severe wind with a terrifying noise on days that were unfortunate due to the punishment that came to them. So that We may make them suffer humiliation and disgrace in this world, and indeed, the punishment of the Hereafter that awaits them is more humiliating for them. They will not find anyone to help save them from the punishment.",
  41017:
      "As for the people of Saleh, the Thamūd, We guided them by making the path of truth clear to them, but they preferred deviance over guidance to the truth. Hence, the blast of humiliating punishment annihilated them because of the disbelief and sins they would commit.",
  41018:
      "And We saved those who believed in Allah and His messengers and feared Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And We rescued them from the punishment that came upon their people.",
  41019:
      "And on the Day when the enemies of Allah will be gathered towards the Fire, the appointed angels (of punishment) will thrust every last one of them into it. They will not be able to escape from it.",
  41020:
      "When they come to the Fire that they will be driven toward and deny the actions they did in this world, their own ears, eyes, and skin will testify to their sins and disbelief in the worldly life.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Turning away from the truth is the cause of destruction in the world and the Hereafter.\n2. Arrogance and being conceited with one’s strength both prevent a person from submitting to the truth.\n3. The punishment of the world and the Hereafter will be piled upon the disbelievers.\n4. The disbelievers being destroyed and believers being saved is a divine custom of Allah.\n5. One’s own limbs will testify against him on the Day of Judgement.",
  41021:
      "And the disbelievers will ask their skins: Why do you testify against us by stating what we used to do in the worldly life? Their skins will reply: The one who grants everything the ability to speak gave us the ability to speak. He is the one who created you initially when you were in the worldly life, and to Him, you will return in the Hereafter to give account and be recompensed.",
  41022:
      "You did not use to hide your sins to the degree that your ears, eyes, and skin cannot testify against you because you did not believe in accountability, punishment, or reward after death. Instead, you thought that Allah (may He be Exalted) was unaware of many things you did and that they remained hidden from Him. Thus, you were deceived.",
  41023:
      "And that very evil thought you had concerning your Lord destroyed you, so because of it, you became the ones who lost out in this world and the Hereafter.",
  41024:
      "If these people against whom their ears, eyes, and skins testified are to be patient, the Fire will be their abode and dwelling place they will take shelter in. And if they seek to lift the punishment from themselves and gain Allah's pleasure and entry into Paradise, they never achieve either of them.",
  41025:
      "We sent upon these disbelievers companions from the devils, who would constantly be close to them, beautifying their evil actions and rejection of the resurrection, so they made them forget it and neglect to work towards it. The punishment is binding upon them as it was upon the nations previously from the humans and Jinn. Indeed, they are the losers who will lose themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection when they enter the Fire.",
  41026:
      "When the disbelievers cannot refute the evidence, they urge one another [by saying]: Do not listen to this Quran that Muhammad recites to you, and do not submit to it. Rather, shout and raise your voices when he recites it to you so that perhaps he stops reciting it and calling to it so that you can gain the upper hand over him, and we can have a break from him.",
  41027:
      "So we will make those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His messengers suffer a severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection. We will recompense them with punishment for the worst of their actions, i.e., ascribing partners with Allah and sins.",
  41028:
      "That recompense for those who disbelieved in Him and rejected His messengers is the Fire, in which they will live forever, never to come out of it. It is retribution for their rejection of the signs of Allah and not believing in them despite their clarity and depth of evidence.",
  41029:
      "And those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His messengers will say: O our Lord, show us who from the humans and Jinn led us astray: Iblis who introduced disbelief and inviting towards it and the son of Adam who introduced bloodshed. We will put them in the Fire under our feet so that they are the lowest of the people and the ones most severely punished.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Thinking evil about Allah is a trait from the traits of disbelief.\n2. Disbelief and sins are causes of the satans ruling over the humans.\n3. The followers will desire that those they followed are the most severely punished on the Day of Judgement.",
  41030:
      "After mentioning the recompense awaiting His enemies, Allah mentions the recompense awaiting His allies, stating: \n Indeed, those who say: Our Lord is Allah; we have no Lord besides Him, and they are steadfast in complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, the angels will descend upon them when death nears them, saying: Do not fear death or whatever comes after it and do not grieve over what you will leave behind in this world. Take the glad tidings of Paradise you were promised for your faith in Allah and good deeds.",
  41031:
      "We were your friends in the worldly life; we used to correct you and protect you, and we will also be your friends in the Hereafter, so our friendship with you is continuous. In Paradise, you can fulfill whatever your hearts desire and crave, and you will get whatever you seek.",
  41032:
      "It is a provision prepared for you by a merciful Lord forgiving the sins of those of His slaves who repent to Him.",
  41033:
      "There is no one whose speech is better than the one who calls towards Allah's Oneness and acts upon His law while doing good actions that please Him, saying: Indeed, I am one of those who submit and humble myself to Allah. Indeed, whoever does all that is the best in speech.",
  41034:
      "Doing good deeds in obedience to Allah that please Him and doing evil and committing sins that anger Him are not equal. Respond with conduct that is better to the one who does wrong. If you do so, you will soon find that the previous enmity between you disappears, and it will be as if he is now a close, affectionate friend.",
  41035:
      "Only those who are patient with the harm caused to them and the difficulties they face from the people are given the ability to display this praiseworthy character. Only those who are incredibly fortunate are granted the ability to do so because of the abundant goodness and immense benefit there is in it.",
  41036:
      "And if the Devil whispers evil to you at any time, hold fast to Allah and seek refuge in Him. He is All-Hearing of whatever you say and Omniscient of your situation.",
  41037:
      "Among Allah's signs that demonstrate His greatness and oneness are the alternating of the night and the day and the sun and moon. O, people, do not prostrate to the sun nor the moon; rather, prostrate to Allah, who created them all, if you truly worship Him.",
  41038:
      "So if they show arrogance and turn away, not prostrating to Allah the Creator, the angels with Allah exalt and praise Him (may He be Exalted) throughout the day and night anyway, and they do not become bored of their worship of Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The status of steadfastness is great according to Allah.\n2. Steadfastness is a means of security.\n3. Calling towards Allah has a great status and is the most virtuous of actions.\n4. Bearing patience upon harm and countering with the best of character are two traits which a caller towards Allah has to have.",
  41039:
      "Among Allah's signs that demonstrate His omnipotence, oneness, and ability to resurrect is that you see the earth without any plants. Then, when We send down rainwater, it begins to move due to the hidden growth of seeds, and it rises. Indeed, the One who revived this barren earth through growth is the One who will revive the dead and resurrect them to take them to account and recompense them. Indeed, He is Omnipotent over everything; reviving the earth after it has become barren is not impossible for Him, nor is reviving the dead and resurrecting them from their graves.",
  41040:
      "Indeed, those who deviate from Allah's signs, rejecting or distorting them and turning others away, are not hidden from Us. Allah knows who they are. So, is the one who will be thrown into the Fire better than the one who will be safe from the punishment on the Day of Resurrection? O, people, do whatever good or evil you wish, for Allah has made good and evil clear to you, and He sees whatever you do of it. None of your actions are hidden from Him.",
  41041:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieve in the Quran when it reaches them from Allah will be punished on the Day of Resurrection. Certainly, it is a mighty and impervious book; no one can distort it or change it in any way.",
  41042:
      "Falsehood cannot reach it from any direction by removing, adding, changing, or distorting anything from it. It is a revelation from One who is Wise in His creation, decree, and legislation and praiseworthy in all conditions.",
  41043:
      "After mentioning those who deny the Scripture (Quran), Allah comforted and consoled His Messenger with what his brothers before him from the messengers suffered of rejection, ridicule, and slander, stating: \n O Messenger, the rejection directed towards you is the same that has been directed toward the messengers before you. So be patient because your Lord forgives those of His slaves who repent to Him. However, those who persist upon sins and do not repent, for them is a painful punishment.",
  41044:
      "Had We revealed this Quran in a language other than that of the Arabs, the disbelievers among them would have said: Why are its verses not made clear to us so that we can understand them? Can the Quran be in any language other than Arabic, while the one who brings it is an Arab? O Messenger, tell these people: For those who believe in Allah and His messengers, the Quran is guidance from deviance and a cure for the hearts from ignorance and what it entails. As for those who do not have faith in Allah, their ears are deaf, and they are blinded by it, so they do not understand it. These people are called from a distant place, so how can they hear the voice of the caller?",
  41045:
      "Indeed, We gave Moses the Torah, and [people] differed over it. Some believed in it, while others disbelieved. Had Allah not promised that judgment would be passed between the slaves on the Day of Resurrection in matters they disputed over, judgment would already have been passed upon those who disputed over the Torah, and those upon falsehood would have been destroyed. Indeed, the disbelievers are highly doubtful of the authenticity of the Quran.",
  41046:
      "Whoever does righteous deeds will reap the benefits of his actions because Allah does not benefit from anyone's good deeds. And whoever commits evil deeds, the consequences only affect him, as no sins can harm Allah. Allah will soon recompense each person according to what they deserve. O Messenger, your Lord is not oppressive to His slaves; He will never reduce even a single good deed of theirs nor increase an evil one.",
  41047:
      "To Allah alone, the knowledge of the hour returns. He alone knows when it will occur. No one besides Him knows this. No fruits emerge from their protective sheath, and no female conceives except by His knowledge. Nothing of that escapes Him. On the day when Allah will call the polytheists who used to worship idols together with Him, reproaching them for their worship of those idols: Where are My partners that you used to worship besides Me and claim they are My partners? The polytheists will say: We confess before you. There is not one of us who testifies now that you have a partner.",
  41048:
      "The idols that they used to call on will disappear, and they will be certain that they will have no escape from Allah's punishment.",
  41049:
      "Man does not tire of asking for health, wealth, children, and other favors. If he is afflicted by poverty, sickness, and the like, then he becomes extremely despondent of Allah's mercy.",
  41050:
      "If We were to let him taste health, riches, and well-being from Us after difficulty and sickness had afflicted him, he would certainly say: This is mine because I am worthy and deserving of it. I do not think the hour will take place. If it is assumed that the hour could take place, then I would have the very best by Allah. Just as He favored me in this world because I deserved that, He will favor me in the Hereafter. We will certainly tell those who rejected Allah about the disbelief and the sins they did, and We will make them taste a torment of extreme severity.",
  41051:
      "When We bless man with the favor of health, well-being, and the like, he becomes unmindful of Allah's remembrance and obedience and turns away in pride. When sickness, poverty, and the like afflict him, he supplicates to Allah plentifully, complaining to Him of what has afflicted him so that He will remove it. He does not thank His Lord when He blesses him and is not patient when He tests him.",
  41052:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who reject: Tell me, if this Quran was from Allah and then you rejected and disbelieved in it, what would be your condition? Who is more wrong than the person who is stubborn toward the truth despite it being apparent and despite the clarity and strength of its evidence?",
  41053:
      "We will show the disbelievers of the Quraysh Our signs from the lands spread across the Earth that Allah will allow the Muslims to conquer. We will also show them Our signs in themselves through the conquest of Mecca, which will make clear to them and remove all doubt that the Quran is the undeniable truth. Is it not enough for these polytheists that the Quran is true by Allah's testimony that it is from Him? Who can be a greater witness than Allah? If they were seeking the truth, they would have sufficed with the testimony of their Lord.",
  41054:
      "Indeed, these polytheists doubt the meeting of their Lord on the Day of Resurrection as they deny the resurrection and do not believe in the Afterlife. Therefore, they do not prepare for it with righteous actions. Indeed, Allah's knowledge and power encompass everything.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The knowledge of the hour is only with Allah alone.\n2. The way disbelievers deal with Allah’s favours and retribution is haphazard and disorderly.\n3. Allah’s knowledge and power encompasses everything.",
  42000:
      "The Consultation (Surah Ash-Shuraa)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nClarifying the perfection of Allah's law, emphasizing the obligation to follow it, and warning against violating it.\n•    Explanation:",
  42001:
      "Hā Mīm - 'Ain Sīn Qāf – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  42002:
      "Hā Mīm - 'Ain Sīn Qāf – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  42003:
      "This is how this revelation is revealed to you, O Muhammad, and to those before you from Allah's prophets. Allah is The Mighty in taking retribution against His enemies and The Wise in His planning and creation.",
  42004:
      "Everything in the heavens and on Earth belongs to Him alone. He created, owns, and controls all of it. He is High in His being and in terms of His status and domination, and Majestic in His being.",
  42005:
      "From His Majesty (may He be Exalted) is that the heavens could split apart despite their greatness and height. The angels exalt the praises of their Lord out of submission and in reverence of Him, and they seek forgiveness from Allah for those on Earth. Indeed, Allah is the One who forgives the sins of those slaves of His who repent, and He is merciful to them.",
  42006:
      "For those who take idols besides Allah, whom they align with and worship alongside Allah, Allah lies in wait for them. He records their actions, and He will recompense them for that. You, O Messenger, are not in charge of them, and you will not be questioned about their actions. You are only the one who conveys the message.",
  42007:
      "Just as We sent revelation to the prophets before you, O Messenger, We have revealed an Arabic Quran to you so that you may warn Mecca and the Arab towns around it and then all humanity and warn people of the Day of Resurrection when Allah will gather the early and the latter peoples on one plain for reckoning and recompense. There is no doubt in the occurrence of that day, on which people will be divided into two groups: One group will be in Paradise, and these are the believers, and one group will be in the Fire, and these are the disbelievers.",
  42008:
      "If Allah willed to make them one nation on the religion of Islam, He would have done so and entered them all into Paradise. But, His wisdom demanded that He guide whoever He wills into Islam and then admit them into Paradise. Those who wrong themselves by disbelief and sins will have no one to protect them and no helper to rescue them from Allah's punishment.",
  42009:
      "Instead, these polytheists have taken allies whom they align with besides Allah. Allah is the true Protector. Others besides Him can bring no benefit nor harm. He gives life to the dead by resurrecting them for reckoning and recompense. He has power over all things, and nothing is outside His ability (may He be Exalted).",
  42010:
      "Whatever you, O People, differ in about the principle and subsidiary matters of your religion, the judgment for that rests with Allah. His book and the Sunnah of His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم must be referred to. The One who possesses these attributes is my Lord. It is on Him that I rely in all my affairs, and it is to Him that I turn by repenting to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s greatness is apparent in everything.\n2. The supplication for good by the angels in favour of those who have faith.\n3. The messenger’s task is to convey and show people the path towards goodness.\n4. People in the afterlife will be in two groups: Wretched and fortunate.\n5. The Qur’an and the Sunnah are references for the believers in all their affairs, especially when there is disagreement.",
  42011:
      "Allah is the Creator of the heavens and the Earth without any precedent. He made spouses for you from amongst your own kind. He also made for you pairs of camels, cattle, and sheep so that they can multiply for your sake. He creates you through the spouses that He made for you by your marrying one another. He provides a livelihood for you through the cattle that He made for you from their meat and milk. Nothing of His creation resembles Him. He is the One who hears the statements of His slaves and the One who sees their actions. Nothing of that escapes Him, and He will recompense them for their actions: if good, then with good, and if evil, then with bad.",
  42012:
      "To Him alone belong the keys to the treasures of the heavens and the Earth. He expands the provision for whomever of His slaves He wills as a test to see whether they are grateful or not. He restricts it for whoever of His slaves He wills, as a trial to see whether they are patient or become angry with Allah's decree. He has knowledge of all things. Nothing in which lies the interests of His slaves is hidden from Him.",
  42013:
      "He has ordained for you religious matters similar to what We instructed Noah to convey and act on and what We have revealed to you, O Messenger. He has ordained for you similar to what We instructed Abraham, Moses, and Jesus to convey and act on. In summary: Uphold the religion and leave out division therein. What you call the polytheists towards, such as declaring Allah's Oneness and leaving the worship of others besides Him, is difficult for them. Allah chooses whichever of His slaves He wills and guides them to His worship and obedience, and He guides to Him those of them who return to Him by repenting from their sins.",
  42014:
      "The disbelievers and the polytheists only became divided after the proof of the mission of Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was established. Their division was only on account of rivalry and oppression. Were it not for what had already been in Allah's knowledge that the punishment would be postponed from them until a time determined in His knowledge, which is the day of resurrection, Allah would have decided between them and punished them quickly on account of their rejection of Allah and denial of His messengers. Those Jews who were made to inherit the Torah, and those Christians who were made to inherit the Gospel after their predecessors, and these polytheists are in doubt about and deny this Quran which Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم has brought.",
  42015:
      "Call to this upright religion and remain firm on it as Allah has instructed you. Do not follow their false desires. Say to them when disputing with them: I have faith in Allah and in the scriptures which Allah sent down to His messengers. Allah has instructed me to judge between you with justice. Allah, the One whom I worship, is both our Lord and your Lord. We have our deeds, whether good or bad, and you have your deeds, whether good or bad. There is no quarrel between us after the evidence is apparent and the path is clear. Allah will bring us all together, and to Him is the return on the Day of Resurrection. He will then recompense each one as He deserves, and then it will become clear who is true, who is false, who is right, and who is wrong.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The religion of the prophets in their fundamentals is one religion.\n2. The importance of unity in speech and the danger of disagreement therein.\n3. Some of the components for the success of calling to Allah are: Validity of principle, steadfastness on it, avoiding the following of desires, justice, focussing on common ground, leaving out futile debate, and reminding of the common end.",
  42016:
      "Those who quarrel with invalid arguments about this religion sent down to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم after people have responded to his call due to the strength of its proof and have entered into it; the argument of these people who quarrel is void and holds no weight with their Lord and with the believers. It has no effect. They have earned Allah's anger due to their disbelief and rejection of the truth, and they will have a severe punishment that awaits them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  42017:
      "After mentioning the invalidity of the disbeliever's evidence, Allah mentions the origin of the authentic evidence that a Muslim argues with, which is the Quran, stating: \n Allah is the One who sent down the Quran with the truth, in which there is no doubt. In it, He commanded justice so that people judge by it. The hour that these people deny may be close, and it is known that everything that is coming is near.",
  42018:
      "Those who do not believe in it seek to hasten it because they do not believe in reckoning, reward, or punishment. But those who have faith in Allah are fearful of it because they do not know their fate after it, and they certainly know it to be the truth in which there is no doubt. Indeed, those who dispute the Hour and doubt its occurrence are in error, which is far from the truth.",
  42019:
      "Allah is kind towards His slaves. He provides for whomever He wills and expands their provision, and He restricts it for whomever He wills out of mercy for them, even though it may appear otherwise. He is the Strong, Whom none can overpower, and the Mighty, Who takes retribution from His enemies.",
  42020:
      "Whoever wants the rewards of the Hereafter and works for it, We will multiply his reward for him by multiplying the reward of a good deed by ten times up to seven hundred times or even more. Whoever only wants the worldly life, I will give him his allotted share in it, and he will not have any share in the Afterlife as he preferred this world over it.",
  42021:
      "Or do these polytheists have deities besides Allah, who have ordained for them religious matters that Allah did not authorize them to ordain, such as ascribing partners to Allah, declaring unlawful what He made lawful and declaring lawful what He made unlawful? Had it not been for the fixed time that Allah had set to decide between those who differ and that He will postpone them until such time, He would have decided between them. Those who wrong themselves by ascribing partners to Allah and committing sins will have a painful punishment that awaits them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  42022:
      "You, O Messenger, will see those who wrong themselves by ascribing partners to Allah and committing sins, fearing punishment for their wrongdoing. The punishment will inevitably fall on them. Their mere fear that is devoid of repentance will not be of any use to them. Those who have faith in Allah and His messengers and do righteous actions will be in contrast to them. They will be enjoying luxury in the gardens of Paradise. They will have whatever type of endless bliss they wish for with their Lord. That is the great bounty that no other bounty can come close to.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The fear of a believer for the terrors of the Day of Resurrection assists in his preparation for it.\n2. Allah’s grace to His servants is apparent.\n3. The danger of giving preference to the world over the Hereafter.",
  42023:
      "That is the good news that Allah gives at the hand of His Messenger to those who have faith in Allah and His Messengers and do righteous actions. Say, O Messenger: I do not ask of you any reward for conveying the truth besides one reward, the benefit of which returns to you, which is that you love me because of my blood relationship with you. Whoever does a good deed, We will multiply its reward for him by multiplying the reward of a good deed by ten times. Allah forgives the sins of those of His slaves who repent to Him and is grateful for the righteous actions they do seeking His pleasure.",
  42024:
      "One of the claims of the polytheists is that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم made up the Quran and then said it is from his Lord. Allah says in response to them: If you had told yourself to fabricate a lie, I would have sealed off your heart. As this is not the case, this shows that the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم is truthful and receives the revelation from his Lord. Allah eradicates the falsehood of the fabricator and preserves the truth through His words that He sends down to His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. He knows what is in the hearts of His slaves. Nothing is hidden from Him.",
  42025:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the One who accepts the repentance of His slaves from disbelief and sins when they repent to Him. He overlooks the wrongdoings that they committed. He knows everything that you do. Nothing of your actions is hidden from Him, and He will give you the recompense for them.",
  42026:
      "He responds to the supplication of those who have faith in Allah and His messengers and gives them even more out of His bounty, which they did not ask for. Those who reject Allah and His Messengers will have a strong punishment awaiting them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  42027:
      "If Allah had extended the provision for all of His slaves, they would have transgressed on Earth with oppression. But He (may He be Exalted) sends down provision to the extent that He wills to expand or restrict it. He is Well-Aware and Observant of the states of His slaves. He gives for a reason and also withholds for a reason.",
  42028:
      "He is the One who sends down the rain to His slaves after they had lost hope of its coming down. He spreads His mercy by causing crops to sprout from the earth after sending down the rain. He is the One Who takes charge of the affairs of His slaves, the One Who deserves praise in every situation.",
  42029:
      "Among Allah's signs that prove His power and oneness is the creation of the heavens and the creation of the Earth and the wondrous creations that He spread throughout them. He is able to bring them all together for the gathering and recompense whenever He wills. He is not incapable of doing this, just as He was not incapable of creating them the first time.",
  42030:
      "Whatever difficulty afflicts you, O people, in yourselves and your wealth, it is because of the sins that your hands earned. Allah overlooks many of them and does not take you to task for them.",
  42031:
      "You are not able to save yourselves from your Lord by running away when He wants to punish you. You do not have anyone besides Him to take charge of your affairs nor anyone to help you by removing the punishment if He intends it for you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The person who calls to Allah does not seek a reward from people.\n2. Expansion and narrowing of provision is subject to divine wisdom that may be hidden from many people.\n3. Sins and wrongdoings are causes of difficulties.",
  42032:
      "Among Allah's signs that prove His omnipotence and oneness are the ships sailing the ocean like mountains in height and elevation.",
  42033:
      "If Allah wished to make the wind that moves them still He would have done so, and (in that case) they would remain fixed on the ocean motionless. In that which has been mentioned about the creation of ships and the subjugation of the winds, there are clear signs of Allah's power for every person who is patient in difficulty and trials, and who is grateful for Allah's favors upon him.",
  42034:
      "Or if He (may He be Exalted) willed to destroy those ships by sending stormy winds, He would have done so on account of the sins people earn. He overlooks many of the sins of His slaves and does not punish them for those sins.",
  42035:
      "When those ships are destroyed by the stormy winds sent, those who dispute Allah's signs to refute them will know they cannot escape destruction. So, they will only call on Allah and leave those beside Him.",
  42036:
      "The wealth, fame, and children you have been given, O people, is the enjoyment of this worldly life that will vanish and come to an end. The everlasting bliss is the bliss of Paradise that Allah has prepared for those who have faith in Allah and His messengers and rely on him alone in all their matters.",
  42037:
      "[And for] those who distance themselves from major and vile sins and when they are angry at those who offend them by words or deeds, forgive their mistake and do not punish them for it. This pardon is a grace they offer when there is goodness and benefit in it.",
  42038:
      "[And for] Those who respond to their Lord by doing what He instructed and leaving out what He prohibited and complete their ritual prayer in the most perfect manner; those who consult one another in matters of importance to them and who spend from what He has provided for them seeking Allah's pleasure;",
  42039:
      "Those who, when afflicted by oppression, defend themselves in honor and respect for themselves if the oppressor is not worthy of pardon. This defense is justified, especially if there is no benefit in pardoning [the oppressor].",
  42040:
      "Whoever wants to take his right is allowed to do so but in equal measure without any excess or transgression. Whoever pardons the one who wrongs him, does not take him to task for that wrong, and sets right the relationship with his brother, then his reward is with Allah. He does not love those who do wrong by oppressing people in their selves, wealth, or honor. Rather, He detests them.",
  42041:
      "Those who defend themselves will not be blamed as they have taken their right.",
  42042:
      "Blame and retribution will only be for those who oppress people and commit sins on Earth. For such people, there will be a painful torment in the Hereafter.",
  42043:
      "As for those who are patient and overlook the harm caused to them by others, such patience will bring good for them and society. This is a praiseworthy thing, and only a person of great fortune is blessed with this.",
  42044:
      "Those whom Allah does not bless with guidance and lets them stray from the truth will have no one to take charge of their affairs after Him. You will see those who wrong themselves by disbelief and sins when they see the punishment on the Day of Resurrection, longingly saying: If only we could return to the world and repent to Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Patience and gratitude are means that lead to pondering over the signs of Allah.\n2. The status of consultation in Islam is great.\n3. The importance of pardoning the wrongdoer, because Allah loves those who pardon.\n4. The permissibility of taking the oppressor to task with the equivalent of his oppression.",
  42045:
      "You will see, O Messenger, these wrongdoers when they are exposed to the Fire, while they are humiliated and disgraced, looking at people surreptitiously due to their extreme fear of it. Those who had faith in Allah and His messengers will say: The true losers are those who lost themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection because of the punishment they received from Allah. Indeed, those who wrong themselves by disbelief and sins will be in a lasting torment that will never end.",
  42046:
      "They will have no allies to help them by rescuing them from Allah's punishment on the Day of Resurrection. Those whom Allah does not bless with the truth and lets them go astray will never have any path that leads them to guidance to the truth.",
  42047:
      "Respond, O people, to your Lord by rushing to comply with His commands, avoid His prohibitions, and abandon procrastination before the Day of Resurrection comes, which cannot be pushed back when it arrives. You will have no place to take refuge, and you will not be able to deny the sins you have perpetrated in this world.",
  42048:
      "If they turn away from what you instruct them, then We have not sent you, O Messenger, as a guardian over them to watch their actions. Your duty is only to convey what you have been instructed to convey, and their reckoning is left to Allah. When We give a man a taste of Our mercy of riches, health, etc., he rejoices in it. But when a trial of difficulty befalls them on account of their sins, their nature is to be ungrateful for Allah's favors and become angry at what Allah had in His wisdom decreed.",
  42049:
      "To Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth. He creates whatever He wills and bestows whomever He wills with daughters and whomever He wills with sons, or grants whomever He wills with both sons and daughters and makes whoever He wills barren and childless. He knows what occurs and what will occur in the future. This is on account of the completeness of His knowledge and perfection of His wisdom. Nothing is hidden from Him; nothing is outside His ability.",
  42050:
      "To Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth. He creates whatever He wills and bestows whomever He wills with daughters and whomever He wills with sons, or grants whomever He wills with both sons and daughters and makes whoever He wills barren and childless. He knows what occurs and what will occur in the future. This is on account of the completeness of His knowledge and perfection of His wisdom. Nothing is hidden from Him; nothing is outside His ability.",
  42051:
      "It is not correct for a human being to be spoken to by Allah except through revelation that He sends through inspiration or by another means, or by speaking directly to him such that he hears His speech but does not see Him, or by sending an angel as a messenger such as Gabriel, who then reveals to the human messenger with Allah's permission what Allah wishes to reveal. He (may He be Exalted) is high in His Being and His Attributes and is wise in His creation, decree, and laws.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The necessity of rushing to fulfil Allah’s instructions and avoid His prohibitions.\n2. The task of the Messenger is to convey, and the results are in Allah’s Hands.\n3. The disbeliever’s rejection of Allah’s favours is evidence against him.\n4. Allah sends revelation to His prophets in various ways, based on reasons known to Him, (may He be glorified).",
  42052:
      "Just as We sent revelation to the prophets before you, O Messenger, We revealed a Quran to you from Us. Prior to it, you did not know about the heavenly scriptures revealed to the messengers, and you did not know what faith is. But We revealed this Quran as a light by which We guide whomever of Our slaves We wish. You show people a straight path, which is the religion of Islam.",
  42053:
      "The path of Allah to Whom belongs whatever is in the heaven and whatever is in the earth. He created, owns, and controls all of it. Definitely, all matters return to Allah alone in their estimation and planning.",
  43000:
      "The Ornaments of Gold (Surah Az-Zukhruf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning not to be tempted by this world's pleasures as it may lead to polytheism.\n•    Explanation:",
  43001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  43002:
      "Allah swore by the Quran, which clearly explains the path that guides toward the truth.",
  43003:
      "We have revealed it as a Quran in the language of the Arabs in the hope that you, O people whose language it was revealed in, will comprehend and understand its meanings to transmit it to other nations.",
  43004:
      "This Quran is in the Preserved Tablet, which is high, lofty, and contains wisdom. Its verses are wise in what they command and prohibit.",
  43005:
      "Should We leave off revealing the Quran unto you just because of the immensity of your polytheism and sins? We won't do that. Instead, We will do the opposite as mercy upon you.",
  43006: "How many a prophet did We send to the previous nations!",
  43007:
      "Whenever a prophet came from Allah to those previous nations, they would mock him.",
  43008:
      "We destroyed those who were mightier than those nations, so We are not incapable of destroying those who are weaker than them. The description of the destruction of the previous nations has been mentioned in the Quran, such as that of 'Ād, Thamūd, the nation of Lot, and the people of Midian.",
  43009:
      "O Messenger, if you ask these rejecting polytheists: Who created the heavens, and who created the Earth? They will say in response to your question: The Mighty, who none can overpower, and the Omniscient of everything, created them.",
  43010:
      "Allah is the One who made the Earth stable and firm for you. He made paths in it for you through its mountains and valleys in the hope that you will be guided by them in your travels.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of revelation for the guidance of people. It is like the spirit in the body.\n2. The guidance attributed to the Messenger (peace be upon him) is the guidance of giving direction not the guidance of granting success.\n3. The affirmation by the idolaters of Allah’s oneness in lordship will not benefit them on the day of resurrection.",
  43011:
      "[He is also] the One who sends down enough water from the heavens that suffices you, your animals, and crops. With that water, We revive barren land in which there is no vegetation. Just as Allah revives that barren land with vegetation, He will revive you for the resurrection.",
  43012:
      "He made all the different varieties, such as night and day, male and female, etc. He has made ships and livestock for you, which you ride on your travels, boarding the ships over the sea and riding the livestock over land.",
  43013:
      "He created all that for you, in the hope that you settle yourselves on the backs of your mounts during your travels and then remember the blessing of your Lord over you, in that He has made them subservient to you when you mount them, and say with your tongues: The One who made these mounts subservient to us is pure and Exalted. We control them and would not have been able to do so if Allah had not made them subservient to us.",
  43014:
      "And indeed, we will certainly return to our Lord alone for reckoning and recompense.",
  43015:
      "The polytheists claimed that some of the creation are the offspring of the Creator (may He be Exalted) when they said: The angels are the daughters of Allah. Indeed, the one who makes these kinds of statements is very ungrateful and deviant.",
  43016:
      "O polytheists, do you say Allah has chosen daughters for Himself from among the things He creates while He has privileged you with male offspring?! What an absurd distribution this is, which you claim?!",
  43017:
      "When one of them is given the good news of the birth of a female whom he attributes to his Lord, his face becomes gloomy out of severe grief and sadness, and he himself becomes full of anger. So how can he attribute to his Lord the very thing that he himself is saddened by when given the good news of it?",
  43018:
      "Do they attribute to their Lord the one who is brought up in adornment and is unclear in speech when arguing due to its femininity?",
  43019:
      "They also regard the angels as feminine while they are, in reality, the slaves of The Merciful. Were they present at the time Allah created them so that they would know that they are females?! The angels will record this statement of theirs, and they will be questioned regarding it on the Day of Resurrection. Then, they will be punished for it because of their lies.",
  43020:
      "And they say, using divine decree as evidence: If Allah had willed for us not to worship the angels, we would not have worshipped them. So because He willed for it to happen, it proves He was happy with it. They make this statement out of ignorance; they are only lying.",
  43021:
      "Or, have I given these polytheists a book before the Quran that allows them to worship other than Allah, which they are holding fast to and using as evidence?",
  43022:
      "No! That has not happened. Rather, they use their blind following as evidence, saying: Indeed, we found our forefathers before us upon a belief, and they used to worship idols. We are continuing in their footsteps in worshipping them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Every blessing requires gratitude.\n2. The idolaters are deviated in their ideas of their Lord, such that they attribute daughters to Him whilst they dislike them for themselves.\n3. Using divine decree as an excuse for committing sins is invalid.\n4. Seeing is a fundamental in proving reality.\n5. Following blindly is dangerous.",
  43023:
      "And just as these people have lied and used the blind following of their forefathers as evidence, We did not send any messenger to any community before you, O Messenger, except that those living in luxury in that village said: Indeed, we found our forefathers upon a belief, and we are following in their footsteps. So your nation is not any different in that regard.",
  43024:
      "Their messenger asked them: Will you follow your forefathers even if I brought you something that is better than the belief they were upon? They said: Indeed, we reject whatever you and the messengers before you have been sent with.",
  43025:
      "We took retribution from the nations before you that rejected the messengers and destroyed them. So ponder over how the outcome of those who rejected their messengers was because their outcome was painful.",
  43026:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when Abraham told his father and his people: Indeed, I am free from the idols you worship instead of Allah.",
  43027:
      "Except for Allah, who created me, because He will soon guide me to follow His true religion, which will benefit me.",
  43028:
      "Abraham made this monotheistic statement of his (there is none worthy of worship besides Allah) remain in his progeny after him so that some of them would continue worshiping Allah alone and not attribute any partners with Him, hoping that they turn to Allah having repented from ascribing partners with Him and having repented from sins.",
  43029:
      "I did not hasten the destruction upon these rejecting polytheists. Rather, I let them enjoy themselves by letting them remain in this world, and I let their forefathers do the same until the Quran and a clear Messenger, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, came to them.",
  43030:
      "And when this Quran came to them, which was the undoubted truth, they said: This is sorcery which Muhammad intends to bewitch us with. We reject it and will never believe in it.",
  43031:
      "The rejecting polytheists say: Why did Allah not reveal this Quran upon one of the two great men of Mecca or Taif instead of revealing it upon Muhammad, the impoverished orphan?",
  43032:
      "O Messenger, do they distribute the mercy of your Lord, so they can give it to and prevent from it whomsoever they wish, or does Allah do that? We distributed their provisions between them in this world, making some rich and some poor so that they are subservient to each other. The mercy of your Lord to His slaves in the Afterlife is better than the temporary, mortal things of this world that these people hoard.",
  43033:
      "Were it not that humanity would become of one disbelieving creed, We would have made in the houses of those who disbelieved in Allah roofs of silver and silver stairs upon which they could climb.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Following blindly was one of the causes of the previous nations deviating.\n2. It is necessary to proclaim innocence from disbelief and disbelievers.\n3. Monotheism remained in the progeny of Abraham (peace be upon him).\n4. Apostleship is a divine honour. It has no connection with human standards.\n5. The distribution of sustenance is down to the wisdom of Allah.\n6. The worldly life is insignificant to Allah, and because of it’s insignificance He gives to disbelievers as He wishes.",
  43034:
      "And We would make doors of silver for their houses and give them elevated seats of silver to recline on as a trial and to lead them into destruction gradually.",
  43035:
      "We would also give them gold. All that is only the temporary enjoyment of this world; its benefit is little because of its ultimate extinction. However, O Messenger, the bounties of the Afterlife are better according to your Lord for those who are mindful of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  43036:
      "Whoever does not look into the Quran, turning away from it, will be punished by a devil set upon him, never leaving him and tempting him more and more.",
  43037:
      "Indeed, these devil companions who have been set upon those who turn away from the Quran, prevent them from the religion of Allah. They are unable to fulfill His commands and refrain from things He has not allowed; they think that they are guided to the truth, and so they do not repent from their deviance.",
  43038:
      "Until the one who turns away from the remembrance of Allah comes to Us on the Day of Resurrection and says longingly: O companion! If only there had been the distance of the east and west between you and me! You were such a disgraceful companion!",
  43039:
      "Allah will say to the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection: After you have oppressed yourselves by committing polytheism and sins, your sharing the punishment will not benefit you today because your partners will not bear anything from your torment.",
  43040:
      "Indeed, these people are deaf from hearing the truth and blind from seeing it. So, are you, O Messenger, capable of making the deaf hear, guiding the blind, or guiding the one clearly astray from the straight path?",
  43041:
      "If We were to take you away by causing you to die before We torment them, We would take retribution from them by punishing them in this world and the next.",
  43042:
      "Or if We were to show you some of the punishment We have prepared for them, indeed, We possess the power over them, and they cannot overpower Us in the slightest.",
  43043:
      "So, O Messenger, hold fast to whatever your Lord has revealed to you and practice it; you are on the path of truth in which there is no uncertainty.",
  43044:
      "And indeed, this Quran is an honor for you and your nation. On the Day of Resurrection, you will be questioned regarding having faith in it, following its guidance, and inviting to it.",
  43045:
      "O Messenger, ask those messengers We sent before you: Did Allah make deities to be worshipped instead of the Merciful?",
  43046:
      "Verily, We sent Moses with Our signs to Pharaoh and the leaders of his people. He told them: Indeed, I am the Messenger of the Lord of all creation.",
  43047:
      "Then, when he brought My signs to them, they began to laugh at them mockingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Turning away from the Qur’an is dangerous.\n2. It is obligatory to hold fast to the revelation that was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\n3. The Qur’an is an honour for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his nation.\n4. All the divine messages from Allah coincided in rejecting ascribing partners with Allah.\n5. Mocking the truth is a trait from the traits of disbelief.",
  43048:
      "We showed Pharaoh and his leaders proof after proof to establish the authenticity of Moses' (peace be upon him) message; each proof was greater than the previous one. I seized them with the torment in this world in the hope that they turn away from their disbelief, but to no avail.",
  43049:
      "So when some of the punishment came upon them, they said to Moses (peace be upon him): O sorcerer! Pray to your Lord for us, asking Him to remove this punishment just as He said He would if we believed. If it is removed from us, we will be guided to the truth.",
  43050:
      "Then, when We removed the punishment from them, they began breaking their covenant and did not fulfill it.",
  43051:
      "Pharaoh called out among his people, bragging about his kingdom: O my people! Do I not own the country of Egypt and these rivers that flow beneath my palaces? Do you not see my kingdom and recognize my greatness?",
  43052:
      "And Pharaoh said: Therefore, I am better than Moses, the weak fugitive who cannot even speak well.",
  43053:
      "Why did Allah who sent him not cast down golden bracelets on him so that it becomes clear that he is His Messenger, or why did the angels not come with him, following one another?",
  43054:
      "So Pharaoh lured his people, and they followed him in deviance. Indeed, they were a nation that went away from the obedience of Allah.",
  43055:
      "Then, when they angered Us by continuing upon disbelief, We took retribution from them and drowned them all.",
  43056:
      "So, We made Pharaoh and his people a precursor for the people and the disbelievers from your nation who would follow in their footsteps. We also made them a lesson for those who take heed so they do not do as they did and then are afflicted with what they were afflicted with.",
  43057:
      "When the polytheists thought that Jesus, whom the Christians worshipped, was included in the statement of Allah, the Exalted: {Indeed, you [disbelievers] and what you worship other than Allah is the firewood of Hell. You will be coming to [enter] it} [Al-Anbiya:98], and Allah had prohibited worshipping him just like He had prohibited the worship of idols; your people, O Messenger, began persisting in argument, saying: We are pleased that our idols are of the same status as Jesus. So Allah revealed, refuting them: {Indeed, those for whom the best [reward] has preceded from Me - they are from it far removed} [Surah Al Anbiya: 101].",
  43058:
      "And they say: Are our deities better, or is Jesus better? Ibn Al-Ziba'ra and others did not make this comparison out of the love to attain truth, but rather out of love of argumentation. They are a nation with a quarrelsome nature.",
  43059:
      "Jesus, the son of Mary, is nothing but a slave from Allah's slaves whom He favored with messengership. He made him an example for the Israelites to use as proof of Allah's ability since He created him without a father, just like He created Adam without parents.",
  43060:
      "O children of Adam, if We had wished to destroy you, We would have and would have made the angels succeed you on Earth in your place. They would worship Allah and not ascribe partners with Him at all.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Breaking covenants is from the traits of the disbelievers.\n2. The wrongdoer is dim-witted; whoever wants to lead him astray can do so.\n3. Earning the anger of Allah will inevitably result in loss.\n4. The people of deviance strive to distort the meanings of Qur’anic text to suit their desires.",
  43061:
      "Indeed, When Jesus descends towards the end of time, he will be a sign from the major signs of the Hour. So do not doubt the Hour's occurrence and follow me in whatever I have brought to you from Allah. What I have brought is the straight path in which there is no deviance.",
  43062:
      "And do not let the Devil turn you away from the straight path through his lure and deception. Indeed, he is an enemy whose enmity is clear.",
  43063:
      "After Jesus (peace be upon him) brought clear signs of his messengership to his people, he said to them: I have brought wisdom to you from Allah so that I can make clear to you some matters of your religion you differ in. So be mindful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, and obey me in whatever I command you with and prohibit you from.",
  43064:
      "Indeed, Allah is my Lord and your Lord; we have no Lord other than Him, so devote your worship to Him alone. This monotheism is the straight path in which there is no deviance.",
  43065:
      "Then, groups from amongst the Christians disagreed regarding Jesus. Some of them say he is a god, some say he is the son of God, and others say he and his mother are both gods. So woe be to those who oppress themselves by attributing divinity to Jesus, or sonship, or saying that he is one of the Trinity! Woe be to them from a painful punishment that awaits them on the Day of Resurrection.",
  43066:
      "These disputing parties in regards to Jesus await nothing except the Hour, which will come to them suddenly, while they do not even perceive its arrival. If it comes to them while they are upon disbelief, then their abode is a painful torment.",
  43067:
      "Those who befriend each other upon disbelief and deviance will be enemies to one another on the Day of Resurrection, except those who are mindful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Their friendship is everlasting and will never break.",
  43068:
      "Allah will say to them: O, My slaves! There is no fear upon you today in what you will face, nor will you grieve over what you lost out on from the good of the worldly life.",
  43069:
      "Those who believed in the Quran that was sent down upon their Messenger and submitted to it, fulfilling its commands and refraining from what it did not allow.",
  43070:
      "Enter Paradise; you and those who have faith like you. You will be pleased with the everlasting blessings you will encounter, which shall never finish nor expire.",
  43071:
      "Their slaves will roam among them with golden plates and handleless cups. In Paradise, there is whatever the hearts desire and whatever delights the eyes. You will reside in it eternally.",
  43072:
      "That Paradise I have described for you is the one Allah made you inherit from His grace due to your deeds.",
  43073:
      "There are many fruits in it for you that shall never finish, which you can eat from.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The descension of Jesus is one of the major signs of the Hour.\n2. Satan is an enemy of the children of Adam.\n3. The friendship of the wrongdoers will break on the Day of Judgement, whilst the friendship of the Allah-conscious will remain forever.",
  43074:
      "Upon mentioning the reward of the heedful, Allah mentions the recompense awaiting their opposite (i.e., the wrongdoers). He states: \n Indeed, the criminals who commit disbelief and sins will be in the torment of Hell on the Day of Resurrection, wherein they shall remain forever.",
  43075:
      "The punishment will not be lessened for them. They will lose all hope in the mercy of Allah in it.",
  43076:
      "And We did not oppress them by entering them into the Fire; rather, they oppressed themselves by disbelieving.",
  43077:
      "They will call out to Malik, the gatekeeper of the Fire, saying: O Malik! Our Lord should make us die so that we are relieved of this punishment! Malik will answer them: You are to remain forever in the punishment. You will not die, nor will the punishment stop.",
  43078:
      "Indeed, I brought the undisputed truth to you in this world, but the majority of you disliked the truth.",
  43079:
      "So, if they plot against the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and hatch an evil plan against him, We will, indeed, hatch a plan against them that will be greater than theirs.",
  43080:
      "Or do they think that We do not hear the secrets they hide within their hearts or whisper to one another? Nay! We hear them all, and the angels with them write everything they do.",
  43081:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those who attribute daughters to Allah (Allah is Transcendent and far beyond what they say): Allah does not have a child. He is free and sanctified from that. I am the first to worship Him (the Exalted) and declare Him free from anything not befitting Him.",
  43082:
      "The Lord of the heavens, the Earth, and the Throne is pure of the statements of these polytheists who ascribe partners, wives, and children to Him.",
  43083:
      "So, O Messenger, leave them to continue in whatever falsehood they are engrossed in and let them enjoy themselves until they meet the day they have been promised, the Day of Resurrection.",
  43084:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the true deity in the heavens and the true deity on Earth. He is the most Wise in His creation, decree, and management. He is Omniscient of the conditions of His slaves; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  43085:
      "Allah's goodness and blessings continue to increase (may He be Exalted). To Him alone belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the Earth and whatever lies between them. And with Him alone is the knowledge of the Hour in which the Day of Resurrection will occur; no one else knows it. You will return to Him alone in the Hereafter for accountability and requital.",
  43086:
      "Those that the polytheists worship instead of Allah are not able to intercede in front of Allah, except those that testify that there is none worthy of worship except Allah while understanding their testimony, e.g., Jesus, Ezra, and the angels.",
  43087:
      "If you were to ask them: Who created you? They would definitely say: Allah created us. So how can they then turn away from His worship after this acknowledgment?!",
  43088:
      "With Allah (may He be Exalted) is the knowledge of the complaint of His Messenger when they rejected him and his statement regarding them: O my Lord! Indeed, these people are a nation that does not believe in what you sent me to convey to them.",
  43089:
      "So ignore them and say to them whatever repels their evil (this was in Mecca) they will soon realize what punishment they will face.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbelievers will lose hope of ever coming out of the hellfire.\n2. Disliking the truth is very dangerous.\n3. The plots of the disbelievers turn on them, even if it be after a while.\n4. The knowledge of the hour is exclusive to Allah.\n5. The oneness in Lordship necessitates oneness in Allahhood.",
  44000:
      "The Smoke (Surah Ad-Dukhan)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThreatening the polytheists by detailing the punishment that awaits them imminently and in the future.\n•    Explanation:",
  44001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  44002:
      "Allah swore by the Quran, which clearly explains the path that guides toward the truth.",
  44003:
      "Indeed, We revealed the Quran on the Night of Decree; it is a night of much goodness. Indeed, We warn through this Quran.",
  44004:
      "On this night, every precise matter related to provisions, lifespans, etc., is decided which Allah will make happen that year.",
  44005:
      "We decide every precise matter of Ours; indeed, We are the One who sends the messengers.",
  44006:
      "We send the messengers as a mercy from your Lord, O Messenger, for those to whom they are sent. Indeed, He (may He be Exalted) is All-Hearing of His slaves' words and Omniscient of their actions and intentions; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  44007:
      "He is the Lord of the heavens, the Earth, and whatever lies between them. If you are convinced of that, then have faith in My Messenger.",
  44008:
      "Nothing is worthy of worship besides Him. He gives life and causes death; no one does that except Him. He is your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers before you.",
  44009:
      "These polytheists are not convinced of that; rather, they are in doubt about it and distract themselves from it with the falsehood they are in.",
  44010:
      "So wait, O Messenger, the punishment of your people that will come soon, on a day when the sky will bring forth an apparent smoke, which they will see with their eyes due to severe hunger.",
  44011:
      "It will encompass your people and be said to them: This punishment that has afflicted you is a painful torment.",
  44012:
      "They will then beg their Lord, asking him, O our Lord! Turn the punishment that you sent upon us away from us. If you turn it away from us, we will believe in You and Your Messenger.",
  44013:
      "How can they take heed and repent to their Lord now when a Messenger came to them before with a clear message, and they knew of his truthfulness and honesty?!",
  44014:
      "But they turned away from believing in him and said about him: He is a pupil taught by others; he is not a messenger. They also said: He is a madman.",
  44015:
      "Indeed, when We turn the punishment away from you for a short while, you will return to your disbelief and rejection.",
  44016:
      "Wait for them, O Messenger, on the day when We will seize the disbelievers of your people with the greatest seizing on the day of Badr. We will take retribution from them for their disbelief in Allah and for rejecting His messengers.",
  44017:
      "And verily I tested the people of Pharaoh before them, and their noble Messenger came to them from Allah calling them towards His Oneness and worship. He was Moses (peace be upon him).",
  44018:
      "Moses said to Pharaoh and his people: Leave the Israelites to me because they are the slaves of Allah; you have no right to take them as slaves. Indeed, I am a messenger to you from Allah. I am trustworthy in conveying what He has commanded me to convey; I will not take anything away from it nor add anything to it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The initial revelation of the noble Qur’an upon the Prophet was on the Night of Decree.\n2. The Night of Decree is in the month of Ramadan.\n3. The teachings of the Prophets free the weak from the grasp of tyrants.",
  44019:
      "And do not show arrogance to Allah by leaving His worship and assuming superiority over His slaves. Indeed, I will bring to you a clear proof.",
  44020:
      "And I have sought protection in my Lord and your Lord from you killing me by stoning.",
  44021:
      "If you do not believe in whatever I have brought, then leave me alone and do not approach me to harm me.",
  44022:
      "Then Moses supplicated to his Lord: This nation, i.e., Pharaoh and his people, is a criminal nation that deserves a swift punishment.",
  44023:
      "So Allah commanded Moses to take his people away at night and informed him that Pharaoh and his people would pursue them.",
  44024:
      "He also commanded him that when they all cross the sea, they leave it standing as it was because Pharaoh and his people were to be destroyed by drowning in it.",
  44025:
      "How many gardens and flowing springs did Pharaoh and his people leave behind?!",
  44026: "And how many farms and beautiful places did they leave behind?!",
  44027:
      "And how many lives of luxuries they used to live did they leave behind!",
  44028:
      "Whatever has been described to you happened to them, and we made another nation, i.e., the Israelites inherit their gardens, springs, farms, and structures.",
  44029:
      "Neither the heavens nor the Earth cried over Pharaoh and his people when they drowned, nor were they given respite to repent.",
  44030:
      "And verily, We saved the Israelites from the humiliating punishment as Pharaoh and his people would kill their children and spare their women.",
  44031:
      "We saved them from the punishment of Pharaoh. Indeed, he was an arrogant one from those who transgressed the command and religion of Allah.",
  44032:
      "And verily, We selected the Israelites knowingly over the people of their time because of their many Prophets.",
  44033:
      "And We granted them miracles through which We gave strength to Moses, and in which there was an obvious blessing for them, like the Manna and Salwa and other than them.",
  44034:
      "Indeed, these rejecting polytheists will say, denying the resurrection:",
  44035:
      "It is only our first death that we will die; there is no life after that, and we will not be resurrected after this death.",
  44036:
      "O Muhammad! If you are truthful in your claim that Allah will resurrect the dead for requital and accountability, then bring our forefathers who have died back to life.",
  44037:
      "O Messenger, are these denying polytheists stronger and more resistant, or are the people of Tubba' and those after them like 'Ād and Thamūd? We destroyed them all. Indeed, they were criminals.",
  44038:
      "And We did not create the heavens, the Earth, and everything between it in jest and amusement.",
  44039:
      "We only created the heavens and the Earth due to profound wisdom, but most polytheists do not know that.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory for a believer to seek refuge in his Lord to protect him from the plots of his enemies.\n2. Supplicating against the disbelievers is legislated when they do not accept the call and fight the callers.\n3. The universe does not grieve over the death of a disbeliever because of his insignificance to Allah.\n4. The creation of the heavens and the earth is due to a profound wisdom which the heretics are ignorant of.",
  44040:
      "The Day of Resurrection, when Allah will decide between the slaves, is the appointed time for all of creation in which Allah will gather them.",
  44041:
      "The Day when no relative will benefit his relative or friend benefit his friend nor will they be saved from Allah's punishment, because authority on that day will be for Allah. Nobody will be able to claim it.",
  44042:
      "Except the person Allah has mercy on, for he will benefit from the good action he has sent forward. Allah is the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in His creation, decree, and plan.",
  44043:
      "After mentioning the Resurrection, Allah explains how people will be divided on that Day according to the nature of their recompense, stating: \n The tree of Zaqqum that Allah has grown at the bottom of the Inferno.",
  44044:
      "Is the food of the extremely sinful who will eat of its horrible fruit!",
  44045:
      "This fruit is like black oil, boiling in their stomachs from its intense heat.",
  44046: "Like the boiling of extremely hot water.",
  44047:
      "It will be said to the keepers of the Fire: Grab him and drag him violently and harshly towards the middle of the Inferno.",
  44048:
      "Then pour hot water over the head of this person being punished, so that the punishment is never separated from him.",
  44049:
      "It will be said to him mockingly: Taste this painful torment. You are the mighty who is not treated unjustly, noble amongst your people.",
  44050:
      "This is the punishment you used to doubt would occur on the Day of Resurrection, but now your doubt has been removed by you seeing it.",
  44051:
      "Those who are mindful of their Lord through complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will be in a place of residence that is safe from every misfortune that could afflict them.",
  44052: "In gardens and flowing springs.",
  44053:
      "They will wear fine and thick silk in Paradise. They will be facing one another and not see each other's nape.",
  44054:
      "Just as We will honor them with what is mentioned in Paradise, We will marry them to beautiful women with beautiful wide eyes, with the whitest whites and the blackest blacks.",
  44055:
      "They will call their attendants therein to bring them every fruit they wish, safe from their being cut off and from their harm.",
  44056:
      "Living therein forever, they will not taste death therein except the first death in the worldly life, and their Lord will save them from the punishment of the Fire.",
  44057:
      "As grace and kindness from your Lord to them. That which is mentioned, namely entering them into Paradise and saving them from the Fire, is the great success which no success can compare with.",
  44058:
      "We have made this Quran easy and facilitated it for you by revealing it in your language of Arabic, O Messenger, so that they take heed.",
  44059:
      "So await your help and their destruction; they are awaiting your destruction.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The punishment in the afterlife, for the disbeliever, will be both physical and mental.\n2. The pleasure in the afterlife, for the believer, will be both physical and mental.\n3. The great success is salvation from the fire and entering Paradise.",
  45000:
      "The Crouching (Surah Al-Jathiyah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDetailing the different conditions of the creation from legislative verses and signs in the universe, refuting the arguments of those who reject the resurrection, and alarming them.\n•    Explanation:",
  45001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  45002:
      "The revelation of the Quran is from Allah, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in His creating, decreeing, and planning.",
  45003:
      "In the heavens and Earth are proof of the power of Allah and His oneness for the believers because they are the ones who take heed of the signs.",
  45004:
      "Also, in your own creation, O people, from a drop of semen, then a blood clot, then a piece of flesh, and in the creation of the beast that Allah will send to crawl upon the face of the Earth. All these signs show Allah's oneness for those sure that Allah is the creator.",
  45005:
      "And in the alternation of the night and day, and the rainwater Allah sent down from the sky, then He gave life to the Earth through it by making plants grow in it after it was dead without any plants, and in the alternation of the winds by bringing them from one direction at times and other directions at other times for your benefit, are proof for people who understand. They use them as proof of Allah's oneness, His power to resurrect, and His power over everything.",
  45006:
      "These verses and proof We read to you in truth, O Messenger. So, if they do not believe in the speech of Allah, which He revealed to His slave, and in His proof, which speech will they believe in after it, and which proof after it will they accept?",
  45007:
      "Allah's punishment and destruction are for every extremely sinful liar.",
  45008:
      "This disbeliever listens to the verses of Allah in the Quran being recited to him, then continues in the disbelief and sins he is in, arrogant in himself, abstains from following the truth, as though he has not heard these verses being read to him. So inform him, O Messenger, of what he will dislike in the Hereafter, which is a painful punishment that awaits him there.",
  45009:
      "And when something of the Quran reaches him, he takes it as a joke to mock. Those attributed with this quality of mocking the Quran will have a disgraceful punishment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  45010:
      "In front of them will be the Fire, which awaits them in the Hereafter, and the actions they earned will not help them with Allah at all, nor will the idols they took to worship besides Him remove anything from them. And they will have a great torment on the Day of Resurrection.",
  45011:
      "This book that We revealed to Our Messenger Muhammad is a guide to the true path. And those who disbelieve in the verses of their Lord which were revealed to His Messenger will have a bad, painful punishment.",
  45012:
      "Allah alone is the One who subjugated for you, O people, the sea in which ships sail with His order so that you seek His grace through different lawful trades and are thankful for Allah's favors upon you.",
  45013:
      "And He subjugated whatever is in the heavens, such as the sun, moon, and stars, and whatever is on Earth, such as rivers, trees, mountains, and so forth. In subjugating that for you is proof of Allah's power and His oneness for people who ponder over His signs and take heed from them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Lying and persistently sinning, being proud and mocking Allah’s words, are qualities of misguided people, and Allah has threatened the person attributed with these.\n2. Allah’s favours upon His servants are many, and amongst them are Allah’s subjugating what is in the universe for them.\n3. Favours require the servants to be grateful to the Allah who has granted them.",
  45014:
      "O Messenger, say to those who have faith in Allah and accepted His messengers: Forgive those who did bad to you from the disbelievers who do not hope for Allah's reward nor do they fear His punishment, because Allah will reward both the patient believers and the transgressing disbelievers for the actions they used to earn in this world.",
  45015:
      "Whoever does righteous deeds, the result of those deeds for him; Allah does not need his actions. Whoever commits evil, the result of his evil is that he will be punished for it; his evil does not harm Allah. Then, to Us alone, you will be returned so We can reward everyone with what they deserve.",
  45016:
      "We granted the Israelites the Torah and the command to decide between people according to its rule. We made most of the prophets amongst them from the children of Abraham (peace be upon him). We provided them with different types of good things and granted them virtue over all those of their time.",
  45017:
      "We gave them proof that clarifies the truth from falsehood. They did not differ except after the proof was established against them by sending Our Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. Nothing led them to this difference except some of them oppressing others out of greed for leadership and fame. O Messenger, your Lord will decide between them on the Day of Resurrection what they used to differ about in this world, so He will clearly show who was right and who was wrong.",
  45018:
      "O Messenger, then We put you on an ordained way regarding the matter of Islam and that which calls them to faith and good actions. So follow this way and do not follow the desires of those who do not know the truth, as their desires lead them away from the truth.",
  45019:
      "Those who do not know the truth will not be able to hold back Allah's punishment from you if you follow their desires. The oppressors from all sects and creeds help and support one another against the believers. And Allah is the helper of those mindful of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  45020:
      "This Quran, which is revealed to Our Messenger, is enlightenment through which people can see the truth from falsehood, guidance to the truth, and mercy for people who have conviction because they are the ones who are guided through it to the straight path so that their Lord is pleased with them and then enters them into Paradise and distances them from the Fire.",
  45021:
      "Those who commit disbelief and sins through their limbs think We will reward them like those who believed in Allah and did good deeds, making them equal in this life and the Hereafter. Wretched is this judgment of theirs.",
  45022:
      "Allah created the heavens and Earth with complete wisdom. He did not create them in vain. He created them so each soul can be rewarded with the good or bad it earned. Allah will not oppress them by decreasing their good deeds or increasing their bad deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Pardoning and forgiving the oppressor when he does not cause corruption on earth and transgress the limits of Allah is an excellent characteristic which Allah ordered the believers with if they are optimistic of a good outcome.\n2. The necessity of following the sacred law and staying far from following the desires of people.\n3. Just as believers and disbelievers are not equal in qualities, likewise they are not equal in reward.\n4. Allah’s creating the heavens is in accordance with complete wisdom which materialistic atheists are unaware of.",
  45023:
      "O Messenger, look at the one who followed his desires and made it his object of worship, which he cannot oppose. Then Allah led him astray despite his knowledge because he deserved to be misguided, and Allah sealed his heart so he could not listen in a manner that benefits, and Allah put a veil on his eyes, which stops him from seeing the truth. So who can cause him to accept the truth after Allah has led him astray? Do you not remember the harm of following desires and the benefit of following Allah's sacred law?",
  45024:
      "And the disbelievers who denied the resurrection said: There is no life besides this worldly life of ours, so there is no life after it. Generations die never to return, and other generations come to life. Only the alternation of the night and day is what makes us die. They have no knowledge to support their denial of the resurrection. They are only assuming, and assumptions do not benefit the truth.",
  45025:
      "When you recite Our clear verses to the polytheists who deny the resurrection, they have no proof which they can use except their saying to the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم and his Companions: Bring our dead fathers back to life if you are true in your claim that we will be resurrected after our death.",
  45026:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Allah gives you life by creating you, then He will cause you to die, then He will gather you after your death on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and recompense; on that day, which is undoubtedly coming. But most people do not know, so they do not prepare for it with righteous actions.",
  45027:
      "To Allah alone belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the kingdom of Earth, so there is nobody to be truly worshipped in them besides Him. And on the day the Hour occurs in which Allah will raise the dead for reckoning and recompense, the people of falsehood who used to worship others besides Allah and strive to refute the truth and establish falsehood will lose.",
  45028:
      "And you will see on that day, O Messenger, every nation crouching on its knees, awaiting what will be done with them. Every nation will be called towards its book of deeds, which the guarding angels wrote. Today, you will be rewarded, O people, for the good and bad you used to do in the worldly life.",
  45029:
      "This is Our book, in which Our angels used to write your actions, which is speaking against you truthfully, so read it. We used to order the guarding angels to write what you used to do in the worldly life.",
  45030:
      "As for those who believe and do righteous actions, their Lord will enter them into Paradise through His mercy. That reward Allah granted them is the clear success that no success can compare with.",
  45031:
      "As for those who disbelieved in Allah, it will be said to them to rebuke them: Were My verses not recited to you, but you were too proud to believe in them, and you were a transgressing people, gaining disbelief and sins?",
  45032:
      "When it is said to you: Allah's promise, in which He has promised His slaves He will resurrect them and reward them, is true without a doubt, and the Hour is true without a doubt, so work for it, you say: We do not know what this Hour is. We only assume doubtfully that it is coming, and we are not convinced it will come.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Following desires destroys the one who does so.\n2. Assuming does not benefit the truth at all, especially in the matter of belief.",
  45033:
      "The evil consequences of the disbelief and sins they committed in the worldly life will appear to them, and the punishment they used to mock when warned of it will befall them.",
  45034:
      "Allah will tell them: Today, I will leave you in the Fire just as you forgot meeting this day of yours, and so did not prepare for it through faith and good actions. Your abode, which you will take refuge in, is the Fire, and you do not have any helpers to repel Allah's punishment from you.",
  45035:
      "That punishment you are being punished with is because you took the words of Allah as a joke, which you would mock, and life with its pleasures and desires deceived you. So today, these disbelievers who used to mock Allah's words will not be taken out of the Fire. Rather, they will remain in it forever, and neither will they be returned to the worldly life to do good deeds, nor will their Lord be pleased with them.",
  45036:
      "So for Allah alone is praise, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the Earth, and Lord of all the creation.",
  45037:
      "And for Him is grandeur and greatness in the heavens and the Earth, and He is the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in His creating, decreeing, and planning.",
  46000:
      "The Wind-Curved Sandhills (Surah Al-Ahqaf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming humanity's need for the divine message and cautioning those who turn away from it.\n•    Explanation:",
  46001:
      "Hā Mīm – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah.",
  46002:
      "The revelation of the Quran is from Allah, the Mighty, whom nobody can overpower, Wise in His creating, decreeing, and legislation.",
  46003:
      "I did not create the heavens and the Earth and what is between them in vain, but rather, I created all of it with truth and complete wisdom. Amongst that is for His slaves to recognize Him through them and so worship Him alone and not associate any partner with Him, and so that they fulfill the demands of their being made deputy on Earth until a fixed time which Allah alone knows. And those who disbelieve in Allah are turning away from the Book of Allah they are being warned through without paying attention to it.",
  46004:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who turn away from the truth: Tell me about the idols you worship besides Allah: what parts of the earth have they created? Did they create mountains or rivers? Or do they have a partnership and share with Allah in creating the heavens? Bring me a book revealed from Allah before the Quran or some trace of knowledge that the previous people left if you are true in your claim that your idols deserve to be worshipped.",
  46005:
      "No one is more misguided than the one who worships an idol besides Allah that cannot respond to his call until the Day of Resurrection. And these idols, which they worship besides Allah, are oblivious to their worshippers who call upon them, let alone benefiting them or bringing them harm.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Mocking the verses of Allah is disbelief.\n2. The danger of being deceived by the pleasures and desires of the world.\n3. Allah is the supremely Great.",
  46006:
      "As well as not benefiting them in this world, when they are raised on the Day of Judgment, they will be enemies to those who used to worship them and disassociate themselves from them. They will deny having any knowledge of their worship.",
  46007:
      "And when Our verses revealed to Our Messenger are read to them, the disbelievers say regarding the Quran when it came to them at the hands of their Messenger: This is clear magic. It is not a revelation from Allah.",
  46008:
      "Do these polytheists say that Muhammad has made up this Quran and attributed it to Allah? Say to them, O Messenger: If I have made it up on my part, you do not have power over any plan for me if Allah wants to punish me, so how can I put myself at risk of punishment by fabricating against Him? Allah knows best about what you engage in defaming His Quran and slandering me. He (may He be glorified) is sufficient as a witness between me and you. And He forgives the sins of His slaves who repent to Him and is Merciful to them.",
  46009:
      "O Messenger, tell these polytheists who reject your prophethood: I am not the first Messenger Allah has sent for you to find my call strange, as many messengers came before me. I do not know what Allah will do with me nor what He will do with you in this life. I only follow what Allah reveals to me, so I do not say or do except according to what He reveals. And I am only a warner who clearly warns of His punishment.",
  46010:
      "O Messenger, tell these deniers: Tell me if this Quran is from Allah and you deny it, and a witness from the Israelites testifies that it is from Allah, relying on what is in the Torah, and then he believes in it, while you are too arrogant to believe in it. Are you not then the oppressors? Allah does not enable the oppressors to follow the truth.",
  46011:
      "And those who disbelieved in the Quran and what their Messenger brought to them say: If what Muhammad brought was true and it guides towards good, these paupers, slaves, and weak people would not have preceded us to it. And because they are not guided to what their Messenger brought them, they will say: This which he has brought us is an old lie, and we do not follow lies.",
  46012:
      "And before this Quran was the Torah, the book Allah revealed to Moses (peace be upon him) as a guide to be followed in truth and as a mercy for those who believe in it and follow it amongst the Israelites. And this Quran revealed upon Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is a book that confirms the books before it, in the Arabic language, so that he can warn through it those who wronged themselves through associating partners with Allah and committing sins. It is a glad tiding to the righteous who have perfected their relationship with their Creator and their relationship with His creation.",
  46013:
      "Indeed, those who say: Our Lord is Allah; we have no Lord besides Him, then become firm in faith and good actions, there will be no fear in them in what they face in the Hereafter, nor will they grieve over the fortune of this worlds which escaped them or what they left behind them.",
  46014:
      "Those with such qualities are the people of Paradise who will live in it forever as a reward for their good deeds in this world.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Everyone who is worshipped besides Allah will refute the disbelievers who worshipped them.\n2. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) is not the first of the messengers, but rather the last of them.\n3. The Prophet (peace be upon him) not having knowledge of the Ghaib, except what Allah informs him of from it.\n4. The presence of that which establishes the prophethood of our Prophet (peace be upon him) in the previous books.\n5. Explaining the virtue of steadfastness and the reward for those who practice it.",
  46015:
      "And We commanded man emphatically that he should be kind to his parents in their lifetime and after their death with what does not oppose the legislation. And in particular, his mother, who carried him with difficulty and gave birth to him with hardship. From the time he was carried in the womb until the beginning of his weaning is thirty months. When he completes his mental and physical strength, he says: My Lord, inspire me to thank You for the favor you have blessed my parents with and me and inspire me to do good actions which please you, and accept them from me. And make my children righteous for me. I have repented to You from my sins and am amongst those who submit to Your obedience and surrender to Your commands.",
  46016:
      "Those are the ones from whom We accept the good deeds they did and overlook their sins, so We do not hold them to account due to them. And they are amongst the people of Paradise. This promise they have been given is faithful and will occur.",
  46017:
      "After giving an example of being dutiful to one's parents and encouraging it, Allah warns against being undutiful to them through another example, stating: \n And the one who said to his parents: Woe unto you. Do you promise I will be taken out of my grave alive after I die, whereas many nations have passed where people died, but none of them were resurrected? And his parents seek help from Allah to guide their son towards faith, and they say to their son: Woe unto you if you do not believe in the Resurrection; so, believe in it. Allah's promise of Resurrection is true without a doubt. But he says, restating his denial of the Resurrection: This which is said regarding the Resurrection is nothing, but something related from the books of the previous people and what they wrote. It is not proven to be from Allah.",
  46018:
      "Those are the ones for whom punishment is a certainty amongst the nations before them from the jinn and men. They are the losers, losing themselves and their families by entering the Fire.",
  46019:
      "And each group, the group of Paradise and the group of the Fire will be ranked according to their actions. The ranks of the people of Paradise are high, while the levels of the people of the Fire are low. And so that Allah gives them the full recompense of their actions, and they will not be oppressed on the Day of Judgment by their good deeds being decreased or their evil deeds being increased.",
  46020:
      "On the Day when those who rejected Allah and His messengers will be exposed to the Fire to be punished, it will be said to them in rebuke: You have exhausted your share of the pleasures of this life, and you fully enjoyed them. On this day, you will be recompensed with the punishment, which will disgrace and shame you due to your arrogance on earth, which you had no right to do, and your leaving Allah's obedience through disbelief and sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Explaining the status of righteousness in Islam, especially with respect to the mother, and warning of disobedience.\n2. Explaining the danger of increasing in worldly pleasures, as they distract from the Afterlife.\n3. Explaining the severe warning for the people of pride and transgression.",
  46021:
      "O Messenger, remember Hūd, the brother of 'Ād in lineage, when he warned his people of Allah's punishment befalling them when they were in their homes in Aḥqāf in the south of the Arabian Peninsula. Messengers had warned their people before Hūd and after him, saying to their people: Do not worship anyone except Allah alone; do not worship anything besides Him. O people, I fear for you the punishment of a great day, which is the Day of Judgment.",
  46022:
      "His people told him: Have you come to us to turn us away from worshipping our gods? That will never happen. So, bring us the punishment you threaten us with if you are truthful in your claim.",
  46023:
      "He said: The knowledge of the time for punishment is only with Allah, and I do not know it. I am only a messenger who conveys to you what I have been sent with. However, I see you as people who are ignorant of what benefits you, and you abandon it; and what harms you, you embrace it.",
  46024:
      "Then, when the punishment they asked to befall them quickly came to them, and they saw a cloud appearing in one direction of the sky, heading towards their valleys; they said: This is a cloud which will bring us rain. Hūd told them: The matter is not as you think, i.e., that it is not a raincloud; in fact, it is the punishment you wanted to be hastened. It is a wind that contains a painful punishment.",
  46025:
      "Destroying everything it passed by which Allah ordered to be destroyed, they were killed, and only the houses in which they lived were left visible, bearing witness to their inhabiting them before. With this kind of painful punishment, We punish the transgressors who persist in their disbelief and sins.",
  46026:
      "And We granted the people of Hūd the means of empowerment which We have not given you, and We gave them hearing to hear with a vision to see with, and hearts to understand with. But their hearing did not benefit them or their imagination or intellect. They did not repel Allah's punishment from them when it came to them, as they used to disbelieve in Allah's signs and the punishment which they used to mock and which their prophet Hūd (peace be upon) used to warn them of, finally befell them.",
  46027:
      "And We destroyed the cities around you, O people of Mecca; We destroyed 'Ād, Thamūd, the people of Lot, and the people of Midian. We gave them different proof and evidence in the hope they would turn back from their disbelief.",
  46028:
      "So why did their idols not help them? The idols they took as gods besides Allah, and they used to seek closeness through worship and sacrifice. They did not help them; rather, they disappeared when they needed them the most. And that is the lie and fabrication they invented, i.e., that these idols will benefit and intercede for them with Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The messengers do not have knowledge of the Ghaib, except what their Lord has informed them of.\n2. The people of Hud were deceived when they thought the punishment which was going to befall them was rain, so they did not repent before it seized them suddenly.\n3. The power of Ad was more than the power of Quraish, but Allah still destroyed them.\n4. The intelligent is he who takes lesson from others and the ignorant is he who takes lessons from himself.",
  46029:
      "Remember, O Messenger, when I sent you a group of the jinn to listen to the Quran that was revealed to you? When they came to hear it, they said to one another: Be quiet so that we can listen to it. When the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم completed his recitation, they returned to their people to warn them of Allah's punishment if they did not believe in this Quran.",
  46030:
      "They said to them: O our people, we have heard a book that Allah has revealed after Moses, confirming the previous scriptures revealed by Allah. This book we heard guides us to the truth and refers to a straight path, which is the path of Islam.",
  46031:
      "O our people, respond to the truth that Muhammad calls you towards and believe he is a messenger from his Lord. Allah will forgive your sins and save you from the painful torment that awaits you if you do not respond to the truth that he calls you towards and do not believe that he is a messenger from his Lord.",
  46032:
      "Those who do not respond to the truth that Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم calls them towards will not be able to escape from Allah by fleeing. They will not have, besides Allah, any protectors to rescue them from the punishment. Such people have deviated from the truth.",
  46033:
      "Do these polytheists who deny the Resurrection not understand that Allah, Who created the heavens and the Earth, and did not tire in creating them despite their hugeness and vastness, can give life to the dead for reckoning and recompense? Indeed, He can bring them back to life. He (may He be Exalted) is Omnipotent over everything; He is not hindered from bringing the dead to life.",
  46034:
      "On the Day when those who rejected Allah and His messengers will be exposed to the Fire to be punished, it will be said to them in rebuke: Is this punishment that you see not real? Or is it a lie like you used to say in the world? They will say: Indeed, by Our Lord, it is the truth. It will then be said to them: Taste the punishment for disbelieving in Allah.",
  46035:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with the rejection of your people just as the Messengers of Resolve were patient. These were the messengers in addition to our Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم: Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus (peace be upon them). Do not seek to hasten the punishment for them. The deniers from your people, on the day they will see the punishment you warned about in the Hereafter, it will be as if they did not live in this world except for an hour of a day due to the length of their punishment. This Quran revealed to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is a warning to all people and the jinn, and only those who go against Allah by disbelief and sins will be destroyed by the punishment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is part of good etiquette to listen to the speaker and pay attention to him.\n2. The prompt response by those jinn who were guided to the truth is a message of encouragement for human beings.\n3. Responding to the truth demands rushing towards spreading it.\n4. Patience is a quality of the prophets (peace be upon them).",
  47000:
      "Muhammad (Surah Muhammad)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nInspiring the believers to fight in order to strengthen them and weaken the disbelievers.\n•    Explanation:",
  47001:
      "Those who reject Allah and turn people away from Allah's religion, Allah will nullify their deeds.",
  47002:
      "And those who believe in Allah, do righteous deeds and believe in what Allah has revealed to His Messenger Muhammad, and what He has revealed to His Messenger Muhammad is the truth from their Lord, Will remit their wrongdoings and won't take them to the task. He will set right their affairs in this world and the Hereafter.",
  47003:
      "That mentioned recompense for the two groups is because those who reject Allah follow falsehood, and those who believe in Allah and His Messenger follow the truth from their Lord. Thus, their recompense differs just as their efforts differ. Just as Allah showed His decision about the two groups, believers and disbelievers, Allah gives people their examples so that similarities can be matched.",
  47004:
      "O believers, when you come face-to-face with those disbelievers who wage war against you, strike their necks with your swords and persevere in fighting them until you subdue them and eradicate their power. Once you have stopped them, tie the chains of the captives. When you capture them, as dictated by common interests [of the Muslims], you can be graceful to them by releasing them for no ransom, ransoming them for wealth or something else, killing them, or enslaving them. Continue fighting and capturing them until the war ends by the disbelievers accepting Islam or by your entering into a treaty with them. The mentioned trial of the believers with the disbelievers, the alternation of fortunes, and the victory of one over the other is Allah's decision. If Allah willed to defeat the disbelievers without a fight, He would have done so, but He ordained striving in His path to test some of you with others. He pushes to see who of the believers fights and who doesn’t. He tries the disbeliever with the believer: If the believer is killed, he enters Paradise; if the believer kills him, he enters the Fire. Those who are killed in Allah's path, Allah will never let their deeds go to waste.",
  47005:
      "He will enable them to follow the truth and set their affairs right in their worldly life.",
  47006:
      "He will enter them into Paradise on the day of resurrection, whose description He gave them in the world, so they recognized it and showed them their places in the Hereafter.",
  47007:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act on what He legislated for them, if you help Allah by helping His Prophet and His religion and fighting the disbelievers, He will help you by granting you dominance over them. He will keep your feet firm in battle when you face them.",
  47008:
      "For those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger, there will be loss and destruction, and Allah will nullify the reward of their deeds.",
  47009:
      "That punishment will befall them because they detested the Quran Allah revealed to His Prophet. After all, it contained the mention of Allah's Oneness, so Allah destroyed their deeds, and they were losers in this world and the Hereafter.",
  47010:
      "Have these deniers not traveled the Earth and reflected on the ultimate demise of those who had denied before them? It was a painful end. Allah destroyed their homes above them and killed them and their children and wealth. Disbelievers in every time and place will receive similar punishment.",
  47011:
      "That mentioned recompense is for the two groups because Allah helps those who have faith in Him, and the disbelievers have no one to help them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The usage of overwhelming force in the battlefield is the best means to render an enemy impotent.\n2. Being graceful, taking ransom, killing, and enslavement are options in Islam for dealing with a disbelieving captive and one of these may be applied as per demands of the circumstance.\n3. Allah’s helping the believers is contingent on their helping His religion.",
  47012:
      "Allah will enter those who believe in Allah and His Messenger and who do righteous deeds into gardens beneath whose palaces and trees rivers will flow. Those who reject Allah and His Messenger enjoy the world by pursuing their desires and eating like cattle eat. They have no concerns other than their stomachs and private parts. On the day of resurrection, they will go to the Fire, their final abode.",
  47013:
      "We have destroyed many towns of the previous nations with more strength, wealth, and children than Mecca, whose people evicted you from it when they denied their messengers, and they had no helper to rescue them from Allah's punishment when it came to them. Thus, nothing can prevent Us from destroying the people of Mecca if We intend to do so.",
  47014:
      "Are those who have clear proof and glaring evidence from their Lord and therefore worship Him with insight the same as those whom the Devil has beautified their evil actions? They followed what their desires dictated to them by worshipping idols, taking on sin, and denying the messengers.",
  47015:
      "The description of Paradise that Allah promises those who fear Him by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions is as follows: There are rivers of water whose smell and taste have not changed over time. In it, there are rivers of milk whose taste has not changed. There are rivers of wine that are delicious to those who drink and rivers of honey free from all impurities. Therein, they will get all types of fruit that they wish for. Above all, they will receive an expiation of their sins from Allah, who will not take them to account. Can the person with this recompense be equal to those who will remain in the Fire, never to come out, and who will be given boiling water to drink, which will cut the intestines of their stomachs due to its extreme heat?",
  47016:
      "Some of the hypocrites listen to you, O Messenger, but without acceptance and instead turn away until when they leave your presence, they say to those whom Allah had given knowledge: What did he just say? They pretend to be ignorant and turn away. They are the ones whose hearts Allah has sealed, and thus no good reaches it, and they follow their desires, which have made them blind to the truth.",
  47017:
      "Those guided to the path of truth and to follow what the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم brought, their Lord will increase them in guidance and direction to all good, and He inspires them to do that which will protect them from the Fire.",
  47018:
      "Are the disbelievers waiting for anything but the hour to come on them suddenly without them having any prior knowledge of it? Its signs have already arrived, such as the mission of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and the splitting of the moon. How will they then take heed when the hour comes? It is unlikely that the reminder will be of benefit to them.",
  47019:
      "Have certainty, O Messenger, that there is no being deserving of worship besides Allah, and seek forgiveness for your sins from Allah. Seek forgiveness from Him for the sins of the believing men and women. Allah knows your movements during the day and your resting place at night. Nothing is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The disbeliever’s concern is limited to enjoying fleeting pleasures in the world.\n2. A comparison between the recompense of the believers and the recompense of the disbelievers will show the vast difference between them, so that the intelligent person can choose to be a believer and the foolish person can choose to be a disbeliever.\n3. An exposition of the bad manners displayed by the hypocrites with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\n4. Knowledge precedes statements and action.",
  47020:
      "Those who believe in Allah say, longing for Allah to reveal to His Messenger a surah containing the instruction for fighting: Why does Allah not reveal a surah in which fighting is mentioned? When Allah reveals a clear surah containing the mention of fighting, you, O Messenger, will see those hypocrites in whose hearts there is doubt looking at you like one unconscious on account of extreme fear and terror. So, woe to them for withdrawing from fighting and being afraid of it.",
  47021:
      "They should follow Allah's instruction and speak only good words that is better for them. So, when fighting is imposed on them, and the matter becomes severe, if they are true to Allah, having faith in Him and following Him, it would be better for them than hypocrisy and going against Allah's instructions.",
  47022:
      "If you turn away from believing in Allah and following Him, it is most likely that you will make mischief on Earth by disbelief and sins and cut family ties, just as you used to do pre-Islam.",
  47023:
      "Those who are described as mischief makers on Earth and cutting family ties are the ones whom Allah has distanced from His mercy. He has made their ears deaf to hearing the truth with acceptance and submission and has prevented their sight from seeing it while reflecting on its meanings.",
  47024:
      "Will these people who turn away not ponder the Quran and reflect on what is in it? If they consider it, it will guide them to every good and distance them from evil. Or are there locks on the hearts of these people that are tightly closed so that no advice reaches them and no reminder benefits them?",
  47025:
      "Those who turn back from their belief towards disbelief and hypocrisy after the proof has been established against them and the truth of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم has become clear to them; the Devil is the one who has beautified their disbelief and hypocrisy and has raised their vain hopes.",
  47026:
      "They became misled because they secretly told the polytheists who hated what Allah had revealed to His Messenger: we will obey you in some matters, such as discouragement from fighting [for the Cause of Allah]. Allah knows everything they hide and their innermost intentions; nothing is hidden from Him. And He exposes what He wishes of their hidden intentions to His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  47027:
      "How horrific do you think their state will be, and the severity of their punishment when the appointed angels remove their souls, striking their faces and backs with steel hammers?",
  47028:
      "The severe punishment will occur when their souls are removed because they followed everything that brought Allah's wrath on them, such as disbelief, hypocrisy, and opposition to Allah and His messenger. They hated what would have gotten them closer to their Lord and gained them His pleasure, such as believing in Allah and following His Messenger. Thus, Allah nullifies their deeds.",
  47029:
      "Do those hypocrites who harbor doubts in their hearts think Allah will not bring out and expose their malice? He will undoubtedly bring it out by testing them with trials to distinguish the person who is truthful in belief from the liar. The believer will become apparent, and the hypocrite will be exposed.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Legislation of striving in Allah’s path distinguishes the hypocrites from the rank of the believers.\n2. The importance of reflecting over the Book of Allah and the danger of neglecting it.\n3. Disbelief and hypocrisy are causes for punishment in the Transitory Stage.",
  47030:
      "If We wished to inform you of the hypocrites, O Messenger, We would have shown them to you, and you would have recognized them by their marks. You will soon recognize them by their manner of speech. Allah knows your deeds; nothing is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you.",
  47031:
      "We will test you, O believers, with striving in Allah's path and fighting and killing the enemy until it becomes apparent, those of you who strive in Allah's path and those who are steadfast in fighting the enemy. We will test you so that We know the truthful person from the liar.",
  47032:
      "Those who reject Allah and His messenger, who abstain from Allah's religion themselves and also prevent others from it, and who go against the Messenger and oppose him after it has become clear that he is a prophet, they do not harm Allah. They only harm themselves, and Allah will nullify their deeds.",
  47033:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated, follow Allah and follow the Messenger by fulfilling their instructions and avoiding their prohibitions, and do not nullify your deeds by disbelief and ostentation.",
  47034:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah and turn themselves and people away from Allah's religion and then perish as disbelievers without repenting; Allah will not overlook their sins by covering them. Instead, He will take them to task for it and enter them into the Fire to remain there forever.",
  47035:
      "So do not become weak, O believers, when facing your enemy, and call them to peace before they call you to it when you are dominant and have the upper hand over them. Allah is close to you with His help and support. He will not reduce the reward of your good deeds at all. Instead, He will increase you out of His bounty.",
  47036:
      "The life of the world is only idle play and amusement. An intelligent person should not become preoccupied with it and turn away from striving for his Hereafter. If you believe in Allah and His messenger and fear Allah by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions, He will give you the reward of your deeds in full without any reduction, and He will not ask you for all your wealth. He will only ask you for the Zakat.",
  47037:
      "If He had to ask you for all of your wealth and insist on this request from you, you would become miserly with it, and He would bring out the hatred to spend in the way of Allah from your hearts. Thus, He is not asking it from you out of kindness.",
  47038:
      "Here, you are being called to spend a part of your wealth in Allah's path, and you are not asked to spend it all. Some of you desist from the required spending out of miserliness. Whoever is too miserly to pay a portion of his wealth in Allah's path is being miserly to his own detriment, as he deprives himself of the reward of spending. Allah is Self-sufficient and does not need your spending. You are the ones in need of Him. If you turn back from Islam to disbelief, He will destroy you and bring about another people beside you. Then they will not be like you; rather, they will be obedient to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The hypocrites have certain attributes by which they can be recognised no matter how hard they try to conceal them.\n2. Tests are a divine practice to distinguish the believers from the hypocrites.\n3. Allah supports His believing servants by His help and guidance.\n4. It is Allah’s kindness to His servants that He does ask them to spend all of their wealth in Allah’s path.",
  48000:
      "The Victory (Surah Al-Fath)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nGiving the Prophet and the believers glad tidings of triumph and empowerment.\n•    Explanation:",
  48001:
      "I have given you, O Messenger, a clear victory by the Treaty of Hudaybiyah.",
  48002:
      "So that Allah may forgive you for your sins, those that occurred previous to this victory and those that will occur in the future and complete His favor on you by assisting your religion and guiding you to a straight path in which there is no crookedness, which is the straight path of Islam.",
  48003:
      "Allah will help you against your enemies with formidable support that no one can repel.",
  48004:
      "Allah is the One who sent down [the feeling of] stability and tranquility into the hearts of the believers so that they increase their belief. To Allah alone belongs the forces of the heavens and the earth; he supports with them whoever of His slaves He wishes. Allah knows what is in the best interests of His slaves, and He is Wise in the assistance and support He gives.",
  48005:
      "To enter those men and women who believe in Allah and His Messenger into gardens with streams flowing under their palaces and trees and wiping away their wrongdoings from them and not taking them to account for it. What has been mentioned about attaining the objective of Paradise and removing the fear of accountability in the sight of Allah is an unparalleled success.",
  48006:
      "And to punish the hypocrites, male and female, and to punish those men and women who ascribe partners to Allah, and those who think that Allah will not assist His religion and His word will not be raised and that fortune will turn against the believers. Punishment befell them, and Allah became angry with them because of their disbelief and evil thoughts, and He expelled them from His mercy and prepared for them in the Afterlife Hell, which they will enter to remain there forever. What a miserable place of return for them!",
  48007:
      "And to Allah belong the soldiers of the heavens and the earth, with which He supports whomever of His slaves He wills, and Allah is All-Mighty, and no one can overcome Him, Most-Wise in His creation, decrees, and administration of affairs.",
  48008:
      "O Messenger, We have sent you as a witness to give testimony against your nation on the day of resurrection and as one to give good news to the believers of the victory and empowerment Allah has prepared for them in this world and of the bliss He has prepared for them in the Hereafter, and to warn the disbelievers of the humiliation and defeat at the hands of the believers that He has prepared for them in this world, and the painful punishment awaiting them that He has prepared for them in the Hereafter.",
  48009:
      "In the hope that you will believe in Allah and His Messenger, revere and honor His messenger, and exalt Allah at the beginning and end of the day.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The treaty of Hudaibiyya was the beginning of a great victory for Islam and the Muslims.\n2. Serenity is one of the effects of faith that brings about tranquility and stability.\n3. The danger of having evil thoughts about Allah, because Allah treats people in accordance to what they think of Him, (may He be glorified).\n4. The obligation of honouring and revering the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).",
  48010:
      "Those of the people of Mecca who pledged allegiance to you, O Messenger, during the Pledge of Satisfaction to fight the Meccan polytheists are pledging allegiance to Allah. Allah is the One who ordered them to fight the polytheists, and He is the One who rewards them. The Hand of Allah is above their hands at the time of giving the pledge, and He is aware of them, and nothing is hidden from Him. So, he who breaches his pledge and fails to fulfill the promise he made to Allah in terms of supporting His religion shall bear the harm of breaking his pledge. Allah is not harmed by this, and whoever fulfills what he promised Allah in terms of supporting His religion, He will give him a great reward, which is Paradise.",
  48011:
      "Those desert Arabs whom Allah kept behind from accompanying you, O Messenger, on your journey to His House will say to you when you reproach them: Taking care of our wealth and looking after our children kept us busy from going out with you. So, ask for forgiveness from Allah on our behalf for our sins. They ask what is not in their hearts with their tongues by asking the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم to seek forgiveness for them; they have not repented their sins. Say to them: No one can do anything for you against Allah if He intends good or bad for you. Instead, Allah is well aware of what you do. Nothing of your actions is hidden from Him, no matter how much you try to conceal it.",
  48012:
      "The reason for your failure to join the Messenger in combat is not the excuse you gave him of being busy caring for your possessions and children. Rather, you thought that the Messenger and his companions would all perish and would not return to their families in Madīnah. The Devil beautified this in your hearts. Your thoughts led you to think wickedly about your Lord: that He would not help His Prophet. You became a doomed people because of your negative thoughts about Allah and because you fell behind from joining His Messenger [in battle].",
  48013:
      "The person who does not believe in Allah and His Messenger is a disbeliever. We have prepared on the Day of Resurrection for those who deny Allah a blazing fire by which they will be punished.",
  48014:
      "To Allah alone belongs the control of the heavens and the earth. He forgives the sins of those of His slaves whom He wills and enters them into Paradise through His Grace. He torments those of His slaves whom He wills out of His Justice. Allah forgives the sins of those of His slaves who repent to Him, and He is merciful towards them.",
  48015:
      "Those whom Allah kept behind, when you, O believers, set off to take the spoils of Khaybar which Allah had promised you after the Treaty of Hudaybiyah, will say: Let us go out with you to get some of it. These people who were left behind want to change, by their request, Allah's promise that He made to the believers after the Treaty of Hudaybiyah to give them alone the spoils of Khaybar. Say to them, O Messenger: You will never follow us to those spoils because Allah has promised us that the seizures of Khaybar are only for those present at Hudaybiyah. They will say: Your preventing us from following you to Khaybar is not an instruction from Allah, but because you are jealous of us. The matter is not as these people who were left behind claim. Instead, they do not understand Allah's instructions and prohibitions except a little, so they have fallen into going against Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The status of the pledge of allegiance of Al-Ridwan is great in Allah’s sight and the people of this pledge are the best people on the face of the earth.\n2. Presenting false excuses is the attribute of those who are weak in faith.\n3. Those who are weak in faith are few in number at the time of anxiety but many at the time of desiring something.",
  48016:
      "O Messenger, to test those Bedouins who failed to travel to Mecca with you, say to them: You will soon be called to fight against a strong, courageous group of people whom you shall either have to fight in the path of Allah, or they may enter into Islam without a fight. If you obey Allah in the fighting He is calling you to, He will give you a good reward, i.e., Paradise. If you turn away from His obedience, just like you turned away from traveling with the Messenger to Mecca, He will inflict a painful punishment on you.",
  48017:
      "There is no sin on a person excused due to blindness, disability, or illness if he fails to fight in the path of Allah. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger, He will enter him into gardens and trees and palaces of which rivers flow; whoever turns away from their obedience, Allah will inflict a painful punishment on him.",
  48018:
      "Verily, Allah was pleased with the believers when they gave you their oaths at al-Hudaybiyah under the tree. Allah knew of their faith, sincerity, and honesty, bringing tranquility to their hearts. And He rewarded them with a close victory, i.e., the victory over Khaybar, as consolation for them missing out on being able to enter Mecca.",
  48019:
      "And He also granted them many spoils of war they took from the people of Khaybar. Allah is the Almighty whom no one can overcome; the Wise in His creation, decree, and control.",
  48020:
      "O believers, Allah promises you much war booty in future Islamic victories. Still, He gave you the spoils of Khaybar in advance and stopped the hands of the Jews when they intended to capture your families after you. And He has done this so that these advanced spoils become a sign for you of the help of Allah and His support for you. And Allah guides you to a straight path in which there is no deviance.",
  48021:
      "And Allah promises you the spoils of war you have yet to be able to attain. Allah alone can let you acquire them; they are part of the plans and knowledge of Allah. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  48022:
      "O believers, if those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger were to fight you, they would turn their backs, defeated and fleeing. They would not find any guardian who would take care of their affair, nor any helper who would help them fight against you.",
  48023:
      "The believers being victorious and then defeating the disbelievers is established in every place and era; Allah's divine practice is prevalent in the nations that have passed before these rejectors. O Messenger! You will never find change in the way of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an informs of matters of the future which occurred afterwards, like the victories of Islam. It is a definitive proof that the noble Qur’an is a revelation from Allah.\n2. The rulings of the Shariah are based on gentleness and ease.\n3. The reward of those who took part in Bay4at Al-Ridwan is part advanced in this world, and part saved for them in Hereafter.\n4. The truth and people of the truth being ultimately victorious over falsehood and its people is a divine custom of Allah.",
  48024:
      "He is the One who prevented the polytheists from harming and getting to you when approximately 70 men came to Hudaybiyah, intending to cause you harm. He stopped you from them; you did not kill them or cause them any damage. Instead, you freed them after Allah enabled you to capture them. And Allah is watchful over your actions; none of your actions are hidden from Him.",
  48025:
      "They are the ones who disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and stopped you and the sacrificial animals from the Sacred Mosque. The animals remained barred from reaching the Haram, where they were to be sacrificed. Had it not been for a few believing men whom you did not know were believers, and by killing the disbelievers, you could have killed them also, and incurred sin and would have had to pay blood money unknowingly, Allah would have allowed you to liberate Mecca so that He may enter into His mercy whomever He wished, i.e., the believers in Mecca. If the disbelievers were distinguished from the believers in Mecca, Allah would have punished those who disbelieved in Him and His Messenger with a painful punishment.",
  48026:
      "Remember when those who disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger harbored in their hearts the pride of ignorance, an ignorance linked to desires and not the truth? They haughtily rejected the entrance of Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم into Mecca in the year of the treaty of al-Hudaybiyah, fearing and blaming him that he would overpower them and take control over it. Therefore, Allah sent down tranquility from Himself upon His Messenger and the believers so their anger did not lead to them confronting the polytheists with the same actions. Allah made the believers firm upon the statement of truth, i.e., there is none worthy of worship except for Allah, and kept them firm upon fulfilling their rights which they fulfilled. The believers were more worthy of this statement than others and more deserving of it because of the goodness within their hearts that Allah knew of. And Allah is aware of everything; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  48027:
      "Indeed, Allah made the dream of His Messenger a reality; He showed it to him in his sleep and informed his companions of it. The dream was that he and his companions were entering the sacred house of Allah in safety from their enemies, with some of them having shaved their heads and others having only trimmed their hair, indicating the completion of their acts of pilgrimage. O believers! Allah knows what is in your best interests more than you. So instead of making the dream a reality by letting you enter Mecca that year, He will grant you a victory very soon, i.e., the signing of the treaty of al-Hudaybiyah and the conquest of Khaybar that followed it at the hands of the believers who had witnessed al-Hudaybiyah.",
  48028:
      "Allah is the One who sent His Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم with a clear message and a true religion: the religion of Islam, so that He may make it prevail over all other opposing religions. Allah has testified to that, and He is sufficient as a witness.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Preventing from the path of Allah is a crime that deserves a painful torment.\n2. Allah’s management of the requirements of His servants is beyond their limited understanding.\n3. We have been warned against taking pride in our forefathers and gender on account of religion.\n4. The dreams of the prophet are true, and they are a type of revelation.\n5. It is not necessary that a true dream becomes a reality immediately.\n6. The prevailing of the religion of Islam is a divine promise and custom of Allah that will soon occur.",
  48029:
      "Muhammad is Allah's Messenger, and his companions are strict against the disbelievers that are at war with you and merciful, affectionate, and friendly among themselves. You will see them bowing and prostrating, seeking from Allah that He grace them with forgiveness, a generous reward, and that He becomes pleased with them. Their mark is on their faces due to prostrating in obedience to Allah. That is how the Torah has described them: the book revealed to Moses (peace be upon him). As for their mention in the Gospel, which was shown to Jesus, they are likened in their assisting one another and perfection like crops that have emerged as trim, then strengthened and stood straight up, pleasing the farmers with their strength and perfection. It is so that the disbelievers are angered by the power, steadfastness, and perfection they see within them. And Allah has promised those of the companions who believe in Him and do good deeds forgiveness for their sins; they will not be taken to account over their sins, and the great reward of Paradise.",
  49000:
      "The Rooms (Surah Al-Hujurat)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe rectification of one's speech and explaining its impact on an individual's faith and the ethics of society.\n•    Explanation:",
  49001:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow whatever He legislates, do not precede Allah or His Messenger in speech or action. Fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and refrain from that which He has prohibited. Indeed, Allah hears your statements and is aware of your actions. He does not miss any of them and will soon recompense you accordingly.",
  49002:
      "O you who believe in Allah and follow whatever He legislates, show good manners with His Messenger: do not raise your voices in his presence nor speak loudly to him out of respect for him, and do not call out his name as you do amongst each other. Rather, call him gently, saying, O Prophet, or O Messenger, it is feared that the reward of your deeds become nullified if you do so while you do not even realize it.",
  49003:
      "Indeed, those who lower their voices near Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم are the ones whose hearts Allah has examined for fear of Him and chosen them for it. For them is forgiveness for their sins; they will not be accounted for them, and they will receive a great reward on the Day of Judgment, which will be that Allah enters them into Paradise.",
  49004:
      "O Messenger, indeed, most of the Bedouins who call out to you from behind your wives' houses do not understand.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) enjoy a privilege over all people since Adam, except for the Prophets.\n2. Showing mercy to the believer and strictness to the combatant disbeliever has been legislated by Allah.\n3. Coherence and assisting one another are characteristics of the companions of the Messenger (peace be upon him).\n4. Disbelief is feared upon whoever finds dislike in his heart for the noble companions.\n5. It is obligatory to show good manners to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and to his sunnah and his inheritors (the scholars).",
  49005:
      "O Messenger, if these people who call out to you from behind your wives' houses were to have waited and not called out to you until you came out to them, then talked to you in lowered voices, it would have been better for them than calling out to you from behind the dwellings, because it would have been more dignified and respectful. And Allah Forgives the sins of those who repent and others. He forgives them for their ignorance and is merciful to them.",
  49006:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated, if a wrongdoer brings some news about a group of people to you, verify the truth and do not hasten towards accepting it, in fear that if you take it without verifying it, you could harm a group of people ignorantly. Then, after having hurt them, you will regret it when the false nature of the news becomes clear to you.",
  49007:
      "O believers, know that amongst you is Allah's Messenger upon whom revelation descends, so beware of lying if he receives revelation informing him of your lying. He is better aware of your needs; if he were to obey you in many of the things you suggest, you would surely fall into difficulty, which he would not want for you. However, through His grace, Allah has made belief beloved to you and beautified it in your hearts so you accept it while making you hate disbelief, disobedience, and sin. Those who possess these qualities are the ones who are treading the path of correctness and righteousness.",
  49008:
      "The beautification of goodness and hating of evil that you have achieved is only through the grace of Allah, which He bestowed upon you and favored you. And Allah is aware of those of His slaves who are grateful to Him, and so He gives them success. He is Wise in that He places each thing in its appropriate place.",
  49009:
      "O believers, if two groups of believers fight each other, then reconcile between them by calling them to let the law of Allah judge between them. Then, if one of the two rejects the reconciliation and transgresses, fight the transgressing group until it returns to accepting the command of Allah. If it returns, reconcile the two groups with fairness and justice. And be fair in your judgment between them. Indeed, Allah loves those who are honest in their judgment.",
  49010:
      "The believers are brothers in Islam, and brotherhood in Islam demands that you, O believers, reconcile between your quarreling brothers. And be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and refraining from that which He has prohibited, in the hope that you will be shown mercy.",
  49011:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated, a group of you should not mock another; perhaps those being mocked are better, according to Allah. Proper consideration is only for what Allah considers. And a group of women should not mock another group of women; perhaps the group being mocked is better, according to Allah. Do not taunt the souls of your brothers because they are like your own souls, and do not call others with names they do not like, as was the case of a few of the Anṣār before the arrival of Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم. Whoever does that is a wrongdoer, and that is an evil trait to be tainted with after having believed. Whoever does not repent from these sins wrongs themselves by placing themselves in situations of destruction due to their sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory to verify the truth of news, especially the news of a person suspected of deviance.\n2. It is obligatory to reconcile between two quarrelling groups of Muslims. Fighting the group that insists on transgression and rejects reconciliation is also legislated.\n3. From the rights of brotherhood in faith is reconciling between two quarrelling people. Another is distancing oneself from anything that hurts another’s feelings, i.e. mocking, taunting and calling names.",
  49012:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, avoid most suspicions not based on causes and indications that give them credence because some forms of suspicion are sinful, like suspecting one who is pious. And do not pursue the faults of believers behind their backs, nor mention another in a manner he dislikes, because mentioning him in a way he dislikes is like eating his dead flesh. Would any of you wish to eat the dead flesh of his dead brother? Therefore, hate backbiting him because it is the same thing. And fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and refraining from what He has prohibited. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving of those of His slaves who repent, Ever-Merciful to them.",
  49013:
      "O people, We have indeed created you from one male: your father, Adam, and one female: your mother, Eve. Therefore, your lineage is the same, so some of you should not be boastful of your lineage to others. Then, We made you into many nations and dispersed tribes so that you may recognize one another; not so that you take pride in them because distinction can only be due through having fear of Allah. Hence He said: the noblest from among you is the one who fears Him most. Indeed, Allah is Aware of your conditions, Knowing of what levels of perfection and deficiency you are on; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  49014:
      "When some Bedouins came to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, they said, we believe in Allah and His Messenger. O Messenger! Say to them: You have not yet believed; instead, say: we have submitted and obeyed. Faith has not yet entered your hearts; it is hoped that it does enter. O Bedouins! If you obey Allah and His Messenger in faith, in doing good deeds, and in refraining from the unlawful, Allah will not decrease the reward of your deeds in the slightest. Indeed, Allah forgives those of His slaves who repent and is merciful to them.",
  49015:
      "The believers are only those who believe in Allah and His Messenger and then do not mix their belief with doubts and strive in the way of Allah with their wealth and souls, not holding back on anything. Those are the ones truthful in their belief.",
  49016:
      "O Messenger, tell these Bedouins: Are you teaching Allah and informing Him about your religion, while Allah knows all that is in the heavens and on Earth? He knows everything, and nothing is hidden from him, so He does not need you to inform Him about your religion.",
  49017:
      "O Messenger, these Bedouins recount their favor upon you by mentioning their Islam. Say to them: Do not recount you're entering the religion of Allah as a favor upon me; its benefit, if gained, will return to you alone. Rather, Allah recounts His favor upon you that He granted you the ability to enter His religion if you are truthful in your claim that you have entered into it.",
  49018:
      "Indeed, Allah knows the unseen of the heavens and the earth; nothing is hidden from him. And Allah is watchful of your actions; none of them are hidden from Him, and He will soon recompense you for your good and bad deeds.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Thinking suspiciously of good people is a sin, while taking precautions from the people of evil and being suspicious of them is permissible.\n2. The humans coming from one origin demands that they do not take pride over one another in lineage.\n3. Faith is not just speech without the necessary beliefs; rather, it is belief with the heart, proclaiming with the tongue, and practicing upon the integrals.\n4. Guiding and granting ability is in the power of Allah alone.",
  50000:
      "The Letter Qaf (Surah Qaf)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAdmonishing hearts through the realities of death and resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  50001:
      "Qāf – This surah begins with disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceded in Surat Al-Baqarah. Allah swore by the noble Quran because of its meanings, abundant goodness, and blessings that you shall be resurrected on the Day of Judgment to be taken into account and recompensed accordingly.",
  50002:
      "The cause of their rejection was not that they expected you to lie because they knew your honesty. Instead, they are amazed that a messenger came to warn them from their own kind and not from the angels. They say, in amazement, a human messenger coming to us is bizarre!",
  50003:
      "Will we be resurrected after we have died and turned into dust? Resurrection and life returning to our bodies after decomposing is far-fetched; it is impossible.",
  50004:
      "Indeed, We know how much of their bodies the earth eats away after their death; it is not hidden from Us. We have a book that preserves everything We have decreed for them in their lives and after their deaths.",
  50005:
      "Rather, these polytheists rejected the Quran when His Messenger brought it to them. They are uncertain about it; they cannot stay firm on anything.",
  50006:
      "After mentioning the rejection of the Resurrection by polytheists, Allah reminds them of the evidence for its occurrence, stating: \n Do these people who reject the resurrection not ponder over the sky above them: how We created it, made it, and adorned it with the stars We placed in it, and it has no cracks to spoil it? Can the One who created this sky not resurrect the dead back to life?",
  50007:
      "And We spread the earth in a manner that made living on it suitable, placing within it firm mountains so that it does not shake. We also caused all the beautiful plants and trees to grow on it.",
  50008:
      "We created all that as a source of enlightenment and a reminder for every slave who turns to his Lord in obedience.",
  50009:
      "And We sent down rainwater from the sky, which contains abundant benefits and goodness. With that water, We then cause gardens and the crops you harvest - such as barley and other than it - to grow.",
  50010:
      "We also cause tall date palms to grow with closely arranged minute flowers, one above the other.",
  50011:
      "We cause all that to grow as provision for the slaves so that they can eat from it. We also revive through the rainwater barren lands with no growth. Just as We revive the barren earth with this rainwater, We will also restore the dead who will emerge alive.",
  50012:
      "O Messenger, before these people who have rejected you, many nations rejected their Prophets. The people of Noah, the people of the Well, and the Thamūd denied their Prophets.",
  50013:
      "The 'Ād, the people of Pharaoh, and the people of Lot all denied their Prophets.",
  50014:
      "The people of Shuayb: the people of the Thicket, also denied their Prophet. The punishment that Allah promised them was then established.",
  50015:
      "Were We incapable of creating you in the first instance that We are now incapable of resurrecting you? Rather, they are utterly confused about being created again after already being created.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The idolaters regard messengership for humans to be significant, yet they attribute the quality of lordship to a stone!\n2. The creation of the heavens, the earth, the sending of rain, causing barren lands to grow, and the initial creation are all evidence of the resurrection.\n3. Rejection of the Messengers was a tradition of the previous nations, and punishing the rejectors is a divine custom of Allah.",
  50016:
      "Verily, We created man and know the thoughts and desires that pass through his mind. We are closer to him than the vein in his neck connected to his heart.",
  50017:
      "When the two receiving angels receive his deeds: one sitting on his right, and the other seated on his left.",
  50018:
      "He does not utter anything except that an angel is present, observing whatever he says.",
  50019:
      "The pangs of death are a reality and will come; there is no escaping from them. O, negligent human! That is what you used to turn away from and put off and flee from.",
  50020:
      "The angel appointed to blow the trumpet will blow for the second time. That is the Day of Judgment, the day of the punishment the disbelievers and sinners have been warned of.",
  50021:
      "Each soul will come with an angel dragging it and another angel to testify to the deeds of that soul.",
  50022:
      "It will be said to this human that is being dragged; indeed, you neglected this day because your desires and pleasures deceived you. So, We have removed your heedlessness from you by the punishment and horror you see before you. Your eyesight is sharp today, so now you can see everything you were neglectful of!",
  50023:
      "His companion, the angel appointed to him, will say, these are his actions We have with me that We present, without any increase nor decrease.",
  50024:
      "Allah will say to the two angels: the one dragging him and the testifier, Throw into hell every stubborn rejector of the truth.",
  50025:
      "The one often avoiding the truth which Allah has made obligatory for him, a transgressor of the limits of Allah, doubter in whatever promise or warning he is given.",
  50026:
      "The one who attributes another deity with Allah and makes him a partner in worship. So throw him into a severe punishment.",
  50027:
      "His (Devil) companion will say, seeking to distance himself from him, O our Lord! I did not make him transgress, he had already gone far astray himself.",
  50028:
      "Allah will say: Do not argue in front of Me; there is no benefit in that because I gave the message to you in the world beforehand with severe warnings that My messengers brought to you warning those who disbelieved in Me and disobeyed Me.",
  50029:
      "My word cannot be changed, and I do not turn back on My promise. I do not oppress My slaves by decreasing their good deeds or increasing their evil deeds. Instead, I recompense them for whatever they have done.",
  50030:
      "On the Day, We will say to Hell: Are you full of all the disbelievers and sinners that have been thrown into you? It will reply to its Lord, saying: Are there any more? It will want more, angry for the sake of its Lord.",
  50031:
      "After mentioning the severe threat to the disbelievers, Allah mentions what He has prepared for His believing slaves, stating: \n And Paradise will be brought close for those fearing their Lord by fulfilling His commands and refraining from things he did not allow. They will see all the blessings within it without it being far from them.",
  50032:
      "It will be said to them: This is what Allah promised every one of you who frequently repents to his Lord and upholds whatever his Lord made obligatory for him.",
  50033:
      "Whoever fears Allah in private, where none can see him except Allah, meets Allah with a pure heart while frequently turning to Him in [in repentance, etc.].",
  50034:
      "It will be said to them: Enter Paradise in total safety from everything you dislike. It is a day of eternity, one which is everlasting.",
  50035:
      "They will have whatever they wish therein, and it will run out, and with Us, there are even more blessings for them that no eye has ever seen, or any ear has ever heard of, or any heart of man has ever imagined. One of them is seeing Allah. May He be glorified.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah knows of the good and bad thoughts that cross the hearts.\n2. Some of the traits of the people of disbelief are: preventing goodness and doubting.\n3. Allah is the Just.",
  50036:
      "How many a nation have We destroyed prior to these denying polytheists amongst the people of Mecca?! They searched in the lands hoping to find a place to run to, but they did not find it.",
  50037:
      "That destruction of the previous nations mentioned is a reminder and lesson for the one who has the heart to understand, listens attentively with the presence of mind, and is not absentminded.",
  50038:
      "And We created the heavens, and the earth and whatever is between the sky and the world in six days, despite Our power to make them in one moment, and We were not affected by fatigue as the Jews say.",
  50039:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with what the Jews and others say, and pray the Fajr prayer to your Lord, praising Him before sunrise, and pray 'Asr before sunset.",
  50040: "Pray to Him at night, and exalt Him after the prayers.",
  50041:
      "O Messenger, listen on the day the angel appointed to blow the trumpet a second time calls from a close place.",
  50042:
      "On that Day, the creation will hear the loud sound of the resurrection, in truth, without any doubt. That day that they will hear the sound will be when the dead come out of their graves to be taken into account and recompensed.",
  50043:
      "We alone give life and death. There is nobody to give life and death besides Us. And to Us alone is the return of the slaves on the Day of Judgment.",
  50044:
      "On the Day the earth breaks away from them, they will come out quickly. That is an easy gathering for Us.",
  50045:
      "We know best what these deniers say. And you do not have authority over them, O Messenger, to force them to accept faith. You are only a conveyer of what Allah has ordered you to convey, so remind them with the Quran, the one who fears my warning to the disbelievers and the sinful because the fearful is the one who takes advice and listens to the reminders when given.",
  51000:
      "The Winnowing Winds (Surah Adh-Dhariyat)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the jinn and humans by acknowledging that their sustenance is solely from Allah so that they devote their worship exclusively to Him.\n•    Explanation:",
  51001: "Allah swears by the wind, which scatters dust.",
  51002: "And by the clouds that carry plenty of water.",
  51003: "And the ships which sail in the sea with ease.",
  51004:
      "And by the angels which distribute the issues concerning the slaves which Allah has ordered them to distribute.",
  51005:
      "The reckoning and recompense which Allah promises you are valid without a doubt.",
  51006:
      "And the reckoning of the slaves will occur on the Day of Judgment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Taking heed from historical incidents is the way of those who have understanding hearts.\n2. Allah’s creating the universe in six days is due to wisdom which Allah knows, perhaps one of them being to explain the practice of doing things gradually.\n3. The disrespect of the Jews in describing Allah with tiredness after He created the heavens and the earth. This is disbelief in Allah.",
  51007: "And Allah swears by the sky, which is beautiful and stretched out.",
  51008:
      "O, people of Mecca, you are saying contradictory and conflicting things. Sometimes you say: The Quran is magic; then you say it's poetry. And you say that Muhammad is a magician at times, and at other times you say he is a poet.",
  51009:
      "He is diverted away from believing in the Quran and the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم and away from Allah's knowledge due to His knowing that he will not believe, so he will not be guided.",
  51010:
      "Cursed are these liars who said regarding the Quran and their Prophet whatever it is that they said.",
  51011:
      "Those who are ignorant and heedless about the place in the hereafter and care for it not.",
  51012: "They ask when the Day of Recompense is, but they do not work for it.",
  51013:
      "So, Allah answers their question by saying the day they will be tormented in the Fire.",
  51014:
      "It will be said to them: Taste your punishment. This is [the punishment] you were warned about, and to make a mockery of it, you asked for it to befall you quicker.",
  51015:
      "Those fearing their Lord by carrying out His commands and refraining from His prohibitions will be in gardens and running springs on the Day of Judgment.",
  51016:
      "They are experiencing the generous reward their Lord has given them because, previous to that, they used to do good in the life of this world.",
  51017: "They used to pray at night, only sleeping a little.",
  51018: "And in the morning, they seek forgiveness from Allah for their sins.",
  51019:
      "And in their wealth is a right for the beggar amongst people, the one who does not ask out of shyness, and those who are deprived of sustenance for whatever reason.",
  51020:
      "And the earth and the mountains, seas, rivers, trees, plants, and animals Allah has placed in them are proof of Allah's power for those convinced that Allah is their Creator and the One who fashioned them.",
  51021:
      "And in yourselves, O people, is proof of Allah's power; do you not see to take heed?",
  51022:
      "And in the heavens is your worldly and religious provision; in this world is what you have been promised, good and bad.",
  51023:
      "By the Lord of the heavens and earth, the resurrection is true without any doubt, just as there is no doubt in your speech when you speak [to each other].",
  51024:
      "O Messenger, has the story of the guests of Abraham (peace be upon him) - the angels whom he honored - come to you?",
  51025:
      "When they came to him and said: Peace. Abraham replied: Peace and said: These are people we do not recognize.",
  51026:
      "Then he discreetly went to his family and brought a whole plump calf from them [to eat], thinking they were normal human beings.",
  51027:
      "He moved the calf closer to them, saying softly: Will you not eat this food placed before you?",
  51028:
      "When they did not eat, he concealed his fear of them, but they understood this and said to him, to put him at ease: Do not be frightened. We are messengers from Allah. And they informed him of what will please him, i.e., that he will have a son with much knowledge. The one regarding whom glad tidings were given was Isaac (peace be upon him).",
  51029:
      "When his wife heard the glad tiding, she came screaming out of happiness, slapped her face, and said in surprise: Will an old woman give birth when she is barren?",
  51030:
      "The angels told her: What we have informed you of is what your Lord has said. And there is nobody to refute what He said. He is Wise in His creation and decree. He is Omniscient of His creation and what is in their best interests.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Doing good actions and making them sincerely for Allah is a means of entry into Paradise.\n2. Part of the etiquette of hosting guests is to reply to greetings in a better manner, presenting the spread of food discreetly, preparing for the guests before they arrive, not excluding anything from the spread of food, taking care to present it and do so quickly, putting it close to the guest and speaking to them softly.",
  51031:
      "Abraham (peace be upon him) asked the angels: What is your purpose? And what do you intend?",
  51032:
      "The angels replied: Allah has sent us to a nation of criminals who commit despicable sins.",
  51033: "So that We can send stones of hard clay upon them.",
  51034:
      "Marked in the presence of your Lord, O Abraham, and sent upon those who transgress the limits of Allah and who go to the extreme in disbelief and commit acts of disobedience.",
  51035:
      "So We took out whoever was in the city from the believers among Lot's people so that the punishment which will befall the criminals will not befall them.",
  51036:
      "But We only found one house of Muslims in their city, which was the household of Lot (peace be upon him).",
  51037:
      "And We left in the city of Lot signs of the torment which will show that the torment befell them so that those who fear the painful torment, which afflicted them, take lessons from it and then not do what they did.",
  51038:
      "[There is a sign] in [the story of] Moses when We sent him to Pharaoh with clear proofs as a sign for those who fear the painful torment.",
  51039:
      "But Pharaoh turned away from the truth, considering his power and army. He said regarding Moses (peace be upon him): He is a magician who does magic on people or an insane person who says what he does not understand.",
  51040:
      "So We seized him and all his armies and threw them in the sea, so they were drowned and destroyed. Then, Pharaoh will be held accountable for his blameworthy actions: the rejection of the message and his claim of divinity.",
  51041:
      "And in [the story of] 'Ād, the people of Hūd, is a sign for those who fear the painful torment when We sent upon them the wind which did not carry rain or pollinate trees, nor were there any blessings in it.",
  51042:
      "It did not spare any soul, property, or anything else it came upon, except that it destroyed it and left it like scattered ruins.",
  51043:
      "And in [the story of] Thamūd, the people of Saleh (peace be upon him), is a sign for those who fear the painful torment when it was said to them: Enjoy yourselves before your term of life ends.",
  51044:
      "But they were arrogant towards their Lord's command and haughty towards belief in Him and His obedience, so the thunderbolt of torment seized them while they were waiting for it to descend, as they were promised the torment three days before it came.",
  51045:
      "So they could not repel the torment that befell them, nor did they have any power to defend themselves.",
  51046:
      "And We destroyed the people of Noah by drowning them before these people who have been mentioned. They were people who abandoned Allah's obedience, so they deserved His punishment.",
  51047:
      "And We constructed the sky and perfected its construction with strength, and We are expanding its edges.",
  51048:
      "And We made the Earth like a spread for those who live on it. So how excellent are We who prepared it for them!",
  51049:
      "And We created all things in pairs, like the male and female, sky and Earth, and the land and sea, so that you remember the Oneness of Allah who created everything in pairs, and you remember His power.",
  51050:
      "So, flee from Allah's punishment towards His reward by obeying Him and not disobeying Him. I am a clear warner to you, O people, of His punishment.",
  51051:
      "And do not set up alongside Allah another deity to worship instead of Him. I am a clear warner to you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Deep, unwaivering faith is of a greater rank than merely submitting outwardly to Allah.\n2. Allah’s destroying the nations that denied is a lesson for all people.\n3. Fear of Allah necessitates running towards Him through good actions, not running away from him.",
  51052:
      "As the people of Mecca rejected, the previous nations rejected. No Messenger from Allah came to them except that they said: He is a magician or insane.",
  51053:
      "Did the predecessors among the disbelievers and those who came after advise one another to reject the messengers? No, instead, their transgression has united them on this.",
  51054:
      "So turn away from these rejectors, O Messenger, for you are not blameworthy, as you have conveyed to them what you were sent with to them.",
  51055:
      "And do not let their turning away from you prevent you from advising and reminding them. Advise and remind them, as reminding benefits those who believe in Allah.",
  51056:
      "And I did not create jinn and humans except for My worship alone. I did not create them to associate partners with Me.",
  51057: "I do not want any provision from them or want them to feed Me.",
  51058:
      "Allah is the Provider for His slaves; they all need His provision. He is the Possessor of power, the Ever Mighty; nothing can overpower Him. All the jinn and humans submit to His power; may He be Exalted.",
  51059:
      "Those who have wronged themselves by rejecting you, O Messenger, have a share of the torment, like the share of their companions before them, which has a fixed period. So they should not ask Me to hasten it before its time.",
  51060:
      "So destruction and loss are for those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His messengers on the Day of Resurrection, the day in which they are promised that the punishment will be sent upon them.",
  52000:
      "Mount Tur (Surah At-Tur)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nArguments and evidences to refute the doubts of the deniers against the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم.\n•    Explanation:",
  52001:
      "Allah swore by the mountain on which He spoke to Moses (peace be upon him).",
  52002: "And he swore by the written Book [Quran].",
  52003:
      "[Written] on a spread open parchment like the [previously] revealed books.",
  52004:
      "And He swore by the House, which the angels in the heavens inhabit with the [constant] worship of Allah.",
  52005:
      "And He swore by the raised sky, which serves as the canopy of the Earth.",
  52006: "And He swore by the sea filled with water.",
  52007:
      "O Messenger, the torment of your Lord against the disbelievers will come to pass.",
  52008: "Nobody can avert it from them and save them from it befalling them.",
  52009:
      "On the Day in which the sky will move and shake violently, fully announcing the onset of the Day of Resurrection.",
  52010: "And the mountains will move away from their places.",
  52011:
      "So destruction and loss on that Day will be for those who reject Allah's torment, which He promised the disbelievers.",
  52012:
      "Those who playfully indulge in their vain discourse do not care about resurrection or being brought back to life.",
  52013:
      "On the Day they will be pushed with force and harshness towards the Fire.",
  52014:
      "And it will be said to them rebukingly: This is the Fire that you used to reject when your messengers used to warn you of it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. All types of disbelief still remain disbelief, even though it may vary from place to place, time to time and from people to people.\n2. Allah’s testifying to the Prophet’s (peace be upon him) conveying the message.\n3. The wisdom behind creating jinns and mankind is to establish the worship of all in all its manifestations.\n4. The conditions of the universe will soon change on the day of judgment.",
  52015: "Is this torment which you see magic, or are you not seeing it?",
  52016:
      "Taste the heat of this Fire and endure it. Be patient in enduring its heat or do not; your patience or impatience is all the same. You will only be recompensed Today for the disbelief and acts of disobedience you used to commit in the worldly life.",
  52017:
      "After mentioning the recompense of those who reject faith, Allah mentions the recompense of the heedful believers, stating: \n Those who fear their Lord by fulfilling His commands and abstaining from His prohibitions will be in gardens and great bliss, which will never end.",
  52018:
      "They will be enjoying the pleasures of food, drink, and marriage that Allah will have given them. And their Lord (may He be Exalted) will have protected them from the torment of the Inferno. Hence, they succeeded by achieving their desired pleasures and being saved from trouble.",
  52019:
      "It will be said to them: Eat and drink what you desire, in satisfaction without fearing harm or pain from what you eat and drink, as a recompense for your excellent deeds in the worldly life.",
  52020:
      "Reclining on adorned couches lined up, We will marry them to fair-skinned women with beautiful wide eyes.",
  52021:
      "Those who believed and whose children followed them in belief, We will elevate their children to them, so they are delighted, even though they [children] did not reach their level of deeds. And We will not decrease anything from the reward of their deeds. Every person will be held for the bad deeds he earned; nobody else will bear any of his deeds.",
  52022:
      "And We will provide these people of Paradise with different fruits and all the meat they desire.",
  52023:
      "They will give cups of wine to one another, bearing no resemblance to the wine of this world, free from false speech and sin which arises from intoxication.",
  52024:
      "And youthful slaves, who are like protected pearls due to their clear and fair skin, will serve them.",
  52025:
      "The people of Paradise will turn to one another, asking each other about their conditions in the worldly life.",
  52026:
      "They will respond to them: In the worldly life, we used to be among our families, fearful of Allah's torment.",
  52027:
      "So Allah favored us by guiding us to Islam and protected us from the scorching hot torment.",
  52028:
      "We used to worship Him in the worldly life and supplicate to Him to protect us from the torment of the Fire. He is Kind and Truthful in His promise to His slaves and Merciful to them. Part of His kindness and mercy upon us is that He guided us to believe in Him, admitted us into Paradise, and distanced us from the Fire.",
  52029:
      "So remind with the Quran, O Messenger, for you are not, with the belief and intellect that Allah has favored you, a soothsayer with a jinn, nor are you insane.",
  52030:
      "Do these polytheists say that Muhammad is not a messenger but a poet for whom we await death to seize so we can be relieved of him?",
  52031:
      "O Messenger, say to them: Await my death, and I will await the torment which will befall you due to rejecting me.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Gathering parents and children in Paradise on one level, even though the actions of some of them were deficient, to honour them all so that the happiness is complete.\n2. Nothing disliked occurs due to drinking the wine of the afterlife.\n3. Whoever fears his Lord in his worldly life, He will protect him in the Hereafter.",
  52032:
      "Or do their intellects tell them to say that He is a soothsayer and insane? Thus, they combine what cannot be gathered in one person. Rather, they are a people who transgress the bounds; hence, they do not refer to any sacred law or intellect.",
  52033:
      "Or do they say that Muhammad fabricated this Quran, and nothing has been revealed to him? He has not fabricated it; instead, they are too arrogant to believe in it, so they say He has fabricated it.",
  52034:
      "So let them produce a discourse like it, even if it be fabricated, if they are truthful in their claim that he has fabricated it.",
  52035:
      "Or have they been created without a creator to create them? Or did they create themselves? The existence of a creation without a creator or a creation that creates itself is impossible, so why do they not worship their Creator?",
  52036:
      "Or did they create the heavens and the Earth? Still, they are uncertain that Allah is their Creator; if they had been certain of that, they would have declared His Oneness and believed in His Messenger.",
  52037:
      "Or do they possess the treasures of your Lord's provision, giving it to whom they wish, or do they own prophethood to grant or withhold it from whom they want? Or are they the controllers and disposers according to their wishes?",
  52038:
      "Or do they have a ladder to climb to the sky in which they listen to Allah's revelation, which He sends to tell them they are on the truth? So let the one who listens among them to that revelation bring clear proof to affirm you in your claim that you are on the truth.",
  52039:
      "Or does He, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, have daughters which you dislike for yourselves, while you have sons which you prefer?",
  52040:
      "Or do you, O Messenger, seek reward from them for what you convey to them from their Lord, due to which they are burdened with something they cannot bear?",
  52041:
      "Or do they know the unseen so that they write for people what they learn from the unseen and inform them of what they want from there?",
  52042:
      "Or do these rejectors intend to plot against you and your religion? Trust in Allah, as those who disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger are the ones who will be plotted against, not you.",
  52043:
      "Or do they have a deity worthy of worship instead of Allah? Free and sanctified is Allah from the partner they attribute to him. None of what was mentioned has happened, and it is all unthinkable.",
  52044:
      "And if they were to see a piece of the sky falling, they would say: This is an ordinary pile of clouds. So they do not take heed or believe.",
  52045:
      "So leave them, O Messenger, in their stubbornness and denial until they meet their Day in which they will be punished, the Day of Resurrection.",
  52046:
      "The Day when their plot will avail them neither a little or a lot, nor will they be helped by being saved from the torment.",
  52047:
      "And for those who wronged themselves through polytheism and committing acts of disobedience, there is a torment before the torment of the Hereafter: in this life through being killed and imprisoned, and in the barzakh (transitory stage) through the torment of the grave. However, most of them do not know that, so they remain in disbelief.",
  52048:
      "After mentioning the falsehood that the polytheists are upon, Allah commands His Messenger not to be bothered by them and to be patient in the face of their rejection, stating: \n Be patient, O Messenger, with the decree of your Lord and His divine law, as you are in Our sight and protection. And exalt your Lord with praise when you arise from your sleep.",
  52049:
      "And at night, exalt your Lord and pray to Him, and pray the Fajr (dawn) prayer after the stars have disappeared due to the daylight.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Tyranny is a cause of misguidance.\n2. The miraculous nature of the Qur’an is clear from multiple facets.\n3. Punishment the Transitory Stage is real.",
  53000:
      "The Star (Surah An-Najm)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nEstablishing the authenticity of revelation and that it originates from Allah.\n•    Explanation:",
  53001: "He (may He be Exalted) swore by the star when it fades away.",
  53002:
      "Muhammad, Allah's Messenger, did not deviate from the path of guidance, nor did he go astray. Rather, he is rightly guided.",
  53003: "Nor does he utter this Quran according to his whims.",
  53004:
      "This Quran is only a revelation that Allah revealed to him through Gabriel; peace be upon him.",
  53005: "An angel of great strength, Gabriel, taught him it.",
  53006:
      "And Gabriel (peace be upon him) is of excellent form, so he rose, appearing to the Prophet in his true form, in which Allah created him.",
  53007: "While Gabriel was on the highest part of the horizon.",
  53008:
      "Then Gabriel (peace be upon him) came close to the Prophet. Then, he came even closer.",
  53009:
      "So his closeness to him was the distance of two bow lengths, or even closer.",
  53010:
      "So Gabriel (peace be upon him) revealed to Allah's slave, Muhammad, that which He revealed.",
  53011: "Muhammad's heart did not reject what his eyes saw.",
  53012:
      "So how can you, O polytheists, argue with him about what Allah showed him when he was taken on the night journey?",
  53013:
      "And Muhammad had seen Gabriel in his true form another time on the night he was taken on the journey.",
  53014:
      "At the Lote Tree of the utmost boundary, which is a huge tree in the seventh heaven.",
  53015: "Near this tree is the Garden of Refuge [Paradise].",
  53016:
      "When the Lote Tree was covered by the command of Allah by something great whose true nature only Allah knows.",
  53017:
      "Muhammad's sight did not swerve left or right or go beyond its limit.",
  53018:
      "Muhammad saw the greatest signs of his Lord, which show His power, on the night he ascended to the heavens. He saw Paradise, the Fire, and other things.",
  53019:
      "Have you, O polytheists, considered these idols you worship instead of Allah: Lat and Uzza,",
  53020:
      "And Manat, the third one among your idols? Tell me, do they possess any benefit or harm for you?",
  53021:
      "O polytheists, do you have males whom you prefer, while He (may He be Exalted) has females whom you dislike?",
  53022: "This distribution which you made with your desires is unjust.",
  53023:
      "These idols are mere names without meaning, so they have no share of divine qualities. You and your fathers named them on your own. Allah did not reveal any proof for them. The polytheists do not follow in their beliefs except assumptions and what they desire from what the Devil has made attractive in their hearts. And their Lord's guidance has come to them on the tongue of Muhammad, but they were not guided.",
  53024:
      "Or should man have whatever he desires, such as idols interceding with Allah?",
  53025:
      "No, he will not have what he desires. To Allah alone belongs the Hereafter and the first [life]; He grants from them whatever He wishes and withholds whatever He wishes.",
  53026:
      "How many angels are in the heavens whose intercession cannot help if they intend to help someone, except after Allah permits intercession for whom He wishes among them and He is pleased with the one for whom the intercession is made? Allah will never allow one considered a partner [in worship] to intercede, and He will never be pleased with the one for whom the intercession is made if he worships this partner instead of Allah.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an’s praising the Noble Prophet’s status.\n2. The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw Gabriel in his real form.\n3. Intercession does not occur except through two condition: permission for the intercessor and being pleased with the one being interceded for.",
  53027:
      "Those who do not believe in the resurrection in the Hereafter give the angels female names because they believe they are Allah's daughters. Allah is Transcendent and far beyond what they say.",
  53028:
      "They have no knowledge to rely on in giving them female names; they merely follow fabrications and delusion. Assumption is not a substitute for the truth and thus cannot take its place.",
  53029:
      "So turn away, O Messenger, from whoever turns their back on Allah's remembrance without showing any concern for it, only desiring the life of this world, and therefore do not work for their Hereafter because they do not believe in it.",
  53030:
      "What these polytheists say about giving the angels female names is the extent of their knowledge because they are ignorant. They have not reached certainty. Your Lord, O Messenger, knows best who has deviated from the path of truth, and He knows best who is guided to its path. Nothing of that is hidden from Him.",
  53031:
      "To Allah alone belongs whatever is in the heavens and on Earth. He created, owns, and plans all of it so that He may recompense those who do evil actions in the worldly life with the torment they deserve and recompense the believers who do righteous deeds with Paradise.",
  53032:
      "Those who avoid major sins and acts of disobedience but fall into minor sins will have their minor sins forgiven if they avoid the major ones and increase in acts of obedience. Your Lord, O Messenger, is of vast forgiveness. He forgives the sins of His slaves when they repent from them. He (may He be Exalted) knew best about their states and affairs when He created their father, Adam, from dust and when you were in the wombs of your mothers, being created in one form after another. None of that is hidden from Him. So do not praise yourselves through commendation and asserting piety. He (may He be Exalted) knows best about those who fear Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.",
  53033:
      "Have you seen the evil state of the one who turned away from Islam after coming close to it?",
  53034:
      "He gave a little wealth and then stopped because miserliness was his innate quality. Despite this, he asserts himself to be pious.",
  53035:
      "Does he know the unseen so that he sees and speaks about it? No! He is, instead, fabricating lies against Allah.",
  53036:
      "Or has this person, who fabricated lies against Allah, not been informed of what is in the earlier scriptures that Allah had revealed to Moses?",
  53037:
      "And the scriptures of Abraham who fulfilled and completed everything His Lord tasked him with?",
  53038: "That no person will bear the sin of another.",
  53039: "And each person will only receive the reward for the deeds he did.",
  53040: "And that his deeds will be openly seen on the Day of Resurrection.",
  53041:
      "Then he will be given the recompense of his deeds in full without reduction.",
  53042:
      "And that to your Lord, O Messenger, will be the return and destination of His slaves after they die.",
  53043:
      "And that He makes whoever He wills happy and makes him laugh, and whoever He wills sad and makes him cry.",
  53044:
      "And He causes the living to die in this world and brings the dead to life by resurrecting them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Classification of sins as major and minor sins.\n2. Prohibition of claiming purity of self.",
  53045: "And He created the pairs: Male and female",
  53046: "From a sperm-drop when it is placed in the womb.",
  53047:
      "And that He will undertake to recreate them for the resurrection after they die.",
  53048:
      "And He enriches whoever of His slaves He wills by making him the owner of wealth, and He gives wealth that people take as possessions that they acquire.",
  53049:
      "And He is the Lord of Sirius, the star worshipped by some polytheists alongside Allah.",
  53050:
      "And He destroyed the first [people of ] 'Ād, who were the people of Hūd when they persisted in their disbelief.",
  53051: "And He destroyed Thamūd, the people of Saleh, sparing none.",
  53052:
      "He destroyed the people of Noah before 'Ād and Thamūd. The people of Noah were more unjust and greater in transgression than 'Ād and Thamūd, because Noah lived among them for nine hundred and fifty years, inviting them to Allah's Oneness, but they did not respond to him.",
  53053:
      "And He raised the towns of the people of Lot to the sky, then turned them over and dropped them to the ground.",
  53054:
      "He then struck and covered them with stones after they had been raised to the sky and dropped to the ground.",
  53055:
      "So which of your Lord's signs demonstrating His power do you dispute with, O humanity, and not take a lesson from?",
  53056: "This messenger sent to you is like the previous messengers.",
  53057: "The Day of Resurrection has drawn near.",
  53058: "No one can push it back, and no one can disclose it besides Allah.",
  53059: "Do you marvel that this Quran recited to you is from Allah?",
  53060:
      "And you laugh mockingly at it and do not cry when hearing its admonitions?",
  53061: "While you are neglectful of it, not giving it any attention?",
  53062: "So prostrate to Allah alone and worship Him alone.",
  54000:
      "The Moon (Surah Al-Qamar)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding about the blessing of making the Quran easy and its verses and admonitions.\n•    Explanation:",
  54001:
      "The coming of the Hour has drawn near, and the moon was split [in two] in the time of the Prophet, the splitting of which was one of the tangible signs of the Prophet.",
  54002:
      "When the polytheists see any sign or proof of the Prophet's truthfulness, they turn away from accepting it and say: The evidence and proof we have seen are false magic.",
  54003:
      "They rejected the truth that came to them and followed their desires in this rejection. Whether good or bad, every matter will be settled for the one who deserves it on the Day of Resurrection.",
  54004:
      "There have come to them the stories of the nations that Allah destroyed because of their disbelief and wrongdoing that were sufficient to deter them from falling into the same.",
  54005:
      "What has come to them is profound wisdom to establish the evidence against them. The warnings do not benefit people who do not believe in Allah and the Last Day.",
  54006:
      "Since they do not follow the right path, leave them, O Messenger, and turn away from them, waiting for the Day when the angel appointed to blow the trumpet will call towards a horrific matter, the like of which was not known by creation previously.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Not being affected by the Qur’an is a sign of misfortune.\n2. The danger of following desires for the soul in the world and the Hereafter.\n3. Not taking a lesson from the destruction of the nations is an attribute of the disbelievers.",
  54007:
      "Their sight will be downcast. They will come out of their graves as if, in their rush towards the place of reckoning, they are swarming locusts.",
  54008:
      "[They will be] rushing to the caller to that place. The disbelievers will say: This is a hard Day because of the severity and horrors therein.",
  54009:
      "After mentioning the disbelievers turning away from the call of our Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم, Allah consoles him by informing him that the previous nations also rejected their messengers. He states: \n Before these people rejected your invitation, O Messenger, the people of Noah also rejected. They rejected Our slave, Noah (peace be upon him), when We sent him to them. They said that He was insane, and they rebuked him with various forms of swearing, abuse, and threats if he did not stop inviting them.",
  54010:
      "So Noah supplicated to His Lord: My people have overwhelmed me, and they did not respond to me. So help me over them with a torment that you send down on them.",
  54011: "So We opened the gates of the sky with continuous pouring water.",
  54012:
      "We caused the Earth to burst open, becoming springs from which water gushed. The water coming down from the sky met with the water gushing from the ground for a matter that Allah had determined in eternity. Everyone was drowned besides those whom Allah saved.",
  54013:
      "We carried Noah on a ship [made] of planks and nails, saving him and those with him from drowning.",
  54014:
      "This ship was sailing on the colliding waves of water under Our gaze and protection as a victory for Noah, whose people rejected him and disbelieved in what he brought from Allah.",
  54015:
      "We have left this torment that We meted out to them as a lesson and admonition. Is there anyone to take a lesson from that?",
  54016:
      "Then how was my torment to those who rejected me? And how was my warning that I will destroy them?",
  54017:
      "We have made the Quran easy to remember and take lessons from, so is there anyone to heed the lessons and admonishments that it contains?",
  54018:
      "Ād rejected their Prophet, Hūd (peace be upon him). So reflect, O people of Mecca, how [dreadful] was my torment to them? And how was my warning to others about their torment?",
  54019:
      "We sent on them a severe, cold, and screaming wind on a day of evil and misfortune that will continue with them until they reach Hell.",
  54020:
      "It snatched people up from the ground and threw them on their heads like the trunks of date palms uprooted from their plantations.",
  54021:
      "So reflect, O people of Mecca, how [dreadful] was my torment to them? And how was my warning to others about their torment?",
  54022:
      "We have made the Quran easy to remember and take lessons from, so is there anyone to heed the lessons and admonishments that it contains?",
  54023:
      "Thamūd rejected what their messenger, Saleh (peace be upon him) warned them about.",
  54024:
      "They condemningly said: Should we follow a single human being from among us? If we follow him in this state, we will be far from what is correct, misguided, and in difficulty.",
  54025:
      "Has revelation been revealed to him while he is just one person, and has he been chosen for it instead of all of us? No, he is a boastful liar.",
  54026:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, they will soon come to know who the boastful liar is, Saleh or them?",
  54027:
      "We will extract a she-camel from the rock and send it as a test to them. So wait, O Saleh, and watch what they do to it and what is done to them, and be patient with their harm.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is acceptable in the sacred law to make a prayer against a disbeliever who persists in disbelief.\n2. The deniers’ being destroyed and the believers’ being saved is a divine custom.\n3. The memorization of the Qur’an has been made easy.",
  54028:
      "And tell them that the water from their well must be divided between them and the she-camel: one day for it and one day for them. Each turn will be attended by its owner alone on the day allocated to him.",
  54029:
      "So they called their companion to kill the she-camel, and he took a sword and killed it, fulfilling the instruction of his people.",
  54030:
      "So reflect, O people of Mecca, how [dreadful] was my torment to them? And how was my warning to others about their torment?",
  54031:
      "We sent against them a single scream, which destroyed them, and they became like twigs used by a person who makes a fence for his sheep.",
  54032:
      "We have made the Quran easy to remember and take lessons from, so is there anyone to heed the lessons and admonishments that it contains?",
  54033:
      "The people of Lot rejected what their messenger, Lot (peace be upon him), warned them about.",
  54034:
      "We sent against them a wind that threw stones on them except the family of Lot (peace be upon him). The torment did not afflict them, as We had rescued them from it as Lot had traveled away with them before the torment came down in the last part of the night.",
  54035:
      "We rescued them from the torment as a favor from Us upon them. Like this recompense with which We recompensed Lot, We will recompense those who show gratitude to Allah for His favors.",
  54036:
      "Lot warned them of Our torment, but they disputed with one another about his warning, and they rejected it.",
  54037:
      "Lot's people tried to tempt him to give them access to the angels who were his guests, intending to do an indecent act. We obliterated their eyes so they could not see them, and We said to them: Taste my torment and the result of My warning to you.",
  54038:
      "In the morning, a torment came to them, which will stay with them until they reach the Hereafter. Then, the torment of the Hereafter will come to them.",
  54039:
      "They will be told: Taste My punishment that I have sent down upon you and the result of Lot's warning.",
  54040:
      "We have made the Quran easy to remember and take lessons from, so is there anyone to heed the lessons and admonishments that it contains?",
  54041:
      "Our warning also came to the people of Pharaoh on the tongue of Moses and Aaron (peace be upon them).",
  54042:
      "They rejected the proofs and evidence that came to them from Us, so We punished them for their rejection thereof with the punishment of the Mighty, whom none can overpower, the Most Powerful, who is not incapable of anything.",
  54043:
      "Are your disbelievers, O people of Mecca, better than those disbelievers mentioned: The people of Noah, 'Ād, Thamūd, the people of Lot, and Pharaoh and his people? Or do you have immunity from Allah's torment that the heavenly books have brought?",
  54044:
      "Or do these disbelievers from the people of Mecca say: We are all united and victorious against those who intend evil against us and wish to break up our unity?",
  54045:
      "Soon, the group of these disbelievers will be defeated, and they will turn their backs on the believers. This occurred on the day of Badr.",
  54046:
      "In fact, the Hour they reject is their appointed time to be tormented. The Hour is more catastrophic and bitter than the torment of this world that they received on the day of Badr.",
  54047:
      "Those guilty of disbelief and sins are misguided from the truth and in torment and difficulty.",
  54048:
      "On the Day when they will be dragged in the Fire on their faces, it will be said to them rebukingly: Taste the torment of the Fire.",
  54049:
      "We have created everything in existence with a prior decree from Us, in accordance with Our knowledge, will, and what We had written in the Preserved Tablet.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The punishment includes those who commit the crime as well as those who go along with them in it.\n2. Being thankful to Allah for His favours is a means of safety from the punishment.\n3. The Qur’an’s informing us of the defeat of the idolaters on the day of Badr before it occurred was miracle of the Ghaib.",
  54050:
      "When We intend something, our command is a single word: Be, and what We intend comes into existence quickly, in the blink of an eye.",
  54051:
      "We have destroyed those who resemble you in disbelief from the previous nations. Can anyone take a lesson from this and desist from disbelief?",
  54052:
      "Everything the slaves have done is written in the books of the guardian angels, from whom nothing escapes.",
  54053:
      "Every small and big action or statement is written in the books of deeds and the Preserved Tablet, and they will be recompensed for it accordingly.",
  54054:
      "Those who fear their Lord by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions will enjoy themselves in gardens and flowing rivers.",
  54055:
      "In a seat of truth, in which there will be no futility or sin, near a Sovereign Who owns everything, the Powerful Who is not incapable of anything. So do not ask about the perpetual bliss they will receive.",
  55000:
      "The Beneficent (Surah Ar-Rahman)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding the jinn and humans about Allah's hidden and manifest blessings and the impact of His Mercy in this world and the Hereafter.\n•    Explanation:",
  55001: "The Most Merciful, possessor of vast mercy.",
  55002:
      "He taught the Quran to people by making its memorization easy and facilitating the understanding of its meanings.",
  55003: "He created man perfectly and formed him in the best manner.",
  55004:
      "He taught him how to express what is within his mind in speech and writing.",
  55005:
      "He decreed a perfectly calculated course for the sun and moon so that people could know the number of years and calculations.",
  55006:
      "Plants without stems and trees prostrate to Allah (may He be Exalted) in submission and surrender to Him.",
  55007:
      "And the sky, He raised it above the Earth to be its canopy. He established justice on Earth and instructed His slaves with it.",
  55008:
      "He established justice so that you, O people, are not unjust and deceitful in weighing and measuring.",
  55009:
      "Weigh justly between yourselves, and do not give a short weight or measure when you measure or weigh for others.",
  55010: "And the Earth, He prepared it for the creation to settle on.",
  55011:
      "On it are trees that produce fruit and date palms that have date stalks that split open to reveal [clusters of] dates.",
  55012:
      "On it are grains with husks like wheat, barley, and plants whose fragrances you find pleasant.",
  55013:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55014:
      "He created Adam (peace be upon him) from dried clay with a ringing sound like that of baked clay.",
  55015: "And He created the father of the jinn from a smokeless flame.",
  55016:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55017:
      "The Lord of the two points of sunrise and sunset in the winter and summer.",
  55018:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The necessity of believing in predestination.\n2. The writing of deeds whether small or big in the book of deeds.\n3. The status of justice in Islam.\n4. Allah’s favours require us to recognise and be grateful for them, not to deny and reject them.",
  55019:
      "Allah merged the two seas, the salty and the sweet, that converge according to what the eye sees.",
  55020:
      "Between them is a barrier that prevents each one from crossing over to the other, so that the sweet remains sweet and the salty remains salty.",
  55021:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55022: "From both these seas, pearls and coral emerge.",
  55023:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55024:
      "He (may He be Exalted) alone has control of the ships that sail in the sea like mountains.",
  55025:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55026:
      "Every creation that is on the face of the earth will inevitably perish.",
  55027:
      "And the face of your Lord, O Messenger, the Possessor of majesty, favor, and bounty over His slaves, will remain and will never perish.",
  55028:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55029:
      "The angels in the heavens and the jinn and humans on Earth ask Him for their needs. Every day, he brings about a matter from the affairs of His slaves, such as giving life, death, provision, etc.",
  55030:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55031:
      "We will attend to your reckoning, O humans and jinn, and recompense each one with the reward or punishment he deserves.",
  55032:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55033:
      "Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection, when He gathers the jinn and humans: O assembly of jinn and humans, if you can find an exit from any part of the heavens and Earth, then do so. You will never be able to do so except with power and evidence, and where do you have that?",
  55034:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55035:
      "A flame of smokeless fire and smoke without a flame will be sent upon you, O humans and jinn, and you will not be able to protect yourselves from that.",
  55036:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55037:
      "When the sky splits open for the angels to descend from it, it will become rose-colored like oil.",
  55038:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55039:
      "On that great Day, no human or jinn will be asked about their sins because Allah knows their deeds.",
  55040:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55041:
      "The guilty ones will be recognized on the Day of Resurrection by their marks, which are black faces and blue eyes. Their forelocks will be tied to their feet, and they will be thrown into Hell.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The meeting of the salty and sweet sea without mixing is one of the manifestations of Allah’s power.\n2. The proof that all created things will perish and showing that permanence is only for Allah.\n3. Establishing the attribute of wajh for Allah in the meaning that is appropriate for Him without any resemblance or likeliness.",
  55042:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55043:
      "It will be said to them in rebuke: This is the Hell that the guilty ones used to reject in the worldly life, which is now before their eyes and which they cannot deny.",
  55044: "They will alternate between it and scalding water.",
  55045:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55046:
      "The one who fears standing before his Lord in the Hereafter, and therefore believed and did righteous deeds, will have two gardens.",
  55047:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55048: "These two gardens will have huge fresh branches producing fruit.",
  55049:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55050:
      "In both gardens, there will be two springs flowing between them with water.",
  55051:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55052: "There will be two types of fruit to enjoy in both of them.",
  55053:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55054:
      "Reclining on spreads, whose inner lining will be of thick silk, and the fruits they will pluck from the two gardens will be close and within reach of a person standing, sitting, or reclining.",
  55055:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55056:
      "In them, there will be women who will restrict their gaze to their husbands, whose virginity was not broken by any man or jinn before their husbands.",
  55057:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55058: "As though they are rubies and coral in their beauty and purity.",
  55059:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55060:
      "What is the recompense of those who followed their Lord well, except that Allah should reward them well?",
  55061:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55062: "Below those two mentioned gardens are another two gardens.",
  55063:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55064: "Both of them will be dark green.",
  55065:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55066:
      "In both gardens, springs will forcefully gush forth with water. The gushing of their water will not stop.",
  55067:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55068:
      "There will be abundant fruit in both gardens, huge date palms, and pomegranates.",
  55069:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The diversification of punishment of the disbelievers.\n2. The importance of the fear of Allah and thinking of the awe of standing before Him.\n3. The recompense is according to the deed.",
  55070:
      "There will be women with good characters and beautiful faces in all these gardens.",
  55071:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55072:
      "There will be maidens with gorgeous eyes concealed in tents to protect them.",
  55073:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55074: "Before their husbands, no human or jinn had come close to them.",
  55075:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55076:
      "Reclining on cushions covered with green covers and beautiful carpets.",
  55077:
      "So which of Allah's numerous favors to you, O assembly of jinn and humans, do you reject?",
  55078:
      "Great and full of goodness is the name of your Lord, the Possessor of majesty, favor, and bounty over His slaves.",
  56000:
      "The Inevitable (Surah Al-Waqi'ah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the conditions of the servants on the Day of Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  56001: "When the inevitable [Day of] Resurrection takes place.",
  56002:
      "There will be no soul that will reject it like how it used to reject it in the worldly life",
  56003:
      "It will debase the wicked disbelievers by entering them into the Fire and elevate the believers, who fear Allah, by entering them into Paradise.",
  56004: "When the Earth is shaken violently,",
  56005: "And the mountains are completely crushed into pieces.",
  56006: "They will become scattered dust due to the crushing.",
  56007: "You will be divided into three categories on that Day.",
  56008:
      "The people of the right will receive their books in their right hands. How high and great their rank will be!",
  56009:
      "The people of the left will receive their books in their left hands. How despicable and wretched their rank will be!",
  56010:
      "The Forerunners in doing good deeds in the world will be the Forerunners in the Hereafter to enter Paradise.",
  56011: "They are the ones who will be brought close to Allah.",
  56012: "In gardens of bliss, they will enjoy different types of pleasure.",
  56013: "A group from this nation and from previous nations.",
  56014:
      "A few people at the end of time will be the foremost ones brought close [to Allah]",
  56015: "On couches woven with gold.",
  56016:
      "Reclining on these couches facing each other, no one will look at the back of another.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The denial of the disbelievers will end when they see the scenes of resurrection.\n2. The magnitude of the incidents that will accompany the resurrection.\n3. The different levels of the people of Paradise is in accordance to their differing deeds.",
  56017:
      "Youths who never reach old age or die will roam around them to serve them.",
  56018:
      "They will roam around them holding handleless jugs, jugs with handles, and glasses of unlimited wine that flow in Paradise.",
  56019:
      "It is not like the wine of the world; its drinkers will not suffer from headaches, nor will they be intoxicated.",
  56020:
      "These youths will also roam around them with fruits they may choose from.",
  56021:
      "They will also roam around them with the meat of birds that they desire.",
  56022: "They will also have beautiful, wide-eyed women in Paradise,",
  56023: "Like pearls protected within their shells.",
  56024:
      "All as a reward for the righteous deeds they used to do in the worldly life.",
  56025:
      "They will not hear foul language in Paradise or something leading to sin.",
  56026:
      "They will only hear the angels greeting them and the greetings from each other.",
  56027:
      "And the people of the right: who are the people of the right? How great their rank and status with Allah is!",
  56028: "They will be among harmless, thornless lote trees.",
  56029: "And clusters of bananas neatly arranged in rows with one another.",
  56030: "And an enlongated, continuous shade that will never disappear.",
  56031: "And flowing water that never stops.",
  56032: "And abundant unlimited fruit that are.",
  56033:
      "[Their supply] will never be interrupted because they are not seasonal, nor will anything prevent their desire for them at any time.",
  56034: "And elevated, high-class spreads placed on the couches.",
  56035:
      "We created the aforementioned wide-eyed women in an extraordinary way.",
  56036: "We made them virgins, previously untouched.",
  56037: "They are very loving to their husbands and of equal age.",
  56038:
      "We created them for the people of the right, those who will be taken towards the right as a sign of their success [in the Hereafter].",
  56039: "They are a group from the nations of the previous prophets.",
  56040:
      "And a group from the nation of Muhammad, which is the last of all nations.",
  56041:
      "As for the people of the left: who are the people of the left? How bad their condition and destination are!",
  56042: "They will be in scalding wind and water.",
  56043: "And in the shade of black smoke.",
  56044: "Neither will it be pleasant, nor will it be a good sight.",
  56045:
      "Before they came to the torment, they enjoyed the worldly life's luxuries, caring only for their desires.",
  56046:
      "They used to persist in disbelieving in Allah and worshipping idols instead of Allah.",
  56047:
      "They also used to deny the resurrection and say, regarding it, mocking it and considering it far-fetched: When we die and become dust and decomposed bones, will we be resurrected after that?",
  56048: "Will our forefathers, who died before us, also be resurrected?",
  56049:
      "O Messenger, tell these deniers of the resurrection: The earlier and later generations of people from them...",
  56050:
      "will soon be inevitably gathered on the Day of Resurrection to be reckoned and recompensed accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Good deeds are a means to acquiring blessings in the Afterlife.\n2. The people will be requited differently on the Day of Judgement according to their deeds.\n3. Persisting on sins is dangerous.",
  56051:
      "Then, O rejectors of the resurrection and misguided from the straight path, you will, on the Day of Resurrection, eat from the fruits of the tree of Zaqqum, which are the worst and most disgusting of fruits.",
  56052:
      "Then, O rejectors of the resurrection and misguided from the straight path, you will, on the Day of Resurrection, eat from the fruits of the tree of Zaqqum, which are the worst and most disgusting of fruits.",
  56053: "Filling your hungry bellies with the fruits of that bitter tree.",
  56054: "Then, on top of that, you will drink scalding water.",
  56055:
      "You will drink so much of it, just like a camel suffering from burning thirst drinks.",
  56056:
      "The aforementioned bitter fruit and scalding water are the hospitality you will receive on the Day of Recompense.",
  56057:
      "O rejectors, We have created you after you were non-existent, so why do you not believe that We will resurrect you after you have died?",
  56058:
      "O people, have you seen the semen you ejaculate into the wombs of your wives?",
  56059: "Do you create that semen, or is it We who create it?",
  56060:
      "We have decreed death among you; each of you has a fixed [amount of] time that he will neither go beyond nor fall short of, and We are not incapable...",
  56061:
      "[We are not incapable] of changing the form and appearance you currently know of and recreating you into a form and appearance you do not know.",
  56062:
      "You know how We created you initially, so do you not take heed and realize that the One who created you in the first place can resurrect you after you die?",
  56063: "Have you seen the seeds you plant on the Earth?",
  56064: "Do you make that seed grow, or do We make it grow?",
  56065:
      "If We wished to turn that crop into debris, We could do so after it was close to ripening and being harvested. You would then remain shocked at what affected it.",
  56066: "You would say: We were tormented by losing what we had spent.",
  56067: "Rather, we have been deprived of provision.",
  56068: "Have you seen the water you drink when you are thirsty?",
  56069:
      "Do you cause it to come down from the clouds in the sky, or do We send it down?",
  56070:
      "If We wished to make that water extremely bitter, such that it would be of no use for drinking nor irrigation, We would have done so. Will you not be grateful to Allah for sending it down as palatable and a mercy for you?",
  56071: "Have you seen the Fire that you kindle for your use?",
  56072:
      "Do you make the trees from which it is kindled grow, or do We cause it to grow, being kind to you?",
  56073:
      "We have made this fire for you as a reminder of the Fire of the Hereafter, and We have made it a means of benefit for the travelers among you.",
  56074:
      "So, O Messenger, free your Lord, the Greatest, from that which does not befit Him.",
  56075: "Allah swore by the positions and locations of the stars.",
  56076:
      "And [taking] an oath by these locations is great if only you were to understand its magnificence, as there are unlimited signs and lessons in it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The initial creation is a proof of the obvious ease of resurrection.\n2. Sending down rain, causing the earth to grow and fire from which people benefit, are all blessings that require people to be grateful for, because Allah is capable of taking them away whenever He wishes.",
  56077:
      "O people, the Quran that is recited to you is a noble Quran because of its great benefits.",
  56078:
      "It is in a record protected from people's eyes, i.e., the Preserved Tablet.",
  56079: "Only the angels, pure of sin and defects, can touch it.",
  56080:
      "It is a revelation from the Lord of the creations to His Prophet Muhammad.",
  56081:
      "O polytheists, do you then reject this discourse and not believe in it?",
  56082:
      "And do you show your gratitude to Allah for the favors He has provided you with by rejecting Him and attributing the rain to the setting of stars, by saying: It rained upon us due to the setting of so and so star.",
  56083:
      "After presenting evidence for the Resurrection, Allah draws attention to His ability to bring the dead back to life. He highlights their inability to avoid death, as the One who can take life can also restore it. Allah states: \n Why not when the soul reaches the throat,",
  56084: "And at that time, you look at the dying person in front of you,",
  56085:
      "While We, through Our knowledge, power, and Angels, are closer to the dying person than you are, but you do not see these angels,",
  56086:
      "Why not then? If you are not going to be resurrected, as you claim, to be recompensed for your deeds,",
  56087:
      "Return this soul that is leaving the dying person among you, if you are truthful. You cannot do it.",
  56088: "So, if the deceased is one of The Forerunners in doing good deeds,",
  56089:
      "Then he will be in such comfort, after which there will be no tiring, and in good provision and mercy. He will have a garden where he will live in luxury, enjoying whatever he desires.",
  56090:
      "And if the deceased is from the people of the right, do not worry about their condition because they will be in peace and security.",
  56091:
      "And if the deceased is from the people of the right, do not worry about their condition because they will be in peace and security.",
  56092:
      "And if the deceased is from the rejectors of what the Messenger brought and is misguided from the straight path,",
  56093:
      "Then his hospitable reception, which he will be presented with, is scalding water.",
  56094: "And he will have to burn in the Fire of the Inferno.",
  56095:
      "O Messenger, this which We have narrated to you is convincingly true, in which there is no doubt.",
  56096:
      "So free and sanctify the name of your Lord, the Greatest, from all defects.",
  57000:
      "The Iron (Surah Al-Hadid)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nElevation of souls through belief and spending in Allah's path.\n•    Explanation:",
  57001:
      "Every creation of His in the heavens and the Earth is free and sanctify Allah [from any deficiency]. He is the Almighty whom no one can overpower; the Wise in His creation and decree.",
  57002:
      "To Him alone belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He gives life to whoever He wishes to give life to and causes death to whoever He wishes to cause death to. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; there is nothing that He is incapable of.",
  57003:
      "He is the First; nothing existed before Him. He is the Last; nothing will exist after Him. He is the Apparent; there is nothing above Him. He is the Intimate; there is nothing without Him, and He knows everything; nothing escapes His knowledge.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Belief that celestial bodies have an effect in rainfall is an act of disbelief and one of the habits of the times of ignorance.\n2. The principle is that humans cannot see the angels except if Allah wishes due to some wisdom.\n3. The ranks of the believers differ according to their deeds.",
  57004:
      "He is the One who created the heavens and the Earth in six days, starting from Sunday and finishing on Friday, yet He is capable of having created them in less than the duration of the blinking of an eye. He (may He be Exalted) then rose over His Throne as it befits Him, may He be Exalted. He knows everything that enters the Earth, i.e., every drop of rain, seed, etc.; He knows everything that emerges from it, i.e., every plant, mineral, etc.; He knows everything that descends from the sky, i.e., rain, revelation, etc., and He knows everything that ascends to it, i.e., angels, souls, and deeds of the slaves, etc. And He is with you wherever you are, O people, in terms of His knowledge; nothing is hidden from Him, and He sees everything you do. None of your deeds are hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  57005:
      "To Him alone belongs the dominion of the heavens and the Earth, and to Him alone, all affairs return. He will then reckon the creation on the Day of Resurrection and recompense them for their deeds accordingly.",
  57006:
      "He enters the night into the day, the darkness arrives, and people sleep; He enters the day into the night, the light arrives, and people go about their work. He is aware of everything that the breasts of His slaves contain; none of it is hidden from Him.",
  57007:
      "Believe in Allah and His Messenger, and spend from the wealth of which Allah has made you trustees, using it according to what Allah has legislated for you. So those of you who believe in Allah and spend their wealth in His path, for them is a great reward with Him, which is Paradise.",
  57008:
      "And what stops you from believing in Allah when the Messenger is inviting you towards Allah, hoping that you believe in your Lord (may He be Exalted) and Allah had taken a covenant from you to believe in Him when He took you out from the loins of your fathers, if you are believers?",
  57009:
      "He is the One who sends down clear verses upon His slave Muhammad to take you out of the darkness of disbelief and ignorance and into the light of belief and knowledge. And indeed, Allah is kind and merciful to you that He sent His Prophet to you as a guide and a bearer of glad tidings.",
  57010:
      "And what prevents you from spending in the path of Allah when the inheritance of the heavens and the Earth belongs to Allah? O believers! Those of you who spent their wealth in the path of Allah, seeking His pleasure before the conquest of Mecca, and fought the disbelievers in aid of Islam cannot be equal to those who spent their wealth in His path and fought the disbelievers after the conquest of Mecca. Those who spent their wealth before the conquest and fought in the path of Allah are greater in rank in the sight of Allah and higher in status than those who spent their wealth in His path and fought the disbelievers after its conquest. However, Allah has promised both groups Paradise, and He is informed of all that you do; none of your deeds are hidden from Him, and He will soon recompense you for them accordingly.",
  57011:
      "Who is it that will spend his wealth, happily, for the pleasure of Allah, so that Allah may grant him a multitude of rewards for the wealth he has spent, and he will receive on the Day of Resurrection a noble reward which is Paradise?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Wealth belongs to Allah. Humans have only been made as caretakers of it.\n2. The believers differ in rank according to precedence in faith and acts of piety.\n3. Spending in the path of Allah is a means of attaining blessings and increase in wealth.",
  57012:
      "On that Day, you will see believing men and women with their light shining ahead of them and on their right. They will then be told: Today, you have good news of gardens with rivers flowing beneath their palaces and trees, which you will remain in forever. That reward is the greatest success that cannot be equaled by any other.",
  57013:
      "After mentioning the condition of the believers on that Day, Allah mentions the condition of the hypocrites, stating: \n On that Day, the male and female hypocrites will say to those who believed in Allah and His Messenger: O believing men and women! Wait for us; perhaps we can take a flare of your light that will help us cross the Bridge? It will be said to the hypocrites, mocking them: Turn back and find the light you can use for yourselves! A wall will then be placed between them, which will have a door; the inner side on which the believers are will have mercy, while the outer side on which the hypocrites are will have torment.",
  57014:
      "The hypocrites will call out to the believers: Were we not with you upon Islam and obedience? The Muslims will reply: Yes, you were with us, but you tempted yourselves with hypocrisy and destroyed yourselves, and you anticipated that the believers would be defeated, so you can then announce your disbelief. You also doubted the help of Allah coming for the believers and in the resurrection after death. False hopes also deceived you until death came to you while you were chasing them, and the Devil also deceived you about Allah.",
  57015:
      "O hypocrites, today no ransom will be accepted from you from Allah's torment, nor from those who disbelieved in Allah openly, and your destination and the destination of the disbelievers is the Fire. It is most deserving of you, and you are most deserving of it; what an evil destination!",
  57016:
      "Has the time not come for those who believe in Allah and His Messenger that their hearts soften and become tranquil through the remembrance of Allah (may He be Exalted) and through the promises and warnings revealed in the Quran? Has the time not come that they do not become like the Jews who were given the Torah and the Christians who were given the Gospel, in terms of their hearts hardening? This hardening of hearts was due to the prolonged period between them and the coming of their Prophets. Most of them abandoned Allah's obedience, preferring His disobedience.",
  57017:
      "Know that Allah revives the Earth by causing it to germinate after it has dried up. We have clearly explained the proofs and evidence of Allah's capability and Oneness so that perhaps you may understand them and know that the One who revives the Earth after its death is also capable of resurrecting you after your death and is capable of making your hearts soft after they have become hard.",
  57018:
      "The men and women who spend some of their wealth in charity happily and without reminding the person of the favor or causing harm will have their reward multiplied for them. Each good deed will be multiplied by ten the like thereof up until seven hundred times or more. In addition, they will receive a generous reward from Allah, which is Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah recounts His favours upon the believers by telling them that He will grant them a light that will shine in front of them and from their right sides.\n2. There will be no light on the Day of Judgement for the hypocrites.\n3. Wishing misfortune upon the believers and doubting in the resurrection, together with being deceived by false hopes and Satan are some of the traits of the hypocrites.\n4. The severity of heedless from Allah, in that it causes hardnening of the heart.",
  57019:
      "Those who believe in Allah and His messengers without differentiating between them are the truthful ones. The martyrs have their generous reward prepared for them with Allah, and they will also have a light that shines in front of them and on their right sides on the Day of Resurrection. As for those who disbelieved in Allah and His messengers and rejected Our verses revealed to Our Messenger, they are the people of the Inferno, which they will enter on the Day of Resurrection and remain therein forever, never to come out of it.",
  57020:
      "Know that the life of this world is only a pastime that the bodies play with; futility that the hearts engage in; beauty that you adorn yourselves with; boasting with one another over possessions and ownership; and taking pride in the abundance of wealth and offspring. It is just like the rainfall that pleases the farmers with the growth it brings, but the green growth does not last long before it begins to dry. Then, O onlooker, you see it after its greenery has turned yellow. Allah then turns it into broken bits falling apart. And in the Hereafter, there will be severe torment for the disbelievers and the hypocrites, and a special forgiveness from Allah for the sins of His believing slaves.",
  57021:
      "O people, hasten towards righteous deeds such as repentance and other deeds, through which you will achieve forgiveness for your sins. Through them, You will acquire a paradise, the width of which is the width of the heavens and the Earth. Allah has prepared this Paradise for those who believe in Him and His messengers. That reward is Allah's grace that He grants whoever of His slaves He wishes. He (may He be Exalted) is the bestower of great grace on His believing slaves.",
  57022:
      "No calamity afflicts the people on Earth, such as drought, etc., nor a personal calamity, except that it was recorded in the Preserved Tablet before We created the creation. Indeed, that is easy for Allah.",
  57023:
      "O people, that is so that you do not grieve over anything you miss out on and do not boast about the favors Allah has given you. Allah does not love anyone who is arrogant and boastful over what Allah has granted him.",
  57024:
      "Those who are miserly in spending whatever is obligatory for them to spend and instruct others to be miserly are losers. Whoever turns away from the obedience of Allah will never harm Allah; he only harms himself. Allah is Independent; He does not need the obedience of His slaves, and He is praiseworthy in every state.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Abstinence from the world and the desires attached to it, together with an eagerness in the Afterlife and the everlasting blessings within it, both help in treading the straight path.\n2. It is necessary to believe in predestination.\n3. One of the benefits of believing in predestination is not grieving over missing out on any shares of the world.\n4. Stinginess and commanding it are blameworthy traits which a believer should not have.",
  57025:
      "We have sent Our messengers with clear evidence and manifest proofs and sent down books with them and the balance so that people would uphold justice. We also sent down iron, which has great strength; weapons are made from it, and it has many other benefits for the people in their trades and occupations. And so that Allah knows in such a way that is manifest to the people who it is, that supports Him and His messengers without seeing Him. Allah is Strong and Almighty; nothing can overcome His decree, nor is He incapable of doing anything.",
  57026:
      "And We sent Noah and Abraham (peace be upon them) as messengers. We placed messengerships, and revealed books among their offspring. So from among their offspring are those who were rightly guided to the straight path and are successful, but most of them abandoned Allah's obedience.",
  57027:
      "Then We followed them up with Our messengers, sending them one after the other to their nations. We sent Jesus, the son of Mary, after them and gave him the Gospel, placing gentleness and mercy in the hearts of those who believed in and followed him. They were affectionate and merciful to one another but innovated extremism into their religion and abandoned marriage and comforts, which We had made permissible. We did not seek that from them; they obligated it upon themselves and innovated in the religion. We only sought that they follow the pleasure of Allah, which they did not do, and so We granted those who believed among them their reward. However, most abandoned Our obedience by rejecting what Our Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم brought to them.",
  57028:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, fear Allah by fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions; He will give you double the reward for believing in Muhammad and the previous messengers. He will also grant you a light through which you will be guided in your worldly life and which you shall use on the Bridge on the Day of Resurrection. He will also forgive your sins by covering them and not tormenting you for them; and Allah (may He be Exalted) is forgiving of the sins of His slaves and merciful towards them.",
  57029:
      "O believers, verily, We have clearly explained Our great grace, which We have prepared for you in the form of multiplied rewards, so that the people of the previous Book, i.e., the Jews and Christians, know that they cannot access any of Allah's grace in terms of being able to give it or withhold it from whosoever they wish, and so that they also know that true grace is in Allah's Hand alone, may He be Exalted; He grants it to whosoever He wishes of His slaves. And Allah is the bestower of great grace, which He exclusively gives to whichever of His slaves He wishes.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The status of justice in the divine religions is mentioned.\n2. Being related through blood to the people of faith and piety does not help a person at all, as long as he himself is not a believer.\n3. The prohibition of innovation in religion is mentioned.",
  58000:
      "The Dispute (Surah Al-Mujadalah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating Allah's comprehensive knowledge and profound understanding to nurture awareness of Him and as a warning against defying Him.\n•    Explanation:",
  58001:
      "O Messenger, verily Allah has heard the words of the woman [She was Khawlah bint Tha'labah] who was discussing the issue of her husband with you [who was Aws bin Al-Samit] after he had pronounced dhihar on her. She was complaining to Allah about what her husband had done to her, and Allah was listening to your exchange of words; nothing is hidden from Him. Indeed, He is The Hearing of the speech of His slaves and The Seeing of their actions; none of them are hidden from Him.",
  58002:
      "Those who pronounce dhihar on their women, by one of them saying to his wife: You are like my mother upon me, have lied in this statement of theirs, for their wives are not their mothers. Their mothers are only those who gave birth to them. And indeed, when they say that statement, they say a terrible word and a lie. And, indeed, Allah is surely pardoning and forgiving, for He has legislated expiation for them as a means of ridding them of sin.",
  58003:
      "And those who say this terrible word then want intercourse with those whom they pronounced dhihar on, then they must atone by freeing a slave before they have intercourse with them. You are commanded with that mentioned ruling as a deterrent from dhihar. And Allah is Well-Informed of what you do. Nothing from your deeds is hidden from Him.",
  58004:
      "So whoever cannot find a slave to free, it is necessary upon him to fast for two months consecutively before he has sexual intercourse with the wife he pronounced dhihar on. Then whoever is incapable of fasting for two months consecutively should feed sixty poor people. This command I have given is so that you believe that Allah is the One who has commanded you with it and so you carry it out. These rulings that We legislate for you are Our (Allah's) limits He has set for His slaves, so do not transgress them. As for those who disbelieve in the commands of Allah and the limits He has set, will face a painful punishment.",
  58005:
      "Indeed, those who oppose Allah and His Messenger have been debased and humiliated just as those who opposed Him from the past nations were debased and humiliated. And we have certainly sent down clear verses. [Prepared] for the disbelievers in Allah, His messengers, and His verses is a humiliating torment.",
  58006:
      "The Day Allah resurrects them all, leaving out none of them. Then He will inform them of what they did in abhorrent deeds in the worldly life. Allah tallied those deeds against them, so nothing of their actions escaped Him. They forgot them then found them written in their sheets [of deeds], which leave nothing small nor large except that they tallied it. And Allah is Observant over all things; nothing of their deeds is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is kind to the weak among His servants, because He helps them and lessens the obligation of worship on them.\n2. The supplication of an oppressed person will be accepted, even though it may be after a while.\n3. Zihar is one of the major sins, because it is effectively prohibiting that which Allah has made permissible.",
  58007:
      "Have you not perceived, O Messenger, that Allah knows what is in the heavens and the Earth? Nothing within them is hidden from Him. There is no secret conversation between three individuals except that He (may He be Exalted) is their fourth by His knowledge. And there is no secret conversation between five individuals except that He (may He be Exalted) is their sixth by His knowledge, and not less than that number, nor more except that He is with them by His knowledge wherever they are. Nothing is hidden from Him of their talk. Then, on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will inform them of what they did. Indeed, Allah is Omniscient; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  58008:
      "Have you not perceived, O Messenger, the Jews who would secretly discuss if they saw a believer? So Allah forbade them from discussing secretly. Then they go back to what Allah forbade them from, and they secretly discuss between themselves with what entails sin, such as backbiting the believers, enmity towards them, and disobedience to the Messenger. And if they come to you, O Messenger, they greet you with a greeting which Allah did not greet you with, saying: As-sammu' alayka (death be upon you),intending [his] demise. And they say in rejection to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم: Would not Allah torment us for what we say? For if he were truthful in what he claims of being a Prophet, Allah surely would have tormented us for what we say about him!Hell is enough punishment for what they said. They will suffer its heat, so how gruesome the destination that they head toward.",
  58009:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, do not secretly discuss with what entails sin, enmity, or disobedience to the Messenger so that you will not be like the Jews. And secretly discuss what entails obedience to Allah and abstaining from disobeying Him. And take heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, for He is whom you will be solely gathered to on the Day of Resurrection for account and recompense.",
  58010:
      "Secret discussion containing sin, enmity, and disobedience to the Messenger is but from the Devil's embellishing and his whispering to his allies to bring sorrow to the believers [by the fact] that they are plotted against. The Devil and his embellishments are not harmful to the believers except by Allah's wish and desire. Let the believers rely upon Allah in all their affairs.",
  58011:
      "After mentioning the etiquette of speaking, Allah specifies the etiquette of gatherings, stating: \n O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, if it is said to you: make space in a seated gathering, and they make space in them, Allah will make space for you in life in this world and the Afterlife. And if it is said to you: rise from some of the seats so that the people of virtue may sit in them and they rise from them, Allah (may He be Exalted) will raise those who believed amongst you and those who were given knowledge in tremendous degrees. And Allah is Well-Informed of what you do. Nothing of your actions is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you [based] upon them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s, may He be glorified, knowledge is vast.\n2. Three people should not have a private conversation leaving one person out, because that could cause him grief by thinking they are talking about him.\n3. Satan invites towards evil and discord between the hearts of people.\n4. From the etiquettes of a gathering is that you create space for others in them.\n5. requital is of the same nature as the deed: whoever wishes for a good requital should do good deeds.",
  58012:
      "When the Companions [of the Messenger] were secretly discussing a great deal with the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, Allah said: O you who have believed, when you want to talk privately with the Messenger, give some charity before you talk in private with him. Giving in charity will be better and purer for you because it is an act of obedience to Allah that purifies the hearts. But if you do not find anything you can give in charity, there is no harm in you talking in private with him because Allah is Forgiving of the sins of His slaves, and He is Merciful towards them by not burdening them except with what they are capable of.",
  58013:
      "Have you feared poverty from putting forth charity when you secretly discuss with the Messenger?! So if you do not do what Allah commanded from it and He has turned to you in repentance when He permitted you to leave it, then come to prayer in the most complete manner, give zakat (obligatory alms) of your wealth, and obey Allah and his Messenger. Allah is Well-Informed of what you do. Nothing of your actions is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you for them.",
  58014:
      "Have you not perceived, O Messenger, the hypocrites who allied with the Jews whom Allah was angered with due to their disbelief and acts of disobedience? These hypocrites are not from the believers nor the Jews. Rather, they go back and forth, not to them nor to them. They swear that they are Muslims and did not carry the news of the Muslims to the Jews. They are liars in what they swear by.",
  58015:
      "Allah has prepared a severe torment for them in the Afterlife when He will enter them into the lowest depths of the Fire. Indeed, what they were upon of disbelieving acts in the worldly life was vile.",
  58016:
      "They took their faith, which they swear by as a safeguard from being killed for disbelief, whereby they outwardly showed Islam as a means to protect their blood and wealth. Then they diverted people from the truth by demoralizing and hindering the Muslims. Therefore, for them awaits a humiliating torment. It will debase and disgrace them.",
  58017:
      "Neither their wealth nor their children will avail them anything from Allah. Those are the people of the Fire who enter it, remaining in it eternally. The torment will not cease for them.",
  58018:
      "The Day Allah will resurrect them all, not leaving any of them except that He resurrected them for recompense. Then they will swear to Allah that they were not upon disbelief nor hypocrisy and that they were but believers doing what contented Allah. They swear to Him in the Afterlife just as they would swear to you, O believers, in the worldly life that they are Muslims. They think that with this faith, which they swear by to Allah, that they are upon something that brings benefit to them or fends off harm from them. They are truly the liars in their faith in the worldly life and Afterlife.",
  58019:
      "The Devil has seized control of them, then made them forget to remember Allah through his whispering, so they did not do what pleases Him. Those described with these attributes are the soldiers of Iblis (Satan) and his followers. Indeed, Iblis's soldiers and followers the losers in the worldly life and Afterlife, for they have sold guidance for misguidance and the Garden [of Paradise] for the Fire.",
  58020:
      "Indeed, those who oppose Allah and His Messenger are amongst those whom Allah debases in the worldly life and Afterlife, and they are disgraced from the disbelieving nations.",
  58021:
      "Allah decreed in His preceding knowledge: I will undoubtedly triumph, My Messengers and I, over Our enemies in evidence and strength. Indeed, Allah is Powerful in supporting His messengers and Mighty, taking vengeance upon their enemies.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Uncertainty and not being able to stand firm on one position is one of the traits of the hypocrites.\n2. Swearing an oath to something that is a lie is a gravely reprehensible.\n3. From the divine customs of Allah is that He will grant victory to those of Faith, a custom which never changes, however delayed it may seem.",
  58022:
      "You will not find, O Messenger, a people believing in Allah and the Day of Resurrection loving and allying those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, even if these enemies to Allah and His Messenger were their fathers, sons, brothers, or close associates whom they ascribe to. That is because faith prevents allying with the enemies of Allah and His Messenger, and because the relationship of faith is superior to all relationships, so it is prioritized when they are conflicting. Those who do not ally with those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, even if they are relatives, are those whom Allah has made faith firm in their hearts so that it does not change. And He strengthened them with clear evidence from Him and light. On the Day of Resurrection, He will enter them into gardens of permanent residence. Rivers flow beneath its castles and trees, remaining in it forever. Its delight does not cease from them, and they do not disappear from it. Allah will be content with them, never displeased with them after it. They would be content with Him for what He gave them of the delight that does not run out. From it is seeing Him, may He be Exalted. Those described with what was mentioned are Allah's soldiers, who conform to what He commanded and abstain from what he forbade from. Indeed, Allah's soldiers are the victors by attaining what they seek and what they miss from dread in the worldly life and the Afterlife.",
  59000:
      "The Banishment (Surah Al-Hashr)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating Allah's power and might in weakening the Jews and hypocrites, as well as revealing their disunity, while on the other hand, showing affection for the believers.\n•    Explanation:",
  59001:
      "Everything in the heavens and the Earth from creation has exalted Allah and vindicated Him of what does not befit him. He is the Mighty whom none overpowers, the Wise in His creation, legislation, and predetermination.",
  59002:
      "He is the One who expelled [the tribe of] Banu An-Nadeer, who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, from their homes in Medina for their first expulsion from Medina to the Levant. They are from the Jews, people of the Torah. He expelled them for breaking their covenant and being with the polytheists against Him. He expelled them to the Land of the Levant. You did not think, O believers, they would be expelled from their homes due to their might and strength. And they assumed that their forts, which they perfected, would secure them from Allah's punishment and torment. But Allah's retribution came from where they did not expect when His Messenger commanded fighting them and banishing them from their homes. Allah placed intense fear in their hearts. They destroy their homes with their own hands from within so that the Muslims would not benefit from them, and the Muslims destroy them from the outside. So take admonishment, O people of sight, from what occurred to them due to their disbelief. So do not be like them, so you avoid receiving their requital and the punishment that they were punished with.",
  59003:
      "Had it not been that Allah had decreed exile for them, He would have punished them in the world with execution and captivity, as He did with their brothers from Banu Qurayzah. And for them in the Afterlife is the punishment of the Fire that awaits them, wherein they shall live forever.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Faith in Allah contradicts befriending His enemies.\n2. The connection of faith is the strongest of connections between the people of faith.\n3. Faith in Allah is the cause of success in the world and the afterlife.",
  59004:
      "That happened to them because they opposed Allah and His Messenger through disbelief and breaking covenants. And whoever opposes Allah, then Allah is severe in punishment, and His severe punishment will reach him.",
  59005:
      "What you cut, O believers, of date palms to enrage Allah's enemies in the Battle of Banu An-Nadeer or left standing on their trunks to benefit from was by Allah's command and not a cause for corruption on Earth, as they wrongly claim. And Allah will surely debase with it those outside of His obedience among the Jews who broke their covenant and chose the path of treachery over the path of fulfillment.",
  59006:
      "And as for what Allah gave back to His Messenger from the wealth of Banu An-Nadeer, then you did not hasten your horses nor camels in pursuit of it, and no burden fell upon you from it, but rather, Allah gives His messengers rule over whom He wills. He had given His Messenger rule over Banu An-Nadeer, so he conquered their lands without combat. Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing can hinder Him.",
  59007:
      "The wealth Allah bestowed upon His Messenger from the townspeople without combat belongs to Allah; He designates it to whom He wills. It is for the Messenger, for his relatives from Banu Hashim and Banu Al-Muttalib as compensation to them for what they were forbidden of charity, for the orphans, for the poor, and for the stranger whose travel provision has been exhausted. [That is] so that the circulation of wealth is not limited to the affluent in exclusion of the poor. And the money the Messenger gave you from booty without battle, then take it, O believers, and what he forbade you from, then desist. And heed Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Indeed, Allah is severe in punishment, so beware of His retribution.",
  59008:
      "A portion of this wealth is for the poor among Al-Muhajireen (the Emigrants) in the path of Allah, who were forced to leave their properties and children. They hope that Allah favors them with provision in the worldly life and contentment in the Afterlife. They support Allah and His Messenger through struggle in Allah's path. The ones described with those attributes are those truly firm in faith.",
  59009:
      "After praising the Al-Muhajireen (the Emigrants), Allah praises the Al-Ansar (the Supporters) as well, stating: \n And Al-Ansar (the Supporters), who resided in Medina before Al-Muhajireen and chose faith in Allah and His Messenger, love those who emigrated to them from Mecca. They do not find anger nor malice in their hearts against Al-Muhajireen in the path of Allah when they are given anything from the ransom, and they [Al-Ansar] are not given. They put Al-Muhajireen before themselves in terms of the allocations of the worldly life, even if they [Al-Ansar] are considered poor and in need. And whomsoever Allah protects their soul's yearning for wealth such that they spend it in the path of Allah, are the victors by attaining what they hope for and salvation from what they flee from.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Treating Allah and His Messenger as enemies is a direct cause of incurring loss in the world and the afterlife.\n2. Fay’ has been legislated and its avenues of expenditure stipulated.\n3. The Migrant companions and the Helpers are both virtuous.\n4. Giving preference to others is a great trait from the traits of Islam, which manifested itself in the Helpers most beautifully.",
  59010:
      "And the ones who came after these individuals and those who followed them in excellence until the Day of Resurrection say: O Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers in religion who preceded us in faith in Allah and His Messenger, and do not put malevolence and malice in our hearts toward anyone among the believers. Our Lord, indeed, you are Kind with your slaves, and Merciful to them.",
  59011:
      "Have you not recognized, O Messenger, those who concealed disbelief and outwardly exhibited faith? They say to their brothers in disbelief from the Jews, the followers of the distorted Torah: Stay in your homes, for we will not betray you nor hand you over. Then, if the Muslims expel you from them, we will surely go out united with you, and we will not obey anyone who wants to prevent us from going out with you. And if they fight you, we will certainly help you against them.Allah testifies that, indeed, the hypocrites are surely lying in their claim of going out with the Jews if they are expelled and fighting with them if they are fought.",
  59012:
      "If the Muslims expel the Jews, they will certainly not go out with them. And if they fight them, they will certainly not support or help them. And if they support and help them against the Muslims, they will certainly flee, running away from them. Then the hypocrites will not be supported after that. Rather, Allah will debase and humiliate them.",
  59013:
      "You, O believers, are certainly more frightening in the hearts of the hypocrites and Jews than Allah. That is due to the intensity of their fear of you and the weakness of their fear of Allah, because they are people who do not comprehend or understand. If they had comprehended, they would have known that Allah is more deserving to be feared and terrified of, for He is the One who gave you reign over them.",
  59014:
      "The gathered Jews do not fight you, O believers, except in towns fortified with defensive walls or behind walls, for they cannot face you out of their cowardice. Their strife between themselves is strong due to the enmity between them. You think they are upon a single word and that their ranks are unified. The reality is that their hearts are divided and differ. That difference and enmity is because, indeed, they are not rational. If they had reason, they would have known the truth, followed it, and not differed regarding it.",
  59015:
      "The example of these Jews in regards to their disbelief and the calamity that befell them is what befell Mecca's polytheists not long ago, for they tasted the evil of their disbelief's consequences. So those who were killed were killed and those who were captured were captured on the day of Badr, and they have a painful torment awaiting them in the Afterlife.",
  59016:
      "The example of those listening to the hypocrites is like the example of the Devil when he adorns disbelief for humans. Then, when a human disbelieves because of the Devil's adornment of disbelief toward him, he [the Devil] says: Indeed, I am innocent of you because of your disbelief. Indeed, I fear Allah, Lord of the creation.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The connection of faith is not affected by the prolonging of time or the changing of place.\n2. The friendship of the hypocrites is a delusive friendship which disappears at times of difficulty.",
  59017:
      "The conclusion of Satan's matter and the humans who obeyed him is in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, remaining in it forever. That is the recompense that awaits them. It is the recompense of those who wronged themselves by transgressing Allah's bounds.",
  59018:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, take heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And a soul should ponder what it has put forward of righteous work for the Day of Resurrection and take heed of Allah. Indeed, Allah is well-informed of what you do. Nothing of your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  59019:
      "And do not be like those who forgot Allah by leaving off complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, so Allah made them forget their souls. Thus, they did not do what would save them from Allah's anger and His punishment. Those who forgot Allah and so did not comply with His commands and did not avoid His prohibitions are the ones outside Allah's obedience.",
  59020:
      "The people of the Fire are not equal to the people of Paradise. Rather, their recompense is different, just like their actions in the worldly life are different. The people of Paradise are the victors by attaining what they seek and are saved from what they fear.",
  59021:
      "If we sent down this Quran onto a mountain, you would have seen, O Messenger, that mountain, despite its firmness, lowly and breaking apart from the severity of [its] fear of Allah. [That is] due to what is in the Quran of deterring admonishments and severe threats. We give these examples to the people so they may work their minds and then accept reproval from what its verses contain of admonishments and morals.",
  59022:
      "He is Allah; there is no rightful object of worship besides Him, Knower of what is absent and what is present; nothing of that is hidden from Him. He is Vastly Merciful in the worldly life and Afterlife and bestows His mercy in both of them to whom He wills. His mercy encompasses all creation. He is the King, the One exalted and pure from any deficiency, free from every defect, the One who affirms the truth of His messengers with astonishing signs, the Observer over the actions of His slaves. He is the Mighty who none defeat, the Dominator who compels everything with His dominance, the Superior. Allah is vindicated and pure from what the polytheists associate with Him of idols and otherwise.",
  59023:
      "He is Allah; there is no rightful object of worship besides Him, Knower of what is absent and what is present; nothing of that is hidden from Him. He is Vastly Merciful in the worldly life and Afterlife and bestows His mercy in both of them to whom He wills. His mercy encompasses all creation. He is the King, the One exalted and pure from any deficiency, free from every defect, the One who affirms the truth of His messengers with astonishing signs, the Observer over the actions of His slaves. He is the Mighty who none defeat, the Dominator who compels everything with His dominance, the Superior. Allah is vindicated and pure from what the polytheists associate with Him of idols and otherwise.",
  59024:
      "He is Allah, the Creator who created everything, the one who brings things into existence, the Former of His creations as He wishes. To Him (may He be Exalted) belong the Excellent Names encompassing His lofty attributes. Whatever is in the heavens and the Earth exalts Him from every deficiency. He is the Mighty whom none defeat, the Wise in His creation, legislation, and predetermination.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory to take account of one’s soul in the world before it is taken to account on the Day of Judgement.\n2. Requital on the Day of Judgement will be according to one’s actions.\n3. The Qur’an has a great effect on the soul.\n4. It is obligatory to envision the greatness of the lofty attributes of Allah and His most beautiful names.",
  60000:
      "She Who is Tested (Surah Al-Mumtahanah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning the believers from allying with the disbelievers.\n•    Explanation:",
  60001:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, do not take My enemies and your enemies as allies by allying and exchanging affection with them. They have disbelieved in what has come to you at the hand of your Messenger of the religion. They expelled the Messenger from his home and likewise expelled you from your homes in Mecca, not observing any relation or tie of kinship, for nothing other than [the fact that] you believed in Allah, your Lord. If you go out for the sake of jihad (struggle) in My path, seeking my contentment, do not secretly give them the news of the Muslims as affection for them while I know what you hide of that and what you disclose. Nothing of that or anything else is hidden from Me. And whosoever makes such an alliance and mutual affection with the disbelievers has deviated from the middle of the road, gone astray from the truth, and become far from what is correct.",
  60002:
      "If they defeat you, they will show what they conceal in their hearts of enmity, extend their hands to you with harm and strikes, let loose their tongues in disparagement and denigration, and hope you disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger so that you may be like them.",
  60003:
      "Your kinship ties will never benefit you or your offspring if you ally with the disbelievers for their sake. On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will separate between you and admit the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of the Fire into the Fire, so you will be of no use to one another. Allah is watchful of your actions; none of them are hidden from Him (may He be Exalted) and He will soon requite you for them.",
  60004:
      "O believers, you have a beautiful example to follow in Abraham (peace be upon him) and the believers who were with him when they said to their disbelieving people: We have nothing to do with you and the idols you worship instead of Allah. We have disbelieved in the religion you are upon; enmity and hatred have become apparent between us and you until you believe in Allah alone and do not ascribe anyone as a partner to Him. So it is necessary for you to proclaim innocence from your disbelieving nation just like they did, except for the statement Abraham (peace be upon him) made to his father: I will surely seek forgiveness on your behalf from Allah. Do not follow him in that because it was before Abraham despaired of his father [ever believing]. It is therefore not allowed for a believer to seek forgiveness on behalf of a polytheist. You cannot prevent any punishment of Allah from yourself. O our Lord, upon You we rely in all our affairs, to You we return in repentance, and to You is our return on the Day of Resurrection.",
  60005:
      "O our Lord, do not make us a tribulation for those who disbelieved by giving them rule over us, so they would say: If they were on the truth, we would not have been given rule over them.Our Lord, forgive us our sins. Indeed, you are the Mighty whom none defeat, the Wise in Your creation, legislation, and predetermination.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is forbidden to intimately befriend the disbelievers.\n2. The disclose confidential information about the people of Islam to their enemies is a major sin.\n3. The enmity of the disbelievers is a deep-rooted enmity, in which intimately befriending them has no effect.\n4. It is prohibited to seek forgiveness on behalf of those who have died in the state of disbelief.",
  60006:
      "This beautiful example is only followed by those who hope for good from Allah in the worldly life and Hereafter. And whosoever turns away from this beautiful example, Allah is indeed free of need of His slaves, not requiring their obedience. He is the one extolled in every circumstance.",
  60007:
      "Perhaps Allah will cause love between you, O believers, and those whom you opposed of the disbelievers, where Allah would guide them to Islam so that they would be brothers to you in religion. Allah is able. He can turn their hearts to faith. Allah is forgiving to whoever repents of His slaves; merciful to them.",
  60008:
      "Allah does not prohibit you from those who have not fought you on account of your Islam and who have not expelled you from your home that you would give them fine treatment and be just between them by giving them their rights upon you. Allah loves those who are just to themselves, their families, and what they are in charge of.",
  60009:
      "Allah only forbids you from those who fought you because of your faith, expelled you from your homes, and assisted in your expulsion. He forbids you from allying with them. Whoever of you allies with them are those wronging their [own] souls by heading to the roads of destruction because of violating the command of Allah.",
  60010:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He has legislated, if the believing women come to you emigrating from the land of disbelief to the land of Islam, then test them in the truthfulness of their faith. Allah is more knowledgeable of their faith; nothing is hidden from Him of what their hearts envelop. So if you know them to be believers, after the test, according to what is apparent to you of their truthfulness, then do not send them back to their disbelieving husbands. It is not permissible for the believing women to marry disbelievers or the disbelievers to marry the believing women. And give their husbands what they expended for their dowries. There is no sin upon you, O believers, to marry them after their 'iddah (waiting period before a woman becomes permissible for another man) concludes if you give them their dowries. And whoever has a wife who disbelieves or apostates from Islam should not hold on to her due to the severance of their marriage by her disbelief. Ask the disbelievers for what you expended as dowries for your apostating wives, and let them ask what they expended as dowries for their wives who entered Islam. That which is cited, of returning the dowries from your side and their side, is the ruling of Allah. He (may He be Exalted) rules between you with what He wishes. And Allah is Omniscient of the states of His slaves and their actions; nothing of them is hidden from Him, and He is wise in what He legislates for His slaves.",
  60011:
      "And if it were supposed that some of your women would go out to the disbelievers as apostates and you sought their dowries from the disbelievers and they did not give it, then you were to gain spoils from the disbelievers, then provide the husbands whose wives left as apostates the like of what they expended as dowries. Take heed of Allah, whom you believe in, by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A Muslim must ask Allah for firmness, because hearts are between the two fingers of the Merciful and He turns them as He wishes, so that He turns them from disbelief to faith and from enmity to love.\n2. The difference in the law with respect to disbelievers who are at war and those at peace with the Muslims.\n3. The prohibition of marriage to a disbelieving woman, besides one from the people of the scripture, whether this is at the outset or during the course of the marriage. The prohibition of a Muslim woman being married to a disbelieving man whether this is at the outset or during the course of the marriage.",
  60012:
      "O Prophet, if the believing women come to you giving you their pledge, such as what occurred in the conquest of Mecca, that they would not associate anything as partners with Allah, but rather worship Him alone, and [pledge] that they would not steal, commit zina (unlawful sexual intercourse), kill their children following the custom of the people of the Age of Ignorance, ascribe their children from zina to their husbands, disobey you in what is proper, such as his prohibition from wailing, shaving, and tearing clothes [all in anguish of a death], then exchange the pledge with them and ask Allah for the forgiveness of their sins after pledging to you. Indeed, Allah is forgiving to those who repent from His slaves; merciful to them.",
  60013:
      "At the beginning of the surah, there was a warning against allying with Allah's enemies, and at the end, there is a warning against it as an affirmation of what preceded. Allah the Exalted states: \n O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, do not ally with a people whom Allah was angry with and who do not have certainty in the Afterlife. Rather, they despair of it, just like their despair of their dead returning to them, because they disbelieve in the Resurrection.",
  61000:
      "The Rank (Surah As-Saff)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nMotivating the believers to support the religion.\n•    Explanation:",
  61001:
      "All that is in the heavens and the Earth exalt Allah, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, from what does not befit Him. He is the Mighty who none defeat, the Wise in His creation, predetermination, and legislation.",
  61002:
      "O you who believe in Allah, why do you say: We did something, and in reality, you did not do it?! Just as one of them says, he fought with his sword and struck, while he did not fight with his sword nor strike.",
  61003:
      "Allah considers that abhorrent matter to be tremendous, that is, saying what you do not do. So it does not befit a believer that he be dishonest with Allah. His actions should affirm his words.",
  61004:
      "Indeed, Allah loves the believers who fight in His path, in pursuit of His contentment, as a row standing side by side as if they are a structure whose parts are fixed to one another.",
  61005:
      "After mentioning battle and praising the believers who joined forces to fight in His path, Allah mentions the defiance of the companions of Moses and Jesus towards their respective messengers as a warning to the believers against defying their Prophet. He states: \n And remember, O Messenger, when Moses (peace be upon him) said to his people: O my people, why do you harm me by violating my command while you know that I am indeed Allah's Messenger to you?! Then, when they leaned and deviated away from what he brought them of the truth, Allah inclined their hearts away from the truth and uprightness. Allah does not grant success to the truth to the people outside His obedience.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The legitimacy of pledging allegiance to the person in charge to hear and obey and to be mindful of Allah.\n2. Obedience to the person in charge is only in acceptable matters.\n3. An evil end usually serves as a result of those whose actions betray their words.",
  61006:
      "And remember, O Messenger, when Jesus, son of Mary (peace be upon him) said: O Israelites, indeed, I am Allah's Messenger. He sent me to you affirming what was sent down before me of the Torah, so I am not an innovation among the messengers, and [sent me] conveying the good news of a messenger coming after me. His name is Ahmad. Then, when Jesus came with proofs indicating his truthfulness, they said: This is clear magic, so we will not follow him.",
  61007:
      "And no one is more wrongful than the one who fabricates falsehood about Allah where he would make rivals [with Allah], worshipping them instead of Him, while he is called to Islam, the religion of pure tawheed (singular worship) of Allah. Allah does not grant success to what contains their guidance and virtue to the people wronging themselves with shirk (associating partners) [with Allah] and acts of disobedience.",
  61008:
      "These liars wish to extinguish the light of Allah with what is uttered by them of corrupt words and besmearing the truth. Allah will complete His light against their wishes by making His religion prominent from the east to the west of the Earth and elevating His word.",
  61009:
      "Allah is the One who sent His Messenger Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم with the religion of Islam, the religion of guidance and direction to good, beneficial knowledge and righteous action, in order to raise it above all religions despite the wishes of the polytheists who hate that it be established on the Earth.",
  61010:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, should I direct and guide you to a profitable trade that would save you from a painful torment?",
  61011:
      "This profitable trade is that you believe in Allah and His Messenger and strive in His path (may He be Exalted) by spending your wealth and expending your souls in pursuit of His contentment. That mentioned action is good for you, if you know, so hasten to it.",
  61012:
      "And the profit of this trade is that Allah will forgive you your sins, enter you into gardens in which rivers flow under its castles and trees, and enter you into fine palaces in gardens of settlement, never displaced from them. That mentioned reward is the great victory that no victory comes close to.",
  61013:
      "And from the profit of this trade is another feature you love, and it is given in advance in the worldly life. It is that Allah would support you against your enemy and a conquest near at hand. He will guide you to it, which is the conquest of Mecca and others. Inform, O Messenger, the believers of what pleases them of support in the worldly life and attaining Paradise in the Hereafter.",
  61014:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, be the supporters of Allah by supporting His religion, which your Messenger came with like the support of the Disciples when Jesus (peace be upon him) said: Who are my supporters to Allah?So they swiftly replied to him: We are the supporters of Allah.So, a group of the Israelites believed in Jesus (peace be upon him), and another group disbelieved in him. Then we aided those who believed in Jesus against those who disbelieved in him, so they became triumphant over them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The previous messages brought the good news of our prophet (peace be upon him).\n2. Empowering the religion is a divine practice.\n3. Faith and striving in Allah’s path are means to enter Paradise.\n4. The believer’s recompense from Allah, is sometimes quick and sometimes delayed.",
  62000:
      "Friday (Surah Al-Jumu'ah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe privilege and virtue of this nation due to its Messenger. Enumerating the virtue of Friday.\n•    Explanation:",
  62001:
      "All creation in the heavens and the Earth exalt Allah from everything that does not befit Him from attributes of deficiency and sanctify Him. He alone is the sole King of the dominion, exalted above every deficiency, the Mighty whom none defeat, the Wise in His creation, legislation, and predetermination.",
  62002:
      "He is the One who sent among the Arabs who do not read nor write a Messenger of their kind, reciting upon them the verses which He sent down to him, purifying them of disbelief and poor character, and teaching them the Quran and sunnah (the way of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم). And indeed, before he was sent to them, they were in misguidance from the clear truth when they would worship idols, spill blood, and sever kinship ties.",
  62003:
      "And He sent this Messenger to other people among the Arabs and others who have not yet come, and they will come. He is the Mighty whom none defeat, the Wise in His creation, legislation, and predetermination.",
  62004:
      "That which was mentioned of sending the Messenger to the Arabs and others is the favor of Allah; He bestows it to whom He wills. Allah possesses great benevolence, and from His great benevolence is Him sending the Messenger of this nation to all people.",
  62005:
      "Allah reminds us of the blessings He has bestowed upon us, such as sending the Messenger and revealing the Quran. He then mentions how some of Moses's followers turned away from acting upon the Torah as a warning for us to avoid following their footsteps. Allah states: \n The example of the Jews, who were obliged to uphold what is in the Torah and then deserted what they were obliged with, is like the example of a donkey carrying large books, not knowing what is carried on it: are they books or something else? Atrocious is the example of the people who rejected the verses of Allah. Allah does not grant success in attaining the truth to the unjust people.",
  62006:
      "Say, O Messenger: O you have remained on Judaism after its alteration, if you claim that you are indeed the allies of Allah, designating you with alliance in exclusion of the rest of the people, then hope for death so that He may hasten for you what He designated you with, according to what you claim, of honor if you are truthful in what you claim about being the allies of Allah in exclusion of the rest of the people.",
  62007:
      "And they will never hope for death. Rather, they hope for eternity in the worldly life because of what they did of disbelief, acts of disobedience, injustice, distorting the Torah, and replacing it. Allah is Omniscient of the unjust. Nothing of their deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  62008:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those Jews: Indeed, death, which you flee from, will meet you no matter what, whether hastened or delayed. Then on the Day of Resurrection, you will be returned to Allah, Knower of what is present and what is absent; nothing of them is hidden from Him. Then He will inform you of what you used to do in the worldly life and recompense you accordingly.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The state of the Arabs prior to Islam was in ignorance and loss.\n2. The mission of our prophet (peace be upon him) included all men and jinn.\n3. Refutation of the claim made by the Jews that they are Allah’s friends, by challenging them to desire for death if they are true in their claim.",
  62009:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, if the mu'adhin (caller to prayer) calls to the prayer of Friday after the speaker ascends the pulpit, then hurry to the mosques to attend the sermon and prayer and leave off selling so that it does not busy you from obedience. That command to go [to the sermon and prayer] and leave off selling after the call of the Friday prayer is better for you, O believers, if you knew that. So conform to what Allah commanded you.",
  62010:
      "Then, if you finish the Friday prayer, disperse in the land, searching for permissible income and fulfilling your needs. Ask for Allah's favor through permissible income and profit. Remember Allah with much remembrance as you search for provision. Do not let your search for provision cause you to forget Allah's remembrance. [All that] in hopes of attaining what you love and salvation from what you flee.",
  62011:
      "And if some Muslims eye trade or leisure, they disperse, going out to them and leaving you, O Messenger, standing on the pulpit. Say, O Messenger: What is with Allah of reward for righteous action is better than the trade and leisure you went out to, and Allah is the best of providers.",
  63000:
      "The Hypocrites (Surah Al-Munafiqoon)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the reality of hypocrites and warning against them.\n•    Explanation:",
  63001:
      "When the hypocrites, who outwardly profess Islam and inwardly conceal disbelief, come to your gathering, O Messenger, they say: We testify that you are truly Allah's Messenger. Allah testifies that the hypocrites are lying in their claim that they testify from the depth of their hearts that you are His Messenger.",
  63002:
      "They made their oaths, which they swear by, claiming faith as a screen and protection for them from being killed and captured. They divert people from faith with what they cast of doubt and delving into bad news and tribulations. Indeed, their actions of hypocrisy and false oaths were atrocious.",
  63003:
      "That is because they believed hypocritically [i.e., concealing disbelief], and faith did not reach their hearts. Then they secretly disbelieved in Allah, so He sealed their hearts because of their disbelief; therefore, faith does not enter them. Then, because of that seal, they do not comprehend what is beneficial and virtuous for them.",
  63004:
      "And if you see them, O observer, their states and appearances impress you because of the beauty and delight they possess. If they speak, you listen to their speech due to the eloquence it has. In your gathering, O Messenger, it is as if they are propped logs, not understanding or grasping anything. They think every voice is targeting them due to the cowardice within them. They are truly the enemy, so take caution of them, O Messenger, that they spread your secrets or plot a scheme against you. Allah cursed them. How do they turn from faith with the clarity of its evidence and clearness of its proofs?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The obligation of rushing to the Friday prayer after the call.\n2. The prohibition of trading after the second call on the day of Friday.",
  63005:
      "And if it is said to these hypocrites: Come to Allah's Messenger apologizing for what was uttered from you, and he will request forgiveness for you from Allah for your sins,they would lean their heads in mockery and ridicule, and you would see them avoiding what they were commanded while being too arrogant to accept the truth and submit to it.",
  63006:
      "O Messenger, it is the same whether you request the forgiveness of their sins or not. Allah will not forgive them for their sins. Indeed, Allah does not grant success to the people outside His obedience, adamant upon their disobedience.",
  63007:
      "They are the ones who say: Do not spend your wealth on those with Allah's Messenger from the poor and Bedouins around Medina so that they disperse from him. To Allah alone belong the treasures of the heavens and the treasures of the Earth. He provides them for whom He wills among His slaves. However, the hypocrites do not know that the treasures of provision are in His hand; may He be Exalted.",
  63008:
      "Their head, Abdullah bin Ubay, says: If we return to Medina, the more mighty, and they are my people and I, shall expel the lowly from it, and they are Muhammad and his companions. Might is only for Allah, His Messenger, and the believers, and it is not for Abdullah bin Ubay and his companions. However, the hypocrites do not know that might is for Allah, His Messenger, and the believers.",
  63009:
      "After mentioning the efforts of hypocrites to be stingy in spending to prevent people from Allah's path, Allah warns the believers against that and commands them to spend in His cause, stating: \n O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, let not your wealth nor your children busy you from prayer and other obligations of Islam. Whosoever's wealth and children busy him from what Allah obligated upon him of prayer or otherwise are truly the losers who will have lost their souls and families on the Day of Resurrection.",
  63010:
      "And spend from what Allah provided you with of wealth before death comes to one of you, then he would say to his Lord: My Lord, would you not delay me for a short while. Then I would donate from my wealth in the way of Allah and be from the righteous slaves of Allah whose deeds were good.",
  63011:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) will not delay a soul if its conclusion comes and its lifetime ends. Allah is well-informed of what you do. Nothing of your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly. If they are good, then good, and if evil, then evil.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Turning away from advice and being arrogant are attributes of the hypocrites.\n2. Honour is for Allah, His messenger and the believers and humiliation is for their enemies.\n3. The danger of wealth and children is they preoccupy one from Allah’s remembrance.\n4. The obligation of rushing to do good deeds before death.",
  64000:
      "Mutual Fraud (Surah At-Taghabun)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning against matters that will lead to regret and detriment on the Day of Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  64001:
      "All creation in the heavens and the Earth exalt Allah and declare Him free of what does not befit Him of attributes of deficiency. The dominion is His alone, so there is no king besides Him. The best of praise is due to Him, and He is Omnipotent over everything; nothing hinders Him.",
  64002:
      "He is the One who created you, O people. Then some of you are disbelievers in Him, their destination is the Fire, and some of you are believers in Him, their destination is Paradise. Allah sees what you do; nothing of your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense you accordingly.",
  64003:
      "He created the heavens and the Earth with a true purpose and did not create them in vain. He fashioned you, O people, so He made your forms excellent as benevolence and grace from Him. If He wished, He would have certainly made them atrocious. To Him alone is the return on the Day of Resurrection. Then He will recompense you based on your deeds. If good, then good, and if evil, then evil.",
  64004:
      "He knows what is in the heavens and the Earth, and He knows what you hide of deeds and what you disclose. Allah is knowledgeable of what is in the breasts of good or evil. Nothing from that is hidden from Him.",
  64005:
      "Has not the news of the rejecting nations before you reached you, O polytheists, such as the people of Noah, 'Ād, Thamūd, and others? They tasted the punishment of the disbelief they were upon in the worldly life, and they have a painful torment in the Hereafter. Nay, that has reached you, so take a lesson from what their matter led to, then repent to Allah before what happened to them happens to you.",
  64006:
      "That torment only afflicted them because their messengers would come to them from Allah with clear arguments and manifest proofs, and then they said in objection to the messengers being of humanity: Would humans guide us to the truth?!So they disbelieved and turned away from faith in them, which did not harm Allah at all. He is free of the need for their faith and obedience. That is because their obedience does not increase anything for Him. Allah is self-sufficient, not needing any of His slaves, and praised in His statements and actions. So they disbelieved and turned away from faith in them, then they did not harm Allah at all. He was free of need for their faith and obedience. That is because their obedience does not increase anything for Him. Allah is self-sufficient, not needing any of His slaves, and praised in His statements and actions.",
  64007:
      "Those who disbelieved in Allah claim that Allah will not resurrect them [to be] living after their death. Say, O Messenger, to these deniers of the Resurrection: Nay, by my Lord, you will surely be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection. Then you will be informed of what you did in the worldly life. That Resurrection is easy for Allah, for He initially created you, so He is able to resurrect you [to be] living after your death for account and recompense.",
  64008:
      "So believe, O people, in Allah, His Messenger, and the Quran We sent down upon our Messenger. Allah is aware of what you do. Nothing of your deeds is hidden from Him, and He will recompense accordingly.",
  64009:
      "Remember, O Messenger, the day when Allah will gather you for the Day of Resurrection to give you the recompense for your actions. That is the day when the loss of the disbelievers will become clear, as the believers will inherit the homes in Paradise of the people of the Fire, and the people of the Fire will inherit the homes in the Fire of the people of Paradise. Those who have faith in Allah and do righteous deeds, Allah will remit their sins from them and enter them into gardens, under the palaces and trees of which rivers flow, to live in them forever and never to come out, the bliss of which will not end. That which they attained is the best form of success, which no other success can come close to.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The division of people into the wretched and the fortunate.\n2. Faith and good deeds are means to attaining success in the world and the afterlife.",
  64010:
      "Those who disbelieve in Allah and reject Our verses, which We sent down to Our Messenger are the people of the Fire, remaining in it eternally. Their destination is an atrocious one.",
  64011:
      "No calamity befell anyone in their self, wealth or children except by the decree of Allah and His predetermination. And whoever believes in Allah, His decree, and His predetermination, Allah gives their heart success by submission to His command and contentment with His decree. Allah is knowledgeable of everything. Nothing is hidden from Him.",
  64012:
      "Obey Allah and obey His Messenger. Then if you turn away from what His Messenger came to you with, the sin of that turning away is on you. Nothing is incumbent upon Our Messenger except informing what We commanded him to inform you of, and he has informed you of that.",
  64013:
      "Allah is the rightful object of worship. There is no rightful object of worship besides Him. Let the believers rely upon Allah alone in all their affairs.",
  64014:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, indeed, some of your spouses and children are enemies to you because they busy you from the remembrance of Allah and jihad (struggle) in His path, and they deter you. So beware of them affecting you. And if you pardon their blunders and turn away and conceal them, then Allah will forgive your sins and show you mercy. The recompense is according to the type of action.",
  64015:
      "Your wealth and children are only a tribulation and test for you, for they may prompt you towards prohibited income and forsaking obedience to Allah. Allah has a great reward for those who give precedence to His obedience over the obedience of children and their preoccupation with wealth. This great reward is Paradise.",
  64016:
      "So take heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions as much as you can find a means to obey Him. And listen and obey Allah and His Messenger, and expend your wealth, which Allah provided you, in the avenues of good. Whomsoever Allah protects from his soul's craving are the ones attaining what they seek and saved from what they flee.",
  64017:
      "If you loan Allah a fine loan by spending from your wealth in His path, He will multiply your reward by making the good deed [from] ten times its like to seven hundred times to many multiples, and He will overlook your sins. Allah is thankful, giving much reward for little action and forbearing, not hastening punishment.",
  64018:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) is the knower of what is absent and what is present, nothing of that is hidden from Him, the Mighty whom none defeat, the Wise in His creation, legislation, and predetermination.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Belief in predestination is one of the pillars of faith.\n2. The task of the messengers is to convey Allah’s message. Guidance is in Allah’s hands.\n3. The need to be aware of the temptation of wealth and family.\n4. Imposition of duties are within the limits of the capacity of the one on whom they are imposed.\n5. The danger of innate greed.\n6. Reward is multiplied for those who spend in Allah’s path.",
  65000:
      "Divorce (Surah At-Talaq)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining the rulings pertaining to divorce, respecting its boundaries, and the fruits of heedfulness.\n•    Explanation:",
  65001:
      "O Prophet, if you or any of the men from your nation intend to divorce your wives, then he should issue a divorce to her, considering her 'iddah (waiting period until she is permissible for another man). That is that the divorce should be issued during a period of purity between two separate menses, in which he has not had sexual relations with her. Also, keep track of the 'iddah, so that you are able to take your wives back within it if you intend to do so. And be mindful of Allah by fulfilling His commands and refraining from the things He has not allowed; do not force your divorced wives out of the homes they live in until their 'iddah finishes, except if they commit an obvious shameful act like adultery. Those are the limits of Allah He has set for His slaves; whoever trespasses the limits of Allah has, indeed, oppressed himself by placing himself in a situation of doom because of disobeying his Lord. O divorcée, you do not know; perhaps Allah may create a longing in the heart of the spouse, and he may take his wife back.",
  65002:
      "So if they approach the end of their 'iddah then take them back based on desire and excellent companionship or abstain from taking them back until they finish their 'iddah so they would control their own matter while [you are] giving them their rights. And if you wished to take them back or separate from them, then have two just ones among you witness to cut off [any] dispute. And come forth, O witnesses, with the testimony seeking the Face of Allah. He who believes in Allah and the Day of Resurrection is reminded by that which was mentioned of rulings because he is who will benefit by reminder and admonition. Whoever takes heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, Allah will make a way out for him for all that he falls into of strain and difficulty.",
  65003:
      "And He will provide Him from where he did not imagine and would not be in his deliberation. Whosoever relies on Allah in his affairs, then He suffices him. Indeed, Allah executes his commands. Nothing hinders Him, and nothing escapes Him. Allah has set an interval for everything at which they end. Hence, for adversity, there is an interval, and for ease, there is an interval. Neither is perpetual for the human being.",
  65004:
      "[Regarding] the divorced women who despair of menstruation due to their old age, if you have doubted the manner of their 'iddah, then their 'iddah is three months. And for those who have not reached the age of menstruation due to their youth, their 'iddah is likewise three months. And [as for] the pregnant women, the end of their 'iddah from divorce or death [of the husband] is when they give birth to what they carry. Whosoever takes heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, Allah will facilitate his affairs and make every arduous matter easy for him.",
  65005:
      "That which was mentioned of the rulings of divorce, taking back [the wife after divorce], and 'iddah is the ruling of Allah. He sent it down to you, O believers, to act upon it. Whoever takes heed of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, He will wipe out his misdeeds, which he carried out, and grant him a great reward in the Hereafter. It is entering Paradise and achieving the delight that is not [ever] exhausted.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Address to the Prophet (peace be upon him) is an address to his nation also, as long as there is no exclusivity established.\n2. It is obligatory to provide shelter and expenses to wife one have issued a revocable divorce to.\n3. It is only possible to revoke a revocable divorce before the waiting period finishes.\n4. It is advisable to appoint witnesses to prevent disputes.\n5. The waiting period of a divorced woman with whom marriage has been consummated is three months is she does not menstruate due to old or young age.\n6. The waiting period of a pregnant woman who has either been divorced or widowed, is until she gives birth.\n7. There are numerous benefits of Allah-consciousness, and it is a great quality.",
  65006:
      "After mentioning the ruling of divorce and raj'ah (taking back the divorcee during her waiting period), Allah legislates the obligation of lodging and expenses for divorced women, stating: \n Have the divorcées reside, O husbands, where you reside according to your capacity, so Allah does not burden you with other than that. Do not harm them in spending, residence, or otherwise in hopes of straining them. And if the divorced women are pregnant, spend on them until they deliver what they carry. Then, if they nurse your children for you, give them the wage of their nursing and refer to what is customary regarding the wage. Then, if the husband is frugal about what the wife wants of wages and she becomes miserly such that she is not content except with what she wants, then let the father employ a different wet nurse to nurse his child.",
  65007:
      "Let he who has abundance in wealth spend on his divorcée and child from his abundance. And whosoever is constrained in his provision, then let him spend from what Allah gave him of it. Allah does not burden a soul except that which He granted it, so He does not burden beyond it nor more than the soul can bear. After his constrained state and its hardship, Allah will bring about abundance and self-sufficiency.",
  65008:
      "After mentioning several commands, Allah warns against turning away from those commands and says that the result would be terrible. He states: \n And how many were the towns We punished severely for disobeying their Lord and His messengers (may peace be upon them)! We held them gravely accountable for their wrongdoings and afflicted them with a vicious torment in this world and in the Hereafter.",
  65009:
      "So they tasted the punishment of their evil deeds, and their end was loss in the worldly life and Hereafter.",
  65010:
      "Allah prepared an intense torment for them. So take heed of Allah, O people of reason who have believed in Allah and His Messenger, by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions such that what happened to them does not happen to you. Allah has sent down to you a reminder that reminds you of the evil consequence of disobeying Him and the excellent result of obeying Him.",
  65011:
      "This reminder is a Messenger from Him who recites the clarifying verses of Allah upon you, with no confusion in them, in the hopes of purging those who believed in Allah, affirmed the truth of His Messenger and did righteous actions from the darknesses of misguidance to the light of guidance. And whosoever believes in Allah and does righteous action, Allah will enter him into gardens where rivers flow beneath its palaces and trees, remaining in it forever. Allah has made His provision magnificent, where He has entered him into a garden whose delights do not cease.",
  65012:
      "Allah is the One who created seven heavens and created seven earths like His creation of seven heavens. Allah's command of manifestation and legislation descends between them in the hopes that you know Allah is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability. And that indeed He (may He be Exalted) has encompassed everything in terms of knowledge, so nothing in the heavens nor the Earth is hidden from Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory to provide shelter and expenses for a woman issued a revocable divorce, as long as she remains in her waiting period. It is also obligatory for a pregnant divorcee.\n2. There is no obligation upon a divorced woman who has given birth to breastfeed the child.\n3. The burden of obligation is only issued according to one’s capability.\n4. It is established that there are seven earths.",
  66000:
      "Prohibition (Surah At-Tahreem)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nCall to establish households upon venerating Allah's limits and prioritizing His contentment alone.\n•    Explanation:",
  66001:
      "O Messenger, why do you make impermissible that which Allah has made permissible for you from seeking pleasure with your slave girl Mariah, wanting to please your wives in doing so after they expressed protective jealousy over her? Allah is Forgiving towards you and is Merciful to you.",
  66002:
      "Allah has legislated for you the nullification of your oaths through expiation if you find that which is better than them or if you broke them. Allah is your Supporter; He is Omniscient of your conditions and what benefits you, and He is All-Wise in His legislation and predetermination.",
  66003:
      "And remember when the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم mentioned something only to Hafsah, and that was that he would never again go close to his slave, Maria. So after Hafsah informed Aisha of the news, and Allah informed His Messenger of his secret having been spread, he reprimanded Hafsah and told her part of what she had said, not mentioning the other part. So she asked him: Who informed you of this? He replied: The Omniscient and All-Aware of every hidden thing informed me of it.",
  66004:
      "It is necessary that you both seek repentance because your hearts had leaned to loving what Allah's Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم disdains from avoiding his slave girl and forbidding her from himself. If you insist on resuming your act of ruining relationships for him, then indeed, Allah is his ally and supporter. Likewise, Gabriel and the best believers are his allies and supporters. And the angels, after the support of Allah for him, are his helpers and supporters against whoever hurts him.",
  66005:
      "Perhaps if His Prophet divorced you, His Lord (may He be Exalted) would exchange him wives better than you, complying with His commands, believers in Him and His Messenger, being obedient to Allah, repentant of their sins, worshipping their Lord, fasting, previously married women and virgins, no one having had intercourse with them before him. However, he did not divorce them.",
  66006:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, prepare protection for yourselves and your families from a fire ignited with people and stones. Upon this Fire are angels who are harsh and severe upon whoever enters it. They do not disobey the command of Allah when He commands them, and they do what He commands them without delay or neglect.",
  66007:
      "It is said to the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection: O you who have disbelieved in Allah, do not present excuses today for what you were upon of disbelief and acts of disobedience, for your excuses will not be accepted. On this Day, you are but recompensed for what you used to do in the worldly life of disbelief in Allah and rejecting His Messengers.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Expiation for oaths has been legislated.\n2. Allah mentions the status of the Prophet (peace be upon him) according to his Lord, and His defending him.\n3. A believer is responsible for himself and his family.",
  66008:
      "O you who believe in Allah and act by what He legislated for them, repent to Allah from your sins with true repentance. Perhaps your Lord will wipe out your evil deeds from you and enter you into gardens in which rivers flow beneath its palaces on the Day of Resurrection, the Day Allah will not debase the Prophet nor those who believed with Him by entering them into the Fire. Their light goes before them, and on their rights [as they are] on the Sirat (the bridge over the Fire), they will say: O our Lord, make our light complete until we reach Paradise, so we not be like the hypocrites whose lights are extinguished on the Sirat, and forgive us our sins. Indeed, you are Omnipotent over everything, so You are unhindered from completing our light and pardoning our sins.",
  66009:
      "O Messenger, struggle against the disbelievers by sword, and the hypocrites by tongue, and upholding the hudood (legislated punishments). Be severe with them until they hold you in awe. Their refuge that they shelter in on the Day of Resurrection is Hell, and their destination that they return to is a terrible one.",
  66010:
      "Allah gives an example of those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers, in that their relationship with the believers does not benefit, by giving the example of the case of the wives of two prophets among the prophets of Allah: Noah and Lot, peace be upon them. For they were two wives of two righteous slaves, then they betrayed their husbands by what they were upon of deterring from the way of Allah and supporting the people of disbelief from their communities. So them being the wives to these two righteous slaves did not benefit them, and it was said to them: Enter the Fire along with those entering it of the disbelievers and the wicked.",
  66011:
      "And Allah gave an example of those who believe in Allah and His messengers, in that their relationship to the disbelievers does not hurt them nor affect them so long as they are upright on the truth, by giving the example of the case of Pharoah's wife when she said: O my Lord, build a house for me near you in Paradise, and save me from the coercion of Pharoah, his authority, and his evil actions. And save me from those wronging themselves by following him in his transgression and wrongdoing.",
  66012:
      "And Allah gave an example of those who believe in Allah and His messengers, in the case of Mary, daughter of 'Imran, who guarded her private parts from zina (unlawful sexual intercourse), so Allah commanded Gabriel to blow in them so she became pregnant with Jesus, son of Mary, without a father, by the power of Allah. She affirmed the legislation of Allah, His books sent down upon His messengers, and was among those obedient to Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Sincere repentance is a means of every goodness.\n2. Relationships through allegiance or blood will not benefit on the Day of Judgement if there is a difference in religion.\n3. Chastity and keeping far away from suspicion are among the qualities of pious believing women.",
  67000:
      "The Dominion (Surah Al-Mulk)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nIllustrating the perfection of Allah's dominion such that it inspires fear and awe of Him and warning of His punishment.\n•    Explanation:",
  67001:
      "Allah's vast goodness, the One who solely possesses the dominion, is magnified and abundant. He is Omnipotent over everything; nothing is beyond His capability.",
  67002:
      "The One who created death and created life to test which of you, O people, is better in action. He is the Almighty whom no one can defeat, the Forgiver of the sins of those who repented among His slaves.",
  67003:
      "The One who created seven heavens; each heaven is a layer above the previous one without contact between heaven and heaven. You will not witness, O observer, any discrepancy or unsuitability in what Allah created. So look again: Do you see splitting or fracturing? You will never see that. You will only see a perfected, masterful creation.",
  67004:
      "Then, look again, time after time; your eyesight will return lowly, exhausted, and will cease looking, having not seen any defect or fault in the creation of the sky.",
  67005:
      "And most verily, We adorned the nearest heaven to the Earth with illuminating stars, and We made those stars flames with which the devils who eavesdrop are repelled such that they burn them. And We have prepared for them the blazing fire in the Hereafter.",
  67006:
      "And for those who disbelieve in their Lord, there is the torment of the kindled fire on the Day of Resurrection. Evil is the place of return that they return to.",
  67007:
      "When they are thrown into the Fire, they will hear an ugly, intense sound as it boils, like the boiling of a boiler.",
  67008:
      "Its parts almost separate from each other and become distinct due to the intensity of its fury upon those who enter it. Each time a wave of its disbelieving people is thrown into it, the angels appointed over it will ask them in rebuke: Did not a Messenger come to you in the worldly life, frightening you of the torment of Allah?",
  67009:
      "The disbelievers will say: Yes, a messenger came to us to frighten us of the torment of Allah, so we rejected him and told him: Allah did not send revelation. You messengers are just in great misguidance from the truth.",
  67010:
      "And the disbelievers will say: If we had been listening with a listening that is beneficial or reasoning with the reason of who distinguishes the truth from the falsehood, we would not be amongst the people of the Fire. Rather, we would have believed in the messengers, affirmed the truth of what they came with, and been among the companions of Paradise.",
  67011:
      "They confessed against themselves about disbelief and rejection, so they deserved the Fire. So away with the people of the Fire.",
  67012:
      "After mentioning the traits of the people of disbelief and their recompense, Allah proceeds to mention the traits of the people of belief and their recompense. He states: \n Indeed, those who fear Allah in private have forgiveness for their sins. And they have a great reward, which is Paradise.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah created death and life to test the actions of His servants.\n2. Allah’s creation is free of any faults; it is perfect.\n3. Hell will be furious with the disbelievers and angry, in protective jealousy for Allah may He be glorified.\n4. Confession is a clear evidence against the confessor.",
  67013:
      "O people, speak secretly or openly, for Allah knows it. Indeed, He, Immaculate is He, is knowledgeable of what is in the hearts of His slaves; nothing from that is hidden from Him.",
  67014:
      "Does the One who created all creation not know what is secret and what is more concealed than what is secret?! He is The Subtle with His slaves, The Aware of their affairs; nothing of them is hidden from Him.",
  67015:
      "He is the One who made the Earth soft and easy for you to live on, so traverse its sides and borders and eat from His provision that He prepared for you within it. To Him alone is your resurrection for accountability and requital.",
  67016:
      "Do you feel safe from Allah, who is in the sky causing the Earth to split beneath you, just as He caused it to split beneath Qarun after it was easy and subdued for living upon, then it will quake with you after its stillness?!",
  67017:
      "Or do you feel safe from Allah, who is in the sky, sending down stones upon you from the sky just like He sent them upon the people of Lot? Then you will know My warning to you when you see My punishment, but you will not benefit from it after seeing the torment.",
  67018:
      "And most verily, the nations that came before these polytheists denied, so the torment of Allah descended upon them when they insisted on their disbelief and rejection, so how was My reprimand upon them? Verily, it was a severe reprimand.",
  67019:
      "Do these rejectors not see how the birds above them as they fly spread their wings in the air at times and close them upon themselves at other times? Nothing keeps them from falling to the Earth except Allah. Indeed, He sees everything; nothing is hidden from Him.",
  67020:
      "There is no army for you, O disbelievers, that can prevent you from the torment of Allah if He wishes to torment you. The disbelievers are but deluded; the Devil tricked them, so they were deceived by him.",
  67021:
      "And no one will provide for you if Allah prevents His provision from reaching you. Rather, the crux is that the disbelievers have persisted in argumentativeness, arrogance, and refraining from the truth.",
  67022:
      "So is the one who walks falling on his face, landing upon it, and is a polytheist, more guided, or the believer who walks straight on a straight path?",
  67023:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these rejecting polytheists: Allah is the One who created you and made for you ears you hear with, eyes you see with, and hearts you reason with. Little do you thank Him for the favors He has bestowed upon you.",
  67024:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these rejecting polytheists: Allah is the One who dispersed you throughout the Earth and spread you in it, not your idols, which do not create anything. To Him alone, on the Day of Resurrection, will you be gathered for account and requital, not to your idols. So fear Him and worship Him alone.",
  67025:
      "And the rejectors of the resurrection, considering it far-fetched, say: O Muhammad, when will this promise that you and your companions promised us to occur come if you are truthful in your claim that it is coming?!",
  67026:
      "Say, O Messenger: The knowledge of the Hour is only with Allah. No one knows when it will happen except Him. I am only a clear warner in my warning to you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah is aware of what the hearts of His servants conceal.\n2. Disbelief and sins are causes of the punishment of Allah in the world and the afterlife.\n3. Disbelief in Allah is darkness and confusion, while faith in Him is light and guidance.\n4. The knowledge of the hour is only with Allah alone.",
  67027:
      "So when the promise inflicts them, and they see the torment close to them on the Day of Resurrection, the faces of those who disbelieved in Allah will change by blackening. It will be said to them: This is what you used to request and hasten in the worldly life.",
  67028:
      "O Messenger, reprimand these rejecting polytheists by telling them: If Allah took my life and the life of the believers that are with me or had mercy on us by delaying our demise, then who will save the disbelievers from a painful punishment? No one will save them.",
  67029:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: He is The Vastly Merciful who invites you to worship Him alone. We have believed in Him, and upon Him alone have we relied in our affairs. So you will soon know, inescapably, who is in clear deviance and who is on a straight path.",
  67030:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists: Tell me, if the water you drink from were to become sunken into the Earth, making you unable to reach it, who would bring you abundant flowing water? No one other than Allah.",
  68000:
      "The Pen (Surah Al-Qalam)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAllah's (may He be Exalted and Transcendent) testimony of the Prophet's صلى الله عليه وسلم exemplary character, defense of him, and making him steadfast.\n•    Explanation:",
  68001:
      "Nūn – The discussion on its counterparts preceded the beginning of Surah Al-Baqarah. Allah swore by the Pen and whatever the people write with their pens.",
  68002:
      "O Messenger, you are not a madman due to the prophethood Allah has bestowed upon you. Rather, you are free of the madness the polytheists accused you of.",
  68003:
      "You will definitely be rewarded endlessly for what you suffer by carrying this message to the people without reminding them of your favors upon them.",
  68004:
      "And indeed, you are certainly upon the great character that the Quran has come with, so you embody what is in it in the most comprehensive manner.",
  68005: "So you will soon see, and these deniers will see.",
  68006:
      "When the truth is revealed, it will be clear in which of you is the madness.",
  68007:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, knows who has strayed from His path, and He is most knowledgeable of the ones guided to it. So He knows that they are indeed the ones who have deviated from it and that you, indeed, are the one who guides to it.",
  68008: "So, O Messenger, do not obey those rejecting what you have brought.",
  68009:
      "They wish that you were soft and gentle with them at the cost of the religion, so they are soft and gentle with you.",
  68010:
      "And do not obey every lowly person who is abundant in taking oaths with falsehood,",
  68011:
      "Abundant in backbiting people, abundant in carrying gossip between them to break up their relations,",
  68012:
      "Abundant in preventing good, transgressing against the people in their wealth, dignity, and souls; abundant in sins and acts of disobedience.",
  68013: "Harsh, hard, ascribed without relation among his people, adopted,",
  68014:
      "Because he was a person with wealth and children, he became arrogantly unaccepting of faith in Allah and His Messenger.",
  68015:
      "When Our verses are read to him, he says: This what is written from the fables of the earlier generations.",
  68016:
      "We will place a mark on his nose, which will disfigure and remain with him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Messenger (peace be upon him) is an embodiment of the character of the Qur’an.\n2. The traits of the disbelievers are blameworthy traits. It is obligatory upon a believer to distance himself from them, and from following anyone with them.",
  68017:
      "Indeed, We have tested these polytheists with drought and hunger, just as We tested the people of the garden when they swore that they would surely harvest its fruits in the morning, hastening so that no poor person would eat from them.",
  68018:
      "And they did not make an exception in their oath by saying: If Allah wills.",
  68019:
      "So Allah sent a fire to it, and it consumed it while its owners were asleep, unable to fend off the fire from it.",
  68020: "So it became black like a dark night.",
  68021: "So they called each other in the morning,",
  68022:
      "Saying: Leave early to your crop before the destitute arrive if you are to pluck its fruits.",
  68023:
      "So they made their way to their crop quickly, talking to each other in a hushed voice.",
  68024:
      "Saying to each other: No needy person should enter the garden upon you today.",
  68025:
      "And they went at the start of the morning, determined to forbid their fruits, claiming they could do so.",
  68026:
      "Then, when they saw them burnt, they said to each other: Surely, we have lost the way there.",
  68027:
      "[No,] rather, we are prohibited from plucking its fruits by what came about from us resolving to prohibit the needy from it.",
  68028:
      "The best of them said: Did I not tell you, when you resolved on what you resolved upon of prohibiting the needy from it: Will you not exalt Allah and repent to Him?",
  68029:
      "They said: Exalted be our Lord; indeed, we were wronging ourselves when we resolved to prevent the destitute from the fruits of our garden.",
  68030: "So they began to go back on their statements in the way of blame.",
  68031:
      "Out of regret, they said: O our loss. Indeed, we were transgressing the limit by prohibiting the destitute from their rights.",
  68032:
      "Hopefully, our Lord will compensate us with what is better than the garden. Indeed, we are yearning to Allah alone. We hope for pardon from Him and seek goodness from Him.",
  68033:
      "Just like this torment by deprivation of provision, we torment those who disobey Us. Certainly, the punishment of the Hereafter is greater. If only they were to know its severity and permanence.",
  68034:
      "Indeed, by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, those who are heedful of Allah have gardens of delight near their Lord, reveling in it. Their delight will never cease.",
  68035:
      "Should We make the Muslims [those who submit] like the disbelievers in terms of requital, as the polytheists of Mecca claim?!",
  68036:
      "What is wrong with you, O polytheists? How do you conclude this skewed, crooked conclusion?!",
  68037:
      "Or do you have a book in which you read that the obedient and disobedient are equal?",
  68038:
      "Indeed, in that case, you would have in that book whatever you choose in the Afterlife. Nay, you do not have that.",
  68039:
      "Or, do you have covenants incumbent upon Us, assured with oaths, that whatever you conclude for yourselves is yours?",
  68040:
      "Ask, O Messenger, those saying this statement: Which of them guarantees it?!",
  68041:
      "Or do they have associates other than Allah who make them equal in requital with the believers? Then let them bring forth these associates of theirs if they are truthful in their claim that they have made them equal in requital with the believers.",
  68042:
      "Horror will appear on the Day of Resurrection, and our Lord will uncover His Shin. The people will be called to prostrate, so the believers will prostrate, and the disbelievers and hypocrites will remain unable to.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Preventing the right of the poor is the cause of wealth being destroyed.\n2. A believer and disbeliever are not equal in requital, just as they are not equal in their qualities.",
  68043:
      "Their eyes debased, lowliness and regret enveloping them. In the life of this world, it had been requested from them that they prostrate to Allah while they were free from what they are in today [The Day of Resurrection].",
  68044:
      "So, O Messenger, leave Me and whoever denies this Quran that has been revealed to you. We will drive them to the torment, little by little, from where they do not realize that it is a method of leading them on gradually and drawing out their destruction.",
  68045:
      "And I give them respite for a period so that they go on in their sin. Indeed, My plan for the people of disbelief and rejection is firm, so they will not escape Me nor be safe from My punishment.",
  68046:
      "Do you seek, O Messenger, reward for what you invite them towards so they take on a significant undertaking because of that, and hence this is why they shun you? The reality is the opposite, for you do not seek reward from them. So what prevents them from following you?",
  68047:
      "Or do they know the unseen, so they write what appeals to them of arguments that they argue against you with?",
  68048:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with what your Lord has decided of drawing out their destruction by [granting them] respite. And do not be like the companion of the whale, Jonah (peace be upon him), in annoyance with his people, when he called his Lord as he was distressed in the darkness of the sea and the darkness of the whale's stomach.",
  68049:
      "Had the mercy of Allah not reached him, the whale would have cast him upon barren land while being blameworthy.",
  68050:
      "So his Lord chose him. Thus, He made him one of His righteous slaves.",
  68051:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieved in Allah and rejected His Messenger could almost drop you with their eyes due to how severe their stares are at you when they hear this Quran revealed to you. And they say, in adherence to their desires and turning away from the truth: Indeed, the Messenger who has brought it is certainly a madman.",
  68052:
      "The Quran that has been revealed unto you is but an admonition and a reminder to humans and Jinn.",
  69000:
      "The Reality (Surah Al-Haqqah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAffirming that the occurrence of the Resurrection and the recompense on [that day] is true, without a doubt.\n•    Explanation:",
  69001:
      "Allah mentions the hour of the resurrection that is incumbent on everyone.",
  69002:
      "Then He magnifies its importance by asking this question: What is al-Haqqah (the Calamity)?",
  69003: "And what will inform you what this Al-Haqqah is?",
  69004:
      "Thamūd, the people of Saleh, and 'Ād, the people of Hūd, denied the Day of Resurrection that will make people's hair fall out due to the severity of its horrors.",
  69005:
      "So as for Thamūd, Allah certainly destroyed them with the scream that reached the pinnacle of severity and horror.",
  69006:
      "And as for 'Ād, Allah destroyed them with a severe, cold wind with a harsh, vexing sound that reached the pinnacle of harshness upon them.",
  69007:
      "Allah sent it upon them for seven nights and eight days, destroying every last one of them. So you would see the people destroyed in their homes, thrown onto the ground as if, after their destruction, they were worn-out date palm trunks fallen upon the ground.",
  69008:
      "So do you see any remaining soul from them after what befell them of torment?\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Patience is a praiseworthy quality, necessary for the callers towards Allah and others.\n2. Allah sends different punishments upon the deserving disbelievers and sinners, showing His perfect justice and complete omnipotence.",
  69009:
      "And Pharaoh, the nations before him, and the towns that were afflicted by being flipped upside down, the people of Lot, [all] committed the wrongful acts of ascribing partners with Allah and other sins.",
  69010:
      "Each of them disobeyed their messenger, who was sent to them, and rejected him, so Allah seized them with a seizure in excess of what would complete their destruction.",
  69011:
      "Indeed, when the water exceeded its limit in height, We carried those whom you were in their loins [i.e., your ancestors] cruising on the Ark that Noah (peace be upon him) built based on Our command, so it became a means of carrying you.",
  69012:
      "So that We make the ark and its story an admonition through which the destruction of the people of disbelief and the salvation of the people of faith could be evidenced, and [so] that retentive ears could retain what they hear.",
  69013:
      "Then, when the appointed angel blows one blowing into the trumpet, it being the second blowing.",
  69014:
      "And the Earth and mountains are raised, then crushed [with] one severe blow that disperses the pieces of the Earth and the pieces of its mountains.",
  69015: "So on the Day when all that happens, the Resurrection will occur.",
  69016:
      "And the sky will split on that Day because of the angels descending from it, for on that Day, it will be weak after it had been strong and held together.",
  69017:
      "The angels will be on its edges and sides. And eight angels close [to Allah] will carry the throne of your Lord on that great Day.",
  69018:
      "On that Day, you will be presented, O people, before Allah. No concealed matters of yours are hidden from Allah, whatever they might be. Rather, Allah knows and observes it.",
  69019:
      "As for the one given the book of his deeds in his right [hand], he will say out of happiness and joy: Take and read the book of my deeds.",
  69020:
      "Indeed, I knew and was convinced in the worldly life that I would be resurrected and meeting my reward.",
  69021:
      "So he [will] be in a contented state of life due to what he sees of endless delight.",
  69022: "In a paradise that is elevated in position and rank.",
  69023: "Its fruits are close to whoever grasps them.",
  69024:
      "In hospitality, it will be said to them: Eat and drink food and drink containing no harm because of what you put forth of good deeds in the days passed in the worldly life.",
  69025:
      "And as for the one who is given the book of his deeds in his left [hand], then he will say, from the intensity of regret: O, if only I had not been given the book of my deeds for what it contains of evil deeds warranting my anguish.",
  69026: "And O, if only I did not know what my account would be.",
  69027:
      "If only the death which I died was the death after which I would never be revived.",
  69028: "My wealth did not protect me at all from Allah's torment.",
  69029:
      "My argument has deserted me, as well as what I used to rely on of strength and prestige.",
  69030:
      "And it will be said: Take him, O angels, and shackle his hands to his neck.",
  69031: "Then put him into the Fire so that he suffers its heat.",
  69032: "Then fasten him with a chain seventy cubits long.",
  69033: "Indeed, he would not believe in Allah the Great.",
  69034: "And he would not encourage others to feed the needy.",
  69035:
      "So on the Day of Resurrection, he will have no relative to defend him from the torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Taking the book of deeds in one’s right hand on the Day of Judgement is a sign of good fortune, while taking it in one’s left is a sign of misfortune.\n2. It is important in Islam to feed the poor and encourage people to do so.",
  69036:
      "And he will not have any food to eat except the secretions of the bodies of the people of the Fire.",
  69037:
      "None will eat that food except the people who sin and act disobediently.",
  69038: "Allah swore by what you see.",
  69039: "And swore by what you do not see.",
  69040:
      "Indeed, the Quran is surely the speech of Allah. His noble Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم recites it upon the people.",
  69041:
      "And it is not the saying of a poet because it is not structured as a poem. Little do you believe.",
  69042:
      "And it is not the saying of a soothsayer, for the speech of the soothsayers is a different matter than this Quran. Little do you realize.",
  69043: "Rather, it is sent down by the Lord of all creation.",
  69044:
      "And if Muhammad fabricated some statements about Us that We did not say,",
  69045:
      "We would have surely taken vengeance upon him and seized him with Our strength and ability.",
  69046: "Then we would surely sever the vein connected to his heart.",
  69047: "And there would not be any among you who could prevent Us from him.",
  69048:
      "And indeed, the Quran is surely an admonition for those heedful of their Lord by complying with his commands and avoiding his prohibitions.",
  69049:
      "And indeed, We surely know that among you are those who lie about this Quran.",
  69050:
      "And indeed, the rejection of the Quran is surely a great regret on the Day of Resurrection.",
  69051:
      "And indeed, the Quran is surely the truth of certainty in which there is no dispute and no doubt that it is from Allah.",
  69052:
      "So, O Messenger, exalt your Lord above what does not befit Him and mention the name of your Great Lord.",
  70000:
      "The Ascending Stairways (Surah Al-Ma'arij)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the condition of the creation on the Day of Resurrection and their recompense.\n•    Explanation:",
  70001:
      "A supplicator among the polytheists supplicated for a torment upon himself and his people if this torment were to occur. He was mocking, but it will manifest on the Day of Resurrection,",
  70002:
      "Upon the disbelievers in Allah. There is no one who can repel this torment,",
  70003:
      "From Allah, the possessor of loftiness, degrees, virtues, and bounties.",
  70004:
      "The angels and Gabriel rise to Him in those degrees on the Day of Resurrection. And it is a long day. Its length is fifty thousand years.",
  70005:
      "So be patient, O Messenger, with patience exhibiting no distress or complaint.",
  70006:
      "Indeed, they see this torment as far-fetched and impossible to occur.",
  70007: "And We see it close, definitely occurring.",
  70008:
      "The Day when the sky will be like molten copper, gold, and other [metals].",
  70009: "And the mountains will be like wool in lightness.",
  70010:
      "And relatives will not ask each other about their condition because each one will be preoccupied with themselves.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Qur’an is free of poetry and fortune-telling.\n2. Fabricating and attributing lies to Allah may He be glorified is dangerous.",
  70011:
      "Every human will witness their relative; they will not be hidden from them. Still, no one will ask anyone [about their condition] because of the horror of the situation. The one deserving of the Fire will wish to offer his children for the torment instead of himself.",
  70012: "And ransom his wife and brother.",
  70013: "And ransom his close associates who stand with him during adversity.",
  70014:
      "And ransom all who is on the Earth, of humans, Jinn, or others [so that] then that ransom would save and rescue him from the torment of the Fire.",
  70015:
      "The matter is not as this criminal hopes. Indeed, it is the Fire of the Hereafter, flaming and burning.",
  70016:
      "It severely splits the skin on the head from the intensity of its heat and flames.",
  70017:
      "It calls him who turned away from the truth, distanced himself from it, did not believe in it, and did not act,",
  70018:
      "[Who] collected his wealth and was stingy in spending from it in the way of Allah.",
  70019: "Indeed, the human being was created with great eagerness.",
  70020: "If harm inflicts him from illness or poverty, he is impatient.",
  70021:
      "And if what is pleasing occurs to him, of luxury and sufficiency, he is very resistant to spending it in the way of Allah.",
  70022:
      "Except for the praying ones, for they are free of those lowly attributes,",
  70023:
      "Those who are consistent with their prayers, not preoccupied from them, and perform them within their specified times.",
  70024: "And those who have an obligatory specified portion in their wealth,",
  70025:
      "Which they pay to he who asks them and he who does not ask them from those who have been prevented from provision for any reason.",
  70026:
      "And those who affirm the Day of Resurrection, the Day Allah will recompense everyone with what they deserve.",
  70027:
      "And those who fear torment from their Lord, despite what they put forth of righteous deeds.",
  70028:
      "Indeed, the torment of their Lord is frightening. No rational person feels secure from it.",
  70029:
      "And those who protect their private parts by covering them and keeping them away from obscenities.",
  70030:
      "Except from their wives or what they own of slave girls, then they are not blameworthy in enjoying them with intercourse and what is less than it.",
  70031:
      "So whoever seeks enjoyment [with their private parts] with other than what was mentioned of wives and slave girls, then those are the ones transgressing the bounds of Allah.",
  70032:
      "And those maintaining their pledges that they pledged to people and what they were entrusted with of wealth, secrets, and otherwise. They do not betray [in] their trusts and do not break their pledges.",
  70033:
      "And those who maintain their testimonies in the appropriate manner such that they are not affected by kinship or enmity.",
  70034:
      "And those who maintain their prayers by performing them in their times in a purified state with tranquility, nothing busying them from it.",
  70035:
      "Those described with those attributes will be honored in gardens by attaining everlasting bliss and beholding the noble Face of Allah.",
  70036:
      "What is it, O Messenger, that has led these polytheists within your nation to rush to accuse you of being a liar?",
  70037: "Surrounding you from your right and your left, groups upon groups.",
  70038:
      "Does every one of them hope that Allah will enter him into the Garden of Delight, relishing in what is in it of permanent delight while he is remaining in his [state of] disbelief?!",
  70039:
      "The matter is not as they envision. Indeed, we created them from what they know, for we have created them from base water, so they are weak, not possessing benefit or harm for themselves. Then how do they become arrogant?!",
  70040:
      "Allah the Exalted swore by Himself, the Lord of the East and the West, the Sun and the Moon, and all of the stars: Indeed, We are certainly able,\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The people of the hellfire will wish to save themselves from it using every possible method they know of from their worldly experiences, but there is no way it will ever happen.",
  70041:
      "To replace them with others, from those who obey Allah, and destroy them. We are not incapable of that, and we are not defeated when we wish for their destruction and replacement with others.",
  70042:
      "So leave them, O Messenger, to delve into what they are upon of falsehood and misguidance and frolic during their lives until they encounter the Day of Resurrection, which they were promised in the Quran.",
  70043:
      "The Day they will quickly come out of their graves as if racing to a marker.",
  70044:
      "Their eyes will be humble, and debasement will shroud them. That is the Day they were promised in the worldly life, and they were unconcerned about it.",
  71000:
      "Noah (Surah Nuh)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDemonstrating the methodology of calling to Allah through the story of Noah.\n•    Explanation:",
  71001:
      "Indeed, we sent Noah to his people, calling them to alarm them before a painful torment would come to them as a result of what they were upon of shirk (associating partners) with Allah.",
  71002:
      "Noah said to his people: O my people, indeed I am a warner to you, clearly warning of a torment awaiting you if you do not repent to Allah.",
  71003:
      "And my warning to you obliges that I tell you: Worship Allah alone, do not associate anything as partners with Him, take heed of Him by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, and obey me in what He commanded you with.",
  71004:
      "Indeed, if you do so, Allah will forgive you for your sins that do not relate to the rights of the slaves [the creation], and He will extend the life of your nation to a time specified within Allah's knowledge, to dwell upon the Earth as long as you are upright upon that. Indeed, death can not be postponed when it comes. If you knew, you would have rushed to faith in Allah and repentance from what you are upon of shirk and misguidance.",
  71005:
      "Noah said: O my Lord, indeed, I called my people to Your worship and Your tawheed (exclusion in worship) continuously, night and day.",
  71006:
      "And my call did not increase them except in fleeing and distance from what I call them to.",
  71007:
      "And indeed, each time I call them, it will cause the forgiveness of their sins, which is worshipping You alone, obedience to You, and obedience to Your messenger; they close their ears with their fingers to prevent hearing my call, cover their faces with their clothes so as not to see me, persist in the polytheism they are upon, and become arrogant of accepting and yielding to what I call them to.",
  71008: "Then, indeed, my Lord, I called them openly.",
  71009:
      "Then, I raised my voice in the call. I also acted in concealed secretness and called them in a low voice, varying the approaches of my call to them.",
  71010:
      "So I told them: O my people, ask for forgiveness from your Lord by repenting to him. Indeed, He (may He be Exalted) is oft-forgiving to the sins of those among his slaves who repent to Him.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Neglect of the afterlife is dangerous.\n2. Worshipping Allah and being mindful of Him is a means of sins being forgiven.\n3. It is necessary for the callers towards Allah to persist in their work, and use different methods of calling towards Him.",
  71011:
      "For indeed, if you do that, Allah will continuously send down the rain upon you whenever you need it, so no drought will befall you.",
  71012:
      "And He will give you wealth and children in abundance and produce gardens for you to eat the fruits from and rivers from which you can drink and provide water to your crops and livestock.",
  71013:
      "What is your issue, my people, [such that] you do not fear the greatness of Allah when you disobey Him without any concern?!",
  71014:
      "While He had created you stage after stage from a drop, then a clot of blood, then a piece of flesh.",
  71015:
      "Have you not seen how Allah created seven heavens, one above the other?",
  71016:
      "And He made the Moon in the lowest heaven as a light for the people of the Earth, and He made the Sun luminous.",
  71017:
      "And Allah created you from the Earth by creating your father Adam from dust. Then you are nourished by what it grows for you.",
  71018:
      "Then He returns you to it after your death. Then He brings you out of it for the resurrection.",
  71019: "And Allah spread the Earth out for you and made it ready to live on.",
  71020:
      "In the hope that you would traverse wide paths through it in pursuit of permissible income.",
  71021:
      "Noah said: O my Lord, indeed, my people have disobeyed me in what I commanded them with of your Tawheed and worshipping you alone. The lowly ones among them followed their leaders, whom you have bestowed bounty upon with wealth and progeny, so what you bestowed upon them did not increase them except in misguidance.",
  71022:
      "And the seniors among them deceitfully plotted a great plot by provoking those under them against Noah.",
  71023:
      "And they said to their followers: Do not leave the worship of your gods. Do not leave the worship of your idols, Wadd, Suwaa', Yaghuth, Ya'uq, and Nasr.",
  71024:
      "They certainly misguided many people with these idols of theirs. Do not, O Lord, increase those wronging themselves by persisting upon disbelief and acts of disobedience, except in misguidance from the truth.",
  71025:
      "Because of the misdeeds they undertook, they were drowned by the flood in this world. So they were put into the Fire immediately after their death. Then they did not find in those other than Allah [any] supporters saving them from the drowning or the Fire.",
  71026:
      "And when Allah informed him that no one from his people would believe except those who had believed, Noah said: O my Lord, do not leave anyone among the disbelievers [to] go around or move.",
  71027:
      "Indeed, our Lord, if You leave them and give them respite, they will misguide Your believing slaves, and they would not give birth except to a person of wickedness who does not obey You, severe in disbelief, not thanking You for Your bounties.",
  71028:
      "My Lord, forgive me my sins, forgive my parents, forgive whoever enters my household as a believer, forgive the male and female believers, and do not increase those wronging themselves with disbelief and acts of disobedience except in destruction and loss.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Seeking forgiveness is a means of rainfall and abundance in wealth and children.\n2. The role of the elders in leading the juniors astray is clearly evident.\n3. Sins are the cause of destruction in the world and facing a punishment in the afterlife.",
  72000:
      "The Jinn (Surah Al-Jinn)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nInvalidating the religion of the polytheists by describing the state of the Jinn and their faith upon hearing the Quran.\n•    Explanation:",
  72001:
      "Say, O Messenger, to your nation: Allah revealed to me that a group of the Jinn listened to my recitation of the Quran at Batn Nakhlah. So when they returned to their people, they said to them: Indeed, we heard recited speech, impressive in its articulation and eloquence.",
  72002:
      "This speech we heard directs to what is right in creed, word, and action. So we have believed in it and will not associate anyone as partners with our Lord, who sent it down.",
  72003:
      "And we have believed that He, exalted be our Lord's greatness and grandeur, did not take a wife nor child as the polytheists say.",
  72004:
      "And that it was Iblis who would say a crooked statement about Allah by attributing a wife and child to Him, may He be Exalted.",
  72005:
      "And that we presumed that the polytheists of the humans and Jinn were not lying when they claimed that He had a wife and child. So we believed what they said, blindly following them.",
  72006:
      "And that there were men from humans in the Days of Ignorance who would seek protection with men from the Jinn when they would lodge at a frightful place, then one of them would say: I seek refuge with the chief of this valley from the evil of the fools of his people. So the men from the humans increased in fear and terror of the men from the Jinn.",
  72007:
      "And that the humans thought as you thought, O Jinn, that Allah would not revive anyone after his death for account and recompense.",
  72008:
      "And that we sought the news of the sky, then found the sky had been filled with strong guards from the angels guarding it from the eavesdropping we used to engage in. And it had been filled with ignited fire that was cast at anyone who came close to it.",
  72009:
      "And that in the past, we would take stations in the sky, listening from them to what the angels circulate. Then we would inform the soothsayers on Earth of it. The affair has changed. So whoever of us listens now finds an ignited fire prepared for him. If he approaches, it is sent upon him and burns him.",
  72010:
      "And that we do not know the reason for this stern defense: Was evil intended for the people of Earth, or was it that Allah wanted good for them? For the news of the sky has been cut off from us.",
  72011:
      "And that, O community of Jinn, some of us are of the heedful and righteous, and some of us are of the disbelievers and wicked. We were different types and different [in] desires.",
  72012:
      "And that we have ascertained that we will not escape Allah (may He be Exalted) if He wishes a matter for us, and we will not escape Him by fleeing due to His encompassing grasp of us.",
  72013:
      "And that when we heard the Quran, which guides to what is most upright, we believed in it. So whoever believes in his Lord will not fear any deficiency in his good deeds nor any sin added to his past sins.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The profound effect of the Qur’an on those who listen to it with a sound heart.\n2. Just as deviation is found in human beings it is also found in the jinn, in fact to a greater degree.\n3. Seeking help from the jinn is one of the forms of associating partners with Allah.\n4. The nullification of fortune telling after the mission of the Prophet (peace be upon him).\n5. One of the etiquettes of the believer is that he does not attribute evil to Allah.",
  72014:
      "And that among us are Muslims (those who submit), resigned to Allah with obedience, and among us are those who are deviant from the right path and uprightness. So whoever humbles himself to Allah with obedience and good work are those who have aimed towards guidance and correctness.",
  72015:
      "And as for the ones who deviated off the right path and uprightness, they are lumber for Hell, fueling it along with their like from the humans.",
  72016:
      "And just as He revealed to him [the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم] that a group of the Jinn listened to him, He [also] revealed to him that if the Jinn and humans become upright on the path of Islam and act upon what it contains, Allah would surely provide them much water to drink and provide them with various bounties.",
  72017:
      "To test them in it: would they thank Allah's bounty or deny it? And whoever turns away from the Quran and what it contains of admonishments, his Lord will put him into a taxing torment that he will be unable to bear.",
  72018:
      "And that the places of prostration (Masājid) are for Him (may He be Exalted) not for other than Him. So do not supplicate in them to anyone alongside Allah, for then you would be like the Jews and Christians in their synagogues and churches.",
  72019:
      "And that when the slave of Allah, Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, stood to worship his Lord in Batn An-Nakhlah, the Jinn were almost piled upon him due to the severe crowding when they were listening to his recitation of the Quran.",
  72020:
      "Say, O Messenger, to those polytheists: Indeed, I but supplicate exclusively to my Lord, and I do not associate anyone as a partner with Him in worship, whomever they may be.",
  72021:
      "Say to them: Indeed, it is not in my hands to protect you from a harm Allah has preordained for you, nor can I bring about a benefit that Allah prevented you from.",
  72022:
      "Say to them: No one will save me from Allah if I disobey Him, and I will not find in other than Him a refuge to seek refuge in.",
  72023:
      "But rather, what I can do is convey to you what Allah commanded me to and convey His message, which He sent me with to you. And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, then, indeed, his ending will be to enter Hellfire and remain therein eternally. He will never depart it.",
  72024:
      "And the disbelievers [will] remain in their disbelief until they behold, on the Day of Resurrection, what they were promised with, in the worldly life, of torment. Then they will know who has the weakest support and the fewest helpers.",
  72025:
      "Say, O Messenger, to these polytheists denying the resurrection: I do not know if the torment you are promised is near or if it has a period that no one knows except Allah.",
  72026:
      "He (may He be Exalted) is the knower of all the unseen; nothing is concealed from Him, so He does not show His unseen to anyone. Rather, it remains exclusively in His knowledge.",
  72027:
      "Except for whom Allah (may He be Exalted) is pleased with as a messenger, acquaints him with whatever He wills, and He sends guardian angels who protect the Messenger from the front and from behind, and no one other than the messenger is made aware of this.",
  72028:
      "In hopes that the Messenger may know that messengers before him had delivered the messages of their Lord, which He commanded them to deliver, due to the care Allah encompassed it with. Allah's knowledge encompasses what the angels and messengers have, so nothing from that is concealed from Him. He enumerated the number of all things, so nothing from them is concealed from Him (may He be Exalted).\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Injustice leads to entry into hellfire.\n2. The importance of steadfastness in achieving good objectives.\n3. Going against Allah and His messenger leads to entry into hellfire.\n4. Revelation is protected from interference by the satans by flames that are thrown at them if they attempt to listen.",
  73000:
      "The Enshrouded One (Surah Al-Muzzammil)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining the factors that help one take on the hardships of calling to Allah.\n•    Explanation:",
  73001:
      "O you who is wrapped in his clothes [meaning the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم].",
  73002: "Pray the night except for a little of it.",
  73003:
      "Pray half of it if you wish, or pray a little less than half such that you pray a third.",
  73004:
      "Or add to it until you reach two-thirds. And make the Quran clear when you recite it, and be unhurried in its recitation.",
  73005:
      "O Messenger, indeed, we will send down the Quran to you. It is a heavy word due to what it contains of obligations, limits, rulings, manners, and otherwise.",
  73006:
      "Indeed, the hours of the night are when the heart is more in line with the recitation and more correct in speech.",
  73007:
      "Indeed, during the day, you manage your tasks, so you get busied with them from the recitation of the Quran. So, pray at night.",
  73008:
      "And remember Allah with the various types of remembrances. And dedicate yourself to Him (may He be Exalted) by making worship exclusive to Him.",
  73009:
      "Lord of the East and Lord of the West. There is no rightful object of worship except Him, so take Him as a trustee you rely on in all your affairs.",
  73010:
      "And be patient with what the rejectors say of mockery and profanity. And desert them without causing any harm.",
  73011:
      "And do not be concerned with the matter of the rejectors, the people of indulgence in the pleasures of the worldly life. Leave them and me, and wait for them for a little while until their end comes.",
  73012:
      "Indeed, in the Hereafter, we have heavy restraints and an ignited fire.",
  73013:
      "And food that throats choke on due to its bitterness and painful torment, in addition to what has preceded.",
  73014:
      "That torment will occur to the rejectors on the day the Earth and mountains will quake, and the mountains will be as fluid, dispersed sand due to the severity of its horrors.",
  73015:
      "Indeed, we sent to you a messenger who is a witness of your deeds on the Day of Resurrection, just as we sent a messenger to Pharoah, who was Moses, peace be upon him.",
  73016:
      "Pharoah disobeyed the messenger sent to him from his Lord, so we punished him with a severe punishment in the worldly life with drowning and in the Afterlife with the torment of the Fire. So do not disobey your messenger lest what befell him should befall you.",
  73017:
      "So how will you protect yourselves, if you reject Allah and deny His Messenger, from a long, severe day that will make the heads of young children white because of the severity of its horror and its length?",
  73018:
      "[When] the sky [is] fractured from its horrors. Allah's promise is inevitable and inescapable.",
  73019:
      "Indeed, this admonition, which clarifies what horror and adversity are on the Day of Resurrection, is a reminder. The believers benefit from it. So whoever wishes to take a road that leads to his Lord takes it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of standing in prayer at night, reciting the Qur’an, remembering Allah, and being patient for the caller to Allah.\n2. Enduring difficulties and tests, requires an effective and strict nurturing.\n3. Luxury and an abundance of enjoyments is a barrier to Allah’s path.",
  73020:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, knows that you sometimes pray less than two-thirds of the night, sometimes half of it, and sometimes a third of it, and a group of the believers stand with you [in prayer]. And Allah determines the night and the day and enumerates their hours. He (may He be Exalted) knew that you cannot enumerate and match its hours, so it burdens you to stand most of it to ensure what is requested [is done]. So because of that, He has turned to you in repentance, so pray from the night that which is made easy. Allah knew that there would be among you, O believers, ill ones exhausted by disease, others traveling seeking Allah's provision, and others fighting the disbelievers to pursue the contentment of Allah and to make the word of Allah most superior. Standing in prayer burdens these [mentioned], so pray from the night what is made easy for you. And come to the obligatory prayer in the most complete manner, give Zakat (obligatory alms) of your wealth, and spend from your wealth in the path of Allah. And what you put forth for yourselves of good, you will find with Allah on the Day of Resurrection better and greater in reward. And seek forgiveness from Allah. Indeed, Allah is forgiving to those who repent from His slaves, merciful to them.",
  74000:
      "The Cloaked One (Surah Al-Muddathir)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe command to give the utmost effort in calling the rejectors and warning them with the Hereafter and the Quran.\n•    Explanation:",
  74001:
      "O you who is enshrouded with his clothes (the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم).",
  74002: "Get up and instill fear with regards to Allah's punishment.",
  74003: "And aggrandize your Lord.",
  74004: "And purify yourself from sins and your clothes from impurities.",
  74005: "And stay away from the worship of idols.",
  74006:
      "And do not vainly recount what you have done for your Lord by considering your good deeds to be much.",
  74007: "And be patient, for Allah's sake, upon whatever harm you face.",
  74008: "So when the second blowing is blown into the horn,",
  74009: "Then that day is a difficult one,",
  74010: "Not easy upon the disbelievers in Allah and his messengers.",
  74011:
      "Leave me, O Messenger, and whom I created alone in his mother's stomach without wealth or child (referring to al-Waleed bin al-Mughirah).",
  74012: "I produced abundant wealth for him.",
  74013:
      "I made sons for him, present with him, and witnessing gatherings with him. They do not separate from him for travel due to the abundance of his wealth.",
  74014: "I extended his life, provision, and offspring for him.",
  74015:
      "Then, while disbelieving in Me, he craves that I give him more after what I have given him from all that.",
  74016:
      "The matter is not as he imagined. Indeed, he opposed Our verses revealed to Our Messenger, rejecting them.",
  74017:
      "I will task him with a burden from the torment that he will be unable to bear.",
  74018:
      "Indeed, this disbeliever, whom I bestowed upon with those bounties, thought over what he would say about the Quran to invalidate it, and he determined that within himself.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Difficulties in affairs brings about ease in them.\n2. The necessity of purity from outward and inward filth.\n3. Bestowing a transgressor with favours is not honouring him; it is gradually leading him into destruction.",
  74019: "So cursed and tormented is he, how he determined.",
  74020: "Again, cursed and tormented is he, how he determined.",
  74021: "Then he reevaluated and pondered what he would say.",
  74022:
      "Then his face frowned and wrinkled when he did not find what to criticize the Quran with.",
  74023:
      "Then he turned away from faith and became arrogantly stubborn from following the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم.",
  74024:
      "Then he said: This, what Muhammad brought, is not the speech of Allah. Rather, it is sorcery he narrates from others.",
  74025: "This is not the speech of Allah. Rather, it is the speech of humans.",
  74026:
      "I will put this disbeliever into a level from the levels of the Fire, which is Saqar. He will suffer its heat.",
  74027: "And what will inform you, O Muhammad, what Saqar is?!",
  74028:
      "It doesn't leave anything from those tormented in it except that it comes upon it and does not let it go. Then it returns to as it was, then it [Saqar] comes upon it, and so on, again and again.",
  74029: "Extreme in burning and altering skin.",
  74030: "Upon it are nineteen angels, and they are its guards.",
  74031:
      "And We did not make the guards of the Fire except angels. Humans have no power over them. We did not make this many of them except as a test for those who disbelieved in Allah, so that they might say what they said, causing their torment to be multiplied. This is also to show the Jews who were given the Torah and the Christians who were given the Gospel that the Quran was divinely revealed, confirming what was in their books. This is also so that believers would increase in faith when the People of the Book agreed with them. And it would also leave no doubt amongst the Jews, the Christians, and the believers. And this is also so those hesitant in their faith and the unbelievers ask: What did Allah will by this strange number?This is a source of misguidance for those who object to this number and a source of guidance for those who believe in it. Allah misguides whomever He wishes to misguide and guides whomever He wishes to guide. No one knows the abundance of Allah's army except for Him; may He be Exalted. The Fire is nothing more than a source of reminder for humanity. Through it, they know the majesty of Allah (may He be Exalted).",
  74032:
      "The truth is not as some of the polytheists claim that he would suffice his companions [against] the guards of Hell until he clears them away from it. Allah swore by the Moon.",
  74033: "And swore by the night when it retreats.",
  74034: "And swore by the morning when it illuminates.",
  74035: "Indeed, Hellfire is one of the great tribulations.",
  74036: "Terrifying and frightening for people.",
  74037:
      "For whoever of you, O people, wishes to move forth with faith in Allah and righteous action or fall back with disbelief and acts of disobedience.",
  74038:
      "Every soul is requited with what deeds it gained. So either its actions bring disaster upon it, or they rescue and save it from destruction.",
  74039:
      "Except for the believers, for they will rescue themselves from destruction with the good they did from their deeds.",
  74040:
      "They will be in gardens, asking one another on the Day of Resurrection.",
  74041:
      "About the disbelievers who destroyed themselves by committing acts of disobedience.",
  74042: "They will say to them: What made you enter Hell?",
  74043:
      "So the disbelievers will answer them saying: We were not among those who would perform the obligatory prayer in the worldly life.",
  74044: "And we would not feed the needy from what Allah gave us.",
  74045:
      "And we were with the people of falsehood, going with them wherever they would and speaking with the people of misguidance and error.",
  74046: "And we used to reject the Day of Recompense.",
  74047:
      "And we continued with its rejection until death came to us. So it prevented us from repentance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Man’s responsibility for his actions in the world and the afterlife.\n2. Not feeding those in need is one of the causes for entrance into the fire.",
  74048:
      "On the Day of Resurrection, the mediation of intercessors from the angels, prophets, and pious people will not benefit them because the requirement for an intercession's acceptance is contingent upon the approval for whom the intercession is made.",
  74049: "What made these polytheists shun the Quran?",
  74050:
      "As if they are, in their shunning and fleeing from it, wild donkeys strongly running away.",
  74051: "That fled from a lion in fear of it.",
  74052:
      "Rather, each one of these polytheists wishes that an open book appear at his head informing him that Muhammed صلى الله عليه وسلم is a messenger from Allah. The reason for that is not a shortage of evidence and weakness of arguments. It is but obstinance and arrogant stubbornness.",
  74053:
      "The matter is not so [i.e., they will not each get a book]. Rather, their persistence in their misguidance is because they do not believe in the torment of the Hereafter, so they have remained in their disbelief.",
  74054: "Is it not that this Quran is an admonishment and reminder?",
  74055:
      "So whoever wants to read the Quran and be admonished by it will read it and be admonished by it.",
  74056:
      "And they will not be admonished except as Allah wishes for them to be admonished. He (may He be Exalted) is befitting to be heeded by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. And He is befitting to forgive the sins of his slaves when they repent to Him.",
  75000:
      "The Resurrection (Surah Al-Qiyamah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nIllustrating Allah's ability to resurrect the creation and gather them on the Day of Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  75001:
      "Allah swore by the Day of Resurrection, the Day the people will rise for the Lord of the worlds.",
  75002:
      "And He swore by the decent soul that blames itself for shortcomings in good deeds and for performing evil deeds. He swore by these two matters that He will surely resurrect the people for account and recompense.",
  75003:
      "Does the human being think that We will not gather his bones for resurrection after his death?",
  75004:
      "Nay, along with gathering them, we are able to return his properly created fingertips just as they were.",
  75005:
      "Rather, in denial of the resurrection, the human wants to continue upon his wickedness in the future without deterrence.",
  75006:
      "He asks about the Day of Resurrection as if it is farfetched: When will it occur?",
  75007:
      "So when the vision becomes confused, and he is shocked when he sees what he used to reject.",
  75008: "And the light of the Moon disappears.",
  75009: "And the bodies of the Sun and Moon come together.",
  75010: "The wicked human will say on that Day: Where is the escape?!",
  75011:
      "There is no escape on that Day, no refuge for the wicked person to seek refuge in, and no protector for him to seek protection with.",
  75012:
      "O Prophet, on that Day, account and recompense will return and be relegated to your Lord.",
  75013:
      "On that Day, the human will be informed of what deeds he put forth and what he left behind.",
  75014:
      "Rather, the human is a witness upon himself, as his limbs bear testimony against him to what sins he committed.",
  75015:
      "And if he came with excuses, arguing by them for his own sake as having done no evil, they would not benefit him.",
  75016:
      "O Messenger, do not move your tongue in haste [for fear] that it may escape from you.",
  75017:
      "Indeed, it is upon Us to gather it in your chest and make its recitation firm upon your tongue.",
  75018:
      "When our messenger Gabriel recites [the Quran] for you [O Prophet], then listen attentively to its recitation.",
  75019:
      "Then it is upon Us to explain it to you.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The servant’s will is restricted by Allah’s will.\n2. The desire of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) to memorise whatever of the Qur’an was revealed to him. Allah assured him that He will gather it fully in his chest and memory and that he will not forget any part of it.",
  75020:
      "Nay, the matter is not as you [disbelievers] have claimed of the impossibility of the Resurrection, for you know that the one able to create you initially is not impeded from reviving you after your death. But the reason for your rejection of the Resurrection is your love for the life of this world, which is quick to finish.",
  75021:
      "And your desertion of the Hereafter, whose path is performing what Allah commanded you with of acts of obedience and leaving what He forbade you from of prohibitions.",
  75022:
      "The faces of the people of faith and happiness on that Day will be beautiful and radiant.",
  75023: "Looking at their Lord, relishing in that.",
  75024:
      "And the faces of the people of disbelief and hardship, on that day, will be frowning.",
  75025:
      "Certain that a great punishment and painful torment will descend upon them.",
  75026:
      "The matter is not how the polytheists imagine that they will not be tormented if they die. So when the soul of one of them reaches the top of his chest,",
  75027:
      "And some people say to each other: Who will recite treatment upon this one so that he is cured?!",
  75028:
      "And the one approaching the moment of death of their illness is certain that it is indeed the parting of the worldly life by death,",
  75029:
      "And the adversities come together at the end of the worldly life and the beginning of the Afterlife,",
  75030: "When that occurs, the deceased one is driven to his Lord.",
  75031:
      "So the disbeliever did not affirm what his messenger came with, nor did he pray to Allah, may He be Exalted.",
  75032: "Instead, he rejected what his messenger came with and shunned him.",
  75033:
      "Then this disbeliever went to his family, strutting in his walk out of arrogance.",
  75034:
      "So Allah threatens the disbeliever that his torment has neared and gotten close to him.",
  75035:
      "He then repeated the sentence as a form of emphasis and stated: Again, nearer to you [O disbeliever] lies your doom and nearer.",
  75036:
      "Does the human being think Allah will leave him disregarded without obliging him with legislation?",
  75037: "Was not this human once a drop of semen poured into the womb?",
  75038:
      "Then, after that, was a piece of solid blood, so Allah created him and made his creation proportioned?",
  75039: "Then He made from his kind two types, male and female?!",
  75040:
      "Is not the One who created the human from a drop and then a blood clot able to bring life to the dead again for account and recompense?! Nay, rather, He is able.",
  76000:
      "The Human Being (Surah Al-Insan)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding the human of the origin of his creation and his destination, and describing what Allah has prepared for His allies in Paradise.\n•    Explanation:",
  76001:
      "An extended period had passed upon the human being in which he was non-existent, without mention.",
  76002:
      "Indeed, we created the human being from a drop mixed between the water of the man and the water of the woman. We test him with what we obligate him with of duties. So, We made him hear and see to perform what we assigned him from the legislation.",
  76003:
      "Indeed, We clarified for him the road of guidance upon the tongues of Our messengers, so that has become clear from the road of misguidance. So after that, he is either to be guided to the straight path and then become a believing slave, thankful to Allah, or he is to stray from it and then become a disbelieving slave, denying the signs of Allah.",
  76004:
      "After mentioning the two categories of guided and misguided, Allah mentions their recompense, stating: \n Indeed, we have prepared chains for the disbelievers in Allah and His messengers, with which they will be pulled into the Fire, [and prepared] binds that they will be bound in, and an ignited Fire.",
  76005:
      "Indeed, the believers obedient to Allah will drink on the Day of Resurrection from a full cup of wine mixed with camphor for its pleasant smell.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The danger of love of the world and neglect of the afterlife.\n2. The establishment of choice for man, which is Allah’s showing honour to him.",
  76006:
      "This drink prepared for the people of obedience is from a spring that is easy to take from, abundant, and never drying up. The slaves of Allah quench their thirst with it. They pour it and make it flow wherever they wish.",
  76007:
      "And the attributes of the slaves who drink from it are that they fulfill what they obligate on themselves of acts of obedience. They fear a Day whose evil is widespread and distributed, which is the Day of Resurrection.",
  76008:
      "And they donate food while they are in a state of loving it due to their need for it and craving it. They give it to those in need of the poor, orphans, and prisoners of war.",
  76009:
      "And they secretly say within themselves that they do not feed them except for the Face of Allah, so they do not want reward or praise for feeding them.",
  76010:
      "[They say] Indeed, we fear from our Lord a Day in which the faces of those in hardship will frown due to its severity and horridness.",
  76011:
      "So Allah, by His favor, protected them from the evil of that great Day. He gave them beauty and light in their faces, in honor to them, and joy in their hearts.",
  76012:
      "And because of their patience upon acts of obedience, and with what Allah predetermined, and against acts of disobedience, Allah awarded them a garden in which they delight, and silk they wear.",
  76013:
      "Reclining therein on adorned couches. They do not see, in this garden, any sun whose rays would hurt them, nor any severe cold. Rather, they are in continuous shade, with no heat or cold.",
  76014:
      "Its shade is close to them. Its fruits are subdued for whoever takes it, so he takes it comfortably and easily, such that those laying, sitting, and standing can reach it.",
  76015:
      "And slaves circulate about them with silver vessels and cups, whose color is pure, when they want to drink.",
  76016:
      "They are pure in color, like glass, except they are made of silver. They are sized according to what they want, not more than that or less.",
  76017:
      "And these honored ones are given a cup of wine mixed with ginger to drink.",
  76018: "They drink from a spring in the Garden named Salsabeel.",
  76019:
      "And young adult slaves who remain in their youth circulate about them. If you saw them, you would have thought them scattered pearls due to the beauty of their faces, the splendor of their colors, abundance, and dispersion.",
  76020:
      "And if you saw what is there in the Garden, you would have seen delight that cannot be described and seen a great kingdom that no kingdom comes close to.",
  76021:
      "Green elegant clothes having adorned their bodies. They are of fine silk and thick, heavy silk. And they are dressed therein with bracelets of silver. Allah gives them drink with a beverage free from any contaminants.",
  76022:
      "And it is said to them, in their honor: Indeed, this delight which We bestowed upon you was a reward for you upon your righteous deeds, and your action was accepted by Allah.",
  76023:
      "O Messenger, indeed, We sent the Quran down upon you in parts, and We did not send it down upon you all at once.",
  76024:
      "So be patient with what Allah determines regarding fate or legislation. And do not obey a sinner with what he calls to of sin, nor a disbeliever in what he calls to of disbelief.",
  76025:
      "And remember your Lord with the Fajr (dawn) prayer at the beginning of the day and the prayers of Dhuhr (early afternoon) and 'Asr (late afternoon) at the end of it.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Fulfilling a vow, feeding the needy, sincerity in action and fearing Allah are all means to achieving salvation from the hellfire and entering Paradise.",
  76026:
      "And remember Him with the two night prayers, maghrib (sunset) and 'ishaa` (evening). And get up for tahajjud [night prayer after waking up at night] after them.",
  76027:
      "Indeed, these polytheists love the life of this world and covet it. They leave behind them the Day of Resurrection, which is a heavy day due to what it contains of adversities and tribulations.",
  76028:
      "We created them and strengthened their creation by reinforcing their joints, limbs, and otherwise. If We had willed their destruction and replacement with the likes of them, We would have destroyed and replaced them.",
  76029:
      "Indeed, this surah [chapter] is an admonishment and reminder. So whoever wishes to take a path that leads him to his Lord's gratification takes it.",
  76030:
      "And you do not wish to take a path to Allah's gratification except that Allah wishes that from you, for the matter all goes back to Him. Indeed, Allah is knowledgeable of what befits His slaves and what does not befit them. [He is] wise in His creation, predetermination, and legislation.",
  76031:
      "He enters whom He wishes of His slaves into His mercy. So He makes them successful by leading them to faith and righteous action. And He prepared for those who wronged themselves with disbelief and acts of disobedience a painful torment in the Afterlife. It is the torment of the Fire.",
  77000:
      "The Emissaries (Surah Al-Mursalat)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThreatening deniers with destruction on the Day of Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  77001:
      "Allah swore by the winds, which are continuous like the mane of a horse.",
  77002: "And swore by the winds of severe gusts.",
  77003: "And swore by the winds that disperse the rain.",
  77004:
      "And swore by the angels who descend with what distinguishes between truth and falsehood.",
  77005: "And swore by the angels who descend with revelation.",
  77006:
      "They descend with revelation as an exoneration from Allah to the people and a warning to the people of the torment of Allah.",
  77007:
      "Indeed, what you are promised of resurrection, account, and reward will undoubtedly occur and is inevitable.",
  77008: "So if the stars' light is erased and their glow disappears.",
  77009: "And the sky fractures due to the descent of the angels from it.",
  77010:
      "And the mountains are plucked from their places and then crumbled until they become dust.",
  77011: "And if the messengers are gathered for a specified time.",
  77012:
      "For a great Day. They were postponed for testimony upon their nations.",
  77013:
      "For the Day of Separation between the slaves so that the rightful one becomes clear from the wrongful one, and the happy from the wretched.",
  77014:
      "And what has informed you, O Messenger, what the Day of Separation is?!",
  77015:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors who reject what the messengers came with from Allah.",
  77016:
      "Did We not destroy the previous nations when they disbelieved in Allah and rejected His messengers?!",
  77017:
      "Then we make the rejectors of the later ones come after them, so we destroy them as we destroyed them [the previous nations].",
  77018:
      "Just like the destruction of those nations, we destroy the criminals rejecting what Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم came with.",
  77019:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that day for those who reject Allah's threat of the criminal's torment.",
  77020:
      "Did We not create you, O people, from a small amount of base water, which is the drop [of semen]?",
  77021:
      "Then we placed that measly water in a secure place, which is the womb of the woman?",
  77022: "For a known period, which is the period of pregnancy.",
  77023:
      "So we determined the form of the newborn, its size, color, and other than that? So how splendid determiners We are for all that.",
  77024:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of Allah's ability.",
  77025: "Did We not make the Earth encompass all people,",
  77026:
      "Encompassing their living with residence upon it and its buildings, and their dead with burial within it,",
  77027:
      "And we made firm, tall mountains in it, preventing it from quaking, and gave you drink, O people, with sweet water? So the one who created that is not impeded from your resurrection.",
  77028:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of Allah's bounties upon them.",
  77029:
      "And will be said to the rejectors of what their messengers brought: Walk, O rejectors, to what you used to reject of the torment.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Attachment to the world and forgetting the afterlife is dangerous.\n2. The servant’s will is subservient to Allah’s will.\n3. Destroying those nations who denied is a divine practice.",
  77030: "Walk to the shade of the Fire's smoke, separated into three bodies.",
  77031:
      "There is no coolness of shade in it, and it does not prevent the fervor of the Fire and its heat from passing through to them.",
  77032:
      "Indeed, the Fire casts sparks. Each spark is like a castle in its greatness.",
  77033:
      "As if the sparks it casts, in its blackness and immensity, are like black camels with their colors leaning towards yellow.",
  77034:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day to the rejectors of Allah's torment.",
  77035: "This is a Day in which they do not say anything.",
  77036:
      "And it is not permitted for them to give excuses to their Lord for their disbelief and misdeeds such that they could give Him excuses.",
  77037:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of the news of that Day.",
  77038:
      "This is the Day of Separation between the creation. We gathered you and the previous nations on one ground.",
  77039:
      "So if you have a trick you can trick with for salvation from the torment of Allah, then trick Me.",
  77040:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of the Day of Separation.",
  77041:
      "Indeed, those heedful of their Lord, by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, are amid the extensive shade of the trees of the Garden [of Paradise] and the springs of sweet flowing water.",
  77042: "And whatever fruits that they desire to eat.",
  77043:
      "It will be said to them: Eat from the wholesome things and drink a beverage that is easy to consume with no contaminants because of what you used to do in the worldly life of righteous deeds.",
  77044:
      "Indeed, just like this reward that We awarded you with, We reward the people of excellence for their deeds.",
  77045:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of what Allah has prepared for the heedful.",
  77046:
      "And it will be said to the rejectors: Eat and relish the pleasures of life for a short time in this world. Indeed, by disbelieving in Allah and rejecting His messengers, you are criminals.",
  77047:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors of their recompense on the Day of Judgment.",
  77048:
      "And if it is said to these rejectors: Pray to Allah, they do not pray to Him.",
  77049:
      "Destruction, torment, and loss are on that Day for the rejectors who reject what the messengers came with from Allah.",
  77050:
      "So if they do not believe in this Quran, which was sent down from their Lord, then which other speech would they believe in?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah looks after the human in the mother’s womb.\n2. The earth is vast enough for those that live upon it that are living, and those within it who are dead.",
  78000:
      "The Tidings (Surah An-Naba)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining the evidence for the ability to resurrect and instilling fear of the outcome.\n•    Explanation:",
  78001:
      "What are these polytheists asking one another about after Allah has sent His Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم to them?",
  78002:
      "They are asking one another about the great news, referring to this Quran, which was revealed upon their Messenger and contains news of the Resurrection.",
  78003:
      "They differed regarding this Quran, describing it as sorcery, poetry, fortune-telling, or legends of old.",
  78004:
      "The matter is not as they claim. These deniers of the Quran will soon know the outcome of their evil denial.",
  78005: "Then that will be made certain for them.",
  78006:
      "Did We not spread the earth out for them, suitable for their residence?",
  78007:
      "And did We not put mountains on it like stakes to stop it from shaking?",
  78008:
      "And We created you, O people, of different types: some of you are males while others are females.",
  78009:
      "And We made your sleep as a break from your activity so that you may rest.",
  78010:
      "And We made the night a cover for you with its darkness, like the clothing you cover your private areas with.",
  78011:
      "And We made the day as a period of earning and searching for a living.",
  78012: "And We made seven firm skies above you, perfected in construction.",
  78013: "And We made the sun an extremely bright and radiant lamp.",
  78014: "And We sent down abundantly flowing water from clouds ready to rain.",
  78015:
      "So that through it, We can extract different types of grains and plants.",
  78016:
      "And extract gardens that entwine with one another due to the severe overlapping of the branches of their trees.",
  78017:
      "When Allah mentioned these blessings that show His ability, He followed it up by mentioning the Revival and Resurrection because the one who can create these blessings can also resurrect the dead and hold them to account. He says: \n Indeed, the Day of Separation between the creation is a fixed, appointed time that will not be postponed.",
  78018:
      "The Day the angel will blow into the horn again, upon which, O people, you shall come in many groups.",
  78019:
      "And the sky will be opened, with crevices and gaps resembling open doors.",
  78020:
      "And the mountains will be made to move until they become dispersed dust particles, becoming like a mirage.",
  78021: "Indeed, Hell is watching, lying in wait.",
  78022:
      "[It is] for the unjust a place of return which they will be made to return to.",
  78023: "Wherein they shall dwell for ages and eons without end.",
  78024:
      "They will not experience cold breezes in it that cool them from the heat of the blaze, nor will they taste any drink they can enjoy.",
  78025:
      "They will only taste scorching hot water and the flowing pus of the people of the Fire.",
  78026: "As a recompense for their disbelief and deviance.",
  78027:
      "Indeed, in the world, they did not fear Allah taking them to account in the Afterlife because they did not believe in the Resurrection. So, if they had feared the Resurrection, they would have believed in Allah and acted righteously.",
  78028:
      "And they vehemently rejected Our verses We revealed to Our Messenger.",
  78029:
      "We recorded and counted all their deeds, which are written in their book of deeds.",
  78030:
      "Endure this everlasting torment, O transgressors, for We will not increase you in anything except torment upon your anguish.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The blessings of Allah upon His servants are numerous.\n2. Transgression is a cause of entering the hellfire.\n3. The punishment will be doubled on the disbelievers.",
  78031:
      "Indeed, those mindful of their Lord by following His commands and avoiding His prohibitions, there is a place of triumph they sought to attain: Paradise.",
  78032: "It is full of orchards and grapevines,",
  78033: "Full-bosomed women of equal age,",
  78034: "And full glasses of wine.",
  78035:
      "In Paradise, they will not hear any false speech. They will neither hear lies, nor will they lie to one another.",
  78036:
      "All of that will be from what Allah will give them in graciousness and benevolence, which will be sufficient for them.",
  78037:
      "[He is] the Lord of the heavens, the earth, and whatever is between them; the Most Merciful of this world and the hereafter. No one on earth or in the heavens can ask Him except those whom He permits.",
  78038:
      "On the Day when Gabriel and the angels will stand in rows, not speaking to intercede on behalf of anyone except whom the Most Merciful permits them to intercede for and utters a true statement (e.g., the statement proclaiming the oneness of Allah).",
  78039:
      "That which has been described to you is the day that will come without a doubt. Therefore, whoever wishes salvation from Allah's torment on that day should take the path of performing good deeds that will please his Lord.",
  78040:
      "O people, I have indeed warned you of an impending torment that will occur on the day when a person sees what deeds he put forth in the world. The disbeliever will say, wishing to be rid of the torment: If only I had become dust like the animals when it is said to them [the animals] on the Day of Resurrection: Become dust.",
  79000:
      "Those Who Drag Forth (Surah An-Nazi'at)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding of Allah and the Last Day.\n•    Explanation:",
  79001:
      "Allah swore by the angels who pull out the souls of the disbelievers harshly and severely.",
  79002:
      "And He also swore by the angels who gently remove the souls of the believers easily and smoothly.",
  79003:
      "He also swore by the angels who wade between heaven and earth with Allah's command.",
  79004:
      "And He swore by the angels who compete with one another to carry out Allah's command.",
  79005:
      "He also swore by the angels who execute Allah's command (i.e., the angels appointed to [record] the deeds of the slaves). He swore by all of those matters that He will certainly resurrect people for reckoning and recompense.",
  79006:
      "On the Day when the earth will tremble upon the first blowing of the horn,",
  79007: "The second blow will follow it.",
  79008:
      "The hearts of disbelievers and the wicked will be fearful on that day.",
  79009: "The effects of humiliation will appear on their faces.",
  79010: "They used to say: Will we live again after we die?!",
  79011: "When we become decomposed, empty bones, will we return after that?!",
  79012:
      "They would say: If we return, that return will be a loss, and the person returning will be beguiled.",
  79013:
      "The matter of the Resurrection is easy, for it will only be a single scream from the angel appointed to blow.",
  79014:
      "Then suddenly, everyone will be alive on the face of the earth after they were dead within it.",
  79015:
      "O Messenger, has the news of Moses with his Lord, and his enemy, Pharaoh, come to you?!",
  79016:
      "When his Lord (may He be Exalted) called out to him at the sanctified Valley of Tuwa.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah-consciousness is the cause of entry into Paradise.\n2. Everything in Paradise is good and beneficial.\n3. A disbeliever will desire that he become dust like the animals, who will be told on the Day of Judgement: “Become dust”.\n4. The soul of the disbeliever will be taken with severity and harshness, while the soul of the believer will be taken with kindness and gentleness.",
  79017:
      "Among what He told him [was]: Go to Pharaoh; indeed, he has overstepped the limits in injustice and arrogance.",
  79018:
      "So say to him: O Pharaoh, do you want to purify yourself from disbelief and acts of disobedience?",
  79019:
      "And I can direct you to your Lord, who created and nurtured you, so you fear Him, do what makes Him content, and avoid what angers Him.",
  79020:
      "Moses (peace be upon him) then showed him the great sign indicating he was a messenger from his Lord: the Hand and the Staff.",
  79021:
      "So Pharaoh did nothing except reject this sign and disobeyed what Moses (peace be upon him) commanded him with.",
  79022:
      "Then he turned away from belief in what Moses (peace be upon him) brought, striving to disobey Allah and oppose the truth.",
  79023:
      "Then he gathered his people and followers to overpower Moses (peace be upon him), so he called out, saying:",
  79024:
      "I am your Lord, the Most High, and there is no obedience incumbent upon you to anyone other than Me.",
  79025:
      "So, Allah seized and punished him in the world by drowning him in the sea, and He will punish him in the Afterlife by entering him into the severest torment.",
  79026:
      "Indeed, in Our punishing of Pharaoh in this world and the Afterlife, there is certainly an admonition for the one who fears Allah because he benefits from [such] admonitions.",
  79027:
      "O rejectors of resurrection: Is your origination, or the origination of the heavens that He built, harder for Allah?",
  79028:
      "He made the pinnacle of the heavens vertically high and leveled: there are no breaks, cracks, or defects in them.",
  79029:
      "And He darkened [the sky's] night when the sun sets and manifested its light when it rises.",
  79030:
      "As for the earth, after He created the heavens, He spread it out and placed its benefits within it.",
  79031:
      "He extracted water from it as flowing springs and made plants grow on it, which the livestock graze on.",
  79032: "And He made the mountains firm on the earth.",
  79033:
      "All of that is for your benefit, O people, and for [the benefit] of your livestock. For the One who created all this is not incapable of recreating you anew.",
  79034:
      "Alas, the Resurrection will occur when the second blow [of the trumpet] comes, covering everything with its terror.",
  79035:
      "On the day when it comes, a person will remember the work they put forth, whether good or evil.",
  79036: "And Hell will be brought and unveiled clearly for all to see.",
  79037: "As for the one who transgressed the limits of deviance.",
  79038:
      "And favored the temporary worldly life over the everlasting Afterlife.",
  79039: "Then indeed, the Fire is his abode he will take shelter in.",
  79040:
      "And as for the one who feared his standing before his Lord and stopped his soul from following its desires from what Allah prohibited, then Paradise is his abode that he will take shelter in.",
  79041:
      "And as for the one who feared his standing before his Lord and stopped his soul from following its desires from what Allah prohibited, then Paradise is his abode that he will take shelter in.",
  79042:
      "O Messenger, these rejectors of Resurrection ask you: When will the Hour occur?",
  79043:
      "You do not have any knowledge regarding it such that you can mention it to them, nor is that an affair of yours. Your affair is only to prepare for it.",
  79044: "The total knowledge of the Hour is with your Lord alone.",
  79045:
      "You are only a warner to the one who fears the Hour because he is the one who benefits from your warning.",
  79046:
      "It will be as if, on the day they see the Hour, [truly] witnessing [it], that they did not remain in their worldly lives except for a single evening or morning.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is obligatory to be kind when addressing the one you are inviting.\n2. Pharaoh claimed divinity.\n3. The punishment of the transgressors is a lesson for those who take heed.\n4. Fearing Allah and stopping oneself from fulfilling impermissible desires is one of the causes of entering Paradise.\n5. The knowledge of the Hour is from the Ghaib that only Allah knows.",
  80000:
      "He Frowned (Surah 'Abasa)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding the disbelievers who think they do not need their Lord through evidence for the Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  80001:
      "The Messenger of Allah's face صلى الله عليه وسلم frowned and he turned away.",
  80002:
      "Because of the arrival of Abdullah bin Umm Maktoom, who came asking for guidance. He was blind and had come when the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم was busy with the chiefs of the polytheists, hoping they would be guided.",
  80003:
      "O Messenger, how would you know; perhaps this blind man could be purified of his sins!",
  80004:
      "Or that he may take heed of the admonitions he hears from you so he benefits from them?",
  80005:
      "As for the one who feels he does not need to believe in what you have come with due to the wealth he possesses,",
  80006: "You approach and stand before him.",
  80007:
      "What [blame] will there be on you if he is not purified of his sins for failing to repent to Allah?",
  80008: "As for the one who hastens toward you, searching for virtue,",
  80009: "Fearing his Lord,",
  80010:
      "You are preoccupied against him with others among the senior polytheists.",
  80011:
      "The matter is not like that. It (the Quran) is only an admonition and a reminder for whoever accepts it.",
  80012:
      "So, whoever wishes to remember Allah remembers Him and takes heed of what is in this Quran.",
  80013: "For this Quran is in honorable pages with the angels,",
  80014: "Raised in a high place, pure; no impurity or filth reaches them.",
  80015: "And they are in the hands of angelic messengers.",
  80016:
      "They are honorable in the eyes of their Lord, frequent performers of goodness and acts of obedience.",
  80017:
      "The disbelieving human is cursed; how severe is his disbelief in Allah?",
  80018:
      "From what did Allah create him such that he be arrogant on earth and disbelieve in Him?",
  80019:
      "He created him from a little bit of water, then determined his creation stage after stage.",
  80020:
      "Then, after these stages, He made the exit from his mother's belly easy for him.",
  80021:
      "Then, after what He decreed of life for him, He caused him to die. Then He made a grave for him, which he remains in until he is resurrected.",
  80022:
      "Then, when He wishes, He will resurrect him for reckoning and recompense.",
  80023:
      "It is not like this disbeliever imagines: that he has fulfilled Allah's rights upon him, for he has not fulfilled the obligations Allah mandated upon him.",
  80024:
      "So, let the human who disbelieves in Allah look at his food which he eats: how did it occur?",
  80025:
      "It originates from the rain descending from the sky with force and abundance.",
  80026:
      "Then, We part the earth, splitting it open through [the sprouting of] plants.",
  80027: "Then We grow therein grains of wheat, corn, and other [crops].",
  80028:
      "And We grow therein fresh grapes and alfalfa as fodder for their livestock.",
  80029: "And We grow therein olives and date palms.",
  80030: "And We grow therein orchards of abundant trees.",
  80031: "And We grow therein fruits and that which your livestock graze.",
  80032: "For your benefit and the benefit of your livestock.",
  80033:
      "So, when the great scream comes, that will deafen the ears: the second blowing of the trumpet.",
  80034: "On that Day, man will flee from his brother.",
  80035: "And he will flee from his mother and father.",
  80036: "And he will flee from his wife and children.",
  80037:
      "Each one of them will have what distracts them from the other due to the extreme despair that day.",
  80038: "The faces of the blissful on that day will be luminous,",
  80039:
      "Laughing, and delighted with what Allah had prepared for them from His mercy.",
  80040:
      "And the faces of the wretched will have dust on them on that day.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Allah’s reprimand of His Prophet in regard to ‘Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum proves that the Qur’an is from Allah.\n2. One should pay attention to the ones seeking knowledge and guidance.\n3. The horrors of the Day of Judgement are severe, such that man will only be concerned about himself; even the Prophets will be saying: “I worry about myself only, I worry about myself only!”",
  80041: "Darkness will come over them (their faces).",
  80042:
      "Those described above in that state will be the ones who combined disbelief and depravity.",
  81000:
      "The Overthrowing (Surah At-Takwir)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe perfection of the Quran in reminding the soul of the disruption of the universe on [the Day of] Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  81001: "When the mass of the sun is gathered, and its light vanishes.",
  81002:
      "And when the stars fall one after the other, and their light is erased.",
  81003: "And when the mountains are moved from their places.",
  81004:
      "And when the pregnant she-camels whose people once used to compete with one another for will be neglected and abandoned.",
  81005: "And when wild animals are gathered with human beings on one plain.",
  81006: "And when the seas are lit until they become a fire.",
  81007:
      "And when souls are paired with their like: a sinner will be paired with a sinner, and a pious person will be paired with a pious person.",
  81008: "And when the girl buried alive is asked by Allah.",
  81009: "For what crime were you killed by the person who killed you?",
  81010:
      "And when the slaves' pages of deeds are spread so that each person can read their book of deeds.",
  81011:
      "And when the sky is peeled like the skin is peeled away from a sheep.",
  81012: "And when the Fire is kindled.",
  81013: "And when Paradise is brought near to the heedful.",
  81014:
      "When that occurs, every soul will know what actions it put forth for that day.",
  81015: "Allah swore by the hidden stars before their emergence at night,",
  81016:
      "Following their orbits, and disappearing upon the morning's emergence, like an antelope entering its den, i.e., it's home.",
  81017:
      "And He swore by the first part of the night when it approaches and the last part when it recedes.",
  81018: "And He swore by the morning when its light emerges.",
  81019:
      "Indeed, the Quran sent down to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is Allah's speech that was conveyed by a trustworthy angel, Gabriel (peace be upon him), whom Allah entrusted it to.",
  81020:
      "One who possesses strength and great rank with the Lord of the Throne, may He be Exalted.",
  81021:
      "The inhabitants of the heavens obey him. [He is] entrusted with what he receives from revelation.",
  81022:
      "Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم, who is in your company and whose intellect, trustworthiness, and truthfulness you know, is not insane as you slanderously claim.",
  81023:
      "Your companion has seen Gabriel in the form that he was created in the clear sky's horizon.",
  81024:
      "Your companion is not miserly with you [by] not conveying what he was commanded to convey to you, nor does he take any reward as the fortune-tellers take.",
  81025: "This Quran is not the speech of a devil banished from Allah's mercy.",
  81026:
      "So which path will you tread to deny it is from Allah after all these proofs?",
  81027:
      "The Quran is only a reminder and admonition for the Jinn and humanity.",
  81028: "For whomever of you wishes to be upright on the path of truth.",
  81029:
      "And you do not wish for uprightness or otherwise except that Allah, the Lord of all creation, wishes that.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A person will be gathered with those who resemble him in good or evil.\n2. Burying daughters alive is a great sin about which Allah will question the perpetrator on the day of judgment.\n3. The servant’s will is subservient to Allah’s will.",
  82000:
      "The Cleaving (Surah Al-Infitar)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning mankind from being deceived and forgetting the Day of Resurrection.\n•    Explanation:",
  82001: "When the sky splits apart because of the angels descending from it.",
  82002: "And when the stars fall one after the other, becoming scattered.",
  82003: "And when the seas open into one another and merge.",
  82004:
      "And when the soil of the graves overturns due to the resurrection of the dead from them.",
  82005:
      "Upon that, every soul will know what it put forth of action and what it left behind of unperformed acts.",
  82006:
      "O man who has rejected his Lord, what has made you go against the command of your Lord when He gave you respite and did not hasten your punishment out of His grace?",
  82007:
      "The One who brought you into existence after you were non-existent and made your limbs balanced and proportional.",
  82008:
      "He created you in whatever form He wished to create you. He has favored you as He did not create you in the form of a donkey, monkey, dog, or something else.",
  82009:
      "The matter is not as you perceive, O deluded ones. Rather, you reject the Day of Recompense, failing to work for it.",
  82010: "Indeed, upon you are angels recording your deeds.",
  82011: "Noble in Allah's sight, scribes who write down your deeds.",
  82012: "They know of every deed you do, then they write it down.",
  82013:
      "Indeed, those who are abundant in virtuous acts and obedience will certainly be in everlasting bliss on the Day of Resurrection.",
  82014:
      "And indeed, the people of depravity will certainly be in a fire blazing over them.",
  82015:
      "They will enter it on the Day of Recompense, suffering from its heat.",
  82016:
      "They will never be absent from it. Instead, they will remain in it forever.",
  82017: "What will inform you, O Messenger, what the Day of Judgment is?",
  82018: "Then [once again], what will inform you what the Day of Judgment is?",
  82019:
      "The Day when no one will be able to benefit anyone. The entire matter on that day will belong to Allah alone, acting as He wishes and no one else besides Him.",
  83000:
      "The Defrauders (Surah Al-Mutaffifeen)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning the rejecting wrongdoers of the Day of Resurrection and giving the believers glad tidings of it.\n•    Explanation:",
  83001: "Destruction and loss be upon those who shortchange.",
  83002:
      "They are the ones who, when they have something measured by others, take their full right without any deficiency.",
  83003:
      "And if they measure or weigh for others, they shortchange in volume and weight. That was the state of Medina's people upon the Prophet's صلى الله عليه وسلم migration to them.",
  83004:
      "Do these people who do this evil act not know they will be resurrected before Allah?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Arrogance is an obstacle to following the truth.\n2. The angels record the deeds of the servants by Allah’s order.\n3. The ability of the Creator to create man in any form He wishes.",
  83005:
      "For reckoning and recompense on a great day, due to the tribulations and horrors it contains.",
  83006:
      "The Day when people will stand before the Lord of all creation to face reckoning.",
  83007:
      "The matter is not as you imagined that there is no resurrection after death. The book of the people of depravity from among the disbelievers and hypocrites will surely be in loss in the nethermost depth of the earth.",
  83008: "What will inform you, O Messenger, what Sijjīn is?",
  83009:
      "Indeed, their book is written and will not vanish. There will be nothing added or omitted from it.",
  83010: "Destruction and loss will be for the rejectors on that day.",
  83011:
      "Those who reject the Day of Recompense in which Allah requites His slaves for their actions in the world.",
  83012:
      "None rejects that day except every person who transgresses Allah's limits with abundant sins.",
  83013:
      "When Our verses sent down to Our Messenger are recited to him, he (the rejector) says: They are stories of the earlier nations and are not from Allah.",
  83014:
      "The matter is not as these rejectors envision. Instead, the acts of disobedience they used to gain overtook and shrouded their minds, so they did not see the truth with their hearts.",
  83015:
      "Indeed, they will surely be prevented from seeing their Lord on the Day of Resurrection.",
  83016: "Then, indeed, they will enter the Fire, suffering its heat.",
  83017:
      "Then on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said to them in rebuke: This torment that you faced is what you used to deny in the world when your Messenger informed you of it.",
  83018:
      "The matter is not as you perceived in that there will be no reckoning nor recompense. Indeed, the book of obedient people will be in 'Illiyyun.",
  83019: "What will inform you, O Messenger, what 'Illiyyun is?",
  83020:
      "Indeed, their book is written and will not vanish. There will be nothing added or omitted from it.",
  83021:
      "This book is witnessed by the angels near [to Allah] from every heaven.",
  83022:
      "Indeed, those who do abundant acts of obedience will be in everlasting bliss on the Day of Resurrection.",
  83023:
      "On adorned couches, looking at their Lord and at everything that delights their souls and makes them happy.",
  83024:
      "If you see them, you will see in their faces the effect of gratification in all its beauty and splendor.",
  83025:
      "Their slaves will give them drinks of wine whose containers are sealed.",
  83026:
      "It will give off the fragrance of musk until its very end. For this noble reward, the competitors must compete by doing what Allah is content with, and leaving what earns His discontent and anger.",
  83027: "This sealed drink will be mixed from the spring of Tasnim.",
  83028:
      "This is a spring in the highest part of Paradise, from which those near [to Allah] will drink, pure and untainted. The rest of the believers will drink from it, [but it will be] mixed with other than it.",
  83029:
      "Indeed, those who committed crimes with what they were upon of disbelief used to laugh mockingly at those who believed.",
  83030:
      "When they passed by the believers, they would wink at one another in ridicule and derision.",
  83031:
      "When they would return to their families, they would return happy with what they were upon of disbelief and ridicule of the believers.",
  83032:
      "When they watched the Muslims, they would say: Indeed, these people are surely astray from the path of truth, as they abandoned the religion of their forefathers.",
  83033:
      "Allah did not appoint them to preserve their deeds such that they could make this statement of theirs.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The danger of sins for the heart.\n2. The disbelievers will be deprived of seeing their Lord on the day of judgment.\n3. Mocking the people of religion is a trait of the disbelievers.",
  83034:
      "So, on the Day of Resurrection, those who believed in Allah will laugh at the disbelievers just as the disbelievers used to laugh at them in the world.",
  83035:
      "On adorned couches, they will look at what Allah prepared for them of everlasting bliss.",
  83036:
      "The disbelievers will have been awarded the humiliating torment for their [evil] deeds in the worldly life.",
  84000:
      "The Sundering (Surah Al-Inshiqaq)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding the human being of their return to their Lord, demonstrating their weakness and fluctuating situation.\n•    Explanation:",
  84001: "When the sky ruptures because of the angels descending from it",
  84002: "And listens submissively to its Lord, as it rightly should.",
  84003: "When Allah stretches the earth as leather is stretched.",
  84004:
      "And [the earth] throws out the treasures and the dead in them, emptying itself of them.",
  84005: "And listens submissively to its Lord, as it rightly should.",
  84006:
      "O human being, verily, you are either doing good or evil and will face it on the Day of Resurrection so that Allah may recompense you for it.",
  84007:
      "After describing humanity's acts in general, Allah proceeds to provide details about the state of those who performed good deeds on the Day of Resurrection, stating: \n As for the one given his book of deeds in his right hand.",
  84008:
      "He will have an easy reckoning with Allah, and his actions will be presented to Him without his being taken into account.",
  84009: "And he will return to his family delighted.",
  84010:
      "As for the one who is given his book in his left hand behind his back.",
  84011: "He will call out for destruction to himself.",
  84012: "And he will enter the Fire and be made to suffer its heat.",
  84013:
      "He was amongst his family rejoicing over his acts of disbelief and sins.",
  84014: "He thought that he would not come back to life after death.",
  84015:
      "On the contrary, Allah will bring him back to life just as He created him the first time. Indeed, His Lord was watchful over his condition. None of that was hidden from Him, and He will recompense him for his actions.",
  84016: "Allah swore by the redness of the horizon after sunset.",
  84017: "And He swore by the night and what is gathered therein.",
  84018:
      "And [by] the moon, when it comes together and is complete, becomes a full moon.",
  84019:
      "You, O people, will surely mount upon (i.e., pass through) state after state: from a drop, then a clot, then a piece of flesh, then life, then death, and then resurrection.",
  84020:
      "What is the matter with these disbelievers who do not have faith in Allah and the Last Day?!",
  84021:
      "And when the Quran is recited to them, they do not prostrate to their Lord?!",
  84022:
      "Instead, those who disbelieve reject what their messengers brought to them.",
  84023:
      "Allah knows best what their hearts contain. None of their deeds are hidden from Him.",
  84024:
      "Inform them, O Messenger, of a painful torment that awaits them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The sky and the earth are subjugated to their Lord.\n2. Every person is striving either for good or evil.\n3. The sign of fortune on the day of judgment is receiving one’s book in the right hand. The sign of misfortune is receiving it in the left hand.",
  84025:
      "Except for those who believed in Allah and did righteous deeds, for them is a reward that will never cease: Paradise.",
  85000:
      "The Mansions of the Stars (Surah Al-Buruj)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining Allah's Power, His all-encompassing Knowledge, His support for His allies, and His seizing of His enemies.\n•    Explanation:",
  85001:
      "Allah swore by the sky, encompassing the various stages of the sun, moon, and other celestial bodies.",
  85002:
      "And He swore by the Day of Resurrection in which He promised to gather together all of creation.",
  85003:
      "He then swore by every witness, like the prophet who is a witness over his nation, and everything witnessed, like the nation that is witnessed against by its prophet.",
  85004: "Cursed are those who made a great pit in the earth.",
  85005: "They lit a fire in the pit and threw the believers into it alive,",
  85006: "while they sat around that pit filled with fire.",
  85007:
      "They are witnesses to the torture and exemplary punishment they inflicted upon the believers; they were present during it.",
  85008:
      "The disbelievers did not fault the believers for anything other than their belief in Allah, the Almighty, Whom none can overpower, and the One who is Praised for everything.",
  85009:
      "To Him Alone belong the dominion over the heavens and the earth. He is well aware of everything. No affair of His slaves is hidden from Him.",
  85010:
      "Indeed, those who tortured the believing men and women with fire to turn them away from believing in Allah alone, and did not repent afterward to Allah from their sins, will be in the torment of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. They will be punished by the Fire, which will burn them as a recompense for burning the believers with fire.",
  85011:
      "Those who believed in Allah and did righteous deeds will have gardens with rivers flowing underneath their palaces and trees. This is the reward that has been prepared for them, and this is the ultimate level of success to which no other success comes close.",
  85012:
      "Your Lord's seizure of the oppressor, O Messenger, is powerful indeed, even if He grants him respite for some time.",
  85013:
      "Indeed, it is He who originates creation and punishment, and it is He who restores them.",
  85014:
      "He is Oft-Forgiving of the sins of His slaves who repent, and He loves His friends who are mindful of Him.",
  85015: "Owner of the Noble Throne.",
  85016:
      "Doer of what He wills: pardoning the sins of whoever He wills and punishing whoever He wills. None can compel Him; may He be Exalted.",
  85017:
      "O Messenger, has the news reached you of the armies that set out to battle against the truth and stood against it?",
  85018:
      "[They were the armies of] Pharoah and Thamūd, the people of Saleh (peace be upon him).",
  85019:
      "The impediment to these people's belief is not due to news not reaching them about the destruction of nations that rejected faith before them. Rather, they deny what their messenger came with to follow their own desires.",
  85020:
      "Allah encompasses their deeds and keeps a record of them. He misses nothing from their actions, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  85021:
      "The Quran is neither poetry nor rhyme, as its deniers claim. Rather, it is a noble Quran.",
  85022:
      "[It is] in a tablet that is preserved against any change, distortion, omission, or addition.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. A believer is tested in proportion to his faith.\n2. Giving preference to the safety of one’s faith over the safety of one’s body is a sign of salvation on the day of judgment.\n3. Repentance with its requirements wipes out what is before it.",
  86000:
      "The Nightcommer (Surah At-Tariq)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nExplaining Allah's power and His all-encompassing ability to create man and bring him back to life.\n•    Explanation:",
  86001:
      "Allah swore by the sky, and He swore by the star that knocks at night.",
  86002: "What will inform you, O Messenger, of the status of this great star?",
  86003: "It is the star that pierces the sky with its glimmering light.",
  86004:
      "There is no soul except that Allah has assigned to it an angel recording its deeds for reckoning on the Day of Resurrection.",
  86005:
      "So let the human ponder what Allah created him from, so that Allah's omnipotence and man's inability become clear to him.",
  86006: "Allah created him from spurting water that is spilt into the womb.",
  86007:
      "This water emerges from between the backbone and chest bones of a man.",
  86008:
      "Indeed, since He, the Exalted, created him from that ignoble water, He has the ability to resurrect him after death for reckoning and recompense.",
  86009:
      "On the Day when secrets are tested, the intentions, beliefs, and the like that the hearts used to harbor will be exposed. Because of this, the righteous among them will become distinguished from the corrupt.",
  86010:
      "A person will not have any strength on that day that will prevent them from Allah's torment or an aid to assist them.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The angels preserve man and his actions, whether good or bad, so that he is taken to account for them.\n2. The weakness of the plot of the disbelievers when compared to Allah’s plan, may He be glorified.\n3. Fear of Allah is a reason for taking heed and admonishment.",
  86011:
      "Allah swore by the sky that contains rain because it comes down from the sky time after time.",
  86012:
      "He swore by the earth that cracks open to reveal the plants, fruit, and trees within it.",
  86013:
      "Indeed, this Quran that is sent down to Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم is a word that separates truth from falsehood, honesty from lying.",
  86014:
      "It (The Quran) is not frivolous or falsehood. Rather, it is solemn and true.",
  86015:
      "Indeed, the rejectors of what their Messenger brought plot many schemes to rebuff and invalidate his call.",
  86016:
      "And I plot a scheme to make the religion apparent and nullify falsehood.",
  86017:
      "So, give respite, O Messenger, to these disbelievers. Give them a brief respite, and do not seek to hasten their torment and destruction.",
  87000:
      "The Most High (Surah Al-A'la)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding the soul of the Hereafter and freeing it from worldly attachments.\n•    Explanation:",
  87001:
      "Vindicate your Lord, who is high above His creation, uttering His Name when you remember and revere Him.",
  87002: "Who created man in due proportion and balanced his stature.",
  87003:
      "And determined the species, types, and attributes for all creation. He guided every creation to what is appropriate and suitable for it.",
  87004: "Who brought out from the earth what your animals graze on.",
  87005:
      "Then, He turned it into a dry, blackish straw after it had been green and fresh.",
  87006:
      "We will have you recite, O Messenger, the Quran and gather it within your chest, and you will not forget it. So do not race with Gabriel in recitation out of your eagerness to not forget it.",
  87007:
      "Except for what Allah wishes you to forget for a wisdom. Indeed, He (may He be Exalted) knows what is exposed and what is hidden. Nothing of that is hidden from Him.",
  87008:
      "We will make it easy for you to do the deeds that content Allah and enter you into Paradise.",
  87009:
      "Therefore, advise people with what we revealed to you from the Quran, and remind them so long as the reminder is heard.",
  87010:
      "The one who fears Allah will pay heed to your admonition because he is the one who benefits from admonition.",
  87011:
      "The disbeliever will stay away and run from admonition. He will be the most miserable person in the Afterlife because he will enter the Fire.",
  87012:
      "The one who will enter the Great Fire of the Afterlife suffers and bears its heat forever.",
  87013:
      "Then, he will remain eternally in the Fire. He will neither die as a relief to his insufferable torment nor be able to live a good and decent life.",
  87014:
      "The one who purified himself from shirk (associating partners with Allah) and sins has achieved the objective.",
  87015:
      "And remembered his Lord with the various types of remembrance that He ordained, and performed the prayer in the manner it is ought to be performed.",
  87016:
      "Rather, you prioritize the worldly life and give preference to it over the Hereafter despite the vast disparity between them.",
  87017:
      "The Hereafter is certainly better and superior to worldly existence due to what it contains of delights and pleasures, and it is [infinitely] more lasting. That is because what it contains of bliss shall never cease.",
  87018:
      "Indeed, these instructions and reports We mentioned to you are certainly in the scriptures revealed before the Quran.",
  87019:
      "They are the scriptures revealed to Abraham and Moses (peace be upon them).",
  88000:
      "The Overwhelming (Surah Al-Ghashiyah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding of the Hereafter and its reward and punishment, and considering the evidence for Allah's power.\n•    Explanation:",
  88001:
      "Has word come to you, O Messenger, of the Resurrection that will overwhelm people with its horrors?",
  88002:
      "For people on the Day of Resurrection will either be wretched or blissful. The faces of the wretched will be humiliated and downcast.",
  88003:
      "Tired and strained by chains they will be dragged by and the fetters they will be shackled with.",
  88004: "Those faces will enter a hot fire and suffer its heat.",
  88005: "They will be given to drink from a spring of intensely hot water.",
  88006:
      "They will not have any food to nourish them except among the vilest and filthiest of it from a plant called Shibriq. If it dries up, it becomes poisonous.",
  88007:
      "It neither fattens those who eat it nor does it satisfy their hunger.",
  88008:
      "The faces of the blissful on that day will be full of delight, beauty, and happiness from the bounty they find themselves in.",
  88009:
      "Content with their righteous deeds that they performed in the world, for they will have found the reward of their actions stored for them and multiplied.",
  88010: "In a paradise elevated in place and rank.",
  88011:
      "In the garden, they will not hear any word of falsehood and frivolity, let alone hear any prohibited word.",
  88012:
      "In this paradise, there are flowing springs that they will cause to erupt and direct however they wish.",
  88013: "In it (Paradise) are high couches.",
  88014: "And cups laid out and ready to drink from.",
  88015: "In it are cushions packed closely next to one another.",
  88016: "In it are many carpets spread out everywhere.",
  88017:
      "Allah highlights the contrast between the wretched and the fortunate in the Hereafter. He then draws the attention of the non-believers towards the beauty of His creation and the power it demonstrates. This serves as evidence for them to believe in Him and gain entry into Paradise, thereby becoming among the blissful. He states: \n Do they not look reflecting at the camels, how Allah created them and subjugated them to human beings?!",
  88018:
      "And look at the sky, how He raised it so that it became a preserved ceiling above them that does not fall on them?!",
  88019:
      "And look at the mountains, how He erected them, stabilizing the earth with them such that it does not shake with the people?!",
  88020:
      "And look at the earth, how He spread it out, and made it prepared for people to settle down upon?!",
  88021:
      "After directing them to witness the manifestation of His power, Allah directs His Messenger, stating: \n So admonish, O Messenger, these people and instill fear of Allah's torment. You are but a reminder; all that is upon you is to remind them. As for them attaining faith, that is in Allah's hand alone.",
  88022:
      "You do not have the power to compel them to believe.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The importance of purifying the soul from outward and inward filth.\n2. Inference from created things about the existence of the Creator and His greatness.\n3. The task of the caller is to invite, not to make people follow guidance, because guidance is in Allah’s Hand.",
  88023:
      "However, whoever turns away from faith and rejects Allah and His Messenger,",
  88024:
      "Then Allah will torment him on the Day of Resurrection with the greatest torment by entering him into Hell where they will remain eternally therein.",
  88025: "To Us alone is their return after their death.",
  88026:
      "Then, holding them accountable for their actions is indeed upon Us alone. It is not upon you or anyone else.",
  89000:
      "The Dawn (Surah Al-Fajr)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nClarifying the end result of the oppressors, the wisdom behind tribulation, and reminding of the Hereafter.\n•    Explanation:",
  89001: "Allah (may He be Exalted) swore by the dawn.",
  89002:
      "And swore by the first ten nights of Dhul-Hijjah (11th month of the Islamic lunar calendar).",
  89003: "And swore by the things that come as even and odd.",
  89004:
      "And swore by the night when it arrives, remains, and recedes. The complement of these oaths is: You will certainly be recompensed for your deeds.",
  89005:
      "Is there, in that which was mentioned, an oath that persuades the person of reason?",
  89006:
      "Do you not see, O Messenger, what your Lord did with 'Ād, the people of Hūd, when they rejected their Messenger?!",
  89007:
      "The tribe of 'Ād, which traced its lineage back to its forefather Iram, whose people were lofty in stature.",
  89008: "The likes of which Allah never created in the lands.",
  89009:
      "And [did you not see] how your Lord dealt with Thamūd, the people of Saleh, who would split the stones of the mountains and make homes out of them in the [Valley of] Al-Hijr?",
  89010:
      "And [did you not see] how your Lord dealt with Pharaoh, who had stakes with which he would torment people?",
  89011:
      "All these people transgressed the limits of compulsion and injustice; each [nation] transgressed them in their respective land.",
  89012:
      "So, their increased spreading of disbelief and acts of disobedience caused much corruption within it.",
  89013:
      "Subsequently, Allah made them suffer His severe torment and eradicated them from the face of the earth.",
  89014:
      "Indeed, your Lord, O Messenger, watches over and observes the people's actions, so as to recompense the virtuous with Paradise and the malevolent with the Fire.",
  89015:
      "As nations that Allah destroyed were blessed with power and protection, Allah clarifies that those blessings are not evidence of Allah being pleased with them, stating: \n So, as for a human being, it is from his nature that when his Lord tests him such that He honors and blesses him with wealth, children, and prestige, he thinks that it is because he is held in esteem with Allah. Thus, He says: My Lord has honored me because I am worthy of being honored by Him.",
  89016:
      "And as for when He tests him such that He restricts his provision, then, indeed, he thinks it is because of his insignificance in the sight of his Lord. Thus, he says: My Lord has disgraced me.",
  89017:
      "Nay, for the matter is not as this human envisions that life's bounty is evidence of Allah's contentment with His slave and that misfortune is evidence of the slave's dishonor in the sight of his Lord. Instead, the reality is that you do not honor the orphan with what Allah has provided you of provision.",
  89018:
      "Nor do you encourage each other to feed the poor, who cannot find anything to sustain themselves with.",
  89019:
      "You fiercely devour the rights of the weak, from women and orphans, without considering whether it is permissible.",
  89020:
      "And you love wealth abundantly, so you act miserly in spending it in the path of Allah, hanging onto it.",
  89021:
      "These actions are not befitting of you, for remember when the earth will be moved vigorously and shaken.",
  89022:
      "And your Lord will come, O Messenger, to judge between His slaves, and the angels will also come arranged in rows.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The first ten nights of Dhul-Hijjah enjoy a virtue over the rest of the days of the year.\n2. The affirmation of the coming of Allah on the Day of Judgement as befits His majesty, without anthropomorphizing, likening or descriptively designating.",
  89023:
      "And on that day, Hell will be brought, having seventy thousand reins, each with seventy thousand angels dragging it. On that day, the human being will remember his shortcomings with Allah. But how will the realization on that day benefit him when that will be a day of recompense, not action?",
  89024:
      "He will say, out of intense regret: If only I had put forth good deeds for my Afterlife, which is the true life.",
  89025:
      "On that Day, no one will inflict punishment like Allah's punishment because it will be more severe and longer lasting.",
  89026:
      "Neither will anyone bind in chains like His binding of the disbelievers therein.",
  89027:
      "After mentioning the recompense of the disbelievers, Allah mentions the recompense of the believers, stating: \n As for the believer's soul, it will be said to it at the time of death and on the Day of Resurrection: O sound soul, reassured through faith and righteous action,",
  89028:
      "Return to your Lord, pleased with Him because of the abundant reward you will receive, and Him (may He be Exalted) being pleased with you because of the righteous deeds you possess.",
  89029: "Now enter among My righteous slaves.",
  89030:
      "And enter with them into My Paradise, which I have prepared for them (i.e., My righteous slaves).",
  90000:
      "The City (Surah Al-Balad)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing a human being's neediness, constant struggles, and the means to salvation.\n•    Explanation:",
  90001:
      "Allah swore by the sacred land, which is the Honored [city of] Mecca.",
  90002:
      "Permissible is what you do therein, O Messenger, of killing whoever deserves to be killed and capturing whoever deserves to be captured.",
  90003:
      "And Allah swore by the father of humanity and by all of his descendants.",
  90004:
      "Verily, We have created the human being to undergo weariness and distress from suffering worldly adversities.",
  90005:
      "Does the human think that when he commits sins, no one has power over him, nor are they able to take retribution from him, even if it is his Lord who created him?",
  90006: "He says: I spent a lot of extensively amassed wealth.",
  90007:
      "Does this person who boasts about what he spends think that Allah does not see him and that He will not take him into account regarding his wealth, specifically from where he earned it and on what he spent it?",
  90008: "Did We not create eyes for him with which he sees?",
  90009: "And a tongue and lips with which he speaks?",
  90010: "And We acquainted him with the path of virtue and the path of evil?",
  90011:
      "He is called to traverse the arduous path that separates him from Paradise, so he passes and crosses into it.",
  90012:
      "And what will inform you, O Messenger, about the arduous path that he must cross to enter Paradise?",
  90013: "It is to free a slave, male or female.",
  90014: "Or to feed on a day of famine in which food is scarce,",
  90015: "A child who has lost his father, whom he is related to,",
  90016: "Or a poor person who has no possessions.",
  90017:
      "Then, by being from those who believed in Allah and called one another to be patient in acts of obedience, in refraining from sins, and in tribulation, they advised one another to show mercy toward Allah's slaves.",
  90018:
      "Those characterized with those [preceding] traits are the people of the right.\n\n• Beneficial Points: Freeing slaves, feeding the needy at times of difficulty, bringing faith in Allah and encouraging one another to be merciful and patient are all means of entering Paradise.",
  90019:
      "And those who disbelieved in Our verses that were sent down to Our Messenger are the people of the left.",
  90020:
      "A sealed fire will be set upon them on the Day of Resurrection, in which they will be tormented.",
  91000:
      "The Sun (Surah Ash-Shams)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe longest oath in the Quran emphasizing the importance of purifying the soul through acts of obedience and the severe loss of tainting it through disobedience.\n•    Explanation:",
  91001:
      "Allah swore by the sun, and by the time of sunrise after appearing from its eastern horizon.",
  91002:
      "And swore by the moon when it follows behind it after [the sun's] setting.",
  91003:
      "And swore by the daytime when it reveals whatever is on the face of the earth with its light.",
  91004:
      "And swore by the night when it covers the face of the earth, causing it to become dark.",
  91005: "And swore by the sky and its perfect structure.",
  91006:
      "And swore by the earth and its expansiveness so people can live upon it.",
  91007: "And swore by each soul and by Allah's creation of balance in it.",
  91008:
      "Then He made it understand, without teaching, what is evil so it could avoid it and what is good to approach it.",
  91009:
      "The one who has purified his soul by adorning it with virtues and freeing it of atrocities has attained his objective.",
  91010:
      "And the one who has secretly buried his soul in sins and acts of disobedience has lost.",
  91011:
      "After mentioning the loss of the one who corrupts their soul and conceals it with disobedience, He mentions Thamūd as an example, stating: \n Thamūd rejected their Prophet Saleh due to their transgressing the limits in committing sins and acts of disobedience.",
  91012:
      "When the most wretched among them stood up after his people appointed him for the task.",
  91013:
      "Allah's messenger Saleh (peace be upon him) said to them: Leave the camel of Allah alone; let it drink on its [assigned] day and do not harm it.",
  91014:
      "Then, they rejected their Messenger regarding the camel. The most wretched among them killed it with the people's approval, and consequently, they all became complicit in the sin. As a result, Allah imposed His torment upon them and destroyed them with a scream for their sins. He equally punished them all with destruction.",
  91015:
      "Allah inflicted them with the torment that destroyed them; unafraid of its consequences, may He be Exalted.",
  92000:
      "The Night (Surah Al-Layl)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the condition of creation regarding belief and spending for Allah's sake and the situation of each group.\n•    Explanation:",
  92001:
      "Allah swore by the night when it covers the face of the earth with its darkness.",
  92002:
      "And Allah swore by the day when it reveals itself, becoming apparent.",
  92003: "And He swore by His creation of the two genders: male and female.",
  92004:
      "Indeed, your work, O people, is diverse. So among it are good deeds, which are the cause for entering Paradise, and evil deeds, which are the cause of entering the Fire.",
  92005:
      "So as for the one who only gives whatever is obligatory, such as Zakat (obligatory alms), mandatory family expenses, and expiation, and is heedful of that which Allah has prohibited him from,",
  92006: "And believes in the compensation that Allah has promised him,",
  92007:
      "Then we will make righteous deeds and spending for Allah's sake easy for him.",
  92008:
      "And as for the one who is miserly with his wealth such that he does not spend it toward his obligations and feels self-sufficient through his wealth from needing Allah, such that he does not ask Allah anything from His bounty,",
  92009:
      "And rejects what Allah promised him of compensation and reward for spending his wealth in Allah's path,\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. It is important to purify and nurture the soul in doing good.\n2. Those who help each other in sin, are all equally guilty of it.\n3. Sins are the means of being punished in this world.",
  92010:
      "Then, We will make performing evil deeds easy and doing good difficult for him.",
  92011:
      "The wealth that he was miserly with will not benefit him when he perishes and enters the Fire.",
  92012: "Indeed, it is upon Us to clarify the path of truth from falsehood.",
  92013:
      "And indeed, the Afterlife and the worldly life belong to Us; We deal with them as We wish, and that is not for anyone other than Us.",
  92014:
      "So, I warn you, O people, of a kindled fire if you have disobeyed Allah.",
  92015:
      "None will suffer the heat of this Fire except the most wretched (i.e., the disbeliever).",
  92016:
      "The one who rejected what the Messenger صلى الله عليه وسلم brought and turned away from complying with Allah's command.",
  92017:
      "The especially heedful one will be distanced from it (i.e., the Fire). Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) is amongst the first to be intended by this verse and what follows it.",
  92018:
      "The one who spends his wealth in avenues of virtue to be purified of sin.",
  92019:
      "He does not spend whatever he spends from his wealth to repay any favor done for him by anyone.",
  92020:
      "Through his spending, He only seeks [to behold the] Countenance of his Lord, who is High above His creation.",
  92021:
      "And he will surely be pleased with the generous reward that Allah will grant him.",
  93000:
      "The Morning Hours (Surah Ad-Duha)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing Allah's concern for His Prophet in all his affairs, from beginning to end.\n•    Explanation:",
  93001: "Allah swore by the beginning of the day.",
  93002:
      "And He swore by the night when it darkens, and the people's bustling settles.",
  93003:
      "Your Lord has not left you, O Messenger, nor does He hate you, as the polytheists would say when the revelation paused.",
  93004:
      "And the abode of the Afterlife is undoubtedly better for you than the worldly life, for it contains everlasting bounties that never cease.",
  93005:
      "Your Lord will grant you and your nation abundant rewards until you become content with what He has blessed you and your nation with.",
  93006:
      "He certainly found you a child having lost your father, so He made a refuge for you with your compassionate grandfather Abdul Muttalib and then your uncle Abu Talib.",
  93007:
      "He found you in a state where you did not know what scripture or faith was, so He taught from that what you did not know.",
  93008: "And He found you poor, so He made you self-sufficient.",
  93009:
      "Therefore, do not treat the one who lost their father in childhood poorly, nor belittle them.",
  93010: "And do not rebuke the one asking out of need.",
  93011:
      "And be grateful for the favors of Allah upon you and talk about them.",
  94000:
      "The Relief (Surah Ash-Sharh)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThe blessings bestowed upon the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم by giving him perfected intangible blessings.\n•    Explanation:",
  94001:
      "Verily, We have expanded your chest, causing you to love receiving revelation.",
  94002:
      "And We [Allah] forgave you for all your preceding misdeeds and removed the burden from the Days of Ignorance you lived through.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The status of the Prophet (peace be upon him) according to his Lord is unparalleled.\n2. Being grateful for the favours of Allah is a right of His over His servants.\n3. It is obligatory to show mercy to the weak, and show kindness to them.",
  94003: "Exhausting you to the extent that it almost broke your back.",
  94004:
      "And We elevated for you your mention; you are mentioned in the adhan (call to prayer), the iqamah (call to initiate the prayer), and in other than them.",
  94005:
      "Indeed, with difficulty and strain, there is ease, facilitation, and alleviation.",
  94006:
      "Indeed, with difficulty and strain, there is much ease, facilitation, and alleviation. When you realize that, the harm from your people will neither intimidate you nor deter you from calling toward Allah.",
  94007: "So, when you finish your work, strive to worship your Lord.",
  94008: "And make your desire and resolve toward Allah alone.",
  95000:
      "The Fig (Surah At-Tin)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAllah's blessings upon mankind by establishing their innate nature and form and perfecting the final message.\n•    Explanation:",
  95001:
      "Allah swore by the fig and the place it grows, and the olive and the place it grows, referring to the land of Palestine in which Jesus (peace be upon him) was sent as [a prophet].",
  95002:
      "And He swore by Mount Sinai, where Allah privately conversed with Moses (peace be upon him).",
  95003:
      "And He swore by Mecca, the sacred land which gives sanctuary to whoever enters it, and in which Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم was sent [as a prophet].",
  95004:
      "We have indeed created the human being with the most proportional form and the best appearance.",
  95005:
      "Then We cause him to regress to extreme old age and senility in this world; he does not benefit from his body, just as he does not benefit from it if he corrupts his natural disposition and heads towards the Fire.",
  95006:
      "Except for those who have believed in Allah and performed righteous actions, even if they grow extremely old, they have an everlasting reward that never ceases: Paradise. [That is] because they purified their natural disposition.",
  95007:
      "So, O human being, what causes you to reject the Day of Recompense after seeing the many signs of His ability?",
  95008:
      "Is Allah not the most just and fair of judges by appointing the Day of Resurrection for recompense? Is it conceivable that Allah leaves His slaves in vain, without judging between them, such that He would not recompense the virtuous for their good and the sinner for their evil?",
  96000:
      "The Clot (Surah Al-'Alaq)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nMankind is between being guided through revelation and misguided through arrogance and ignorance.\n•    Explanation:",
  96001:
      "Recite, O Messenger, what Allah reveals to you, starting with the name of your Lord, who created everything.",
  96002:
      "He created the human being from a clot of congealed blood after it had been a drop of semen.",
  96003:
      "Recite, O Messenger, what Allah reveals to you. Your Lord is the Most Generous, and none can come close to His generosity, for He is abundant in magnanimity and benevolence.",
  96004: "The One who taught script and writing through the pen.",
  96005: "He taught the human being that which he did not know.",
  96006:
      "Truly, a depraved human being like Abu Jahl certainly crosses the limit by overstepping Allah's boundaries.",
  96007:
      "Because he views himself as self-sufficient through his possession of prestige and wealth.",
  96008:
      "Indeed, to your Lord, O human being, is the return on the Day of Resurrection. So He will requite each person with what they deserve.",
  96009:
      "Have you seen anything more astonishing than the matter of Abu Jahl, who prevents our slave Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم when he prays at the Kaabah?",
  96010:
      "Have you seen anything more astonishing than the matter of Abu Jahl, who prevents our slave Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم when he prays at the Kaabah?",
  96011:
      "What if this person [who Abu Jahl] prevented is upon guidance and foresight from his Lord?!",
  96012:
      "Or [a person who] would instruct the people to be heedful of Allah by complying with His commands and avoiding His prohibitions; is such a person supposed to be prevented?!\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The pleasure of Allah is the loftiest of objectives.\n2. The importance of reading and writing has been emphasised in Islam.\n3. Wealth is dangerous if it leads to arrogance and distances one from the truth.\n4. Prohibiting good is one of the traits of disbelief.",
  96013:
      "What if this preventer rejects what the Messenger has come with and turns away from it; does he not fear Allah?!",
  96014:
      "Does the preventer of this slave from prayer not realize that Allah sees whatever he does and that nothing is hidden from Him?",
  96015:
      "The matter is not as this ignorant individual perceives. Certainly, if he does not refrain from harming My slave and rejecting him, We will surely seize him, violently dragging him from the front of his head to the Fire.",
  96016:
      "The person of that forelock is a liar in speech and erroneous in deed.",
  96017:
      "So, when he is seized by the front of his head towards the Fire, let him call his companions and associates, asking for their help to save him from the torment.",
  96018:
      "We will summon the guardians of Hell; fierce angels that do not disobey Allah's commands and do as they are ordered. Let him then see which of the two groups is stronger and more capable.",
  96019:
      "It is not as this wrongdoer assumes: that he can cause harm to reach you. So do not obey him in command or prohibition. Prostrate to Allah and draw closer to Him through acts of obedience, for they draw [one] closer to Him.",
  97000:
      "The Power (Surah Al-Qadr)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the virtues of the Night of Decree.\n•    Explanation:",
  97001:
      "Indeed, We sent down the Quran in its entirety to the lowest heaven, just as We began sending it down to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم on the Night of Decree of the month of Ramadan.",
  97002:
      "Do you know, O Prophet, what lies in this night of goodness and blessing?",
  97003:
      "This night is a night of great virtue, for it is better than a thousand months for the one who stands [in prayer] with faith and hope for reward.",
  97004:
      "The angels and Gabriel (peace be upon him) descend in it by their Lord's permission (may He be Exalted) with every matter Allah has decreed to happen that year, whether it be provision, death, birth, or otherwise from what Allah decreed.",
  97005:
      "This blessed night is virtuous, all of it, from its beginning until its end with the break of dawn.",
  98000:
      "The Clear Proof (Surah Al-Bayyinah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the perfection and clarity of Muhammad's message.\n•    Explanation:",
  98001:
      "Those from the Jews, Christians, and polytheists who disbelieved will not leave their consensus and agreement upon disbelief until clear evidence and manifest proof come to them.",
  98002:
      "This clear evidence and manifest proof is the Messenger whom Allah sent to recite the purified pages; only the purified touch it.",
  98003:
      "In those pages, there are true reports and just rulings, which direct people towards that which ensures their righteousness and guidance.",
  98004:
      "Neither the Jews who were given the Torah nor the Christians who were given the Gospel differed [regarding the final Prophet] except after Allah sent them His [last] Prophet. Some became Muslim, and others persisted in disbelief despite knowing their Prophet's truthfulness.",
  98005:
      "The criminality and stubbornness of the Jews and the Christians are evident, for they were not commanded in this Quran except with what their scriptures already had of worshipping Allah alone, refraining from ascribing partners [with Him], establishing prayer, and giving zakat (obligatory alms). Hence, they have been commanded with a straight religion devoid of deviance.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The Night of Decree enjoys a greater virtue than the rest of the nights of the year.\n2. Sincerity in worship is one of the conditions of its acceptance.\n3. Disbelief is the worst trait found amongst the creation, whereas faith in Allah is the purest and loftiest attribute.\n4. Fearing Allah is the means of attaining His pleasure.\n5. The earth will testify against the deeds on the children of Adam.",
  98006:
      "Indeed, those who disbelieved from the Jews, Christians, and polytheists will enter Hell on the Day of Resurrection, remaining therein forever. Those are the worst of creation due to their disbelief in Allah and rejection of His Messenger.",
  98007:
      "Indeed, those who believed in Allah and performed righteous deeds, are the ones who are the best of creation.",
  98008:
      "Their reward with their Lord, may He be Exalted and Transcendent, is gardens in which rivers flow beneath its trees and palaces, remaining therein forever. Allah is pleased with them because they believe in Him and obey Him. And they are pleased with Him because what reaches them of His mercy. This mercy is attained by the one who fears his Lord and so complies with His command and avoids His prohibitions.",
  99000:
      "The Earthquake (Surah Az-Zalzalah)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding of the terrors of the Day of Resurrection and the precise accounting within it.\n•    Explanation:",
  99001:
      "When the earth will be shaken vigorously, which will happen on the Day of Resurrection.",
  99002:
      "And the earth will expel what it contains from the dead and other things.",
  99003:
      "And the human being will say, out of bewilderment:What is the matter with the earth? It is moving and shaking!",
  99004:
      "On that great Day, the Earth will report what was committed upon it of good and evil.",
  99005: "Because Allah will have informed it and commanded it to do so.",
  99006:
      "On that great Day in which the earth will quake, people will depart from the place of reckoning in groups to witness the deeds they committed in the world.",
  99007:
      "So, whoever does a small ant's weight in virtual and benevolent deeds will see it before him.",
  99008:
      "And whoever does a small ant's weight in evil deeds will see it as well.",
  100000:
      "The Galloping Steeds (Surah Al-'Adiyat)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning mankind against ingratitude and greed by reminding them of the Hereafter.\n•    Explanation:",
  100001:
      "Allah swore by the horses that gallop such that their breathing can be heard due to the intensity of the galloping.",
  100002:
      "And swore by the horses that spark fire with their hooves when they strike stones from the intensity of the strike upon them.",
  100003: "And swore by the horses that charge at the enemy in the morning.",
  100004: "Creating clouds of dust from their galloping.",
  100005:
      "Then, they end up with their riders amidst the enemy group.\n\n• Beneficial Points: It is in the nature of man to love wealth.",
  100006:
      "Indeed, the human being certainly withholds the virtue his Lord seeks from him.",
  100007:
      "And indeed, he is certainly a witness to his withholding of virtue; he cannot deny that clear reality.",
  100008:
      "And indeed, he is miserly with his wealth due to his extreme love for it.",
  100009:
      "Does this person, deceived by the worldly life, not realize what awaits him when Allah resurrects the dead in their graves and extracts them from the earth for accountability and recompense? [The day] when intentions, beliefs, and all else within the hearts will be made apparent.",
  100010:
      "Does this person, deceived by the worldly life, not realize what awaits him when Allah resurrects the dead in their graves and extracts them from the earth for accountability and recompense? [The day] when intentions, beliefs, and all else within the hearts will be made apparent.",
  100011:
      "Indeed, their Lord will certainly be All-Informed on that day; none of His slaves' affairs will be hidden from Him, and He will recompense them accordingly.",
  101000:
      "The Calamity (Surah Al-Qari'ah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nThrashing the hearts to evoke the terrors of the [Day of] Resurrection and people's conditions on the scales.\n•    Explanation:",
  101001:
      "[It is] the Hour that thrashes people's hearts from the immensity of its horrors.",
  101002:
      "What is this hour that thrashes people's hearts from the immensity of its horrors?",
  101003:
      "And what can make you comprehend, O Messenger, what this Hour that thrashes people's hearts from the immensity of its horrors is? Indeed, it is the Day of Resurrection.",
  101004:
      "The Day when the people's hearts are struck, they will resemble scattered moths spread all over the place.",
  101005:
      "And the mountains will be like fluffed wool in their agile movement and motion.",
  101006: "So, as for the one whose righteous deeds outweigh his evil deeds,",
  101007:
      "Then he will be in a pleasant life, which he will attain in Paradise.",
  101008: "And as for the one whose evil deeds outweigh his righteous deeds,",
  101009:
      "His abode and permanent residence on the Day of Resurrection will be Hell.",
  101010: "And what can make you comprehend, O Messenger, what it is?",
  101011: "It is a fire of intense heat.",
  102000:
      "The Rivalry in Worldly Increase (Surah At-Takathur)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nReminding those who hoard wealth and are distracted with this worldly life with the graves and the being called to account.\n•    Explanation:",
  102001:
      "O people, boasting with one another over wealth and offspring has distracted you from Allah's obedience.",
  102002: "Until you die and enter your graves.",
  102003:
      "You should not have let boasting about these matters distract you from worshipping Allah; you will come to know the consequences of that preoccupation.",
  102004: "Then you will surely know its consequences.",
  102005:
      "If you were to truly know with certainty that you are to be resurrected to Allah and that He will requite you for your deeds, you would not have become preoccupied with boasting with one another over wealth and offspring.",
  102006:
      "By Allah, you will most surely witness the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.",
  102007:
      "Then, you will most surely truly witness it with undoubtful certainty.",
  102008:
      "On the Day of Judgment, Allah will surely inquire about the bounties He granted you, such as your health, independence, and other similar blessings.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. The danger of boasting with one another and being proud of wealth and offspring.\n2. The disbelievers will witness the hellfire on the Day of Judgement.\n3. On the Day of Judgement, the people will be questioned regarding the favours Allah favoured them with in the world.",
  103000:
      "Time (Surah Al-'Asr)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWays to be saved from loss.\n•    Explanation:",
  103001:
      "Allah (may He be Exalted) swore by the time of 'Asr (the late afternoon).",
  103002: "Indeed, the human being is surely in loss and destruction.",
  103003:
      "Except for those who believed in Allah and His messengers, performed virtuous deeds, and encouraged truth towards one another and stayed patient upon it. Those described with these qualities are saved in their worldly life and the Hereafter.",
  104000:
      "The Traducer (Surah Al-Humazah)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nWarning against mocking the believers due to being deceived by abundant wealth.\n•    Explanation:",
  104001:
      "Evil consequences and severe torment are upon the one who frequently backbites and slanders people.",
  104002:
      "Whose concern is to amass wealth and count it; he has no concern other than that.",
  104003:
      "He thinks his amassed wealth will save him from death, remaining immortal in this worldly life.",
  104004:
      "The matter is not as this ignorant person envisions; he will certainly be thrown into Hellfire that crushes and breaks everything thrown into it from its agonizing torment.",
  104005:
      "And what can make you comprehend, O Messenger, this fire that smashes everything thrown into it?",
  104006: "Indeed, it is the blazing fire of Allah.",
  104007: "That penetrates the bodies of people until it reaches their hearts.",
  104008:
      "Verily, it closes up around those punished within it, sealing them in.",
  104009:
      "With towering extended columns, such that they are unable to leave it.",
  105000:
      "The Elephant (Surah Al-Fil)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing Allah's Omnipotence and His assault on those who invaded His Sacred House.\n•    Explanation:",
  105001:
      "O Messenger, do you not know how your Lord dealt with Abraha and his army, known as the People of the Elephant, when they intended to demolish the Kaaba?",
  105002:
      "Verily, Allah made their evil plot to destroy it in vain, for they did not achieve what they hoped to try to turn the people away from the Kaaba. They did not accomplish any part of it.",
  105003: "He sent birds upon them that came to them in flocks upon flocks,",
  105004: "Striking them with stones of clay.",
  105005:
      "So, Allah made them like the leaves of crops eaten and trampled upon by animals.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Whoever does not bring faith, do good deeds and encourage others in remaining steadfast upon the truth and being patient, has lost out.\n2. Backbiting and taunting people is forbidden.\n3. Allah defends His sacred house.",
  106000:
      "Quraysh (Surah Quraysh)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nNoting Allah's blessing upon the Quraysh and Allah's right upon them.\n•    Explanation:",
  106001: "Because of the custom of the Quraysh and their familiarity,",
  106002:
      "With the winter journey to Yemen and the summer journey to the Levant in safety,",
  106003:
      "Let them worship Allah alone, the Lord of this Sacred House who made this journey easy for them, and let them not ascribe any partners to Him.",
  106004:
      "Who fed them from hunger and gave them security from fear, through the reverence he placed in the hearts of the Arabs for the Sacred Sanctuary and its inhabitants.",
  107000:
      "The Small Kindnesses (Surah Al-Ma'un)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the attributes of those who reject Judgment Day.\n•    Explanation:",
  107001:
      "Do you know the one who denies recompense on the Day of Resurrection?",
  107002: "For he is the one who harshly repulses the orphan from his need.",
  107003: "And does not enjoin upon himself nor others to feed the pauper.",
  107004:
      "So, destruction and torment be upon those who perform the prayer, who are heedless of their prayer, unconcerned with it to the point that its time expires.",
  107005:
      "So, destruction and torment be upon those who perform the prayer, who are heedless of their prayer, unconcerned with it to the point that its time expires.",
  107006:
      "Who show off through their prayers and deeds, failing to perform their virtuous deeds sincerely for Allah.",
  107007:
      "And they avoid helping others with that which there is no harm [to them] in helping with.",
  108000:
      "The Abundance (Surah Al-Kawthar)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing Allah's blessing upon His Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم as abundantly good and defending him.\n•    Explanation:",
  108001:
      "Indeed, We have granted you, O Messenger, abundant goodness. Among it is the river of Kawthar in Paradise.",
  108002:
      "So give the thanks [due to] Allah for this blessing by praying and slaughtering for His sake alone, as opposed to the offerings of sacrifice the polytheists perform, seeking nearness to their idols.",
  108003:
      "Indeed, your hater is cut off from every goodness and will be forgotten. If recalled, he will be mentioned negatively.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. In Islam, security is important.\n2. Turning the orphan away and not encouraging others to feed the poor are traits of the disbelievers.\n3. The status of prayer in Islam is emphasised.\n4. Showing off is one of the illnesses of the heart, and it nullifies deeds.\n5. Being grateful for favours increases them.",
  109000:
      "The Disbelievers (Surah Al-Kafiroon)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nAbsolving oneself from disbelief and its people.\n•    Explanation:",
  109001: "Say, O Messenger: O you disbelievers in Allah.",
  109002:
      "I will not presently nor in the future worship the idols you worship.",
  109003: "Nor are you worshipping what I worship, and that is Allah alone.",
  109004: "Nor am I worshipping what you have worshipped of idols.",
  109005: "Nor are you worshipping what I worship, and that is Allah alone.",
  109006:
      "You have your religion, which you have invented for yourselves, and I have my religion, that Allah sent down to me.",
  110000:
      "The Divine Support (Surah An-Nasr)\nMedinan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nGiving the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم the good news of victory and the completion of the mission.\n•    Explanation:",
  110001:
      "When Allah's victory, O Messenger, arrives for your religion, becoming fortified, and the conquest of Mecca comes to pass.",
  110002: "And you see the people entering Islam, delegation after delegation.",
  110003:
      "Then know that is a sign of nearing the end of the duty you were sent with. So, exalt your Lord by praising Him, thanking Him for the blessing of victory and conquest, and seeking His forgiveness. Indeed, He is the Accepter of Repentance, receiving His slaves' contrition and forgiving them.",
  111000:
      "The Rope of Palm Fiber (Surah Al-Masad)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nDescribing the loss of Abu Lahab and his wife.\n•    Explanation:",
  111001:
      "Both hands of the paternal uncle of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم, Abu Lahab, son of 'Abd al-Muttalib, have perished from his futile deeds, for he used to harm the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم. His efforts have failed.",
  111002:
      "What need did his wealth and children fulfill for him? They did not defend him against torment nor bring him mercy.",
  111003:
      "He will enter the blazing Fire on the Day of Resurrection and suffer its heat.",
  111004:
      "And his wife, Umm Jamil, who used to harm the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم by throwing thorns into his path, will also enter it.",
  111005:
      "Around her neck will be a tightly bound rope, with which she will be led into the Fire.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. There should be clear distinction from the disbelievers.\n2. Favours should be repaid with gratitude.\n3. Abu Lahab and his wife are both wretched.",
  112000:
      "The Sincerity (Surah Al-Ikhlas)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nSingling out Allah with worship and perfection and exalting Him from having a son, father, or partner.\n•    Explanation:",
  112001:
      "Say, O Messenger: He is Allah, singular in the [attribute] of being worshipped. There is none worthy of worship other than Him.",
  112002:
      "He is the Master to whom belongs complete supremacy in the attributes of perfection and beauty, whom all creation seek for their needs.",
  112003:
      "The One who does not give birth to anyone, nor did anyone give birth to Him. He has neither offspring (may He be Exalted) nor parent.",
  112004: "Nor is there anyone like Him from His creation.",
  113000:
      "The Daybreak (Surah Al-Falaq)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nEncouragement to hold fast to Allah against evil.\n•    Explanation:",
  113001:
      "Say, O Messenger: I seek refuge in the Lord of the morning, and I seek His protection.",
  113002: "From the evil of what harms from [all of] creation.",
  113003:
      "And I seek refuge in Allah from the evils that appear at night of harmful creatures and thieves.",
  113004:
      "And I seek refuge in Him from the evil of the sorceresses who blow into knots.",
  113005:
      "And I seek refuge in Him from the evil of the jealous one when he acts out of jealousy.",
  114000:
      "Mankind (Surah An-Nas)\nMeccan Surah\n•    Surah Objective(s):    \nEncouragement to seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the Devil and his whisperings.\n•    Explanation:",
  114001:
      "Say, O Messenger: I seek refuge in the Lord of the people and seek His protection.",
  114002:
      "The Sovereign of humanity, who does whatever He wishes with them. They have no [absolute] ruler other than Him.",
  114003: "He is their rightful deity; they do not have a true god except Him.",
  114004:
      "[I seek refuge] from the devil's evil, who casts his whisper upon the human being when he neglects Allah's remembrance and delays it when he does remember.",
  114005: "He casts his whispers into people's hearts.",
  114006:
      "And he (the devil) could be from humanity as well as from the jinn.\n\n• Beneficial Points:\n1. Affirmation of the qualities of perfection for Allah and negation of any deficiencies from Him.\n2. Magic is affirmed to be true, and it is possible to treat it.\n3. Satanic whispers can be countered with the remembrance of Allah and seeking refuge in Him from Satan.",
};

String? getTafsirMokhtasar(int surah, int ayah) =>
    _mokhtasar[surah * 1000 + ayah];
